COLLDATA("sh28171","en",[[1,"My nation is a nation shown mercy; there is no punishment for it in the Hereafter. When the Day of Resurrection comes, every Muslim man will be given a man from the People of the Book, and it will be said: O Muslim, this is your ransom from the Fire."],[2,"Two men brought a dispute over a camel to the Prophet ﷺ, each claiming it was his. Each of them came with two witnesses testifying that the camel was his, so the Prophet ﷺ ruled that it should be split in half between them."],[3,"Do not marry women except to suitable matches, and no one should give them in marriage except their guardians, and there is no dowry less than ten dirhams."],[4,"There is no one whom I will not recognize on the Day of Resurrection. He said: How will you recognize them, O Messenger of Allah, among the multitude of creatures? He said: \"Consider if you entered an enclosure containing dark black horses, and in it was a horse with a white blaze and white stockings—would you not recognize it among them?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"My nation on that day will have white blazes and white stockings from ablution.\""],[5,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over Madinah twice—and he was blind—to lead the people in prayer."],[6,"The jinn were sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twice, and the nobles of the jinn were in Nasibin."],[7,"Jibril used to come to me in the form of Dihyah al-Kalbi. Anas said: Dihyah was a large, handsome, fair-skinned man."],[8,"When I was taken up (on the Night Journey), I passed by people who had fingernails of copper, scratching their faces and chests. I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: These are those who consume the flesh of people and attack their honor."],[9,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[10,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick man from his Companions who was in pain—and I was with him. He took hold of his hand and placed his hand on his forehead—and he considered that part of completing the visit to the sick—and said: Allah said: I inflict My fire upon My believing servant so that it may be his portion of the Fire in the Hereafter."],[11,"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise: four before Zuhr, two after it, two before 'Asr, two after Maghrib, two after 'Isha, and two before Fajr."],[12,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not leave us in confusion about our religion: he forbade us from blowing into the drink."],[13,"If you swear an oath, then see what is better, do that which is better and expiate your oath."],[14,"O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, do not ask for authority, for if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it, but if you are given it after asking, you will be left to it. And if you swear an oath, then see something else better than it, do that which is better and expiate your oath."],[15,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the like of it. No one narrated this hadith from ʿUrfuṭah except al-Walīd b. ʿAbbād, nor from al-Walīd except Ismāʿīl b. ʿAyyāsh. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. al-Ḍaḥḥāk was alone in transmitting it."],[16,"He used to raise his hands when saying the takbīr for bowing, and when saying the takbīr as he went down into prostration."],[17,"There is no Muslim who commits a sin except that the angel entrusted with recording his sins waits for three hours. If he seeks Allah’s forgiveness for that sin within any of those hours, it will not be held against him on the Day of Resurrection."],[18,"Whoever of you comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform the ritual bath."],[19,"I went early to Ṣafwān b. ʿAssāl al-Murādī, and he said: What brought you early, O Zirr? I said: I am seeking knowledge. He said: Go early as a scholar or a learner, and do not go beyond that, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There is no Muslim servant who seeks knowledge except that the angels lower their wings for him, out of pleasure with what he does. He said: Then I asked him about wiping over the leather socks, and I said: I have some unease about that. He said: When we traveled with the Prophet ﷺ, we were commanded not to remove our leather socks for three nights and their days, except for major ritual impurity, but not for defecation, urination, or sleep. And for the resident it is a day and a night."],[20,"Iḥṣān is of two kinds: chastity and marriage."],[21,"From ʿUrwah b. al-Zubayr, that he came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said: O Ibn ʿAbbās, how long have you led people astray! He said: And what is that, O ʿUrayyah? He said: A man enters the state of iḥrām for Hajj or ʿUmrah, and when he has performed the circumambulation, you claim that he is released from iḥrām, but Abū Bakr and ʿUmar used to forbid that. He said: Are they, woe to you, more preferable to you than what is in the Book of Allah and what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prescribed for his companions and his nation? ʿUrwah said: They were more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah and what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prescribed than I and you. Ibn Abī Mulaykah said: So ʿUrwah refuted him."],[22,"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform the ritual bath."],[23,"Any woman who fasts without her husband’s permission, and he wants her for something, and she refuses him, Allah records for her three major sins."],[24,"Three supplications are answered without doubt: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of a parent against his child, and the supplication of the traveler."],[25,"Information is not like seeing with one's own eyes; for Allah, exalted is He, told Musa b. Imran what his people had done after him, and he did not throw down the tablets, but when he saw it with his own eyes he threw down the tablets."],[26,"When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[27,"The Prophet ﷺ had Safiyyah observe an istibra' of one menstrual cycle."],[28,"Take a midday nap, for Shaytan does not take a midday nap."],[29,"Whoever does you a favor, repay him. If you are unable to repay him, then supplicate for him until you know that you have thanked him, for Allah is thankful and loves the thankful."],[30,"Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat is deducted from his deeds every day."],[31,"Do not make the mosques thoroughfares, except for dhikr or prayer."],[32,"Whoever removes something harmful from the path of the Muslims, Allah records a good deed for him, and if a good deed is recorded for him, He admits him to Paradise by it."],[33,"Do not eat reclining, and do not step over people's necks on Friday."],[34,"They mentioned kinship ties in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we said, 'Whoever maintains his kinship ties will have his lifespan extended.' He said, 'It is not that his lifespan is increased. Allah, exalted is He, said: \"When their term comes, they will not remain behind an hour, nor will they precede [it].\" But it is a man who has righteous offspring who supplicate for him after him, and that reaches him. That is what is meant by his lifespan being extended.'"],[35,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite aloud 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim'."],[36,"By My might and majesty, I will surely take vengeance on the wrongdoer in this world and the Hereafter, and I will surely take vengeance on the one who sees someone wronged and is able to help him but does not do so."],[37,"If one of you has a servant who has spared him his hardship, let him feed him; if he does not do so, let him hand him a morsel."],[38,"That his father had sent him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an errand. He said: I found him sitting with his companions in the mosque, and I was not able to speak to him. When he prayed Maghrib, he stood praying voluntary rakʿahs until the muezzin called the adhan for ʿIsha’ and the people gathered. Then he prayed the obligatory prayer and stood praying voluntary rakʿahs until those who remained in the mosque left. Then he went to his home, and I followed him. When he heard my footsteps, he said, “Who is this?” and turned toward me. I said, “Ibn ʿAbbas.” He said, “The cousin of the Messenger of Allah?” I said, “The cousin of the Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Welcome to the cousin of the Messenger of Allah. What brings you?” I said, “My father sent me with such-and-such.” He said, “Have you just come?” I said, “No.” He said, “Since you have not left at this hour of yours, you will not leave.” Then he entered his house and I entered with him. I said to myself: I will certainly observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tonight. He slept until I heard his snoring, then woke up and cast his eyes to the sky and recited these verses from Surat Al ʿImran: “Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth…” the five verses, until he reached “…indeed, You do not break Your promise.” Then he said: “O Allah, place in my hearing light, and in my sight light, and above me light, and below me light, and on my right light, and on my left light, and grant me light with You.” Beside him was a small basin of brass with a cover on which there was a siwak. He used the siwak, then performed ablution, then prayed two rakʿahs. Then he went back and slept again until I heard his snoring, then woke up and recited the verses and made the supplication, then used the siwak, then performed ablution, then prayed two rakʿahs. Then he slept until I heard his snoring, then woke up and recited the verses, then made the supplication, then used the siwak, then performed ablution, then prayed two rakʿahs. Then he slept until I heard his snoring, then woke up and recited the verses and made the supplication, then used the siwak, then performed ablution, then prayed a prayer in which I knew he was performing Witr. Then he said, “Has the boy slept?” I said, “No.” I got up and performed ablution, then came and stood at his left side. He took hold of my ears with his two fingers and turned me around until he placed me on his right side. Then he prayed the two rakʿahs of Fajr, then went out for the prayer."],[39,"Five signs have passed, and five remain: the splitting of the moon has passed—we have seen it—the smoke has passed, the great seizure has passed, and the Romans have passed."],[40,"Actions are only by intentions, and each person will have only what he intended. Whoever’s emigration was to Allah and His Messenger, his emigration is to Allah and His Messenger. Whoever’s emigration was for worldly gain he might attain or a woman he might marry, his emigration is to what he emigrated for."],[41,"He forbade fasting on Friday unless [a person is already fasting] days before it."],[42,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I feared that I might have been doomed. He said, “Why?” I said: Allah forbade a man to be praised for what he has not done, and I find myself loving praise. Allah forbade pride, and I find myself loving beauty. Allah forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Would you not be pleased to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise praiseworthy?” He said: Of course, O Messenger of Allah. So he lived praiseworthy, and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylimah."],[43,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on the night when the group of jinn came to him. A man from the jinn brought a flame of fire to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Jibril said: O Muhammad, shall I teach you words that if you say them, his flame will be extinguished and he will fall on his nose? Say: I seek refuge in the Noble Face of Allah, and in the perfect words of Allah, which no righteous or wicked person can surpass, from the evil of what descends from the sky and what ascends in it, and from the evil of what He has created in the earth and what comes out of it, and from the evil of the trials of the night and the day, and from the evil of the visitors of the night and the day, except a visitor who comes with good, O Most Merciful."],[44,"Eloquence, all eloquence, is a branch of Satan."],[45,"You will continue fighting the disbelievers until you fight a people with small eyes, snub noses, whose faces are like hammered shields."],[46,"Whoever of you attends the Friday prayer should perform a major ablution."],[47,"A group of my community will continue fighting at the gates of Damascus and its surroundings, and at the gates of Jerusalem and its surroundings. The desertion of those who desert them will not harm them; they will remain victorious until the Hour comes."],[48,"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer should perform a major ablution."],[49,"Whoever comes to Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[50,"The Prophet ﷺ prohibited the sale and gift of wala' (the right of inheritance from a freed slave)."],[51,"People will be raised on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. Aisha said: \"What about the private parts?\" He said: \"On that day, each person will have enough to preoccupy him.\""],[52,"The Prophet ﷺ taught a man to say when he went to bed: 'O Allah, I turn my face to You, and I entrust my back to You, and I commit my affair to You, and I submit myself to You, in fear and hope of You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You have revealed, and in Your Prophet whom You have sent.' If he dies that night, he will be forgiven."],[53,"Fasting is a shield from the Fire."],[54,"O Allah, intensify Your punishment on Mudar, and make it years of famine like the years of Joseph."],[55,"Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and they give fatwas without knowledge, so they go astray and lead others astray."],[56,"Whoever comes to Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[57,"You and your wealth belong to your father."],[58,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a leather tent of his. I greeted him, then said: 'May I enter?' He said: 'Enter.' So I put my head in, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing ablution thoroughly. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may I enter completely?' He said: 'All of you.' When I entered, he said to me: 'Count six signs before the Hour: the death of your Prophet.' Awf said: I was struck by that with a grief like none before. He said: 'Say: One.' I said: 'One.' He said: 'And the conquest of Jerusalem, and a tribulation that will occur among you, reaching the homes of the Arabs, and a disease that will afflict you like the qu'as of sheep, and wealth will become widespread among you, until a man is given a hundred dinars and remains discontented, and a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar, but they will betray you and come against you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand.'"],[59,"Hijrah is of two kinds: one is to abandon sins, and the other is to migrate to Allah and His Messenger. Hijrah does not cease as long as repentance is accepted, and repentance remains accepted until the sun rises from the west. When it rises, every heart will be sealed with what it contains, and people will be spared from action."],[60,"Until one moonlit, clear night, two women from Khuza'ah came and circumambulated the House, then mentioned Isaf and Na'ilah, two idols they used to worship. I stuck my head out from behind the curtains and said: 'Mount one of them on the other.' They became angry and said: 'By Allah, if our men were present, you would not have said this.' I went out following their tracks until they met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Who are you two? From whom are you? From where have you come? What brought you?' They told him the news. He said: 'Where did you leave the Sabian?' They said: 'We left him between the curtains and the building.' He said to them: 'Did he say anything to you?' They said: 'Yes, a word that fills the mouth.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, then they slipped away. I came forward until I reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then I greeted him at that point. He said: 'Who are you? From whom are you? From where are you? From where have you come? What brought you?' I began to inform him of the news. He said: 'From where were you eating and drinking?' I said: 'From the water of Zamzam.' He said: 'Indeed, it is a food that satisfies.' With him was Abu Bakr, who said: 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me to feed him supper.' He said: 'Yes.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out walking, and Abu Bakr took my hand until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at the door of Abu Bakr's house. Then Abu Bakr entered his house and brought some raisins from the raisins of Ta'if, and began throwing them to us handful by handful, and we ate from them until we were full. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O Abu Dharr.' I said: 'At your service.' He said: 'A land has been shown to me, a land of palm trees, which I think is Tihamah. Go out to your people and call them to what you have entered.' He said: So I went out until I came to my mother and brother and informed them of the news. They said: 'We have no desire to turn away from the religion you have entered.' So they became Muslims. Then we went out until we came to Madinah, and I informed my people. They said: 'We have believed you, but we will meet Muhammad ﷺ.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, we met him. Ghifar said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Dharr has informed us of what you taught him, and we have become Muslims and testified that you are the Messenger of Allah.' Then Aslam of Khuza'ah came forward and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have desired and entered what our brothers and allies entered.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Aslam, may Allah grant them peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them.' Then Abu Bakr took my hand and said: 'O Abu Dharr.' I said: 'At your service, O Abu Bakr.' He said: 'Were you devoted to worship in your Jahiliyyah?' I said: 'Yes, I saw myself standing before the sun, praying continuously until its heat hurt me, then I would fall as if I were a worn-out garment.' He said to me: 'Where did you face?' I said: 'I do not know except where Allah directed me, until Allah brought Islam to me.'"],[61,"O son of Adam, if you give what is surplus, that is better for you, and if you withhold it, that is worse for you. Begin with those you support, and Allah does not blame for sufficiency. The upper hand is better than the lower hand."],[62,"The first thing for which the servant will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection is that it will be said: Did I not make your body healthy? And give you to drink from cold water?"],[63,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a military expedition he undertook, and the people were afflicted by severe hunger. The people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to slaughter some of their riding camels, and the Messenger of Allah was about to grant them permission in that matter. Then Umar b. al-Khattab said: Consider, O Messenger of Allah—if we slaughter our riding camels, then meet our enemy tomorrow while we are hungry and on foot? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What do you think, O Umar? He said: Summon the people with the remnants of their provisions, then supplicate for us for blessing in it, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will surely suffice us through your supplication, if Allah wills. He said: It was as though a covering had been over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and was removed. He called for a cloth and ordered that it be spread out. Then he summoned the people with the remnants of their provisions, and they came with what they had. Among the people were those who brought a handful of food or a bowl, and among them were those who brought something like an egg. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that it be placed on that cloth. Then he supplicated for blessing in it and spoke as much as Allah willed him to speak. Then he called out in the army and they came. Then he ordered them and they ate and were satisfied, and they filled their vessels and their provision bags. Then he called for a small water skin and it was placed before him. Then he called for water and poured it into it. Then he ejected some saliva into it and spoke as much as Allah willed him to speak. Then he inserted his little finger into it, and I swear by Allah, I saw the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gushing forth like springs of water. Then he ordered the people, and they drank and gave water to others and filled their water skins and their water vessels. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars showed. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger. No one meets Allah with these two on the Day of Resurrection except that he enters Paradise, whatever he was upon."],[64,"Whoever has bad character among slaves, riding beasts, and children, then recite in his ear: 'Do they seek other than the religion of Allah?'"],[65,"He forbade breastfeeding from a foolish woman."],[66,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us one morning and delivered a sermon that made the hearts tremble and the eyes shed tears. We said: O Messenger of Allah, you have admonished us with the admonition of one bidding farewell, so give us a covenant. He said: You must have taqwa of Allah, and hearing and obedience, even if an Abyssinian slave is placed over you. Those who remain after me will see great disagreement, so you must adhere to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided, righteous caliphs. Cling to it with your molar teeth. And beware of newly introduced matters, for every bid'ah is misguidance."],[67,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me what is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me. He looked up at me and then looked down, and said: 'A little prophet.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, a little prophet of good or a little prophet of evil? He said: Rather a little prophet of good. Do not eat the meat of domesticated donkeys, nor any fanged beast of prey."],[68,"We came to the Messenger of Allah as a delegation of seven or eight, all of us seeking some need, and I was the last of them to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have left behind those who claim that emigration has ceased. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Your need is better than their need. Emigration will never cease as long as the disbelievers are fought."],[69,"When one of you points his spear at a man, if the tip of his spear is at the base of his throat and he says: There is no god but Allah, then let him lift the spear away from him."],[70,"Iyaḍ b. Ḥimār al-Nahshalī gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a horse, and he said: I dislike the froth of the polytheists."],[71,"He used to raise his hands level with his shoulders when he said the takbir, when he bowed, and when he prostrated."],[72,"I asked Aisha about the character of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: His character was the Quran. He became angry for its anger and was pleased for its pleasure."],[73,"When one of you puts on sandals, let him start with the right, and when he takes them off, let him start with the left."],[74,"The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is a trustee. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins."],[75,"The Prophet ﷺ placed one hand over the other in prayer."],[76,"The night prayer is two by two, and when you fear the approach of dawn, then pray one witr."],[77,"Whoever sits in a gathering where there is much idle talk, let him say before he gets up: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise. There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.' For it will be forgiven for him what occurred in that gathering."],[78,"A believer is not stung from the same hole twice."],[79,"The prayer of the night and the day is two by two."],[80,"If a muhrim cannot find an izar, let him wear trousers, and whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear khuffs."],[81,"People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, and a caller will call out: 'Is it not just of Me to assign to every people what they used to worship?' Then their gods will be raised for them, and they will follow them until no one remains except the believers. It will be said to them: 'What is the matter with you?' They will say: 'We do not see our god whom we used to worship.' He said: 'Then He—Blessed and Exalted—will manifest Himself to them.'"],[82,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: 'Which land is most sacred?' It was said: 'Makkah.' He said: 'Which month is most sacred?' He said: 'Dhu al-Hijjah.' He said: 'Which day is most sacred?' He said: 'The Day of Sacrifice, the day of the greatest Hajj.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: 'Indeed your blood and your wealth are sacred to you until you meet your Lord, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours.' So I do not think it is right that blood be shed in the sanctuary of Allah."],[83,"A son of his died, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to him condoling him on his son. He wrote to him: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Mu'adh b. Jabal. Peace be upon you. I praise Allah, besides whom there is no god, to you. To proceed: May Allah magnify your reward, inspire you with patience, and grant us and you gratitude. For our souls, our wealth, our families, and our children are among the wholesome gifts of Allah and His loaned deposits. He gave you enjoyment through him in happiness and joy, and He took him from you with abundant reward. Prayer, mercy, and guidance. If you seek reward, then be patient, and do not let your grief nullify your reward so that you regret. Know that grief does not bring back the dead, nor does it repel sorrow, and what is to come is as if it has already been. Peace.'"],[84,"The poor Muslims will enter Paradise five hundred years before their rich. We said: 'Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'They are those who, when there is a place of destruction, they are sent into it, and when there is booty, others are sent. They are the ones who are kept away from the doors.'"],[85,"Whoever wakes up and forgets, then eats or drinks while fasting, Allah has fed him and given him drink."],[86,"O Banu Hashim, O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, O Safiyyah, paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah, O Fatimah, daughter of Muhammad, let me not see any of you coming tomorrow carrying the Hereafter while you come carrying the dunya. My allies among you on the Day of Resurrection are only the pious. My example among you is only that of a man whose people seek his sincere advice. He came to them and said: 'O my people, you have been raided! You have been taken by surprise! Woe to the morning! I am the warner, death is the raider, and the Hour is the appointed time.'"],[87,"Visit each other occasionally; you will increase in love."],[88,"A time will come upon you when nothing will be more precious than three things: a lawful dirham, a brother whose company brings comfort, or a sunnah that is acted upon."],[89,"There is no divorce for one who does not possess, and no manumission for one who does not possess."],[90,"A man among us freed a slave who was his only property, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned him to slavery, then sold him."],[91,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[92,"Do not harm the living by [weeping over] the dead."],[93,"He used to kiss while fasting."],[94,"When the sun rises from its west, Iblis will fall down prostrating and call out: 'My God, command me to prostrate to whomever You will.' His zabaniyyah will gather to him and say: 'O their master, what is this supplication?' He will say: 'I asked my Lord to grant me respite until the appointed time, and this is the appointed time.' Then the Beast of the Earth will emerge from a crack in al-Safa, and its first step will land in Antioch. Then it will come to Iblis and slap him."],[95,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated on a muddy day, until I could see the trace of that on his forehead and the tip of his nose."],[96,"There is no man who teaches his child the Quran in this world, except that his father will be crowned on the Day of Resurrection with a crown in Paradise, by which the people of Paradise will recognize him for teaching his child the Quran in this world."],[97,"The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, when they met, they shook hands, and when they returned from a journey, they embraced."],[98,"Between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."],[99,"Some people of Paradise will look at some people of the Fire and say, 'Why have you entered the Fire? By Allah, we entered Paradise only because of what we learned from you.' They will say, 'We used to say but not do.'"],[100,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'My father died without performing Hajj. Shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?' He said, 'Do you think if your father had a debt and you paid it off, would it be settled on his behalf?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father.'"],[101,"Remorse is repentance."],[102,"Among sins are sins that prayer, fasting, Hajj, and Umrah do not expiate. They said, 'What expiates them, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Anxieties in seeking a livelihood.'"],[103,"Whoever wears an agate ring will never cease to see good."],[104,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote while we were in the land of Juhaynah: 'I had permitted you the skins of dead animals, so do not benefit from the dead animal's skin or sinew.'"],[105,"In the black seed there is healing for every disease except death."],[106,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the funeral procession."],[107,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the Hour. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What have you prepared for it?' He said, 'Love of Allah and His Messenger.' He said, 'Then you will be with those whom you love.'"],[108,"When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[109,"When he was ill, he would take a handful of black seed (shūnīz) and drink water and honey with it."],[110,"No prize is lawful except for a camel’s hoof or a horse’s hoof."],[111,"When a man says to another, “O disbeliever,” then disbelief becomes incumbent upon one of them."],[112,"I heard Muʿāwiyah—and he had a lock of women’s hair—say: “The daughter of Qaraẓah told me that women wear this, and it is from God’s mercy to you that I came to know that, for I have knowledge of it. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Whoever adds to his hair something that is not from it, then he adds falsehood to it.’”"],[113,"The flank pain (khāṣirah) is the vein of the kidney; when it throbs it harms its owner, so treat it with heated water."],[114,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Gabriel: “Does your Lord pray?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “And what is His prayer?” He said: “Glory and Holiness, My mercy has preceded My wrath.”"],[115,"He forbade two prayers: prayer after ʿaṣr until the sun sets, and after ṣubḥ until the sun rises; and fasting on the day of fiṭr and the day of aḍḥā. He said: “A woman is not married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt.” And he forbade wrapping oneself in al-ṣammāʾ, and that a man sit wrapped in a garment with nothing over his private parts, and that a woman travel beyond two days except with her husband or a maḥram, and that a man set out except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and the Aqṣā Mosque."],[116,"God has forbidden wine and its price, and forbidden swine and its price, and forbidden carrion and its price."],[117,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Khaybar, and it was said: “O Messenger of God, the donkeys have been exhausted.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Abū Ṭalḥah, and he called out: “God and His Messenger forbid you the flesh of domestic donkeys, for it is filth.”"],[118,"He witnessed the marriage contract of a man from the Anṣār with the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon and gave the Anṣārī woman in marriage, and said: “Upon harmony, good, and auspicious omen; sprinkle (daffifū) on your companion’s head.” So they sprinkled on his head, and baskets with fruit and sugar came, and were scattered over them. The people held back and did not snatch. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “How beautiful is forbearance! Will you not snatch?” They said: “O Messenger of God, you forbade us from snatching on such-and-such a day.” He said: “I only forbade you from snatching in the armies, and I did not forbid you from snatching at wedding feasts. So snatch.” Muʿādh b. Jabal said: “By God, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ urging us and we urging him to that snatching.”"],[119,"He used to consider the exception (istithnāʾ) even after a year, then he recited: “And do not say of anything, ‘I will do that tomorrow,’ except [you add] ‘If God wills.’ And remember your Lord when you forget” (Q 18:23–24). He said: “When you remember.”"],[120,"His father ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar said one day: “The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘Do not prevent women their shares of the mosques.’” I said: “As for me, I will prevent my family; whoever wishes may prevent his family.” My father turned and said: “May God curse you, may God curse you, may God curse you! You hear me say that the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded that they not be prevented, and you say, ‘I will prevent my family’?” Then he wept and stood up angry."],[121,"The mu'adhdhin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches."],[122,"God takes the souls at the time of their death. He said: \"The souls of the living and the dead meet in sleep, and they ask one another. Then God withholds the souls of the dead and sends the souls of the living back to their bodies.\""],[123,"The martyrs are on the bank of a river at the gate of Paradise, in a green pavilion. Their provision comes out to them from Paradise morning and evening."],[124,"A man clung to another man for his right, and pressed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever seeks, let him seek with decency, whether fulfilled or not.\""],[125,"The Prophet ﷺ came to us when I had a young brother. He said: \"Abu 'Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?\""],[126,"Retaliation is not taken for a wound until it heals."],[127,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the shaving of the heads of al-Hasan and al-Husayn, the two sons of 'Ali b. Abi Talib, on their seventh day. So their heads were shaved, and he gave in charity the weight of it in silver, and he did not find a sacrificial animal."],[128,"The heart of an old man remains young in love of two things: love of life and love of wealth."],[129,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would often supplicate with these words: \"O God, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from miserliness and cowardice, from inability and laziness, from the burden of debt, and from being overpowered by men.\""],[130,"I am the most self-sufficient of partners from association. Whoever associates anything with Me, then it is entirely for him. Whoever associates anything with Me, then it is entirely for him."],[131,"Gabriel ﷺ said to the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"How are the people of Badr among you?\" He said: \"They are our most excellent.\" Gabriel said: \"And whoever of the angels witnessed Badr, they are our most excellent.\""],[132,"When my community walks with a swaggering gait, and the Persians and the Byzantines serve them, some of them will be set upon others."],[133,"He slaughtered his sacrificial animal, made a dish from it, then brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"From my sacrificial animal.\" He said: \"When did you slaughter it?\" He said: \"Before I prayed.\" So he ordered him to repeat it."],[134,"When he ordered the people to raise their hands in the rain prayer, he was wearing a black khamīṣa (a square garment). He wanted to take hold of its lower part to shift it, but it was heavy and overcame him, so he took hold of its edge from over his shoulders and turned the two sides, one over the other, and made what was at the back come to the outside."],[135,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a raiding party or an army, he said: \"Raid in the path of Allah, fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child or an old man.\" He said to their commander: \"When you besiege a fortress or the people of a village, call them to one of three things: to enter Islam, or to pay the jizya, or to fight you. And when you besiege the people of a fortress or the people of a village, and they want to come down upon the judgment of Allah, do not bring them down upon the judgment of Allah, for you do not know whether you will attain in them the judgment of Allah or not. But bring them down upon your judgment and the judgment of your companions. And when you besiege the people of a fortress or the people of a village, and they ask you to give them the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger, do not give them the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger, but give them your protection and the protection of your companions. For if you break your protections and the protections of your fathers, that is better for you than breaking the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger.\""],[136,"Seek the hour that is hoped for on Friday, between the ʿaṣr prayer and the setting of the sun, and it is the extent of this — meaning his fist."],[137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman, and I was among those who stoned them."],[138,"He forbade that dates and raisins be soaked together, and grapes and unripe dates together."],[139,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast all of Shaʿbān, except a little of it."],[140,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying for the people while Umāma bt. Abī al-ʿĀṣ was on his shoulder, and when he prostrated he put her down."],[141,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My father died without performing Hajj; should I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"If your father had a debt, would you pay it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then the debt owed to Allah is more deserving.\""],[142,"We were one day with the Prophet ﷺ when the Jews entered upon him, and he saw them with white beards. He said: \"What is the matter with you that you do not change [the white]?\" It was said: \"They dislike it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"But you should change it, and beware of black.\""],[143,"If the weeping of David ﷺ and the weeping of all the people of the earth all together were weighed against the weeping of Adam, it would not equal it."],[144,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"O Messenger of Allah, when should we abandon enjoining good and forbidding evil, when they are the masters of the deeds of the righteous?\" He said: \"When what befell the Children of Israel befalls you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what befell the Children of Israel?\" He said: \"When the best among you flatter the wicked among you, when jurisprudence becomes among the worst of you, and when kingship becomes among the young of you, then at that time a trial will clothe you, you will charge and be charged against.\""],[145,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Muhammad, I have never been sent to any prophet more beloved to me than you. Shall I not teach you names from the names of Allah that are among His most beloved names to Him, by which He is called? Say: O Light of the heavens and the earth, O Adornment of the heavens and the earth, O Compeller of the heavens and the earth, O Pillar of the heavens and the earth, O Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, O Responder to those who cry for help, O Aid of those who seek aid, O Ultimate Goal of worshippers, O Reliever of the distressed, O Comforter of the sorrowful, O Answerer of the call of the distressed, O Remover of hardship, O God of the worlds, O Most Merciful of the merciful. Every need is fulfilled through You.\""],[146,"Khalid b. al-Walid complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about insomnia at night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"When you go to your bed, say: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, be for me a protector from the evil of Your creation.\""],[147,"There is no Muslim man on earth who calls upon Allah with a supplication except that Allah grants it to him, or averts from him harm equal to it, as long as he does not supplicate for sin or cutting off family ties, and as long as he does not become impatient.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is his impatience?\" He said: \"He says: 'I have supplicated and supplicated, but I have not been answered.'\" A man from the people said: \"Then we will supplicate a lot, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Allah is even more.\""],[148,"When the soul of the believer is taken, the people of mercy among Allah's servants receive it as you receive a bearer of good news from the people of this world. They say: \"Let your companion rest, for he was in severe distress.\" Then they ask him: \"What did so-and-so do, and did so-and-so get married?\" If they ask him about a man who died before him, he says: \"Alas, that one died before me.\" They say: \"Indeed, to Allah we belong and to Him we return. He was taken to his mother, the abyss. What an evil mother and what an evil nurturer!\" And he said: \"Your deeds are presented to your relatives and clansmen among the people of the Hereafter. If they are good, they rejoice and are glad, and say: 'O Allah, this is Your grace and mercy, so complete Your blessing upon him and cause him to die upon it.' And the deeds of the evildoer are presented to them, and they say: 'O Allah, inspire him with a righteous deed that pleases You and brings him near to You.'\""],[149,"The most beloved of My servants to Me are those who are quickest to break the fast."],[150,"Part of the perfection of prayer is praying in sandals."],[151,"The Prophet ﷺ divorced Hafsah, and the people were grieved by that. Her maternal uncle Uthman b. Maz'un and her brother Qudamah entered upon her. While they were with her, grieving, the Prophet ﷺ entered upon Hafsah and said: \"O Hafsah, Gabriel came to me just now and said: 'Allah sends you greetings of peace and says to you: Take back Hafsah, for she is one who fasts and prays, and she will be your wife in Paradise.'\""],[152,"Three are not to be visited: the one with sore eyes, the one with a toothache, and the one with a boil."],[153,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: \"An eye for an eye, and a nose for a nose.\""],[154,"The Prophet ﷺ detained a man on suspicion, and intercession was made for him, so he released him."],[155,"Whoever Allah has blessed with a blessing and wants it to remain, let him say often: 'There is no might nor power except with Allah.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: 'And why did you not say, when you entered your garden: What Allah wills! There is no power except with Allah.'"],[156,"The people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter."],[157,"\"Is the Mahdi from among us or from other than us, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Rather, from us. Through us God will seal [the religion] as through us He opened [it], and through us they will be rescued from polytheism, and through us God will unite their hearts after clear enmity, just as through us He united their hearts after the enmity of polytheism.\" Ali said: \"Will they be believers or disbelievers?\" He said: \"[They will be] put to trial and a disbeliever.\""],[158,"He was asked about the first signs of the Hour, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"The first of the signs of the Hour is a fire that will emerge from the east and drive them to the west.\""],[159,"Whoever prays on the night of Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha, his heart will not die on the day when hearts die."],[160,"The slogan of my community when they are carried across the bridge [Sirat] is: \"O You besides whom there is no god but You.\""],[161,"God loves the one who loves dates."],[162,"I asked Abdullah b. Abbas and Abdullah b. Umar: How was the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ at night? They said: \"Thirteen [rakʿahs]: eight, and he performed witr with three, and two rakʿahs after dawn.\""],[163,"I used to scrape the semen from the garment of the Messenger of God."],[164,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established brotherhood between the Quraysh and the Ansar, and he made brotherhood between Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf. Saʿd said to him: \"I have wealth, so it is between me and you in two halves, and I have two wives. Consider which of them is more pleasing to you, and I will divorce her, and when she becomes lawful, marry her.\" He said: \"May God bless you in your family and your wealth. Show me the market.\" He did not return until he came back with dates and dried curd, having made a surplus. The Messenger of God ﷺ saw on me a trace of yellow [perfume] and said: \"What is this?\" I said: \"I married a woman from the Ansar.\" He said: \"What did you give her as a bridal gift?\" I said: \"The weight of a date pit in gold.\" He said: \"Hold a wedding feast, even if with a sheep.\""],[165,"I ate for the Messenger of God ﷺ a wedding feast in which there was no bread and no meat. I said: \"What was it, O Abu Hamza?\" He said: \"Dates and sawiq.\""],[166,"Perform ablution from that which has been touched by fire."],[167,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding ablution from that which the fire has touched."],[168,"He would rise in the morning in a state of janabah, and then he would fast."],[169,"He would rise in the morning in a state of janabah from his wives, and then he would rise fasting that day."],[170,"I am the leader of the messengers, and I do not boast. I am the seal of the prophets, and I do not boast. I am the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted, and I do not boast."],[171,"Prayer in the congregational mosque: the obligatory prayer equals an accepted Hajj, and the supererogatory prayer is like an accepted Hajj. Prayer in the congregational mosque is superior to other mosques by five hundred prayers."],[172,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinating while facing the qiblah."],[173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought refuge from seven deaths: from sudden death, from snakebite, from being devoured by a wild beast, from drowning, from burning, from falling onto something or something falling on him, and from being killed while fleeing from the battlefield."],[174,"I would not love to have this world and all it contains in exchange for this verse: 'O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah...' (Q. 39:53)."],[175,"Ali b. Abi Talib mounted me behind him on a mule. When he placed his foot in the stirrup, he said: 'In the name of Allah.' When he was settled, he said: 'Praise be to Allah.' When he was fully mounted, he said: 'Praise be to Allah who has subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it, and indeed to our Lord we will return.' Then he praised Allah three times, then said 'Allahu akbar' three times, then said: 'O Allah, forgive me my sin, for none forgives sins except You.' Then he laughed. I said to him: 'Why do you laugh?' He said: 'I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said the same, then laughed. I said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you laugh?' He said: 'I laughed at Allah's wonder at the servant who says: O Allah, forgive me my sin, for none forgives sins except You. Allah says: He knows that none forgives sins besides Me.'"],[176,"When one of you approaches his wife, let him cover himself. For if he does not cover, the angels feel shy and leave, and Satan attends. If a child results between them, Satan has a share in it."],[177,"If I take away the two dearest things of My servant, and he remains patient and seeks reward, I will recompense him with Paradise for them."],[178,"Whoever relieves a Muslim of a hardship in this world, Allah will relieve him of a hardship from the hardships of the Day of Resurrection. Whoever conceals the faults of a Muslim, Allah will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever makes things easy for a Muslim, Allah will make things easy for him on the Day of Resurrection. Allah is in the service of the servant as long as the servant is in the service of his brother."],[179,"The example of Bilal is like that of a bee that goes out in the morning eating from the sweet and the bitter, then ends up all sweet."],[180,"While he was reciting Surah al-Baqarah and his horse was tied, the horse moved about in its tether. He raised his head and saw something like a lamp hanging between the sky and the earth. He went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him. The Messenger of God said: \"Recite, O Usayd b. Hudayr. Do you know what that was?\" He said: No. He said: \"That was the sakina, which drew near because of your voice. Had you continued reciting, the people would have woken up looking at it.\""],[181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while we were praying after dawn and said: \"There is no prayer after dawn except two rak'ahs.\""],[182,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"I practice coitus interruptus with my wife.\" He said: \"Why?\" He said: \"Out of concern for the child.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If it is for that reason, then no. That would not have harmed Persia and Byzantium.\""],[183,"Jabir b. Abd Allah was asked about coitus interruptus, and he said: \"We used to practice it during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and it was not held against us.\""],[184,"There is no prayer better than the dawn prayer on Friday in congregation, and I do not think that anyone among you who attends it will be other than forgiven."],[185,"Whoever performs wudu and does it well, then gathers his clothes, then goes out to the mosque, ten good deeds are recorded for him with every step. He remains in prayer as long as he is waiting for the prayer, and he is recorded among those who pray from the time he leaves his house until he returns."],[186,"Say: He is God, the One, equals a third of the Quran, and Say: O disbelievers, equals a quarter of the Quran. He used to recite them in the two rak'ahs of dawn and said: \"These two rak'ahs contain the desire of all time.\""],[187,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded that every walled garden contribute a canopy for the mosque."],[188,"Ali b. Abi Talib is the keeper of my basin on the Day of Resurrection, in which there are goblets as numerous as the stars. The width of my basin is the distance between al-Jabiya and Sana'a."],[189,"When Fatima bt. Asad b. Hashim, the mother of Ali, died, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her, sat at her head, and said: \"May God have mercy on you, O my mother. You were my mother after my own mother. You would go hungry and feed me, go without clothes and clothe me, deny yourself good food and give it to me, seeking thereby the face of God and the abode of the Hereafter.\" Then he ordered that she be washed three times and three times more. When they reached the water containing camphor, the Messenger of God ﷺ poured it over her with his own hand. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ took off his shirt and dressed her in it, and she was shrouded over it. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ called Usama b. Zayd, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, Umar b. al-Khattab, and a black slave to dig, and they dug her grave. When they reached the niche, the Messenger of God ﷺ dug it with his own hand and removed its soil with his own hand. When he finished, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered and lay down in it, and said: \"God is the One who gives life and causes death, and He is living and does not die. Forgive my mother, Fatima bt. Asad, prompt her with her proof, and widen her entrance, by the right of Your Prophet and the prophets before me, for You are the Most Merciful of the merciful.\" Then he said the takbir over her four times, then he, al-Abbas, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq placed her in the grave."],[190,"He was asked about a stray sheep, and he said: \"It is yours, or your brother's, or the wolf's.\" He was asked about a stray camel, and he said: \"What do you have to do with it? It has its own water-skin and its own shoes. Leave it until its owner comes.\""],[191,"Whoever eats of these green vegetables should not come near our mosque: garlic, leeks, onions, and radishes. For the angels are harmed by what harms the children of Adam."],[192,"A great, fat man will come on the Day of Resurrection, yet he will not weigh the wing of a mosquito. Then he said: 'Recite: \"We shall not give them any weight on the Day of Resurrection.\"'"],[193,"Whoever takes as allies other than his rightful patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him any obligatory or supererogatory act. And whoever innovates something in this city of mine or gives shelter to an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. No obligatory or supererogatory act will be accepted from him."],[194,"Whoever says when the caller calls to prayer: 'O Allah, Lord of this complete call and the established prayer, send blessings upon Muhammad and be pleased with me with a pleasure after which there is no displeasure,' Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will respond to him."],[195,"Indeed the Dajjal is one-eyed, and indeed your Lord is not one-eyed. Written between his eyes is 'disbeliever,' which the literate and the illiterate among the believers will read. With him are a Paradise and a Fire, but his Fire is a Paradise and his Paradise is a Fire."],[196,"We used to consider hypocrisy (riya') at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as the major polytheism."],[197,"I missed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night while he was with me in my bed. I found him prostrating, facing the qiblah with the tips of his fingers, and I heard him saying: 'I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, and in You from You. I praise You, but I cannot fully enumerate all that is in You.' When he finished, he said: 'O A'ishah, has your devil taken hold of you?' I said: 'Do you not have a devil?' He said: 'There is no human being but he has a devil.' I said: 'Even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Even me, but I called upon Allah and He aided me against him, so he submitted.'"],[198,"The five prayers are an expiation for what is between them."],[199,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade an emigrant (Muhajir) from selling on behalf of a Bedouin."],[200,"I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined."],[201,"The first to change the religion of Ibrahim was 'Amr b. Luhayy b. Qama'ah b. Khindif, the father of Khuza'ah."],[202,"Five are not required to attend the Friday prayer: the woman, the traveler, the slave, the child, and the people of the desert."],[203,"God—mighty and majestic—has three sacred things. Whoever guards them, God will guard for him the affairs of his religion and his worldly life, and whoever neglects them, God will not guard anything for him.” It was said, “What are they, O Messenger of God?” He said, “The sanctity of Islam, my sanctity, and the sanctity of my kin.”"],[204,"There is no contagion, no hāmah, no Ṣafar, and a sick person should not be brought among healthy ones."],[205,"The faith of a Berber does not go beyond his collarbones."],[206,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say—and he mentioned Quraysh—: “They have four qualities: they are the most upright of people in times of tribulation, the quickest to recover after calamity, the most likely to return after fleeing, the best to the poor and the orphan, and the most resistant to the oppression of kings.”"],[207,"Do not precede the month by a day or two, except a man who was accustomed to fasting; then let him fast."],[208,"A man came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said, “I have vowed to slaughter myself.” Ibn ʿAbbās said, “You have a good example in the Messenger of God.” Then he recited: “And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice” with a ram, so he slaughtered it."],[209,"It is as if you are piercing them with arrows by the poetry you say against them."],[210,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his companions, and he gave me a young goat. I found it to be a jadhaʿ, so I returned to him and said, “O Messenger of God, it is a jadhaʿ.” He said, “Then sacrifice it.”"],[211,"Saʿd b. ʿUbādah asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about a vow that was upon his mother, and he said, “Fulfill it on her behalf.”"],[212,"I found one hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of God, and he mentioned the hadith."],[213,"A man looked at the Messenger of God ﷺ through a curtain of his, and in the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ there was a comb. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “If I knew that he was looking at me, I would have poked his eye.”"],[214,"They both went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tabūk. A man bit another man, and he pulled his hand out of his mouth, and his front tooth came out. He came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking retaliation. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Would he leave his hand in your mouth for you to bite it as a stallion bites?” So the Messenger of God declared it void."],[215,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh so much that I could see his uvula; he only smiled. And when he saw clouds or wind, it would be recognized in his face."],[216,"The one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one drowned in the path of Allah is a martyr, and the one who dies of an abdominal illness in the path of Allah is a martyr."],[217,"Silver for silver, like for like, with no increase in it."],[218,"My father taught me words which he claimed ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb taught him. And ʿUmar claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught them to him: The greetings, the prayers, the good things, the blessed things are for Allah. Peace be upon the Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."],[219,"The banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was black and his standard was white, and on it was written: There is no god but Allah; Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."],[220,"When one of you sells a commodity, he should not conceal a defect if it has one."],[221,"It is as if I can see the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he prostrated."],[222,"I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after he had come out of the privy, and I greeted him, but he did not return my greeting until he placed his hand on a wall and wiped his face and his hand, then he greeted me."],[223,"On the day they conquered Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw fires blazing, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What are these fires?' They said: 'They are over the meat of domestic donkeys.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Spill what is in them and break them' – meaning the pots. A man from the people said: 'Or shall we wash them, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Or that.'"],[224,"He used to prostrate in 'When the sky splits apart' and in 'Recite in the name of your Lord.'"],[225,"Whoever dies without having a pledge of allegiance on him dies a death of ignorance."],[226,"Whoever is killed in a blind dispute – a throwing that occurs among them – with a stone, or a stick, or a whip, it is a mistake, and its blood money is the blood money of a mistake. And whoever is killed deliberately, it is retaliation. Whoever prevents that, upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath; neither ransom nor compensation will be accepted from him."],[227,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: O Abu Hurayrah, do not enter upon a ruler; but if you are overcome by that, then do not overstep my Sunnah, and do not fear his sword—his sword is that you enjoin upon them the fear of God and obedience to Him."],[228,"He brought some food close to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said to his companions: Mention the name of God, and let each person eat from what is nearest to him."],[229,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul while he was in the shade, and he said: Ibn Abi Kabshah has dusted us over. His son Abdullah b. Abdullah said: By the One who honored you and sent down the Book upon you, if you wish, I will bring you his head. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: No, but be dutiful to your father and treat him well."],[230,"Whatever inheritance was divided in the Jahiliyyah remains upon its division; and whatever inheritance Islam came upon is upon the division of Islam."],[231,"Envy is only in two cases: a man to whom God gave the Quran and he stood by it, making lawful what it makes lawful and forbidding what it forbids; and a man to whom God gave wealth and he used it to maintain his relatives and kin and acted in obedience to God with it."],[232,"Do you know who the Muslim is? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. They said: Then who is the believer? He said: The one whom people trust with their lives and their wealth. They said: Then who is the emigrant? He said: The one who abandons evil and avoids it."],[233,"Zuhrah b. Ma'bad al-Qurashi narrated to me that he used to go out with his grandfather Abdullah b. Hisham to the market to buy food, and Abdullah b. Umar and Abdullah b. al-Zubayr would meet him and say: Include us, for the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed for blessing for you."],[234,"A woman from Khath'am asked him for a ruling during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and she said: O Messenger of God, God's obligation of Hajj upon His servants has found my father an old man who cannot sit firmly on the riding camel; can I perform Hajj on his behalf? The Prophet ﷺ said to her: Yes."],[235,"Whoever says: May God reward Muhammad on our behalf as he deserves, tires seventy scribes for a thousand mornings."],[236,"Whoever falls ill or travels, he has the like of the reward of what he used to do while healthy and resident."],[237,"I perfumed the Messenger of God ﷺ with my own hand, and he went around to his wives, then entered the morning in a state of ihram."],[238,"I had forbidden you three things: visiting graves—so visit them, but do not say anything indecent; and I had forbidden you the meat of sacrificial animals—so eat and store it; and I had forbidden you to soak [dates] in certain vessels—so drink in whatever you like, but do not drink any intoxicant."],[239,"Her husband divorced her three times, and the Prophet ﷺ did not grant her housing or maintenance."],[240,"A group of the Companions sent me to Ibn ʿUmar to ask him about the middle prayer. He said: We used to say that it is the prayer during which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was turned toward the qiblah: the ẓuhr prayer."],[241,"Send abundant blessings upon me on the radiant night and the brilliant day, for your blessings are presented to me."],[242,"When one of you stands for prayer, let him begin by leveling the place of his prostration, and not leave it until, when he bends down to prostrate, he blows, then prostrates. For one of you to prostrate on a live coal is better than prostrating on his breath."],[243,"Prayer is the best thing placed, so whoever is able to increase, let him increase."],[244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered a ram, then said: 'This is on my behalf and on behalf of my community.'"],[245,"When a believer meets a believer, greets him, takes his hand, and shakes it, their sins fall away as leaves fall from a tree."],[246,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a cloudy day, during a journey, facing other than the qiblah. When he finished the prayer and said the salutation, the sun appeared. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed facing other than the qiblah. He said: Your prayer has been raised to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with its due."],[247,"Allah, Exalted is He, has placed the truth upon the tongue and heart of ʿUmar."],[248,"When one of you meets his brother during the day several times, let him greet him each time."],[249,"Whoever wishes to have his lifespan extended and his provision expanded, let him maintain ties of kinship."],[250,"When I test My servant with his two beloved ones and he remains patient, I compensate him for them with Paradise."],[251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while Bilal was giving the iqamah for the morning prayer. He saw a man praying the two rak'ahs of Fajr and said to him: \"Two prayers together?\""],[252,"Ibn Umar would not mention the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he wept."],[253,"Whoever fasts Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise whose outside is seen from its inside and its inside from its outside."],[254,"Whoever fasts Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, Allah will build for him a palace in Paradise of pearl, ruby, and chrysolite, and will write for him a release from the Fire."],[255,"A man from the people of al-Awali would invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at midnight to barley bread, and he would respond."],[256,"There is no one who recites the talbiyah except that the stones and trees to his right and left also recite the talbiyah."],[257,"Whoever attends Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[258,"Whoever attends Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[259,"Whoever attends Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[260,"Do not give preference to some prophets over others."],[261,"He declared what lies between the two lava tracts of Madinah inviolable: that its game be not hunted."],[262,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar used to pray before the sermon on the two Eids."],[263,"The wasīlah is a rank with God above which there is no rank, so ask God to grant it to me.”"],[264,"The ʿumrā is in the position of inheritance."],[265,"For one who passes in front of a person praying to remain for forty is better for him than to pass in front of him.”"],[266,"The surplus water of a well is not to be withheld."],[267,"The hadith is as you know."],[268,"There is no harm and no reciprocating harm."],[269,"He was asked about the khāṭṭ (writing/line). He said: “It is a remnant of knowledge.”"],[270,"If a man were killed in the path of God, then brought to life, then killed in the path of God, he would not enter Paradise until his debt is settled on his behalf, there being no gold or silver there."],[271,"One who remembers God among the heedless is like one who remains steadfast among those who flee."],[272,"There is no commander of ten or more but he will come on the Day of Resurrection fettered; God will either pardon him as He wills or punish him as He wills."],[273,"Whoever abandons the Friday prayer three times without excuse, God seals his heart."],[274,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sacrificed a horned, black-eyed, virile ram."],[275,"A believer does not steal from the spoils."],[276,"The tooth-stick is a means of purifying the mouth and pleasing the Lord."],[277,"You must hear and obey in what you love and what you hate, in your ease and your hardship, and even when others are given preference over you. And do not dispute the matter with its people."],[278,"When the people of Hell are driven to it, it will meet them and scorch them with a blast that will leave no flesh upon a bone but will cast it upon the tendon."],[279,"He used to give the Zakat al-Fitr as a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley."],[280,"The martyr does not feel the pain of being killed except as one of you feels the sting of a pinch."],[281,"Whoever recites 'Say: He is Allah, the One' ten times, a palace is built for him in Paradise. Whoever recites it twenty times, two palaces are built for him. Whoever recites it thirty times, three are built."],[282,"It is not lawful for a woman to fast while her husband is present except with his permission, nor to permit a man into his house while he is averse. And whatever she gives in charity from what she earns, he has half the reward of her charity."],[283,"The woman was created from a crooked rib, so you will never keep company with her but there is crookedness in her. If you go to straighten her, you will break her, and breaking her is divorcing her."],[284,"Do not weep for the religion when you entrust it to its people, but weep for it when you entrust it to other than its people."],[285,"A people will come forth from the direction of the east and they will prepare the way for the Mahdi's authority."],[286,"There is no man who is put in charge of ten but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand bound to his neck until judgment is passed between him and them."],[287,"Whoever visits my grave after my death is like the one who visited me during my life."],[288,"The wide-eyed maidens of Paradise were created from saffron."],[289,"Indeed, Allah has placed the truth upon the tongue and heart of Umar."],[290,"I memorized six things from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: There is no divorce except after marriage, no emancipation except after ownership, no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience, no orphanhood after reaching puberty, no silence for a whole day until night, and no continuous fasting without break."],[291,"In the end of time there will be a tribulation in which people will be sifted as gold and silver are sifted in the mine."],[292,"Whoever eats with his left hand, a devil eats with him; and whoever drinks with his left hand, a devil drinks with him."],[293,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinating while standing."],[294,"People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection walking, barefoot, and uncircumcised. It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will women look at men?\" He said: \"On that day every person among them will have enough concern to distract him.\""],[295,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray until his feet were about to crack. Then after that he became heavy, and he would pray sitting. When he wanted to finish the surah, he would stand and complete it, then bow."],[296,"Deeds performed during the time of turmoil are like emigration to me."],[297,"No nation was ever transformed in form and then had descendants."],[298,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man who was being supported between two sons. He asked about him, and they said: \"He vowed to walk to Hajj on foot.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has no need for this man to torment himself.\" And he ordered him to ride."],[299,"Abu Dharr said: O Messenger of God, the wealthy have taken the reward. They pray as we pray, and they fast as we fast, but they have surplus wealth, and we have nothing to give in charity. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: O Abu Dharr, shall I not teach you words by which you may catch up with those who preceded you, and no one after you will overtake you except one who does the like of your deed? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Say 'God is most great' after every prayer thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, glorify Him thirty-three times, and seal it with 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things.'"],[300,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and shook his hand. The Prophet ﷺ did not withdraw his hand from the man's hand until the man withdrew his hand. Then he said to him: O Messenger of God, Uthman has come. He said: A man from the people of Paradise."],[301,"When the Prophet ﷺ broke his fast with a people, he would say: May the fasting break their fast with you, and may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you."],[302,"He performed ablution three times each, then said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, his sins will depart from his face, his hands, and his feet."],[303,"I asked my father Abd Allah b. Utbah b. Mas'ud: What do you remember of the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: I remember that he took me when I was five or six years old, seated me in his lap, wiped my head with his hand, and prayed for blessing for me and for my descendants after me."],[304,"He forbade the sale of risk."],[305,"He forbade the sale by throwing a pebble."],[306,"The one who strives on behalf of the widow and the needy is like the one who fights in the path of God."],[307,"The Friday bath is obligatory on every adult."],[308,"The example of the Quran when its companion commits to it and stands with it by night and day is like tethered camels: if their owner keeps them tethered, he holds them; if he releases their tethers, they go away. So too is the companion of the Quran."],[309,"When he heard the hadith of Rafi' b. Khadij: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade leasing land, Ibn Umar said: We used to lease it for the spring channel and for some of what comes out of it of straw."],[310,"He forbade that people's livestock be milked except with their permission."],[311,"He would, upon seeing the crescent moon, say: \"A crescent of goodness and right guidance; I believe in the One who created you and made you proportionate.\""],[312,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ imposed one-tenth on rain-fed land and on that irrigated by rivers, and half of one-tenth on that irrigated by means of a camel drawing water."],[313,"This nation will not abandon any practice of the earlier peoples until it adopts it."],[314,"Whoever recites a single letter of the Quran will have a good deed recorded for him, and I do not say that Alif Lam Mim is a single letter. Rather, Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, Mim is a letter, Dhal is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Kaf is a letter."],[315,"I used to write the Quran."],[316,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah while around the House there were three hundred and sixty idols. He began striking them with a stick he had, saying: \"Truth has come and falsehood has vanished; indeed falsehood is bound to vanish. Truth has come, and falsehood cannot originate anything nor repeat it.\""],[317,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ, and he was holding the hand of Umar b. al-Khattab. Umar said: \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, you are more beloved to me than everything except my own self.\" He said: \"No, by Him in whose hand is my soul, until I am more beloved to you than your own self.\" Umar said: \"Now you are more beloved to me than my own self.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Now, O Umar.\""],[318,"A neck will emerge from the Fire with a tongue with which it speaks and two eyes with which it sees. It will say: \"I have been ordered to seize every obstinate tyrant, everyone who called upon another god besides Allah, and everyone who killed a soul without right.\""],[319,"When one of you is praying, he should not raise his gaze to the sky; his eyesight should not be snatched away."],[320,"I have not seen anyone more closely resembling the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than this boy, meaning Umar b. Abd al-Aziz."],[321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray at night while I was lying crosswise between him and the qiblah."],[322,"We used to lease out our land, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that."],[323,"Indeed, a man keeps begging until he comes on the Day of Resurrection with no piece of flesh on his face."],[324,"Whoever visits a sick person, seventy thousand angels are appointed over him to pray for him."],[325,"Food for food, like for like."],[326,"Whoever eats from this tree, let him not approach our mosque until its smell has gone from him."],[327,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ wearing a saffron-dyed garment, and he disliked it when he saw it on me, and said: 'These are only the clothes of the disbelievers.'"],[328,"Indeed, God does not love the obscene, nor the one who acts obscenely."],[329,"The thief's hand is not cut off except for the value of a shield or more, a quarter of a dinar and above."],[330,"The hand is not cut off except for a quarter of a dinar or more."],[331,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to her: 'O Aisha, if obscenity were a man, it would be an evil man, and if modesty were a man, it would be a truthful man.'"],[332,"I perfumed the Messenger of God ﷺ with my own hands before he departed (from Muzdalifah)."],[333,"Aqiqah is performed for the boy, and his head is not touched with blood."],[334,"In camels there is a fara', and in sheep there is a fara'."],[335,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Muhassir, he urged on his mount and said: \"You must use small pebbles for throwing.\""],[336,"Is it possible that one of you keeps a flock of sheep at a distance of two or three miles, comes for Friday prayer but does not attend it three times, and so Allah seals his heart?"],[337,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the earrings of the Throne, and they are not hanging."],[338,"He passed by him while he was praying sitting, and said: \"For the one sitting there is half the prayer of the one standing.\""],[339,"The Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the dowry of women is twelve uqiyyahs, and an uqiyyah is forty dirhams, making four hundred and eighty. The Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the ghusl from janabah is one sa', and for wudu two ratls; and the sa' is eight ratls. The Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding what the earth produces of wheat, barley, raisins, and dates when it reaches five wasqs—and the wasq is sixty sa's, making three hundred sa's—is with this sa' that the Sunnah established."],[340,"No one weeps except one of two men: a wicked person perfecting his wickedness, or a righteous person perfecting his righteousness."],[341,"Whoever drinks wine, Allah removes the light of faith from his interior."],[342,"When he tied his turban, he let it hang down in front of him and behind him."],[343,"Keep paying it to them as long as they perform the five prayers."],[344,"I entered upon Umm Salamah, the Mother of the Believers, and she said: \"Where are you from?\" I said: \"From the people of Kufah.\" She said: \"Are you the ones who revile the Prophet ﷺ?\" I said: \"We do not know anyone who reviles the Prophet ﷺ.\" She said: \"Yes, do you not curse 'Ali? And curse those who love him?\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved him."],[345,"Whoever here is from Ma'add, let him stand up. I went to stand, but he said: \"Sit down.\" Then he said it a second time, and I stood up, but he said: \"Sit down.\" Then he said it a third time, and I stood up, but he said: \"Sit down.\" I said: \"Who are we, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"You are from Quda'ah b. Malik b. Himyar.\""],[346,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"Whoever I am his mawla, 'Ali is his mawla.\""],[347,"When Umar b. al-Khattab was made caliph, he forbade the people from mut‘ah of women and said: “This is only something that was permitted to the people when the people were few, but then it was made forbidden for them after that. So I will not come upon anyone doing that today except that I will inflict punishment on him.”"],[348,"The best of Allah’s servants in station on the Day of Resurrection is a just and gentle ruler, and the worst of Allah’s servants in station with Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a tyrannical and harsh ruler."],[349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lashed eighty lashes for wine."],[350,"He used to wake up in a state of major ritual impurity from his wives, then complete his fast."],[351,"He forbade that a woman be married along with her paternal aunt, or along with her maternal aunt."],[352,"I am Yahya b. Ayyub, and Ibn Lahi‘ah, from ‘Uqayl b. Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, from Qabisah b. Dhu’ayb, and ‘Urwah b. al-Zubayr, and ‘Ubayd Allah b. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the like of it."],[353,"Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like."],[354,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out with a forelock and said: “The women of the Children of Israel used to put this on their heads, so they were cursed and the mosques were made forbidden for them.”"],[355,"The fitrah is five: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, using the toothstick, trimming the nails, and plucking the armpit hair."],[356,"Prayer in congregation is better than praying alone by twenty-five degrees."],[357,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Baqi‘ al-Gharqad, then performed ablution and washed his face and hands, wiped his head, and took water with his right hand and sprinkled it over his feet, washing them."],[358,"Some Muslims were with the polytheists, increasing the numbers of the polytheists. An arrow would be shot and strike one of them, killing him, or he would be struck and killed. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning them: “Those whom the angels take while they are wronging themselves; they say, ‘In what were you?’ They say, ‘We were oppressed in the land’” — the verse."],[359,"Part of the excellence of a person's Islam is his leaving alone that which does not concern him."],[360,"O Allah, whoever is given charge of any affair of my Ummah and is kind to my Ummah, be kind to him; and whoever makes things difficult for them, make things difficult for him."],[361,"The martyrs are three: a believer with excellent faith who meets the enemy and is true to Allah until he is killed—that is the one to whom people will raise their necks on the Day of Resurrection; a believer with excellent faith who meets the enemy and is struck by a stray arrow that kills him—that one is in the second degree; and a believer who has wronged himself, meets the enemy and is true to Allah until he is killed—that one is in the third degree."],[362,"Wudu is required from what fire has touched."],[363,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Umar b. al-Khattab, and some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat together after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and discussed the greatest of major sins, but they had no knowledge about it. So they sent me to Abdullah b. Amr b. al-As to ask him about that. He informed me that the greatest of major sins is drinking wine. I came back and told them, but they rejected that and all of them went to him. He told them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A king of the Children of Israel seized a man and gave him the choice of drinking wine, killing a child, committing adultery, eating pork, or being killed if he refused. He chose to drink wine, and when he drank it, he did not refrain from anything they wanted from him.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us at that time: 'No one drinks it but that his prayer is not accepted for forty nights, and he will not die with any of it in his bladder except that Paradise is forbidden to him. And if he dies within the forty days, he dies a death of Jahiliyyah.'"],[364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about the cat: 'It is not impure.'"],[365,"Wherever you are, send blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me."],[366,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise."],[367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the mosque of Mina when some Bedouins came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to a human being?' He said: 'Good character.'"],[368,"The believer who mixes with people and endures their harm is better than the believer who does not mix with people and does not endure their harm."],[369,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a choice, and we chose him, and that was not counted as divorce."],[370,"An Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj."],[371,"When you see a red column in the direction of the east in Ramadan, store up food for your year, for it will be a year of hunger."],[372,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ten of his companions—Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, al-Zubayr, and others—were on Mount Hira, it shook with them. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Be still, Hira, for there is upon you only a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.\""],[373,"When a man passes in front of one of you while he is praying, let him push him away. If he refuses, then let him fight him."],[374,"He forbade the use of gourds and vessels smeared with pitch for making nabidh in them."],[375,"Gold for silver is usury unless it is hand to hand. Wheat for wheat is usury unless it is hand to hand. Dates for dates is usury unless it is hand to hand."],[376,"He used to bathe in the qadah, which is the faraq. And I and he used to bathe from a single vessel."],[377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send sacrificial animals from Madinah, and I would twist their garlands, and then he would not abstain from anything that a person in ihram abstains from."],[378,"Safiyya bt. Huyayy menstruated after she had performed the ifadah. I mentioned her menstruation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Is she going to hold us back?\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, she had already performed the ifadah and circumambulated the House, and she menstruated after the ifadah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Then let her depart.\""],[379,"A woman from Khath'am asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a ruling during the Farewell Pilgrimage—while al-Fadl b. al-Abbas was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation of Hajj upon His servants has found my father an old man who cannot sit firmly on a mount. Can I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Yes.\""],[380,"Bashir b. Sa'd brought al-Nu'man to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"I have given this son of mine a slave as a gift.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Have you given this gift to all your children?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then take it back.\""],[381,"Whichever man pollinates a palm tree and then sells its trunk, the fruit of the palm belongs to the one who pollinated it, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."],[382,"He caught up with Umar b. al-Khattab in a riding party—while Umar was swearing by his father—and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out: \"Indeed, Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Whoever swears, let him swear by Allah, or else be silent.\""],[383,"He saw in a dream some men among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Laylat al-Qadr is in the last seven nights of Ramadan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I see that your dreams have agreed upon the last seven nights. So whoever seeks it, let him seek it in the last seven nights."],[384,"None of you should make a man get up from his seat and then sit in it."],[385,"Let not one of you sell over the sale of another, and let not one of you propose over the proposal of another."],[386,"Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has lost his family and his wealth."],[387,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while facing the east, saying: Behold, the trial is here; behold, the trial is here—from where the horn of Satan rises."],[388,"Any slave owned by partners, if one of them frees his share, then a fair value is established for the one who freed him, and he becomes completely free if his wealth reaches that amount."],[389,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, his reward decreases by two qirats every day. And he used to command us to pursue dogs and kill them wherever we found them in Madinah."],[390,"It is not right for a Muslim who has something to bequeath to spend two nights except with his will written at his head."],[391,"When any of you sees a funeral procession, if he is not walking with it, let him stand until it passes or is put down before that."],[392,"The example of one who gives charity and then takes it back is like a dog that vomits and then returns to its vomit."],[393,"A good dream is from Allah, and grief is from Satan. Some dreams are what a man tells himself. If any of you sees a dream he dislikes, let him get up and pray two rak'ahs. I dislike shackles in sleep, and I like fetters because they indicate steadfastness in religion. The dream of a believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood. In the last part of time, the dream of a believer will hardly be false. The most truthful of you in speech will be the most truthful in dreams."],[394,"When your Prophet ﷺ was bowing or prostrating, he would say: Glory be to You and praise; I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You."],[395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a matter that was beneficial to us, and the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is to be obeyed. He forbade us to lease land in return for a portion of its produce or for minted silver, and he forbade us from the earnings of a cupper."],[396,"My Cistern extends from ʿAdan to ʿAmmān al-Balqāʾ. Its water is sweeter than honey, more fragrant than musk, and whiter than milk. Its cups are as many as the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks a single drink from it will never thirst again. The first people to reach it will be the poor emigrants, disheveled of hair and soiled of clothes—those who do not marry women who live in luxury and for whom doors of rulers are not opened."],[397,"Let me not find that I contended with any of you at the Cistern, saying, “This is one of my Companions,” and it is said, “You do not know what they introduced after you.” Abū al-Dardāʾ said, “O Prophet of Allah, supplicate Allah not to make me one of them.” He said, “You are not one of them.”"],[398,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his expeditions. We stopped at a place, and we came to him there. He raised his hands and said, “Faith and wisdom are here, up to Lakhm and Judhām.”"],[399,"I am as My servant thinks of Me. If he thinks good, then good; if he thinks evil, then evil."],[400,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “What is your Cistern that you talk about?” He said, “It is like the distance between al-Bayḍāʾ and Buṣrā. Allah will supply me in it with a cup so large that no human knows from what it was created or where its two ends are.” ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said takbīr and said, “As for the Cistern, the poor emigrants will come to it—those who fight in the path of Allah and die in the path of Allah. I hope that He will grant me that cup so I may drink from it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “My Lord promised me to admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my community without reckoning. Then each thousand will intercede for seventy thousand. Then my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will scoop with His two hands three scoops.” ʿUmar said takbīr and said, “The first seventy thousand, Allah will let them intercede for their fathers, sons, and clans. I hope Allah will place me in one of the last scoops.” The bedouin said, “O Messenger of Allah, does it have fruit?” He said, “Yes, and in it is a tree called Ṭūbā. It corresponds to al-Firdaws.” He said, “Which tree of our land does it resemble?” He said, “It does not resemble any tree of your land. But have you been to Syria?” He said, “No, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “It resembles a tree in Syria called the walnut. It grows on one trunk, then its top spreads out.” He said, “How large is its base?” He said, “If a young camel of your family’s camels set out to circle it, it would not complete the circuit before its collarbone breaks from old age.” He said, “Does it have grapes?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “How large is a cluster of them?” He said, “A month’s journey for the pied crow, not turning aside and not tiring.” He said, “How large is a single grape from it?” He said, “Did your father ever slaughter a large animal from his sheep?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “He skinned its hide and gave it to your mother, saying, ‘Tan this, then cut from it buckets for us to water our livestock with’?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Will that satisfy me and my household?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “And the majority of your clan.”"],[401,"A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “How long was between him and Nūḥ?” He said, “Ten generations.” He said, “How long was between Nūḥ and Ibrāhīm?” He said, “Ten generations.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, how many were the messengers?” He said, “Three hundred and fifteen.”"],[402,"My Lord promised me to admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my community without reckoning, and each thousand will intercede for seventy thousand. Then my Lord will scoop three scoops with His two hands.” Qays said: I said to Abū Saʿīd, “Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “Yes, with my ears, and my heart retained it.” Abū Saʿīd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “And that, if Allah wills, will encompass the emigrants of my community, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will complete the rest from our bedouins.”"],[403,"Every human being of the children of Adam was created with three hundred and sixty joints."],[404,"Let people cease from abandoning the Friday prayers, or Allah will seal their hearts, and then they will be among the heedless."],[405,"They traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and they sped up the march until it was evening. The prayer became due at the Messenger of God ﷺ, when a horseman came and said: 'O Messenger of God, I went ahead of you all until I climbed such-and-such a mountain, and there I found Hawazin with their camels, their women in howdahs, their livestock, and their sheep, gathered at Hunayn.' The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and said: 'Those are the spoils of the Muslims all together, if God wills.' Then he said: 'Who will be our guard tonight?' Anas b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi said: 'I will, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Mount.' So he mounted a horse of his and came to the Messenger of God. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'Face this mountain pass until you are at its highest point, and we must not be caught off guard from your direction tonight.' When morning came, the Messenger of God ﷺ went out to his prayer place and prayed two rak'ahs, then said: 'Have you sensed your horseman?' A man said: 'O Messenger of God, we have not sensed him.' The call to prayer was given, and the Messenger of God ﷺ, while in prayer, kept turning toward the pass. When he finished his prayer and said the salutation, he said: 'Rejoice, for your horseman has come to you.' We began looking through the gaps in the trees in the pass, and there he was, coming until he stood before the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'I went until I was at the highest point of this pass, where the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me. When morning came, I ascended both sides of the pass and looked, but I saw no one.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'You have done well, and there is no blame on you for what you do after this.'"],[406,"Whoever licks honey three mornings every month will not be afflicted by a great calamity."],[407,"Whoever keeps a horse in the path of God, its fodder and its droppings will be in his scale on the Day of Resurrection."],[408,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out, and a Bedouin confronted him and said: 'When is the Hour?' He said: 'What have you prepared for it?' The Bedouin said: 'I have not prepared for it any good that I can commend myself for, except that I love God and His Messenger.' He said: 'You will be with those you love.'"],[409,"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I saw men whose tongues were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: 'O Gabriel, who are these?' He said: 'These are preachers from your nation who command people to do what they do not do.'"],[410,"The lower garment of the believer reaches to the middle of his shins, and there is no blame on him for what is between that and the ankles. Whatever is below the ankles is in the Fire."],[411,"I am not of idle play, and idle play is not of me."],[412,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me and Mu'adh b. Jabal to Yemen. I said: 'O Messenger of God, advise us.' He said: 'Cooperate with each other and do not disobey each other; make things easy and do not make them difficult.'"],[413,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ bow, and he placed his hands on his knees."],[414,"Whoever is killed under a blind banner, fighting for a group or supporting a group, his killing is that of the pre-Islamic period."],[415,"She had a sheep that she used to milk, and the Messenger of God ﷺ missed it. He asked Umm Salamah about it, and Umm Salamah said: 'It died, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Why did you not make use of its hide?' They said: 'O Messenger of God, it is carrion.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Tanning makes it lawful, just as vinegar makes wine lawful.'"],[416,"When we arrived in Madinah, we began rushing from our mounts to kiss the hands and feet of the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Mundhir al-Ashajj waited until he came to his baggage, put on his garment, and then came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'You have two qualities that God, Mighty and Exalted, loves: forbearance and deliberation.' Al-Mundhir said: 'Praise be to God who has created me with two qualities that God and His Messenger love.'"],[417,"A man came to Ibn Umar and asked him about this verse: “Fight them until there is no fitnah” (Q 2:193). Ibn Umar said, “We fought alongside the Prophet ﷺ until there was no fitnah. So go, you and your companions, and fight until there is fitnah.”"],[418,"Aqil b. Abi Talib dueled a man on the day of Mu’tah and killed him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him his ring and his spoils as a reward."],[419,"I was near the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man said, “I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except giving water to the pilgrims.” Another said, “I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except maintaining the Sacred Mosque.” Another said, “Jihad in the path of Allah is better than what you have said.” Umar rebuked them and said, “Do not raise your voices near the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it is Friday. But when you have prayed the Friday prayer, I will enter and ask him about what you have differed over.” Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “Have you made the giving of water to the pilgrims and the maintenance of the Sacred Mosque equal to one who believes in Allah…?” (Q 9:19)."],[420,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the beginning of his mission, when he was hiding. I said, “What are you?” He said, “I am a prophet.” I said, “What is a prophet?” He said, “A messenger of Allah.” I said, “Has Allah sent you?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “With what has He sent you?” He said, “That you worship Allah, break the idols, and maintain family ties.” I said, “Yes, He has sent you. Who has followed you in this?” He said, “A free man and a slave,” meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal. Amr b. Abasah used to say, “I am a quarter of Islam, for I embraced Islam.” Then I said, “Shall I follow you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “No, but return to your people. When you hear that we have prevailed, come to us.”"],[421,"Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about the lower garment applies to the shirt."],[422,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up from his sitting place and intended to return to it, he would leave his sandals or something that was with him there."],[423,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he dispatched a military expedition in one of the directions. Then a bringer of good news came to him to announce that a woman had taken charge of the enemy’s affairs. So he fell prostrate, then raised his head saying, “Men are ruined when they obey women.”"],[424,"A woman with istihadah performs ghusl from one menstrual period to the next."],[425,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, fix prices for us.” He said, “Rather I will supplicate to Allah.” Then another man came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, fix prices for us.” He said, “Rather Allah raises and lowers. I hope to meet Allah while no one has a complaint against me.”"],[426,"When he began the prayer, he would say: “Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You,” like the saying of the Prophet."],[427,"Whoever begins with asking before greeting, do not answer him."],[428,"When the last of this nation curses its first, then whoever has knowledge should make it known, for the one who conceals knowledge on that day is like one who conceals what was revealed to Muhammad."],[429,"Whoever kills a muʿāhad (one with whom Muslims have a covenant) will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance is found from a distance of five hundred years' travel."],[430,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrating on his forehead at the hairline."],[431,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about this verse: 'He is able to send upon you a punishment from above you or from beneath your feet.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'It will certainly come to pass, and its interpretation has not yet occurred.'"],[432,"In the latter days there will be a people who are brothers in public and enemies in secret.\" It was said: 'O Messenger of God, how will that be?' He said: 'It will be through their desire for one another and their fear of one another.'"],[433,"I was about to order that the prayer be established, then order a man to lead the people in prayer, then take bundles of firewood and go to people who do not attend the prayer, and burn their houses down upon them."],[434,"A man from Thaqīf whose kunyah was Abū Tammām gave the Messenger of God ﷺ a waterskin of wine. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'It has been forbidden, O Abū Tammām.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, shall I sell it?' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'The One who forbade drinking it also forbade its price.'"],[435,"We used not to keep the meat of sacrificial animals for more than three days. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to eat it and to take it as provision."],[436,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wiping over his leather socks after the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah."],[437,"Ubayy b. Kaʿb taught me the Qurʾān, so I gave him a bow as a gift. He went to the Prophet ﷺ wearing it, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'You are wearing a bow from Hell.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, we sometimes attend their food and eat from it.' He said: 'As for what is prepared for you, if you eat it, you eat it with your own share of sin. As for what is prepared for someone else that you attend and eat from, there is no harm in it.'"],[438,"'Where is our mother Khadījah?' He said: 'In a house of reeds, with no idle talk or toil, between Maryam and Āsiyah, the wife of Pharaoh.' I said: 'Of these reeds?' He said: 'No, rather of reeds strung with pearls, sapphires, and rubies.'"],[439,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade accepting the invitation to the food of the sinful (fāsiqūn)."],[440,"When the last ten nights of Ramadan came, the Prophet ﷺ observed iʿtikāf in the mosque. After the Prophet ﷺ prayed the ʿAṣr prayer on the twenty-second day, he said: 'We shall stand in prayer tonight, if God wills. Whoever wishes to stand, let him stand.' That was the night of the twenty-third. The Prophet ﷺ led us in congregational prayer after the evening prayer until a third of the night had passed, then he left. On the night of the twenty-fourth, he did not say anything and did not stand. On the night of the twenty-fifth, he stood after the ʿAṣr prayer on the twenty-fourth day and said: 'We shall stand tonight, if God wills'—meaning the night of the twenty-fifth—'whoever wishes, let him stand.' The Prophet ﷺ prayed until half the night had passed. On the night of the twenty-sixth, he stood and said: 'We shall stand, if God wills'—meaning the night of the twenty-seventh—'whoever wishes to stand, let him stand.' Abū Dharr said: We steeled ourselves for the night prayer. The Prophet ﷺ led us until two-thirds of the night had passed, then he went to a tent in the mosque. I said to him: 'We had hoped, O Messenger of God, that you would lead us until morning.' He said: 'O Abū Dharr, if you pray with your imam and leave when he leaves, the qunūt of your night will be recorded for you.'"],[441,"Whoever traces his lineage to nine disbelieving forefathers, seeking honor through them, he will be their tenth in the Fire."],[442,"“O Abu al-Mundhir, I have been commanded to present the Qur’an to you.” He said, “In Allah I have believed, at your hands I have submitted, and from you I have learned.” He said: The Prophet ﷺ repeated the statement. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, and I was mentioned there?” He said, “Yes, by your name and your lineage in the highest assembly.” He said, “Then recite, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[443,"“O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of fever?” He said, “Good deeds continue to flow for the one afflicted with it as long as a foot twitches or a vein throbs.” Then he said, “O Allah, I ask You for a fever that does not prevent me from going out in Your cause, nor from going out to Your House, nor to the mosque of Your Prophet.” And Ubayy was never touched except that he had a fever."],[444,"If someone whose religion and character please you comes to you, then marry him. If you do not, there will be tribulation in the land and widespread corruption."],[445,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in one of his military expeditions: “Take many of these sandals, for one of you remains a rider as long as they are on his feet.”"],[446,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will call a servant from among His servants and make him stand before Him, then question him about his status just as He questions him about his wealth."],[447,"There is none of you but his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will ask him, saying: “My servant, what deceived you concerning Me? What did you answer the messengers?”"],[448,"He used to recite in the night prayer “By the fig and the olive.”"],[449,"It is from the Sunnah not to go out on the day of Fitr until you have eaten, and not on the day of sacrifice until you return."],[450,"The Prophet ﷺ combed through his beard."],[451,"While we were praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he heard the clamor of men behind him. When he finished his prayer, he said, “What is the matter with you?” They said, “We hurried to the prayer.” He said, “Do not do that. Let one of you pray what he catches up with and make up what he missed.”"],[452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at al-Hazwara and said, “By Allah, I know that you are the best of Allah’s land and the most beloved of Allah’s land to Allah, and had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left.”"],[453,"You should marry virgins, for they have sweeter mouths, more fertile wombs, and are more content with little."],[454,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, chose me and chose companions for me, and made among them viziers, supporters, and in-laws. Whoever reviles them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."],[455,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is with the debtor until he pays off his debt, so long as his debt is not in what Allah dislikes."],[456,"A man stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and they saw weakness in his standing, so they said, \"How incapable is so-and-so!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You have eaten your brother and backbitten him.\""],[457,"There is no divorce for one who does not own, and no manumission for one who does not own."],[458,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a dark, black night, and we stopped at a place. Each man took stones and arranged them as a mosque and prayed toward them. When morning came, we found we had not faced the qiblah. We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we prayed this night not facing the qiblah.\" Then Allah revealed: \"To Allah belong the east and the west, so wherever you turn, there is the face of Allah.\""],[459,"The first for whom depilatory paste was made and who entered the bathhouse was Sulayman b. Dawud. When he entered it and felt its heat and distress, he said, \"Oh! From the punishment of Allah! Oh, oh, before 'oh' will not avail.\""],[460,"A period of forty days was set for the woman in post-natal bleeding."],[461,"Treating people gently is charity."],[462,"The Prophet ﷺ married Umm Salamah for household goods worth ten dirhams."],[463,"The sutrah of the imam is the sutrah of those behind him."],[464,"Rejoice, for Allah has brought you your settlement. I praised Allah. He said, \"Did you not pass by the four kneeling camels?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Their necks and what is on them are yours. On them are clothing and food, a gift to me from the chief of Fadak. Take them and pay your debt.\" So I did. I unloaded their burdens and fed them. Then I stood for the call to the dawn prayer. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed, I went out to al-Baqi', put my fingers in my ears, and called out: \"Whoever has a claim of debt against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let him come.\" I kept selling and paying until no debt remained on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on earth, until there was left in my hand two uqiyyahs, or one and a half uqiyyahs. Then I went to the mosque, and most of the day had passed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting alone in the mosque. I greeted him, and he said to me, \"What happened with what you had?\" I said, \"Allah has settled everything that was against His Messenger; nothing remains.\" He said, \"Is there anything left over?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"See that you relieve me of it, for I will not enter upon any of my wives until you relieve me of it.\" No one came to us until evening. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the night prayer, he called me and said, \"What happened with what you had?\" I said, \"It is with me; no one has come to us.\" He spent the night in the mosque until morning. He prayed the second day until near the end of the day, when two riders came. I took them, fed them, and clothed them. When he prayed the night prayer, he called me and said, \"What happened with what you had?\" I said, \"Allah has relieved you of it, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said takbir and praised Allah out of fear that death might overtake him while he still owed it. Then I followed him until he came to his wives. He greeted each wife individually until he reached his sleeping place. That is what you asked me about, ﷺ. This hadith is not reported from Bilal except through this chain, and it is uniquely transmitted by Mu'awiyah b. Sallam."],[465,"I was standing by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a rabbi from the Jewish rabbis came and said: Peace be upon you, O Muhammad. I pushed him a shove by which he nearly fell, and said to him: Will you not say, 'O Messenger of Allah'? The Jew said: We only call him by the name his family gave him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: My name is Muhammad, the name my family gave me. The Jew said: I have come to ask you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Will it benefit you if I tell you?\" He said: I hear with my two ears. He made a mark with a stick he had with him and said: \"Ask.\" The Jew said: Where will the people be on the day when the earth is changed to other than the earth and the heavens? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They will be in the darkness before the bridge.\" He said: Who will be the first of the people to cross? He said: \"The poor among the emigrants.\" The Jew said: What will their greeting be when they enter Paradise? He said: \"A portion of the liver of the whale.\" He said: What will their lunch be after that? He said: \"For them will be slaughtered the nun of Paradise that eats from its edges.\" He said: What will their drink be with it? He said: \"From a spring called Salsabil.\" He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: I have come to ask you about something that no one on earth knows except a prophet, or a man, or two men. He said: \"Will it benefit you if I tell you?\" He said: I hear with my two ears. He said: I have come to ask you about the child. He said: \"The fluid of the man is white, and the fluid of the woman is yellow. When they combine, and the man's semen prevails over the woman's, they will have a male by Allah's permission. If the woman's semen prevails over the man's, they will have a female by Allah's permission.\" The Jew said: You have spoken the truth, and you are a prophet. Then he left and went away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He asked me about what he asked me, and I had no knowledge of any of it until Allah brought it to me.\""],[466,"Recite the Qur'an, for it will come on the Day of Resurrection as an intercessor for its companions. Recite the two bright ones: Surat al-Baqarah and Surat Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or as if they were two flocks of birds in rows, pleading for their companions. Recite Surat al-Baqarah, for taking it is a blessing, leaving it is a regret, and the sorcerers cannot overpower it."],[467,"\"When my Ummah does fifteen traits, affliction will befall them.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are they? He said: \"When the war booty is distributed among the powerful, the trust is treated as spoil, zakat is considered a fine, a man obeys his wife and is undutiful to his mother, voices are raised in the mosques, a man honors his friend and is harsh to his father, a man is honored out of fear of his evil, the leader of the people is the worst of them, singing girls and musical instruments are adopted, wine is drunk, and silk is worn. Then await metamorphosis, earthquakes, and sinking.\""],[468,"\"O Abu Dharr, how will you be when you are among the dregs of the people?\" And he interlaced his fingers. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me? He said: \"Be patient, be patient. Mix with people according to their character, and differ from them in their deeds.\""],[469,"Whoever wakes up and his concern is the world, he has nothing of Allah. Whoever does not care about the Muslims is not one of them. Whoever willingly gives humiliation from himself, not forced, is not one of us."],[470,"Regarding His words, mighty and glorious: 'or a remnant of knowledge' he said: \"Good handwriting.\""],[471,"I asked 'Abd Allah b. Busr: Where is our state compared to the state of those before us? He said: \"Glory be to Allah, by Allah, if they were raised from the graves they would not recognize you except that they would find you standing praying.\""],[472,"Any man who is given an 'umra, it is for him and his descendants after him; those who inherit him from his descendants inherit it. Or if he is given a ruqba, it has the same status as an 'umra."],[473,"Straighten your rows, for part of the excellence of prayer is straightening the row."],[474,"When there are three, two should not converse privately excluding the one."],[475,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, you are more beloved to me than myself, and you are more beloved to me than my family, and more beloved to me than my children. I am in the house and I remember you, and I cannot bear it until I come to you and look at you. When I remember my death and your death, I know that when you enter Paradise you will be raised with the prophets, and when I enter Paradise I fear that I will not see you. The Prophet ﷺ did not answer him until Jibril came down with this verse: 'Whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger, those are with those whom Allah has blessed - the prophets, the truthful ones...'"],[476,"There is no hadd punishment on a slave girl until she is married. If she is married, then upon her is half of what is upon free married women."],[477,"He forbade that a pregnant woman be had intercourse with until she gives birth."],[478,"Whoever touches his private part must perform ablution."],[479,"A man will enter Paradise such that no household or chamber in Paradise will remain but they will say: 'Welcome, welcome! Come to us, come to us!'\" Abu Bakr said: 'What do you think of that man on that day?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Yes, and that is you, O Abu Bakr.'"],[480,"\"Who will propose to Umm Kulthum bt. Uqbah?\" I said: 'So-and-so and so-and-so.' He said: 'Where are you regarding Abd al-Rahman b. Awf? For he is the leader of the Muslims and the best of them.'"],[481,"He used to go around his wives with a single washing."],[482,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ's caller to prayer came to him for the night prayer on a night of wind and rain, he would order him to append to his call: 'Pray in your dwellings.'"],[483,"Do you know what the example of this fire of yours is compared to the fire of Hell? It is darker in blackness than the smoke of this fire of yours by seventy times."],[484,"Indeed, a servant whose body I have made healthy and whose provision I have expanded, yet he does not come to Me every four years, is indeed deprived."],[485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Which of the people is most beloved to you?' He said: 'Aishah.' They said: 'We do not mean among women.' He said: 'Then her father.'"],[486,"Take it, O Banu Talhah, as a perpetual inheritance, one that will never cease; no one will take it from you except an oppressor."],[487,"The Prophet ﷺ sent three men to Caesar, to Chosroes, and to the ruler of Alexandria, and he sent Amr b. al-As to the Negus. When Amr came to the Negus, he found that those who were with him used to enter bowing through a small door. When Amr saw the small door and their entry through it, he turned his back, then entered walking backwards. When he entered through it, he straightened up. The Abyssinians were startled and intended to kill him. They said: 'What prevented you from entering as we enter?' He said: 'We do not do that with our Prophet, and he is more deserving that it be done to him.' The Negus said: 'Leave him, he has spoken the truth.'"],[488,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he finished the two Eid prayers, he would come to the middle of the prayer place, stand, and look at the people, how they were leaving and what their appearance was. Then he would stand for a while, then leave."],[489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and we entered with him through the gate of Banu 'Abd Manaf—the one people call the gate of Banu Shaybah—and we went out with him to Madinah through the gate of al-Hazwarah, which is the gate of the tailors."],[490,"When he touched the Black Stone, he would say: \"O Allah, with faith in You, belief in Your Book, and following the Sunnah of Your Prophet.\""],[491,"The best rows for men are the first ones, and the worst are the last ones; the best rows for women are the last ones, and the worst are the first ones."],[492,"Your appointed term in relation to the nations before you is like the time between the afternoon prayer and sunset."],[493,"If he refuses, then return him; if he refuses, then fight him, for he is but a devil."],[494,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him ahead from Muzdalifah to Mina among the weak members of his family."],[495,"'Umar b. al-Khattab sent for me, inviting me to the pre-dawn meal, and said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it the blessed morning meal.\""],[496,"When he got up at night, his tooth-stick and water for ablution were placed for him."],[497,"We used to pray the two rak'ahs before Maghrib during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[498,"No one has a greater favor upon me than Abu Bakr. He supported me with his wealth and his self, and married me to his daughter."],[499,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, and the cooking pots boiled with the meat of domesticated donkeys. He ordered us to overturn them, and he distributed to every ten of us a sheep."],[500,"A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim."],[501,"Umm Sulaym sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she had made for him a dish of dates and butter. I looked for him and found him in the house of a servant of his who was a tailor, and he had made for him food containing small grains and gourd. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began eating the gourd and pushing aside the small grains with his forefinger. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sulaym has made for you a dish of dates and butter, and she would like you to eat from it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and ate from it. She said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, Anas—supplicate to Allah for him.\" He said, \"O Allah, lengthen his life, increase his wealth and children, and forgive him.\""],[502,"Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have ordered their killing. So kill from them every pure black one."],[503,"There is no amputation for a plunderer, nor for a snatcher, nor for a traitor."],[504,"The one in ihram should not marry, nor propose, nor be proposed to. And none of you should sell over the sale of his brother, nor propose over the proposal of his brother until he gives permission."],[505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left nothing on the day he died except a white mule, his weapons, and land that he made as charity."],[506,"In the month of Ramadan there is the sound, in Dhu al-Qa'dah the tribes are distinguished, and in Dhu al-Hijjah the pilgrim is robbed."],[507,"When a woman goes out of her house while her husband dislikes that, every angel in the sky and everything she passes by, except jinn and humans, curses her until she returns."],[508,"He entered upon A'ishah one morning, and she said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, teach me the name of Allah by which if He is called He answers, and if He is asked by it He gives.\" The Prophet ﷺ turned his face away, so she got up and performed ablution, then said, \"O Allah, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and by Your great name by which if You are called You answer, and if You are asked by it You give.\" He said, \"By Allah, it is indeed among these names.\""],[509,"I sat in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a gathering, than which I never sat before it or after it any more enviable to me: the Prophet of Allah ﷺ came out while people were at his chamber arguing about the Qur'an. He came out of the house as if pomegranate seeds had been crushed on his face, or as if blood were dripping from his face, and said: 'O people, was this what you were commanded—to argue about the Qur'an, one part of it against another? The Qur'an was not revealed so that one part of it would contradict another. If a part is ambiguous, then believe in it.'"],[510,"Wheat for barley, two for one, hand to hand; and it is not permissible on credit."],[511,"Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women in prayer."],[512,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Advise me.' He said: 'Leave off he said and he said, asking too many questions, and wasting wealth.'"],[513,"When deficiency fell among the Children of Israel, a man would see his brother committing a sin and forbid him from it, but then he would meet him the next day and what he saw from him did not prevent him from being his companion, his table companion, and his drinking companion. So Allah struck the hearts of some of them against others, and the Qur'an was revealed concerning them: 'Cursed were those who disbelieved among the Children of Israel by the tongue of David and Jesus, son of Mary'—the verse—up to His saying: 'many of them were defiantly disobedient.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'No, by the One in whose hand is my soul, not until you seize the hand of the wrongdoer and force him back to the truth completely.'"],[514,"When the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution, he would run his fingers through his beard."],[515,"There is no marriage except with the permission of a guardian who is mature, or a ruler."],[516,"Whoever does not trim his mustache is not one of us."],[517,"Whoever says in the morning and in the evening: 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,' nothing will harm him."],[518,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'When the victory of Allah and the conquest comes,' he said: 'The conquest of Makkah; the Prophet's ﷺ own death was announced to him: seek forgiveness of your Lord, and know that your term has come.'"],[519,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me during the Umrah of Hudaybiyyah when I had many insects in my hair, and said: 'O Ka'b, this is indeed harmful?' I said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, is there a concession?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes, offer a sacrificial animal, or fast three days, or feed six poor people.'"],[520,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a found item that is found in inhabited land in a watercourse. He said: 'Announce it for a year; if its owner comes, then it is his, otherwise it is yours.' He was asked about a found item found in enemy territory, and he said: 'For it and for buried treasure is one fifth.' He was asked about a stray sheep, and he said: 'Take it, for it is for you, your brother, or the wolf.' He was asked about a stray camel, and he said: 'Leave it, for with it are its shoes and its water skin; it will come to water and eat from trees.' He was asked about the mountain guard (protected livestock), and he said: 'He is beaten several times and the fine is multiplied on him; but if it is from the pen and reaches the value of a shield—which is one dinar—then amputation applies; and if it is less than that, he is beaten several times and the fine is multiplied.'"],[521,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took my hand and said: “No two believers meet and each takes the hand of his companion, taking it only out of love for Allah, and then they part, except that they are forgiven.”"],[522,"She entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to her: “Do you have a husband?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “How are you toward him?” She said: “I do not fall short except in what I am unable to do.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Look to where you stand with him, for he is your Paradise and your Hell.”"],[523,"Whoever would be pleased to look at the person most resembling the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in guidance, manner, and conduct when he leaves his house until he returns, let him look at 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud."],[524,"Your mother has come to Basra, and she is the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this world and his wife in the Hereafter."],[525,"A woman entered the Fire because of a cat which she tied up: she neither gave it water nor fed it, nor let it loose to eat from the insects of the earth until it died in its tether. And a prostitute entered Paradise: she passed by a dog at a well, wanting water but unable to reach it, so she took off her leather sock – or her boot – and tied it to her veil, then drew water for it and gave it to drink until she had quenched its thirst."],[526,"Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has indeed fought, and whoever looks after his family with good has indeed fought."],[527,"I spent the night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He got up for his need, wearing a Byzantine jubbah, and he cleaned himself, then performed ablution and wiped over his khuffs. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, why don't you take them off?” He said: “I put them on in a state of purity.”"],[528,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, how can that be?” He said: “Faith departs from him; if he repents, it returns to him.”"],[529,"Nothing of this world ever amazed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor did anything of it please him except piety."],[530,"I am not about to look into My servant's right until My servant looks into My right."],[531,"Whoever leaves the first row for fear of harming anyone, Allah doubles for him the reward of the first row."],[532,"When one of you performs ablution, let him rinse his mouth and sniff water into his nose, and the ears are part of the head."],[533,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"How will you be when a quarter of Paradise is yours, and for the rest of mankind three quarters of it?\" They said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"How will you be when half is yours?\" They said: \"That is even more.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: \"The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows, of which you will have eighty rows.\""],[534,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her while in a state of ihram, and consummated the marriage after exiting ihram. Then she died at Sarif, and that is her grave beneath the canopy."],[535,"I went on the campaign of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year eight, in Ramadan. It happened to fall on a Friday, a rainy day, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal and he called out: \"Pray at your mounts.\""],[536,"Tayammum is a single strike for the face and the palms."],[537,"Beware of pride, for pride may be in a man even if he wears a cloak."],[538,"The Messenger of Allah commanded him to call out among the people of Mina in two garments: \"Let no one fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking.\""],[539,"I was overtaken by menstruation while I was with the Messenger of Allah on his bed, so I slipped away until I was on the ground. He said: \"What is the matter with you?\" I told him that I had started menstruating, so he ordered me to tie my waist-wrapper up to the middle of my thighs and to come back."],[540,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the prayer has caught the prayer."],[541,"Whoever of you comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[542,"Aflah b. Abi al-Qu'ays asked permission to enter upon her, so she said: \"Let me ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She asked him, and he said: \"Let him enter upon you, for he is your paternal uncle.\" And he said: \"What is forbidden by breastfeeding is what is forbidden by lineage.\""],[543,"He used to pray while she was lying crosswise in front of him on the bed."],[544,"He was asked about a man who breaks wind during his prayer. He said: \"He should not leave until he hears a sound or detects an odor.\""],[545,"I came upon a she-ass when I had nearly reached the age of puberty, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying with the people. I passed beyond part of the row, then I let it loose and returned and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not repeat anything for me."],[546,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted in the year of the conquest until he reached al-Kadid, then he broke his fast, and his companions broke their fast. They follow the most recent, then the most recent, of the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that is the abrogating, decisive one."],[547,"When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break your fast. If it is obscured for you, then complete thirty days."],[548,"Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever attends it until it is buried has two qirats. And whoever eats of this vegetable should not come near our mosque."],[549,"A man came to Ibn Umar and said, \"What do you say about Ali?\" He said, \"That is his house.\" He said, \"What do you say about Uthman?\" He said, \"What can I say about a man who committed a sin between himself and God, and God forgave him, and committed a sin between you and him, and you killed him?\""],[550,"Whoever lives in the desert becomes harsh, whoever follows game becomes heedless, and whoever goes to the ruler is put to trial."],[551,"Whoever supports two slave-girls until they reach maturity, he and I will enter Paradise like this\" – and he pointed with his two fingers, the thumb and the one next to it."],[552,"Seven things are from the sunnah for a child on the seventh day: he is named, circumcised, the harm is removed from him, his ear is pierced, an aqiqah is offered for him, his head is shaved, and he is smeared with the blood of his aqiqah, and charity is given of the weight of his hair in gold or silver."],[553,"I saw Anas b. Malik wearing a red fur garment, and he said, \"Our blankets at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we would wear them and pray in them.\""],[554,"Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating. Umar went to the Prophet ﷺ and he commanded him to take her back, then if it seemed appropriate to him, he could divorce her while she was pure, at the beginning of her waiting period."],[555,"Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or allies himself with other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people."],[556,"There is no morning or evening but the patches of the earth call to one another: \"O neighbor, has a righteous servant passed by you today who prayed on you or remembered God?\" If she says, \"Yes,\" she sees for herself thereby a virtue over it."],[557,"The Rukn will come on the Day of Resurrection greater than Abu Qubays, having a tongue and two lips, testifying for those who touched it with truth; it is the right hand of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with which He shakes the hands of His creation."],[558,"I have not left after me a trial more harmful to men than women."],[559,"A woman will not remain upright for you upon a single nature; she is only like a rib: if you straighten it, you break it; if you leave it, you enjoy her while she still has crookedness."],[560,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the dawn prayer in the mosque, and behind him were the believing women. When he gave the greeting, they would go out wrapped in their cloaks, not being recognized due to the darkness before dawn."],[561,"I was given the strength of forty men in might and sexual intercourse, and no believer is given but the strength of ten. Desire was made into ten parts: nine parts were placed in women and one part in men. Were it not for the modesty cast upon them along with their desires, every man would have nine lustful women."],[562,"Do not prevent the maidservants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, but let them not come except without perfume."],[563,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a single day except with a husband or a mahram."],[564,"O people, do not be excessive in the dowries of women, for if it were an honor among people or piety before Allah, the most deserving of it would be the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He did not marry any of his wives, nor did he give any of his daughters in marriage, except for twelve uqiyyah and a nashsh. Yet one of you would be excessive in a woman's dowry until he says, 'I have burdened myself for you with the hanging of the water-skin.' He said: I was a young boy and I did not know what the hanging of the water-skin was."],[565,"The Jews used to say: If a man has intercourse with his wife from behind her in her private part, his child will be cross-eyed. So Allah, exalted is He, revealed: 'Your wives are a tilth for you.'"],[566,"There was shown to me what will be opened for my nation after me, and it pleased me. So Allah, exalted is He, revealed: 'And the Hereafter is better for you than the first' up to His saying: 'so you will be satisfied.' He gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces of pearl, their dust is musk, in each palace what befits it."],[567,"Indeed, the recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger—he said: They are from 'Ukl."],[568,"Whoever's last words are: 'There is no god but Allah' will not enter the Fire."],[569,"I said to 'Ali: 'Tell me about this march of yours—is it a covenant that the Messenger of God ﷺ entrusted to you?' He said: 'No, but it is an opinion I held.'"],[570,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at Madinah and said: 'God has purified the people of this city as long as the stars do not lead them astray.'"],[571,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delayed the 'Isha' prayer one night until the people slept, then they woke up. 'Umar came and said: 'The prayer, O Messenger of God.' So he went out and led them in prayer, and he did not mention that they performed ablution."],[572,"Whoever sees someone who has been favored over him in wealth and physical form, let him look to one who is below him."],[573,"Thus is the believer: he combines excellence and compassion, while the hypocrite combines evil and heedlessness. By God, I have not found, in the past or in the future, a servant who increases in excellence except that he increases in fear and compassion from Him, nor have I found, in the past or in the future, a servant who increases in evil except that he increases in heedlessness. No one narrated this hadith from 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Umar except Mubarak b. Fadala."],[574,"Glorification (tasbih) in prayer is for men, and clapping is for women."],[575,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from selling what I do not have."],[576,"When I learned what the people of the slander had said, I resolved to go to a well and throw myself into it."],[577,"If I take someone's beloved and he remains patient and seeks reward, I will not be content with any reward for him less than Paradise."],[578,"When a man narrated to me from the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would make him swear an oath, and if he swore, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me—and Abu Bakr was truthful—that he ﷺ said: 'There is no servant who commits a sin, then prays two rak'ahs, then seeks God's forgiveness, except that He forgives him.'"],[579,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim."],[580,"O 'Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for authority, for if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it, but if you are given it because of asking, you will be left to it. And if you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do that which is better and expiate for your oath."],[581,"Regarding the words of God, Mighty and Majestic: “Whatever you cut down of [their] palm trees or left standing on their roots, it was by God’s permission” [Q 59:5], he said: “Al-līnah is the date palm.” “And so that He might disgrace the transgressors” [Q 59:5] – he said: “They brought them down from their fortresses and were commanded to cut the palm trees, and that caused unease in their hearts. The Muslims said: ‘We cut some and left some. We must ask the Messenger of God ﷺ: will we have a reward for what we cut, and will we bear a burden of sin for what we left?’ So God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: ‘Whatever you cut down of [their] palm trees or left standing on their roots, it was by God’s permission, and so that He might disgrace the transgressors.’”"],[582,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper, and whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not sit at a table where wine is passed around."],[583,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the fast of ʿĀshūrāʾ and said: “Whoever is fasting, let him complete his fast, and whoever is not fasting, let him fast for the rest of his day.”"],[584,"Abū Bakr had a seat near the Prophet ﷺ from which he would not move except for al-ʿAbbās, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was pleased by that. One day al-ʿAbbās approached, and Abū Bakr moved aside for him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “What is the matter with you?” He said: “O Messenger of God, your uncle has arrived.” The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at him, then turned to Abū Bakr smiling and said: “This is al-ʿAbbās, who has come wearing white garments, and his descendants after him will wear black, and twelve men from among them will rule.” When al-ʿAbbās came, he said: “O Messenger of God, what did you say to Abū Bakr?” He said: “I said nothing but good.” He said: “You have spoken truly, by my father and mother, you say nothing but good.” He said: “I said: My uncle has come wearing white garments, and his descendants after him will wear black, and twelve men from among them will rule.”"],[585,"He used to deliver the sermon leaning on a palm trunk. When the pulpit was built, the trunk moaned, and the Prophet ﷺ embraced it, and it became still."],[586,"Rain was withheld during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ in Madinah, until prices rose and people feared ruin for their wealth, and we feared ruin for ourselves. We said: “Call upon your Lord to send us rain.” The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hands toward the sky, and by God, we saw not a single white cloud in the sky, and by God, he did not lower his hand until I saw the sky split open from here and there, until I saw piled clouds, and it poured for seven nights and their days, from one Friday to the next, while the sky continued to pour. They said: “We fear drowning; call upon your Lord to withhold it.” I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ raising his hands, and we saw no greenness in the sky, and he said: “O God, around us and not upon us.” He said: By God, he did not lower his hand until I saw the sky breaking apart."],[587,"The month is twenty-nine days. When you sight the crescent, fast, and when you sight it, break the fast. If it is obscured for you, then estimate it."],[588,"Quraysh did not cease to be restrained from me until Abū Ṭālib died."],[589,"The most beloved supplication to the Messenger of God ﷺ was to supplicate three times."],[590,"The Prophet ﷺ accepted the testimony of a midwife."],[591,"When al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī wanted to go out to Iraq, Ibn ʿUmar said to him: “Do not go out, for the Messenger of God ﷺ was given the choice between this world and the Hereafter, and he chose the Hereafter, and neither you nor anyone of your descendants will attain it.” When he insisted on going out, Ibn ʿUmar said to him: “I entrust you to God from being killed.”"],[592,"Guard yourselves from people by thinking ill of them."],[593,"The minimum of menstruation is three [days], and its maximum is ten."],[594,"A man is on the verge of being concerned about who will accept his charity from him, and he will not find him."],[595,"Whoever revives dead land, it belongs to him, and there is no right for an unjust root."],[596,"Five animals are all sinful; they are to be killed in the sacred precinct and outside it, and the pilgrim in ihram kills them: the kite, the snake, the mouse, the scorpion, and the biting dog."],[597,"Qatada was asked about a man who missed a rakʿa of the dawn prayer until the sun rose, and he said."],[598,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ relieved himself, I brought him water, and he would cleanse himself with it and wipe his hand on the ground."],[599,"Today is the day of staking, and tomorrow is the race, and the goal is Paradise or the Fire, and the one who perishes is the one who enters the Fire. I am the first, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq is the second, and Umar b. al-Khattab is the third, then the people after me are according to precedence, the first then the first."],[600,"I met Abu Hurayra in Syria, and he said to me: \"Are you al-Farazdaq?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Are you the poet?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Indeed, if you remain, you will meet people who say: 'There is no repentance for you,' so beware of cutting off your hope from God.\""],[601,"Loyalty belongs to the one who frees, and meat was given as charity to Barira, and she gifted some of it to Aisha, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is charity for her, and a gift for us.\""],[602,"Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if he has seen me while awake, for Satan cannot take my form."],[603,"Whoever humiliates a friend of mine has challenged me to war."],[604,"Between my grave and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."],[605,"We did not think that the Messenger of God ﷺ died on the day he died while he loved a man, and that God would enter him into the Fire. It was said to him: He used to employ you? He said: God knows best, but he loved a man. They said: Who is he? He said: \"He loved 'Ammar b. Yasir.\""],[606,"The delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: We saw him praying in two sandals facing each other."],[607,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Khaybar, the people fell upon garlic and began eating it, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever eats of this vegetable, let him not approach our mosque."],[608,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ on his mount on the Day of Sacrifice saying: Let my community take its rites, for I do not know whether I will perform Hajj after this year of mine."],[609,"The Prophet of God ﷺ used to throw on the first day at forenoon the Jamrat al-'Aqabah once, and after that at the sun's decline."],[610,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ throwing pebbles like the small stones thrown with the fingers."],[611,"The Friday bath is obligatory on whoever has reached puberty among those who attend Friday."],[612,"He forbade the jallalah—its meat, its milk, and its back (riding)."],[613,"The Messenger of God ﷺ shaved his head, and a group of his companions did so, and some of them shortened their hair."],[614,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, God, Mighty and Majestic, will give the man from the community of Muhammad the Jew and the Christian, and it will be said: Ransom yourself from the Fire with this."],[615,"Excellent condiment is vinegar."],[616,"A time will come upon people when a strong camel and two water-skins will be dearer to a man than what he owns."],[617,"You will indeed conquer the city of Heraclius, or Caesar's, and divide its wealth by the shields. The crier will make them hear that the Dajjal has replaced them among their families, so they will throw away what they have and go out and fight."],[618,"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him. Masruq said: I said: Did you hear it from her? He said: Yes. So I traveled to Madinah and mentioned that to 'A'ishah and said: We dislike death. She said: It is not like that. Rather it is at the time of death: the believer sees what he has with Allah and loves to meet Him, and the disbeliever hates death, and Allah hates him at that time."],[619,"Do not leave the mosque until I teach you a verse from a surah that was not sent down upon anyone before me except Sulayman b. Dawud. The Prophet ﷺ went out until he reached the threshold of the door, then said: With what do you open your prayer and recitation? I said: With Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim. He said: It is that, it is that. Then he brought out his other foot."],[620,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and whatever intoxicates in large amounts, a small amount of it is forbidden."],[621,"When did you used to pray 'Asr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: While the sun was white and pure."],[622,"The days and nights will not pass until the happiest person in this world is Luka' b. Luka'."],[623,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on his she-camel. He said: Beware of treachery, for it is an evil inner garment. Beware of injustice, for it will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of stinginess, for it destroyed those before you until they shed their blood and severed their ties of kinship."],[624,"The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon and said: To proceed."],[625,"Security and well-being are two blessings in which many people are deceived."],[626,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ walking in a funeral procession, and he rode when he returned on a bare horse with nothing on it but its bridle."],[627,"Ask Allah for the wasilah for me, for no servant asks it for me in this world except that I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[628,"I entered upon Abu al-Darda' to visit him in his illness and said: O Abu al-Darda', do you not like to be healthy so that you do not fall ill? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Headache and fever cling to a person until they do not leave upon him a sin equal to the weight of a mustard seed."],[629,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the House and prayed two rak'ahs to the left of the second pillar."],[630,"When you prostrate, place your palms on the ground, for the palms prostrate just as the face prostrates."],[631,"Do not curse time, for Allah is time."],[632,"You should wear white garments; wear them and shroud your dead in them."],[633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the Jamrat al-'Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice in the forenoon, and threw the rest after the sun had passed its zenith."],[634,"Two kinds of my community will not receive my intercession: a tyrannical ruler and an extremist in religion."],[635,"I saw a dog following behind Malik b. Dinar, and I said, 'What is this, O Abu Yahya?' He said, 'This is better than an evil companion.'"],[636,"The Children of Israel said, 'O Musa, does your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, create creatures and then punish them?' Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to him, 'Sow.' So he sowed. Then He said, 'Harvest.' So he harvested. Then He said, 'Thresh it.' So he threshed it, and the chaff gathered. He said, 'For what is this suitable?' He said, 'For the fire.' He said, 'Thus I do not punish any of My creatures except those who deserve the fire.'"],[637,"Men and women boasted, and Abu Hurayrah said, 'Women will be more numerous in Paradise than men.' Umar b. al-Khattab looked at the people and said, 'Do you hear what Abu Hurayrah is saying?' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The first group to enter Paradise will have faces like the full moon on the night of its fullness, and the second group will have faces like the brightest star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives, the marrow of whose shins will be visible through the skin, and there will be no unmarried person in Paradise.'"],[638,"I entered upon Abu Musa while he was eating chicken meat, and he said, 'Come.' I said, 'I saw it eating filth, so I would prefer not to eat it.' He said, 'Sit, for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eating it.'"],[639,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had intercourse with one of his wives and was too lazy to get up, he would strike his hand on the wall and perform tayammum."],[640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me three years after Khadijah."],[641,"Jibril kept instructing me about the neighbor, until I thought he would make him an heir."],[642,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a land called ʿAdhirah, and he named it Khadirah."],[643,"Help your brother whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. If he is an oppressor, restrain him; and if he is oppressed, take [his right] for him."],[644,"I stayed as a guest with my maternal aunt Maymunah. She was menstruating that night and not praying, so she threw me a cloak, placed a pillow beside her, and spread [a bed] for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came from the mosque, he took off his garment, took a piece of cloth and wore it, then lay down beside her."],[645,"The servant does not attain the true reality of faith until he gets angry for Allah and is pleased for Allah. When he does that, he has deserved the true reality of faith. Indeed, my beloved and my allies are those who are remembered through my remembrance, and I am remembered through their remembrance."],[646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: 'She is like the man; if she has an emission, she must perform ghusl, and if she does not have an emission, she does not have to perform ghusl.'"],[647,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ spit into his garment during the prayer, then rub it with his finger."],[648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered our house - and a water skin was hanging - and he drank from it while standing. My mother got up and cut off the mouth of the water skin and said: 'No one will drink from it after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[649,"Whoever conceals an indecency, it is as if he has brought back to life a buried infant."],[650,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention Muʿawiyah, and he said: 'O Allah, make him a guide, rightly guided, and guide through him.'"],[651,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with this hand of mine, and we kissed it, and that was not disapproved."],[652,"A man from the Ansar became blind, so he sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Mark out a mosque for me in my house so that I can pray in it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and his people had gathered to him, but one man among them was absent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What happened to so-and-so?' Some of the people mentioned him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Did he not witness Badr?' They said: 'Yes, but he is such-and-such.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.'"],[653,"There is no governor of three (persons) but he will meet God with his right hand fettered; his justice will release it, or his tyranny will keep it bound."],[654,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a man who had committed fornication, and he questioned him, and he confessed. So he gave orders concerning him, and he was stripped, and behold he was emaciated of body, paralyzed. He said: 'What would flogging leave of this one? Nothing.' So he called for a palm branch with a hundred twigs, and struck him with it one strike."],[655,"O Guardian of Islam and its people, make me steadfast in it until I meet You."],[656,"O God, I seek refuge in You from a heart that is not humble, from a soul that is not satisfied, from knowledge that does not benefit, and from a supplication that is not heard. O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of these four. O God, forgive me my sins, my errors, and my deliberate acts."],[657,"Whoever kills a protected soul without its right will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and the fragrance of Paradise is found from a distance of a hundred years' journey."],[658,"\"Indeed, those who have divided their religion and become sects—you are not associated with them in anything.\" He said: \"They are the people of innovation and desires from this nation.\""],[659,"I used to play with dolls in the house of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[660,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the soothsayers, and he said: \"They are nothing.\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, but they sometimes tell of something and it turns out to be true.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"That is a word of truth which a jinni snatches and pours into the ear of his protégé like the cackling of a hen, and they mix into it a hundred lies.\""],[661,"God will seize the earth and fold the heaven with His right hand, then He will say: 'I am the King. Where are the kings of the earth?'"],[662,"\"O Abu Hurayrah, I adjure you by God, did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say—answer on behalf of the Messenger of God ﷺ—'O God, support him with the Holy Spirit?'\" Abu Hurayrah said: \"Yes.\""],[663,"When God revealed concerning poetry what He revealed, Ka'b b. Malik came to the Messenger of God and said: \"O Messenger of God, God has revealed concerning poetry what you know. What do you think?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The believer indeed strives with his sword and his tongue.\""],[664,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to bring out the adolescent girls, the secluded virgins, and the menstruating women, so that they may witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims. A woman said: \"O Messenger of God, what if one of them does not have a garment?\" He said: \"Let her sister clothe her with a portion of her garment,\" meaning on the day of Eid."],[665,"Abu Qatada had a thick head of hair. He asked the Prophet ﷺ about it, and he said: 'Honor it and oil it.'"],[666,"The growth of hair in the nose is protection against leprosy."],[667,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a woman who had been killed in one of his battles and said: 'This one was not fighting.' He then forbade killing women and children."],[668,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'O Ali, you have a treasure in Paradise, and you are the possessor of its two horns. Do not follow one glance with another, for the first is yours, but the second is not.'"],[669,"The Prophet ﷺ had a blanket dyed with wars and saffron, with which he would go around to his wives. On the night of this one, she would sprinkle it with water, and on the night of this one, she would sprinkle it with water."],[670,"Be cupped on the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first of the month."],[671,"Keep a white rooster, for a house with a white rooster is not approached by a devil, a sorcerer, or the little dwellings around it."],[672,"Excellent is the tooth-stick of the olive tree, from a blessed tree; it sweetens the mouth and removes decay. It is my tooth-stick and the tooth-stick of the prophets before me."],[673,"Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. If he is oppressed, help him against the one who oppresses him. If he is an oppressor, restrain him from oppression."],[674,"I never saw anyone more handsome than the Messenger of God ﷺ in a red robe."],[675,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[676,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would recite in the witr: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' 'Say: O disbelievers,' and 'Say: He is God, the One.'"],[677,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: “All compliments, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.”"],[678,"Whoever offers one of his children [in death] patiently and seeking reward, they will shield him from the Fire by Allah’s permission."],[679,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: He fears six traits for his Ummah: the leadership of youths, the proliferation of police, bribery in judgment, severing ties of kinship, taking blood lightly, and a generation who take the Qur’an as musical instruments, putting forward a man who is not the most learned in jurisprudence among them, nor the most knowledgeable, nor the most virtuous, to sing to them in song."],[680,"He forbade killing the harmless creatures that inhabit houses."],[681,"Do not revile my Companions. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if one of you were to spend the like of Uhud in gold, it would not reach the measure of one of them, nor even half of it."],[682,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not admit his wife into the bathhouse. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table upon which wine is passed around."],[683,"The example of one who learns knowledge but does not relate it is like the example of one who hoards a treasure and does not spend from it."],[684,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were eating upon a shield. He sat down and ate with us, and he did not touch water."],[685,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of the Ansar who were laughing, and said: “Make much mention of the destroyer of pleasures.”"],[686,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting facing the Ka’bah, holding his knees with his hands."],[687,"There is no zakat on less than five wasqs, no zakat on less than five camels, and no zakat on less than five uqiyyahs."],[688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man naming his slave or his child Harith, Murrah, Walid, Hakam, Abu al-Hakam, Aflah, Najih, or Yasar. And he said: “The most beloved of names to Allah are those by which He is worshiped, and the truest of names is Hammam.”"],[689,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, he faced it and said: You are sacred; how great is your sanctity and how sweet is your fragrance, but the believer has greater sanctity in the sight of God than you."],[690,"When a person sneezes, respond to him with a blessing even if he is behind seven seas. Whoever blesses a sneezer, pleurisy, toothache, and earache depart from him."],[691,"Whoever eats a meal at the expense of a Muslim man, God will feed him the like of it from Hell. Whoever is clothed with a garment at the expense of a man, God will clothe him with the like of it from Hell. Whoever makes a Muslim man stand in a position of showing off and reputation, God will make him stand in a position of showing off and reputation on the Day of Resurrection."],[692,"A man wanted to pledge allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and noticed traces of yellow perfume on him, so he refused to accept his pledge and said: The perfume of men is that whose scent is apparent while its color is hidden, and the perfume of women is that whose color is apparent while its scent is hidden."],[693,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ with a cousin of mine, and in his hand was a tooth-stick (siwāk) he was using. I said: O Messenger of God, appoint us as governors, for we have wealth. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: We do not wish to appoint over our work anyone who is eager for it."],[694,"Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call."],[695,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: 'And take the station of Ibrāhīm as a place of prayer.'"],[696,"Five are pests that are to be killed in the sanctuary: the kite, the crow, the scorpion, the mouse, and the biting dog."],[697,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, my mother died suddenly, and I think that had she spoken she would have given charity. Will she have a reward if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes."],[698,"People are like mines. The best of them in the pre-Islamic era are the best of them in Islam, if they attain understanding."],[699,"Do not initiate the greeting of peace with them, and when you meet them on a road, force them to its narrowest part."],[700,"For one of you to sit on a live coal and have it burn his clothes until it reaches his flesh is better for him than to sit on a grave."],[701,"Whoever prays over a funeral procession has a qīrāṭ, and whoever prays over it and follows it until it is buried has two qīrāṭs."],[702,"A servant may give in charity a single date from good earnings, and he places it where it is due, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, receives it with His right hand; then He continues to nurture it as one of you would best nurture his foal, until it becomes like a mountain or even greater."],[703,"Woe to the heels from the Fire."],[704,"Allah does not conceal [the faults of] a servant in this world except that Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection."],[705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he began the prayer, raised his hands to his shoulders."],[706,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to give him the pledge of allegiance, and he said: 'Go and dye [your hands with henna], then come to me so that I may accept your pledge.'"],[707,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man supplicating with both his fingers together, so he forbade him and said: 'Supplicate with one of them, the right one.'"],[708,"Shall I show you how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution? He took water with his hand, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then took water with his hand and brought his other hand to it, and washed his face, then he took water and washed his hand and forearms, then he did the same with the other, then he wiped his head, then he took water and sprinkled it on his feet and wiped both his feet, while wearing sandals."],[709,"O Muslim women, let none of you look down upon a gift for her neighbor, even if it be a burnt hoof."],[710,"Do not turn away a beggar, even if with a burnt hoof."],[711,"ʿAlī ordered ʿAmmār to ask the Prophet ﷺ about sexual fluid, and he said: 'He should wash his penis and perform ablution.'"],[712,"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will we have intercourse with our wives in Paradise?' He said: 'Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, a man will have intercourse with a hundred virgins in a single morning.'"],[713,"It does not harm any of you with a little of his wealth, whether he marries or with much, after he has it witnessed."],[714,"Indeed I am your forerunner at the Pond, and indeed the distance between its two ends is like the distance between Sana'a and Aylah, and indeed the pitchers in it are as numerous as the stars."],[715,"Every supplication is veiled until blessings are invoked upon Muhammad ﷺ and the family of Muhammad."],[716,"Perform ablution from what the fire has changed."],[717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to marry a man to a woman, so he said: \"O So-and-so, would you like me to marry you to So-and-so? O So-and-so, would you like me to marry you to So-and-so?\""],[718,"The best of marriages is the easiest of them."],[719,"Whoever says Allahu Akbar thirty-three times after every prayer, and says Subhan Allah thirty-three times, and says Alhamdulillah thirty-three times, and says: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things' - completing one hundred - his sins will be forgiven even if they were more than the foam of the sea."],[720,"He owed his father some wasqs of dates. We said to the man: Take the fruit of our palm trees, but he refused. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and with him was Umar, and he supplicated for us for blessing in it. Then we harvested it and gave the man everything that was his, and the estimated yield of our palm trees remained the same. So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, and he said: 'Inform Umar.' So I informed him, and he said: 'I knew, O Messenger of Allah, that when you supplicated for them for blessing in it, it would be blessed.'"],[721,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her on the day of the conquest, and he prayed the Duha prayer four rak'ahs."],[722,"Umm Hani' claimed that he - meaning the Prophet ﷺ - ate a shoulder, and did not perform ablution."],[723,"The Prophet ﷺ ate from the meat of a sheep, and did not perform ablution."],[724,"Indeed, people will come out of the Fire."],[725,"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness."],[726,"For everything there is a lineage, and the lineage of Allah is: Say, ‘He is Allah, [who is] One.’"],[727,"What is between my grave and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my cistern."],[728,"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[729,"“This is the son of Adam,” and he placed his hand under his chin, then spread his hand and said: “This is his hope.”"],[730,"A time will come upon people when they are wolves; whoever is not a wolf, the wolves will eat him."],[731,"Whoever is afflicted with a calamity in his wealth or in himself, and he conceals it and does not complain about it to people, it is incumbent upon Allah to forgive him."],[732,"When Allah created the Garden of Eden, He created in it what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined. Then He said to it: ‘Speak,’ and it said: ‘The believers have indeed succeeded.’"],[733,"Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row. And he used to come to us at prayer and wipe our shoulders and chests, saying: ‘Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.’"],[734,"The best thing to which mounts are ridden is this mosque of mine and the Ancient House."],[735,"Say, ‘He is Allah, [who is] One’ equals a third of the Qur’an."],[736,"Indeed, when the believer is attended by death, the angels come to him with a silk cloth containing musk and bundles of sweet basil, and his soul is drawn out as a hair is drawn out of dough. And it is said: ‘O tranquil soul, come out pleased and pleasing, and pleased with you.’ Then the silk cloth is folded over it and it is sent up to the highest of the high. And when the disbeliever is attended by death, the angels come with a coarse cloth containing a live coal, and his soul is wrenched out with a violent wrenching. And it is said: ‘O wicked soul, come out angry and with anger upon you, to humiliation and punishment.’ And when his soul comes out and is placed upon that coal, it makes a hissing sound, and the coarse cloth is folded over it and it is taken away to the lowest of the low."],[737,"Safety of the people of the earth from dissension is allegiance to Quraysh. Quraysh are the people of Allah—three times. If any Arab tribe opposes them, they become the party of Iblis."],[738,"Nothing makes water impure except what changes its smell or taste."],[739,"When the Prophet ﷺ dispatched a raiding party, he said: “In the name of Allah, and in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill children.”"],[740,"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing."],[741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ craved dates, so a saa‘ of ‘ajwah dates was brought. When they brought it, he found it objectionable and said: “Where did you get this?” They said: “We sent two saa‘s and received one saa‘.” He said: “Return it, return it; we have no need of it.”"],[742,"Among the signs of the Hour are that miserliness and obscenity will appear, the treacherous will be trusted, the trustworthy will be considered treacherous, and clothing will appear worn by women who are clothed yet naked, and the lowly will rise above the noble.” “Is that so, O ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud? Did you hear it from my beloved?” He said: “Yes, by the Lord of the Ka‘bah.”"],[743,"I am your forerunner ahead of you. If you do not find me, then I will be at the Hawd. The Hawd is between Aylah and Makkah. Men and women will come with vessels and water-skins."],[744,"When one of you intends to marry a woman, there is no harm in looking at her."],[745,"A man asked ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Umar about fasting on the Day of ‘Arafah. He said: “While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we considered it equal to fasting two years.”"],[746,"Usamah b. Zayd was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from ‘Arafah to Muzdalifah, then al-Fadl rode behind him from Muzdalifah to Mina. Both of them reported: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles.”"],[747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to separate the even and odd prayers with a taslim, and he would make us hear it."],[748,"Blessing has been placed for my ummah in its early morning."],[749,"The support of my community is through its wicked ones."],[750,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding this verse: \"For those who do good is the best [reward] and more\" (Yunus 10:26): When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, a caller will call out: \"O people of Paradise, you have a promise with God that He wishes to fulfill for you.\" They will say: \"And what is it? Has He not whitened our faces, made our scales heavy, removed us from the Fire, and admitted us to Paradise?\" Then the veil will be lifted for them, and they will look upon God, Mighty and Majestic. Nothing will be more beloved to them than looking upon Him, and that is the \"more\" (al-ziyadah)."],[751,"The Messenger of God ﷺ assigned the call to prayer (adhan) to us and our clients, the water-giving (siqayah) to Banu Hashim, and the custodianship of the Kaaba (hijabah) to Banu 'Abd al-Dar."],[752,"The night prayer is two [units] by two [units]. If you fear that dawn will overtake you, then pray one [unit] as witr."],[753,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a woman during his Hajj, and she brought out a young boy in her hand and said: \"O Messenger of God, is there Hajj for this one?\" He said: \"Yes, and you have a reward.\""],[754,"Al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, when he gave wealth as a speculative partnership (mudarabah), stipulated upon his partner: \"Do not travel with it by sea, do not descend with it into a valley, and do not buy with it any animal with a moist liver (i.e., livestock). If you do, you are liable.\" His condition was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he approved it."],[755,"My family took me to the Prophet ﷺ while I was a young boy, and he wiped his hand over my head.\" [The narrator] said: \"I saw Abu 'Atiyyah with black hair and beard, and he had reached one hundred years of age."],[756,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was in the mosque, Abu Jahl b. Hisham, Shaybah and 'Uqbah, the two sons of Rabi'ah, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, and Umayyah b. Khalaf were there. Abu Jahl said: \"Which of you will go to the slaughtered camel of Banu so-and-so and bring us its stomach contents and cast them upon Muhammad?\" The most wretched and most foolish of them, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, went and brought it and threw it upon his shoulders while the Messenger of God ﷺ was prostrating, and he did not pay attention [to them]. Ibn Mas'ud said: \"I was standing and could not say anything, for I had no clan to protect me. Then Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, heard of that, and she came and removed it from her father, then she faced Quraysh and reviled them, but they did not respond to her at all. The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his head as he would raise it at the completion of his prostration. When he finished his prayer, he said: 'O God, against Quraysh! O God, against Quraysh! O God, against 'Uqbah, 'Utbah, Umayyah b. Khalaf, Abu Jahl b. Hisham, and Shaybah.' The Messenger of God ﷺ left the mosque, and Abu al-Bakhtari met him, and with Abu al-Bakhtari was a whip in his two little fingers. When he saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, he noticed something wrong in his face, so he took hold of him and said: 'Come, what is the matter with you?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Let go of me.' He said: 'God knows, I will not let go of you until you tell me what is wrong with you, for something bad has befallen you.' When the Messenger of God ﷺ knew that he would not let him go, he informed him, saying: 'Abu Jahl ordered that filth be thrown upon me.' Abu al-Bakhtari said: 'Come to the mosque.' The Prophet ﷺ refused, but Abu al-Bakhtari took him and brought him into the mosque. Then he went to Abu Jahl and said: 'O Abu al-Hakam, are you the one who ordered that filth be thrown upon Muhammad?' He said: 'Yes.' He raised the whip and struck his head with it, and the men fell back one upon another. Abu Jahl said: 'Woe to you! It is for him. Muhammad only wanted to cast enmity between us and save himself and his companions.'"],[757,"Travel is a piece of torment; it prevents one of you from his sleep, his pleasure, his food, and his drink. So when one of you has fulfilled his purpose from his journey, let him hasten to return to his family."],[758,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque upon us and said: \"Who is here? Do you hear? After me there will be rulers who act contrary to obedience to God, Mighty and Majestic. Whoever shares in their deeds and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never come to me at the Basin (al-Hawd). Whoever does not share in their deeds and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Basin.\""],[759,"The first news that came to us in Madinah of the sending of the Messenger of God ﷺ was that a woman of the people of Madinah had a companion (tabi') from the jinn who came in the form of a bird and perched on a trunk of theirs. She said to him: \"Will you not come down to us and talk to us, and we will talk to you, and warn us and we will warn you?\" He said: \"No, for a Prophet has been sent in Makkah who has forbidden adultery and prevented us from settling [there].\""],[760,"The slain person will come, holding onto his killer, with his jugular veins gushing blood before the Possessor of Glory, and he will say: \"O Lord, ask this one why he killed me?\" He will say: \"Why did you kill him?\" He will say: \"I killed him so that the glory might be for so-and-so.\" It will be said: \"It is for God.\""],[761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he spoke, it was seen like light coming out from between his front teeth."],[762,"A man set free six slaves of his at the time of death, and he had no property other than them. The Prophet ﷺ cast lots among them, freed two, and kept four in bondage."],[763,"A man set free six slaves of his at the time of death, and he had no property other than them. The Prophet ﷺ cast lots among them, freed two, and kept four in bondage."],[764,"May Allah curse the Jews. Fats were forbidden to them, but they sold them and consumed their price."],[765,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on the Day of Tarwiyah at Mina the Zuhr and Asr prayers."],[766,"Two hungry wolves sent among a flock of sheep whose owner has neglected them, tearing and eating, are not swifter in destroying them than love of wealth and status is in destroying the religion of a Muslim man."],[767,"If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but your companion is the close friend of Allah. And the Quran was sent down in seven modes, each mode having an outward and an inward meaning."],[768,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was sent after eight thousand prophets, four thousand of whom were from the Children of Israel."],[769,"The Prophet ﷺ came while Ali ؓ was sleeping in the dust, and said: 'The most deserving of your names is Abu Turab. You are Abu Turab.'"],[770,"Regarding His saying: 'Those who exchanged the favor of Allah with disbelief and caused their people to alight in the house of ruin' - the verse - he said: It was revealed concerning the two boastful clans of Quraysh: Banu Makhzum and Banu Umayya. As for Banu Makhzum, Allah cut off their remnants on the Day of Badr, and as for Banu Umayya, they were given enjoyment for a time."],[771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs at Mina, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman for part of his rule."],[772,"Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah' with certainty will enter Paradise."],[773,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, one day before the Tarwiyah: \"Our stopping place tomorrow, Allah willing, is at al-Khayf al-Ayman, where the polytheists drew lots for disbelief.\""],[774,"There is no young person who grows up in worship until death overtakes him, except that Allah gives him the reward of ninety-nine siddiqs."],[775,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon, I entered the mosque and sat down. He said, \"Have you prayed the two rak'ahs?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then pray them.\""],[776,"\"O Aisha, this is Jibril reciting peace upon you.\" I said, \"And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\" She went on to add more, but the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Peace ends at this.\" Then he said, \"May the mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you, O people of the house.\""],[777,"Every son of Adam will decay, except the coccyx bone, and from it the creation will be reassembled on the Day of Resurrection."],[778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit with a letter in his hand and said, \"I will surely give this letter to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. Stand, O Uthman b. Abi al-As.\" Uthman b. Abi al-As stood, and he handed it to him."],[779,"When you buy sandals, make them new, and when you buy a garment, make it new."],[780,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks."],[781,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw his face in the mirror, he would say: \"Praise be to Allah who formed my creation and made it proportionate, and shaped the image of my face and made it beautiful, and made me one of the Muslims.\""],[782,"The daughter of Ghaylan came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I cannot attain purity, so should I abandon prayer?\" He said, \"That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. When the time of menstruation has passed, keep away from the blood, then perform ghusl and pray.\""],[783,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[784,"What is between the east and the west is qiblah."],[785,"The blood money for a dhimmi is the blood money for a Muslim."],[786,"Regarding His saying: \"And among those around you of the Bedouins are hypocrites, and among the people of Madinah are those who have persisted in hypocrisy. You do not know them; We know them. We will punish them twice, then they will be returned to a great punishment\" (Qur'an 9:101). He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on a Friday as a preacher and said: 'Stand, O so-and-so, and leave, for you are a hypocrite. Leave, O so-and-so, for you are a hypocrite.' He expelled them by their names and exposed them. Umar b. al-Khattab had not attended that Friday due to some business he had. Umar met them as they were leaving the mosque, and he hid from them out of shame that he had not attended the Friday prayer, thinking that the people had dispersed. They also hid from Umar, thinking that he had learned of their affair. Umar entered the mosque and found that the people had not dispersed. A man said to him: 'Rejoice, O Umar, for Allah has exposed the hypocrites today.' This is the first punishment, and the second punishment is the punishment of the grave."],[787,"When one of you swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do that which is better and make expiation for his oath."],[788,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is ablution from a new covered earthenware jar more beloved to you or from the public water stations?' He said: 'No, rather from the public water stations. Indeed, the religion of Allah is pure and tolerant.' He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send to the public water stations, and water would be brought to him and he would drink it, hoping for the blessing of the hands of the Muslims."],[789,"This nation will continue to be in goodness as long as when it speaks it is truthful, when it judges it is just, and when mercy is sought from it, it shows mercy."],[790,"Gabriel ﷺ commanded me to judge by an oath with a witness."],[791,"Wednesday is a day of continuous ill fortune."],[792,"He used to pray twenty rak'ahs in Ramadan, aside from the witr."],[793,"Abu Talhah saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ binding his stomach with a stone from hunger. He said: 'O Umm Sulaym, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ binding his stomach with a stone from hunger. Prepare some food for him.' She made a flatbread like the size of a sandgrouse. He invited the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the flatbread. Then Umm Sulaym brought a small butter skin and squeezed it, producing about a date-stone's amount of ghee, and she seasoned the flatbread with it. Then he invoked blessing over it and said: 'Invite the people of the mosque.' He invited them, and seventy men ate from that flatbread. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and those in the house ate, then he sent some of it to his wives, and there remained more than there had been."],[794,"When he began the prayer, he would start with 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.'"],[795,"A man complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about poor memory. He said: 'Seek help from your right hand for your memory.'"],[796,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave after he had been buried for two nights."],[797,"This wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with its right, then what an excellent aid it is."],[798,"Umm Sulaym menstruated after she had performed the ifadah, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to depart."],[799,"If people knew what is in attending the night prayer on Wednesday night, they would come to it even crawling."],[800,"I attended Abu Bakr al-Siddiq. A man came to him and said: \"O caliph of the Messenger of God, this man wants to take all my wealth and ruin me.\" Abu Bakr said to him: \"What do you say?\" He said: \"Yes.\" Abu Bakr said: \"You only have of his wealth what suffices you.\" He said: \"O caliph of the Messenger of God, did not the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'You and your wealth belong to your father'?\" Abu Bakr said: \"Be content with what God, Mighty and Majestic, has been content with.\""],[801,"When he traveled, he prayed two rak'ahs until he returned."],[802,"\"By the One in whose hand is my soul, all of you will enter Paradise except those who refuse and stray from God like a camel strays.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, who refuses to enter Paradise?\" He said: \"Whoever obeys me enters Paradise, and whoever disobeys me enters the Fire.\""],[803,"\"It is a duty upon Muslims to perform ghusl on Friday, and for a man to perfume himself from his wife's perfume.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, who does not find perfume?\" He said: \"Water is perfume.\""],[804,"I said to my father: \"Which of the people is best after the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He said: \"Abu Bakr.\" I said: \"Then who?\" He said: \"Then 'Umar.\""],[805,"\"Spread out your garment.\" So I spread it out, and the Messenger of God ﷺ spoke to me for most of the day, then he spat into my garment, then I gathered my garment to my belly, and I did not forget anything after that."],[806,"Whoever sees a snake and does not kill it out of fear of it is not of me."],[807,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer, then said: \"My companions were weighed tonight. Abu Bakr was weighed and balanced, then 'Umar was weighed and balanced, then 'Uthman was weighed and balanced.\""],[808,"I was riding behind Abu Talhah, and his knee was touching the knee of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they were both raising their voices together with the talbiyah for hajj and 'umrah."],[809,"The Messenger of God ﷺ heard a sound that alarmed him. Gabriel ﷺ came to him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What is this sound, O Gabriel?\" He replied: \"This is a rock that fell from the edge of Hell seventy years ago, and this is the moment it reached its bottom. God wished to let you hear its sound.\" After that day, the Messenger of God ﷺ was never seen laughing to his full mouth until God took him."],[810,"When dawn breaks, there is no prayer except the two rak'ahs of dawn."],[811,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the expulsion of Banu al-Nadir from Madinah, some people among them came to him and said: \"We have debts that have not yet become due.\" He said: \"Reduce them and collect early.\""],[812,"There is no Friday prayer incumbent upon a traveler."],[813,"Whoever prays six rak'ahs after Maghrib without speaking anything in between, they are equal for him to the worship of twelve years."],[814,"Regarding His saying: \"and the righteous among the believers,\" he said: \"It was revealed concerning Abu Bakr and Umar.\""],[815,"O Salman, do you know what Friday is? - three times - I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: \"Your father Adam was assembled.\" Then he said: \"But I will tell you about Friday: whoever comes to Friday, purifies himself as commanded, then walks to the mosque, and remains silent until he finishes his prayer, it will be an expiation for what preceded it of Fridays.\""],[816,"Do not make use of anything from the carcass, neither hide nor sinew."],[817,"Everything has its sweepings, and the sweepings of the mosque are: 'No, by God' and 'Yes, by God.'"],[818,"A boy was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ and urinated on him, so he sprinkled water on it. A girl was brought and urinated on him, so he washed it."],[819,"A people will soon recite the Quran, drinking it as they drink water, but it will not go beyond their collarbones.\" Then he placed his hand on his throat and said: \"It will not go beyond here."],[820,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her regarding her Hajj: \"Your reward is according to the extent of your spending.\""],[821,"I was with 'Ali b. Abi Talib when Ibn Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah came. 'Ali said to him: \"Welcome, son of my brother! Come here to me.\" He seated him with him, then said: \"By Allah, I hope that I and your father are among those of whom Allah said: 'And We shall remove whatever rancor is in their breasts...'\" the verse."],[822,"We used to place for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three covered vessels: one for his ablution water, one for his tooth-stick, and one for his drink."],[823,"Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, borrowed three hundred dirhams. Her family said to her: \"Will you borrow when you have nothing to repay?\" She said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever takes on a debt while intending to repay it, Allah will help him.'\""],[824,"I said to 'Umar b. al-Khattab: \"I know people who, if this verse were revealed to them, would regard the day it was revealed and take it as a festival.\" 'Umar said: \"Which verse?\" He said: \"'Today I have perfected for you your religion...'\" to the end of the verse. 'Umar said: \"I know on which day it was revealed: 'Today I have perfected for you your religion' on a Friday, the Day of 'Arafah, and both are festivals for us.\""],[825,"When you build the mosque of San'a', place it to the right of a mountain called Dayn."],[826,"Whoever prefers anyone over Abu Bakr and 'Umar among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah has disparaged the Muhajirun and the Ansar, and twelve thousand of the Companions of Muhammad."],[827,"The people will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection naked and barefoot. Umm Salamah said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what a disgrace! Will some of us look at others?\" He said: \"The people will be preoccupied.\" I said: \"What will preoccupy them?\" He said: \"The unfolding of the scrolls, in which are the weights of motes and mustard seeds.\""],[828,"I was among the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Bilal would bring us our iftar in Ramadan while we were still in daylight, and we would say: \"O Bilal, has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ broken his fast?\" He would say: \"Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, I did not leave him until he had broken his fast.\" Then he would put down his hand and eat, and we would eat. And he would bring us our suhur, and he would uncover the curtain of the tent so that we could see our food."],[829,"I was present when al-Hajjaj b. Yusuf was beating al-'Abbas b. Sahl b. Sa'd al-Sa'idi regarding the matter of Ibn al-Zubayr. His father Sahl came out in a waist-wrapper and a cloak, and shouted at al-Hajjaj: \"Will you not honor the bequest of the Messenger of Allah concerning us?\" He said: \"And what did the Messenger of Allah bequeath concerning you?\" He said: \"He bequeathed: 'Treat well the good-doers among the Ansar and pardon their wrongdoers.'\" So he released him."],[830,"The best of gatherings are the most spacious."],[831,"Shall I inform you of those for whom the Fire will be forbidden tomorrow? It will be forbidden for every gentle, soft, easy, and approachable person."],[832,"When one of you performs ablution for prayer, he should not interlace his fingers."],[833,"Whoever loves that his record should please him, let him increase in it in seeking forgiveness."],[834,"He used to drink in three breaths. When he brought the vessel near his mouth, he would mention Allah's name, and when he moved it away, he would praise Allah. He would do that three times."],[835,"Ibn Umar, when he began the prayer, used to start with 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful' in the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah) and in the surah that followed it, and he mentioned that he heard that from the Messenger of Allah."],[836,"He used to trim his nails and clip his moustache on Friday before going out to the prayer."],[837,"Allah will illuminate those who walk to the mosques in the darkness with a shining light on the Day of Resurrection."],[838,"When rain came to them and the gutters flowed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no drought upon you this year.'"],[839,"May Allah have mercy on those who shave (their heads). We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten?' He said: 'May Allah have mercy on those who shave.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten?' He said—on the third or fourth time—'and those who shorten.'"],[840,"O Abu Hurayrah, hold a wedding feast even if with a sheep."],[841,"Abu Dharr came to us and took hold of the ring of the door of the Ka'bah and called out at the top of his voice: 'O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There is no prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets, and no prayer after the dawn prayer until the sun rises, except in Makkah, except in Makkah.'"],[842,"Bind knowledge. I said: What is binding it? He said: Writing."],[843,"The water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for."],[844,"Good character melts away sins as water melts ice, and bad character spoils deeds as vinegar spoils honey."],[845,"Two hungry wolves let loose among a flock are not more destructive to it than a man's love for honor and wealth is to his religion."],[846,"Indeed, before you is a cistern as wide as the distance between Jarba' and Adhruh."],[847,"Mounts are not to be saddled except for three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Aqsa Mosque."],[848,"Indeed, when a man gives his wife water to drink, he is rewarded. He said: So I went to her and gave her water to drink, and I told her what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[849,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when this verse was revealed: 'Then they did not bring four witnesses' [Quran 24:4]. I said: O Messenger of Allah, until they bring four witnesses? The frustrated one has already fulfilled his need. He said: He did not even stand up before his cousin, his father's brother, came with his wife carrying a child, and she was saying: 'He is from you,' and he was saying: 'He is not from me.' Then the verse of mutual cursing was revealed. He said: I was the first to speak of it and the first to be tested by it."],[850,"We were on a journey, and I felt lonely at night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with you?' I said: I am in this place on a dark night, and I fear for you. He said: 'No, indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will send us a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love, to guard us for the rest of our night.' She said: While I was like that, I saw a dark figure approaching us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who is this?' He said: I am Sa'd b. Malik, I have come to guard you for the rest of this night of yours. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laid his head down and slept."],[851,"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing."],[852,"The child of adultery will not enter Paradise, nor any of his offspring up to seven fathers."],[853,"My father and I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he led us in prayer. When he said the salam, the people gestured with their hands to the right and left. He saw them and said: 'What is the matter with you, turning your hands right and left as if they were the tails of restless horses? When one of you says the salam, let him greet the one on his right and the one on his left.' So when they prayed with him again, they did not do that. He said: And we sat with him, and he said: 'Islam will remain manifest until there are twelve commanders or caliphs, all of them from Quraysh.'"],[854,"The most beloved of deeds to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is prayer at its proper time—or he said: at its earliest time."],[855,"Many a disheveled, dusty one with two worn garments, turned away from people's doors, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath."],[856,"Indeed, in the mosque there is a spot before this pillar that if people knew of it, they would not pray in it except that a lot would be drawn for them. She had a group of his companions and the sons of the emigrants with her, and they said: O Mother of the Believers, where is it? She refused to tell them, so they stayed with her for a while, then left, but 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr remained. They said: She will tell him about that place, so they watched him in the mosque to see where he would pray. He came out after a while and prayed at the pillar that his son 'Amir b. 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr prayed toward, and it was called the Pillar of the Lot. 'Atiq said: It is the pillar that is in the middle between the grave and the pulpit; to its right toward the pulpit are two pillars, and between it and the pulpit are two pillars, and between it and the courtyard are two pillars, and it is in the middle of that, and it is called the Pillar of the Lot."],[857,"Faith is among the people of the Hijaz, while harshness and coarseness are in Rabi'ah and Mudar."],[858,"When the prayer and the evening meal are both ready, begin with the evening meal."],[859,"Deeds are of seven kinds: two that save, two that are rewarded in kind, one multiplied tenfold, one multiplied seven hundredfold, and one whose reward only Allah knows. As for the two saving deeds: whoever meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, worshipping Him sincerely, associating nothing with Him, Paradise becomes due for him; and whoever meets Allah associating something with Him, the Fire becomes due for him. Whoever does an evil deed is recompensed for it; whoever intends a good deed but does not do it is credited with its like; whoever does a good deed is credited tenfold; whoever spends his wealth in the path of Allah, the dirham he spends is multiplied seven hundredfold, and the dinar seven hundredfold; and fasting—no one knows the reward of the one who fasts except Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[860,"Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[861,"No servant prostrates to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, a single prostration except that Allah raises him a degree by it and removes from him a sin by it."],[862,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and said: 'Go until you come to Abu Bakr, and you will find him sitting in his house with his legs drawn up. Say to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and says: Rejoice in Paradise. Then go until you come to the mountain pass, and you will meet 'Umar there on a donkey, his baldness shining. Say to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and says: Rejoice in Paradise. Then go until you come to the market, and you will meet 'Uthman there selling and buying. Say to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and says: Rejoice in Paradise after severe trial.' So I went and came to Abu Bakr, and I found him in his house sitting with his legs drawn up, just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said. I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and says: Rejoice in Paradise.' He said: 'Where is the Messenger of Allah?' I said: 'In such-and-such a place.' He got up and went to him. Then I came to the mountain pass, and there was 'Umar on a donkey, his baldness shining, just as the Messenger of Allah had said. I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and says: Rejoice in Paradise.' He said: 'Where is the Messenger of Allah?' I said: 'In such-and-such a place.' He went to him. Then I went until I came to the market, and I met 'Uthman there selling and buying, just as the Messenger of Allah had said. I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and says: Rejoice in Paradise after severe trial.' He said: 'Where is the Messenger of Allah?' I said: 'In such-and-such a place.' He took me by the hand and we came together to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. 'Uthman said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, Zayd came to me and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and says: Rejoice in Paradise after severe trial. So what trial will befall me, O Messenger of Allah? By the One who sent you with the truth, I have not wished for what is not mine, nor longed for anything, nor touched my private part with my right hand since I pledged allegiance to you.' He said: 'It is that.'"],[863,"He heard Sa'id b. Zayd testify about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he was with him as the tenth of ten. He said: 'Abu Bakr is in Paradise, 'Umar is in Paradise, 'Uthman is in Paradise, 'Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf is in Paradise, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas is in Paradise.' And if I wish, I will tell you the ninth. The people said: 'Who is he, O Sa'id?' He said: 'He is me.' Then he wept."],[864,"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing."],[865,"I was a business partner of the Prophet ﷺ before Islam. When I came to Madinah, he said: 'Do you recognize me?' I said: 'Yes, you were my partner; you did not argue or deceive.'"],[866,"He would sleep during his prostration, and his sleep was only known by his snoring; then he would stand up and continue his prayer."],[867,"Any woman who marries without a guardian, her marriage is invalid, her marriage is invalid. If he consummates the marriage, she is entitled to the dowry because of what he made lawful of her private part. The ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."],[868,"When death approached the Prophet ﷺ, they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, give us your final instructions.' He said: 'I instruct you to treat well the first forerunners among the Emigrants and their descendants after them. If you do not do so, neither obligatory nor voluntary acts will be accepted from you.'"],[869,"When My servant complains, and after three days he still shows the illness, he has complained against Me."],[870,"Whoever is absent from Madinah for three days, when he returns, his heart is saturated with aversion."],[871,"When he applied kohl, he would apply it three times with the probe to the right eye and two times to the other, making it an odd number."],[872,"I am the guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise for one who abandons argumentation even when he is in the right, and of a house in the middle of Paradise for one who abandons lying even in jest, and of a house in the highest part of Paradise for one who has good character."],[873,"Whoever grants respite to someone in difficulty or waives [the debt] for him, Allah will shade him in the shade of His Throne on the Day of Resurrection."],[874,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he prohibited nabīdh made in earthen jars, and I witnessed him when he commanded drinking it, and he said: 'Avoid every intoxicant.'"],[875,"He ransomed his oath with ten thousand dirhams. Then he said: 'By the Lord of this mosque, if I had sworn, I would have sworn truthfully. It is only something with which I ransomed my oath.'"],[876,"He used to order the burying of the blood when he was cupped."],[877,"When 'When comes the help of Allah and the victory' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Fāṭimah and said: 'It has been announced to me that my soul [will soon be taken],' so she wept. He said: 'Do not weep, for you will be the first of my family to join me,' so she laughed. One of the Prophet's ﷺ wives saw her and said to her: 'We saw you weeping, then you laughed.' She said: 'He told me: \"It has been announced to me that my soul [will soon be taken],\" so I wept. Then he said: \"Do not weep, for you will be the first of my family to join me,\" so I laughed.'"],[878,"The killer has no share of the inheritance."],[879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man milking a sheep and said: 'O so-and-so, when you milk, leave some for its young, for it is among the most dutiful of beasts.'"],[880,"When hardship befell his family, the Prophet ﷺ would command them to pray, and then he recited: 'And command your family to pray and be steadfast therein' (Q 20:132)."],[881,"The Prophet ﷺ went out one morning and said: 'The Fire has been kindled, and tribulations have come like patches of the dark night. If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'"],[882,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'Teach me something that will benefit me.' He said: 'When you lie down to sleep, recite: \"Qul yā ayyuhā al-kāfirūn\" (Sūrat al-Kāfirūn), for it is a disavowal of shirk.'"],[883,"Whoever grants his brother a reprieve in a sale, Allah will overlook his stumble on the Day of Resurrection."],[884,"They order me to revile my Companions. Nay, may Allah bless them and forgive them."],[885,"The dining table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never lifted from before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while there was any leftover food on it ever."],[886,"We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we would recite the talbiyah on behalf of the children and throw the jamarāt on their behalf."],[887,"The debtor is held captive by his debt, complaining to Allah of loneliness."],[888,"An army in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took as spoils food and honey, and the fifth (khums) was not taken from them."],[889,"Seek provision in the hidden treasures of the earth."],[890,"Three of the Anṣār—no one among the people surpassed them in merit after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Saʿd b. Muʿādh, Usayd b. Ḥuḍayr, and ʿAbbād b. Bishr."],[891,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves that when one of you does a deed, he does it with perfection."],[892,"A man used to lead his people in prayer and would recite in every rakʿah: \"Qul huwa Allahu aḥad\" along with another sūrah. His companions said to him: 'You recite this sūrah—meaning \"Qul huwa Allahu aḥad\"—and then do not consider it sufficient, but you recite another sūrah with it. Either confine yourself to it, or recite the other sūrah and leave it.' He said: 'I will not do that. If you are pleased, then so be it; otherwise, your affair is up to you.' He was one of the best among them, and they disliked that anyone other than him lead them. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: 'What prevents you from doing what your people instruct you to do, and what compels you to this sūrah?' He said: 'I love it.' He said: 'Your love of it will admit you to Paradise.'"],[893,"The believer eats in one intestine, while the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[894,"I was with al-Farazdaq in prison, and al-Farazdaq said: \"May God not save me from the hands of Malik b. al-Mundhir b. al-Jarud if I did not set out walking in Makkah and meet Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and ask them, saying: 'I am from the people of the east, and some people are coming out against us, killing those who say: There is no god but God, while others are safe.' They said to me—and otherwise may God not save me from Malik b. al-Mundhir—'We heard our beloved ﷺ say: Whoever kills them will have the reward of a martyr or two martyrs, and whomever they kill will have the reward of a martyr.'\""],[895,"The strongest of your Lord's creation are ten: mountains, and iron cuts mountains, and fire consumes iron, and water extinguishes fire, and the clouds subjected between heaven and earth carry water, and the wind carries the clouds, and man shields himself from the wind with his hand and goes about his need in it, and intoxication overcomes man, and sleep overcomes intoxication, and worry prevents sleep. So the strongest of your Lord's creation is worry."],[896,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey and the travel became intense, if he mounted before the shade shifted, he would delay the noon prayer until the first time of the afternoon prayer entered, then he would dismount and pray them together. Then he would delay the sunset prayer until the disappearance of the twilight began, then he would dismount and pray them together—sunset and evening prayers."],[897,"Whoever visits a sick person plunges into mercy, and if he sits with him, he becomes immersed in it."],[898,"Fresh dates were gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he began eating with his right hand and taking the pits with his left hand, then throwing them away."],[899,"An 'umrah to the next 'umrah is an expiation for what is between them, and an accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[900,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray over a funeral, and we could only see the sun on the tops of the walls."],[901,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution: he washed his face three times, washed his hands three times, wiped his head and ears, and washed his feet three times. And I saw him another time perform ablution once each."],[902,"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated."],[903,"Three traits—whoever has them, God will call him to an easy reckoning and admit him to Paradise. I said: What are they, O Messenger of God? He said: \"You maintain ties with those who cut you off, you give to those who deprive you, and you forgive those who wrong you.\""],[904,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would pray the morning prayer when light spread across the sky, the noon prayer when the sun declined, the afternoon prayer while the sun was white and clear, the sunset prayer when the fasting person broke his fast, and he would delay the evening prayer."],[905,"When one of you proposes to a woman, there is no sin on him to look at her, if he is only looking at her for the proposal, as long as she does not know."],[906,"Regarding the saying of God, Mighty and Majestic: “It throws sparks like castles” (Q 77:32), he said: Indeed, it is not like trees and mountains, but rather like cities and fortresses."],[907,"A man has more right to the front of his mount and the front of his bed, and to lead the prayer in his quarters."],[908,"Whoever prays twelve rakʿahs voluntarily in a day, a house will be built for him in Paradise."],[909,"The first group to enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection will have faces like the image of the full moon at night. Those who come after them will be like the most brilliant shining star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives, on each wife a garment through which the marrow of her shin is seen from behind the flesh, just as red wine is seen through a white glass."],[910,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray four [rakʿahs] before ʿAṣr."],[911,"Three things—if a person is not guilty of any one of them, then God, Mighty and Majestic, will forgive him whatever else he does: one who dies without associating anything with Him, was not a sorcerer and did not follow sorcerers, and did not bear a grudge against his brother."],[912,"The best of the martyrs in the sight of God is Ḥamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib."],[913,"The Prophet of God ﷺ was asked: “O Messenger of God, do the people of Paradise sleep?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Sleep is the brother of death, and the people of Paradise do not sleep.”"],[914,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a grave and said: “Who is the occupant of this grave?” They said: “So-and-so.” He said: “Two rakʿahs are more beloved to this one than the rest of your worldly life.”"],[915,"The Messenger of God ﷺ departed from ʿArafāt while saying: “To You it runs, its girth strap anxious, its religion opposing the religion of the Christians.”"],[916,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a ṣāʿ."],[917,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: I take your pledge upon that you do not associate anything with Allah, do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, do not commit adultery, do not steal, and do not drink. Whoever does any of that and its prescribed punishment is carried out on him, it is an expiation for him. Whoever Allah conceals, his reckoning is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic. And whoever does none of that, I guarantee him Paradise."],[918,"I said to ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar: Al-Mukhtar claims that revelation comes to him. He said: He has spoken the truth, and indeed the devils do inspire their allies."],[919,"He used to give salutation to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."],[920,"Do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and let none of you bid against the bid of his brother. A city-dweller must not sell on behalf of a Bedouin. Leave people alone; Allah provides for some of them through others. And a woman must not demand the divorce of her sister."],[921,"He used to pray two rakʿahs before the ʿAsr prayer."],[922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Bakr and commanded him to proclaim these words. Then he sent ʿAli after him. While Abu Bakr was on one of the roads, he heard the grumbling of the Messenger of Allah's she-camel. Abu Bakr came out in alarm, thinking it was the Messenger of Allah, and behold it was ʿAli. He handed over the letter of the Messenger of Allah to him, and he appointed him over the pilgrimage season, and he commanded ʿAli to proclaim these words. They both went and performed the pilgrimage. ʿAli stood during the days of Tashriq and proclaimed: The protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger is absolved from every polytheist. So travel freely in the land for four months. No polytheist may perform pilgrimage after this year, no one may circumambulate the House naked, and none will enter Paradise except a believer. ʿAli kept proclaiming them, and when his voice became hoarse, Abu Hurayrah stood up and proclaimed them."],[923,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Ibn Masʿud."],[924,"Do not say about anything: I will do that tomorrow, except if Allah wills. And remember your Lord when you forget and say: If Allah wills."],[925,"About terrors that he saw at night that prevented him from the night prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Khalid b. al-Walid, shall I not teach you words that you say? You will not say them three times except that Allah removes that from you. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, for I complained of that to you only hoping for this from you. He said: Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from His wrath, His punishment, the evil of His servants, from the whisperings of the devils, and that they come to me. Aisha said: Only a few nights passed before Khalid b. al-Walid came and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, by the One who sent you with truth, I did not complete the words you taught me three times before Allah removed from me what I used to find. I do not care if I enter upon a lion in its den at night."],[926,"He came to Abu Saʿid al-Khudri and said: O Abu Saʿid, we have heard that you narrate a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about riba; explain it to us. Abu Saʿid said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Gold for gold, like for like, no increase and no deferred payment. Silver for silver, like for like, no increase and no deferred payment. And do not sell what is absent for what is present. My eyes saw it and my ears heard it."],[927,"It is not proper for a Muslim man who has something to bequeath to spend two nights without his will being with him. Ibn ʿUmar said: Not two nights have passed over me since I heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that I have a will with me."],[928,"I used to hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when evening came upon him in my house, saying: We have entered the evening and the dominion belongs to Allah, praise, might, strength, power and authority are in the heavens and the earth, and everything belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds. O Allah, by You we enter the morning, by You we enter the evening, by You we live, by You we die, and to You is the return. And when morning came he would say: We have entered the morning and the dominion belongs to Allah, praise, strength, might, power and authority are in the heavens and the earth, and everything belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds. O Allah, by You we enter the evening, by You we enter the morning, by You we live, by You we die, and to You is the resurrection."],[929,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught us the istikhāra prayer. He said: “Let one of you say: O God, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek Your power by Your might, and I ask You of Your abundant favor. For You are able and I am not able, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If this matter—naming it by its name—is good for me in my religion and in my livelihood, and good for me in the outcome of my affair, and good for me in all matters, then decree it for me and bless me in it. And if other than that is better for me, then decree for me the good wherever it may be and make me content with it.”"],[930,"He used to have cupping done on the top of his head and between his shoulders, and he would say: “Whoever lets these bloods flow, it will not harm him to not treat anything with anything.”"],[931,"It is not lawful for a woman to mourn for anyone more than three days, and she mourns for her husband for her waiting period until her waiting period ends."],[932,"We went out with the women with whom we had contracted temporary marriage, until we came to the mountain pass of al-Rikāb. We said: “O Messenger of God, these are the women with whom we contracted temporary marriage.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “They are unlawful until the Day of Resurrection.” So they bade us farewell at that place, and it was named the Farewell Pass. Before that it was only the Pass of al-Rikāb."],[933,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her, and she brought him a vessel that held a mudd and a third, or a mudd and a quarter, for his ablution. I poured water on his hand three times. Then he took the vessel from me, set it down, rinsed his mouth and nose, washed his face three times, washed his hands three times, wiped his head twice and his ears, outside and inside, then washed his feet."],[934,"The night prayer is two by two. If you fear the morning, then perform one witr."],[935,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, and Abu Bakr was made successor, and some Arabs disbelieved, Umar said: “O Abu Bakr, how can you fight the people when the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God. Whoever says: There is no god but God has protected from me his property and his life, except by its right, and his reckoning is with God’?” Abu Bakr said: “I will certainly fight those who separate prayer from zakāt. By God, if they withhold from me a young goat that they used to give to the Messenger of God ﷺ, I will fight them for withholding it.” Umar said: “By God, it was only that I saw God had opened Abu Bakr's chest to fighting, and I knew it was the truth.”"],[936,"Paradise has been forbidden to the prophets until I enter it, and it has been forbidden to the nations until my nation enters it."],[937,"Secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord. Acts of kindness protect from evil deaths. Maintaining ties of kinship increases lifespan and protects from poverty. And say often: There is no power and no strength except with God, for it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise, and in it is a cure for ninety-nine ailments, the least of which is anxiety."],[938,"A man came to him and said: “O Prophet of God, I have relatives whom I maintain ties with, but they cut me off. I am good to them, but they are bad to me.” He said: “If it is as you say, then God, Mighty and Majestic, will remain a supporter with you against them.”"],[939,"When one of you wakes from sleep, let him not dip his hand into his water for purification until he pours water on it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[940,"The purification of the vessel of one of you, if a dog licks it, is to wash it seven times, the first with dust."],[941,"A man called out to the Messenger of God: “O Messenger of God, may a man pray in a single garment?” He said: “Does every one of you have two garments?”"],[942,"When the call to prayer is given, let none of you come to it running; rather, let him come to it with calmness and dignity. Let him pray whatever he catches, and make up whatever he missed."],[943,"Whoever forgets and eats or drinks while fasting, let him complete his fast, for it is God, Mighty and Majestic, who fed him and gave him drink."],[944,"A good deed is multiplied tenfold, and fasting is for Me, and I reward it. The change in the mouth of the fasting person is more fragrant to God than the scent of musk."],[945,"The angels curse one of you if he points a piece of iron at his brother, even if he is his brother from the same father and mother."],[946,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade two ways of dressing and two kinds of transactions: that a man walk in a single garment with nothing covering his private parts, or wrap himself in a single garment and then raise it over his shoulder; and he forbade mulāmasa and ilqāʾ sales."],[947,"Do not go out to meet caravans. Whoever meets one and buys something from it, its owner has the option when he reaches the market."],[948,"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan cannot take my form."],[949,"When time draws near, the dream of a believer will scarcely be false. The most truthful of them in dreams are the most truthful in speech. The dream of a believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood. A righteous dream is glad tidings from God. A dream is something a man tells himself, and a wet dream is from Satan. If one of you sees what he dislikes, let him not speak of it."],[950,"Abraham did not lie except three times: two were for the sake of God—his saying, “I am sick,” and his saying, “Rather, the largest of them did this.” And he passed by a land ruled by a tyrant, and Sarah was with him. The tyrant sent to him: “Who is this woman with you?” He said, “She is my sister.” Then he sent to him: “Send her to me.”"],[951,"Delay the prayer in extreme heat, for the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell."],[952,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he said: “There will be rulers after me who delay the prayer beyond its time.” I said: “O Messenger of God, what should one who lives to see them do?” He said: “Pray the prayer at its proper time. Then, if you are present with them for the prayer, pray [with them].”"],[953,"I asked 'A'ishah: How did the Prophet ﷺ pray? She said: \"When he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting; and when he prayed standing, he bowed standing.\""],[954,"I asked 'A'ishah about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: \"He would fast until we said, 'He has fasted,' and he would break his fast until we said, 'He has broken his fast.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not fast a complete month since he came to Madinah, except the month of Ramadan.\""],[955,"The night prayer is in pairs of two, and the witr is one rak'ah at the end of the night."],[956,"There are no two Muslims who lose three children before they reach the age of accountability but that Allah admits them to Paradise by His abundant mercy toward them. And no Muslim spends a pair of anything from his wealth in the way of Allah but that the gatekeepers of Paradise hasten to meet him."],[957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us at Mina, and said in his sermon: 'What day is this?' We remained silent until we thought he would name it something other than its name. He said: 'Is this not the Day of Sacrifice?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What month is this?' We remained silent until we thought he would name it something other than its name. He said: 'Is this not Dhu al-Hijjah?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What land is this?' We remained silent until we thought he would name it something other than its name. He said: 'Is this not the Sacred Land?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honor are inviolable to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Let the one present convey to the one absent, for it may be that he conveys it to one who is more mindful than he, or more retentive than he. Indeed, do not revert after me as misled people, striking the necks of one another.'\""],[958,"A man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leaving six slaves, with no property other than them. He had freed them at his death. The matter was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he cast lots among them, freeing two and keeping four enslaved; he freed by lot."],[959,"'A'ishah was asked about what makes ghusl obligatory. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When a man sits between a woman's four limbs and the circumcised parts touch, ghusl becomes obligatory.'"],[960,"O Messenger of Allah, I comb my hair and braid it tightly, so how should I perform ghusl from janabah and menstruation? He said: 'Pour three handfuls of water over your head with your hands.'"],[961,"Seventy thousand from my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment; they do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, do not practice pessimism, and upon their Lord they rely."],[962,"The woman is like a rib; if you straighten her, you break her, and if you leave her, you enjoy her despite her crookedness."],[963,"Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Indeed Allah commands you to supplicate with these words, for He will grant you one of them: O Allah, I ask You for hastening of Your relief, patience in Your affliction, and departure from this world to Your mercy.'"],[964,"He would give one taslim in prayer, to his right."],[965,"'Abdullah b. 'Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating—a single divorce—during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. 'Umar asked the Prophet ﷺ about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to take her back, then keep her until she became pure, then menstruate another menstrual period while with him, then keep her until she became pure. Then if he wanted to divorce her, he should divorce her before having intercourse with her. For that is the waiting period which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has commanded."],[966,"Whomever Allah provides with a righteous wife, Allah has assisted him with half of his religion, so let him fear Allah regarding the second half."],[967,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[968,"My community is a community that is shown mercy. Allah placed its punishment by its own hands. On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will give to every Muslim man a man from the People of the Book, and he will be his ransom from the Fire."],[969,"O Prophet of Allah, I wanted to free this slave boy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Rather, give him to some of your maternal aunts who are among the Bedouins, so that he may tend livestock for them, for that is greater in reward for you."],[970,"No one should address the people with admonition except a ruler, one who is ordered to do so, or a hypocrite."],[971,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is not ashamed of the truth: do not approach women in their anuses."],[972,"A group of people came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and delivered speeches. The people were amazed at their speech. The Prophet ﷺ said: Speak as you normally speak, for some eloquence is sorcery, and embellished speech is from Satan."],[973,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[974,"Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."],[975,"He forbade marrying a woman in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt; and two ways of wearing clothes: the samma' (wrapping the garment over one shoulder and leaving the other uncovered) and a man wrapping himself in a single garment with nothing covering his private parts; and fasting on the Day of Sacrifice and the Day of Breaking the Fast; and praying after the morning prayer until the sun rises, and after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets."],[976,"When one of you comes to the prayer, let him come with tranquility. Whatever you catch, pray; and whatever you miss, complete."],[977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who wears men's clothing and the man who wears women's clothing."],[978,"Whoever washes a dead body, let him perform ghusl; and whoever carries it, let him perform wudu'."],[979,"And with this chain: Zuhayr b. Muhammad narrated to us, from al-'Ala', from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the hadith:"],[980,"When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, spoke to Musa in tongues before his own tongue, Musa began saying: 'O Lord, I do not understand this.' Until He spoke to him in the last of the tongues before his own tongue, and he said: 'O Lord, is there anything among Your creation that resembles Your speech?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'The closest of My creation in resemblance to My speech is the most intense thunderclap that is heard.'"],[981,"Allah does not seize knowledge from people by snatching it away from them, but He seizes knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders, who are asked and give fatwas without knowledge, so they go astray and lead others astray."],[982,"Whoever is able to marry but does not marry is not of me."],[983,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not look at a man who has intercourse with his wife in her anus."],[984,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made mercy into one hundred parts. He kept ninety-nine parts with Him and sent down one part to the earth. From that one part creatures show mercy to one another, so that a mare lifts her hoof from her foal for fear of injuring it."],[985,"The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then 'Umar."],[986,"Whoever cheats us is not of us."],[987,"He performed 'aqiqah for himself after he was sent as a Prophet."],[988,"I do jest, but I say only the truth."],[989,"O Allah, bless my Ummah in its early mornings."],[990,"Whoever attends the Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[991,"Seek out the orphans with regard to their property, lest zakat consume it."],[992,"Whoever loves the Ansar, it is out of love for me that he loves them; and whoever hates the Ansar, it is out of hatred for me that he hates them."],[993,"A man's paternal uncle is of the same stock as his father, and the Prophet ﷺ took from al-Abbas the zakat of two years in advance in one year."],[994,"Knowledge is of three kinds: a speaking Book, a past Sunnah, and 'I do not know'."],[995,"Be dutiful to your fathers, and your sons will be dutiful to you; and be chaste, and your women will be chaste."],[996,"When he had not met the enemy at the beginning of the day, he would delay until the winds blew and it was the time of prayer, and he would say: 'O Allah, by You I attack, and by You I maneuver, and there is no might and no power except with Allah.'"],[997,"By Allah, I shall certainly raid Quraysh; then he said: 'If Allah wills.' Then he said: 'By Allah, I shall certainly raid Quraysh;' then he said: 'If Allah wills.' Then he said: 'By Allah, I shall certainly raid Quraysh;' then he said: 'If Allah wills.'"],[998,"There is no misyar marriage in Islam. Whoever engaged in misyar in the Jahiliyyah, I have attached him to his male relatives. And whoever claims a child not from his own lawful union, he does not inherit and is not inherited from."],[999,"It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best?' He said: 'A tolerant Hanifiyyah (pure monotheism).'"],[1000,"Women have no role in concluding the marriage contract. Maymunah entrusted her affair to Umm al-Fadl, who delegated it to al-Abbas, and he gave her in marriage to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[1001,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding the prostration in Surah Sad: \"David the Prophet ﷺ prostrated in repentance, and we prostrate in gratitude.\""],[1002,"Whoever says: 'Praise be to God before anyone else, and praise be to God after anyone else, and praise be to God in every condition' will be given a reward like the worship of one who worships God, Mighty and Majestic."],[1003,"When a matter distressed him, he would say: 'There is no god but God, the Magnificent, the Forbearing; there is no god but God, Lord of the Noble Throne; there is no god but God, Lord of the heavens and the earth, and Lord of the Mighty Throne.'"],[1004,"I asked Ibn Abbas, or he was asked: 'Which charity is best?' He said: 'The Prophet ﷺ was asked: \"Which charity is best?\" He said: \"Water.\" I said: \"O Prophet of God, which charity is best?\" He said: \"Water. Do you not see that when the people of the Fire call for help to the people of Paradise, they say: Pour upon us some water or whatever God has provided you?\"'"],[1005,"Whoever holds the stirrup of his Muslim brother, neither hoping for his reward nor fearing him, God will forgive him."],[1006,"Buy slaves, but beware of the Zanj, for their lives are short and their sustenance is little."],[1007,"The master of seeking forgiveness is to say: 'O God, You are my Lord; there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I adhere to Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You.' Whoever says it after evening falls and then dies that night will enter Paradise, and whoever says it after waking from sleep will enter Paradise."],[1008,"When you attend your dying ones, close their eyes, for the sight follows the soul, and speak good, for the angels say 'Amen' to what the household says."],[1009,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and slipped between his shirt and his skin, and kissed the place of the seal. I said: 'What is it that is not permissible to withhold?' He said: 'Salt.' I said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Water and fire.'"],[1010,"Deliberateness, moderation, and good demeanor are one part of twenty-four parts of prophethood."],[1011,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said about one of the doors of the mosque: 'If only we had left this door for the women.'"],[1012,"I was among those who hastened in the heavy baggage of the Prophet ﷺ on the night of Jam‘."],[1013,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered the Ka‘bah, and in it there were six columns, “so he supplicated at each column but did not pray.”"],[1014,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us this supplication just as he taught us a surah from the Qur’an: “I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Jahannam, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the false messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal), and I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death.”"],[1015,"I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touching any corner other than the two Yamani corners."],[1016,"Amputation is for a quarter dinar and above."],[1017,"Whoever grows a grey hair in Islam, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1018,"Whoever preserves me regarding my companions will come to me at the Hawd (the Pond), and whoever does not preserve me regarding my companions will not see me on the Day of Resurrection except from afar."],[1019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us, when we began the prayer, to say: “Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You; blessed is Your name; exalted is Your majesty; and there is no god besides You.” And Umar b. al-Khattab used to do that. And Umar taught us, saying: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say it.”"],[1020,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bade farewell to a man from his companions, he said: “May Allah provide you with taqwa, forgive your sin, and bring you good wherever you turn.”"],[1021,"Whoever says in the morning and in the evening: “O Allah, You created me, and You guide me, and You feed me, and You give me drink, and You cause me to die, and You bring me to life,” he will not ask for anything except that Allah will grant it to him. He said: Then I met Abdullah b. Salam and said: Shall I not tell you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah many times, from Abu Bakr many times, and from Umar many times? He said: Yes. So I told him this hadith, and he said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. These words were given by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to Musa ﷺ , and he used to supplicate with them seven times every day, and he would not ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for anything except that He granted it to him."],[1022,"Whoever receives an apology but does not accept it will not come to me at the Hawd."],[1023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the people pollinating date palms and said: “What is wrong with the people?” He said: They are pollinating, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “No pollination,” or “I do not think pollination is of any use.” He said: So they abandoned pollination, and the people’s dates turned out to be inferior. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am not a farmer nor an owner of palms; pollinate.”"],[1024,"A dinar you spend on yourself in the cause of Allah, and a dinar you spend on your horse in the cause of Allah, and a dinar you spend on your family in the cause of Allah. The best of them is the dinar you spend on your family."],[1025,"Malik b. al-Huwayrith visited us and we said: If only you would lead us in prayer. He said to us: Let your imam lead the prayer, and I will tell you what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When one of you visits his brother, he should not lead him in prayer, but one of them should lead the others."],[1026,"There is no harm and no reciprocating of harm."],[1027,"A man does not take out his charity until it releases from him the jaws of seventy devils."],[1028,"The angels do not cease to send blessings upon one of you as long as his dining table is set."],[1029,"No Muslim who has seen me, nor one who has seen one who has seen me, nor one who has seen one who has seen one who has seen me will enter the Fire."],[1030,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came to a pool of water, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted and we dismounted. The time for prayer came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Bilal, stand and give the call to prayer. Bilal went and relieved himself, then came to the pool and washed his face and hands, and reached for his leather socks, and he was wearing two black leather socks, and that was before the eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called to him: O Bilal, wipe over the leather socks and the head covering."],[1031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prohibit the flesh of domesticated donkeys."],[1032,"The hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was above the wafra and below the jumma."],[1033,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drove one hundred garlanded camels in the Farewell Pilgrimage."],[1034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me ahead with his heavy baggage from Muzdalifah."],[1035,"His father was killed by the polytheists on the day of Uhud, then they mutilated him and cut off his nose and ear. Jabir said: I kept looking at him and at what was done to him. The Ansar came and covered him with a cloth. Then I uncovered the cloth, and when I saw what was done to him I cried out. The Ansar came and covered him with the cloth again, and they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah! Do you not see what Jabir is doing? He said: Leave him, for by Allah, the angels have not ceased to shade him with their wings. Later, I said: O Prophet of Allah, my father has left a debt upon himself. He said: When the dates are ripe, inform me. When the dates were ripe, I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he supplicated for him, and there was in his palm trees more than enough to pay his debt, and there remained surplus like what he used to have surplus."],[1036,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one night during the month of Ramadan and prayed in the mosque. Some men prayed behind him, following his prayer. The people woke up and talked about that. When it was the second night, he went out and prayed in the mosque. When it was the third night, he did not go out. The people shouted and knocked on his door, but he did not come out. When morning came, he said: \"Your location was not hidden from me, but I feared that it would be made obligatory upon you, and then you would not be able to keep up with it.\""],[1037,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite a surah. While I was sitting in the mosque, I heard a man reciting it differently from my recitation, and he mentioned it."],[1038,"Some dates were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"What is this? It is not from our dates.\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I sold two sa's of our dates for one sa' of these dates.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is usury. Return it. Then sell our dates and buy for us from these.\""],[1039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that doors be closed and that one say: 'In the name of Allah.' And if you find nothing but a stick, place it across it and say: 'In the name of Allah.' And extinguish the lamp, and one should say: 'In the name of Allah.'"],[1040,"Perform ablution from (eating) what has been touched by fire."],[1041,"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person will have the like of his reward, without any decrease in his reward."],[1042,"None of you should use my kunya."],[1043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted ruqya (incantation) for every venomous sting."],[1044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Magians and said: \"They let their moustaches grow and shave their beards, so differ from them.\""],[1045,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on one of his expeditions and passed by some Arab households. He sent to them: \"Is there any water for the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" They said: \"We have no water except in the skin of a dead animal, which we tanned with milk.\" He sent to them: \"Its tanning is its purification.\" So it was brought to him, and he performed ablution, then prayed."],[1046,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey when a man said: 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"(He is upon) the fitra.\" Then he said: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He has come out of the Fire.\" We rushed to him and found he was a livestock owner whom the prayer time had come upon, so he called it out."],[1047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man being punished in his grave because of tale-bearing, and he passed by a man being punished in his grave because of urine."],[1048,"The Messenger of God ﷺ pawned his coat of mail to a Jew and took barley for his family."],[1049,"There did not come morning in the household of Muhammad with a sāʿ of grain or a sāʿ of dates, though he had nine wives."],[1050,"A woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “A boy was born to me, so I named him Muhammad and gave him the kunya Abu al-Qasim. It was mentioned to me that you will dislike that.” He said, “What is it that made my name lawful and my kunya unlawful, and what is it that made my kunya unlawful and my name lawful?”"],[1051,"I am the master of mankind on the Day of Resurrection. My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will call me, and I will say: “Here I am, at Your service; good is in Your hands. Blessed and Exalted are You. Here I am, at Your service, responding with obedience. The guided one is he whom You guide. Your servant is before You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. Blessed and Exalted are You.”"],[1052,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled with an oath together with a witness."],[1053,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah, the people of Makkah said, “Muhammad’s companions have hunger and emaciation.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered them to jog around the House, to show them that they were not like that and that they were strong and well. They jogged three rounds and walked four."],[1054,"Indeed, I am about to command my young men to gather bundles of firewood… [the rest of the hadith]."],[1055,"Comb your beards."],[1056,"My uncle brought me to Madinah in the pre-Islamic era and sold me to al-Hubab b. ʿAmr, the brother of Abu al-Yasar b. ʿAmr. I bore him ʿAbd al-Rahman b. al-Hubab; then he died. His wife said, “Now, by God, you will be sold for his debt.” So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I am a woman from Qays ʿAylan. My uncle brought me to Madinah in the pre-Islamic era and sold me to al-Hubab b. ʿAmr. I bore him ʿAbd al-Rahman b. al-Hubab, then he died. His wife said, ‘Now you will be sold for his debt.’” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Who is the guardian of al-Hubab?” It was said, “His brother Abu al-Yasar.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent for him and said, “Set her free. When you hear of slaves arriving to me, come to me and I will compensate you with one.” So they set me free. Then slaves arrived to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he compensated them with a boy instead of me."],[1057,"Use ithmid (antimony) for your eyes, for it causes the hair to grow, removes dirt, and clarifies the vision."],[1058,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ became gravely ill, and I was with him among a group of Muslims, Bilal called him to prayer. He said, “Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” ʿAbd Allah b. Zamʿah said: I went out and found ʿUmar among the people, and Abu Bakr was absent. I said, “O ʿUmar, stand and lead the people in prayer.” He stood and said the takbir. The Messenger of God ﷺ heard his voice—and ʿUmar was a loud-voiced man—and said, “Where is Abu Bakr? God and the Muslims refuse that”—twice. Then he sent for Abu Bakr, who came after ʿUmar had prayed and then led the people in prayer. ʿAbd Allah b. Zamʿah said: ʿUmar said to me, “Woe to you! What have you done to me, O Ibn Zamʿah? By God, when you ordered me, I thought only that the Messenger of God ﷺ had commanded you to do that. Had it not been for that, I would not have led the people in prayer.” I said, “By God, the Messenger of God did not order me, but when I did not see Abu Bakr, I thought you were the most entitled of those present to lead the people in prayer.”"],[1059,"The last instruction of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: “Two religions shall not remain in the Arabian Peninsula.”"],[1060,"He said: “O Messenger of God, I own a riding animal that I work and travel on. It may be that this month comes upon me while I find strength, and I would love to fast—O Messenger of God, it is easier for me than to delay it so that it becomes a debt. Should I fast it, O Messenger of God, or break my fast?” He said: “Whichever you wish, O Hamzah.”"],[1061,"Indeed God, Blessed and Exalted is He, is protective of the Muslim, so let him be protective."],[1062,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ proclaiming the Hajj. When we arrived in Makkah, the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to make it an 'Umrah, and he said: “Had I known beforehand what I came to know afterward, I would have made it an 'Umrah, but I have driven the sacrificial animal and combined the Hajj and the 'Umrah.”"],[1063,"The Messenger of God ﷺ clothed me in a striped silk garment, and I wore it. I went to the Prophet ﷺ in the morning, and when he saw it on me, he said: “I did not clothe you in it for you to wear it; I only sent it to you so that you could clothe the women with it.”"],[1064,"The she-camel of the Messenger of God ﷺ, al-Jad'a', was stolen. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If God returns her to me, I will surely thank my Lord, Mighty and Majestic.” She ended up among a tribe of the Arabs in which there was a Muslim woman. Whenever the camels went out to pasture, she went out alone, and whenever the camels knelt down, she knelt alone, placing her chest on the ground. God put it into her mind to flee on her. She saw the people were heedless, so she mounted her, then urged her on, and she reached Madinah in the morning. When the Muslims saw her, they rejoiced and walked beside her until they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw her, he said: “Praise be to God.” The woman said: “O Messenger of God, I vowed that if God saved me on her, I would slaughter her and feed her meat to the poor.” He said: “What a bad reward you have given her! There is no vow for you except with what you own.” Then they waited to see if the Messenger of God ﷺ would initiate a fast or a prayer, and they thought he had forgotten. So they said: “O Messenger of God, you had said: ‘If God, Mighty and Majestic, returns her to me, I will surely thank my Lord, Mighty and Majestic.’” He said: “Did I not say: ‘Praise be to God’?”"],[1065,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding the two rak'ahs after 'Asr."],[1066,"Hudhayfah wore new clothes and said: “Praise be to God who has covered my private parts and beautified me among His servants.” Then he said: “When the Messenger of God ﷺ wore new clothes, he would say something similar.”"],[1067,"Every town will be entered by the terror of the Dajjal except Madinah. He will come to it to enter it, and he will find at its gate an angel with a drawn sword, who will turn him away from it."],[1068,"A man from my Ummah will emerge who speaks according to my Sunnah. God, Mighty and Majestic, will send down rain from the sky for him, and the earth will bring forth its blessings for him. The earth will be filled with fairness and justice through him, just as it was filled with tyranny and oppression. He will rule over this Ummah for seven years, and he will descend at Jerusalem."],[1069,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was in Makkah, he would recite the Qur'an aloud. The polytheists would drive people away from him and say: “Do not listen to this Qur'an, and make noise during it, so that you may prevail.” When he made his recitation quiet, those who wished to hear the Qur'an could not hear it. So God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: “And do not recite [too] loudly in your prayer or [too] quietly, but seek a way between that.”"],[1070,"A Jewish woman entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in 'A'ishah's house, and she said: “Poison upon you.” I said: “Poison upon you and the curse.”"],[1071,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer while completing it fully."],[1072,"A man invited the Messenger of God ﷺ to barley bread and rancid fat."],[1073,"I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, and behind Abu Bakr, and behind Umar, and behind Uthman. They used to begin the recitation with “Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.”"],[1074,"Seven of the companions of the Messenger of God would suck on a single date, and they ate leaves until their cheeks became swollen."],[1075,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was alone in his house, he would be engaged in serving his family."],[1076,"This verse was revealed: “Those who spend their wealth by night and day, secretly and openly”—it was revealed concerning expenditures on horses in the path of God."],[1077,"Indeed, horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. Their people are aided upon them, and the one who spends on them is like one who stretches out his hand in charity. Their urine and their dung will be for their owners on the Day of Resurrection as musk of Paradise."],[1078,"Indeed, when a servant has a station that has preceded from God, Mighty and Majestic, which he has not attained by his deeds, God afflicts him in his body, or in his wealth, or in his child. Then He gives him patience over that until He causes him to reach the station that had preceded for him from God, Mighty and Majestic."],[1079,"When my community deems six things lawful, destruction will be upon them: when mutual cursing appears among them, and they drink wine, and they wear silk, and they take singing girls, and men suffice with men, and women with women."],[1080,"The Promised Day is the Day of Resurrection; the Witnessed is the Day of Arafah; and the Witness is the Day of Friday. The sun has not risen nor set on a day better than Friday. In it is an hour in which no Muslim asks God for good but that He answers him, nor seeks refuge from anything but that God grants him refuge."],[1081,"There was no garment more beloved to the Messenger of God ﷺ than the shirt."],[1082,"Whoever frightens this quarter of the Ansar has frightened what is between these two—and he placed his palms on his sides."],[1083,"Two men brought a dispute to the Prophet ﷺ. He said to the claimant, “Bring your proof.” He had no proof, so the Prophet ﷺ said, “Then the oath is upon him.” The man was distressed by that and said, “My right will be lost by his oath.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever swears an oath by which he intends to take the right of his brother falsely, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify him, and he will have a painful punishment.” When the man heard that, he refrained from the oath and acknowledged the other man's right."],[1084,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marry Maymūnah while he was in a state of iḥrām? She said: No; he married her only when both of them were outside iḥrām."],[1085,"Indeed, the act of obedience most swift in reward is maintaining ties of kinship. A household may be wicked, yet their wealth grows and their numbers increase if they maintain their kinship ties. And the acts of disobedience most swift in punishment are transgression and betrayal. The false oath strips away wealth, diminishes offspring, and leaves the homes desolate."],[1086,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has a tablet of green chrysolite placed beneath the Throne, upon which is written: I am Allah; there is no god but Me, the Most Merciful of the merciful. I have created three hundred and some odd character traits. Whoever comes with one of these traits along with the testimony that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise."],[1087,"He used to perform the witr prayer while mounted on his camel, and he mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ used to do that."],[1088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded his wives to perform tamattuʿ and ordered cattle for them."],[1089,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck ʿUmar's chest with his hand three times when he embraced Islam, saying: O Allah, remove the rancor in his heart and replace it with faith. He said that three times."],[1090,"When you dress and when you perform ablution, begin with your right sides."],[1091,"Abū Shuʿayb had a servant who was a butcher. When he saw the hardship that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions were enduring, he ordered his servant to bring them meat enough for five, and he sent word to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Come to us as the fifth of five. He came, but a sixth person was with them. When they reached Abū Shuʿayb's door, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You sent for me and five others, but this man followed us. If you give him permission, he will enter; otherwise he will return. Abū Shuʿayb said: I have given permission; let him enter, O Messenger of Allah."],[1092,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over his leather socks and turban during the expedition of Tabūk."],[1093,"In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the sacrificial animals among us were camels and cattle."],[1094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pray inside the Kaʿbah, but when he entered he fell down in prostration, then raised his head and supplicated."],[1095,"Regarding this verse: “If they come to you, judge between them or turn away from them. If you judge, judge between them with justice. Indeed, Allah loves those who act justly.” He said: They were from Banū al-Naḍīr; when they killed someone from Banū Qurayẓah, they paid them half the blood money, but Banū Qurayẓah, when they killed someone from Banū al-Naḍīr, paid them the full blood money. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the blood money equal between them, the full amount."],[1096,"Indeed, from raisins, dates, wheat, and barley comes wine."],[1097,"The first to recognize the Messenger of God ﷺ after the defeat, and after the people said 'The Messenger of God ﷺ has been killed,' was..."],[1098,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to go around to his wives with a single washing."],[1099,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me the call to prayer word by word: 'God is the Greatest, God is the Greatest, God is the Greatest, God is the Greatest. I bear witness that there is no god but God, I bear witness that there is no god but God. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Come to prayer, come to prayer. Come to success, come to success. God is the Greatest, God is the Greatest. There is no god but God.'"],[1100,"The mistresses of the women of the people of Paradise, after Maryam daughter of Imran, are Fatimah and Khadijah, then Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh."],[1101,"I brought the Messenger of God ﷺ water for ablution, and he wiped over his socks, sandals, and turban."],[1102,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to break his fast, when he was fasting, with milk. I brought him a bowl of milk and placed it beside him, and he covered it while he was praying."],[1103,"Make tharid, even if with water."],[1104,"Whosever mawla I am, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be at enmity with whoever is at enmity with him."],[1105,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, what do you think of a man who seeks good and remembrance? What is for him?' He said: 'Nothing for him,' saying that three times. 'Indeed, God, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept any deed except that which is sincere for Him and by which His face is sought.'"],[1106,"During the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, there was a black cloak. When his pain became severe, he would put it on his face at times, and at other times he would uncover it and say: 'May God curse a people who took the graves of their prophets as places of worship,' warning his community against that."],[1107,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ taking the pledge of allegiance from women in the year of the conquest at al-Safa. A woman came whose hand was like a man's hand, and he refused to accept her pledge until she went and changed her hand with yellow dye. And a man came to him with an iron ring on his hand, and he said: 'God has not purified a hand on which there is an iron ring.'"],[1108,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised God, mighty and glorious, and extolled Him, then said: 'O people, there is no prayer without ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention God’s name over it. He does not believe in God who does not believe in me, and he does not believe in me who does not acknowledge the right of the Anṣār.'"],[1111,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the day of the Trench: 'They distracted us from the afternoon prayer' — and he did not pray it that day until the sun had set — 'may God fill their graves, their hearts, and their homes with fire.'"],[1112,"I met my uncle carrying a banner and said, 'Where are you heading?' He replied, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife and ordered me to strike his neck and seize his property.'"],[1113,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went to a people's refuse pit and urinated. I brought him water and poured it over him. He performed ablution, wiped his head and his leather socks, then stood and prayed."],[1114,"I asked Ubayy b. Kaʿb about the two protective surahs [al-Muʿawwidhatān], and he said: 'I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about them, and he said: \"It was said to me, so I said.\" Ubayy said: \"He said to us, so we said.\"'"],[1115,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths precede their testimonies and whose testimonies precede their oaths."],[1116,"I asked Ubayy b. Kaʿb about the Night of Decree, and he said: 'It is the night of the twenty-seventh, based on the verse that.'"],[1117,"I came to Ṣafwān b. ʿAssāl al-Murādī and asked him about wiping over leather socks. He said: 'When we traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he commanded us not to remove our leather socks for three nights and their days except in the case of major ritual impurity. But for defecation or urination, no.'"],[1118,"Whoever eats with people should not take two dates at once. If he wants to do so, let him seek their permission; if they allow him, then let him do it."],[1119,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him. He stipulated to me: 'You must testify that there is no god but God and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger, perform the five prayers, fast Ramadan, pay zakah, perform pilgrimage to the House, and strive in the way of God.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, there are two that I cannot do. By God, I have only ten she-camels, the milk animals of my family and their burden carriers. As for jihad, they claim that whoever flees incurs God’s wrath. I fear that when battle is present, my soul will become greedy and I will hate death.' The Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew his hand, then shook it, then said: 'No charity and no jihad — then with what will you enter Paradise?' So I pledged allegiance to him on all of them."],[1120,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mixing unripe dates with ripe dates."],[1121,"The companions of your Prophet used to dislike wearing silk, yet they brought it into their homes."],[1122,"Abu Bakr became very angry with a man, so much so that his color changed. Abu Bakr was a man of sharp temper. Abu Barzah said: When I saw that from him, I said, 'O khalifah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, if you command me, I will strike his neck.' It was as if cold water was poured on him, and his anger left the man. He said, 'May your mother be bereaved of you, Abu Barzah! That is not for anyone after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[1123,"The prophets were presented to me. A prophet would come with only one man, another would come with two men, and a prophet would come with only a small group, like that. Then my ummah was presented to me, and I raised my head, and there were the hills filling the space between me and the horizon."],[1124,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ. He asked for a drink, and a cup containing nabidh was brought to him. When he brought it close to his mouth, he noticed its sharpness and returned it."],[1125,"\"O Ali, there will be a fitnah, and you will argue with your people.\" I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me?' He said, \"Judge by the Book,\" or he said, \"Follow the Book.\""],[1126,"I entered upon Tamim al-Dari while he was governor of Bayt al-Maqdis, and he was cleaning barley for his horse. I said, 'O governor, was there no one to take care of this for you?' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever cleans barley for his horse in the path of Allah, then stands with it until he feeds it to the horse, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, records for him a good deed for every grain of barley.'"],[1127,"\"Preserve me in my companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them.\""],[1128,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man performing wudu, washing his khuffs. He poked him with his foot and said, \"This is not the Sunnah. We were commanded to wipe over the khuffs, like this,\" and he passed his hands over his khuffs."],[1129,"When he prayed over a deceased person, he would say: 'O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our males and our females, our young and our old. Whoever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon Islam, and whoever of us You take in death, take him in death upon faith. O Allah, Your pardon, Your pardon.'"],[1130,"A Muslim woman was captured by the enemy. They had previously captured a she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She saw a moment of negligence from the people, mounted the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and vowed to slaughter the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah. He said: \"What a bad reward you have given it! There is no vow for the son of Adam in what he does not own, nor in disobedience to Allah.\""],[1131,"If you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do that which is better and expiate for your oath. Do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it by asking, you will be left to it; but if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it."],[1132,"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with perfume containing musk when he entered ihram, before he entered ihram, and on the Day of Sacrifice before he circumambulated the House."],[1133,"\"Take from me: Allah has made a way for them. The previously married with the previously married: one hundred lashes and stoning. The virgin with the virgin: one hundred lashes and exile for a year.\""],[1134,"Regarding His statement: “And he certainly saw him in the clear horizon” (Q 81:23), he said: “He saw him with his heart, and did not see him with his eyes.”"],[1135,"O daughter of Qays, indeed residence and maintenance are only for the one who has the right of return."],[1136,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “On what do you pledge allegiance to me?” I said: “On hearing and obedience.” The Messenger of God ﷺ prompted me: “In what I am able, and sincere counsel to every Muslim.”"],[1137,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and he bought a camel from me. I sold it to him on condition that I would have its back until we arrived. When we arrived, I brought him the camel, and he ordered that I be given its price. Then he said: “It is yours.” I left with it, and a man from the Jews met me. I told him, and he began to marvel. He said: “He gave you the price and gifted you the camel?” I said: “Yes.”"],[1138,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded wiping over the leather socks during the expedition of Tabuk: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."],[1139,"Perform ablution from what fire has touched."],[1140,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited me during an illness I had, and I said: “O Messenger of God, I have no one but a daughter of mine; shall I bequeath all my wealth in the way of God?” He said: “A third, and a third is much. If you leave your heirs wealthy it is better than leaving them destitute, begging people with their hands. You will not spend any expenditure seeking thereby the face of God except that you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth. Perhaps God will raise you and benefit people through you and harm others through you.” Then he said: “O God, complete the emigration of my companions.” But the wretched Saʿd b. Khawla—the Messenger of God ﷺ mourned for him that he died in Makkah."],[1141,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the prayer of fear with his companions, and he mentioned the hadith."],[1142,"Three things, whoever has them will find the sweetness of faith: that God and His Messenger be dearer to him than anything else, that he hate to return to disbelief as he hates to be thrown into the Fire, and that he love a man only for the sake of God, Mighty and Majestic."],[1143,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ intended to enter ihram, he would wash his head with marshmallow, then anoint it with a little oil, not much."],[1144,"We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent his wives to perform ʿumrah and left me, and I felt hurt. I said: “O Messenger of God, you sent your wives for ʿumrah and left me.” He said: “O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, take your sister out to al-Tanʿīm, then let her circumambulate the House and go between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, then let her shorten her hair, then come to me before I depart.” That was on the night of al-Ḥaṣba. ʿĀʾishah said: “He only stayed the night of al-Ḥaṣba because of me.”"],[1145,"Ghifār—may God forgive her, and Aslam—may God keep her safe."],[1146,"There will be discord at the death of a caliph. A man from Banu Hashim will come out and go to Makkah. The people will bring him out from his house against his will and pledge allegiance to him between the Rukn and the Maqam. An army will be equipped and sent against him from Syria, and when they reach al-Bayda', they will be swallowed up by the earth. Then the bands of Iraq and the abdal of Syria will come to him. A man will arise in Syria whose maternal uncles are from Kalb; an army will be equipped and sent against him, and Allah will defeat them. The rout will be upon them: that is the Day of Kalb. The loser is he who loses out on the spoils of Kalb. He will open the treasures, distribute the wealth, and Islam will lay its neck upon the earth. He will live by that for seven years—or he said: nine years."],[1147,"We were with Hudhayfah, and some of us said to him, \"Narrate to us, O Abu 'Abd Allah, what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"If I did, you would stone me.\" We said, \"Glory be to Allah! We would do that to you?\" He said, \"What if I told you that one of your mothers would come to you in a battalion, numerous in number and fierce in might, fighting you—would you believe me?\" They said, \"Glory be to Allah! Who would believe that?\" Hudhayfah said, \"Al-Humayra' will come to you in a battalion driven by her non-Arab soldiers from where their faces are driven.\" Then he stood and entered a private chamber of his."],[1148,"A people will enter Hell, then they will come out, and they will enter Paradise. They will be known therein by their names; they will be called 'the people of Hell' (al-Jahannamiyyun)."],[1149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded women to give charity and urged them to do so, saying, 'Give charity, for you are the majority of the inhabitants of the Fire.' A woman among them said, 'Why is that, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Because you curse much, delay doing good, and are ungrateful to your husbands.'"],[1150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed five rak'ahs for Zuhr or 'Asr. It was said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?' He said, 'No.' They said, 'You prayed five with us.' So he faced the qiblah, prostrated twice while sitting, then said the salam, and then said, 'These two prostrations are for the one who thinks he has added or omitted from his prayer.'"],[1151,"My maternal uncle Hani' b. Niyar slaughtered his sacrifice before going out to the prayer, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to offer another sacrifice in its place. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a jadha'ah (a year-old sheep) that is better than a musinnah (an older sheep).' He said, 'Sacrifice it, but it will not suffice for anyone after you.'"],[1152,"I think that if anyone were to be spared from the squeezing of the grave, Sa'd b. Mu'adh would have been spared. Indeed, he was squeezed with a squeezing."],[1153,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah led us in prayer, and he stood up after the first two rak'ahs. We said subhan Allah to him, but he gestured with his hand, meaning 'stand up,' so we stood up. When he finished his prayer, he prostrated twice while sitting after saying the salam, then said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did this and said: If he remembers before he fully stands, let him sit; and if he does not remember until he has fully stood, let him continue his prayer and then prostrate twice after the salam.'"],[1154,"While we were walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he passed by some boys playing, among them was a boy. It was as if that angered the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said to him, 'Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?' The boy said, 'Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Be off with you! You will never exceed your station.' 'Umar said, 'O Messenger of Allah, let me strike his neck.' He said, 'O 'Umar, if he is the one you fear, you will never be able to kill him.'"],[1155,"We were walking with the Prophet ﷺ when a snake appeared. We rushed toward it, but it entered a crevice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You have been protected from its evil, and it has been protected from your evil.'"],[1156,"We were young men with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to us, 'Whoever among you can afford marriage, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards chastity. Whoever cannot afford it, let him fast, for it is a shield for him.'"],[1157,"I witnessed the conquest of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we captured female captives. We practiced 'azl (coitus interruptus) with them. Some of us said to others, 'You do this while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is among you? If only you would ask him.' So we asked him, and he said, 'Not every water results in a child. It is only something that, when Allah wills it to be, it is. No one can repel it.'"],[1158,"I performed the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Messenger of God ﷺ. I saw Bilal and Usamah; Bilal was leading his riding camel by its halter, and the other was holding up his garment to shade him from the heat, until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah. Then he departed, having put his garment under his right armpit and over his left shoulder. I saw the protrusion of his right shoulder, like a gathering. He stood before the people and spoke at length. Among what he said was: 'If a maimed black slave is appointed over you and leads you by the Book of God, listen to him and obey.'"],[1159,"Ibn ʿUmar was asked about ʿAli and ʿUthman, and he said: 'As for ʿAli, do not ask about him. Look at his standing with the Messenger of God ﷺ: he closed our doors in the mosque and kept his door open. As for ʿUthman, he committed a great sin on the day the two armies met, and God pardoned him. And he committed a sin against you lesser than that, and you killed him.'"],[1160,"The two angels came to Muhammad ﷺ. One of them said: 'Recite the Qur'an in one mode.' The other said: 'Increase for him.' He kept asking for more until he said: 'Recite the Qur'an in seven modes.'"],[1161,"Whoever swears an oath to wrongfully deprive a Muslim of his property, God, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden him Paradise and made the Fire obligatory for him.' It was said: 'O Messenger of God, even if it is something small?' He said: 'Even if it is a tooth-stick from an arak tree.'"],[1162,"The believer's lower garment extends to mid-calf, and there is no blame on him for what is between that and the ankles. Whoever trails his garment out of arrogance, God will not look at him."],[1163,"When ʿUthman was besieged, he looked down upon them from the top of his house and said: 'I remind you by God, do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding the army of hardship: \"Who will spend an accepted expenditure?\"—while the people were exhausted and in hardship—and I equipped a third of that army from my own wealth?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I remind you by God, do you know about Rumah? No one could drink from it except for a price, so I bought it with my own wealth and made it for the rich, the poor, and the wayfarer?' They said: 'Yes.' And he enumerated other things."],[1164,"I asked Ibn ʿAbbas about coitus interruptus. He said: 'You have asked much about it. If the Messenger of God ﷺ said anything about it, then it is as he said. If he did not say anything about it, then I say about it: \"Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you will.\" So if you wish, practice coitus interruptus, and if you wish, do not practice it.'"],[1165,"Whoever keeps a horse in the way of God, its feed and its droppings will be in his scale on the Day of Resurrection."],[1166,"Ibn ʿUmar was on a journey when he heard the sound of a flute-player. He put his fingers in his ears and turned aside from the road. He said: 'O Nafiʿ, do you hear it?' I said: 'No.' So he returned to the road, then said: 'This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.'"],[1167,"The one who serves water to the people is the last of them to drink."],[1168,"The Prophet ﷺ took a bite of a shoulder, ate, then prayed without performing ablution."],[1169,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ reciting Surat al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer."],[1170,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ forbidding nabīdh made from the gourd and the glazed jar."],[1171,"I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of God ﷺ, from a single vessel, both of us from janābah."],[1172,"When you are told that the plague has fallen in a land, do not go forward to it; and if it falls in a land while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it."],[1173,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Zamzam and drank while standing."],[1174,"Ibn ʿUmar was asked about walled enclosures in which there is human excrement, people's urine, and the dung of beasts. He said: 'When the rains flow over it and the winds dry it, there is no harm in praying in it,' mentioning that from the Prophet."],[1175,"The supplication of the wronged is not turned back, even if he is a sinner; his sin is upon himself."],[1176,"Dāwūd ﷺ used not to eat except from the work of his own hand."],[1177,"The head of the religion is sincere counsel (naṣīḥah). They said: 'To whom, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'To God, Mighty and Majestic, to His religion, to His Book, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to the Muslims in general.'"],[1178,"He used to gesture in the prayer."],[1179,"Whoever would like to read the testament of the Messenger of God ﷺ, let him read these verses: 'Say: Come, I will recite what your Lord has forbidden to you...' up to His saying: 'That He has enjoined upon you, that you may be mindful' (Q 6:151–153)."],[1180,"The Prophet ﷺ asked her: 'Who is proposing to Umm Kulthūm bt. ʿUqbah?' She said: 'So-and-so and so-and-so, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf.' He said: 'Marry ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, for he is among the best of the Muslims, and among their best is one who is like him.'"],[1181,"The prayer would be called, and a man would present himself to the Messenger of God ﷺ and speak to him about a need, and he would detain him until some of the people began to doze."],[1182,"Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf married a woman for the weight of a date stone of gold."],[1183,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Ramadan, and he fasted and his Companions fasted with him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ broke his fast, and some of his Companions broke their fast with him, while some of them fasted. The one who fasted was better than the one who broke his fast."],[1184,"He was asked about elderly women: Did they attend the prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Yes, and the young women too. They used to pray behind our shoulders with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: And 'A'ishah said: If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had seen from women then what they are upon today, he would have prevented them."],[1185,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to touch some of his wives while he was fasting."],[1186,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us on the day of 'Ashura' and said: This is a day whose fasting has not been made obligatory upon you. So whoever wishes may fast."],[1187,"Abu Usayd, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, married a woman, and he invited the Prophet ﷺ to his wedding. His wife, the bride, was serving us and giving us date nabidh to drink, which she had prepared the night before and strained."],[1188,"Any man whose cousin comes to him and asks him from his surplus wealth, and he withholds it, Allah will withhold His surplus from him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever withholds water in order to withhold thereby the surplus of pasture, Allah will withhold His surplus from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1189,"Attach the wealth to the obligatory shares, and whatever remains is for the nearest male."],[1190,"When one of you finds a louse in the mosque, let him bury it, or let him remove it from the mosque."],[1191,"He passed by some people who had set up a chicken as a target and were shooting at it. He took it away and said: Whoever takes anything in which there is a soul as a target will not die in this world until a calamity befalls him."],[1192,"Overlook the sin of the generous person, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, takes him by the hand at his stumble."],[1193,"A woman entered upon me, and I brought her food. She said: I am fasting. The Prophet ﷺ said: Is it for making up Ramadan? She said: No. He said: Then break your fast and make up for it another day."],[1194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for him, saying: O Allah, bless Ali b. Shayban, and bless Ali."],[1195,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1196,"People will increase, while my Companions will decrease, so do not revile them. Whoever reviles them, upon him is the curse of Allah."],[1197,"On the Day of Resurrection it will be said to the image-makers: Give life to what you have created."],[1198,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave."],[1199,"On buried treasure, a fifth is due."],[1200,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My sister vowed to walk to the House. He said: Tell your sister to ride, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has no need of your sister tormenting herself. The man said: My mother owes a Hajj; shall I perform it on her behalf? He said: Yes."],[1201,"The Prophet ﷺ was occupied with something concerning the polytheists, so he did not pray Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, or Isha. When he finished, he prayed them afterwards, the first then the next, and that was before the prayer of fear was revealed."],[1202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Hassan b. Thabit: Satirize the polytheists, and Jibril is with you."],[1203,"The sun rises between the two horns of a devil."],[1204,"Fruit is not to be sold until it ripens."],[1205,"Seventy thousand of my community will enter Paradise without reckoning; they do not cauterize, do not seek ruqya, do not believe in omens, and upon their Lord they rely."],[1206,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ drinking standing and sitting, praying in sandals and barefoot, and leaving the prayer from his right side and his left side."],[1207,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave his wives a choice, and it was not a divorce."],[1208,"The one who strives for the widow and the needy is like the one who fights in the path of God, or like the one who stands in prayer at night and fasts during the day. And the guardian of the orphan—whether related to him or not—if he fears God, Mighty and Majestic, then I and he will be in Paradise like these two,\" meaning his index and middle fingers."],[1209,"Regarding this verse: 'Take [the path of] forgiveness' (Qur'an 7:199), he said: \"God, Mighty and Majestic, commanded His Prophet ﷺ to take forgiveness from the character of the people."],[1210,"The accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[1211,"A single suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition."],[1212,"It is as if I am looking at the glistening of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of God's ﷺ hair while he was in a state of ihram."],[1213,"Whoever loses his sight in this world, God, Mighty and Majestic, will give him light on the Day of Resurrection if he was righteous."],[1214,"The muezzin who seeks reward is like the martyr wallowing in his blood; he may supplicate to God as he wishes between the call to prayer and the iqamah."],[1215,"Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it; and if the month is obscured to you, then complete the number as thirty."],[1216,"A man's spending on his dependents is charity."],[1217,"I was holding the hand of al-A'mash, and he said: \"I recited the Qur'an to Yahya b. Waththab thirty times, each time reciting 'and the punishment (al-rujz),'\" and likewise Yahya recited to 'Alqamah, and 'Alqamah to Ibn Mas'ud, and Ibn Mas'ud to the Prophet ﷺ."],[1218,"The best jihad is of the one whose horse is hamstrung and his blood is shed."],[1219,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel."],[1220,"The expiation for a gathering is that the servant says after rising: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You.'"],[1221,"A man came to Zayd b. Thabit and asked him about something. Zayd said to him: 'Go to Abu Hurayrah, for while I, Abu Hurayrah, and so-and-so were in the mosque one day, supplicating and remembering our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and sat with us, and we fell silent. He said: \"Return to what you were doing.\" Zayd said: So I and my companion supplicated before Abu Hurayrah, and the Prophet ﷺ was saying ameen to our supplications. Then Abu Hurayrah supplicated, saying: \"O Allah, I ask You for the like of what my two companions asked You, and I ask You for knowledge that is not forgotten.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Ameen.\" We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we ask Allah for knowledge that is not forgotten.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Dawsī youth has beaten you to it.\""],[1222,"On the day of the conquest, he was on a camel, holding a staff with a crook, with which he was touching the corner, disliking that people should be pushed away from it."],[1223,"Change grey hair and do not imitate the Jews and Christians."],[1224,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer; the thief does not steal while he is a believer; and the drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer."],[1225,"O company of merchants, you attend your sales with idle talk and oaths, so mix it with some charity."],[1226,"If only one day remained of this world, Allah would lengthen that day until He sends a man from my family, whose name matches my name and whose father's name matches my father's name. He will fill the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with oppression and tyranny."],[1227,"Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan cannot imitate me."],[1228,"Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah' sincerely will enter Paradise. It was asked: 'What is its sincerity?' He said: 'That it restrains him from what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden.'"],[1229,"When a man says to another man, 'O disbeliever,' disbelief becomes incumbent upon one of them."],[1230,"He forbade the price of a cat."],[1231,"Were it not that I would make things difficult for my ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak with every wudu."],[1232,"The Prophet ﷺ led them in the Maghrib prayer reciting “Those who disbelieved and hindered [others] from the path of Allah.”"],[1233,"A servant keeps seeking the pleasure of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and so he remains in that state. Then Allah says: “O Jibril, My servant so-and-so is seeking to please Me, so My pleasure is upon him.” He said: “Then Jibril ﷺ says: ‘May the mercy of Allah be upon so-and-so,’ and the bearers of the Throne say it, and those around them say it, until the inhabitants of the seven heavens say it, and then it descends to the earth.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This is the verse that Allah sent down to you in His Book: ‘Indeed, those who have believed and done righteous deeds – the Most Merciful will appoint for them affection.’ And a servant keeps seeking the displeasure of Allah, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: ‘O Jibril, so-and-so is angering Me, indeed My anger is upon him.’ Then Jibril says: ‘May the anger of Allah be upon so-and-so,’ and the bearers of the Throne say it, and those below them say it, until the inhabitants of the seven heavens say it, and then it descends to the earth.”"],[1234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform witr with three [rakʿahs]. In the first he recited “Competition in [worldly] increase diverts you,” “Indeed, We sent it down,” and “When the earth is shaken.” In the second he recited “By time,” “Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar,” and “When the victory of Allah comes.” In the third he recited “Say, O disbelievers,” “May the hands of Abu Lahab perish,” and “Say, He is Allah, [who is] One.”"],[1235,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: “And We will surely let them taste the nearer punishment before the greater punishment,” he said: “The calamities of this world.” He said: “And the smoke has already passed.”"],[1236,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the zakah three times. And he said: “Whom do you count as a martyr among you?” They said: “The one who is killed in the path of Allah.” He said: “Then the martyrs of my ummah would be few. Being killed in the path of Allah is martyrdom, the plague is martyrdom, death in childbirth is martyrdom, burning is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, tuberculosis is martyrdom, and a stomach ailment is martyrdom.”"],[1237,"I was present with the Prophet ﷺ in a circle, and in his hand were pebbles. They glorified Allah in his hand, and among us were Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and Ali. Those in the circle heard their glorification. Then the Prophet ﷺ handed them to Abu Bakr, and they glorified with Abu Bakr, and those in the circle heard their glorification. Then they were returned to the Prophet ﷺ, and they glorified in his hand. Then the Prophet ﷺ handed them to Umar, and they glorified in his hand, and those in the circle heard their glorification. Then the Prophet ﷺ handed them to Uthman b. Affan, and they glorified in his hand. Then he handed them to us, and they did not glorify with any of us."],[1238,"Among what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: “Allah tests the servant while He loves him, in order to hear his supplication.”"],[1239,"And with the same chain: Shuʿba narrated to us from Hammad from Abu Waʾil from Abdullah b. Masʿud the like of it. “No one narrated this hadith from Shuʿba except Abu Jabir. Abu Hatim was alone in narrating it.”"],[1240,"Nabidh used to be prepared for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the evening. He would drink it that night and the following day, and that night and the following day, and that night and the following day. When evening came, he would give it to the servants or pour it out."],[1241,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ retired to his bed, he would say: “To You I have submitted myself, to You I have entrusted my affair, to You I have turned my back, out of desire and fear of You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I believe in the Book You have sent down and in the Messenger You have sent.”"],[1242,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade pairing dates [when eating], unless one of you seeks his brother’s permission."],[1243,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched Jaʿfar b. Abī Ṭālib to Abyssinia, he bade him farewell and supplied him with these words: “O Allah, grant me gentleness in making every difficult thing easy, for making every difficult thing easy is easy for You; and I ask You for ease and well-being in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[1244,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, boasted to His angels about His servants on the evening of ʿArafah in general, and He boasted about ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb in particular."],[1245,"My father said: “O Prophet of Allah, should I perform ablution if I touch my penis?” He said: “It is a part of you.”"],[1246,"He forbade a man to eat with his left hand and to drink with his left hand."],[1247,"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."],[1248,"Glorification is for men, and clapping is for women."],[1249,"We were forbidden to follow funeral processions, but it was not made binding upon us."],[1250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a woman in a howdah, and her son was with her. She raised her head and said: “O Messenger of Allah, does this [child] have a Hajj?” He said: “Yes, and you have a reward.”"],[1251,"Sufyān al-Thawrī passed by Asad b. ʿUbaydah and greeted him, but Asad seemed not to return the greeting. Sufyān went back to him and said: “O Asad, I passed by you, greeted you, and you did not return it.” Asad excused himself by saying he had been busy, but Sufyān seemed not to accept that from him. Then Asad said to him: “O Sufyān, has your standing reached the point that I should know something from Allah that you do not know?”"],[1252,"The Messenger of Allah forbade selling silver for gold on credit."],[1253,"A man came before the Prophet ﷺ and was overcome by trembling. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Take it easy. I am not a king. I am only the son of a woman of Quraysh who used to eat dried meat.”"],[1254,"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made Friday obligatory upon you from this day of mine, in this year of mine, in this month of mine, as an obligatory duty. Whoever abandons it out of aversion to it, while he has a just or unjust leader, then indeed may Allah not unite his affairs, nor bless him in his matter. Indeed, he has no prayer, no zakat, no fasting, no Hajj. Indeed, a woman must not lead a man in prayer, a Bedouin must not lead an emigrant, and a wicked person must not lead a righteous one, unless he is a ruler whose sword and whip are feared."],[1255,"I said to Maʿrūf al-Karkhī: O Abū Maḥfūẓ, I saw in this town a person who inclined toward the way of the abdāl. He remained silent, then said: O Allah, except for that one called Bishr al-Ummī."],[1256,"O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A devastating tribulation will come upon the people, leaving the forbearing bewildered. The one sleeping during it is better than the one sitting, the one sitting is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one hastening.' So cut your bowstrings and smash your swords against stones."],[1257,"Two men should not go out to relieve themselves, sit conversing, with their private parts exposed, for indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, detests that."],[1258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade soaking [dates] in gourds, green jars, hollowed stumps, and pitch-coated vessels."],[1259,"Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[1260,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel."],[1261,"He used to give the zakat al-fitr as one ṣāʿ of dates or one ṣāʿ of barley."],[1262,"When the muezzin called for the dawn prayer, he would pray two brief rakʿahs."],[1263,"Kaʿb b. ʿUjra suffered harm to his head, so he shaved it. The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to offer a sacrificial cow."],[1264,"If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have another, and nothing fills his mouth except dust. Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[1265,"I was commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no god but Allah.' Whoever says: 'There is no god but Allah' has protected his wealth and his life from me, except for its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed in His Book—then he mentioned that some people were arrogant, and He said: 'When it was said to them, \"There is no god but Allah,\" they were arrogant.' And He, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'When those who disbelieved harbored in their hearts the zealotry of the Age of Ignorance, Allah sent down His tranquility upon His Messenger and upon the believers and made them adhere to the word of piety, and they were more deserving of it and its people.' That is: 'There is no god but Allah.'"],[1266,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I would love to fight in the way of Allah and be killed, then be brought back to life, then be killed, then be brought back to life."],[1267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting (wisal). A man among the Muslims said, \"But you fast continuously.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Which of you is like me? I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.\" When they refused to stop continuous fasting, he fasted continuously with them for a day, then another day, then they saw the new moon. He said, \"If it had been delayed, I would have increased you\"—as a punishment for them when they refused to stop."],[1268,"Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in the darkness of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."],[1269,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying Duha with six rak'ahs, and I have not abandoned them since.\" Al-Hasan said: \"And I have not abandoned them since.\""],[1270,"Preemption (shuf'ah) belongs to the partner and the neighbor until they relinquish it."],[1271,"Qays b. 'Ubad and Ibn al-Kawwa' were with 'Ali b. Abi Talib when they were wounded on the day of Siffin. He said, \"For what are we killing ourselves? Let us go to this man and ask him: Was this [practice] in the time of the Prophet ﷺ or is it an opinion he holds?\" So we went until we came to him and said, \"Our wounds have reached what you see, and we remind you of Allah and Islam. Is this something the Prophet ﷺ entrusted to you, or an opinion you hold?\" He said, \"What do you want with this?\" They said, \"We remind you of Allah and Islam,\" twice or thrice. He said, \"Rather, it is an opinion I hold. The Prophet ﷺ did not entrust me with anything regarding it. But 'Uthman was killed, and the people pledged allegiance [to me], and I saw that I have the most right to it.\" They said to him, \"For what do we shed our lifeblood over the opinion of men?\" So they sat in their houses."],[1272,"I was with Muhammad b. Sulayman b. 'Ali b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas—and with him was a man—when a small son of his brother Ja'far was brought to him. He seated him in his lap and began to stroke his head like this, from its front to its back, turning his hair. The boy became annoyed, so the man who was with him said, \"May Allah keep the amir righteous, the boy is annoyed.\" He said, \"Be quiet.\""],[1273,"He forbade letting one's garment hang down (sadl) during prayer."],[1274,"I gave a she-camel in the way of Allah, and I wanted to buy from her offspring—or he said, from her progeny—so I asked the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"Leave her until she comes on the Day of Resurrection, she and all her offspring together, in your scale.\""],[1275,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man from Quraysh approached. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought him near and seated him close. When he stood up, he said, \"O Buraydah, do you know this man?\" I said, \"Yes, this is the middle of Quraysh in lineage and the wealthiest of them,\" three times. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I informed you of my knowledge about him, and you know better.\" He said, \"This is one for whom Allah will not give any weight on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1276,"Regarding the saying of Allah: 'He knows the treachery of the eyes—when you look at her, do you intend betrayal or not?—and what the breasts conceal—if you are able to, will you commit adultery with her or not?' Shall I inform you of what follows it: 'And Allah judges with truth; He is able to reward the good deed with good and the evil deed with evil. Indeed, Allah is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing.'\""],[1277,"Seek the Night of Decree on the seventeenth, or the nineteenth, or the twenty-first, or the twenty-third, or the twenty-fifth, or the twenty-seventh, or the twenty-ninth."],[1278,"The Prophet ﷺ was occupied on the day of the Trench from the Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha prayers. He ordered Bilal, who called the adhan and iqamah, and he prayed Zuhr. Then he ordered him, and he called the adhan and iqamah, and he prayed Asr. Then he ordered him, and he called the adhan and iqamah, and he prayed Maghrib. Then he ordered him, and he called the adhan and iqamah, and he prayed Isha. Then he said: There is no people on the face of the earth remembering Allah at this hour except you."],[1279,"I entered upon Ali after Isha and he said: What brings you at this hour? I said: I love you. He said: By Allah, do you love me? I said: Yes, by Allah, I love you. He said: Shall I teach you a supplication the Prophet ﷺ taught me? I said: Yes. He said: Say: O Allah, open the ears of my heart to Your remembrance, grant me obedience to You and obedience to Your Messenger, and acting upon Your Book."],[1280,"I saw myself before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the bed with the place of the funeral, and he was praying, and I disliked to remain standing, so I slipped away from beside the legs of the bed. And I saw myself and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, and upon me and upon him was a single garment."],[1281,"The Prophet ﷺ drank while standing."],[1282,"O Muhammad, when you see people fighting over worldly gains, then strike your sword against the largest rock in the Harrah, strike it until it breaks, then sit in your house until an erring hand comes to you or a decreed death. So I did what the Prophet ﷺ commanded me."],[1283,"By Allah, I am not more entitled to this wealth than any of you, but according to our positions from the Book of Allah and the distribution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is no Muslim except that he has a known share of this wealth, whether given or withheld, except an owned slave."],[1284,"The Prophet ﷺ set out on the expedition of Tabuk on Thursday, and he liked to set out on Thursday."],[1285,"He forbade qaza (shaving part of the head and leaving part)."],[1286,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I will not leave any gathering I sat in during disbelief except that I will openly declare Islam in it. He came to the mosque, and in it were groups of Quraysh, sitting in circles, and he began to openly declare Islam and bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. The polytheists rose and began to beat him, and he beat them. When they overwhelmed him, a man rescued him. I said to Umar: Who was the man who rescued you from the polytheists? He said: That was al-As b. Wa'il al-Sahmi."],[1287,"Hand me the khumrah (small mat). I said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand."],[1288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on the day of Adha without adhan or iqamah. He gave a sermon to the men, then went to the women and gave them a sermon and urged them to give charity, until the goods with Bilal became abundant."],[1289,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Jam (Muzdalifah), and the people were around him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come from the mountain of Tayyi, and I have exhausted myself and my mount. By Allah, I did not leave any hill except that I stood upon it. Is there any Hajj for me? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever catches the dawn prayer with us at Jam and had departed before that from Arafat, whether by night or day, has completed his rites and his Hajj is complete."],[1290,"None of you should say, “I am ṣarūra.”"],[1291,"I said to al-Aʿmash, “They disapprove of our reciting two words: ‘mā antum bi-muṣrikhiyy’ and another word.” He said, “Tell them that I recited to al-Aʿmash, and al-Aʿmash recited to Yaḥyā b. Waththāb, and Yaḥyā recited it to ʿAlqama, and ʿAlqama recited to ʿAbd Allāh, and ʿAbd Allāh recited to the Messenger of Allah. Whoever has a chain like this, let them bring it.”"],[1292,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. I saw him relieve himself, then he returned and performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[1293,"Abū Mūsā entered upon al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī to visit him when he was ill. ʿAlī said to him, “Have you come to us as a visitor, O Abū Mūsā, or as one visiting your nephew?” He said, “Rather, I have come as a visitor.” ʿAlī said, “Indeed, I heard him—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—say: ‘Whoever visits a sick person plunges into mercy, and when he sits down, it immerses him.’”"],[1294,"The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; my ummah comprises eighty of them, and the rest of the nations forty rows."],[1295,"When the muezzin gave the iqāma while he was eating, he would not stand up until he finished his food."],[1296,"O Allah, make Madinah beloved to us as we love Makkah, or more. O Allah, bless us in our ṣāʿ and our mudd, and transfer its fever to al-Juḥfa."],[1297,"May Allah brighten the face of a person who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for perhaps the one to whom it is conveyed is more retentive than the one who hears."],[1298,"The star never rose in the morning while a people had an affliction except that it was lifted from them."],[1299,"In every prayer there is recitation: the Opening of the Book and whatever is easy, and whoever does not recite, it is deficient."],[1300,"He forbade mutilation."],[1301,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to his companions while they were disputing about predestination, one citing a verse and another citing a verse, and it was as if a pomegranate seed had been burst in his face. He said, “Is this what you have been commanded: to strike the Book of Allah against itself? Look at what you have been commanded to do and follow it, and what you have been forbidden from, avoid it.”"],[1302,"It is imminent that whoever among you lives will see Isa ibn Maryam as a just ruler and judge. The jizya will be abolished, the cross will be broken, the pig will be killed, and war will lay down its burdens."],[1303,"Abu Musa al-Ash'ari fell unconscious, and his wife, the daughter of Abu Dawmah, wept over him. When he regained consciousness, he said: \"I declare myself free from that which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared himself free: from the one who shaves (the head in lamentation), wails, or tears (the clothes).\""],[1304,"You will never recite a surah more beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, nor more effective than: Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak. So if you are able not to abandon it, then do so."],[1305,"When you hear of a plague in a land, do not enter it; and if it occurs while you are in it, do not leave it fleeing from it."],[1306,"Do not ask for authority, for if you ask for it and are given it, you will be left to yourself; but if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it. And if you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath."],[1307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate meat twice in one day."],[1308,"O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge and acceptable deeds ..."],[1309,"When he led them in prayer and said: \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" they did not raise their heads from bowing to stand until they saw him prostrating."],[1310,"None loves the Ansar but a believer, and none hates them but a hypocrite."],[1311,"Wala' (clientage) is a bond like kinship; it is not to be sold, nor given as a gift."],[1312,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling wala' and giving it as a gift."],[1313,"Whoever suppresses his anger, Allah will avert punishment from him; and whoever guards his tongue, Allah will conceal his faults."],[1314,"Whoever does not face the qiblah and does not turn his back to it while defecating, a good deed is written for him and an evil deed is erased from him."],[1315,"I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's. The Prophet ﷺ got up at night, performed wudu, then prayed eight rak'ahs, then performed witr with three, then lay down."],[1316,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: Is there jihad for women? He said: Their jihad is the Hajj."],[1317,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, the people said: Enjoy temporary marriage. I went out with a cousin of mine; he had a cloak and I had a cloak. We proposed to a woman in Makkah. His cloak was better than mine, and I was more handsome and younger than him. She said: A cloak like a cloak, and a man more handsome than a man. I married her and consummated the marriage. Then I returned, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ giving a sermon, saying: I had permitted you temporary marriage, but Gabriel ﷺ came to me and informed me that it is forbidden until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever among you has entered upon a woman, let him not return to her, and do not take back anything of what you have given them."],[1318,"The Prophet ﷺ raised his hands when he began the prayer."],[1319,"The purification of the vessel of one of you, if a dog licks it, is to wash it seven times, the first of them with dust."],[1320,"When Umar was stabbed, it was said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, appoint a successor, for if your shepherd came to you having left your flock untended, you would say: Have you left my sheep without a shepherd? So how about the community of Muhammad ﷺ? Umar said: If I leave it, one better than me left it—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—and if I appoint, one better than me appointed—meaning Abu Bakr. Then he said: The consultation is to these six with whom the Prophet ﷺ died while he was pleased with them: Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and Sa'd."],[1321,"Those who love one another for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will be in the shade of Allah on the day when there is no shade but His shade, on pulpits of light. People will be terrified but they will not be terrified. When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends a punishment for the people of the earth, He remembers them and turns the punishment away from them because of His remembrance of them."],[1322,"A burden from the burdens of the Prophet ﷺ will come upon you, so woe to you from them and woe to you on their account."],[1323,"The one you call Surah al-Tawbah is the Surah of Punishment. You do not read from it, of what we used to read, except a quarter of it."],[1324,"Allah the Exalted will grasp the earth on the Day of Resurrection with His left hand, and the heavens will be in His right hand, then He will say: I am the King."],[1325,"Whoever relieves a distress of a Muslim in this world, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will relieve a distress of the Hereafter from him. Whoever conceals the fault of a Muslim, Allah will conceal his fault in this world and the Hereafter. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is in aid of the servant as long as the servant is in aid of his brother."],[1326,"Abu Dharr was with a small flock of his in Madinah. When he came, the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “O Abu Dharr,” but he remained silent. He repeated it to him, but he remained silent. He said, “O Abu Dharr, may your mother be bereaved of you.” He said, “I am in a state of major ritual impurity.” He called for a servant girl to bring water for him, and she came to him with it. He screened himself with his mount and performed the ritual bath. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Clean earth is sufficient for you, even if you do not find water for twenty years. If you find it, then let it touch your skin.”"],[1327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a choice, and we chose him, so it was not a divorce."],[1328,"When you come to prayer, come with dignity and tranquility. Pray what you catch up with, and make up what you missed."],[1329,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will gather the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection on a single plain. Then a caller will call out from beneath the Throne: “O people of tawhid! Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has pardoned you.” The people will then stand and some will cling to others regarding the injustices of this world. Then a caller will call out: “O people of tawhid! Let some of you pardon others, and upon Me is the reward.”"],[1330,"I presented the Quran to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Jibril commanded me to present the Quran to you.”"],[1331,"There is no person who has a prayer at night, and sleep overcomes him regarding it, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, writes for him the reward of his prayer, and his sleep is a charity upon him."],[1332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never asked for anything and said, “No.”"],[1333,"On the day of Badr, al-Abbas was taken captive, and no shirt was found for him that would fit him."],[1334,"I was on the day when Sa'd b. Mu'adh judged concerning Banu Qurayzah a boy upon whom the razor had not yet passed, so no judgment was passed upon me."],[1335,"The Hour will not come until Isa son of Maryam descends to the earth as a just ruler and an equitable judge. He will break the cross, kill the pig and the ape, the jizyah will be lifted, and the prostration will be entirely one for Allah, Lord of the worlds."],[1336,"Do not face the qiblah or turn your backs to it with defecation or urination, but turn eastward or westward."],[1337,"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."],[1338,"Bring your flocks and yourselves indoors when the sun sets until the darkness of the night has passed, for the devil emerges at that time. Shut your doors, extinguish your lamps, for the little mischief-maker may set the house ablaze. Cover your vessels, even if by placing a stick across them, for the devil does not open a door nor uncover a cover."],[1339,"None of you should walk in a single sandal, nor eat with his left hand, nor lie on his back placing one leg over the other, nor wrap himself in al-samma' (a manner of wrapping that leaves no opening for the hands)."],[1340,"Regarding His saying: 'God will establish those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter' (Quran 14:27), he said: 'When a believer dies, he is made to sit up on his grave, and it is said to him: Who is your Lord? He says: God is my Lord. Then it is said to him: Who is your Prophet? He says: Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah. This is repeated to him three times.'"],[1341,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when Abu Bakr and 'Umar came. He said: 'These two are the masters of the elderly of Paradise, from the first and the last, except for the prophets and messengers. Do not inform them, O 'Ali.'"],[1342,"The Prophet ﷺ carried Hasan and said: 'O God, I love him, so love him, and love those who love him.'"],[1343,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ wearing two red garments and greeted, but he did not return the greeting."],[1344,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ taking 'Ali by the hand, and he said: 'This is my ally, and I am his ally.'"],[1345,"There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to God, the Mighty and Majestic."],[1346,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and with us was a camel-driver called Anjasha. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'O Anjasha, drive gently with the glass vessels.'"],[1347,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ with a broth before him containing gourd, and he kept seeking it out and eating it."],[1348,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed ten with regard to wine: its presser, the one who has it pressed, its seller, its buyer, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its drinker, its pourer, and the one who consumes its price."],[1349,"Among the signs of the Hour are obscenity and vulgarity, severing ties of kinship, betraying the trustworthy, and entrusting the treacherous."],[1350,"Allah does not bestow any blessing upon a servant, and he says, “Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds,” except that what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives is better than what he receives."],[1351,"Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, whether it falls short or reaches its target, will have the like of the reward of freeing four persons from the descendants of Isma'il."],[1352,"Whoever goes out in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will have the like of what touches him of dust as musk for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1353,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, wrote a book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and it is with Him upon the Throne. From that book He sent down two verses with which He concluded Surat al-Baqarah. Indeed, Satan does not enter a house in which they are recited for three nights."],[1354,"Regarding His saying: “You are only a warner, and for every people is a guide” (13:7), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The warner and the guide is a man from Banu Hashim.”"],[1355,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about ablution. He said: “If you are fasting, sniff water gently.”"],[1356,"When he performed ablution, he would run his fingers through his beard and between his toes, and he claimed that he saw the Prophet ﷺ doing that."],[1357,"Whoever says: “There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner,” with his heart obeying it and his tongue humbled by it, and “I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,” Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will forbid him from the Fire."],[1358,"There will be over you rulers who delay the prayer from its times. If you witness that, pray the prayer at its time and make your prayer with them a supererogatory one."],[1359,"Whoever spends a pair of anything from his wealth in the path of Allah, the gatekeepers of Paradise will call him, all of them calling him to what is with them: “O servant of Allah, this is better.” And whoever buries three of his own children from his loins, Allah will admit him to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy toward them."],[1360,"O people, enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong before you call upon Allah and He does not answer you, and before you seek His forgiveness and He does not forgive you. Indeed, enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong does not hasten death. And indeed, when the rabbis of the Jews and the monks of the Christians abandoned enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong, Allah cursed them upon the tongue of their prophets, then affliction enveloped them all."],[1361,"My father had stopped praying with us. I said to him: “What is the matter with you, O father, that you have stopped praying with us?” He said: “Because you make it too brief.” I said: “Then where is the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: ‘Among you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need’?” He said: “I heard ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud say that.” And he would remain long in bowing and prostration."],[1362,"The Prophet ﷺ heard Abu Musa's recitation and said, \"This man has been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud.\""],[1363,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ prostrate in [Surah] Sad."],[1364,"Regarding His saying, \"Establish prayer at the sun's decline,\" he said: \"When the sun passes its zenith.\""],[1365,"When the gaze enters, there is no permission."],[1366,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapping himself with it."],[1367,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping at Lahy Jamal while he was fasting."],[1368,"He prostrated in [Surah] \"When the sky is split open.\""],[1369,"When we stopped at a place, we would glorify Allah until we unloaded the baggage."],[1370,"When the Prophet ﷺ stopped at a place, he would not depart from it until he prayed Zuhr."],[1371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out from Mina on the day of Arafah. When his mount set off with him, upon it was a velvet cloth bought for four dirhams, he said: \"O Allah, make it an accepted Hajj, with no ostentation in it and no seeking of reputation.\""],[1372,"You shall enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, or the worst among you will be given power over you, then the best among you will supplicate and it will not be answered for you."],[1373,"Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ: a nobleman and a lowly man. He responded to the lowly one but did not respond to the nobleman. The nobleman said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you responded to this one but did not respond to me?\" He said, \"This one remembered Allah, so He remembered him; but you forgot Allah, so He forgot you.\""],[1374,"None gives shelter to a stray animal but one who is himself astray."],[1375,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, O best of creation.' He said: 'That is my father Ibrahim ﷺ .'"],[1376,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every beast of prey with fangs and every bird with talons."],[1377,"Have mercy on those on earth, and the One in heaven will have mercy on you."],[1378,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan, and in the Friday prayer: Surat al-Jumu'ah and Idha Ja'aka al-Munafiqun."],[1379,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a man from the Ansar, and I heard him say: 'O God, forgive him, have mercy on him, and honor his hospitality.'"],[1380,"Whoever says in the evening: 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, all of them, from the evil of what He has created,' nothing will harm him."],[1381,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded in three garments, with no shirt and no turban among them."],[1382,"He poured water for the Messenger of God ﷺ from a small vessel after he had relieved himself, and he performed ablution: he washed his face, and then tried to take his hands out of his jubba, but its sleeves were too tight. So he took them out from under the jubba and performed ablution, and he wiped over his leather socks. Then we came to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, who had already prayed one rak'ah, so we prayed one rak'ah with him and made up the rak'ah we had missed."],[1383,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought fresh dates, and he said: 'Where did you get this?' They said: 'We had some inferior dates, so we sold two sa's for one sa.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Return it to its owner, sell it for money, then buy dates with that.'"],[1384,"We were forbidden to enter upon women whose husbands are absent except with their husbands' permission."],[1385,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about His saying: 'God will bring a people whom He loves and who love Him.' He said: 'These are a people from Yemen, then from Kindah, then from al-Sakun, then from Tujib.'"],[1386,"If I were to take a bosom friend, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafa as a bosom friend."],[1387,"No people claim a man as their own except that he inherits from them."],[1388,"The Prophet ﷺ went on a military expedition and traveled that day until nightfall. When night came, he dismounted and the people encamped around him. He, Abu Talha the husband of Umm Anas, and so-and-so and so-and-so—four of them—slept, with the Prophet ﷺ resting his head on the foreleg of his mount. Then he slept and the four slept beside him. When a portion of the night had passed, they raised their heads and did not find the Prophet ﷺ at his mount, so they went searching for him until they met him coming toward them. They said: 'May Allah make us your ransom! Where were you? We were alarmed for you when we did not see you.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was sleeping where you saw me, and I heard in my sleep a rumbling like the rumbling of a mill, or a whirring like the whirring of a mill. I was startled in my sleep, so I jumped up and went on my way. Then Gabriel ﷺ met me and said: \"O Muhammad, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent me to you just now to give you a choice. Choose either that half of your community enters Paradise, or intercession on the Day of Resurrection.\" So I chose intercession for my community.' The four men said: 'O Prophet of Allah, make us among those for whom you intercede.' He said: 'It is guaranteed for you.' Then the Prophet ﷺ and the four came forward until ten men met him. They said: 'Where is our Prophet, the Prophet of mercy?' He said: 'He told them what he had told the group.' They said: 'May Allah make us your ransom! Make us among those for whom you intercede on the Day of Resurrection.' He said: 'It is guaranteed for you.' Then they all came to the great mass of people and called out among the people: 'This is our Prophet, the Prophet of mercy.' He told them what he had told the group, and they all cried out: 'May Allah make us your ransom! Make us among those for whom you intercede on the Day of Resurrection.' He called out three times: 'I call Allah to witness, and I call those who hear to witness, that my intercession is for whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[1389,"The passing away of my community will be by stabbing and the plague. They said: 'As for stabbing, we know it; what is the plague?' He said: 'The stabbing of your enemies among the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom.'"],[1390,"In this purse of mine is a hadith; if I were to tell it to you, you would stone me. Then he said: 'O Allah, may I not reach the age of sixty.' They said: 'What is the age of sixty?' He said: 'The rule of boys, the selling of judgment, the proliferation of security forces, testimony based on acquaintance, taking trust as booty and charity as a fine, and a generation that takes the Quran as musical instruments.' Hammad said: 'And I think he said: and the belittling of blood.'"],[1391,"I have been given from it something I do not think anyone has been given except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—meaning sexual intercourse."],[1392,"I did not think that any of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ desired this world, until it was revealed about us on the day of Uhud: 'Among you are some who desire this world, and among you are some who desire the Hereafter.'"],[1393,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[1394,"A person remains in ease of his religion as long as he does not shed forbidden blood."],[1395,"Whoever goes to a soothsayer, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights."],[1396,"On the night of Muzdalifa, the Prophet ﷺ prayed Maghrib and Isha with one iqama."],[1397,"Whoever goes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[1398,"The Prophet's ﷺ ring was of silver, its bezel from it."],[1399,"She granted protection to two men, and 'Ali wanted to kill them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We have granted protection to whomever Umm Hani' has granted protection.'"],[1400,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Friday prayer Surat al-Jumu'ah and 'When the hypocrites come to you' (al-Munafiqun)."],[1401,"He used to deliver the Friday sermon leaning his back against a wooden post. When the people became numerous, he said: 'Build a pulpit for me.' They built him a pulpit that had only two steps. When he moved from the wooden post to the pulpit, the wooden post yearned. Anas said: 'By Allah, I heard the wooden post yearning like a she-camel that has lost its young, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended to it from the pulpit, embraced it, and it became still.'"],[1402,"I have heard the recitation and found them close to one another, so recite as you have been taught. Beware of excessive strictness and disagreement, for it is only like one of you saying: 'Come' and 'Come here.'"],[1403,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people on a very hot day. He saw a man standing—as if he were a Bedouin—in the sun. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Why do I see you standing?' He replied: 'I vowed not to sit until you finish your sermon.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Sit, this is not a vow. A vow is only that by which the face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is sought.'"],[1404,"We used to make headbands containing wars and saffron, and we would tie them around the lower parts of our heads when entering ihram, then enter ihram in that state. We would sweat in them and perform ablution while wearing them until we exited ihram."],[1405,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage on a gray mule, with Khalid b. al-Walid leading him."],[1406,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas led us in prayer and stood up after two rak'ahs. They said: 'Glory be to Allah.' He continued. Then when he said the salam, he prostrated twice and said: 'This is what we did with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[1407,"\"Lead your people in prayer.\" I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I experience whispering.' He struck his hand on my chest, and I no longer felt it after that. He said to me: 'Lead your people in prayer. Whoever leads a people in prayer should keep it light, for behind him are the elderly, the weak, and those with needs.'"],[1408,"You will complete seventy nations on the Day of Resurrection; we are the best of them and the last of them."],[1409,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar used to begin with the prayer before the sermon on the day of 'Id."],[1410,"Prayer would be about to commence, and a man would stand up and speak to the Messenger of God ﷺ, until some of the people would doze off."],[1411,"A daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away, and they used to carry men and women on biers alike. So I said: O Messenger of God, I was in Abyssinia, and they are Christians, People of the Book, and they make for a woman a coffin above which are ribs, disliking that anything of her form be described. Shall I make for your daughter a coffin like it? He said: \"Make it.\" So she is the first for whom a coffin was made and used in Islam — for Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of God."],[1412,"Do not revile Tubba', for he had become Muslim."],[1413,"Every Thursday evening, the night of Friday, he used to say: \"The most truthful speech is the Book of God, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[1414,"If the inhabitants of the heaven and the inhabitants of the earth gathered together to kill a Muslim man, God would cast them all into the Fire."],[1415,"He was in the house of his maternal aunt Maymunah, and the Prophet's ﷺ water for purification was placed for him. He asked: \"Who placed it?\" They said: Ibn 'Abbas. So he struck my shoulders — or my chest — and said: O God, give him understanding in the religion and teach him interpretation."],[1416,"I was on the verge of ordering Bilal to commence the prayer, then turning to a people who heard the call but did not respond, and burning their houses down upon them."],[1417,"A woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ asking him: What is lawful for a man from his wife while she is menstruating? He said: What is above the navel."],[1418,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying while I was opposite him."],[1419,"It was practiced until the Prophet ﷺ passed away. Has any Qur'an been revealed after the Prophet ﷺ?\" — meaning the tamattu' form of Hajj."],[1420,"An old woman named Mulaykah sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he came to us. Prayer time arrived, so I went to a mat of ours that had become worn and sprinkled it with water. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and I stood with two young girls behind him, and the old woman stood behind us."],[1421,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ when they had finished the circumambulation, and he said: \"O Abu Muhammad, what did you do regarding touching the corner?\" He said: I touched and I left off. He said: \"You have done right.\""],[1422,"He passed by the market of Madinah and stopped at it, then said: “O people of the market, how incapable you are!” They said: “And what is that, O Abu Hurayrah?” He said: “That is the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being distributed, and you are here not going to take your share of it!” They said: “And where is it?” He said: “In the mosque.” So they rushed out to the mosque, and Abu Hurayrah waited for them until they returned. He said to them: “What is the matter with you?” They said: “O Abu Hurayrah, we went to the mosque, entered it, and did not see anything being distributed.” Abu Hurayrah said to them: “Did you not see anyone in the mosque?” They said: “Yes, we saw people praying, people reciting the Qur’an, and people discussing the lawful and the unlawful.” Abu Hurayrah said to them: “Woe to you! That is the inheritance of Muhammad ﷺ.”"],[1423,"This affair will continue to be strong and elevated until twelve from Quraysh rule."],[1424,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent out an army or a raiding party, he would summon its commander and command him to fear Allah and to treat those Muslims with him well. Then he said: “Raid in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not embezzle, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child or an old man. If you come to the people of a fortress or a village, do not grant them the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger; rather grant them your protection and the protection of your fathers, for if you violate your protection and the protection of your fathers, that is better for you than violating the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger. And if you besiege the people of a fortress or a village, do not make them descend upon the judgment of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and the judgment of His Messenger, for you do not know whether you will attain the judgment of Allah regarding them or not; but make them descend upon your judgment.”"],[1425,"He used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1426,"When the Prophet ﷺ entered the toilet, he would not lift his garment until he was near the ground."],[1427,"I asked Ibn ʿUmar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: “Do you know ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar? I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, so ʿUmar came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him. He said: ‘Command him to take her back, then when she becomes pure, let him divorce her if he wishes at the beginning of her waiting period.’” I said: “Does she count that divorce?” He said: “What else?”"],[1428,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the men who imitate women, and cursed the women who imitate men."],[1429,"Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in the religion."],[1430,"The life-grant (ʿumrā) is permissible."],[1431,"Whoever owns a mahram relative, he is free."],[1432,"The zakah al-fitr during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was only dates, raisins, and barley; it was not wheat."],[1433,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying, “Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah.” He said: “Who is Shubrumah?” He said: “My father.” He said: “Have you ever performed Hajj?” He said: “No.” He said: “Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj for your father.”"],[1434,"Two Bedouins came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. One of them said, \"O Messenger of God, which people are best?\" He said, \"The one whose life is long and whose deeds are good.\" The other said, \"O Messenger of God, the ways of Islam and its laws have become numerous for me, so what do you command me?\" He said, \"Let your tongue never cease to be moist with the remembrance of God, exalted is He.\""],[1435,"Part of what we memorized from the Messenger of God ﷺ is that incantations, amulets, and love-charms are from polytheism."],[1436,"The Ansar are my legacy and my trusted ones, so accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers."],[1437,"The month of Ramadan entered, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"This month has entered, and it is the blessed month of God. In it is a night; whoever is deprived of it has been deprived of good, and no one is deprived of its good except the truly deprived.\""],[1438,"Whoever strikes a whip unjustly will have retaliation taken from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1439,"Whoever does a favor to any of the descendants of Abd al-Muttalib and is not recompensed for it in this world, then I will recompense him tomorrow when he meets me."],[1440,"The Messenger of God ﷺ approached one day with two scrolls in his hand, looking at them. His companions said, \"By God, the Prophet of God is unlettered; he neither reads nor writes,\" until he drew near to them. He unrolled the one in his right hand and said, \"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a book from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, with the names of the people of Paradise, their fathers' names, and their tribes, summarized for them, nothing added to its end. Your Lord has finished.\" Then he unrolled the other one in his hand for the people of the Fire and said the like of that."],[1441,"The prohibition of wine descended upon the Messenger of God ﷺ when there was no origin of grapes in Makkah, and the vessels were filled with unripe dates and dried dates. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered them, and they were overturned."],[1442,"There is no incantation except for the evil eye or a poisonous sting."],[1443,"I came to Abd Allah b. Mas'ud six times and did not hear him narrate anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ. One day he narrated a hadith from the Prophet ﷺ and then said, \"Or something like this, or close to this,\" and his face changed."],[1444,"He used to go out when Ibn al-Tayyah called the adhan at the first dawn and say, \"What a good time for the witr this is,\" and he would interpret this verse: 'And by the dawn when it breathes.'"],[1445,"Whoever reaches the morning of Friday, then washes and performs a full bath, goes early, walks and does not ride, draws near and does not engage in idle talk, then for every step he has a deed from the deeds of righteousness: fasting and prayer."],[1446,"Whoever goes to a diviner or a soothsayer and believes him in what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ."],[1447,"If the servants did not sin, Allah would create creatures who sin, then they would seek Allah's forgiveness, and He would forgive them. He is the Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful."],[1448,"Whoever recites Surat al-Kahf, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection from his place to Makkah. Whoever recites ten verses from its end, then the Dajjal appears, he will not be harmed. Whoever performs wudu and says: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You. There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance,' it will be written on parchment, then placed in a seal, and it will not be broken until the Day of Resurrection."],[1449,"A man among us would have two or three names, and he would be called by some of them, and perhaps he disliked that, so the verse was revealed: 'Do not insult one another with nicknames.'"],[1450,"Whoever touches his penis, or his groin, or his testicles should perform wudu as he does for prayer."],[1451,"The Prophet ﷺ went out for the morning prayer and saw a man praying. The Prophet ﷺ tapped his shoulder and said: 'Are you praying the morning prayer four times, or twice?'"],[1452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the day of Ashura and said: 'That is a day that the people of the Jahiliyyah used to fast. Whoever wishes may fast it, and whoever wishes may leave it.'"],[1453,"Breaking the fast while traveling is a concession."],[1454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform wudu thoroughly."],[1455,"Dates were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began to inspect them."],[1456,"Khadijah bore the Messenger of Allah ﷺ six children: Abdullah, al-Qasim, Zaynab, Ruqayyah, Umm Kulthum, and Fatimah. Mariyah bore him Ibrahim ﷺ ."],[1457,"O Allah, make clear to us about wine. So the verse was revealed: 'O you who believe, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated' [up to the end of the verse]. The Prophet ﷺ called Umar and recited this verse to him, but it did not seem to satisfy what Umar wanted. He said: 'O Allah, make clear to us about wine.' Then it was revealed: 'They ask you about wine and gambling. Say: In them is great sin.' The Prophet ﷺ called Umar and recited it to him, but it did not seem to satisfy what he wanted. He said: 'O Allah, make clear to us about wine.' Then it was revealed: 'O you who believe, wine, gambling, stone altars, and divining arrows are only filth from Satan's work' up to His saying: 'So will you desist?' He recited it to him, and Umar said: 'We desist, O Lord.'"],[1458,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"Are you not pleased that you are to me of the status of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophethood and no inheritance?\""],[1459,"Indeed, al-Wasilah is a rank with Allah above which there is no rank, so ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to grant me al-Wasilah over His creation."],[1460,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention charity, and he said: \"Part of charity is manumitting a slave and freeing him.\" A man said: \"Are they not one and the same?\" He said: \"No, manumitting him is that you set him free, and freeing him is that you help in his ransom.\" He said: \"And if I do not do that?\" He said: \"Then a prolific milch animal given as a loan, or kindness to a relative.\""],[1461,"\"Who is the master of the Arabs?\" They said: \"You, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"I am the master of the children of Adam, and 'Ali is the master of the Arabs.\""],[1462,"Whoever ties a knot and then blows into it has practiced sorcery, and whoever practices sorcery has committed shirk, and whoever hangs something is left to it."],[1463,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at a place, he liked to pray Zuhr there before departing. He said: \"He stopped at a place, and when he wanted to depart, he gave the call to prayer, then prayed while the sun was almost at the middle of the sky.\""],[1464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a military expedition he had undertaken. The Prophet's companions ﷺ were struck by hunger and their provisions ran out. They came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining to him about what had befallen them and asking his permission to slaughter some of their riding camels. He permitted them, so they went out and passed by 'Umar. He said: \"Where have you come from?\" They told him that they had asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to slaughter some of their camels. He said: \"Did he permit you?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I adjure you by Allah to return with me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So they returned with him. 'Umar went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you permit them to slaughter their riding camels? Then what will they ride?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What should I do? I do not have anything to give them.\" 'Umar said: \"Rather, O Messenger of Allah, command those who have surplus provisions to bring them, and you gather it all on something, then supplicate over it, then distribute it among them.\" So he did that. He called them with their surplus provisions: some came with a little, and some with a lot. He placed it on something, then supplicated over it as Allah willed him to supplicate, then distributed it among them. There remained not one of the people except that he filled whatever container he had, and there was still surplus left over. At that point he said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Whoever brings this testimony on the Day of Resurrection without doubt, Allah will admit him to Paradise.\""],[1465,"We used to say regarding His saying: 'And they withhold the ma'un'—the cooking pot and the bucket and the like of that, for people cannot do without them."],[1466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the closing of the doors that opened into the mosque, except for the door of Abu Bakr."],[1468,"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom."],[1469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a Jew to borrow from him on credit until a time of ease. He said: \"What time of ease? He is the one who has neither root nor branch.\" I returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: \"The enemy of Allah has lied. If he had given to us, we would have repaid him.\""],[1470,"Whoever drags his garment out of pride in this world, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1471,"A group from the tribes of 'Ukl and 'Urayna came to Madinah and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we were people of livestock and not people of cultivated land, so we found Madinah unhealthy for us.\" He ordered them to go out to the camels of zakah and drink from their milk and urine. They did so and recovered. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and disbelieved after their Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent someone to pursue them, and they were brought after the sun had risen high. He cut off their hands and feet, gouged out their eyes, and they were not given water to drink until they died."],[1472,"The Qur'an was sent down on the Night of Decree in the month of Ramadan to the lowest heaven all at once, then it was sent down in stages."],[1473,"A believer does not see a fault of his brother and cover it for him except that Allah will enter him into Paradise."],[1474,"Whoever sees a fault of his brother and covers it for him, Allah will enter him into Paradise."],[1475,"He forbade blowing during prostration and blowing on food."],[1476,"He would not sleep until he recited: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah and Tabarak alladhi bi yadihi al-mulk."],[1477,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My father is an elderly man who cannot perform Hajj. Shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"Do you think that if your father had a debt and you paid it off, would that not suffice for him?\""],[1478,"Hoarding food in Makkah is a form of heresy."],[1479,"The Prophet ﷺ named 'Abdullah b. al-Zubayr and performed tahnik for him."],[1480,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the market of Dhu al-Majaz before he migrated, going around among the people saying: \"O people, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him.\" Behind him was a man saying: \"O people, this one is telling you to abandon the religion of your forefathers.\" I asked: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"His uncle, Abu Lahab.\""],[1481,"If a man's debtor becomes bankrupt and he finds his exact property with him, he is more entitled to it than the other creditors."],[1482,"When you rise for the prayer, come to it with tranquility. Whatever you catch, pray it, and whatever you miss, make it up."],[1483,"The most beloved of My servants to Me are the quickest to break the fast."],[1484,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah at sunset and did not pray Maghrib until he reached Sarif, which is nine miles away."],[1485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give me something, and I would say, 'O Messenger of Allah, give it to someone more needy than I.' Once he gave me some wealth, and I said the same thing, intending not to take it. He said, 'Take it, and keep it as wealth or give it in charity. If Allah gives you wealth without your asking for it, take it. And whatever is turned away from you, do not pursue it yourself.'"],[1486,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the wives of the Ansar, and their descendants."],[1487,"He said, 'What do you say when you go to your bed?' I said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'When you go to your bed in a state of purity, rest your head on your right hand and say: O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, turned my face to You, and entrusted my back to You, in fear and hope of You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You have revealed and Your Messenger whom You have sent. No servant says this in his night and then dies, except he dies upon the fitrah.'"],[1488,"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, sincerely believing in both, and performs the five prayers, Allah will forbid his face from the Fire."],[1489,"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, sincerely believing in both, and prays, fasts, gives the zakat, and performs Hajj to the House, Allah will forbid him from the Fire."],[1490,"The prayer in congregation surpasses the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five degrees."],[1491,"The Prophet ﷺ sent 'Attab b. Asid to Makkah and said, 'Convey to them four matters: two conditions in a sale are not valid, nor a sale combined with a loan, nor profit from what is not guaranteed.'"],[1492,"He used to say the salam in the even unit of the odd prayer and in the odd unit of it."],[1493,"No people gather to remember Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, except that angels surround them, tranquility descends upon them, mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."],[1494,"To give my ring in charity is dearer to me than a thousand dirhams I would gift to the Kaaba."],[1495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the latter night prayer until nearly a third of the night had passed. Then he went out to the mosque and found only a few people in it, so he became angry and said, \"I was on the verge of commanding some men, when the prayer is called, to stay behind and go to the houses of those who do not attend the prayer and burn their houses down upon them.\" And he ﷺ said, \"If a man were to invite the people to a meal, they would come to him, yet for the prayer, the call is made and they do not come to it.\""],[1496,"I have not forgotten from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for indeed I have not forgotten that he used to give salutation to his right and to his left at the closing salutation of the prayer, saying: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,' until the side of his face became visible to us."],[1497,"A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ went out with Ammar b. Yasir on an expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ammar had a wet dream, so he started rolling in the dust. When he returned, he informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to Ammar: \"You rolled like a donkey rolls. It would have been sufficient for you\"—and he moved his hands toward the ground—\"to place them like this.\" Salama said: \"To strike your hands on the earth, then wipe your face and forearms, and pray.\""],[1498,"If I had not heard it from the Prophet ﷺ except once, or twice, or three, or four, or five, or six times, I would not have narrated it. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever performs ablution and does it well, sin departs from his hearing, his sight, his hands and his feet.'"],[1499,"Regarding His saying: 'and they do not disobey you in what is right' (Quran 60:12), Umm Atiyya said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stipulated upon us that we should not wail."],[1500,"The believer dies with sweat on the brow."],[1501,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Ammar b. Yasir and his family while they were being tortured for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and he said: 'Rejoice, O family of Yasir, for your appointment is Paradise.'"],[1502,"The Hour will not come until many mines appear, which none will inhabit but the riffraff of people."],[1503,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. I said: Did he seek forgiveness for you? He said: 'Yes, and for you,' and he recited this verse: 'And seek forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women' (Quran 47:19)."],[1504,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a messenger who called out: 'No bowstring collar should remain on the neck of any camel unless it is cut off.'"],[1505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us with four statements and said: 'Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not sleep, and it is not befitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the scale and raises it. The deeds of the day are presented to Him before the night, and the deeds of the night before the day. His veil is light; if He were to remove it, the splendors of His Face would burn everything His sight reaches.'"],[1506,"He witnessed the Prophet ﷺ stand up after two rak'ahs and forget to sit, so he continued his standing and prostrated twice after he had said the salam at the end of his prayer."],[1507,"The Prophet ﷺ passed through some streets of Madinah and saw a dead black man whom they had thrown onto the road. He asked some of those present about him, saying, \"Whose slave is this?\" They said, \"A slave belonging to the family of so-and-so.\" He said, \"Did you use to see him praying?\" They said, \"We would sometimes see him praying and sometimes not praying.\" He said, \"Get up and wash him and shroud him.\" So they got up, washed him, and shrouded him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and prayed over him. When he said the takbir, he said, \"Glory be to God, glory be to God.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his prayer, his companions said to him, \"O Messenger of God, we heard you say whenever you said the takbir: 'Glory be to God, glory be to God.' Why did you say 'Glory be to God, glory be to God'?\" He said, \"The angels almost came between me and him because of the great number of their prayers over him.\""],[1508,"No one should make his brother get up from his seat and then sit in his place."],[1509,"Two should not hold secret counsel to the exclusion of the third."],[1510,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw mucus in the direction of the qiblah in the mosque, so he took something and scraped it off, and said, \"None of you should spit in the direction of his qiblah, for God, Mighty and Majestic, faces him; rather, he should spit to his left or under his foot.\""],[1511,"Sawdah gave her day with the Messenger of God ﷺ to ʿAʾishah."],[1512,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling the right of inheritance (walāʾ) and giving it as a gift."],[1513,"While I was with the Prophet ﷺ in the Ḥijr, al-Ḥakam b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ passed by, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Woe to my ummah from what is in the loins of this one.\""],[1514,"There is no prayer after dawn except two rak'ahs."],[1515,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was my partner in the pre-Islamic era, and he was the best partner: he neither deceived nor disputed."],[1516,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave the example of provision as a walled garden with a gate. What is around the gate is level ground, while what is around the wall is rough and rugged. Whoever approaches it from its gate obtains all of it and remains safe, and whoever approaches it from its wall falls into ruggedness and roughness, until when he reaches it, he has nothing but the provision that God, Mighty and Majestic, has made easy for him."],[1517,"Feeding food and good speech will enable you to enter Paradise. O Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, feed food and speak good words."],[1518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and he looked at a hole in front of his face and said: 'If hardship were to come until it entered this hole, ease would come until it brought it out.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: 'So, surely with hardship comes ease. Surely with hardship comes ease.'"],[1519,"O company of the Ansar, exchange gifts, for a gift removes ill will and bequeaths love. By Allah, if a foreleg were gifted to me, I would accept it, and if I were invited to a shoulder, I would respond."],[1520,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I love Allah and His Messenger.' He said: 'You will be with those you love.'"],[1521,"When he traveled, he would say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from hardship in travel and gloom in the return. O Allah, contract the earth for us and make the journey easy for us. O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Guardian over the family.' When he was about to return, he would say: 'Returning, repentant, worshipping, praising our Lord.' When it was the day his family arrived, he would say: 'Return, return to our Lord, a return that leaves no sin upon us.'"],[1522,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds, earthenware jars, hollowed-out stumps, and pitch-coated vessels."],[1523,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate: 'O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.' Aisha said: 'I said: By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, do you fear while you are the Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'O Aisha, the hearts of the children of Adam are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful. Whomever He wills to turn from misguidance to guidance, or from guidance to misguidance, He does.'"],[1524,"This son of mine is a chief, and I hope that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will bring about reconciliation through him between two groups of the Muslims."],[1525,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Hajj and Umrah."],[1526,"All of you are shepherds, and each is responsible."],[1527,"A man accused his wife and disowned her child during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them, and they performed mutual cursing as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said. Then he ruled the child belonged to the woman and separated the two who had cursed each other."],[1528,"When the drop falls into the womb and forty nights pass, the angel comes and says: 'O Lord, male or female?' The Lord, Mighty and Majestic, dictates, and the angel writes. He says: 'What is his provision? What is his lifespan?' The Lord dictates, and the angel writes. He says: 'Wretched or blessed?' The Lord dictates, and the angel writes. Then he folds the page."],[1529,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ commanding the offering of a firstborn from sheep: one from every fifty sheep."],[1530,"I was with 'Ali on the day of the Nahrawan, and he said, \"Search for the maimed one.\" So they searched but did not find him. 'Ali said, \"By God, I have not lied and have not been lied to.\" Then 'Ali got up and walked among the slain. He came to a group lying in a low spot of the ground among the slain. He said, \"Turn these over.\" They turned them over, and there was the maimed one, on whose arm was something like a woman's breast. He said the takbir and said, \"God and His Messenger have spoken the truth.\""],[1531,"\"Who spoke?\" They said, \"Abu Sa'id.\" He said, \"I never thought a man would confront me when he knew my kinship to the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" Abu Sa'id said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid it and prohibit it.\" After that, when Ibn 'Abbas was asked about it, he would say, \"We met someone more knowledgeable than us, so he informed us, and we desisted.\""],[1532,"\"O Ka'b b. 'Ujra, do the vermin of your head bother you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then shave and sacrifice a sheep, or fast three days, or feed six poor persons.\""],[1533,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote to Chosroes and Caesar and to every tyrant, calling them to God, Mighty and Majestic, when this verse was revealed to him: And this Quran was revealed to me that I may warn you thereby and whomever it reaches."],[1534,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks when traveling for three days and their nights, and when resident for a day and a night."],[1535,"Four collected the Quran during the lifetime of the Prophet ﷺ: Ubayy b. Ka'b, Zayd b. Thabit, Abu Zayd, and Mu'adh b. Jabal.\""],[1536,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution washing each part twice, twice."],[1537,"I was combing the Prophet's ﷺ hair while I was menstruating."],[1538,"The caller of the Prophet ﷺ announced that the qibla had been changed to the Sacred House. The imam had already prayed two rak'ahs, so they turned around and prayed the remaining two rak'ahs facing the Sacred House."],[1539,"Whoever keeps a dog that is not a hunting dog or a herding dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day.\""],[1540,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a group from Banu 'Amir, and we said, \"O Messenger of God, we find stray camels.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"A Muslim's stray is a brand of the Fire.\""],[1541,"A vow does not avert anything from destiny; it only extracts from the miser."],[1542,"The Prophet ﷺ stoned."],[1543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds and vessels smeared with pitch."],[1544,"When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is entrusted with something, He returns it. Luqman ﷺ said to his son: 'Entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the seal of your deeds.'"],[1545,"\"Some people will recite the Qur'an and it will not pass beyond their throats. Among them is a man with a defective hand, or a hand with a defect, with small hairs on its edges.\" On the day of Nahrawan, Ali said: 'Search for him.' They did not find him, then they followed him and found him. Ali said: 'Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth.'"],[1546,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we hear things from you that we would like to memorize. Should we write them down?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'What about when you are angry or pleased?' He said: 'Yes, for I speak nothing but the truth in anger and pleasure.'"],[1547,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a loan combined with a sale, two conditions in a sale, selling what is not yet received, and profit from what is not guaranteed."],[1548,"I traveled with the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar, and I never saw them pray more than two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs."],[1549,"No people sit remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic, except that a caller from the sky calls out to them: 'Rise forgiven, for your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds.'"],[1550,"Pray witr, O people of the Qur'an."],[1551,"Regarding this verse: 'O you who believe, when you contract a debt...' up to His saying: 'But if one of you trusts another,' he said: 'This verse abrogated what came before it.'"],[1552,"I bought my oath once for seventy thousand, because I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever seizes the right of a Muslim by an oath will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him.'"],[1553,"Four things are decreed for the son of Adam: creation, character, lifespan, and provision."],[1554,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying when a Bedouin passed by with a milch camel of his. The Prophet ﷺ gestured to him, but he did not understand. Umar called out to him: 'O Bedouin, [look] behind you.' When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: 'Who spoke?' They said: 'Umar.' He said: 'This one has no understanding.'"],[1555,"When three are gathered, two should not converse privately apart from the third, for that grieves him. A woman should not describe another woman to her husband such that it is as if he is looking at her. Whoever seizes the property of a Muslim by his oath will meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him."],[1556,"When the month of Ramadan arrives, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, the devils are chained, and a caller cries out: 'O seeker of good, come forward; O seeker of evil, desist,' until the month departs."],[1557,"Allah has not created a disease without creating a cure for it: those who know it know it, and those who are ignorant of it are ignorant of it – except sam, which is death."],[1558,"When one of you is in prayer and feels an impurity or filth, he should not depart until he hears a sound or finds a smell."],[1559,"Regarding wiping over the leather socks: Umar said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it, so we did it.'"],[1560,"No barley bread, little or much, would remain over from the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1561,"Whoever begins the day fasting and then has a wet dream, is cupped, or is overcome by vomiting, no makeup is required of him; whoever deliberately vomits must make it up."],[1562,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while part of my garment was on him, and I was menstruating."],[1563,"Gabriel ﷺ came to me, and I said: 'O Gabriel, tell me about the virtues of Umar in heaven.' Gabriel said: 'If I were to tell you of Umar's virtues for as long as Noah remained among his people – a thousand years less fifty – his virtues would not be exhausted. Indeed, Umar is one of the good deeds of Abu Bakr ؓ.'"],[1564,"He said: 'How do you perform ablution?' He replied: 'You ask me how I perform ablution, but you do not ask me how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution? I saw him perform it three times three times.'"],[1565,"Use condiment, even if only with water."],[1566,"Excellent are those who use the toothpick from my community."],[1567,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about cheese. He said: \"Cut it with a knife, mention the name of Allah, and eat.\""],[1568,"All flies are in the Fire except bees, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing them and burning food."],[1569,"Salman al-Farisi entered upon Umar b. al-Khattab while he was reclining on a cushion, so he threw it to him. Salman said: Allah is Greatest; Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Then Umar said..."],[1570,"Spirits are assembled hosts; those that recognize one another are in harmony, and those that are unfamiliar with one another are at variance."],[1571,"When speech becomes prevalent, action is stored away, tongues differ, hearts detest one another, and every relative severs the ties of kinship, then at that time Allah curses them, making them deaf and blinding their sight."],[1572,"A man from the people said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if a man pays the zakat of his wealth? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever pays the zakat of his wealth, its evil has departed from him.\""],[1573,"When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me."],[1574,"A man from Abyssinia came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, you have been favored over us in colors and prophethood. What do you think if I believe in the like of what you believe in and act like what you act upon, will I be with you in Paradise? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, he has by it a covenant with Allah, and whoever says: Glory be to Allah, Allah writes for him one hundred thousand good deeds.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, how can we perish after this? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, a man on the Day of Resurrection will come with deeds which, if placed on a mountain, would weigh it down. Then a blessing from Allah's blessings will come and almost consume all of that, were it not for what Allah bestows of His mercy.\" Then it was revealed: \"Has there come upon man a period of time...\" up to His saying: \"And when you look, you will see bliss and a great kingdom.\" The Abyssinian said: O Messenger of Allah, will my eye see in Paradise the like of what your eye sees? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" The Abyssinian wept until his soul departed. Ibn Umar said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lowering him into his grave.\""],[1575,"The Prophet ﷺ spoke during the prayer forgetfully, and he continued from what he had prayed."],[1576,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while two disputants were arguing before him. He said: \"Judge between them.\" I said: May my father and mother be your ransom, you are more entitled to that. He said: \"Judge between them.\" I said: On what basis? He said: \"Exercise judgment; if you are right, you get ten good deeds, and if you err, you get one good deed.\""],[1577,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"The Hajj is in months well-known\": \"Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, and Dhu al-Hijjah.\""],[1578,"The Messenger of God ﷺ put me in charge of the captives of Banu Qurayzah. I would look at the boy's private part; if I saw that he had grown pubic hair, I struck his neck, and if I did not see that he had grown pubic hair, I put him among the spoils of the Muslims."],[1579,"He threw the pebble from the bottom of the valley and said: \"This—by the One besides whom there is no god—is the standing place of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down.\""],[1580,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"Recite to me.\" I said: \"Should I recite to you, when it was sent down upon you?\" He said: \"I love to hear it from someone other than myself.\" So I began and recited Surat al-Nisa' until I reached: 'So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and We bring you against these as a witness?' His eyes ﷺ filled with tears, so I stopped. He said to me: \"Ask, and you will be given.\""],[1581,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other, except the Sacred Mosque."],[1582,"A crescent and a crescent would pass by us, and we would not light a fire in the dwelling of the Messenger of God ﷺ. I said to her: \"O maternal aunt, by what did you live?\" She said: \"By the two black things: water and dates.\""],[1583,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ three days before his death saying: \"Let no one die unless he thinks well of God, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[1584,"When one of you prostrates, let him be moderate in his prostration and not spread his forearms like a dog spreads."],[1585,"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes possession of it."],[1586,"I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and I was forbidden to tuck up a garment or hair."],[1587,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for a dead person more than three days, except for her husband."],[1588,"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection is a tyrannical leader."],[1589,"A man said: \"O Messenger of God, which jihad is best?\" He said: \"A word of truth in the presence of a tyrannical ruler.\""],[1590,"He commanded the woman with istihada to perform wudu for every prayer."],[1591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and did not sit in the first two rak'ahs, so he performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he said the salam."],[1592,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over the martyrs of Uhud, saying takbir over them nine times, nine times, then seven times, seven times, then four times, four times, until he met Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[1593,"My husband divorced me three times, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'You have no maintenance and no lodging.'"],[1594,"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[1595,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a group of the Ansar in their home. They slaughtered a sheep for him and prepared food from it. He took some meat to eat, chewed it for a while, and could not swallow it. He said: 'What is the matter with this meat?' They said: 'It is a sheep belonging to so-and-so. We slaughtered it so that its owner would come and we could satisfy him with its meat.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Feed it to the prisoners.'"],[1596,"When one of you doubts and does not know what he has prayed, let him strive to ascertain the correct number until he is certain, then let him complete based on his certainty, then let him perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[1597,"The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; my ummah comprises eighty of those rows."],[1598,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting."],[1599,"Do not curse the leaders, and supplicate for their righteousness, for their righteousness is righteousness for you."],[1600,"Dust in the nostrils of a servant in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell will never combine."],[1601,"I sat with the Prophet ﷺ more than a hundred times. He would sit with his companions while they recited poetry to one another, and sometimes they would recall matters of the Jahiliyyah and laugh, and the Prophet ﷺ would smile with them."],[1602,"May Allah have mercy on one who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for perhaps the one to whom it is conveyed is more retentive than the one who heard it."],[1603,"Two sales in one sale are not lawful."],[1604,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: What do you think of a man who meets me in a desolate land wanting my property? He said: Remind him of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he does not take heed? He said: Then seek help against him from the Muslims around you. He said: What if there is no one around me? He said: Then seek help against him from the ruler. He said: What if the ruler is far from me? He said: Then fight in defense of your property until you become one of the martyrs of the Hereafter, or you protect your property."],[1605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me on the day of the conquest of Makkah while I was fasting. I brought him a cup of milk, and he drank, then said: Drink. I said: I am fasting. He said: Is it a makeup fast? I said: No. He said: Then drink. So I drank."],[1606,"When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, wills to create a soul, and the man has intercourse with the woman, his fluid flies into every vein and nerve of hers. Then on the seventh day, Allah brings to him every vein between him and Adam. Then he recited: In whatever form He willed, He assembled you."],[1607,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, stretch out your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you for myself and for my daughter al-Huwaysilah. Even if I lied against Allah, I would deceive you. He said: Khalid b. al-Walid charged upon us with his cavalry, so we said: We are Muslims, and he left us. We raided al-Ubullah with him and divided its spoils, filling our hands."],[1608,"The best of the people of the East are Abd al-Qays."],[1609,"Whatever intoxicates in large quantities, a small quantity of it is unlawful."],[1610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray four rak'ahs before Jumu'ah and four after it, making the salam at the end of them as one rak'ah."],[1611,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, if a matter befalls us in which there is no clear statement, neither command nor prohibition, what do you order us? He said: Consult the jurists and the devout worshippers, and do not act solely on the opinion of a special few."],[1612,"I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him for the exchange. I have met someone more knowledgeable about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than me, and he informed me that it is unlawful."],[1613,"Whoever has a child born to him and would like to offer a sacrifice on his behalf, let him do so."],[1614,"The Magians were mentioned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"They let their moustaches grow and shave their beards, so be different from them.\" Ibn ʿUmar used to take hold of his moustache and trim it as one trims a sheep."],[1615,"I divorced my wife during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ while she was menstruating. ʿUmar mentioned that to the Messenger of God, and the Messenger of God ﷺ returned to ʿAbd Allāh his wife. When she became pure, he said: \"Divorce her if you wish, or keep her.\""],[1616,"We were eating dates on a shield, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by us after he had come from relieving himself. We said, \"Come,\" so he came forward and ate dates with us, and he did not touch water."],[1617,"Two groups of this community will not receive my intercession: the Murjiʾa and the Qadariyya."],[1618,"I served the Messenger of God ﷺ when I was ten years old, and he passed away when I was twenty years old."],[1619,"The Messenger of God ﷺ fell from a horse and his right side was scraped, so he prayed with us sitting, and we lined up behind him sitting. When we finished, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The imam is appointed only to be followed. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he says, 'God hears the one who praises Him,' say, 'Our Lord, to You be praise'; when he prays standing, pray standing; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting, all of you.\""],[1620,"His uncle struck a man from the polytheists and killed him, wounding himself in the process. He began to say, \"I have killed myself.\" This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"He will have two rewards.\""],[1621,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[1622,"He said to his companions: \"Learn Surat al-Baqara, for taking it is a blessing, leaving it is a regret, and the idle ones cannot master it.\""],[1623,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed effeminate men and masculine women."],[1624,"Ablution is the key to prayer."],[1625,"He lent the Prophet ﷺ some weapons, which were eighty coats of mail. Safwan said to him: \"Is it a guaranteed loan or a usurpation?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Rather, it is a guaranteed loan.\""],[1626,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[1627,"The Beast will emerge from the most sacred of mosques. While they were sitting, the earth rang out; and while they were like that, it split open."],[1628,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ retired to his bed, he would place his right hand under his right cheek and say: \"O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants.\""],[1629,"I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has conceived."],[1630,"I have not seen the like of Paradise: its seeker sleeps; and I have not seen the like of the Fire: its fleer sleeps."],[1631,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the lead, Abu Bakr prayed, and Umar came third; then a trial struck us, and whatever Allah willed happened."],[1632,"O Banu Hashim, you will face harsh treatment after me, so seek help against it through the slaves of the people."],[1633,"Whoever remembers Allah and his eyes overflow from fear of Allah until his tears reach the ground, Allah will not punish him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1634,"Whoever sends blessings upon me, his blessing reaches me, and I send blessings upon him, and besides that ten good deeds are written for him."],[1635,"Whoever swears an oath in order to seize thereby the wealth of a Muslim, he will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him—He may punish him or forgive him.\""],[1636,"The polytheists used to depart from Arafah before sunset and would not depart from Muzdalifah until the sun had passed its zenith. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ differed from them: he departed from Arafah after sunset when the fasting person breaks his fast, then he departed from Muzdalifah before sunrise.\""],[1637,"I handed the banner to 'Abd Allah b. Rawaha, and he was killed. Then he handed it to Thabit b. Aqram al-Ansari, who handed it to Khalid b. al-Walid. He said, 'Why didn't you hand it to me?' He replied, 'You know more about fighting than I do.'"],[1638,"Allah, Exalted is He, has decreed justice. When one of you intends to slaughter, let him sharpen his blade and give rest to his sacrificial animal."],[1639,"Sadaqah is not lawful for us or for our freed clients."],[1640,"The Dajjal is red, fair-skinned, huge and bulky; the hair of his head is like the branches of a tree; his eye is like the morning star. I likened him to 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qatan, from Khuza'ah."],[1641,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eating with three fingers: the thumb, the one next to it, and the middle finger. Then I saw him licking his three fingers before wiping them—licking the middle one, then the one next to it, then the thumb."],[1642,"The Negus married the Prophet ﷺ to Umm Habibah, and he paid a dowry on his behalf from his own wealth of two hundred dinars."],[1643,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen, he said: '[Say]: O people, I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah to you. Know that the final return is to Paradise or to the Fire—eternity without death, and residence without departure—in bodies that do not die.'"],[1644,"O Messenger of Allah, how should we invoke blessings upon you? He said: 'Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and his wives and his progeny, as You blessed Ibrahim; and grant blessings upon Muhammad and his wives and his progeny, as You granted blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'"],[1645,"The Prophet ﷺ killed a man of Quraysh on the day of Badr in execution. Then he said: 'No Qurayshi shall be killed in execution after this day except the man who killed 'Uthman b. 'Affan. So kill him. If you do not, you will be killed like sheep.'"],[1646,"No servant invokes blessings upon me except that the angels invoke blessings upon him for as long as he invokes blessings upon me. So let him do so much or little."],[1647,"Mu'adh had a dispute with a man, and they brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He ruled that one of them should take an oath. The other said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you have allowed him to swear falsely regarding my land, and he will take it.' The Prophet ﷺ then said, 'Indeed, if he swears falsely...' and he made a severe statement."],[1648,"Whoever consumes the flesh of his brother in this world, it will be brought near to him on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: 'Eat it alive as you ate it dead.' So he will eat it, grimacing and crying out."],[1649,"Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like, with no excess between them."],[1650,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when I was brought before him, he said, \"Indeed, I have asked God to aid me with a famine that will emaciate you, and with terror that He will cast into your hearts.\" He said with his hand altogether, \"Indeed, I had sworn thus and thus that I would not believe in you nor follow you. But the famine kept emaciating me, and the terror kept being cast into my heart, until I stood before you. By God who sent you, is it He who sent you with what you say?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"And is it He who commanded you with what you command us?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then what do you say about our women?\" He said, \"They are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish. Feed them from what you eat, clothe them from what you wear, and do not beat them or starve them.\" He said, \"Should any of us look at his brother's private parts when we are together?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then when we are apart?\" He said, and the Messenger of God ﷺ pressed one of his thighs against the other, \"God is more worthy that you should be shy before Him.\" He said, and I heard him say, \"People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection wearing the mark of servitude, and the first parts of a person to speak will be his hand and his thigh.\""],[1651,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us as I stand among you today and said, \"Be good to my Companions, then to those who come after them. Then lying will spread until a man testifies without being asked to testify, and until he swears without being asked to swear. Whoever desires the best part of Paradise, let him cling to the community, for Satan is with the solitary one, and he is farther from two. Let none of you be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and troubled by his evil deed is a believer.\""],[1652,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me the call to prayer, saying, \"Say: God is most great, God is most great; God is most great, God is most great. I bear witness that there is no god but God; I bear witness that there is no god but God. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Then repeat, and say: I bear witness that there is no god but God; I bear witness that there is no god but God. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Come to prayer; come to prayer. Come to success; come to success. God is most great; God is most great. There is no god but God.\""],[1653,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah, he entered the mosque and touched the Black Stone, then proceeded to his right, jogged three circuits, and walked four. Then he came to the Maqam and said, 'And take the station of Abraham as a place of prayer,' then prayed two rak'ahs—with the Maqam between him and the House—then came to the House after the corner and touched the Black Stone, then went out to al-Safa."],[1654,"He used to pray on a khumrah (small mat) and prostrate on it."],[1655,"Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but God enters Paradise."],[1656,"Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it has a qirat of reward, and whoever walks with the funeral until it is buried has two qirats of reward. A qirat is like Mount Uhud."],[1657,"He used to recite in the Witr: 'Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High', 'Say: O disbelievers', and 'Say: He is God the One'."],[1658,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform Witr with 'Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High', 'Say: O disbelievers', and 'Say: He is God the One'."],[1659,"There are six whom I have cursed, and every prophet whose supplication is answered: the one who adds to the Book of God, the one who denies God's decree, the one who makes lawful God's prohibitions, the one who makes lawful from my family what God has forbidden, and the one who abandons the Sunnah."],[1660,"Was the Messenger of God ﷺ intimate while fasting? She said, \"Yes, but he was the most able of you to control his desire.\""],[1661,"I used to know that the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had ended only by the takbir."],[1662,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was holding my hand on the morning of the eighteenth of Ramadan, he happened to glance and saw a man being cupped. He said: \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[1663,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[1664,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade garments dyed with safflower, qassi (a kind of silk garment), gold rings, and garments bordered with silk brocade. Then he said: \"And know that I am one of your sincere advisers.\""],[1665,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey when a man dozed off on his mount. Another man took an arrow from his quiver, and the man woke up startled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to frighten another Muslim.\""],[1666,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted the meat of horses and forbade the meat of domestic donkeys."],[1667,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: \"What is your name?\" He replied: \"Nu'm.\" He said: \"You are 'Abdullah.\""],[1668,"Whoever commits a sin and knows that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, if He wills, will punish him, and if He wills, will forgive him, then it is a right upon Allah to forgive him."],[1669,"A man entered the mosque announcing a lost animal. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May you not find it.\" He then confirmed it and said: \"Yes.\""],[1670,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the grave of a woman after she had been buried."],[1671,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"I have been commanded to teach you the Qur'an.\" I said: \"Was I mentioned there?\" He said: \"Yes.\" Ubayy wept. He said: \"I do not know whether out of longing or fear.\""],[1672,"Ghaylan b. Salamah had ten wives when he embraced Islam. The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to choose four."],[1673,"A man passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'What a bad servant of God and brother of the clan!' Then he entered upon him afterwards, and I saw him turn toward him with his face, as if he had a status with him."],[1674,"I asked Anas b. Malik about wiping over the leather socks. He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ used to wipe over them.'"],[1675,"May God have mercy on a servant who had a grievance of his brother against him concerning honor, wealth, or status, and he sought pardon from him before it was taken. There will be no dinar or dirham then. If he had good deeds, they will be taken from his good deeds; if he had no good deeds, some of the evil deeds of his companion will be placed upon his evil deeds."],[1676,"The Messenger of God ﷺ amputed for a quarter dinar."],[1677,"The slave has his food and clothing, and he is not burdened with work except what he can bear."],[1678,"There is no servant who asks for something while he has what suffices him, except that it will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches or gashes or a disfigurement on his face. It was said: 'O Messenger of God, what suffices him?' He said: 'Fifty dirhams.'"],[1679,"Prostration is on seven body parts: the hands, the feet, the knees, and the forehead."],[1680,"Raising the hands: when you see the House, on al-Safa and al-Marwah, at Arafah, at Jam' (Muzdalifah), when throwing the pebbles, and when the prayer is called."],[1681,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and taught him the times of prayer. Gabriel went forward, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was behind him, and the people were behind the Messenger of God ﷺ. He prayed Zuhr when the sun declined. Then he came to him when the shadow was equal to his height, and he did as he had done: Gabriel went forward, the Messenger of God ﷺ behind him, and the people behind the Messenger of God, and he prayed Asr. Then he came to him when the sun set, and he did as he had done: Gabriel went forward, the Messenger of God behind him, and the people behind the Messenger of God, and he prayed Maghrib. Then he came to him when the twilight disappeared, and he did as he had done: Gabriel went forward, the Messenger of God behind him, and the people behind the Messenger of God, and he prayed Isha. Then he came to him when the dawn broke, and he did as he had done: Gabriel went forward, the Messenger of God behind him, and the people behind the Messenger of God, and he prayed the morning prayer. Then he came to him the second day when a man's shadow was equal to his height, and he did as he had done the day before, and he prayed Zuhr. Then he came to him when a man's shadow became equal to his height, and he did as he had done the day before, and he prayed Asr. Then he came to him when the sun set, and he did as he had done the day before, and he prayed Maghrib. Then he came to him when the twilight disappeared, and he did as he had done the day before, and he prayed Isha. Then he said: 'Between these two prayers is the time.'"],[1682,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed one day wearing a striped cloak (namirah). He said to a man among his companions: 'Give me your striped cloak and take my striped cloak.' The man said: 'O Messenger of God, your striped cloak is better than my striped cloak.' He said: 'Yes, but there is a red thread in it, and I feared that I might look at it and it would tempt me.' And he confirmed it. He said: 'Yes.'"],[1683,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and the companions of the Messenger of God were Muhajirun because they abandoned the polytheists. And there were Muhajirun among the Ansar, because Madinah was a land of polytheism, so they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of al-Aqabah."],[1684,"We used to say during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ: Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman."],[1685,"We said: O Messenger of God, will we see our Lord, Mighty and Majestic? He said: Do you see the sun on a day with no clouds? We said: Yes. And do you see the moon on a night with no clouds? We said: Yes. He said: Then you will surely see your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, until one of you will dispute with his Lord, disputing. He will say: My servant, do you remember such-and-such a sin? He will say: My Lord, did You not forgive me? He will say: By My forgiveness you have reached this."],[1686,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him not bring his wife into the bathhouse. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table where wine is passed around."],[1687,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the thicket, I began to menstruate, so I slipped away to get my menstrual garments. The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed and said: Have you menstruated? I said: Yes. She said: The Prophet ﷺ used to kiss while fasting, and they used to bathe from a single vessel."],[1688,"When one of you defecates, let him wipe three times."],[1689,"The Prophet ﷺ sent out a raiding party, and they took spoils. Among them was a man who said: I am not one of them; I fell in love with a woman and followed her. Let me look at her once, then do with me what you will. They looked, and behold, she was a tall, dark woman. He said to her: Submit, Hubaysh, before life runs out. What do you think, if I followed you and caught up with you at Halba, or found you at al-Khawaniq, would it not be right for a lover to be rewarded who endured night journeys and the cords of travel? She said: Yes, may I be your ransom. So they brought him forward and struck his neck. Then the woman came and stood over him, and she gasped once or twice, then died. When they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him that, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Was there not among you a merciful man?"],[1690,"I was a young unmarried man, and I used to spend the night in the mosque. Whenever one of them saw a dream, he would bring it to the Messenger of God ﷺ to interpret it."],[1691,"When one of you follows a funeral procession, let him not sit until the bier is placed on the ground."],[1692,"Whoever drags his garments out of pride, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1693,"He asked Aisha about kissing for the fasting person. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to kiss while fasting, then she laughed."],[1694,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he saw me in a disheveled state. He said: Do you have any wealth? He said: Yes, all kinds of wealth God has given me. He said: If you have wealth, then let it be seen upon you."],[1695,"Indeed God, Mighty and Majestic, will question every shepherd about what He entrusted to him, whether he preserved it or neglected it."],[1696,"The accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise, and one Umrah to the next Umrah is an expiation for what is between them."],[1697,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ strike his right hand upon his left hand in the prayer."],[1698,"A thief was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Kill him.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, he only stole.” He said, “Cut off his hand.” So his hand was cut off. Then he was brought a second time, and he said, “Kill him.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, he only stole.” He said, “Cut off his hand.” Then he was brought a third time, and he said, “Kill him.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, he only stole.” He said, “Cut off his hand.” Then he was brought a fourth time, and he said, “Kill him.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, he only stole.” He said, “Cut off his hand.” Then he was brought a fifth time, and he said, “Kill him.” Jabir said, “So we took him away to a livestock pen, then we attacked him. He fell on his back, and we stoned him and killed him. Then we threw him into a well and cast stones upon him.”"],[1699,"This is the one for whom the Throne shook, and the gates of heaven were opened for him, and seventy thousand angels witnessed him. He was squeezed once, then released."],[1700,"Nothing after women was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than horses."],[1701,"I have been permitted to narrate about an angel from among the angels, one of the bearers of the Throne: between his earlobe and his shoulder is a distance of four hundred years’ journey."],[1702,"The Prophet ﷺ gouged out the eyes of those men of the ʿUrayna tribe only because they had gouged out the eyes of the shepherds."],[1703,"He forbade nabīdh made in earthenware jars."],[1704,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it in the rightful ways of its destruction, and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom, and he acts upon it and teaches it."],[1705,"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."],[1706,"A bad deed is one, or I forgive it. A good deed is ten, or I increase it. Whoever comes to Me with an earth-full of sins, but does not associate anything with Me, I will make it forgiveness for him. Whoever draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him an arm’s length. Whoever draws near to Me an arm’s length, I draw near to him a fathom. Whoever comes to Me walking, I come to him at speed."],[1707,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was saying, “They are the greatest losers, by the Lord of the Kaʿba.” I said, “Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Those who have the most wealth, except one who does with his wealth like this and like this. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no man dies leaving camels, cattle, or sheep whose zakāh he did not pay, except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection as large and fat as they ever were, goring him with their horns and trampling him with their hooves. Every time the last of them passes, the first of them returns, until judgment is passed among the people.”"],[1708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders and say, “Straighten your rows and do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Let those of you with intelligence and reason stand closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them.”"],[1709,"The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's belly for forty nights, then he becomes a clinging clot for the like of that, then he becomes a lump of flesh for the like of that. Then the angel comes to him and says: 'My Lord, male or female? Wretched or blessed? What is the provision? What is the lifespan?' So your Lord decrees and the angel writes."],[1710,"We were with Hudhayfah in the mosque when a man entered through the gates of Kindah and began praying a prayer without completing its bowing and prostration. Hudhayfah said: 'Since when have you been praying this prayer?' He said: 'Since forty years.' He said: 'You have not prayed since forty years, and if you were to die, you would die upon other than the natural disposition of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[1711,"Umar came to the Black Stone and touched it, and said: 'I know that you are a stone, and were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing you, I would not kiss you.'"],[1712,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."],[1713,"Mut'ah was mentioned to Abu Dharr, and he said: 'It was only a concession for us, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[1714,"A man from the People of the Book said: 'O Abu al-Qasim, you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink.' He said: 'Yes, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, one of them will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, intercourse, and desire.' He said: 'The one who eats will have need (to relieve himself)?' He said: 'The need of one of them is a sweat that exudes like the fragrance of musk, and his belly will become lean.'"],[1715,"When you are three, two should not hold secret counsel apart from the third, for that grieves him."],[1716,"Regarding the saying of Allah: 'And spend in the way of Allah and do not throw yourselves into destruction' [al-Baqarah 2:195], he said: 'It was revealed concerning spending.'"],[1717,"He entered ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah. That was mentioned to Umar, and he said: 'You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.'"],[1718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left neither a dinar nor a dirham, nor a sheep, nor a camel, and he made no bequest."],[1719,"Every prophet has an answered supplication, and I have stored away my supplication as intercession for my community."],[1720,"Be brief in prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need."],[1721,"The people of Yemen have come to you. They are softer in hearts and gentler in souls. Faith is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni, and hardness and coarseness of heart are among the camel-owners, the people of the East, in Rabi'ah and Mudar."],[1722,"Whoever kills himself with an iron weapon, his weapon will be in his hand, stabbing himself in the belly in the Fire, abiding therein forever. Whoever throws himself off a mountain will keep falling into the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever. Whoever drinks poison will keep drinking it in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever."],[1723,"When one of you prostrates, let him keep his posture straight and not spread his forearms like a dog spreads them."],[1724,"When one of you finishes his food, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies."],[1725,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapping it around himself."],[1726,"Some Bedouins from 'Uraynah came to the Prophet ﷺ, but they found Madinah unhealthy, until their complexions turned yellow and their bellies swelled. The Prophet ﷺ sent them to some milch camels of his and ordered them to drink from their milk and urine. They drank until they recovered, then they killed the herdsman and drove off the camels. The Prophet ﷺ sent after them, and they were brought back. He cut off their hands and feet on opposite sides and gouged out their eyes. Amir al-Mu'minin 'Abd al-Malik b. Marwan said to Anas, while he was narrating this hadith: \"Was it for disbelief or for a sin?\" He said: \"For disbelief.\" Then he said: \"This verse was revealed after he cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes: 'The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger...' (al-Ma'idah 5:33).\""],[1727,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever avoids them has safeguarded his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into them is likely to fall into major sins, like a shepherd grazing around a sanctuary, likely to trespass into it. Indeed, every king has a sanctuary, and Allah's sanctuary is His limits."],[1728,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made sacred for my tongue what lies between the two lava tracts of Madinah. Then Banu Harithah came, and he said: \"You have left the sanctuary.\" Then he looked and said: \"No, rather you are within it.\""],[1729,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ contracted Khaybar for half of what it produced of crops or dates. He used to give his wives every year one hundred wasqs: eighty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley."],[1730,"The head of disbelief is toward the East, and pride and arrogance are among the owners of camels and sheep, while tranquility and dignity are among the owners of goats."],[1731,"The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, while the believer eats in one intestine."],[1732,"The Prophet ﷺ assigned Khaybar on the basis of half share."],[1733,"There is no prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and none after ‘Asr until the sun sets."],[1734,"The Prophet ﷺ recited with them in Maghrib: “Those who disbelieved and hindered from the way of Allah.”"],[1735,"“Shall I tell you about your men in Paradise?” We said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “The Prophet is in Paradise, the truthful one is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn is in Paradise, and a man who visits his brother in a distant part of the city—he visits him only for Allah—is in Paradise. Shall I tell you about your women in Paradise?” We said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Every loving and fertile woman who, when she becomes angry or is mistreated, says, ‘Here is my hand in your hand; I shall not sleep until you are pleased.’”"],[1736,"Umm Ayman gifted the Prophet ﷺ a bird between two loaves of bread. The Prophet ﷺ came and said, “Do you have anything?” She brought him the bird, so he raised his hands and said, “O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me from this bird.” Then ‘Ali came, so I said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is busy; the Prophet ﷺ just entered a moment ago.” But the Prophet ﷺ cut something from the bird, then raised his hand and said, “O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me from this bird.” Then ‘Ali came, and the voice rose between me and him, so the Prophet ﷺ said, “Let him in, whoever he is,” and he entered. Then the Prophet ﷺ said, “O my Lord, my ally,” three times. So he ate with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they both finished."],[1737,"The Ansar came to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-‘Aqabah. He said, “Arise, O ‘Ali, and receive their pledge.” He said, “On what shall I pledge them, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “That Allah is obeyed and not disobeyed, and that you protect the Messenger of Allah, his family, and his offspring from what you protect yourselves and your children from.”"],[1738,"“O Allah, You know that no one of this Ummah worshipped You after its Prophet ﷺ before me. I worshipped You six years before anyone of this Ummah worshipped You.”"],[1739,"“One of you remains in prayer as long as he is waiting for the next prayer, and the angels continue to pray for one of you as long as he remains in his mosque, saying: ‘O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him,’ as long as he does not break his wudu.’ A man from Hadramawt said, ‘What is that breaking, O Abu Hurayrah?’ He said, ‘Allah is not shy of the truth: a silent or audible passing of wind.’”"],[1740,"He used to supplicate: “O Allah, benefit me with what You have taught me, and teach me what benefits me.”"],[1741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade urinating in flowing water."],[1742,"We said, “O Messenger of Allah, these pebbles that we throw every year—we think they decrease.” He said, “Whatever is accepted from them is raised, and were it not for that, you would see them like mountains.”"],[1743,"When the verse “If you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphans” was revealed, they feared the same concerning women, that they would not give them their due. So the verse “Then marry those that please you of women” up to His saying “That is more suitable that you may not be unjust” was revealed."],[1744,"A promise is a gift."],[1745,"Whoever attends the Friday prayer, washes and performs a full bath, then goes early and arrives first, then draws near to the imam, remains silent, and listens, will have for every step the reward of a year's fasting and praying."],[1746,"Visit occasionally and love will increase."],[1747,"We were commanded to perform a full bath on Friday."],[1748,"There are no days in which good deeds are more beloved to Allah than these ten days. It was said, \"Not even jihad in the path of Allah?\" He said, \"Not even jihad, except for a man who goes out with his life and wealth and returns with none of that.\""],[1749,"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not to flee, but we did not pledge allegiance to him to die."],[1750,"Every religion has a character, and the character of this religion is modesty."],[1751,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, 'And they intended what they did not attain'—he said: A man named al-Aswad intended to kill the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1752,"The witr prayer is not obligatory, but it is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1753,"In Paradise there is a rolling place of musk, like the rolling place of your animals in this world."],[1754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was concealed by a curtain with images on it. He tore it down and said: 'The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[1755,"There is no newborn born except that five verses from the Opening of the Book are written in the sutures of his head."],[1756,"Umm Kulthum came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the husband of Fatimah is better than my husband.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent for a while, then said: 'Your husband is loved by Allah and His Messenger, and he loves Allah and His Messenger. I will tell you more: if you enter Paradise and see his station, you will not see any of my companions surpassing him in rank.'"],[1757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a servant who commits a sin? He said: He is pardoned seventy times every day."],[1758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about coitus interruptus? He said: Do you create it? Do you provide for it? Leave it in its resting place."],[1759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the five prayers and said: Whoever guards them, they will be for him a light, a proof, and a salvation on the Day of Resurrection."],[1760,"Whoever fasts a day of Ramadan in quietness and silence, a house will be built for him in Paradise of green chrysolite or red ruby."],[1761,"My intimate friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I will never abandon until I meet him: fasting three days of every month, the two rak'ahs of Duha, and praying Witr before sleeping."],[1762,"My Ummah will remain upon the natural disposition as long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars appear."],[1763,"The people of Nahrawan are cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ."],[1764,"Allah does not disappoint a servant who stands in the middle of the night and begins Surah al-Baqarah and Al 'Imran. And what an excellent treasure for a man are al-Baqarah and Al 'Imran."],[1765,"The Prophet ﷺ used to fast until we would say, 'He will not break his fast,' and he would break his fast until we would say, 'He will not fast.' And most of his fasting was in Sha'ban."],[1766,"Umar said: 'Which of you will narrate to us a hadith he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about tribulation?' Hudhayfah said: 'I will narrate to you as he said.' Umar said: 'You are bold about it, so narrate.' Hudhayfah said: 'The tribulation of a man in his family, his wealth, his child, and his neighbor is expiated by prayer, fasting, enjoining good, and forbidding evil.' Umar said: 'I am not asking you about that. I ask you about the one that surges like the waves of the sea.' Hudhayfah said: 'There is no harm upon you from it, O Commander of the Believers. Between you and it is a closed door.' Umar said: 'Will it be opened or broken?' Hudhayfah said: 'It will be broken.' Umar said: 'Then it will not be closed until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1767,"People from 'Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They found Madinah unhealthy, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to go to the milch camels of charity so that they might drink from their milk. They drank until they became healthy, then they killed the herdsman and drove away the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent after them, and they were brought back. He cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes."],[1768,"This is the day of 'Ashura', so fast it. Whoever has already eaten, let him complete the rest of his day. And he sent to the people of the villages and the Ansar around Madinah, ordering them to fast the rest of their day."],[1769,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the times of prayer. He said: Pray with us these two days. He ordered Bilal when dawn broke to give the adhan, then ordered him and he gave the iqamah, and he prayed. Then he ordered him and he gave the adhan when the sun declined, then ordered him and he gave the iqamah and prayed. Then he ordered him and he gave the adhan for Asr while the sun was high, then ordered him and he gave the iqamah and prayed. Then he ordered him and he gave the adhan for Maghrib when the sun had set, then ordered him and he gave the iqamah and prayed. Then he ordered him when the twilight had disappeared and he gave the adhan for Isha, then ordered him and he gave the iqamah and prayed. Then on the next day, he ordered him and he gave the adhan for Fajr when dawn broke, then ordered him when it had become bright and he gave the iqamah and prayed. Then he ordered him and he gave the adhan for Zuhr when the shadow of everything became equal to it, then ordered him and he gave the iqamah and prayed. Then he ordered him when the shadow of everything became twice its length and he gave the adhan for Asr, then ordered him and he gave the iqamah and prayed. Then he ordered him and he gave the adhan for Maghrib when the sun had set, then ordered him and he gave the iqamah and prayed. Then he delayed Isha until close to a third of the night, then he said: \"What is between these two is a time.\""],[1770,"Indeed, the people of Illiyyin, one of them looks down upon Paradise and his face shines for them as the moon shines for the people of this world on the night of the full moon. And indeed, Abu Bakr and Umar are among them and have been blessed."],[1771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the muscle of my calf, below it, and said: \"This is the place of the lower garment. If you refuse, then lower than that. If you refuse, then the lower garment has no right to the ankles.\""],[1772,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[1773,"Two men among the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, one of them used to hasten the prayer and the breaking of the fast, and the other used to delay it. She said: Which of them is the one who hastens the prayer and the breaking of the fast? We said: Ibn Mas'ud. She said: \"Thus was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do.\""],[1774,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother made a month's fast obligatory upon herself, and she died without completing it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you think that if she had a debt, you would pay it?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Then Allah's debt is more deserving of being paid.\""],[1775,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, but you fast continuously. He said: \"You are not like me. My Lord feeds me and gives me drink.\""],[1776,"Marry, O young men, for it is more effective in lowering the gaze and guarding chastity. And whoever cannot, then let him fast, for it is a shield for him."],[1777,"He used to kiss while fasting."],[1778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while fasting, between Makkah and Madinah."],[1779,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I broke my fast one day in Ramadan deliberately and had intercourse with my wife during it. He said: \"Free a slave.\" He said: I cannot find one. He said: \"Sacrifice a camel.\" He said: I cannot find one. He said: \"Give in charity twenty sa's of dates, or nineteen, or twenty-one.\" He said: I cannot find it. Then a basket containing twenty sa's of dates was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Give this in charity.\" He said: There is no household in Madinah more in need of it than us. He said: \"Then feed it to your family.\""],[1780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me wearing two garments dyed with safflower, and said: \"Did your mother command you to do this?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then wash them.\""],[1781,"Whoever fasts three days of a sacred month: Thursday, Friday, and Saturday, the worship of two years will be written for him."],[1782,"The Messenger of God ﷺ drank while standing."],[1783,"Ali narrated a hadith, and a man called him a liar. Ali said: 'I will pray against you if you have spoken falsely.' He said: 'Pray.' So he prayed against him, and he did not move until his sight went away."],[1784,"Gabriel taught me to recite on one mode, and I kept requesting more from him and he increased me until it reached seven modes."],[1785,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in the afternoon prayer one day, and he stood up in the two rak'ahs, then did not sit until he completed his prayer, then he prostrated two prostrations while sitting."],[1786,"He forbade temporary marriage (mut'ah)."],[1787,"There is no obligatory charity on horses and slaves."],[1788,"The letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ to the People of the Book was: 'O People of the Book, come to a word that is equitable between us and you' to the end of the verse."],[1789,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died in my house, on my day, and between my chest and my thigh, and he mixed his saliva with mine. She said: 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr entered with a toothstick in his hand. The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at it, and I thought that he liked to use it for cleaning his teeth. I took it, softened it, then gave it to him, and he used it to clean his teeth. I never saw a mouth more beautiful than his. Then he wanted to hand it to me, but his hand failed. When I saw that, I took it from him."],[1790,"There was a woman in Jiyad called Umm Mahzul, and she used to commit fornication. She stipulated for whoever married her that she would provide for his expenses. A man asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to marry her, and the Messenger of God ﷺ recited: 'The fornicator marries not except a fornicatress' to the end of the verse."],[1791,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mixing dates and raisins."],[1792,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and bore the testimony of truth. He said: 'O Wahshi, sit and tell me how you killed Hamzah.' So I told him, and he said: 'Hide your face from me, so that I do not see you.'"],[1793,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began the takbir in prayer, he raised his hands when saying the takbir until they were level with his shoulders. Then when he said the takbir and bowed, he did the same. Then when he said, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' he did the same, and he said, 'Our Lord, to You belongs all praise.' He did not do that when prostrating, nor when rising from prostration."],[1794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Amr b. Jud'an: 'When you buy sandals, choose good ones, and when you buy a garment, choose a good one.'"],[1795,"He is not one of us who turns a wife against her husband, and he is not one of us who turns a slave against his master."],[1796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him and Aws b. al-Hadathan, and he called out: 'None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking.'"],[1797,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on a khumrah (small mat)."],[1798,"We are not inherited from; what we leave behind is charity."],[1799,"The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, while the believer eats in one intestine."],[1800,"Every qunut (obedience) in the Quran is obedience."],[1801,"We were in the mosque when 'Ali came out to us at the end of the night and said: 'Where is the one asking about the witr?' We gathered around him, and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed witr at the beginning of the night, then he performed witr in its middle, then he performed witr at this hour. And he passed away while performing witr at this hour.'"],[1802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about al-Hasan b. 'Ali: 'Indeed this son of mine is a master, and Allah will reconcile through him two great factions of the Muslims.'"],[1803,"Two types of the people of Hell I have not yet seen: women who are clothed yet naked, inclined and inclining, on their heads like the humps of bukht camels, and people with whips like the tails of cattle. They will not enter Paradise, nor find its fragrance."],[1804,"He entered ihram for Hajj in Dhul-Qa'dah, and his head became infested with lice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him while he was lighting a fire under his pot, and said: 'It seems the vermin of your head are bothering you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Shave your head, and offer a sacrificial animal.' I said: 'I cannot find a sacrificial animal.' He said: 'Then feed six poor people.' He said: 'I cannot find (the means).' He said: 'Then fast three days.' He said: 'I shaved and fasted three days.'"],[1805,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from al-Ta'if until, when he was in Batn Nakhla, the people surrounded him and crowded around him. He passed by a tree branch, and it caught on his cloak, and his cloak remained [snagged]. He turned to us with his face as if it were a piece of the moon, and as if his neck were rivulets of gold, and said: 'O people, let me have my cloak. Do you fear that I be miserly? By the One in whose hand is my soul, if I had with me as many livestock as the trees of Awtas, red camels, I would distribute them among you.'"],[1806,"The believer is not a defamer, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed."],[1807,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ smeared with khaluq, wearing patched garments, having entered ihram for 'umrah. He said: 'How do you command me, O Messenger of Allah, regarding my 'umrah?' Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'And complete the Hajj and 'Umrah for Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Where is the one asking about 'umrah?' He said: 'I am he.' He said: 'Cast off your clothes, bathe, and cleanse yourself as much as you are able; and whatever you would do in your Hajj, do it in your 'umrah.'"],[1808,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived at the conquest, the conquest of Makkah, he alighted at the upper part of Makkah, and he prayed eight rak'ahs. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer?' He said: 'The Duha prayer.'"],[1809,"I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from this—and she pointed to a vessel placed like a sa'—we would both draw from it together, and I would pour water over my head three times with my hands, and I would not undo any of my hair."],[1810,"The 'aqiqah for a boy is two equivalent sheep, and for a girl one sheep."],[1811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud and the takbir just as he taught us a surah from the Quran."],[1812,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram. I said: 'Did he marry her in Makkah?' He said: 'No, but he married her on part of the road.'"],[1813,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, I braid my hair tightly; should I undo it when I am in a state of janabah?' He said: 'It is sufficient for you to take three handfuls of water with your hand and pour them over your head, then wash the rest of your body, and you will then be purified.'"],[1814,"When one of you prays and has nothing in front of him to screen him, and one of you wants to pass in front of him, let him prevent him; and if he refuses, let him fight him."],[1815,"I prayed behind Zayd b. Arqam over a funeral, and he said the takbir five times. Then 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla walked up to him, took hold of his hand, and said: 'Have you forgotten?' He said: 'No, but I prayed behind my close friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ, and he said the takbir five times.'"],[1816,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade me from sleeping except on witr."],[1817,"I saw Abu Bakr al-Siddiq dyeing with henna and katam. 'Umar did not dye. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever grows a gray hair for the sake of Allah, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1818,"I asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: Who are the people of the house from whom Allah has removed impurity and purified them with a thorough purification? He counted them on his hand, five: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn. Abu Sa'id said: In the house of Umm Salamah this verse was revealed."],[1819,"The first of my Ummah for whom I will intercede are the people of Madinah, then the people of Makkah, then the people of al-Ta'if."],[1820,"Whoever wakes up healthy in his body, secure in his dwelling, with his daily sustenance, it is as if the world has been gathered for him."],[1821,"When Kisra dies, there will be no Kisra after him. When Qaysar dies, there will be no Qaysar after him. By the One in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will certainly be spent in the way of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."],[1822,"The one who prays before sunrise and before sunset will never enter the Fire."],[1823,"When we went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we would not remove our leather socks for three days and their nights, not for defecation, nor urination, nor sleep, except for major impurity."],[1824,"She wanted to give as charity some rotten meat, and the Prophet ﷺ said to her: 'Would you give in charity what you would not eat?'"],[1825,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade seeking out the faults of women."],[1826,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the morning prayer and said: 'Was so-and-so present?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Is so-and-so present?' They said: 'No.' Then he said: 'These two prayers are the heaviest of prayers upon the hypocrites. If they knew what was in them, they would come to them even if they had to crawl. The first row is like the row of the angels, and if you knew its virtue, you would race to it. A man's prayer with another man is purer than his prayer alone, and his prayer with two men is purer than his prayer with one man. The more people there are, the more beloved it is to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic.'"],[1827,"Whoever sends blessings upon me in a book, the angels will continue to seek forgiveness for him as long as my name is in that book."],[1828,"Regarding the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: 'And when his Lord revealed Himself to the mountain, He made it collapse to dust' (Quran 7:143), the Prophet ﷺ indicated with his little finger, saying: 'From His light He made it collapse.'"],[1829,"There is no nation except that some of it will be in Paradise and some of it in the Fire, except my nation, for it will be in Paradise."],[1830,"When it was the day of Umm Habibah with the Prophet ﷺ, someone knocked on the door. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'See who this is.' They said: 'Mu'awiyah.' He said: 'Give him permission to enter.' He entered, and on his ear was a pen of his with which he writes. He said: 'What is this pen on your ear, O Mu'awiyah?' He said: 'A pen I have prepared for Allah and His Messenger.' He said: 'May Allah reward you well on behalf of your Prophet. By Allah, I did not employ you as a scribe except by revelation from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and I do nothing, small or great, except by revelation from Allah, Mighty and Majestic. How will you be when Allah has clothed you with a garment?'—meaning the caliphate. Umm Habibah stood up and sat before him, and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will Allah clothe my brother with a garment?' He said: 'Yes, but in it there are flaws, and flaws, and flaws.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, then supplicate for him.' He said: 'O Allah, guide him with guidance, keep him away from ruin, and forgive him in the Hereafter and in the first (life).'"],[1831,"Indeed Musa said: 'O Lord, tell me who is the most honorable of Your creation to You.' He said: 'The one who hastens to My desire as an eagle hastens to its desire, and the one who is devoted to My righteous servants as a child is devoted to people, and the one who becomes angry when My sacred limits are violated as a tiger is angry for itself, for when a tiger is angry it does not care whether people are few or many.'"],[1832,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on the expedition to Tabuk, and he went to relieve himself. I poured water for him, and he washed his face three times, and his hands three times, and wiped his head, then wiped over his leather socks."],[1833,"In the time of the Prophet ﷺ, a sinking of the earth was mentioned toward the east. Some people said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will the earth swallow a land in which there are Muslims?' He said: 'Yes, if the majority of its inhabitants are wicked.'"],[1834,"Two men went out on a journey, and the prayer time came upon them while they had no water. They performed tayammum with clean earth and prayed. Then they found water. One of them repeated the prayer, and the other did not repeat it. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said to the one who did not repeat: 'You have acted according to the Sunnah, and your prayer sufficed you.' And he said to the one who performed ablution and repeated: 'You have two rewards.'"],[1835,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'like a niche'—he said: 'the inner being of Muhammad ﷺ.' And 'the glass' is 'his heart,' and 'the lamp' is 'the light that is in his heart. It is lit from a blessed tree'—the tree is Ibrahim, 'an olive, neither eastern nor western'—'neither Jew nor Christian.' Then he recited: 'Ibrahim was neither a Jew nor a Christian, but he was a hanif, a Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists.'"],[1836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to bring a woman to her husband when she had not received any of her dowry."],[1837,"When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created the intellect, He said to it: 'Stand,' and it stood. Then He said to it: 'Turn back,' and it turned back. Then He said to it: 'Sit,' and it sat. He said: 'By My might, I have not created anything better than you, nor more noble than you, nor more excellent than you, nor more beautiful. Through you I take, and through you I give, and through you I make known, and through you I punish, and through you is reward, and upon you is punishment.'"],[1838,"Whoever curses any one of my Companions, upon him is the curse of Allah."],[1839,"Whoever drinks from a silver vessel, he only causes fire to gurgle in his belly."],[1840,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he disliked three tribes: Thaqif, Banu Hanifah, and Banu Umayyah."],[1841,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sneezed, he would cover his face."],[1842,"If one of you touches his private part with his hand, with no barrier between them, then ablution becomes obligatory for him."],[1843,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say not once, not twice, not three times, until it reached ten times: Any man who marries a woman with a small or large dowry, but has no intention of fulfilling her due right, deceives her; if he dies without fulfilling her due right, he will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection as an adulterer. And any man who takes on a debt not intending to repay its owner his due right, deceives him until he takes his wealth; if he dies without repaying it, he will meet Allah as a thief."],[1844,"The things I fear most for my community are seeking rain by the stars, the tyranny of rulers, and denying divine decree."],[1845,"Umm Sulaym sent me with fresh dates to the Prophet ﷺ on a plate, when the date palms first ripened. He said: I entered upon him and placed it before him, and he ate some of it. Then he took my hand and we went out. He had recently married Zaynab bt. Jahsh. He passed by some of his wives, and with them were men conversing. They congratulated him, and the people congratulated him, saying: 'Praise be to Allah who has gladdened your eye, O Messenger of Allah.' He continued until he came to Aisha, and there were two men with her. He disliked that, and when he disliked something it was known in his face. So I went to Umm Sulaym and informed her. Abu Talha said: 'If what your son says is true, something will surely happen.' When evening came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, ascended the pulpit, and recited this verse: 'O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you...' the entire verse."],[1846,"Some people mentioned pride in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: 'O Prophet of Allah, I love beauty, even in the strap of my whip and the lace of my sandal. Do you fear anything for me in that?' He said: 'No.' We said: 'Then what is pride?' He said: 'Pride is rejecting truth and looking down on people.'"],[1847,"The Prophet ﷺ heard disputants at his door, so he went out to them and said: 'O Allah, I am only a human being. Disputants come to me, and perhaps one of them is more eloquent in his argument than another, so I judge in his favor and think he is truthful. Whatever I judge in his favor from a Muslim's right, it is only a piece of the Fire, so let him take it or leave it.'"],[1848,"The believer is fragile and patching up; blessed is he who dies while patching up."],[1849,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, even the size of a sand-grouse's nest, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will build for him a house in Paradise."],[1850,"Regarding wiping over the leather socks: three days for the traveler, and for the resident one day until night."],[1851,"The first thing a servant will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection is prayer. If it is sound, then the rest of his deeds will be sound; if it is corrupt, then the rest of his deeds will be corrupt."],[1852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated on Thursday evening, saying: 'O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar b. al-Khattab or Amr b. Hisham.' Umar embraced Islam on Friday morning."],[1853,"A woman was divorced during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and she remained twenty nights then gave birth. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, and he said: 'Take charge of your own affair.'"],[1854,"I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for four qualities for my community, and He granted me three and withheld one. I asked Him that my community should not apostatize all at once, and He granted me that. I asked Him that He should not set an enemy over them from other than themselves, and He granted me that. I asked Him that He should not punish them with what He punished the nations before them, and He granted me that. I asked Him that He should not make their might between themselves, and He withheld it from me."],[1855,"Three people God will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them, and for them is a painful punishment: a man who swears about merchandise that he was given more for it than he was, and he is lying; a man who swears a false oath after the afternoon prayer to seize thereby the property of a Muslim man; and a man who withholds surplus water, for God, Mighty and Majestic, will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'Today I withhold from you My surplus as you withheld surplus of what...'"],[1856,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from the battle of Hunayn, and was on part of the road, the people asked him and pressed upon him, and his she-camel became frightened. A samura tree caught his cloak, so the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Return my cloak to me. Do you fear stinginess from me? By God, if God granted you as many camels as the number of samura trees of Tihama, I would distribute them among you, and you would not find me stingy, nor cowardly, nor a liar.' Then when it came to dividing the fifth, a man stood up asking him to consider lawful a needle or thread. He said: 'Return the thread and the needle, for theft from the spoils is disgrace, fire, and shame upon its people on the Day of Resurrection.' Then he picked up a hair from the top of a camel's hump and said: 'I have nothing from what God has granted you as spoils, not even the like of this, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you.'"],[1857,"What I fear most for my community after me is a man who interprets the Qur'an and places it in other than its proper places, and a man who thinks he is more entitled to this matter than others."],[1858,"When it was revealed: 'Who is it that will lend God a good loan?' Ibn al-Dahdah said: 'Does our Lord ask us for a loan from our wealth, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I have two gardens, one in the highland and the other in the lowland. I have lent the better of them to my Lord.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'It is for the orphan who is with you.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Many a cluster of dates in Paradise belongs to Ibn al-Dahdah, hanging low.'"],[1859,"The believer is fragile and patching up; blessed is he who dies while patching up."],[1860,"Three people will be given their reward twice: a man from the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, then lived to see the Prophet ﷺ and believed in him; a man who had a slave woman, freed her, and married her; and a slave who feared God and obeyed his masters."],[1861,"Do not lift the stick from your family, and make them fear God, Mighty and Majestic."],[1862,"He forbade muhaqala, muzabana, and mulamasa."],[1863,"He forbade shighar."],[1864,"The cry of the newborn when he is born is a touch from Satan."],[1865,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the Day of Conquest with a black turban on his head."],[1866,"Allah will grasp the earth with His Hand and the heavens in His Right Hand, then say: 'I am the King.'"],[1867,"The example of the companion of the Qur'an, if he commits to it and rises with it during his night, is like tied camels: if their owner ties them, he holds them; but if he releases them, they run loose."],[1868,"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water.\" Ibn Umar used to say: \"O Allah, remove the affliction from us."],[1869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed five rak'ahs, then prostrated twice while sitting."],[1870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn with two rams."],[1871,"My Ummah is a community that is shown mercy, forgiven for them: they enter their graves with their sins, and come out of their graves with no sins upon them, their sins being expiated by the believers seeking forgiveness for them."],[1872,"When dinner is served and the call to prayer is given, begin with dinner and do not rush away from your dinner."],[1873,"Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan.\" Al-Shafi'i added in his narration: \"Ibn Umm Maktum would not call the adhan until it was said to him: 'It is morning, it is morning.'"],[1874,"Consult women regarding their own marriages."],[1875,"When it is the seventh day, shed blood on his behalf, remove the harm from him, and name him."],[1876,"We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast, to delay our pre-dawn meal, and to place our right hands over our left hands in prayer."],[1877,"When you see a servant granted indifference to this world and fewness of speech, draw near to him, for he is endowed with wisdom."],[1878,"None of you should say: 'O Allah, prompt me with my proof,' for the disbeliever is prompted with his proof, but let him say: 'O Allah, [grant me] the proof of faith at the time of death.'"],[1879,"Shall I inform you of the most wretched of the wretched?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"One upon whom the poverty of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter are combined.\""],[1880,"A person is attacked [by jinn] in four situations: when he sleeps alone, when he sleeps on his back, when he sleeps in a saffron-dyed blanket, and when he bathes in open land. Whoever can avoid bathing in open land [should do so], and if he must, let him draw a line [around himself]."],[1881,"O Allah, bless us in our Syria and in our Yemen. A man said, \"And in our east, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"O Allah, bless us in our Syria and in our Yemen.\" The man said, \"And in our east, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"O Allah, bless us in our Syria and Yemen, for from there the horn of Satan rises, and there is nine-tenths of disbelief, and there is the incurable disease.\""],[1882,"\"If I had this world and all it contains [I would give it] for this verse: 'O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.'\" A man said to him, \"Even one who associated others [with Allah]?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Except one who associated others [with Allah].\""],[1883,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two horned, black-and-white rams, one on behalf of himself and his household, and the other on behalf of himself and those of his community who had not sacrificed."],[1884,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, takes the scholars by taking [them], and takes knowledge with them. Then there arise young people who leap upon one another like a wild ass upon a wild ass, and the old man among them is deemed weak."],[1885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of 'araya [unpicked dates] by estimating their quantity."],[1886,"Good deeds like mountains will follow a man on the Day of Resurrection, and he will say, 'How is this?' It will be said, 'By your child's seeking forgiveness for you.'"],[1887,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray in a single garment."],[1888,"Satan comes to one of you and says, 'Who created the sky?' He says, 'Allah.' Then he says, 'Who created the earth?' He says, 'Allah.' Then he says, 'Who created Allah?' If any of you experiences that, let him say, 'I believe in Allah and His Messenger.'"],[1889,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1890,"Two men disputed over a palm tree. The Messenger of God ﷺ cut a frond from its fronds and found its length to be five cubits, and he made that its protected zone."],[1891,"A gift of grapes from al-Ta'if was given to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He gave me a bunch and said, 'Take it to your mother,' but I ate it on the way. He said, 'What happened to the bunch?' I said, 'I ate it.' So he named me Ghudar. He said: Al-Nu'man used to say on his pulpit, 'Indeed, the calamity, the whole calamity, is that you do evil deeds in evil oaths.'"],[1892,"When the believer falls ill, that purifies him just as the bellows removes the dross of iron."],[1893,"Gabriel ﷺ came to me wearing green garments with pearls hanging from them."],[1894,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite: 'Does he think that his wealth will make him immortal?'"],[1895,"He would wake up junub from intercourse, not from a wet dream."],[1896,"He wiped over the leather socks."],[1897,"Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it. When you come to it, eat from its trees, even from its thorny trees."],[1898,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to travel with the Qur'an to the land of the enemy, fearing that the enemy might get hold of it."],[1899,"When one of you dies, his seat is shown to him morning and evening. If he is one of the people of Paradise, then from the people of Paradise, and if he is one of the people of the Fire, then from the people of the Fire. It is said, 'This is your seat until God resurrects you to it.'"],[1900,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three days, except for her husband."],[1901,"Let none of you milk anyone's livestock without his permission. Would any of you like his storeroom to be approached, his cabinet broken open, and his food taken out? Their livestock's udders only store their food for them, so let no one milk anyone's livestock except by his command."],[1902,"Amputation is for a quarter dinar and above."],[1903,"The dust in the path of God and the smoke of Hell will never combine in the belly of a Muslim man."],[1904,"We have not obtained anything from this world of yours except your women."],[1905,"I used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of God ﷺ. When revelation came down upon him, he was seized by intense distress and sweated profusely like pearls, then it was relieved from him. I would enter upon him with a piece of shoulder blade or a fragment and write while he dictated to me. I would not finish until my leg was about to break from the weight of the Quran, and until I said: I will never walk on my leg again. When I finished, he said: 'Read it,' and I would read it. If there was an omission in it, he would correct it, then I would go out with it to the people."],[1906,"Perform ablution from what fire has touched."],[1907,"I said: O Messenger of God, tell me something I can hold fast to. He said: Control this for yourself, and he pointed to his tongue."],[1908,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a drinker while he was at Khaybar. He threw dust in his face, then commanded his companions, and they struck him with their sandals and whatever they had in their hands, until he said to them: 'Be gentle.' So they were gentle. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed away, and that was his sunnah. Then Abu Bakr flogged for wine forty lashes. Then Umar flogged forty lashes at the beginning of his rule, then he flogged eighty at the end of his caliphate. Then Uthman flogged the prescribed punishment of forty, then Mu'awiyah the prescribed punishment of forty."],[1909,"The keys of the unseen are five, then he recited this verse: 'Indeed, God has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs. No soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, God is All-Knowing, All-Aware.'"],[1910,"His father wrote to him: Meet Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah and ask her how the Messenger of God ﷺ ruled for her. He said: Malik b. Aws b. al-Hadathan informed me that Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah informed him that her husband Sa'd b. Khawlah died while she was in Makkah with the Messenger of God ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and she was pregnant. She did not wait long after him before she gave birth. Abu al-Sanabil b. Ba'kak b. al-Sabbaq of Banu 'Abd al-Dar proposed to her, but she refused to marry him. He said: You are not lawful until you observe the longer of the two terms. She sought the ruling of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he permitted her to marry."],[1911,"Horses: goodness is tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."],[1912,"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs, God will build for him a house in Paradise: four before Zuhr, two after it, two before Asr, and two before Fajr."],[1913,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on a red camel."],[1914,"I was with Ibn Abbas, and a man came to him and said: O Abu Abbas, what do you say about me? He replied: What could I possibly say about you? The man said: I am an official who works with a pen. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: On the Day of Resurrection, the holder of the pen will be brought in a coffin of fire, locked with locks of fire. If he used it in obedience to Allah and seeking His pleasure, the coffin will be opened for him, but if he used it in disobedience to Allah, the coffin will plunge with him for seventy autumns, until the pen maker and the ink-pot maker."],[1915,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: May a fasting person kiss? He said to him: Ask this one, meaning Umm Salamah. She informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven your past and future sins. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Indeed, I am the most pious of you toward Allah and the most knowledgeable of you of His limits."],[1916,"On the hump of every camel there is a devil, so when you ride them, glorify Allah, and do not neglect your needs."],[1917,"Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers."],[1918,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to equip an army. He looked at al-Abbas and said: This is al-Abbas, the uncle of your Prophet, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most maintaining of ties."],[1919,"Habib ibn Maslamah came to Qays ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah during the first fitnah while he was on a horse, and he moved back in the saddle for him. He said: Ride. But Habib refused to ride. Qays said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The owner of the mount is more entitled to its front. Habib said: I am not ignorant of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, but I fear for you."],[1920,"The one who deliberately passes in front of a man while he is praying will wish on the Day of Resurrection that he were a dry tree."],[1921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people during the Farewell Pilgrimage. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, take your rites of pilgrimage from me, for I do not know; perhaps I will not perform Hajj after this year of mine."],[1922,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1923,"May Allah curse those who come to women in their anuses."],[1924,"I am amazed at a people who sought this knowledge, until when they attained some of it, they became tutors to the sons of kings."],[1925,"Whoever remains silent is saved."],[1926,"Whoever wishes to be safe, let him adhere to silence."],[1927,"Whoever teaches his son the Qur'an by looking at it, Allah will forgive his previous and future sins; and whoever teaches it to him by heart, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection in the form of the full moon, and it will be said to his son: Recite. Every time he recites a verse, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will raise the father a degree by it, until he reaches the end of what he has memorized of the Qur'an."],[1928,"When the middle of Sha'ban comes, then break the fast."],[1929,"He used to teach 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf to read, and he mentioned the lengthy hadith of the Saqifah, and in it he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not exaggerate in praising me as the Christians exaggerated in praising 'Isa; I am only Allah's servant and His Messenger, so say: Allah's servant and His Messenger. And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned, and we stoned with him."],[1930,"'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas, when he prayed over funerals as imam, would say takbir, then recite the Opening of the Book, then pray upon the Prophet ﷺ, then say takbir, then depart."],[1931,"He forbade a man from praying in trousers without anything else on him."],[1932,"I entered upon Anas b. Malik in his tent during the caliphate of 'Abd al-Malik and said to him: I hope Allah has kept you back so that you may be a witness over this community. He said: I bear witness that they have gone to bed and risen opposing those before them, because they pray, but there is delay in the prayer."],[1933,"When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him. Then he fell silent, and they said: In what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He employs him in a righteous deed before he dies."],[1934,"Every good deed the son of Adam performs is multiplied tenfold, up to seven hundred times, except fasting; it is for Me, and I reward it."],[1935,"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said to me: Shall I not teach you a word the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me? I said: Yes, uncle. He said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with me, he said: Shall I not teach you a word from the treasure of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom. He said: Say often: There is no might and no power except with Allah."],[1936,"Witr is obligatory upon every Muslim; whoever is able to perform witr with five, let him do so; whoever is not able to perform witr with five, let him do so with three; whoever is not able to do so with three, let him do so with one; whoever is not able to do so with one, let him gesture."],[1937,"He met ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, took him by the hand and squeezed it. ʿUmar was a strong man, so he said, “Release my hand, O lock of tribulation.” ʿUmar said, “And what is the lock of tribulation?” He said, “I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ one day while he was sitting with people gathered around him, and I sat at the back of them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, ‘No tribulation will afflict you as long as this one is among you.’”"],[1938,"If you had seen us with our Prophet ﷺ, you would have thought that our smell was the smell of sheep. Our clothing was wool, and our food was the two black things: water and dates."],[1939,"O people, I forbid you from false hair. He came with a black cloth and threw it before them and said, “It is this which a woman puts on her head.”"],[1940,"God, Blessed and Exalted, supports this religion with people who have no share of virtue."],[1941,"The Prophet ﷺ gave them a sermon and said, “The ʿumrā is permissible.”"],[1942,"Do not mix raisins and dates, nor unripe dates and dates."],[1943,"Whoever relieves a hardship of this world for his brother, God will relieve a hardship of the Hereafter for him. God helps a servant as long as the servant helps his brother."],[1944,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Bilāl, “When you give the call to prayer, recite it slowly; and when you give the iqāma, say it quickly. Leave between your call and your iqāma enough time for the eater to finish eating, the drinker to finish drinking, and the one in need to relieve himself if he enters to do so. And do not stand until you see me.”"],[1945,"The people who had apostatized from Asad and Ghaṭafān came to Abū Bakr after the Messenger of God ﷺ, asking him for peace. He said, “On condition that we take from you the ring and the weapon, and you are left to follow the tails of cattle until God, Mighty and Majestic, shows the successor of His Prophet ﷺ and the believers a course of action by which they may excuse you. And you testify that our slain are in Paradise and your slain are in Hell. And you pay blood money for our slain, and we do not pay blood money for your slain.” ʿUmar said, “O successor of the Messenger of God, the matter is as you said, except that our slain were killed in the path of God and have no blood money.”"],[1946,"A woman from the wives of al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī prepared food in some of his land, and he ate. Then he had the food removed. A client of his came, and he called for the food, but the man said, “O Abū ʿAbd Allāh, I do not want it.” He said, “Why?” He said, “We ate a little while ago at ʿUbayd Allāh b. al-ʿAbbās’s.” Al-Ḥusayn said, “His father was the chief of Quraysh. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, ‘O Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, feed others.’”"],[1947,"A servant will not believe until he believes in predestination, its good and its evil, and knows that what befell him would not have missed him, and what missed him would not have befallen him."],[1948,"The Prophet ﷺ gave permission for nabīdh in earthenware jars after he had forbidden it."],[1949,"He came with a water-skin from the Prophet ﷺ, in which the Prophet ﷺ had washed his face, rinsed his mouth, spat into the water, and washed his hands and forearms. Then he filled the water-skin and said: 'Do not come to any water except that you fill the water-skin with what remains in it. When you reach your land, sprinkle that spot with it and take it as a mosque.' He said: So they took it."],[1950,"When 'Abd al-Rahman b. Zayd b. al-Khattab died, they wanted to take him out at night. Ibn 'Umar said: 'If only you would delay him until morning, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"It rises with the two horns of a devil.\"'"],[1951,"\"Shall I inform you of the best of the Ummah after its Prophet?\" I said: \"Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom.\" He said: \"Abu Bakr.\" Then he said: \"O Abu Juhayfah, shall I inform you of the best of the Ummah after Abu Bakr?\" I said: \"Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom.\" He said: \"'Umar b. al-Khattab.\" He said: \"O Abu Juhayfah, shall I inform you of the best of them after 'Umar?\" I said: \"Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom.\" He said: \"Another man,\" but he did not name him."],[1952,"A man who had killed someone was brought to him, and he handed the killer over to the victim's guardian to execute him. When he was taken away with a rope around his neck, the Prophet ﷺ said to his companions: \"The killer and the killed are in the Fire.\" A man went and mentioned to the guardian what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said, so he released him. I saw him when he was released, walking away, dragging his rope."],[1953,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa'."],[1954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up one night, raised his head to the sky, and began turning his gaze, saying: \"Glory be to Allah! What trials have been sent down tonight, and what treasures have been opened? Wake the occupants of the rooms, for many a woman clothed in this world will be naked on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1955,"Protect your wealth with zakah, treat your sick with charity, and prepare for affliction with supplication."],[1956,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave after the deceased had been buried."],[1957,"Nothing interrupts the prayer except hadath, and I am not ashamed to tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not ashamed of: hadath is passing wind or breaking wind."],[1958,"'Ali adjured the people: \"Who heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of Ghadir Khumm: 'Do you not know that I am closer to the believers than their own selves?'\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then whoever I am his mawla, 'Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\" Twelve men stood up and testified to that."],[1959,"About a man who buys a sacrificial animal or a camel, then sells it and buys a fatter one—he mentioned a concession."],[1960,"When you go to your bed, recite: 'Say: O disbelievers' to its end, for it is a disavowal of polytheism."],[1961,"When the Prophet ﷺ did not go on a military expedition, he would give his weapons to Ali or Usamah."],[1962,"He used to warm himself with it after the ritual bath."],[1963,"“And warn your closest kindred” (26:214). He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered thirty men over a bowl of milk, and most of them would eat a young goat, yet they ate until they were full and drank until they were quenched."],[1964,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ carrying al-Hasan b. Ali on his shoulder, saying: “O Allah, I love Hasan, so love him.”"],[1965,"On the day of Awtas, he said: “A pregnant woman is not to be had intercourse with until she gives birth, nor a non-pregnant one until she menstruates once.”"],[1966,"“Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar” (108:1). He said: “A river in Paradise, hollow, with vessels of gold and silver, known only to Allah.”"],[1967,"You will be the radiant and marked ones on the Day of Resurrection from the traces of ablution. So whoever of you can extend his radiance, let him do so."],[1968,"The son of Adam has never encountered anything since Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created him more severe than death. Then he said: “Indeed death is easier than what comes after it. They will encounter such terror on that day that sweat will bridle them, until if ships were launched in it, they would sail.”"],[1969,"A man came to Ibn Masʿud and said: “I recited the Mufassal in one rakʿah.” ʿAbdullah said: “Rather, you recited it hastily like the recitation of poetry, or like the scattering of dry dates. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do as you did. He used to recite the paired chapters: al-Rahman and al-Najm in one rakʿah, with twenty surahs from the Mufassal, according to the arrangement of ʿAbdullah, the last of them being ‘When the sun is wrapped up’ and al-Dukhan.”"],[1970,"ʿAʾishah surpasses women as tharid surpasses all other food."],[1971,"Ali flogged Shuraḥah on Thursday and stoned her on Friday, and said: “I flogged her according to the Book of Allah, and stoned her according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah.”"],[1972,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray while I was lying crosswise in front of him."],[1973,"‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud used to stand up every Thursday evening, and I did not hear him in any evening but that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — more than once. I looked at him, and he was leaning on a staff, and I saw the staff shaking."],[1974,"‘Umar b. al-Khattab escorted us when we set out for Kufah on foot, leading a donkey or a she-donkey. We said: O Commander of the Faithful, we adjure you by Allah, do ride. But he refused, until we had gone three or four miles. Then some of us said to one another: You have made things hard for the Commander of the Faithful. So we dismounted. One of them said: Why do you think I walked with you to this place? They said: You intended thereby to honor us and safeguard the Ansar. He said: That is so, but besides that, what else? I said: We do not know. He said: You will come to a people who will ask you to feed them with narrations, so reduce the narration from the Messenger of Allah, and I am your partner in that."],[1975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a stray camel. He said: Leave it; it has its tough feet and its water-skin, it eats from the trees and drinks from the water until its owner takes it. Then it was said to him: A stray sheep? He said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. Then it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the mountain livestock? He said: Its fine and its like with it, and lashes as a punishment. But if it is brought into the fold, and its value reaches the price of a shield, then cutting off the hand applies. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and hanging fruit? He said: Its fine and its like with it, and lashes as a punishment. But if it is brought into the threshing floor, and its value reaches the price of a shield, then cutting off the hand applies. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and a found item? He said: What is in an inhabited village or a well-trodden road, announce it for a year. If you find its owner, then return it; otherwise, enjoy it. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and buried treasure? He said: On buried treasure, one-fifth is due."],[1976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition, and they met the enemy and pressed on in killing until they came to the children. When the expedition returned, word of that reached the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Did I not forbid you? They said: They are only the children of the polytheists. He said: Are not the best of you the children of the polytheists? Then he ordered a caller to announce: Verily, every newborn is born upon the fitrah."],[1977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to my father: How many gods do you worship today? He said: Seven — six in the earth and one in the heaven. He said: Which one of them do you count on for your desire and your fear? He said: The one in the heaven. He said: O Husayn, if you submit, I will teach you two words that will benefit you. So when Husayn became a Muslim, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me the two words you promised me. He said: O Allah, inspire me with my right guidance, and protect me from the evil of my own self."],[1978,"Two people should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third, for that hurts the believer, and Allah the Exalted dislikes hurting the believer."],[1979,"The hand of the Most Merciful is above the head of the muezzin, and he is forgiven as far as his voice reaches — wherever it reaches."],[1980,"Allah the Exalted wrote a Book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and He sent down from it two verses with which He sealed Surat al-Baqarah. They are not recited in a house for three days but that no devil comes near it."],[1981,"I pray on my mount wherever it faces me? He said: Yes. I said: Is it from the Sunnah? He said: Yes."],[1982,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in three Suhuli garments, without a shirt or a turban."],[1983,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated in ‘When the sky is split asunder’ and ‘Recite in the name of your Lord’."],[1984,"I spent a night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I used to hear him when he finished his prayer and settled in his bed, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in You from You. O Allah, I cannot praise You enough, even if I strive, but You are as You have praised Yourself."],[1985,"He says regarding Banu Tamim three things: I will never cease loving them forever. Some camels of the zakah camels from Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “These are the camels of my people,” making them his people. And ‘A’ishah had a vow to free a slave from the descendants of Isma‘il, and captives from Khawlan were brought to him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Free from among them, for they are from the descendants of Isma‘il, and they are the severest of people against the Dajjal,” meaning Banu Tamim."],[1986,"When a man goes to another man and kills him, the one killed is in Paradise and the killer is in the Fire."],[1987,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on a military expedition, and he did not finish until the prayer time that the Messenger of Allah used to observe had passed into evening. When he finished with them, he looked and saw that the ‘Asr prayer had passed into evening, so he prayed. When he finished his prayer, he supplicated against his enemy, saying: “O Allah, whoever distracted us from the middle prayer, fill their houses with fire, fill their bellies with fire, and fill their graves with fire.”"],[1988,"When the surah “When the help of Allah comes and the victory” was revealed, the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was announced to him when it was revealed. He then began the most intense exertion in the matter of the Hereafter. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said after that: “The help of Allah has come, victory has come, and the people of Yemen have come.” A man said to him: “O Messenger of Allah, who are the people of Yemen?” He said: “A people whose hearts are tender and whose inner selves are soft. Faith is Yemeni and understanding is Yemeni.”"],[1989,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his military expeditions, and a man asked him: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about those who play?” He remained silent and did not reply a word. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his expedition and gained victory over them, he saw a boy who had fallen from a lookout post of his, and the boy was digging in the ground. A caller announced: “Where is the questioner?” The man came to the Prophet ﷺ , and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited killing children. Then he said: “Allah knows best what they would have done.”"],[1990,"When the servants stand for the reckoning, a people will come with their swords on their shoulders, dripping blood, and they will crowd at the gate of Paradise. It will be said: “Who are these?” It will be said: “The martyrs; they were alive and provided for.” Then a caller will announce: “Let him whose reward is upon Allah stand up and enter Paradise.” Then he will announce a second time: “Let him whose reward is upon Allah stand up and enter Paradise.” He said: “And who is the one whose reward is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic?” He said: “Those who pardon people.” Then he will announce a third time: “Let him whose reward is upon Allah stand up and enter Paradise,” and so many thousands stood up and entered it without reckoning."],[1991,"My beloved Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I will never abandon: he enjoined upon me the Witr before sleeping, the full bath every Friday, and fasting three days of every month."],[1992,"“How will you be when the companion of the horn has placed the horn in his mouth, inclined his forehead, waiting for when he is commanded, and then blows?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, what should we say?” He said: “Say: Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs.”"],[1993,"My father Safwan migrated to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Madinah and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam. The Prophet ﷺ extended his hand to him and wiped it, and Safwan said to him: “I love you, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “A person is with the one he loves.”"],[1994,"“Take from me; Allah has made a way for them: the virgin with the virgin, one hundred lashes and banishment; and the previously married with the previously married, one hundred lashes and stoning.”"],[1995,"Ja‘far b. Abi Talib came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the land of Abyssinia, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed him between his eyes and said: “I do not know whether I am more delighted at Ja‘far’s arrival or at the conquest of Khaybar.”"],[1996,"When the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” none of us would bend his back until the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, then we would prostrate after him."],[1997,"He used to say the talbiyah: “Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni‘mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak.”"],[1998,"Indeed, a good quality may be in a man, and through it Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sets right all of his deeds. And a man’s purification for his prayer: Allah expiates his sins by it, and his prayer remains as a supererogatory act for him."],[1999,"When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[2000,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[2001,"He was sitting with al-Mughirah b. Shu‘bah when a man came and spoke ill of ‘Ali. Sa‘id became angry and said: “Are the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoken ill of in your presence? I bear witness that Abu Bakr is in Paradise, that ‘Umar is in Paradise, that ‘Uthman is in Paradise, that ‘Ali is in Paradise, that Talhah is in Paradise, that al-Zubayr is in Paradise, that Sa‘d is in Paradise, and that ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf is in Paradise. And if I wished to name the ninth, I would name him.” The people then said to him and increased upon him."],[2002,"The first person to pray with the Prophet ﷺ was Abu Bakr."],[2003,"Some people asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: “We go far away from water for three months or five, and we find no water, and among us are menstruating women, those in a state of major ritual impurity, and women in post-natal bleeding.” He said: “You must use the earth.”"],[2004,"I indeed know a stone that used to greet me before I was sent as a Prophet; I still recognize it now."],[2005,"‘Uthman ؓ came with dinars and placed them in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began turning them over and saying: “Whatever ‘Uthman does after this day will not harm him.”"],[2006,"Do not precede the month until you see the new crescent or complete the number of days before it."],[2007,"When a man swears an oath and says: “If Allah wills,” he has made an exception."],[2008,"Whoever looks into a people’s house without their permission, it has become lawful for them to gouge out his eye."],[2009,"None of you should say: 'O Allah, forgive me if You will,' but let him be firm in asking, for there is no one to compel Him."],[2010,"Regarding His saying: 'Say: I ask of you no reward for it, except that you preserve me in my kinship'—do not call me a liar and do not harm me."],[2011,"I saw Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ face the Stone, kiss it, and then say: 'By Allah, I know that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit me, and had I not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing you, I would not have kissed you.'"],[2012,"A man from the Ansar passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sad, and the man had food that people gathered around, and he entered his mosque to pray. While he was thus, he dozed off, and someone came to him in his sleep and said: 'I know why you are sad.' Then he mentioned the story of the adhan. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Indeed.'"],[2013,"Do not turn around in your prayer, for there is no prayer for the one who turns around."],[2014,"These dinars and dirhams destroyed those before you, and I do not think they will be anything but your destroyers."],[2015,"On the day when some of the signs of your Lord come—he said: 'The rising of the sun from its west.'"],[2016,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ from Madinah, and we encountered a swarm of locusts. We met them with our whips and sticks, and they fell into our hands. We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said: 'There is no harm in the catch of the sea.'"],[2017,"When the Prophet ﷺ sat in prayer for the tashahhud, he placed his hands on his knees, then raised his index finger next to the thumb, while the rest of his fingers on his right hand remained clenched as they were."],[2018,"The briber and the bribed are in the Fire."],[2019,"What do you call those from the people of the villages who enter among you and have no lineage or kinship with you? I said: 'We call them 'ulūj and siqāṭ.' Aisha said: 'We used to call them Muhājirūn in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[2020,"Take the predawn meal, for there is blessing in the predawn meal."],[2021,"There is no vow except in that wherein Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is obeyed, and no oath in anger, and no manumission or divorce in what one does not own."],[2022,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[2023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perfume himself with the best perfume he could find when entering ihram."],[2024,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over the leather socks."],[2025,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wudu, wipe over his turban, and wipe over his leather socks."],[2026,"Establish the prayer, give the zakah, perform Hajj and Umrah, and be upright so that uprightness is established for you."],[2027,"Whoever recites 'Say: He is Allah, the One' it is as if he recited one-third of the Quran."],[2028,"Whoever sells date palms that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise; and whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the master unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."],[2029,"The Prophet ﷺ took a bite from a shoulder, then prayed without performing wudu."],[2030,"I saw Sa'd b. Malik perform witr with one rak'ah, then he said: \"Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do.\""],[2031,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ prostrated in 'Read in the name of your Lord' (Surah al-Alaq)."],[2032,"When one of you wishes, let him wish for much, for he is only asking his Lord, Mighty and Majestic."],[2033,"The Prophet's ﷺ voluntary night prayer consisted of thirteen rak'ahs."],[2034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was six years old, and I was taken into his household when I was nine. I stayed with him for nine [years]."],[2035,"I found two dinars, so I brought them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Make them known for a year.' So I made them known for a year, then I brought them back to him. He said: 'Keep their container, their tie, and their number, and make use of them. When their owner comes, return them to him.'"],[2036,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived, Usamah b. Zayd did not come to the Prophet ﷺ for several days. Then he came to him, and when he looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he wept. He said to him: 'You stayed away from us as long as you did, and then you come to grieve us.'"],[2037,"The children of the polytheists are the servants of the people of Paradise."],[2038,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on a donkey while traveling to Khaybar, with the qiblah behind him."],[2039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon his companions while they were conversing and talking. They said: 'We were remembering what we were in during the days of ignorance, and how Allah, Mighty and Majestic, guided us, and the misguidance we were in.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You have done well,' and it pleased him. He said: 'Be like this' or 'Do like this.'"],[2040,"I entered upon Umar and he said: 'O Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, do you fear that people will abandon Islam and leave it?' I said: 'No, if Allah wills. How could they abandon it when the Book of Allah and the Sunnahs of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are among them?' He said: 'If anything of that were to happen, it would be the Banu so-and-so.'"],[2041,"You must practice archery, for it is the best of your games."],[2042,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he bowed, place his palms on his knees and spread his fingers apart."],[2043,"The Prophet ﷺ measured a span for her from the hem of her garment."],[2044,"I asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri about vessels. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade vessels, except for water-skins that could be tied shut.'"],[2045,"He forbade muḥāqalah and muzābanah: a man selling his date-palm crop for such-and-such a load of dry dates in exchange for such-and-such a load of fresh dates. If there was an increase, it was for the buyer; and if there was a shortfall, it was upon the buyer."],[2046,"We complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the intense heat, but he did not take up our complaint. He said: “When the sun has passed its zenith, then pray ẓuhr.”"],[2047,"If I were to take an intimate friend, I would have taken Abū Bakr as an intimate friend, but the brotherhood of Islam is superior."],[2048,"Close the doors that open into the mosque, except the door of Abū Bakr ؓ."],[2049,"A dream is one of forty-six parts of prophethood, and the dream of a believer seldom errs in the latter days."],[2050,"If people knew what lies in solitude, no rider would ever travel alone at night, and no man would ever sleep alone in a house."],[2051,"ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ sent me and said: “Do you know on what mission I am sending you? On the same mission on which the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me: leave no image without breaking it, and no raised grave without leveling it.”"],[2052,"What is forbidden by suckling is what is forbidden by lineage."],[2053,"A man said: “Praise be to God, much.” The angel found it too great to record, and he referred it back to his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. It was said to him: “Write it as My servant said it: much.”"],[2054,"I said to Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. al-Ḥusayn: “May I be your ransom, what do you think of this intercession that the people of Iraq talk about? Is it true?” He said: “Intercession for what?” He said: “The intercession of Muḥammad ﷺ.” He said: “True, by God. By God, my uncle Muḥammad b. ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah narrated to me, from ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘I will intercede for my community until my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, calls me and says: “Are you satisfied, O Muḥammad?” I will say: “Yes, I am satisfied.”’”"],[2055,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the woman who joins hair extensions and the one who has them joined, and the woman who tattoos and the one who has herself tattooed.” A woman said: “There are some of his family who do that.” He said: “Go and look.” So she looked and saw nothing."],[2056,"If Satan comes to one of you during prayer and says: “You have broken your ablution,” let him not leave until he hears a sound or detects an odor."],[2057,"Fasting on the Day of ʿArafah is an expiation for the past year and the coming year."],[2058,"I used to comb the Prophet's ﷺ hair while I was menstruating."],[2059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding sciatica: Take the fat tail of an Arabian ram, neither too small nor too large, melt it, and drink it for three days on an empty stomach."],[2060,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said: Fast if you wish, or break your fast if you wish."],[2061,"There is no servant who has wealth and does not pay its zakat except that it will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, and sheets of Hellfire will be heated for him, and his side and back will be branded with them, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, judges between His servants on a day whose length is fifty thousand years of what you count. Then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of camels who does not pay their zakat except that they will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as numerous as they ever were, and he will be thrown on his face in a vast, level plain, and they will trample him, the first of them and the last of them, every time the first pass, the last return, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, judges between His servants on a day whose length was fifty thousand years of what you count. Then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of livestock who does not pay its zakat except that it will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as numerous as it ever was, and he will be thrown on his face in a vast, level plain, and it will trample him with its hooves and gore him with its horns, none of them having twisted horns, broken horns, or no horns. Every time the last of them pass, the first of them are returned to him, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, judges between His servants on a day whose length was fifty thousand years of what you count. Then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about horses? He said: \"Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. Horses are of three kinds: for one man they are a reward, for another a covering, and for another a burden. As for the one for whom they are a reward: a man who keeps them and prepares them for the cause of Allah. Whatever they consume from their bellies is a reward for him, and if he grazes them in a meadow, he has a reward for what they consume from their bellies, and if they run one or two rounds, he has a reward for every step they take, and if he comes to a river and waters them from it, he has a reward for every drop they consume into their bellies, to the point that he is even rewarded for their dung and urine. As for the one for whom they are a covering: a man who keeps them for dignity, beauty, and honor, and does not forget the rights of their backs and bellies in his hardship and ease. As for the one upon whom they are a burden: a man who keeps them out of pride, arrogance, showing off to people, and extravagance over them.\" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about donkeys? He said: \"Allah has not revealed anything to me about them except this comprehensive, unique verse: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it' (Quran 99:7-8).\""],[2062,"He used to dye his beard yellow."],[2063,"Abu Thaʿlabah al-Khushani came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the delegation of Yemen and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land where only drink makes us well, and there is a drink made from honey called bitʿ, and a drink made from corn called mizr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whatever intoxicates in large amounts, a small amount of it is unlawful.\""],[2064,"He forbade gold rings and iron rings."],[2065,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[2066,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: Who has the best voice for the Quran among people? He said: \"The one who, when you hear his recitation, you think that he fears Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[2067,"He used to pray on a mat."],[2068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me with furnishings worth forty dirhams."],[2069,"Let not urine be soaked in a basin in the house, for the angels do not enter a house in which urine is soaked; and do not urinate in your bathing place."],[2070,"No man attends the Friday prayer without engaging in idle talk or ignorance therein, and perfects his ablution, and attends it with the imam, except that it is an expiation for what is between it and the following Friday; nor does he perform an obligatory prayer except that it is an expiation for what is between it and the following prayer."],[2071,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the place of the lower garment. He took hold of the muscle of my calf and said: “To here; but if you refuse, then the lower garment has no right below that.”"],[2072,"He said regarding the day of Ashura: “We used to fast it, then it was abandoned.”"],[2073,"I did not pass by any group of angels on the night I was taken on the night journey except that they commanded me to practice cupping."],[2074,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of the Ansar shooting at a pigeon, and he said: “Do not take a living being as a target.”"],[2075,"I said: O Messenger of God, what are these four rak‘ahs that you pray at the time of the sun's decline? He said: “This is the hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, and they are not closed until the noon prayer is performed; so I like to send forth good in advance.”"],[2076,"Friday was presented to the Messenger of God ﷺ. Gabriel came with in his palm something like a white mirror, in the middle of which was like a black dot. He said: “What is this, O Gabriel?” He said: “This is Friday. Your Lord presents it to you so that it may be a festival for you and for your people after you. In it there is good for you: you will be the first, and the Jews and Christians will come after you. In it there is an hour in which no one asks his Lord for good that is allotted for him except that He gives it to him, or seeks refuge from evil except that He wards off from him what is greater than it. We call it in the Hereafter the Day of Increase. That is because your Lord has taken in Paradise a wide valley of white musk. When it is Friday, He descends from ‘Illiyyin and sits on His throne, and the throne is surrounded by pulpits of gold studded with jewels. The truthful and the martyrs come and sit on them, and the people of the chambers come from their chambers until they sit on the dune, a white dune of fragrant musk. Then He manifests Himself to them and says: 'I am the One who fulfilled My promise to you and completed My favor upon you. This is the place of My honor, so ask of Me.' They ask Him for His good pleasure. He says: 'My good pleasure has brought you into My abode and granted you My honor, so ask of Me.' They ask Him for His good pleasure, and He bears witness to them that He is pleased with them. Then He opens for them what no eye has seen and no human heart has conceived, until the time of their departure from Friday. It is a green emerald or a red ruby, with its rivers flowing through it and its fruits hanging down, containing their spouses and servants. They are not more eager for anything in Paradise than for Friday, so that they may increase in looking upon their Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and His honor. For that reason it is called the Day of Increase.”"],[2077,"A man related a hadith in the presence of al-Hasan, and al-Hasan said: “Who told you this?” He said: “The fuqaha'.” He said: “Have you ever seen with your own eyes a true faqih?” Then he said: “Do you know who the faqih is? The faqih is the one who renounces this world, desires the Hereafter, is knowledgeable in this religion, and adheres to knowledge.”"],[2078,"He said to him: “O ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Amr, how will it be with you when you remain among the dregs of people whose covenants and trusts have become corrupted, and they have differed and become like this,” and he interlaced his fingers? He said: “What do you command me, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Keep to what you know and abandon what you reject; keep to your own self, and beware of their common people.”"],[2079,"Gabriel ﷺ commanded me to use the tooth stick so persistently that I feared I would wear my teeth down to the gums."],[2080,"An imam known as Abu Rimthah led us in the afternoon prayer in our prayer place, and with us was a man who had witnessed the first takbir. When Abu Rimthah finished, the man stood up to make up what he had missed. Abu Rimthah looked at him and said: “I prayed this prayer, or one like it, with the Prophet ﷺ. Abu Bakr and ‘Umar were placed forward in prayer. There was a man who had witnessed the first takbir of the prayer. The Prophet ﷺ prayed, then he gave the greeting to the right and left, until I saw the whiteness of his cheeks, then he turned away as Abu Rimthah turned away—meaning himself—and faced the people. The man who had caught the first takbir with him stood up to make up what he had missed. ‘Umar went to him, seized him by the shoulder, and pushed him, then said: 'Sit down, for the People of the Book were ruined only because there was no separation between their prayers.' The Prophet ﷺ raised his eyes to him and said: 'May God cause you to hit the mark, O Ibn al-Khattab.'”"],[2081,"When evil appears on the earth, Allah sends His punishment upon the people of the earth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if righteous people are among them? He said: \"Yes, even if righteous people are among them; they will be afflicted by what afflicts the people, then they will return to the mercy of Allah.\""],[2082,"Barirah was married to a slave, then she was freed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice regarding her marriage."],[2083,"A man wore a garment like the garment of the Prophet ﷺ, then he came to a household in Madinah and said: The Prophet ﷺ has commanded me to inspect whichever household I wish. They said: Our knowledge of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is that he does not command indecencies. He said: So they prepared a room for him and sent a messenger to the Messenger of Allah, informing him. He said to Abu Bakr and Umar: \"Go to him; if you find him alive, kill him, then burn him with fire, and if you find that he has already been dealt with, then burn him. I think you will find that he has already been dealt with.\" They went and found that he had gone out at night to urinate and was bitten by a viper and died. They burned him with fire, then returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of the news. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[2084,"When I was taken up to the heaven, I did not pass by any heaven except that I found in it my name: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq behind me."],[2085,"Water is not made impure by anything."],[2086,"When the Prophet ﷺ said the salam at the end of the prayer, he said: \"O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.\""],[2087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was alone in a garden, and a man with a weak voice came and greeted. He said: Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise. I opened, and it was Abu Bakr, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. He praised Allah and sat. Then another came and greeted. He said: \"Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.\" I opened, and it was Umar, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then another came and greeted. He said: \"Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise after a trial that will befall him.\" I opened the door, and it was Uthman, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. He praised Allah and then sat."],[2088,"Quraysh gathered in Dar al-Nadwah and mentioned the Prophet ﷺ. Some of them said: He is a sorcerer. They said: He is not a sorcerer. Some said: He is a soothsayer. They said: He is not a soothsayer. Some said: He is possessed. They said: He is not possessed. They said: He separates a man from his beloved. The polytheists departed upon that. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he wrapped himself in his garments and was covered. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: O you wrapped in garments, O you covered one."],[2089,"O people, I have a right over you, and the Imams from Quraysh have a right over you as long as they uphold three things: when mercy is sought from them they show mercy, when they judge they are just, and when they make a covenant they fulfill it. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither ransom nor compensation will be accepted from him."],[2090,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast three days of every month, but sometimes he would delay that until the fasts of the whole year accumulated upon him, and sometimes he would delay it until he fasted Sha'ban."],[2091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dowry."],[2092,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to them in the land of Juhaynah: Do not make use of anything from dead animals, neither hide nor sinew."],[2093,"There is no prayer after the late afternoon prayer until the sun sets, and no prayer after the dawn prayer until the sun rises,\" and no fasting on the day of the two festivals,\" and a woman may not travel for more than three nights except with a guardian (dhu mahram) accompanying her, and no journey should be undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Aqsa Mosque."],[2094,"Be moderate in your prostration, and none of you should spread out his forearms like a dog spreads them out in prostration. By Allah, I surely see you from behind my back when you bow and prostrate."],[2095,"There were four sunnah practices concerning Barirah: Her husband divorced her, and he was a slave, so the Prophet ﷺ gave her the choice. He ordered her to observe the waiting period of a free woman,\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said: \"Do you have anything you can feed us?\" They said: \"Nothing except some meat that was given as charity to Barirah, which she gave to us as a gift.\" He said: \"It is charity for her, but a gift for us,\" and he ate from it. Her masters stipulated that they would not sell her unless the patronage (wala') would remain with them. He said: \"Buy her and set her free, for the patronage belongs to the one who gave the money.\""],[2096,"Take care of the Quran. By the One in whose hand is my soul, it slips away from the hearts of men more swiftly than a hobbled camel slips away to its tethers."],[2097,"Say: He is Allah, the One, is equal to a third of the Quran."],[2098,"He was asked: Which Islam is best? He said: \"The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\" It was said: \"And which jihad is best?\" He said: \"The one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is spilled.\" It was said: \"And which prayer is best?\" He said: \"Lengthy humble standing (qunut).\""],[2099,"Ibn Mas'ud was asked, and it was said to him: \"A man married a woman but did not specify a dower for her, and he died before consummating the marriage.\" He said: \"I have not heard anything about this matter. Come back to me so I can look into it.\" They returned, then came back to him. He said: \"I will give my considered opinion about it. If I am correct, it is Allah who guided me; if I err, the error is from me. I think she should have a dower like that of her peers, with no reduction or excess, and she inherits, and she must observe the waiting period.\" Ma'qil b. Sinan al-Ashja'i said: \"He testifies that he heard the Prophet ﷺ rule exactly as you have ruled in the case of a woman of theirs called Barwa' bt. Washiq.\""],[2100,"A woman kept coming to Ibn Mas'ud for a month, and each time he would send her back. Her husband had died without specifying a dower for her. 'Abdullah said: \"I will give my opinion on this. If it is right, it is from Allah; if it is wrong, it is from the son of Umm 'Abd. She is entitled to a dower like that of one of her peers, and she inherits, receiving one-fourth or one-eighth.\" With him was a man from Ashja' among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \"I call Allah to witness that the Prophet ﷺ ruled in this way for a woman of ours called Barwa' bt. Washiq.\""],[2101,"I heard 'Ali asking the people: 'Whoever heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever's mawla I am, 'Ali is his mawla,\" let him stand up.' Twelve men stood up and testified."],[2102,"I heard 'Ali asking the people: 'Whoever heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever's mawla I am, 'Ali is his mawla\"?' Thirteen men stood up and testified that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever's mawla I am, 'Ali is his mawla.\""],[2103,"A man from the Ansar known as Abu Madhkur manumitted a slave of his to be effective after his death (tadbir), but then the Prophet ﷺ sent for him and sold him (the slave)."],[2104,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for more than three days, except for a husband."],[2105,"Whoever leaves snakes (i.e., avoids killing them) out of fear of vengeance is not of us."],[2106,"The believer is the mirror of the believer."],[2107,"No servant has benefited, after Islam, with anything better for him than a believing wife: when he looks at her she pleases him, and when he is absent from her she guards him in herself and his property."],[2108,"The wedding feast on the first day is a duty, on the second a courtesy, and on the third ostentation and reputation-seeking."],[2109,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ saw us off and said: Reduce your narrations from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I am your partner."],[2110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in three garments, one of which was a shirt."],[2111,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the people on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah to pledge allegiance. Abu Sinan b. Mihsan came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I pledge allegiance to you on what is in your heart. He said: \"And what is in my heart?\" He said: I will strike with my sword before you until Allah grants you victory or I am killed. So he accepted his pledge, and the people pledged allegiance on the pledge of Abu Sinan."],[2112,"The mut'ah (temporary marriage) was only for us, the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, specifically — meaning the mut'ah of Hajj."],[2113,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a woman and stood at her middle."],[2114,"A servant lies until he is recorded with Allah as a liar, and tells the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful one."],[2115,"A sheep died in one of the houses of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: Why did you not make use of its skin?"],[2116,"Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, enters Paradise, even if he commits fornication and even if he steals."],[2117,"We used not to know the hypocrites except by their hatred of 'Ali ؓ."],[2118,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque, except the Sacred Mosque."],[2119,"When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[2120,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us extra spoils besides our share of the fifth, and I received an old camel."],[2121,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform witr with 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High', 'Say, O disbelievers', and 'Say, He is Allah, the One'."],[2122,"If one of you passes wind, let him perform wudu'."],[2123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made two rak'ahs obligatory during travel, just as he made four obligatory while resident."],[2124,"Abu al-Darda' gave a sermon and said, 'Whoever is overtaken by dawn, there is no witr for him.' 'A'ishah said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would be overtaken by dawn and then perform witr.'"],[2125,"Whoever follows a funeral procession until he prays over it, then leaves, will have a qirat of reward. If he follows it, prays over it, then sits until the burial is completed, he will have two qirats, each of which is greater than Uhud."],[2126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that animals be tied and shot as targets."],[2127,"I saw myself scraping semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and then he prayed."],[2128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade inciting animals against each other."],[2129,"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has pardoned for this Ummah mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they are forced to do."],[2130,"Whoever sees good in his dream, let him praise Allah and mention it; and whoever sees other than that, let him seek refuge in Allah and not mention it, for it will not harm him."],[2131,"Indeed the servant commits a sin, and when he remembers it, what he has done grieves him. And when Allah sees that what he has done has grieved him, He forgives him."],[2132,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the best earnings. He said: A man's work with his hands, and every accepted sale."],[2133,"He used to pray two rak'ahs after 'Asr."],[2134,"He used to say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the burden of debt, from the domination of the enemy, from the ruin of the unwed, and from the trial of the Dajjal.'"],[2135,"He is not from us who slaps his cheeks, tears his garments, and calls with the call of Jahiliyyah."],[2136,"None of you should spit in front of him during prayer, nor to his right, but let him spit to his left."],[2137,"None of you should prostrate while spreading his forearms like a dog."],[2138,"The dream is from Allah, and the bad dream is from Shaytan. So if any of you sees what he dislikes, let him spit to his left and seek refuge from its evil, for it will not harm him."],[2139,"The fatwa that the Ansar used to give: 'water from water' was a concession in the beginning of Islam."],[2140,"Two should not hold secret counsel excluding the third."],[2141,"A man should not make another man get up from his place and then sit in it; but if he returns, he is more entitled to it."],[2142,"When one of you becomes drowsy on Friday, he should change his place."],[2143,"His uncle 'Amir b. al-Akwa' was wounded on the day of Khaybar and killed a man, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He will have two rewards.'"],[2144,"There is no man who is put in charge of a people and then does not protect them as he protects himself and his family, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will admit him into the Fire of Hell."],[2145,"O Zayd, give the zakah of your head along with the people, even if you find nothing but a thread."],[2146,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing in prayer without performing voluntary prayers until his feet became swollen. It was said: 'Do you exert yourself like this, and what is this exertion when Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins?' He said: 'Should I not be a grateful servant?'"],[2147,"Al-Hasan b. 'Ali b. Abi Talib delivered a sermon. He praised Allah and extolled Him, and he mentioned the Commander of the Faithful 'Ali ؓ, the seal of the trustees, the successor of the seal of the prophets, and the trustee of the truthful ones and the martyrs. Then he said: 'O people, a man has departed from you whom the first ones did not precede and the last ones will not overtake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give him the banner, and Jibril would fight on his right and Mika'il on his left, and he would not return until Allah granted him victory. Allah took his soul on the night in which the successor of Musa was taken, and his spirit was raised on the night in which the spirit of 'Isa b. Maryam was raised, and on the night in which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down the Criterion. By Allah, he left no gold, no silver, and nothing tied up for him. In his treasury there was only seven hundred and fifty dirhams left over from his stipend, with which he intended to buy a servant for Umm Kulthum.' Then he said: 'Whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am al-Hasan b. Muhammad, ﷺ. Then he recited this verse, the words of Yusuf: \"And I have followed the religion of my fathers, Ibrahim, Ishaq, and Ya'qub\" (12:38). Then he resumed speaking from the Book of Allah and said: 'I am the son of the bringer of good tidings, and I am the son of the warner, and I am the son of the Prophet, and I am the son of the one who calls to Allah by His permission, and I am the son of the luminous lamp, and I am the son of the one who was sent as a mercy to the worlds, and I am from the People of the House from whom Allah has removed impurity and purified them thoroughly, and I am from the People of the House whose love and guardianship Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made obligatory, for He said in what He revealed to Muhammad ﷺ: \"Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it except love for the near relatives\" (42:23).'"],[2148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali: 'None loves you but a believer, and none hates you but a hypocrite.'"],[2149,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to 'Ali: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has adorned you with an adornment with which He has not adorned any of His servants with anything like it. Allah, Exalted, has endeared the poor to you and closeness to them, and has made you an Imam for them with whom they are pleased, and has made them followers for you who are pleased with you. So blessed is the one who loves you and is truthful about you, and woe to the one who hates you and lies about you. As for those who love you and are truthful about you, they will be your neighbors in your abode and your companions in your Paradise. As for those who hate you and lie about you, it is incumbent upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to make them stand in the stations of the liars.'"],[2150,"Gold for gold, like for like; silver for silver, like for like; dates for dates, like for like; salt for salt, like for like."],[2151,"We asked our Prophet ﷺ about walking with a funeral procession. He said: 'Walk at a pace below a trot. If it is good, it will be hastened to it; and if it is evil, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral procession is followed and does not follow, and he is not one of us who goes ahead of it.'"],[2152,"I said to 'Ali: 'O Commander of the Faithful, do you have any revelation besides what is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic?' He said: 'No, by Him who split the grain and created the soul, I do not know of anything except an understanding that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives a man in the Qur'an, and what is in the page.' I said: 'What is in the page?' He said: 'The blood-money and the ransoming of the captive, and that a Muslim should not be killed for a disbeliever.'"],[2153,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I stay behind from the prayer because so-and-so prolongs it for us. I never saw the Prophet ﷺ get angry about anything more intensely than he got angry about this. He said: O people, among you are those who repel others. Whoever of you leads the people in prayer should lighten it, for among them are the young, the old, and the one with a need."],[2154,"The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone, but they are two signs among the signs of God, mighty and majestic. When you see that, then you should perform prayer."],[2155,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, and he pointed with his hand toward Yemen: Faith is here, and harshness and hardness of heart are among the clamorous people who shout loudly at the rising of the sun, where the horn of Satan appears near the roots of camels' tails, in Rabīʿah and Muḍar."],[2156,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymūnah while he was in a state of iḥrām."],[2157,"O people of Madinah, remember the Day of Deliverance. They said: What is the Day of Deliverance? He said: The Dajjāl will come until he encamps at Dhubāb. Then there will not remain in Madinah any polytheist man or polytheist woman, any disbeliever man or disbeliever woman, any hypocrite man or hypocrite woman, any sinful man or sinful woman except that he or she goes out to him. The believers will be saved. That is the Day of Deliverance."],[2158,"If they appoint Abū Bakr as successor, they will find him a submissive, trustworthy, ascetic man in this world, desirous of the Hereafter. If they put ʿUmar in command, they will find him strong and trustworthy; no blame of any blamer affects him in [matters of] God. If they put ʿAlī in command—and I do not think they will do it—they will find him a guide, rightly guided, who will take them along the straight path."],[2159,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me seventy sūrahs before Zayd b. Thābit embraced Islam."],[2160,"There is no prize except for an arrowhead, a hoof, or a camel's foot."],[2161,"O God, forgive the Anṣār, the descendants of the Anṣār, the descendants of the descendants of the Anṣār, and the clients of the Anṣār."],[2162,"She arrived intending ʿumrah, but she menstruated before she could circumambulate the House. She asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered her to enter into iḥrām for ḥajj. When she completed her rites, she said: O Messenger of God, my sisters return with both ḥajj and ʿumrah, while I return with only a ḥajj? He said: Go out with your brother. So she went out with him to al-Tanʿīm. The Messenger of God ﷺ stopped at al-Abṭaḥ waiting for her. Thus it became a sunnah for the people."],[2163,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us while we were in a house. He took hold of the two doorposts, then said: I have a right over you, and the leaders of Quraysh have a right as long as they practice three things: if they judge, they are just; if they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; and if they make a covenant, they fulfill it. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people."],[2164,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform witr with [Sūrat] Sabbihi isma rabbika l-aʿlā, [Sūrat] Qul yā ayyuhā l-kāfirūn, and Qul huwa Llāhu aḥad."],[2165,"Whoever fasts one day in the path of God, God will distance him from the Fire by seventy autumns."],[2166,"A man came when the Messenger of God ﷺ had already prayed, and he said: “Is there not a man who will give charity to this one, so that he may pray with him?”"],[2167,"The night prayer is two by two, and when you fear the approach of dawn, then pray one rakʿah as witr."],[2168,"It is not proper for a person who has a bequest to spend two nights without having his bequest written down."],[2169,"The Prophet ﷺ had curly hair that reached his shoulders."],[2170,"The congregational prayer surpasses the prayer of one alone by twenty-five degrees."],[2171,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “O God, purify me with snow, hail, and cold water. O God, purify me from sins as a white garment is purified from dirt.”"],[2172,"Gentleness does not enter anything but that it beautifies it, and it is not removed from anything but that it disgraces it."],[2173,"ʿUmar asked the Prophet ﷺ about a man who sleeps while he is in a state of major ritual impurity. He said: “He should perform ablution, then sleep.”"],[2174,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed his night prayer, he would perform witr, then he would come to his bed. When the caller announced the prayer, he would jump up from his bed. If he was in a state of major ritual impurity, he would pour water over himself; and if he was not, he would perform ablution for prayer, then come and pray."],[2175,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ take ʿAli by the hand, and he was saying: “This is my ally and I am his ally. I befriend those who befriend him, and I am an enemy to those who are his enemies.”"],[2176,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood between the men and the women, urged the men to give charity, then turned to the women and urged them to give charity. Zaynab, the wife of ʿAbd Allah, sent Bilal to him, saying: “Convey peace to the Messenger of God ﷺ from a woman among the Emigrants, but do not reveal her identity. Ask him: Does she have a reward if she gives charity to her husband from the Emigrants, who has nothing, and to orphans in her care, who are the sons of her brother, directing her charity to them?” Bilal came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Yes, she has two rewards: the reward of kinship and the reward of charity.”"],[2177,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the state of ihram when his riding camel stood upright with him."],[2178,"No soul is killed except that upon the son of Adam is a portion of it, because he was the first to institute killing."],[2179,"The saddles should not be fastened except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and the Mosque of the Aqsa."],[2180,"Abu Taybah cupped the Prophet ﷺ, and he gave him a sa' of food and ordered his family to reduce [the tax] for him."],[2181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me on the Day of Sacrifice: 'Bring [them]; pick up for me some pebbles.' So I picked up for him pebbles like the pebbles of khazf. He said: 'With the like of these, throw. Indeed, those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion.'"],[2182,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise."],[2183,"The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four things: about his body in what he wore it out, about his life in what he spent it, about his wealth from where he acquired it and in what he spent it, and about the love of the People of the House. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the sign of loving you? He struck his hand on the shoulder of Ali ؓ."],[2184,"One of us would menstruate in a garment, and when it was the day of her purity she would wash what had been affected by it, then pray in it. And one of you today frees her servant to wash her clothes on the day of her purity."],[2185,"Ghusl on Friday is recommended, and it is not obligatory."],[2186,"Whoever recites the Quran in this manner will be with the noble, righteous scribes, and whoever stumbles in it will have two rewards."],[2187,"The one consulted is entrusted, so when he is consulted, let him advise with what he would do for himself."],[2188,"I entered while the Prophet ﷺ was bowing, so I bowed outside the row, then I walked until I entered the row. The Prophet ﷺ said when he finished: 'May Allah increase you in keenness, but do not do it again.'"],[2189,"I never saw the private area of the Messenger of God ﷺ at all."],[2190,"We went on seven military expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ, eating locusts."],[2191,"The first thing for which a servant will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer. God (Mighty and Majestic) will say to His angels: 'Look at the prayer of My servant. Did he complete it or fall short in it?' If he completed it, it will be recorded for him as complete. If he had fallen short in it, it will be said: 'Look and see whether My servant has any supererogatory prayer with which you may complete his obligatory prayer.' Then the rest of his deeds will be taken into account after that."],[2192,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the gourd and pitch-coated vessels."],[2193,"Ten men of Quraysh are in Paradise: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, 'Umar is in Paradise, 'Uthman is in Paradise, 'Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Sa'd is in Paradise, Sa'id is in Paradise, 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf is in Paradise, and Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah is in Paradise."],[2194,"Whoever God has deprived of his sight and he is patient and seeks [God's] reward, it is a right and duty upon God that his eyes shall never see the Fire."],[2195,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the dabb lizard. He said: 'A nation that was transformed, and God knows best.'"],[2196,"I heard Mu'awiyah giving a sermon, saying: 'One day I poured out the water for the Messenger of God ﷺ to perform his ablution. He raised his head to me and said: 'You will indeed take charge of the affairs of my community after me. When that happens, accept from their doers of good and overlook their wrongdoers.'' He said: 'And I never ceased to hope for it until I rose to this position of mine.'"],[2197,"The visitor of a sick person wades in mercy, and when he sits with him, he immerses himself in it."],[2198,"A person is with the one he loves."],[2199,"God's wrath is severe upon one who wrongs someone who finds no helper besides Me."],[2200,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about lost property. He said: 'Lost property is not permissible [to appropriate]. Whoever finds something should announce it. If its owner comes, he should return it to him. If he does not come, he should give it in charity. Then if [the owner] comes, he should let him choose between the reward [of charity] and what belongs to him.'"],[2201,"Perform wudu from what the fire has changed."],[2202,"When we returned from Tabuk, a man asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: When is the Hour? He said: \"One hundred years will not pass over the people while on the face of the earth there is a soul born today.\""],[2203,"Whoever dies while setting up a rival to God, God will place him in the Fire. And 'Abd Allah said: Another one I did not hear from the Messenger of God ﷺ; I hope it is true: No servant dies without setting up a rival to God except that God will admit him to Paradise."],[2204,"Muhammad b. Maslama al-Ansari asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for a sword, so he gave it to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ stipulated to him while the sword was in his hand before he handed it to him, saying: \"Here, O Muhammad, fight with it against the polytheists as long as they are fought; but when you see the Muslims fighting one another, then strike it against Uhud and break it.\""],[2205,"A Bedouin came to the Messenger of God and said: O Messenger of God, our clothes in Paradise, will we weave them with our hands? He said: The people laughed, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Why do you laugh? At an ignorant man asking a knowledgeable one? No, O Bedouin, rather they will be split open from the fruits of Paradise."],[2206,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[2207,"Whoever builds a mosque for God, God will build for him a house in Paradise."],[2208,"War is deception."],[2209,"Whoever gives respite to one in difficulty until his ease, God, Mighty and Majestic, will give him respite for his sin until his repentance."],[2210,"When one of you stands in prayer, let him not close his eyes."],[2211,"I was sitting with the Prophet of God ﷺ when a man came who had performed wudu, and on his foot there was a spot the water had not reached. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Go and complete your wudu. So he did."],[2212,"Preemption applies to every partnership in a dwelling or a walled garden; it is not lawful for him to sell it until he informs his partner, who may take it or leave it."],[2213,"Gabriel ﷺ said to me: “Give Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearls, in which there is no clamor and no toil.”"],[2214,"I said to al-Rubayyi‘ bt. Mu‘awwidh b. ‘Afrā’: “Describe the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to me.” She said: “When I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I saw him like the rising sun.”"],[2215,"‘Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said: “I have not regretted anything as much as I regret that I did not ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the wind.” Abū Hurayrah said: “Indeed I asked him about it. I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what is the wind from?’ He said: ‘It is from the spirit of Allah. He sends it with mercy, and He sends it with punishment.’”"],[2216,"You burn, you burn; when you pray Fajr it washes them away. Then you burn, you burn; when you pray Ẓuhr it washes them away. Then you burn, you burn; when you pray ‘Aṣr it washes them away. Then you burn, you burn; when you pray Maghrib it washes them away. Then you burn, you burn; when you pray ‘Ishā’ it washes them away. Then you sleep, and nothing is recorded against you until you wake."],[2217,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: “The witr before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and the bath on Friday.”"],[2218,"Perform ablution from what the fire has changed."],[2219,"The best condiment is vinegar."],[2220,"We sighted the new moon of Dhū al-Ḥijjah as a large crescent. Those who minimized it said: “From two nights,” and those who maximized it said: “From three nights.” When we arrived in Makkah, I met Ibn ‘Abbās and asked him about the Day of Tarwiyah. He counted for me from that day. I said: “We sighted it as a large crescent.” He said: “The Prophet ﷺ extended it to its sighting.”"],[2221,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer and forgot something in the prayer, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he recited the tashahhud, then he gave the salutation."],[2222,"Cling to love for us, the People of the House, for whoever meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while he loves us will enter Paradise through our intercession. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no servant’s deeds will benefit him except by recognizing our right."],[2223,"He used to forbid eating leeks and onions."],[2224,"When the son of Adam died, Adam said to his wife Ḥawwā’: “Your son has died.” She said: “What is death?” He said: “He does not eat, he does not drink, he does not walk, and he does not strike.” When he said that, she wailed. He said: “Wailing is upon you and upon your daughters, while I and my sons are innocent of it.” Thus mourning became the practice of women."],[2225,"A man came to Abu Musa and said: \"A man died and left his daughter, his son's daughter, and a sister.\" He said: \"The daughter gets half, the sister gets half, and Ibn Mas'ud will come to you and say the same thing.\" So I went to Ibn Mas'ud and said: \"Abu Musa told me such and such.\" Ibn Mas'ud said: \"I would then be astray and not among the guided: the daughter gets half, the son's daughter gets the completion, and the sister gets a third. This is how the Messenger of God ﷺ ordained it.\""],[2226,"The Prophet ﷺ stopped at the back of Marr. A limb of game was given as a gift, so he returned it to the messenger and said to him: \"Convey peace to him and say: 'Were we not in a state of ihram, we would not have returned it to you.'\""],[2227,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, may a man pray in a single garment?\" He said: \"Does every one of you have two garments?\""],[2228,"Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and confuses him until he does not know how much he has prayed. If any of you finds that, let him prostrate twice while sitting."],[2229,"I brought my son to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who had not yet eaten food. He placed him on his lap, and the boy urinated on the garment of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He called for water and sprinkled it on his garment, but did not wash it."],[2230,"Whoever performs ablution should rinse his nose, and whoever uses stones to clean himself should use an odd number."],[2231,"He saw the Messenger of God ﷺ lying on his back in the mosque with one of his legs placed over the other."],[2232,"There is no misfortune that befalls a Muslim but that it expiates for him, even the thorn that pricks him."],[2233,"The gecko is a little transgressor."],[2234,"Whoever wrongfully takes a piece of land, he will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths."],[2235,"He said: \"O Messenger of God, I fear that I may have perished.\" He said: \"Why?\" He said: \"I find myself loving pride, and God, Mighty and Majestic, forbids us to raise our voices above your voice, and I have a loud voice.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Thabit, are you not pleased that you will live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise?\""],[2236,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mut'ah with women on the day of Khaybar, and forbade eating the meat of domestic donkeys."],[2237,"He gifted the Messenger of God ﷺ a wild donkey while he was at Waddan or al-Abwa', and he returned it to him. He said: Then he recognized in my face the sadness of his returning it to me, and he said: 'It is not that we are returning it to you, but we are in a state of iḥrām.'"],[2238,"While I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a man came to him and said: 'O Messenger of God, I am ruined.' He said: 'Woe to you, what is the matter?' He said: 'I had intercourse with my wife while fasting in Ramadan.' He said: 'Can you find a slave to free?' He said: 'No, by God, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Are you able to fast two consecutive months?' He said: 'No, by God, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Can you find food to feed sixty poor people?' He said: 'No, O Messenger of God.' Then he turned away from him. While they were in that state, a basket of dates was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Where is the one who came?' He was called for, and he said to him: 'Take this and give it in charity.' The man said: 'To someone poorer than my family, O Messenger of God? By God, there is no household between its two lava fields poorer than us.' The Prophet ﷺ laughed until his canine teeth showed, then said: 'Take it and feed it to your family.'"],[2239,"Abu Bakr went out in the midday heat, and Umar heard of that, so he went out and found Abu Bakr. He said: 'O Abu Bakr, what brought you out at this hour?' He said: 'By God, I find nothing in my belly but the pangs of hunger.' Umar said: 'And I, by God, nothing brought me out but that.' While they were like that, the Prophet ﷺ came out to them and said: 'What brought you two out at this hour?' They said: 'It brought us out; by God, we find nothing in our bellies but the pangs of hunger.' He said: 'And I, by the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing brought me out but that. So get up.' They got up and went off until they came to the door of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. Abu Ayyub used to keep food for the Messenger of God ﷺ, whether it was food or milk, but on that day he was delayed and did not come at his usual time, so he fed it to his family and went off to his palm trees to work in them. When they came to the door of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, a woman came out and said: 'Welcome to the Messenger of God and those with him.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: 'Where is Abu Ayyub?' She said: 'He will come to you, O Prophet of God, this hour.' The Messenger of God ﷺ turned back, and Abu Ayyub saw him while he was working in his palm trees, so he came running until he caught up with the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'Welcome to the Prophet of God and those with him.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, this is not the time you used to come to me.' So the Prophet ﷺ returned, and he went to a cluster of dates and cut it down. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'What did you intend by this?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, I wanted you to eat from its fresh dates, its half-ripe dates, and its dry dates. And I will surely slaughter an animal for you along with it.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'If you slaughter, do not slaughter a milch animal.' So he took a young goat or kid of his and slaughtered it, and said to his wife: 'Bake bread, and I will cook. You know more about baking.' He set to work on half of the kid and cooked it, and roasted the other half. When the food was ready, it was placed before the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions. The Messenger of God ﷺ took some of the kid and placed it on a loaf, and said: 'O Abu Ayyub, take this to Fatimah, for she has not had anything like this for days.' When they had eaten and were full, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Bread and meat and half-ripe dates and dry dates and fresh dates,' and his eyes filled with tears. Then he said: 'This is the comfort about which you will be asked on the Day of Resurrection.' That weighed heavily on his companions, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'When you obtain something like this and stretch out your hands, say: In the name of God and the blessing of God. And when you are full, say: Praise be to God who has fed us and quenched our thirst and bestowed blessings and favored us. For this is sufficient with this.' The Messenger of God ﷺ used never to have someone do him a known favor without wishing to repay him, so he said to Abu Ayyub: 'Come to us tomorrow.' Abu Ayyub did not hear him, so Umar said to him: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ is ordering you to come to him.' When he came to him, he gave him a slave girl, saying: 'O Abu Ayyub, take good care of her, for we have seen nothing but good as long as she was with us.' When Abu Ayyub brought her home, he said: 'I find no better way to fulfill the Messenger of God's ﷺ instruction than to set her free.' So he set her free."],[2240,"I will not find any of you placing one leg over the other and then singing, while neglecting to recite Surah al-Baqarah."],[2241,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, a man who is the protector of his people and defends his companions, will his share be like the share of others?' He said: 'May your mother lose you! Are you provided for and given victory except through your weak ones?'"],[2242,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray leaning against a palm trunk. A Roman passed by and said: 'If Muhammad would invite me, I would make for him something more comfortable than this.' She said: So he was invited on behalf of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he made for him a pulpit with four steps. The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit and gave a sermon, and the trunk moaned as a she-camel moans. The Messenger of God ﷺ came down to it and said: 'What is the matter with you? If you wish, I will call upon God to return you to your place, and if you wish, I will call upon God to admit you to Paradise and you will bear fruit there, so that the sent prophets of God and His righteous servants may eat from your fruit.' He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Yes.' Then the trunk sank into the ground and vanished."],[2243,"Any man who declares another man an unbeliever, if he is indeed an unbeliever, then it is so; otherwise the one who said it has become an unbeliever."],[2244,"I entered Paradise and heard a sound in front of me. It was said: 'This is Bilal.' And I saw Umm Sulaym bint Milhan in Paradise."],[2245,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Umm Atiyyah: 'When you circumcise, cut a small part and do not excise, for that is brighter for the face and more pleasing to the husband.'"],[2246,"I witnessed Ali on the pulpit adjuring the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'Whoever heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say what he said on the day of Ghadir Khumm, let him testify.' Twelve men stood up, among them Abu Sa'id, Abu Hurayrah, and Anas b. Malik, and they testified that they heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever's mawla I am, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be an enemy to whoever shows enmity to him.'"],[2247,"Obedience to God is obedience to the father, and disobedience to God is disobedience to the father."],[2248,"The excellence of Aishah over other women is like the excellence of tharid over all other foods."],[2249,"My Ummah is a Ummah to whom mercy is shown: they will not be punished in the Hereafter. On the Day of Resurrection, a man from the Jews or the Christians will be given to every Muslim man, and it will be said: “O Muslim, this is your ransom from the Fire.”"],[2250,"His grandfather ʿUmayr b. Ḥabīb b. Khumāsha – who had reached puberty during the lifetime of the Prophet ﷺ – gave a bequest to his children, saying: “O my sons, beware of sitting with fools, for sitting with them is a disease. Whoever bears patiently with a fool is pleased, and whoever answers him regrets. Whoever does not accept the little that a fool offers will accept much [harm]. When any of you wants to command good or forbid evil, let him prepare himself to patiently endure harm and trust in the reward from God, mighty and majestic, for whoever trusts in the reward from God will not be harmed by the touch of injury.”"],[2251,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said to me: “O Aḥnaf, whoever laughs a lot loses dignity; whoever jokes is belittled; whoever does something excessively becomes known for it; whoever talks a lot makes many slips; whoever makes many slips loses modesty; whoever loses modesty loses scrupulousness; and whoever loses scrupulousness, his heart dies.”"],[2252,"I went to Umm Salama to console her over [the death of] al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī. She said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ entered and sat on a bed of hers. Fāṭima came to him with a water skin and placed it down. He said: ‘Call Ḥasan, Ḥusayn, and your cousin ʿAlī.’ When they gathered with him, he said: ‘O God, these are my special ones and my household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.’”"],[2253,"Amputation is for [stealing] a quarter of a dinar."],[2254,"There is no prayer except with the Fātiḥa of the Book and two verses along with it."],[2255,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was consoled over his daughter Ruqayya, the wife of ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān, he said: “Praise be to God; burying daughters is one of the noble deeds.”"],[2256,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters that many people do not know whether they are lawful or unlawful. Whoever leaves them is more prudent for his honor and religion, and whoever falls into them is likely to fall into the unlawful, like a shepherd grazing near a sanctuary is likely to enter it. Indeed, every king has a sanctuary, and God’s sanctuary is His prohibitions."],[2257,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, then turned his cloak over and wiped his face with it."],[2258,"He asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Who is it?” He replied: “Me.” He said: “Me, me!” as if he disliked that."],[2259,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about a woman who has a wet dream: does she have to perform ghusl? He said: “Yes, if she finds fluid, she should perform ghusl.”"],[2260,"Two bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ. One of them said: “Who is the best of people, O Muhammad?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “He who lives long and does good deeds.” The other said: “The laws of Islam have become numerous for us; which should we hold to?” He said: “Keep your tongue moist with the remembrance of God.”"],[2261,"A time will come upon the people when whoever does not have yellow and white will not enjoy life."],[2262,"Charity does not decrease wealth. No man forgives an injustice except that Allah increases him in honor thereby, so forgive and Allah will honor you. No man opens a door of begging for himself except that Allah opens a door of poverty upon him."],[2263,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given the Quran and he recites it during the hours of night and day, following what is in it, so a man says: If only Allah had given me the like of what He gave so-and-so, I would recite it as he recites. And a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends and gives charity, and a man says the like of that."],[2264,"Umar bequeathed the land of Khaybar to the poor, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Retain its principal and give its produce in charity, and it will continue to run on that basis to this day.\""],[2265,"The passing away of my nation will be through stabbing and the plague. We said: We know stabbing, but what is the plague? He said: \"The piercing of your enemies among the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom.\""],[2266,"When the verse 'And those who hoard gold and silver' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perish gold and silver!\" They said: What wealth should we acquire? He said: \"A thankful heart, a remembering tongue, and a righteous wife.\""],[2267,"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: \"I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created, scattered, and made, and from every evil eye.\""],[2268,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about His saying: 'Those who are heedless of their prayers.' He said: \"They are those who delay them beyond their proper time.\""],[2269,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was performing ablution, and in front of him was a vessel of about one mudd, and if it increased, it increased little, and if it decreased, it decreased little. He washed his hands, rinsed his mouth and snuffed water three times each, washed his face three times, ran his fingers through his beard, washed his forearms three times each, wiped his head and ears twice each, and washed his feet until he cleansed them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is this how ablution is done? He said: \"This is how my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me.\""],[2270,"A person will be with those whom he loves."],[2271,"The prayer of the penitent is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun."],[2272,"I am Ahmad, Muhammad, the Gatherer, the One who comes last, and the Seal."],[2273,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us wearing a cotton garment as a shawl, with a short spear in his hand, leaning on Usama b. Zayd. He planted it in front of him, then prayed facing it."],[2274,"We have seen ourselves from near. When we performed Hajj, we used to say: 'Here I am, magnifying You with an excuse. These are Zubayd, who have come to You in a shortened manner, cutting through soft ground and rugged mountains. They have left the rivals empty-handed and empty.' And we have seen ourselves standing at the bottom of Muhassir, fearing that the jinn might snatch us away. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to us: 'Move away from the bottom of Urana, for they are your brothers once they have submitted.' And he taught us the talbiya: 'Here I am, O God, here I am. Here I am, You have no partner, here I am. Praise and grace are Yours, and the dominion. You have no partner.'"],[2275,"After me there will be trials in which a man will awaken as a believer and reach evening as a disbeliever, or reach evening as a believer and awaken as a disbeliever.' I said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, which of the men is most rightly guided?' He said: 'A man between these two sanctuaries, among a few, who performs the prayer at its appointed times, performs Hajj and Umra, and remains so until a stray hand reaches him, or a decisive death.'"],[2276,"Al-Zubayr encountered a thief and interceded for him. It was said to him: 'Wait until we bring him to the ruler.' He said: 'If he reaches the ruler, then may God curse the intercessor and the one for whom intercession is made, as the Messenger of God ﷺ said.'"],[2277,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[2278,"Ali b. Abi Talib came out to us in intense heat wearing winter clothes, and he came out to us in winter wearing summer clothes. Then he called for water, drank it, wiped the sweat from his forehead, and returned to his house. I said to my father: 'O father, did you not see what the Commander of the Believers did? He came out to us in winter wearing summer clothes, and he came out to us in summer wearing winter clothes.' Abu Layla said: 'I did not notice.' So he took his father's hand and went to Ali, and told him what he had done. Ali said to him: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me while I had sore eyes, and he spat into my eyes and said: \"Open your eyes.\" I opened them, and I have not suffered from them until this hour. And he prayed for me, saying: \"O God, remove from him heat and cold.\" So I have felt neither heat nor cold until this day of mine.'"],[2279,"I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck up hair or clothing."],[2280,"The prayer of the congregation exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-some, or twenty-five."],[2281,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon and said: 'Tamim al-Dari told me that he sailed the sea with some of his people, and the wind drove them to an island in the sea. There they came upon a shaggy beast. They said: \"What are you?\" It said: \"I am al-Jassasa.\"'"],[2282,"Whoever is asked about knowledge that he knows and conceals it will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."],[2283,"Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If it is obscured to you, complete the number of thirty."],[2284,"There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, no prayer for one who has no purification, and no religion for one who has no prayer. The position of prayer in the religion is like the position of the head in the body."],[2285,"Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, raisins for raisins, salt for salt, like for like, hand to hand. Whoever gives more or takes more has engaged in riba."],[2286,"No one among you will have his deeds save him. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: Not even I, unless God envelops me with mercy and grace. If He were to take me to task for what these have committed, He would destroy me."],[2287,"God, Blessed and Exalted, has ninety-nine names. Whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."],[2288,"No human does a deed more saving from punishment than the remembrance of God. It was said: Not even jihad in the way of God? He said: Not even jihad, unless you strike with your sword until it breaks."],[2289,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us while we were sitting, and said: The first of you to reach me at the Pool will be the one with the longest hand. So we began measuring our arms to see which of us had the longest hand. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: That is not what I mean; I mean the most generous of you in hand."],[2290,"Fudayk went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, they claim that whoever does not emigrate is ruined. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: O Fudayk, establish the prayer, pay the zakat, shun evil, and dwell wherever you wish in the land of your people."],[2291,"I acquired land in Khaybar such that I had never acquired property more precious to me. I said: O Messenger of God, I have acquired land in Khaybar such that I have never acquired property more beloved to me, and I intend to give it as charity. He said: Retain its original and give its produce as charity."],[2292,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubruma. He said: And who is Shubruma? The man said: A man who instructed me to perform Hajj on his behalf. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubruma."],[2293,"God does not take away knowledge by snatching it away from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give rulings without knowledge, and they go astray and lead others astray."],[2294,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr or Asr and gave salutation after two rak'ahs. Dhu al-Yadayn said: Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? The Prophet ﷺ said: What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying? They said: He has spoken the truth. Then he completed the two rak'ahs with them, then he prostrated two prostrations of forgetfulness while sitting after he had already given salutation."],[2295,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the Day of Conquest, and around the Ka'bah there were three hundred and sixty idols. He began piercing them, and they fell on their faces, while he said: Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is bound to perish."],[2296,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he passed by a village of ants that had been burned. He said: It is not appropriate for anyone to punish with the punishment of God, Mighty and Majestic."],[2297,"Gold for silver is usury unless it is hand to hand."],[2298,"The Prophet ﷺ went to a water-skin of theirs, bent its mouth, and drank while standing."],[2299,"Rabah b. Zayd narrated to us, from Abdullah b. Sa'id b. Abi Asim, from Wahb b. Munabbih, from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[2300,"I entered upon Abu al-Tufayl Amir b. Wathila and found him in good spirits. I said, 'O Abu al-Tufayl, tell me who are the group whom the Messenger of God ﷺ cursed?' He was about to tell me when his wife Sawda said, 'Enough, O Abu al-Tufayl. Has it not reached you that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O God, I am only a human being. Whichever believing servant I have invoked against, make it a purification and mercy for him\"?'"],[2301,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I want to go on jihad.' He said, 'Are your parents alive?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then strive in serving them.'"],[2302,"Among what people have retained from the words of earlier prophethood is: 'If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[2303,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from reciting while I was in a state of major ritual impurity, and he forbade me—and I do not say he forbade you—from wearing garments dyed with safflower, from purple saddle cushions, from wearing gold rings, and from wearing qassi fabric."],[2304,"None of you should say, 'My soul has become evil,' but let him say, 'My soul has become weary.'"],[2305,"The Messenger of God ﷺ heard disputants at his door, so he went out to them and said, 'I am only a human being, and litigants come to me. Perhaps some of them is more eloquent in his argument than others, and I judge in his favor, thinking he is truthful. Whoever I judge in favor of with the right of a Muslim, it is only a piece of the Fire; let him take it or leave it.'"],[2306,"It is not appropriate for anyone to say, 'I am better than Yunus b. Matta.'"],[2307,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered with Mariya al-Qibtiyya, his concubine, into the house of Hafsa bt. Umar, and she found her with him. She said, 'O Messenger of God, in my house among the houses of your wives?' He said, 'She is forbidden to me to touch, O Hafsa, and keep this secret for me.' She went out until she came to Aisha and said, 'O daughter of Abu Bakr, shall I give you good news?' She said, 'About what?' She said, 'I found Mariya with the Messenger of God ﷺ in my house. I said, \"O Messenger of God, in my house among the houses of your wives? And with me you do this among your wives?\" The first joy was that he forbade her to himself. Then he said to me, \"O Hafsa, shall I give you good news?\" I said, \"Yes, by my father and mother, O Messenger of God.\" He informed me that your father will assume authority after him, and that my father will assume it after your father, and he made me keep it secret, so keep it secret.' Then God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning that: 'O Prophet, why do you prohibit what God has made lawful for you,' meaning Mariya, 'seeking the pleasure of your wives,' meaning Hafsa, 'and God is Forgiving, Merciful,' meaning for what you did. 'God has ordained for you the dissolution of your oaths. God is your Protector, and He is the Knowing, the Wise. And when the Prophet confided a matter to one of his wives,' meaning Hafsa, 'and she disclosed it,' meaning to Aisha, 'and God made it known to him,' that is, through the Quran, 'he acknowledged part of it,' Hafsa acknowledged what she had revealed about the matter of Mariya, 'and turned away from part,' from what she had informed about Abu Bakr and Umar, and did not reproach her for it. 'When he informed her of it, she said, \"Who told you this?\" He said, \"The Knowing, the Aware has informed me.\"' Then he turned to her, reproaching her, and said, 'If you two repent to God, your hearts have inclined, but if you support one another against him, then indeed God is his Protector, and Gabriel, and the righteous of the believers,' meaning Abu Bakr and Umar, 'and the angels after that are supporters. Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you, will give him in exchange wives better than you—Muslim, believing, devout, repentant, worshipping, fasting, previously married and virgins.' He promised him from the previously married: Asiya bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh, and the sister of Nuh, and from the virgins: Maryam bt. Imran and the sister of Musa (peace be upon them)."],[2308,"How amazing is the believer and his distress at illness! If he knew what he has in illness, he would love to be ill forever.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head to the sky and laughed. It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, why did you raise your head to the sky and laugh?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I marveled at two angels who were looking for a servant in a prayer place where he used to be, but they did not find him. So they returned and said: 'Our Lord, Your servant so-and-so: we used to record for him, each day and night, the deeds he used to do. We found that You had detained him in Your ropes.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'Write for My servant the deeds he used to do each day and night, and do not diminish anything from them. Upon Me is the reward for what I detained him from, and for him is the reward for what he used to do.'\""],[2309,"\"O boy, shall I not gift you? Shall I not grant you? Shall I not give you?\" He said: I said: \"Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: I thought he would give me a piece of wealth. He said: \"Four rak'ahs that you pray every day. If you cannot, then every Friday. If you cannot, then every month. If you cannot, then every year. If you cannot, then once in your lifetime: you say the takbir, then recite the Mother of the Qur'an (al-Fatihah) and a surah. Then you say: 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great' fifteen times. Then you bow, and you say it ten times. Then you rise, and you say it ten times. Then you prostrate, and you say it ten times. Then you rise, and you say it ten times. Then you prostrate, and you say it ten times. Then you rise, and you say it ten times. Then you do the same in all of your prayer. When you finish, you say after the tashahhud and before the taslim: 'O Allah, I ask You for the success of the people of guidance, the deeds of the people of certainty, the sincerity of the people of repentance, the determination of the people of patience, the earnestness of the people of watchfulness, the seeking of the people of longing, the worship of the people of piety, and the knowledge of the people of learning until I fear You. O Allah, I ask You for fear that restrains me from disobeying You, so that I may act in obedience to You with deeds that make me deserving of Your pleasure, and that I may be sincere to You in repentance out of fear of You, and that I may purify my counsel for You out of love for You, and that I may rely upon You in all matters with good thoughts of You. Glory be to the Creator of the Fire.'\" If you do that, O Ibn 'Abbas, Allah will forgive your sins: small and large, old and new, secret and open, deliberate and mistaken.\""],[2310,"It was said to him: \"We see you wearing sandals made of tanned leather (sibtiyyah).\" He said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing them.\""],[2311,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us, and two men stepped over to him: a man from the Ansar and a man from Thaqif. The Ansari beat the Thaqafi to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the Thaqafi: \"The Ansari has beaten you to the question.\" The Ansari said: \"Perhaps, O Messenger of Allah, he is more eager than I, so he is released [from any blame].\" He said: Then the Thaqafi asked him about prayer, and he informed him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the Ansari: \"If you wish, I will tell you what you came to ask about, and if you wish, you may ask me and I will inform you.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you tell me.\" He said: \"You came to ask me about the reward you have when you head to the Ancient House (the Ka'bah), the reward for standing at 'Arafah, the reward for throwing the pebbles, the reward for shaving your head, and the reward when you bid farewell to the House.\" The Ansari said: \"By the One who sent you with truth, I came to ask about nothing else.\" He said: \"When you head to the Ancient House, you do not lift a foot or put one down, you or your mount, except that a good deed is written for you and a degree raised for you. As for your standing at 'Arafah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says to His angels: 'O My angels, what has brought My servants?' They say: 'They came seeking Your pleasure and the Garden.' Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: 'I call Myself and My creation to witness that I have forgiven them as many as the days of eternity, the number of rain drops, and the number of grains of sand in 'Alij.' As for your throwing the pebbles, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: 'No soul knows what joy is hidden for them as a reward for what they used to do.' As for shaving your head, there is not a hair of yours that falls to the ground except it will be light for you on the Day of Resurrection. As for the House when you bid farewell, you will depart from your sins like the day your mother gave birth to you.\""],[2312,"I said to Ibn 'Umar: \"When you head to Makkah, you pray on your mount. Why do you do that?\" He said: \"Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing it, I would not do it.\""],[2313,"When the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah, the people of Makkah said: \"Muhammad's companions are afflicted with hunger and thinness.\" So the Prophet ﷺ ordered them to run during the first three circuits to show them that they had strength. They used to run three circuits and walk four."],[2314,"Mu'awiyah circumambulated the House and began to touch all the corners. Ibn 'Abbas said to him: \"Why do you touch these two corners when the Prophet ﷺ did not touch them?\" Mu'awiyah said: \"No part of the House is abandoned.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"Indeed, you have in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example.\" Mu'awiyah said: \"You have spoken the truth.\""],[2315,"Had it not been that your people were recent in disbelief, I would have demolished the House and added to it what was diminished from it, placed it on the ground, and made for it two doors: a door to enter from and a door to exit from, so that there would be no crowding."],[2316,"Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like, weight for weight."],[2317,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ on the pulpit forbidding gold for gold and silver for silver except weight for weight."],[2318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on the day of 'Arafah at 'Arafat."],[2319,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rak'ahs."],[2320,"When one of you is asked by his neighbor to fix a piece of wood into his wall, he should not refuse him."],[2321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the earnings of a prostitute and the stud fee of a stallion."],[2322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sale by deception (gharar)."],[2323,"The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer."],[2324,"Fast when you see it (the new moon), and break your fast when you see it. If it is obscured from you, then complete the month as thirty days."],[2325,"I hear the crying of a child behind me while I am in prayer, so I shorten my prayer for fear that his mother may be distressed."],[2326,"The one addicted to wine will not enter Paradise, nor the one who reminds others of his favors to God, nor the one who is disobedient to his parents."],[2327,"The food of two persons is sufficient for four, and the food of four persons is sufficient for eight."],[2328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed eight rak'ahs together and seven rak'ahs together while he was resident, not traveling. I asked: Where was this? He said: In Madinah."],[2329,"The trustworthy ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ knew that Ibn Umm 'Abd was among the closest of them to God as a means of approach."],[2330,"Whoever flays the back of a Muslim without right will meet God while He is angry with him."],[2331,"Blessed is the one who controls his tongue, whose house is spacious for him, and who weeps over his sin."],[2332,"Whoever slaps his slave without right, its expiation is to set him free."],[2333,"Whoever marries a woman for her status, God will only increase him in humiliation; and whoever marries her for her wealth, God will only increase him in poverty; and whoever marries her for her lineage, God will only increase him in baseness. But whoever marries a woman only to lower his gaze, to guard his chastity, or to maintain his kinship ties, God will bless her for him and bless him for her."],[2334,"Look at those who are lower than you, and do not look at those above you, for that is more likely that you will not belittle the blessing of God, Mighty and Majestic."],[2335,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to eat horse meat, and he forbade us from the meat of donkeys."],[2336,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was commanding us to perform the ritual bath on Friday from the pulpit."],[2337,"Some Arabs used to bring us meat, and we felt uneasy about it. We mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'Make them swear that they slaughtered it, then mention the name of God and eat.'"],[2338,"When one of you writes to someone, let him begin with his name, and when he writes, let him sprinkle dust on his letter, for that is more likely to succeed."],[2339,"Whoever prays the Friday prayer and fasts that day, visits a sick person, attends a funeral, and witnesses a marriage, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."],[2340,"Whoever dies while stationed in the path of God, God will protect him from the trial of the grave."],[2341,"Whoever frightens a believer without right, it is incumbent upon God not to protect him from the terrors of the Day of Resurrection."],[2342,"There will be men from my nation who eat varieties of food, drink varieties of drink, wear varieties of clothing, and speak with affectation in their speech. Those are the worst of my nation."],[2343,"I asked ʿAʾishah: 'When you traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ and performed Hajj or went on a military campaign with him, what would you prepare for him as provisions?' She said: 'I would prepare for him a bottle of oil, a comb, a mirror, scissors, a kohl container, and a toothstick.'"],[2344,"I said: O Messenger of God, direct me to a deed that will admit me into Paradise. He said: Do not get angry, and Paradise is yours."],[2345,"Everything has a master, and the master of a gathering is the spot facing the qiblah."],[2346,"The one who raises his head before the imam and puts it down is not safe from God turning his head into the head of a donkey."],[2347,"Your mother and your father, and your sister and your brother, and then the next closest and the next closest."],[2348,"He did not consider stipulating conditions in Hajj to be anything, and he would say: Sufficient for you is the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ."],[2349,"Whoever is hungry or in need and conceals it from people and lays it before God, Mighty and Majestic, it is incumbent upon God, Mighty and Majestic, to open for him a good lawful provision."],[2350,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, God will gather the creatures on one plain, then He will raise for each people the deities they used to worship, and they will lead them into the Fire. The monotheists will remain, and it will be said to them: What are you waiting for? They will say: We are waiting for a Lord whom we used to worship unseen. It will be said to them: Do you recognize Him? They will say: If He wills, He will make Himself known to us. Then He, Blessed and Exalted, will manifest Himself to them, and they will fall down prostrating to Him. It will be said to them: O people of monotheism, raise your heads, for God has made Paradise incumbent for you, and He has placed in the Fire a Jew or a Christian in place of every man."],[2351,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set the waiting period of Barirah as the waiting period of a divorced woman."],[2352,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would not pray while he felt something in his stomach."],[2353,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one night in Ramadan while the people were praying, and said: Let not some of you recite loudly over others, for that harms the one praying."],[2354,"The generous person is near to God, far from the Fire, near to Paradise, and near to people. The miser is far from God, far from Paradise, far from people, and near to the Fire. A generous ignorant person is more beloved to God, Mighty and Majestic, than a miserly worshipper."],[2355,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the prescribed prayer sitting on the ground, and he sat during the glorification on the ground, gesturing with a slight motion."],[2356,"He gave the Prophet ﷺ the good news of al-Abbas's acceptance of Islam, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed him."],[2357,"I caught a bird in Banu Harithah, and Rafi' b. Khadij took it from me and released it, saying: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made unlawful what lies between the two lava fields of Madinah.'"],[2358,"I said to my father: 'O father, who was the man who rescued you from the polytheists on the day they struck you?' He said: 'That was al-'As b. Wa'il al-Sahmi.'"],[2359,"Ka'b b. 'Ujrah met me and said: 'Shall I give you a gift?' I said: 'Yes, give it to me.' He said: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah, how should we invoke blessings upon you, the people of the household? For we have already learned how to greet you.' He said: 'Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'"],[2360,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the night prayer, and he said: 'Two by two.'"],[2361,"'Perish gold and silver!' He said it three times. 'Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what wealth should we acquire?' He said: 'A remembering tongue, a grateful heart, and a believing wife.'"],[2362,"When he delivered the Friday sermon, he would say: 'When one of you sets out for Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl.'"],[2363,"She is not lawful for the first husband until the other has tasted her honey."],[2364,"Seventy thousand of my community will enter Paradise without reckoning. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, who are they?' He said: 'Those who do not seek ruqya, do not cauterize, do not believe in omens, and upon their Lord they rely.'"],[2365,"The Prophet ﷺ said to al-Ashajj, Ashajj 'Abd al-Qays: 'You have two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation.'"],[2366,"A sword from Najran was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ. When it came to him, he gave it to Muhammad b. Maslamah and said: 'Fight with this in the path of Allah. When the necks of the people differ, strike the stone with it, then enter your house and remain like a thrown saddlecloth until an erring hand kills you or an appointed death comes to you.'"],[2367,"If you were not to sin, Allah would bring a people who sin, then seek Allah's forgiveness, and He would forgive them."],[2368,"O ‘A’ishah, beware of the sins that are deemed insignificant, for they have a seeker from Allah."],[2369,"She saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the morning of the Jamrah [i.e., the day of stoning at Mina] saying: ‘O people, none of you should kill one another, and throw pebbles like the small stones of khadhf [i.e., pebbles used for throwing].’"],[2370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the dwellings of Banu ‘Amr b. ‘Awf on a Wednesday, and he saw fortifications around their wealth and lands that he had not seen before. He said to them: ‘O assembly of the Ansar.’ They replied: ‘At your service, O Messenger of Allah, with our fathers and mothers [as ransom] for you.’ He said: ‘Would you, when you descend for your festival—meaning Friday—stay until you hear my words?’ They said: ‘Yes, O Messenger of Allah, with our fathers and mothers [as ransom] for you.’ When Friday came, they attended the Friday prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he finished and performed two voluntary rak‘ahs at his place of prayer. Before that, when he prayed Friday, he would go to his house and pray those two rak‘ahs there. But on that day, he performed them as voluntary prayers in the mosque. When he finished, he turned to face them, and the Ansar followed him from the mosque until they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to them: ‘O assembly of the Ansar.’ They said: ‘At your service, O Messenger of Allah, with our fathers and mothers [as ransom] for you.’ He said: ‘In the time of ignorance, when Allah was not worshipped, you used to carry the burden [i.e., assist the weak] with your wealth, do good deeds, and maintain ties of kinship. Then when Allah blessed you with Islam and Muhammad ﷺ came, you began to fortify [your gardens]. In what the son of Adam eats there is reward, in what the bird eats there is reward, and in what the beast of prey eats there is reward.’ The people departed, and none remained except that he demolished two or three breaches in his wealth—meaning he demolished parts of the walls of their orchards—so that the poor could enter and eat from the dates."],[2371,"Regarding His saying [in the Qur’an]: ‘By your life’ (la-‘amruka), he said: ‘[It means] by your life, O Muhammad.’"],[2372,"I entered upon Umm Salamah in Madinah, and between me and her was a veil. I heard her say: The most frequent supplication of the Prophet ﷺ was: ‘O Turner of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.’ He said: ‘There is no human being except that his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful. If He wills, He causes it to deviate, and if He wills, He guides it.’"],[2373,"Whoever says in the morning: ‘Glory be to Allah, my Lord, the Magnificent, and with His praise’ one hundred times, and in the evening likewise, no one among creation will match what he brought except someone who says the like of what he said or more."],[2374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never left my house except that he raised his sight to the sky and said: ‘O Allah, I seek refuge in You from leading others astray or being led astray, from causing others to slip or being made to slip, from acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly, and from wronging others or being wronged.’"],[2375,"The guide to good is like the doer of it."],[2376,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a woman, then he entered upon Zaynab bt. Jahsh and fulfilled his need from her. Then he came out and said: ‘The woman comes in the form of a devil and goes in the form of a devil. So whoever finds that [desire], let him go to his wife, for that will subdue what is in his soul.’"],[2377,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be said: ‘O people of the gathering, lower your gaze; Fatimah bt. Muhammad is passing by.’ He said: ‘She will pass by wearing two green garments.’"],[2378,"A man called Shihab was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: ‘Rather, you are Hisham.’"],[2379,"The Prophet ﷺ would come to us, and we would bring him a vessel of ours containing water. He would take a mudd and a half or a third of the mudd of Madinah, and I would pour water for him. He would wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth and nose, wash his face three times, wash his forearms three times each, wipe his head once, wipe his ears, both their outer and inner parts, and purify his feet."],[2380,"When the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution, he wiped his head with the leftover water in his hand, starting from the back of his head, then drawing it down to his neck, then drawing it back to the back of his head."],[2381,"The key to prayer is purification; its prohibition is the takbir; and its release is the taslim."],[2382,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel, which was the faraq."],[2383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from relieving himself under a fruit-bearing tree, and he forbade relieving oneself on the bank of a flowing river."],[2384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade tale-bearing and listening to tale-bearing."],[2385,"A woman asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about purification after menstruation. He said: 'Take your piece of cotton.' She said: 'What should I do with it?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt shy, so Aisha said to her: 'Come to me and I will tell you: pass it over the place where the blood comes out.'"],[2386,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and ran his fingers through his beard."],[2387,"Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection with the color of blood but the fragrance of musk."],[2388,"I seek Allah's forgiveness seventy times a day."],[2389,"If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him immerse it fully, for in one of its wings there is disease and in the other there is a cure."],[2390,"Injury caused by a beast is without liability, and a well is without liability, and on buried treasure one-fifth is due."],[2391,"Whoever buys a sheep that has been left unmilked for some time has the option for three days: if he wishes, he may return it along with a saa' of food, not wheat."],[2392,"Three are those whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, and theirs will be a painful punishment: a man who came to a people upon an inclusive Islam, then broke their staff until they deemed the sacred things lawful and shed blood, and an oppressive ruler.\" And he said: \"Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah."],[2393,"Whoever begs while he has forty dirhams or their equivalent is importunate, and that is like the lapping of water."],[2394,"Gabriel kept exhorting me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[2395,"Take the Quran from four: two men from the Emigrants and two men from the Helpers: from Abd Allah b. Masud, Salim the mawla of Abu Hudhayfa, Ubayy b. Kab, and Muadh b. Jabal.\" And he singled out Abd Allah b. Masud with a word, saying: \"Whoever wishes to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite according to the recitation of Ibn Masud."],[2396,"O Muawiya b. Hudayj, beware of hating us, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: No one hates us or envies us except that he will be driven away from the Pool on the Day of Resurrection with whips of fire."],[2397,"Tufayl b. Amr al-Dawsi came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, would you like a fortified stronghold and protection? He meant a stronghold that belonged to Daws in pre-Islamic times. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ declined that because of what Allah had reserved for the Helpers. When the Prophet ﷺ emigrated to Madinah, Tufayl b. Amr emigrated to him, and a man from his people emigrated with him. The man found the climate of Madinah unsuited to him and became distressed. He took some broad-bladed arrows he had and cut his finger joints with them, and his hands bled profusely until he died. Tufayl b. Amr saw him in his sleep, in a good appearance, covering his hands. He said: What did your Lord do with you? He said: He forgave me because of my emigration to His Prophet ﷺ. He said: Why do I see you covering your hands? He said: It was said to me: We will not repair what you corrupted. Tufayl related this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Allah, and for his hands, forgive."],[2398,"The letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in the land of Juhayna two months before his death: that you should not make use of any part of the dead animal, neither hide nor sinew."],[2399,"A sheep belonging to Maymuna died, so we tanned its skin and used to make nabidh in it until it became a worn-out waterskin."],[2400,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate against four individuals, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"Not for you is the decision whether He turns to them or punishes them, for indeed they are wrongdoers.\" Then Allah guided them to Islam."],[2401,"Indeed, the people of the Fire will grow for the Fire until the distance between the lobe of one of his ears and his shoulder becomes a seven-hundred-year journey, the thickness of his skin is forty cubits, and his molar is greater than Uhud."],[2402,"Whoever would like Allah to enlarge his provision and extend his lifespan, let him maintain his ties of kinship."],[2403,"He used to drink in three breaths."],[2404,"He met the Prophet ﷺ and came upon a grave whose occupant was being punished. He said: \"This one used to eat the flesh of people.\" Then he called for a fresh palm stalk and placed it on the grave, and said: \"Perhaps it will be lightened for him as long as this remains fresh.\""],[2405,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the sermon of need: \"Praise be to Allah; we praise Him and seek His help. Whomever Allah guides, none can lead astray, and whomever He leads astray, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. O you who believe, fear Allah and speak a right word...\" [to the end of the verse]; \"O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims\"; \"O people, fear your Lord, who created you from one soul...\" [to the end of the verse]."],[2406,"I saw the Ansar doing something for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ such that I did not see any one of them except that I loved him for it."],[2407,"The king of the Byzantines sent gifts to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and among what he sent was a jar containing ginger. He gave every person a piece, and he gave me a piece."],[2408,"A Jewish woman brought a poisoned sheep to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ate from it. She was brought, and it was said: \"Shall we not kill her?\" He said: \"No.\" And I continued to recognize it in the palate of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2409,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ receiving the pledge of allegiance from the people at Qarn Masfalah. Men, women, young and old came to him and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam and the shahada. I said: \"What is the shahada?\" Muhammad b. al-Aswad informed me, saying: \"Upon the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\""],[2410,"Complete the rows, for if there is any deficiency, it is in the back."],[2411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade solid silk, but if either its warp or its weft is silk, there is no harm in wearing it. And he forbade silver vessels."],[2412,"The best of days with Allah is the Day of Sacrifice, then the Day of Resting, in which the people settle, and it is the day following the sacrifice. Five or six sacrificial camels were brought before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they began vying toward him, as to which of them he would begin with. When their sides fell, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said a low word that I did not understand. I said to the man beside me: \"What did he say?\" He said: \"Whoever wishes may cut a piece.\""],[2413,"On the day of Khaybar, he forbade every fanged beast of prey and every taloned bird, and he forbade the mujaththama (animals killed by being held and thrown), and that pregnant captives be had intercourse with until they give birth to what is in their wombs."],[2414,"The Prophet ﷺ took a hair from the war booty and said: \"I have no right to this except what any one of you has, except the fifth, and it is returned to you. So return the thread and the needle, and beware of embezzlement, for it is disgrace, shame, and fire.\""],[2415,"I was a boy carrying the limb of a camel, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributing meat at al-Ji'ranah. A woman came to him, and he spread his cloak for her. I said: \"Who is this?\" It was said: \"His mother who nursed him.\""],[2416,"The best rows of men are the first ones, and the worst are the last ones; the best rows of women are the last ones, and the worst are the first ones."],[2417,"Whoever says, “There is no god but Allah,” will enter Paradise."],[2418,"Prayer on the back of a mount is like this and this and this."],[2419,"The delay in payment by a rich man makes his honour liable to be injured and renders him liable to punishment."],[2420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me to recite poetry, saying: “Do you relate any of the poetry of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt?” I recited to him one hundred rhyming lines, and each time I passed a verse, he would say, “Go on.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He almost submitted in his poetry.”"],[2421,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Do you know which day this is?” She said: He was referring to the day that they call the Day of Heads. They said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “This is the middle of the Days of Tashriq.” He said: “Do you know which land this is?” They said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “This is the Sacred Mash‘ar.” Then he said: “I may not meet you after this year of mine. Verily, your blood, your wealth, and your honour are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, until you meet your Lord and He asks you about your deeds. So let those of you who are present convey to those who are absent. Have I conveyed the message?” When we arrived in Madinah, we did not remain but a short time until he died ﷺ."],[2422,"Whoever does not ask Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, He becomes angry with him."],[2423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ‘Ali on an expedition, and I saw him raising his hands and saying: “O Allah, do not let me die until You show me ‘Ali.”"],[2424,"Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under Allah’s protection, so beware lest Allah demand from you anything of His protection."],[2425,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping while fasting and in the state of ihram."],[2426,"He forbade breaking the valid currency of the Muslims that circulates among them except for a necessary reason, such as breaking a dirham to turn it into silver, or breaking a dinar to turn it into gold."],[2427,"He forbade combing the hair except every other day."],[2428,"Umar went out to pray for rain, and he brought al-Abbas with him to pray for rain. He said: 'O Allah, when we suffered drought in the time of our Prophet, we sought intercession through Your Prophet. O Allah, now we seek intercession through the uncle of Your Prophet ﷺ.'"],[2429,"The inscription on the ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was three lines: one line 'Muhammad', one line 'Messenger', and one line 'Allah'."],[2430,"Before the Hour there will be trials like patches of dark night, in which a man will wake up a believer and become an unbeliever by evening, and people will sell their religion for a paltry worldly gain."],[2431,"When one of you enters upon his brother and he offers him food, let him eat and not ask about it; and if he offers him a drink, let him drink and not ask about it."],[2432,"Whoever cuts down a lote tree, Allah will plunge his head into the Fire."],[2433,"Regarding the building of the Kaaba, he said: 'When they saw the Prophet ﷺ enter through the door, they said: \"The trustworthy one has come.\"'"],[2434,"Three will not enter Paradise, and three Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection. As for the three who will not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the cuckold, and the woman who imitates men. As for the three whom Allah will not look at: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the habitual drinker of wine, and the one who reminds others of his gifts."],[2435,"Abu Tayba cupped the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Uyayna b. Hisn or al-Aqra b. Habis entered upon him and said: 'What is this?' He said: 'This is cupping, and it is the best of the remedies you use.'"],[2436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while in ihram because of a pain he felt in his head."],[2437,"We used to come to the Prophet ﷺ, and when something of the Quran was revealed to him, he would tell us. One day he said to us: 'Allah, the Exalted, said: \"We have sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakat. If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would seek a second, and if he had a second, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. And Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents.\" '"],[2438,"When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was taken on the night journey and then morning came in Makkah, he sat apart in sorrow. The enemy of Allah Abu Jahl came to him and said mockingly: 'Has anything happened?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What?' He said: 'I was taken on a night journey to Jerusalem.' He said: 'And then you woke up among us?' He said: 'Yes.' He did not show that he disbelieved him, fearing that if he called his people, they would reject the story. He said: 'What if I call your people? Will you tell them what you told me?' He said: 'Yes.' Abu Jahl said: 'Tell your people what you told me.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'I was taken on a night journey last night.' They said: 'To where?' He said: 'To Jerusalem.' They said: 'And then you woke up among us?' He said: 'Yes.' Some clapped, some put their hands on their heads in astonishment at the lie, as they claimed. Among the people were some who had traveled to that mosque. He said: 'Can you describe the mosque for us?' He said: 'Yes.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'I described it to them until some of the description became unclear to me. Then the mosque was brought and placed before me, and I looked at it, and I continued to describe it to them while looking at it, until it was placed near the house of Aqil—or the house of Iqal.' The people said: 'As for the description, by Allah, he has got it right.'"],[2439,"A man may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise for seventy years, and then his life is sealed with a deed of the people of the Fire, and he becomes one of the people of the Fire. And a servant may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire for seventy years, and then his life is sealed with a deed of the people of Paradise, and he becomes one of the people of Paradise."],[2440,"I enjoin a man to be good to his mother, I enjoin a man to be good to his father, I enjoin a man to be good to his patron who is close to him, even if he has from him something that harms him."],[2441,"Whoever is given a gift while there are people with him, they are his partners in it."],[2442,"I went early to the Messenger of God ﷺ and we sat at the door. He heard two men disagreeing about a verse, so he came out to us with anger recognizable on his face and said: Those before you were destroyed only because of their frequent disagreement."],[2443,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into solid ghee. He said: Take what is under it and around it and throw it away, then eat the rest."],[2444,"Mercy is not removed except from a wretched person."],[2445,"Three men from those before you went out seeking provision for their families. Rain overtook them, so they took refuge in a mountain or a cave. A rock fell and blocked them. They said to one another: The rock has fallen and the trace is gone, and no one knows your place except God, Mighty and Majestic. Supplicate by the most reliable of your deeds. One of them said: I had parents, and I used to milk for them into a vessel. When I came to them while they were sleeping, I would stand until they woke up, whenever they woke up, and I disliked that their sleep should be disturbed in their heads. When they woke up, they drank. O God, if You know that I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then open a way for us. A third of the rock moved. The second said: O God, if You know that there was a woman who pleased me, and I wanted her, but she refused to let me have her until I gave her a payment. When she took her payment and her self was settled, I left her. O God, if You know that I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then open a way for us. Two-thirds of the rock moved. The third said: O God, if You know that I hired a worker to work for a day, and he worked and came seeking his wages. I gave him, but he did not take it and was dissatisfied, so I invested it for him until it became all kinds of wealth. Then he came seeking his wages, and I said: Take all this. If I wished, I would not have given him except his wages. O God, if You know that I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then open a way for us. The final third of the rock moved, and they went out walking."],[2446,"Seek help in fulfilling needs by keeping them secret, for everyone with a blessing is envied."],[2447,"A man was tending a she-camel of his in front of Uhud when it became ill, so he slaughtered it with a wooden peg. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said: Eat it."],[2448,"He would not leave anything in his house with crosses on it except that he broke it."],[2449,"When a man tells a hadith and then turns away, it is a trust."],[2450,"Whoever drinks from a silver vessel, he only makes fire gurgle in his belly."],[2451,"No vein of a believer is ever struck except that God removes a sin from him by it, writes a good deed for him, and raises a degree for him."],[2452,"The part of the sheep most beloved to the Messenger of God ﷺ is the foreleg, and we used to think that the Jews were the ones who poisoned him in it."],[2453,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[2454,"Whoever is granted a favor should repay it; if he cannot, he should mention it, for if he mentions it he has shown gratitude. One who pretends to have what he has not obtained is like one wearing two garments of falsehood."],[2455,"None hoards except a sinner."],[2456,"He forbade leasing land."],[2457,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from selling what I do not have."],[2458,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had himself cupped and paid the cupper; had it been unlawful, he would not have given him."],[2459,"He used to shorten the prayer between Madinah and Makkah, fearing none but God, mighty and majestic."],[2460,"A funeral procession passed by Ibn Abbas and Hasan b. Ali; one of them stood and the other remained seated. The one standing said to the one seated: “Did the Messenger of God ﷺ not stand?” He replied: “Yes, and he also sat.”"],[2461,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned a people who recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their throats; they pass through the religion as an arrow passes through its target, then they do not return to it."],[2462,"He used to pray standing and sitting; when he prayed standing he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting he bowed sitting."],[2463,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are ambiguous matters. I will strike for you a parable about that: God has protected a sanctuary, and God’s sanctuary is what He has forbidden. Whoever grazes around the sanctuary will soon encroach upon it."],[2464,"Shall I not tell you what 'Ali told me? He said: Among them is one with a defective hand, or a stunted hand, or a hand cut short. Were it not that you would become proud (or heedless), I would inform you of what God has promised those who fight them on the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ. We said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah—he said it three times."],[2465,"The Prophet of God ﷺ used to recite to me this verse: 'And whoever fears God, He will make for him a way out, and provide for him from where he does not expect. And whoever puts his trust in God, then He is sufficient for him' (Quran 65:2-3). He kept repeating it to me until I dozed off. Then he said: 'O Abu Dharr, how will you act when you are expelled from Madinah?' I said: 'I will go to ease and comfort, and I will be like one of the doves of the Haram.' He said: 'How will you act when you are expelled from Makkah?' I said: 'To ease and comfort, to Syria and the Holy Land.' He said: 'How will you act when you are expelled from Syria?' I said: 'Then, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will place my sword upon my shoulder.' He said: 'Or better than that: you will hear and obey, even if he is an Abyssinian slave.'"],[2466,"I said to 'A'ishah: 'Did the Messenger of God ﷺ pray the Duha prayer?' She said: 'No, except when he returned from a journey.' I said: 'Did he pray sitting?' She said: 'Yes, after the people had worn him down (with age).' I said: 'Did he join the surahs (in prayer)?' She said: 'The Mufassal (the shorter surahs).' I said: 'Did he fast an entire month?' She said: 'I do not know that he fasted an entire month except Ramadan, nor did he break his fast for an entire month such that he would not fast some of it, other than Ramadan.'"],[2467,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me on an errand for him. Then he encountered me while I was going out on the road to Madinah. He took my hand, and we went off until we climbed Uhud. He turned toward Madinah and said: 'Woe to its mother—a town whose people will abandon it when it is at its most fruitful.' I said: 'O Prophet of God, who will eat its fruit?' He said: 'The birds and beasts of prey will eat it. And the Dajjal will not enter it. Whenever he wants to enter it, an angel will meet him at every one of its mountain passes and turn him back.' Then he turned, and when we were at the door of the mosque, there was a man praying. He said: 'He is speaking truthfully.' I said: 'O Prophet of God, this is so-and-so, the most prayerful person in Madinah.' He said: 'Do not let him hear you, or you will destroy him.'"],[2468,"I said to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: 'Write down (hadiths) for us.' He said: 'We will not write for you, nor will we make it a Quran. But take from us as we used to take from the Prophet of God ﷺ.' And Abu Sa'id used to say: 'Narrate (hadiths) to one another, for one hadith reminds of another.'"],[2469,"Disputing about the Quran is disbelief."],[2470,"I asked: 'Did the Messenger of God ﷺ perform Witr at the beginning of the night or at the end?' She said: 'Sometimes he performed Witr at the beginning, and sometimes at the end.' I said: 'God is most great, praise be to God who has made the matter flexible.' I said: 'When he was in a state of major impurity, did he perform the ritual bath at the beginning of the night or at the end?' She said: 'Sometimes he bathed at the beginning, and sometimes at the end.' I said: 'God is most great, praise be to God who has made the matter flexible.' I said: 'Did he recite aloud in his prayer or quietly?' She said: 'Sometimes he recited aloud, and sometimes quietly.' I said: 'God is most great, praise be to God who has made the matter flexible.'"],[2471,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to fast on 'Ashura'."],[2472,"Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom."],[2473,"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."],[2474,"The Prophet ﷺ came out upon a people who had set up a live pigeon as a target and were shooting at it. He said: 'These are the mujaththamah (animals tied up and shot); eating them is not lawful.'"],[2475,"Whoever takes so much as a handspan of land, God will collar him with it from seven earths."],[2476,"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the weak and the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women."],[2477,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ when I was a boy, and I went before him and took his hand for him to accept my pledge of allegiance, but he withdrew it and did not accept my pledge."],[2478,"The sacrificial animal (al-aḍḥā) is an obligation upon me, and it is a sunnah for you."],[2479,"There was a young man who served the Prophet ﷺ and was quick in his needs. He said: \"Ask me for something you need.\" He replied: \"Supplicate for me for Paradise.\" He said: \"So he raised his head and sighed, and said: 'Yes, but help me by making much prostration.'\""],[2480,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by the food sellers and saw good-looking food. He inserted his hand into it, and beneath it was bad food. He said: \"Sell this separately and that separately. Whoever cheats us is not of us.\""],[2481,"A funeral was brought, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Does your companion owe a debt?\" They said: \"Yes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Pray over your companion.\" A man said: \"It is upon me.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over him."],[2482,"Among the sources of piety is your learning what you do not know from what you already know, and falling short in what you already know is a lack of increase in it. Indeed, a man is only made indifferent to knowledge of what he does not know by the little benefit he gains from what he already knows."],[2483,"When you see those who praise excessively, throw dirt in their faces."],[2484,"The Qadariyyah are the Magians of this community. If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend their funerals."],[2485,"Use ithmid (antimony) at bedtime, for it grows hair and clears the vision."],[2486,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a found item. He said: \"Recognize its container and its tying, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes and recognizes its number and its tying, give it to him; otherwise it is yours.\""],[2487,"The servant remains in good as long as he does not become impatient. It was said: O Messenger of God, how does he become impatient? He said: \"He says: I have supplicated and it has not been answered for me.\""],[2488,"Caution does not avail against destiny, and supplication benefits in what has descended and what has not descended. Indeed, supplication meets affliction and they wrestle with one another until the Day of Resurrection."],[2489,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his prayer, he would wipe his forehead with his right hand, then say: \"In the name of God, besides whom there is no god, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. O God, remove from me anxiety and grief.\""],[2490,"O Messenger of God, if I coincide with the Night of Decree, what should I ask God for? He said: Ask Him for well-being."],[2491,"Indeed God, Blessed and Exalted, has detachments of angels who descend and stand over gatherings of remembrance on earth. So come in the morning and evening in the remembrance of God, and remind yourselves of God. Whoever loves to know his station with God, let him look at how God's station is with him, for God, Mighty and Majestic, places the servant with Him where the servant places Him with himself."],[2492,"Verily, the caretakers of the houses of God are the people of God, Mighty and Majestic."],[2493,"I am more knowledgeable of what is with the Dajjal than he. Indeed, with him is a fire that burns and a river of cold water. So whoever encounters him, let him not perish by it. Let him close his eyes and fall into the one he sees as fire, for it is cold water for them."],[2494,"The cover between the eyes of the jinn and the private parts of the children of Adam, when they put off their clothes, is that they say: In the name of God."],[2495,"I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: Do you know Abd Allah b. Umar? He divorced his wife while she was menstruating. Umar asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, and he ordered him to take her back. I said: Does it count as a divorce? He said: Yes. What do you think if he was unable and acted foolishly?"],[2496,"Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy. When he sits with him, it immerses him, and God appoints seventy thousand angels to pray for him until evening."],[2497,"A man used to sell wine in a ship at sea, and he used to mix it with water. With him in the ship was a monkey. The monkey took the purse, climbed with it up the mast, and began emptying a dinar into the ship and a dinar into the water until he divided it into two halves."],[2498,"I was among those who washed Umm Kulthum, daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The first thing the Messenger of God ﷺ gave us was the waist-wrapper, then the shift, then the veil, then the outer wrap, then she was wrapped in the larger garment."],[2499,"O Fāṭimah, arise and witness your sacrifice, for with every drop of its blood you are forgiven every sin you have committed. And say: 'Indeed, my prayer, my rites of sacrifice, my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. And this I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims.' Then ʿImrān said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is this for you and the people of your house specifically, so that you are the ones entitled to it, or for the Muslims generally?' He said, 'Rather, for the Muslims generally.'"],[2500,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not bring his wife into the public bath. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the public bath except with a waist-wrapper. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table on which wine is drunk."],[2501,"I heard Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq ؓ on the pulpit delivering a sermon, saying: 'O people, you recite this verse: \"O you who have believed, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided.\" And indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When people see an evil and do not change it, Allah will soon encompass them all with punishment.\"'"],[2502,"He used to recite over the funeral prayers the Opening of the Book (al-Fātiḥah)."],[2503,"A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ and they praised the deceased with good, so he said, 'It is assured.' Then another funeral procession passed and they spoke ill of it, so he said, 'It is assured.' It was said, 'What is assured?' He said, 'You are Allah's witnesses on earth; if you will, good, and if you will, evil.'"],[2504,"When a man comes to a people and they say, 'Welcome,' then welcome to him on the day he meets his Lord. And when a man comes to a people and they say, 'May you have drought,' then drought for him on the day he meets his Lord."],[2505,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral was brought, and the people praised it with good, so the Prophet ﷺ said, 'It is assured.' Then another was brought, and it seemed the people spoke ill of him, so the Prophet ﷺ said, 'It is assured.' The companions of the Prophet ﷺ said, 'So-and-so was brought and he said, \"It is assured.\" Then so-and-so was brought and he said, \"It is assured.\"' The Prophet ﷺ heard them and said, 'What is this?' ʿUmar said, 'May my father and mother be your ransom. So-and-so was brought and the people praised him greatly, and you said, \"It is assured.\" Then so-and-so was brought and the people spoke ill of him, and you said, \"It is assured.\"' He said, 'Your brother was brought and you testified as you testified, so your testimony became assured. Then your brother so-and-so was brought and you testified as you testified, so your testimony became assured. You are Allah's witnesses on earth, some of you over others.'"],[2506,"I was among those upon whom drowsiness was cast on the day of Uḥud."],[2507,"A man will be given in Paradise the strength of so-and-so many women. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, can he bear that?' He said, 'He will be given the strength of a hundred.'"],[2508,"There is no servant except that he has three friends. As for one friend, he says, 'What you spend is yours, and what you withhold is not yours.' That is his wealth. As for another friend, he says, 'I am with you, but when you come to the king's door, I will leave you.' That is his family and servants. As for another friend, he says, 'I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you leave.' That is his deeds, and he says, 'You were indeed the least of the three to me.'"],[2509,"Indeed in Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years and does not cross it."],[2510,"And from ʿImrān, from Muḥammad b. Ziyād, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it."],[2511,"A man remains in prayer as long as he is in the place of prayer where he prayed, provided he does not invalidate his ablution."],[2512,"He said concerning the Night of Decree: It is the twenty-seventh or twenty-ninth night. On that night, the angels on earth are more numerous than the number of stars."],[2513,"Nothing is more honorable to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than supplication."],[2514,"I gave a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me: \"Have you become a Muslim?\" He said: No. So he said: \"I have been forbidden the gifts of the polytheists,\" and he returned it."],[2515,"Whatever the two revilers say, the sin is upon the one who started, unless the wronged one transgresses."],[2516,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man reviles me, so should I revile him back? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The two revilers are two devils who exchange insults and lies.\""],[2517,"The Prophet ﷺ looked toward Yemen and said: \"O Allah, turn their hearts toward us, and bless us in our sa' and our mudd.\""],[2518,"People wake up in drought, then Allah brings them provision from Himself, and they wake up as polytheists, saying: \"We were given rain because of such-and-such a star.\""],[2519,"\"Beware of the sins that are considered insignificant, for they accumulate against a man until they destroy him.\" Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave them the example of people who camped in a desolate land, and meal time came. So one man brought this, and another brought a small stick, until they gathered a large pile of that, then they kindled a fire, and it cooked whatever was thrown into it."],[2520,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say in the sermon: \"Praise be to Allah; we seek His help and His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our own souls. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead, and whomever He misleads, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has been guided, and whoever disobeys them only harms himself, and will not harm Allah in the least.\""],[2521,"When he feared a people, he would say: \"O Allah, we place You before their necks, and we seek refuge in You from their evils.\""],[2522,"Paradise is of bricks of gold and bricks of silver."],[2523,"When Allah granted Job well-being, He rained upon him locusts of gold, and he began to take them by hand and place them in his garment. It was said to him, 'O Job, are you not satisfied?' He said, 'Who can be satisfied with Your mercy?'"],[2524,"Allah has not sent down any disease but that He sent down for it a cure; those who know it know it, and those who are ignorant of it are ignorant of it, except for sam. It was asked, 'What is sam?' He said, 'Death.'"],[2525,"He used to visit Umm Sulaym, and she would honor him with something she made for him. I had a small brother whose kunya was Abu 'Umayr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came one day and said, 'O Umm Sulaym, why do I see your son heavy-hearted?' She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, his sparrow that he used to play with died.' The Prophet ﷺ began to say, 'O Abu 'Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?'"],[2526,"When he traveled and wanted to offer voluntary prayer, he would face his camel toward the qiblah, say the takbir, and then pray wherever it turned."],[2527,"Love of Quraysh is faith, and hatred of them is disbelief; love of the Arabs is faith, and hatred of them is disbelief. Whoever loves the Arabs has loved me, and whoever hates the Arabs has hated me."],[2528,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one of the two afternoon prayers and prayed two rak'ahs, then said the salam. He went to a piece of wood placed across the mosque, and the people hurried out of the mosque, saying, 'The prayer has been shortened.' Among the people were Abu Bakr and 'Umar, but they were hesitant to speak to him. Among the people was a man called Dhu al-Yadayn, who said, 'O Messenger of Allah, did you forget or has the prayer been shortened?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I did not forget, nor has the prayer been shortened.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says?' They said, 'Yes.' So he came and prayed what remained of his prayer, then said the salam, then said the takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head, then said the takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer. It was said to him, 'Did he [finally] say the salam?' He said, 'I was informed that 'Imran b. Husayn said: He said the salam.'"],[2529,"Guarantee me six things and I will guarantee you Paradise: when one of you speaks, let him not lie; when he promises, let him not break it; when he is entrusted, let him not betray; lower your gazes; guard your private parts; and restrain your hands."],[2530,"Three qualities, whoever has them will find the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else; that he loves a person only for the sake of Allah; and that he would prefer to be thrown into the Fire rather than return to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it."],[2531,"O people, come to your Lord. Indeed, what is little and sufficient is better than what is abundant and distracting. O people, there are only two paths: the path of good and the path of evil. Why would you make the path of evil more beloved to you than the path of good?"],[2532,"O people, guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date."],[2533,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who is a Muslim?' He said, 'One from whose tongue the Muslims are safe.'"],[2534,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[2535,"The Messenger of God ﷺ acquired a gold ring and wore it for three days. Then gold rings became widespread among his Companions, so he discarded it and acquired a silver ring, and engraved on it: “Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” It remained on his hand until he died, on Abu Bakr’s hand until he died, on Umar’s hand until he died, and on Uthman’s hand for six years. When paperwork increased for him, he gave it to a man from the Ansar to seal with it. The man came to a well belonging to Uthman, and it fell into it. They searched for it but did not find it. So he acquired a silver ring and engraved on it: “Muhammad is the Messenger of God.”"],[2536,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited wearing a gold ring."],[2537,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Duba'ah bt. al-Zubayr: Perform Hajj and stipulate: My place of exiting ihram is wherever You confine me."],[2538,"He prohibited prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets."],[2539,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered ihram when his she-camel stood upright with him."],[2540,"The Messenger of God ﷺ continued the talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[2541,"No man gives another man a guarantee of safety for his blood and then kills him, except that the killer is absolved of the slain man."],[2542,"The Prophet ﷺ amputated for a shield."],[2543,"The Prophet ﷺ turned Ma'iz b. Malik away three times."],[2544,"Ma'iz came to the Prophet ﷺ and confessed to adultery. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: Perhaps you kissed, or fondled, or touched. He said: No. He said: Then did you do such-and-such?—not using a euphemism. He said: Yes. So he ordered that he be stoned."],[2545,"I asked Ali: Do you have anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ besides the Quran? He said: No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, except that God, Mighty and Majestic, grants understanding of His Book, or what is in the scroll."],[2546,"He prohibited fasting on the Day of 'Arafah at 'Arafah."],[2547,"Umm al-Harir, when a man from the Arabs died, it became very hard on her. It was said to her, \"O Umm al-Harir, what is the matter with you that when a man from the Arabs dies, it becomes very hard on you?\" She said, \"I heard my master say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, part of the approach of the Hour is the destruction of the Arabs.'\""],[2548,"Milk was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of 'Arafah, so he drank and gave to drink to the one on his right."],[2549,"The two sons of Mulaykah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, our mother used to be mindful of her husband and honor the guest, and she died in the Jahiliyyah. So where is our mother?\" He said, \"Your mother is in the Fire.\" They stood up and that was hard on them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them back, so they returned, and he said, \"My mother is with your mother.\" A man from the hypocrites said, \"And what does this avail his mother at all, while we tread on his heels?\" Then a young man from the Ansar—I have not seen a man who asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more questions than him—said, \"O Messenger of Allah, where is your father?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for them both, and I will indeed stand at the Praised Station.\""],[2550,"He prescribed oil and wars for pleurisy."],[2551,"I bought two slave boys who were brothers, and I wanted to sell one of them and keep the other. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me, saying, \"Sell them both together or keep them both together.\""],[2552,"Whoever fasts the entire year, Allah will constrict Hell for him like this,\" and he closed his fingers upon ninety."],[2553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at a house in which there were a group of Quraysh, and he took hold of the two doorposts, then said, \"Is there anyone in the house except a Qurashi?\" They said, \"No, except a nephew of ours.\" He said, \"The nephew of a people is one of them.\" Then he said, \"Indeed, this matter will continue to be in Quraysh as long as, when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; when they judge, they are just; and when they divide, they are equitable. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither repentance nor ransom will be accepted from him.\""],[2554,"A woman has no authority over her wealth when her husband has taken charge of her marriage bond."],[2555,"He said to 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, \"Do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it upon asking, you will be left to it, but if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it. And if you swear an oath and then see something better than it, expiate for your oath and do that which is better.\""],[2556,"I was sitting with 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud on the day of 'Ashura' and in front of him was a bowl of tharid. Al-Ash'ath b. Qays entered and said, \"Come to the meal, O Abu Muhammad.\" He said, \"Did you not fast this day?\" 'Abd Allah said, \"We used to fast it before Ramadan was revealed. When Ramadan was revealed, we fasted it and abandoned what was other than it.\""],[2557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me saying, \"Go to your people and command them to fast this day,\" meaning the day of 'Ashura'. I said, \"I do not think I will reach them except after they have already eaten.\" He said, \"Then command them to fast the rest of their day.\""],[2558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to venerate the day of 'Ashura', to the extent that he would call for his small children and the suckling infants of Fatimah, and say to their mothers, \"Do not breastfeed them until nightfall,\" and he would put his saliva in their mouths. His saliva sufficed them."],[2559,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'Not equal are those believers who sit [at home], other than those who are disabled'—he said: 'They were a people who, at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, would not go on military expeditions with him because of ailments, pains, and illnesses. Others were healthy. So the sick were more excused than the healthy.'"],[2560,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a group of people passing around an unsheathed sword, so he said: 'May Allah curse the one who did this! Did I not forbid this?'"],[2561,"On the day of Hunayn, I saw something black like a striped cloak between the sky and the earth. When it reached the ground, it spread out in the earth as ants, and the polytheists were routed."],[2562,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Bilal and found with him heaps of dates. He said: 'What is this, O Bilal?' Bilal replied: 'Dates I have stored for you.' He said: 'Woe to you, O Bilal! Do you not fear that they will have a vapor in the Fire? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear scarcity from the Owner of the Throne.'"],[2563,"Three things my beloved Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined upon me; I will never abandon them: fasting three days of every month, performing the ritual bath on Friday, and not sleeping except after praying Witr."],[2564,"'Recite the Quran. When you recite it, do not seek abundance through it, do not go to extremes in it, do not neglect it, and do not earn a living by it.' And he said: 'Women are the inhabitants of the Fire.' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers, sisters, and daughters?' Then he mentioned their ingratitude toward the husband's rights and their neglect of his rights."],[2565,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which sin is greatest?' He said: 'That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you.' I said: 'Then which?' He said: 'That you kill your child fearing that he will eat with you.' I said: 'Then which?' He said: 'That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.' Then he recited: 'And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, and do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, and do not commit adultery.'"],[2566,"Mu'adh b. Jabal used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he would come and lead his people in prayer."],[2567,"He forbade fasting on the day of Fitr and the day of sacrifice."],[2568,"Do not boast about your forefathers who died in the pre-Islamic period. For by the One in whose hand is my soul, the dung beetle rolling its ball with its nose is better than your forefathers who died in the pre-Islamic period."],[2569,"Whoever would like his building to be made prominent for him and his ranks to be raised, let him pardon the one who wronged him, give to the one who deprived him, and maintain ties with the one who cut him off."],[2570,"I came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting among a group of his companions, among them Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ. I caught the end of the hadith while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying: 'Whoever prays four rak'ahs before 'Asr, the Fire will not touch him.' I gestured with my hand like this—moving his hand—: 'This is a good hadith.' Umar b. al-Khattab said to me: 'What you missed from the beginning of the hadith is even better, even better.' I said: 'O Ibn al-Khattab, then bring it.' So Umar b. al-Khattab said."],[2571,"Allah loves that His concessions be acted upon, just as He loves that His strict commands be acted upon."],[2572,"I was among those who went to Umar as part of a delegation. He began asking each man, one by one: \"What tribe are you from? Who are you?\" When he reached me, he said: \"What tribe are you from? Who are you?\" I said: \"I am Hanzala, from Anaza.\" He gestured toward the east, spread his fingers, and said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Anaza is a tribe from here, oppressed yet victorious.'\""],[2573,"Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ at a time other than his usual time. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to meet him and said: \"O Jibril, why do I see your color changed?\" He replied: \"I have not come to you except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has commanded me regarding the keys of the Fire.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Jibril, describe the Fire to me and describe Jahannam to me.\" Jibril said: \"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded Jahannam and it was kindled for a thousand years until it turned white. Then He commanded and it was kindled for a thousand years until it turned red. Then He commanded and it was kindled for a thousand years until it turned black. So it is black and dark; its sparks do not give light, and its flames are not extinguished. By the One who sent you with the truth, if an opening the size of a needle's eye were opened from Jahannam, everyone on earth would die from its heat. By the One who sent you with the truth, if a garment from the garments of the Fire were hung between heaven and earth, everyone on earth would die from its heat. By the One who sent you with the truth, if one of the keepers of Jahannam were to appear before the people of this world and they looked at him, everyone on earth would die from the ugliness of his face and the stench of his odor. By the One who sent you with the truth, if a single link of the chain of the people of the Fire, which Allah described in His Book, were placed on the mountains of this world, they would crumble and not come together again until they reach the lowest earth.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Enough, O Jibril, lest my heart split and I die.\" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at Jibril while he was weeping and said: \"Do you weep, O Jibril, while you are with Allah in the station that you are?\" He said: \"Why should I not weep? I am the most deserving of weeping. Perhaps I am, in Allah's knowledge, not in the state I am currently in, and I do not know; perhaps I will be tested as Iblis was tested, for he was among the angels. And what do I know? Perhaps I will be tested as Harut and Marut were tested.\" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wept and Jibril ﷺ wept, and they continued weeping until they were called: \"O Jibril and O Muhammad, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has granted you both safety from disobeying Him.\" Then Jibril ﷺ ascended, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and passed by a group of the Ansar who were laughing and playing. He said: \"Do you laugh while Jahannam is behind you? If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, and you would not be able to swallow food and drink, and you would go out to the high places crying out to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\" Then he was called: \"O Muhammad, do not make My servants despair. I have sent you as a facilitator, not as one who makes things difficult.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Be moderate and draw near.\""],[2574,"We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not take something for yourself in Mina to shade yourself in?\" He said: \"O Aisha, Mina is the resting place of whoever arrives first.\""],[2575,"\"We have learned how to greet you with peace, so how do we invoke blessings upon you?\" He said: \"Say: O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent prayers and blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.\""],[2576,"\"The best of us after our Prophet ﷺ are Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ.\""],[2577,"\"Shall I not give you a gift that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have learned how to greet you with peace, so how do we invoke blessings upon you?' He said: 'Say: O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent prayers upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'\""],[2578,"\"While we were walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he saw a group of people and said: 'Why have these people gathered?' It was said: 'They are digging a grave.' He said: The Prophet ﷺ was startled and hurried ahead of his companions until he reached the grave. He threw dust onto it and faced it, then he wept ﷺ until the soil was wet from his tears. Then he turned to us and said: 'My brothers, for a day like this, so prepare.'\""],[2579,"\"During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he raised his head from bowing, they would remain standing until they saw him prostrating, having placed his forehead on the ground.\""],[2580,"\"Whoever gives a gift of silver or provides milk to drink, or gives a small skin of water as a gift, it is equal to freeing a slave. And whoever says: 'There is no god but Allah, alone without partner, His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is capable of all things' ten times, it is equal to freeing a slave.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us and wipe our shoulders and chests, saying: \"Do not let your rows differ, lest your hearts differ. Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His angels send blessings upon the first rows.\""],[2581,"\"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Which people are best?' He said: 'My generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then a people will come whose testimony precedes their oath and whose oath precedes their testimony.'\""],[2582,"\"Feed the hungry, visit the sick, and free the captive.\""],[2583,"There is no one but has a jinn companion appointed to him. They said: Even you? He said: “Even me, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, helped me against him, so he submitted. Thus he only commands me to do good.”"],[2584,"Jibril took me by the hand and showed me the gate of Paradise through which my Ummah will enter. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, I wish I had been with you to see it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, you will be the first of my Ummah to enter Paradise.”"],[2585,"Wretched is the slave of the dinar, wretched is the slave of the dirham, wretched is the slave of the khamisa. If he is given, he is pleased, and if he is denied, he is displeased. Wretched and turned upside down; and if he is pierced by a thorn, may it never be extracted. Blessed is a servant who holds the reins of his horse in the path of Allah, his hair disheveled and his feet dusty: if assigned to guard duty, he is in the guard; if assigned to the rear, he is in the rear; if he intercedes, his intercession is not accepted; if he seeks permission, it is not granted to him."],[2586,"When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, decrees that a man will die in a certain land, He creates for him a need there."],[2587,"A man’s prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer [alone] by twenty-five degrees."],[2588,"A man brought a black slave girl to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I owe a believing slave. The Prophet ﷺ asked her: “Who is your Lord?” She pointed to the sky and said: Allah. He said: “And who am I?” She said: His Messenger, and she pointed with her hand to the earth. The Prophet ﷺ said to the man: “Set her free, for she is a believer.”"],[2589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to eat garlic, and said: “Were it not that the angel descends upon me, I would eat it.”"],[2590,"I was riding behind Abu Talha at Khaybar, and the fighting had grown intense. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: “Allahu akbar! Khaybar is conquered! Khaybar is destroyed! When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned.”"],[2591,"The people of Madinah were afflicted by severe drought and famine. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit and delivered the Friday sermon. Some people stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, wealth has perished, we fear destruction for ourselves, prices have risen and rain has stopped. Ask Allah to send us rain. Anas said: I did not see any white cloud in the sky. He ﷺ stretched out his hand and supplicated. By Allah, he had hardly drawn back his hand before I saw clouds coming from here and from there, and they became piled up. Then rain fell for seven days, until by Allah a young man could hardly return to his family because of the severity of the rain. On the following Friday, while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon, some people from the mosque stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, houses have collapsed and roads are cut off; ask Allah to withhold it from us. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ smile, then he raised his hands and said: “Around us, not upon us.” Anas said: I did not see any green in the sky. By Allah, he had not withdrawn his hand before I saw the sky clearing from here and here around Madinah, and in the morning, what surrounded it was like a ring."],[2592,"The Prophet ﷺ once sent a man to one of the Pharaohs of the Arabs, saying: Invite him to me. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, he is too arrogant for that. He said: Go to him and invite him. So he went to him and said: The Messenger of Allah invites you. He replied: Messenger of Allah! And what is Allah? Is He of gold, or of silver, or of copper? He returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, saying: I told you, O Messenger of Allah, that he is too arrogant for that. He said: “Return to him and invite him.” So he went back and repeated the same words, and the man gave the same answer as before. He returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: “Return to him and invite him.” So he went back a third time. While they were exchanging words, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent a cloud over his head, and it thundered and lightning flashed, and a thunderbolt fell from it and carried away the top of his skull. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “He sends thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills, while they dispute about Allah, and He is severe in assault.”"],[2593,"On the Day of Resurrection, sealed scrolls will be brought and placed before Allah, Blessed and Exalted. He will say: “Discard these and accept those.” The angels will say: By Your might, we have seen nothing but good. He will say, Mighty and Majestic: “This was not done for My sake, and today I accept only that by which My Face was sought.”"],[2594,"Hospitality is three days; whatever is beyond that is charity."],[2595,"When you see a man searching for a lost animal in the mosque, say: 'May you not find it.' And when you see him selling in the mosque, say: 'May Allah not make your trade profitable.'"],[2596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never addressed us except that he said: 'There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant.'"],[2597,"I met Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for his household, mentioning Ali, Fatimah, and others. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, am I from the People of the House?' He said: 'Yes, as long as you do not stand at the gate of a ruler or come to an official to ask of him.'"],[2598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was upset with Safiyyah over something. Safiyyah said to me: 'Would you like to appease the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I will give you my day?' So I wore a veil of mine dyed with saffron, sprinkled it with water, then came and sat beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to me: 'Away from me, for it is not your day.' I said: 'That is the bounty of Allah which He gives to whom He wills,' and I informed him of the matter, and he was pleased with her."],[2599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey and we were with him. A camel of Safiyyah fell ill, and Zaynab had extra riding camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'Verily Safiyyah's camel has fallen ill, so if you could give her one of your camels.' She said: 'Should I give to this Jewess?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and avoided her for the rest of Dhu al-Hijjah, all of Muharram and Safar, and some days of Rabi' al-Awwal, until she had packed up her belongings and her bed, thinking that he had no need of her. Then one day while she was sitting at midday, she saw his shadow approaching, so she returned her bed and belongings."],[2600,"It is not permissible for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days."],[2601,"The Quran was revealed stating that only ten known sucklings or five known sucklings make marriage forbidden."],[2602,"None of you should say: 'My soul has become wicked.' Rather, let him say: 'My soul has become weary.'"],[2603,"In the sermon of Utbah b. Ghazwan in Basrah: 'Indeed the world has announced its departure and is turning away swiftly. Nothing remains of it except a remnant like the dregs in a vessel which one of you pours out. Indeed you will inevitably depart from it, so depart with the best of what is with you. Indeed I was the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had no food except tree leaves until our mouths became ulcerated. We have now become such that each of us is a ruler. I saw myself as one of seven who shared a cloak, tearing it into pieces among us. Indeed it is astonishing that a great rock is thrown into Hell and falls for seventy autumns without reaching its bottom. Indeed it is astonishing that the distance between two panels of the gates of Paradise is forty days, and a day will come upon it when it is crowded to suffocation.'"],[2604,"A man from the desert asked the Prophet ﷺ about the night prayer. He replied with his finger like this: 'Two by two, and the witr is one rak'ah at the end of the night.'"],[2605,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the House in the year of the conquest on his mount, touching the corner with his staff."],[2606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Eid prayer without any adhan or iqamah, then delivered the sermon after the prayer. Then he went to the women, accompanied by Bilal, stood before them and urged them to give charity. And how many rings and necklaces were thrown into Bilal's garment until it was filled."],[2607,"The killing of a believer unjustly, without [depriving him of] his property, is martyrdom."],[2608,"None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a wooden beam in his wall."],[2609,"We entered upon Aisha, and they mentioned the judiciary. Aisha said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Indeed, the just judge will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and will face such severity of reckoning that he will wish he had never judged between two people even over a single date.'"],[2610,"He is not one of us who shaves [the head], tears [the clothes], and wails."],[2611,"Abu Musa said on the day of Ashura: 'Fast this day, for the Prophet ﷺ commanded us to fast it.'"],[2612,"He prohibited Qunut in the dawn prayer."],[2613,"There will be rulers over you who will delay the prayer beyond its proper times. It will be counted for you and against them, so pray with them as long as they pray the prayer for you."],[2614,"I said: 'O Prophet of God, which part of the night is most beloved to you, if it is decreed for me to pray two rak'ahs during it?' He said: 'The middle of the night, and few are those who do it.'"],[2615,"I prayed beside Ibn Umar. When he finished praying, he struck my thigh with his hand and said: 'Shall I teach you the greeting of the prayer as the Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us?' Then he recited these words: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'"],[2616,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, which deeds are best?' He said: 'Establishing the prayer at its proper time.'"],[2617,"Indeed, in Friday there is an hour such that no Muslim servant coincides with it, asking God for good, except that He grants it to him."],[2618,"When dinner is served and the prayer is called, begin with dinner."],[2619,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to me, so I went out to him. I found him feverish, having bound his head with a cloth. He said: \"Take my hand, O Fadl.\" So I took his hand until he reached the pulpit and sat upon it. Then he said to me: \"Call out among the people.\" I called out among the people, and they gathered to him. He praised God, the Mighty and Majestic, and extolled Him. Then he said: \"O people, it has come close to me that I should discharge my responsibilities from among you. Whoever I have flogged on the back, here is my back, let him take retaliation from it. Whoever I have insulted his honor, here is my honor, let him take retaliation from it. Whoever I have taken wealth from him, here is my wealth, let him take retaliation from it. Let no man say: 'I fear enmity from the side of the Messenger of God.' Indeed, enmity is not of my nature nor of my disposition. Indeed, the most beloved of you to me is the one who takes his right if there is one, or releases me, so that I meet God with a contented soul. Indeed, I do not consider that sufficient for me until I stand among you several times.\" Then he descended ﷺ and prayed Zuhr. Then he returned to the pulpit and repeated his speech concerning enmity and other matters. Then he said: \"O people, whoever has anything with me, let him return it, and let him not say: 'It is the shame of this world.' Indeed, the shame of this world is better than the shame of the Hereafter.\" A man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of God, I have three dirhams with you.\" He said: \"We do not accuse a speaker of lying, nor do we ask him to swear an oath. How did it come to be that I owe you?\" He said: \"Do you remember the day a beggar passed by you and you ordered me, so I gave him three dirhams?\" He said: \"Give them to him, O Fadl.\" Then another man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of God, I have three dirhams which I had embezzled in the cause of God.\" He said: \"Why did you embezzle them?\" He said: \"I was in need of them.\" He said: \"Take them from him, O Fadl.\" Then he ﷺ said: \"Whoever of you fears something, let him stand so that I may supplicate for him.\" A man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of God, I am indeed a liar, and I am indeed a hypocrite, and I am indeed given to excessive sleep.\" He said: \"O God, provide him with truthfulness and faith, and remove from him sleep when he desires.\" Then another man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of God, I am indeed a liar, and I am indeed a hypocrite, and there is nothing of all things but that I have done it.\" Umar said: \"O this one, you have disgraced yourself.\" He said: \"Hush, O son of al-Khattab, the disgrace of this world is easier than the disgrace of the Hereafter. O God, provide him with truthfulness and faith, and turn his affair to good.\" Umar spoke a word, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Umar is with me and I am with Umar, and the truth after me is with Umar wherever he is.\""],[2620,"It was as if he testified to this testimony without certainty, going back to his heart. He used to hear people say something, so he would say it. None narrated this hadith from Muhammad b. Amr with this completeness except Hammad b. Salama. Abu Umar al-Darir was alone in transmitting it."],[2621,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud used to deliver sermons to us in Kufa, and he would say: \"The wretched is one who was made wretched in his mother's womb, and the blessed is one who was made blessed in his mother's womb.\" Hudhayfa b. Asid, a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \"It is amazing concerning this man's statement. He says: 'The blessed is one who was made blessed in his mother's womb, and the wretched is one who was made wretched in his mother's womb.'\" Abd Allah said: \"O Hudhayfa, what amazes you about this?\" Then he said: \"Shall I tell you the explanation of that?\" Then he raised the hadith and said: \"Indeed, there is an angel entrusted with the womb. When God, the Mighty and Majestic, wills to create something, by God's permission, the angel says: 'O Lord, its lifespan?' So your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then he says: 'O Lord, its sustenance?' So your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then he says: 'Wretched or blessed?' So your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Thus it is, neither more nor less.\""],[2622,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entrusted me with three things: \"The ritual bath on Friday, the Witr prayer before sleep, and fasting three days of every month.\""],[2623,"Ibn Abbas narrated to them about the beginning of Abu Dharr's Islam. He said: When it reached him that a man had emerged in Makkah claiming that he was a prophet, he sent his brother and said: \"Go until you bring me news of him and what you hear from him.\" His brother went until he heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, then returned to Abu Dharr and informed him that he commanded good and forbade evil, and commanded noble character. Abu Dharr said: \"You have not satisfied me.\" So he took a worn waterskin containing his water and provisions. Then he set out until he came to Makkah. He was afraid to ask anyone about anything, and he did not meet the Messenger of God ﷺ. He entered the mosque and wandered in it until evening. When it became dark, Ali b. Abi Talib passed by him and said: \"Who is the man?\" He said: \"A man from Ghifar.\" He said: \"Come to the house.\" So he went with him, neither of them asking the other about anything. When morning came, Abu Dharr went out seeking. When evening came, he slept in the mosque. Ali b. Abi Talib passed by him and said: \"It is time for the man to know his place.\" On the third day, Ali made a promise to him that if he told him his matter, he would conceal it and keep it hidden. So he informed him that it had reached him that a man had emerged in Makkah claiming that he saw things, so he sent his brother, but he did not bring him what would satisfy him, so he came himself. Ali said to him: \"I am going out, so follow me. If I see what I fear for you, I will stand as if I were pouring water.\" So Ali went out and Abu Dharr went out following his tracks, until he entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and Abu Dharr entered following his tracks. He informed the Messenger of God ﷺ and heard from him, and he accepted Islam. Then he said: \"O Messenger of God, command me with your order.\" He said: \"Return to your people until my news reaches you.\" He said: \"By God, I will not return until I proclaim Islam openly.\" So he went to the mosque and stood crying out at the top of his voice: \"I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" The polytheists said: \"The man has apostatized (to Islam).\" Then they rose against him and beat him until he fell. Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib passed by him, bent over him, and said: \"You have killed the man, O assembly of Quraysh. You are merchants, and your route passes by Ghifar. Do you want the road to be cut off?\" So they desisted from him. The next day, he returned to his statement, and they jumped on him and beat him until he fell. Al-Abbas passed by him, bent over him, and said to them the like of what he had said the day before, so they desisted from him. This was the beginning of Abu Dharr's Islam ؓ."],[2624,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to deliver sermons to us, and he would remind us of the days of God until we recognized that in his face, as if he were a man fearing that the matter would befall them in the morning. And when he had recently been with Jibril ﷺ, he would not smile broadly until it was lifted from him."],[2625,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about coitus interruptus ('azl). He said: \"It does not matter if you do not do it, for it is but divine decree.\""],[2626,"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet (with salam) to his right and to his left."],[2627,"The example of the believer is like the bee: it eats only what is good, and it produces only what is good."],[2628,"He used to greet (with salam) to his right: \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of God,\" and to his left the like of that, until the side of his face would appear to them."],[2629,"Al-Fadl was older than me, so he used to mount me behind him, and I would be in front of him. I and my brother rode behind on a female donkey, and we reached the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying with the people at Arafah. We dismounted in front of him and entered (the prayer) and prayed, and left the donkey grazing in front of him, and he did not interrupt his prayer."],[2630,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called out for a saddle blanket and a bowl, saying: \"Who will increase?\" A man gave him a dirham, and another gave him two dirhams, and he sold it."],[2631,"Whoever slanders his brother with one slanderous word, Allah will feed him the like of it from the fire of Hell."],[2632,"Fast when you see it and break your fast when you see it."],[2633,"For every traitor there will be a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which his treachery will be known."],[2634,"Whoever says when the sun sets: 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,' nothing will harm him that night."],[2635,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over his socks."],[2636,"The Prophet ﷺ took a ring of gold and wore it for three days. Then gold rings became widespread, so he threw it away and took a ring of silver and engraved on it: 'Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah' ﷺ."],[2637,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, let me strike the neck of Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah, for he has disbelieved.' He said: 'And what would make you know, O Ibn al-Khattab? Perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of Badr and said: \"Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.\"'"],[2638,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was speaking to us at the door of the chambers, Abu Bakr and Umar came with a group of people, some of them answering others and some refuting others. When they saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ they fell silent. He said: 'What is the speech I just heard, some of you answering others and some refuting others?' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr claimed that good deeds are from Allah and evil deeds are from the servants, and Umar said: \"Evil and good are both from Allah.\" Some people followed this one and some followed that one, so they answered each other and refuted each other.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to Abu Bakr and said: 'What did you say?' He repeated his first statement. Then he turned to Umar and he repeated his first statement. He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will judge between you two with the judgment of Israfil between Jibril and Mika'il.' That became magnified in the hearts of the people and they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, did Jibril speak about this?' He said: 'Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, they were the first of Allah's creation to speak about it. Mika'il spoke with the statement of Abu Bakr, and Jibril spoke with the statement of Umar. Jibril said to Mika'il: \"If we, the inhabitants of heaven, disagree, the inhabitants of earth will disagree, so let us resort to Israfil for judgment.\" They resorted to him, and he judged between them with the true nature of divine decree: its good and its evil, its sweet and its bitter, all of it is from Allah, Mighty and Majestic. And I will judge between you two likewise.' Then he turned to Abu Bakr and said: 'O Abu Bakr, if Allah, Blessed and Exalted, had willed not to be disobeyed, He would not have created Iblis.' Abu Bakr said: 'Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.'"],[2639,"Shall I not teach you five things? Love the poor and be close to them; look at those who are below you and do not look at those above you; maintain family ties even if they cut you off; speak the truth even if it is bitter; and say often: 'There is no might and no power except with Allah.'"],[2640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a stray camel. He said: 'What do you have to do with it? It has its own water-skin and its own shoes. It eats trees and drinks water until its owner finds it.' Then he was asked about a stray sheep, and he said: 'It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.' And he was asked about the mountain treasure, and he said: 'He must pay its value and a like amount, and lashes as a deterrent.'"],[2641,"Ziyad sent money to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ and gave preference to Aisha. The messenger began to apologize to Umm Salamah, and she said: 'Does Ziyad apologize to us? The one who used to prefer her over us was greater in preference than Ziyad: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[2642,"A sheep of Maymunah died, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'Why did you not make use of its hide?' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how can we make use of it when it is dead?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The purification of the hide is its tanning.'"],[2643,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to lighten the two rakʿahs before the Fajr prayer, to the point that I would say: Did he recite in them the Mother of the Book?"],[2644,"Permission was given to the menstruating woman to depart when she menstruates."],[2645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, and salt for salt, except like for like, equal for equal; and sell wheat for barley however you wish, but it is not valid on credit; and sell gold for silver however you wish, but it is not valid on credit."],[2646,"A man asked while the Prophet ﷺ was sitting, and a man gave him. Then the people followed suit. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever sets a good precedent that is followed after him will have his reward and the like of the reward of those who follow him, without any reduction in their rewards. And whoever sets an evil precedent will bear its burden and the like of the burdens of those who follow him, without any reduction in their burdens."],[2647,"The noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one: Yusuf b. Yaʿqub b. Ishaq b. Ibrahim, may Allah bless them all."],[2648,"Verses have been sent down to me the like of which have never been sent down to me: the two protecting surahs."],[2649,"Marry, for the best of us was the one with the most wives."],[2650,"Abu Taybah cupped the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered for him a saʿ of dates and spoke to his masters, and they reduced his levy."],[2651,"A man from the Ansar came with two camels, and he hastened to feed them at night. He heard the muʾadhdhin of Muʿadh when he called the iqamah for prayer, so he entered and began the prayer with Muʿadh, who recited Surat al-Baqarah. When the young man saw that, he turned to his own prayer and left Muʿadh. Muʿadh said: I will mention what the Ansari did to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Ansari came to the Prophet of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I entered the Maghrib prayer with Muʿadh, and he began Surat al-Baqarah, so I turned to my own prayer and left Muʿadh. Then Muʿadh entered, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: O Muʿadh, are you a troublemaker? Are you a troublemaker? Recite 'By the sun and its brightness' and 'By the night when it covers' and the like of them."],[2652,"The Jews killed a man from the Ansar at Khaybar, so his relatives came to the Prophet ﷺ, a people called al-Aharisah. When they reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man from the people spoke, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The eldest, the eldest. He said: Let fifty of you swear. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we swear to what we did not see, or shall we accept the oaths of the Jews? Then camels were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he paid the blood money from his own side with one hundred camels. He said: I saw them, and a young she-camel of them kicked me."],[2653,"Knowledge comes only by learning, and forbearance comes only by pretending to be forbearing. Whoever seeks good will be given it, and whoever guards against evil will be protected from it. Three things: whoever has them will not dwell in the highest ranks—and I do not say to you Paradise—whoever practices divination, or draws lots, or is turned back from a journey by superstition."],[2654,"A man should not judge between two men while he is angry."],[2655,"The Black Stone and the Maqām will come on the Day of Resurrection with a tongue and lips greater than Abū Qubays, testifying with fidelity for those who fulfilled their duty to them."],[2656,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was lying under a tree with his hand under his head. I said, \"O Messenger of God, will you not supplicate against these people who we fear may turn us away from our religion?\" He turned his face away from me. I moved around to face him again, and he turned his face away from me three times, each time I said the same and he turned away. On the third time he sat up and said, \"O people, fear God. By God, a believer before you would have a saw placed on his head and be split in two, yet he would not abandon his religion. Fear God, for God, Mighty and Majestic, will open for you and provide.\""],[2657,"When the Negus died, the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Seek forgiveness for your brother.\" Some people said, \"He commands us to seek forgiveness for him, yet he died in the land of Abyssinia?\" Then it was revealed: \"And indeed among the People of the Scripture are those who believe in God and what has been sent down to you\" [Q Āl ʿImrān 3:199]."],[2658,"When he stood for prayer, he faced them and said, \"Straighten your rows,\" twice, \"for I see you from behind me just as I see you in front of me.\""],[2659,"When he performed the full bath after major ritual impurity, he washed his hands three times before dipping them into the water. Then he took water with his right hand and poured it over his left, then washed his private parts. Then he rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, and washed his forearms three times each. Then he poured water over his head once, and when he left his bathing place he washed his feet."],[2660,"Whoever sends one prayer upon me, God sends ten upon him for it."],[2661,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, I have two neighbors, one facing my door and the other distant from my door but closer in neighborhood. With which of them should I begin?\" He said, \"The one facing your door.\""],[2662,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ stayed with me, I saw him persistently pray four rakʿahs before the noon prayer. I said, \"O Messenger of God, I see you persistently praying four before noon.\" He said, \"It is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, and no gate remains closed until the noon prayer is performed. I love that good deeds be raised for me in that hour.\""],[2663,"The fingers will be thoroughly cleansed in ablution, or the Fire will consume them."],[2664,"Ibn ʿAbbās fell seriously ill and gathered his sons and family. He said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever performs Hajj from Makkah on foot until he returns to it, for every step he has seven hundred good deeds of the Ḥaram.'\" A man asked, \"What are the good deeds of the Ḥaram, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Each good deed is a thousand good deeds.\""],[2665,"Whoever commits a sin and then regrets it, God, Mighty and Majestic, forgives him that sin before he even asks for forgiveness. Whoever receives a blessing from God and knows it is from God, God records gratitude for it before he even praises Him. Whoever is clothed by God with a garment and knows that God is the one who clothed him, the garment does not reach his knees before he is forgiven."],[2666,"The righteous will pass away, one after another, until only the dregs remain like the dregs of dates. Allah will not care about them."],[2667,"Whoever is appointed as a judge has been slaughtered without a knife."],[2668,"Allah does not give permission to any prophet as He gives permission to a man with a beautiful voice reciting the Qur'an. And he heard Abu Musa's recitation, and said: \"This one has been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud.\""],[2669,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with his companions, and when he finished his prayer, he turned to the people and said: \"Do you recite while the imam is reciting?\" They remained silent. Then he said it three times. Some people said: \"We do.\" He said: \"Then do not do that. Let each of you recite the Fatihah of the Book to himself.\""],[2670,"If a man confesses to adultery four times, and then stoning is ordered for him, but he flees, he is to be left alone."],[2671,"A dirham of usury is greater in sin with Allah than thirty-six acts of adultery."],[2672,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in a state of ihram."],[2673,"I poured water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was at home and when traveling. He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, after defecating and urinating, except for sleeping and major ritual impurity."],[2674,"What interrupts the prayer if there is not before you something like the rear part of a saddle? He said: A woman, a donkey, and a black dog. I said: What is the matter with the black dog as opposed to the white and the red? He said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said: 'The black dog is a devil' three times."],[2675,"The Prophet ﷺ entered my house and said: \"Why do I not see any blessing in your house?\" I said: \"What blessing have you missed in my house?\" He said: \"I do not see a sheep in it.\""],[2676,"I asked Uqbah b. Amr about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood up to the mosque and said the takbir. Then he bowed and placed his hands on his knees with his fingers lower than that, and he kept his upper arms away from his sides. He bowed until every part of him was still. Then he stood up until every part of him was still. Then he prostrated, placing his hands on the ground, and kept his upper arms away from his sides. He prostrated until every part of him was still. Then he sat until every part of him was still. Then he prostrated again. He did this until he had prayed four rak'ahs. Then he said: \"This is how I saw the Prophet ﷺ pray.\""],[2677,"\"There is no envy except in two cases: a man whom Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has taught the Qur'an, and he recites it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day; and a man to whom Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has given wealth, and he spends it in the way of Allah during the hours of the night and the hours of the day.\""],[2678,"I saw in a dream that they took the pillar of the Book and carried it toward al-Sham. When the tribulation occurs, safety will be in al-Sham."],[2679,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud was teaching a man the tashahhud. Abd Allah said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger.\" The man said: \"Alone, with no partner.\" Abd Allah said: \"That is indeed so, but we stop at what we have been taught.\""],[2680,"He noticed a man praying without completing the bowing or the prostration, so he said: \"If this man were to die, he would die upon other than the religion of Jesus ﷺ .\""],[2681,"\"Seek\" or he said: \"Look for trustworthiness among Quraysh, for the trustworthy one from Quraysh has two merits over the trustworthy one from other than them, and the strong one from Quraysh has two merits over the strong one from other than them.\""],[2682,"Whoever does not have wealth to give as charity, let him seek forgiveness for the believing men and women, for that is charity."],[2683,"The night prayer is in twos, and when one of you fears that dawn is near, then a single one makes his prayer odd-numbered."],[2684,"I spoke to the Prophet ﷺ about a need. I spoke to him while there was yellow dye on my hands. He said to me: \"Go and wash it off,\" three times. I went with a towel and began tracing with it the traces of the perfume from between my fingers, washing it until it was gone. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to me: \"Ask your need,\" so I conveyed it to him."],[2685,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you and you speak to us, our hearts soften, but when we leave you and see women and do such and such, we find our hearts changed at that moment.\" He said: \"If you remained as you are with me, the angels would shake your hands.\""],[2686,"When the prayer is announced, let one of you walk calmly; let him pray what he catches up with and make up what he missed."],[2687,"The people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they wearied him with questions. He ascended the pulpit and said: \"You will not ask me about anything except that I will make it clear to you.\" I began looking right and left, and I saw every man wrapping his head in his garment, weeping. A man stood up who, when he quarreled with men, was called by other than his father. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?\" He said: \"Your father is Hudhafah.\" Umar stood up and said: \"We are content with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as Prophet. We seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger, and from the evil of tribulations.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have never seen the like of today in good and evil. Paradise and Hell were shown to me until I saw them within the wall.\""],[2688,"Many times I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying the prayer while donkeys were jostling in front of him."],[2689,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he stood for prayer. He stood for a long time, then bowed for a long time, then prostrated, then repeated the like of it. Ikrimah said: Ibn Abbas said: I was beside the Prophet ﷺ and I did not hear the recitation."],[2690,"The spear was planted in front of the Prophet ﷺ at Arafat; he was praying, and the donkeys passed beyond the spear."],[2691,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the hour in Jumu'ah on the pulpit, indicating its brevity with his finger."],[2692,"The names of the two angels who come in the grave are Munkar and Nakir, and the names of Harut and Marut while they are in heaven were 'Azra and 'Uzayr."],[2693,"If a nation from the nations bears witness, and they are forty men or more, Allah accepts their witness."],[2694,"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, how many times did the Prophet ﷺ perform 'Umrah? He said to him: Four, one of them in Rajab. We heard the sound of 'Aishah's toothstick in the room, so he said to her: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman claims that the Prophet ﷺ performed 'Umrah four times, one of them in Rajab. She said: May Allah have mercy on Abu 'Abd al-Rahman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never performed 'Umrah except when he was with him, and he never performed 'Umrah in Rajab at all."],[2695,"He gave the inheritance to the son of Zam'ah's slave woman because he was born on Zam'ah's bed, and he said to Sawdah: As for you, veil yourself from him."],[2696,"A Bedouin from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Peace be upon you, O boy of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: And upon you be peace. He said: I am a man from your maternal uncles, from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr, and I am the messenger of my people to you and their delegate. I will ask you, so my questioning of you will be intense, and I will adjure you, so my adjuration of you will be intense. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: Ask, O brother of Banu Sa'd b. Bakr. He said: Who created you and created those before you and who is to be created after you? He said: Allah. He said: I adjure you by that, did He send you? He said: Yes. He said: Who created the seven heavens and the seven earths and causes provision to flow between them? He said: Allah. He said: I adjure you by that, did He send you? He said: Yes. He said: We have found in your Book and your messengers commanded us to pray night and day five prayers at their times, so I adjure you by that, did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: We have found in your Book and your messengers commanded us to fast the month of Ramadan, so I adjure you by that, did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: We have found in your Book and your messengers commanded us to take from the fringes of our wealth and give it to our poor, so I adjure you by that, did He command you? He said: Yes. Then he said: As for the fifth, I will not ask about it, and I have no desire for it, meaning lewd acts. Then he said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will act upon these and whoever obeys me from my people. Then he turned back, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then he said: If he is truthful, he will surely enter Paradise by them."],[2697,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I will never abandon: sleeping on Witr, the Duha prayer, and fasting three days every month."],[2698,"I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them, but do not say anything improper. I forbade you from the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, so eat and keep. I forbade you from drinking in gourds, green jars, pitch-covered vessels, and hollowed stumps, so drink, but do not drink anything intoxicating. 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, what is intoxicating? He said: Drink it, O 'Umar, and if you fear it, leave it."],[2699,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has increased you a prayer, and it is Witr."],[2700,"He prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ while a woman was behind him, until people came later."],[2701,"The hypocrites today are worse than the hypocrites who were in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. That is because those concealed it, while these proclaim it openly."],[2702,"He entered upon 'A'ishah on the day about which there is doubt concerning Ramadan, and she said: \"O slave girl, mix some sawiq for him.\" He said: \"I am fasting.\" She said: \"Have you preceded the month?\" I said: \"No, but I fasted all of Sha'ban, and that coincided with this day.\" She said: \"Some people used to precede the month and fast before the Prophet ﷺ, so Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'O you who believe, do not put yourselves forward before Allah and His Messenger.'\""],[2703,"Abu Hurayrah said to me: \"I see you have small feet. If you can ensure they have a place tomorrow at the Hawd, then do so.\" I said: \"And what is that?\" He said: \"I heard him say—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—'I have a Hawd to which my Ummah will come, as wide as the distance between San'a' and Yathrib.'\""],[2704,"Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their excessive questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. When I command you to do something, do it, and when I forbid you from something, abstain from it as much as you are able."],[2705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named himself with names, some of which we remembered. He said: \"I am Muhammad, Ahmad, al-Muqaffi, the Prophet of Mercy, and the Prophet of Malhamah.\""],[2706,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a man from the Ansar. When he approached his house, he heard him talking inside. When he asked permission and entered, he saw no one. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"I heard you talking to someone other than yourself.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I entered those inner rooms distressed by people's talk because of the fever I have, and someone entered upon me. I have never seen a man after you with a nobler presence or better speech than him.\" He said: \"That was Jibril ﷺ. Among you are men such that if one of them were to swear by Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, He would fulfill his oath.\""],[2707,"I taught Ibn Sirin the tashahhud. I narrated to him from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he took my tashahhud and abandoned his own."],[2708,"Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have commanded the killing of every completely black dog. Kill the jet-black dogs among them, for they are the cursed ones from the jinn."],[2709,"He did not seek the virtue of fasting one day over another after Ramadan except the day of 'Ashura'."],[2710,"I have not seen anyone better than Fatimah except her father. She said: There was something between them, so she said: \"O Messenger of Allah, ask her, for she does not lie.\""],[2711,"Two men came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage asking him for charity. He raised his gaze to them and lowered it, and saw they were two strong men. He said: \"If you wish, I will give you from it, but there is no share in it for a wealthy person or for a strong person who can earn.\""],[2712,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy in Madinah to lead the people in prayer."],[2713,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to offer him a camel of mine, and I saw him pray Duha with six rak'ahs."],[2714,"The Prophet ﷺ allowed kissing and cupping for the fasting person."],[2715,"Do not torture your children by pressing the uvula (for treating throat disease)."],[2716,"Umm Hani' ؓ narrated that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ entered upon her at the time of the conquest and prayed the forenoon prayer (Duha) as six rak'ahs."],[2717,"\"The best of this Ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then 'Umar.\" And he said: \"If I wished, I would name the third.\""],[2718,"'Uthman said to Ibn 'Umar: \"Go and be a judge.\" He replied: \"Will you excuse me, O Commander of the Believers? For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever is a judge and judges in ignorance will be among the people of the Fire. And whoever is a knowledgeable judge and judges with truth or justice, he will seek to slip away with nothing.' So what can I hope for after this?\""],[2719,"O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah! If you have rulers upon whom you enter and you confirm their lies and assist them in their oppression, then you are not of me and I am not of you, and you will not approach me at the Cistern. And whoever enters upon them and does not confirm their lies and does not assist them in their oppression, then he is of me and I am of him. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah! Verily, flesh and blood that grow from ill-gotten gain (suht) will not enter Paradise; every flesh and blood that grow from suht, the Fire is more deserving of it. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah! People are of two kinds: one who sets out in the morning and ransoms his own soul, thus freeing it, and one who sets out and destroys it. O Ka'b! Prayer is a proof, fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin just as ice (jalid) melts away on a smooth rock (safa)."],[2720,"Any child who performs Hajj then reaches the age of accountability (bulugh al-hinth) must perform another Hajj. Any bedouin who performs Hajj then migrates (to Madinah) must perform another Hajj. Any slave who performs Hajj then is freed must perform another Hajj."],[2721,"We were one thousand four hundred — meaning on the day when water was scarce — and the Prophet ﷺ called for a small vessel of water and placed his hand in it. The water began to gush forth from between his fingers. So they bathed, performed ablution, and drank."],[2722,"Four rak'ahs before Zuhr are like their equivalent after 'Isha, and four rak'ahs after 'Isha are like their equivalent from the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr)."],[2723,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has cursed wine itself, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its seller, its buyer, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its server, its drinker, and the one who consumes its price."],[2724,"When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it in fully, for in one of its wings there is poison and in the other there is a cure."],[2725,"O Messenger of Allah! I take a sheep to slaughter it and I feel mercy for it. He said: \"And the sheep — if you have mercy on it, Allah will have mercy on you.\""],[2726,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will support this religion with people who have no share of good."],[2727,"A disbeliever does not inherit from a Muslim, nor does a Muslim inherit from a disbeliever."],[2728,"When a woman gives charity from her husband's wealth without causing harm, she gets its reward, her husband gets the reward for what he earned, and the treasurer gets the like of that."],[2729,"Perform ablution from that which fire has changed its color."],[2730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling animals for animals, two for one, on credit, but he saw no harm in it hand to hand."],[2731,"When a boy has not yet eaten food, his urine is to be poured over; and when it is a girl, it is to be washed once."],[2732,"When allegiance is given to two caliphs, kill the latter of them."],[2733,"When he made the talbiyah, he would say: \"Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak.\""],[2734,"We used to prepare nabidh for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a waterskin whose top was tied, with a spout, hung up. We would prepare it in the morning, and he would drink it in the evening; and we would prepare it in the evening, and he would drink it in the morning."],[2735,"He said on the Day of Badr, while he was in a tent: \"O Allah, I ask You for Your covenant and promise. O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped after today.\" Abu Bakr took him by the hand and said: \"Enough for you, O Messenger of Allah, for you have importuned your Lord.\" He was in his coat of mail, bringing out his hand and saying: \"The assembly will be defeated and they will turn their backs. Nay, the Hour is their appointed time, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter.\""],[2736,"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forbids his flesh to the Fire."],[2737,"None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a piece of wood on his wall."],[2738,"Regarding the statement of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'And We shall remove from their breasts any rancor' (Qur'an 7:43), he said: 'When the believers are cleared from the reckoning, they will be made to stand at an arch between the Fire and Paradise, and they will settle the grievances that were between them in this world. When they are purified, they will be commanded to enter Paradise. By Allah, they will be more knowledgeable of their dwellings in Paradise than they were of their dwellings in this world.'"],[2739,"Eating the meat of domestic donkeys was forbidden."],[2740,"We used to recognize the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he came toward us by the fragrance of his scent."],[2741,"I never touched silk, nor silk brocade, nor anything softer than the skin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2742,"He prayed over a baby boy or baby girl, and said: 'If anyone were to survive the squeezing of the grave, this baby would have survived.'"],[2743,"He used to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebble."],[2744,"I came to Anas b. Malik and said: 'Tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He led us in the noon prayer, and he recited in a low voice al-Mursalat, al-Nazi'at, 'Amma yatasa'alun, and similar surahs."],[2745,"When the Prophet ﷺ disliked something, it would be seen in his face."],[2746,"When he walked briskly in the middle of the watercourse, he said: 'O Allah, forgive and have mercy, for You are the Most Mighty, the Most Noble.'"],[2747,"On the day of Hunayn, the people fled from the Prophet ﷺ except al-Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith. The Prophet ﷺ commanded that a call be made: 'O companions of Surah al-Baqarah! O assembly of the Ansar!' Then the call became intense among the Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj. When they heard the call, they came forward. By Allah, I could only liken them to camels yearning for their young. When they met, the fighting intensified, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Now the oven is heated.' He took a handful of pebbles, threw them, and said: 'They are defeated, by the Lord of the Ka'bah!' And 'Ali b. Abi Talib was among the fiercest fighters that day."],[2748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who steps in filth with his sandals. He said: 'Dust is a purifier for them.'"],[2749,"Whoever washes a dead person should perform a full bath."],[2750,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on a donkey, facing toward Khaybar."],[2751,"The likeness of a wicked person among a people is like a group who boarded a ship at sea and divided it up, so each one of them got a place. One of them went to his place to make a hole in it. They said, 'Do you want to drown us?' He said, 'What concern is it of yours from my spot?' If they leave him, they drown and he drowns with them; but if they seize his hand, they are saved and he is saved. That is the likeness of a wicked person."],[2752,"If a man were to invite people to a bone or two sheep's trotters, they would answer him; yet they are called to this prayer in congregation and do not come to it. I was on the point of ordering a man to lead the people in congregational prayer, then going to a people who heard the call but did not respond, and setting fire to them. Indeed, none stays away from it except a hypocrite."],[2753,"It is food and drink, and it is blessed—he said it three times. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me, 'Which people are you from?' I said, 'From Ghifar.' He said—and Ghifar used to waylay pilgrims—and it was as if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew back from me. He said to Abu Bakr, 'Let us go, O Abu Bakr.' So he took us to Abu Bakr's house, and he brought us raisins, and we ate from them. I stayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he taught me Islam, and I recited something of the Qur'an. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I want to make my religion public.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I fear for you that you will be killed.' I said, 'It must be so.' He said, 'I fear for you that you will be killed.' I said, 'It must be so, O Messenger of Allah, even if I am killed.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell silent about me. Quraysh were sitting in circles conversing in the mosque, so I said, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' The circles scattered, and they rose against me and beat me until they left me like a red idol, and they thought they had killed me. I got up and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he saw the state I was in and said to me, 'Did I not forbid you?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, there was a need in my soul, and I fulfilled it.' I stayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he told me, 'Return to your people, and when you hear of my emergence, come to me.' I came back and had delayed, and I met Unays, and he wept and said, 'O my brother, I did not think you were anything but killed when you delayed. What did you do? Did you meet your companion whom you sought?' I said, 'Yes. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' Unays said, 'O my brother, I have no aversion to you. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,' and he became Muslim on the spot. Then I came to my mother, and when she saw me she wept and said, 'O my son, you delayed so long that I feared you had been killed. What did you do? Did you meet your companion whom you sought?' I said, 'Yes. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' She said, 'What did Unays do?' I said, 'He became Muslim.' She said, 'I have no aversion to you both. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' Then I stayed among my people, and many of them became Muslim, until news of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ emergence reached us, and I came to him. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Yazid al-Madani except by Abu Tahir, the freedman of al-Hasan b. Ali. Ja'far b. Sulayman was alone in transmitting it."],[2754,"I entered the mosque and recognized hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I asked Umm Sulaym, 'Do you have anything?' She gestured with her two hands and said, 'I have something.' I said, 'Prepare it; knead dough.' I sent Anas and said, 'Go and whisper in his ear and invite him.' When Anas came back, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This is a man who has come to you to give us something. Did Abu Talha send you to invite us?' Anas said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Get up, in the name of Allah.' Anas turned and hurried until he came to Abu Talha and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come to you with the people.' Abu Talha said, 'I met him at the door on the landing of the stairs and said, \"What have you done to us, O Messenger of Allah? I only recognized hunger in your face, so I prepared something for you to eat.\" He said, 'Enter and rejoice.' He entered, and the dish was brought, and he began smoothing it with his hand, then said, 'Is there any?' as if he meant condiment. We brought him our small butter-skin, which had something in it—or perhaps nothing—and he took it in his hand, and ghee poured from it. He said, 'Admit to me ten at a time.' They were about a hundred. They entered and ate until they were full. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about the leftover food, 'Eat, you and your dependents.' So they ate and were full."],[2755,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard an ugly name, he changed it."],[2756,"Whoever I am mentioned in his presence, let him send blessings upon me, for whoever sends blessings upon me once, blessings will be sent upon him ten times."],[2757,"There is no Muslim man or woman who is afflicted with a calamity and remembers it—even if it is old—and renews the saying 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return' except that Allah renews for him at that time and gives him the reward of the day he was afflicted."],[2758,"The gates of heaven are opened in the middle of the night, and a caller calls out: 'Is there any supplicant, that he may be answered? Is there any asker, that he may be given? Is there any distressed person, that he may be relieved?' No Muslim remains who calls with a supplication except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, answers him—except an adulteress who goes about with her private parts, or a tax collector."],[2759,"Do not say about your dead anything but good."],[2760,"Two women came to Dawud ﷺ —a wolf had eaten one of their two sons—and they were disputing over the remaining one. Dawud judged it for the older woman. When they went out, they came to Sulayman, and he said, 'How did he judge between you?' They told him, and he said, 'Bring me a knife.' Abu Hurayrah said, 'I was the first person I heard say \"knife\" from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; we used to call it a blade.' The younger woman said, 'Why?' He said, 'To split him between you two.' She said, 'Give him to her.' So Sulayman judged it for the younger woman, and he said, 'If he were your son, you would not have been willing to split him.'"],[2761,"Angels do not enter a house in which there is an image or a dog."],[2762,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on the road to Makkah and passed by a mountain called Jumdan. He said: \"This is Jumdan. Move on. The mufarridun have preceded,\" twice. They said: \"Who are the mufarridun, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Those men and women who remember Allah much.\" \"May Allah have mercy on those who shave their heads,\" he said. They said: \"And those who shorten their hair, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"May Allah have mercy on those who shave their heads.\" They said: \"And those who shorten their hair, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"May Allah have mercy on those who shave their heads.\" They said: \"And those who shorten their hair, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"And those who shorten their hair.\""],[2763,"Hasten to perform good deeds before trials like pieces of a dark night, when a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, or a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning, selling his religion for a worldly gain."],[2764,"Every good deed that the son of Adam does, I will reward him for it from ten good deeds up to seven hundred times over, except fasting. It is for Me, and I will reward for it. He leaves his food for My sake, and he leaves his desire for My sake. It is for Me, and I will reward for it. Fasting is a shield. Whoever is fasting should not behave obscenely or act foolishly. If someone insults him or harms him, let him say: 'I am fasting, I am fasting.'"],[2765,"How will you be, O 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr, when you are among the dregs of people?\" He said: \"And what is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"That is when their trusts and covenants become confused and they become like this,\" and he interlaced his fingers. He said: \"So what should I do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Act according to what you know, and leave what you disapprove of; attend to your own self, and leave the common people.\""],[2766,"Indeed, the religion began as something strange, and it will return to being strange as it began, so blessed are the strangers."],[2767,"Do you know who the bankrupt one is?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the bankrupt among us is the one who has no dirham and no property.\" He said: \"The bankrupt one in my community is the one who comes on the Day of Resurrection with prayer, fasting, and charity, but he had insulted this one, consumed the wealth of that one, struck this one, and reviled that one. So he will be seated, and this one will be given from his good deeds, and that one will be given from his good deeds. If his good deeds run out before he settles what he owes of wrongdoing, some of their sins will be taken and thrown upon him, and then he will be thrown into the Fire.\""],[2768,"A man may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise for a long time, then Allah ends his deeds with the deeds of the people of the Fire, and He makes him one of the people of the Fire. And a man may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire for a long time, then Allah ends his deeds with the deeds of the people of Paradise, and He makes him one of the people of Paradise."],[2769,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and believe in me and what I have brought. If they do that, they protect their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[2770,"This world is the believer's prison and the disbeliever's paradise."],[2771,"There will come upon people a time when a man will invite his cousin and relative, saying: 'Come to ease and comfort.' Madinah would be better for them, if only they knew."],[2772,"The Hour will not arise until Madinah expels its wicked people as the bellows expel the dross of iron."],[2773,"Verily the heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so cool down the prayer."],[2774,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have relatives whom I maintain ties with but they cut me off; I am forbearing with them but they treat me ignorantly; and I do good to them but they mistreat me. He said: If you are as you say, then it is as if you are feeding them hot ashes, and Allah will remain a supporter against them as long as you continue in that."],[2775,"Whoever keeps a dog that is not a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."],[2776,"They were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey when they passed by the grave of Abu Righal. They said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: This is the grave of Abu Righal, and he was the father of Thaqif. He was a man from Thamud, and his dwelling was in the Haram. When Allah destroyed his people with what He destroyed them, He protected him because of his location in the Haram. Then he departed until when he reached here, he died and was buried, and a branch of gold was buried with him. So we hurried to it and extracted it."],[2777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mu'adh to Yemen and said: You will come upon a People of the Book, so let the first thing you call them to be the worship of Allah. When they come to know Allah, inform them that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has prescribed prayers upon them in their day and night. When they do that, inform them that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has prescribed zakat on their wealth."],[2778,"Abu Basra Humayl b. Basra met Abu Hurayrah while he was coming from al-Tur and said: If I had met you before you went there, you would not have gone. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The saddles of mount are only struck for three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the al-Aqsa Mosque."],[2779,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not look on the Day of Resurrection at one who drags his garment out of pride."],[2780,"When one of you prays, let him not allow anyone to pass in front of him; if the person refuses, then let him fight him, for he is a devil."],[2781,"He donated a horse in the path of Allah, then found it with its owner who had neglected it, and he had little wealth, so he wanted to buy it back. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: Do not buy it, even if he gives it to you for a dirham, for the one who takes back his gift is like a dog that returns to its vomit."],[2782,"When the servant performs ablution and rinses his mouth and sniffs water into his nose, his sins depart from his face until they leave from beneath his eyelashes. When he washes his hands, his sins depart from his hands until they leave from beneath his fingernails. When he wipes his head, his sins depart from his head until they leave from between his ears. When he washes his feet, his sins depart from his feet until they leave from beneath his toenails."],[2783,"I heard 'Umar say: O Allah, grant me martyrdom in Your path and death in the city of Your Prophet. I said: And how can that be? He said: Allah will bring it about when He wills."],[2784,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on the road to Makkah when a fog came upon us and separated the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: Where are the people? I said: The fog has separated them. He said: Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak until he completed it. I said it, and he said: The people and creation have never sought refuge with the like of it."],[2785,"When this verse was revealed: “And those who accuse chaste women and then do not bring four witnesses…” Saʿd b. ʿUbādah said: “If I saw a man with my wife, should I wait until I bring four witnesses?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Yes.” He said: “No, by the One who sent you with the truth! If I saw him, I would hasten upon him with the sword.” He said: “Look, O assembly of the Ansār, at what your chief is saying. Indeed Saʿd is jealous, and I am more jealous than him, and God, Mighty and Majestic, is more jealous than me.”"],[2786,"Fāṭimah came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him for a servant and complained to him about the work. He said: “You will not find that with us.” Then he said: “Shall I not direct you to what is better than a servant? Glorify God thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times when you go to your bed.”"],[2787,"The curse of God, the angels, and all people is upon a man who claims a people as his patrons without the permission of his patrons."],[2788,"When God, Mighty and Majestic, loves a servant, He says to Gabriel: “I love so-and-so, so love him.” Gabriel loves him, then Gabriel calls out to the inhabitants of heaven: “God, Mighty and Majestic, loves so-and-so, so love him.” So they love him, then acceptance is placed for him on earth. And evil is the opposite of that."],[2789,"We arrived in Madinah when a man from Banū Ghifār called Sibāʿ b. ʿUrfuṭah had been appointed as deputy over Madinah. We prayed the morning prayer with him, and in the first rakʿah he recited Sūrah Maryam, and in the other “Woe to the defrauders.” Among us was a man who defrauded, so when we finished the prayer we said: “Woe to so-and-so.” Then we went to him and caught up with the Messenger of God ﷺ after he had conquered Khaybar. He asked the people’s permission to allocate for us from the spoils, and they permitted him, so he allocated for us."],[2790,"He disliked a man resting one of his legs upon the other during prayer."],[2791,"These places of filth are attended by devils. When one of you enters them, let him say: “In the name of God, O God, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils, and from the accursed Satan.”"],[2792,"Let not fear of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it, or from reminding of something great, for speaking the truth or reminding of something great neither brings death nearer nor pushes provision farther away."],[2793,"When the sun is eclipsed, pray a prayer like the shortest prayer you have ever prayed."],[2794,"He forbade sleeping before the last evening prayer and conversing after it."],[2795,"Women came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, men have taken the virtue and jihād. Command us a deed by which we may attain the virtue of jihād in the way of God.” He said: “The work of one of you in her house lets her attain the deed of the fighter in the way of God.”"],[2796,"O Anas, perfect your ablution and your lifespan will be increased. Greet whoever you meet from my community and your good deeds will multiply. When you enter your house, greet, and the good of your house will increase. Show mercy to the young and honor the old."],[2797,"He prohibited on the day of Khaybar the flesh of domestic donkeys, and (also prohibited) the jallālah (an animal that eats dung), riding it, and eating its meat. He also prohibited that a woman be married along with her paternal aunt or along with her maternal aunt."],[2798,"The camel owners and the sheep owners boasted to each other in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Pride and arrogance are among the camel owners, while tranquility and dignity are among the sheep owners.'"],[2799,"The Prophet ﷺ entered one of the gardens of Madinah and sat on the edge of a well. Abu Bakr came seeking permission, so he said: 'Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.' Then Umar came seeking permission, so he said: 'Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.' Then Uthman came seeking permission, so he said: 'Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise along with affliction.'"],[2800,"I prayed behind Abu Hurayrah, and he would say takbir when lowering and when rising. I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: 'It is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[2801,"The Messenger of God ﷺ met Jibril ﷺ and extended his hand to him, but he refused to take it. The Messenger of God ﷺ called for water, performed wudu, then extended his hand to him, and he took it. He said: 'O Jibril, what prevented you from taking my hand?' He replied: 'You had taken the hand of a Jew, and I disliked that my hand touch a hand that had been touched by the hand of a disbeliever.'"],[2802,"Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under God's protection, so beware lest God seek you for anything of His protection."],[2803,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said on the day of Khaybar: 'I will surely send a man whom God will not disgrace.' He sent for Ali, who was in the saddle grinding, and none of you would grind. They brought him with inflamed eyes. He said: 'O Prophet of God, I can hardly see.' He blew into his eyes and shook the banner three times, then handed it to him, and victory was granted through him. He brought Safiyyah bt. Huyayy. Then he said to his cousins: 'Which of you will be my ally in this world and the Hereafter?' He said to each man among them: 'O so-and-so, will you be my ally in this world and the Hereafter?' three times, and each said: 'No.' Until he passed by the last of them. Ali said: 'O Prophet of God, I am your ally in this world and the Hereafter.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'You are my ally in this world and the Hereafter.' He said: He sent Abu Bakr with Surah al-Tawbah, then sent Ali after him. Abu Bakr said: 'O Ali, perhaps God and His Messenger are displeased with me.' Ali said: 'No, but the Prophet of God ﷺ said: \"It is not proper that anyone convey from me except a man from me and I am from him.\"' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ placed his garment over Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, then said: 'God only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you completely.' And he was the first to embrace Islam among the people after Khadijah. He said: Ali risked his own life, wearing the Prophet's ﷺ garment and sleeping in his place. He said: The polytheists were throwing at the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[2804,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at a group that had approached and said: 'The Azd have come to you, the finest of people in faces, the sweetest in mouths, and the most truthful in meeting.' Then he looked at a crowd that had approached and said: 'Who are these?' They said: 'This is Bakr b. Wa'il.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O God, mend their broken, shelter their outcast, and do not show me a beggar among them.'"],[2805,"Whoever endears himself to people with what they love, but openly opposes God with what He hates, will meet God, Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him."],[2806,"Disbelief in God is claiming a lineage that is not known, and disbelief in God is disowning a lineage even if it is slight."],[2807,"A strike with a whip is sufficient for you against a snake, whether you hit it or miss it."],[2808,"The bath on Friday is obligatory upon every adult male, and he should use a toothstick and touch perfume."],[2809,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping during Ramadan."],[2810,"Do not urinate in stagnant water."],[2811,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade nibadh and limas."],[2812,"None of you should pray while he feels any discomfort from filth."],[2813,"A man complained to the Prophet ﷺ about poor memory, so he said: \"Seek help with your right hand.\""],[2814,"Aisha asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \"O Messenger of God, I have two neighbors; to which of them should I give first?\" He said: \"To the one whose door is closer to you.\""],[2815,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded a man, when he lay down to sleep, to say: \"O God, I have turned my face to You, and I have leaned my back upon You, in fear and desire toward You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down and Your Prophet whom You sent.\""],[2816,"Whoever misses three Friday prayers without excuse, a seal is placed upon his heart."],[2817,"The Prophet ﷺ entered ihram for his Hajj during one of the two evening prayers."],[2818,"Woe to the heels from the Fire."],[2819,"The best treatment you use is cupping and sea costus."],[2820,"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I came to the lowest heaven, and there I saw men whose tongues and lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: \"O Gabriel, who are these?\" He said: \"These are the orators of your community.\""],[2821,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he said: “O Aisha, if only we had someone to talk to us.” I seized the opportunity from him and said: “Should we not send for Abu Bakr?” He remained silent. Then he said: “O Aisha, if only we had someone to talk to us.” I seized the opportunity from him and said: “Should we not send for Umar?” He remained silent toward me. Then he called a servant of his and whispered to him, and suddenly Uthman was asking permission to enter. He gave him permission, and he leaned over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leaned over him, and they began whispering to each other. By Allah, I do not know what they were saying. When he raised his head, he turned to leave, but the Prophet ﷺ called him and said: “O Uthman, perhaps Allah will clothe you with a shirt, and if the hypocrites want you to take it off, do not take it off.” He said this three times. I said to her: “O Mother of the Believers, where were you regarding this hadith?” She said: “I forgot it, by the Lord of the Kaaba, until the man was killed.”"],[2822,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on his mount wherever it turned with him, east or west, and he would perform witr on it."],[2823,"Indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has disliked three things for you: gossip and idle talk, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."],[2824,"The son of Adam is created with ninety-nine deaths beside him; if the deaths miss him, he falls into old age until he dies."],[2825,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage when the sacrificial camels were brought. He said: “Call Abu al-Hasan for me.” So he called Ali, and he said: “Take the lower part of the spear,” and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took its upper part. When he finished, he mounted the mule and seated Ali behind him."],[2826,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, or rejects something I commanded, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[2827,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, in what lies the salvation of this nation?” He said: “In the word that I presented to my uncle, but he refused it: the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.”"],[2828,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was circumambulating the House, his sandal strap broke. A man untied a strap from his sandal and handed it to him, but he refused to take it and said: “This is a favor, and I do not accept favors.”"],[2829,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to travel, he would set out on Thursday."],[2830,"When one of you intends to travel, let him bid farewell to his brothers, for they add good to his supplication through their supplications."],[2831,"Islam has not eradicated anything like it has eradicated miserliness."],[2832,"Do not declare anyone among the people of your qiblah to be an unbeliever because of a sin, even if they commit major sins, and pray behind every imam, and strive in jihad with every commander."],[2833,"It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he said the salam to his right: \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,\" and to his left: \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.\""],[2834,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the witr: \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,\" and \"Say: O disbelievers,\" and \"Say: He is Allah, the One.\""],[2835,"He was prostrating in Makkah when Iblis came and wanted to step on his neck, so [Jibril] blew at him a blow with his wing, and his feet did not settle on the ground until he reached the Jordan."],[2836,"Hafsah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, when you fall ill you put forward Abu Bakr?\" He said: \"It is not I who put him forward; rather, it is Allah who put him forward.\""],[2837,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and caught up with him at al-Baqi'. I heard him say: \"Peace be upon the people of the dwellings, the believers.\" Then my sandal strap broke, and he said to me: \"Raise your foot?\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my bachelorhood has grown long, and I am far from the abode of my people.\" He said: \"O Bashir, will you not praise Allah who took you by the forelock to Islam from among Rabi'ah: a people who think that were it not for them, the earth would have overturned with all upon it?\""],[2838,"Whoever ascends the mountain pass, the pass of al-Murar, then there will be forgiven for him what was forgiven for the Children of Israel. Jabir said: \"The first to ascend it were our horses, the Banu al-Khazraj, then the people followed.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"All of you is forgiven except the owner of the red camel.\" We said: \"Come, let the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seek forgiveness for you.\" He said: \"If I find my stray camel, that is more beloved to me than that your companion seek forgiveness for me.\" And behold, he was looking for a stray camel."],[2839,"What an excellent man Bilal is, and the mu'adhdhins will have the longest necks of all people."],[2840,"If he eats from the hadiy voluntarily, then he has incurred a loss."],[2841,"He came to 'A'ishah and asked permission to enter, but she disliked to grant him permission. When the Prophet ﷺ came, she said: \"O Prophet of Allah, Abu Qu'ays came to me and I refused to grant him permission.\" He said: \"Let your paternal uncle enter upon you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it was the woman who breastfed me, not the man.\" He said: \"He is your paternal uncle, so let him enter upon you.\""],[2842,"I was at the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when 'Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn came and sat to one side. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: \"You are upon good,\" and he had a Khaybari cloak, and he covered them with it and said: \"I am at war with whoever wages war against you, and at peace with whoever makes peace with you.\""],[2843,"He used to shake hands with women from under the garment."],[2844,"Indeed, your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has in the days of your time refreshing breezes, so expose yourselves to them, that perhaps one of you may be touched by a breeze from them after which he will never be wretched again."],[2845,"He used to say when the wind blew strongly: “O Allah, make it a fertilizing wind, not a barren one.”"],[2846,"What did the Prophet ﷺ say to your father concerning the Night of Decree? He said: My father was a desert dweller, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with a night in which I should come down (from the desert). He said: Come down on the twenty-third night. When he turned away, he said: “Seek it in the last ten.”"],[2847,"Whatever the sea casts up and then recedes from, eat it; but whatever dies in it or floats, do not eat it."],[2848,"The days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking, so no one should fast them."],[2849,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade me from drinking from a vessel of silver."],[2850,"I had a nosebleed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he said to me: “Perform ablution.”"],[2851,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I will never abandon as long as I live: the Witr prayer before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and the Duha prayer."],[2852,"Whatever of the lower garment is below the two ankles is in the Fire."],[2853,"I asked Aisha about the voluntary prayer of the Prophet ﷺ during travel. She said: “Two rak‘ahs after every prayer.”"],[2854,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in one of the mountain passes of Madinah when he heard a man praying at night and reciting the Mother of the Qur’an. The Prophet ﷺ stood and listened until he finished it, then said: “There is nothing like it in the Qur’an.”"],[2855,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go out to the cemetery walking and return walking, as did Abu Bakr and Umar."],[2856,"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are matters that are doubtful. Whoever avoids them is more careful for his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into doubtful matters is likely to fall into the unlawful, like a shepherd grazing around a sanctuary who is likely to graze within the sanctuary without realizing it."],[2857,"When Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ with the Quran, the first thing he would recite to him was Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim. When Jibril said Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim a second time, the Prophet ﷺ knew that he had completed the surah."],[2858,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Ali to Fatimah, he said: \"O Ali, do not go in to your wife until you give her something.\" He said: \"I have nothing, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Give her your Hutamiyyah coat of mail.\""],[2859,"No man has camels and does not pay what is due on them in their strength and their milk, except that on the Day of Resurrection he will be thrown down for them in a wide, level plain. They will come as numerous as they ever were, and as fat, lively, and large as they ever were, and they will trample him with their hooves. Every time the last of them passes, the first of them returns, on a day whose length is fifty thousand years.\" And he said similar regarding sheep, and he said similar regarding gold and silver."],[2860,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I bought the allotted land of the Banu So-and-so and made such-and-such profit from it.\" He said: \"Shall I not tell you of something that brings greater profit than that?\" He said: \"Does such a thing exist?\" He said: \"A man who learns ten verses.\" So the man went and learned ten verses, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him."],[2861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked for any odor to be noticed from him that would cause annoyance."],[2862,"I am holding onto your waists, saying: Beware of the Fire, beware of the prescribed punishments—three times. Then I will be your forerunner at the pond. Whoever arrives there will have succeeded. Men will be brought, and just when I recognize them and they recognize me, they will be snatched away from me. I will say: My Lord, my companions. It will be said: They kept turning back on their heels."],[2863,"We were in severe need. My family told me to go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him for something. So I went, and the first thing I heard the Prophet ﷺ say was: \"Whoever seeks to be self-sufficient, Allah will enrich him. Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will keep him chaste. And whoever asks us, we will not withhold anything from him if we find it.\" So I said to myself: I will certainly seek self-sufficiency and Allah will enrich me, and I will certainly seek chastity and Allah will keep me chaste. And I did not ask the Prophet ﷺ for anything."],[2864,"The distance between the two ends of my pond is like the distance between Sanaa and Madinah."],[2865,"I certainly turn to Allah in repentance seventy times a day."],[2866,"When we returned from the campaign of Hudaybiyyah, we had been prevented from our rites. We were between grief and sorrow, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: \"Indeed, We have granted you a clear conquest\" to the end of the verse. So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"A verse has been sent down to me that is better than the world and all that is in it.\""],[2867,"Abu al-Jawza, shall I not tell you? Shall I not gift you? Shall I not give you?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever prays four rak'ahs, reciting in each rak'ah the Mother of the Quran and a surah, then when he finishes the recitation he says: Subhan Allah, wal-hamdu lillah, wa la ilaha illa Allah, wa Allahu akbar—this is one—until he completes fifteen. Then he bows and says it ten times. Then he rises and says it ten times. Then he prostrates and says it ten times. Then he rises and says it ten times. Then he prostrates and says it ten times. Then he raises his head and says it ten times. That is seventy-five in each rak'ah, until he finishes four rak'ahs.\" He said: \"Whoever prays them, every sin of his will be forgiven, small and great, old or new, past or yet to come.\""],[2868,"That the Prophet ﷺ went out to al-Safa from the gate of Banu Makhzum."],[2869,"Part of the excellence of a person's Islam is leaving that which does not concern him."],[2870,"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him."],[2871,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents."],[2872,"Between his eyes is written: 'Kafir' (disbeliever)."],[2873,"When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was taken on the night journey in Paradise, a river was presented to him whose banks were hollowed-out rubies. The angel who was with him struck it with his hand and extracted musk. He said to the angel who was with him: 'What is this?' He said: 'This is al-Kawthar which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given you.' He said: 'Then the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary was raised for me, and I saw a great light near it.'"],[2874,"Indeed, when the disbeliever performs a good deed, he is given a taste of it in this world. As for the believer, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, stores his good deeds for the Hereafter and provides him sustenance in this world as a reward for his obedience."],[2875,"When the people of Paradise see them, they will say: 'Who are these?' It will be said: 'These are the people of Hellfire.'"],[2876,"I came upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reciting: 'The mutual rivalry for worldly increase has distracted you' (Qur'an 102:1). He said: 'The son of Adam says: \"My wealth, my wealth.\" And what do you have of your wealth, O son of Adam, except what you eat and consume, or what you wear and wear out, or what you give in charity and send forth?'"],[2877,"When Allah decreed the creation, He wrote in a book with Him: 'My mercy prevails'—or he said: 'has preceded'—'over My wrath.'"],[2878,"The woman is 'awrah, and when she goes out, Satan seeks to tempt her, and she is never closer to Allah than when she is in the depth of her house."],[2879,"No sun rises or sets except that there are two angels on its sides calling out, heard by everything on earth except the two heavy ones (jinn and mankind): 'O people, come to your Lord. Indeed, what is little and sufficient is better than what is much and distracting.' And no sun sets except that there are two angels on its sides calling out: 'O Allah, give compensation to the one who spends, and give destruction to the one who withholds.'"],[2880,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicating at 'Arafah, with his hands raised to his chest like a poor person asking for food."],[2881,"There will be leaders who do not follow my guidance and do not practice my Sunnah, and there will be men whose hearts are the hearts of devils in human bodies.\" I said: What should I do if I live to see that? He said: \"You should hear and obey the supreme ruler, even if he strikes your back and takes your wealth; hear and obey."],[2882,"After me, men will administer your affairs who will introduce to you what you disapprove of, and disapprove of what you recognize. There is no obedience to one who disobeys God."],[2883,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I have married off my daughter, and I would like you to help me with something. He said: \"I have nothing, but come tomorrow and bring me a wide-mouthed bottle and a stick of wood, and the sign between me and you is that I will close the side of the door.\" He said: So he brought him a wide-mouthed bottle and a stick of wood, and he began wiping the sweat from his forearms until the bottle was full. Then he said: \"Take it, and instruct your daughter that when she wants to perfume herself, she should dip this stick into the bottle and perfume herself with it.\" He said: So when she perfumed herself, the people of Madinah could smell that perfume, and they were called the House of the Perfumed Ones."],[2884,"I came as a delegate with my grandfather Hidhyam to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: O Messenger of God, I have sons with beards and others, and this is the youngest of them. The Messenger of God ﷺ brought me close and wiped my head, and said: \"May God bless you.\" Al-Dhayyal said: I saw Hanzalah when a man with a swollen face or a sheep with a swollen udder was brought to him, and he would say: In the name of God, on the place of the palm of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would wipe it, and the swelling would go away."],[2885,"Ammar is such and such and such, so long as he does not reach old age."],[2886,"He used to give two salutations in prayer."],[2887,"No two men love each other for the sake of God except that the one more beloved to God, the Mighty and Majestic, is the one who loves his companion more intensely."],[2888,"Fast from one white (moon) to the next white (moon)."],[2889,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed wearing sandals and leather socks."],[2890,"Recite the Quran with sadness, for it was revealed with sadness."],[2891,"Indeed, in Paradise there are chambers whose exteriors can be seen from their interiors, and their interiors from their exteriors. God has prepared them for those who love one another for His sake, visit one another for His sake, and spend on one another for His sake."],[2892,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in his sandals, and sometimes he would take them off."],[2893,"I saw Anas b. Malik at the corner and said: Tell me about the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ, how was it? For I have heard that you used to perform his ablution for him. He said: \"Yes.\" He called for water for ablution, and a basin and a carved cup were brought — he says: as if carved from the earth — and it was placed before him. He poured water over his hands and thoroughly washed his palms, then rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, then brought out his right hand and washed it three times, then washed the left one three times, then wiped his head once, except that he passed it over his ears and wiped them, then he put both his palms into the water."],[2894,"Two men traveled through a vast desert: a worshipper and another who was given to wrongdoing. The worshipper became so thirsty that he collapsed, and his companion kept looking at him, having a small container with some water. He kept looking at him while he lay prostrate and said: By God, if this righteous servant dies of thirst while I have water, I will never attain any good from God; and if I give him my water to drink, I will surely die. So he put his trust in God and resolved, and he sprinkled some of his water on him and gave him the rest to drink. He got up and they crossed the desert. Then on the Day of Resurrection, the one given to wrongdoing will be brought to account and ordered to the Fire. The angels will drive him, and he will see the worshipper and say: O so-and-so, do you not know me? He will say: And who are you? He will say: I am so-and-so who preferred you over myself on the day of the desert. He will say: Yes, I know you. He will say to the angels: Stop. They will stop, and he will come and stand, and he will call upon his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, saying: O Lord, You know the favour he did me, and how he preferred me over himself. O Lord, grant him to me. He will say to him: He is yours. He will come and take his brother by the hand and enter him into Paradise."],[2895,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"Gather your companions.\" So I went looking for them in the mosque one by one, waking them, and we came to the door of the Prophet ﷺ and entered. A plate of food, about two mudds of barley, was placed before us. He said to us: \"Eat in the name of God.\" And when the plate was placed, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is nothing in the household of Muhammad except what you see.\" We ate until we were full, and some remained of it. We were between seventy and eighty. It was said to Abu Hurayrah: What was it like when you finished? He said: \"The same as when it was placed, except that it had the traces of fingers.\""],[2896,"When the Prophet ﷺ became gravely ill, and ʿĀʾishah and Ḥafṣah were with him, ʿAlī entered. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he raised his head and said: \"Come close to me, come close to me,\" and he leaned him against himself. He remained with him until he passed away. When he died, ʿAlī stood up and locked the door. Al-ʿAbbās came with the Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib and they stood at the door. ʿAlī kept saying: \"You were always good in life and good in death,\" and his fragrance spread, a pleasant scent the like of which they had never experienced. Someone said: \"It is the scent of your longing, like the longing of a woman. Turn to your companion.\" ʿAlī said: \"Let al-Faḍl b. al-ʿAbbās enter to me.\" The Anṣār said: \"We adjure you by God for our share in the Messenger of God,\" so they let in a man from among them called Aws b. Khawlī, carrying a water jar in one of his hands. They heard a voice in the house: \"Do not strip the Messenger of God ﷺ; wash him as he is in his shirt.\" So ʿAlī washed him, inserting his hand under the shirt, while al-Faḍl held the garment away from him and the Anṣārī poured water. On ʿAlī's hand was a cloth, inserting his hand under the shirt."],[2897,"The Arabs used to make one year a month and another year two months, and they would not perform the Hajj correctly except once every twenty-six years. That is the postponement (al-nasīʾ) which God, Mighty and Majestic, mentioned in His Book. When the year came in which Abū Bakr performed Hajj with the people, the Hajj coincided with its proper time that year, and God called it the Greater Hajj. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ performed Hajj in the following year, and the people began the months anew. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Time has returned to its original state as it was on the day God created the heavens and the earth.\""],[2898,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in Makkah at [the recitation of] al-Najm, and the Muslims, the polytheists, the jinn, and humans prostrated with him."],[2899,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is due, begin with the evening meal."],[2900,"He forbade mixing fresh ripe dates and unripe dates."],[2901,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out one day from his house, accompanied by some of his companions. He took one of the roads of Madinah and passed by the courtyard of some people, where a dead kid was thrown in their yard. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood over it, looking at it, then turned to his companions and said: \"Do you see this kid? It became worthless to its owners, so they threw it away.\" They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"By God, the world is more insignificant to God than this kid is to its owners when they threw it away like this.\""],[2902,"\"O God, forgive those who shave their heads.\" A man from the people said: \"O Prophet of God, and those who shorten?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O God, forgive those who shave their heads.\" The man said: \"O Prophet of God, and those who shorten?\" Until on the fourth time he said: \"And those who shorten.\""],[2903,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"I long for jihad, but I am unable to do it.\" He said: \"Are either of your parents still alive?\" He said: \"My mother.\" He said: \"Then strive to please God in being dutiful to her. If you do that, you will be a pilgrim, a performer of ʿumrah, and a mujāhid — if your mother is pleased with you. So fear God and be dutiful to her.\""],[2904,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he was eating the heart of a palm tree with the people, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Among the trees there is a tree that is like the Muslim man.\" The people fell silent until I almost asked the Messenger of God ﷺ though I was the youngest of the people. Then he said: \"It is the palm tree.\""],[2905,"I asked al-Husayn b. Ali about the tashahhud of Ali, and he said: It is the tashahhud of the Prophet ﷺ. So I said..."],[2906,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never given a choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them."],[2907,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some boys and greeted them."],[2908,"The Prophet ﷺ proclaimed them both, meaning: Hajj and Umrah."],[2909,"Whoever says 'Glory be to Allah', ten are recorded for him; and whoever says it ten times, a hundred are recorded for him. Whoever seeks Allah's forgiveness, He forgives him. Whoever assists in a dispute with wrongdoing or without knowledge remains in Allah's displeasure until he desists. Whoever's intercession blocks one of Allah's prescribed punishments has opposed Allah. Whoever dies owing a dinar or a dirham, it will be deducted from his good deeds, for there is neither dinar nor dirham there."],[2910,"This community will have twelve leaders; those who abandon them will not harm them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ whispered a word that I did not hear. I said to my father: What was the word that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whispered? He said: \"All of them are from Quraysh.\""],[2911,"Whoever kills a person under a covenant without right will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance can be found from a distance of five hundred years."],[2912,"Between the east and the west is the qiblah."],[2913,"The husband of Barirah was a slave."],[2914,"Umar performed Hajj in the year of the famine, the year sixteen. When he was between al-Suqya and al-Arj in the middle of the night, a rider appeared to him on the road and shouted: 'O caravan, is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among you?' Umar said to him: 'Woe to you, are you sane?' He said: 'Sanity brought me to you. Has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away?' They said: 'He has passed away.' He wept and the people wept. He said: 'Who took charge of the matter after him?' They said: 'The son of Abu Quhafah.' He said: 'The pious one of Banu Taym?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Is he with you?' They said: 'He has passed away.' He said: 'Then he supplicated, and the people supplicated.' He said: 'Who took charge of the matter after him?' It was said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab.' He said: 'The fair-skinned one of Banu Adi?' They said: 'Yes, he is the one speaking to you.' He said: 'Why did you not mention the white one of Banu Umayyah or the bald one of Banu Hashim?' They said: 'That already happened. What is your need?' He said: 'I met the Messenger of Allah while I was Abu Aqil al-Juayli, at the pool of Juayl. I embraced Islam and pledged allegiance, and I drank with him a drink of sawiq. He drank the first part of it and gave me the last part. By Allah, I have continued to feel its fullness whenever I am hungry, its coolness whenever I am thirsty, and its quench whenever I am parched until this day of mine. Then I climbed this white mountain, I, my wife, and daughters of mine. I used to pray in it five prayers every day and night, fast one month in the year, and slaughter for the tenth of Dhu al-Hijjah. That is what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me, until this year entered. By Allah, no sheep remained for us except one sheep, which the wolf attacked last night and ate part of it, and we ate part of it. Help, help!' Umar said: 'Help has come to you. Meet us at the water in the morning.' Umar went on until he came to the water, and he began waiting and delayed the departure because of him, but he did not come. He called the keeper of the water and said: 'Abu Aqil al-Juayli has with him three daughters and his wife. When he comes to you, spend on him, his family, and his children until I pass by you on my return, if Allah wills.' When Umar completed his Hajj, he returned and called the keeper of the water and said: 'What did Abu Aqil do?' He said: 'He came to me the next day, the day you told me, and he was feverish. He fell ill with me for some nights, then he died. That is his grave.' Umar turned to his companions and said: 'Allah did not approve of your trial for him.' Then he stood among the people and prayed over him, and he took charge of his daughters and wife, and he used to spend on them."],[2915,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to rub his mouth with the siwak."],[2916,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for some of his wives with a pot of harisah."],[2917,"'Umar addressed us at al-Jabiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us as I stand among you, and said: Honor my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will spread until a man gives testimony without being asked to testify, and a man takes an oath without being asked to take an oath. Whoever desires the best of Paradise, let him keep to the congregation, for Satan is with the lone individual and is further from two. Indeed, no man should be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. Indeed, whoever is pleased by his good deeds and distressed by his evil deeds is a believer."],[2918,"Islam is built on five: that Allah be worshipped, establishing the prayer, giving the zakat, performing the Hajj of the House of Allah, and fasting Ramadan. A man from the nobles of the people of Syria who was sitting with him said: 'Do you command the worship of Allah?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then he counted fasting before Hajj.' He said: 'I would only make it the last of them, thus I heard it from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[2919,"That he mentioned wiping over the leather socks in the presence of 'Umar, Sa'd, and 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar. 'Umar said: 'Sa'd is more knowledgeable than you.' Then 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas said: 'O Sa'd, we do not deny that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped, but did he wipe after Surat al-Ma'idah was revealed?' He said: 'No one spoke, for it made everything clear, and it was the last surah of the Qur'an to be revealed except for Bara'ah.'"],[2920,"Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise. Abu al-Darda' said: 'Even if he commits adultery and steals?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Even if he commits adultery and steals, in spite of Abu al-Darda'.'"],[2921,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon and said in his sermon: My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of from what He taught me on this day: Every wealth I have bestowed upon My servant is lawful. I created all My servants as pure monotheists, but the devils came to them and diverted them from their religion, forbade them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, looked upon the people of the earth and despised them, both non-Arabs and Arabs, except for remnants of the People of the Book. And He said: I have sent you only to test you and to test by you. I have sent down upon you a Book that water will not wash away, which you read while asleep and awake. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to come to Quraysh. I said: O Lord, then they will smash my head until it becomes like bread. He said: Drive them out as they drove you out, fight them and We will support you, spend and We will spend on you, send an army and I will send five times its like from the angels."],[2922,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."],[2923,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has servants who know people by their appearance."],[2924,"We prayed Zuhr behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he finished his prayer, he turned to us angrily and called out with a voice that reached even the young women in their chambers, saying: O assembly of those who have submitted but faith has not entered their hearts, do not harm the Muslims, and do not seek their faults. For whoever seeks the fault of his Muslim brother, Allah will expose his own faults, even if he is in the privacy of his own home."],[2925,"Pulpits of gold will be placed for the prophets, on which they will sit, but my pulpit will remain, and I will not sit on it. I will stand before my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, upright for my community, fearing that He might send me to Paradise while my community remains after me. Then I will say: O Lord, my community, my community. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: O Muhammad, what do you want Me to do with your community? I will say: O Lord, make their reckoning fair. Then they will be brought and judged. Some of them will enter Paradise by the mercy of Allah, and some will enter Paradise by my intercession. I will continue to intercede until I am given writs for men who had been sent to the Fire, so much so that Malik, the keeper of the Fire, will say: O Muhammad, you have left none of your community to the wrath of your Lord."],[2926,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel from janabah, and I would say: Leave some for me, leave some for me."],[2927,"A man being killed defending his property is martyrdom."],[2928,"Indeed, Allah (Mighty and Sublime) loves lofty matters, and He detests their trivialities."],[2929,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, he raised his hands when he opened the prayer, when he said the takbir for bowing, and when he raised his head from bowing."],[2930,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of the dawn prayer before the sun rises has not missed it, and whoever catches one rak'ah of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets has not missed it."],[2931,"The Friday prayer is two rak'ahs, the Eid al-Fitr prayer is two rak'ahs, the Eid al-Adha prayer is two rak'ahs, and the travel prayer is two rak'ahs—complete, not shortened—according to the words of the Prophet ﷺ."],[2932,"Whoever aids a wrongdoer in falsehood to invalidate a truth by his falsehood has disowned himself from the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger. And whoever consumes a dirham of usury, it is like thirty-three acts of fornication. And whoever's flesh grows from ill-gotten gains, the Fire is more entitled to him."],[2933,"Umm Bani Abi Talhah came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not ashamed of the truth. Is a woman required to perform ghusl if she sees what a man sees?' I laughed and said: 'Does a woman have wet dreams?' He said: 'Yes, otherwise how would the child resemble its mother?'"],[2934,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled regarding the fetus with a ghurrah: a male slave, or a female slave, or a horse, or a mule."],[2935,"I was eating with the Prophet ﷺ some hais in a bowl. 'Umar passed by, and he called him, and he ate. Then his finger touched my finger, and he said: 'Hass! Oh! Oh! If only I were obeyed regarding you, no eye would ever see you.' Then the verse of hijab was revealed."],[2936,"We did not fast twenty-nine days with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more often than we fasted thirty days."],[2937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that your father's neck be struck with patience; he did not inherit him. He said: 'Who will care for the children after me?' He said: 'They will have the Fire. Sufficient for you is what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approved for you.'"],[2938,"Among the signs of a hypocrite: when he speaks, he lies; when he promises, he breaks his promise; and when you entrust him, he betrays you."],[2939,"Indeed, the people of the highest degrees will be seen by those below them just as you see the star in the sky. And indeed, Abu Bakr and 'Umar are among them, and how excellent they are!"],[2940,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “She has irregular bleeding,” and she claimed that he said: “That is a vein. So when it comes, leave prayer; and when it departs, perform ghusl, wash the blood from yourself, then pray.”"],[2941,"Two traits—or two qualities—are easy, but few practice them: the five prayers. Glorify Allah ten times, praise Him ten times, and magnify Him ten times after each prayer. That is one hundred and fifty on the tongue, and one thousand five hundred in the scale. And when you retire to your bed, glorify, magnify, and praise Allah one hundred times. That is one hundred on the tongue and one thousand in the scale."],[2942,"I seek Allah’s forgiveness every day and repent to Him one hundred times."],[2943,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you with salam, but how should we invoke blessings upon you?” He said: “Say: O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent prayers upon Ibrahim. Indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim. Indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.”"],[2944,"He used to shorten the prayer at al-‘Aqiq."],[2945,"I asked ‘A’ishah: “What would you provide for the Prophet ﷺ when you traveled with him, or performed Hajj, or went on a military expedition?” She said: “I would provide him a bottle of oil, a comb, a mirror, two scissors, a kohl container, and a siwak.”"],[2946,"Whoever says at the time of his death: “There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah,” the Fire will never consume him."],[2947,"Whoever drags his izār out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[2948,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman with irregular bleeding. He said: “She should count the days of her regular periods, then perform ghusl after each purity, then use a cloth, and pray.”"],[2949,"The Prophet ﷺ finished his tawāf at al-Marwah."],[2950,"Al-‘Abbās came to visit the Prophet ﷺ during his illness, so he lifted him and seated him in his sitting place on the bed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “May Allah raise you, O uncle.” Al-‘Abbās said: “Here is ‘Alī seeking permission.” He said: “Let him enter.” So he entered, and with him were al-Hasan and al-Husayn. Al-‘Abbās said: “These are your children, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “And they are your children, O uncle.” He said: “Do you love them?” He said: “May Allah love you as He loves them.”"],[2951,"Al-‘Abbās said: “O Messenger of Allah, we recognize rancor in the faces of some people.” He said: “How do you recognize it?” He said: “A group sits in conversation; when I appear to them they stop because of my kinship to you. If they were sincere to Allah and His Messenger, they would not stop because of my kinship to you.” He said: “Do you know them?” He said: “Yes.” Al-‘Abbās placed his hand on the Prophet’s forearm ﷺ, then entered the mosque. Al-‘Abbās said to him: “This group is among them.” The Prophet ﷺ took al-‘Abbās’s hand and raised it, then said: “Whoever does not love this uncle of mine for Allah and for his kinship to me is not a believer.”"],[2952,"Whoever engages in a military expedition at sea in the path of God—and God knows best who truly campaigns in His path—has fulfilled all his obedience to God, sought Paradise in every way it can be sought, and fled from the Fire in every way it can be fled from."],[2953,"When a man wakes his wife during the night, and they both perform ablution and pray, they are recorded among the men who remember God often and the women who remember God often."],[2954,"I had forbidden you to visit graves; now visit them, but do not utter anything obscene. I had forbidden you (to drink from) certain vessels; now drink from whatever vessel you wish, but do not become intoxicated. I had forbidden you (to keep) the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days; now keep as much as you wish."],[2955,"There is no prophet or ruler who does not have two types of close associates: one that commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and one that does not spare any effort to corrupt him. Whoever is protected from the evil of the latter is indeed protected."],[2956,"On the morning after I had a wet dream, I went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him that I had experienced a wet dream. He said, 'Do not enter upon women.' No day that came upon me was harder than that."],[2957,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade shaving the back of the neck, except for cupping."],[2958,"Whoever spends two pairs (of anything) from his wealth in the path of God, the doorkeepers of Paradise will call him on the Day of Resurrection, each one inviting him to what he has: 'O so-and-so, this is better.'"],[2959,"Bear witness to this Stone as a good thing, for on the Day of Resurrection it will be an intercessor whose intercession is accepted. It has a tongue and two lips, and it will testify for whoever touches it."],[2960,"The children of the polytheists are servants of the people of Paradise."],[2961,"When one of you fights his companion, let him avoid his face."],[2962,"He forbade during the expedition of Awtas that a man have intercourse with a pregnant captive until she gives birth."],[2963,"O God, bless my community in its early mornings."],[2964,"I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He put his hand under his chin and ran his fingers through his beard. I said, “What is this?” He said, “This is what my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to do.”"],[2965,"He asked her about the vessels which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade. She said, “He forbade al-dubbāʾ, al-ḥantam, al-naqīr, and al-muzaffat.” I said, “What are these green jars—are they al-ḥantam?” She said, “No, they are the red jars. Pitch used to be carried in them, and wine used to be carried in them from Egypt to Madinah, so he forbade them.”"],[2966,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[2967,"He used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday, in the first rakʿah, “Alif Lām Mīm, the revelation of the Book… the prostration” (Q 32), and in the second rakʿah, “Has there come upon man…” (Q 76)."],[2968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform the major ablution on Friday."],[2969,"I was sent only as a mercy, guided."],[2970,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ, “How can I know when I have done well and when I have done evil?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “When you hear your neighbors say, ‘You have done well,’ then you have done well. And when you hear them say, ‘You have done evil,’ then you have done evil.”"],[2971,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, he spread his arms so that the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[2972,"He disliked—or forbade—sleeping before it and talking after it."],[2973,"Part of the perfection of prayer is the straightening of the rows."],[2974,"Among what people have retained from the earlier prophethood is: “If you feel no shame, do as you wish.”"],[2975,"No one will enter Paradise except with a pass: “In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is a book from Allah for so-and-so, son of so-and-so. Admit him into a lofty garden, whose clusters of fruit are near.”"],[2976,"Indeed, I have a right over Quraysh, and indeed, Quraysh have a right over you: as long as they rule, they act justly; and when they are entrusted, they fulfill the trust; and when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy. So whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of God."],[2977,"Indeed, the Ansar are my inner garment to which I resort. So accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers, for they have fulfilled what was upon them, and what remains is what is for them."],[2978,"When he saw rain, he would say: \"O God, (make it) a beneficial downpour.\""],[2979,"Indeed, when a servant gives charity from what is good, God accepts it from him. He takes it with His right hand and nurtures it as one of you nurtures his colt or his young camel. A man may give a date in charity, and it grows for him in the hand of God—or he said: in the palm of God—until it becomes like a mountain. So give charity."],[2980,"The upper giving hand is better than the lower receiving hand."],[2981,"A man said: What is sin, O Messenger of God? He said: \"Sin is what chafes in your heart, so abandon it.\" He said: Then what is faith? He said: \"Whoever is distressed by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed is a believer.\""],[2982,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ while there were people with him. A man among those present said: Indeed I love this man for the sake of God. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Have you informed him?\" He said: No. He said: \"Then go to him and inform him.\" So he went to him and informed him. The man said: May He for whose sake you loved me love you. He said: Then he returned to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he told him what he said. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You will be with the one you love, and you will have what you hoped for.\""],[2983,"The Messenger of God ﷺ heard some people disputing about the Quran, so he said: \"Those before you were only destroyed by this: they struck the Book of God, parts of it against other parts. But the Book of God was revealed confirming parts of it other parts. So do not deny parts of it by other parts. Whatever you know of it, speak it; and whatever you are ignorant of, refer it to its knower.\""],[2984,"There was a Makhzumi woman who used to borrow goods and deny having received them. So the Prophet ﷺ ordered that her hand be cut off."],[2985,"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[2986,"There is no shighar (type of marriage exchange) in Islam."],[2987,"There is no shighar (type of marriage exchange) in Islam."],[2988,"Whoever swears and says, 'If Allah wills,' will not break his oath."],[2989,"And give them from the wealth of Allah that He has given you. He said: 'A quarter of the contract (mukatabah).'"],[2990,"Indeed, a man may perform the deeds of the people of good for seventy years, but when he makes a bequest, he is unjust in his bequest, so his deeds are sealed with the worst of his actions and he enters the Fire. And a man may perform the deeds of the people of evil for seventy years, but he is just in his bequest, so his deeds are sealed with the best of his actions and he enters Paradise. Then Abu Hurayrah would say: 'Recite if you wish: These are the limits of Allah ... and for him is a humiliating punishment.'"],[2991,"The Prophet ﷺ ransomed the prisoners of Badr, and the ransom for each one of them was four thousand. He killed 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt before the ransom. 'Ali b. Abi Talib stood before him and killed him in retaliation. He said: 'Who will care for the children, O Muhammad?' He said: 'The Fire.'"],[2992,"I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he wiped over his leather socks after Surah al-Ma'idah was revealed."],[2993,"None of you should urinate in his bathing place and then perform ablution in it, for most of whispering (waswas) comes from that."],[2994,"I came to Madinah and entered the mosque for the 'Asr prayer. I advanced to the first row, but a man came, took me by the shoulder, and moved me back, taking my place after the imam had already said the takbir and I had said the takbir. When we finished the prayer, he turned to me and said: 'I only moved you back because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us that the Muhajirun and Ansar should pray in the first row, and I knew you were not one of them, so I moved you back.' I asked: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Ubayy b. Ka'b.'"],[2995,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the people of Quba': 'What is this purification for which you have been singled out in this verse: In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, none of us comes out from the privy except that he washes his posterior.'"],[2996,"Indeed, salam (peace) is one of the names of Allah, so spread it among yourselves."],[2997,"Hamzah was killed on the day of Uhud, and a man from the Ansar was killed with him. Safiyyah bt. 'Abd al-Muttalib came with two garments to shroud Hamzah with them, but the Ansari had no shroud. The Prophet ﷺ drew lots between the two garments, then shrouded each of them in one garment."],[2998,"The best with which you change gray hair is henna and katam."],[2999,"Captives were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was a woman among the captives searching. When she found a child among the captives, she took him, pressed him to her belly, and suckled him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do you think this woman would throw her child into the Fire?' We said: 'No, by Allah, while she is able not to throw him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah is more merciful to His servants than this woman is to her child.'"],[3000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the day of sacrifice and said: “Whoever faces our qiblah, prays our prayer, and performs our sacrifice, let him not slaughter until he has prayed.” A man stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is a day on which meat is disliked, and I hastened my sacrifice to feed my family, my household, and my neighbors.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Repeat with another sacrifice.” He said: “I have a milking kid that is dearer to me than two meat sheep.” He said: “Slaughter it, for it is the best of your sacrifice, and no sacrifice after you will suffice for anyone.”"],[3001,"The jet-black dog is a devil."],[3002,"Whoever would like Allah to prolong his life, expand his provision, and avert from him an evil death, let him fear Allah and maintain family ties."],[3003,"The Prophet ﷺ looked toward Iraq, Syria, and Yemen and said: “O Allah, turn their hearts to obedience to You, and relieve what is behind them.”"],[3004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left neither gold nor silver, nor sheep nor camel. He left only a portion of barley, from which we ate for a time; then I measured it, and I wished I had not measured it."],[3005,"If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him immerse it completely, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure."],[3006,"Women do not have the middle of the road."],[3007,"When a boy knows his right hand from his left, command him to pray."],[3008,"He is not a liar who reconciles between people by saying good or conveying good."],[3009,"We used to say of the killer of a believer when he died: ‘He is in the Fire,’ and we used to say of one who committed a major sin and died upon it: ‘He is in the Fire,’ until Allah revealed this verse: Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that."],[3010,"Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be made to wear it around his neck on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."],[3011,"The bad breath of a fasting person is better in the sight of Allah than the scent of musk."],[3012,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was at the standing place at Jamʿ, and I said: O Messenger of God, I have come from the mountain of Ṭayyiʾ, and I have exhausted myself and worn out my mount. By God, I have not left any hill but I stood upon it. So is there any ḥajj for me, O Messenger of God? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever prays this prayer with us, and has come to ʿArafah, by night or by day, has completed his rites and his ḥajj is complete."],[3013,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I am not able to learn the Qurʾān, so teach me what will suffice me to say in the prayer. He said: Say: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is most great, and there is no power nor strength except through God. He said: O Messenger of God, this is for God, so what is for me to say? He said: Say: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me well-being, and provide for me. When the man turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said: Indeed, this one has attained all good, or: has learned all good, or something like this."],[3014,"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan cannot imitate me, nor the Kaʿbah."],[3015,"Whoever does not trim his moustache is not one of us."],[3016,"There are no tents after tents that were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, from which God wards off affliction as He wards off from these tents."],[3017,"We, the company of prophets, were commanded three things: to hasten the breaking of the fast, to delay the pre-dawn meal, and to place the right hand over the left in prayer."],[3018,"Do not sever relations, do not turn your backs on one another, do not hate one another, and be servants of God as brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days."],[3019,"Have mercy on those on earth, and the One in heaven will have mercy on you."],[3020,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to kiss and embrace while fasting, and which of you can control his desire as the Messenger ﷺ could control his?"],[3021,"The first to be called to Paradise are the ḥammādūn, those who praise God in ease and in hardship."],[3022,"ʿAmr b. Luḥayy b. Qamaʿah b. Khindif."],[3023,"For the traveler, three days and their nights; for the resident, a day and a night."],[3024,"I am the foremost of the Arabs to Paradise, Suhayb is the foremost of the Romans to Paradise, Bilal is the foremost of the Abyssinians to Paradise, and Salman is the foremost of the Persians to Paradise."],[3025,"There is no man among a people who commits sins while they are more numerous and mightier than him, and then they flatter him regarding his affair, except that Allah punishes them."],[3026,"When the Prophet ﷺ returned from a journey, he would pray two rak'ahs."],[3027,"When he said the takbir, he would raise his hands until they were level with his ears, saying: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You, blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god besides You.'"],[3028,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the two afternoon prayers—Zuhr or 'Asr—and said the salam after two rak'ahs. The swift among the people left, saying: 'The prayer has been shortened, the prayer has been shortened.' Among the people were Abu Bakr and 'Umar, but they were hesitant to speak to him. He went to a piece of wood in the mosque against which he used to place his hand. A man called Dhu al-Yadayn—long of hands—and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call him 'Dhu al-Yadayn,' said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?' He said: 'I did not forget, nor has it been shortened.' Then he asked the people, and they said: 'Dhu al-Yadayn has spoken the truth.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned and prayed two rak'ahs like his bowing or longer, then prostrated twice."],[3029,"Whoever performs ablution after ghusl is not from us."],[3030,"I saw 'Umar b. al-Khattab kissing the Stone and saying: 'By Allah, I know that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit, and had I not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing you, I would not have kissed you.'"],[3031,"Every prophet has a supplication with which he prayed and Allah answered him. I have deferred my supplication as intercession for my nation."],[3032,"The people of Paradise will miss people whom they used to know in this world, so they will come to the prophets and mention them, and they will intercede for them and be granted intercession. It will be said to them: 'The freed ones,' and all of them are freed ones. The water of life will be poured upon them."],[3033,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing gold and stringing it. A woman threw away a gold bracelet, and it remained in the mosque for days, no one taking it."],[3034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and when he finished, he said: 'Is there anyone here from Banu So-and-so?' No one answered him. Then he said: 'Is there anyone here from Banu So-and-so?' No one answered him. Then he said: 'Is there anyone here from Banu So-and-so?' A man said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, here is So-and-so.' He said: 'Your companion is being held back at the gate of Paradise because of a debt he owes.' A man said: 'His debt is on me, O Messenger of Allah.'"],[3035,"He would fast the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth of the month."],[3036,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a drink, and on his right was a Bedouin, and on his left was Abu Bakr. He drank, then 'Umar said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, give it to Abu Bakr.' But he gave it to the Bedouin, and said: 'The right-hand side, then the next right-hand side.'"],[3037,"Three people will be given their rewards twice on the Day of Resurrection: a man who had a slave woman, taught her good manners, then freed her and married her—he will have his reward twice; an owned slave who fulfils the right of Allah and the right of his master—he will have his reward twice; and a man who believed in his prophet, then lived until the Prophet ﷺ, believed in him and followed him—he will have his reward twice."],[3038,"This son of mine is a leader, and Allah will bring about reconciliation through him between two groups of Muslims."],[3039,"Indeed it is blessed; indeed it is the food of taste; indeed it is blessed; indeed it is the food of taste; indeed it is blessed; indeed it is the food of taste. Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me to honour him tonight.' He said: So he permitted him, and he went to a house and entered it, opened a door, and took handfuls of Ta'ifi raisins for us. He said: That was the first food I ate in Makkah until I left it. Then he said to me: 'I have been commanded to go out to a land of palm trees, and I think it is Yathrib. Go, for you are the messenger of the Messenger of Allah to your people.' When I came to my brother, he said: 'O my brother, what have you brought us?' or words to that effect. I said: 'I met him, became a Muslim, and pledged allegiance, and I called my brother to Islam.' He said: 'And I have already become a Muslim and pledged allegiance.' Then we came to our mother and called her to Islam. She said: 'I have no desire to turn away from your religion, and I have already become a Muslim and pledged allegiance.' He said: Then we departed and came to our people, and called them to Islam. Half of them became Muslim, and their leader Ima' b. Rahadah became Muslim and led them in prayer. The remaining half said: 'Leave us until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passes by us.' He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by them, and the remaining half became Muslim. He said: And Aslam said: 'We become Muslim on the same basis that Ghifar became Muslim.' He said: So they became Muslim. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Aslam—may Allah keep them safe; Ghifar—may Allah forgive them.' No one narrated this hadith from 'Abd Allah b. Bakr b. 'Abd Allah al-Muzani except Rawh b. Aslam, and no one narrated it from Rawh b. Aslam except al-Mufaddal b. Ghassan al-Ghallabi and Hajjaj b. al-Sha'ir."],[3040,"Visit occasionally, and you will increase in love."],[3041,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the people of the A'raf. He said: 'A people who were killed in the way of Allah while disobedient to their fathers. Martyrdom prevented them from entering the Fire, and disobedience prevented them from entering Paradise. They will be standing on a wall between Paradise and the Fire until their fat melts and their flesh withers, until Allah finishes the reckoning of all creatures. When He finishes the reckoning of all creatures, He will envelop them with mercy from Him and admit them to Paradise.'"],[3042,"The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins."],[3043,"I prayed and clasped my hands together, and my father forbade me and said: 'We used to do that, then we were commanded to place them on the knees.'"],[3044,"Islam began as something strange and will return to being strange as it began, so blessed are the strangers.' It was said: 'Who are the strangers?' He said: 'Those who set things right when people have become corrupted.'"],[3045,"A man may be among the people of prayer, zakat, hajj, 'umrah, and jihad—until he mentioned the shares of good—and he will not be rewarded on the Day of Resurrection except according to the measure of his intellect."],[3046,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not harm his neighbour. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honour his guest.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is his honour?' He said: 'His gift of hospitality is three nights; whatever is after that is charity.'"],[3047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr: 'When do you perform witr?' He said: 'I perform witr at the beginning of the night.' And he said to 'Umar: 'When do you perform witr?' He said: 'I perform witr at the end of the night.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Abu Bakr adopted caution, and 'Umar adopted strength.'"],[3048,"O son of Adam, if you were to commit sins as much as would fill the earth, but you did not associate anything with Me, I would grant you forgiveness as much as would fill the earth."],[3049,"Giving permission is part of announcing a death, and announcing a death is from the affairs of the pre-Islamic era."],[3050,"The best of you is the one who reads the Qur'an and teaches it."],[3051,"A boy of theirs died, and his father grieved over him with the deepest grief. A man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, called Hawshab, said: 'Shall I not tell you of something similar that I witnessed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'There was a man who used to frequent the Prophet ﷺ with his son. He stayed away for some days without coming to the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"What has become of so-and-so?\" They said: \"His son, who used to accompany him, has died.\" The Prophet ﷺ met him and said: \"Would it please you, O so-and-so, that your son be with you as the most energetic of youths? Would it please you, O so-and-so, that your son be a middle-aged man like the best of middle-aged men? Or it will be said to you: 'Enter Paradise as a reward for what was taken from you.'\""],[3052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek a private place for urinating just as he would seek a private place for lodging."],[3053,"The Prophet ﷺ would not go out on the day of Fitr until he had eaten, and he would not eat on the day of Sacrifice until he returned and ate from his sacrificial animal."],[3054,"O Aisha, the quickest of people to perish will be your people. I said: 'From Taym, may Allah make me your ransom?' He said: 'No, but this quarter of Quraysh; death will ravage them, and people will envy them.' I said: 'What will be the survival of people after them?' He said: 'They are the backbone of people; when they perish, people will perish.'"],[3055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque of Quba and saw them praying the Duha prayer, so he said: 'This is the prayer of the penitent.' He said: 'And they used to pray it when the young camels felt the heat.'"],[3056,"He used to pray witr with three units: he would recite in the first 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High', in the second 'Say, O disbelievers', and in the third 'Say, He is Allah, the One'."],[3057,"He forbade, or it was forbidden, that a man urinate in stagnant or still water, then perform ablution from it or bathe from it."],[3058,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep and I pity it.' He said: 'And the sheep, if you pity it, Allah will pity you.'"],[3059,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on some nights carrying his water for ablution when he heard a caller, so he said: 'O Anas, pour it out.' The caller said: 'O Allah, help me with what will save me from what You have made me fear.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'If only he had said its sister phrase.' It was as if the man was inspired with what the Messenger of Allah wanted, so he said: 'And grant me the longing of the truthful for what You have made them long for.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Alive, O Anas! Put down the ablution water and go to this caller and tell him to supplicate for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Allah may help him with what He has sent him with, and supplicate for his nation that they may accept what their Prophet has brought them in truth.' So I went to him and said: 'Supplicate for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Allah may help him with what He has sent him with, and supplicate for his nation that they may accept what their Prophet has brought them in truth.' He said: 'Who sent you?' I disliked to inform him and I had not asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission, so I said: 'What concern is it to you, may Allah have mercy on you, with what I ask of you?' He said: 'Will you not tell me who sent you?' So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him what he said, and he said: 'Tell him: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah.' He said to me: 'Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and welcome to his messenger. I was more deserving of coming to him. Convey peace to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him: Al-Khidr conveys peace to you and says to you: Allah has preferred you over the prophets as He preferred the month of Ramadan over all other months, and He has preferred your nation over all nations as He preferred the day of Friday over all other days.' When I turned away from him, I heard him say: 'O Allah, make me of this nation, the one on whom mercy is shown, rightly guided, and forgiven.'"],[3060,"May Allah brighten (the face of) a servant who hears my word, comprehends it, and memorizes it. For many a bearer of knowledge conveys it to one more knowledgeable than himself. Three things about which the heart does not harbor treachery: sincerity of action for Allah, giving sincere counsel to those in authority, and holding fast to the community."],[3061,"Keep women unclothed and they will stay in their chambers."],[3062,"Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer should perform the ritual bath."],[3063,"Whoever swears an oath and makes an exception, then does it and then breaks it, no expiation is upon him."],[3064,"The Hour will not rise until the world is dominated by the basest of the base (Lukaʿ son of Lukaʿ). The best of people is a believer between two noble ones."],[3065,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter. He said: \"Throw it away and what is around it, and eat (the rest) if it is solid.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if it is liquid?\" He said: \"Make use of it.\""],[3066,"Do not be harsh upon yourselves, for those before you perished only because of their harshness upon themselves. You will find their remnants in the monasteries and hermitages."],[3067,"Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from his heart, Allah will cause him to reach the stations of the martyrs even if he dies on his bed."],[3068,"If a neighbor asks a man to insert a piece of wood into his wall, he should not prevent him."],[3069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by the structure of a dome belonging to a man of the Ansar and said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"A dome.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Every building\"—and he gestured with his hand above his head like this—\"larger than this is a burden on its owner on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[3070,"Whoever acts deliberately hits the mark, or nearly does. Whoever acts hastily errs, or nearly does."],[3071,"Whoever is constant in four rakʿahs before the midday prayer and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire."],[3072,"Whoever touches his private part must perform ablution."],[3073,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded in three white Yemeni cotton garments."],[3074,"She said concerning the meat of sacrificial animals: We used to prepare some of it, and people would bring it to Madinah; they would not eat it except for three days. That was not a strict command, but he wanted them to eat from it."],[3075,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the illness in which he died: Bind my head, that I may go out to the mosque. So I bound his head with a yellow bandage, and then he went out to the mosque, supported between two men."],[3076,"Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and the one who spends on horses is like one who extends his hand in spending and does not withhold it."],[3077,"When I was taken up to the lowest heaven, I entered the Garden of Eden, and an apple fell into my hand. When I placed it in my hands, it split open, revealing a wide-eyed, beautiful houri, whose eyelashes were like the leading edges of eagles' wings. I said to her, 'Who are you?' She said, 'I am for the caliph after you.'"],[3078,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us saying: Seek refuge with God from the pit of sorrow. They said: O Messenger of God, what is the pit of sorrow? He said: \"A pit in a valley in the depths of Hell, from which Hell seeks refuge four hundred times every day. God has prepared it for the reciters who show off by their deeds. And the most hateful of creation to God, Mighty and Majestic, is a reciter who visits the governors.\""],[3079,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me the call to prayer of nineteen words, and the iqamah of seventeen words."],[3080,"There is no one who greets me but God returns my soul to me so that I may return the greeting."],[3081,"They said: O Messenger of God, the muezzins surpass us. He said: Say as the muezzin says, and when you finish, ask and you will be given."],[3082,"Three: whoever possesses one of them is guaranteed by God. Whoever goes out in the path of God is guaranteed by God: if He takes his soul, He will admit him to Paradise, and if He returns him to his family, then with whatever he attained of reward and booty. A man who is in the mosque is guaranteed by God: if He takes his soul, He will admit him to Paradise, and if He returns him to his family, then with whatever he attained of reward and booty. And a man who enters his house to sleep is guaranteed by God."],[3083,"Whoever prays the prayer at its proper time, completes its ablution, and perfects its standing, humility, bowing, and prostration, it departs white and shining, saying: May God preserve you as you preserved me. And whoever prays the prayer at other than its proper time, does not complete its ablution, and does not perfect its humility, bowing, or prostration, it departs black and dark, saying: May God neglect you as you neglected me. Then, when it reaches where God wills, it is folded up like an old garment is folded, and then it is struck with it on his face."],[3084,"Whoever says in the morning three times: “O Allah, to You belongs praise; there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I believe in You, sincerely devoting my religion to You. I have entered the morning upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I repent to You from the evil of my deeds, and I seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You,” then if he dies that day, he will enter Paradise. And if he says in the evening three times: “O Allah, to You belongs praise; there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have entered the evening upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I repent to You from the evil of my deeds, and I seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You,” then if he dies that night, he will enter Paradise.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to swear an oath that he would not swear about anything else, saying: “By Allah, no servant says it on a day when he arises in the morning and then dies that day except that he enters Paradise, and if he says it in the evening and then passes away that night, he enters Paradise.”"],[3085,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon to the people at Mina on a mule, wearing a green striped cloak, and a man from the people of Badr was before him interpreting for him. I came and inserted my hand between his feet and his sandal strap, and I marveled at its coolness."],[3086,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in an open space with nothing in front of him."],[3087,"O Messenger of Allah, some people like the humps of camels and the tails of sheep while they are still alive? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whatever is cut from a live animal is carrion.”"],[3088,"Whoever's neighbor asks him to drive a wooden peg into his wall, he should not prevent him."],[3089,"When a girl is born, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends an angel to her who escorts blessing, saying: “A weak one has come out from a weak one; her guardian will be aided until the Day of Resurrection.” And when a boy is born, Allah sends an angel to him from heaven, who kisses him between his eyes and says: “Allah sends you greetings of peace.”"],[3090,"I was sitting before the Prophet ﷺ while he was mentioning well-being and the great reward that Allah has prepared for its possessor if he is grateful, and mentioning affliction and the great reward that Allah has prepared for its possessor if he is patient. I said: “By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, that I be granted well-being and be grateful is dearer to me than that I be afflicted and be patient.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “The Messenger of Allah loves well-being along with you.”"],[3091,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has servants whom He keeps alive in well-being, causes to die in well-being, resurrects in well-being, and admits to Paradise in well-being."],[3092,"Three people whose testimony of “there is no god but Allah” is not accepted: the rider and the one ridden, the female rider and the one ridden by her, and the unjust imam."],[3093,"Abu Talha came to Umm Sulaym, the mother of Anas b. Malik, and Abu Talha was his stepfather. He said: “Do you have anything, O Umm Sulaym? I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was teaching the people of the Suffa Surah al-Nisa’, and he had tied a stone to his stomach from hunger.” She said: “I had some barley, so I ground it, then sent me to the markets,” and the markets were their gardens, “so I brought them some firewood, and made it into a flat loaf. Then he said: ‘Do you have any condiment?’ She said: ‘I had a small skin of ghee, but I do not know if anything remains in it.’ I brought it to him and squeezed it. He said: ‘The squeezing of two is more effective than the squeezing of one.’ So they both squeezed it and extracted from it something like a date. She greased the loaf with it. Then he called me and said: ‘O Anas, seek out the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ I said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘I left him with the people of the Suffa teaching them. Invite him, but do not invite anyone else with him; be careful not to disgrace me.’ So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he saw me, he said: ‘Perhaps your father sent you to us?’ I said: ‘Yes.’ He said to the people: ‘Go.’ They departed that day, and they were eighty men. He held my hand, and when I approached the house I pulled my hand from his. Abu Talha began looking for me in the house and throwing stones at me, saying: ‘You have disgraced me before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ Then he went out to him and told him the news. He said: ‘It will not harm you.’ Then he told them to sit, and they sat. Then he entered, and we brought him the loaf. He said: ‘Is there any condiment?’ Umm Sulaym said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, we had a small skin, and Abu Talha and I squeezed it.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Bring it, for the squeezing of three is more effective than the squeezing of two.’ So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought it, and he squeezed it with them. They extracted from it something like a date, and they wiped the loaf with it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped it with his hand, then invoked blessing upon it. Then he said: ‘Invite ten for me.’ So I invited ten, and they ate until they belched from fullness. They kept entering ten by ten until they were all full. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat, and we sat with him, and we ate until there was leftover.”"],[3094,"He went out for his need, and al-Mughira followed him with a water skin containing water. He took out his hands from under a fur garment, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks."],[3095,"Whoever dies on Friday or on Friday night is protected from the trial of the grave."],[3096,"O Hassan, satirize the polytheists, and Jibril is with you."],[3097,"One of you will not die until he has received his provision in full, so do not be slow in seeking provision. Fear Allah and be moderate in seeking; take what is lawful and leave what is forbidden."],[3098,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ let his forelock hang down as the People of the Book do, then later he parted it as the Arabs do. Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was uncertain about a matter practiced by the polytheists and the People of the Book - as long as no revelation had come concerning it - he would act according to the practice of the People of the Book."],[3099,"The previously married woman is to be consulted about herself; if she remains silent, that is her permission, but if she refuses, then there is no coercion over her."],[3100,"My pulpit is on one of the water channels of Paradise, and between my pulpit and the house of Aishah is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."],[3101,"You must use the siwak, for it is pleasing to the Lord and purifying for the mouth."],[3102,"Allah has cursed the people of qadar, those who deny some decree and affirm some decree."],[3103,"He used to say the takbir on the day of Fitr and Adha seven times in the first rak'ah and five times in the second, before the recitation."],[3104,"The tashahhud of the Prophet ﷺ was: In the name of Allah and by Allah, the best of names. Greetings, pure words, and prayers belong to Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. He sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner, and that the Hour is coming, there is no doubt about it. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. O Allah, forgive me and guide me. This is in the first two rak'ahs."],[3105,"In the year of Banu Lihyan, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Let one man from every two of you go out, and let the one who remains behind look after the family and property of the warrior, and he will have half of his reward."],[3106,"Whoever fasts a day seeking the Face of Allah, Allah will distance him from Hell as far as a crow flies from when it is a fledgling until it dies of old age."],[3107,"Headache and fever do not cease to afflict the believer, even if his sins are like Mount Uhud, until they leave him with sins the weight of a mustard seed."],[3108,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has already decreed for every servant of His creation five things: his deeds, his term, his provision, his traces, and his resting place."],[3109,"Indeed, behind you are the days of patience. Whoever holds fast during them to the like of what you are upon will have the reward of fifty of you.” They said, “O Prophet of Allah, or of them?” He said, “No, rather of you.” They said, “O Prophet of Allah, or of them?” He said, “No, rather of you” — three times or four."],[3110,"Marwan b. al-Hakam asked Abu Hurayrah: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the prayer over the funeral? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, You created him and You guided him to Islam, and You took his soul, and You are most knowing of his secret and his open deeds. We have come to You as intercessors, so forgive him and have mercy on him.”"],[3111,"He saw Salman al-Farisi while he was stationed at the coast of Hims, and he said, “What is this?” He said, “A frontier guard.” Salman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Ribat for a day in the path of Allah is like fasting a month and standing in prayer during it. Whoever dies as a frontier guard, the reward of the deeds he used to do continues to flow to him, and he is safe from the trial, and he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a martyr.”"],[3112,"When a man performs ghusl on Friday, touches perfume, remains silent and does not engage in idle talk until the imam finishes his sermon, and prays some rakʿahs if it appears to him, the sins between that Friday and the next Friday plus three extra days are expiated for him."],[3113,"He used to trade in wine during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came from Syria with wine in skins, intending to trade. He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have brought a good drink.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It has been forbidden after you.” Kaysan said, “Should I go and sell it, O Prophet of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It has been forbidden, and its price has been forbidden.” So Kaysan went to the skins, took hold of their legs, and poured them all out."],[3114,"Indeed, the Muslim attains the rank of the one who fasts and stands in prayer by his good character."],[3115,"She said regarding the meats of sacrificial animals: We used to prepare some of it, and some people would bring it to Madinah, but they would not eat it except for three days. It was not a strict command, but he ﷺ intended that they should eat from it."],[3116,"It reached Muʿawiyah that ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr b. al-ʿAs narrated that there would be a king from Qahtan. He became angry and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “This affair shall remain in Quraysh. No one opposes them except that Allah will throw him on his face into the Fire.”"],[3117,"It reached ʿAʾishah that Ibn ʿUmar was saying, “Sudden death is a wrath upon the believers.” She said, “May Allah forgive Ibn ʿUmar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only said: ‘Sudden death is a relief for the believers and a wrath upon the disbelievers.’”"],[3118,"Muʿawiyah b. Abi Sufyan proposed to Umm al-Dardaʾ after the death of Abu al-Dardaʾ, and Umm al-Dardaʾ said: I heard Abu al-Dardaʾ say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Any woman whose husband dies and she marries after him, she belongs to the last of her husbands.” And I would not choose you over Abu al-Dardaʾ. So Muʿawiyah wrote to her: “Then you must fast, for it is a means of cutting off desire.”"],[3119,"He advised a man who lived in the desert: “When you call the adhan for prayer, raise your voice with the call, for no jinn, human, tree, or anything hears your voice except that it will testify for you on the Day of Resurrection. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that.”"],[3120,"A woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ seeking a need. He said, \"Sit in whichever road of Madinah you wish until I sit with you.\""],[3121,"A man who had never done any good removed a thorny branch from the road; either it was on a tree and he cut it, or it was lying on the ground and he removed it. God, Mighty and Majestic, thanked him for that and admitted him to Paradise."],[3122,"Wine is the mother of all indecencies and the greatest of major sins. Whoever drinks it may fall upon his mother, his maternal aunt, and his paternal aunt."],[3123,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[3124,"Do not keep company except with a believer, and let no one eat your food except a God-fearing person."],[3125,"Regarding His saying, 'like molten metal,' he said: 'Like the dregs of oil; when it is brought near him, the skin of his face falls into it.'"],[3126,"The Prophet ﷺ fasted continuously for two days and a night. Gabriel came to him and said, 'God has accepted your continuous fast, but it is not lawful for anyone after you. That is because God, Blessed and Exalted, says: \"Then complete the fast until the night.\" So there is no fasting after nightfall. And He has commanded me to perform the witr prayer after dawn.'"],[3127,"Overlook the slips of people of good character, as long as it is not a prescribed punishment."],[3128,"Regarding 'Every day He is in a matter,' he said: 'It is of His matter that He forgives a sin, relieves a distress, raises a people, and lowers others.'"],[3129,"I said, 'O Messenger of God, tell me about the words of God, Mighty and Majestic: \"And houris with wide eyes.\"' He said, 'Houris means fair ones; wide-eyed means large-eyed. The eyelashes of a houri are like the wing of an eagle.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, tell me about the words of God, Mighty and Majestic: \"As though they were rubies and corals.\"' He said, 'Their purity is like the purity of pearls inside shells, untouched by hands.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, tell me about His words: \"In them are good and beautiful ones.\"' He said, 'Good in character and beautiful in face.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, tell me about His words: \"As though they were hidden eggs.\"' He said, 'Their delicacy is like the delicacy of the membrane inside the egg, next to the shell, which is the thin white skin.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, tell me about His words: \"Loving and of equal age.\"' He said, 'They are those who were taken in the abode of this world as old, decrepit, grey-haired women. God created them after old age and made them virgins.' He said, 'Loving means affectionate and beloved. Of equal age means born at the same time.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, are the women of this world better or the houris of Paradise?' He said, 'The women of this world are better than the houris, as the outer garment is better than the lining.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, why is that?' He said, 'Because of their prayers, their fasting, and their worship of God, Mighty and Majestic. God will clothe their faces with light and their bodies with silk, white in color, green in garments, yellow in jewelry. Their incense burners are pearls, and their combs are gold. They say: \"Surely we are eternal and will never die. Surely we are blissful and will never be miserable. Surely we are resident and will never depart. Surely we are content and will never be displeased. Glad tidings to the one for whom we are and who is for us.\"' I said, 'A woman among us may marry two, three, or four husbands, then die and enter Paradise, and they enter with her. Who among them will be her husband?' He said, 'O Umm Salamah, she will be given a choice and will choose the one with the best character among them, and she will say: \"My Lord, this one had the best character with me in the abode of this world, so marry me to him.\" O Umm Salamah, good character has taken the good of this world and the Hereafter.'"],[3130,"Gold for gold, silver for silver: do not prefer some over others."],[3131,"Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night, the devotion of a night will be recorded for him."],[3132,"A Hajj for one who has not performed Hajj is better than ten military expeditions, and a military expedition for one who has performed Hajj is better than ten Hajjs, and a military expedition at sea is better than ten military expeditions on land. Whoever crosses the sea is as if he crossed all the valleys, and the one who vomits therein is like the one who wallows in his blood."],[3133,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ walked, it was as though he were leaning forward."],[3134,"When one of you defecates, let him wipe with three stones, for that is sufficient for him."],[3135,"He used to perform Witr with three [rak'ahs]. In the first rak'ah he would recite \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,\" in the second \"Say: O disbelievers,\" and in the third \"Say: He is God, the One\" and \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak\" and \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.\""],[3136,"If a woman from among the women of the people of Paradise were to look down upon the earth, she would fill the space between them with fragrance, and she would illuminate what is between them, and her crown upon her head is better than this world and all that is in it."],[3137,"All of you will be in Paradise except the one who bolts from God, Mighty and Majestic, like a camel bolts from its owner."],[3138,"A child cannot repay his parent unless he finds him a slave and then sets him free."],[3139,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he wiped over the leather socks."],[3140,"The womb is a branch of the Merciful. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him; and whoever severs it, I sever him."],[3141,"For two who love each other, nothing has been seen like marriage."],[3142,"He asked 'A'ishah about the fasting of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and she said: 'He used to fast all of Sha'ban until he joined it to Ramadan, and he used to seek to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.'"],[3143,"Whoever loves to meet God, God loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet God, God hates to meet him.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, there is none of us but hates death.' He said: 'It is not that. When the believer receives the glad tidings from God, he loves to meet God, and God is more loving of meeting him. But when the disbeliever receives what he hates, he hates to meet God, and God, Mighty and Majestic, is more hating of meeting him.'"],[3144,"We slaughtered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a camel for seven people. It was said to Jabir: \"What about a cow?\" He said: \"It is like it.\" He said: \"And Jabir witnessed al-Hudaybiyyah.\" He said: \"And on that day we slaughtered seventy camels.\""],[3145,"\"Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"As for the people of the Fire, they are every coarse, arrogant miser who is proud. As for the people of Paradise, they are the weak and the downtrodden.\""],[3146,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud said to Ibn al-Nawwahah: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Were it not that you are a messenger, I would kill you.' But today you are not a messenger. Arise, O Kharashah, and strike his neck.\" So he went to him and struck his neck."],[3147,"\"O Abu Dharr, which mountain is this?\" I said: \"Uhud.\" He said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it would not please me that I had it as pieces of gold which I spent in the cause of Allah, leaving from it a qirat.\" I said: \"A qintar, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"A qirat.\" I said: \"A qintar, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"A qirat.\" Then he said to me the third time: \"O Abu Dharr, I only say what is less, and I do not say what is more.\""],[3148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a raiding party to go out. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should we go out tonight or stay until morning?\" He said: \"Do you not love to spend the night in one of the gardens of Paradise?\""],[3149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during his illness in which he died: \"Indeed it makes death easy for me that I was shown you, my wife, in Paradise.\""],[3150,"Whoever maintains four rak'ahs before the noon prayer and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire."],[3151,"When he heard the muezzin, he said as he said."],[3152,"Make your graves level."],[3153,"Whoever grows a gray hair in the cause of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever shoots an arrow at the enemy, whether he misses or hits, it is like freeing a slave. And whoever frees a Muslim slave, it is his ransom from the Fire, limb for limb."],[3154,"Whoever wipes the head of an orphan, for him is a good deed for every hair."],[3155,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took him by the hand and said: \"O Abu Sa'id.\" I said: \"At your service, Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Three things, whoever has them, Paradise is assured for him.\" I said: \"What are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Whoever is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger.\" He said: \"And the fourth, O Abu Sa'id, has excellence greater than what is between heaven and earth by a hundred degrees, and it is jihad.\""],[3156,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not wear silk or gold."],[3157,"A man called out to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, who are the martyrs?” He said: “The martyrs are those who fight in the first rank and do not turn their faces away until they are killed. Those are the ones who will meet in the lofty chambers of Paradise. Your Lord laughs at them. Indeed, when God, Mighty and Majestic, laughs at His believing servant, there is no reckoning upon him.”"],[3158,"A man asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Which of the Muslims is best, O Messenger of God?” He said: “The one from whose tongue and hand the people are safe.”"],[3159,"There is no servant who glorifies God, Mighty and Majestic, with one glorification, or praises Him with one praise, or magnifies Him with one magnification, except that God, Mighty and Majestic, plants for him a tree in Paradise thereby, its root of gold and its top of jewels, crowned with pearls and rubies, its fruits like the breasts of virgins, softer than butter and sweeter than honey. Whenever he picks something from it, it returns to its place.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: “Neither cut off nor forbidden.”"],[3160,"When ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb was stabbed and ordered the consultative council, his daughter Ḥafṣah entered upon him and said: “O father, the people are saying that these men whom you have placed in the council are not satisfactory?” He said: “Support me.” So they supported him, while he was in his condition, and he said: “What could they say about ʿUthmān? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘On the day ʿUthmān dies, the angels of heaven will pray over him.’ I said: ‘For ʿUthmān specifically or for the people generally?’ He said: ‘Rather for ʿUthmān specifically.’” He said: “And what could they say about ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf? I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he was severely hungry, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān came with two loaves of bread between which was fat, and he placed them before the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: ‘May God suffice you in the matter of your worldly life; as for the Hereafter, I am its guarantor.’ What could they say about Ṭalḥah? I saw the Prophet ﷺ when his saddle fell on a cold night, and he said: ‘Who will set my saddle right and have Paradise?’ Ṭalḥah rushed to the saddle and set it right, and the Prophet ﷺ said: ‘You have Paradise owed by me, O Ṭalḥah, tomorrow.’ What could they say about al-Zubayr? I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he slept, and he kept fanning the face of the Prophet ﷺ until he woke up. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: ‘Have you not ceased, O Abū ʿAbd Allāh?’ He said: ‘I have not ceased, may my father and mother be your ransom.’ He said: ‘This is Gabriel conveying peace to you and saying to you: I am bound to fan away from your face the sparks of Hell on the Day of Resurrection.’ What could they say about ʿAlī? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘O ʿAlī, your hand is with my hand on the Day of Resurrection; you will enter with me wherever I enter.’”"],[3161,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I am a sharp-tongued man, and most of that is against my family.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? I seek forgiveness from God a hundred times in the day and night.”"],[3162,"Good reaches the house that is frequented faster than the knife reaches the camel’s hump."],[3163,"Roasted meat was never lifted from before the Messenger of God ﷺ except that a carpet was carried with it."],[3164,"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I did not pass by any group of angels except that they said: “Command your community to practice cupping.”"],[3165,"When the Compeller, Mighty and Majestic, takes the two precious things of a servant, his reward for them is Paradise."],[3166,"When he prayed and finished his prayer, he wiped his right hand over his head and said: “In the name of God, besides whom there is no god, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. O God, remove from me worry and sorrow.”"],[3167,"The Prophet ﷺ said one day to his companions: “Take your shield.” They said: “May our fathers and mothers be your ransom, O Messenger of God, has an enemy appeared?” He said: “Take your shield from the Fire. Say: ‘Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is most great, and there is no might nor power except with God.’ For they are those that go before, and they are those that ward off, and they are those that follow, and they are the enduring righteous deeds.”"],[3168,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I see dreams that make me sick.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"The good dream is from Allah, and the bad one is from Shaytan. If any of you sees that, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge from its evil, for it will not harm him.\""],[3169,"I was sitting in Ariha when Wathila b. al-Asqa' passed by me, leaning on 'Abd Allah b. al-Daylami. He seated him, then came to me and said, \"How strange...\""],[3170,"When the believer sits in his grave after those who attended his burial have turned away, it is said, 'What is this man who is called Muhammad?' If he was a believer, he says, 'He is the servant of Allah and His Messenger,' and it is said to him, 'Sleep; may your eyes sleep.' If he was not a believer, he says, 'By Allah, I do not know. I heard people saying something, so I said it, and they engaged in disputation, so I did too.' Then it is said, 'May your eyes never sleep.'"],[3171,"People came to him during the Farewell Pilgrimage. Some said, 'I shaved before sacrificing.' He said, 'No harm.' Another said, 'I sacrificed before throwing the pebbles.' He said, 'No harm.' He then said, 'All of 'Arafa is a standing place, all of Muzdalifa is a standing place, and every road of Makkah is a path and a place of sacrifice.'"],[3172,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to pray or bury our dead during three times: when the sun begins to rise until it has risen high, when the sun is at its zenith until it declines, and when the sun turns yellow before setting until it has set."],[3173,"The Day of 'Arafa, the Day of Sacrifice, and the Days of Tashriq are our festival, O people of Islam. They are days of eating and drinking."],[3174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were in the Suffa and said, 'Which of you would like to go out every morning to Buthan or al-'Aqiq and bring back two large-humped, beautiful she-camels without committing sin or severing ties of kinship?' They said, 'All of us, O Messenger of Allah, would love that.' He said, 'For one of you to go out every morning to the mosque and learn two verses from the Book of Allah is better for him than two she-camels, and than three, and than their number of camels.'"],[3175,"Learn the Book of Allah, be constant in reciting it, acquire it, and chant it. By the One in whose hand is my soul, it slips away from men's chests faster than a pregnant camel escapes from its hobble."],[3176,"Do you know who the Muslim is? They said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'He from whose hand and tongue the Muslims are safe.' They said, 'Who is the believer?' He said, 'He whom the believers trust with their lives and their wealth.' They said, 'Who is the emigrant?' He said, 'He who abandons evil and avoids it.'"],[3177,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for me and said, 'Take your sword and your weapon.' So I took my sword and my weapon, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him performing ablution. He looked at me, raising his gaze and then lowering it, and said, 'O 'Amr, I intend to send you on an expedition. May Allah give you spoils and protect you, and I will give you a good share of wealth.' I said, 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I did not embrace Islam for wealth, but I embraced Islam out of desire for Islam and to be with you.' He said, 'O 'Amr, how excellent is righteous wealth for a righteous man.'"],[3178,"When a judge judges and strives, then reaches the right decision, he has two rewards. When he judges and strives, then errs, he has one reward."],[3179,"We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ young lambs (jadh'a of sheep)."],[3180,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days of Shawwal, it is as if he has fasted a year."],[3181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the plague and said: The one who flees from it is like the one who flees from the battlefield, and the one who remains patient in it has the reward of a martyr."],[3182,"Sahl b. Saʿd al-Sāʿidī passed by me while I was sitting in the mosque and said: Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? I said: Yes, of course. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever is in the mosque waiting for the prayer is in prayer."],[3183,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[3184,"Supplication is the marrow of worship."],[3185,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he prolonged the standing with us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would, when he prayed, keep his standing light, but during that he made us hear him saying: O Lord, am I to be among them? Then he leaned with his right hand to reach for something. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed, then hastened after that. When he said the taslīm, he sat and we sat around him. He said: I knew that my long standing would disturb you. We said: Yes, we heard you say: O Lord, am I to be among them? He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing of what you have been promised in the Hereafter was shown to me in this standing of mine except that it was presented to me, even the Fire was presented to me. Something of it came toward me until it was level with my place, and I feared that it would overwhelm you, so I said: O Lord, am I to be among them? Then Allah diverted it from you, and it came back in pieces like carpets. I looked into it and saw ʿAmr b. Ḥidthān, the brother of Banū Ghifār, leaning on his bow in Hell, and I saw in it the Ḥimyarī woman, the owner of the cat, who tied it up and neither fed it nor gave it water nor let it loose to seek what it might eat, until she died in that state."],[3186,"Whoever strangles himself in this world and kills himself with it will strangle himself in the Fire, and whoever stabs himself will stab himself in the Fire, and whoever throws himself from a height will throw himself into the Fire."],[3187,"The change in the mouth of the fasting person is more fragrant with Allah than the scent of musk."],[3188,"Whoever wishes humiliation upon Quraysh, Allah (Mighty and Majestic) will humiliate him."],[3189,"He forbade the price of a dog and a cat."],[3190,"When you eat food, take off your sandals, for it is more comfortable for your feet."],[3191,"He asked Ibn ʿAbbās: We raid this Maghrib, and they are people of a religion, and they have water skins containing milk and water. Ibn ʿAbbās said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Tanning is purification."],[3192,"It is not lawful for anyone who believes in God and the Last Day to give his water to another man's child."],[3193,"The camp of the Muslims on the day of the great battle will be beside a city called Damascus, among the best cities of Syria."],[3194,"When he went to his bed, he would say: \"My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants.\""],[3195,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[3196,"He used to say, when he said \"God hears the one who praises Him\": \"O God, our Lord, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will. You are most worthy of praise and glory. The truest thing a servant says—and we are all Your servants—is: no one can withhold what You give, and no one can give what You withhold, nor does the fortune of the fortunate avail him against You.\""],[3197,"It was shown to the Messenger of God ﷺ what would be conquered for his community after him, piece by piece, and he rejoiced at that. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"And your Lord will surely give you, and you will be pleased.\" He said: \"So God gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces, in each palace whatever befits him of youths and servants.\""],[3198,"God, Mighty and Majestic, has made the greeting of peace a salutation for our community and a guarantee of safety for the people under our protection."],[3199,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to his wives: \"Your situation concerns me after I am gone, and none will be able to endure you except the patient.\" Then she said: \"May God give your father to drink from Salsabil,\" and he had given the Prophet's wives ﷺ forty thousand."],[3200,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated, he would keep his upper arms away from his body until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[3201,"Whoever sits on the bed of a woman whose husband is absent will have a serpent set upon him on the Day of Resurrection."],[3202,"He used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[3203,"During the time of Khaybar, we ate horses and wild donkeys, but the Prophet ﷺ forbade us the domesticated donkey."],[3204,"He would not turn around when he walked. Sometimes his cloak would catch on a tree or something, and he would not turn around until they removed it, because they would jest and laugh; they felt safe from his turning around ﷺ."],[3205,"May Allah forgive a man who removed from the path of the Muslims a thorny branch, whatever of his sins has preceded."],[3206,"Jibril commanded me to say takbir, or he said: 'Advance the takbir.'"],[3207,"My Companions will have a slip after me, which Allah will forgive them due to their companionship. A people after them will imitate them, and Allah will cast them upon their nostrils into the Fire."],[3208,"Whoever acts deliberately will hit the mark or come close, and whoever acts hastily will err or come close."],[3209,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no deity but Allah.' When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth, except by its right. It was asked: 'What is its right?' He said: 'Adultery after being married, or disbelief after Islam, or killing a soul, for which he is killed.'"],[3210,"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not seize knowledge by snatching it away from people, but He seizes it by taking away the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders who are asked and give rulings without knowledge; they go astray and lead others astray."],[3211,"Ibn 'Umar, when he combined Maghrib and 'Isha', said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hasten in such a manner. He prayed it once, then I did not see him pray it before that or after that.'"],[3212,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys on a hot day. A man would put his hand on his head from the intense heat. None of us was fasting except the Prophet of Allah and Ibn Rawahah."],[3213,"My intimate friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I preserve: the forenoon prayer, that I not leave it in travel or residence; fasting three days of every month; and I do not sleep except on witr, by which I complete the entire time."],[3214,"I said to Anas: 'What did you find objectionable about our condition during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'You do not complete the rows.'"],[3215,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3216,"When Allah loves a people, He afflicts them with trials."],[3217,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out equipping an expedition, and al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib appeared. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This is the uncle of your Prophet, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most maintainer of its ties,” and perhaps he said: “and the most tender of them.”"],[3218,"Whoever eats from this tree should not approach our mosque."],[3219,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the Day of Ashura and extolled it, then said to those around him: “Whoever among you has not eaten, let him fast this day of his, and whoever among you has already eaten, let him fast the remainder of his day.”"],[3220,"The Prophet ﷺ took my hand and said: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created the soil on Saturday, created in it the mountains on Sunday, the trees on Monday, the unpleasant things on Tuesday, the light on Wednesday, spread in it the beasts on Thursday, and He enumerated as women enumerate. He created Adam after the afternoon on Friday, in the last hour of the hours of the day, between the afternoon prayer and nightfall.”"],[3221,"There is no deed of a day or night but it is sealed upon. When the believer falls ill, the angels say: “Our Lord, Your servant so-and-so You have detained.” He says: “Seal for him upon his deeds until he recovers or dies.”"],[3222,"I am the first to be permitted to raise his head, and I will raise my head and recognize my community on my right and on my left.” It was said to him: “How will you recognize them, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Blazing with light on their faces and limbs from the traces of prostration, and their offspring, their light will be before them.”"],[3223,"The one who recites the Quran quietly is like the one who gives charity quietly, and the one who recites the Quran aloud is like the one who gives charity openly."],[3224,"Pray over your dead by night and day, the young and the old, the male and the female: four [takbirs]."],[3225,"Among the greatest of major sins are associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the false oath. No one swears by Allah an oath of endurance and introduces into it the like of a mosquito's wing but it will be a black spot in his heart on the Day of Resurrection."],[3226,"The distinction between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the meal before dawn."],[3227,"Abd Allah b. Amr b. al-As sent me to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and said: “Ask her: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss while fasting? If she says no, then say: Indeed Aishah relates that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting.” Abu Qays said: I came to her, and she said: “Free or slave?” I said: “Slave.” She said: “Come closer.” I came closer and said: “Abd Allah b. Amr sent me to you to ask you: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss while fasting?” She said: “No.” I said: “Indeed Aishah relates that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting?” She said: “Perhaps he used to kiss her; he could not control himself due to love for her.”"],[3228,"He prepared food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions and invited them. When they entered, the food was placed. A man among the people said, 'I am fasting.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Your brother invited you and took pains for you, then you say, \"I am fasting\"? Break your fast, then fast another day in its place if you wish.'"],[3229,"Whoever asks about me, or is pleased to look at me, let him look at one who is disheveled, pale, and prepared, who has not placed a brick upon a brick nor a reed upon a reed. A flag was raised for him, so he hastened to it. Today is the training ground, tomorrow is the race, and the goal is Paradise or the Fire."],[3230,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abān b. Saʿīd b. al-ʿĀṣ to Madinah on an expedition toward Najd. Abū Hurayrah said: They came to us after we had conquered Khaybar, before we had divided the spoils, and the halters of their horses were of palm fiber. Abān b. Saʿīd said, 'O Messenger of Allah, give us a share.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do not give them a share.' Abān said, 'You, O hyrax, who came down from the mountaintop!' And he did not give them anything from the spoils."],[3231,"Whoever fasts a day in the cause of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire seventy autumns."],[3232,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was dying. He had a cup with water in it. He would dip his hand into the cup, then wipe his face with the water, then say, 'O Allah, help me through the agonies of death.'"],[3233,"He asked ʿAṭāʾ b. Abī Rabāḥ, 'Has permission been granted for women to pray while riding on mounts?' He said, 'No permission has been granted for them in that, neither in hardship nor in ease.'"],[3234,"Ḥuwayṭib b. ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā was with ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar on a journey. ʿAbd Allāh began to pray on his mount, nodding with his head in the direction he was traveling. Ḥuwayṭib said to him, 'Did you hear this, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' ʿAbd Allāh laughed and said, 'Yes, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[3235,"He asked Makḥūl about the fear prayer. He said: ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar used to relate that he prayed it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbīr, and a group of us formed a row behind him while another group faced the enemy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in one rakʿah and two prostrations, like half of the dawn prayer. Then they departed and faced the enemy. The other group came and prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did the same. Then he said the salām, and every man from the two groups stood and prayed a rakʿah and two prostrations for himself."],[3236,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[3237,"Whoever fasts a day in the cause of Allah, the Fire will be distanced from him a journey of one hundred years."],[3238,"Muʿādh b. Jabal incurred a debt during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until it encompassed all his wealth. Muʿādh was one of the righteous Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. Muʿādh said, 'O Messenger of Allah, when I embraced Islam, I never intended to withhold from Islam any wealth I possessed, and I spent my wealth in the cause of Islam. That left upon me a great debt. Summon my creditors and ask them to be lenient with me. If they are lenient, that is the proper way. If they refuse, then divest me of my property for them.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned his creditors and offered them to be lenient with him. They said, 'We want our wealth.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave them all of Muʿādh's wealth. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Muʿādh to part of Yemen to compensate him. Muʿādh obtained from Yemen some wealth from the perquisites of governance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while Muʿādh was in Yemen. Some of the people of Yemen apostatized, and Muʿādh fought them along with commanders whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had appointed over Yemen until they returned to Islam. Then he came during the caliphate of Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq with great wealth. ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb came to him and said, 'You have come with great wealth. I think you should go to Abū Bakr and seek his permission for it. If he permits it for you, it becomes lawful for you; otherwise you should give it to him.' Muʿādh said, 'You know, O ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me only to compensate me when he gave my wealth to my creditors. I would not give Abū Bakr anything of what I have brought unless he asks me for it. If he asks me, I will give it to him; if he does not take it, I will keep it.' ʿUmar said to him, 'I have not been negligent of your welfare or mine.' Then ʿUmar got up and left. When he turned away, Muʿādh called him back, and he returned. Muʿādh said, 'I will obey you, and were it not for a dream I saw, I would not obey you. I saw myself in my sleep drowning in a deep flood of water, and I saw you take my hand and save me from it. Come with us to Abū Bakr.' So they went until they entered upon him. Muʿādh mentioned to him something similar to what he had spoken to ʿUmar about his creditors and what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended by compensating him. Then he informed him of the wealth he had brought, saying, 'Even this whip of mine is part of what I brought. Whatever you deem appropriate, take; whatever you deem appropriate, make lawful for me.' Abū Bakr said to him, 'It is all yours, O Muʿādh.' ʿUmar turned to Muʿādh and said, 'O Muʿādh, now it has become lawful for you.' Thus Muʿādh became one of the wealthiest of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and he was the first man to acquire wealth from the perquisites of governance."],[3239,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, a woman passed by him. He got up and went to one of his wives, then came back to us with his head dripping water. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it seems something happened.' He said, 'Yes, so-and-so passed by me, and desire for women entered my heart. I got up and went to one of my wives. Do likewise, for among the best of your deeds is coming to what is lawful.'"],[3240,"O 'Isa, I will raise after you a community: if what they love befalls them, they praise and give thanks; and if what they hate befalls them, they seek reward and are patient. Yet there is no forbearance and no knowledge. He said: My Lord, how can this be when there is no knowledge and no forbearance? He said: I shall give them from My forbearance and My knowledge."],[3241,"You must observe the night prayer, for it is the practice of the righteous before you, and it is a means of nearness to your Lord and an expiation for evil deeds."],[3242,"Beware of the believer's insight, for he sees by Allah's light."],[3243,"I sold the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a young camel, then I came to collect its price. I said: O Messenger of Allah, pay me the price of my young camel. He paid me with an older camel. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is better than my young camel. He said: It is better for you; the best of people are those who are best in repayment."],[3244,"He used to grant as extra share in a military expedition one quarter after the fifth, and when returning he would grant one third after the fifth."],[3245,"We used to perform incantations in the Jahiliyyah, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, how should we perform incantations for that? He said: Present your incantations to me. He said: No harm in incantations as long as they do not involve shirk."],[3246,"Before the Hour there will be years of deception: the trustworthy one will be accused, the accused will be trusted, and the ruwaybidah will speak. They said: What is the ruwaybidah? He said: The foolish one who speaks about public affairs."],[3247,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."],[3248,"Were it not that your people are recent from disbelief, I would demolish the Ka'bah and make for it two doors, and I would include in it part of what Quraysh left out because they were unable to complete it."],[3249,"He went in to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he had separated from his wives, and he was on a bed of woven palm leaves. I looked and saw nothing in the house to catch the eye except the hide of a calf, whose smell was rising. I said: You are the Messenger of Allah and His chosen one, while Kisra and Caesar are in silk brocade and silk? He said: Are you in doubt, O Ibn al-Khattab? Those are a people whose reckoning has been hastened for them."],[3250,"Whoever walks to a prescribed prayer while in a state of purity, his reward is like that of a pilgrim in ihram. Whoever walks to the Duha prayer, his reward is like that of one performing 'Umrah. A prayer following a prayer with no idle talk between them is a record in 'Illiyyin."],[3251,"Whoever among you sleeps after having touched something greasy before washing his hand, and then something happens to him, let him blame no one but himself."],[3252,"Evil is the food of a wedding feast to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out. And whoever is invited to a wedding feast and does not respond has disobeyed God and His Messenger.\" I did not say it."],[3253,"He said, \"What did so-and-so do?\" referring to an orphan girl who was with her. I said, \"We gave her in marriage to her husband.\" He said, \"Did you send along with her a slave girl to beat the tambourine and sing?\" She said, \"What should she say?\" He said, \"She should say: We have come to you, we have come to you, so greet us and we will greet you. Were it not for the red gold, it would not have settled in your valley; were it not for the brown wheat, your maidens would not have grown plump.\""],[3254,"Three things are obligatory upon me and voluntary for you: Witr, the toothstick, and night prayer."],[3255,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, we hunt with these dogs.\" He said, \"If you send your trained dog and mention God's name over it, then what it catches for you is yours, even if it kills, unless it eats. If it eats, do not eat, for I fear it caught it only for itself. And if other dogs mix with them, do not eat.\""],[3256,"The family of Muhammad ﷺ never had their fill of wheat bread until he ﷺ passed away."],[3257,"I saw seventy of the people of the Suffa, none of them had a full garment; either a burdah or a rida', which they tied around their necks. Some reached mid-calf, and some reached the ankles. He would gather it with his hand, fearing that his private parts would be exposed."],[3258,"The distance between the shoulders of a disbeliever in Hell is a journey of three days for a fast rider."],[3259,"I was struck by severe hardship, so I went to 'Umar and asked him to open a verse from the Book of God for me. He entered his house, then opened it for me. I went not far before I fell on my face from hardship. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ was standing at my head, and he said, \"Abu Hurayrah!\" I said, \"At your service, O Messenger of God, and happily!\" I told him what I was in, and he recognized what was wrong with me. He went to his saddle and ordered for me a wooden bowl of milk. I drank from it, then he said, \"Drink again, O Abu Hurayrah.\" I drank again until my back straightened and became like an arrow. Then I met 'Umar, and I mentioned what had happened to me and said, \"God took charge of that which someone more deserving than you should have done. I asked you to recite the verse when I was better at reciting it than you.\" 'Umar said, \"By God, I wish I had let you in; that would be dearer to me than red camels.\""],[3260,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ seeking hospitality, but he did not have anything to host him with. He said, \"Is there any man who will host this one, may God have mercy on him?\" A man from the Ansar came and took him to his home. He said to his wife, \"Honor the guest of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" She said, \"By God, we have nothing but the children's food.\" He said, \"Put the children to sleep, light the lamp, and bring it near to the guest of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and make him think we are eating with him. Then extinguish the lamp and leave it to the guest of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" She did so. He said: Abu Talhah came to the Prophet ﷺ the next day, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God has marveled—or: laughed—at so-and-so and so-and-so,\" meaning Abu Talhah and his wife. And He revealed about them this verse: \"And they prefer others over themselves, even if they are in privation.\""],[3261,"The first group of my community to enter Paradise will be on the image of the moon on the night of the full moon. Those who follow them will be on the light of the most brilliant star in the sky. They will not urinate, defecate, spit, or blow their noses. Their combs will be of gold, their sweat will be musk, their incense burners will be aloeswood, and their wives will be the wide-eyed houris. Their character will be that of one man, on the image of their father Adam, sixty cubits tall."],[3262,"My example and the example of the prophets is like a man who built a house, completed it, and beautified it, except for a place for one brick in one of its corners. People began to go around his building, marveling and saying, \"Why did he not place a brick here to complete his building?\" I am that brick, and I am the seal of the prophets; there is no prophet after me."],[3263,"My example and your example is like a man who kindled a fire, and these insects and moths began to fall into it while he was trying to keep them away from it, but they plunged into it. I am holding onto your waist-wrappers, saying, \"Come away from the fire, come away from the fire,\" but you overpower me and plunge into it."],[3264,"When the Prophet ﷺ dug the trench, the Muslims suffered severe hardship, to the extent that the Prophet ﷺ tied a rock on his stomach from hunger, and so did his Companions. So I slaughtered a young she-goat and ordered my family to bake some barley bread that they had, and they cooked the she-goat. Then I invited the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of what I had prepared. He said, 'Go and prepare what you have until I come to you.' So I went and prepared what we had. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with the entire army. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it is only a young she-goat that I prepared for you and a few of your Companions.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Bring a large bowl.' I brought him a large bowl. Then he said, 'Put some condiment in it.' Then he invoked blessing upon it. Then he said, 'In the name of Allah.' Then he said, 'Let ten men enter.' I did so, and whenever they ate and were satisfied, they left, and I let another ten enter, until the entire army had eaten, and the food was as it was."],[3265,"There will come upon my Ummah a time when reciters will be many and jurists few; knowledge will be taken away, and harj will increase.' They said, 'What is harj?' He said, 'Killing among yourselves. Then after that there will come a time when men will recite the Qur'an but it will not go beyond their collarbones. Then there will come a time when the hypocrite, the polytheist, will argue with the believer."],[3266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two horned, black and white rams. He brought one of them forward and said, 'In the name of Allah, from You and to You, this is on behalf of Muhammad and his family.' Then he brought the other forward and said, 'In the name of Allah, from You and to You, this is on behalf of whoever declares Your Oneness from my Ummah.'"],[3267,"The best charity is that given to a hostile relative."],[3268,"'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf married a woman for a weight of a date pit in gold."],[3269,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to rise in prayer on the balls of his feet."],[3270,"Labbayk with a Hajj and an 'Umrah together."],[3271,"Some people from Himyar came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him. A man among them said, 'I love women, and I like to come to my wife mounted from behind, so what do you think?' Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed: 'Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish' (2:223). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Come to her frontally or from behind, as long as it is in the vagina.'"],[3272,"Whoever is overtaken by Ramadan while he still owes another Ramadan that he has not made up, it will not be accepted from him."],[3273,"Whoever sends blessings upon Muhammad and says, 'O Allah, grant him the nearest station with You on the Day of Resurrection,' my intercession becomes assured for him."],[3274,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the bathhouse. He said, 'After me there will be bathhouses, and there is no good in bathhouses for women.' She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what if she enters it wearing a waist wrapper?' He said, 'No, even if she enters it with a waist wrapper, a chemise, and a head covering. No woman removes her head covering outside her husband's house except that she tears the veil between herself and her Lord.'"],[3275,"Bathing on Friday is obligatory for every adult male, and he should touch some perfume, even if it is perfume of his wife."],[3276,"Whomever Allah wishes good for, He grants him understanding in the religion."],[3277,"People will emerge who pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the target; they will be killed at Mount Lubnan or Mount al-Jalil."],[3278,"Do not revile Tubba', for he had embraced Islam."],[3279,"He was the owner of the foreleg. He said: The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'Hand me the foreleg,' so I handed it to him. Then he said: 'Hand me the foreleg,' so I handed it to him. Then he said: 'Hand me the foreleg,' so I said: 'O Prophet of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If you kept handing it to me, you would continue to hand it to me.'"],[3280,"It was said to Umar b. al-Khattab: 'Tell us about the matter of the hour of hardship.' Umar said: 'We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Tabuk in intense heat. We stopped at a place where we were afflicted with thirst, such that we thought our necks would snap. A man would go seeking water and return thinking his neck would snap. A man would slaughter his camel, squeeze its stomach contents, drink it, and place what remained on his liver. Abu Bakr said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah has accustomed you to good in supplication, so supplicate for us.\" He said: \"Would you like that?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: So he raised his hands and did not lower them until the clouds gathered and rained, then it ceased, and they filled what they had.'"],[3281,"When someone died, he would say: 'Send him ahead to our predecessor Uthman b. Maz'un, and what an excellent predecessor he is.'"],[3282,"O son of my brother, come, I will treat you with the ruqyah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: 'In the name of Allah I treat you, and may Allah heal you from every disease in you. Remove the affliction, O Lord of the people; heal, for there is no healer but You.'"],[3283,"Every nation has a trial, and the trial of my nation is wealth."],[3284,"O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best? He said: 'The service of a slave in the cause of Allah, or the shade of a tent, or a stud camel.'"],[3285,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I used to pray in a single garment, and in it there was what there was. She said: 'I pray in it and he prays in it.'"],[3286,"When Allah wishes good for a servant, He sweetens him. He said: 'Do you know what sweetening him means?' They said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'He opens for him a righteous deed before his death, until his loved ones and those around him are pleased with him.'"],[3287,"The martyr is forgiven at the first drop of his blood, married to two maidens of Paradise, and allowed to intercede for seventy of his family. The one stationed in ribat, if he dies in his station, Allah writes for him the reward of his deeds until the Day of Resurrection, and he is provided with sustenance morning and evening, married to seventy maidens of Paradise, and it is said to him: 'Stand and intercede until the reckoning is finished.'"],[3288,"Whoever has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, and a child is decreed between them, and that child is afflicted with leprosy, let him blame none but himself."],[3289,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent him to Yemen, he said: 'Do not touch the Qur'an unless you are pure.'"],[3290,"Keep revisiting the Qur'an, for it slips away from men's chests more quickly than birds escape to their nests."],[3291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sit after he had said the taslim until he said: 'O Allah, You are Peace and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.'"],[3292,"The most beloved of deeds to Allah is the prayer at its earliest time."],[3293,"He used to lease out his land, until Rafi' b. Khadij told him that the Prophet ﷺ forbade leasing land, so he abandoned that."],[3294,"Does the one who raises his head before the imam not fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey?"],[3295,"When you pray, do not spit in front of you, nor to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty, or under your foot."],[3296,"He forbade a man from slaughtering his sacrificial animal before he had prayed."],[3297,"Do not precede Ramadan by fasting a day or two days, unless it is a fast that one of you already observes."],[3298,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the afternoon prayers — Zuhr or 'Asr — and he stood up after two rak'ahs. A man called Dhu al-Yadayn stood up to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, did you forget or has the prayer been shortened?' He said: 'Rather I forgot.' So he stood and prayed the two rak'ahs, then prostrated twice while sitting, then said the taslim."],[3299,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from wearing gold and from silver-plating drinking vessels. The women spoke to him about wearing gold, but he refused that for us, and he granted us a concession for silver-plating drinking vessels."],[3300,"O Allah, bless my Ummah in its early morning."],[3301,"The Prophet ﷺ applied perfume before entering ihram."],[3302,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted women to go out for the dawn prayer and the night prayer."],[3303,"The sacrifice is on the day you sacrifice, and the breaking of the fast is on the day you break the fast."],[3304,"The children of Adam are on various levels. Among them is one who is born a believer, lives a believer, and dies a believer. Among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a disbeliever. Among them is one who is born a believer, lives a believer, and dies a disbeliever. Among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a believer."],[3305,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to trade in the Haram up to Syria."],[3306,"The Prophet ﷺ missed a young man who used to sit with him. He said: 'Why do I not see so-and-so?' They said: 'He has been afflicted with a fever,' and they used to call fever 'iʿtibāṭ'. He said: 'Let us go and visit him.' When he entered upon him, the boy wept. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Do not weep, for Jibril ﷺ ...'"],[3307,"Perform the Fajr prayer when it is light, for that is greater in reward."],[3308,"Mutʿah was only for the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ specifically."],[3309,"The womb is a branch of the Most Merciful, attached to the two sides of the Most Merciful. It says: 'O Allah, maintain ties with the one who maintains ties with me, and cut off the one who cuts me off.'"],[3310,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."],[3311,"I do not ask you for any reward for it, except that you love me for my own sake because of my kinship with you, and that you preserve the kinship between me and you, and do not harm me."],[3312,"There are no two Muslims who have three children die before reaching the age of accountability, except that they will be forgiven by the abundance of His mercy toward them."],[3313,"The prayer is cut off by a donkey, a woman, and a black dog."],[3314,"Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an as fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd."],[3315,"People are merely like a hundred camels; you will not find among them a single riding camel."],[3316,"This is Jibril, and he is conveying salam to you. I said: 'And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[3317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married al-Kilabiyyah. When she entered upon him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew near to her, and she said: 'I seek refuge in Allah from you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You have sought refuge with the Mighty. Go back to your family.'"],[3318,"Indeed, Allah has placed truth upon the tongue of 'Umar and his heart."],[3319,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3320,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Who are the family of Muhammad?' He said: 'Every pious one.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: 'His allies are none but the pious.'"],[3321,"The one who drinks from gold and silver vessels is only gulping down the fire of Hell into his belly."],[3322,"Use ithmid (antimony); for it grows the hair and removes impurities, and it clears the eyesight."],[3323,"When one of you wakes from sleep and wants to perform ablution, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[3324,"The best of people are my generation, then the second, then the third, then there will come a people in whom there is no good."],[3325,"He used to have cupping done, and he did not wrong the cupper in his wage."],[3326,"You must keep to the first row, and you must keep to the right side, and beware of the row between the pillars."],[3327,"Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him."],[3328,"Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you: it commanded them to sever ties, so they severed their kinship ties, and it commanded them to shed blood, so they shed their blood.” A man stood up and said, “O Messenger of God, which Islam is best?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The best Islam is that from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”"],[3329,"We were forbidden to follow funerals, but it was not made emphatic upon us, and we were commanded to go out on the day of Fitr and the day of Adha, and that the women in seclusion and the menstruating women should go out, and the menstruating women should be kept away from the prayer place of the people, so that they may witness the gathering of the Muslims and their supplication."],[3330,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed Zuhr as five rak'ahs, and it was said, “O Messenger of God, has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “What is that?” They said, “You prayed five.” He said, and he prostrated twice."],[3331,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted ruqyah for every venomous sting."],[3332,"I said, “O Messenger of God, may God bless you. As for those in whose hearts is deviation,” he said, “Those who argue about it. When you see them, they are the ones God meant, so beware of them.”"],[3333,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream, and I said, “O Messenger of God, ask forgiveness for me,” but he was silent toward me. Then I said, “O Messenger of God, indeed Sufyan b. Uyaynah…"],[3334,"Indeed, two assurances have descended from heaven. One of them has passed, and that is the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the other is seeking forgiveness."],[3335,"I saw Ibn Umar in prayer leaning when he stood, so I said, “What is this?” He said, “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ doing it.”"],[3336,"Whoever deliberately abandons the prayer has openly disbelieved."],[3337,"An increase in lifespan was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No soul is delayed when its term comes, and indeed the increase in lifespan is the righteous offspring whom God grants to the servant, who then supplicate for him after his death, and their supplication reaches him in his grave. That is the increase in lifespan.”"],[3338,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of people among whom was a man wearing khalūq perfume. He greeted them and turned away from the man. The man said to him: “O Messenger of God, you greeted them but turned away from me?” He replied: “Indeed, between your eyes is redness.”"],[3339,"Whoever recites the Qur’an by heart or looking at the mushaf is given a tree in Paradise; if a crow were to hatch beneath one of its leaves and that hatchling then grew old, old age would overtake it before it could cut through that leaf."],[3340,"Whoever walks in fulfillment of his Muslim brother’s need, God writes for him seventy good deeds for every step he takes."],[3341,"There is no prayer after ‘Asr until the sun sets, and no prayer after Fajr until the sun rises."],[3342,"When he wanted to sleep, he would blow into his palms and recite the mu‘awwidhāt into them, then wipe them over his face."],[3343,"A Muslim man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I bought a slave, so what should I do with him?” He said: “He is your brother in Islam. Do not burden him with work beyond his ability, feed him from your food, and clothe him from your clothing. If you dislike him, then sell him.”"],[3344,"I was pouring water for the Prophet’s ﷺ ablution while he was at my maternal aunt Maymūnah’s. When he came out, he said: “Who placed my ablution water for me?” She said: “My sister’s son, O Messenger of God, Ibn ‘Abbās.” He said: “O God, grant him understanding in the religion and teach him the interpretation.”"],[3345,"He prohibited khazf (throwing pebbles with the fingers)."],[3346,"I take revenge on one I hate by means of one I hate, then I will consign both of them to the Fire."],[3347,"Whoever devotes himself entirely to God, God suffices him for every burden and provides for him from where he does not expect. Whoever devotes himself entirely to this world, God entrusts him to it."],[3348,"The most truthful speech is that in whose presence one sneezes."],[3349,"Three things: whoever brings them along with faith will enter from whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes, and will be married to as many houris as he wishes: whoever pays off a hidden debt, forgives his killer, and recites after every prescribed prayer ten times: “Say: He is Allah, the One.” Abu Bakr said: “Or one of them, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Or one of them.”"],[3350,"Anas b. Malik showed me the ablution. He took a small water vessel and placed it on his left side, and poured water on his right hand and washed it three times. Then he turned the vessel to his right hand and performed ablution three times three times, and wiped his head three times. He took fresh water for his ear canals and wiped his ear canals. I said to him: “You have wiped your ears.” He said: “O boy, they are part of the head, not part of the face.” Then he said: “O boy, did you see and understand, or should I repeat for you?” I said: “It is sufficient for me, and I have understood.” He said: “Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution.”"],[3351,"Umm Salama said: “O Messenger of Allah, shall I go out with you to battle?” He said: “O Umm Salama, jihad has not been prescribed for women.” She said: “I will treat the wounded, tend the baggage, and give water to drink?” He said: “Then yes.”"],[3352,"Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3353,"The poor among the Emigrants will surely enter Paradise five hundred years before their rich."],[3354,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey while he was riding his mount, and it shied. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is wrong with your mount that it shied?” He said: “It heard the voice of a man being punished in his grave, so it shied because of that.”"],[3355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded in a battle he fought that bells be cut off."],[3356,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a state of major ritual impurity, he would not eat until he performed the ablution he does for prayer."],[3357,"On the Day of Resurrection, wrongs among people and their rights will be brought like mountains, and Allah will continue to settle them until nothing of them remains."],[3358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed the owner of an 'ariyya to sell it by estimating its amount in dry measure."],[3359,"When a man sneezes and says: “Praise be to Allah,” the angels say: “Lord of the worlds.” When he says: “Lord of the worlds,” the angels say: “May Allah have mercy on you.”"],[3360,"Every newborn is held in pledge for his 'aqiqah."],[3361,"He was asked: Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray when he entered the House? He said: \"Between the two pillars.\""],[3362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray at night until his feet became swollen. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, has not Allah forgiven you your past and future sins? He said: \"Should I not be a grateful servant?\""],[3363,"While the Prophet ﷺ was traveling, a woman came with a son of hers and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: \"Yes, and for you is a reward.\" She said: What is his reward when he stands at 'Arafah? He said: \"There will be written for his parents, for every person standing at the standing-place, the number of hairs on their heads, as good deeds.\""],[3364,"Whoever performs Hajj and visits my grave after my death, it is as if he visited me in my lifetime."],[3365,"Whoever is a means of connecting his Muslim brother to a person of authority in conveying a good or bringing joy, Allah will raise him to the highest levels of Paradise."],[3366,"Allah accepts charitable gifts, and He accepts only what is good from them, and He takes it with His right hand, then nurtures it for its owner as one of you nurtures his colt or his young camel, until a morsel becomes like Mount Uhud."],[3367,"He was at a funeral and saw people walking without cloaks, and he said: \"In my presence is this done? I considered supplicating against you with a supplication that you would walk in other than your forms.\" He said: After that, no one was seen walking without a cloak."],[3368,"Pride is My lower garment, and greatness is My cloak; whoever contests Me for them, I will punish him."],[3369,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only stood for the funeral that passed by him because it was the funeral of a Jew, so he stood for it."],[3371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted trousers for the sick person if he does not find a waist-wrapper, and leather socks if he does not find sandals."],[3372,"My cistern is between Aylah and Sanʿāʾ. It has two spouts, one of gold and the other of silver. Its vessels are as numerous as the stars of the sky, whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, and its fragrance is more pleasant than musk. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst again."],[3373,"He saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wearing a black turban."],[3374,"Let none of you come to his family at night unexpectedly."],[3375,"We arrived with the Messenger of God ﷺ while we were crying the talbiya loudly for Hajj. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to make it an ʿUmrah and to come out of iḥrām, so we did."],[3376,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while we were discussing truffles. He said: \"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a healing for the eyes.\""],[3377,"There is no treacherous person but he will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be known."],[3378,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and he ruled concerning buried treasure that one-fifth is due."],[3379,"Do not hasten to anything that you think if you hasten to it you will attain it, and do not delay anything that you think if you delay it it will be averted from you, if God has decreed it upon you."],[3380,"The most thieving of people is the one who steals from his prayer. It was said: \"O Messenger of God, how does he steal from his prayer?\" He said: \"He does not complete its bowing or its prostration. And the most miserly of people is the one who is miserly with the greeting of peace.\""],[3381,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Khaybar, and he said about a man who was with him: \"This one is from the people of the Fire.\" When the fighting began, he fought the fiercest fighting until wounds weakened him. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, the one you claimed was from the people of the Fire fought fiercely.\" He said: \"Indeed, he is still from the people of the Fire.\" When the wounds pained him, he reached for his quiver, took out an arrow, and killed himself with it. They came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, God has confirmed your words. The one you told us was from the people of the Fire took an arrow from his quiver and killed himself with it.\" He ordered Bilāl to announce among the people: \"Surely, none enters Paradise except a believer, and God supports this religion with a sinful man.\""],[3382,"Shall I teach you the words that Moses ﷺ spoke when he crossed the sea with the Children of Israel?\" We said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Say: O God, to You belongs praise, and to You is the complaint, and You are the One sought for help, and there is no might and no power except with God, the Magnificent.\" He said: \"I have not abandoned them since I heard them from Shaqīq.\" And Shaqīq said: \"I have not abandoned them since I heard them from ʿAbd Allāh.\" And ʿAbd Allāh said: \"I have not abandoned them since I heard them from the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" Al-Aʿmash said: \"Then someone came to me in my sleep and said: 'O Sulaymān, add to these words: And we seek Your help against the corruption within us, and we ask You for the rectification of all our affairs.'\""],[3383,"Love your beloved moderately, lest he become your enemy one day; and hate your enemy moderately, lest he become your beloved one day."],[3384,"When he ﷺ dispatched a raiding party, he would say: 'Raid in the name of God, in the path of God. Fight those who disbelieve in God. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, and do not be cowards.'"],[3385,"Whoever performs the major ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday, his sins and errors are forgiven for him. Then when he begins walking to the Friday prayer, for every step he takes he receives the reward of twenty years of deeds. Then when he finishes the Friday prayer, he is rewarded with the deeds of two hundred years."],[3386,"When you seek a need and you love that it succeed, then say: 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner, the Most High, the Magnificent. There is no god but God alone, with no partner, the Forbearing, the Generous. In the name of God, besides whom there is no god, the Ever-Living, the Forbearing. Glory be to God, Lord of the Mighty Throne. And praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. As if they, on the day they see what they are promised, will not have remained except an hour of a day. A notification. So will any be destroyed except the defiantly disobedient people? As if they, on the day they see it, will not have remained except an evening or its morning. O God, I ask You for that which necessitates Your mercy, and the determinations of Your forgiveness, and the spoils of every righteousness, and safety from every sin. O God, do not leave for me any sin but that You forgive it, nor any worry but that You relieve it, nor any debt but that You settle it, nor any need among the needs of this world and the Hereafter but that You fulfill it by Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.'"],[3387,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and we passed by a village of ants that had been burned. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Indeed, it is not appropriate for a human to punish with the punishment of God.'"],[3388,"Indeed, God promised me to admit into Paradise four hundred thousand of my community. Abu Bakr said to him: 'Give us more, O Messenger of God.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'And like this,' and he joined his hands. Umar said: 'That is enough for you, O Abu Bakr.' Abu Bakr said: 'Let me be, O Umar, and what is it to you if He admits us all into Paradise?' Umar said: 'Indeed, God, if He wills, can admit His creation into Paradise with one handful.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Umar has spoken the truth.'"],[3389,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some women of the Ansar at a wedding of theirs, while they were singing: 'And he gifted her a ram that coughed in the pen, and your husband is in the gathering, and he knows what tomorrow holds.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'No one knows what tomorrow holds except God.'"],[3390,"They both pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ when they were seven years old. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw them, he smiled and extended his hand, and they pledged allegiance to him."],[3391,"The pen is lifted from three: the sleeper until he wakes, the insane until he regains his sanity, and the child until he reaches maturity or has a wet dream."],[3392,"The Messenger of God ﷺ encamped at al-Hijr, and the people drew water from its well. Then he departed from it, and when he had mounted and was about to leave, he ordered the people not to drink from its water, nor to perform ablution with it, and that any dough kneaded with its water should be fed to camels. The people did so."],[3393,"Whoever separates from the Muslims by a handspan has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck. Whoever dies without having an imam (leader/caliph) over him, his death is a death of ignorance (Jahiliyyah). Whoever dies under a blind banner, supporting tribalism, his death is a death of ignorance."],[3394,"Truffles are from manna, and their water (juice) is a cure for the eye. Ajwa dates are from Paradise, and they are a cure for poison. He said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ prescribed for sciatica the fat-tail of a ram."],[3395,"Whoever attends the Friday prayer should perform the major ritual bath (ghusl)."],[3396,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed in his house, and I said, 'O Messenger of God, may I wipe over the leather socks?' He said, 'Yes.' I said, 'For a day?' He said, 'And two days.' I said, 'And three, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'Yes, and whatever seems appropriate to you.'"],[3397,"The night prayer is two rak'ahs at a time, and when you fear the approach of dawn, then pray one rak'ah as witr."],[3398,"When he sits between her four parts and the circumcised part touches the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory."],[3399,"Do not prevent the female servants of God from the mosques of God, and let them go out without perfume."],[3400,"\"Who will go to Madinah and not leave any grave or idol without breaking it, or any image without defacing it?\" A man stood up and said, 'I will, O Messenger of God,' but then he was afraid of the people of Madinah and sat down. Ali said: 'So I went, then came back and said, \"O Messenger of God, I did not leave any grave in Madinah without leveling it, nor any idol without breaking it, nor any image without defacing it.\" He said, \"O Ali, do not be a troublemaker, nor arrogant, nor a merchant—except a merchant of good.\""],[3401,"She asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about a mouse that fell into ghee. He said, 'Take it out and throw away what is around it.'"],[3402,"The prayer in congregation surpasses the prayer of an individual by twenty-five prayers."],[3403,"It was said to Ali b. Abi Talib: 'Tell us about the voluntary prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ during the day.' He said: 'You cannot bear it.' They said: 'Tell us, you.' He said: 'When the sun was here, from the direction of the late afternoon, he would pray two rak'ahs. Then he would wait until the sun was here, from the direction of midday, and pray four rak'ahs. Then he would pray two rak'ahs after the noon prayer.'"],[3404,"Ibn Umar, when he intended to enter ihram, would go to Dhu al-Hulayfah and spend the night there. When morning came, he would mount his riding camel, and when it stood upright he would begin the talbiyah. He claimed that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do that."],[3405,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me to recite Surah Ha-Mim. I went to the mosque and found a man among the people of the mosque. I said to him, 'Do you recite this surah?' He said, 'Yes,' and he recited a different version that I did not recite. I said, 'Who taught you?' He said, 'The Messenger of God.' I said, 'The Messenger of God taught me.' Then I met another man and said, 'Do you recite this surah?' He said, 'Yes.' I said, 'Recite,' and he recited the same as my companion. I said, 'Who taught you?' He said, 'The Prophet ﷺ.' I said, 'And the Messenger of God ﷺ taught me.' So I went to the Prophet ﷺ while he was sitting, and I said, 'He differed with me in the recitation.' His face changed and he became angry, and he gestured to Ali, who was with him. The Messenger of God spoke, and Ali said: 'The Messenger of God commands that each man among you recite what he has learned, for those before you were destroyed only by disagreement.'"],[3406,"We said, 'O Messenger of God, how will you recognize those of your nation whom you have not seen on the Day of Resurrection?' He said, 'They will be radiant, with white marks on their faces and limbs from the traces of ablution.'"],[3407,"The best of this nation after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then Umar, then a man—meaning himself."],[3408,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: Shall I not teach you words which, if you say them, you will be forgiven—though you are already forgiven? (They are:) There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; there is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."],[3409,"The passing away of my nation will be through stabbing and the plague. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this stabbing we know; what is the plague? He said: The piercing of your enemies from among the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom."],[3410,"I said to Ibn Abbas: Is there repentance for one who kills a believer intentionally? He said: No. I said: Then what about His saying: 'And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery—and whoever does that will meet a penalty. The punishment will be doubled for him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will abide therein humiliated, except for those who repent, believe, and do righteous deeds. For them Allah will replace their evil deeds with good deeds'? He said: This is a Makkan verse which was abrogated by a Madinan verse: 'And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, to abide therein, and Allah's wrath is upon him, and He has cursed him and prepared for him a great punishment.'"],[3411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done, and the cupper complained to him until he wept, so he sent to his masters that they should lighten his tax."],[3412,"The best generation is the generation in which I am, then the second, then the third, then the fourth; then Allah will not care about them at all."],[3413,"When he heard the muezzin say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, he would say: And I, and I. And when he said: And I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, he would say: And I, and I."],[3414,"The people of the highest degrees are seen by those below them as you see the shining star on the horizon of the sky; and indeed Abu Bakr and Umar are among them and are blessed."],[3415,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: Which part of the night is most answered in supplication? He said: The last depths of the night."],[3416,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me: When you go to your bed, say: O Allah, I submit myself to You, and turn my face to You, and entrust my affair to You, and lean my back upon You, out of fear and hope in You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and Your Prophet whom You sent. If you die that night, you die upon the natural disposition; and if you wake up, you attain good."],[3417,"We were with Umm Salamah, asking her about the letters of the Quran. A man said: O Mother of the Believers, I sometimes say to myself something which, if I uttered it, would nullify my reward, and if it were known, my neck would be struck. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being asked about the like of what you asked, and he said: That speech is only given to a believer."],[3418,"He was asked about the position of the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr. He said: The bravest of us on the day of Badr was the one who kept close to the knee of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3419,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ drinking from this well while standing, and he gestured with his hand toward Zamzam."],[3420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on one of the Fridays: “O assembly of Muslims, this is a day that Allah has made a festival for you, so wash, and use the toothstick.”"],[3421,"If a person knew what will come to him after death, he would not eat a morsel or drink a sip unless he was weeping and striking his chest."],[3422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me a kunya."],[3423,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ, and when he did not remember a man’s name, he would say: “O servant of Allah.”"],[3424,"The Messenger of Allah performed the Hajj and the `Umrah together as qiran, and performed a single tawaf for both."],[3425,"The Prophet ﷺ cut off (the hand) for a shield whose value was five dirhams."],[3426,"“I am leaving among you the two weighty things, one of which is greater than the other: the Book of Allah, a rope extended from the heaven to the earth, and my `itra, the people of my house. They will not separate until they return to me at the pool.”"],[3427,"Khamr itself has been forbidden, and intoxication from every drink."],[3428,"When the Prophet ﷺ encamped at a place, he would not depart until he prayed two rak`ahs, or a prayer with which he bade farewell to the place."],[3429,"Umar asked about the Magians, so Abd al-Rahman b. `Awf said: “I bear witness regarding the Messenger of Allah that he said: ‘The Magians are a sect of the People of the Book, so treat them as you treat the People of the Book.’”"],[3430,"The prayer at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was two rak`ahs, and it was increased in the prayer of the resident, while the traveler’s prayer remained as it was."],[3431,"He used to rise in the morning in a state of major ritual impurity without having had a wet dream, then he would perform ghusl and fast."],[3432,"I saw Muhammad b. Maslamah standing on a wall looking at the sister of al-Dahhak b. Qays. I said: \"Do you do this while you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When Allah places in a man's heart the intention to propose to a woman, there is no harm in examining her appearance.'\""],[3433,"\"Whoever leaves his home in the morning seeking knowledge, the angels spread their wings for him, pleased with what he is doing.\" And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed Allah has opened a gate toward the west, the width of which is seventy years, then He will not close it until the sun rises from it.\" I said: \"Tell me more, may Allah have mercy on you.\" He said: \"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey when a Bedouin with a loud voice came to him and said: 'O Muhammad, stop so that I may ask you. O Muhammad, stop so that I may ask you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ answered him with a voice similar to his, saying: 'Come here, come here.' The Bedouin said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what about a man who loves a people and recognizes their virtue but does not perform deeds like theirs?' He said: 'He will be with those whom he loves on the Day of Resurrection.'\" I said:"],[3434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mut'ah with women on the day of Khaybar."],[3435,"I poured water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose and blew it out, washed his face and his forearms, and wiped over his forelock, over the turban, and over the leather socks."],[3436,"Umar b. al-Khattab sent for Ibn Mas'ud, Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, and Abu al-Darda' and said: \"What is this hadith that you are narrating so much from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" Then he detained them in Madinah until he was martyred."],[3437,"Indeed, secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord, Blessed and Exalted."],[3438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying the two rak'ahs of Fajr while they were praying the morning prayer, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Which of the two have you made your prayer?\""],[3439,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \"What is the right of camels?\" He said: \"To slaughter the fat ones, to lend the stud for breeding, and to milk them on the day they come to water.\""],[3440,"Ibn Abbas addressed us and said: \"Had the people not sought vengeance for the blood of Uthman, they would have been stoned from the sky.\""],[3441,"I saw the Lord of Might in a dream, and He said: \"By My might and majesty, I will surely honor his resting place,\" meaning Sulayman al-Taymi."],[3442,"O seeker of knowledge, go to Hammad b. Zayd and benefit from his forbearance and knowledge, then bind it with a chain."],[3443,"Regarding His saying: \"Allah only intends to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household,\" he said: \"It was revealed concerning five: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn.\""],[3444,"A man passed by him letting his cloak or garment drag, so he called out to him: \"O servant of Allah, raise your garment, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever drags his clothes out of pride, Allah will not look at him, whether in what is lawful or unlawful.'\""],[3445,"I said to my father: \"Who is the best of people after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Abu Bakr.\" I said: \"Then who?\" He said: \"Then 'Umar.\""],[3446,"A man who had stabbed another man in the thigh with a horn was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. The one whose thigh was stabbed said: \"Give me retaliation, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah said: \"Treat it, and wait with it until we see what it becomes.\" The man said again: \"Give me retaliation, O Messenger of Allah.\" He replied to him similarly. The man said: \"Give me retaliation, O Messenger of Allah.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him retaliation. Then the leg of the one who sought retaliation withered, while the one from whom retaliation was taken healed. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ nullified its blood money."],[3447,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not grant her any dwelling or maintenance."],[3448,"He forbade the earnings of a cupper and the dower of a prostitute."],[3449,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[3450,"Salim b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar was sitting with al-Hajjaj, and al-Hajjaj said to him: \"Get up and strike the neck of this man.\" So Salim took the sword, took the man, and headed toward the gate of the palace. His father saw him heading with the man, and said: \"Do you think he will do it?\" He repeated that two or three times. When Salim came out with him, he said to him: \"Did you pray the morning prayer?\" The man said: \"Yes.\" Salim said: \"Then take whichever road you wish.\" Then Salim came back and threw down the sword. Al-Hajjaj said to him: \"Did you strike his neck?\" He said: \"No.\" Al-Hajjaj said: \"Why?\" He said: \"I heard my father say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever prays the morning prayer is under Allah's protection until evening.'\""],[3451,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel."],[3452,"We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and our reward fell upon Allah. Among us were those who died without enjoying any of their reward. Among them was Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, who was killed on the day of Uhud. Nothing was found for him except a striped cloak. When his head was covered with it, his feet stuck out, and when his feet were covered with it, his head stuck out. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Cover his head with it, and put idhkhir over his feet.' And among us are those whose fruit has ripened, and they are gathering it."],[3453,"The bath is one sa', and ablution is one mudd."],[3454,"Sometimes the Messenger of God ﷺ would contend with some of his wives over a single vessel from which they would bathe."],[3455,"A dead person died, and they passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ and invited him to pray over him. He said: \"Does your companion owe a debt?\" They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God, two dinars.\" He said: \"Pray over your companion.\" A man from his relatives said: \"I will bear it, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"It is upon you, and he is free from it.\" He said: \"Yes.\" Then the Messenger of God prayed over him. Later he met him and said: \"What have you done?\" He said: \"I have not finished.\" He said: \"Relieve your companion, then hasten to settle it.\" Then he met him and said: \"I have settled it, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Now you have relieved your companion.\""],[3456,"No one is more patient in the face of harm than God. They ascribe a rival to Him, yet He provides for them and grants them well-being."],[3457,"Indeed, among the best of your garments is white, so clothe your living in it and shroud your dead in it. And among the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears the sight and makes the hair grow."],[3458,"The best of what a person leaves behind after his death are three: a righteous child who supplicates for him, an ongoing charity whose reward reaches him, and knowledge that is acted upon after him."],[3459,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would wish for a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and God relents to whoever repents."],[3460,"God will take hold of the earth on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded up in His right hand, then He will shake them and say: \"I am the King.\""],[3461,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[3462,"He used to say in the prostration of Quran recitation at night: \"My face has prostrated to the One who created it, and split open its hearing and sight.\""],[3463,"The poor of my community will enter Paradise forty autumns before their rich. I said: \"O Messenger of God, describe them to us.\" He said: \"They are those whose clothes are shabby and whose hair is disheveled, who are not granted permission to enter upon rulers, and who do not marry women accustomed to luxury. They fulfill everything that is upon them, but they are not given everything that is due to them.\""],[3464,"I saw Abu Dharr al-Ghifari holding the two doorposts of the Kaaba and saying: \"Whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am Abu Dharr al-Ghifari. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The likeness of my household among you is like the ark of Noah among the people of Noah: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind from it perishes. And like the gate of Hittah among the Children of Israel.'\""],[3465,"Abu Musa addressed us and said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and said: 'O people, beware of polytheism, for it is more hidden than the crawling of an ant.' Someone whom God willed to speak said: 'How can we beware of it, O Messenger of God, when it is more hidden than the crawling of an ant?' He said: 'Say: O God, we seek refuge in You from associating anything with You that You know, and we seek Your forgiveness for what we do not know.'\""],[3466,"When Jibril comes with the revelation, the first thing he casts upon me is: 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim.'"],[3467,"Whoever is entrusted with any affair of the Muslims and deceives them, he will be in the Fire."],[3468,"All flies are in the Fire except the bee."],[3469,"It is from the Sunnah to alight at al-Abtah on the evening of departure (from Mina)."],[3470,"He forbade (using) gourds, green jars, and hollowed stumps."],[3471,"A sick (camel) should not be brought to water among healthy ones."],[3472,"Whoever says 'La ilaha illallah', it will benefit him one day of his lifetime, even if it is after punishment befalls him."],[3473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up one morning with a heavy heart, and he remained so until evening, and woke up again the same way. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you heavy-hearted?' He said: 'Jibril promised to come to me and he has never broken a promise to me.' They looked, and there was a puppy under a shelf of theirs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that puppy to be taken out, and ordered that place to be washed with water. Then Jibril came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'You promised to come to me and you have never broken a promise to me?' He said: 'Do you not know that we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image?'"],[3474,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about these two surahs (al-Mu'awwidhatayn). He said: 'It was said to me, and I said; so say as I said.'"],[3475,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by us while we were picking the fruit of the arak tree. He said: 'Take the black ones from it, for I used to pick them when I was shepherding sheep.' They said: 'You shepherded, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Yes, and there is no prophet except that he shepherded them.'"],[3476,"About the pregnant woman who fears for herself and breaks her fast, and the nursing woman who fears for her child."],[3477,"The mukatab (a slave with a contract of manumission) pays blood money according to the portion of him that has been freed as the diyah of a free person, and according to the portion that remains enslaved as the diyah of a slave."],[3478,"Whoever has had his two precious ones [eyes] taken, and he is patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied with a reward less than Paradise for him."],[3479,"Swearing [by Allah] sells the goods but wipes out the earnings."],[3480,"Ibn Umar once stood up to lead the prayer, then said to a man from the group: “Step forward and lead, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘If one of you has a discharge, let him perform ablution.’”"],[3481,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Ḥaḍramī to Bahrain, I followed him and saw three qualities in him. I do not know which of them was more amazing: We reached the shore of the sea, and he said: “Say ‘Bismillah’ and plunge in.” He said: So we said “Bismillah” and plunged in, and we crossed, and the water only touched the lower parts of our camels’ hooves. When we returned, we were with him in a waterless desert, and we had no water with us. We complained to him, so he prayed two rakʿahs then supplicated, and there was a cloud like a shield. Then it let down its spouts, and we drank and gave water to our mounts. And he died, so we buried him in the sand. When we had traveled not far, we said: “A wild beast will come and eat him.” So we went back, but we did not see him."],[3482,"Three things make your brother’s love sincere for you: you make room for him in the gathering, you call him by the names he loves most, and you visit him when he is ill."],[3483,"There is no morning that Allah creates in which an angel in heaven or on earth knows what Allah will do on that day. And indeed, a servant has his provision. Even if the two heavy ones, jinn and mankind, gathered to prevent any of that from him, they would not be able to."],[3484,"Every loan is charity."],[3485,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the funeral of a man from the Anṣār. We reached the grave, but it had not yet been dug. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down, and we sat around him, as if birds were on our heads."],[3486,"People are like a hundred camels, among which you cannot find a single riding camel. He said: And the Prophet ﷺ said: “We do not know of anything better than a hundred of his like except a believing man.”"],[3487,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to me that I should marry my two precious daughters to ʿUthmān."],[3488,"ʿUthmān is in Paradise."],[3489,"The sick person is not visited except after three days."],[3490,"I was walking with Ibn Umar when he passed by some people who had set up a bird as a target and were shooting at it. Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed whoever does this."],[3491,"While I was on a donkey of mine, my feet almost touching the ground because of its small size, I suddenly came upon the bald spot of Ali b. Abi Talib, the Commander of the Faithful, gleaming in the moonlight. I said: O Commander of the Faithful, where are you heading? He said: For something I need. I said: Won't you ride? He said: Yes. So I moved to the back of the donkey and said: Ride, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: I will not, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The owner of the mount has more right to its front, and the owner of the horse has more right to its front."],[3492,"How excellent a young man Khuraym is, if only he would shorten his hair and raise his lower garment. Khuraym said: My hair does not go past my ears, nor my lower garment past my heels."],[3493,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I will not abandon until I die: not to sleep except having prayed witr, to fast three days every month, and to pray the forenoon prayer."],[3494,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[3495,"Whoever recites Yasin in a day and a night, seeking the countenance of Allah, will be forgiven."],[3496,"Al-Abbas, the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was among those who guarded him. When this verse was revealed: 'O Messenger, convey what has been sent down to you from your Lord; and if you do not, then you have not conveyed His message. And Allah will protect you from the people,' the Messenger of Allah ﷺ discontinued the guard."],[3497,"A letter came to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, in which was written: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Ziyada b. Jahwar. Peace be upon you. I praise to you Allah, there is no god but He. To proceed: I remind you of Allah and the Last Day. To proceed: every religion that people follow will be set aside except Islam, so know that."],[3498,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we seized some domestic donkeys, so we slaughtered them and cooked them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed, so he ordered a crier, who announced among the people: The meat of domestic donkeys is not lawful; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has forbidden it. They also found onions and garlic in the gardens and ate from them, and the people were hungry. They went to the mosque, and the smell of onions and garlic was in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever eats this foul plant should not come near us in our mosque."],[3499,"A promise is a debt."],[3500,"A promise is a debt."],[3501,"O people of Madinah, remember the Day of Deliverance. He said it three times. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Day of Deliverance? He said: The Dajjal will come until he camps at Dhubab, and no disbeliever, male or female, no polytheist, male or female, no hypocrite, male or female, will remain in Madinah but that they will go out to him. On that day the believers will be left pure, and that is the Day of Deliverance."],[3502,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had two garments that he would wear for his Friday prayer, and when he finished, we would fold them until the next Friday."],[3503,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, are we better or those who will come after us? He said: \"If one of them were to spend the like of Mount Uhud in gold, he would not reach a mudd of one of you, nor even half of it.\""],[3504,"Busrah bt. Safwan asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who inserts her hand into her private part. He said: \"She must perform wudu.\""],[3505,"The quickest part of the earth to be ruined is its left side, then its right side."],[3506,"Whoever eats what is lawful, acts according to the Sunnah, and people are safe from his harm will enter Paradise. They said: O Messenger of Allah, there are many such people in your Ummah. He said: \"And there will be such in generations after me.\""],[3507,"The leaders are from Quraysh: the righteous among them are leaders of their righteous, and the wicked among them are leaders of their wicked. Each has a right, so give every rightful one his right. And if an Ethiopian slave with mutilated nose and ears is appointed over you, listen to him and obey, as long as one of you is not made to choose between his Islam and the striking of his neck. If he is made to choose between his Islam and the striking of his neck, let him stretch out his neck—may his mother be bereaved of him—for there is no worldly life or Hereafter after the loss of his Islam."],[3508,"Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."],[3509,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a choice, and we chose him, so it was not a divorce."],[3510,"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will hold a creditor against his debtor in the strongest way anything is held against another. He will say: O Lord, how can I repay him when You have raised me barefoot and naked? From where? Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: I will give them from your good deeds what they gave you. So it will be thrown onto the good deeds of the people. If that covers it, then fine; otherwise, I will take from the bad deeds of the people and throw them onto your bad deeds."],[3511,"We were on a journey, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Do you have water with you?\" I said: Yes. He dismounted from his riding animal, then walked until he was hidden from me. When he returned, I met him with the water vessel. He performed wudu: he washed his hands, washed his face, and he was wearing a Syrian jubbah with tight sleeves, so he took his hand out from under the jubbah and washed his forearms. He wiped his head, then I reached for his leather socks to remove them, but he said: \"Leave them, for I put them on while they were pure,\" and he wiped over his leather socks."],[3512,"She was with her mother Bint al-ʿAjmāʾ during the days of Hajj at Mina, when Budayl b. Warqāʾ al-Khuzāʿī came to them on the riding animal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and called out: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ says: Whoever is fasting should break his fast, for these are days of eating and drinking."],[3513,"On the Day of Sacrifice, he came to us with parts of a cow. We said: What is this? They said: The Prophet ﷺ sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives."],[3514,"I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tihamah, until when he was at 'Usfan his companions came to him and said: O Messenger of God, hunger has exhausted us, so permit us to eat the camels used for riding. He said: \"Yes.\" 'Umar was informed of that, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Prophet of God, what have you done? You ordered the people to eat the riding camels, so on what will they ride? He said: \"What do you think, O Ibn al-Khattab?\" He said: I think that you should order them—and you are better in opinion—to gather the surplus of their provisions in a cloth, then you supplicate God for them, for God will answer you. So he ordered them, and they gathered the surplus of their provisions in a cloth, then he supplicated God for them, then he said: Bring your vessels. So every person among them filled his vessel. Then the Prophet ﷺ permitted departure. When they departed, they were given rain as much as God willed, and the Prophet ﷺ dismounted and they dismounted with him, and they drank from the water, they and the livestock. Then he addressed them, and a group of three came. Two sat with the Prophet ﷺ and the other went away. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Shall I inform you about the three? As for one, he was shy, and God was shy of him; as for the other, he came repentant, and God turned to him; as for the other, he turned away, and God turned away from him.\""],[3515,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled with a bridle of fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[3516,"We did not rejoice at anything after Islam as much as we rejoiced at a hadith the Messenger of God ﷺ narrated to us. He said: The believer is rewarded for guiding someone to the right path, for expressing with his tongue on behalf of a non-Arab, for removing harm from the road—even for a small item that is in his garment and he searches for it with his hand and misses it, so his heart beats for it, and then he finds it; its reward is written for him."],[3517,"I said: O Messenger of God, will there be evil after this good? He said: \"Yes, evil and tribulation.\" I said: Will there be good after this evil? He said: \"Yes, a truce upon corruption, and a community upon impurity within it.\" I said: Will there be evil after this good? He said: \"Yes, a deaf and blind tribulation, and callers calling to the Fire. That you should die, O Hudhayfah, biting on a tree trunk is better than responding to any of them.\""],[3518,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a piece of gold, the first charity that came to him from a mine. He said: \"What is this?\" They said: Charity from a mine of ours. He said: There will be mines, and in them will be the worst of the creation of God, Mighty and Majestic."],[3519,"Whoever attends the Friday prayer, let him perform the ablution (ghusl)."],[3520,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I have wealth and dependents, and my father has wealth and dependents, and he wants to take my wealth to add to his wealth. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You and your wealth belong to your father.\""],[3521,"God loves gentleness in all matters."],[3522,"Black banners will come out from Khurasan; nothing will turn them back until they are planted in Ilya' (Jerusalem)."],[3523,"One who severs ties of kinship will not enter Paradise."],[3524,"Whoever would like his provision to be expanded and his lifespan extended, let him maintain ties of kinship."],[3525,"I saw the young camel of Ibn Maghafalah, that companion of ours, when I was a boy, and I approached it until it kicked me—meaning the judgment of the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding qasamah."],[3526,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray while carrying Umama bt. Abi al-As b. al-Rabi, who was the daughter of Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he bowed he would put her down, and when he stood he would carry her, until he finished his prayer."],[3527,"We complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, but he did not heed our complaint. He said: “Increase in saying, ‘There is no might and no power except with God,’ for it repels ninety-nine doors of affliction, the least of which is anxiety.”"],[3528,"I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of God, and my kin, the People of my House. They will never separate until they return to me at the Pool."],[3529,"The people of knowledge from the family of Muhammad ﷺ and Aisha bt. Abi Bakr knew—so ask her—that the companions of the black one with the breast-like growth are cursed upon the tongue of the unlettered Prophet, and he who fabricated has failed."],[3530,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Madinah, and his riding camel knelt with him between the house of Jafar b. Muhammad b. Ali and the house of al-Hasan b. Zayd. The people came to him and said, “O Messenger of God, the lodging!” His camel then moved on with him, so he said, “Leave it, for it is commanded.” Then it went out with him until it brought him to the site of the pulpit, where it knelt with him. Then it became restless. There was a shelter belonging to some people there that they used to sprinkle, maintain, and cool themselves in, until the Messenger of God ﷺ dismounted from his camel and sought the shade, entering it. Abu Ayyub came to him and said, “O Messenger of God, my house is the nearest of houses to you, so move your baggage to me.” He said, “Yes.” So he took his camel to the house. Then another man came to him and said, “O Messenger of God, stay with me.” He said, “A man stays with his baggage wherever it is.” The Messenger of God ﷺ remained in the shelter for twelve nights until he built the mosque."],[3531,"The imam is responsible; whatever he does, do the same."],[3532,"Whoever a man accepts Islam at his hands, Paradise becomes due for him."],[3533,"We were with Tawus at the Station when we heard a clamor. Tawus said, “What is this?” He was told, “People whom Ibn Hisham has seized for a cause, and he has placed collars on them.” Then I heard Tawus narrate from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no one who introduces an innovation in this community that did not exist but that he will be afflicted with it before he dies.”"],[3534,"In Hell there is a valley, and in the valley there is a well called Habhab. It is incumbent upon God to make every stubborn tyrant dwell in it."],[3535,"The ruler of the Copts gifted the Messenger of God ﷺ two slave girls who were sisters and a mule. As for the mule, the Messenger of God ﷺ rode it. As for one of the slave girls, he took her as a concubine, and she bore Ibrahim. As for the other, he gave her to Hassan b. Thabit al-Ansari."],[3536,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man gesturing with two fingers, so he said, “Use one, use one.”"],[3537,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave Khadija the good news of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearl, with no noise or toil in it."],[3538,"The Prophet ﷺ bought from a Bedouin—he said: I think he said: from Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'a—a load of khbat or a load of wheat or grain. When the sale was concluded, he said to him: \"Choose.\" The Bedouin said: \"I have never seen the like of today. May God grant you long life, from whom are you?\" He said: \"From Quraysh.\""],[3539,"\"I prayed with 'Abd Allah b. Abi Awfa over the funeral of a daughter of his, and he said the takbir over her four times.\" Then he said: \"This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.\""],[3540,"I said to my father: \"O father, who is the best of people after the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He said: \"Abu Bakr, then 'Umar.\""],[3541,"The ruin of my community lies in three things: in the Qadariyya, in tribalism, and in transmitting reports from unreliable sources."],[3542,"Charity given by a relative to a relative is both charity and maintaining kinship ties."],[3543,"He would not sleep at night or during the day without waking except that he used the siwak before performing ablution.\""],[3544,"The muezzins and those who recite the talbiya will come out of their graves, the muezzin calling the adhan and the one reciting the talbiya saying the talbiya."],[3545,"\"There is no shighar.\" They said: \"What is shighar, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Marrying a woman in exchange for another woman, with no dower between them.\""],[3546,"It was said: \"O Messenger of God, should we perform witr after the adhan of dawn?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Perform witr before the adhan.\" He said: The Prophet's ﷺ adhan was after the break of dawn. They said: \"Should we perform witr after the adhan?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Perform witr before the adhan.\" They said the third time: \"Should we perform witr after the adhan?\" He said: \"Perform witr after the adhan.\" Thus he granted them a concession."],[3547,"The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined upon me ten rak'as that I do not abandon: two rak'as before the morning prayer, two rak'as before the noon prayer, two rak'as after the noon prayer, two rak'as after the sunset prayer, and two rak'as after the night prayer."],[3548,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would go out to the morning prayer with his head dripping from the ritual bath, then he would observe the fast that day."],[3549,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, a man loves a people but has not yet caught up with them?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A person is with those whom he loves.\""],[3550,"I entered upon A'ishah and said: O Mother of the Believers, a woman gives something from her husband's house as charity—is it for her or for her husband? She said: \"It is between them.\""],[3551,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque, until when the sun rose the Messenger of God ﷺ went out and I followed him. He said: \"Come with us so that we may enter upon Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ.\" He entered upon her, and she was asleep, lying down. He said: \"O Fatimah, what makes you sleep at this hour?\" She said: \"I have been feverish since last night.\" He said: \"Where is the supplication that I taught you?\" She said: \"I forgot it.\" He said: \"Say: O Living, O Self-Sustaining, by Your mercy I seek help; set right all my affairs for me, and do not entrust me to any person or to myself for the blink of an eye.\""],[3552,"My intercession is for the people of major sins among my community."],[3553,"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[3554,"There is no place in the seven heavens the size of a foot, a span, or a palm except that in it is an angel standing, bowing, or prostrating. Then on the Day of Resurrection they will all say: Glory be to You, we have not worshipped You as You deserve to be worshipped, except that we have not associated anything with You."],[3555,"He used to give two salutations."],[3556,"I am Ahmad, and I am Muhammad, and I am al-Hashir after whom people will be gathered, and I am al-Mahi through whom God erases disbelief. When the Day of Resurrection comes, the banner of praise will be with me, and I will be the leader of the messengers and the possessor of their intercession."],[3557,"The accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise, and two Umrahs expiate what is between them."],[3558,"Whoever consumes a morsel at the expense of a Muslim, God will feed him the like of it from Hell; and whoever is clothed with a garment at the expense of a Muslim, God will clothe him with the like of it from Hell; and whoever takes a position of repute at the expense of a Muslim, God will set him up in a position of ostentation and repute on the Day of Resurrection."],[3559,"All matters, their good and their evil, are from God. And he said: \"Destiny is the system of monotheism. Whoever affirms the oneness of God and believes in destiny has grasped the firmest handhold, and whoever does not believe in destiny has negated monotheism.\" And he said: \"No one who denies destiny will enter Paradise.\""],[3560,"Whoever fasts a day in the path of God, God will place between him and the Fire a trench as wide as the distance between heaven and earth."],[3561,"Whoever washes a dead body and fulfills the trust in it—meaning he conceals whatever may appear at that time—will be as free of his sins as on the day his mother bore him. She said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Let the most knowledgeable among you wash him; if he does not know, then a man whom you consider to have piety and trustworthiness.\""],[3562,"Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock. The ruler is a shepherd and is responsible for his subjects. The man is a shepherd and is responsible for his wife and for what his right hand possesses. The woman is a shepherd over the rights of her husband and is responsible for her household and her children. The slave is a shepherd over the rights of his master and is responsible for his property. So each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible. Therefore prepare an answer for those questions.\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, and what is their answer?\" He said: \"Righteous deeds.\""],[3563,"Whoever is a means for his Muslim brother to reach one in authority in order to fulfill a righteous need or ease a difficulty, God will help him cross the bridge on the Day of Resurrection when feet slip."],[3564,"In sacrificial camels, the one-eyed is not permitted, nor the emaciated, nor the mangy, nor the one whose teats have been cut off."],[3565,"God has obligated upon the wealthy Muslims in their wealth an amount sufficient for their poor. The poor will never suffer from hunger or nakedness except because of what the rich do. Indeed, God will call them to a severe reckoning on the Day of Resurrection and punish them with a terrible punishment."],[3566,"The Messenger of God ﷺ often said to me: \"O A'ishah, what did your verses do?\" I said: \"Which of my verses do you mean, for they are many, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"About gratitude.\" I said: \"Yes, by my father and mother. The poet said: 'Raise your weak one, lest his weakness one day brings you down, and then the consequences catch up with you, having grown. He will repay you or praise you, and indeed one who praises you for what you did is like one who repaid. The noble man, when you wish to connect with him, you will not find his rope worn out or weak in strands.'\" He said: \"Yes, O A'ishah. When God gathers the creation on the Day of Resurrection, He will say to a servant of His servants, to whom another servant of His servants had done a kindness: 'Did you thank him?' He will say: 'O Lord, I knew that was from You, so I thanked You for it.' He will say: 'You have not thanked Me, since you did not thank the one through whose hands I caused it to happen.'\""],[3567,"Whoever buys a sheep that has been left unmilked for some time is entitled to the choice: if he wishes, he may return it along with a measure of dates."],[3568,"Whoever does not thank people has not thanked God, Mighty and Majestic."],[3569,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked: Which deeds are most virtuous? He said: Prayer at its proper time, then kindness to parents, then striving in the path of God."],[3570,"Abu Taybah cupped the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he gave him his payment. Had it been forbidden, he would not have given it to him."],[3571,"Does one of you not fear, when he raises his head before the imam, that God will turn his head into the head of a donkey?"],[3572,"Do not go to excess in the dowries of women, for if it were a source of honor in this world and the next, then the most entitled among you to it and the foremost among you in it would be Muhammad the Messenger of God ﷺ and his family. He did not marry any of his wives or give any of his daughters in marriage for more than twelve uqiyyahs."],[3573,"When my community walks with a swagger, and the Persians and Byzantines serve them, some of them will be set upon others."],[3574,"Among the supplications of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the cessation of Your favor, the transformation of Your well-being, the suddenness of Your vengeance, and all of Your wrath.”"],[3575,"O God, whoever wrongs the people of Madinah or frightens them, frighten him, and upon him be the curse of God, the angels, and all people; neither obligatory nor supererogatory deeds will be accepted from him."],[3576,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a man who had placed his foot on the side of a sheep while sharpening his blade, and the sheep was looking at him. He said, “Will you not do this before? Do you want to kill it twice?”"],[3577,"When one of you cooks a pot, let him increase its broth and then give some of it to his neighbor."],[3578,"The daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ fell ill, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to Uthman, “Stay with her, for she must have either me or you, and you are more entitled.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ left him with her. When God granted victory, the Messenger of God ﷺ sent to give him the glad tidings that God had completed their count with you."],[3579,"When we migrated to Madinah, the Messenger of God ﷺ divided us into groups of ten. I was in the ten that included the Messenger of God ﷺ. We had a sheep whose milk we drank among ourselves. One night he was late, and we had already set aside his share. I went to it while hungry and drank. Then the Prophet ﷺ came while I had not yet slept. He went to the vessel in which we kept the milk but found nothing in it. I said, “O Messenger of God, shall I slaughter it for you?” He said, “No.”"],[3580,"Whoever leads a blind man forty cubits, it is for him like freeing a slave."],[3581,"Return the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you."],[3582,"When one of you eats, let him lick his three fingers, for he does not know in which of them the blessing lies."],[3583,"No man among the emigrants may remain in Makkah after completing the pilgrimage rites for more than three days."],[3584,"The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who emigrates from what God, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden."],[3585,"Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abd Allah b. Rabah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God ﷺ"],[3586,"I saw Ali perform ablution from a waterskin belonging to the tribe of Taym, washing each part three times, and he said: \"This is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[3587,"Mention the good qualities of your dead, and refrain from mentioning their faults."],[3588,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, looked into the hearts of His servants and found the heart of Muhammad to be the best of the hearts of His servants. Then He looked into the hearts of His servants after the heart of Muhammad and found the hearts of his Companions to be the best of the hearts of His servants. So He chose them for His religion; they fight for His religion. Whatever the Muslims see as good is good in the sight of Allah, and whatever they see as evil is evil in the sight of Allah.\""],[3589,"I have been commanded to wear sandals and a ring."],[3590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with two bundles in his hand: one of gold and the other of silk. He said: \"These two are forbidden for the males of my nation and permissible for the females of my nation.\""],[3591,"The imam is a guarantor, and the muezzin is a trustee. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."],[3592,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[3593,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon, a man came stepping over people's necks until he sat close to the Prophet ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: \"What prevented you, O so-and-so, from attending the Friday prayer?\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I was eager to put myself in the place that you see.\" He said: \"I saw you stepping over the necks of the Muslims and harming them. Whoever harms a Muslim has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed Allah.\""],[3594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined the Hajj and Umrah only because he knew that he would not go out after that."],[3595,"Whoever desires the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him."],[3596,"Part of happiness is a righteous wife, a good dwelling, and a good mount. And part of misery is a bad wife, a bad mount, and a bad dwelling."],[3597,"He used to supplicate, saying: O Allah, make the most ample of Your provision for me at the time of my old age and the end of my life."],[3598,"It is from a woman's felicity that her betrothal is easy and her dowry is easy. 'Urwa said: And I say: It is from the first of her ill omens that her dowry is great."],[3599,"Whoever enters a horse between two horses while he is confident that it will not be outstripped, that is gambling."],[3600,"Love is from Allah, and fame is in the heaven. So when Allah loves a servant, Jibril calls out: Verily, your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him; thus love for him is placed on the earth."],[3601,"Delaying payment by a rich man is an injustice; and if you are referred to a wealthy man, accept the referral."],[3602,"Judges are of three types: a man who judged and strove and was correct—for him is Paradise; a man who judged and strove and erred—for him is Paradise; and a man who judged and was unjust—he is in the Fire."],[3603,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks, not removing them, and pray in them. It was said to him: After the revelation of al-Ma'idah? He said: Yes."],[3604,"My community will continue upon the natural disposition as long as they delay the dawn prayer until it is bright."],[3605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the leather socks."],[3606,"Do not revile the rooster, for it calls to prayer at the proper time."],[3607,"The gates of heaven are opened for five things: for the recitation of the Qur'an, for the meeting of the two armies, for the descent of rain, for the supplication of the wronged, and for the call to prayer."],[3608,"Whoever does not abandon obscene talk and lying, Allah has no need for him to abandon his food and drink."],[3609,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated in the dawn prayer during [recitation of] Tanzil al-Sajdah."],[3610,"Our arrival to the Messenger of God ﷺ was five years after the Hijrah. We went out attached to Quraysh in the year of the Confederates, and I was with my brother al-Fadl, and with us was our servant Abu Rafi‘, until we reached al-‘Arj. Then we turned onto his riding route, and we took that route via al-Jathjathah, until we came out upon Banu ‘Amr b. ‘Awf, and we entered Madinah. We found the Messenger of God ﷺ at the Trench, and on that day I was eight years old, and my brother was thirteen years old."],[3611,"I was commanded to fight the people until they say, 'There is no god but God.' When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their property except for its right, and their reckoning is upon God, Mighty and Majestic."],[3612,"On one of his expeditions, he had with him some of his companions. The time of prayer came, and the people found no water to perform ablution with. They said, 'O Messenger of God, we find no water to perform ablution with.' A man from the group went and brought a vessel with little water. The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, then extended his fingers over the vessel, and all the people performed ablution until they had enough for what they wanted."],[3613,"I missed the Messenger of God ﷺ one night from his bed, and I thought he had gone to his slave woman Mariyah. I got up feeling along the wall, and I found him standing praying. I put my hand into his hair to see whether he had performed a major ablution or not. When he finished, he said, 'Has your devil taken you, O 'A'ishah?' I said, 'Do I have a devil, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'Yes.' I said, 'And for all the children of Adam?' He said, 'Yes.' I said, 'And for you?' He said, 'Yes, but God helped me against him, so he submitted.'"],[3614,"Two [persons] whose prayer does not go beyond their heads: a slave who runs away from his masters until he returns to them, and a woman who disobeys her husband until she returns [to obedience]."],[3615,"We were sitting with 'Abd Allah b. Mughaffal, and he narrated to us that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Do not throw pebbles [with the fingertips], for no game is taken thereby and no enemy is struck down thereby, but it breaks a tooth and puts out an eye.'"],[3616,"I was with Ibn 'Umar on a journey, and he hastened the pace until the sun set. I called to him, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, the prayer!' He continued until the stars appeared, then he dismounted and prayed Maghrib, and prayed 'Isha' as two rak'ahs, then he said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ, when a matter urged him on, would pray like this.'"],[3617,"The Prophet ﷺ used to deliver the sermon leaning on a palm trunk. When the pulpit was made, the trunk yearned [with a moaning sound], so the Prophet ﷺ descended and embraced it, and it became silent."],[3618,"We used to forbid you from visiting graves, but visit them, for they remind of the Hereafter. And I forbade you from steeping [dates] in gourds, green jars, and pitch-coated vessels, so steep in whatever seems good to you, but avoid every intoxicant."],[3619,"I was on the point of ordering a man to lead the people in Friday prayer, then burning the houses of those who stay away from it."],[3620,"'Ammar b. Yasir said to Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas: 'What is wrong with you that you do not go out with 'Ali? Have you not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A group will come out of my community who will pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the game; 'Ali b. Abi Talib will kill them. He said it three times.' Sa'd said, 'Yes, by God, I have heard it, but I preferred seclusion until I find a sword that cuts the disbeliever and is kept away from the believer.'"],[3621,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting during a voluntary prayer until it was one or two years before his death. Then I saw him praying sitting in his voluntary prayer, and he would recite the surah slowly, so that his recitation of it would be longer than [the recitation of] a longer surah."],[3622,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode a horse and was thrown from it, and his right side was scraped. He prayed one of the prayers with us one day while sitting, and we prayed behind him sitting. Then when he said the salam, he said: “The imam has only been appointed to be followed. When the imam prays standing, pray standing; when he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; when he prostrates, prostrate; and when he says, ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him,’ say, ‘Our Lord, and to You be praise.’ And when he prays sitting, then pray sitting, all of you.”"],[3623,"The example of the one who goes early to the prayer—meaning the Friday prayer—is like the example of the one who offers a she-camel as a sacrifice; then the one who comes after him is like the one who offers a cow; then the one who comes after him is like the one who offers a ram; then the one who comes after him is like the one who offers a chicken; then the one who comes after him is like the one who offers an egg."],[3624,"Do not undertake a journey except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and the Aqsa Mosque. And a woman must not travel for more than two days unless her husband or a mahram is with her. And two days are not to be fasted in the year: the day of Fitr and the day of Adha. And there is no prayer after two prayers: after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises, and after the Asr prayer until the sun sets."],[3625,"I took the Prophet ﷺ by the hand and said, “I never heard him say when he visited a sick person: ‘Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal; You are the Healer, there is no healer except You.’” He raised his head and said: “Rather: O Allah, with the highest company; rather: O Allah, with the highest company.”"],[3626,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his Companions: “Which of you woke up fasting this morning?” Abu Bakr said: “I did.” He said: “Which of you visited a sick person?” Abu Bakr said: “I did.” He said: “Which of you followed a funeral procession?” Abu Bakr said: “I did.” Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “Congratulations! Whoever completes these, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.”"],[3627,"A man passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was urinating and greeted him with salam, but he did not respond to him. When he finished, he struck his hands [on the ground] and performed tayammum, then he returned the greeting to him."],[3628,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not visit a sick person except after three days."],[3629,"O people, strive for Paradise with all your effort, and flee from the Fire with all your effort. For the seeker of Paradise does not sleep, and the one fleeing from the Fire does not sleep."],[3630,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date."],[3631,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ touched me while he was fasting."],[3632,"Sa'dan b. Yahya narrated to us, from Hurayth b. Abi Matar, from al-Hakam and Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad and 'Alqama, from 'A'isha something similar. No one narrated this other hadith from Hurayth, from al-Hakam and Hammad, except Sa'dan b. Yahya. Sulayman b. 'Abd al-Rahman was alone in narrating it."],[3633,"There will be after me a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will the earth be sunk while there are righteous people in it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Yes, when the majority of its inhabitants are wicked.\""],[3634,"Allah has pardoned my ummah for what their souls whisper, as long as they do not act upon it or speak of it."],[3635,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying: O Allah, call me to account with an easy reckoning. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the easy reckoning? He said: \"O Aisha, He will look into his book and overlook his sins. As for the one whose reckoning is disputed, he is destroyed.\""],[3636,"O Banu Salima, who is your leader today? They said: Al-Jadd b. Qays, but we find him stingy. He said: \"And what disease is worse than stinginess? Rather, your leader is Amr b. al-Jamuh.\""],[3637,"I asked my Lord a question, and I wish I had not asked. I said: O Lord, there were messengers before me, among them those for whom You subjected the winds, and among them those who revived the dead. He said: Did I not find you an orphan and give you refuge? Did I not find you astray and guide you? Did I not expand your chest for you and remove your burden from you? I said: Yes, O Lord."],[3638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from sitting between two men except with their permission."],[3639,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him disheveled and dusty in the appearance of a Bedouin. He said to him: What wealth do you have? He said: Allah has given me every kind of wealth. He said: \"When Allah bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves to see its trace on him.\""],[3640,"A surah of the Quran, it is only thirty verses, argued on behalf of its companion until it admitted him to Paradise, and it is Surah Tabarak."],[3641,"Beware of these two foul herbs that you eat and then enter our mosques. If you must eat them, then kill them thoroughly by fire."],[3642,"Whoever is appointed as a judge has been slaughtered without a knife."],[3643,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man swearing by trustworthiness, so he said: \"Are you the one who swears by trustworthiness?!\""],[3644,"A parent has not given a child anything better than good manners."],[3645,"I used to bathe, myself and the Messenger of God ﷺ, from a single vessel, and I would say: Leave some for me, leave some for me."],[3646,"My community is like rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."],[3647,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called for water for ablution and performed ablution one time one time, and said: This is the ablution without which God does not accept prayer. Then he performed ablution two times two times, and said: This is the ablution of the nations before you. Then he performed ablution three times three times, and said: This is my ablution and the ablution of the prophets before me."],[3648,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ heard the call to prayer, he would say: O God, Lord of this perfect call and the established prayer, bless Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, and place us in his intercession on the Day of Resurrection. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever says this at the call to prayer, God will place him in my intercession on the Day of Resurrection."],[3649,"Al-Nāqūr is the trumpet, and it is a horn. And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: How can I be at ease when it has been placed in the mouth?"],[3650,"It will be said to the disbeliever: Who is your Lord? He will say: I do not know. At that moment he is deaf, blind, and dumb. Then he will be struck with a sledgehammer, which if a mountain were struck with it, it would turn to dust, and everything hears it except the two heavy ones (humans and jinn). He said: And I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite: God confirms those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter, and God leads the wrongdoers astray."],[3651,"A man from the Children of Israel used to dig up graves. He said to his family: When I die, burn me, then take my bones and grind them, then look for a windy day and scatter me in it. That was done to him. His Lord said to him: Why did you do that? He said: Out of fear of You, O Lord. So God forgave him."],[3652,"Disputing about the Quran is disbelief."],[3653,"Wine is the mother of all evils. Whoever drinks it, his prayer is not accepted for forty days. If he dies while it is in his stomach, he dies the death of the pre-Islamic ignorance."],[3654,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed behind Abu Bakr ؓ."],[3655,"My beloved ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of every month, bathing on Friday, and praying witr before sleeping."],[3656,"An old man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, teach me a deed by which I may draw near to my Lord, Mighty and Majestic. He said: You must strive in the way of God. He said: I am not able to do that; I have become too old and weak for it. He said: Then be a muezzin."],[3657,"When the call to prayer is given in a village, Allah secures it from His punishment on that day."],[3658,"Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand between Paradise and Hell. Then a caller will call out: 'O people of Paradise!' They will look up, and it will be said to them: 'Do you recognize this?' They will say: 'O our Lord, this is death.' It will then be slaughtered between Paradise and Hell, and it will be said to them: 'Eternal life, no death.'"],[3659,"The best of this nation after its Prophet is Abu Bakr and Umar."],[3660,"I undertook a guarantee for a fine."],[3661,"I have not left after me any trial more harmful to men than women."],[3662,"There is no divorce except after marriage."],[3663,"He used to say: 'I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in Your mercy from Your torment, and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot count praise of You; You are as You have praised Yourself.'"],[3664,"The Quran is the speech of Allah, not created. Whoever says the Quran is created is a disbeliever."],[3665,"A free woman is not to be subjected to coitus interruptus except with her permission."],[3666,"A man should not look at another man's private parts, and a woman should not look at another woman's private parts. A man should not lie skin to skin with another man, and a woman should not lie skin to skin with another woman."],[3667,"If a bucketful of Hell were placed in the middle of the earth, the stench of its odor and the intensity of its heat would harm everything between the east and the west. And if a single spark of Hell were in the east, those in the west would feel its heat."],[3668,"Allah is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."],[3669,"Whoever claims lineage from other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him."],[3670,"I do not eat reclining."],[3671,"Seek refuge in God from greed that leads to stinginess, and from greed that leads to no greed."],[3672,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3673,"The Prophet's ﷺ concubine, the mother of Ibrahim, was in an upper room of hers. A Copt used to come to her, bringing her water and firewood. People said about that: 'A foreigner entering upon a foreign woman.' That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent ʿAli b. Abi Talib and ordered him to kill the man. ʿAli went and found him on a palm tree. When the Copt saw the sword with ʿAli, he fell, threw off the cloak that was on him, and jumped. He was found to be castrated. ʿAli returned to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, when you command one of us to do something and then he sees otherwise, should he consult you?' He said: 'Yes.' He informed him of what he saw of the Copt. Then the mother of Ibrahim gave birth to Ibrahim, and the Prophet ﷺ was in doubt about him until Gabriel ﷺ came and said: 'Peace be upon you, O father of Ibrahim,' and he was reassured by that."],[3674,"Paradise is adorned from year to year for the month of Ramadan, and the wide-eyed maidens adorn themselves from year to year for the month of Ramadan. When the month of Ramadan enters, Paradise says: 'O God, make for us in this month inhabitants from Your servants,' and the wide-eyed maidens say: 'O God, make for us in this month spouses from Your servants.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever guards himself in the month of Ramadan, does not drink intoxicants in it, does not slander a believer in it, and does not commit a sin in it, God will marry him every night to a hundred maidens and build for him a palace in Paradise of gold, silver, ruby, and chrysolite. If the world were gathered and placed in that palace, it would be only like a goat's tether in this world. Whoever drinks intoxicants in it, slanders a believer in it, or commits a sin in it, God nullifies his deeds for a year. So beware of the month of Ramadan, for it is God's month. If you are negligent in it, He has made for you eleven months in which you may enjoy and take pleasure, and He has reserved for Himself the month of Ramadan, so beware of the month of Ramadan.'"],[3675,"Umm Sulayman, his wife, asked ʿAʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, about the meat of sacrificial animals. She said: 'ʿAli b. Abi Talib returned from a military expedition and entered upon Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Meat from a sacrificial animal was brought to him, but he refused to eat it until he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Eat it from Dhu al-Hijjah to Dhu al-Hijjah.\""],[3676,"A man came to al-Hasan and al-Husayn and asked them. They said: 'Begging is only permissible for three: overwhelming need, heavy debt, or crushing burden,' and they gave him. Then he came to Ibn ʿUmar, who gave him without asking him. The man said to him: 'I came to your two cousins, and they asked me, but you did not ask me.' Ibn ʿUmar said: 'The two sons of the Messenger of God ﷺ were only teaching knowledge.'"],[3677,"Some Arabs came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to embrace Islam, wearing wool. I said: 'I will stand between these people and the Messenger of God ﷺ,' then I said to myself: 'He is conversing privately with the people,' but my soul would not let me but to go to him. I heard him say: 'You will raid the Arabian Peninsula and God will grant you victory, then you will raid Persia and God will grant you victory, then you will raid the Dajjal and God will grant you victory.'"],[3678,"On the day of Khaybar, the people suffered hunger, so they took domestic donkeys and slaughtered them, and boiled their pots. That reached the Prophet ﷺ. Jabir said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered us, and we overturned the pots, and he said: \"God will bring you provision that is more lawful for you than this and better than that.\" So we overturned the pots that day while they were boiling.' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys, the meat of horses and mules, every predator with fangs, every bird with talons, and he forbade animals killed by strangling, stolen property, and plunder.'"],[3679,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a beggar stood before us. The people remained silent. Then he returned and asked, and some of the people gave him a ring or something. The people followed suit and gave him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever initiates a good practice that is followed, he will have its reward and the like of the rewards of those who follow it, without diminishing their rewards in anything. Whoever initiates an evil practice that is followed, he will bear its burden and the like of the burdens of those who follow it, without diminishing their burdens in anything.'"],[3680,"When one of you wakes from sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[3681,"He walked to the Messenger of God ﷺ with rancid fat, bread, and barley. He used to say: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, the family of Muhammad does not wake up with a ṣāʿ of wheat, nor a ṣāʿ of dates.' At that time, they were the people of nine households."],[3682,"Al-ʿAbbās sent me to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I came to him in the evening while he was in the house of my maternal aunt Maymūnah. The Messenger of God ﷺ got up to pray during the night. When he prayed the two rakʿahs before dawn, he said: 'O God, I ask You for mercy from You by which You guide my heart, gather my affairs, mend my disarray, restore my affection, set aright my religion, safeguard my absent ones, elevate my present ones, purify my deeds, whiten my face, inspire me with right guidance, and protect me from every evil. O God, grant me true faith and certainty after which there is no disbelief, and mercy by which I attain the honor of Your generosity in this world and the Hereafter. O God, I ask You for success at the meeting, the hospitality of the martyrs, the life of the happy, the companionship of the prophets, and victory over enemies. O God, I bring my need to You, even if my judgment falls short and my deeds are weak, for I am in need of Your mercy. I ask You, O Decider of affairs, O Healer of hearts, as You set boundaries between the seas, to protect me from the torment of the blazing fire, from the call of destruction, and from the trial of the graves. O God, whatever good my judgment falls short of, my deeds are too weak for, and my intention or hope does not reach, which You have promised to any of Your servants or which You will give to any of Your creation, I desire it from You and ask You, O Lord of the worlds. O God, make us rightly guided and guiding, not astray nor leading astray, at war with Your enemies and at peace with Your friends. We love people through Your love and we are hostile, through Your enmity, to those who oppose You. O God, this is the supplication and upon You is the response. O God, this is the effort and upon You is the reliance. There is no might nor power except with God. O God, Possessor of the firm rope and the right command, I ask You for security on the Day of Warning and Paradise on the Day of Eternity with the drawn-near witnesses, those who bow and prostrate, and those who fulfill covenants. Indeed, You are Merciful and Loving, and You do what You will. Glory be to the One who has girded Himself with might and spoken of it. Glory be to the One to whom alone glorification is due. Glory be to the Possessor of might and splendor. Glory be to the Possessor of power and generosity. Glory be to the One who has counted all things by His knowledge. O God, place for me light in my heart, light in my grave, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, light in my blood, light in my bones, light before me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light above me, light below me. O God, increase me in light, grant me light, and place for me light.'"],[3683,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would send us out and we had no food except salaf of dates. We would divide them handful by handful until we ended up with date by date. He said: I said: 'And what benefit can a single date, one by one, give you?' He said: 'Do not say that. By God, as soon as we lost it, we became disordered.'"],[3684,"I came to Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ for a need and saw him relieve himself and wipe over his leather socks. I said to him: 'Do you wipe over leather socks?' He said: 'Yes, when you meet your father, ask him.' Ibn ʿUmar said: 'I met my father ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb and asked him about that. He said: 'Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ did it, so we did it.'"],[3685,"God has not created any disease except that He has created a cure for it. Those who know it know it, and those who are ignorant of it are ignorant of it, except death."],[3686,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Muṣʿab b. ʿUmayr when he returned from Uḥud and stopped over him and his companions. He said: 'I bear witness that you are alive in the presence of God. Visit them and greet them. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no one greets them except that they return the greeting until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[3687,"Indeed, God created the Garden of Eden and built it with His own hand: one brick of gold and one brick of silver. He made its mortar musk, its soil saffron, and its pebbles pearls. Then He said to it: 'Speak.' It said: 'The believers have succeeded.' The angels said: 'Blessed are you, abode of kings.'"],[3688,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ vomited and broke his fast? I met Thawbān, the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and said: 'Abū al-Dardāʾ said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ vomited and broke his fast?\"' He said: 'And I poured water for him and he performed ablution.'"],[3689,"I heard Jarīr b. ʿAbd Allāh, who was our commander, say: 'I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, then I turned back. He called me and said: \"I will not accept from you until you pledge allegiance,' and sincere counsel to every Muslim.'\" So I pledged allegiance to him."],[3690,"Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is deficient, deficient, deficient."],[3691,"Seventy thousand from my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. It was said: 'O Messenger of God, who are they?' He said: 'They are those who do not seek ruqyah, do not cauterize, do not practice divination, and upon their Lord they rely.' He said: 'Affliction kept befalling us until we cauterized; then we did not succeed nor prosper.'"],[3692,"Nothing is more noble to God than supplication."],[3693,"A man is in prayer as long as he remains in the place of prayer in which he prayed, so long as he does not invalidate his ablution."],[3694,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling fruit until it is ripe, and wool while still on the back, and milk in the udder."],[3695,"Muʿāwiya wrote to al-Mughīra b. Shuʿba: 'Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.' So al-Mughīra wrote to him: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say when he finished the prayer: 'There is no god but God alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the good fortune of a fortunate person avails nothing against You.' And he used to forbid gossip, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."],[3696,"Whoever is displeased with his provision and airs his complaint and does not endure patiently, no deed will ascend for him to God, and he will meet God while He is angry with him."],[3697,"The slaughtering of the fetus is the slaughtering of its mother."],[3698,"She said: 'Throw me the small mat in the mosque.' I said: 'I am menstruating.' He said: 'Your menstruation is not in your hand; throw it to me.' She said: 'So I threw it to him, and he prayed on it.'"],[3699,"Hospitality is for three days; whatever is beyond that is charity."],[3700,"Tanning the hide is its purification."],[3701,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade killing frogs and said: 'Their croaking is glorification.'"],[3702,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ sent ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān to Abū Bakr asking him for their inheritance from the Messenger of God ﷺ. ʿĀʾisha said: 'I was the one who turned them back from that. I sent to them: Do not do so. Have you not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity\"? So they went back.'"],[3703,"Fāṭima spoke to Abū Bakr concerning her inheritance from the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'Will your daughter inherit you, and I will not inherit my father?' He said: 'May my father be your ransom and may my father be your father's ransom: he used to say: \"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity.\"'"],[3704,"If a dog laps from the vessel of any one of you, he should not put anything in it until he washes it seven times."],[3705,"If the two parties to a sale disagree while the merchandise is still in its original state and has not been consumed, then the word is that of the seller, or they may revoke the sale."],[3706,"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."],[3707,"The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit—an evil example is not for us."],[3708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us istikhārah for a matter just as he taught one of us a sūrah from the Qur'an: “O Allah, I ask You to choose for me by Your knowledge, and I ask You to grant me ability by Your power, and I ask You of Your great bounty; for You are able and I am not able, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if there is good in this matter for my religion, my worldly life, and the outcome of my affair, then decree it for me; and if other than that is better for me, then make good easy for me wherever it may be, and turn away evil from me, and make me content with Your decree.”"],[3709,"Ismāʿīl b. ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, from al-Masʿūdī, from Ḥammād and al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it regarding istikhārah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ḥakam except al-Masʿūdī."],[3710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the killing of dogs in Madinah. Then Ibn Umm Maktūm came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I am blind.” So he granted him a concession for some days, then ordered his dog to be killed, and it was killed."],[3711,"Ibn Umm Maktūm came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I am blind, my house is far, and I hear the call to prayer.” He said: “Then if you hear the call, come, even if crawling.”"],[3712,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that wine has been forbidden?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “I have wine belonging to an orphan.” So he ordered it to be poured out, and it was poured out."],[3713,"Ibn Masʿūd entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was standing delivering a sermon. He sat down next to Ubayy and asked him about something, but Ubayy did not answer him. When the Prophet finished his prayer, Ibn Masʿūd said to Ubayy: “What prevented you from answering me?” He said: “Indeed, you did not pray the Friday prayer with us.” He said: “Why?” He said: “Because you spoke while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ubayy has spoken the truth.”"],[3714,"A Muslim man was standing on a rock praying in Makkah. The Prophet ﷺ passed by him and said: “Indeed, Allah does not become weary until you become weary.”"],[3715,"O Allah, forgive the Anṣār, the children of the Anṣār, the grandchildren of the Anṣār, their wives, and their offspring."],[3716,"Ubayy came and said: O Messenger of God, something happened from me tonight: some women gathered in my house who do not recite, so I prayed eight rak'ahs with them, then I performed witr. The Prophet ﷺ remained silent, as if in approval."],[3717,"When you pray, be brief, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, the sick, and those who have needs."],[3718,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed eight rak'ahs with us in the month of Ramadan and performed witr. The next night we gathered in the mosque, hoping he would pray with us. He said: I feared, or disliked, that it would be made obligatory upon you."],[3719,"He met Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah, driving a camel of his with two water-skins on it, and a water-bag on the camel's neck. I said: O Abu Dharr, what is with you? He said: I have my work. He said: I said: Tell me, may God have mercy on you. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'There are no two Muslims between whom three children die, who have not reached the age of accountability, except that they are forgiven by the virtue of His mercy toward them.' I said: Tell me more, may God have mercy on you. He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever spends a pair of anything from his wealth in the path of God, the gatekeepers of Paradise will meet him, each of them calling him to what he has.' I said: A pair of what? He said: 'If he is an owner of horses, then two horses; if an owner of camels, then two camels; if an owner of cattle, then two cows'—until he counted various kinds of this sort."],[3720,"I have not fasted twenty-nine days with the Messenger of God ﷺ more often than I fasted thirty with him."],[3721,"He was asked about the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He poured water in the open courtyard, then said: Where is the one asking about the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ? Then he washed his hands three times, his face three times, his forearms three times, wiped his head until it almost dripped, and washed his feet three times three times. Then he said: This is the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[3722,"The Prophet ﷺ came while we were sitting and said: I have never entered upon a morning except that I sought forgiveness from God in it a hundred times."],[3723,"Whoever frees a Muslim or believing slave, God will protect every limb of his from the Fire by every limb of that slave."],[3724,"Do not show gloating over your brother, lest God pardon him and afflict you."],[3725,"The scriptures of Abraham were sent down on the first night of the month of Ramadan, the Torah was sent down on the sixth night of Ramadan, the Gospel was sent down on the thirteenth night of Ramadan, the Psalms were sent down on the eighteenth night of Ramadan, and the Quran was sent down on the twenty-fourth night of Ramadan."],[3726,"He forbade a man from bathing in the leftover water of a woman, or a woman from bathing in the leftover water of a man, but they should both scoop water together."],[3727,"On the night the Messenger of God ﷺ was taken on the night journey to the Aqsa Mosque, when he returned he was between the Maqam and Zamzam, with Gabriel on his right and Michael on his left, and they flew with him until he reached the seven heavens. When he returned, he said: I heard glorification in the highest heavens along with much glorification: The highest heavens glorified the One of awe, trembling before the One of loftiness with what is exalted: Glory be to the Most High, the Supreme; glory be to Him, and exalted is He."],[3728,"He sent a milch-camel with me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me, 'Milk it.' So I milked it. Then he said, 'O Nuqadah, leave the milk's inviter,' so I left its teats standing, and I did not exhaust all the milk."],[3729,"No people gather in a gathering and then disperse without remembering Allah, except that gathering will be a regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."],[3730,"The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."],[3731,"I ate a tharidah of wheat bread with fat meat, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and began to belch. The Prophet ﷺ said to me, 'Restrain your belching, for the people who eat their fill most in this world will be the hungriest in the Hereafter.'"],[3732,"While the Prophet ﷺ was walking between me and another man, he came upon two graves and said, 'The occupants of these two graves are being punished. Bring me a palm stalk.' Abu Bakrah said, 'I and my companion raced, and I brought him a palm stalk. He split it in two and placed one in this grave and one in that grave.' He said, 'Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they remain moist. Indeed, they are being punished for something not major: backbiting and urine.'"],[3733,"We were in the land of the Romans when a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, from Banu Sulaym, called Maʿn b. Yazid al-Sulami, passed by us. He said, 'I found a red jar containing dinars, so I brought it to him. He took out a fifth and said, \"Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'No spoil is given except after the fifth,' I would have given it to you.\" Then he offered me some of his share, but I said, \"I have no need of it.\"'"],[3734,"There will be troubles and more troubles. Whoever you see walking toward the community of Muhammad ﷺ to divide their unity, kill him."],[3735,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a gold ring on his hand, and he began to tap it with a stick he had. When the Prophet ﷺ was distracted, he threw it away. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'I think we have only caused you pain and made you lose.'"],[3736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt pain one day and sent for ʿUthman. She said, 'I heard him say, \"Allah will clothe you with a shirt. If they want you to remove it, do not remove it.\"' She was asked, 'Where were you? Why did you not mention this before?' She said, 'I forgot it.'"],[3737,"Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot impersonate me."],[3738,"The one who drinks from a silver vessel only gulps the fire of Hell into his belly."],[3739,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Uhud, he placed his women in a fortress called Fariʿ and put Hassan b. Thabit with them. Hassan would look out at the Prophet ﷺ, and when the fighting intensified against the polytheists, he would intensify with him while in the fort, and when he returned, he would return behind him. Some Jews came, and one of them climbed the fort until he looked down on us. I said to Hassan, 'Get up and kill him.' He said, 'That is not in me. If that were in me, I would have been with the Prophet ﷺ.' Safiyyah said, 'I struck his head until I cut it off. When I cut it off, I said, \"O Hassan, get up and throw his head at them, for they are below the fort.\" He said, \"By Allah, that is not in me.\" She said, 'I took his head and threw it at them. They said, \"By Allah, we know that Muhammad would not leave his family without anyone with them.\" And they dispersed.' She said, 'Saʿd b. Muʿadh passed by us with a yellowness on him as if he had just camped before that, reciting rajz and saying: \"Slowly, a little; the battle will soon catch up. Carry on! No harm in death when the appointed time has come.\"'"],[3740,"She saw the Messenger of God ﷺ eat a shoulder, then stand for prayer without performing ablution."],[3741,"The Prophet ﷺ used to fast continuously from pre-dawn to pre-dawn."],[3742,"Take the pre-dawn meal, even with something small."],[3743,"Enter upon the Mother of the Believers, ʿĀʾishah, and convey my greetings of peace to her. So I entered upon her and said, “One of your sons conveys greetings of peace to you.” She said, “And upon him be peace and the mercy of God.” I said, “He asks you to narrate to him about ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān, for people have said much about him among us when he was killed.” She said, “As for me, I bear witness that ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān was in this house, while the Prophet of God ﷺ and Jibrīl were receiving revelation—he came to the Prophet ﷺ on a very hot night, and whenever revelation descended upon him, a heaviness would descend upon him. God, majestic is His mention, says: “Indeed, We will cast upon you a weighty word” [Q 73:5]. The Prophet of God ﷺ was patting ʿUthmān’s shoulder and saying, ‘Write, ʿUthmān.’ God would not have placed anyone in that station with His Prophet except a noble man. So whoever reviles ʿUthmān, upon him is the curse of God.”"],[3744,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, whenever he left his house, would pass by the Mothers of the Believers and greet them before coming to his gathering. When he returned to his house, he would pass by them. Every time he passed, he found a man sitting at ʿĀʾishah’s door. He said to him, “Why do I see you sitting here?” He said, “A right that I am seeking from the Mother of the Believers.” So ʿUmar entered upon her and said, “O Mother of the Believers, is seven thousand not sufficient for you each year?” She said, “Yes, but I have obligations, and I heard Abu al-Qāsim ﷺ say: ‘Whoever has a debt that concerns him to repay, or intends to repay it, will never cease to have a guardian from God with him.’ So I love that a guardian from God should never cease to be with me.”"],[3745,"The blood of a person who bears witness that there is no god but God is not lawful except for one of three reasons: a married person who commits adultery after having been married, a man who intentionally kills a believer and is executed for it, and a man who goes out as a warrior against God and His Messenger, so he is killed and crucified, or banished from the land."],[3746,"I entered upon ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers, and she had a slave girl of hers wearing a cotton shift worth five dirhams. She said, “Raise your head to my slave girl and look at her, for she is too proud to wear it in the house. I had a shift from among them during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and no woman in Madinah would be adorned except that she sent to me to borrow it.”"],[3747,"I entered upon ʿĀʾishah and asked her about the two rakʿahs after ʿAṣr. She said, “By the One who took his soul ﷺ, he did not leave them until he met God. And he did not meet God until he had become too weak to pray standing, and he used to pray most of his prayers sitting.” Umm Ayman said to her, “ʿUthmān used to forbid them.” She said, “You speak truly, but the Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray them, and he did not pray them in the mosque for fear of making it burdensome for his community, and he loved whatever lightened their burden.”"],[3748,"I entered upon ʿĀʾishah, and ʿĀʾishah said: I entered upon Barīrah, who was a mukātabah (a slave with a contract of manumission). She said, “Buy me and set me free.” I said, “Yes.” Barīrah said, “My masters will not sell me unless they stipulate my walāʾ (patronage).” ʿĀʾishah said, “I have no need for that.” The Messenger of God ﷺ heard about that and mentioned it to ʿĀʾishah. She told him what they had said. He said, “Buy her and set her free, and let them stipulate whatever they wish.” So ʿĀʾishah bought her, and her masters stipulated the walāʾ. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Walāʾ belongs to the one who sets free, even if they stipulate a hundred conditions.”"],[3749,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, “Do women go out on the day of Eid?” He said, “Yes.” It was said, “What about a young woman who has not yet married?” He said, “Yes, and if she does not have a garment to wear, let her borrow the garment of her companion.”"],[3750,"A woman stretched out her hand to the Prophet ﷺ with a letter, and he withdrew his hand. She said, “O Messenger of God, I stretched out my hand to you with a letter, and you did not take it.” He said, “I do not know whether it is the hand of a woman or the hand of a man.” She said, “Rather, it is the hand of a woman.” He said, “If you were a woman, you would have dyed your nails with henna.”"],[3751,"We returned with the Messenger of God ﷺ from al-Ḥudaybiyyah until when the Messenger of God ﷺ reached Kurāʿ al-Ghamīm, suddenly the people began to rush toward the Messenger of God ﷺ. Some of the people said to others, “What is with the people?” They said, “Revelation has come to the Messenger of God ﷺ.” So we went out until we found the Messenger of God ﷺ standing at Kurāʿ al-Ghamīm. When the people gathered, he recited to them: “Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory” [Q 48:1]. Some of the people said to him, “O Messenger of God, is it a victory?” He said, “Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, it is indeed a victory.”"],[3752,"By the One in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, the Hour will not come until obscenity and miserliness appear, the trustworthy is betrayed and the treacherous is trusted, and the wuʿūl perish and the tuḥūt appear.\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, what are the wuʿūl and what are the tuḥūt?\" He said, \"The wuʿūl are the faces of people and their nobles, and the tuḥūt are those who were under people's feet, not known.\""],[3753,"I saw men from the Arabs come to the Messenger of God ﷺ and say, \"O Messenger of God, we own livestock, and we give its sadaqah. Is that sufficient for us instead of the zakah of Ramadan?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"No. Pay it on behalf of the young and the old, the free and the slave, for it is a purification for you.\""],[3754,"Religion is sincerity, religion is sincerity,\" three times. They said, \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To God, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to their common people.\""],[3755,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, \"Sit until Gabriel comes to me, and you can greet him and he will supplicate for good for you.\" Gabriel came and stood at the door, then turned back and did not enter. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with Gabriel? He turned back and did not enter.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ met him another time and said, \"O Gabriel, ʿAʾishah sat to greet you and for you to supplicate for good for her, but you turned back from our door and did not enter upon us.\" Gabriel said, \"I came to enter upon you, but I found that foul little creature in your house, and we do not enter a house in which there is that little creature or images.\""],[3756,"God and His angels send blessings upon those who join the rows, and no servant joins a row but God raises him a degree by it, and the angels sprinkle blessing upon him."],[3757,"No one asks God but God gives him what he asked, or averts from him harm equal to it, as long as he does not supplicate for sin or severing kinship."],[3758,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to the market and saw food piled up. He put his hand into it and brought out food that was moist, which the rain had affected. He said to its owner, \"What made you do this?\" He said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, it is one food.\" He said, \"Would you not separate the moist on its own and the dry on its own, so they buy what they recognize? Whoever cheats us is not one of us.\""],[3759,"I went out on a journey, and when I returned, ʿUmar said to me, \"Who accompanied you?\" I said, \"A man from Banu Bakr b. Waʾil accompanied me.\" ʿUmar said, \"Have you not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Your brother the Bakri, but do not trust him'?\""],[3760,"He asked Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah, and he said, \"We have sheep and servant boys, and they are at Tharir, and they beat down this ḥublah fruit for their sheep.\" Kharijah said, \"It is the fruit of the samur tree.\" Jabir said, \"No.\" Then he said, \"Do not beat down or cut from the protected reserve of the Messenger of God ﷺ, but shake them gently.\" Then Jabir said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid cutting the masad.\""],[3761,"O ʿAʾishah, beware of sins that are deemed insignificant, for they have a seeker from God."],[3762,"There is no harm and no reciprocation of harm. A man may place a wooden beam on his neighbor's wall. If you are in doubt about a road, make it seven cubits."],[3763,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and said, \"O people, O assembly of those who believe with their tongues but faith has not penetrated their hearts,\" until he made the young women in their curtained rooms hear, \"do not harm the Muslims, and do not pursue their faults. For whoever pursues his brother's fault, God will pursue his fault until He exposes it in the interior of his house.\""],[3764,"I said: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: Fear God wherever you are, and treat people with good character."],[3765,"No people ever sit in one of the houses of God, reciting the Book of God and studying it among themselves, except that mercy envelops them, tranquility descends upon them, the angels surround them, and God mentions them to those near Him. Whoever follows a path seeking knowledge, God makes easy for him a path to Paradise. Whoever's deeds slow him down, his lineage will not speed him up."],[3766,"He entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah. He mentioned that to Umar, who said: 'You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.'"],[3767,"The first thing the servant is asked about on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer. If it is sound, he has succeeded; if it is corrupt, he has failed and lost."],[3768,"Umar b. al-Khattab addressed the people at al-Jabiyah, saying: O people, whoever wishes to ask about the Quran, let him go to Ubayy b. Ka'b. Whoever wishes to ask about the obligatory shares, let him go to Zayd b. Thabit. Whoever wishes to ask about fiqh, let him go to Mu'adh b. Jabal. Whoever wishes to ask about wealth, let him come to me, for God has made me its guardian and distributor. I begin with the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, then the first Muhajirun who were expelled from their homes and their properties—and he recited the entire verse. Whoever hastened to the Hijrah, the giving hastens to him; whoever was slow in the Hijrah, the giving is slow to him. Let no man blame anyone but the resting place of his mount."],[3769,"A man came to Umar b. al-Khattab and said: 'The hyena has eaten us.' Mis'ar said: meaning the year [of drought]. Umar asked him: 'From whom are you?' He kept asking about his lineage until he recognized him, and he turned out to be wealthy. Umar said: 'If a man had a valley or two valleys, he would seek a third.' Ibn Abbas said: 'Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, then God turns in mercy to whoever repents.' Umar said to Ibn Abbas: 'From whom did you hear this?' He said: 'From Ubayy b. Ka'b.' He said: 'Then when it is morning, come to me.' So he went early to his mother, Umm al-Fadl, and mentioned that to her. She said: 'What do you have to do with speaking in Umar's presence?' Ibn Abbas feared that Ubayy might have forgotten. His mother said to him: 'Ubayy is unlikely to have forgotten.' He went early to Umar, who had a whip with him. They went to Ubayy, who came out to them after performing ablution. He said: 'I had a discharge of madhy, so I washed my penis'—or 'my private part'—Mis'ar was unsure. Umar said: 'Is that sufficient?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did you hear it from the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.' And he asked him about what Ibn Abbas had said, and he confirmed it."],[3770,"There is no judge who judges between people except that he will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with an angel holding him by the back of his neck until he stops him at the edge of Hell. Then he raises his head to the sky. If God, may His mention be exalted, says: 'Throw him,' he falls for forty autumns."],[3771,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ gave drink, he said: 'Begin with the elder, or with the elders.'"],[3772,"Seek needs from those with handsome faces."],[3773,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and confessed to adultery, and she was pregnant. He delayed her for a year until she gave birth. Then he ordered that her clothes be fastened tightly around her, then he ordered that she be stoned. Then he prayed over her. A man said to him: 'Do you pray over her when she committed adultery and you stoned her?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'She has repented with such a repentance that if seventy of the people of Madinah repented with it, it would be accepted from them. Have you found anything better than that she gave up her own life?'"],[3774,"The people of Yemen have come to you. They have the softest hearts. Faith is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni, and fiqh is Yemeni."],[3775,"I said to Ibn Umar: 'Did you witness the Pledge of Ridwan with the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'What was he wearing?' He said: 'A cotton shirt, a stuffed jubbah, a cloak, and a sword. I saw al-Nu'man b. Muqarrin al-Muzani standing at his head, holding up the branches of the tree over his head while the people were pledging allegiance to him.'"],[3776,"The Prophet ﷺ disliked every fanged beast of prey, and every bird with talons."],[3777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to pray at night, whether little or much, and to end that with an odd number."],[3778,"Anas b. Malik mentioned seventy of the Ansar. He said: When night fell upon them, they would go to a teacher in Madinah and spend the night with him studying the Quran. Then in the morning, whoever had strength would gather firewood and draw fresh water, and whoever had means would get a sheep and prepare it; so it would be hanging in the rooms of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by morning. When Khubayb was killed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent them. He said: Among them was my maternal uncle Haram b. Milhan. They came upon a clan of Banu Sulaym. He said: Haram said to their leader, \"Shall I inform these people that we are not after them, so that they let us pass?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So he went to them and told them that. A man from among them met him with a spear and pierced him through. When Haram felt the spear in his belly, he said, \"Allahu akbar! I have won, by the Lord of the Kaaba!\" He said: They closed in on them, and none of them remained to report. He said: \"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ grieve over any expedition as he grieved over them.\" Anas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, every time he prayed the dawn prayer, raise his hands supplicating against them. Later, Abu Talhah came to me and said: \"Do you know what happened to the killer of Haram?\" I said, \"What about him? May Allah do such-and-such to him.\" Abu Talhah said, \"Do not say that, for he has accepted Islam.\""],[3779,"He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was asleep, and the Prophet ﷺ woke up and embraced Halah to his chest, saying: \"Halah, Halah, Halah.\""],[3780,"I said to Ubayy b. Ka'b: \"Ibn Umm 'Abd said: 'Whoever stands in prayer all year will attain Laylat al-Qadr.'\" Ubayy said: \"By Allah, it is in Ramadan, and it is the night of the twenty-seventh.\""],[3781,"We met 'Ali, and he was wearing two garments in winter. We said to him: \"Do not be deceived by this land of ours, for our land is cold, not like your land.\" He said: \"I used to feel cold, but when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Khaybar, I said, 'I have sore eyes.' He spat into my eyes, and since then I have felt neither cold nor heat, and my eyes have not become sore.\""],[3782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent al-Walid b. 'Uqbah to Banu Wali'ah, and there had been enmity between them in pre-Islamic times. When he reached Banu Wali'ah, they went out to meet him to see what he intended, but he feared the people and returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"Banu Wali'ah wanted to kill me and withheld the zakat.\" When Banu Wali'ah learned what al-Walid had said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, al-Walid lied. But there was enmity between us and him, and we feared he would punish us for what had been between us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Banu Wali'ah must stop, or I will send to them a man who is like my own self, to kill their fighters and take their offspring captive—and he is this one.\" Then he struck his hand on the shoulder of 'Ali b. Abi Talib. He said: And Allah revealed concerning al-Walid: \"O you who believe, if a wicked person comes to you with news...\" the verse."],[3783,"It is as if I can see a rider who will come to you and settle among you, saying: \"The land is our land, the city is our city, and you are only our slaves and hired laborers.\" He will stand between widows and orphans and what Allah has granted as booty to their fathers."],[3784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called 'Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn, and covered them with a cloak, then said: \"Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you completely.\" He said: It was revealed concerning them."],[3785,"When you enter the mosque with arrows, hold them by their heads so that you do not wound any Muslim."],[3786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed three people by execution on the day of Badr: he killed al-Nadr b. al-Harith from Banu 'Abd al-Dar, Tu'aymah b. 'Adiyy from Banu Nawfal, and 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt."],[3787,"When Allah created creation, He sent Jibril and divided people into two groups: He made the Arabs one group and the non-Arabs one group. The best of Allah's choice was among the Arabs. Then He divided the Arabs into two groups: He made Yemen one group and Mudar one group, and Quraysh one group. The best of Allah's choice was among Quraysh. Then He brought me out from the best of those I am from."],[3788,"There will be in the latter days a people who dye their hair black; Allah will not look at them on the Day of Resurrection."],[3789,"The group of jinn who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were the jinn of Nasibin; they came to him at Nakhlah."],[3790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would kiss, then go out to the prayer without renewing his ablution."],[3791,"Uthman prohibited tamattuʿ and qiran (combining Hajj and ʿUmrah). News of that reached ʿAli, so he went out saying, 'Labbayk with a Hajj and an ʿUmrah together.' Uthman said to him, 'Have I not prohibited this?' He said, 'I would not abandon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the prohibition of anyone.'"],[3792,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in a dwelling, and he was branding camels. He said, 'Has the daughter of Milhan given birth?' I said, 'Yes,' and I handed the infant to the Prophet ﷺ."],[3793,"Whoever desires the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him."],[3794,"Recitation in the latter part of the night is witnessed, and that is better."],[3795,"The Prophet ﷺ stood (in prayer) until his feet became swollen. It was said to him, 'Do you do this when your past and future sins have been forgiven?' He said, 'Should I not be a grateful servant?'"],[3796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the signal in prayer the tasbih (saying 'subhan Allah') for men and clapping for women."],[3797,"He was present at Uhud with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a stone hit him on his leg, and he continued to limp from it until he died."],[3798,"Those who have incurred wrath are the Jews, and those who are astray are the Christians."],[3799,"Perform Hajj and ʿUmrah repeatedly, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows remove the dross of iron."],[3800,"Zamzam water is for whatever it is drunk for."],[3801,"Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and ʿUmar."],[3802,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ led them in the ʿAsr prayer, then stood among them as a speaker and said in his sermon: 'Indeed, this world is green and sweet, and Allah is making you successors in it, so He is watching how you act. Beware of the world and beware of women. Indeed, every treacherous one will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection, according to the measure of his treachery, placed near his anus. Indeed, the greatest treachery is the treachery of a leader of the common people. Indeed, anger is a burning coal placed on the heart of the son of Adam. Do you not see when one becomes angry, how his eyes turn red and his jugular veins swell? So whoever experiences any of that, if he is standing let him sit down, and if he is sitting let him cling to the ground. Indeed, people in anger are of different ranks: a man quick to anger and quick to calm down—that is neither against him nor for him; a man slow to anger and slow to calm down—that is neither against him nor for him; a man slow to anger and quick to calm down—that is for him; and a man quick to anger and slow to calm down—that is against him. Indeed, the son of Adam was created in stages: a servant may be created a believer, live as a believer, and die as a believer; a servant may be created a disbeliever, live as a disbeliever, and die as a disbeliever; a servant may be created a believer, live as a believer, and die as a disbeliever; and a servant may be created a disbeliever, live as a disbeliever, and die as a believer.' He also mentioned: 'Indeed, people in seeking are of different ranks: a man who, when he seeks, is harsh, and when he is sought from, fulfills—that equals that; a man who, when he seeks, withholds, and when he is sought from, is taken from—that equals that; a man who, when he seeks, withholds and takes, and when he is sought from, fulfills—that is better for him; and a man who, when he seeks, withholds, and when he is sought from, defrauds—that is worse for him. Indeed, might one of you see an evil and not change it? Indeed, sixty-nine nations have passed before you, and you are completing seventy. Indeed, what has passed of the world compared to what remains is like what has passed of this day of yours compared to what remains.' That was when the sun had turned yellow and was about to set."],[3803,"When Abu Talib died, they waited for the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'O uncle, how quickly I have felt your loss.'"],[3804,"The first of our rites this day is prayer, then sacrifice after the prayer. He said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered my sacrifice before praying, wanting to have a meal ready for my neighbors. I have a young goat that is dearer to me than the meat of two sheep. Shall I slaughter it?' He said: 'Yes, but it will not suffice for anyone after you.'"],[3805,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided the people of Khaybar while they were going out in the morning. They were watching and said: 'Muhammad and the army, Muhammad and the army.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned.'"],[3806,"Al-ʿAbbas sent ʿAbdullah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a need. He found with him a man, so he returned and did not speak to him. He (the Prophet) said: 'Did you see him?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'That was Jibril. Indeed, he will not die until his sight goes and he is given knowledge.'"],[3807,"Six traits: no Muslim dies in one of them except that Allah guarantees to admit him to Paradise: a man who goes out as a warrior, and if he dies in that state, Allah guarantees him; a man who follows a funeral procession, and if he dies in that state, Allah guarantees him; a man who visits a sick person, and if he dies in that state, Allah guarantees him; a man who performs ablution well, then goes out to a mosque for his prayer, and if he dies in that state, Allah guarantees him; a man who comes to a leader only to honor and respect him, and if he dies in that state, Allah guarantees him; and a man in his house who does not backbite a Muslim, does not bring upon himself displeasure, and does not resent him, and if he dies in that state, Allah guarantees him."],[3808,"No one who witnessed Badr and Al-Hudaybiyyah will enter the Fire."],[3809,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray much standing and sitting. When he prayed standing, he bowed standing; and when he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting."],[3810,"Suraqah b. Malik stood up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me about our deeds that we do—are we taken to account for them at the outset, good for good and evil for evil, or is it something that the divine decrees have already preceded and the pens have dried upon?' He said: 'O Suraqah, the divine decrees have already preceded and the pens have dried upon.' He said: 'Then why do we act, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Act, O Suraqah, for every doer is facilitated for what he was created for.' He said: 'O Suraqah, now you strive.'"],[3811,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, when I have intercourse with my wife and we separate without me ejaculating, should I perform ghusl?' He said: 'Yes. I did that with my wife, and we did not ejaculate, so we performed ghusl.'"],[3812,"It was only revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Your wives are a tilth for you,” as a concession regarding coming to the rear."],[3813,"ʿUthmān wanted him to take up the judgeship, but he refused and said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Judges are of three types: one is saved, and two are in the Fire. The one who judges unjustly or according to whim is destroyed, and the one who judges by the truth is saved.”"],[3814,"When the verse “The gathering will be routed and turn their backs” was revealed, I said: Which gathering is this? Then on the day of Badr, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ with a drawn sword in his hand, saying: “The gathering will be routed and turn their backs.”"],[3815,"Whoever is prompted to say “There is no god but God” at death will enter Paradise."],[3816,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took the bottom of the valley, and the people took the mountain pass. Seven masked men came, and when the Messenger of God ﷺ saw them—Ḥudhayfa was the guide and ʿAmmār the vanguard—he said: “Block what is before you two.” They did nothing. The Messenger of God looked at them and said: “O Ḥudhayfa, do you know who the people are?” I said: “I do not recognize any of them except the owner of the red camel, for I know that he is so-and-so.”"],[3817,"The Prophet ﷺ used to offer two rams as sacrifice."],[3818,"The Qaḥṭānī will certainly drive the people with his staff."],[3819,"There is no prescribed punishment for a slave woman until she is married. When she is married, she incurs half the punishment of free married women."],[3820,"No one has a greater favor upon me than Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq. He supported me with his self and his wealth, and gave me his daughter in marriage."],[3821,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution three times for each part."],[3822,"My father came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I was with him. My father said to him: “Supplicate God for me and my son.” He said: “Then he wiped my head and accepted his pledge of allegiance to Islam.”"],[3823,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to a grave recently buried and said: “Whose grave is this?” It was said: “The grave of so-and-so.” Then he prayed over him, and I was among those who prayed over him."],[3824,"No people abandoned jihad except that Allah enveloped them all with punishment."],[3825,"Any man who has a share in a slave and then frees him becomes responsible for the shares of his partners."],[3826,"One ʿumrah to the next ʿumrah is an expiation for what is between them, and the accepted hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[3827,"No one hears the call in this mosque of mine and then leaves it except for a need, and then does not return to it, except a hypocrite."],[3828,"The Hour will not come until Allah is disbelieved in openly, and that is when they speak about their Lord."],[3829,"I asked my Lord that I not marry into any family or have any family marry into mine except that they be with me in Paradise, and He granted me that."],[3830,"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar and Abu Hurayrah met, and I was sitting with them while I was a boy, and he said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, the people claim that I lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Which land would carry me and which sky would shade me if I did? He replied: You are better than that. Then Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'If the people were to take one valley and the Ansar another valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar.' Ibn ʿUmar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that. And Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been one of the Ansar.' He said: You spoke the truth; I heard him say that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And he did not narrate anything that day except that he confirmed it. He said: And I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I will come to Hell and strike its gate, and it will be opened for me, and I will enter and praise Allah with praises such as no one before me has praised Him, nor will anyone after me. Then I will bring out from it whoever said \"La ilaha illa Allah\" sincerely. Then people from Quraysh will come to me and be attributed to me, and I will recognize their lineage but not their faces, and I will leave them in the Fire.' He said: And I heard Abu Hurayrah say: My beloved ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I have not abandoned since I parted from him, nor will I abandon them until I meet him: fasting three days of every month, the Duha prayer, and not sleeping except after performing Witr."],[3831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting, and which of you has more control over his desire than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"],[3832,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri was standing praying toward one of the pillars of the mosque, and a man from the family of ʿUqbah b. Abi Muʿayt passed in front of him, so he prevented him. He came again, so he pushed him in the chest, and the young man became angry. Then he went to Marwan b. al-Hakam and complained about Abu Saʿid. Abu Saʿid then came to him, and Marwan said to him: What is the matter with your nephew that he complains about you? Abu Saʿid said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When one of you prays, let him pray toward a sutrah. If someone passes in front of him, let him prevent him. If he returns, let him fight him, for he is a devil.'"],[3833,"He prohibited killing the jannan (small snakes that live in houses)."],[3834,"How wonderful is the affair of the believer! Indeed, all of his affair is good, and that is only for the believer. If good befalls him and he is grateful, it is good for him; and if harm befalls him and he is patient, it is good for him."],[3835,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a man, I think from Qays, came and said: O Messenger of Allah, curse Himyar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. He came from the other side, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. Then he came from the other side and he turned away from him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: May Allah have mercy on Himyar. Their hearts are Islam, their deeds are peace, and their hands are food, a people of security and faith."],[3836,"You will raise armies. A man said: O Messenger of God, choose for me. He said: \"Upon you is Syria, for it is the choice of God from His lands; in it are His chosen from His servants. Whoever turns away from that, let him join his Yemen and water from its pools, for God has guaranteed me Syria and its people.\""],[3837,"There is no amputation for a snatched or plundered item."],[3838,"\"When twelve of Banū ʿAmr b. Kaʿb perish, the pecking and mutual pecking will be until the Hour rises.\""],[3839,"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is forbidden."],[3840,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about Gog and Magog. He said: \"Gog is one nation, and Magog is one nation; each nation is four hundred thousand nations. A man does not die until he sees a thousand male descendants between his hands from his loins, each one having borne arms.\" I said: O Messenger of God, describe them to us. He said: \"They are three kinds: one kind of them is like the cedar.\" I said: What is the cedar? He said: \"A tree in Syria, the height of the tree is one hundred and twenty cubits into the sky.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"These are those for whom neither trick nor iron stands. A kind of them spreads out with one ear and covers himself with the other. They pass by no elephant, wild beast, camel, or pig but they eat it; and whoever of them dies, they eat him. Their vanguard is in Syria and their rear is in Khurasan. They drink the rivers of the east and the Lake of Tiberias.\""],[3841,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ complained, he swallowed a palmful of black seed."],[3842,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to fast on Saturday and Sunday more than he fasted on other days, and he said: \"They are two festival days for the polytheists, so I like to differ from them.\""],[3843,"After every prayer, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: \"O God, Lord of Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil, protect me from the heat of the Fire and from the punishment of the grave.\""],[3844,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was told that I said: I will stand in prayer at night and fast during the day as long as I live. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Are you the one who said: By God, I will fast during the day and stand at night as long as I live?\" I said: I said it, O Messenger of God. He said: \"You cannot do that. Pray and sleep, fast and break your fast. Fast three days of every month, for a good deed is multiplied tenfold, and that is like fasting forever.\" I said: I can do better than that. He said: \"Then fast one day and break fast two days.\" I said: I can do better than that. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Fast one day and break fast one day; that is the fast of David, and it is the most moderate fasting.\" I said: I can do better than that. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is nothing better than that.\""],[3845,"The last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ said was: \"Take my place in caring for my household.\""],[3846,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was fasting, he would not pray until we brought him fresh dates and water, and he would eat and drink if it was the season of fresh dates; and if it was winter, he would not pray until we brought him dried dates and water.\""],[3847,"When Suhayl b. ʿAmr came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: Will you not stop until I send you a man who will strike your necks over the religion? Some of them said: Am I he, O Messenger of God? He said: \"No.\" Another said: Am I he? He said: \"No, but he is the mender of the sandal.\" And ʿAlī was mending the sandal."],[3848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ assigned to ʿUthmān a share of the spoils of Badr, though he did not witness Badr."],[3849,"The Prophet ﷺ heard something, so he delivered a sermon and said to the Anṣār: \"Were you not lowly and God exalted you through me? Were you not astray and God guided you through me? Were you not fearful and God gave you security through me? Will you not respond to me?\" They said: \"What thing shall we answer you?\" He said: \"You say: Did your people not expel you and we sheltered you? Did your people not call you a liar and we believed you?\" He enumerated things for them. He said: \"They fell on their knees,\" and said: \"Our wealth and our lives are yours.\" Then it was revealed: \"Say: I ask of you no reward for it, save love of kinship.\""],[3850,"No one keeps up the ḍuḥā prayer except one who is oft-returning [to God]."],[3851,"God, Mighty and Majestic, made this land sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and He fashioned it when He fashioned the sun and the moon, and what lies before it from the sky is sacred. It was not lawful for anyone before me, and it was made lawful for me for an hour of a day, then it returned as it was. It was said to him: \"This is Khālid b. al-Walīd killing.\" He said to him: \"Arise, O so-and-so, go to Khālid b. al-Walīd and tell him to lift his hand from killing.\" So the man went to him and said to him: \"The Prophet ﷺ says: 'Kill whom you have power over.'\" So he killed seventy persons. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He sent to Khālid b. al-Walīd: \"Did I not forbid you from killing?\" He said: \"So-and-so came to me and commanded me to kill whom I had power over.\" So he sent to him: \"Did I not command you to command Khālid not to kill anyone?\" He said: \"You intended a matter, and God intended a matter, and God's matter was above your matter, and I could only do what was.\" So the Prophet of God ﷺ fell silent and did not respond to him at all."],[3852,"The Messenger of God ﷺ burned some of the property of Banū al-Naḍīr."],[3853,"Charity to the poor is charity, and to a relative it is charity and maintaining ties."],[3854,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us, when we were with him, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights, except due to major ritual impurity, but [we may] due to defecation, urination, and sleep."],[3855,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Nakhl, and he led us in the noon prayer. The polytheists thought to attack them, but they said: \"Leave them, for they have after this a prayer that is dearer to them than their children.\" Then Gabriel ﷺ descended and informed him, so the Messenger of God ﷺ led his companions in the afternoon prayer."],[3856,"Whoever reaches Ramadan and does not fast it has become wretched, and whoever reaches his parents or one of them and does not honor them has become wretched, and whoever I am mentioned before and does not invoke blessings upon me has become wretched."],[3857,"The honor of a letter is its seal."],[3858,"We were with ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar, and they mentioned the pilgrims of the people of Yemen and what they do during it. Some of the people reviled them. Ibn ʿUmar said: \"Do not revile the people of Yemen, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The ornament of the pilgrims is the people of Yemen.'\""],[3859,"Gabriel came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was at Tabūk and said: \"O Muhammad, attend the funeral of Muʿāwiya b. Muʿāwiya al-Muzanī.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ went out, and Gabriel descended with seventy thousand angels. He placed his right wing upon the mountains and they were humbled, and he placed his left wing upon the lands and they were humbled, until he looked upon Makkah and Madinah. The Messenger of God ﷺ, Gabriel, and the angels prayed over him. When he finished, he said: \"O Gabriel, by what did Muʿāwiya b. Muʿāwiya al-Muzanī attain this rank?\" He said: \"By reciting 'Say: He is God, One' while standing, sitting, walking, and riding.\""],[3860,"I was a boy during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Let us go to a person whose affair we have seen.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ set out walking with his Companions, until they entered two gardens in a long alley, and they came to a small door at the far end of the alley. They entered a house, and saw no one in the house except a woman sitting. There was a huge waterskin full of water. They said, \"We see a waterskin but do not see its carrier.\" They spoke to the woman, and she pointed to a velvet cloth in a corner of the house and said, \"Look what is under the velvet cloth.\" They uncovered it, and under it there was a person. He raised his head, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Ugly is the face!\" He said, \"O Muhammad, why do you speak obscenely to me?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"I have hidden something for you, so tell me what it is.\" And he said to his Companions, \"I have hidden for him Surah al-Dukhan.\" He said, \"Surah al-Dukhan?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Be gone! What God wills happens.\" Then he left."],[3861,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not leave behind a sheep, nor a camel, nor a dinar, nor a dirham, and he did not bequeath anything."],[3862,"The people sighted the new moon, and I informed the Messenger of God ﷺ that I had seen it. So the Messenger of God ﷺ fasted and ordered the people to fast."],[3863,"The night prayer is in pairs, and the salutation (is the ending)."],[3864,"Gabriel brought the Buraq to the Prophet ﷺ and placed it before him, and it carried him along. When it reached a low-lying place, its front legs lengthened and its hind legs shortened so that it became level with him; and when it reached an elevated place, its front legs shortened and its hind legs lengthened so that it became level. Then a man appeared to him on the right side of the road, and he called out to him: \"O Muhammad, to the road!\" twice. Gabriel said, \"Go on and do not speak to anyone.\" Then a man appeared to him on the left side of the road alone, and he said to him, \"To the road, O Muhammad,\" twice. Gabriel said to him, \"Go on and do not speak to anyone.\" Then a beautiful, gorgeous woman appeared to him, and Gabriel said to him, \"Do you know who the man on the right side of the road is?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"No.\" He said, \"That is the Jews; they called you to their religion.\" Then he said, \"Do you know who the man who called you on the left side of the road is?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"That is the Christians; they called you to their religion. Do you know who the beautiful, gorgeous woman is?\" He said, \"That is the world; she calls you to herself.\" Then we went on until we came to Jerusalem, and there was a group of people sitting. When they saw him, they said, \"Welcome to Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet.\" Among the sitting group there was an old man. Muhammad ﷺ said, \"Who is this?\" He said, \"This is your father Abraham.\" Then he asked, \"Who is this?\" He said, \"Moses.\" Then he asked, \"Who is this?\" He said, \"This is Jesus, son of Mary.\" Then the prayer was established, and they pushed one another until they put Muhammad ﷺ forward. Then they brought drinks, and Muhammad chose milk. Gabriel said to him, \"You have chosen the natural disposition.\" Then it was said to him, \"Arise with me to your Lord.\" He arose and entered, then came back, and he said to him, \"What did you do?\" He said, \"Fifty prayers were prescribed upon my community.\" Moses said to him, \"Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten it for your community, for you cannot bear this.\" He returned, then came back, and Moses said to him, \"What did you do?\" He said, \"He reduced it to twenty-five prayers.\" Moses said to him, \"Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten it for your community, for your community cannot bear this.\" He returned, then came back until he reduced it to five. Moses said to him, \"Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten it for your community.\" He said, \"I am too shy of my Lord to go back to Him again. He has said to me: For every return you made, you have a request that I will grant you.\""],[3865,"Woe to the rulers, woe to the trustees, woe to the overseers! One of them will surely experience a day when he wishes he were suspended from a star forever and that he had never been put in authority over even two people."],[3866,"Aisha wanted to buy Barira and set her free, but her masters said, \"No, unless you make the wala' (patronage) ours.\" She mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"Buy her, for the wala' belongs to the one who frees.\" So she bought her and set her free. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and said, \"What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of God? Indeed, whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of God, it is invalid.\" He said: She was married to a slave of Banu al-Mughirah called Mughith, and the Messenger of God ﷺ gave her the choice. He said: And Ibn Abbas narrated that Abu Bakr narrated that the Messenger of God ﷺ imposed upon her the waiting period of a free woman."],[3867,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by an idol made of brass and struck its back with the back of his hand, then said, \"Lost and disappointed is the one who worshipped you instead of God.\" Then Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ, and with him was an angel. The angel withdrew, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with him that he withdrew?\" He said, \"He detected from you the smell of brass, and we cannot tolerate the smell of brass.\""],[3868,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set out on the expedition of Hunayn on the eighteenth of Ramadan, while he was fasting. They passed by a river and stared at it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them, \"Will you drink?\" They said, \"Shall we drink while you are fasting?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ called for a vessel and drank. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the expedition of Hunayn and al-Ta'if, he came to al-Ji'ranah and distributed the spoils there, and performed 'umrah from there."],[3869,"When he recited while sitting and an ayah remained, he would stand up, recite it, and then bow."],[3870,"If there are two caliphs on the earth, kill one of them."],[3871,"The Messenger of God ﷺ marked the grave of Uthman b. Maz'un with a rock."],[3872,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught him this supplication in the witr: “O God, guide me among those You have guided, bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, for You decree and none decrees over You. No one whom You befriend is humbled. Blessed and exalted are You, our Lord.”"],[3873,"The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, while the believer eats in one intestine."],[3874,"Regarding “Those who are too proud to worship Me,” he said: “—meaning My supplication—they will enter Hell abased.”"],[3875,"He forbade killing the jinn that live in houses."],[3876,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “Are you not pleased, O ʿAlī, that when the prophets are gathered on one plain, naked, barefoot, on foot, their necks cut off by thirst, the first to be called will be Ibrāhīm, and he will be clothed with two white garments, then he will stand at the right of the Throne. Then a stream from Paradise will burst forth to my basin, and my basin is wider than the distance between Buṣrā and Ṣanʿāʾ. In it there are as many silver drinking cups as the stars of the sky. Then I will be called and will drink and perform ablution, then be clothed with two white garments, then stand at the right of the Throne. Then you will be called and you will drink and perform ablution and be clothed with two white garments, and will stand with me. And I will not be called to any good but you will be called to it.”"],[3877,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen, and I said: “O Messenger of God, I am a young man, and I do not know how to judge.” The Messenger of God ﷺ placed his hand between my shoulders and said: “God will guide your heart and make your tongue steadfast.” ʿAlī said: “I did not fail in judging between any two people until I sat in this seat of mine.”"],[3878,"The night prayer is in pairs, and when you fear the approach of dawn, perform one rakʿah as witr."],[3879,"Hospitality is for three days; whatever is beyond that is charity."],[3880,"Any man who gives his son a gift and the son takes possession of it, then the father becomes needy, the son is more entitled to it. If the son has not taken possession of it and the father becomes needy, the father is more entitled to it."],[3881,"A woman may not give charity from her husband's house except with his permission."],[3882,"Whatever a man spends on himself to remain chaste is charity, and whatever he spends on his wife, children, and household is charity."],[3883,"The example of one who takes back his gift is like a dog that eats until it is full, then vomits, then returns to it and eats it."],[3884,"He used to pray the two rakʿahs after ʿaṣr, and he forbade them."],[3885,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb recited this verse: “Today I have perfected for you your religion,” while Kaʿb was with him. Kaʿb said: “I know a people of a religion: had it been sent down upon them on a day, they would have taken it as a festival.” ʿUmar said: “It was sent down on the evening of ʿArafah, on a Friday.”"],[3886,"Jibrīl descended upon the Prophet ﷺ at the very beginning of revelation and taught him ablution. When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he took some water in his hand and sprinkled his private parts with it."],[3887,"Jibrīl came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Muḥammad, commend Muʿāwiyah to my care, for he is trustworthy over the Book of Allah, and what an excellent trustee he is.”"],[3888,"He used to recite Yā Sīn in the dawn prayer."],[3889,"He used to recite in the noon and afternoon prayers: “By the sky and the night-comer,” and “By the sky with its constellations.”"],[3890,"At the end of time there will be a tribulation in which people will be sifted as gold is sifted in the mine. Do not revile the people of Syria, but revile their wicked ones, for among them are the abdāl. A cause from heaven is about to be sent against the people of Syria and scatter their assembly, until even foxes, were they to fight them, would defeat them. Then a man from my household will come out with three banners. The one who exaggerates says they are fifteen thousand; the one who undercounts says they are twelve thousand. Their watchword is “amit, amit.” They will meet seven banners, under each of which a man seeks kingship, and Allah will slay them all. Allah will restore to the Muslims their affection, their blessing, their distant ones and their near ones."],[3891,"A delegation of the Christians of Najrān came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: sixty riders, among them twenty-four of their nobles. Of those twenty-four, three were the ones to whom their affairs reverted: al-ʿĀqib, the trustee of the people and man of judgment, holder of their counsel, without whose opinion and command they acted not—his name was ʿAbd al-Masīḥ; al-Sayyid, their scholar, keeper of their baggage and gathering place; and Abū Ḥārithah b. ʿAlqamah, brother of Bakr b. Wāʾil, their bishop, learned man, imam, and keeper of their places of worship. Abū Ḥārithah had been honored among them until his knowledge of their religion was esteemed. The kings of Byzantium, being Christians, had honored him, accepted him, built churches for him, and lavished honors upon him because of what reached them of his striving in their religion. When they set out from Najrān toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Ḥārithah sat on his mule, heading toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with a brother of his called Kurz b. ʿAlqamah riding at his side. When Abū Ḥārithah’s mule stumbled, Kurz said: “May the far one perish,” meaning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Rather you have perished.” He said: “And why, brother?” He said: “By Allah, he is the Prophet we have been awaiting.” Kurz said to him: “What prevents you, since you know this?” He said: “What these people have done for us: they honored us, put us in command, and showed us generosity, yet they refused anything but opposition to him. If I did otherwise, they would strip from us everything you see.” His brother Kurz b. ʿAlqamah concealed this about him."],[3892,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."],[3893,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is more excellent than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."],[3894,"I heard ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit of Kufa saying: “O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Beware of the clothing of monks, for whoever becomes a monk or imitates them is not of me.”"],[3895,"We were such that no one was more entitled to one’s preference than one’s brother."],[3896,"A man's spending on his family is charity."],[3897,"The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam; in it is food that nourishes and a cure for illness. By Allah, there is no water on the face of the earth worse than the water of a well in the valley of Barhut; it is like the legs of locusts from the vermin, flowing in the morning and dry by evening, with no moisture in it."],[3898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prohibit breastfeeding except after ten sucklings, or a few more than ten."],[3899,"When Allah wills to lead a servant astray, He blinds him to stratagems."],[3900,"A man came to Ibn ʿUmar and said: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ speak about intimate conversation? Ibn ʿUmar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will bring a servant near to Him and place over him His protection and concealment from people, and will make him acknowledge his sins. He will say: Do you acknowledge such-and-such sin? He will say: Yes, my Lord. And He will say: Do you acknowledge such-and-such sin? He will say: Yes, my Lord. When He has made him acknowledge his sins and he sees that he is ruined, He will say: I concealed them for you in the world, and I forgive them for you today. Then he will be given the book of his good deeds. As for the hypocrite and the disbeliever, it will be called out before the witnesses: These are the ones who lied against their Lord."],[3901,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about palm trees, and he said: They are the firmly rooted in the mire, and the nourishers in time of drought."],[3902,"I was in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a circle that included Abu Saʿid al-Khudri and ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr. Al-Husayn b. ʿAli passed by and greeted; the people returned his greeting, but ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr remained silent. Then Ibn ʿAmr raised his voice after the people fell silent and said: And upon you be peace, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Then he turned to the people and said: Shall I not tell you who is the most beloved of the people of the earth to the people of heaven? They said: Yes. He said: It is this one who has just departed. By Allah, I have not spoken a word to him, nor has he spoken a word to me since the nights of Siffin. By Allah, for him to be pleased with me is more beloved to me than to have the like of Uhud. Abu Saʿid al-Khudri said to him: Will you not go to him in the morning? He said: Yes. So they agreed to go to him in the morning, and I went with them. Abu Saʿid asked permission and was admitted, so we entered. Then he asked permission for Ibn ʿAmr, and he kept at it until al-Husayn granted him permission, and he entered. When Abu Saʿid saw him, he moved over for him, as he was sitting next to al-Husayn, and al-Husayn pulled him toward himself. Ibn ʿAmr stood and did not sit. When he saw that, he let go of Abu Saʿid, moved over for him, and he sat between them. Abu Saʿid related the story, and he said: Is it so, O Ibn ʿAmr? Do you know that I am the most beloved of the people of the earth to the people of heaven? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah, you are the most beloved of the people of the earth to the people of heaven. He said: Then what made you fight me and my father on the day of Siffin? By Allah, my father is better than me. He said: Yes, but ʿAmr complained about me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: ʿAbd Allah stands at night and fasts during the day. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Pray and sleep, fast and break your fast, and obey ʿAmr. When the day of Siffin came, he made me swear an oath. By Allah, I did not increase their numbers, nor draw a sword for them, nor thrust with a spear, nor shoot an arrow. Al-Husayn said to him: Do you not know that there is no obedience to a creature in disobedience to the Creator? He said: Yes. He said: And so it was as if he accepted it from him."],[3903,"Does not the one who raises his head while the imam is prostrating fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey?"],[3904,"Wear white garments, for they are purer and more pleasant, and shroud your dead in them."],[3905,"I entered upon ʿAli in his house and said: O best of people after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Gently, woe to you, O Abu Juhayfah. Shall I not tell you who is the best of people after the Messenger of Allah? Abu Bakr and ʿUmar. Woe to you, O Abu Juhayfah, love for me and hatred for Abu Bakr and ʿUmar do not come together in the heart of a believer."],[3906,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."],[3907,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade hosting one of the two litigants without the other."],[3908,"When it is Friday, increase your blessings upon me, for your blessings are shown to me. And ask for the wasila for me.” They said, “O Messenger of God, what is the wasila?” He said, “The highest degree with me in Paradise.”"],[3909,"I heard Mu'awiya in Makkah on the day of 'Ashura saying: “The Messenger of God ﷺ fasted it, so whoever among you has not fasted it, let him fast it.”"],[3910,"That some goods of hers were stolen, and the Messenger of God ﷺ heard her supplicating, so he said: “Do not lighten [the sin] on his behalf.”"],[3911,"There is no marriage without a guardian, and if they dispute, then the sultan is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."],[3912,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed in Tabuk twenty nights shortening the prayer."],[3913,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure is one fifth."],[3914,"That he heard a man saying: “Here is greenery (Khadira).” So he said: “O Labbayk, we have taken your omen from your mouth. Take us out to greenery.” So they went out to it, and no sword was drawn in it."],[3915,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the closing of the doors except the door of 'Ali. They said: “O Messenger of God, you have closed all the doors except the door of 'Ali?” He said: “I did not close your doors, but God closed them.”"],[3916,"My two ears heard, and my heart comprehended, the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: “Whoever claims descent from other than his father while he knows his father, God has forbidden Paradise to him.”"],[3917,"Go out and call among the people: “From God, not from His Messenger: May God curse the one who cuts down the lote-tree.”"],[3918,"Whoever keeps hair, let him treat it well or shave it."],[3919,"That 'Ali came on the day of Basra with gold or silver, and he struck it and said: “Be white and be yellow, and deceive other than me. Deceive the people of Syria tomorrow when they prevail over you.” His saying that distressed the people, and that was mentioned to him, so he called the people to prayer, and they entered upon him. Then he said: “My close friend ﷺ said: 'O 'Ali, you will come to God with your Shi'a pleased and well-pleasing, and your enemy will come to Him angry and with heads raised in punishment.'” Then 'Ali brought his hand to his neck, showing them how the raising of the head in punishment is."],[3920,"When one of you rises to pray, let him give it his full attention until he finishes from it, and beware of turning around during the prayer, for one of you is in intimate conversation with his Lord as long as he is in prayer."],[3921,"No one who commits incest with a mahram will enter Paradise."],[3922,"Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, spoke privately with Musa in one hundred and forty thousand words over three days, all of them counsels. When Musa heard the speech of human beings, he despised them because of what had entered his ears from the speech of the Lord. Among what He privately said to him was: 'O Musa, those who put on airs for Me do not do so with anything like renunciation of the world, and those who seek nearness to Me do not draw near with anything like piety from what I have forbidden them, and the worshippers do not worship Me with anything like weeping out of fear of Me.' Musa said: 'O God of all creation, O Master of the Day of Judgment, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, what have You prepared for them? What have You rewarded them?' He said: 'O Musa, as for those who renounce the world, I grant them My Paradise; they will settle wherever they wish. As for those who are pious from what I have forbidden them, there is no servant who meets Me on the Day of Resurrection except that I scrutinize his account and question him about what was in his hands, except the pious ones. I am shy of them and honor them, so I enter them into Paradise without reckoning. As for those who weep from fear of Me, they have the highest company; they will not be shared in it.'"],[3923,"This religion will remain sound; whoever opposes it or fights against it will not harm it, until twelve rulers rule, all of them from Quraysh."],[3924,"When Rajab entered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: 'O Allah, bless us in Rajab and Sha'ban, and let us reach Ramadan.'"],[3925,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the house of Umm Salamah, and found men with him. I sat until they left. When he came out, I drew near to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, a matter that brings me close to Allah—I would like to ask you about it, since I have doubts about it.' He said: 'You have done well, O Umm Sulaym.' I said: 'Should a woman perform ghusl if she sees in her dream what a man sees?' Umm Salamah said: 'May your hands be dusty, O Umm Sulaym! You have exposed women.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Rather, may your hands be dusty, O Umm Salamah! Do you not see that were it not for that, the child would not resemble his father? Yes, if you see that, then perform ghusl.'"],[3926,"I was helped by the east wind, and ʿĀd was destroyed by the west wind."],[3927,"No one hoards but a sinner."],[3928,"—and I had vowed to bury him with the duff if he returned from Makkah. While I was like that, Umar sought permission to enter, so I went with the duff to the side of the room and covered it with a blanket, and I said: 'O Prophet of Allah, you are more deserving of being held in awe.' He said: 'The devil has not met Umar since he embraced Islam except that he fell on his face.'"],[3929,"An ʿUmrah in Ramadan is equal to a Hajj."],[3930,"What is one of you waiting for except wealth that leads to tyranny, or poverty that causes forgetfulness, or a sickness that corrupts, or old age that senilizes, or a death that comes suddenly, or the Dajjal, and the Dajjal is the worst absent thing awaited, or the Hour, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter."],[3931,"Whoever is killed under a blind banner, calling to tribalism, and supports his own group, his killing is a killing of ignorance."],[3932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered into his prayer and we said the takbir with him. He gestured to the people to stay as they were. We remained standing until the Prophet of Allah ﷺ came to us having performed ghusl, with his head dripping water."],[3933,"The walimah is a right and a sunnah. Whoever is invited and does not respond has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. As for the khurs, the i'dhar, and the tawkir, you have the choice in them.\" He said: I said: \"By Allah, I do not know what the khurs, the i'dhar, and the tawkir are.\" He said: \"The khurs is the birth, the i'dhar is the circumcision, and the tawkir is when a man builds a house, settles among a people, prepares food, and invites them. They have the choice: if they wish, they respond, and if they wish, they stay away."],[3934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted Abu Bakr and Umar, and they gave him their opinions, and Abu Bakr was right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Umar, Allah hates that Abu Bakr should err.\""],[3935,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on a donkey while going to Khaybar, praying with the qiblah behind him."],[3936,"Three things my beloved ﷺ enjoined upon me: two prostrations before the morning prayer, the two prostrations of the forenoon, and the witr after the evening prayer."],[3937,"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful."],[3938,"One of you says to his wife: \"I have divorced you, I have taken you back.\" This is not the divorce of Muslims. Divorce the woman in the beginning of her purity."],[3939,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful."],[3940,"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs of the forenoon, a house will be built for him in Paradise."],[3941,"Whoever among you swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do that which is better and expiate for his oath."],[3942,"She was given as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with her were her dolls."],[3943,"The people of innovation are the worst of creation and creatures."],[3944,"He used to pray four (rakʿahs) before Jumuʿah and four after it."],[3945,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: The excellence of knowledge is better than the excellence of worship, and the best of your religion is piety (waraʿ)."],[3946,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us with his face reddened, while we were disputing about a verse of the Qur’an. He said: “What is this that you were engaged in?” We said: “A verse of the Qur’an about which we were disputing.” He said: “Do not dispute about the Qur’an, for disputing about the Qur’an is disbelief.”"],[3947,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the lizard (ḍabb). He said: “I do not eat it, and I do not forbid it.”"],[3948,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the time of ʿIshā’. He said: “When the night fills the belly of every valley.”"],[3949,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, the hyena has devoured us (i.e., our livestock).” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Other than that I fear more for you: when worldly wealth is poured upon you abundantly. Would that my community not wear gold.”"],[3950,"“O Messenger of God, ‘those who give what they give while their hearts are fearful’ (Qur’an 23:60) — are they the ones who commit sins and acts of disobedience?” He said: “No, O ʿĀ’ishah. They are those who pray and give charity, while their hearts are fearful.”"],[3951,"Woman was created from a rib. Her likeness is like the rib: if you try to straighten it, it breaks; and if you leave it, it remains crooked."],[3952,"He is not of us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, and calls with the call of the Age of Ignorance (Jāhiliyyah)."],[3953,"He used to come to a tree between Makkah and Madinah, then sit beneath it, and he claimed that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to come to it."],[3954,"A man came to Ibn ʿUmar and asked him about nabīdh made in earthen jars. He said: “That is among what God and His Messenger have forbidden.” Then he came to Ibn ʿAbbās and informed him of what Ibn ʿUmar said, and Ibn ʿAbbās said: “Ibn ʿUmar spoke the truth.”"],[3955,"God surely raises a servant, through good character, to the degree of one who fasts and prays (constantly)."],[3956,"The angels submitted willingly, and the Anṣār submitted willingly, and ʿAbd al-Qays submitted willingly."],[3957,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of every month, performing the witr before sleeping, and the two rakʿahs of ḍuḥā."],[3958,"Abū Ṭālib fell ill and the Prophet ﷺ visited him. He said to him, “O son of my brother, supplicate your God whom you worship to heal me.” He said, “O Allah, cure my uncle.” Then Abū Ṭālib got up as if he had been released from a bond. He said to him, “O son of my brother, your God whom you worship indeed obeys you.” He said, “And you, O uncle, if you obey Allah, He will indeed obey you.”"],[3959,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a ṣāʿ."],[3960,"Abū Ṭalḥah ordered two mudds of barley to be prepared, then sent me to invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I went to him and invited him. He said to those with him, “Get up.” I walked in front of him until I entered upon Abū Ṭalḥah. He said, “What have you done?” I said, “I invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to the people, ‘Get up.’” Abū Ṭalḥah said, “You have embarrassed us before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Did you not know what we have?” I said, “Yes, but I could not say anything to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the door, he entered with ten people, and he spoke as Allah willed. Then he said, “Eat.” When they were full, they left, and ten more entered, until eighty men ate from it, and there remained enough to satisfy the household."],[3961,"Bring out of the Fire whoever has in his heart the weight of a barley grain of faith. Then He will say: Bring out of the Fire whoever has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith. Then He will say: By My might, I will not make the one who believed in Me for an hour of night or day like the one who did not believe in Me."],[3962,"When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces."],[3963,"When the Muslims were routed on the day of Ḥunayn, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on his gray mule, whose name was Duldul, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “Duldul, press down,” and she pressed her belly to the ground until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a handful of dust and threw it in their faces, and said, “Ḥā Mīm, they will not be helped.” Then the people were routed, and we did not shoot them with an arrow, nor stab with a spear, nor strike with a sword."],[3964,"When you come to Friday prayer, then perform the ritual bath."],[3965,"Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform the ritual bath."],[3966,"A neck will emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, having a sharp tongue, and it will call out: I have been charged today with three: with every obstinate tyrant, with whoever set up another god besides Allah, and with whoever killed a soul without a soul."],[3967,"Whoever says when he reaches the morning: “Glory be to Allah and with His praise” a thousand times, he has purchased himself from Allah, and at the end of his day he will be a freedman of Allah."],[3968,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some children and greeted them."],[3969,"I will tell you about people's affairs and their characters: A man who is quick to anger and quick to relent — there is nothing against him nor for him; it is a standoff. A man who is slow to anger and quick to be pleased — that is for him and not against him. A man who is quick to anger and slow to be pleased — that is against him and not for him. A man who fulfills what is for him and fulfills what is against him — that is neither against him nor for him, a standoff. A man who fulfills what is against him and does not fulfill what is for him — that is for him and not against him. A man who fulfills what is for him and withholds from people what is for them — that is against him and not for him."],[3970,"Two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and each of them came with upright witnesses of equal number, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew lots between them and said: ‘O Allah, decide between them.’"],[3971,"We descended with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Among us were those who said takbir and among us were those who said tahlil, and our takbir-sayers did not fault our tahlil-sayers, nor did our tahlil-sayers fault our takbir-sayers."],[3972,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying, and al-Hasan and al-Husayn — or one of them — came and climbed onto his back. When he prostrated, he raised his head and said with his hand, so he held him — or held them — then said: ‘What an excellent mount your mount is.’"],[3973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at al-Aswaf with Bilal beside him, and he let his legs dangle into the well and uncovered his thighs. Abu Bakr came seeking permission, so he said: ‘O Bilal, give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.’ Abu Bakr entered and sat to the right of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let his legs dangle into the well, and uncovered his thighs. Then Umar came seeking permission, and he said: ‘Give him permission, O Bilal, and give him glad tidings of Paradise.’ He entered and sat to the left of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let his legs dangle into the well, and uncovered his thighs. Then Uthman came seeking permission, and he said: ‘Give him permission, O Bilal, and give him glad tidings of Paradise, along with a trial that will befall him.’ Uthman entered and sat facing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let his legs dangle into the well, and uncovered his thighs."],[3974,"He used to say the talbiyah: ‘Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni‘mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak.’"],[3975,"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."],[3976,"We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he raised his head from bowing, none of us would bend his back until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his forehead on the ground."],[3977,"Whoever touches his private part and his testicles should perform the ablution he performs for prayer."],[3978,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade meeting caravans before they reached the market. Whoever meets one and buys from it, its owner has more right to it when he arrives."],[3979,"Abu Sufyan passed by with Mu‘awiyah behind him, and he was a man of tall stature, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘O Allah, deal with the owner of the spearheads.’"],[3980,"He was asked about monkeys and pigs, and he said: Indeed, Allah did not become angry with a people and then give them offspring or posterity."],[3981,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced to us his own death, with my father as his ransom, a month before he died. When the parting drew near, he gathered us to him in the house of our mother ʿĀʾishah, then he looked at us, his eyes welled with tears, and he spoke firmly. He said: Welcome to you, may Allah keep you alive, have mercy on you, shelter you, help you, raise you, benefit you, guide you, provide for you, grant you success, keep you safe, and accept you. I enjoin upon you the fear of Allah, and I entrust you to Allah, and I appoint Him as successor over you. Indeed, I am to you a clear warner from Him. Do not exalt yourselves above Allah regarding His servants and His lands, for Allah said to me and to you: 'That is the abode of the Hereafter, which We assign to those who do not desire exaltation in the earth nor corruption, and the outcome is for the righteous.' And He said: 'Is there not in Hell a dwelling for the arrogant?' Then he said: 'The appointed time has drawn near, and the return is to Allah, to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, to the Garden of Refuge, to the highest companion, to the fullest cup, and to the good fortune and pleasant life.' We said: Who will wash you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: 'The men of my household, the nearest then the next nearest.' We said: How should we shroud you? He said: 'In these clothes of mine, if you wish, or in a Yemeni robe, or in white Egyptian cloth.' We said: Who among us will pray over you? Then we wept and he wept. Then he said: 'Gently, may Allah forgive you and reward you well on behalf of your Prophet. When you have washed me and shrouded me, place me on my bier in this house of mine at the edge of my grave. Then leave me for a while, for the first to pray over me will be my companion and close friend Jibrīl, then Mīkāʾīl, then Isrāfīl, then the Angel of Death with his hosts. Then enter to me in groups, pray over me and greet me with peace, and do not harm me with a wailing woman, nor with clamor, nor with lamentation. Let the men of my household and their women begin the prayer over me, then you. Convey abundant greetings from me to those of my companions who are absent, for I have indeed greeted those who pledged allegiance to me upon my religion until the Day of Resurrection.' We said: Who will place you in your grave? He said: 'My family along with many angels, who see you from where you do not see them.'"],[3982,"The sick person prays standing; if he experiences hardship, he prays sitting; if he experiences hardship, he prays lying down, gesturing with his head; if he experiences hardship, he glorifies Allah."],[3983,"I entered upon ʿĀʾishah, while I was then a slave, before I was freed, and said to her: O Mother of the Believers, at which hour did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray most often? She said: From the sun's decline until it tips."],[3984,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Fāṭimah approached. She stood facing the Prophet ﷺ, opposite him. He said: 'Come closer, O Fāṭimah,' so she came a little closer. Then he said: 'Come closer, O Fāṭimah,' so she came a little closer. Then he said: 'Come closer, O Fāṭimah,' so she came until she stood before him. ʿImrān said: I saw a pallor appear on her face, and the blood drained away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spread his fingers, then placed his palm between her collarbones, raised his head, and said: 'O Allah, Satisfier of hunger, Fulfiller of need, Raiser of the lowly, do not let Fāṭimah, daughter of Muḥammad, go hungry.' Then I saw the pallor of hunger leave her face and the blood return. Later I asked her about it, and she said: 'I was not hungry after that, O ʿImrān.'"],[3985,"She set out for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she menstruated. She did not become pure until she reached Minā and ʿArafāt, and she completed the rites of Hajj. Then she circumambulated the Kaʿbah and went between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her brother: 'Take her out of the Sacred Precinct and let her perform ʿUmrah,' so he had her perform ʿUmrah from al-Tanʿīm."],[3986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who tattoos and the one who is tattooed, the woman who extends hair and the one for whom it is extended, the one who makes a woman lawful and the one for whom she is made lawful, the consumer of ribā, and the one who feeds it."],[3987,"O people, whoever hates us, the People of the House, Allah will gather him on the Day of Resurrection as a Jew. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he fasts and prays? He said: 'Even if he fasts and prays, and claims that he is a Muslim. O people, by that he has protected himself from having his blood shed and from paying the jizyah from his hand while he is humbled. My nation was shown to me in clay, and the bearers of banners passed by me, so I sought forgiveness for ʿAlī and his followers.'"],[3988,"A woman passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing a bow over her shoulder. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'May Allah curse the women who imitate men, and the men who imitate women.'"],[3989,"We were men in Madinah who bought loads in the market of Madinah. We named ourselves, and the people called us al-samāsirah (brokers). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called us by something better than what we called ourselves, and said: 'O assembly of merchants, indeed buying and selling is attended by idle talk and oaths, so mix it with something of charity.'"],[3990,"The best of you are those with the best character, and good character is part of faith."],[3991,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a concession to Sahlah bt. Suhayl regarding suckling specifically, and Umm Salamah did not act upon it."],[3992,"I saw ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUmar while he was kneading in prayer, supporting himself on his hands when he stood. I said, “What is this, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kneading in prayer.”"],[3993,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb wrote to Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ: “I want to divide the black land of Kufa among the Muslims who conquered it.” Saʿd wrote back to him: “O Commander of the Faithful, we have conquered a people whom Allah created with the softest hearts, the most generous souls, the greatest blessing, and the most open-handed. Their hands are food and their tongues are peace. If you see fit, O Commander of the Faithful, not to disperse them or divide them, and not to turn us away from the direction through which Allah granted us victory, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: ‘The might of the Arabs is in the points of their spears and the hooves of their horses.’”"],[3994,"All lands will vanish on the Day of Resurrection except the mosques, for they will join together with one another."],[3995,"Today is the betting, tomorrow the race, and the goal is Paradise. The perished one is he who enters the Fire. I am the first, Abū Bakr is the second, ʿUmar is the third, and the people after us are according to their precedence, the first then the first."],[3996,"The sunnah is of two kinds: a sunnah within an obligatory act, and a sunnah outside an obligatory act. The sunnah that is within an obligatory act has its basis in the Book of Allah. Adhering to it is guidance and abandoning it is misguidance. The sunnah that has no basis in the Book of Allah—adhering to it is a virtue and abandoning it is not a sin."],[3997,"Whoever does not perform the witr, there is no prayer for him."],[3998,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “O Yazīd b. Asad, do not do to people anything except what you would love to be done to you.”"],[3999,"When the strap of the Prophet’s ﷺ sandal broke, he would walk in one sandal while the other was in his hand until he found a strap and put it on."],[4000,"Whatever intoxicates in large quantities, a small quantity of it is forbidden."],[4001,"I walked behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to test whether he disliked that. He reached for me with his hand and brought me forward. Then I lagged behind to test whether he disliked that. He reached for me with his hand and brought me forward. Then I lagged behind to test him, and he reached for me with his hand and brought me forward. So I knew that he disliked that."],[4002,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is equivalent to a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."],[4003,"He used to teach them that when a woman enters upon her husband, the man should stand and she should stand behind him, and they should pray two rakʿahs, and he should say: “O Allah, bless me in my wife and bless my wife in me. O Allah, provide for them from me and provide for me from them. O Allah, join us together as long as You join us in goodness, and separate us if You separate us to goodness.”"],[4004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbīr over funerals seven times, five times, and four times, so say as many takbīrs as the imam says when you put him forward."],[4005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to his companions, “Come with us to Banū Wāqif to visit the blind man,” and he was blind."],[4006,"He forbade ḥantam jars and naqīr vessels."],[4007,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed with traces of mud on his sandals and a cloak on him, and he began protecting it so that the cloak would not be affected."],[4008,"He was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said, “Allah knows best what they would have done.”"],[4009,"We were with Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī in the mosque, and a man was turning over an arrow. Abū Saʿīd said, “Does this man not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade turning over weapons in the mosque and unsheathing them?”"],[4010,"The people of Yemen have come to you. They have the softest hearts. Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni. Indeed, tranquility and dignity are among the owners of sheep. Indeed, pride and arrogance are among the owners of horses and camels, and among the rough Bedouins who own camels."],[4011,"Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."],[4012,"Take your shields, take your shields. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, against an enemy that has come?” He said, “No, but against the Fire. Say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great. For they will come on the Day of Resurrection as those that go before and those that lag behind, and they are the enduring good deeds.”"],[4013,"A man entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he brought him close and made his seat near. When he left, I said, “O Messenger of Allah, were you not complaining about this man?” He said, “Yes, but among the worst of people are those who are honored out of fear of their evil.”"],[4014,"I came to Ibn ʿUmar along with Umayya b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Khālid b. Asīd and said, “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, when did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform the witr?” He said, “In the last part of the night.”"],[4015,"Some people will come out from the direction of the east, intending to reach a man at the House, until when they are in a desert plain of the earth, the earth will swallow them. Then those who stayed behind from them will catch up with them and suffer what befell them.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what about someone who was forced to go out?” He said, “He will suffer what the people suffer, then Allah will resurrect every person according to his intention.”"],[4016,"Whoever asks you by Allah, give to him; whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge; whoever invites you, accept his invitation; and whoever gives you a gift, even a sheep's trotter, accept it."],[4017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, wiped over his leather socks, and prayed all the prayers with a single ablution. ʿUmar said to him, \"You have done something you did not use to do.\" He said, \"I did it deliberately, O ʿUmar.\""],[4018,"He forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[4019,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ giving a quarter as extra share at the start of an expedition and a third on his return in a military campaign."],[4020,"May Allah protect you from rulers who will come after me.\" He said, \"And who are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Whoever enters upon them and confirms their lies and helps them in their oppression is not of me, and he will not come to my Cistern. Know, O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that fasting is a shield and prayer is a proof. O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Samura, Allah Almighty has refused to admit to Paradise any flesh nourished by unlawful gain; the Fire is more fitting for it.\""],[4021,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the dawn prayer al-Wāqiʿa and similar surahs."],[4022,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the collection of charity, and a man would come with the amount of his wealth and his charity. I wept, and he said, \"O Abū Dharr, why do you weep?\" I said, \"The wealthy have gone with the reward.\" He said, \"How so?\" I said, \"They pray as we pray, they fast as we fast, and they find something to give in charity while we do not.\" He said, \"Rather, the wealthy are the lowest, except those who say with their wealth this way and that way, and few are they.\" I said, \"How, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"There is no owner of camels who does not pay their zakah in their abundance and hardship except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection in a wide, flat, barren land, trampling him with their hooves; every time the first of them passes, the last of them returns to him, until judgment is passed among the people.\" I said, \"And horses, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Horses are for three groups: whoever acquires them as a preparation for the cause of Allah, their hardship and ease will be for him; and by Allah, if they cut across wide open spaces and then climbed one or two high places and descended upon a green pasture, that would be for him. And whoever acquires them out of pride, they will be a burden on him on the Day of Resurrection.\" They said, \"And donkeys, O Prophet of Allah?\" He said, \"Allah has not revealed anything concerning them except this single unique verse: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.'\""],[4023,"A single vessel, about half a faraq in capacity, used to be placed for me and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He would begin before me, and then he and I would bathe together from it."],[4024,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the sun, and it was delayed for an hour of the day."],[4025,"Going out to the prayer ground on the two Eids is from the Sunnah."],[4026,"Reciting aloud in the two Eid prayers is from the Sunnah."],[4027,"I embraced Islam only after al-Māʾida was revealed, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping after I became Muslim."],[4028,"Ali sold a slave and separated a woman from her son. The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade him and revoked the sale."],[4029,"Envy almost overtook destiny, and need almost became disbelief."],[4030,"He used to recite on the pulpit: “Say, O disbelievers” and “Say: He is God, the One.”"],[4031,"The Magians of this community are those who deny the divine decree."],[4032,"He embraced Islam while he had eight wives. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded him to choose four of them."],[4033,"Women have no share in the middle of the road; let them walk along its edges and not take to its center."],[4034,"Ribāṭ for one day in the path of God is better than fasting a month and standing in prayer during it. Whoever dies as a murabit in the path of God will be protected from the trial of the grave, and his righteous deeds will continue to run for him until the Day of Resurrection."],[4035,"Every newborn is born upon the fiṭrah, until his parents make him a Jew or a Christian, just as you produce camels—do you find any among them with a slit ear until you slit it yourselves?"],[4036,"When the Khawārij separated from ʿAlī, he went out in pursuit of them, and we went out with him. We reached the army of the people, and they had a humming like the humming of bees from reciting the Qur’an. Among them were people with calloused foreheads and people wearing burnooses. When I saw them, doubt entered me about that. So I withdrew, planted my spear, dismounted from my horse, placed my shield, and spread my armor over it. I took hold of my horse’s rein and stood praying facing my spear, saying in my prayer: “O God, if fighting these people is obedience to You, then permit it; and if it is disobedience, then show me Your innocence.” He said: While I was like that, ʿAlī came forward on the mule of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he came alongside me, he said: “Seek refuge in God from doubt, O Jundub.” So I came hastening to him, and he dismounted and stood praying. Then a man came forward on a horse, galloping, and said: “O Commander of the Faithful.” He said: “What do you want?” He said: “Do you have any need concerning the people?” He said: “And what is that?” He said: “They have crossed the river and gone.” He said: “They have not crossed it.” I said: “Glory be to God.” Then another came, faster in running, and said: “O Commander of the Faithful.” He said: “What do you want?” He said: “Do you have any need concerning the people?” He said: “And what is that?” He said: “They have crossed the river and gone.” I said: “God is greater.” Then ʿAlī said: “They have not crossed it.” Then another came spurring his horse, and said: “O Commander of the Faithful.” He said: “What do you want?” He said: “Do you have any need concerning the people?” He said: “And what is that?” He said: “They have crossed the river.” Then ʿAlī said: “They have not crossed it, and they will not cross it. They will surely be killed before it—a covenant from God and His Messenger.” I said: “God is greater.” Then I stood, held the stirrup for him, and he mounted his horse. Then I returned to my armor, put it on, went back to my horse, mounted it, put my foot in the stirrup, and went out walking alongside him. He said to me: “O Jundub.” I said: “At your service, O Commander of the Faithful.” He said: “As for me, I will send a man to them with the muṣḥaf, calling them to the Book of their Lord and the Sunnah of their Prophet. He will not turn his face toward us until they shoot him with arrows. O Jundub, no ten of us will be killed and no ten of them will escape.” We came to the people while they were in their camp where they had been, not having moved. ʿAlī called out among his companions and arranged them in rows, then came to the row from one end to the other twice, saying: “Who will take this muṣḥaf, go with it to these people, call them to the Book of their Lord and the Sunnah of their Prophet, and he will be killed, and for him is Paradise?” No one answered him except a young man from Banū ʿĀmir b. Ṣaʿṣaʿa. When ʿAlī saw how young he was, he said to him: “Return to your place.” Then he called out a second time, and no one came out to him except that young man. Then he called out a third time, and no one came out to him except that young man. So ʿAlī said to him: “Take it.” He took the muṣḥaf, and ʿAlī said: “Indeed, you will be killed, and you will not turn your face toward us until they shoot you with arrows.” The young man went out walking with the muṣḥaf toward the people. When he drew near enough for them to hear, they stood up and began fighting before he could return. A man shot him with arrows, and he turned his face toward us and sat down. Then ʿAlī said: “Now attack the people.” Jundub said: “By this hand of mine, after the doubt that had entered me had passed, I killed eight before I prayed the noon prayer, and not ten of us were killed and not ten of them escaped, as he said.”"],[4037,"Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under God’s protection, and his reckoning is upon God."],[4038,"Supplication is not rejected between the iqāmah and the call to prayer."],[4039,"When three are on a journey, one of them should lead them in prayer."],[4040,"Indeed my ummah is a nation shown mercy; there is no punishment upon it. Its punishment is only in this world: earthquakes, tribulations, and killing."],[4041,"\"Whoever prays before sunrise and before sunset, and bears witness that there is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise.\" An old man from the people of Basra heard it and said: \"Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes,\" three times."],[4042,"Purify your courtyards, for the Jews do not purify their courtyards."],[4043,"The likeness of my ummah is only the likeness of rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."],[4044,"People on the Day of Resurrection are of four kinds, and deeds are of six: among them is one who is given ample provision in this world and ample provision in the Hereafter; among them is one who is given ample provision in this world but straitened in the Hereafter; among them is one who is straitened in this world and given ample provision in the Hereafter; and among them is one who is wretched in this world and the Hereafter. And the deeds are: two obligatory ones, a like for a like, tenfold, and seven hundredfold. The two obligatory ones: whoever dies without associating anything with Allah enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating something with Allah enters the Fire. As for the like for a like: one who intends a good deed, and one who does an evil deed. And the tenfold: one who does a good deed. And the seven hundredfold: spending in the cause of Allah."],[4045,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was lying crosswise in front of him."],[4046,"Indeed the black person, when he is hungry, steals; and when he is full, commits adultery. And they have two qualities: truthfulness in generosity and courage."],[4047,"No one should tell stories to the people except a ruler, one commanded, or an affected pretender."],[4048,"He was asked about a man who has a sacrificial animal offered voluntarily, and it becomes disabled before it reaches its destination. He said: \"He should slaughter it, then smear its sandal with its blood, then strike its side with it; and if he eats from it, he must make it up.\""],[4049,"He used to go out for the dawn prayer with his head dripping water, from intercourse without a wet dream, then he would fast that day."],[4050,"I went out one day with ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, and a Bedouin caught up with him and said to him: \"The saying of Allah: 'And those who hoard gold and silver and do not spend it in the cause of Allah' [Quran 9:34].\" Ibn ʿUmar said: \"Whoever hoards them and does not pay their zakat, then woe to him. This was only before the zakat was revealed. When it was revealed, Allah made it a purification for wealth.\" Then he turned and said: \"I would not care if I had gold the size of Uhud, whose amount I knew, and I paid zakat on it and worked with it in obedience to Allah.\""],[4051,"Ibn ʿUmar heard a man say: \"The miser is more excusable than the oppressor.\" Ibn ʿUmar said: \"You lie. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The miser will not enter Paradise.'\""],[4052,"Do not envy a wicked person for a blessing, for you do not know what he will face after his death. He has with Allah a killer that does not die."],[4053,"A man wounded another man and [the wounded man] wanted to exact retaliation, but the Prophet ﷺ prohibited retaliation from the wounder until the wounded man recovered."],[4054,"On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ: “Take charge of the throats of the people—may my father and mother be your ransom.” Saʿd would place his arrow in the center of his bow and say: “O Allah, Your arrow and in Your cause; O Allah, grant victory to Your Messenger.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, answer Saʿd when he calls upon You.”"],[4055,"Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever counts them will enter Paradise."],[4056,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he passed by al-ʿAbbās and said: “O uncle, bring your sons and follow me.” He went with six of his sons: al-Faḍl, ʿAbd Allāh, ʿUbayd Allāh, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Qutham, and Maʿbad. The Prophet ﷺ brought them into a house and covered them with a black cloak of his, striped with red, and said: “O Allah, these are the people of my house and my family, so shield them from the Fire as I have shielded them with this cloak.” He said: “No mud brick or door remained in the house but that it said ameen.”"],[4057,"The world is cursed, and what is in it is cursed, except a scholar or a student, the remembrance of Allah, and whatever is connected to it."],[4058,"Wretched is the servant of the dinar and the dirham, whose only concern is a dinar or a dirham that he obtains and takes."],[4059,"The stars are a safeguard for the inhabitants of the sky, and my Companions are a safeguard for my community."],[4060,"Learn the Qur’an and teach it to the people, learn the shares of inheritance and teach them to the people. Soon a time will come upon the people when two men will dispute over an inheritance share and not find anyone to judge between them."],[4061,"Help your children to be dutiful; whoever wishes can extract disobedience from his child."],[4062,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿĀʾishah: “O ʿĀʾishah, abandon acts of disobedience, for that is the best abandonment, and guard the prayers, for they are the most excellent form of righteousness.”"],[4063,"Fāṭimah bt. Qays was married to him, and he divorced her. She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “She has no right to maintenance.”"],[4064,"The chief of the martyrs on the Day of Resurrection will be Hamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, and a man who stood before a tyrannical ruler, forbade him and commanded him, and the ruler killed him."],[4065,"Indeed Allah averts calamity from a hundred households among his neighbors because of one righteous Muslim."],[4066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military expedition. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you are sending us when we have no provisions, no food, and no knowledge of the road.' He said, 'You will pass by a man with a handsome face who will feed you food, give you drink, and guide you to the road, and he is from the people of Paradise.' When the people stopped at my place, they began signaling to one another and looking at me. I said, 'What is the matter with you? You signal to one another and look at me.' They said, 'Rejoice at the glad tidings from Allah and His Messenger, for we recognize in you the description given by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They told me what he had said to them. So I fed them, gave them drink, provided them with provisions, and went out with them until I guided them to the road. Then I returned to my family, instructed them regarding my camels, and then went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, 'What do you call to?' He said, 'I call to the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fast of Ramadan.' I said, 'If we answer you to this, are we safe regarding our families, our blood, and our wealth?' He said, 'Yes.' So I became Muslim and returned to my people, informing them of my Islam. Many of them became Muslim at my hands. Then I emigrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. While I was with him one day, he said to me, 'O ʿAmr, would you like me to show you a sign of Paradise? He eats food, drinks drink, and walks in the markets.' I said, 'Yes, may my father be ransomed for you.' He said, 'This man and his people are a sign of Paradise,' and he pointed to ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib. Then he said to me, 'O ʿAmr, would you like me to show you a sign of the Fire? He eats food, drinks drink, and walks in the markets.' I said, 'Yes, may my father be ransomed for you.' He said, 'This man and his people are a sign of the Fire,' and he pointed to a man. When the strife occurred, I remembered the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I fled from the sign of the Fire to the sign of Paradise. And do you think the Umayyads will kill me after this? I said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'By Allah, even if I were in a hole within the depths of a hole, the Umayyads would extract me and kill me.'"],[4067,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to turn to his right and his left during prayer. Then Allah revealed: 'Successful indeed are the believers, those who in their prayer are humbly submissive.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became humble and no longer turned to his right or his left."],[4068,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three years old, Abu Bakr when he was sixty-three, and ʿUmar when he was sixty-three."],[4069,"The ears are part of the head."],[4070,"A man used to sacrifice a single sheep on behalf of himself and his household. Then people began to vie with one another, and it became a competition."],[4071,"The affairs of this ummah will continue to be close together,\" or he said, \"harmonious, as long as they do not speak about children and divine decree."],[4072,"Gentleness is a blessing, and harshness is an ill omen."],[4073,"He used to pray between Zuhr and ʿAsr."],[4074,"I have not seen anyone among Allah's creation more similar to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in religion, sitting, or walking than Fatimah. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her, she would welcome him, rise from her seat, kiss his hand, and seat him in her place. When she entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would welcome her, rise to her, kiss her hand, and seat her in his place. She entered upon him while he was in his house, and he whispered to her, and she wept. Then he whispered to her again, and she laughed. ʿA'ishah said: I said to the women, 'I used to think that this woman had superiority over other women; while she was weeping, she then laughed.' I asked her afterwards, 'What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whisper to you?' She did not tell me. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, I asked her, and she said, 'He said: I am going to die in this illness of mine. I grieved and wept. And he whispered to me that I would be the first of his family to join him, and I was pleased with that and laughed.'"],[4075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed wine, its drinker, its presser, the one who has it pressed for him, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the one who consumes its price."],[4076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabīdh made in earthen jars, then he permitted it."],[4077,"It has reached me that a stone is thrown from the edge of Hell and does not reach its bottom for forty years. Indeed, you marveled—yet by Allah, it will surely be filled. And it has reached me that between two of the gates of Paradise is a distance of forty years, and by Allah, a day will come to it when it is crowded and thronged. I have seen myself with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as the seventh of seven, and our mouths were sore from eating leaves. And I have seen myself and Saʿd: we split a burdah into two halves, and I wore one half and Saʿd wore the other half. Today there is none among us but is a governor over one of these garrison towns. And it has reached me that there was never a prophethood except that it was followed by kingship. I seek refuge with Allah from being great in my own eyes but contemptible in the eyes of people. You will test the rulers after me."],[4078,"A poor woman came to me carrying her two sons, and I gave her three dates to eat. She gave each of her two sons one date and raised one date to her mouth to eat it, but her two sons asked her for it, so she split the date she intended to eat between them. Her action amazed me, and I mentioned her and what she had done to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Allah has made Paradise obligatory for her and freed her from the Fire.'"],[4079,"I declare sacred what lies between the two lava tracts of Madinah, just as Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred."],[4080,"Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last seven nights."],[4081,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[4082,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he took some pebbles, and they glorified in his hand. Then he put them down and they fell silent. Then he took them and they glorified in his hand. Then he gave them to Abū Bakr, and they glorified in his hand. Then the Prophet ﷺ took them and they glorified in his hand. Then he put them down and they fell silent. Then he gave them to ʿUmar, and they glorified in his hand. Then the Prophet ﷺ took them and they glorified in his hand. Then he put them down and they fell silent. Then he gave them to ʿUthmān, and they glorified in his hand. Then he gave them to ʿAlī, and he placed them in his hand and they fell silent."],[4083,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then he turned and faced the people and said: 'O Allah, bless us in our city, and bless us in our mudd and our ṣāʿ. O Allah, bless us in our Shām and our Yemen.' A man said: 'And Iraq, O Messenger of Allah?' He remained silent. Then he said: 'O Allah, bless us in our city, and bless us in our mudd and our ṣāʿ. O Allah, bless us in our Haram, and bless us in our Shām and our Yemen.' A man said: 'And Iraq, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'From there the horn of Satan will appear, and trials will stir.'"],[4084,"The Dajjāl will descend at this salt marsh, and most of those who go out to him will be women, so much so that a man will go to his beloved—whether his mother, sister, or wife—and tie her firmly or she will join him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then they will be given power over him and his followers—and his followers are the Jews—and they will kill them, so much so that one of them will hide behind a stone or a tree, and the stone or tree will say: O believer, this is a Jew behind me, kill him.'"],[4085,"Are stones and trees many? [He asked] three times. We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, my intercession is more numerous than stones and trees.'"],[4086,"The earth will never be devoid of forty men like Ibrāhīm, the Friend of the Most Merciful. Through them people are given rain and given victory. Whenever one of them dies, Allah replaces him with another."],[4087,"Whoever revives dead land, it belongs to him."],[4088,"God will raise up for the people of the Fire a black, dark cloud. It will be said, “O people of the Fire, what do you seek?” They will recall the clouds of this world and say, “Our Lord, drink.” So He will rain upon them chains that add to their chains, shackles that add to their shackles, and coals that blaze upon them."],[4089,"The Prophet ﷺ supplicated for blessing at the pre-dawn meal."],[4090,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from a journey, he would kiss his daughter Fatimah."],[4091,"The Negus gave Umm Habibah a bridal gift of two hundred dinars on behalf of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4092,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you were to lower one of you by a rope to the seventh earth, he would come upon his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. Then he recited: “He is the First and the Last, the Outward and the Inward, and He has knowledge of everything.”"],[4093,"Whatever intoxicates in a farq, a single sip of it is unlawful."],[4094,"A man belched in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he said, “Restrain your belching, for the one among you who is fullest in this world will be the hungriest on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[4095,"He was sitting at the base of the pulpit of the Messenger of God ﷺ addressing the people when a man from the desert came to him and said, “O Messenger of God, what about the night prayer?” He said, “Yes, two by two. If you fear that dawn will overtake you or catch you, pray one rakʿah and it will make odd what has passed.”"],[4096,"Whoever does not press his nose with his forehead to the ground in his prostration, his prayer is not accepted."],[4097,"ʿUmar b. al-Khattab appointed Muʿadh over Syria. He wrote to him: “Give the people their stipends and lead them in raids.” While he was giving the people, at the end of the day, a man from the countryside came from such-and-such a place and said to him, “O Muʿadh, who will see to my stipend? I am a man from the countryside from such-and-such a place. Perhaps I will return to my family before nightfall.” He said, “By God, I will not give you until I give these,” meaning the people of the city. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “All the prophets will enter Paradise before David and Solomon by two thousand years. The poor of the Muslims will enter Paradise before their rich by forty years. The righteous slaves will enter Paradise before the free by forty years. The people of cities will enter Paradise before the people of villages by forty years. Cities excel by the Friday prayer, the congregational prayers, and the circles of remembrance. When affliction comes, they alone are singled out for it.”"],[4098,"I said to Anas b. Malik, “When did you used to pray the afternoon prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “While the sun was white and clear.”"],[4099,"Do not abandon the night prayer, even if it be only the milking of a ewe."],[4100,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ to Makkah. He used to shorten the prayer until we arrived in Makkah, and he stayed there ten days, shortening the prayer."],[4101,"War is deception."],[4102,"The Messenger of God ﷺ combined the first prayer (Zuhr) with ʿAṣr, and Maghrib with ʿIshāʾ. It was said to him about that, and he said: “I did this so that my community would not be put to hardship.”"],[4103,"Whoever meets the enemy and remains steadfast until he is killed or prevails will not be tested in his grave."],[4104,"Whoever catches the rakʿah has caught the prostration."],[4105,"The Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ were afflicted by hunger during his time. Two men approached until they overlooked some orchards, and there were dates in one of the orchards. One of them went down, and the other was afraid. He ate until he was full, then began to scoop dates into his clothes. The owner of the orchard came, snatched his garment, tied him to a palm tree, took a splinter, and hurt him severely with beating. Then he brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I found this man in my orchard; he ate until he was full, then began to scoop dates into his clothes.” The other man said: “O Messenger of God, my companion and I came while we were hungry. I went down, but my companion was afraid. I ate and took some for my companion. Then this man came and did such-and-such to me and such-and-such.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Go and give him his garment back, and measure out for him a wasq in place of what you beat him for.”"],[4106,"Whoever dies while owing a fast, his guardian may fast on his behalf."],[4107,"They said: “O Messenger of God, the polytheists wear trousers and do not wear an izar (waist-wrapper)?” He said: “Wear trousers, and wear the izar.” They said: “O Messenger of God, the polytheists go barefoot and do not wear sandals?” He said: “Go barefoot and wear sandals; oppose the allies of Satan as much as you can.”"],[4108,"When the believer falls ill, God purifies him as the bellows purifies the dross of iron."],[4109,"Whoever grants respite to a debtor in difficulty or gives him charity, God will shade him in His shade on the Day of Resurrection."],[4110,"Muʿāwiyah prayed ʿAṣr, then Ibn al-Zubayr stood up and prayed after it. Muʿāwiyah said: “O Ibn ʿAbbās, what are these two rakʿahs?” He said: “It is an innovation, and its doer is an innovator.” When he finished, he said: “What did you two say?” They said: “We said such-and-such.” He said: “I did not innovate. My maternal aunt ʿĀʾishah told me.” Muʿāwiyah sent to ʿĀʾishah, and she said: “He has spoken the truth. Umm Salamah told me.” So he sent to Umm Salamah: “ʿĀʾishah told us from you such-and-such.” She said: “She has spoken the truth. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to me one day and prayed after ʿAṣr. I stood behind him and prayed. When he finished, he said: ‘What is the matter with you?’ I said: ‘O Prophet of God, I saw you praying, so I prayed with you.’ He said: ‘An agent for the alms came to me, and I was afraid for him, so I met him, and then I forgot to pray two rakʿahs after ʿAṣr.’”"],[4111,"Between a man and polytheism and disbelief is only the abandonment of prayer."],[4112,"The throne of Iblis is upon the sea. Then he dispatches his raiding parties, and they cause trials. The greatest of them in his sight is the greatest of them in trial."],[4113,"Regarding buried treasure, one-fifth is due."],[4114,"Command them to pray at seven years of age, and strike them for it at thirteen."],[4115,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting among a group of the Muhajirun and the Ansar; Ali b. Abi Talib was on his left, and al-Abbas was on his right, when al-Abbas and a man from the Ansar quarreled. The Ansari spoke harshly to al-Abbas, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the hand of al-Abbas and the hand of Ali and said: 'From the loins of this one will come forth a youth who will fill the earth with oppression and injustice, and from the loins of this one will come forth a youth who will fill the earth with justice and equity. So when you see that, then adhere to the young Tamimi, for he will come from the east, and he is the bearer of the banner of the Mahdi.'"],[4116,"The best jihad in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection is those who meet in the battle line and do not turn their faces away until they are killed. Those are the ones who will disport themselves in the lofty chambers of Paradise. Your Lord looks upon them. Indeed, when your Lord laughs to a people, there is no reckoning upon them."],[4117,"Every lineage and marriage tie will be severed on the Day of Resurrection, except my lineage and my marriage ties."],[4118,"We entered upon Abdullah b. Unays, and he said: 'Shall I show you how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, and how he prayed?' We said: 'Yes.' So he washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nostrils three times, washed his face and his arms up to the elbows three times, wiped his head from front to back, and touched his ears, and washed his feet three times. Then he took a garment and wrapped it around himself and prayed. And he said: 'This is how I saw my beloved, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, perform ablution and pray.'"],[4119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the spoils of the killed enemy to the killer."],[4120,"When he prayed over a deceased person, he would say: 'O Allah, You created him, and You guided him to Islam, and You took his soul, and You know best his secret and his public affairs. We have come to intercede for him, so accept our intercession for him.'"],[4121,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he sent us food, he would eat some of it. Then he sent us food, but he did not eat from it. I said: 'This is food from which you did not eat.' He said: 'There is in it an herb that I dislike, so eat it.' I said: 'I dislike what you dislike.'"],[4122,"I do not narrate to you except what my two ears heard and my heart retained from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Even if I had heard it only once, or twice, or three times, or four times, or five times, or six times, or seven times, I would think that I should not narrate it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If you are upon a united community, and someone comes to split your unity and break your staff, then kill him, whoever he may be among the people.'"],[4123,"He used to give us admonition intermittently on certain days, for fear that we would become bored."],[4124,"There will be rulers after me who will lead you in prayer. If they complete its bowing and prostration, then it is for you and for them. But if they fall short, then it is for you and against them."],[4125,"Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him. If he does it, it is recorded as ten up to whatever Allah wills. And whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, it is not recorded against him. If he does it, it is recorded against him as one, or Allah may erase it."],[4126,"The rights of a Muslim over a Muslim are five: if he is sick, visit him; if he dies, attend his funeral; if he passes by, greet him; if he sneezes, say may Allah have mercy on you; and if he invites him, even if only to a sheep's trotter, accept."],[4127,"When you buy gold with silver, do not part from him while there remains any confusion between you and him."],[4128,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a small bird (hummarah) flying over the heads of his companions, and said, 'Who has distressed this one?' A man from the Ansar said, 'I did, O Messenger of Allah. I took some of its eggs, or its chicks.' So he ordered him to return them."],[4129,"Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, like for like. Whoever increases or asks for an increase has committed riba. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the owner of your dates buys one sa' for two sa's.' So he sent for him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my dates are such and such, so they will not take them unless I give them more.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not do that.'"],[4130,"I was given the concluding verses of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne."],[4131,"Whoever repents before his death by the time it takes a she-camel to recover from her labor pains, Allah will turn to him in mercy."],[4132,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the stoning of the jamarat: 'What do we get from it?' I heard him say: 'You will find its reward with your Lord when you are most in need of it.'"],[4133,"Allah only grants victory to the Muslims through the supplication of the weak and oppressed among them."],[4134,"Woe to the heels from the Fire."],[4135,"People are from various trees, and I and ʿAlī are from a single tree."],[4136,"By God, we did not recognize our hypocrites in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ except by their hatred of ʿAlī."],[4137,"Trade with the wealth of orphans so that zakāt does not consume it."],[4138,"Paradise is forbidden to all nations until I and my community enter it, the first then the next."],[4139,"A caller will call out in the Fire: O Ḥannān, O Mannān."],[4140,"A skin of wine was given as a gift to the Prophet ﷺ after it had been forbidden. When it was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Wine has indeed been forbidden.” Some of them said, “If only they sold it and gave its price to the poor Muslims.” The Prophet ﷺ ordered it to be poured out in one of the valleys of Madinah, and he said: “May God curse the Jews; their fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and consumed their prices.”"],[4141,"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was delivering a sermon and saying: “O people, which month is most sacred?” They said, “This month.” He said, “Which day is most sacred?” They said, “This day,” and it was the Day of Sacrifice. He said, “Which land is greatest in sanctity with God?” They said, “This one.” He said, “Indeed, your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you on this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, until the day you meet your Lord. Have I conveyed?” The people said, “Yes.” He raised his hands to the sky and said, “O God, bear witness.” Then he said, “O people, have I conveyed?” They said, “Yes.” He raised his hands to the sky and said, “O God, bear witness.” Then he said, “Let the one present among you convey to the absent.” Wābiṣah said, “We witnessed and you were absent, and we convey to you as the Messenger of God ﷺ said.”"],[4142,"A woman does not have sexual contact with a woman but that they are both adulteresses, and a man does not have sexual contact with a man but that they are both adulterers."],[4143,"Bilāl came to the Prophet ﷺ at the time of the call to prayer for the dawn prayer and found him asleep. He called out, “Prayer is better than sleep,” and the Messenger of God ﷺ did not disapprove of it and included it in the call to prayer. So no prayer is called before its time except the dawn prayer."],[4144,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with an old man accompanying him. He said, “O so-and-so, who is this with you?” He said, “My father.” He said, “Do not walk in front of him, do not sit before him, do not call him by his name, and do not cause others to revile him.”"],[4145,"I am the first to enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection and I will intercede, and men of my community will meet Jesus son of Mary and witness the fighting against the Dajjāl."],[4146,"A man said, “O Messenger of God, we used to raid in the pre-Islamic era. What do you command us?” He said, “Slaughter in whatever month it may be, and be dutiful to God and feed others.”"],[4147,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ dispatched a military expedition, he would say: “Raid in the name of God and in the path of God, and fight those who disbelieve in God. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child, a woman, or an old man.”"],[4148,"Should I send you upon what the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me upon? He said: “Do not leave any raised grave without leveling it, nor any image without obliterating it.”"],[4149,"An army will be swallowed up in a desert land."],[4150,"The child of unlawful intercourse bears none of the sin of his parents. Then he recited: “And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another.”"],[4151,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking one another’s necks. A man is not held accountable for the crime of his brother or the crime of his father.”"],[4152,"Whoever conceals a testimony when summoned to it is like one who gives false testimony."],[4153,"Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him."],[4154,"Whoever points a piece of iron at his brother, the angels continue to curse him until he puts it down, even if he is his brother from the same father and mother."],[4155,"I saw Abraham on the night I was taken on the night journey. He said: “O Muhammad, convey peace to your community, and inform them that Paradise has good soil and sweet water, and that it is a plain, and its plants are the saying: ‘Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, God is greatest, and there is no power nor strength except with God.’”"],[4156,"Whoever goes to the Friday prayer, let him perform the ritual bath."],[4157,"Regarding His saying: “Then He sent down upon you, after distress, security—drowsiness,” he said: “Sleep was cast upon us on the day of Uhud.”"],[4158,"He used to test the believing women who emigrated to him with this verse: “O Prophet, when the believing women come to you...”"],[4159,"Abu Bakr and ʿUmar are the chiefs of the mature men of the people of Paradise, from the first and the last, except the prophets and the messengers."],[4160,"It was said: O Messenger of God, when were you written as a prophet? He said: While Adam was between the spirit and the body."],[4161,"He was in the house of Maymunah, and he placed purification water for the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Who placed it?\" It was said: Ibn ʿAbbas. He tapped me on my shoulder and said: O God, give him understanding in the religion and teach him interpretation."],[4162,"Whoever learns archery and then forgets it, it is a blessing he has disbelieved."],[4163,"A person’s prayer in his house is better than his prayer in this mosque of mine, except for the obligatory prayer."],[4164,"Fasting is a shield from the Fire. Whoever wakes up fasting should not behave ignorantly that day. If someone behaves ignorantly toward him, he should not insult him or curse him, but should say: I am fasting. By the One in whose hand is my soul, the change in the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk."],[4165,"By God, this world from its beginning to its end is only like when one of you puts his finger in the sea—let him see what comes back to him."],[4166,"He liked, when he went out for a need, to hear: O successful one, O rightly guided one."],[4167,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he performed ablution, wipe his face with the edge of his garment."],[4168,"When you hurry to do good, walk barefoot, for God multiplies the reward of the one who wears sandals."],[4169,"One day they were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the house of ʿAʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a platter of bread and meat was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ from the house of Umm Salamah, and it was placed before the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"Put your hands.\" The Prophet of God ﷺ put his hand, and we put our hands, and we ate. He said: \"ʿAʾishah was preparing food quickly,\" having seen the platter that was brought. When she finished her food, she brought it and placed it, and she lifted the platter of Umm Salamah and broke it, and she spoke and spoke. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Eat in the name of God; your mother is jealous. Then he gave her platter to Umm Salamah and said: \"Food in place of food, and a vessel in place of a vessel.\""],[4170,"The Prophet ﷺ stoned, and Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar, and ʿUthman."],[4171,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, may one of us pray in a single garment?” He said, “Does every one of you find two garments?”"],[4172,"The Prophet ﷺ was never given a choice between two matters but he chose the easier of them."],[4173,"Whoever catches one rakʿah of the Friday prayer has caught it, except that he must make up what he missed."],[4174,"Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold or a vessel of silver only causes the Fire to gurgle in his belly."],[4175,"In the last days there will be unjust rulers, wicked ministers, treacherous judges, and lying jurists. Whoever among you lives to see that time must not be a tax collector for them, nor a ʿarīf, nor a policeman."],[4176,"Whoever drinks wine until he dies, it will be forbidden to him in the Hereafter."],[4177,"A talebearer will not enter Paradise."],[4178,"I used to miss days of fasting in Ramadan and could not make them up except in Shaʿbān."],[4179,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated, he raised his hands until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[4180,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed the witr prayer on his mount."],[4181,"I suffered greatly and with difficulty from prostatic fluid, and I used to wash often because of it. I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said, “Ablution suffices you for it.” I said, “O Messenger of God, what about what gets on my garment from it?” He said, “A handful of water is enough for you: sprinkle it on your garment wherever you see that it has touched it.”"],[4182,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Sahlah bt. Suhayl, who had irregular bleeding, to perform a full bath for every prayer. That was hard for her, so he commanded her to combine the noon and afternoon prayers with one bath, and the sunset and night prayers with one bath, and to bathe for the dawn prayer."],[4183,"No balance has been set for me heavier than good character."],[4184,"I have never prayed behind an imam whose prayer was more complete and more concise than the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4185,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded a crier to call out: 'Verily wine has been forbidden, so do not sell it, do not buy it, and whoever has any of it should spill it.' Abu Talhah said: 'O boy, untie the waterskin and spill it.' So the people spilled it, and on that day they had no wine except unripe dates and dry dates."],[4186,"A group of the Sudanese played with their spears in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I was looking from between his shoulders and his head."],[4187,"Verily God has veiled repentance from the adherent of every innovation."],[4188,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some food, and he put his hand into it, and said: 'Whoever cheats us is not of us.'"],[4189,"Two categories of my community will not come to me at the Pond, and will not enter Paradise: the Qadariyyah and the Murji'ah."],[4190,"The Qadariyyah and the Murji'ah are the Magians of this community. If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend their funerals."],[4191,"He delivered a sermon and said: 'To proceed...'"],[4192,"Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in darkness of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."],[4193,"Whoever loves that men should stand up for him, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4194,"Preserve me in regard to al-ʿAbbas, for he is the remnant of my forefathers."],[4195,"There is no Muslim who wakes up at night and says: “There is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great, and praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. O Allah, forgive me,” except that he is forgiven. If he then resolves, rises, performs ablution, and supplicates to Allah, He answers him."],[4196,"The women of Quraysh are the best women to have ridden camels, most tender to a child and most protective of a husband in his property."],[4197,"Argumentation about the Qur’an is disbelief."],[4198,"I entered upon Shaddad b. Aws while he was weeping. I said, “What makes you weep?” He said, “Two hadiths I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said, “What are they?” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to me, and I saw in his face something that grieved me. I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, what is this that I see in your face?’ He said, ‘Two matters I fear for my community after me: shirk and hidden desire. Indeed, they will not worship a sun, nor a moon, nor an idol, but they will show off in their deeds.’ I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, is that shirk?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ I said, ‘And what is hidden desire?’ He said, ‘A man begins the day fasting, then one of his desires presents itself to him, and he goes along with it and abandons the fast.’”"],[4199,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a young man appeared to us from the mountain pass. When we looked at him, we said, “If only this young man would put his energy, youth, and strength in the path of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard our words and said, “And what is the path of Allah except one who is killed? Whoever strives on behalf of his parents is in the path of Allah, whoever strives on behalf of his dependents is in the path of Allah, and whoever strives to accumulate is in the path of the false god.”"],[4200,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to Quba. A small cup was brought from one of their houses. The Prophet ﷺ put his hand in it, but the cup could not contain it, so he inserted his four fingers and could not insert his thumb. Then he said to the people, “Come to the drink.” Anas said, “My eye saw water springing from between his fingers, and he did not withdraw the cup until they had all drunk from it.”"],[4201,"Whoever sends one prayer upon me, Allah sends ten prayers upon him."],[4202,"A questioner asked him and said, “O Abu al-ʿAbbas, is there repentance for a killer?” Ibn ʿAbbas said, as if amazed at the matter, “What are you saying?” He repeated his question. He said to him, “What are you saying?” two or three times. Then Ibn ʿAbbas said, “How can there be repentance for him? I heard your Prophet ﷺ say: The slain person will come holding his head with one of his hands, seizing his killer with the other, his jugular veins gushing blood, until he brings him to the Throne. The slain person will say to the Lord of the worlds, ‘This one killed me.’ Allah will say to the killer, ‘May you perish,’ and he will be taken to the Fire.”"],[4203,"No marriage is valid except with a guardian and two witnesses, and a dowry, whether small or large."],[4204,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, should I perform Hajj on behalf of my mother? She has died.” He said, “Do you think if she had a debt and you paid it, would it not be accepted from you?” She said, “Yes.” So he instructed her to perform Hajj on her behalf. Another woman came and said, “Should I perform Hajj with my son while he is nursing or small?” He said, “Yes.”"],[4205,"The Prophet ﷺ performed three ʿumrahs in Dhu al-Qaʿdah: one from al-Hudaybiyyah, another in the truce of Quraysh, and the other on his return from Khaybar from al-Jiʿirranah."],[4206,"The flank is the vein of the kidney; when it moves, it hurts its owner. Treat it with burned water and honey."],[4207,"Indeed I seek forgiveness from Allah seventy times in a day and turn to Him."],[4208,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me, so I said: O Prophet of Allah, teach me a deed I can do while sitting, for standing has become difficult for me. He said: \"O Umm Hani'.\" I said: At your service, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Glorify Allah one hundred times, for it equals one hundred slaves; praise Allah one hundred times, for it equals one hundred horses with their gear in the path of Allah; magnify Allah one hundred times, for it equals one hundred camels adorned and prepared for sacrifice; and declare Allah's oneness one hundred times, for it does not pass over any sin except that it erases it.\""],[4209,"While a man was with the Prophet ﷺ on his camel, he cursed it, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not travel with us on a cursed camel.\""],[4210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymuna at Sarif, consummated the marriage with her at Sarif, and she died at Sarif."],[4211,"There will be matters after me and trials. The best of people in them is the believer who is gracious and pious."],[4212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing women and children, and he said: \"They belong to whoever prevails.\""],[4213,"Indeed Allah accepts charity and nurtures it for one of you just as one of you nurtures his foal or young camel."],[4214,"Whoever is given a life grant, it belongs to him and his descendants."],[4215,"A fire will emerge from [......] by which the necks of camels will be illuminated in Busra."],[4216,"The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is the one who emigrates from what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden."],[4217,"Fasting is a shield from the Fire."],[4218,"Shall I not lead you in prayer the way the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed? He called for water for ablution, performed ablution, then stood for prayer. He arranged men in rows and placed the boys behind them. He would say takbir when he prostrated, when he raised his head, and when he stood up from the two rak'ahs, and he would greet to his right and to his left."],[4219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the barber, saying, “Here,” and he shaved his head. Then he handed it to Abu Talhah. Then he shaved the other side and said, “Distribute it among the people.”"],[4220,"I asked Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform qunut? He said: “Yes, after rukuʿ, for a short while.”"],[4221,"The one who goes early to Jumuʿah is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a ram, then like one who offers a chicken” — and I think he said — “like one who offers an egg.”"],[4222,"Prayer in congregation is superior to a man’s prayer alone by twenty-some degrees."],[4223,"I went with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the market of al-Baqiʿ. He put his hand into a sack and took out mixed grain — or he said adulterated grain — and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not one of us who deceives us.”"],[4224,"What assurance does any of you have, if he raises his head before the imam, that Allah will not turn his head into the head of a dog?"],[4225,"Whoever is given any authority over the affairs of the Muslims, and Allah intends good for him, He provides him with a righteous minister: if he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him."],[4226,"Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty or makes it easy for him, Allah will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade."],[4227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me. I said: “I have no aversion to you, O Messenger of Allah, but I do not like to marry while my children are young.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best women who ever rode camels are the women of Quraysh — the most compassionate toward a child in his childhood and the most careful of a husband in what he possesses.”"],[4228,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bring out ʿAbd Allah b. Khatal from beneath the curtains of the Kaʿbah and kill him. Then he said: “No Qurayshi shall be killed in retaliation after this.”"],[4229,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿumrah three times before his Hajj, in Dhu al-Qiʿdah."],[4230,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: How is the grandfather’s share divided? He said: “Why do you ask about that, O ʿUmar? I think you will die before you learn it.” And he died before he learned it."],[4231,"I used to pass by this verse and not know what it was: “by the late afternoon and the ishrāq,” until Umm Hāniʾ bt. Abī Ṭālib told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her, and he called for water for ablution in a large wooden bowl, and it was as if I were looking at the trace of dough in it. So he performed ablution, then he stood and prayed the Ḍuḥā prayer, then he said: “O Umm Hāniʾ, this is the prayer of al-ishrāq.”"],[4232,"Regarding a woman who has a husband, and she has wealth, and he does not permit her to go on Hajj? He said: She may not depart except with her husband’s permission."],[4233,"“I have left you behind to be my successor among my family.” He said: “Am I to remain behind after you, O Prophet of God?” He said: “Are you not pleased that you are to me of the station of Hārūn from Mūsā, except that there is no prophet after me?”"],[4234,"We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten the breaking of the fast, to delay the pre-dawn meal, and to place our right hands upon our left hands."],[4235,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said of al-Marwah: “This is the place of sacrifice, and all the roads and paths of Makkah are places of sacrifice in the ʿumrah.”"],[4236,"I asked Saʿīd b. Jubayr about this verse: “And married women” (Q 4:24). He said: “I have no knowledge of it.” Then I asked al-Ḍaḥḥāk b. Muzāḥim, and I mentioned to him the statement of Saʿīd b. Jubayr. He said: “I bear witness that I heard him ask Ibn ʿAbbās about it, and Ibn ʿAbbās said: ‘It was revealed on the day of Khaybar. When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Khaybar, the Muslims acquired women from among the women of the People of the Book who had husbands. When a man wanted to have intercourse with one of them, she would say: “I have a husband.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about that, and this verse was revealed: “And married women” – the verse – meaning: and the captives from the polytheists who are acquired, there is no harm in that.’ So I mentioned that to Saʿīd b. Jubayr, and he said: ‘Al-Ḍaḥḥāk has spoken the truth.’”"],[4237,"Whoever gives a man security for his blood and then kills him, I am innocent of the killer, even if the slain one is a disbeliever."],[4238,"The likeness of the hypocrite is the likeness of a sheep that wanders between two flocks: when it goes to this one, it butts it, and when it goes to that one, it butts it."],[4239,"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform a full bath."],[4240,"All of you are shepherds, and all of you are responsible for his flock."],[4241,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a choice, and we chose him, and he did not count it as anything."],[4242,"Two types of dress and two types of sale have been forbidden: a man’s wrapping himself in a single garment with his private part exposed to the sky, and his wrapping it over his left shoulder and then raising it; and the transactions of mulāmasa and munābadha."],[4243,"Among what Allah created is a rooster whose talons are on the seventh earth, whose crest is folded beneath the Throne, and whose wings are by the two horizons. When the last third of the night remains, it beats its wings and then says: 'Glory be to the King, the Most Holy; glory be to our Lord, the King, the Most Holy; there is no god for us other than Him.' Then everything between the two horizons hears it except the two heavy species (humans and jinn). They think that roosters only beat their wings when they crow, upon hearing that."],[4244,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of Adam? Was he a prophet?' He said: 'Yes, he was a prophet and messenger. Allah spoke to him directly, saying: \"O Adam, dwell you and your wife in Paradise.\"'"],[4245,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on a small mat (khumra)."],[4246,"Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant in family, wealth, or children, and he says: 'What Allah wills; there is no power except with Allah,' such that he would see in it a defect, short of death.' He then recited: 'If only, when you entered your garden, you had said: What Allah wills; there is no power except with Allah' (Quran 18:39)."],[4247,"He is not of us who practices divination or has it done for him, or practices soothsaying or has it done for him, or practices augury from birds or has it done for him."],[4248,"Shall I inform you of the people of Paradise?' We said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Every weak, oppressed person, clad in two worn-out garments, to whom no attention is paid; if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath. Shall I inform you of the people of the Fire?' We said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Every coarse, arrogant, self-conceited person.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is coarse?' He said: 'Thick-bodied.' I said: 'What is arrogant, self-conceited?' He said: 'The one who regards himself as great.'"],[4249,"Allah will resurrect the servants on the Day of Resurrection, then He will set apart the scholars and say: 'O assembly of scholars, I did not place My knowledge among you while intending to punish you. Go, for I have forgiven you.'"],[4250,"Do not harm the living by (reviling) the dead."],[4251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never given a choice between two matters but that he chose the easier of them, as long as it was not a sin. If it was a sin, he was the furthest of people from it. He never took revenge for himself over anything done to him, until the sacred limits of Allah were violated, and then he would take revenge for Allah's sake."],[4252,"The ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday is obligatory upon every adult who has reached puberty."],[4253,"The orphan girl is to be consulted about her own marriage, and her silence is her consent."],[4254,"Snakes are the metamorphosis of jinn, just as apes and pigs were metamorphosed from the Children of Israel."],[4255,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, mentioning Zamzam: \"It is blessed, a food of nourishment.\""],[4256,"The signs will come one after another, following one another like beads in a string."],[4257,"Do good deeds properly, sincerely, and moderately, for none of you will be saved by his deeds.\" They said, \"Not even you, O Prophet of God?\" He said, \"Not even me, unless God envelops me in mercy and grace.\""],[4258,"The Prophet ﷺ granted al-Zubayr the distance his horse ran on a piece of land called Thurayr. He made the horse run until it stopped, then threw his whip and said, \"Give him up to where the whip reached.\""],[4259,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered in the year of the conquest through the mountain pass of al-Idhkhir."],[4260,"Hudhayfah asked a village chief for water, and he gave him drink in a silver vessel. He threw it at him, then said, \"Had I not already warned him once or twice— The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to drink from gold and silver, and to wear silk and brocade. For them it is in this world, and for us it is in the Hereafter.\""],[4261,"He witnessed that when ʿUthman b. ʿAffan gave the Messenger of God ﷺ what he used to equip the army of hardship, he brought seven hundred ounces of gold."],[4262,"Regarding a pilgrim in ihram who dies: he is shrouded in his two garments, his head is not covered, he is not touched with perfume, and he is washed with water and sidr. He will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah."],[4263,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Muhammad, live as you wish, for you will die; do as you wish, for you will be recompensed for it; love whomever you wish, for you will part from him; and know that the honor of the believer is standing in night prayer, and his might is being self-sufficient from people.\""],[4264,"When ʿAbdullah b. ʿUmar returned to Madinah, he made his camel kneel at al-Batha' near Dhu al-Hulayfah, where the Messenger of God ﷺ had made his camel kneel."],[4265,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray while I was lying crosswise in front of him."],[4266,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh said: \"O Messenger of God, I have prolonged bleeding and do not become pure; should I abandon prayer?\" He said: \"That is not menstruation; it is a vein. When menstruation comes, abandon prayer, and when it departs— or she said: turns away— wash the blood from yourself and pray.\""],[4267,"The people should be led in prayer by the one among them who has the earliest emigration; if their emigration is equal, then by the oldest among them; if they are equal in age, then by the one most knowledgeable in the Qur'an."],[4268,"We used to garland the sheep, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send them as lawful offerings, not making anything forbidden."],[4269,"Let none of you say: 'I forgot such-and-such a verse,' for indeed he is not the one who forgot, but rather he was made to forget."],[4270,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform witr with three [rak'ahs], reciting in the first: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' in the second: 'Say, O disbelievers,' and in the third: 'Say, He is Allah, [who is] One.'"],[4271,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no god but Allah.' If they do that, then their blood and their wealth are protected from me, except for its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[4272,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I am a coward, and I am weak.' He said: 'Come to a struggle that has no hardship in it: the Hajj.'"],[4273,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away on Monday, and he was buried on the night of Wednesday."],[4274,"A time will surely come upon my nation when they will wish for the Dajjal. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, why is that?' He said: 'Because of the hardship and suffering they will encounter.'"],[4275,"I lived eight years of the life of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was born in the year of Uhud."],[4276,"We have entered the evening and the dominion belongs to Allah, and all praise is due to Allah. I seek refuge in Allah, who holds the sky from falling upon the earth except by His permission, from the evil of what He has created, scattered, and brought into being. Whoever says these words is protected from every sorcerer, soothsayer, devil, and envier."],[4277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a donkey that had been branded on its face, and he said: 'May Allah curse the one who did this.'"],[4278,"The Prophet ﷺ did not take off his shoes in prayer except once, and the people then took off their shoes. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Why did you take off your shoes?' They said: 'We saw you take yours off, so we took ours off.' He said: 'Indeed Jibril ﷺ .'"],[4279,"We were with Ibn Abbas in Makkah, so I said, “When we are with you, we pray four [rakʿahs], but when we return to our dwellings, we pray two rakʿahs?” He said, “That is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.”"],[4280,"The Prophet ﷺ entered and heard the sound of a child crying, so he said, “What is wrong with this child of yours that he is crying? Why do you not seek a ruqya for him from the evil eye?”"],[4281,"I saw Aisha praying al-Duha, and she said, “I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray [it] except four rakʿahs.”"],[4282,"Whoever disowns his child in order to disgrace him in this world, Allah will disgrace him on the Day of Resurrection before the witnesses, retribution for retribution.”"],[4283,"Ali b. Abi Talib stood up as a speaker in al-Rahba, praised Allah and extolled Him as He deserves, then said what Allah willed him to say, then called for a cup of Zamzam water and rinsed his mouth from it, wiped [his face], and drank the leftover of his ablution while standing. Then he said, “It has reached me that a man among you dislikes drinking while standing. This is the ablution of one who has not broken his wudu. And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do like this.”"],[4284,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people, whose covenants and trusts have become corrupted, and they have differed and become like this?” And he interlaced his fingers. They said, “What is the way out, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Take what you recognize, and leave what you reject, and keep to your own self, and beware of their common masses.”"],[4285,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it: “Indeed, it is an unrighteous deed.”"],[4286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to wipe over the leather socks, even if one of us came from defecation.”"],[4287,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said that she had committed adultery and was pregnant. He said, “Go away until you give birth to your child,” and if she had not returned to him, he would not have sent for her. She gave birth, then came to him, and he said, “Go away until you have weaned your child.” She came to him, and if she had not come to him, he would not have sent for her. She came after she had weaned him, and he had her stoned.”"],[4288,"Whoever hears the call [to prayer] and does not respond without an excuse, there is no prayer for him.”"],[4289,"He threw the pebble at Jamrah from the bottom of the valley, then said, “This is the standing place of the one upon whom Surah al-Baqarah was sent down.”"],[4290,"O son of Adam, if your sins reached the clouds of the sky, then you asked Me for forgiveness, I would forgive you and not care. O son of Adam, if you came with nearly the earth’s fill of sins, then met Me without associating anything with Me, I would come to you with nearly its fill of forgiveness.”"],[4291,"When Allah intends mercy for a nation of His servants, He takes its prophet before it, making him a forerunner and advance guard before it. When He intends its destruction, He punishes it while its prophet is alive, looking on, and He gladdens his eye with its destruction when they disbelieved him and disobeyed his command."],[4292,"Some slaves from the people of Makkah went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah before dawn and accepted Islam. Their masters from the people of Makkah sent to him: \"By Allah, O Muhammad, they did not come out to you out of desire for your religion; rather they came out fleeing from slavery.\" Some men among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah; return them.\" He became angry, then said: \"I think you, O company of Quraysh, will not stop until Allah sends against you those who will strike your necks for this religion.\" He refused to return them and said: \"They are the freed ones of Allah.\" Others went out after the treaty, so he returned them."],[4293,"Whoever follows a funeral procession from its family until the prayer is offered over it will have one qirat; whoever follows it until it is buried will have two qirats, the smaller of which is like Mount Uhud."],[4294,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in the funeral prayer: 'O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, bless him, and cause him to reach the pool of Your Messenger.'"],[4295,"The first one whom the Truth will shake hands with is Umar, and the first one whose hand He will take and admit him into Paradise."],[4296,"He forbade al-shighar (a type of marriage exchange)."],[4297,"\"Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Aqsa Mosque, and this mosque of mine.\""],[4298,"I came to him—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—wearing a striped cloak, and he was in a garden branding the camels. He said: \"Gently.\""],[4299,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry, no one dared to speak to him except Ali."],[4300,"\"For the traveler three days and nights, and for the resident one day and night,\" regarding wiping over the leather socks."],[4301,"Among the things I have forgotten from various matters, I have not forgotten the greeting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer to his right and left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[4302,"\"What a bad mountain pass is Jiyad.\" He said it twice or three times. They said: \"Why is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"The Beast will come out and cry out three cries that will be heard by all between the east and the west.\""],[4303,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken, there descended upon my father what, had it descended upon the firm mountains, would have crushed them. Kufr appeared, and hypocrisy raised its head. They did not differ over a single point but that my father flew with its decisive share and sufficiency.\" He said: \"She would mention Umar b. al-Khattab and say: By Allah, he was a man of decisive action, unique in his kind, who had prepared for affairs their equals.\""],[4304,"People are indeed like a hundred camels; among them you will not find even one riding camel."],[4305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw mucus in the qiblah of the mosque, so he scraped it off, then said: \"When one of you spits, let him not spit toward the qiblah; let him spit to his left.\""],[4306,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him and Muʿadh to Yemen, and said to them: \"Make things easy, give glad tidings, teach, and do not drive people away.\" When they turned to leave, Abu Musa came back and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, they have a drink made from honey that is cooked until it thickens, and mizr made from barley.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Everything that intoxicates and distracts from prayer is forbidden.\""],[4307,"There is no obedience to any creature in disobedience to Allah."],[4308,"I watched the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not stop the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[4309,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, and I prayed following his prayer from behind him, while he did not know. He began with al-Baqarah and recited from it until I thought he would bow; then he continued. Sufyan said: I only know that he said he prayed four rakʿahs, his bowing was like his standing. He said: I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Why did you not tell me?\" Hudhayfah said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth as a Prophet, I still feel it in my back even now.\" He said: \"Had I known you were behind me, I would have lightened it.\""],[4310,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rakʿahs."],[4311,"When one of you goes to sleep intending to pray at night, let him place a handful of dust at his right side. When he wakes, let him take some of it with his right hand and throw it to his left."],[4312,"I was riding behind my father, and I saw the Prophet ﷺ on a camel saying: \"Labbayk for a Hajj and an Umrah together.\""],[4313,"While I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man came and greeted him, then turned away. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I love this man.\" He said: \"Have you told him?\" I said: \"No.\" He said: \"Tell your brother.\" So I followed him, greeted him, took hold of his shoulders, and said: \"By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah.\" He said: \"By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah.\" And I said: \"Were it not that the Prophet ﷺ commanded me to tell you, I would not have done so.\""],[4314,"A woman used to borrow jewelry during the time of the Prophet ﷺ and then keep it. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Let the woman repent to Allah and His Messenger, and return what she has, but she refused.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Stand, O so-and-so, take her hand and cut it off.\""],[4315,"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful."],[4316,"When the Prophet ﷺ was suffering from the illness in which he passed away, he said: “Summon for me Abu Bakr and his son, so that I may write for them a document lest anyone should covet the affair of Abu Bakr or any wisher should wish [for it].” Then he said: “Allah and the Muslims refuse that,” twice."],[4317,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise."],[4318,"I did not toss and turn during this night except that I heard a voice in the mosque. I said: O Messenger of Allah, that is al-Hawlaʾ bt. Tuwayt; she does not sleep when people sleep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked what I said, until I saw that in his face. Then he said: “Allah does not grow weary until you grow weary.”"],[4319,"I said to ʿAʾishah: With what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform witr? She said: “He used to perform witr with Sabbihisma rabbika al-aʿla (Surah al-Aʿla), Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun (Surah al-Kafirun), and Qul huwa Allahu ahad (Surah al-Ikhlas).”"],[4320,"The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday: on it Adam was created, on it he was admitted to Paradise, and on it he was expelled from it. And the Hour will not commence except on Friday."],[4321,"A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, the obligation of Allah regarding the Hajj has come upon my father while he is an old man who cannot sit firmly on the riding beast. Shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: “Yes.” He said: “Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.”"],[4322,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over a funeral, and he said the salam to his right and to his left."],[4323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named himself for us with names. Among them are those we memorized and among them are those we did not memorize. He said: “I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, al-Muqaffi (the one who follows the other prophets), al-Hashir (the gatherer), the Prophet of repentance, and the Prophet of the epic battle (al-malhamah).”"],[4324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left us while we were still numerous, and none of us had searched... concerning a penetrating wound or a bone-fracturing wound except ʿUmar or Ibn ʿUmar.”"],[4325,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing a lower garment that was rustling. He said: “Who is this?” I said: ʿAbd Allah. He said: “If you are ʿAbd Allah (servant of Allah), then raise your lower garment to the middle of your shins.” His lower garment remained so until he died."],[4326,"A man's she-camel fell with him and he died while he was in a state of ihram. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.”"],[4327,"ʿUmar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have acquired land at Khaybar; I have never acquired property more precious to me than it, so what do you command? He said: If you wish, you may hold its usufruct and give it as charity. He said: So ʿUmar held its usufruct and gave it as charity: it is not to be sold, nor given as gift, nor inherited; [its yield is] for the poor, for freeing slaves, for the cause of God, for the stranded traveler, and for the guest. There is no fault on the one who manages it if he eats from it in a fair manner and feeds a friend, without seeking to amass wealth from it."],[4328,"The stomach is the reservoir of the body, and the veins flow into it. When the stomach is sound, the veins depart with soundness; when the stomach is corrupt, the veins depart with sickness."],[4329,"The talbiyah of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: Labbayka ilāha al-ḥaqq (Here I am, O God of truth)."],[4330,"I entered upon Hind bt. al-Muhallab b. Abī Ṣufrah, the wife of al-Ḥajjāj b. Yūsuf, and in her hand was a spindle with which she was spinning. I said to her: You spin while you are the wife of an emir? She said: I heard my father relate from my grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The one among you with the longest thread will have the greatest reward."],[4331,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ among a number of his companions: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, ʿUthmān, ʿAlī, Ṭalḥah, al-Zubayr, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf, Muʿādh, Ḥudhayfah, and Saʿd, eight years after the Hijrah, in the ninth year. Ḥudhayfah asked him: May my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of God."],[4332,"He used to say: Labbayka allāhumma labbayk, labbayka lā sharīka laka labbayk, inna al-ḥamda wa-al-niʿmata laka wa-al-mulk, lā sharīka lak (Here I am, O God, here I am; here I am, no partner have You, here I am; truly all praise and blessing are Yours, and sovereignty, no partner have You)."],[4333,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed a prayer, either adding to it or omitting from it. Some of the people said to him: Has something new occurred in the prayer? He said: Nothing new has occurred in it; if something new had occurred, I would have informed you. But I am a human being and I forget, so when I forget, remind me. Then he prayed what remained of his prayer, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then said: When one of you prays and does not know whether he added or omitted, let him seek what is correct in that, then prostrate twice while seated."],[4334,"By Him in whose hand is my soul, the killing of a believer is more grave with God on the Day of Resurrection than the passing away of the world."],[4335,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood, and a group of us stood behind him and prayed, while the other group faced the enemy. The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed one rakʿah and two prostrations with the group that was with him, then they departed to face the enemy. Then the group that had not prayed came and prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he prayed one rakʿah and two prostrations with them. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ gave the salutation. Then each of the two groups prayed one rakʿah and two prostrations for themselves."],[4336,"I asked Ubayy b. Kaʿb about the two protective surahs. He said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about them, and he said: No one has asked me about them before you. It was said to me, so I said. Ubayy said: So it was said to us, so we said."],[4337,"Ubayy b. Kaʿb said to me: How many verses do you count in Sūrat al-Aḥzāb? I said: We count it as seventy-two or seventy-three verses. He said: It used to equal Sūrat al-Baqarah, and in it was [the verse]: The old man and the old woman, if they commit adultery, stone them both as a punishment from God, and God is Mighty and Wise."],[4338,"The Night of Power is the night of the twenty-seventh. I said: Abū al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the verse that the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned and we memorized. Then he swore without exception, saying: By Him who sent down the Book upon Muḥammad ﷺ, it is indeed the night of the twenty-seventh."],[4339,"It is not befitting for a Muslim to neglect the one he sustains."],[4340,"Whoever eats dates with a group should not eat two at a time. If he wants to do that, let him ask their permission, and if they permit him, then let him do it if he wishes."],[4341,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mixing unripe dates and ripe dates, meaning to make them into nabidh."],[4342,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ five [nights] before his death saying: “I had among you brothers and friends, and I declare myself free before God of having taken any of you as a bosom friend. If I were to take a bosom friend from my community, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a bosom friend. My Lord has taken me as a bosom friend, just as He took Ibrahim as a bosom friend. Indeed, those before you used to take the graves of their prophets as places of worship, and I forbid you from that.”"],[4343,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established brotherhood between two men of his companions. One of them was killed, and the other lived after him as long as God willed, then he died. The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ started supplicating for him, and the utmost of their supplication was that God join him with his brother who had been killed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Which of the two do you say is more virtuous?” They said: “The one who was killed.” He said: “Do you not give merit to this one’s prayer and fasting? The distance between them is greater than between heaven and earth.” Thus he gave superiority to the one who died [naturally] over the one who was killed."],[4344,"Your love of a thing blinds and deafens."],[4345,"Ill omen is bad character."],[4346,"I came to Makkah and found Abu Hanifah, Ibn Abi Layla, and Ibn Shubrumah there. I asked Abu Hanifah, saying: “What do you say about a man who made a sale and stipulated a condition?” He said: “The sale is invalid and the condition is invalid.” Then I came to Ibn Abi Layla and asked him, and he said: “The sale is valid and the condition is invalid.” Then I came to Ibn Shubrumah and asked him, and he said: “The sale is valid and the condition is valid.” I said: “Glory be to God! Three jurists of Iraq have differed before me on a single issue.”"],[4350,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[4351,"The imam is a guarantor and the mu'adhdhin is a trustee. O God, forgive the mu'adhdhins and guide the imams aright."],[4352,"The key to Paradise is prayer, and the key to prayer is ablution."],[4353,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man say to another: “O shahan shah.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God is the King of kings.”"],[4354,"He has not believed in the Qur'an who deems lawful its prohibitions."],[4355,"My community is of four types: a man who is given wealth and spends it in obedience to God. Another man sees him and says, 'If I had wealth like his, I would do with it as he did.' They are equal in reward. And a man who is given wealth and squanders it and corrupts it. Another man sees him and says, 'If I had wealth like this, I would do with it as he did.' They are equal in sin."],[4356,"Whoever makes a supplication that contains no sin or severing of kinship, God will grant him one of three things: either He will forgive him a past sin, or He will hasten it for him in this world, or He will store it for him in the Hereafter."],[4357,"Regarding the Kharijites, he said: Their example is like a man who shot an arrow and it sped away until it fell. He took it and looked at its notch but saw no grease or blood. Then he looked at its tip but saw no grease or blood. When it carried nothing of grease or blood, likewise these people carry nothing of Islam."],[4358,"When the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever loves to meet God, God loves to meet him, and whoever hates to meet God, God hates to meet him,' she said: 'O Prophet of God, there is none among us but hates death?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'It is not hatred of death. Rather, when a believer is approached by death, he is given glad tidings of God's good pleasure and His Paradise, so nothing is more beloved to him than what he encounters. Thus he loves to meet God, and God loves to meet him. And when an unbeliever is approached by death, he is given tidings of God's punishment and His wrath, so nothing is more hateful to him than what comes to him. Thus he hates to meet God, and God hates to meet him.'"],[4359,"Attend the Friday prayer and draw near to the imam, for I have come to know that some people will be delayed from entering Paradise due to their delay in attending Friday prayer, even if they are among its people."],[4360,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed them and said: 'How long will you refrain from mentioning the evildoer? Expose him so that people may beware of him.'"],[4361,"Adorn your festivals with takbir."],[4362,"Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf is in Paradise, and Sa'd is in Paradise. If I wished, I could name the ninth. They said to him: 'Who is he?' Said said: 'It is he, and the Messenger of God ﷺ is the tenth.'"],[4363,"On honey, a tenth is due for every twelve waterskins; nothing is due on less than that."],[4364,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade eating cats and consuming their price."],[4365,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: 'How are you this morning, O so-and-so?' He replied: 'I praise God to you, O Messenger of God.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'This is what I wanted from you.'"],[4366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when the Negus died: “Your brother Aṣḥama has died.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and prayed over him as he would pray over a funeral, and he said four takbīrs over him."],[4367,"The Banū Salimah wanted to move so that they would be close to the Prophet’s mosque ﷺ. He said: “O Banū Salimah, stay in your dwellings, for your footsteps are recorded.”"],[4368,"The major ablution (ghusl) is with a ṣāʿ, and the minor ablution (wuḍūʾ) is with a mudd."],[4369,"When a man sits between the four limbs of a woman, then the major ablution (ghusl) becomes obligatory."],[4370,"Hang the whip where the people of the house can see it, for it is discipline for them."],[4371,"Allah raised two servants from among His servants and increased them in wealth and children. He said to one of them: “O so-and-so, son of so-and-so.” He said: “Here I am, my Lord, at Your service.” He said: “Did I not increase you in wealth and children?” He said: “Yes, my Lord.” He said: “What did you do with what I gave you?” He said: “I left it for my children, fearing poverty for them.” He said: “Indeed, if you knew true knowledge, you would laugh little and weep much. Indeed, what you feared for them, I have brought upon them.” And He says to the other: “O so-and-so, son of so-and-so.” He says: “Here I am, my Lord, at Your service.” He said to him: “Did I not increase you in wealth and children?” He said: “Yes, my Lord.” He said: “What did you do with what I gave you?” He said: “I spent it in obedience to You, and I entrusted my children after me to Your abundant bounty.” He said: “Indeed, if you knew true knowledge, you would laugh much and weep little. Indeed, what you entrusted for them, I have brought upon them.”"],[4372,"No one should address the people except a ruler, one appointed by a ruler, or a hypocrite."],[4373,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss me, then go out to pray without performing ablution."],[4374,"A delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, wearing cloaks with slits, and upon them were signs of hardship. He was distressed by what he saw of their appearance. He entered his house, then came out and ordered that charity be given, and he urged people to give it. Then he said: “Let a man give charity from a ṣāʿ of his wheat, and let him give charity from a ṣāʿ of his dates.” A man came with a purse and placed it down, then people followed one after another until a pile of clothes and food gathered. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lit up until it became as if it were gilded. Then he said: “Whoever introduces a good practice and it is acted upon after him, he will have its reward and the reward of those who act upon it, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever introduces an evil practice and it is acted upon after him, he will bear its burden and the burden of those who act upon it, without diminishing anything from their burdens.”"],[4375,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the ʿishāʾ prayer until the one who prayed had prayed, and the one who was asleep had awakened, and those who performed tahajjud had done so. Then he came out and said: “Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to pray at this time,” or “this prayer,” or something similar."],[4376,"A man may narrate a hadith intending no harm by it, only to make the people laugh, and because of it he will fall farther than the distance to the sky."],[4377,"ʿAlqamah took my hand, Ibn Masʿūd took ʿAlqamah’s hand, and the Prophet ﷺ took Ibn Masʿūd’s hand, [teaching] the tashahhud in prayer: “All greetings, prayers, and good things are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” Ibn Masʿūd said: “When you finish this, you have completed your prayer. If you wish, remain seated, and if you wish, depart.”"],[4378,"When My servant intends an evil deed but does not do it, do not record it; if he does it, record it as one. If he leaves it for My sake, record it as a good deed. When he intends a good deed but does not do it, record it as a good deed; if he does it, record it as ten times its like up to seven hundred-fold."],[4379,"The Hour will not come upon a believer; Allah will send a pleasant wind before the Hour, and it will blow, and no believer will remain but that he dies."],[4380,"I complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about forgetfulness in prayer. He said: 'When you pray and think that you have completed your prayer while you are in doubt, then recite the tashahhud and finish, then prostrate twice while sitting, then recite the tashahhud between them, and then finish.'"],[4381,"Allah has cursed the procrastinating women. It was said: 'O Prophet of Allah, who are the procrastinating women?' He said: 'The one whose husband calls her to his bed and she says, \"Later,\" until sleep overcomes his eyes.'"],[4382,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed one day by some graves, and with him was a fresh palm branch. He split it in two and placed one on a grave and the other on another grave, then he went on. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you do that?' He said: 'One of them was being punished for tale-bearing, and the other for not guarding against urine. They will not be punished as long as this remains fresh.'"],[4383,"He performed Hajj with him until he stood at Arafat. He said to him: 'O Maysarah, go up into the mountain.' He said: 'So I did. When the people departed, I went to urge my camel on, and he said: \"Wait, a moderate pace between the two paces.\" When I crossed the mountain, I said: 'Shall I stop, O Abu Abd al-Rahman?' He said: 'Go on, O Maysarah.' When we reached Muzdalifah, he stood and called the adhan, then the iqamah for prayer, and prayed Maghrib. Then he called the iqamah and prayed the later Isha prayer. Then we entered the morning and he did at the Mash'ar as he had done at the first Mash'ar. Then he said: \"The polytheists used not to depart from Arafat until the sun appeared on the mountains, becoming like the turbans of men on their faces. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used not to depart until the sun set. The polytheists used not to depart from Muzdalifah until they said: 'Shine, Thabir,' and they would not depart until the sun appeared on the mountaintops like the turbans of men on their faces. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to depart before the sun rose.\""],[4384,"Whoever walks to fulfill a need of his Muslim brother, Allah will shade him with seventy-five thousand angels who supplicate for him, and he will continue wading in mercy until he finishes. When he finishes, Allah writes for him a Hajj and an Umrah. Whoever visits a sick person, Allah shades him with seventy-five thousand angels; he does not lift a foot but a good deed is written for him, nor place a foot but a sin is removed from him and a degree raised for him, until he sits in his place. When he sits, mercy envelops him, and he remains so until he returns to his home."],[4385,"When a servant washes his hands, the sins of his hands depart. When he washes his face, rinses his mouth, cleans his teeth, sniffs water into his nose and blows it out, and wipes his head, the sins of his hearing, sight, and tongue depart. When he washes his forearms and feet, he becomes as on the day his mother gave birth to him. Whoever sleeps in a state of purity while remembering Allah, he will not ask Allah for anything of the affairs of this world or the Hereafter but that He gives it to him."],[4386,"I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I prayed the morning prayer with him in Mina. When he finished his prayer, there were two men behind the people who had not prayed with the people. He said: 'Bring the two men to me.' They were brought, trembling with fear. He said: 'Did you not pray with us?' They said: 'No, O Messenger of Allah, we had prayed in our camps and thought we would not catch the prayer.' He said: 'Do not do that. If you pray in your camps and then catch the prayer, pray it, and it will be a supererogatory prayer for you.' One of them said: 'Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'O Allah, forgive him.' The people crowded around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was then among the most youthful and strongest of men, so I pushed through the people until I took the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed it on my chest. I have never seen anything cooler or more fragrant than the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4387,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding the ghusl on Friday from this pulpit."],[4388,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding the ghusl on Friday."],[4389,"There is no deed more beloved to Allah than a deed done in these days, meaning the ten days, except a man who goes out as a mujahid with his wealth and his life, and then does not return."],[4390,"When the muezzin calls the adhan, Satan turns his back, passing wind. When he falls silent, he comes forward until he whispers between a man and his heart, making him remember what he had not been remembering, until he causes doubt in his prayer so he does not know how much he has prayed. When any of you encounters that and does not know how much he has prayed—whether he added or missed—let him prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness after he says the salam, for they are the two that humiliate Satan."],[4391,"Pray the first prayer before the time of ʿAsr enters, and ʿAsr before the sun turns yellow, and Maghrib before the twilight disappears, and the latter ʿIsha in the middle of the night, and Subh before sunrise."],[4392,"I asked ʿAʾishah about the night prayer of the Prophet ﷺ. She said: \"His water for ablution and his tooth-stick were placed for him, then Allah would awaken him whenever He willed to awaken him during the night. He would use the tooth-stick, perform ablution, then stand and pray nine rakʿahs, and two rakʿahs while sitting. And when he was ill or did not stand at night, he would pray twelve rakʿahs.\""],[4393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer one day. A man came with something until he was out of breath, until he entered the row, and said: \"Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise.\" When he finished, he said: \"Which of you said those words?\" The man said: \"I did.\" He said: \"Twelve angels raced to it, each vying to raise it.\""],[4394,"When you come to the prayer, come with tranquility and dignity. Pray what you catch up with, and make up what you missed."],[4395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw phlegm on the wall of the qiblah, and he became angry."],[4396,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the ʿIsha prayer one night until half the night, then he came out and led us in prayer. When he finished, he stood and addressed us, saying: \"The people have prayed and slept, while you are in prayer as long as you are waiting for the prayer.\""],[4397,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and ordered that it be announced that prayer was to be held in congregation. There he found two men arguing. He stood and addressed the people, saying: \"O people, I came out to inform you of the Night of Decree, but I encountered so-and-so and so-and-so arguing, and I forgot it. So seek it in the remaining ten nights, and seek it in the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth.\""],[4398,"She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in Makkah for some need of hers, and I found him praying Duha, six rakʿahs."],[4399,"I was cut off with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he mounted me on a camel. He passed by me while I was beating it at the rear of the people, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck it with a whip, and it remained at the front of the people. When we arrived in Makkah, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to return it to him, and I found him praying the Duha prayer, six rakʿahs."],[4400,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was asked about four rakʿahs before the Zuhr prayer, with no separation between them by the salam, when the sun declines. He said: \"It is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, and I love that a righteous deed ascend for me in it.\""],[4401,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, his sins and errors are expiated. When he begins walking, twenty good deeds are recorded for him with every step. When he finishes the prayer, he is rewarded with the deed of two hundred years."],[4402,"Whoever washes on Friday and performs a full bath, then goes early and arrives in good time, and draws near to where he can hear the imam's sermon, then remains silent, for every step he takes he will have the reward of a year's deeds—its fasting and its night prayer."],[4403,"We stopped with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at 'Usfan. The polytheists wanted to attack us while we were in the noon prayer. They said: 'But... there is a prayer that is dearer to them than their children, their lives, and their families, so you can attack them.' Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. When the prayer was called, the Messenger of Allah commanded the people, so they put on their weapons and formed two rows. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said takbir and they all said takbir. Then he bowed and they all bowed. Then he prostrated and the first row prostrated with him, while the other row remained standing. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, the first row stood with him, and those in the second row fell in prostration. When they finished the two prostrations and stood, the first row moved back and the second row moved forward. When the polytheists saw what they had done, they knew that the news had reached them. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said takbir and they all said takbir. Then he bowed and they all bowed. Then he prostrated and the first row prostrated, while the other row remained standing until they finished the two prostrations. Then the second row fell in prostration. Then they all sat and recited the tashahhud, then they departed."],[4404,"There will be rulers over you who delay the prayer. So pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them a supererogatory prayer."],[4405,"I have five names: I am Muhammad, Ahmad, al-Muqaffi, al-Hashir, the Prophet of Repentance, and the Prophet of the Great Battle."],[4406,"The thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer, and he does not drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer, and the fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer. But the doors of repentance are open."],[4407,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah said: 'We find in ourselves things that we would hate to speak of, even if we had all that the sun rises upon.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Have you really found that?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'That is pure faith.'"],[4408,"The most complete of the believers in faith is the best of them in character, and the best of you is the best of you to his family."],[4409,"I have been permitted to speak about an angel from the angels of Allah, one of the bearers of the Throne: the distance between his earlobe and his shoulder is a journey of seventy years."],[4410,"The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character, the gentle and easygoing ones, those who befriend and are befriended. And he is not one of us who does not befriend and is not befriended."],[4411,"We saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over the leather socks."],[4412,"He used to come to Quba' both riding and walking."],[4413,"I saw in a dream a black woman with disheveled hair, who came out until she stood at Mahya'a, which is al-Juhfa. I interpreted it that the epidemic of Madinah was transferred to al-Juhfa."],[4414,"The angels washed Adam and said the takbir over him four times, and they said: This is your sunnah, O children of Adam."],[4415,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, tell me a hadith and make it concise. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: Pray the prayer of one bidding farewell, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. Despair of what is in people’s hands and you will be rich. Beware of what requires an apology."],[4416,"An ʿumrah in Ramadan equals a hajj."],[4417,"A man should not sit between a man and his son in a gathering."],[4418,"The best mounts ridden to are this mosque of mine and the Ancient House."],[4419,"O ʿAli, these two are the masters of the middle-aged men of Paradise among the first and the last – meaning Abu Bakr and ʿUmar. Do not inform them of that, O ʿAli."],[4420,"The accepted hajj has no reward other than Paradise, and an ʿumrah to the next ʿumrah is an expiation for what is between them."],[4421,"A man will not leave faith except by denying what he entered into."],[4422,"I recited Surah al-Waqiʿah to the Prophet ﷺ, and when I reached “farawhun wa rayhanun,” the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “farawhun wa rayhanun, O Ibn ʿUmar.”"],[4423,"The boy is held in pledge by his ʿaqiqah; it is slaughtered on his behalf on his seventh day."],[4424,"The Prophet ﷺ said the takbir over his son Ibrahim four takbirs."],[4425,"A man’s greeting with one finger, pointing with it, is the action of the Jews."],[4426,"Whoever goes out with a funeral procession until it is buried will have two qirats of reward. It was asked: What is a qirat? He said: 'Like Mount Uhud.'"],[4427,"Whoever performs ablution and does it well, his sins depart from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet."],[4428,"There is no servant who performs ablution and washes his hands except that his sins depart from his hands; then he washes his face except that his sins depart from his face; then he washes his forearms except that his sins depart from his forearms; then he wipes his head except that his sins depart from his head; then he washes his feet except that his sins depart from his feet."],[4429,"Three types of people Allah hates: a lying king, an arrogant poor person, and a stingy rich person."],[4430,"I never prayed behind your Prophet ﷺ except that I heard him when he finished saying: 'O Allah, forgive me all my errors and sins. O Allah, raise me, mend me, and guide me to righteous deeds and character, for none guides to their righteousness and none turns away their evil from me except You.'"],[4431,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to go out with the army of such-and-such. He said: 'No.' She said: O Prophet of Allah, I do not want to fight; I only want to treat the wounded and the sick. He said: 'Were it not that it would become a sunnah, and it would be said: So-and-so went out, I would have permitted you.'"],[4432,"If any of you were to flee from his provision, it would overtake him just as death overtakes him."],[4433,"The angels curse any of you when he points an iron weapon at his brother, even if he is his brother from the same father and mother."],[4434,"I, Muhammad b. Ali, and another man from the Alawis entered upon Jabir b. Abdullah. He said: 'Who are you two?' The two Alawis identified themselves, and he recognized them, and I identified myself. He said: 'I do not know you.' I said: 'If you do not know me, then Allah knows me.' He said: 'What does Jabir's knowing you avail you?' I said: 'Pray with us as you saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Zuhr when the shadow was like a sandal strap, Asr when the shadow was like it and the extent of a sandal strap, Maghrib when the sun set, Isha when the twilight disappeared, and Fajr when dawn broke. Then the next day he prayed Zuhr when the shadow of everything was like it, then prayed Asr when the shadow of everything was twice its length, then prayed Maghrib when the sun set, then prayed Isha with the last third of the night.'"],[4435,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best?' He said: 'The one whose blood is shed and whose horse is hamstrung.'"],[4436,"The Messenger of Allah drew back a curtain and opened a door during his illness, and he looked at the people praying behind Abu Bakr. He was pleased with that and said: 'Praise be to Allah. No prophet dies until a man from his ummah leads him in prayer.' Then he turned to the people and said: 'O people, whoever among you is afflicted with a calamity after me, let him console himself with his calamity of losing me over the calamity that befalls him, for no one of my ummah after me will be afflicted with the like of the calamity of losing me.'"],[4437,"For every joint, or for every organ, of the son of Adam each day there is a charity, and the two rak'ahs of Duha suffice for all of that."],[4438,"When he prayed, he would spread out his left (foot) and stand his right (foot) upright."],[4439,"Travel is a portion of torment; it prevents one of you from his sleep, his food, his drink, and his pleasure. So when one of you finishes his need, let him hasten to his family."],[4440,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: “May a fasting person kiss?” He said: “And what harm is that? It is a fragrant sprig he smells.”"],[4441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have cupping done on the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first of the month."],[4442,"The prayer was two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs when it was made obligatory; then it was increased in the prayer of residence, and the prayer of travel was left upon the first obligation."],[4443,"Indeed the Magians of this community are those who deny Allah’s decrees. If they fall ill, do not visit them; if you meet them, do not greet them; and if they die, do not attend their funerals."],[4444,"In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a person would pray and his gaze would not go beyond the place of his feet."],[4445,"Center the imam and close the gaps, lest Satan pass through them; and place your sandals between your feet."],[4446,"I said to al-Rubayyiʿ bt. Muʿawwidh b. ʿAfraʾ: “Describe the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to me.” She said: “Had you seen him, you would have seen the sun rising.”"],[4447,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and looked at the seal of prophethood between his shoulders."],[4448,"A slave was owned by ten people. He freed nine of them, and the tenth refused to free his share. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, what about my share?” He said: “Your share is in him.”"],[4449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived and circumambulated the House, prayed two rakʿahs behind the Station of Ibrahim, and walked between Safa and Marwah. “Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have a good example.”"],[4450,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent my maternal uncle to a man from Yemen who had married his father's wife. He said: 'If you catch up with him, strike his neck and confiscate his wealth.'"],[4451,"The Prophet ﷺ entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah, wearing a black turban."],[4452,"Regarding 'Their mark is on their faces from the trace of prostration,' he said: 'It is light on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[4453,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution, and he ran his fingers through his beard from beneath his chin, and he said: 'This is what my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me.'"],[4454,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I desire to go on jihad, but I am unable to.' He said: 'Are either of your parents still alive?' He said: 'My mother.' He said: 'Then give God an excuse in your devotion to her. If you do that, you are a pilgrim, a performer of ʿumrah, and a mujahid, if your mother is pleased. So fear God and be devoted to her.'"],[4455,"The Prophet ﷺ would not rise from a gathering until he said: 'Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You.' Then he would say: 'Indeed this is an expiation for what occurs in the gathering.'"],[4456,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade squatting on one's heels in prayer."],[4457,"He forbade fasting on three days: advancing a day before the moon is sighted, the day of sacrifice, and the day of breaking the fast."],[4458,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said while the sun was rising: 'Do you know where this rises, O Abu Dharr?' I said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'It rises and sets, then it runs to its resting place, and it comes to the Throne and falls down prostrating, until it is said to it: Rise from your rising place. And it had been said to it: Return from where you came. Then it will rise from the west, and that is when no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith' (the verse)."],[4459,"Modesty and faith are joined together; they only depart together."],[4460,"Whoever commits a sin and knows that God has seen it, it will be forgiven for him even if he does not seek forgiveness."],[4461,"We entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ on a Friday, and there was food in front of him from which he was eating. He said: 'Come close and eat from this food.' I said, or one of us said: 'We are fasting, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Did you fast yesterday?' We said: 'No.' He said: 'Do you intend to fast tomorrow?' We said: 'No.' He said: 'Then come close and eat from this food, for Friday is not to be fasted alone; it is taken as a festival.'"],[4462,"I brought good news to Bilal, and he said to me: O ʿAbdullah, what good news do you bring me? I said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Bilal will come on the Day of Resurrection riding a mount of gold, its rein of pearl and ruby, with a banner, and the muʾadhdhins will follow him, and he will admit them into Paradise, so much so that he will admit one who called the adhan for forty mornings, seeking thereby the countenance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[4463,"Any young man who marries in the prime of his youth but his devil cries out: Woe to him, woe to him, he has protected his religion from me."],[4464,"If there remained of my appointed time but a single day, I would meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with a wife, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The worst of you are your unmarried ones."],[4465,"Muʿadh b. Jabal used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, then he would come to his people and lead them in the prayer he had prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4466,"When al-Hajjaj entered upon her, it was said to her: This is the commander al-Hajjaj. She said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: In Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer. As for the liar, we have seen him, and as for the destroyer, you are he."],[4467,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: O Ibn Masʿud, which bond of faith is firmest? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The firmest bond of Islam is allegiance for the sake of Allah, love for His sake, and hatred for His sake. Then he said: O Ibn Masʿud. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said it three times. He said: Do you know which of the people is best? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The best of people are the best of them in deeds when they have understanding in their religion. Then he said: O Ibn Masʿud. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, three times. He said: Do you know which of the people is most knowledgeable? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The most knowledgeable of people is the one most perceptive of the truth when people differ, even if he is deficient in deeds, and even if he crawls on his backside. Those before me divided into seventy-two sects; three of them were saved and the rest perished. A sect that sided with the kings and fought them for their religion and the religion of Jesus son of Mary; they seized them, killed them, and cut them with saws. A sect that had no power to oppose the kings nor to remain among them calling them to the religion of Allah and the religion of Jesus son of Mary, so they wandered in the lands and became monks. He said: They are those of whom Allah said: And monasticism, which they innovated; We did not prescribe it for them—the verse. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever believes in me, follows me, and has affirmed me has observed it as it should be observed, and whoever does not follow me, those are the ones who perish."],[4468,"May Allah protect you from rulers who will come after me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is that? He said: Whoever enters upon them, confirms their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Pond. But whoever does not enter upon them, does not confirm their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing, that one is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at my Pond. No flesh that grows from ill-gotten gains will enter Paradise; every flesh that grows from ill-gotten gains, the Fire is more worthy of it. People go forth in the morning: one sells himself and destroys it, and one ransoms himself and sets it free. Prayer is a proof, fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire."],[4469,"We said: O Messenger of Allah, this greeting upon you, we have learned how to greet you, but how is the prayer upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, bestow blessing upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You bestowed blessing upon Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."],[4470,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I honor most? He said: Your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your father, then the nearest relative, then the next nearest."],[4471,"When one of you prostrates, let him keep straight and not spread his forearms as a dog spreads them."],[4472,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell from a horse of his in Madinah and his foot was dislocated. We came to visit him while he was in an upper room of ʿAʾishah, sitting. We stood behind him and prayed. Then we came to him another time and found him sitting, performing the prescribed prayer. We stood behind him, and he gestured with his hand: Sit. When he finished the prayer, he said: When your imam prays standing, pray standing, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting, and do not stand while he is sitting as the Persians do with their great ones."],[4473,"We used to sell in Madinah and call ourselves brokers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by us and called us by a name better than what we called ourselves. He said: O company of merchants, these sales are attended by idle talk or swearing, so mix them with charity."],[4474,"Indeed, the purest of what a man eats is from his own earnings, and indeed his child is from his earnings."],[4475,"Umarah b. Umayr informed me, from his paternal aunt, from A'ishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: the like of that. None of these hadiths are reported from Umar b. Sa'id except by Ibrahim b. Tahman; Ahmad b. Hafs was alone in transmitting them."],[4476,"Whoever swears a false oath by which he seizes the property of a Muslim, he will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him."],[4477,"A questioner asked the Prophet ﷺ: Does anything obligate ghusl other than water [i.e., semen]? He said: When the two circumcised parts meet and the glans disappears, ghusl becomes obligatory, whether he ejaculates or not."],[4478,"He forbade mutilation."],[4479,"There is no marriage except with a guardian, and any woman who marries without a guardian, her marriage is invalid."],[4480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[4481,"A woman is not to be married in addition to her maternal aunt, nor the maternal aunt in addition to her sister's daughter; a woman is not to be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor the paternal aunt in addition to her brother's daughter; not the younger in addition to the elder, nor the elder in addition to the younger."],[4482,"Rabi'ah came to the Prophet ﷺ asking his permission for the first departure. Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: O Muhammad, Allah conveys peace to you and says to Rabi'ah: Do not depart in the first departure, for no small number of a beloved is insignificant."],[4483,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah. He said: Have you performed Hajj? He said: No. He said: Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah."],[4484,"No one hoards except a sinner."],[4485,"The daughter of the Prophet ﷺ died, and he said: Wash her three times, or five, or more than that if you see fit, with water and lote-tree leaves, and put some camphor in the last wash. When you have finished, inform me. So when we finished, we informed him, and he threw to us his waist-wrapper and said: Shroud her with it."],[4486,"Every one of my Ummah is pardoned, except he who does a deed at night and then comes to the morning while his Lord has concealed it, and says: O so-and-so, I did such and such last night; or he said: He spent the night with his Lord concealing it, and he arises in the morning and tears away the veil of Allah from himself."],[4487,"Regarding His saying: “And from [part of] the night, pray with it as an additional prayer for you,” he said: The additional prayer was only for the Prophet ﷺ."],[4488,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the snake and said: It and the human were created equal. If it sees him, it frightens him, and if it bites him, it causes him pain, so kill it wherever you find it."],[4489,"We used to eat with the Prophet ﷺ and we would hear the food glorifying Allah."],[4490,"We were with ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz on the day of Eid al-Fitr, and he brought out dates to us and said: Eat before you go out. We said to him: Do you have something about this? He said: Yes."],[4491,"Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant and he knows that it is from Allah, except that Allah writes for him gratitude for it before he praises Him for it. And a servant does not commit a sin and then regret it, except that Allah writes for him forgiveness before he seeks forgiveness from Him. And a servant does not buy a garment for a dinar or half a dinar and praise Allah when he wears it, except that it does not reach his knees before Allah forgives him."],[4492,"Whoever relieves a believer of a distress, Allah, the Exalted, will make for him on the Day of Resurrection two branches of light on the Ṣirāṭ, by whose light a world will be illuminated that none can count except the Lord of Might."],[4493,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and there were two cushions in the house with images on them. He said: “What is this, O ʿĀʾishah?” She said: I made them so that you could recline on them. He said: “Do you not know that the image-makers will be told on the Day of Resurrection: Bring to life what you have created?”"],[4494,"\"He whom Allah has given a handsome face, a good name, and placed him in a position that is not shameful for him, he is among the elite of Allah, Mighty and Sublime, from His creation.\" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \"The poet said: You are the condition of the Prophet when he said one day: Seek good in those with handsome faces.\""],[4495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a caller on a rainy day: “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[4496,"When you carry, delay, for the leg is bound and the hand is suspended."],[4497,"Abū Bakr led the people in prayer, and the Prophet ﷺ came out and prayed behind him in the row, wrapped in a single garment."],[4498,"She said: O Messenger of God, you will return with a Hajj and an ʿUmrah while I return with a Hajj only? So he ordered her brother, and he went out with her, and she performed ʿUmrah."],[4499,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, God will command a caller, who will call out: I have established a lineage, and you have established a lineage; I have made the noblest of you the most God-fearing of you, but you refused unless you say: So-and-so son of so-and-so is better than so-and-so son of so-and-so. Today I shall raise up My lineage and cast down your lineages. Where are the God-fearing?"],[4500,"A Jew had a debt of four dirhams against me, and he pressed me for it while the Messenger of God ﷺ was about to set out for Khaybar. I asked him to wait until I returned, saying: Perhaps we may gain some spoils. He then brought me before the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: Give him his due—twice. I said: O Messenger of God, you intend to set out for Khaybar, and perhaps God will grant us spoils there. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Give him his due. When the Prophet ﷺ said something three times, he was not to be contradicted. He said: I was wearing a waist-wrapper and had a headband on my head. When I went out, I said: Buy this waist-wrapper from me, and he bought it for the dirhams he was owed. I then wrapped myself in the headband that was on my head. A woman passed by wearing a cloak, and she clothed me with it."],[4501,"God has forbidden the singing-girl, her sale, her price, her instruction, and listening to her."],[4502,"The women of the Emigrants used to pray the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, then return wrapped in their cloaks, unrecognizable due to the darkness."],[4503,"A child died during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and it was said: A sparrow from among the sparrows of Paradise. ʿĀʾishah said: Glad tidings to him, O Messenger of God. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: Do you not know that God created Paradise and created the Fire, and created for this one its people and for that one its people?"],[4504,"A man prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and began to bow before he bowed and rise before he rose. When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he said: Who did this? He said: I, O Messenger of God; I wanted to know whether you were aware of that or not. He said: Beware of incompleteness in prayer; when the imam bows, bow, and when he rises, rise."],[4505,"It was recited before ʿUmar: Whenever their skins are roasted through, We shall replace them with other skins. ʿUmar said: Repeat it. He repeated it. Muʿādh b. Jabal said: I have its interpretation: It is replaced a hundred times in an hour. ʿUmar said: Thus I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4506,"The Prophet ﷺ entered al-Jiʿrānah, and the people of al-Jiʿrānah knew of his entering; they gathered around him and became numerous. He raised his hands, and it was as if I were looking at the whiteness of his armpits and sides, like the whiteness of silver bars. He said: O people, get away from me. They moved away from him until he reached the mosque. He performed as many rakʿahs as God willed, then mounted his riding camel and set out toward the valley of Sarif until he reached the road to Madinah, and by morning he was at Makkah as if he had spent the night there."],[4507,"Abū Ṭalḥah declared his intention for Hajj and ʿUmrah with a loud cry while his knee touched the knee of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4508,"The fornicatresses who marry themselves off; no marriage is valid without a guardian, two witnesses, and a dowry, whether small or large."],[4509,"I was present with ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib and al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib while they were presenting their dispute to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb concerning the inheritance of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The people said: Judge between them, O Commander of the Believers. ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said: God Almighty says in His Book: Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies God, and He is the Mighty, the Wise, and he recited until His words: And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, abstain from it. Then he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to place it among the poor, the orphans, the wayfarer, the guests of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and his horsemen until the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away. Abū Bakr then took charge of it, and then I took charge of it, and I placed it where the Messenger of God ﷺ used to place it and where Abū Bakr did. Now it has occurred to me to entrust it to you, O ʿAlī, so place it where you saw the Messenger of God ﷺ place it and where you saw me place it."],[4510,"Time will draw near, and knowledge will decrease."],[4511,"The Messenger of God ﷺ disliked the lamp when morning came."],[4512,"The Messenger of God ﷺ amputated for a quarter of a dinar."],[4513,"Whoever performs ablution, it is good and excellent; and whoever bathes, the bath is better."],[4514,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote to them: 'Do not make use of anything from the carcass.'"],[4515,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered Abu Taybah, so he placed the cupping glasses at sunset, then ordered him at the time of the fasting person's breaking, and he cupped him. Then he asked him: 'How much is your due?' He said: 'Two sa's.' So the Prophet ﷺ placed for him one sa'."],[4516,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military expedition. When the people returned, among them was a man recently married. He hastened to his family and found his wife standing at her door. He aimed a spear at her to thrust her, but she said: 'Do not be hasty; look at what is in the house.' He entered the house and found a snake coiled on her bed. He struck its head with the spear, but the snake did not die until the man died. This reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'These houses have inhabitants from the jinn.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing the snakes that are in houses, except the short-tailed one and the one with two white stripes."],[4517,"That al-Zubayr gave a will to [...] on the morning of the Day of the Camel, saying: 'There is no limb of my limbs but it has been wounded with the Messenger of God ﷺ, until that reached even his private part.'"],[4518,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: 'For the resident, a day and a night; and for the traveler, three days and their nights.'"],[4519,"Whoever breaks the fast on a day of Ramadan and dies before making it up, then for each day a mudd is due to a poor person."],[4520,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and he began to combine the noon and afternoon prayers, and the sunset and evening prayers."],[4521,"When he departed before the sun declined, he delayed the noon prayer until he prayed it with the afternoon prayer; and when he departed after the sun had declined, he hastened the afternoon prayer so that he prayed them together. And when he departed before sunset, he delayed the sunset prayer until he prayed them together; and when he departed after sunset, he prayed it with the sunset prayer."],[4522,"Indeed, the parable of the believer is like a tree whose leaves do not fall in winter or summer. The people mentioned many trees, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is the date-palm.\""],[4523,"Whoever does not accept Allah's concession, upon him is sin like the mountains of Arafat."],[4524,"Fasting is a shield as long as one does not tear it. It was said: \"With what does one tear it?\" He said: \"With lying or backbiting.\""],[4525,"Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty or is lenient with him, Allah will shade him in His shade."],[4526,"Sa'd b. Zurara said: \"O people, do you know what you are pledging to Muhammad ﷺ? You are pledging to fight the Arabs and non-Arabs, the jinn and mankind.\" They said: \"We are at war with those who wage war, and at peace with those who make peace.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, stipulate.\" He said: \"You pledge to me that you will testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, give zakat, hear and obey, not dispute the matter with its people, and protect me as you protect yourselves and your families.\""],[4527,"He used to wear a ring on his right hand."],[4528,"There is no zakat on less than five uqiyyas, no zakat on less than five awsuq, and no zakat on less than five camels."],[4529,"When he saw a man with a disfigured appearance, he prostrated; when he saw a monkey, he prostrated; and when he rose from sleep, he prostrated to Allah."],[4530,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Qatada al-Ansari to collect zakat, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions set out in ihram until they camped at Usfan. There they saw a wild donkey. Abu Qatada came while he was not in ihram. They lowered their heads, disliking to direct their eyes lest he notice. He saw it, mounted his horse, and took the spear, but it fell from him. He said: \"Hand it to me.\" We said: \"We will not help you with it in any way.\" He charged at it and wounded it. Then they began roasting from it. Then they said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is among us.\" He had gone ahead of them, so they caught up with him and asked him, and he saw no harm in it."],[4531,"An umrah to the next umrah is expiation for what is between them, and an accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[4532,"On the day of Uhud, they brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a water skin, and he urinated beside the water skin, then drank from it."],[4533,"Adam and Musa (peace be upon them) argued."],[4534,"Whoever comes to me as a visitor, with no need driving him except to visit me, it is incumbent upon me to be an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[4535,"Cupping on the head is a remedy for madness, leprosy, leukoderma, drowsiness, and toothache."],[4536,"A boy came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I intend to go to that direction—for Hajj.” He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked with him and said, “O boy, may Allah provision you with taqwa, direct you to good, and suffice you against worry.” When the boy returned and greeted the Prophet ﷺ, he raised his head toward him and said, “O boy, may Allah accept your Hajj, expiate your sin, and replace what you spent.”"],[4537,"Our freed slaves are from us."],[4538,"Indeed a man may utter a word that is pleasing to Allah, giving it no thought, and because of it Allah will record him as one of the people of His good pleasure until the Day of Resurrection. And indeed a man may utter a word that brings Allah’s wrath, giving it no thought, and because of it Allah will record him as one of the people of His wrath until the day he meets Him."],[4539,"I would be sleeping with my legs in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying at night. When he wanted to prostrate, he would poke my leg, so I would draw them in and he would prostrate."],[4540,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began the prayer, he would say: “I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, as a hanif and a Muslim, and I am not of the polytheists. O Allah, You are the Sovereign; there is no god but You. Glory be to You and praise. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have acknowledged my sin, so forgive me all my sins; none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character; none guides to it but You. Avert from me its evil; none averts it but You. Here I am at Your service, all good is in Your hands, and I am through You and to You. There is no escape from You except to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would recite. When he bowed he said: “O Allah, to You I have bowed, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. You are my Lord. My hearing, my sight, my bones, my marrow, and what my feet carry have humbled themselves to Allah, Lord of the worlds.” When he raised his head he said: “Allah hears the one who praises Him.” Then he would say: “Our Lord, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will besides.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would prostrate and say: “O Allah, to You I have prostrated, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. You are my Lord. My face has prostrated to the One who created it, and fashioned its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the best of creators.”"],[4541,"Indeed a man may utter a word that is pleasing to Allah, giving it no thought, and because of it Allah will record him as one of the people of His good pleasure until the Day of Resurrection. And indeed a man may utter a word that brings Allah’s wrath, giving it no thought, and because of it Allah will record him as one of the people of His wrath until the day he meets Him."],[4542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I used to perform ghusl together from one vessel due to janabah."],[4543,"I said to Ibn ʿAbbas: We pray with you in the mosque, but when we pray in our dwellings we pray two rakʿahs? He said: That is the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ."],[4544,"Maʿiz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said that he had committed adultery. He turned away from him, but he repeated it to him several times, and he turned away from him. Then he asked his people, “Is he insane?” They said, “There is nothing wrong with him.” He said, “Did you do it with her?” He said, “Yes.” So he ordered that he be stoned. He was taken away and stoned, and he did not pray over him."],[4545,"Al-ʿayfah does not create prohibition. We said: What is al-ʿayfah? He said: A woman gives birth, and milk becomes scanty in her breasts, so she breastfeeds her neighbor once or twice."],[4546,"On the day of Hunayn, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Now the oven is heated.” Then he said: “They are defeated, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah; they are defeated, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah.”"],[4547,"Indeed, the creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's belly for forty nights."],[4548,"There is no servant who, when he reaches the morning and when he reaches the evening, says: 'O Allah, You are my Lord; there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I acknowledge Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge my sins, so forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins but You' — if he dies that day, he will enter Paradise, and if he dies that night, he will enter Paradise."],[4549,"\"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of every month, performing the Friday bath, and not sleeping except after praying Witr.\" Al-Zubayr said: 'I have not abandoned them since I heard them from Abu Hurayrah.' And 'Amr said: 'I have not abandoned them since I heard them from Abu (Hurayrah).'"],[4550,"He used to travel with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with Abu Bakr and 'Umar, from Madinah to Makkah. All of them prayed two rak'ahs from the time he left Madinah until he returned to Madinah, both while traveling and while staying in Makkah."],[4551,"When we were in the presence of the enemy with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one of us would be more concerned about checking the knee of his brother as he advanced in the ranks for battle than about his own arrow when it was shot. He would say: 'Move your knee back, for I am seeking (reward) just as you are seeking.' Allah, Exalted is He, said: 'As if they were a solid structure.'"],[4552,"Indeed, it is from the Sunnah of prayer that one stands his right foot upright and lays his left foot on its side."],[4553,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted at al-Hijr, he said: 'Do not enter upon these people who were punished.' Then he ordered the dough, and it was thrown away."],[4554,"Indeed, in Paradise there is a rolling place of musk, like the rolling place of your animals in this world."],[4555,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was complaining, so I said: 'Oh, my head!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is it upon you if that were (to happen), that I should take care of you and attend to you myself?' I said: 'It is as if I can see you, if that were to happen, you would already be consummating marriage with one of your wives.' She said: 'I had not reached evening on that day before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rather, I say: Oh, my head! So call for me your father and the men, for people will wish (for leadership), but Allah and the believers will refuse anyone except Abu Bakr.\""],[4556,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, and Abu Bakr was standing at his head, he said: 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, indeed Abu Quhafah is a very old man, and he is on the outskirts of Makkah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Let us go to him.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, he is more deserving of coming to you.' So Abu Quhafah was brought, his beard and head as white as the thaghamah plant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Change it (the hair) and keep it away from black.'"],[4557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us wearing his garment wrapped around him, and its two ends did not reach, so he tied them."],[4558,"When a Muslim man says to his brother: 'O disbeliever,' then one of them has returned with disbelief."],[4559,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his Companions: “Among trees, there is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it is the one struck as a parable for the believing servant. What is it?” They began mentioning trees of the valley. He said: “It is the date-palm.” ʿAbd Allah said: “It occurred to me, but I was too shy to tell.”"],[4561,"Give every surah its due of bowing and prostration, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited only twenty surahs in ten rakʿahs."],[4562,"The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud just as he taught us a surah of the Qur'an, saying: “Learn it, for there is no prayer without tashahhud.”"],[4563,"Do not swear by your fathers, nor by your mothers, nor by rivals [to Allah], and do not swear by Allah unless you are truthful."],[4564,"Whoever forgets to mention Allah's name at the beginning of his food, let him say when he remembers: “In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end,” for he begins a new meal and it prevents the evil one from whatever he would have gotten from it."],[4565,"No people withhold zakah but Allah afflicts them with years of drought."],[4566,"Al-ʿAbbas and ʿAli came to Abu Bakr when he was appointed caliph, seeking their inheritance from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿAli came seeking Fatimah's share, and al-ʿAbbas came seeking his share of what had been in the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ possession. Abu Bakr said: “I do not think that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: ‘We, the company of prophets, do not inherit. What we leave is charity.’” A group of the Prophet's ﷺ Companions stood and testified to that. They said: “Then leave it in our hands as it was in the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ hand.” He said: “I do not think that. I am the guardian after him, and I am more entitled to it than you two. I will place it where the Prophet ﷺ used to place it.” He refused to hand anything over to them. When ʿUmar became caliph, they came to him. He said: “It is as if I am with ʿUmar when wealth came to him, and he said: ‘Take this wealth and distribute it among your people,’ when permission came to him. He said: ‘There are people at the door from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ He said: ‘Give them permission.’ They entered and sat. Then he came to him and said: ‘ʿAli and al-ʿAbbas are at the door.’ He said: ‘Give them permission.’ They entered. ʿUmar said: ‘What has brought you two? Did you not seek from Abu Bakr what he did not hand over to you?’ They went back and forth with him about it. He said: ‘I will hand it over to you on condition that I take from you a covenant and solemn promise that you will do with it what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do.’ So they took it, and he gave it to them, and they received it. They remained as long as Allah willed, then they disputed between themselves and brought the case to ʿUmar, while with him were people from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. They argued before him and said whatever Allah willed they said. Some of the Prophet's ﷺ Companions said: ‘O Commander of the Faithful, judge between them and relieve each of them from the other.’ ʿUmar said: ‘By Allah, I will never judge in this matter except as I judged before. If you two are unable to handle it, return it to me as I handed it to you.’ So they rose from his presence.”"],[4567,"The disbeliever will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection until sweat bridles him, until he says: “O Lord, give me relief, even if to the Fire.”"],[4568,"Allah has not sent down to the earth since He created Adam until the Hour comes a tribulation greater than the tribulation of the Dajjal. I have said about him something no one has said before: He is Adam-like, curly-haired, his left eye is wiped out, and over his eye is a thick membrane. He will heal the blind and the leper and say: “I am your lord.” Whoever says: “My Lord is Allah,” there is no tribulation upon him, and whoever says: “You are my lord,” has been tried. He will remain among you as long as Allah wills, then ʿIsa son of Maryam will descend, confirming Muhammad ﷺ, and upon his religion he died, as a rightly guided imam and a just judge, and he will kill the Dajjal."],[4569,"Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of a complete light on the Day of Resurrection."],[4570,"Whoever leads a people in prayer while among them is one more versed in the Book of Allah than him, he will not cease to be in lowliness until the Day of Resurrection."],[4571,"Trials are coming to you like patches of a dark night: a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning, selling his religion for a small portion of worldly goods.” I said: “What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Break your hand.” I said: “If it heals?” He said: “Break the other.” I said: “If it heals?” He said: “Break your leg.” I said: “If it heals?” He said: “Break the other.” I said: “Until when?” He said: “Until a sinning hand comes to you or a decisive death.”"],[4572,"I saw ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb urinate, then wipe his penis with dust, then turn to us and say: This is how we were taught."],[4573,"I asked Anas b. Mālik: O Abā Ḥamzah, a man among us lends money and then receives a gift. He replied: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: If one of you lends and then is given a gift or is mounted on an animal, let him not accept it nor ride it, unless that was already customary between them before that."],[4574,"I was favored over those before me with five qualities: I was sent to all people, the red and the black; the earth was made a place of prayer and a means of purification for me; I was aided with terror cast a month's journey ahead; spoils of war were made lawful for me, though they were not lawful for anyone before me; and it was said to me: Ask, and you shall be given. So I delayed my intercession for my community until the Day of Resurrection."],[4575,"Whoever strikes his slave with a ḥadd punishment for an offense the slave did not commit, his expiation is to set the slave free."],[4576,"The wife of Thābit b. Qays b. Shammās obtained a khulʿ divorce from him, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to observe a waiting period of one menstrual cycle."],[4577,"We used to consider al-māʿūn to be: the ax, the cooking pot, and the bucket."],[4578,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the effeminate men and said: Expel them from your homes."],[4579,"Indeed, God, Mighty and Majestic, is modest and generous: He is ashamed, when His servant raises his hands to Him, to turn them back empty, with nothing in them."],[4580,"Whoever would be pleased for God to save him from the anguish of the Day of Resurrection, and to shade him under His Throne, let him give respite to one in financial difficulty."],[4581,"Black seed is a remedy for every disease except al-sām. They said: And what is al-sām, O Messenger of God? He said: Death."],[4582,"Whoever recites the Mother of the Qurʾān and Qul Huwa Allāhu Aḥad, it is as if he has recited a third of the Qurʾān."],[4583,"A man came to some people while they were praying, and Ibn ʿUmar was sitting behind them on something. He said: O Abā ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, what prevents you from praying? He said: I have already prayed, and we have been forbidden to pray twice in one day."],[4584,"The open spaces around the mosque became vacant, so the Banū Salima wanted to be near the mosque. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “O Banū Salima, your dwellings [are recorded]—your traces are written for you.” He said it three times."],[4585,"Three men from a group set out, and rain overtook them, so they took refuge in a cave. While they were in it, a boulder from the heart of the mountain rolled down until it sealed the cave. The people said to one another: “The rain has stopped, the trace has been erased, and no one has seen you except God. Let each man among you consider the best deed he has ever done, mention it, and then supplicate God.” One of them said: “O God, if You know that I was dutiful to my parents, and that I used to bring them their evening drink and give it to them, and that one night I came to them with their evening drink but found that they had gone to their beds and fallen asleep, and I disliked waking them from their sleep, and I disliked returning with their evening drink before giving it to them, and that remained my habit and theirs until dawn broke—if You know that only fear of You carried me to do that, then open a way for us.” He said: It opened until the light entered upon them. The second said: “O God, I sought a woman and desired her, and I spent my wealth on her until when I had won her and sat from her as a man sits from a woman, she said to me: ‘It is not lawful for you to break my seal except by its right.’ So I got up and left her. If You know that only fear of You carried me to do that, then open a way for us.” The boulder tilted and opened until, had the people wished to leave, they could have left. The third said: “O God, You know that I hired laborers, and they did work for me, and I paid them their wages except for one man who left his wage until it multiplied many times over. He came afterward and demanded his wage. I said to him: ‘Take all that is before you, the full amount of your wage.’ If You know that fear of You carried me to do that, then open a way for us.” He said: The boulder tilted and rolled away, and they departed embracing one another."],[4586,"When a woman performs her five [daily prayers], fasts her month [of Ramadan], guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, she will enter from whichever of the gates of Paradise she wishes."],[4587,"A child does not inherit until he cries out loudly, and his crying out is that he screams, sneezes, or weeps."],[4588,"When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, he would say: “O God, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.”"],[4589,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came from the outskirts of Madinah intending to pray, but found that the people had already prayed. So he went to his house, gathered his family, and prayed with them."],[4590,"Whoever reviles the prophets is to be killed, and whoever reviles my companions is to be flogged."],[4591,"A judge does not judge between two parties except while he is full and quenched."],[4592,"There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."],[4593,"While I was in Paradise, I heard the voice of a man reciting the Quran. I said: “Who is this?” They said: “This is Ḥāritha b. al-Nuʿmān.” Thus is righteousness, thus is righteousness, thus is righteousness. And Ḥāritha was among the most righteous of people."],[4594,"I am the Most Merciful. I created the womb and derived its name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I will maintain him, and whoever severs it, I will sever him."],[4595,"People are like a hundred camels: you can hardly find among them a single riding camel."],[4596,"Abdullah b. Umar used to walk in front of the funeral procession. He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to walk in front of it, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman.\""],[4597,"He heard Hassan b. Thabit al-Ansari adjuring Abu Hurayrah, saying: \"O Abu Hurayrah, I ask you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O Hassan, respond on behalf of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit'?\""],[4598,"He saw Umm Kulthum bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing a striped silk Burd."],[4599,"She was married to a man from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj. He went out seeking some runaway slaves of his, and he caught up with them at the edge of al-Qadum. They attacked him and killed him. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking his permission to leave my house, and he said: 'Wait until the prescribed period reaches its term.'"],[4600,"Allah has not sent any prophet nor appointed any caliph but that he has two inner circles: an inner circle that commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and an inner circle that spares no effort to corrupt him. Whoever is protected from the evil inner circle is indeed protected."],[4601,"He used to supplicate in prayer: 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from sin and debt.' They said: 'How often you seek refuge from debt!' He said: 'When a man incurs debt, he speaks and lies, and promises and breaks his promise.'"],[4602,"There is no contagion. A bedouin stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of camels that are in the sand like gazelles, then a mangy camel comes to them and they all become mangy?' He said: 'Then who infected the first one?'"],[4603,"Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call."],[4604,"The day of Ashura was a day that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered to be fasted before Ramadan was made obligatory. Then whoever wished fasted it, and whoever wished broke the fast."],[4605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Sa'd b. Ubadah to fulfill a vow that had been upon his mother, who died before she could fulfill it."],[4606,"They used to eat the meat of sacrificial animals for three days during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, not exceeding that. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them after that to eat and to take provisions."],[4607,"Usamah b. Zayd and Zayd b. Harithah were both there. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me joyful, so I said: 'What is the matter, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Mujazziz just passed by Zayd and Usamah and saw their feet, and he said: These feet are from one another.'"],[4608,"that he looked out from his house while the people were praying, reciting aloud, and he said to them: \"The one praying is in intimate conversation with his Lord, so let him consider what he is conversing with. None of you should raise his voice over the others with the Qur'an.\""],[4609,"Anas b. Malik was asked about selling fruit, and he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling fruit until it ripens."],[4610,"The affliction makes its owner's face white on the day when faces turn black."],[4611,"that the Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning the cupping point in the middle of the head: It is a remedy for insanity, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and toothache. He used to call it \"the rescuer.\""],[4612,"that some men from the Ansar asked permission of the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: Grant us permission, O Messenger of God, to leave the ransom for our nephew Abbas. He said: \"No, by God, you will not pay a single dirham for him.\""],[4613,"The excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."],[4614,"regarding a lost animal, that he used to say: O God, Returner of the lost, Guide out of misguidance, You guide from misguidance; return to me my lost animal by Your might and Your authority, for it is from Your gift and Your bounty."],[4615,"A Jewish woman entered upon me and talked to me, and among her words she said: Yes, by the One who protects you from the trial of the grave. She said: I rebuked her and said: This is not the first of your lies against God and His Messenger. If there were punishment in the grave, God would have informed His Prophet ﷺ. The Jewish woman said: We claim that it has punishment. Aisha said: When the Prophet of God ﷺ entered upon me, I told him what she had said, but he did not reply to me at all. Then, after that, he said: O Aisha, seek refuge in God from the punishment of the grave; for if anyone would have been saved from it, Sa'd b. Mu'adh would have been saved, but it was only a squeezing."],[4616,"The Prophet of God ﷺ passed by the graves of some women of Banu al-Najjar who had died in the pre-Islamic era, and he heard them being punished in their graves for talebearing."],[4617,"We attended a funeral with the Prophet of God ﷺ. When he finished burying it and the people had left, the Prophet of God ﷺ said: He can now hear the sound of your sandals. Munkar and Nakir came to him, their eyes like copper pots, their fangs like the horns of cattle, and their voices like thunder. They sit him up and ask him what he used to worship and who his prophet was. If he was one who worshipped God, he says: I used to worship God, and the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ came with clear proofs, so we believed and followed. That is the word of God: \"God makes firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter.\" It is said to him: Upon certainty you lived, upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised. Then a door to Paradise is opened for him, and his grave is expanded for him. But if he was one of the people of doubt, he says: I do not know; I heard people saying something, so I said it. It is said to him: Upon doubt you lived, upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised. Then a door to the Fire is opened for him, and scorpions and serpents are set upon him. If one of them were to breathe in this world, nothing would ever grow. They bite him, and the earth is commanded to squeeze him until his ribs interlock."],[4618,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ captured us on the day of Hunayn, the day of Hawazin, and went to distribute the spoils and the sheep, I recited this poetry to him: Bestow favor upon us, O Messenger of God, in generosity; for you are the man we hope in and await. Bestow favor upon a remnant whom fate has hindered, whose unity is scattered, and whose times have brought changes. Time has left us a wailing voice over grief, upon their hearts are gloom and overwhelming sorrow. If you do not rescue them with a blessing you spread, O most forbearing of people when tested, bestow favor upon women whom you used to suckle, when your mouth was filled with the rich milk of their breasts. When you were a small child, you used to suckle from them, and what you do and leave adorns you. Do not make us like one whose ostrich has fled, but preserve us, for we are a noble group. We are grateful for blessings even when others are ungrateful, and after this day we have something stored up. Clothe with pardon those whom you used to suckle from their mothers, for pardon is well known. O best of those whom dark bay steeds pranced with, at the time of battle when sparks blaze. We hope for pardon from you which you will wear; this creation is pardoned when you pardon and take victory. So pardon us, may God pardon what you fear on the Day of Resurrection when victory is brought to you. When he heard this poetry, he said: What belonged to me and to the Banu Abd al-Muttalib is yours. Quraysh said: What belonged to us is for God and His Messenger. The Ansar said: What belonged to us is for God and His Messenger."],[4619,"that the Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while they were both in the state of ihram."],[4620,"I will surely find people from my community who will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds like the mountains of Tihamah, and Allah will make them scattered dust.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us so that we will not be among them without knowing.\" He said, \"Indeed, they are from among your brothers, but they are people who, when they are alone with the sacred limits of Allah, violate them.\""],[4621,"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection is an unjust ruler."],[4622,"When the saying of 'Amin' by the people of the earth coincides with the saying of 'Amin' by the people of the heaven, he is forgiven."],[4623,"By Him in whose hand is my soul, Allah never sent down revelation to any prophet between Him and him except in Arabic, then he would afterward convey it to his people in his own tongue."],[4624,"He used to recite: (Our hearts are wrapped) meaning vessels for wisdom. He said: \"The Jews said when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them to learn wisdom: 'How can we learn when our hearts are securely wrapped?' meaning vessels for wisdom.\""],[4625,"Two men from the Ansar recited a surah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had taught them, and they used to recite it. One night they stood to pray with it, but they could not recall a single letter of it. In the morning they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is among those that were abrogated and caused to be forgotten, so turn away from it.\" Al-Zuhri used to recite: 'Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten' with a damma on the nun, lightly pronounced."],[4626,"Ibn Abbas said: (There is no blame on him to go round them both) meaning: whoever leaves it, there is no harm upon him. This reached Aishah, and she said: \"It is not as he said. If it were as he said, it would be 'There is no blame on him not to go round them both.'\" Then she said: \"In pre-Islamic times there were two idols on Safa and Marwah, between which they used to circumambulate. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ destroyed them as he destroyed the idols, the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt uneasy about circumambulating between Safa and Marwah, and they said: 'We used to circumambulate only for the sake of the two idols, and Allah has destroyed them.' So Allah sent down: Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the rites of Allah, meaning among the rituals of Hajj, so do not feel uneasy about going round between them.\""],[4627,"Regarding the saying of Allah: 'And when they hear what has been sent down to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflow with tears,' he said: \"They were sailors, meaning seamen, who came with Ja'far b. Abi Talib from Abyssinia. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the Quran to them, they believed and their eyes overflowed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Perhaps when you return to your land you will abandon your religion.' They said: 'We will never turn away from our religion.' So Allah sent down that concerning their statement.\""],[4628,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days of Shawwal has fasted the entire year."],[4629,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."],[4630,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six days of Shawwal has fasted the whole year."],[4631,"Whoever says after the morning prayer, while still sitting with his legs folded, before speaking: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise; He gives life and causes death; in His hand is all good; and He has power over all things,' ten times, ten good deeds are recorded for him for each time, ten evil deeds are erased from him, ten degrees are raised for him, and they are a protection for him on that day from the accursed Satan and a protection from every disliked thing."],[4632,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the companions of the elevations (al-A'raf). He replied: \"They are men who were killed in the cause of Allah while they were disobedient to their fathers. Their martyrdom prevented them from entering the Fire, and their disobedience prevented them from entering Paradise. So they will be upon a wall between Paradise and the Fire until their flesh and fat wither away, until Allah finishes accounting for the creatures. When Allah finishes accounting for His creatures and none remain but them, Allah will envelop them with His mercy and admit them into Paradise by His mercy.\""],[4633,"When news of the Negus's death reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Go out and pray over a brother of yours whom you have never seen.\" So we went out, and the Prophet ﷺ advanced and we lined up behind him, and he prayed and we prayed. When we finished, the hypocrites said: \"Look at this one, he went out to pray over a Christian infidel whom he has never seen.\" Then Allah revealed: \"And indeed, among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and what has been sent down to you and what was sent down to them, humbling themselves before Allah. They do not sell the verses of Allah for a small price...\" to the end of the verse."],[4634,"Whoever drinks water on an empty stomach, his strength will diminish."],[4635,"Al-Abbas came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I came upon a people conversing, and when they saw me they fell silent. That is only because they found me burdensome.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Have they done that? By the One in whose hand is my soul, none of them believes until he loves you for my love. They hope to enter Paradise through my intercession, but the Banu Abd al-Muttalib do not hope for it.\""],[4636,"I was shown what my community will face after me, and how they will shed each other's blood. That was decreed by Allah just as it was decreed for the nations before you. So I asked Him to grant me His intercession for them on the Day of Resurrection, and He did."],[4637,"Abdullah b. al-Zubayr led us in the Maghrib prayer and he gave the salutation after two rak'ahs, then he got up to touch the Black Stone. The people said: \"Glory be to Allah!\" He turned to them and said: \"If only we had completed your prayer for you.\" They indicated to him that he had not done so. He returned and prayed the remaining rak'ah, then he recited the tashahhud and gave the salutation, and he prostrated twice after the salutation. I went to Ibn Abbas and mentioned that to him, and he said: \"He did not deviate from the Sunnah of his Prophet ﷺ.\""],[4638,"He forbade prayer at three times: at sunrise until the sun rises, at midday, and at sunset."],[4639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling silver for silver except like for like, equal for equal, and forbade selling gold for gold except like for like, equal for equal. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Sell gold for silver however you wish, and silver for gold however you wish.\""],[4640,"Whoever persists in swearing an oath against his family, he is greater in sin."],[4641,"Indeed, talebearing and malice do not combine in the heart of a Muslim."],[4642,"Whoever says when he hears the call to prayer: 'By the right of this perfect call and the established prayer, grant Muhammad the means and the excellence, and raise him to the praiseworthy station which You have promised him,' intercession will be guaranteed for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[4643,"Whoever frees a believing slave, Allah will free every limb of his from the Fire for each limb of the slave."],[4644,"When Allah wills good for a servant, He sweetens him. I said: How does He sweeten him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"He grants him success to do a righteous deed a year before his death, then takes his soul while he is upon it.\""],[4645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dictated to me this verse: \"And indeed We created man from an extract of clay\" up to \"Then We produced him as another creation.\" Muʿadh b. Jabal said: \"So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed. Muʿadh said to him: \"Why did you laugh, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"It was concluded with it: 'So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.'\""],[4646,"Five prayers Allah has made obligatory upon His servants. Whoever performs their ablution well, prays them at their times, and completes their bowing, prostration, and humility, he has a covenant with Allah that He will forgive him. And whoever does not do that has no covenant with Allah; if He wills, He punishes him, and if He wills, He forgives him."],[4647,"Delaying payment by a rich person is wrongdoing. If you are referred to a wealthy person, accept the referral. Do not approach pregnant captives until they give birth. Do not make advance payment for fruit until its owner is secure about it."],[4648,"No man fasts a day in the path of Allah except that Allah distances him from the Fire by a distance of one hundred years."],[4649,"A bedouin came to Abu Hurayrah and said: \"O Abu Hurayrah, narrate to us from the Prophet ﷺ,\" and he repeated it to him three times. Abu Hurayrah did not answer him, poking the ground with a stick he had, not turning to him. When the bedouin saw that, he turned away. Abu Hurayrah said: \"Bring the man back to me.\" When he returned, he said: \"Sit.\" Then he said: \"A bedouin like the other one came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the Prophet ﷺ was poking the ground with a stick of his as you saw me poking. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, curse the people of Yemen,' three times, and he remained silent about him as I did with you. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Where is this questioner who asked me to curse the people of Yemen?' The man stood up to him, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni, and I find the breath of your Lord from the direction of Yemen. Indeed, disbelief, wickedness, and hardness of heart are among the camel-herders, the owners of hair and wool, whom Satan comes upon at the rear of camels.' The man stood up angry and said: 'Come back to me and I will tell you more.'\""],[4650,"Who will guard us tonight? Dhu Mikhmar said: \"I will, O Messenger of Allah.\" He gave him the reins of his she-camel and said: \"Do not be a lukaʿ.\" I went not far, holding the reins of the Prophet's ﷺ she-camel and my she-camel. I let them loose to graze. Then sleep overcame me. Nothing woke me except the heat of the sun on my face. I looked right and left, startled. There were the two camels not far away. I took them and came to the nearest of the people and woke him. Then I asked him: \"Did you pray?\" He said: \"No.\" The people woke one another until the Prophet ﷺ woke up. He said: \"O Bilal, is there water in the vessel?\" He said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He brought him the vessel, and he performed ablution with an ablution, not mixing dust with it. Then he said: \"O Bilal, give the call to prayer,\" while he was unhurried. He gave the call, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs of Fajr, unhurried. Then he commanded Bilal, and he performed the iqamah for prayer. The Prophet ﷺ prayed, unhurried. A man said: \"O Prophet of Allah, did we miss the prayer?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"No, Allah took our souls, then returned them to us, and we prayed.\""],[4651,"The last of the two matters from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was abandoning ablution from what fire has touched."],[4652,"I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a month before his death, and he wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[4653,"Indeed the worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal?\" He said: \"He does not complete its bowing or its prostration.\""],[4654,"There will be a tribulation in which no side will calm down except that another side stirs up, until a caller from the sky announces: 'Your commander is so-and-so.'"],[4655,"I went out to battle with a companion of mine, and ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar accompanied us to bid farewell. When he was about to part from us, he said: \"I have no money to give you, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When Allah is entrusted with something, He preserves it. I entrust Allah with your religion, your trusts, and the endings of your deeds.'\""],[4656,"Whoever drags his garments, Allah will not look at him. Abu Rayhanah said: By Allah, what you have told us has truly distressed me. By Allah, I love beauty so much that I put it even in the strap of my sandal and the lash of my whip—is that from arrogance? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah is beautiful and loves beauty, and He loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant. But arrogance is rejecting the truth and despising people.\""],[4657,"There is no protected pasture except for Allah and His Messenger."],[4658,"He has succeeded who submits, whose provision is sufficient, and who is patient with that."],[4659,"I was the tenth of ten in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Ibn Mas'ud, Ibn Jabal, Hudhayfah, Ibn Awf, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and myself. A young man from the Ansar came, greeted, then sat down and said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the believers is best? He said: \"The one with the best character among them.\" He said: Which of the believers is most astute? He said: \"The one who remembers death most and prepares for it best before it descends upon him—those are the astute ones.\" Then the young man fell silent, and the Prophet ﷺ turned to us and said: O company of Muhajirun, five traits—if you are tested with them and they befall you, and I seek refuge in Allah that you should live to see them: immorality never appears among a people to the point that they practice it openly except that plague and diseases that were not present among their predecessors who came before them spread among them; and they do not diminish the measure and the balance except that they are seized with years of drought, hardship of provision, and the tyranny of the ruler over them; and they do not withhold the zakah of their wealth except that rain is withheld from the sky, and were it not for the animals they would not receive rain; and they do not break the covenant of Allah and His Messenger except that Allah sets their enemy upon them, who then raids them and seizes some of what was in their hands; and as long as they do not judge by the Book of Allah, Allah will make their might turn against one another. Then he ordered Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, who equipped himself for a military expedition to which he was assigned as commander. In the morning he had wrapped his head with a black cotton turban. The Prophet ﷺ came to him, then undid it, and re-wrapped it for him, leaving about four fingers or so hanging from behind, and said: \"Wrap it like this, O Ibn Awf, for it is more proper and more handsome.\" Then he ordered Bilal, and handed him the banner. He praised Allah and invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then said: \"Take it, Ibn Awf, and go forth together in the path of Allah. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not act treacherously, and do not mutilate. This is the covenant of Allah and the practice of your Prophet among you.\""],[4660,"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: If only you would go to Abd Allah b. Ubayy. So he went to him, riding his donkey, and a group of his companions went with him. When they reached him, Abd Allah b. Ubayy said: Move away, for the stench of your donkey has harmed me. A man among the Muslims said: By Allah, the donkey of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has a better smell than you. A man from his people became angry on behalf of Abd Allah, and one of them became angry on behalf of his own people, and there was striking with palm branches and sandals between them. It reached us that this verse was revealed about them: \"If two parties of the believers fight, make peace between them.\""],[4661,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a funeral and said four takbirs, then he came to the grave and threw three handfuls of dust from the side of the deceased's head."],[4662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the night prayer, and he said: \"Two by two, and if you fear that dawn will overtake you, pray one rak'ah as witr.\""],[4663,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning from Mina to Arafat, and among us were those reciting the talbiyah and those saying the takbir."],[4664,"You will be purified just as dates are picked out from the chaff. Your best ones will depart and your worst ones will remain, so if you are able to die, then die."],[4665,"This world will not pass away until it is ruled by a base and vile man. The best of people is a believer between two noble parents."],[4666,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ that the left side of the mosque had fallen into disuse. He said: Whoever maintains the left side of the mosque will have a double portion of the reward."],[4667,"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I passed by the highest assembly, and Jibril was like a worn-out saddle cloth from fear of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[4668,"Whoever seeks to be heard, Allah will make him heard; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose him."],[4669,"He forbade that a woman be married to her paternal aunt or to her maternal aunt."],[4670,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would avoid the initial flow of blood for three (days), then he would resume intimacy after that."],[4671,"He forbade selling what one does not own, which is what is not in your possession, and (he forbade) profiting from what is not guaranteed, and a sale with a loan, and a sale with two conditions, saying: 'This is for cash for such-and-such, and on credit for such-and-such.'"],[4672,"Your children are from your earnings, and indeed the best of what you eat is from your earnings."],[4673,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed five (rakʿahs), then performed two prostrations."],[4674,"He would kiss some of his wives, then go out to prayer without performing ablution."],[4675,"If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have a second one; and if he were given a second, he would love a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah relents to whoever repents."],[4676,"A woman is not to be married to her paternal aunt, nor to her maternal aunt."],[4677,"A Jew passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'O Jew, narrate to us.' He said: 'How do you say, O Abu al-Qasim, when Allah places the sky on this (finger), the earth on this, the mountains on this, the seas on this, and the rest of creation on this?' He said: 'Then Allah revealed: \"They have not appraised Allah with true appraisal.\"'"],[4678,"Whoever eats from this vegetable should not approach our mosque."],[4679,"My close friend Abu al-Qasim, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, may my father and mother be sacrificed for him, enjoined me with three things: fasting three days of every month, sleeping on an odd number (of rakʿahs), and glorifying Allah in the forenoon."],[4680,"He used to supplicate: “O Allah, place in our land its blessing, its adornment, and its tranquility.”"],[4681,"I am the guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise for one who abandons argumentation, even if he is right; and a house in the middle of Paradise for one who abandons lying, even in jest; and a house in the highest part of Paradise for one who makes his character excellent."],[4682,"Allah’s anger is intense toward a woman who brings into a people someone not of them, so that he shares in their wealth and looks upon their private matters."],[4683,"Might is My cloak and pride is My lower garment; whoever contests with Me over either of them, I will punish him."],[4684,"The example of the believer among the people of faith is like the head to the body; he suffers from what afflicts the people of faith just as the head suffers from what afflicts the body."],[4685,"Whoever walks in the darkness of the night to the mosques, Allah will grant him light on the Day of Resurrection."],[4686,"Do not revile the night and the day, nor the sun, nor the moon, nor the wind, for they are a mercy for some people and a punishment for others."],[4687,"The angels do not come near a caravan in which there is a bell, nor a house in which there is a bell."],[4688,"Yazid b. Abi Kabshah led us in the afternoon prayer, then turned to us after his salam and informed us that he had prayed behind Marwan b. al-Hakam, and he prostrated with us two prostrations like these. Then Marwan said: I prayed behind Uthman b. Affan, and he prostrated with us two prostrations like these. Then Uthman said: I was with your Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, I prayed but did not know whether I prayed an even or odd number; then I prayed again and did not know whether I prayed an even or odd number—he said it three times. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ answered him, saying: Satan toys with you in your prayers. Whoever prays and does not know whether he prayed even or odd should prostrate twice, for they complete his prayer."],[4689,"How will it be for you when some of you kill others? They said: Are we today killing each other? He said: That is not what I mean, but rather the killing of Muslims by one another, and the intellects of men will be removed, such that they deem error to be right guidance."],[4690,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I do a deed that is observed and it pleases me. He said: You will have two rewards: the reward of the secret and the reward of the open."],[4691,"There will be severe and harsh trials. The best of people in them will be the Muslims of the desert dwellers, those who do not take anything from the blood of people or their wealth."],[4692,"When he asked about a man's name, if it was good, that would be recognized on his face, and if it was bad, that would be seen on his face. And when he asked about the name of a village, likewise."],[4693,"The most intense regrets of the children of Adam are over three things: a man who had with him a beautiful wife who pleased him, and she bore him a son and then died, and he had nothing with which to hire a wet-nurse for him; a man who was on a horse in a military expedition and saw the spoils, so he raced his companions to them, but when he drew near them, his horse fell and died, so he was beaten to the spoils; and a man who had crops and a watering camel, but when his crops ripened and pleased him, his watering camel died, and he had nothing with which to buy a camel, so his crops perished."],[4694,"I entered the mosque and sat by a room and cleared my throat. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Abu Yahya, come to the midday meal.' I said: 'I am fasting.' He said: 'And I intended to fast, but our mu'adhdhin called the adhan before dawn broke, and in his eyes there was some defect or something.'"],[4695,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my wife does not repel the hand of a toucher?' He said to him: 'Divorce her.' He said: 'I love her.' He said: 'Then enjoy her.'"],[4696,"May Allah have mercy on a servant who is lenient when he judges, lenient when he asks, and lenient when he demands repayment."],[4697,"He went to the mosque of Damascus, and he set out early for the midday rest. He met Shaddad b. Aws and al-Sunabihi with him. I said: 'Where are you heading, may Allah have mercy on you both?' They said: 'We are going here to a sick brother of ours to visit him.' So I went with them until we entered upon that man. They said: 'How has your morning been?' He said: 'I have entered the morning by the blessing of Allah and His grace.' Shaddad said: 'Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: When I afflict a believing servant of Mine, and he praises Me and is patient over what I have afflicted him with, then he rises from his bed that day like the day his mother gave birth to him, free of sins. And the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says to the guardian angels: I have made My servant patient and afflicted him, so record for him the reward you used to record for him before that when he was healthy.\"'"],[4698,"The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four things: about his youth and how he spent it, about his life and in what he exhausted it, about his wealth from where he earned it, and on what he spent it."],[4699,"Allah created mercy as one hundred mercies. He kept with Himself ninety-nine mercies and placed among all His creation one mercy. If the disbeliever knew all the mercy that is with Allah, he would not despair of Paradise. And if the believer knew all the punishment that is with Allah, he would not feel safe from the Fire."],[4700,"Faith is sixty-four doors, or sixty-four branches. The highest of them—or the loftiest—is 'There is no god but Allah,' and the lowest is removing harm from the road."],[4701,"My intercession is for the people of major sins among my community."],[4702,"A gift for life (al-ʿumra) is in the status of inheritance."],[4703,"Any woman who fears her Lord, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, eight gates of Paradise will be opened for her. It will be said to her: 'Enter from wherever you wish.'"],[4704,"When one of you fights, let him avoid the face."],[4705,"Seek favor from the merciful among my community, you will live in their protection; but do not seek it from those whose hearts are hard, for they await My wrath."],[4706,"O Aisha, if modesty were a man, he would be a righteous man; and if obscenity were a man, he would be an evil man."],[4707,"I entered upon Safiyya bt. Shayba—an elderly woman—and said to her: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ marry Maymuna while he was in ihram? She said: No, the Messenger of God ﷺ married her while they were both not in ihram."],[4708,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[4709,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while the Messenger of God ﷺ was giving a sermon and sat down. The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Dharr: 'Have you prayed?' He said: No. He said: 'Stand and pray two rak'as.' So he stood and prayed two rak'as. Then the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Did you seek refuge in them from the evil of the devils of jinn and humans?' I said: O Messenger of God, who was the first of the prophets? He said: 'Adam.' I said: Was he a prophet? He said: 'Yes, one spoken to.' I said: Then who? He said: 'Noah, and between them were ten forefathers.' I said: Then who? He said: 'Abraham, and between them were ten forefathers.' I said: O Messenger of God..."],[4710,"She used to scrape semen from the garment of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4711,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salam."],[4712,"When one of you sees someone afflicted, let him say: Praise be to God who has favored me over him and over many of His servants with a great favor. If he says that, he has shown gratitude for that blessing."],[4713,"God will bring forth a man from my community who has ninety-nine scrolls, each scroll extending as far as the eye can see. He will say to him: 'Do you deny any of this? Did My recording angels wrong you?' He will say: No, my Lord. He will say: 'Rather, you have a good deed with Me, and there is no injustice for you today.' Then a card will be brought out for him on which is written: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. He will say: 'Bring your scales.' He will say: 'What is this card compared to these scrolls?' The card will outweigh, and nothing outweighs the name of God."],[4714,"No one earns anything like the virtue of knowledge that guides its possessor to guidance or restrains him from ruin, and one's religion is not upright until his intellect is upright."],[4715,"Zaynab is the best of my daughters; she was afflicted because of me. This reached Ali b. Husayn, who came to him and said: What is this hadith that reaches me from you in which you diminish Fatima? Urwa said: I would not like to have such and such, and I am diminishing Fatima in a right that is hers. But after this, I promise you never to narrate it again."],[4716,"I came from a marriage, and I did not come from fornication, from Adam until my father and mother gave birth to me."],[4717,"The angels continue to pray for one of you as long as his dining cloth remains spread."],[4718,"He used to kiss her while he was fasting."],[4719,"They pray for one of you as long as he remains in his prayer place and does not invalidate his ablution: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."],[4720,"The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer at the time of committing it."],[4721,"Muhammad b. al-Qasim sent me to al-Bara' b. 'Azib to ask him about the banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what it was. He said: It was black, square, made of a striped cloth."],[4722,"Before he died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say often: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You. I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, I see you saying often: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You. I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance.' He said: 'I have been commanded with a matter,' and he recited: 'When the help of Allah and the victory comes.'"],[4723,"When he heard the call to prayer, he said: 'And I too, and I too.'"],[4724,"The ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was made of silver, and its stone was made of silver."],[4725,"The son of Adam was commanded to prostrate on seven bones. One of them said: And he should not gather up his hair or his garment."],[4726,"He was driving his horse in front of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Blessed is Allah! How are their hooves and their hindquarters?'"],[4727,"A funeral bier was brought for Jabir b. 'Atik, or he said: Sahl b. 'Atik, and he was the first over whom funeral prayer was offered in the funeral place. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped forward and said the takbir, then recited the Opening of the Book aloud. Then he said the second takbir and prayed for himself and for the Messengers. Then he said the third takbir and supplicated for the deceased, saying: O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, and raise his rank. Then he said the fourth takbir and supplicated for the believing men and believing women, then he said the salam."],[4728,"When I take the two precious things of a servant, and he is patient and seeks reward, his recompense will be Paradise."],[4729,"Whoever would be pleased to be moved away from the Fire and admitted to Paradise, let death come to him while he bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and let him come to people with what he loves to be brought to him."],[4730,"I and the guardian of an orphan – for him or for another – will be in Paradise, and the one who strives on behalf of the widow and the needy is like the one who fights in the path of Allah."],[4731,"Some women from the people of Hims entered upon ʿAʾishah. She said, “Perhaps you are among the women who enter the bathhouses?” They said to her, “Indeed we do that.” ʿAʾishah said to them, “Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Any woman who removes her clothes in other than her husband’s house has torn what is between her and Allah.’”"],[4732,"I entered upon ʿAʾishah, and a man called out to her from behind the veil. He asked her about nabidh, and she said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the gourd and the pitch-covered vessel.”"],[4733,"“There will be over you leaders whom you will recognize and whose actions you will disapprove of. Whoever rejects has been absolved, and whoever detests has remained safe, but whoever is pleased or follows…” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, shall we not fight them?” He said, “No, as long as they uphold the prayer.”"],[4734,"Whoever trims his nails on Friday is protected from evil until its like."],[4735,"The recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was prolonged, with no refrain in it."],[4736,"The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and no one plunders a plunder to which the believers raise their eyes while he is a believer."],[4737,"Indeed your Lord is One, and your father is one. There is no superiority of an Arab over a non-Arab, nor of a non-Arab over an Arab, nor of a red person over a black person, nor of a black person over a red person except through piety."],[4738,"Acquire shoes in abundance, for one of you will never cease to be a rider as long as he does so."],[4739,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at ʿAli and said, “No one loves you except a believer, and no one hates you except a hypocrite. Whoever loves you has loved me, and whoever hates you has hated me. My beloved is the beloved of Allah, and my hater is the hater of Allah. Woe to the one who hates you after me.”"],[4740,"O Allah, strengthen Islam with the more beloved of the two men to You: with ʿUmar b. al-Khattab or with Abu Jahl b. Hisham.” And the more beloved of them to Allah was ʿUmar b. al-Khattab."],[4741,"Whoever prays the Duha prayer four rakʿahs, and before the first [i.e., before the Fajr prayer] four rakʿahs, a house will be built for him in Paradise because of it."],[4742,"Cursed is the one who has intercourse with women in their anuses."],[4743,"We used to travel with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he saw a village that he intended to enter, he would say: “O Allah, bless us in it” — three times — “O Allah, provide us its fruits, and make us beloved to its people, and make the righteous among its people beloved to us.”"],[4744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to, when he recited “Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim,” the polytheists would mock him, and they said, “Muhammad mentions the god of al-Yamama.” Musaylima had named himself “al-Rahman.” When this verse was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was commanded not to recite it aloud."],[4745,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his Hajj on the Day of ʿArafa, while he was on his she-camel al-Qaswaʾ, delivering a sermon. I heard him say: “O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my ʿitra, my Ahl al-Bayt.”"],[4746,"Indeed, Allah does not accept the prayer of one whose nose does not touch the ground."],[4747,"He used to dislike a man coming to his family at night [i.e., returning from travel unexpectedly]."],[4748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon and urged maintaining family ties. Then he said: “Whoever has three daughters whom he supports, disciplines, and marries off will enter Paradise.” A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, and two?” He said: “And two.” Then ʿAli said: “I have not lied about Muhammad, Muhammad did not lie about Jabir, and Jabir did not lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[4749,"Whoever has land, let him cultivate it. If he cannot, let him grant it [to someone else to cultivate], and let him not lease it. Do not mix unripe dates with ripe dates, nor dates with raisins. And a life grant is permissible."],[4750,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a sin that deserves a prescribed punishment, so carry out Allah’s prescribed punishment on me and purify me.” He said: “Did you not just perform ablution and do it well, and purify yourself and do it well, and pray with us a short while ago?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Go, for it is your expiation.”"],[4751,"There is no leader of ten but he will come to Allah on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck. If he was good, his chain will be released; if he was evil, an extra chain will be added to his chain."],[4752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, and we were seven people: four from our freed slaves and three from our Arabs, leaning our backs against his mosque. He said: “What has seated you?” We said: “We sat waiting for the prayer.” He said: He paused a little, then turned to us and said: “Do you know what your Lord says?” We said: “No.” He said: “Indeed your Lord says: Whoever performs the prayer at its proper time, maintains it, and does not neglect it out of disregard for its right, he has a pledge from Me that I will admit him to Paradise. And whoever does not perform it at its proper time, does not maintain it, and neglects it out of disregard for its right, he has no pledge from Me; if I will, I punish him, and if I will, I forgive him.”"],[4753,"A day of a just ruler is better than sixty years of worship, and a legal punishment carried out on earth in accordance with its right is purer than forty mornings of rain."],[4754,"They came to Anas b. Malik on a Monday, and he called for lunch for them. Some of the people stepped forward while others held back. He said: “Perhaps you are Monday-people or Thursday-people?”—he said it three times—“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast until it was said that he would never break his fast, and he used to break his fast until it was said that he would never fast the whole year, and the fast most beloved to him was in Shaʿban.”"],[4755,"Ibn Abbas was asked: “Did Muhammad ﷺ see his Lord, Mighty and Majestic?” He said: “Yes, he saw Him in the form of a young man with hair like pearls, as if his feet were in greenery.”"],[4756,"I saw in what a sleeper sees: as if I was under a tree, and as if the tree was reciting Surah Sad. When it reached the verse of prostration, it prostrated, and said in its prostration: “O Allah, write for me a reward by it, remove from me a burden by it, create for me gratitude by it, and accept it from me as You accepted from Your servant Dawud his prostration.” When morning came, I went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him about that. He said: “Did you prostrate, O Abu Saʿid?” I said: “No.” He said: “You were more deserving of the prostration than the tree.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Surah Sad until he reached the verse of prostration, and said in his prostration what the tree said in its prostration."],[4757,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who slaughters and forgets to invoke the name of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The name of Allah is on the tongue of every Muslim.”"],[4758,"When a sin is hidden, it harms only its doer; and when it appears and is not changed, it harms the general public.”"],[4759,"Do not revile my companions. May Allah curse whoever reviles my companions."],[4760,"I said to my father: “O father, who is the best of this community after its Prophet?” He said: “Abu Bakr.” I said: “Then who?” He said: “Then Umar.” Nothing prevented me from asking him about the third except fear that he would put ʿUthman next. I said: “And what are you?” He said: “Your father is a man among the Muslims.”"],[4761,"A morning or an evening journey in the path of Allah is better than the world and what it contains."],[4762,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in the dawn prayer. When he finished, he said: “Is so-and-so present? Is so-and-so present?” referring to a group of hypocrites who had not attended the prayer. Then he said: “Indeed the heaviest prayers for them are these two prayers: the dawn prayer and the evening prayer. If they knew what is in them, they would come to them even crawling.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Keep to the front row, for it is like the row of the angels. If you knew what is in it, you would race to it.” He said: “And your prayer with a man is purer than your prayer alone, and your prayer with two men is purer than your prayer with one man, and the more there are, the more beloved it is to Allah.”"],[4763,"Islam is built upon three: the people of “There is no god but Allah”—do not declare them disbelievers for a sin, and do not testify against them of polytheism; knowledge of the decrees, its good and its evil, from Allah; and jihad continuing until the Day of Resurrection, from when Allah sent Muhammad ﷺ to the last band of Muslims. The tyranny of a tyrant does not nullify that, nor the justice of a just one."],[4764,"When a man adorns himself for the work of the Hereafter while he neither intends it nor seeks it, he is cursed in the heavens and the earths."],[4765,"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from imams of hardship who drive my Ummah into oppression."],[4766,"Hamzah al-Aslami said: O Messenger of Allah, I fast continuously and do not break the fast. Should I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast."],[4767,"Whoever revives dead land, he has a reward in it, and whatever the grazing animals eat from it is charity for him."],[4768,"Indeed, the best of your days is Friday: in it Adam was created, in it he was taken, in it is the blowing of the trumpet, and in it is the thunderclap. So increase in sending blessings upon me in it, for your blessings are presented to me. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how can our blessings be presented to you when you have decayed? He said: They say: You have perished. He said: Indeed, Allah has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the prophets."],[4769,"The Prophet ﷺ named him Muta' and said to him: O Muta', you are obeyed among your people. He mounted him on a piebald horse, gave him the banner, and said to him: O Muta', go to your companions, for whoever enters under this banner of mine is safe from punishment."],[4770,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled by an oath with a witness."],[4771,"Is there anyone among you who can recite a third of the Qur'an in a night? They said: Who can do that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Can one of you not recite 'Say: He is Allah, the One'? For it equals a third of the Qur'an."],[4772,"I missed the Prophet ﷺ, so I followed him to the graveyard. He said: Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. You are our forerunners. Then he turned to me, saw me, and said: Woe to her, if she could, she would do what she did."],[4773,"The best house among the Muslims is a house in which there is an orphan who is treated well, and the worst house among the Muslims is a house in which there is an orphan who is treated badly."],[4774,"No one goes out except that at his door there are two banners: a banner in the hand of an angel and a banner in the hand of a devil. If he goes out for what Allah loves, the angel follows him with his banner, and he remains under the angel's banner until he returns to his house. If he goes out for what displeases Allah, the devil follows him with his banner, and he remains under the devil's banner until he returns."],[4775,"There is no good in trade except for one who does not praise what he sells, does not disparage what he buys, earns lawful profit, gives what is due, and refrains from swearing."],[4776,"Indeed Iblis wailed when the Opening of the Book was sent down, and it was sent down in Madinah."],[4777,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling fresh dates for dry dates and grapes for raisins, and he permitted araya transactions."],[4778,"The neighbor has more right to his adjacent property."],[4779,"Whoever points to a good deed will have the like of the reward of the one who does it."],[4780,"I recited seventy surahs to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I completed the Quran with the best of people, Ali b. Abi Talib."],[4781,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of God from every devil and harmful creature, and from every evil eye."],[4782,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when Ammar sought permission to enter. He said: Welcome to the good one, made good."],[4783,"Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me."],[4784,"Whoever reviles Ammar, God reviles him; and whoever hates Ammar, God hates him."],[4785,"Any slave who marries without the permission of his masters is a fornicator."],[4786,"When Kisra perishes, there will be no Kisra after him; and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him. By Him in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will certainly be spent in the way of God."],[4787,"O assembly of young men, upon you is marriage. Whoever cannot afford it should fast, for it is a shield for him."],[4788,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite: (wa-al-nakhla bāsiqāt) with ṣād."],[4789,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with his brother, whose belly had swollen. He said, \"O Messenger of God, my brother's belly has swollen. I brought him to the physicians, and they ordered me to cauterize him. Should I cauterize him?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Do not cauterize him; return him to his family.\" Then a camel passed by him and struck his belly, and it subsided. He brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \"If you had brought him to the physicians, you would have said, 'The fire healed him.'\""],[4790,"The last thing preserved from the words of prophethood is: 'If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[4791,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a man who pursues a woman unlawfully: may he marry her mother? Or he pursues the mother unlawfully: may he marry her daughter? The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The unlawful does not make the lawful unlawful. Only what is by a lawful marriage makes unlawful.\""],[4792,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks."],[4793,"He used to go around to his wives with a single washing."],[4794,"Three things do not break the fast: vomiting, cupping, and a wet dream."],[4795,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful."],[4796,"If I were to swear, I would be truthful: the most beloved of God's servants to God are the watchers of the sun and the moon—meaning the muezzins—and they will be recognized on the Day of Resurrection by the length of their necks."],[4797,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out one day holding the hand of Abū Dharr and said, \"O Abū Dharr, do you know that before us there is a steep and difficult pass that none will ascend except the light ones?\" A man said, \"O Messenger of God, am I among the light ones or the heavy ones?\" He said, \"Do you have food for a day?\" He said, \"Yes.\" \"And food for tomorrow?\" He said, \"Yes.\" \"And food for the day after tomorrow?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"If you had food for three days, you would be among the heavy ones.\""],[4798,"The one who persists in ribā is like a worshiper of an idol, and the one who persists in wine is like a worshiper of an idol."],[4799,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to keep the night alive with eight rakʿahs, their bowing like their recitation, their prostration like their recitation, and he would say the taslīm between every two rakʿahs."],[4800,"He is not from us who does not honor our elder, show mercy to our younger, fraternize among us, and visit."],[4801,"Woe to the rich from the poor on the Day of Resurrection. They will say: 'Our Lord, they wronged us in the rights You ordained for us over them.' Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'By My Might and Majesty, I will draw you near and distance them.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: 'And those in whose wealth is a known right for the beggar and the deprived.'"],[4802,"He used to gesture during the prayer."],[4803,"Whoever conceals beneficial knowledge will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."],[4804,"The Friday prayer is obligatory upon every one who has reached puberty, and upon the one who goes to the Friday prayer is the ritual bath."],[4805,"Indeed, Allah does not leave any Muslim on Friday except that He forgives him."],[4806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while the people were praying after the break of dawn, and he said: 'There is no prayer after the break of dawn except two rak'ahs.'"],[4807,"Gabriel ﷺ kept enjoining me to be good to the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[4808,"A woman from Aslam called Subay'ah was married to a husband, and he died while she was pregnant. Abu al-Sanabil b. Ba'kak proposed to her, but she refused to marry him. He said: 'It is not lawful for you to marry until you complete the longer of the two terms.' She waited nearly twenty nights, then gave birth. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him, and he said to her: 'Marry.'"],[4809,"Ribāṭ (guarding the frontier) for one day in the way of Allah is better than fasting a day and standing in prayer during it."],[4810,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated, Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked permission of Abu al-ʿĀṣ b. al-Rabīʿ, her husband, to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he permitted her. She arrived to him. Then Abu al-ʿĀṣ followed her to Madinah and sent to her: 'Get me a guarantee of protection from your father.' She went out and looked out from the door of her room while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying the dawn prayer with the people, and she said: 'O people, I am Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I have granted protection to Abu al-ʿĀṣ.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: 'O people, I did not know of this until you heard it. Verily, the lowest of the Muslims may grant protection on behalf of the Muslims.'"],[4811,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb gave ʿAbd Allah b. al-Saʿdī a thousand dinars, but he refused to accept it. ʿUmar said to him: 'I will tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me. He said: \"If Allah directs provision to you without asking or avidity of the soul, then take it, for Allah has given it to you.\"'"],[4812,"He forbade leasing land."],[4813,"Whoever keeps watch for a day in the path of Allah, Allah will place between him and the Fire seven trenches, each trench like the seven heavens and the seven earths."],[4814,"Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will place between him and the Fire a trench like the distance between heaven and earth."],[4815,"My community will never be disgraced as long as they observe the fast of Ramadan. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their disgrace in wasting the month of Ramadan? He said: Violating sanctities during it. Whoever commits adultery in it or drinks wine, Allah curses him, and whoever is in the heavens curses him until the like of it the following year. If he dies before reaching the month of Ramadan, he will have no good deed with Allah by which he can shield himself from the Fire. So be mindful of the month of Ramadan, for good deeds are multiplied in it as they are not multiplied in anything else, and likewise evil deeds."],[4816,"When the Prophet ﷺ entered the last ten nights, he would strive hard, and his family would strive hard."],[4817,"O Allah, bless my community in its early morning, and make it on Thursday."],[4818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha, without fear or rain. It was said: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended not to cause hardship for his community."],[4819,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Witr in every part of the night: its beginning, middle, and end, and his Witr ended at the pre-dawn time."],[4820,"The Prophet ﷺ mounted al-Hasan, al-Husayn, and Abd Allah b. Ja'far on an animal."],[4821,"When you have refused the beggar three times, there is no harm if you then give him more."],[4822,"No group of people gather together and then disperse without remembering Allah, except that they disperse from something more foul than a carcass."],[4823,"Which of you has memorized what the Prophet ﷺ said about tribulation? Hudhayfah said: I have. The tribulation of a man in his family and wealth, which prayer, charity, enjoining good, and forbidding evil expiate. He said: I did not ask you about this; I asked you about the tribulation that surges like the waves of the sea. He said: Between you and it is a closed door. He said: Will that door be opened or broken? He said: Rather it will be broken. He said: Then it will never be closed."],[4824,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."],[4825,"Whoever wears silk and drinks from silver is not of us; and whoever incites a woman against her husband or a slave against his masters is not of us."],[4826,"A man prayed alone behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[4827,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Dubāʿah while she was ill and said: Perform Hajj and stipulate, saying: O Allah, my place of exit is wherever You detain me."],[4828,"In your commanding good and forbidding evil is charity; your removing harm from the road is charity; your pouring from your bucket into your brother's bucket is charity; and your smiling."],[4829,"I saw my master al-Sāʾib: his beard was white and his head was black. I said: O my master, why does your head not turn white? He said: My head will never turn white. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by while I was a boy playing with other boys. He greeted the boys while I was among them, and I returned his greeting among the boys. He called me and said: What is your name? I said: Al-Sāʾib b. Yazīd, son of the sister of Namir. He placed his hand on my head and said: May Allah bless you. So the place where the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touched will never turn white."],[4830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib and Khālid b. al-Walīd, each alone and together. He said: When you are together, ʿAlī is in charge. He said: They took the right and left. ʿAlī went far and captured spoils, and he took a slave girl from the spoils. Buraydah said: I was among the people most hateful of ʿAlī. A man came to Khālid b. al-Walīd and mentioned that he had taken a slave girl from the fifth. He said: What is this? Then another came, then another, then reports followed on that. Khālid called me and said: O Buraydah, you know what has been done. Go with this letter of mine to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He wrote to him, so I went with his letter until I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He took the letter with his left hand — and he was as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: he neither read nor wrote. I used to lower my head when speaking until I finished what I needed; so I lowered my head and spoke, and I reviled ʿAlī until I was done. Then I raised my head and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ angry with an anger I had never seen from him except on the day of Qurayẓah and al-Naḍīr. He looked at me and said: O Buraydah, love ʿAlī, for he only does what he is commanded. He said: I stood up, and there was no one among the people more beloved to me than him."],[4831,"Māʿiz b. Mālik came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, purify me. He said: Woe to you, go back and seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. He said: He went back not far, then came and said: O Messenger of Allah, purify me. He said to him the like of that, until when it was the fourth time, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: From what should I purify you? He said: From adultery. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Is he insane? He was told that he was not insane. He said: Smell him. A man stood and smelled him, and found no smell of wine. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Did you commit adultery? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to be stoned. The people were divided about him: some said he perished with the worst of his deeds and his sin encompassed him; others said no repentance is better than the repentance of one who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, placed his hand in his hand, then said: Kill me with stones. They remained like that for two or three days until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while they were sitting, greeted, then sat and said: Seek forgiveness for Māʿiz b. Mālik. They said: May Allah forgive Māʿiz. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He has repented with a repentance that if divided among a nation would suffice them. Then a woman from Ghāmid of the Azd came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, purify me. He said: Go back, seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. She said: I see you want to send me back as you sent back Māʿiz b. Mālik? He said: From what should I purify you? She said: She is pregnant from adultery. He said: Did you commit adultery? She said: Yes. He said: Then I will not stone you until you give birth to what is in your womb. A man from the Ansar sponsored her until she gave birth. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: The Ghāmidiyyah has given birth. He said: Then I will not stone her and leave her child small with no one to nurse him. A man from the Ansar stood and said: I will nurse him, O Messenger of Allah. So he stoned her."],[4832,"Allah revealed to a prophet of the prophets of the Children of Israel: Say to the people of obedience among your nation: Do not rely on their deeds, for I do not call a servant to account on the Day of Resurrection and then will to punish him but that I punish him. And say to the people of disobedience among your nation: Do not throw themselves down, for I forgive great sins and I do not care. There is no people of a village, people of a city, people of a land, no man in particular, no woman who is for Me as I love but that I am for him as he loves. And there is no city, people of a land, man in particular, woman who is for Me as I love and then turns from what I love to what I hate but that I turn for him from what he loves to what he hates — [except I am for him as he hates]. And there is no people of a village, people of a city, people of a land, man in particular, woman who is for Me as I hate and then turns for Me from what I hate to what I love but that I turn for him from what he hates to what he loves. He is not of me who practices or has omens drawn for him, or practices or has divination done for him, or practices or has magic done for him. I and My creation, and all My creation is Mine."],[4833,"Gabriel said to me: O Muhammad, love whom you will, for you will part from him; do what you will, for you will meet it; live as you will, for you will die. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Gabriel ﷺ was concise with me in the sermon."],[4834,"By Him in whose hand is my soul, nothing has been combined with anything better than forbearance with knowledge."],[4835,"The head of reason after faith is showing affection to people."],[4836,"Three things: whoever does not have them is not of me, nor of Allah. It was said: What are they? He said: \"Forbearance that repels the ignorance of the ignorant, or good character by which he lives among people, or piety that restrains him from disobeying Allah.\""],[4837,"I asked ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn and Abū Hurayrah about a verse from the Book of Allah, about His saying: 'And pleasant dwellings in the Gardens of Eden'? They said: You have asked one well-informed. We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: 'A palace in Paradise of pearl, in it seventy dwellings of red ruby, in every dwelling seventy chambers of green emerald, in every chamber seventy beds.'"],[4838,"We used to witness fighting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when the sun declined he said to us: 'Attack,' so we attacked."],[4839,"Do not alight in the villages, for they are like the graves."],[4840,"Do not pitch tents for the Bedouin; for in the desert is harshness, and the hand of Allah is with the community, and Allah does not care about the straying of one who strays, and let no one ride a beast with more than two, and do not strike the faces of beasts, for everything glorifies His praise, and do not name your sons and brothers 'al-Ḥakam' or 'Abū al-Ḥakam,' for Allah is the Judge."],[4841,"O company of women, command your husbands to wash away from themselves the traces of urine and feces, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wash away from himself the traces of urine and feces,\" and I am ashamed to say it to them."],[4842,"Ḥabīb b. al-Ḥārith came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who commits sins often. He said: Repent to Allah, O Ḥabīb. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I repent and then I return. He said: \"Every time you sin, repent.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, then my sins will become many. He said: \"Allah's pardon is greater than your sins, O Ḥabīb b. al-Ḥārith.\""],[4843,"A people will not succeed whose affair is managed by a woman."],[4844,"I entered with the Prophet ﷺ a garden of some people of the Anṣār, and I handed him an unripe green date, so he ate it, then said: 'O Ibn ʿUmar, this is the first food I have eaten in three days.'"],[4845,"About a man who married a woman and then died before consummating with her and without assigning a dower for her: He said: \"She is entitled to the full dower, and upon her is the waiting period, and she has the inheritance.\" Then Maʿqil b. Sinān said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ pass this judgement in the case of Barwaʿ bt. Wāshiq."],[4846,"Clean yourselves with cold water, for it is a remedy for hemorrhoids."],[4847,"By Allah, I have not gathered you out of desire for a hadith nor out of fear, except for a hadith narrated to me by Tamīm al-Dārī. He came to me, embraced Islam, and pledged allegiance. He informed me that he embarked on a ship with thirty men from Lakhm and Judhām—two tribes of the Arabs from the people of Yemen. They encountered the sea when it was raging, and the waves tossed them about for a month, then cast them near sunset onto an island of the islands of the sea. He said: There we were, and suddenly we came upon a hairy beast, whose front we could not distinguish from its back. We said: Who are you, O beast? Allah permitted it, so it spoke to us with a fluent, articulate tongue, saying: I am al-Jassāsah (the Spy). We said: What is al-Jassāsah? It said: Away from me; go to that monastery at the far end of the island, for in it is a man who longs for news of you. So we went to the monastery, and there we saw a man, the largest man I have ever seen in creation and the most massive in body. His right eye was obliterated, as if his eye were a grape on a plastered wall. His hands were chained to his neck, and his legs were bound with fetters from his knees to his feet. We said to him: Who are you, O man? He said: As for my story, you have now come to know it, so tell me about yours. What brought you to this island? No human has reached this island since I was placed here. Then he said to us: Tell me about the Lake of Tiberias, what has become of it? We said to him: About which of its affairs do you ask? He said: Has its water dried up? Have the wonders within it appeared? We said: No, by Allah. He said: Indeed, it will be. Then he fell silent for a long while, then said: Tell me about the spring of Zughar, what has become of it? We said: About which of its affairs do you ask? He said: Do its people cultivate around it? We said: Yes. He said: Its water will soon disappear, and its people will no longer cultivate around it. Then he fell silent for a long while, then said: Tell me about the date palms of Baysān, what has become of them? We said: About which of their affairs do you ask? He said: Do they bear fruit? We said: Yes. He said: They will no longer bear fruit. Then he fell silent for a long while, then said: Tell me about the unlettered Prophet, what has he done? We said: About which of his affairs do you ask? He said: Has he appeared? We said: Yes. He said: What have the Arabs done with him? We said: Some of them fought him, and some of them believed him. He said: Indeed, whoever believed him, it is better for him—three times. We said: Tell us your story, O man. He said: Do you not know me? We said: If we knew you, we would not have asked you. He said: I am the Dajjāl (the Antichrist). It is near that I will be permitted to come out. When I come out, I will tread the entire land of the Arabs except Makkah and Ṭaybah. Every time I want them, an angel meets me with a drawn sword in his hand and turns me back from them. Abū al-Ashhab said: ʿĀmir said: Fāṭimah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raising his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, then he said: 'Shall I not inform you? This is Ṭaybah'—three times. Then he said: 'Shall I not inform you that he is in the sea of Syria?' Then he fainted for a while, then recovered, then said: 'Rather, he is in the sea of Yemen.' Then he fainted for a while, then recovered, and said: 'He is in the sea of Iraq'—three times. He will emerge when he emerges from a town called Iṣfahān, from one of its villages called Rustuqbād. He will emerge with seventy thousand in his vanguard, wearing the sijān. With him are two rivers: a river of water and a river of fire. Whoever of you reaches that, and it is said to him: Enter the water, let him not enter it, for it is fire. And when it is said to him: Enter the fire, let him enter it, for it is water. No one narrated this hadith from Abū al-Ashhab except Sayf b. Miskīn, and Abū ʿUbaydah was alone in narrating it."],[4848,"When time draws near, wearing tayalisah will abound, trade will abound, wealth will abound, and the owner of wealth will be honored for his wealth. Lewdness will abound, there will be the rule of boys, corruption will abound, the ruler will oppress, and cheating will occur in the measure and the scale. A man raising a puppy will be better for him than raising a child. No elder will be respected and no child will be shown mercy. Children of fornication will abound, to the point that a man will have intercourse with a woman on the main road. The best of them in that era will say: 'If only you would move away from the road!' They will wear sheepskins over wolves' hearts. The best of them in that era will be the flatterer."],[4849,"I set out seeking knowledge until I reached Kufah, and there was Abdullah b. Mas'ud among the people of Kufah. I asked about him and was directed to him. He was in the main mosque. I came to him and said: 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I have come to you seeking knowledge from you, hoping that Allah may benefit us by it after you.' He said to me: 'What tribe are you from?' I said: 'A man from the people of Basrah.' He said: 'From which clan?' I said: 'From this branch of Banu Sa'd.' He said to me: 'O Sa'di, I shall narrate to you a hadith concerning you that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I not direct you to a people who have abundant wealth and great strength, from whom you can seize wealth as booty?\" Or he said: \"abundant?\" He said: \"Who are they?\" The man said: \"This branch of Banu Sa'd, from the people of the sands.\" The Messenger of Allah said: \"Stop! For Banu Sa'd have a great share with Allah.\" Ask, O Sa'di.' I said: 'Abu Abd al-Rahman, is there any knowledge by which the Hour may be known?' He said—and he had been reclining, so he sat up straight—: 'O Sa'di, you have asked me about what I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any knowledge by which the Hour may be known?\" He said: \"Yes, O Ibn Mas'ud. The Hour has signs, and the Hour has portents. Indeed, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that a child will be a cause of anger, rain will be a cause of heat, and the nobles will overflow in abundance. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the treacherous will be trusted and the trustworthy will be betrayed. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that ties of kinship will be maintained among the wicked and severed among the righteous. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that every tribe will be led by its hypocrites and every market by its wicked. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that mihrabs will be distorted and hearts will be ruined. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that a believer in a tribe will be more lowly than a weak lamb. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that men will suffice with men and women with women. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is the rule of boys and the consultation of women. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that mosques will be crowded and pulpits will be elevated. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the ruins of the world will be inhabited and its inhabited places ruined. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that musical instruments, pride, and wine-drinking will appear. O Ibn Mas'ud, among the signs and portents of the Hour is that children of fornication will abound.\"' I said: 'Abu Abd al-Rahman, will they be Muslims?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Abu Abd al-Rahman, and the Quran will be among them?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Abu Abd al-Rahman, how will that be?' He said: 'A time will come upon people when a man divorces his wife, then denies her divorce and continues to have intercourse with her. They are both adulterers as long as they remain so.'"],[4850,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[4851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and saw a man in the mosque who did not complete his bowing or his prostration. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The prayer of a man who does not complete the bowing and prostration is not accepted.'"],[4852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at a man being supported between two men and said: 'What is this?' They said: 'He vowed to walk to Hajj.' He said: 'Allah has no need for this man to kill himself. Tell him to ride.'"],[4853,"Whoever raises a child until he says 'There is no god but Allah,' Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not call him to account."],[4854,"The people of Paradise eat and drink, but they do not spit, blow their noses, defecate, or urinate. Their food becomes a belch and a sweat like the fragrance of musk."],[4855,"He was asked: 'Is slaughter only in the throat and the pit of the neck?' He said: 'If you were to stab it in its thigh, it would suffice.'"],[4856,"I asked Anas b. Malik: 'How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited, he would prolong his voice greatly.'"],[4857,"If a man were to fast voluntarily for Allah and then be given the earth's fill of gold, he would not receive his full reward until the Day of Reckoning."],[4858,"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is for Me, and I shall reward it. And the bad breath of a fasting person is more pleasant to Allah than the fragrance of musk."],[4859,"My beloved ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: the forenoon prayer, not to sleep except after praying Witr, and to fast three days of every month."],[4860,"The lifetime gift (ʿumrā) belongs to the heir."],[4861,"A man fought another man, and one of them bit the hand of his companion. The man pulled his hand away, and the front tooth of the biter fell out. The matter was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"Would one of you bite his brother as the stallion bites?\""],[4862,"Whoever of you goes to relieve himself, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it; turn toward the east or the west."],[4863,"Fasting on the day of ʿArafah is an expiation for two years: the past year and the coming year, and the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ is an expiation for one year."],[4864,"God recited Ṭā-Hā and Yā-Sīn a thousand years before He created Adam. When the angels heard the Quran, they said: \"Blessed be the community upon which this is sent down, blessed be the hearts that carry this, and blessed be the tongues that speak this.\""],[4865,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I considered ordering firewood to be gathered, then ordering the prayer to be called, then ordering a man to lead the people in prayer, then going off to some men and burning their houses down upon them. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if one of them knew that he would find a fatty bone or two good sheep trotters, he would attend the ʿIshāʾ prayer."],[4866,"God created Paradise and created for it its people among their clans and tribes; they will not be increased nor decreased. And He created the Fire and created for it its people among their clans and tribes; they will not be increased nor decreased. A man said: \"O Messenger of God, then why should we act?\" He said: \"Act, for every person is facilitated for that for which he was created.\""],[4867,"There occurred between me and the Prophet ﷺ some words, and he said: \"Shall I appoint ʿUmar between me and you?\" I said: \"No.\" He said: \"Shall I appoint your father between me and you?\" I said: \"Yes.\""],[4868,"ʿAlī is with the Quran and the Quran is with him; they will not separate until they come to me at the Pond."],[4869,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus and said four takbīrs over him."],[4870,"The ʿaqīqah is slaughtered on the seventh, or the fourteenth, or the twenty-first day."],[4871,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar."],[4872,"Whoever of you passes through these markets while carrying arrows, let him grasp the arrowheads."],[4873,"Indeed, Allah laughs at the despair of His servants and their despondency, and at the nearness of mercy to them.\" I said: May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, does our Lord laugh? He said: \"Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, indeed He laughs.\" I said: Then He will not deprive us of good when He laughs."],[4874,"This community will split into seventy-three sects, all of them in the Fire except one.\" They said: And what is that sect? He said: \"That upon which I and my companions are today."],[4875,"Let none of you belittle himself. If he sees a matter concerning Allah about which he ought to speak, he should speak, and Allah will say: What prevented you from speaking? He will say: I feared the people. He will say: I was more deserving that you should fear Me."],[4876,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who has a sacrificial animal offered voluntarily, and it becomes lame or injured before it reaches its destination. He said: \"He should slaughter it, then smear its sandal with its blood, then strike it on its side, and he should not eat from it. If he eats from it, he must make it up."],[4877,"When he went out to Makkah, he performed the ritual bath (ghusl) when he intended to enter the state of ihram."],[4878,"Two men brought a dispute to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"I am only a human being, and I judge between you according to what I hear from you. Perhaps one of you is more eloquent in presenting his argument than his brother. So if I judge in favor of someone giving him something from his brother's right, I am only cutting off for him a piece of the Fire.\""],[4879,"Whoever fulfills their oaths and pays their debts and does not cause others to curse them will be recorded as dutiful, even if he was undutiful during their lifetime. And whoever does not fulfill their oaths and pay their debts and causes them to be cursed will be recorded as undutiful, even if he was dutiful during their lifetime."],[4880,"Ali proposed to me, and that reached Fatimah, and she mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"It was not for her to offend Allah and His Messenger.\""],[4881,"Islam is clean, so keep yourselves clean, for none enters Paradise except the clean."],[4882,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a bowl containing milk and honey. He said: \"Two drinks in one? And two condiments in one bowl? I have no need of it. Indeed, I do not claim that it is forbidden, but I dislike that Allah should ask me about the excesses of this world on the Day of Resurrection. I humble myself before Allah. Whoever humbles himself before Allah, Allah raises him. Whoever is arrogant, Allah lowers him. Whoever is moderate, Allah enriches him. Whoever increases the remembrance of death, Allah loves him.\""],[4883,"Whoever performs his ablution, and when he finishes his ablution says: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, make me among those who repent and make me among those who purify themselves,' the eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him; he may enter from whichever he wishes."],[4884,"A man's she-camel threw him and killed him while he was in ihram. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Bury him in his two garments, and do not touch him with perfume, and wash him with lote-tree leaves and water, and do not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.'"],[4885,"We were on a journey of ours, and we found a whip. A man from the group took it, but we told him not to, and he refused. When we came to Madinah, we met Ubayy b. Ka'b and mentioned that to him. He said: 'I found one hundred dinars at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I brought them to him. He said: \"Announce it for a year.\" When the year was complete, I brought them to him, and he said: \"Announce it for another year.\" I did so. When the year was complete, I brought them to him after three years. He said: \"Note its tie and its number, then make use of it. If someone comes seeking it, give it to him.\"'"],[4886,"Indeed, Isa son of Maryam—there is no prophet or messenger between me and him. Indeed, he is my successor in my community after me. Indeed, he will kill the Dajjal, break the cross, and war will lay down its burdens. Indeed, whoever of you meets him, let him convey peace to him."],[4887,"He used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: 'I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of Allah from every devil and venomous creature, and from every envious evil eye.'"],[4888,"Indeed, Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise."],[4889,"I arrived with the Prophet ﷺ at the place of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and he fell behind. The Prophet ﷺ gestured to him, and we prayed what we caught up with, and we made up what we had missed."],[4890,"My cistern is a month's journey in extent; its corners are equal; its spout is whiter than silver; its fragrance is more pleasant than musk; and its cups are like the stars of the sky."],[4891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go to relieve himself at al-Mughammas."],[4892,"You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, walking, and uncircumcised."],[4893,"Three things, whoever has them has tasted the flavor of faith: the one for whom nothing is dearer than Allah and His Messenger; the one who would prefer to be burned in fire rather than apostatize from his religion; and the one who loves for the sake of Allah and hates for the sake of Allah."],[4894,"Let not fear of the people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or hears it."],[4895,"There will be leaders over you who will let the prayers die beyond their times, so pray the prayer at its proper time, and make your prayer with them a supererogatory one. When al-Hajjaj delayed the prayer beyond its times, I used to pray the prayer at its proper time, and make my prayer with them a supererogatory one."],[4896,"I saw ʿAbd Allah b. Busr, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, sitting in the mosque—he was a very old and aged man—and his servant came to him and said, 'O my master, these camels of yours have been seized for the dung transport(?) of al-Zibla'—meaning the estate of al-ʿAbbas b. al-Walid b. ʿAbd al-Malik that is at the gate of the mosque in Hims—and there were two men with him, so they took him by his upper arms until he stood up. ʿUmar said: I walked with him until he came to al-Zibla, and there were his camels made to kneel, and they were filling dust with the sacks. He took a sack and began opening it for them. Some Christians said, 'This is the companion of your Prophet and you do this to him? If we saw a man from among the companions of ʿIsa, we would carry him on our heads.' The people then leaned to take him, but he said, 'Leave me; I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: How will you be when the rulers oppress you?'"],[4897,"The Islam of Qabath b. Ashyam al-Laythi came about because men from his people and other Arabs came to him and said, 'Muhammad b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib has come out calling to a religion other than our religion.' Qabath got up and went to the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he entered upon him, he said to him, 'Sit down, O Qabath.' Qabath was speechless, or the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, 'Are you the one who said: If the women of Quraysh came out with their head coverings, they would repel Muhammad and his companions?' Qabath said, 'By the One who sent you with the truth, my tongue never moved with it, my lips never whispered it, and no one heard it from me. It was nothing but something that crossed my mind. I bear witness that there is no god but God alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and that what you have brought is true.'"],[4898,"The Prophet of God ﷺ sat in one of the rooms of his wives, and ʿA'ishah was with him. A group of Jews entered upon him and said, 'Al-sam ʿalayka, O Muhammad.' He said, 'And upon you.' They sat and conversed. ʿA'ishah understood their greeting by which they had greeted the Prophet ﷺ, so she gathered her anger and was patient, but she could not control her rage and said, 'Rather upon you be al-sam and the wrath of God and His curse! Is this how you greet the Prophet of God ﷺ?' Then they left. The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'What made you say what you said?' She said, 'Did you not hear how they greeted you, O Messenger of God? By God, I could not control myself when I heard their greeting to you.' The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'No doubt. How did you see me respond to them? Indeed, the Jews are a people who have grown weary of their religion, and they are an envious people. They have not envied the Muslims for anything more excellent than three things: returning the greeting, establishing the rows, and their saying behind their imam in the prescribed prayer: Amin.'"],[4899,"If a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, he should not dip anything in it until he washes it seven times."],[4900,"I had forbidden you three things: visiting graves—so visit them, for visiting them is an admonition and a lesson; and I forbade you the meat of sacrifices beyond three days—so eat and store; and I forbade you nabidh in certain vessels—so drink, but do not drink what is unlawful."],[4901,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was taken, the Arabs apostatized, hypocrisy raised its head, and there befell my father what, had it befallen the mountains, would have crushed them. By God, they did not differ on a single point except that my father flew with its fortune and its share. Then she mentioned Ibn al-Khattab and said: 'He was, by God, resourceful and unique of his kind, who had prepared for every matter its match.'"],[4902,"Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, I am old, blind, with a far-off house, and I have no guide. Do you find any concession for me?' He said, 'Do you hear the call?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I find no concession for you.'"],[4903,"'Islam began as something strange and will return to being strange, so blessed are the strangers.' He was asked, 'And who are they, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'Those who set things right when the people have become corrupt.'"],[4904,"There is no shepherd who is entrusted with a flock but will be asked on the Day of Resurrection: Did he establish among them the command of God, or did he waste it?"],[4905,"The wives of the people of Paradise will sing to their husbands with the most beautiful voices anyone has ever heard. Among what they sing: 'We are the good and beautiful, wives of a noble people, looking with delight of eyes.' And among what they sing: 'We are the everlasting who never die, we are the secure who never fear, we are the residents who never depart.'"],[4906,"Three things: whoever does them trusting in God and seeking reward, it is incumbent upon God to help him and bless him. Whoever strives for the freeing of a slave trusting in God and seeking reward, it is incumbent upon God to help him and bless him. And whoever marries trusting in God and seeking reward, it is incumbent upon God to help him and bless him. And whoever revives dead land trusting in God and seeking reward, it is incumbent upon God to help him and bless him."],[4907,"Abu Hurayrah saw a man whose appearance pleased him, so he said, 'From whom are you?' The man said, 'From those upon whom God has bestowed favor.' He said, 'All of us are from those upon whom God has bestowed favor. From whom are you?' He said, 'From the people of the earth.' He said, 'All of us are from the people of the earth. From whom are you?' He said, 'From the Nabat.' He said, 'Get away from me. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: They are the killers of the prophets and the helpers of the oppressors. When they acquire estates and build lofty buildings, then flee, flee.'"],[4908,"Whoever recites the Qur'an in any mode he can, Allah will record for him ten good deeds, erase from him ten bad deeds, and raise him ten degrees. And whoever recites and pronounces some of it correctly but errs in some, twenty good deeds are recorded for him, twenty bad deeds are erased from him, and he is raised twenty degrees. And whoever recites and pronounces all of it correctly, forty good deeds are recorded for him, forty bad deeds are erased from him, and he is raised forty degrees."],[4909,"Whoever swears an oath that involves severing family ties, its expiation is to not persist in it."],[4910,"He used to encourage the people to pray at night during Ramadan without commanding them to do it as an obligatory matter. He would say: \"Whoever prays at night during Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins will be forgiven.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while the matter was thus, and the matter remained thus during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and the beginning of the caliphate of Umar."],[4911,"Regarding His saying: \"You are only a warner, and for every people there is a guide,\" the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The warner, and the guide is a man from Banu Hashim.\""],[4912,"For the traveler, three days, and for the resident, one day and one night, to wipe over the leather socks."],[4913,"He said to those around him from his ummah: \"Guarantee me six traits and I will guarantee you Paradise.\" I said: \"What are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Prayer, zakah, trustworthiness, chastity, the stomach, and the tongue.\""],[4914,"My close friend ﷺ advised me regarding things I will not abandon until I die: He advised me to pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr, saying: \"In them are the desires of the age,\" and the two rak'ahs of Duha, for it is the prayer of the oft-returning, and two rak'ahs before Zuhr, and two rak'ahs after it, and two rak'ahs before Asr, and two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs after Isha, and to fast three days of every month, saying: \"It is the fasting of the age,\" and to not sleep except upon Witr. And he said to me: \"O Abu Hurayrah, pray two rak'ahs at the beginning of the day and I will guarantee for you its end.\""],[4915,"Allah loves that His concessions be accepted, just as the servant loves the forgiveness of his Lord."],[4916,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a military expedition toward Najd, and I was in it. Our shares of the spoils reached twelve camels each, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave each of us an extra camel as a bonus."],[4917,"The injury caused by an animal is without liability."],[4918,"The Dajjal will emerge from the Jewish quarter of Isfahan, and with him will be seventy thousand Jews wearing cloaks."],[4919,"The people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter."],[4920,"A man was admonishing his brother about modesty, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Leave him, for modesty is part of faith.'"],[4921,"We are not inherited from; what we leave behind is charity."],[4922,"He came to Aisha and asked permission to enter, and she disliked to grant him permission. When the Prophet ﷺ came, she said: 'O Prophet of God, Abu Qu'ays came to me and I refused to grant him permission.' He said: 'Let your uncle enter upon you.' Abu Qu'ays was the brother of Aisha's foster-mother."],[4923,"Glory be to God! What has come upon you, and what are you facing?' three times. He said: Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'Has revelation come down? Has a promise arrived?' He said: 'God forgives on the first night of the month of Ramadan all the people of this qiblah.' Then a man in front of him, shaking his head, said: 'Bakh, bakh!' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'It is as if your chest has become tight?' He said: 'No, but I remembered the hypocrite.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The hypocrite is a disbeliever, and the disbeliever has no share in that.'"],[4924,"He said: 'Throw half of me into the sea and half of me on land.' He said: 'Then He called the sea with what it contained, and the land with what it contained, and said: \"What made you do what you did?\" He said: \"O Lord, fear of You.\" He said: Nothing else rescued him.'"],[4925,"Regarding the Night of Decree: it is the seventh or ninth night, and the angels that night on earth are more numerous than the number of pebbles."],[4926,"The fragrance of Paradise is found at a distance of five hundred years, but no one who reminds others of his deeds, no disobedient child, and no habitual drunkard will find its scent."],[4927,"We entered upon Abdullah b. al-Harith b. Jaz' al-Zubaydi on a Friday, and he called for a basin and urinated into it, and said to the slave girl: 'Cover me,' so she covered him. Then he said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid any of you from urinating while facing the qiblah.'"],[4928,"We were at al-Mirbad when a Bedouin came to us with a piece of leather and said: 'Look at what is in it.' It was a letter from the Messenger of God ﷺ to the Banu Zuhayr b. Uqaysh, a clan of Ukul: 'If you establish prayer, give zakat, and pay the fifth of what you gain as spoils, and the Prophet's share and the select portion, then you are secure with God's protection.' I said: 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'I heard him say: \"Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month removes the rancor of the chest.\"' We said: 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'I see you suspect me.' He took the scroll and left quickly. We asked about him and were told: 'This is al-Namir b. Tawlab al-Ukli.'"],[4929,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ hastened in killing until their killing reached children, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Every newborn is born upon the natural disposition until his parents make him a Jew or a Christian.'"],[4930,"Umm al-Harir, when a man of the Arabs died, it would be hard on her. It was said to her: 'Umm al-Harir, why do we see that when a man of the Arabs dies it is hard on you?' She said: 'I heard my master say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Part of the approach of the Hour is the destruction of the Arabs.\"'"],[4931,"For what the sky and springs water, a tenth is due; for what is watered by artificial means, half of a tenth is due."],[4932,"Whoever is afflicted by a calamity and, when remembering it, says: 'We belong to Allah and to Him we return,' Allah renews for him the reward of that calamity equivalent to what it was on the day it struck him."],[4933,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I bought a slave, so what should I do with him?' He said: 'He is your brother in Islam. Feed him from what you eat and clothe him from what you wear. If you dislike him, then sell him.'"],[4934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to like comprehensive supplications and would leave what was between that."],[4935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the mosque when a Bedouin entered and sat down to urinate. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Stop, stop!' But the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do not interrupt him.' Then he called him and said: 'These mosques are not suitable for any impurity — or as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — they are only for reciting the Quran, prayer, and remembrance of Allah.' Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over the urine."],[4936,"Whoever I am mentioned in his presence, let him invoke blessings upon me, for whoever invokes blessings upon me once, Allah will bless him ten times."],[4937,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah, he allotted the houses as fiefs and allotted to Ibn Mas'ud among those he allotted. His Companions said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, turn him away from us.' He said: 'Then why did Allah send me? Allah does not sanctify a nation that does not give the weak among them their right.'"],[4938,"Umar passed by Mu'adh b. Jabal while he was weeping and said: 'What makes you weep?' He said: 'A hadith I heard from the occupant of this grave — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The least amount of showing off is shirk, and the most beloved servants to Allah are the pious, hidden ones who, when they are absent, are not missed, and when they are present, they are not recognized. Those are the leaders of guidance and the lamps of knowledge.'"],[4939,"He used to pray in the place where al-Hasan and al-Husayn urinated, and he said: 'When a servant prostrates to Allah with one prostration, Allah purifies the place of his prostration to seven earths.'"],[4940,"Digest your food with the remembrance of Allah and prayer, and do not sleep upon it, lest your hearts become hard."],[4941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed me and made my emancipation my dowry."],[4942,"The Black Stone is from the stones of Paradise."],[4943,"When it was revealed: 'In it are verses that are precise — they are the foundation of the Book — and others unspecific. As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow the unspecific part, seeking discord and seeking its interpretation,' the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If you see the quarrelsome ones who dispute about it, they are the ones meant.'"],[4944,"He used to forbid the fasting person from kissing, and he would say: \"None of you has the protection [from slipping] that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had.\""],[4945,"A man called Abu Ma'qil came to me and said, \"Write.\" He wrote: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.\" He said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: My beloved Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined upon me fasting three days of every month, sleeping after performing Witr, and glorifying Allah in the forenoon (Duha)."],[4946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Dhul-Hulayfah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Syria, Yalamlam for the people of Yemen, and Qarn for the people of Ta'if."],[4947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh made in earthenware jars (al-jarr), pitch-coated vessels (al-muzaffat), gourds (al-dubba'), and hollowed-out wood (al-naqir)."],[4948,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Dhul-Hulayfah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Syria, Yalamlam for the people of Yemen, and Qarn for the people of Ta'if.\" Then he said: \"These are for their own people and for anyone who comes to them from elsewhere.\""],[4949,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ and he came to a rubbish dump of a people and urinated standing. He called me and said, \"Why did you keep away?\" So I came until I was at his heels. Then water was brought and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[4950,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed wine, the one who pours it, the one who drinks it, the one who presses it, the one for whom it is pressed, the one who carries it, the one to whom it is carried, the one who sells it, the one who buys it, and the one who consumes its price."],[4951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for them."],[4952,"I went out with Zayd b. Suhan and Salman b. Rabi'ah, and I picked up a whip. They told me to leave it, but I refused. When we arrived in Madinah, I mentioned that to Ubayy b. Ka'b, and he said: You did the right thing. During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I picked up a purse containing one hundred dinars. I told the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he instructed me to announce it for a year. I told him that it had not been claimed. Then he instructed me to announce it again, so I announced it for another year. I told him that it had not been claimed. Then he instructed me to announce it again, so I announced it for a third year. I told him that it had not been claimed. He said: \"Remember its container and its tie, then use it for your needs. If someone comes looking for it, return it to him.\""],[4953,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer one day, then ascended the pulpit and pointed with his hand toward the direction of Qiblah. When he finished, he said: \"Just now, since I prayed with you, I have seen Paradise and Hell displayed before this wall. I have never seen anything like today in good and evil\" — three times."],[4954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer and said: \"Indeed, I see you from behind just as I see you in front of me.\""],[4955,"I and the Hour were sent like these two [fingers]."],[4956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rushed to prevent a cat from passing in front of him during the prayer."],[4957,"Gifts to rulers are misappropriation."],[4958,"Whoever performs ablution should sniff water into the nose and expel it, and whoever uses stones for istinja' should use an odd number."],[4959,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity, he would perform ablution as for prayer."],[4960,"Uthman ؓ performed ablution washing each part three times, then said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution like my ablution.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then prays two rak'ahs without letting his mind wander to anything but good, his previous sins will be forgiven.'"],[4961,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us on the day of Ashura and said: 'This is a day on which fasting has not been made obligatory upon you. I am fasting, so whoever wishes to fast may fast, and whoever wishes to break the fast may do so.'"],[4962,"I ate with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar bread and meat, and they prayed without performing ablution."],[4963,"The vision is from Allah, and the dream is from Satan. If any of you sees something he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah, for it will not harm him."],[4964,"I saw us on the day of Hunayn when the two groups were retreating, and there were not one hundred men with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4965,"Perform Hajj and Umrah repeatedly, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows remove the dross of iron."],[4966,"I came from a journey and went to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'When you come to your wife, act wisely.' So I came to my wife and said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When you come to your wife, act wisely.' She said to me: 'Here I am.'"],[4967,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days from Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the whole year."],[4968,"God did not send a prophet to a people and then take him (in death) except that He placed a period of lethargy after him, and that period of lethargy is filled with Hellfire."],[4969,"Whoever guarantees me what is between his jaws and his legs, I guarantee him Paradise."],[4970,"He would arise in a state of major ritual impurity without having had a nocturnal emission, then he would perform ghusl and fast that day."],[4971,"Do not undertake a journey except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and the Mosque of Jerusalem."],[4972,"Whoever makes a display of his deeds to people, God will make a display of him to His creation on the Day of Resurrection, and He will belittle and degrade him."],[4973,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed witr at the beginning of the night, and in its middle, and then he settled on its end."],[4974,"Regarding His statement, “Indeed, We are sufficient for you against the mockers” (Q 15:95), he said: The mockers were al-Walid b. al-Mughira, al-Aswad b. Abd Yaghuth, al-Aswad b. al-Muttalib Abu Zam'ah from Banu Asad b. Abd al-Uzza, al-Harith b. Ghaytal al-Sahmi, and al-As b. Wa'il al-Sahmi. Then Jibril ﷺ came to him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ complained about them to him. So he showed him Abu Amr al-Walid b. al-Mughira, and Jibril gestured to his vein, and he said, “You have not done anything.” He replied, “I have sufficed you against him.” Then he showed him al-Harith b. Ghaytal al-Sahmi, and he gestured to his belly, and he said, “You have not done anything.” He replied, “I have sufficed you against him.” Then he showed him al-As b. Wa'il al-Sahmi, and he gestured to the sole of his foot, and he said, “You have not done anything.” He replied, “I have sufficed you against him.” As for al-Walid b. al-Mughira, he passed by a man from Khuza'ah who was fletching arrows, and an arrow struck his vein and severed it. As for al-Aswad b. al-Muttalib, he became blind. Some say he became blind in such a way, and others say he went down under a tree and began saying, “O my sons, will you not defend me? I am perishing, being pierced by a thorn in my eye.” They kept saying, “We see nothing.” It continued like that until his eyes became blind. As for al-Aswad b. Abd Yaghuth, sores broke out on his head and he died from them. As for al-Harith b. Ghaytal, the yellow water seized him in his belly until his excrement came out of his mouth, and he died from it. As for al-As b. Wa'il, while he was like that one day, a thorny splinter entered his foot until it filled with pus, and he died."],[4975,"The prayer time arrived, and among the people there were some who did not have wudu. So the Prophet ﷺ called for a large bowl, placed his hand in it, and water began to gush from between his fingers until they all performed wudu. We were nearly eighty."],[4976,"Two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third, for that hurts the believer, and God hates hurting the believer."],[4977,"On the ring of the Messenger of God ﷺ there were three lines: Muhammad on one line, “Messenger” on one line, and “of God” on one line."],[4978,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[4979,"The Isha prayer in congregation is equivalent to standing in prayer for a night, and the Fajr prayer in congregation is equivalent to standing in prayer for a night."],[4980,"Whoever conceals the private fault of his brother, it is as if he brought a buried infant girl back to life."],[4981,"The best of warriors in the path of God is their servant, then the one who brings them news. The one most distinguished in rank before God is the fasting one. And whoever draws a water skin for his companions in the path of God will precede them to Paradise by seventy degrees or seventy years."],[4982,"God will admit to Paradise by a single arrow three people: its maker, who seeks reward through his work; the one who strengthens it; and the one who shoots it."],[4983,"God has overlooked for my community what their souls whisper to them, as long as they do not act upon it or speak of it."],[4984,"Dihya b. Khalifa al-Kalbi said: 'O Messenger of God, shall we not mate a donkey with a horse for you, so that it produces for you a mule that you can ride?' He said: 'Only those who do not know do that.'"],[4985,"Perform the Hajj, for the Hajj washes away sins just as water washes away dirt."],[4986,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'O Ali, shall I not teach you a supplication that if you call upon God with it, you will be forgiven, even if you were already forgiven?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'There is no god but God, the Most High, the Magnificent. There is no god but God, the Most High, the Generous. There is no god but God, Lord of the Magnificent Throne.'"],[4987,"It was said to him: 'You have spoken well of Abdullah b. Masud?' He said: 'What prevents me from that, when I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Learn the Quran from four: from Abdullah b. Masud, Salim the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfa, Ubayy b. Kab, and Muadh b. Jabal.\" Then he said: \"I have considered sending them to the nations as Jesus sent the disciples.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, why not send Abu Bakr and Umar, for they are better?\" He said: \"I cannot do without them. They are to this religion like hearing and sight are to the head.\""],[4988,"I entered upon Muawiya b. Abi Sufyan, and when I left he called me and said: 'Shall I entrust you with a hadith, O nephew, which I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ?' Then he said: 'I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Talha is among those who have fulfilled their vow.'"],[4989,"When God loves a servant, He says to Gabriel: 'I love My servant so-and-so, so love him.' Then Gabriel loves him and says to the inhabitants of heaven: 'God loves His servant so-and-so, so love him.' Then the inhabitants of heaven love him, and acceptance is placed for him on earth."],[4990,"She bought Barira from a man of the Ansar, and they stipulated the right of inheritance. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The right of inheritance belongs to the one who has granted the favor.' He said: 'And the Messenger of God ﷺ gave her the choice, and her husband was a slave. She gave Aisha some meat as a gift, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If only you had prepared for us from this meat?' Aisha said: 'It was given as charity to Barira.' He said: 'It is charity for her, and it is a gift for us.'"],[4991,"She used to perform the major ritual bath from a single vessel together with the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4992,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Makkah as two rakʿahs, the prayer of a traveler."],[4993,"The Messenger of God ﷺ fell ill and said, “Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” ʿAʾishah said, “Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man.” He said, “Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, for you are like the companions of Yusuf.” He said: Abu Bakr stood up during the lifetime of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4994,"We prostrated with the Messenger of God ﷺ in “When the sky is split asunder” and “Read in the name of your Lord.”"],[4995,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ from Madinah to Makkah, and he prayed two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs, until he returned. We stayed in Makkah for ten days, and he shortened the prayer there until he returned."],[4996,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Friday prayer Surat al-Jumuʿah and Surat al-Munafiqun."],[4997,"Witr is not obligatory, but it is a Sunnah established by the Prophet ﷺ."],[4998,"The prayer of al-Adha is two rakʿahs, and the prayer of al-Fitr is two rakʿahs, and the Friday prayer is two rakʿahs, and the traveler's prayer is two rakʿahs, complete and not shortened, according to the words of the Prophet ﷺ."],[4999,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said the takbir over the Negus four times."],[5000,"Regarding a daughter, a son's daughter, and a sister, he said: But I judge by what the Messenger of God ﷺ judged: the daughter gets half, the son's daughter gets one-sixth to complete the two-thirds, and what remains goes to the full sister."],[5001,"A Muslim does not inherit from a polytheist, nor does a polytheist inherit from a Muslim."],[5002,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not go out on the day of Fitr until he had eaten some dates, three, or five, or seven, or less than that or more, an odd number."],[5003,"He said to ʿAli, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn: I am at war with those who wage war against you, and at peace with those who make peace with you."],[5004,"O women of the believers, adhere to tahlil, tasbih, and taqdis, and count with the fingertips, for they will be made to speak and will be questioned. Do not be heedless, lest you forget the mercy."],[5005,"The Messenger of God ﷺ removed his sandals while praying, so those behind him removed their sandals. He said: \"What made you remove your sandals?\" They said: \"We saw you remove them, so we removed them.\" He said: \"Indeed Jibril\""],[5006,"\"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and behind Abu Bakr, and behind Umar, and behind Uthman, and behind Ali, and they used to begin the recitation with: Al-hamdu lillahi rabbi l-alamin, and they used to recite it: Maliki yawmi l-din.\""],[5007,"Abu Shu'ayb had a slave who was a butcher. When he saw the hardship the Messenger of God ﷺ was in, he ordered his slave to prepare food enough for five, and he sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: \"Come to us as the fifth of five.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, and a man followed them. When he reached his door, he said: \"You sent to me to come as the fifth of five, and this man has followed us. If you permit him, he will enter; otherwise he will return.\" He said: \"I permit him, so he will not return.\""],[5008,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[5009,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[5010,"Abu al-Yasar had a debt owed by a man. He came to him to demand payment at his house, and he told the slave girl: \"Say he is not here.\" Then he heard his voice, so he said: \"Come out, for I have heard your voice.\" He came out to him. He said: \"What made you do what you did?\" He said: \"Hardship.\" He said: \"By God?\" He said: \"By God.\" He said: \"Go, for what you owe is forgiven. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty or waives it for him will be in the shade of God on the Day of Resurrection — or in God's shelter.'\""],[5011,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"O Messenger of God, are there horses in Paradise? For I love horses.\" He said: \"If God admits you to Paradise, you will not wish to ride but upon a red ruby that will fly with you in Paradise wherever you wish.\" Then another man came and said: \"O Messenger of God, are there camels in Paradise?\" The Prophet ﷺ did not say to him what he said to his companion; he said: \"If God admits you to Paradise, you will have in it whatever your soul desires and your eye delights in.\""],[5012,"Indeed I have a basin extending from such-and-such to such-and-such, in which there are vessels as numerous as the stars, whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, colder than snow, and more fragrant than musk. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst again, and whoever does not drink from it will never be quenched."],[5013,"Free yourselves from the concerns of this world as much as you can, for whoever's greatest concern is this world, God will scatter his affairs and place his poverty before his eyes. And whoever's greatest concern is the Hereafter, God will gather his affairs for him and place his richness in his heart. And no servant turns his heart to God but God makes the hearts of the believers incline to him with love and mercy, and God is swifter to him with every good."],[5014,"I came to Abu al-Darda' while he was in Syria. He said: \"What brought you, my son, to this land? What urged you to it?\" I said: \"Nothing brought me except maintaining what was between you and my father.\" He took my hand and seated me, and I leaned against him. Then he said: \"How bad is the hour of lying about the Messenger of God ﷺ. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'There is no Muslim who commits a sin, then performs ablution, then prays two rak'ahs or four, obligatory or otherwise, then seeks God's forgiveness, but God forgives him.'\""],[5015,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."],[5016,"There is no might and no power except with Allah; it is a cure for ninety-nine ailments, the least of which is anxiety."],[5017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ owed a man of Banu Sa'idah a wasq of dates. The man came to him demanding repayment, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man from the Ansar to repay him. He repaid him with dates inferior to his own, but the man refused to accept them. He said, 'Do you reject what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gives?' He replied, 'Yes, and who is more entitled to justice than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' The eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ filled with tears, then he said, 'He has spoken the truth. Who is more entitled to justice than I? Allah does not sanctify a community in which the weak cannot take their right from the strong without being hindered.' Then he said, 'O Khawlah, count for him, anoint it, and repay him. There is no debtor who leaves his creditor pleased except that the beasts of the earth and the fish of the seas pray for him. And no servant who delays repaying his creditor while he is able, except that Allah records a sin for him every day and night.'"],[5018,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command Bilal to chant the adhan slowly and to recite the iqamah quickly."],[5019,"He forbade selling an animal for an animal."],[5020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked in the year of the Hajj about ramal, and he said, 'Allah has prescribed sa'y for you, so perform sa'y.'"],[5021,"It is as if I am looking at the glistening of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in ihram."],[5022,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'What clothes should I wear when I intend to enter ihram?' He said, 'Do not wear a shirt, or a qaba', or a turban, or trousers, or leather socks, unless you do not have sandals. If you do not have sandals, then wear leather socks. And do not wear any garment that has been touched by saffron or wars.'"],[5023,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'What clothes may the pilgrim in ihram wear?' He said, 'He should not wear a shirt, or a turban, or a burnous, or trousers, or leather socks, unless he cannot find sandals, in which case he may wear leather socks after cutting them below the ankles. And he should not wear a garment dyed with saffron or wars.'"],[5024,"I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he entered ihram and before he performed the ifadah when he had stoned Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[5025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the state of ihram after dawn when his mount stood up with him."],[5026,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the talbiyah, he would say: 'Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk. Inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak.'"],[5027,"I learned the talbiyah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk. Inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak.'"],[5028,"I received the talbiyah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk. Labbayk, You have no partner, labbayk. Indeed all praise and favor belong to You, and the dominion. You have no partner.\""],[5029,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \"Which hajj is best?\" He said: \"The one with loud talbiyah and abundant shedding of sacrificial blood.\""],[5030,"When we ascended, we said takbir, and when we descended, we said tasbih."],[5031,"Regarding the words of Allah: \"The hajj is [during] well-known months,\" he said: \"Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, and ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. The hajj is not obligated except in them.\""],[5032,"Wiping them removes sins—meaning the two corners."],[5033,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he began with the Black Stone and touched it, then he did ramal for three circuits and walked for four circuits. Then he recited: \"And take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.\" Then he went to the Station and prayed two rak'ahs beside it."],[5034,"He said to the Stone: \"By Allah, I know that you are a stone. Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you, I would not kiss you.\" Then he kissed it."],[5035,"I saw Umar b. al-Khattab kissing the Black Stone and saying: \"I saw Abu al-Qasim ﷺ treat you with great tenderness.\""],[5036,"Whoever wishes may do ramal, and whoever wishes may not do ramal. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only commanded ramal to show the polytheists his strength."],[5037,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah and the polytheists were [watching], the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to do ramal to show them that they had strength. When they passed by the Yamani Corner, he said: \"Hasten.\" So they walked until they reached the Black Stone."],[5038,"We performed hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"The people have said that you have perished from hunger and emaciation. When you enter, do ramal for three circuits so that the people see that you have strength.\" So we did."],[5039,"A man came to Ibn Umar while he was walking in the valley and said: \"O Ibn Umar, you command us to do sa'y while you are walking?\" He said: \"If I walk, I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walk; and if I do sa'y, I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do sa'y. And I am an old man.\""],[5040,"I said to 'A'ishah: I see no sin upon me if I do not perform the sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah. She said: Why? I said: Because I heard him [meaning Allah, or the Prophet ﷺ] say: \"So whoever performs Hajj to the House or performs 'Umrah, there is no sin upon him to perform sa'i between them.\" She said: \"It is not as you say. If it were as you say, it would be: 'There is no sin upon him if he does not perform sa'i between them.' The Hajj of one who does not perform sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah is not complete. This verse was revealed only because in the pre-Islamic period, when they entered ihram for Manat, it was not lawful for them to perform sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah. So Allah revealed: 'Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of Allah. So whoever performs Hajj to the House or performs 'Umrah, there is no sin upon him to perform sa'i between them.' So sa'i between them is one of the rites of Allah.\""],[5041,"He performed tawaf with 'Umar b. al-Khattab. 'Umar began to touch the Black Stone, and Ya'la began to touch all the corners. 'Umar said: \"Did you perform Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Did you see him touch all the corners?\" He said: \"No.\""],[5042,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing a jubbah smeared with yellow perfume, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram for 'Umrah; what should I do? He (the Prophet ﷺ) bowed his head for a long time until we thought that revelation was coming to him. Then he said: \"Where is the one asking about 'Umrah? Take off your jubbah, wash off the yellow perfume, and do in 'Umrah what you do in Hajj.\""],[5043,"Modesty is part of faith, and faith is in Paradise. Obscenity is part of harshness, and harshness is in the Fire."],[5044,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, should I record knowledge? He said: \"Yes.\" I said: What is its recording? He said: \"Writing.\""],[5045,"\"May Allah have mercy on those who shave their heads.\" They said: \"And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"May Allah have mercy on those who shave their heads.\" They said: \"And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah?\" Then after three times he said: \"And those who shorten.\""],[5046,"A mukhannath (effeminate man) was brought to the Prophet ﷺ with his hands and feet dyed. The companions of the Prophet ﷺ began to strike him with their sandals. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Beware of this one and his like regarding your women.\" They said: \"Should we not kill him, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"No. I have been forbidden to kill those who pray.\""],[5047,"Whoever builds a house for Allah - in which Allah is worshipped - from lawful wealth, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise of pearls and rubies."],[5048,"Indeed in Paradise there is a gate called al-Duha. On the Day of Resurrection a caller will call out: \"Where are those who used to persist in the Duha prayer? This is your gate, so enter it by the mercy of Allah.\""],[5049,"\"By the One who sent me with the truth, the world will not come to an end until they are afflicted with sinking into the earth, metamorphosis, and casting of stones from the sky.\" They said: \"And when will that be, O Prophet of Allah?\" He said: \"When you see women riding on saddles, singing girls becoming numerous, false testimony being given, those who pray drinking from vessels of the people of shirk - gold and silver - and men being content with men, and women with women. Then be on your guard and prepare yourselves.\" And he gestured with his hand, placing it on his forehead to cover his face."],[5050,"Leave the beards full, trim the moustaches, pluck the armpit hair, and beware of the two sides [of the moustache?]."],[5051,"The Prophet ﷺ asked Abu Bakr: \"How do you pray witr?\" He said: \"I pray witr at the beginning of the night.\" He said: \"Prudent and cautious.\" Then he asked 'Umar: \"O Abu Hafs, how do you pray witr?\" He said: \"I pray witr at the end of the night.\" He said: \"Strong and assisted.\""],[5052,"Three things: whoever has them, Allah will take him to account with an easy reckoning and admit him into Paradise by His mercy.\" They said: \"What are they, O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom?\" He said: \"You give to the one who deprived you, you maintain ties with the one who cut you off, and you pardon the one who wronged you.\" He said: \"If I do this, what will I have, O Prophet of Allah?\" He said: \"Allah will admit you into Paradise."],[5053,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the greatest kindness?\" He said: \"Your mother.\" She said: \"Then whom?\" He said: \"Then your mother.\" She said: \"Then whom?\" He said: \"Then your mother.\" She said: \"Then whom?\" He said: \"Then your father.\""],[5054,"A guest of his came to Jabir b. 'Abd Allah, so he brought them bread and vinegar, and said: \"Eat, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'What an excellent condiment is vinegar. It is a ruinous thing for a people that they should despise what is presented to them, and it is a ruinous thing for a man that he should despise what is in his house that he may present to his companions.'\""],[5055,"Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who fill the gaps in the rows.\" And he said: \"Between the solitary worshipper and the congregation there are twenty-five degrees."],[5056,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"How may I know that you are the Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Do you think that if I call this cluster from this date-palm, you will testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he called the cluster, and it began to descend from the palm-tree until it fell to the ground, and then it began to leap until it came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said to it: \"Return,\" and it returned, then went back to its place. The bedouin said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.\""],[5057,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about an animal that eats dung. He said: \"Does it not graze on fresh herbage and eat from trees?\" Perhaps he said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then eat its meat.\""],[5058,"When we were forbidden to initiate conversation with the Prophet ﷺ, we used to like that an intelligent bedouin man would come and ask the Prophet ﷺ while we were with him. While we were thus, a bedouin came and said: \"O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and claimed that you claim that Allah sent you.\" He said: \"He spoke the truth.\" He said: \"Then by the One who raised the mountains, lifted the sky, and spread out the earth, did Allah send you?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Your messenger claims that you claim that we owe five prayers in the day and night.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He spoke the truth.\" He said: \"Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Your messenger claims that you claim that we owe fasting for a month in the year.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He spoke the truth.\" He said: \"Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Your messenger claimed that you claim that we owe zakah on our wealth.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He spoke the truth.\" He said: \"Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Your messenger claims that you claim that we owe pilgrimage to the House for whoever is able to make a way to it.\" He said: \"He spoke the truth.\" He said: \"Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not leave any of them, nor will I exceed them.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"If the bedouin is truthful, he will enter Paradise.\""],[5059,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me what Allah has made obligatory on me regarding prayer.\" He said: \"Allah has made obligatory on His servants five prayers.\" He said: \"Is there anything before them or after them?\" He said: \"Allah has made obligatory on His servants five prayers.\" He said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not add anything to them, nor will I subtract anything from them.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He will enter Paradise if he is truthful.\""],[5060,"The expiation of sins is regret."],[5061,"If you were not to sin, Allah would bring a people who sin and then He would forgive them."],[5062,"Regarding the people of the covenant: They keep what they embraced Islam upon of their land, their slaves, and their livestock, and nothing is due from them in any of that except the zakah."],[5063,"When the prayer is established and one of you is fasting, let him begin with dinner before the Maghrib prayer, and do not rush away from your dinner."],[5064,"I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting among the people. He said: I sat down, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What prevented you from praying two rak'ahs before sitting? I replied: I saw you sitting and the people sitting. He said: When any of you enters the mosque, he should not sit until he prays two rak'ahs."],[5065,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sit during the two rak'ahs as if he were sitting on hot stones."],[5066,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the 'Isha' prayer: 'By the fig and the olive.'"],[5067,"When he went to his bed every night, he would bring his palms together, blow into them, and recite in them: 'Say: He is Allah, the One,' 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,' and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.' Then he would wipe with them whatever he could of his body, starting with them over his head, his face, and the front of his body. He would do that three times."],[5068,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an expedition. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Take many sandals, for a man remains a rider as long as he wears sandals."],[5069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: Which deeds are most excellent? He replied: Bringing joy to a believer by satisfying his hunger, clothing his nakedness, or fulfilling his need."],[5070,"The family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a servant girl who served them, called Barrah. A man met her and said to her: O Barrah, cover your little hairs, for Muhammad will not avail you anything against Allah. She informed the Prophet ﷺ, and he came out dragging his cloak with his cheeks reddened—we, the Ansar, would recognize his anger by the dragging of his cloak and the redness of his cheeks—so we took up arms and came to him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, command us with whatever you wish, for by the One who sent you with the truth, if you ordered us concerning our mothers, fathers, and children, we would carry out your command regarding them. He ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, and said: Who am I? We said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes, but who am I? We said: You are Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim b. 'Abd Manaf. He said: I am the master of the children of Adam, and I say this without boasting. I am the first for whom the earth will split open, and I say this without boasting. I am the first from whose head the dust will be shaken off, and I say this without boasting. I am the first to enter Paradise, and I say this without boasting. What is the matter with people who claim that my kinship will not benefit? It is not as they claim. I will intercede and my intercession will be accepted, until even the one for whom I intercede will intercede and his intercession will be accepted, until even Iblis will stretch forth in intercession."],[5071,"A caller calls out every morning: O Allah, give to the one who spends a replacement, and give to the one who withholds destruction."],[5072,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the price of blood."],[5073,"The worst of people in the sight of Allah is the two-faced one, who comes to these with one face and to those with another face."],[5074,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, by what sign will you recognize your nation? He said: They will have white marks on their foreheads and limbs from the traces of ablution."],[5075,"Purify these bodies, and Allah will purify you, for there is no servant who spends the night in a state of purity except that an angel spends the night with him in his undergarment. He does not turn during any hour of the night except that he says: O Allah, forgive Your servant, for he has spent the night pure."],[5076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to embrace while fasting, and kiss while fasting. And which of you is like him? He had the most control over his desire."],[5077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought a caravan that had arrived and made a profit in it of some ounces of gold, then gave it as charity to the widows of Banu Abd al-Muttalib. And he said: I do not buy anything for which I do not have its price."],[5078,"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus is better for him than to have it filled with poetry."],[5079,"Indeed Allah hates the eloquent man who rolls his tongue as a cow rolls its tongue."],[5080,"Charity does not decrease wealth, and Allah does not increase a servant for pardoning except in honor, and no one humbles himself but Allah raises him."],[5081,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, and I was the seventh of seven from Quraysh, and he said: 'Will you not listen?' three times. 'There will be over you leaders or rulers. Whoever enters upon them and confirms them in their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing, is not of me and I am not of him, and I am free of him. And whoever does not enter upon them, and does not confirm them in their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing, is of me and I am of him, and he will meet me and be with me.'"],[5082,"He who is moderate will not be in want."],[5083,"Among trees there is a tree that is like the Muslim man: it is the date-palm."],[5084,"Regarding His saying, 'Nay, I swear by this city,' he said: 'Makkah.' 'And you are free in this city,' he said: 'Makkah.' 'And by the father and what he begot,' he said: 'Adam.' 'Indeed, We created man in toil,' he said: 'in uprightness, in standing.'"],[5085,"Some charity meat was given to Burayrah, and she gave it as a gift to the Prophet ﷺ. It was said to him, 'It is charity meat.' He said: 'It is charity for her, and a gift for us.'"],[5086,"The family of Muhammad ﷺ never ate their fill of wheat bread until he passed away, and no leftover morsel was ever raised from the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he passed away."],[5087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command marriage and strongly forbid celibacy, and he would say: 'Marry the loving and fertile, for I will vie with the prophets through you on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[5088,"As for us, we used to give sadaqat al-fitr as dates."],[5089,"Whoever speaks about the Quran according to his own opinion and happens to be correct has still erred."],[5090,"Al-hamdu li-llahi rabbi al-alamin are seven verses, one of which is: Bismi llahi al-rahmani al-rahim. It is the seven oft-repeated verses and the great Quran, and it is the essence of the Quran and the opening of the Book."],[5091,"A servant does not believe with complete faith until he abandons lying in jest and in disputation, even if he is truthful."],[5092,"Indeed, a man's food is placed before him, and it is not lifted until he is forgiven. It was said: O Messenger of God, why is that? He said: \"He says: Bismi llah when it is placed, and al-hamdu li-llah when it is lifted.\""],[5093,"When the end of time comes, my community will become three factions: a faction that worships God sincerely, a faction that worships God for show, and a faction that worships God to consume people's wealth by it. When God gathers them on the Day of Resurrection, He will say to the one who consumed people's wealth: By My might and majesty, what did you intend by My worship? He will say: By Your might and majesty, I consumed people's wealth by it. He will say: What you collected has not benefited you at all. Take him to the Fire. Then He will say to the one who worshipped Him for show: By My might and majesty, what did you intend by My worship? He will say: By Your might and majesty, showing off to people. He will say: Nothing of it ascended to Me. Take him to the Fire. Then He will say to the one who worshipped Him sincerely: By My might and majesty, what did you intend by My worship? He will say: By Your might and majesty, You know better than I; I intended Your remembrance and Your countenance. He will say: My servant has spoken the truth. Take him to Paradise."],[5094,"It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn a deceased person for more than three days, except for a husband."],[5095,"People will be gathered in three groups: hopeful, fearful, and two on a camel, three on a camel, and ten on a camel. The Fire will gather the rest of them; it will rest with them where they rested, spend the night with them where they spent the night, be with them in the morning where they were in the morning, and be with them in the evening where they were in the evening."],[5096,"Indeed, God will make a servant reach a rank, and he will say: O Lord, how did I attain this rank? He will say: By the seeking of forgiveness of your child for you."],[5097,"Call upon God while you are certain of the answer, and know that God does not answer a supplication from a heedless, distracted heart."],[5098,"Journeys should not be undertaken except to three mosques: the Mosque of al-Khayf, the Sacred Mosque, and this mosque of mine."],[5099,"She used to rub the semen from the garment of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then he would pray in it."],[5100,"Be tolerant, and you will be treated with tolerance."],[5101,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never ate his fill of wheat bread twice in a single day until he met God, the Mighty and Majestic."],[5102,"You are today upon a religion, and I am seeking to outnumber the nations through you, so do not walk backwards after me."],[5103,"The alms of the desert dwellers are to be collected at their watering places and in their courtyards."],[5104,"A dabb lizard was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not eat it. ʿAʾishah said: O Messenger of God, shall we feed it to the poor? He replied: Do not feed them what you do not eat."],[5105,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ḥassān: Satirize the polytheists. O God, support him with the Holy Spirit."],[5106,"When he needed to relieve himself, he would not lift his garment until he was close to the ground."],[5107,"Love your beloved gently, for he may become your enemy one day, and hate your enemy gently, for he may become your beloved one day."],[5108,"Love your beloved gently, for he may become your enemy one day, and hate your enemy gently, for he may become your beloved one day."],[5109,"Stand straight, and your hearts will stand straight, and touch one another, and you will show mercy to one another."],[5110,"The Dajjāl was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: His mother will give birth to him while she is abandoned in her grave; when she gives birth to him, women will bear sinners."],[5111,"The sunnah from the Prophet of God ﷺ was established regarding the dowry of women as twelve ūqiyyahs, each ūqiyyah being forty dirhams, which is four hundred and eighty. The sunnah from the Prophet of God ﷺ was also established regarding the major ablution as one ṣāʿ, the ṣāʿ being eight raṭls, and the minor ablution as one mudd, the mudd being two raṭls. And the sunnah from him was established regarding the tithe: no zakah is due on less than five wasqs, the wasq being sixty ṣāʿs of this ṣāʿ, which is three hundred ṣāʿs."],[5112,"The two men from among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, when they met, they would not part until one of them recited to the other: “By the declining day, surely man is in loss,” then one of them would greet the other."],[5113,"The Prophet ﷺ did not see Jibril in his true form except twice. As for one time, he asked him to show him his true form, so he showed him, and he filled the horizon. As for the second, he was with him when he ascended, as in His saying: “Then he drew near and came down, and was at a distance of two bow lengths or nearer. And He revealed to His servant what He revealed.” When Jibril sensed his Lord, blessed and exalted, he returned to his true form. That is His saying: “And indeed he saw him another time, by the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, near which is the Garden of Refuge,” up to His saying: “He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord.” He said: the creation of Jibril ﷺ ."],[5114,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by us while we were digging a grave. He said: “What are you doing?” We said: “We are digging a grave for this black man.” He said: “His death brought him to his burial place.” Abu Usama said: “Do you know, O people of Kufa, why I have narrated this hadith to you? Because Abu Bakr and Umar were created from the soil of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[5115,"I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he inserted his hand under his chin and combed with his fingers. I said: “What is this?” He said: “Thus my Lord, mighty and majestic, commanded me.”"],[5116,"I sat with the Prophet ﷺ and wept. He said: “What makes you weep? If you wish to join me, then let the provision of a rider suffice you from this world, and do not mix with the rich.”"],[5117,"Whoever hears of a virtue from Allah and does not believe in it will not attain it."],[5118,"Whoever recites the Quran, memorizes it, and preserves it, Allah will admit him to Paradise and grant him intercession for a number of his household, all of whom would otherwise have deserved the Fire."],[5119,"My community will continue to pray these four rakʿahs before ʿAsr until it walks on the earth forgiven with a definitive forgiveness."],[5120,"Whoever forgets a prayer and remembers it while he is with the imam, let him complete his prayer, then make up the one he forgot, then repeat the one he prayed with the imam."],[5121,"The two prostrations of forgetfulness suffice for any addition or omission."],[5122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade ghayl, then said: “Has it harmed Persia and Byzantium?” That is when a man has intercourse with his wife while she is breastfeeding."],[5123,"Every sin Allah may forgive, except a man who dies as a disbeliever, or a man who kills a believer deliberately."],[5124,"The child is from the earnings of the parent."],[5125,"He used to connect Sha'ban with Ramadan."],[5126,"He would not blow on food or drink."],[5127,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped aside, and I stepped aside with him. I drew near to him, and he said, \"Do you have water with you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" So he washed his palms and his face, and then he went to wash his forearms. He was wearing a jubbah, and it was tight, so he took his hand out from under the jubbah and washed it. Then he wiped over his khuffs. Then he came to pray, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf was leading the people in prayer. When they saw the Prophet ﷺ, they cleared their throats. So 'Abd al-Rahman moved to step back, but he gestured to him: \"Continue.\""],[5128,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"May a fasting person kiss?\" He said: \"Ask her\" — meaning Umm Salamah, who was sitting. She said: \"Indeed, he does that.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins?\" He said: \"Indeed, by Allah, I am the most fearful of Allah among you and the most mindful of Him.\""],[5129,"He was in 'Arafah supplicating, raising his hands. The nose-rein of the she-camel fell from his hand, so he picked it up. Then he raised his hands supplicating.\" The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is earnest supplication and humility.\""],[5130,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on the day of Uhud, and when he passed Thaniyyat al-Wada', he came upon a troop of two armies. He said: \"Who are these?\" They said: \"This is 'Abdullah b. Ubayy with six hundred of his allies from the Jews of Banu Qaynuqa'.\" He said: \"Have they embraced Islam?\" They said: \"No, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Tell them to go back, for we do not seek help from polytheists against polytheists.\""],[5131,"Do not sell what you do not have."],[5132,"When the creatures meet on the Day of Resurrection, and the people of Paradise are admitted to Paradise and the people of the Fire are admitted to the Fire, a caller will call out on the Day of Resurrection: \"O people of the gathering, abandon grievances among yourselves, and your reward is upon Me.\""],[5133,"Proclaim marriages publicly."],[5134,"Some people from my community will be punished for their sins, and they will be in the Fire for as long as Allah wills. Then the polytheists will taunt them, saying: \"We do not see that your belief and faith in what you used to differ from us has benefited you.\" Then no monotheist will remain except that Allah will bring him out.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: \"Perhaps those who disbelieved will wish that they had been Muslims\" (Qur'an 15:2)."],[5135,"When the news of the death of the Negus came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Pray over him.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you pray over an Abyssinian?\" So Allah revealed: \"And indeed, among the People of the Scripture are those who believe in Allah and what was revealed to you\" (Qur'an 3:199)."],[5136,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'The dusty earth does not carry, nor does the green sky shade, anyone more truthful in speech than Abu Dharr, who resembles Jesus son of Mary.'"],[5137,"Whoever takes a span of land without right will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths; God will not accept from him any obligatory or supererogatory deed. And whoever claims descent from other than his father, or other than his patrons, has disbelieved."],[5138,"I asked Usama b. Zayd: How did the Messenger of God ﷺ travel when he departed from Arafat? He said: 'At a brisk pace, and when he found an opening, he urged his mount faster.'"],[5139,"I said: O Messenger of God, all of your wives have entered the House except me. He said: 'Go to your relative, to Shayba, and let him open the door for you.'"],[5140,"Excellent! Excellent! Five things, how heavy they are on the Scale: 'Glory be to God,' 'Praise be to God,' 'There is no god but God,' 'God is most great,' and a righteous child who dies and precedes a man."],[5141,"I heard the Commander of the Believers Ali b. Abi Talib while he was on the pulpit saying: 'I will drive away from the pool of the Messenger of God ﷺ with these two short hands of mine the disbelievers and the hypocrites, just as the water-bearers drive away strange camels from their watering places.'"],[5142,"I would tie my waist-wrapper tightly while I was menstruating, then I would enter with the Messenger of God ﷺ under his blanket."],[5143,"It is enough sin for a man that he neglects those whom he is responsible to feed."],[5144,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that the debt is before the bequest, and you recite: 'after any bequest you make or debt'; and that full brothers of the same mother inherit, to the exclusion of half-brothers from the same father."],[5145,"Whoever has three daughters, or the like of them of sisters, and suffices them and provides for them, Paradise is guaranteed for him.' We said: O Messenger of God, and two? He said: 'And two.' We think: What if we said one? He said: 'Yes.'"],[5146,"Al-Hasan used to come to Abu Hurayra while he was a boy, and he would kiss him and say: 'By my father, he resembles the Messenger of God ﷺ, broad between the shoulders.'"],[5147,"May God have mercy on a servant against whom his brother has a claim of injustice in life or property, and he comes to him and seeks to be absolved before the Day of Resurrection, for there is no dinar or dirham there; it is only good deeds.' It was said: O Messenger of God, what if he has no good deeds? He said: 'Sins will be taken from his wrongdoings and placed upon his sins.'"],[5148,"Dye gray hair, and do not bring black near it, and do not imitate your enemies among the polytheists. The best with which you dye gray hair is henna and katam."],[5149,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took gold in one hand and silk in the other, and said: “This is forbidden for the males of my community.”"],[5150,"God has servants whom He singled out for blessings for the benefit of the people. He keeps them in those blessings as long as they give of them; but when they withhold them, He strips them away from them and transfers them to others."],[5151,"Were it not that dogs are a community among communities, I would command that they be killed. So kill every jet-black one among them."],[5152,"He used to pass by the boys and greet them and supplicate for blessing for them."],[5153,"The food of a household may become little, yet their homes shine with light."],[5154,"The likeness of a sick person when he recovers and becomes healthy from his illness is like a hailstone falling from the sky in its purity."],[5155,"No man goes out of his house seeking knowledge but that God makes easy for him a path to Paradise."],[5156,"If it pleases you to look at the coarse, obeyed man among his people, then look at this one—meaning ʿUyaynah b. Ḥiṣn."],[5157,"Ask God of His bounty, for God loves to be asked, and the best of worship is awaiting relief."],[5158,"Whoever acts for God in the congregation and hits the mark, God accepts it from him; and if he errs, He forgives him. And whoever acts for God in division, then if he hits the mark, God does not accept it from him; and if he errs, he takes his seat in the Fire."],[5159,"Go forth as a scholar, or a learner, or a listener, or a lover, and do not be the fifth, lest you perish."],[5160,"The Prophet ﷺ entered one of the gardens of Madinah. He commanded me to close the gate, so I closed it. A man came and knocked on the gate. He said: “Open the gate and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and that he will lead the community after me.” I opened the gate, and it was Abu Bakr. I closed the gate. A man came and knocked on the gate. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Anas, open the gate and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and that he will lead the community after Abu Bakr.” I opened the gate, and it was Umar. I gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and that he would take charge of the affair after Abu Bakr. I closed the gate. A man came and knocked on the gate. He said: “O Anas, open the gate and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will lead the community after Abu Bakr and Umar, and that he will be afflicted with tribulation.” And it was Uthman. He praised Allah and said, “Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return,” then he entered."],[5161,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed voluntary prayer on a mat as an act of gratitude."],[5162,"When one of you has a fever, let him pour cold water over himself at dawn for three nights."],[5163,"He used to sacrifice two horned rams, and he would eat in blackness, look in blackness, and walk in blackness."],[5164,"Let one of you pray in his own mosque and not seek out other mosques."],[5165,"The angels do not accompany a group that has a bell with it."],[5166,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ missed anything of Ramadan, he would make it up in the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah."],[5167,"May Allah brighten a man who hears my words and preserves them. For perhaps a bearer of fiqh is not a faqih, and perhaps a bearer of fiqh conveys it to one who has more understanding than him. Three things upon which the heart of a Muslim man does not harbor deceit: sincerity of action for Allah, sincere counsel to those in authority, and adhering to the community of Muslims, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."],[5168,"The Prophet ﷺ promised her that she would pray in the House, and he ordered her to pray in the Hijr. She said: “You promised me that I would pray in the House.” He said: “It is part of the House. Were it not that your people are recent in their polytheism, I would have attached it to the House.”"],[5169,"Every mention of the word qunūt in the Quran means obedience."],[5170,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I performed tawaf around the House before I threw the pebbles.” He said: “No harm.”"],[5171,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when travel urged him on, combine these two prayers: Maghrib and Isha."],[5172,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from Makkah, he would say the takbir three times, saying: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. We are returning, repenting, worshipping, prostrating to our Lord, praising. God has fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone.”"],[5173,"Ibn ‘Umar encountered severe cold while traveling, so he ordered a caller to announce: “Pray in your dwellings,” and he said: “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, when this occurred, command that.”"],[5174,"When he returned from a journey, he would make his camel kneel at al-Batḥāʾ, which is near Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to make his camel kneel there."],[5175,"When the call to the morning prayer was made, he would pray two brief rak‘ahs before the prayer was established."],[5176,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray while I was lying crosswise in front of him, and I and the Prophet ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel."],[5177,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and when we approached Madinah, I wanted to hurry ahead. He said: “Wait until the woman whose husband is absent has shaved her private parts, and the disheveled woman has combed her hair.”"],[5178,"I asked ‘Āʾishah about wiping over leather socks. She said: “Go to ‘Alī, for he used to travel with the Messenger of God ﷺ.” So I went to ‘Alī, and he said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ set for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident one day and one night.”"],[5179,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a man of handsome appearance and pleasant fragrance came and greeted. He said: “O Prophet of God, may I come close to you?” He said: “Come close.” He came close until he almost touched him, then said: “O Messenger of God, tell me what is Islam?” He said: “You testify that there is no god but God and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of God, establish the prayer, give the zakah, and fast Ramaḍān.” He said: “Then if I do this, I am a Muslim?” He said: “Yes.” The man said: “You have spoken the truth.” He said: “O Prophet of God, tell me what is faith (al-īmān)?” He said: “That you believe in God, His angels, His Book, His messengers, and the resurrection, and you believe in the divine decree, all of it, its good and its evil.” He said: “Then if I do that, I am a believer?” He said: “Yes.” The man said: “You have spoken the truth.” He said: “What is spiritual excellence (al-iḥsān)?” He said: “You fear God as though you see Him, and if you do not see Him, He sees you, and you love for people what you love for yourself.” He said: “Then if I do that, I am a doer of excellence?” He said: “Yes.” The man said: “You have spoken the truth.” The man said: “Then when is the Hour?” He said: “The one questioned knows no more about it than the questioner, but it has signs and indications.” He said: “What are they?” He said: “When you see the barefoot, naked, destitute become kings of the people, and you see shepherds of sheep competing in tall buildings, and the slave woman gives birth to her mistress.” The man said: “You have spoken the truth.” Then he departed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Bring the man to me.” ‘Umar said: “We sought him but could not find him.” Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “God is greatest. Gabriel wanted to teach you your religion.”"],[5180,"The well is without liability, and the mine is without liability."],[5181,"No harm and no reciprocal harm in Islam."],[5182,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in Ṣād."],[5183,"The Prophet ﷺ was taking a midday nap when a son of Khadījah called Hālah arrived. She said: “Hālah, Hālah.” So the Prophet ﷺ said: “Fear God, O ‘Āʾishah.”"],[5184,"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection is an unjust leader."],[5185,"When the two circumcised parts meet, or when the circumcised part touches the circumcised part, the full bath becomes obligatory."],[5186,"Whenever he came from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would narrate to his people and teach them. One day a man said to him, as if he were jesting: “Nothing is left for Suraqah except to teach you how to relieve yourselves.” Suraqah said: “When you go to relieve yourselves, avoid sitting in the shade and on the path. Take arrows, brace yourselves on your legs, and use an odd number of stones.”"],[5187,"Let none of you belittle himself: if he sees a matter about which something should be said and does not say it, he will meet Allah having neglected it, and He will say: “What prevented you from speaking about it?” He will reply: “My Lord, I feared the people.” He will say: “I was more deserving of being feared.”"],[5188,"Killing is martyrdom, plague is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, burning is martyrdom, and death in childbirth is martyrdom."],[5189,"A man from Kufa asked Ibn Abbas about nabidh made in earthenware jars. He placed his fingers in his ears and said: “May they be deaf if I lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard him say: ‘All of the mizr is forbidden: its black, red, green, and white.’”"],[5190,"Ali was the bearer of the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ banner on the day of Badr, and Qays b. Sa‘d was the bearer of Ali’s banner, and the bearer of the Muhajirun’s banner in all the campaigns."],[5191,"Only women and perfume were made beloved to me from this world, and the coolness of my eyes was placed in prayer."],[5192,"The believer’s lower garment reaches to the middle of the shin, and there is no blame on him for what is between that and the ankles — or below the ankles — but Allah does not look at one who lets his garment drag out of pride."],[5193,"When the Prophet ﷺ bowed in ruku‘, he made his back level, so that if water were poured on his back, it would stay there."],[5194,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man chasing a bird and said: “A devil following a devil.”"],[5195,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to sleep or eat while in a state of major ritual impurity, he would perform the ablution he does for prayer."],[5196,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise. O Allah, I love them, so love them."],[5197,"Three things I forbade you from: visiting graves, [eating] the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, and drinking from gourd vessels, green jars, and wooden vessels. Now then, visit your brothers and greet them, for in that there is a lesson. Now then, as for the meat of sacrificial animals, eat from it and store it. Now then, every intoxicant is wine, and every wine is unlawful."],[5198,"There will emerge within this community a people whose mark is shaving. They will pass through the religion as an arrow passes through its target, then they will never return to it."],[5199,"He used to deliver the sermon leaning against a palm trunk, resting his back on it. It was said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, Islam has spread and people have become many, and delegations come to you from all horizons. If only you would order something to be made for you to stand on.\" He said to a man, \"Can you make the pulpit?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"So-and-so.\" He said, \"You are not its maker.\" Then he called another and said, \"Can you make the pulpit?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said the same as he said to this one. The man said, \"Yes, if Allah wills.\" He said, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"Ibrahim.\" He said, \"Take up its making.\" When he had made it, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended it, and the trunk—the palm trunk—yearned like a she-camel. The people of the mosque—or he said: the people of Madinah—heard its sound. He descended and embraced it, and it became still. He said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, had I left it, it would have kept yearning until the Day of Resurrection—or it would have kept yearning as long as I did not leave it.\""],[5200,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a stray sheep?\" He said, \"It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about dates hanging on a palm?\" He said, \"Its value, and the like of it with it, and lashes as an exemplary punishment. But when the drying-floor shelters it, then if its value reaches the price of a shield, there is amputation.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a mountain guarded flock?\" He said, \"Its value, and the like of it with it.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a found item?\" He said, \"If it is in a populated village or on a well-traveled road, announce it for a year. If you find its owner, then that is his; otherwise it is Allah's wealth, which He gives to whom He wills. And on buried treasure, the fifth is due.\""],[5201,"\"A pilgrim never becomes destitute.\" It was said to Jabir, \"What is 'destitute'?\" He said, \"He does not become poor.\""],[5202,"I said, \"O my father, you prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, behind Abu Bakr, behind Umar, and behind Uthman. Did they perform qunut in the dawn prayer?\" He said, \"O my son, it is an innovation.\""],[5203,"Allah will fill your hands with non-Arabs, and they will become lions who do not flee, striking your necks and taking your spoils."],[5204,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is called, begin with the evening meal."],[5205,"The best of you are those with the softest shoulders in prayer, and there is no step greater in reward than a step a man takes to fill a gap in a row."],[5206,"A woman should not have skin contact with a woman, and a man should not have skin contact with a man, under a single garment."],[5207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: \"A book Allah has written, in it are the names of the people of Paradise with their names and lineages, summarized for them, nothing added to them and nothing subtracted from them until the Day of Resurrection. The person of Paradise is sealed with the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the person of the Fire is sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire, even if he does any deed. The people of felicity may be led along the path of the people of wretchedness until it is said, 'How similar they are to them; rather, they are from among them,' and then felicity overtakes them and rescues them. And the people of wretchedness may be led along the path of the people of felicity until it is said, 'How similar they are to them; rather, they are from among them,' and then wretchedness overtakes them. Whoever Allah has written as felicitous in the Mother of the Book, He will not take him out of this world until He makes him act with a deed that brings him felicity before his death, even if by the interval between two milkings of a camel.\" Then he said, \"Deeds are by their endings; deeds are by their endings.\""],[5208,"Umar b. al-Khattab said to Ali b. Abi Talib: O Abu al-Hasan, sometimes you were present when we were absent, and sometimes we were present when you were absent. There are three things I will ask you about; do you have knowledge of them? Ali said: What are they? He said: A man loves a man though he has seen no good from him, and a man hates a man though he has seen no evil from him. He said: Yes. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The spirits are in the air, mustered troops; they meet and smell one another. Those that recognize each other come together, and those that fail to recognize each other separate. Umar said: One. And the man who relates a hadith then forgets it, then remembers it. Ali said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: There is no heart that does not have a cloud like the cloud of the moon. While the moon is shining, a cloud passes over it and it darkens; when it clears, it shines again. While a man is relating, a cloud passes over him and he forgets; when it clears, he remembers. Umar said: Two. And he said: A man sees a dream, some of which come true and some of which prove false. He said: Yes. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: No male or female servant sleeps and falls into deep sleep except that his spirit is taken up to the Throne. The dream that does not wake except at the Throne is the one that comes true, and the one that wakes before reaching the Throne is the dream that proves false. Umar said: Three things I was seeking; praise be to God who let me find them before death."],[5209,"God does not intend gentleness for a household except that it benefits them, and He does not withhold it from them except that it harms them."],[5210,"I would not like to spend a night without having a debt upon me, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: No servant has a debt and is concerned about it except that he has aid from God with him until he pays it off. So I would not like God's aid to leave me."],[5211,"The Prophet ﷺ established brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Ibn Mas'ud."],[5212,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the Zuhr prayer: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High.'"],[5213,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the sale of something with an exception until it is known."],[5214,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated, he would turn the palms of his hands toward his face."],[5215,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, God will surely admit into Paradise the one who is corrupt in his religion yet foolish in his livelihood, and by the One in Whose hand is my soul, God will surely admit into Paradise a believer whom the Fire has scorched, and by the One in Whose hand is my soul, God will surely forgive on the Day of Resurrection with a forgiveness that does not cross the heart of any human, and by the One in Whose hand is my soul, God will forgive on the Day of Resurrection with a forgiveness for which Iblis will stretch out in hope that it might reach him."],[5216,"When a man sets out for Hajj with pure provision and puts his foot in the stirrup and calls out: Here I am, O God, here I am, a caller from heaven calls to him: Here I am and at Your service; your provision is lawful, your mount is lawful, and your Hajj is accepted and not sinful. But when he sets out with impure provision and puts his foot in the stirrup and calls out: Here I am, a caller from heaven calls to him: No here I am and no at your service; your provision is unlawful and your spending is unlawful, and your Hajj is not accepted."],[5217,"These wailing women will be made on the Day of Resurrection into two rows in Hell, a row on their right and a row on their left, barking at the people of the Fire as dogs bark."],[5218,"Three things: whoever does not have them, then he will be forgiven for what is besides that, if God wills: one who dies not associating anything with God, one who is not a sorcerer following sorcerers, and one who does not bear malice against his brother."],[5219,"Between my chamber and my prayer place is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."],[5220,"The Arabs' genealogies reach back to their fathers' birthplaces, the growths of wormwood and southernwood."],[5221,"Three persons the angels do not approach: the drunkard, the one perfumed with saffron, and the one in a state of major ritual impurity."],[5222,"When Ja'far b. Abi Talib came from Abyssinia, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'What was the most wondrous thing you saw there?' He said: 'I saw a woman carrying a basket of food on her head. A horseman passed by at a gallop and knocked it off, so she sat down gathering it up. Then she turned to him and said: Woe to you on the day when the King sets up His throne and takes for the wronged from the wrongdoer.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, confirming her words: 'A people is not sanctified'—or 'how can a people be sanctified—when its weak cannot take his right from its strong without being shaken?'"],[5223,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen—and when I set off from him, he sent after me and said: 'Do you know why I sent for you? I sent because of the acquisition. You must not acquire anything except what you have been permitted, for that is stealing from the spoils, and whoever steals from the spoils will come with what he stole on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[5224,"A house in which there are no dates, its people are hungry."],[5225,"When the heat becomes intense, then delay the prayer until it is cooler, for intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[5226,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[5227,"Whoever prays the night prayer in congregation and prays four rak'ahs before leaving the mosque, it is equivalent to the Night of Decree."],[5228,"The best of you are those with the softest shoulders in prayer. And no step taken by a servant is greater in reward than a step a man walks to a gap in the row and fills it."],[5229,"You were commanded to ask forgiveness for your predecessors, but you revile them. Verily, I heard your Prophet ﷺ say: 'This community will not perish until its last ones curse its first ones.'"],[5230,"Five things the Messenger of God ﷺ never abandoned whether at home or on a journey: the mirror, the kohl container, the comb, the hair-parting iron, and the tooth-stick."],[5231,"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day besides the obligatory prayers, God builds for him a house in Paradise: two rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Zuhr, two rak'ahs before Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, two rak'ahs after Isha, and two rak'ahs before Fajr."],[5232,"Go forth early in seeking knowledge, for I asked my Lord to bless my community in its early morning, and to make that on Thursday."],[5233,"I entered upon Jabir b. Abd Allah, and he led us in prayer wearing a single garment, and he mentioned that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray in a single garment."],[5234,"I was forbidden to pray behind those who are conversing and those who are sleeping."],[5235,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the two rak'ahs before dawn: “Say, O disbelievers” and “Say, He is God, the One.”"],[5236,"There is no servant but has a reputation in heaven. If his reputation in heaven is good, it is placed on earth; and if his reputation in heaven is evil, it is placed on earth."],[5237,"I did not fast with the Messenger of God ﷺ twenty-nine days more often than I fasted thirty."],[5238,"The Qur'an was revealed in seven ahruf."],[5239,"There will emerge in this community a people with whips like the tails of cattle. They go forth in God's displeasure and return in His wrath."],[5240,"The Messenger of God ﷺ made a distribution, giving to some people and leaving others. I said, “O Messenger of God, you gave to so-and-so and withheld from so-and-so, though he is a believer.” He said, “Do not say ‘believer’; say ‘Muslim.’”"],[5241,"We were with Anas b. Malik, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ—when a man was brought to him for the funeral prayer—say, “Does your companion owe any debt?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “What benefit is it to you that I pray over a man whose soul is held in pledge in his grave and does not ascend to heaven? If a man guarantees his debt, I will stand and pray over him, for my prayer will benefit him.”"],[5242,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not favor some over others in division. There was hardly a day except that he went around to all of us, and he would touch each wife without intercourse until he reached the one whose day it was, and he would stay with her. Sawdah bt. Zam'ah said to him when she had grown old and feared that he would separate from her, “O Messenger of God, my day with you is for A'ishah.” He accepted that from her. Concerning her and the like of her was revealed: “If a woman fears from her husband contempt or evasion” [Qur'an 4:128]."],[5243,"The funeral prayer was offered over the Messenger of God ﷺ for three days."],[5244,"You have two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness."],[5245,"Habib b. al-Harith came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who often commits sins.\" He said: \"Repent to Allah, O Habib.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I repent and then I return.\" He said: \"Every time you sin, repent.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, then my sins will become many.\" He said: \"Allah's pardon is greater than your sins, O Habib b. al-Harith.\""],[5246,"For the bearer of the Qur'an, if he makes lawful its lawful and prohibits its unlawful, he may intercede for ten of his household, each of whom would have been destined for the Fire."],[5247,"I said to Anas b. Malik: \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ have grey hair?\" He said: \"I do not think there were fifteen white hairs in his head and beard. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to touch them with yellow dye.\""],[5248,"Those who love one another for the sake of Allah will be on a pillar of ruby, with a hollow ruby pavilion sixty miles high in the sky. In every part of it there will be spouses whom the others do not know. One of them will look over the people of Paradise and fill them with light, so that the people of Paradise will say: 'What is this that has happened?' Some will say to others: 'What is this light that has appeared?' Some will say to others: 'A man from among those who love one another for the sake of Allah has looked over you.'"],[5249,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a house crowded with people. He stood at the door. The Prophet ﷺ looked right and left and saw no place, so he took his cloak, folded it, then threw it to him and said: 'Sit on it.' Jarir took it, clutched it and kissed it, then returned it to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'May Allah honor you, O Messenger of Allah, as you have honored me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When a noble person of a people comes to you, honor him.'"],[5250,"Whoever dies ill dies a martyr."],[5251,"Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr and my cousin."],[5252,"When the Prophet ﷺ married me, my mother treated me with everything, but I did not gain weight. She fed me cucumber with fresh dates, and I gained weight in the best way."],[5253,"Whoever cannot find sandals—meaning the pilgrim in ihram—should wear leather socks and cut them below the ankles."],[5254,"My nation on earth is more numerous than the number of pebbles or the number of raindrops."],[5255,"It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will we have intercourse with our wives in Paradise?' He said: 'A man will have intercourse with a hundred virgins in a day.'"],[5256,"I used to perform ablution for the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was standing and he was sitting."],[5257,"I did not give Umm Kulthum in marriage to Uthman except by revelation from heaven."],[5258,"The imam is a guarantor, and the muezzin is a trustee. O God, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."],[5259,"Make your rows straight, for straightening the row is part of excellence in prayer."],[5260,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man with a disability and prostrated; Abu Bakr received a conquest and prostrated; and Umar received a conquest and prostrated."],[5261,"When one of you removes his shoes during prayer, let him not place them in front of him so that he follows them, nor behind him so that his Muslim brother follows them; rather, let him place them between his legs."],[5262,"Spending in Hajj is like spending in the path of God; a dirham is multiplied seven hundred times."],[5263,"My close friend and chosen one ﷺ enjoined upon me three things and forbade me from three things. He commanded me to pray the two rak'ahs of Duha, not to sleep except after performing Witr, and to fast three days of every month. He forbade me, when I prostrate, from squatting like a monkey, pecking like a crow, or turning like a fox."],[5264,"A ruqya for fever was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'Show it to me.' They presented it: 'In the name of God, a head wound of a horned one, salt of the sea of Qiftā.' He said, 'These are covenants that Sulayman ﷺ took upon the creeping creatures. I see no harm in them.' The narrator said: A man was stung while with 'Alqama, and he recited this ruqya over him, and it was as if he was released from a fetter."],[5265,"I entered upon Ali b. Abi Talib and said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, when we leave you we hear hadiths narrated from you that we do not hear from you directly. Did the Messenger of God ﷺ entrust you with anything besides the Book of God?' He said, 'No, except what is in this sheet.' Then he called his servant girl and she brought the sheet, and in it was written: 'Ibrahim ﷺ made Makkah sacred, and I have made Madinah sacred. Its thorn trees shall not be cut, and its game shall not be startled. Whoever commits an offense in it or shelters an offender, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. The believers are one hand against those besides them; the lowest of them may give protection on their behalf. A believer is not to be killed for a disbeliever, nor a covenant holder during his covenant.'"],[5266,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to call the Farewell Pilgrimage the Pilgrimage of Islam."],[5267,"No two men love each other for God's sake in absentia except that the more beloved of them to God is the one who loves his companion more."],[5268,"He (the Prophet ﷺ) was asked about drinks, and he said: \"Shall I not tell you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He forbade the gourd (dubba'), the green jar (hantam), the pitched vessel (muqayyar), and the varnished jar (muzaffat).\" I said: \"What is hantam?\" He said: \"The green and white (jars).\" I said: \"What is muqayyar?\" He said: \"Anything coated with pitch, whether a water-skin or something else.\""],[5269,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one night during Ramadan: \"O 'A'ishah, set up a mat for me at your door.\" So I did, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to it, and those who were in the mosque gathered to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with them. The next night the mosque was crowded and full of people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and prayed the last 'Isha' prayer with them, then returned while the people were still in the mosque. He said: \"O 'A'ishah, what is the matter with the people?\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, they heard about your prayer last night, so they gathered for you to pray with them.\" He said: \"Remove your mat, O 'A'ishah.\" She said: So I did, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ [came out] at the time of the dawn prayer, prayed with the people, then turned to face them and said: \"O people, indeed your presence was not hidden from me, and I did not spend the night—praise be to Allah—unaware. But I feared that it would be made obligatory upon you, so undertake the deeds that you are able to bear, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not tire until you tire.\""],[5270,"You should use this Indian aloeswood (al-'ūd al-hindī), for in it there is a cure for seven ailments, including pleurisy (dhāt al-janb)."],[5271,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say about black seed (al-shūnīz): \"You should use this black seed, for in it there is a cure for everything except death (al-sām).\""],[5272,"He used to pray Maghrib, and men from Banu Salimah would pray with him, then they would leave for Banu Salimah while they could still see the places where arrows fell."],[5273,"Whoever swears a false oath (yamīn maṣbūrah), being lying in it, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[5274,"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is too shy before a Muslim with gray hair, if he is upright and firmly adhering to the Sunnah, to refuse him when he asks Allah—that He would not grant him."],[5275,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey at night, and he said: \"Who is this?\" I said: \"I am al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah.\" He said: \"Hold onto your (camel),\" so I held his she-camel for him, and he went off until I could not see him. Then he returned, and I poured water for his ablution. He rolled up his sleeves, but the sleeve of his jubbah was tight, so he pulled his hands out from beneath it and performed ablution: he washed his hands, his face, and his forearms, wiped his head, and wiped over his khuffs (leather socks). I said: \"Will you not remove your khuffs, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"I put them on while they were pure.\""],[5276,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we have dogs that we hunt with.\" He said: \"Look at these hunting animals (jawāriḥ); teach them from what Allah has taught you, and eat from what they catch for you. Whatever they kill without eating from it, eat from it; but whatever they kill and eat from, do not eat from it.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if other dogs mix with them?\" He forbade that."],[5277,"There is nothing between a man and disbelief (kufr) and polytheism (shirk) except abandoning the prayer (al-ṣalāh)."],[5278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a group of Banu Hashim: \"Is there anyone with you who is not from among you?\" They said: \"No, except the son of our sister—or our freed slave.\" He said: \"If any of you is afflicted by worry or hardship, let him say: 'Allah, Allah is my Lord; I associate nothing with Him.'\""],[5279,"The best of you are those with the softest shoulders in prayer."],[5280,"May Allah bless a person who hears my statement and retains it, then conveys it. For perhaps one who is told it may be more receptive than one who heard it directly. Three things in which the heart of a Muslim believer does not deceive: sincere devotion in action for Allah, giving good counsel to the rulers of the Muslims, and adhering to their community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."],[5281,"O Abu Hurayrah, learn the obligatory shares of inheritance, for it is half of knowledge, and it will be forgotten, and it is the first thing to be taken away from my ummah."],[5282,"Do not raise your eyes to the sky, lest your eyesight be snatched away."],[5283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore a silver ring on his right hand, in which there was an Abyssinian stone, and he would place its stone on the inside of his palm."],[5284,"Whoever visits a sick person remains in mercy until he sits with him, then he is immersed in it. And when he leaves him, he continues to wade through it until he returns from where he set out. And whoever consoles his believing brother for a calamity, Allah will clothe him with garments of honor on the Day of Resurrection."],[5285,"We went out on the day Hubaysh b. Duljah entered Madinah a year after the Battle of al-Harrah. He entered Madinah and ascended the minbar, and the people were alarmed, so we went out with Jabir in the Harrah, and he had lost his sight, and a stone tripped him. He said: 'May Allah make fearful the one who made the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fearful.' He said it twice or three times before we asked him. We said: 'O our father, who made the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fearful?' He said: 'I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever frightens the Ansar has frightened what is between these two sides of me.'"],[5286,"The Prophet ﷺ was told while he was at al-Aqiq: 'You are in the blessed valley or on a blessed plain.'"],[5287,"My uncle Uthman b. Maz'un sent me to bring him a blanket. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and sought his permission while he was at the trench, and he permitted me. He said: 'Whoever you meet from among them, tell them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands them to return.' That was during a severe cold. I went out and met the people, and I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to return.' By Allah, not even two or one of them turned back to me."],[5288,"Umar b. al-Khattab said to his brother Zayd b. al-Khattab on the day of Uhud: 'Take this armor of mine, my brother.' He replied: 'I desire martyrdom as you desire it,' so they both left it."],[5289,"An army during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took as spoils food and honey, and the khums (fifth) was not taken from them."],[5290,"Allah loves that His decisive commands be carried out, just as He hates that His disobedience be committed."],[5291,"There will be at the end of time people who deny the divine decree. Indeed, those are the Magians of this ummah. If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend their funerals."],[5292,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited every fanged beast and every bird with talons."],[5293,"When one of you enters upon his Muslim brother and he feeds him food, let him eat from his food and not ask about it. And if he gives him a drink, let him drink from his drink and not ask about it."],[5294,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and saw him praying in a single garment, wrapped in it. And I ate with him, and he said: 'Mention the name of God over it; eat with your right hand and eat from what is near you.'"],[5295,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and they praised him with evil, but the Prophet ﷺ welcomed him. When he turned away, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The worst of people in station before God on the Day of Resurrection is the one whose evil people fear.'"],[5296,"Woe to the heels from the Fire."],[5297,"All worldly amusement is futile except three things: your shooting with your bow, training your horse, and playing with your family, for they are from the truth. And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is more beloved to me. God, Mighty and Majestic, will admit three people to Paradise because of a single arrow: its maker, who seeks reward in it; the one who gives it; and the one who shoots it. And God, Mighty and Majestic, will admit three to Paradise because of a morsel of bread, a handful of dates, and the like of what benefits the poor: the master of the house who commands it, the wife who prepares it, and the servant who hands it to the poor.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Praise be to God who has not forgotten our servants.'"],[5298,"The poor Muslims came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, the wealthy have taken the ranks. They pray as we pray, fast as we fast, perform Hajj as we perform Hajj, and they have surplus wealth from which they give charity, but we have nothing to give.' He said: 'Shall I not guide you to a deed which, if you do it, you will catch up with those who have preceded you, and no one after you will catch up with you except one who does the like of what you do? Glorify God after every prayer thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times.' That reached the wealthy, and they said the like of what they said, so they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him. He said: 'That is God's bounty which He gives to whom He wills.'"],[5299,"There will be after me leaders who will speak from their pulpits and their word will not be rejected. They will plunge into the Fire as monkeys plunge."],[5300,"Whoever dies as a stationed soldier in the path of God, his provision will flow to him from Paradise, and his deeds will continue to increase for him until the Day of Resurrection, and he will be protected from the two testers of the grave."],[5301,"How could he not have [the capacity] to embezzle when he had [the capacity] to be killed? God, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'And they kill the prophets without right.' But the hypocrites accused the Prophet ﷺ about something, so God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: 'And it was not for a prophet to embezzle.'"],[5302,"I was riding on a donkey of mine and I met the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I moved back onto the rear of the donkey and said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God, ride.' He said: 'You are more entitled to the front of your donkey.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, the donkey is yours.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ rode on its front, and I rode on its rear."],[5303,"While I was in one of the gardens of Madinah, I caught sight of a woman, and I had no concern other than her until she passed by me. Then I followed her with my gaze until I reached the wall, and I turned and my face was scratched and made me bleed. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I am ruined.' He said: 'And what is that, O Abu Tamimah?' I told him, and he said: 'When God, Mighty and Majestic, intends good for a servant, He hastens the punishment of his sin in this world. Our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, is too generous to punish a sin twice.'"],[5304,"Ali b. Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl, and the Prophet ﷺ said: If you marry her, return our daughter to us."],[5305,"My brother and I bought one hundred shares of the shares of Khaybar. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Two hungry wolves left among a flock whose owner has neglected it are not more destructive to it than a Muslim's seeking wealth and honor for the sake of his religion."],[5306,"Hamza and the Prophet ﷺ were discussing the world, and the Prophet ﷺ said: The world is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with its due right will be blessed in it, but many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger will have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[5307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated in the trash area of Banu so-and-so, and he said: O Mughira, do you have water? I said: Yes, a waterskin of water, and he was wearing a Syrian jubbah with tight sleeves. So he performed wudu and wiped over his feet and over his khuffs."],[5308,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage being brought a bone with meat on it while he was circumambulating the House, or on the Day of Sacrifice, and he took a bite from it and did not perform wudu."],[5309,"Whoever goes out as a pilgrim and dies, the reward of a pilgrim will be written for him until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever goes out for Umrah and dies, the reward of one performing Umrah will be written for him until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever goes out as a warrior and dies, the reward of a warrior will be written for him until the Day of Resurrection."],[5310,"What do you say to your rulers when you enter upon them? They said: We say to them what they like. He said: Then when you leave them, what do you say? They said: We say what they do not like. He said: This is what we used to consider hypocrisy at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5311,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the rows and said: Repeat the prayer."],[5312,"Whoever sees someone afflicted and says: Praise be to Allah who has spared me from what He has afflicted you with and favored me over many of those He created with a great favor, that affliction will not befall him."],[5313,"Feeding food and speaking good words will enable you to enter Paradise."],[5314,"Do you know which charity is best? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The manihah: that one lends a dirham or the back of a mount."],[5315,"Wiping is for the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night."],[5316,"I am a guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise, and a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest part of Paradise, for whoever abandons disputation even if he is right, abandons lying even if he is joking, and has good character."],[5317,"Whoever reaches Arafah before the sun rises has attained the Hajj."],[5318,"\"O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion, for there is no religion except Your religion.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, are the hearts of the servants in the hand of God?\" He said: \"Yes, between two fingers of the fingers of God; if He wants to turn the heart of a servant, He turns it.\""],[5319,"It is part of the Sunnah to pray in the cemetery."],[5320,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ touching his beard during the prayer."],[5321,"Labbayk with an Umrah and a Hajj."],[5322,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a man who has intercourse with his wife in her anus. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"That is the minor sodomy.\""],[5323,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to Ali: \"You are to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me.\""],[5324,"I am in Paradise, and Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman, Sa'd, and Sa'id b. Zayd."],[5325,"I used to perform ghusl with the Messenger of God ﷺ from a single vessel, and I would not undo my hair."],[5326,"When the Prophet ﷺ fell ill, he said: \"Bring me a sheet and an inkpot so I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray.\" We disliked that most intensely. Then he said: \"Bring me a sheet so I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray.\" The women from behind the curtain said: \"Do you not hear what the Messenger of God ﷺ is saying?\" I said: \"You are the companions of Joseph. When the Messenger of God ﷺ is ill, you wring your eyes, and when he is well, you ride his neck.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Leave them, for they are better than you.\""],[5327,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away, Abu Bakr and I went to Ali and said: \"What do you say about what the Messenger of God ﷺ left behind?\" He said: \"We are the most entitled of the people to the Messenger of God and to what he left.\" I said: \"And what is in Khaybar?\" He said: \"And what is in Khaybar.\" I said: \"And what is in Fadak?\" He said: \"And what is in Fadak.\" I said: \"By God, not until you cut our necks with saws, then no.\""],[5328,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ sorrowful, not lifting his head. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Why do I see you, O Jibril, sorrowful?” He said: “I saw a blast from Jahannam, and my soul has not returned to me yet.”"],[5329,"I entered upon Ali b. Abi Talib, and he said: “Shall I teach you a supplication that the Messenger of God ﷺ taught me?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Say: O God, open the ears of my heart to Your remembrance, and grant me obedience to You and obedience to Your Messenger ﷺ, and action according to Your Book.”"],[5330,"I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of God ﷺ for ten days; we had no food except the leaves of basham and the thorns of qatad, until the corners of our mouths became sore."],[5331,"Intercession is for whoever says: There is no god but God."],[5332,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought some robes. He sent a robe to Umar. Umar came carrying his robe on his hands and said: “O Messenger of God, you sent me this silk robe, and you said about it what you said?” He said: “I did not send it to you to wear it, but sell it and benefit from its price.”"],[5333,"Whoever takes in an orphan, whether his own or another’s, and cares for him until God makes him self-sufficient, Paradise is guaranteed for him."],[5334,"Sheep are among the animals of Paradise, so wipe their noses and pray in their folds."],[5335,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave me the kunya: Abu Yahya."],[5336,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, by God, I stay away from the dawn prayer because of how long our imam prolongs it.” The Messenger of God ﷺ became angry and addressed the people, saying: “Among you are those who drive people away. When you lead the people in prayer, be brief, for among them are the elderly and those with needs.”"],[5337,"He forbade exchanging money for money."],[5338,"Every newborn is born upon the fitra."],[5339,"When a believer falls ill, God purifies him from sins just as the bellows removes the dross from iron."],[5340,"Whoever eats or drinks forgetfully in Ramadan, there is no makeup due on him, nor expiation."],[5341,"I witnessed Madinah while Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas were there. A man came to its governor and testified before him to sighting the crescent of Ramadan. He asked Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas about his testimony, and they instructed him to accept it. They said: The Messenger of God ﷺ accepted the testimony of a single man for sighting the crescent of Ramadan, and the Messenger of God ﷺ did not accept any testimony for breaking the fast except the testimony of two men."],[5342,"I resolved to send teachers among the people, as Jesus son of Mary sent the disciples to the Children of Israel.\" It was said to him: Where are you with Abu Bakr and Umar—will you not send them? He said: \"I cannot do without them; they are to the religion like the head to the body."],[5343,"The children of the polytheists are servants of the people of Paradise."],[5344,"Whoever withholds grapes during the days of harvest until he sells them to a Jew, a Christian, or anyone who will make them into wine, has certainly plunged into the Fire with clear insight."],[5345,"I heard al-Hajjaj delivering a sermon and he mentioned something I disapproved of. I then mentioned the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ: It is not fitting for a believer to humiliate himself. I said: O Messenger of God, how does he humiliate himself? He said: He exposes himself to trials he cannot bear."],[5346,"The Prophet ﷺ married Safiyya and made her manumission her dower, and he gave a wedding feast for the people with hais on a leather mat."],[5347,"Would any of you be unable to recite a third of the Quran? They said: Who can do that? He said: Can any of you not recite 'Say: He is God, the One'? Indeed it equals a third of the Quran."],[5348,"I will intercede on the Day of Resurrection for everything on the face of the earth, from stone and clod."],[5349,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said about a dead lamb he came upon: Do you see this—how worthless it became to its owners when they threw it away? They said: Yes, by God, O Messenger of God. He said: The world is more worthless to God than this is to its owners when they threw it away."],[5350,"God, Blessed and Exalted, descends every night when the last third of the night remains and says: Who calls upon Me that I may answer him? Who asks of Me that I may give him? Who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him—until dawn breaks."],[5351,"A man from those before you transgressed against himself. When death came to him, he said to his family: When I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter me in the wind over the sea. They did that to him. Then God, majestic is His mention, said to the wind: Gather what is in you. And behold, he was standing. He said: What made you do what you did? He said: Fear of You, O Lord. He said: I have forgiven you."],[5352,"Whoever buys a slave with the intention of freeing him, he should not stipulate to her owners the freeing, for indeed it is his contract from slavery."],[5353,"It is not proper for a scholar to remain silent about his knowledge, nor is it proper for an ignorant person to remain silent about his ignorance. Allah, majestic is His mention, said: 'Ask the people of the Reminder if you do not know.'"],[5354,"Whoever performs ablution thoroughly in severe cold will have a double reward."],[5355,"I asked Aishah about wiping over the leather socks. She said: 'Go to Ali b. Abi Talib, for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So I went to him and asked him. He said: 'We used to travel with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we would not remove our leather socks for three days and their nights, and for a resident, a day and a night.'"],[5356,"I asked Anas b. Malik: 'Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye his hair?' He said: 'No, but Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ dyed with henna and katam.'"],[5357,"Were it not for the emigration, I would have been a man of the Ansar."],[5358,"Intercession is for those who said: 'There is no god but Allah.'"],[5359,"I was commanded to prostrate on seven parts: on the forehead, the two palms, the two knees, and the two feet."],[5360,"Whoever I take his two precious ones (i.e., his eyes), and he is patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise."],[5361,"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, and says something good or conveys something good."],[5362,"Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakrah saw people praying the Duha prayer, and he said."],[5363,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, laughs at the despair of His servants and their hopelessness, while His mercy is near to them."],[5364,"Carry out the prescribed punishments on those whom your right hands possess."],[5365,"One day some people were at the door of the Messenger of God ﷺ disputing about the Qur’an. The Prophet ﷺ came out with his face changed, and he said: “O people, by this the nations before you were destroyed. The Qur’an confirms one part of it another, so do not give the lie to one part of it by another.”"],[5366,"There is no zakat due on a man’s slave or his horse."],[5367,"Whoever eats food should not wipe his hand until he has licked his fingers, for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies."],[5368,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ ate food, he would lick his fingers and say: “Licking the plate is a blessing.”"],[5369,"I passed by your grandfather ‘Abd al-Wahid b. ‘Abd Allah b. Busr while I was on a military expedition and he was governor of Hims. He said to me: “O Abu ‘Amr, shall I not relate to you a hadith that will please you? By God, I have often kept it hidden from the rulers.” I said: “Yes.” He said:"],[5370,"He used to give extra shares of booty in his military expeditions."],[5371,"When he ate, he would say: “Praise be to God who fed and gave drink, and made it easy to swallow, and made for it an exit.”"],[5372,"He used to deliver two sermons and sit between them."],[5373,"When he wanted to supplicate for a people or against a people, he would perform qunut."],[5374,"I saw us at the mountain pass of al-Rawha’ during an expedition led by the Messenger of God ﷺ. ‘Umar saw me and supplicated for me with supplications that I would not exchange for this world and all that it contains."],[5375,"Whoever goes out on this journey for Hajj or Umrah, and then dies, will not be brought to account or judged, and it will be said to him: Enter Paradise."],[5376,"He missed the Friday prayer, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to give a dinar in charity."],[5377,"My household among you is like the ark of Noah ﷺ among his people: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind is destroyed."],[5378,"Wear white garments; let the living among you wear them, and shroud your dead in them."],[5379,"Abu Bakr ؓ became angry with a man, so I said, 'Shall I strike his neck?' He replied, 'That was not for anyone after Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[5380,"I asked my father, 'Who is the best of people after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He replied, 'That is Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ.'"],[5381,"A man came to Abdullah b. Mas'ud and said, 'Which deeds are most virtuous?' He replied, 'You have asked me about what I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Prayer at its proper time, kindness to parents, and jihad in the path of Allah. Had I asked for more, he would have given me more.'"],[5382,"Aisha and Hafsa woke up fasting, then food was gifted to them and they broke their fast. The Prophet ﷺ entered, and one of them asked him about that. He told them, 'Make up a day in its place.'"],[5383,"The Prophet ﷺ entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah wearing a black turban."],[5384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and when he finished he turned to the people and said, 'Did any of you recite with me?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I say, why am I being contested in the Quran?'"],[5385,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said, 'Indeed, every prophet has a legacy and a trust, and my legacy and trust are the Ansar, so protect me in regard to them.'"],[5386,"The women used to pray the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then they would leave wrapped in their cloaks."],[5387,"Whoever rebels against my Ummah while they are united, seeking to divide their community, kill him, whoever he may be."],[5388,"I see that your dreams have concurred that it is in the last ten, meaning Laylat al-Qadr. Whoever among you is seeking it, let him seek it in the last ten."],[5389,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was urinating, and I greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. Then he entered his house, performed ablution, then came out and said: And peace be upon you."],[5390,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled by an oath with a witness."],[5391,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his forelock, his turban, and his leather socks."],[5392,"Three whom the angels do not approach: the junub, the disbeliever, and the one smeared with saffron."],[5393,"In my Ummah there will be the Mahdi. If his reign is short, then seven; otherwise eight; otherwise nine. My Ummah will enjoy in it a blessing the like of which they have never enjoyed. God will send the sky upon them with abundant rain, and the earth will not withhold any of its vegetation, and wealth will be in heaps. A man will stand and say: O Mahdi, give me, and he will say: Take it."],[5394,"Seventy prophets prayed in the mosque of al-Khayf, among them Musa ﷺ. It is as if I am looking at him, wearing two Qatrani cloaks, and he is in ihram on a camel of the Shanu'a camels, muzzled with a nose-rein of palm fiber, having two braids."],[5395,"The people of La ilaha illa Allah will not cease to be in good as long as they do not care what of their worldly affairs is lost for the sake of their religion. But when they do not care what of their religion is lost for the sake of their worldly affairs, then La ilaha illa Allah will be returned upon them, and it will be said to them: You are not truthful."],[5396,"The prayer was prescribed as two rak'ahs. The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed it in Makkah until he came to Madinah, and he prayed it in Madinah as long as God willed, then two rak'ahs were added to the prayer of residence, and the prayer of travel was left as it was."],[5397,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, the people rushed toward him, and I was among those who rushed. When I saw his face, I knew that it was not the face of a liar. I heard him say: O people, feed food, spread peace, maintain family ties, and pray while people are sleeping, and you will enter Paradise in peace."],[5398,"He, when he mentioned A'isha and narrated from her, would say: The innocent one, cleared from above seven heavens, daughter of al-Siddiq, beloved of the Beloved of God, narrated to me."],[5399,"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-some degrees."],[5400,"\"Who killed Dhu al-Thudayya? 'Ali b. Abi Talib?\" He said: \"Yes.\" She said: \"Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A people will emerge who recite the Qur'an, but it will not pass beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game. Their sign is a man with a defective hand.'\""],[5401,"The one who holds fast to my Sunnah when my community is corrupt will have the reward of a martyr."],[5402,"I used to be terrified at night, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"I am terrified at night, so I take my sword, and I do not encounter anything but that I strike it with my sword.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I not teach you words that the Trustworthy Spirit taught me?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Say: 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, which neither righteous nor wicked can transgress, from the evil of what descends from the sky and what ascends therein, and from the evil of the trials of night and day, and from every night-visitor except one who visits with good, O Most Merciful.'\" So he said them, and it left him."],[5403,"Jarir b. 'Abd Allah entered the house while it was full, and he found no place to sit. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw him his waist-wrapper or his cloak and said: \"Sit on this.\" He took it, kissed it, pressed it to himself, and said: \"May Allah honor you, O Messenger of Allah, as you have honored me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When a noble person of a people comes to you, honor him.\""],[5404,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"O my dear son, preserve Allah and He will preserve you. Preserve Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah, and when you seek help, seek help from Allah. The scrolls have dried, and the pens have been lifted. If the community strove to benefit you with something that Allah has not decreed for you, they would not be able to do so. And if the community strove to harm you with something that Allah has not decreed against you, they would not be able to do so.\""],[5405,"Some people from 'Urayna came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found Madinah unhealthy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"If only you would go out to our camels and drink from their milk and urine.\" So they did. When they recovered, they killed the Prophet's shepherd ﷺ, reverted to disbelief, and drove off the camels. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent after them, and they were brought. He cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes."],[5406,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at 'Arafat, and when he said: \"Labbaik Allahumma labbaik,\" he said: \"Indeed, goodness is only the goodness of the Hereafter.\""],[5407,"The Prophet ﷺ said the takbir for them in the dawn prayer, then he gestured to them, then he left and returned with his head dripping, and he led them in prayer. Then he said: \"I am only a human being, and I was in a state of major ritual impurity, but I forgot.\""],[5408,"I came to 'Abd Khayr al-Hamdani, who was the chief of the guards of 'Ali b. Abi Talib. When I entered upon him, he said: \"I heard 'Ali ascend the pulpit, praise Allah, extol Him, and say: 'O people, shall I not inform you of the best of this community after its Prophet? Abu Bakr, and the best of them after Abu Bakr is 'Umar, and the third, if I wished to name him, I would name him.'\""],[5409,"The people of Paradise will enter Paradise hairless, white, with curly hair, kohl-rimmed, thirty-three years old, in the form of Adam ﷺ , sixty cubits tall and seven cubits broad."],[5410,"Leaving a will is a disgrace in this world, and a fire and shame in the Hereafter."],[5411,"Whomever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in the religion."],[5412,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My father is an old man who cannot perform the Hajj. Shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"Yes, perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\""],[5413,"A man said to Abu Hurayrah: \"You have given us legal rulings about everything; it is likely that you will soon give us a ruling about defecation.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever leaves a harmful thing on a path of the Muslims, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people.'\""],[5414,"There is no riba except in deferred payment."],[5415,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never struck any of his wives, nor did he ever strike anything with his hand, except when fighting in the cause of Allah. And nothing was ever taken from him such that he sought retribution from the one who took it, unless the sacred limits of his Lord were violated, in which case he would exact retribution for Allah's sake."],[5416,"If one of you vomits or belches up food during his prayer, let him leave, perform ablution, and then continue from where he left off in his prayer as long as he has not spoken."],[5417,"If you are asked: 'Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill?' say: 'The better and more complete of them.' And if you are asked: 'Which of the two women did he marry?' say: 'The younger of them, and she is the one who came and said: \"O my father, hire him.\"' He said: \"What strength did you see in him?\" She said: \"He lifted a heavy stone and threw it.\""],[5418,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ, and he would not pass by any stone or tree except that it greeted him."],[5419,"There is no one in my ummah who has three daughters or three sisters and supports them until they are independent, except that he will be with me in Paradise like this,\" and he joined his forefinger and middle finger."],[5420,"There is no one in my ummah who has three daughters or three sisters and treats them well, except that they will be a shield for him from the Fire."],[5421,"One religious community does not inherit from another, and the testimony of one religious community is not valid against another, except for my ummah, whose testimony is valid against those other than them."],[5422,"Tell your husbands to wash away the traces of urine and feces from themselves, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command that."],[5423,"The letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ came to the disbelievers: 'Come to a common word between us and you…' to the end of the verse."],[5424,"When Abu Sufyan and his companions encamped against the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud, he said to his companions: 'I saw in a dream that my sword Dhū al-Faqār broke, and that is a calamity; and I saw cows being slaughtered, and that is a calamity; and I saw my armor on me, and it is your city—they will not reach it, God willing.'"],[5425,"On the day of Badr, there were with the Prophet ﷺ one hundred water-carrying camels, and he had two horses: one of them ridden by al-Miqdād b. al-Aswad, and the other by Musʿab b. ʿUmayr and Sahl b. Ḥunayf. His companions took turns riding the camels on the road, and the Messenger of God ﷺ, ʿAlī, and Marthad b. Abī Marthad al-Ghanawī, the ally of Ḥamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, took turns riding one camel."],[5426,"Al-ʿUzzā was in the valley of Nakhlah, al-Lāt was in al-Ṭāʾif, and Manāt was in Qudayd."],[5427,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray twenty rakʿahs in Ramadan, plus the witr."],[5428,"Whoever spends the night with the smell of grease on his hand and then something happens to him, let him blame no one but himself."],[5429,"The Kaʿbah will be destroyed by Dhū al-Suwayqatayn from Abyssinia."],[5430,"He used to recite: 'Māliki yawmi al-dīn' (Master of the Day of Judgment)."],[5431,"Whoever prays in my mosque forty prayers without missing a prayer, God will decree for him freedom from the Fire and salvation from punishment."],[5432,"Do not say, 'The month has decreased.' We fasted with the Messenger of God ﷺ twenty-nine days more often than we fasted thirty."],[5433,"Kill the solitary one, whoever he is among the people."],[5434,"The black one with the breast—Dhū al-Thudyah—is cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ."],[5435,"He saw a man leaving the mosque while the mu'adhdhin was calling the adhan, so he said: \"As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.\""],[5436,"A man asked: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best?\" He replied: \"He whose life is long and whose deeds are good.\" The man asked: \"Which of the people is worst?\" He replied: \"He whose life is long and whose deeds are evil.\""],[5437,"There will be in my ummah twenty-seven lying dajjals, among them four women. I am the Seal of the Prophets; there is no prophet after me."],[5438,"The Prophet ﷺ entered ihram after one of the two 'Isha' prayers."],[5439,"Three things are destructive: greed that is obeyed, desire that is followed, and a man's conceit about himself out of pride. And three things are saving: justice in contentment and anger, moderation in wealth and poverty, and fear of Allah in secret and in public."],[5440,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ advised me, saying: \"O Anas, perform wudu' thoroughly, and your lifespan will be increased. Greet with salam those of my ummah whom you meet, and your good deeds will be multiplied. When you enter your house, greet your household with salam, and the goodness of your house will increase. Pray the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of the often-returning to Allah. Have mercy on the young and honor the old, and you will be among my companions on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[5441,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the ghusl on Friday. He replied: \"Perform ghusl.\""],[5442,"The pilgrim does not utter a single tasbih nor a single takbir except that he is given glad tidings for it."],[5443,"Two 'umrahs expiate what is between them, and an accepted hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[5444,"Whoever purifies himself on Friday and perfects his purification, then goes to the Friday prayer and does not engage in idle talk or foolishness, it will be an expiation for him from that Friday until the next."],[5445,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates the wealthy oppressor, the ignorant elder, and the poor person who is arrogant."],[5446,"Indeed, a stone will weigh as much as seven pregnant she-camels; it will be thrown into Hellfire, and it will fall for seventy autumns without reaching its bottom."],[5447,"The neighbor has the greater right to the preemption of his neighbor, and it is to be awaited if he is absent, when their road is one."],[5448,"Whoever lies against me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[5449,"The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ used to commence recitation with “al-Hamdu lillahi rabbi al-alamin” (Praise be to Allah, Lord of the Worlds)."],[5450,"Isa b. Maryam will surely travel through the pass of al-Rawha as a pilgrim performing Hajj or Umrah."],[5451,"Isa b. Maryam will descend and remain among the people for forty years."],[5452,"The Dajjal will not enter Madinah, but he will descend at the trench, and at every breach there will be angels guarding it. The first to follow him will be women and female slaves. He will go and the people will follow him, but they will turn him back, so he returns angry until he descends at the trench. At that point Isa b. Maryam will descend."],[5453,"Whoever follows the Book of Allah, Allah will guide him from error and protect him from an evil reckoning on the Day of Resurrection. That is because Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: “Whoever follows My guidance will neither go astray nor suffer.”"],[5454,"Whoever begs while he is self-sufficient, he will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with scratches on his face."],[5455,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Should a man smooth the pebbles while he is praying? He said: If it must be done, then only once."],[5456,"Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without a valid reason will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."],[5457,"Abu Dharr took his stipend and went with a servant to buy his needs from the market. Then he used what remained to buy small coins and gave them in charity. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever hoards gold or silver and does not spend it in the way of Allah, it will be embers on the Day of Resurrection with which he will be branded."],[5458,"Abu Dharr al-Ghifari entered the mosque and bowed and hurried. I said: I do not think this old man knows what he is praying. He finished and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No servant prostrates to Allah a single prostration except that Allah raises him a degree by it and writes for him a good deed by it."],[5459,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her while there was a heap of date stones in front of her. He asked her, “What is this?” She said, “I glorify God with it, O Messenger of God.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “I have glorified since I left you more than everything you have glorified.” She said, “How did you say?” He said, “I said: Glory be to God as many as what He has created.”"],[5460,"The king of the east will march to the king of the west and kill him, then the king of the west will march to the king of the east and kill him. Then he will send an army to Madinah and they will be swallowed up. Then he will send an army and it will take captives from the people of Madinah. Then a seeker of refuge will seek refuge in the Sacred Sanctuary, and the people will gather to him like scattered birds coming to water, until three hundred and fourteen are gathered to him, among them women. He will prevail over every tyrant and son of a tyrant, and such justice will appear that the living will wish their dead were alive. He will live for seven years, and if he increases by an hour, then fourteen. Then what is under the earth is better than what is above it."],[5461,"The last funeral prayer the Prophet ﷺ prayed over, he said four takbirs over it."],[5462,"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then the fourth are the worst until the Hour arises."],[5463,"Indeed, the disbeliever will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection until sweat bridles him, so that he will say, “My Lord, give me relief even if it be to the Fire.”"],[5464,"Indeed, God will settle accounts between people on the Day of Resurrection, some from others, even the hornless sheep from the horned one, for the amount that it transgressed against it."],[5465,"On the Day of Resurrection, some people will be commanded to go to Paradise until, when they draw near to it and inhale its fragrance, and look at its palaces and what God has prepared therein for its people, it will be called out: “Turn them away from it; they have no share in it.” So they will return with a regret the like of which the first people did not return. They will say, “Our Lord, if only You had admitted us to the Fire before You showed us what we saw of Your reward and what You prepared therein for Your friends, it would have been easier for us.” He will say, “That is what I wanted for you. When you were alone you confronted Me with grave sins, but when you met people you met them humbly, showing people the opposite of what you gave Me from your hearts. You feared people and did not fear Me. You revered people and did not revere Me. You left things for the sake of people and did not leave for Me. So today I have shown you the painful punishment along with what I have deprived you of reward.”"],[5466,"If two guardians arrange a marriage, the first has more right."],[5467,"Five animals are all wicked and are killed in the sacred and profane areas: the kite, the mouse, the scorpion, the crow, and the biting dog."],[5468,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to depart on the Day of Sacrifice, but Safiyyah began menstruating. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “Will you delay us?” I said, “She has already witnessed the two processions together and performed the circumambulation.” He said, “Then let her depart.”"],[5469,"You will all certainly enter Paradise, all of you together, absolutely, except the one who runs away from God as the camel runs away from its owner."],[5470,"Son of Adam, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I will forgive you for what is in you, and I will not mind. If you were to come to Me with an earthful of sins, I would meet you with an earthful of forgiveness, as long as you do not associate anything with Me. Even if your sins reached the clouds of the sky, and then you sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you."],[5471,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us, and we were called brokers. He said to us: O company of merchants, this selling of yours is attended by swearing and Satan, so mix it with charity."],[5472,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he bowed place his hands on his knees and spread his fingers apart."],[5473,"When Ibn Umar wanted to touch the Black Stone he would say: O God, out of faith in You and belief in Your Book and the Sunnah of Your Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. Then he would invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and touch it."],[5474,"The inhabitants of the lowest heaven certainly see the inhabitants of Illiyyin just as the inhabitants of the world see the star rising on the horizon of the sky, and Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and what excellent ones! I said to Atiyya: What does 'what excellent ones' mean? He said: They are most favored."],[5475,"Your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours."],[5476,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to drink from gold and silver vessels, and to wear silk and brocade, for those are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter."],[5477,"When Abu Talib died, I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: Your misguided uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him. I said: Should I bury him while he is misguided and a disbeliever? He said: Go and bury your father, and do not do anything until you come to me. So I went and buried him, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ covered with dust. He said: Go and bathe. Then I came to him, and he supplicated for me with supplications that I would not wish to exchange for such-and-such."],[5478,"I entered the House, and there was a devil behind the door. I choked him until I felt the coldness of his tongue on my hand. Were it not for the supplication of the righteous servant, he would have remained tied up for people to see."],[5479,"I never prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of God ﷺ who prayed more lightly than the Messenger of God ﷺ while still complete."],[5480,"Whoever grows a gray hair in the path of God, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection. A man said to him: Some men pluck out gray hairs. He said: Whoever wishes may pluck his gray hair, or he said: his light."],[5481,"When shall I meet my brothers? They said: O Messenger of God, are we not your brothers? He said: You are my companions. My brothers are those who believed in me but did not see me."],[5482,"It is not proper for them to be both inveterate cursers and truthful ones."],[5483,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: “What do the Highest Assembly dispute over?” He said: “Over expiations and degrees. As for the degrees: feeding food, spreading peace, and praying at night while people sleep. As for the expiations: perfecting ablution in harsh conditions, walking to the congregational prayers, and awaiting prayer after prayer.”"],[5484,"The likeness of one who frees a slave after his death is that of one who gives a gift after he is full."],[5485,"Written on the gate of the Garden: “Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; Ali is the brother of the Messenger of Allah,” two thousand years before the heavens and the earth were created."],[5486,"He used to pray facing a pillar in the mosque and deliver sermons leaning against it. A’ishah ordered that this pulpit be made for him. When he ascended it and left his place by the pillar, the pillar let out a loud moan when the Prophet ﷺ left his place, out of longing for Allah’s Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ walked to it and embraced it. When he embraced it, the sound we heard subsided. I said: “Did you hear it?” He said: “I and the people of the mosque heard it, and it is one of the pillars next to the room.”"],[5487,"I have not ceased to hope for the caliphate since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “If you gain authority, then act well.”"],[5488,"“Who will listen from me?” I spread my garment, and when he finished I gathered it to myself. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I have not forgotten a single hadith from it."],[5489,"He said: “Hand me a handful of pebbles.” I handed them to him, and he threw them in the faces of the people. None of the people remained but their eyes were filled with pebbles. Then it was revealed: “When you threw, it was not you who threw, but Allah threw.”"],[5490,"Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and Umar, and seek guidance by the guidance of Ammar, and hold fast to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd."],[5491,"Ali and Ibn Abbas spoke about mut‘ah of women. Ali said to him: “You are an erring man. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mut‘ah of women at the Farewell Pilgrimage.”"],[5492,"Do not pray after dawn until the sun has risen, nor after ‘asr until the sun has set, and a woman must not travel for three days except with a mahram, and a woman must not be married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[5493,"Allah will surely bring out of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection people who never did any good, and admit them to the Garden by His mercy after the intercession of those who intercede."],[5494,"People will come out of the Fire and be called in the Garden “the Jahannamis.” They will call upon Allah to remove that name from them, and Allah will erase it from them. When they come out of the Fire, they will sprout as feathers sprout."],[5495,"He used to fondle her while she had a waist-wrapper on up to her knees."],[5496,"The molar tooth of the disbeliever in the Fire is like Mount Uhud."],[5497,"In Paradise there is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has not occurred to the heart of any human."],[5498,"The Hour will not come until killing increases among you—three times. They said, \"What is killing?\" He said, \"Slaughter.\""],[5499,"Say: \"In the bounty of Allah and in His mercy—in that let them rejoice; it is better than what they accumulate.\" He said: The bounty of Allah is the Qur'an, and His mercy is that He made you among its people."],[5500,"Whoever eats this tree should not approach our mosque."],[5501,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, who had spread a cloak, and he sat on it along with Fatimah, Ali, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn. Then the Prophet ﷺ took hold of its edges and wrapped it around them, and then said, \"O Allah, be pleased with them as I am pleased with them.\""],[5502,"He forbade the sale of uncertainty."],[5503,"It was revealed concerning Ali: \"Indeed, those who believe and do righteous deeds—the Most Merciful will appoint for them affection.\" He said: Love in the hearts of the believers."],[5504,"He used to break his fast with dates."],[5505,"Allah created the Garden of Eden with His hand, created its fruits within it, and made its rivers flow through it. Then He looked at it and said, \"Speak.\" It said, \"The believers have succeeded.\" He said, \"By My might and majesty, no miser will be My neighbor in you.\""],[5506,"Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land will come on the Day of Resurrection with it hung around his neck from seven earths."],[5507,"When one of you sneezes, let him say: 'Al-hamdu lillah (praise be to God).' And let the one who is near him say: 'Yarhamuka Allah (may God have mercy on you).' And let him say: 'Yahdikum Allah wa yuslihu balakum (may God guide you and set your affairs right).'"],[5508,"When you see two men of my community fighting over kingship, then take at that time a wooden sword and fight with it."],[5509,"When the verse 'And warn your closest relatives' was revealed, the Messenger of God ﷺ went up to the top of the mountain and said: 'O Banu Abd Manaf, surely I am a warner to you, surely I am a warner to you.'"],[5510,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I owe a slave, and I have a black non-Arab slave girl.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Bring her to me.' He said: 'Do you testify that there is no god but God?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'And do you testify that I am the Messenger of God?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then set her free.'"],[5511,"A man bit the hand of another man, who pulled his hand away, and his front tooth fell out. He came to the Prophet ﷺ, who ruled it invalid. Then he said: 'Would one of you eat the flesh of his brother as a stallion eats, or as a stallion bites?'"],[5512,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote to us while we were in Juhayna, that we should not benefit from the carcass by means of its hide or sinew."],[5513,"The best of this community is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[5514,"A girl from the Ansar was in my care, and I married her off. The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to me on the day of her wedding and said: 'O Aisha, did you not sing for her? Will you not sing for her? For this tribe of the Ansar loves singing.'"],[5515,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during his illness: 'Pour over me water from seven water-skins, from different wells.' So they did."],[5516,"Perform Hajj and Umrah consecutively, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows removes the dross of iron."],[5517,"He forbade sharecropping."],[5518,"The plague is martyrdom for my community, and it is a stabbing by your enemies among the jinn. It appears in the armpits of men and their soft parts. The one fleeing from it is like one fleeing from the battle line, and the one patient with it is like a warrior in the path of God."],[5519,"He disliked that one blow in front of him during prayer, or into his drink."],[5520,"We were with Abu al-Darda' returning from the summer expedition, and he said: 'O people, gather together; I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of God, God has forbidden the rest of his body to the Fire.'"],[5521,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ went out to the market, he would say: 'O God, I ask You for the good of this market and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it. O God, I seek refuge in You lest I strike therein a false oath or a losing bargain.'"],[5522,"He used to recite in the last two [rak'ahs] the Opening of the Book."],[5523,"I saw Abu Dharr holding the ring of the Ka'bah and saying: 'I am Abu Dharr al-Ghifari; whoever does not know me, I am Jundub al-Ghifari. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The likeness of my household is the likeness of Noah's ark; whoever boarded it was saved, and whoever stayed behind drowned.'"],[5524,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not cease wiping before the revelation of al-Ma'idah and after it until God took him."],[5525,"Gabriel ﷺ descended upon him and said: 'O Muhammad, if it pleases you to worship God with the worship due to Him, then say: O God, to You belongs praise, eternal praise with Your eternity; and to You belongs praise, everlasting praise that has no end apart from Your will; and at every glance of an eye and every breath of a soul.'"],[5526,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid continuous fasting. We said: 'O Messenger of God, but you fast continuously?' He said: 'I am not like you; I remain with my Lord, and He feeds me and gives me drink.'"],[5527,"Any man whom God has given knowledge and he conceals it will meet God on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."],[5528,"Creation is God's dependents, and the most beloved of people to God is the one who is best to His dependents."],[5529,"We entered upon 'A'ishah to ask her: 'Did the Messenger of God ﷺ embrace while fasting?' We said to 'Alqamah: 'O Abu Shibl, ask her yourself.' He said: 'I am not the one to speak indecently to her today.' 'A'ishah said: 'What is that?' They said: 'O Mother of the Believers, did the Messenger of God ﷺ embrace while fasting?' She said: 'Yes, but he had the most control of you over his desire.'"],[5530,"A black slave came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'A wayfarer passed by me while I was tending the livestock of my master; may I give him milk from them without his permission?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'I shoot, and I hit the target and I hit but the game escapes.' He said: 'Eat what you hit and leave what escapes.'"],[5531,"There is none more protective of honor than Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and for that reason He forbade immoralities, both open and secret."],[5532,"An old woman from the Ansar came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah that He admits me into Paradise.” The Prophet of Allah said, “Paradise is not entered by an old woman.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ went and prayed, then returned to Aisha, and Aisha said, “She has met hardship and distress from your words.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, “That is indeed so. When Allah admits them into Paradise, He will transform them into virgins.”"],[5533,"There are no two Muslims whose three children die before reaching the age of accountability but that Allah will admit them to Paradise through the bounty of His mercy toward them."],[5534,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a people who had hunted a gazelle and tied it to the pole of a tent. The gazelle said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have given birth and I have two fawns, so permit me to suckle them, then I will return to them.” He said, “Where is the owner of this?” The people said, “We are, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Release her so that she may go to her two fawns and suckle them, and then she will come back to you.” They said, “And who will guarantee us that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “I.” So they released her, and she went, suckled them, and then returned to them, so they tied her up again. Then the Prophet ﷺ passed by them and said, “Where are the owners of this?” They said, “Here we are, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Will you sell her?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, she is yours,” so they released her, and she went away."],[5535,"The Children of Israel wrote a book and followed it, and they abandoned the Torah."],[5536,"When the righteous are mentioned, then come eagerly to Umar. We would not deem the companions of Muhammad ﷺ far from it, that tranquility speaks upon the tongue of Umar."],[5537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to perform a prayer in which he does not complete its bowing and prostration."],[5538,"When one of you comes to Jumu'ah, let him perform ghusl."],[5539,"Do not revile time, for Allah is time."],[5540,"Do not pray in the watering places of camels, but pray in the sheepfolds of sheep."],[5541,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave after the burial."],[5542,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus and said four takbirs over him."],[5543,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey, and his companions halted for a rest at night, and nothing woke them except the sun. Then he stood and commanded the mu’adhdhin, who called the adhan and the iqamah, and he prayed. And Masruq said: “I would not love to have the world and all that is in it in exchange for the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after sunrise.”"],[5544,"He forbade that merchandise be met before it is brought down to the markets."],[5545,"The Prophet ﷺ allotted him three shares on the day of Hunayn: one share for himself and two shares for his horse."],[5546,"When the Prophet ﷺ recited “nor of those who go astray,” he said “Amin,” raising his voice with it."],[5547,"The Prophet ﷺ marked his sacrificial animal and garlanded it."],[5548,"He forbade the price of a dog and the dower of a prostitute."],[5549,"He used to combine two prayers during a journey."],[5550,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[5551,"There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses."],[5552,"There is no marriage except with a guardian and witnesses."],[5553,"O Banu ‘Abd Manaf, let me not find any of you preventing anyone who circumambulates the House from praying at any hour he wishes, whether by night or by day."],[5554,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “Shall I not guide you to the noblest traits of this world and the Hereafter? That you maintain ties with one who cuts you off, give to one who deprives you, and pardon one who wrongs you.”"],[5555,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he heard the sound of a bell, so he said: \"The angels do not accompany a group in which there is a bell.\""],[5556,"That he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to Ali: \"You are to me in the position of Aaron to Moses.\""],[5557,"We used to pray Maghrib with the Prophet ﷺ, then one of us would shoot his arrow and see where it landed."],[5558,"God, mighty is His mention, said: \"Whoever I deprive of his two precious ones, I will compensate him with Paradise instead.\""],[5559,"A man said to al-Hasan b. Salih b. Hayy: \"Should I wipe over the leather socks?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then if my Lord says to me: 'Who commanded you to do this?'\" He said: \"Say: 'Al-Hasan b. Salih b. Hayy.'\" He said: \"Then if someone says to you: 'And you?'\" He said: \"I will say: 'Mansur b. al-Mu'tamir commanded me.'\" He said: \"Then if someone says to Mansur?\" He said: \"He will say: 'Ibrahim commanded me.'\" He said: \"Then if someone says to Ibrahim?\" He said: \"He will say: 'Hammam b. al-Harith commanded me.'\" He said: \"Then if someone says to Hammam b. al-Harith?\" He said: \"He will say: 'Jarir b. Abdullah commanded me.'\" He said: \"Then if someone says to Jarir?\" He said: \"He will say: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me.'\""],[5560,"Regarding His saying: 'I will burden him with a difficult ascent,' he said: \"A mountain of fire in Hell. He will be compelled to climb it. When he places his hand on it, it will melt; when he lifts it, it will return. When he places his foot on it, it will melt; when he lifts it, it will return.\""],[5561,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say about this verse: 'God will keep firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter' - he said: \"In the Hereafter: in the grave.\""],[5562,"Let one of you eat with his right hand and drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."],[5563,"No journey should be undertaken except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and the Farthest Mosque."],[5564,"Three people God will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, and they will have a painful punishment: an adulterous old man with gray hair, a poor man who is arrogant, and a man for whom God has provided goods but he does not sell except with his right hand and does not buy except with his right hand."],[5565,"That the Prophet ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting."],[5566,"We recited it during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ for years: 'And those who do not call upon another god besides God, and do not kill the soul which God has forbidden except by right, and do not commit adultery' - the verse - then it was revealed: 'Except for one who repents and believes,' and I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ rejoice with any joy more intense than his joy at it, and at 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory.'"],[5567,"The Prophet ﷺ performed a single tawaf for both his Hajj and his Umrah."],[5568,"Whoever plays backgammon has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."],[5569,"When the noble person of a people comes to you, honor him."],[5570,"Love the Arabs for three reasons: because I am an Arab, the Quran is in Arabic, and the language of the people of Paradise is Arabic."],[5571,"The first one whom the Truth will shake hands with after me is Umar, and the first one to whom He will extend greetings, and the first one whose hand He will take and enter Paradise."],[5572,"These are the two that necessitate: whoever dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire."],[5573,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray eight rak'ahs at night and then perform Witr with three."],[5574,"Two groups of my community have no share in Islam: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah."],[5575,"A man fell into need and went out to the desert. His wife said: 'O Allah, provide us with what we can knead and what we can bake.' The man returned and the bowl was full of dough, and in the oven there were sides of roasted meat, and the mill was grinding. He said: 'Where is this from?' She said: 'From Allah's provision.' He swept around the mill. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Had he left it, it would have turned—or he said: ground—until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[5576,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the market, he would say: 'O Allah, I ask You for the good of this market, and I seek refuge with You from disbelief and immorality.'"],[5577,"When you go barefoot, go barefoot completely; when you put on sandals, begin with the right; and when you take them off, take off the left first."],[5578,"The most incapable of people is one who is incapable in supplication, and the most miserly of people is one who is miserly with the greeting of salam."],[5579,"The Prophet ﷺ came out to us wearing a silken jubbah, and we had not seen him more handsome in a long time than on that day. Then he stood up in alarm and removed it. Then he came out to us wearing a Yemeni striped cloak and said: 'Silk is the clothing of the people of Paradise. Whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.'"],[5580,"No one of kin comes to his relative asking him for some of the surplus that Allah has given him, and he withholds it, except that Allah will bring out for him on the Day of Resurrection a serpent from Hell called Shuja', which will loll out its tongue, and it will be placed around his neck."],[5581,"The sword of the Prophet ﷺ was slightly curved, and its pommel was of silver."],[5582,"Let one of you ask his Lord for his needs, even if it is for a shoelace when it breaks."],[5583,"People follow the Quraysh: their best follow their best, and their worst follow their worst."],[5584,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[5585,"He used to perform ghusl with a sa' and wudu' with a mudd."],[5586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw no harm in making up Ramadan fasts during the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah."],[5587,"He used to pray on his mount wherever it turned, and he would make the prostration lower than the bowing."],[5588,"The best of this Ummah after its Prophet are Abu Bakr and Umar."],[5589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed the dawn prayer, would not leave his sitting place until the time for prayer was possible. And he said: 'Whoever prays the morning prayer and then sits in his place until the time for prayer is possible, it will be like an accepted 'Umrah and Hajj.'"],[5590,"While I was at a well drawing water, Abu Bakr entered and drew a bucket or two, and his drawing was weak, may Allah forgive him. Then Umar came and drew, and I have never seen a strong man among people who did as he did, until the people had watered their camels and settled them."],[5591,"When the Prophet ﷺ intended to go out on the expedition of Tabuk, he said to Jadd b. Qays: \"O Jadd b. Qays, what do you think about fighting the Banu al-Asfar?\" He replied: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a man fond of women, and when I see the women of Banu al-Asfar I will be tempted, so give me permission and do not tempt me.\" Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: \"And among them is he who says, 'Permit me and do not tempt me.' Unquestionably, into temptation they have fallen. And indeed, Hell will encompass the disbelievers.\""],[5592,"When he returned from an expedition, he would say: \"Returning, repenting, if Allah wills, praising our Lord.\""],[5593,"He said to the people when he married the daughter of 'Ali: \"Will you not congratulate me? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Every tie and lineage will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage.'\""],[5594,"Do not lie about me, for the one who lies about me is indeed audacious."],[5595,"Good is abundant, but those who act upon it are few."],[5596,"A bitch among the Children of Israel was pregnant and about to give birth. A guest came to her owner's family as a visitor, so she said, \"I will not bark at our guest tonight.\" Her puppies howled in her belly. Then it was revealed to a man among them: \"The example of this bitch is the example of a nation that will come after you: their fools will dominate their scholars.\""],[5597,"There was a kid among the Children of Israel whose mother would suckle it and satisfy its thirst. One day it got loose and suckled many sheep but was not satisfied. Then it was revealed to a man among them: \"The example of this kid is the example of a people who will come after you: a man will be given what would suffice a nation or a tribe, yet he will not be satisfied.\""],[5598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the 'umra (life grant) is permissible."],[5599,"The first to shoot an arrow in the way of Allah was Sa'd."],[5600,"None of you will attain the reality of faith until he restrains his tongue."],[5601,"The Prophet ﷺ used to visit us and mix with us. We had a young boy called Abu 'Umayr, so he said: \"O Abu 'Umayr, what happened to the nughayr (little bird)?\""],[5602,"Those who cut down the lote tree will be plunged into the Fire headlong."],[5603,"Leadership: its beginning is regret, its middle is a penalty, and its end is punishment on the Day of Resurrection."],[5604,"The child belongs to the bed."],[5605,"Madinah is the dome of Islam, the abode of faith, the land of emigration, and the place where the lawful and the unlawful are established."],[5606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me, and I said: I have no desire to turn away from you, but I do not like to marry while my children are still young. He said: Do you have any other reason? I said: No. He said: The best women who ever rode camels are the women of Quraysh—the most compassionate toward a small child and the most careful of a husband's property."],[5607,"I saw Jibril ﷺ wearing a red turban, letting it hang down between his shoulder blades."],[5608,"Whoever is killed while seeking the face of Allah, Allah will not punish him."],[5609,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of uncertainty."],[5610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ghusl once every week—meaning: on Friday."],[5611,"He used to say in his prayer: Our Lord, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will after that."],[5612,"I indeed saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his houses on his left; when he finished the prayer, he would head toward his houses on his left."],[5613,"Whoever would like Allah to expand his provision and prolong his life, let him maintain ties with his relatives."],[5614,"I never heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention both his father and mother together for anyone except Sa'd. On the day of Uhud, he said to him: Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom."],[5615,"For every traitor there will be a banner on the Day of Resurrection. The protection of the Muslims is one; the lowest of them may grant it. Whoever violates the protection of a Muslim, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither obligatory nor supererogatory acts will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5616,"When revelation descended upon him, he would get a headache, so he would dye his head with henna."],[5617,"The traitor will have a banner set up for him, and it will be said: 'This is the treachery of so-and-so, and he did such-and-such in it.'"],[5618,"He forbade praying over funerals among the graves."],[5619,"They asked 'Abd Allah b. Abi Awfa about tayammum. He said: The Prophet ﷺ commanded that it be done like this, and he struck the ground with both hands, then shook them off, and wiped his face and hands."],[5620,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: What is recited in the Witr? He said: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' in the first rak'ah, 'Say: O disbelievers' in the second, and 'Say: He is Allah, the One' in the third."],[5621,"Leave the Turks alone as long as they leave you alone, for the first to seize what Allah has bestowed upon my nation will be the Banu Qantura'."],[5622,"Whoever is killed defending against an injustice is a martyr."],[5623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray at night in pairs, and when dawn came he would pray Witr with one rak'ah, and he said: 'Allah is One and loves the odd number.'"],[5624,"Bring me three stones. Then he performed ablution without touching water. He said: 'Throw away the dung, for it is filth.'"],[5625,"Ibn 'Abbas used to wear silk. He was asked about it, and he said: 'Only solid silk was forbidden.'"],[5626,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to love the poor and sit with them, to look at those below me and not at those above me, and to maintain ties of kinship even if they cut me off."],[5627,"The Prophet ﷺ stood among us delivering an address."],[5628,"Visit occasionally and you will increase in love."],[5629,"The Prophet ﷺ manumitted Safiyya and made her emancipation her dower, and married her."],[5630,"Give charity early in the morning, for calamity does not overstep it."],[5631,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youths of the people of Paradise."],[5632,"When this verse was revealed: “The likeness of those who spend their wealth in the way of Allah is as the likeness of a grain that sprouts seven ears, in every ear a hundred grains,” the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My Lord, increase my community.” Then it was revealed: “Who is it that will lend Allah a goodly loan, so that He may multiply it for him manifold?” He said: “My Lord, increase my community.” Then it was revealed: “Only the patient will be paid their reward in full without reckoning.”"],[5633,"Fasting the day of ‘Arafa expiates two years: a past year and a coming year, and fasting ‘Ashura’ expiates a year."],[5634,"The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer, and the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer, but the door of repentance is open."],[5635,"Shall I not tell you about the men among you who are from the people of Paradise? The Prophet is in Paradise, the truthful one is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, and a man who visits his brother for the sake of Allah in a distant part of the city is in Paradise. Shall I not tell you about the women among you who are from the people of Paradise? The loving, prolific woman who, when she is wronged or wrongs someone, says: “Here is my hand in your hand; I will not taste sleep until you are pleased.”"],[5636,"Whoever relieves a believer of one of the distresses of this world, Allah will relieve him of his distresses on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever conceals the faults of a believer, Allah will conceal his faults. Whoever alleviates the hardship of a believer, Allah will alleviate his hardship."],[5637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some people who had performed ablution and said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[5638,"My basin is between Ayla and Makkah."],[5639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to have cupping done on the seventeenth, on the nineteenth, and on the twenty-first."],[5640,"When the last ten days of Ramadan entered, the Prophet ﷺ would fold up his bed, withdraw from women, and make his evening meal a pre-dawn meal."],[5641,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased by night prayer (tahajjud)."],[5642,"Jabir b. Abdullah came to me while I was in the kuttab (elementary Qur'an school) and said: Uncover your belly. So I uncovered my belly, and he kissed it. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to convey salam to you."],[5643,"Whatever the sea recedes from while it is alive and then dies, eat it. Whatever the sea casts out alive and then dies, eat it. And whatever you find dead and floating, do not eat it."],[5644,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade selling a heap of dates when its measure is unknown, and a heap of food."],[5645,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Makkah, Abu Quhafah was brought to him, his head and beard like thagham (a white plant). He said: Change grey hair, and avoid black dye."],[5646,"Uthman b. Affan called for water for ablution and performed ablution for prayer. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever performs ablution and does it well, and prays and does it well, his past sins will be forgiven."],[5647,"He used to take a hair from the side of a camel from the spoils of war and say: I have no more right to it than any one of you. Beware of misappropriation (ghulul), for it is disgrace for its owner on the Day of Resurrection. Return the needle and the thread and whatever is above that. And strive in the cause of Allah against the near and the far, in settled life and in travel, for jihad is a gate from the gates of Paradise; it saves its companion from worry and grief."],[5648,"The lowest heaven is a restrained wave, the second is rock, the third is iron, the fourth is copper, the fifth is silver, the sixth is gold, and the seventh is a ruby."],[5649,"The son of Abdullah b. Ubayy, his father said to him: O my son, seek a garment from the garments of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and shroud me in it, and ask him to pray over me. So he came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you know the nobility of Abdullah, and he asks you for a garment from your garments to shroud him in it, and for you to pray over him. He said: So he gave him a garment from his garments and intended to pray over him. Umar b. al-Khattab said to him: Do you not know Abdullah and his hypocrisy? You pray over him while Allah has forbidden you to pray over him? He said: Where? He said: \"Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them. If you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them.\" He said: Then I will increase beyond seventy. Then Allah revealed: \"And do not pray over any of them who has died ever, and do not stand at his grave.\" He said: And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"It is the same for them whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them\" - the verse. He said: And a man entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and prolonged his sitting. The Prophet ﷺ went out three times so that he would stand and follow him, but he did not. Then Umar entered and saw the man and recognized in the face of the Prophet ﷺ dislike of his sitting. He said: Perhaps you have annoyed the Prophet ﷺ . The man understood and stood up. The Prophet ﷺ said: I stood up three times so that he would follow me, but he did not. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would take a screen, for your wives are not like other women, and that is purer for their hearts. Then Allah revealed: \"O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you for a meal, without awaiting its readiness\" - the verse. So he sent to Umar and informed him of that. He said: And the Prophet ﷺ consulted Abu Bakr and Umar about the captives of the people of Badr. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, spare your people and take ransom, and seek help through it. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, kill them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If you two agreed, you would not be disobeyed. Then he adopted the view of Abu Bakr. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has made slaughter in the land.\" He said: And when it was revealed: \"And We created man from an extract of clay, then We placed him as a drop in a firm lodging\" - the verse, Umar said: Blessed is Allah, the best of creators. Then it was revealed: \"So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.\""],[5650,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have attained from a woman what is short of intercourse with her. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night\" - the verse."],[5651,"Allah's Messenger ﷺ came out to us while we were gathered and said: 'O assembly of Muslims, fear Allah and maintain your family ties, for there is no reward swifter than maintaining family ties. Beware of transgression, for there is no punishment swifter than the punishment of transgression. Beware of disobeying parents, for the fragrance of Paradise is found from a distance of a thousand years, and by Allah, no disobedient child, no one who severs family ties, no old man who commits adultery, and no one who drags his garment out of pride will smell it. Grandeur belongs only to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Every lie is a sin, except what you use to benefit a believer or to repel [harm] from a religion. And in Paradise there is a market in which nothing is sold or bought; it contains only forms. Whoever loves a form of a man or a woman enters it.'"],[5652,"Allah is in the aid of the servant as long as the person is in the aid of his brother."],[5653,"The example of a son of Adam, while beside him are ninety-nine death-causes: if the death-causes miss him, he falls into old age until he dies."],[5654,"Allah dislikes for you three things: gossip, excessive asking, and wasting wealth."],[5655,"You will hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who hear from you."],[5656,"I have not left after me a tribulation more harmful to men than the tribulation of women."],[5657,"Two types of people are insatiable and their craving never ends: one insatiable in seeking knowledge, whose craving never ends, and one insatiable in seeking the world, whose craving never ends."],[5658,"Regarding Allah's saying: 'And do not throw [yourselves] with your [own] hands into destruction, and do good; indeed, Allah loves the doers of good' (2:195), he said: 'The Ansar used to give and spend in charity, then a year of drought befell them, so they held back. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And do not throw [yourselves] with your [own] hands into destruction, and do good; indeed, Allah loves the doers of good.'"],[5659,"Regarding Allah's saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'And do not throw [yourselves] with your [own] hands into destruction,' he said: 'A man would commit a sin and say: \"I will not be forgiven.\" So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And do not throw [yourselves] with your [own] hands into destruction, and do good; indeed, Allah loves the doers of good.'"],[5660,"The Black Stone is from the stones of Paradise, and there is nothing on earth from Paradise other than it. It was white like a crystal, and were it not for the filth of the pre-Islamic ignorance that touched it, no one with an ailment would touch it except that he would be healed."],[5661,"I prayed Maghrib behind Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said the salam after two rak'ahs. Then he stood up and touched the Stone, so they glorified Allah [in astonishment] at him. He returned, completed what remained, and prostrated two prostrations. I went to Ibn 'Abbas and mentioned that, and he said: 'May his father be for Allah! He did not deviate from the Sunnah of his Prophet ﷺ.'"],[5662,"When Allah's Messenger ﷺ entered the mosque, he would say: 'O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your mercy.' And when he left, he would say the same, and he would say: 'O Allah, open for me the gates of Your bounty.'"],[5663,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed, if water were poured on his back, it would settle (stay in place)."],[5664,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray witr with nine (rak'ahs), until when he gained weight, he prayed witr with seven while seated."],[5665,"He used to recite in witr: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, {Say, O disbelievers}, and {Say, He is Allah, [who is] One}."],[5666,"Friday prayer is obligatory upon every adult (who has reached puberty), except a slave, a sick person, a woman, or a child."],[5667,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Makkah, he circumambulated seven times, then went to the Maqam and prayed two rak'ahs, then went to Zamzam and said: 'Draw water.' Were it not that it would become a sunnah, I would have drawn it with my own hand. So he filled the bucket for him, and he filled (a vessel) from it, then he spat into the bucket and said: 'Pour it back into the well.' Then he went to the water-serving place and said: 'Give me to drink.' Al-Abbas said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, this (water) has been touched by many hands and has many flies in it, and we have in the house something better than it.' He said: 'No, give me to drink from this.'"],[5668,"The Prophet ﷺ had a coat of mail pawned with a Jew, and he did not find anything to redeem it until he died."],[5669,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat in prayer, he placed his hand on his knees."],[5670,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them one day: 'This is the day of Ashura, so fast it.' A man from Banu Amr b. Awf stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I left my people; some of them are fasting and some are not.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Go to them. Whoever among them is not fasting, let him abstain (from eating for the rest of the day), and whoever is fasting, let him complete his fast.'"],[5671,"A man from the Muslims came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery.' He turned away from him, until he came to him four times, each time he turned away from him. When he asked him four times and testified against himself four times, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said: 'Do you have insanity?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Have you been married (and consummated the marriage)?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Take him and stone him.'"],[5672,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us: When one of you sneezes, let him say: 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.' When he says that, let those around him say: 'May Allah have mercy on you.' When they say that, let him say: 'May Allah forgive me and you.'"],[5673,"How many a person with two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid, if he swore by Allah, He would fulfill his oath. Among them is Ammar b. Yasir."],[5674,"They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, describe to us your Lord.' So it was revealed: {Say, He is Allah, [who is] One} to its end."],[5675,"I was about to command that the prayer be established, then I would look for those who did not attend the prayer and burn their houses down upon them."],[5676,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ one night, and he performed ablution and stood to pray. I came to him and stood on his left, so he made me stand on his right, then he said the takbir and said: 'Glory be to Allah, the Possessor of dominion, might, pride, and greatness.'"],[5677,"I used to rub it from the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ - meaning semen - then he would pray in it."],[5678,"He would go out when he went out in summer on the night of Friday, and when winter came he would enter on the night of Friday."],[5679,"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a healing for the eyes, and the 'ajwa date is from Paradise and it is a healing for poison."],[5680,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn above three days, except for a husband."],[5681,"Hajj is in the path of Allah; spending in it, a dirham is worth seven hundred."],[5682,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ and 'A'ishah praying in a single garment, half of it over the Prophet ﷺ and half of it over 'A'ishah."],[5683,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would bring his head out to me while he was in i'tikaf, and I would wash it while I was menstruating."],[5684,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head from bowing and said: 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' we would not prostrate until we saw him on the ground."],[5685,"I saw Ibn 'Umar when a man next to him sneezed and said: 'Praise be to Allah and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah.' Ibn 'Umar said: 'And I say: Peace be upon the Messenger of Allah, but this is not how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to say when we sneeze: Praise be to Allah in every situation.'"],[5686,"While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a group from Banu Hashim - or some youths from Banu Hashim - came. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw them, his face reddened and his eyes filled with tears. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we still see in your face something you dislike.' He said: 'We are a household for whom Allah has chosen the Hereafter over this world, and these members of my family will face after me exile and dispersal, until a people come from here, from the east, carrying black banners. They will ask for the truth but will not be given it; then they will ask for the truth but will not be given it.' He said that twice or thrice. 'Then they will fight and be given what they ask for, but they will not accept it until they hand it over to a man from my household, who will fill it with justice just as it was filled with oppression. Whoever lives to see that time, let him go to them even if crawling over snow.'"],[5687,"He used to follow every prayer with two rak'ahs, except the morning prayer, which he made before it."],[5688,"The Prophet ﷺ used to hasten the Maghrib prayer and break the fast when the sun set."],[5689,"Fold your clothes so that their spirits return to them; for if the devil finds a garment folded, he does not wear it, and if he finds it spread out, he wears it."],[5690,"Regarding images, he permitted what is trodden upon and disliked what is set up."],[5691,"Flour was not sifted for the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he had only one shirt."],[5692,"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus is better than for it to be filled with poetry."],[5693,"The Prophet ﷺ was at Arafat supplicating, and he raised his hands. The camel's reins fell, so he picked them up and raised his hands. The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: This is earnest supplication and humble entreaty."],[5694,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say while he was in Madinah: O God, place in it twice the blessing that is in Makkah."],[5695,"Whoever seeks knowledge to vie with the scholars, to dispute with the foolish, or to turn people's faces towards him, then he is in the Fire."],[5696,"The major sins are seven: associating partners with God, killing the soul that God has forbidden except by right, slandering a chaste woman, fleeing from the battlefield, consuming usury, consuming the orphan's wealth, and turning back to Bedouinism after emigration."],[5697,"Overlook the sin of the generous person, for God takes him by the hand whenever he stumbles."],[5698,"No one from the Banu Umayyah will rule for a year except that a descendant of al-Abbas will rule for two years. A man among his companions said: O Abu Hamzah, did the Messenger of God ﷺ say this? He said: Yes, it is as sure as you are here."],[5699,"He addressed us from the pulpit of Kufa when Mu'awiya appointed him over us, saying: O people, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: O people, indeed from grapes comes wine, and from raisins comes wine, and from dates comes wine, and from honey comes wine, and I forbid every intoxicant."],[5700,"Do not lodge them in upper rooms, and do not teach them writing, but teach them spinning and Surat al-Nur."],[5701,"The number of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Badr was three hundred."],[5702,"Whoever recites the two verses at the end of Surat al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him."],[5703,"No Muslim has three children die, but God will admit them both to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy."],[5704,"Abu Talib was inherited by 'Aqil and Talib, and 'Ali did not inherit him. 'Ali said: For that reason we abandoned our share of the mountain pass."],[5705,"The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."],[5706,"He looked at the Ka'bah and said: God has indeed honored you, ennobled you, and magnified you, yet the believer's sanctity is greater than yours."],[5707,"Learn the Qur'an and teach it to people, and learn the obligatory shares of inheritance and teach them to people, for I am about to be taken, and soon two men will differ over an obligatory share and not find anyone to judge between them."],[5708,"There is no night talk except for one who prays or a traveler."],[5709,"No servant ever puts on sandals, or goes barefoot, or wears a garment to go out in pursuit of knowledge, but God forgives his sins as soon as he steps over the threshold of his door."],[5710,"Reviling a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[5711,"Cloaks were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he distributed them among his companions. My father Makhrama said to me: “Come with me to him; perhaps he will give us something from them.” He went to the door and said: “Here he is.” The Prophet ﷺ heard his voice and came out to him with a cloak. It is as if I can see him showing my father the fine qualities of the cloak and saying: “I kept this for you.” Salih b. Hatim said: I said to my father: “Why did the Prophet ﷺ do this for Makhrama?” He said: “It was as if to guard against his tongue.”"],[5712,"The Fire is forbidden for every person who is gentle, soft, easy, and near."],[5713,"It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is ill omen?” He said: “Bad character.”"],[5714,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ashajj ʿAbd al-Qays: “Indeed you have two traits that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness.”"],[5715,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife, a mother, and a father. Which of them is most entitled to my kind treatment?” He said: “Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the closer one and the closer one.”"],[5716,"If I were to take a bosom friend, I would take Abu Bakr as a bosom friend."],[5717,"Say: He is Allah, the One equals a third of the Quran."],[5718,"The most beloved color to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was green."],[5719,"Fleas were mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “They wake one up for prayer.”"],[5720,"A funeral procession of a Jew passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and he stood up. It was said: “It is the funeral of a Jew?” He said: “We only stood for your brothers among the angels.”"],[5721,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in his final illness, he ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt some relief, so he stood with the people behind Abu Bakr, wrapped in a single garment."],[5722,"When you judge, be just; and when you kill, do it well, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is excellent and loves excellence."],[5723,"When Ruqayyah bt. the Prophet ﷺ died, he said: \"Join our righteous predecessor Uthman b. Maz'un.\""],[5724,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in prayer until his feet became swollen. It was said to him, \"Has Allah not forgiven you your past and future sins?\" He said, \"Should I not be a grateful servant?\""],[5725,"We used to perform ablution after touching a leper."],[5726,"He forbade mutilation."],[5727,"Do not fast before Ramadan; fast upon sighting it, and break your fast upon sighting it. If clouds obscure it, then complete thirty days."],[5728,"Do not withhold anything, for I only make lawful what Allah has made lawful in His Book and only make unlawful what Allah has made unlawful in His Book."],[5729,"In Paradise there is a house called the House of Generosity."],[5730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a wedding feast for Umm Salamah with dates and clarified butter."],[5731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought a camel from me, and he excepted its riding to Madinah."],[5732,"Whoever among you does not have a preceding child will not enter Paradise except by crawling on all fours. A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, not all of us have a preceding child.\" He said, \"Is it not a preceding child for one of you that he loses his Muslim brother?\""],[5733,"Marry, for I will boast of your great numbers before the nations. The miscarried fetus will be seen standing at the gate of Paradise, and it will be said to it, 'Enter.' It will say, 'No, until my parents enter.'"],[5734,"I heated water in the sun and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ for ablution. He said, \"O Aishah, do not do that, for it causes leprosy.\""],[5735,"I heard ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr say one day in a gathering of Muslims, among them Ibn ʿUmar: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever makes people hear of his deed, God will make His creation hear of him on the Day of Resurrection, and He will belittle him and debase him.” Then I saw the eyes of Ibn ʿUmar shedding tears."],[5736,"He was only called al-Khiḍr because he stood on a patch of white earth, and it turned green and quivered."],[5737,"Whoever steals a handspan of land or usurps it will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying it down to the lowest of the earths."],[5738,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to dispatch a raiding party, he would send them early in the day and say: “O God, bless my community in its early mornings.”"],[5739,"I was on the verge of ordering Bilāl to pronounce the iqāmah for prayer, then leave and go to a people who heard the call but did not respond, and burn their houses down upon them."],[5740,"Whoever loses a child, male or female, whether it was stillborn or not, whether he is pleased or not, patient or not, his reward is nothing less than Paradise."],[5741,"Three things are destructive, three are saving, three are expiations, and three are ranks. As for the destructive: greed that is obeyed, passion that is followed, and a person's admiration of himself. As for the saving: justice in anger and contentment, moderation in poverty and wealth, and fear of God in secret and in public. As for the expiations: waiting for the next prayer after each prayer, completing ablution in severe cold, and walking to the congregational prayers. As for the ranks: feeding others, spreading peace, and praying at night while people sleep."],[5742,"Do not say Sūrat al-Baqarah, nor Sūrat Āl ʿImrān, nor Sūrat al-Nisāʾ, and likewise the entire Qurʾān. Rather say: the sūrah in which the cow is mentioned, the sūrah in which the family of ʿImrān is mentioned, and so on for the entire Qurʾān."],[5743,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib and Khālid b. al-Walīd, and he said: “If there is fighting, then ʿAlī is in command over you.” Then victory was granted to them, and they captured prisoners. ʿAlī took a beautiful slave girl to send to the Messenger of God ﷺ, but Khālid objected and said, “I will send her to the Messenger of God ﷺ.” When Khālid prevented him, he left and sent Buraydah to the Messenger of God ﷺ. Buraydah said: I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was washing his head, and I spoke ill of ʿAlī in his presence. When we sat before the Messenger of God ﷺ, we did not raise our eyes to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Enough, O Buraydah.” So I raised my head toward the Messenger of God ﷺ and saw his face had changed color. When I saw that, I said: I seek refuge in God from the anger of God and the anger of the Messenger of God. Buraydah said: By God, I will never hate him after what I saw from the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[5744,"No man is put in authority over ten or more people except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck. If he acted well, it will be released from him; if he acted badly, a chain will be added to his chain."],[5745,"The Anṣār said among themselves: What if we collect some wealth for the Messenger of God ﷺ, so that he can stretch out his hand and no one stands between him and it? They said: O Messenger of God, we wanted to collect some of our wealth for you. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it except love for near relatives.” They went out disagreeing with one another and said: Did you not see what the Messenger of God ﷺ said? Some of them said: He only said this so that we fight on behalf of his family and support them. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “Or do they say: He has fabricated a lie against God?” up to His saying: “And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants,” thereby offering them repentance, up to His saying: “And He answers those who believe and do righteous deeds and gives them more of His bounty.” It is they who said this, that they should repent to God and seek His forgiveness."],[5746,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[5747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and commanded that the meat of horses be eaten."],[5748,"Muhammad ﷺ saw his Lord twice: once with his sight and once with his heart."],[5749,"I asked my Lord that I not marry into any family or marry anyone to any family except that they be with me in Paradise, and He granted me that."],[5750,"He said: Would it please you to be a quarter of the people of Paradise? They said takbir. Then he said: Would it please you to be a third of the people of Paradise? They said takbir. Then he said: Would it please you to be half of the people of Paradise? They said takbir. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: On the Day of Resurrection, people will be in one hundred and twenty rows; my Ummah will be eighty of those rows."],[5751,"Learn Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is a blessing, leaving it is a regret, and the idle ones cannot bear it. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The Quran will come on the Day of Resurrection like a pale man, saying to its companion: Do you recognize me? I am the one who kept you awake at night and made you thirsty during the midday heat. Every trader is after his trade, and I am for you today after every trader. Then he will be given sovereignty in his right hand and eternity in his left, and a crown of dignity will be placed on his head, and his parents will be clothed in two garments that the world and all it contains cannot equal. They will say: Our Lord, how did we get this? It will be said to them: Because your child learned the Quran. And the companion of the Quran will be told on the Day of Resurrection: Recite and ascend in ranks, and recite distinctly as you used to recite distinctly in the world, for your station is at the last verse you recite."],[5752,"Paradise has one hundred levels; between each two levels is a journey of five hundred years."],[5753,"A lahd (niche grave) was dug for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, bricks were arranged upon it, and it was taken from the direction of the qiblah."],[5754,"I cannot count how many times I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in the two rak'ahs after Maghrib and the two rak'ahs before Fajr: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, the One.'"],[5755,"It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he said the salam to his right: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings,' and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[5756,"He used to supplicate with these supplications at the beginning of his speech and conclude with them: O Allah, set right our relationships, guide us to the paths of peace, bring us out from darkness into light, turn away from us indecency, both what is apparent and what is hidden, bless us in our hearing, our sight, our spouses, our offspring, and our livelihoods, and accept our repentance. Indeed, You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful. O Allah, make us grateful for Your blessings, praising You for them and accepting them."],[5757,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'He will give them their rewards and increase them from His bounty' - that is intercession for those of whom the Fire has become due, from among those to whom kindness was shown in this world."],[5758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man from the Arabs: When desire or fear befalls you, to whom do you turn? They said: To Allah. He said: Then when He answers you, to whom do you return? They said: To what you know. He said: You know but do not act, and you act but do not know - three times."],[5759,"Women and perfume have been made beloved to me, and the coolness of my eyes has been placed in prayer."],[5760,"No believer is pricked by a thorn or anything more than that except that Allah removes a sin from him because of it and raises him a degree by it."],[5761,"Pardon the slips of the noble."],[5762,"Exchange gifts, you will increase in love."],[5763,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ having dyed his beard with yellow dye. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him: \"What is this dye? Have you married?\" He said: \"Yes.\" The Prophet asked: \"Have you given a wedding feast?\" He said: \"No.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw him a gold date-stone and said: \"Give a wedding feast, even with one sheep.\""],[5764,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, he would not place anything under his feet, except that one day we were rained upon and he placed a leather mat under his feet."],[5765,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \"What is richness?\" He said: \"Despairing of what is in people's hands.\""],[5766,"Two eyes will not see the Fire: an eye that wept out of fear of Allah, and an eye that stayed awake guarding in the path of Allah."],[5767,"Increase in remembering the destroyer of pleasures, meaning death, for it does not occur with much except that it diminishes it, nor with little except that it makes it sufficient."],[5768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to lie down to sleep among people and to sleep on a public road."],[5769,"Allah detests a seventy-year-old man in the appearance of a twenty-year-old, in his gait and his look."],[5770,"I used to scrub the semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5771,"Whoever fasts Ramadan, goes in the morning with a ritual bath to the prayer place, and seals it with charity returns forgiven."],[5772,"Whoever recites: “Say: He is Allah, the One” in the illness from which he dies will not be tested in his grave, will be safe from the constriction of the grave, and the angels will carry him on the Day of Resurrection on their palms until they make him cross the Sirat to Paradise."],[5773,"When one of you prostrates, let him press his palms firmly to the ground; perhaps Allah will release the shackles from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5774,"The believer brings people together and is brought together; and there is no good in one who does not bring people together and is not brought together. And the best of people is the most beneficial to people."],[5775,"For the traveler: three days and their nights; and for the resident: one day and one night."],[5776,"I will certainly give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love, so he gave it to ʿAli."],[5777,"A servant does not believe until I am dearer to him than his own self, my family is dearer to him than his family, my progeny is dearer to him than his progeny, and my very being is dearer to him than his own being."],[5778,"The Prophet ﷺ entered their mosque and drank while standing."],[5779,"The food of two is enough for four, and the food of four is enough for eight."],[5780,"The best of my nation are its scholars; those who when they get angry, they return."],[5781,"I came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have composed poetry in which I praise Allah and extol you. He said: As for what you praised Allah in, bring it; and as for what you extolled me, leave it. So I began to recite to him, and a tall man entered. He said: Stop. When he left, he said: Bring it. So I began to recite to him, and it was not long before he returned. He said to me: Stop. When he left, he said to me: Bring it. I said: Who is this, O Prophet of Allah, that when he enters you say: Stop, and when he leaves you say: Bring it? He said: This is ʿUmar, and he is not part of falsehood in anything."],[5782,"My love is due to those who give generously to one another for My sake, and My love is due to those who visit one another for My sake."],[5783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Suhayl b. 'Amr for water from Zamzam."],[5784,"Whoever fills a gap in a row, Allah raises him a degree thereby and builds for him a house in Paradise."],[5785,"The Prophet ﷺ combined both his parents for Sa'd."],[5786,"Let your house be sufficient for you, and weep at the remembrance of your sin, and hold back your tongue."],[5787,"A woman was divorced during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and she remained for twenty-three or twenty-something [days]. She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Take charge of your own affair.\""],[5788,"I and the Hour have been sent like these two."],[5789,"If seventy men from among us go forth to the Friday prayer, they will be like the seventy of Musa who went to meet their Lord, or better."],[5790,"The Prophet ﷺ was sitting after Maghrib, and his companions were with him, when a caravan passed by traveling. Their driver was reciting, and their leader was chanting. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw them, he stood up and hurried without a cloak. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we will suffice you.\" He said: \"Let me convey to them what was revealed to me concerning their affair.\" He caught up with them and said: \"Where do you intend to go at this hour?\" They said: \"We intend to go to Yemen.\" He said: \"What is your traveling at this hour? For Allah has a great authority in the heaven that He directs to the earth. So do not travel even a step except what a man finds in his stomach and bladder of urine that he cannot avoid, and then not even a step. As for you, O driver of the people, you should use some of the speech of the Arabs from its rajaz, and when you are riding, recite it. And you should travel by night, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has angels appointed who fold the earth for the traveler as papers are folded. And after dawn, the people praise the night journey. Let no poet accompany you, nor a soothsayer, nor a stray animal. Do not turn away a beggar if you desire profit, safety, and good companionship. I am amazed how I can sleep when all eyes sleep, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger forbid you from traveling at this hour.\""],[5791,"I heard Hudhayfah say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, and Allah appointed Abu Bakr as successor. Then Abu Bakr passed away, and Allah appointed 'Umar as successor. Then 'Umar passed away, and Allah appointed 'Uthman as successor.\""],[5792,"He used to recite in the last two [rak'ahs] the Fatihah of the Book, meaning in Zuhr and 'Asr."],[5793,"Islam began as something strange and will return to being strange, so glad tidings to the strangers. And before the Hour there will be trials like patches of dark night, in which a man will be a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning, and a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening. People will sell their religion for a portion of this world."],[5794,"When the collector of zakah comes to you, he should not leave except while he is pleased."],[5795,"The Prophet ﷺ called the Anṣār to write for them [a grant of] al-Baḥrayn. They said, “No, unless you write the like of it for our brothers the Muhājirūn.” He said, “You will see after me selfishness, so be patient until you meet me.”"],[5796,"A Bedouin came and urinated in a corner of the mosque, so the people shouted at him. The Prophet ﷺ restrained them, then ordered a bucket of water, and it was poured over his urine."],[5797,"When Zaynab bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, grief appeared on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then it was relieved from him. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, we saw from you what we had not seen before.” He said, “I remembered Zaynab, her weakness, and the squeezing of the grave. It was made light for her, yet despite that it squeezed her with a squeeze that reached the two east-and-west extremes.”"],[5798,"I knew the corresponding sūrahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray with: al-Dhāriyāt, al-Ṭūr, al-Najm, Iqtarabat, al-Raḥmān, al-Wāqiʿah, Nūn, al-Ḥāqqah, Saʾala Sāʾil, al-Muzzammil, Lā Uqsimu bi-Yawm al-Qiyāmah, Hal Atā ʿalā al-Insān, al-Mursalāt, ʿAmma Yatasāʾalūn, al-Nāziʿāt, ʿAbasa, Waylun li-l-Muṭaffifīn, and Idhā al-Shamsu Kuwwirat."],[5799,"The dream of a righteous man is glad tidings from Allah, and it is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[5800,"The banner that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed to ʿAlī was white."],[5801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to relieve himself, and I met him with water. He said, “Who ordered you to do this?” I said, “No one ordered me to do it.” He said, “You have done well. Rejoice in Paradise.” Then ʿAlī came and I gave him the glad tidings of Paradise."],[5802,"Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abū ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrāḥ."],[5803,"We were discussing the Day of Uḥud while the Prophet ﷺ was standing praying. When he finished and turned away from his prayer, he turned to us and said, “Shall I not tell you about the Day of Uḥud? I saw myself with no one but Jibrīl on my right and Ṭalḥah on my left.”"],[5804,"Two groups of my nation will not receive my intercession: the Murjiʾah and the Qadariyyah."],[5805,"Whoever performs ḥajj on behalf of a deceased person, the one on whose behalf he performed ḥajj receives the like of his reward. Whoever gives a fasting person something to break his fast receives the like of his reward. Whoever guides to good receives the like of the reward of the one who does it."],[5806,"Whoever fulfills their oaths, pays their debts, and does not revile their parents is recorded as dutiful even if he was disobedient. Whoever does not fulfill their oaths, does not pay their debts, and reviles them is recorded as disobedient even if he was dutiful during their lifetimes."],[5807,"Whoever dies without an imam upon him dies a death of jahiliyyah."],[5808,"Jibril ﷺ circumcised the Prophet ﷺ when he purified his heart."],[5809,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: 'What day is this?' We said: 'The day of sacrifice.' He said: 'What month is this?' We said: 'Dhu al-Hijjah, a sacred month.' He said: 'What land is this?' We said: 'A sacred land.' He said: 'Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours. Let the witness convey to the absent.'"],[5810,"Jibril ﷺ said to me: 'There was nothing on earth more hateful to me than Pharaoh. When he believed with his mouth, I began stuffing his mouth with clay, fearing that mercy might reach him.'"],[5811,"O Allah, forgive me for what I have sent forth and what I have delayed, what I have concealed and what I have proclaimed, and what You know better than I. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer, and You have power over all things."],[5812,"He kissed the Stone and said: 'I know that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit. Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing you, I would not have kissed you.'"],[5813,"There will be in my ummah a man who speaks after death."],[5814,"Uqbah b. Amir went out to Maslamah b. Mukhallad while he was governor of Egypt. There had been an incident between him and the doorkeeper. When permission was granted, he entered upon him. Maslamah said: 'Welcome to a brother as a visitor.' Uqbah said: 'I have not come to you as a visitor, but for a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[5815,"Whoever is granted an umra, it belongs to him and his descendants."],[5816,"It is not a shortening but a completion, meaning the two rak'ahs during travel."],[5817,"I was informed that Pharaoh had a broken front tooth."],[5818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never combined his parents for anyone except me. He said: 'Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom.'"],[5819,"Umm Salamah said to me: \"Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reviled among you on the pulpits?\" I said: \"Glory be to Allah, how could the Messenger of Allah ﷺ be reviled?\" She said: \"Is not 'Ali b. Abi Talib reviled, and those who love him? I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love him.\""],[5820,"Say: He is Allah, the One, equals a third of the Qur'an."],[5821,"\"A man from the best of the people of Yemen will appear before you, on his face is the mark of an angel.\" Then I appeared."],[5822,"I was to you as Abu Zar' was to Umm Zar'."],[5823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat on the day of Fitr before going out to the prayer place."],[5824,"He forbade khidhf (throwing pebbles with the fingers), saying: \"It puts out the eye and breaks the tooth.\""],[5825,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ relieving himself between two bricks, facing the qiblah, while he was on the roof of a house."],[5826,"Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."],[5827,"Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ, and be guided by the guidance of 'Ammar, and hold fast to the covenant of Ibn Umm 'Abd."],[5828,"When a slave runs away, the protection (dhimma) is disowned from him."],[5829,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to 'Ali: \"Rejoice, O 'Ali, your life and your death are with me.\""],[5830,"When he wanted to touch the (Black) Stone, he would say: \"O Allah, out of faith in You and belief in Your Book and the Sunnah of Your Prophet ﷺ,\" then he would touch it."],[5831,"The Hajj is 'Arafat."],[5832,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to 'Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."],[5833,"O Allah, have mercy on our successors. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who are your successors? He said: Those who come after me, narrating my hadiths and my sunnah, and teaching them to the people."],[5834,"I entered upon Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan while he had an ulcer on his back, and he was groaning from it with severe groaning. I said: All this from this? He said: I would not like this groaning to not have occurred. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No Muslim is afflicted with any harm in his body except that it is an expiation for his sins, and this is the severest harm."],[5835,"It is as if I am looking at the glint of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reciting the talbiyah."],[5836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made his companions share in the sacrificial animal at Hudaybiyah, one camel between seven."],[5837,"A nation in which the weak cannot take their right without being shaken is not sanctified."],[5838,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the witr prayer on his mount."],[5839,"They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your ummah whom you have not seen? He said: They will have white foreheads and limbs from the traces of wudu."],[5840,"A man who used to backbite people in this world will be brought, and it will be said to him: Eat the flesh of your brother dead, just as you ate it alive. He said: He will eat it, cry out, and grimace."],[5841,"Two types of the people of the Fire I have not yet seen: men with whips like the tails of cattle, striking the people with them; and women clothed yet naked, inclining and making others incline, their heads like the humps of Bactrian camels. They will not enter Paradise, nor find its fragrance."],[5842,"A man should not have skin contact with a man, and a woman should not have skin contact with a woman."],[5843,"Whoever comes to Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[5844,"A rabbi came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Muhammad—or: O Abu al-Qasim—indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will hold the heavens on a finger, the mountains and trees on a finger, the water and the earth on a finger, and the rest of creation on a finger on the Day of Resurrection, then He will shake them and say: 'I am the King, I am the King.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed in amazement at what the rabbi said and in confirmation of it. Then he recited: \"They have not appraised Allah with true appraisal, while the earth entirely will be [within] His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand. Exalted is He and high above what they associate with Him\" (Qur'an 39:67)."],[5845,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up at night, he would clean his mouth with the siwak."],[5846,"Ali said to Abu Mas'ud: \"Are you the one who said: 'A hundred years will not pass upon people while there is a living eye among them'? He only said: 'A hundred years will not pass upon people while there is a living eye among them from those who are alive today.' And indeed the relief and ease of this ummah will be after the hundred [years].\""],[5847,"The scent of a child is from the fragrance of Paradise."],[5848,"These questions are but toil with which a man exhausts his face. Whoever wishes may preserve his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except that a man may ask a man in authority from whom he has no alternative."],[5849,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque. He said: \"Look, which man do you consider most elevated in your eyes?\" I looked, and there was a man wearing a fine garment, surrounded by people. I said: \"This one.\" He said: \"Look, which man do you consider lowest in your eyes?\" I looked, and there was a man wearing a coarse cloak. I said: \"This one.\" He said: \"This one is better in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the earth's fill of the like of that one.\""],[5850,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while his armor was pawned with a Jew for thirty saa's of barley, which he had taken as food for his family."],[5851,"I heard my father say to 'Abdullah: \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Regret is repentance'?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[5852,"Whoever seeks to be heard, Allah will make him heard; and whoever seeks to be seen, Allah will make him seen."],[5853,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali: \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, but there is no prophet after me.\""],[5854,"Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[5855,"I saw him—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—slaughtering them, placing his foot on their sides, saying Bismillah and Allahu Akbar—two horned, amlah rams."],[5856,"Whoever comes to Friday prayer should perform ghusl."],[5857,"The likeness of my household is that of the ark of Nuh. Whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind drowns. The likeness of my household among you is that of the gate of Hittah among the Children of Israel. Whoever enters it is forgiven."],[5858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the conquest: 'This is what my Lord promised me.' Then he recited: 'When the help of Allah and the victory comes.' He said: 'When people entered the religion of Allah in multitudes, and the religion of Allah prevailed over all religion, then people are good, and we are good.'"],[5859,"The lifespans of my Ummah are between sixty and seventy. He ﷺ said: 'And the least of my Ummah are those who reach seventy.'"],[5860,"When Ibn Mas'ud died, Abdullah b. Mas'ud wept over him. They said to him: 'You weep?' He said: 'Yes, my brother in lineage and my companion with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the most beloved of people to me, except for what was from Umar b. al-Khattab.'"],[5861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about monkeys and pigs. He said: 'When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is angry with a people, He does not give them offspring or posterity.'"],[5862,"Three will be given their rewards twice: a slave who fulfills the right of Allah which He has obligated upon him and the right of his masters—he will be given his reward twice on the Day of Resurrection; a man who had a beautiful slave girl, and he educated her well, then freed her, then married her, seeking thereby the face of Allah—he will be given his reward twice; and a man who believed in the earlier scripture, then the later scripture came and he believed in it—he will be given his reward twice."],[5863,"When a slave joins the land of the enemy, his blood becomes lawful."],[5864,"A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ about her father who died without performing Hajj. He said: 'Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.'"],[5865,"Miserliness and faith never combine in the heart of a believer."],[5866,"The one consulted is entrusted."],[5867,"When revelation descended upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, he would feel heavy on account of it, and his forehead would break out in sweat, like pearls."],[5868,"I am told of your whereabouts, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except that I dislike wearying you. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to space out his admonitions to us over the days, out of dislike for causing us boredom."],[5869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: O God, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and self-sufficiency."],[5870,"Whoever dies in either of the two sanctuaries, Makkah or Madinah, will be raised secure."],[5871,"There is no believer but has a sin that befalls him from time to time. The believer is one who forgets, but when reminded, remembers."],[5872,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to the people of Qubāʾ: I hear that God has praised you well concerning purification. What is this purification of yours? They said: By God, O Messenger of God, we know nothing except that our Jewish neighbors we saw washing their backsides from excrement, so we washed as they washed."],[5873,"A roasted bird was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: O God, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me from this bird. Then ʿAlī ؓ came. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw him, he said: O Lord, and to me [too]."],[5874,"A man owes no zakāh on his slave or his horse, except the zakāt al-fiṭr."],[5875,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would sometimes kiss me while he was fasting."],[5876,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would not delay the Maghrib prayer for dinner or anything else."],[5877,"A scorpion stung the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying. When he finished, he said: May God curse the scorpion; it does not spare one who is praying or anyone else. Then he called for water and salt, and began wiping over it and reciting: \"Say: O disbelievers,\" \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak,\" and \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.\""],[5878,"The dream of a believer is one part of seventy parts of prophethood."],[5879,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn above three days, except for a husband."],[5880,"A person is with the one he loves."],[5881,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sought forgiveness for me twenty-five times, all of which I counted with my hand. He said: he would say: “Have you paid your father’s debt on his behalf?” I would say: “Yes.” Then he would say: “May God forgive you.”"],[5882,"The Messenger of God ﷺ traveled to Banu Lihyan, and he put the Kaaba behind him. Then he said: “O Jabir b. Abd Allah.” I came to him, and he sent me for some need of his. I came to him and said: “I have come to them and did such-and-such, but he did not answer me with anything.” So I returned and said: “Perhaps I did not understand the Messenger of God ﷺ.” So I went back to him and said: “I have come to them and did such-and-such.” He said: “I was praying.”"],[5883,"I agreed with my Lord in three things: the veil, the Station of Abraham, and the captives of Badr."],[5884,"Every two parties to a sale have no sale between them until they separate, except the sale with option."],[5885,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for a cupper called Abu Tayba, and he cupped him after the afternoon prayer in Ramadan."],[5886,"We used to sell the ornamented sword and buy it with silver."],[5887,"He used to travel from Makkah to Madinah, praying two rak‘ahs, two rak‘ahs, fearing none but God, blessed and exalted is He."],[5888,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped and paid him his wages; had it been unlawful, he would not have paid him."],[5889,"The soul of the believer comes out like sweat, and I do not like a death like the death of a donkey. It was said: “What is the death of a donkey?” He said: “Sudden death.” He said: “And the soul of the disbeliever comes out from the sides of his mouth.”"],[5890,"No young man honors an elder on account of his age except that God appoints for him someone who will honor him at his age."],[5891,"The best of your youth are those who resemble your elders, and the worst of your elders are those who resemble your youth."],[5892,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"When was your last encounter with Umm Mildam?\" He said: \"What is Umm Mildam?\" He said: \"A heat that occurs between the skin and the bone, sucking the blood and eating the flesh.\" He said: \"I have never complained of it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever wants to look at a man from the people of the Fire, let him look at this one.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Take him away from me.\""],[5893,"May God have mercy on Abu Bakr. He gave me his daughter in marriage, carried me to the abode of emigration, and bought Bilal with his own wealth. May God have mercy on Umar. He speaks the truth even if it is bitter; the truth has left him with no friend. May God have mercy on Uthman, for the angels are shy of him. May God have mercy on Ali. O God, let the truth revolve with him wherever he turns."],[5894,"A woman may not be married along with her paternal aunt, nor along with her maternal aunt."],[5895,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[5896,"Discussion of divine decree is postponed to the worst of my community at the end of time, and arguing about the Quran is disbelief."],[5897,"He prayed behind Ibn Abbas at a funeral, and he recited aloud the Opening of the Book and said: \"I wanted people to know that it is the Sunnah.\""],[5898,"When he prostrated, his knees would touch the ground before his palms, and when he rose in the division of the two units, he rose on his knees and leaned on his thighs."],[5899,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution: he rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his hands three times, wiped his head three times, and washed his feet three times."],[5900,"The Prophet ﷺ taught them the prayer over the deceased: \"O God, forgive our living and our dead, reconcile our differences, and unite our hearts. O God, this is Your servant so-and-so son of so-and-so. We know nothing but good of him, and You know him better. So forgive us and him.\" I said to him, while I was the youngest of the people: \"What if I do not know any good?\" He said: \"Then say only what you know.\""],[5901,"The expiation for a gathering is: \"Glory be to You, O God, and praise be to You. There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.\""],[5902,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ urging support for the army of hardship. Uthman b. Affan stood up and said: \"O Messenger of God, I pledge one hundred camels with their saddles and packs in the path of God.\" I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on the pulpit saying: \"Nothing that Uthman does after this will harm him.\""],[5903,"He forbade qunut in the night prayer."],[5904,"A cow [is sufficient] for seven, and a camel for seven."],[5905,"I passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying, and I greeted him, and he gestured to me."],[5906,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed with them. He recited a surah from the long ones, then bowed five times, and prostrated twice. Then he stood for the second [unit], recited a surah from the long ones, then bowed five times, then prostrated twice. Then he sat as he was, facing the qiblah, supplicating until the eclipse cleared."],[5907,"Whoever carries the four sides of the bier, God expiates forty major sins from him."],[5908,"There is no zakat on vegetables."],[5909,"The servant remains in good as long as he does not hasten. It was said: O Messenger of God, how does he hasten? He said: He says, 'I called upon my Lord, but He did not answer me.'"],[5910,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never gave us a sermon except that he said: 'There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant.'"],[5911,"Whoever humiliates Quraysh, God will humiliate him before his death."],[5912,"When he heard the sound of thunder, he would say: 'O God, do not destroy us with any of Your punishment, and grant us well-being before that.'"],[5913,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was bewitched, so he called upon his Lord. Then he said: 'Did you not know that God, Mighty and Majestic, answered me? Two angels came to me. One sat at my head and the other at my feet. One of them said to the other: What is wrong with the man? He said: He is bewitched. He said: Who bewitched him? He said: Labid b. A'sam the Jew. He said: In what? He said: In a comb and hair combings, in the spathe of a palm tree, in the well of Banu Raysan, beneath the large rock.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O Ali, go to it. Its water was like henna infusion. I wanted to drain it, but he said: God has already healed me.'"],[5914,"He is not one of us who does not honor our elders and have mercy on our young."],[5915,"He met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, while he was on his she-camel al-ʿAḍbāʾ. He said: I said, 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.' He said, 'May Allah forgive you all.' Then I turned around to the other side hoping that he would single me out, and I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.' He said, 'May Allah forgive you all.' Then a man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what about the farāʾiʿ and the ʿatāʾir?' He said, 'Whoever wishes may offer a faraʿ, whoever wishes may offer an ʿatīra, and whoever wishes may not offer an ʿatīra; and in sheep there is their uḍḥiya.' Then he said, 'Verily your blood and your wealth are inviolable upon you, like the sacredness of this day of yours in this month of yours.'"],[5916,"O ʿAlī, command your women not to pray unadorned, even if they should hang a leather strap around their necks."],[5917,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept while sitting until he snored, then he got up and prayed without renewing his ablution."],[5918,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hesitated in a verse during the dawn prayer. When he finished the prayer, he turned his face to the people and said, 'Did Ubayy b. Kaʿb attend the prayer with you?' They said, 'No.' So the people realized that he had looked for him only so that he could prompt him."],[5919,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—and if I wished I could have kissed the place of the seal from him because of my closeness, I would have done so—saying: 'The Throne of the Most Merciful shook on the day he died,' meaning thereby Saʿd b. Muʿādh."],[5920,"I wrote to Nāfiʿ asking him about supplication before fighting. He wrote to me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided Banū al-Muṣṭaliq, killing their fighting men and taking their offspring captive."],[5921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, so we brought out for him a small vessel of brass, and he performed ablution, washing his face three times and his forearms twice each, and he wiped his head, passing his hands forward and back."],[5922,"We entered upon Salmān, and he called for whatever was in the house, and said, 'Were it not that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to put ourselves to trouble for a guest, I would have put myself to trouble for you.'"],[5923,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ measured for Fāṭima a span from her heel, and said, 'This is the train of a woman.'"],[5924,"I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'Not equal are those believers who sit [at home]—other than those who are disabled.' Ibn ʿAbbās said, 'They are people kept back by pains or illnesses, so those were the ones with disability, and the sick person who stayed behind had more excuse than the healthy one who stayed behind.'"],[5925,"I saw my father trim his nails and then bury them, and he said, 'O my little daughter, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do like this.'"],[5926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed a restriction on the wealth of Muʿādh b. Jabal and sold it for a debt he owed."],[5927,"Whoever prays the morning prayer and sits in his prayer place until the sun rises, then prays four rak'ahs, Allah will forgive his sins."],[5928,"O believing women, exchange gifts, even if it is a sheep's hoof, for it strengthens affection and removes grudges."],[5929,"We used to refrain from seeking forgiveness for those who commit major sins, until we heard our Prophet ﷺ say: 'I have reserved my intercession for the major sinners of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection.' So we refrained from much of what was in our hearts, and we hoped for them."],[5930,"May Allah have mercy on the one who is easygoing when buying, when paying, and when demanding payment."],[5931,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in his sandals."],[5932,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her: 'Seek refuge in Allah from the evil eye, for it is real.'"],[5933,"The Prophet ﷺ cut off the hand for a shield worth five dirhams."],[5934,"Whoever attends an imam (ruler), let him speak good or remain silent."],[5935,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Peace be upon you.' He replied to him, then he sat down. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Ten.' Then another came and said, 'Peace be upon you and Allah's mercy.' He replied to him, then he sat down. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Twenty.' Then another came and said, 'Peace be upon you, Allah's mercy, and His blessings.' He replied to him, then he sat down. He said, 'Thirty good deeds.'"],[5936,"We were around the Prophet ﷺ when a man came and said, 'Peace be upon you.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Ten good deeds.' Then another came and said, 'Peace be upon you and Allah's mercy.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Twenty.' Then another came and said, 'Peace be upon you, Allah's mercy, and His blessings.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Thirty good deeds.'"],[5937,"The Prophet ﷺ used to stand by a tree trunk before the pulpit was made. When the pulpit was made, the trunk yearned until we heard its yearning, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on it and it became still."],[5938,"My eyes became inflamed, and the Prophet ﷺ visited me during the inflammation. He said, 'O Zayd, if your eyes were afflicted with what they are, what would you do?' I said, 'I would be patient and seek reward.' He said, 'O Zayd, if your eyes were afflicted with what they are, and you were patient and sought reward, your reward would be nothing less than Paradise.'"],[5939,"He was on a journey and heard a caller saying: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar. He said: Upon the fitrah. Then he said: Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah. He said: He has come out of the Fire. The people hastened to him, and behold, it was a shepherd of sheep; when the prayer time arrived, he gave the adhan."],[5940,"The believer who mixes with people and bears their harm is better than the believer who does not mix with people and does not bear their harm."],[5941,"All of you are shepherds, and all of you are responsible for your flocks."],[5942,"Prices rose during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, set prices for us. He said: Indeed Allah is the One who sets prices, and I hope to meet Allah with none of you having a claim against me for any wrong in religion or worldly matters."],[5943,"Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."],[5944,"I asked my Lord for the heedless ones among the descendants of mankind, and He granted them to me."],[5945,"Al-Hajjaj wanted to appoint him as judge of Basra, so Anas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever seeks judgeship and seeks help for it will be left to himself, and whoever does not seek it and does not seek help for it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will send down an angel to guide him aright."],[5946,"Three people came to the Prophet ﷺ. The first said: Al-salamu 'alaykum, and the Prophet ﷺ replied: Salamun 'alaykum wa rahmatullah. The second came and said: Al-salamu 'alaykum wa rahmatullah, and the Prophet ﷺ replied: Salamun 'alaykum wa rahmatullah wa barakatuh. The third came and said: Al-salamu 'alaykum wa rahmatullah wa barakatuh, and the Prophet ﷺ replied: Wa 'alaykum. Abu al-Fata was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, you added for so-and-so and so-and-so, but you did not add anything for my son? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: We did not find any addition for him, so we returned to him what he said."],[5947,"A son was born to Sulayman b. Dawud, and he said to the devils: Where can we hide him from death? They said: We will take him to the east. He said: Death will reach him. They said: Then to the west. He said: Death will reach him. They said: To the seas. He said: It will reach him. They said: We will place him between heaven and earth. Then the Angel of Death descended and said: O son of Dawud, I was commanded to take a soul. I sought it in the east and did not find it; I sought it in the west and did not find it; I sought it in the seas and in the ends of the earth and did not find it. While I was ascending, I found it and took it. Then his body came and fell upon his throne. That is the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'And We certainly tried Sulayman and placed on his throne a body; then he turned in repentance.'"],[5948,"No body nourished with what is unlawful will enter Paradise."],[5949,"Does not the one who raises his head before the imam fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey?"],[5950,"The Prophet ﷺ saw me while I was giving water to two men from a small water-skin in front of me. I spat, and my spittle fell on my garment, so I began to wash my garment from the water-skin in front of me. The Prophet ﷺ said: O 'Ammar, your spittle and the tears of your eyes are only like the water in your water-skin. You wash your garment only from urine, feces, semen, major impurity, blood, and vomit."],[5951,"We traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ one night, and he made a stop for us to rest in the latter part of the night. We woke up after the sun had risen. He said: 'Depart, depart.' So we departed until when the sun was in the middle of the sky, he dismounted. He ordered Bilal, and he gave the call to prayer. Each man among us prayed two rakʿahs, then he led us in prayer. We said: 'O Messenger of God, should we repeat it tomorrow at its proper time?' He said: 'God has forbidden us from usury; would He accept it from us?'"],[5952,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about stray animals. He said: 'The stray animal of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.'"],[5953,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came, the ugliest of people in face, the ugliest of people in clothing, and the foulest of people in smell—coarse and rough. He stepped over the people's necks and sat down in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: 'Who created you?' He replied: 'God.' He said: 'Who created the sky?' He replied: 'God.' He said: 'Who created the earth?' He replied: 'God.' He said: 'Who created God?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Glory be to God' twice, and he grabbed his forehead. The man got up and left. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Bring me the man.' We looked for him, but it was as if he had never existed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'This is Iblis. He came to make you doubt your religion.'"],[5954,"In Makkah there were two paralyzed men who had a young son. Every morning he would carry them and bring them to the mosque. He would earn a living for them during the day, and when evening came he would carry them back. The Messenger of God ﷺ missed him and asked about him. It was said: 'Their son has died.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If anyone were to be spared for anyone, the son of the two paralyzed men would have been spared.'"],[5955,"The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of God, Mighty and Majestic. When you see that, hasten to prayer."],[5956,"If a man has dirhams in his lap that he is distributing, while another is remembering God, the one who remembers God is better."],[5957,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[5958,"The imam is appointed only to be followed. When he says the takbir, say the takbir, and do not say the takbir until he says it. When he bows, bow, and do not bow until he bows. When he says 'God hears the one who praises Him,' say 'Our Lord, to You belongs all praise.' When he prostrates, prostrate, and do not prostrate until he prostrates. When he raises his head, raise your heads, and do not raise them until he raises his. If he prays sitting, then all of you pray sitting."],[5959,"I heard Muhammad b. Sirin, when a man asked him about forgetfulness in prayer, say: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us that he prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ one of the daytime prayers, and that he prayed two rakʿahs then said the salutation. The quickest of the people left, and they said: 'O Messenger of God, has the prayer been shortened?' Among the people were Abu Bakr and ʿUmar, but they were too awed to speak to him. A man among the Muslims said: 'O Messenger of God, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?' He said: 'It has not been shortened, and I have not forgotten.' A man said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, you forgot. You only prayed two rakʿahs.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Is what Dhu al-Yadayn says true?' They said: 'He has spoken the truth, O Messenger of God.' He then stood up and prayed two more rakʿahs in addition to the first two, then said the salutation, then prostrated twice, similar to his prostration in the prayer or longer."],[5960,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from marrying a woman along with her paternal aunt or along with her maternal aunt."],[5961,"When God sent Adam down to the earth, he stood facing the Kaʿbah and prayed two rakʿahs. God inspired him with this supplication: 'O God, You know my secret and my open, so accept my excuse. You know my need, so grant my request. You know what is in my soul, so forgive my sin. O God, I ask You for faith that touches my heart, and true certainty until I know that nothing will befall me except what You have decreed for me, and contentment with what You have apportioned for me.' God revealed to him: 'O Adam, I have accepted your repentance and forgiven your sin. No one will call upon Me with this supplication except that I will forgive his sin, suffice him in his important affairs, drive away Satan from him, trade for him behind every trader, and the world will come to him submissively even if he does not want it.'"],[5962,"When you attend your dying, close their eyes, for the sight follows the soul. And speak good, for the angels say 'Amen' to what the family of the deceased says."],[5963,"The wrongdoer will come on the Day of Resurrection, until when he is on the bridge of Hell, between the darkness and the rugged terrain, the wronged one will meet him and recognize him, and he will know what he wronged him with. Then those who were wronged will not cease taking retribution from those who wronged them, until they strip them of the good deeds that are in their hands. If they have no good deeds, their bad deeds will be thrown onto them in the same measure as the wrong they did, until they are sent down to the lowest level of the Fire."],[5964,"The evil eye is indeed set upon a man by Allah's permission, until he climbs a high place and tumbles down from it."],[5965,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his journeys, a man was in front of him checking whether there was anything in the road that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked, so he could remove it from him. Then he came upon an old woman who did not cover her nakedness. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is approaching you,' but she turned away. He said it to her three times, and each time she turned away from him. She said: 'What do you order me to do if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is approaching me?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard her words and said: 'Leave her alone, for she is defiant.'"],[5966,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'My servant asked you for food and you did not feed him. Had you fed him, I would have fed you. My servant asked you for water and you did not give him to drink. Had you given him to drink, I would have given you to drink.'"],[5967,"Would any of you like his beloved to be adorned with a bracelet of fire? They said: No. He said: Then do not adorn yourselves with gold. But as for silver, play with it as you wish."],[5968,"A people complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the drought. He said: 'Kneel down and say: O Lord, O Lord,' and he raised his index finger to the sky. They did so, and they were given rain until they wished it would stop."],[5969,"He used to frequently make this supplication: 'O Allah, make me fear You as if I see You always until I meet You. Make me happy through piety toward You, and do not make me wretched through disobedience to You. Choose for me in Your decree, and bless me in Your ordainment, so that I do not wish to hasten what You have delayed or delay what You have hastened. Make my richness within myself, and grant me enjoyment of my hearing and my sight, and make them my heirs. Grant me victory over those who wrong me, and show me my retribution against them, and comfort my eyes with that.'"],[5970,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade plastering graves, building over them, and sitting on them."],[5971,"When the time of prayer came during the era of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man would go out to the road and call: 'Prayer, prayer.' That became difficult for the people, so they said: 'Should we take a bell, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'That is for the Christians.' They said: 'Should we take a trumpet?' He said: 'That is for the Jews.' He said: So Bilal was ordered to say the adhan in pairs and the iqamah singly."],[5972,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade riding on leopard skins."],[5973,"When the death of the Negus reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: 'Your brother the Negus has died, so pray over him.' He stood and prayed over him, with the people behind him."],[5974,"The people of Yemen have come to you. They are the most tender-hearted. Faith is Yemeni, jurisprudence is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."],[5975,"Pride and arrogance are among the owners of horses and camels, while dignity and tranquility are among the owners of sheep. The clamorous ones are the people of the fur (i.e., Bedouin camel-herders)."],[5976,"I had forbidden you from certain vessels, that you should make nabidh in them. Verily, the vessels do not make anything lawful or unlawful. So make nabidh in whatever seems good to you, and avoid every intoxicant."],[5977,"Whoever has this world as his concern and his anxiety, looking to it and intending it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will place poverty before his eyes, scatter his affairs, and nothing will come to him from it except what has been decreed for him. And whoever has the Hereafter as his concern and his anxiety, looking to it and intending it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will place richness in his heart, gather his affairs, and the world will come to him in submission."],[5978,"O my son, keep my secret, and you will be a believer, for I have never told anyone his secret. Indeed, my mother and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ asked me, but I did not tell them his secret, and I will never tell his secret to anyone. Then he said: O my son, perform ablution thoroughly, and your lifespan will be increased, and your two guardian angels will love you. Then he said: O my son, if you are able not to sleep except upon ablution, then do so, for whoever death comes upon while he is upon ablution will be given martyrdom. Then he said: O my son, if you are able to never cease praying, then do so, for the angels never cease to send blessings upon you as long as you pray. Then he said: O my son, beware of turning around during prayer, for turning around during prayer is ruin. If it is absolutely necessary, then in the voluntary prayer, not the obligatory. Then he said to me: O my son, when you bow, place your palms on your knees, spread your fingers, and raise your hands away from your sides. When you raise your head from bowing, let every limb settle in its proper position, for Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at one who does not straighten his back. Then he said to me: O my son, when you prostrate, do not peck like a rooster pecks, do not sit like a dog sits, and do not spread your forearms on the ground like a wild beast. Spread the tops of your feet on the ground, put your buttocks on your heels, for that will be easier for you on the Day of Resurrection in your reckoning. Then he said to me: O my son, be thorough in the ghusl from major ritual impurity, and you will emerge from your place of washing with no sin or error upon you. I said: May my father and mother be your ransom, what is thoroughness in ghusl? He said: Wet the roots of the hair and cleanse the skin. Then he said to me: O my son, if you are able to make some of your prayer in your house, then do so, for it will increase the good of your house. Then he said to me: O my son, when you enter upon your family, give the greeting of peace; it will be a blessing upon you and your household. Then he said to me: O my son, when you leave your family, let your gaze not fall upon anyone of the people of the qiblah except that you greet him, and you will return having increased your good deeds. Then he said: O my son, if you are able to pass the evening and the morning with no deceit in your heart toward anyone, then do so. Then he said to me: O Anas, when you leave your family, let your gaze not fall upon anyone of the people of the qiblah except that you think he has excellence over you, then do so. Then he said to me: O my son, that is from my Sunnah. Whoever revives my Sunnah has loved me, and whoever loves me will be with me in Paradise. Then he said to me: O my son, if you preserve my bequest, then nothing will be more beloved to you than death. No one narrated this hadith in its complete form from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib except 'Ali b. Zayd, and no one from 'Ali b. Zayd except 'Abd Allah b. al-Muthanna. Muslim b. Hatim was alone in narrating it from al-Ansari, from his father, and Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Abi Yazid was alone in narrating it from 'Abbad al-Minqari."],[5979,"Two circumambulations, their performer's sins are forgiven no matter how great they are: a circumambulation after the dawn prayer whose completion is at sunrise, and a circumambulation after the afternoon prayer whose completion is at sunset. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what if it is before that or after that? He said: It will be joined to it."],[5980,"A servant whose fire will not be extinguished, whose worms will not die, and whose punishment will not be lightened: the one who associates partners with Allah; a man who drags another man to a ruler without guilt and has him killed; and a man who is undutiful to his parents."],[5981,"A man from Banu Kilab came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the stud fee of a stallion. He forbade him, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, we provide the stallion and are honored (with a gift). So he gave him a concession regarding the honorarium."],[5982,"Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant in family, wealth, or children such that he says, 'What Allah wills, there is no power except with Allah,' and then sees in it an affliction short of death. He used to interpret this verse: 'And why did you not, when you entered your garden, say: What Allah wills, there is no power except with Allah' (al-Kahf 18:39)."],[5983,"Do you not know that the forbearing person was nearly a prophet? Then he turned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: By al-Lat and al-'Uzza, I will not believe in you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said to him: O Bedouin, what made you say what you said? You have spoken untruth and not honored my assembly. He said: And you still speak to me—showing contempt for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—by al-Lat and al-'Uzza, I will not believe in you, or this lizard will believe in you. He brought out a lizard from his sleeve and threw it before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: If this lizard believes in you, I will believe in you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O lizard. The lizard spoke in clear Arabic speech, understood by all the people: At your service, at your service, O Messenger of the Lord of the worlds. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to it: Whom do you worship? It said: The One whose Throne is in the heaven, whose authority is in the earth, whose path is in the sea, whose mercy is in Paradise, and whose punishment is in the Fire. He said: Who am I, O lizard? It said: You are the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds and the Seal of the Prophets. Whoever believes in you has succeeded, and whoever denies you has failed. The Bedouin said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are truly the Messenger of Allah. I came to you when there was no one on the face of the earth more hateful to me than you, and by Allah, you are now more beloved to me than myself and my parents. I have believed in you with my hair, my skin, my inner being, my outer being, my secret, and my public. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Praise be to Allah who has guided you to this religion that prevails and is not prevailed upon. Allah does not accept it except with prayer, and He does not accept prayer except with the Qur'an. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him al-Hamd and Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have never heard in al-basit or in al-rajaz anything more beautiful than this. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: This is the speech of the Lord of the worlds, not poetry. When you recite Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad once, it is as if you have recited a third of the Qur'an; when you recite it twice, it is as if you have recited two-thirds; and when you recite it three times, it is as if you have recited the entire Qur'an. The Bedouin said: What an excellent god our God is: He accepts the little and gives the abundant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Give to the Bedouin. So they gave him until they made him giddy. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to give him a she-camel by which I seek nearness to Allah, below the Bukhti breed and above the Bedouin breed, and she is ten months pregnant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You have described what you will give; shall I describe to you what Allah will give you as reward? He said: Yes. He said: You will have a she-camel of hollow pearl, its legs of green emerald, its neck of yellow chrysolite, upon it a howdah, and upon the howdah fine silk and brocade. It will pass over the Bridge like flashing lightning. The Bedouin left the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and met a thousand Bedouins on a thousand mounts, with a thousand spears and a thousand swords. He said to them: Where are you heading? They said: We are going to fight this one who lies and claims to be a prophet. The Bedouin said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said to him: Have you turned renegade? He said: I have not turned renegade. He told them the story, and they all said: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he met them without a cloak. They dismounted from their riding animals, kissing what they turned toward of him, saying: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: Command us with something that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ loves. He said: You will be under the banner of Khalid b. al-Walid. He said: No group from the Arabs believed as they did—a thousand men altogether—except Banu Sulaym. No one narrated this hadith in its complete form from Dawud b. Abi Hind except Kahmas, and no one from Kahmas except Mu'tamir. Muhammad b. 'Abd al-A'la was alone in narrating it."],[5984,"The Day of Sacrifice is the day of the greater Hajj."],[5985,"Three things are from rudeness: a man wiping dust from his face before finishing his prayer, blowing dust in prayer from the place of his face, and urinating while standing."],[5986,"Is any of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an in a night? They said: O Messenger of Allah, who is able to recite a third of the Qur'an? He said: Is any of you unable to recite Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad?"],[5987,"Whoever eats seven dates of 'Ajwah of Madinah in a day, poison will not harm him that day; and whoever eats them at night, poison will not harm him."],[5988,"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."],[5989,"When one of you uses stones for istijmar, let him make it odd, for Allah is odd and loves the odd."],[5990,"'Uthman entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and confided with him for a long time, while I was below them. I was not startled except that 'Uthman was kneeling on his knees, saying: \"Out of injustice and enmity, O Messenger of Allah?\" So I thought that he informed him of his killing."],[5991,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a choice, and it was not a divorce."],[5992,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go to the desert."],[5993,"Indeed a man from the people of 'Illiyyin will look down upon the people of Paradise as if he were a shining star, and indeed Abu Bakr and 'Umar are among them and favored."],[5994,"Indeed I dislike a woman who leaves her house dragging her garment, complaining about her husband."],[5995,"Whoever has two garments, let him wear both; and whoever has one garment, let him wrap it around his waist, and not wrap himself in the wrapping of the Jews."],[5996,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about madhy. He said: \"In it is wudu'.\" And I asked him about semen. He said: \"In it is ghusl.\""],[5997,"Indeed I give and withhold, I entrust it to what is in his heart. Among them is Ibn Taghlib."],[5998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from selling what I do not have."],[5999,"There will soon come upon the people a time when they will not enjoin what is good, nor forbid what is evil."],[6000,"My intercession on the Day of Resurrection is for the one who bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah."],[6001,"Perform witr, O people of the Qur'an."],[6002,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ during the expedition of al-Muraysi', the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq, and their battle cry was: 'O victorious one, grant death!'"],[6003,"He was on an expedition, and a man from the polytheists challenged a man from the Muslims and killed him. Then another Muslim came out to him and the polytheist killed him. Then he approached and stood before the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'What do you fight for?' He said: 'Our religion is that we fight people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that we fulfill the due right of Allah.' He said: 'By Allah, this is indeed good. I believe in this.' Then he turned to the Muslims, charged against the polytheists, and fought until he was killed. He was carried and placed with his two companions whom he had killed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'These are the people of Paradise with the strongest love for one another.'"],[6004,"Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their excessive questioning of their prophets and their differing with their prophets. So whatever I command you to do, do as much of it as you are able, and whatever I forbid you, abstain from it."],[6005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was lying across in front of him."],[6006,"Shall I tell you who is most beloved of you to Allah? We said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah,' and we thought he would name a man. He said: 'The most beloved of you to Allah is the most beloved of you to the people.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I tell you who is most hateful of you to Allah?' We said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah,' and we thought he would name a man. He said: 'The most hateful of you to Allah is the most hateful of you to the people.'"],[6007,"A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, being shaken violently like the shaking of a waterskin. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You should walk at a moderate pace for your funerals, without hurrying. If the deceased was good, you are hastening him to it; and if he was evil, then God only removes the people of the Fire far away. The funeral is followed, and it does not follow; there is none with it who goes ahead of it.'"],[6008,"The image-makers will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: 'Bring to life what you have created.'"],[6009,"To sit with a people who remember Allah after the dawn prayer until sunrise is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves from the descendants of Isma'il. And to sit with a people who remember Allah from the 'Asr prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves from the descendants of Isma'il."],[6010,"He was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the tree, the day when the sacrificial animals were detained before reaching their place of sacrifice. A man came to him that day and said: 'O Muhammad, what makes you do what I see? Do you want these people to enter, while we dislike them, from among the scattered tribes?' He said: 'These are better than you and better than those who follow your example. They believe in Allah and the Last Day. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, they are indeed good.' ؓ"],[6011,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in the year of al-Hudaybiyah pairing seven of his companions for one camel."],[6012,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us and said four things: \"Indeed God, Mighty and Majestic, does not sleep, nor is it befitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the balance and raises it. The deeds of the day are raised to Him before the deeds of the night, and the deeds of the night before the deeds of the day. His veil is fire; if He were to remove the veil, the radiance of His face would burn every thing that His sight reaches.\" Then he recited: 'It was proclaimed: Blessed is whoever is in the Fire and whoever is around it.'"],[6013,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, which people are most beloved to God? And which deeds are most beloved to God, Mighty and Majestic?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The most beloved of people to God are those most beneficial to people, and the most beloved of deeds to God is joy that you bring to a Muslim, or you relieve him of a distress, or you pay off a debt for him, or you drive away hunger from him. And that I walk with a brother of mine to fulfill his need is more beloved to me than that I seclude myself in this mosque—meaning the Mosque of Madinah—for a month. Whoever restrains his anger, God will conceal his faults, and whoever suppresses his rage—even though if he wished he could act upon it—God, Mighty and Majestic, will fill his heart with security on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever walks with his brother to fulfill his need until he secures it for him, God, Mighty and Majestic, will secure his foot upon the Bridge on the day when feet slip upon it.\""],[6014,"Visit the sick, and command them to pray for you, for the supplication of the sick is answered and his sin is forgiven."],[6015,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: \"No Qurayshi shall be killed in retaliation after this day until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6016,"I entered upon A'ishah, and she called for food and said, \"Eat. How rarely do I feel full from food but that I wish to weep and I do weep.\" I said, \"O Mother of the Believers, why is that?\" She said, \"I remember the condition in which the Messenger of God ﷺ left this world. The Messenger of God ﷺ never ate his fill twice in a day of wheat bread until he met God.\" He said: And A'ishah said, \"A woman from the Ansar entered upon me and saw that the bedding of the Messenger of God ﷺ was a coarse cloak. She said, 'Does he have no bedding other than this?' I said, 'No, by God, he has no bedding other than it.' So she took a strip of fine cloth and stuffed it with wool, then brought it to me and said, 'Let this be the bedding of the Messenger of God ﷺ.' When he came, he said, 'O A'ishah, what is this?' I told him, and he said, 'Return it.' She said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ left my presence while I had not returned it, and I was pleased that it should be in my house. Then he came and said, 'O A'ishah, did I not command you to return it?' I said, 'O Messenger of God, I did not return it, and I loved that it be in my house.' He said, 'O A'ishah, return it, for if I wished, God would have caused gold and silver to flow with me.'\""],[6017,"Five harmful creatures are to be killed in the sacred and non-sacred areas: the mouse, the scorpion, the kite, the vicious dog, and the crow."],[6018,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and caught up with him at al-Baqi', and I heard him say, \"Peace be upon the inhabitants of these dwellings among the believers.\" My sandal strap broke, and he said, \"Raise your foot.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, my solitude has grown long and I have been far from my people's abode.\" He said, \"O Bashir, will you not praise God who took you by the forelock to Islam from among Rabi'ah—a people who think that were it not for them, the earth would overturn with all upon it?\""],[6019,"Indeed there will be troubles upon troubles. Whoever you see walking toward the community of Muhammad ﷺ while they are united in order to divide them, kill him, whoever he may be."],[6020,"Indeed the Qur'an was revealed in seven dialects, all of which are healing and sufficient."],[6021,"Indeed I am your forerunner at the Basin, and the distance between its two ends is like that between San'a' and Aylah, and the pitchers in it are like the stars."],[6022,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited five things: the price of a dog, the price of a pig, the price of wine, the earnings of a prostitute, and the stud fee of a stallion."],[6023,"On the day of Badr: Return what you have with you of the spoils. Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi raised the sword of Banu al-'A'idh b. al-Marzuban, and al-Arqam recognized it, so he said: Grant it to me, O Messenger of Allah, and he gave it to him."],[6024,"Indeed Dawud the Prophet ﷺ said: My God, what is due to You from Your servants when they visit You in Your House? He said: Every visitor has a right upon the visited one. O Dawud, they have upon Me that I grant them well-being in this world and forgive them when I meet them."],[6025,"A man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ was stung, and it afflicted him as much as Allah willed. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Indeed, had he said when evening came – or: in the evening – 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,' three times, it would not have harmed him."],[6026,"There is no deceased person who dies and a group of Muslims numbering one hundred prays over him, all of them interceding for him, but that their intercession is accepted for him."],[6027,"She slaughtered a sheep in her house, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to her: Feed us from your sheep. She said to the messenger: Nothing remains of it except the neck, and I am ashamed to send the neck to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The messenger returned and informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Go back and say: Send it, for it is the guide of the sheep, the closest part of the sheep to goodness, and the furthest from harm.'"],[6028,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'And give its due on the day of its harvest,' he said: They used to give something to those who came to them, apart from the obligatory charity."],[6029,"Two brothers had land between them, and one of them gave his share as a life-grant to their mother. When she died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided it between them."],[6030,"Cool down the prayer, for the intensity of heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[6031,"The Prophet ﷺ returned, and when he drew near to Madinah he said: Returning, repenting, worshipping, praising our Lord. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel, the gloom of the return, and an evil sight in family and wealth."],[6032,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the wives of the Ansar, and their descendants."],[6033,"They disputed before the Prophet ﷺ about predestination, and he disliked that intensely, until it was as if pomegranate seeds had been burst on his face. He said: 'What are you doing?' They said: We are disputing about predestination, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Everything is by decree and predestination, even this – and he struck his index finger on the tendon of his other arm."],[6034,"Whoever spends two of a kind from his wealth in the path of Allah, the gatekeepers of Paradise will hasten to him. I said: 'Two camels, two horses, two sheep, two dirhams, two leather socks, two sandals.'"],[6035,"The Prophet ﷺ was sent while I was a boy carrying meat from the plain to the mountain."],[6036,"You will never recite a surah more beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, nor more effective than: “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.” So if you are able not to omit it in any prayer, then do so."],[6037,"When you are praying and a man wants to pass in front of you, repel him. If he returns, repel him. If he returns, repel him. If he returns a fourth time, then fight him, for he is only a devil."],[6038,"When the Prophet ﷺ retired to his bed, he would say: “O Allah, I have submitted my soul to You, and entrusted my affair to You, and leaned my back upon You, out of desire and fear of You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in what You have sent down of the Book and in what You have sent of a Messenger.”"],[6039,"Whoever prays four rak‘ahs before Zuhr, he will have the like of the reward of freeing a slave,” or he said: “four slaves from the descendants of Ishmael ﷺ ."],[6040,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon one of his companions while he was ill and said: “Remove the affliction, O Lord of mankind. Heal, for You are the Healer. There is no healer but You, a healing that leaves no sickness.”"],[6041,"I prayed the morning prayer in Makkah beside an old man. When he finished his prayer, he said: “After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I have not prayed behind anyone whose prayer more closely resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than this young man.” The imam that day was Umar b. Abd al-Aziz. I said, “Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?” He said, “Anas b. Malik.”"],[6042,"We used to carry water in camel skins to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day they wounded his face."],[6043,"Use ithmid (antimony) at bedtime, for it makes the hair grow and clears the eyesight."],[6044,"Do not mix raisins and dried dates, nor unripe dates and dried dates."],[6045,"The Prophet ﷺ addressed them and said: “The ‘umra (life grant) is permissible.”"],[6046,"He forbade raisins with dried dates, and unripe dates with dried dates."],[6047,"Whoever sleeps while sitting, no wudu is required of him; but when he lays down on his side, then wudu is required of him."],[6048,"Be of Maʿadd, be rough, and walk barefoot."],[6049,"I asked Anas b. Malik about three things: about the sun, the moon, and the stars—from what were they created? He said..."],[6050,"Whoever is placed in charge of any affair of the people with an intention for the truth, two angels are assigned to him to grant him success and guide him. And whoever is placed in charge of any affair of the people with an intention other than the truth, Allah leaves him to himself."],[6051,"There is no worry except the worry of debt, and no pain except the pain of the eye."],[6052,"Two groups of my community have no share in Islam: the Murjiʾa and the Qadariyya."],[6053,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the Kaʿba has a tongue and two lips. It complained to Allah and said: 'O Lord, my visitors have become few and my pilgrims have become few.' So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to it: 'I will create humble, prostrating humans who yearn for you as a dove yearns for its egg.'"],[6054,"I said to ʿAʾisha: 'O maternal aunt, I have been reflecting on your situation, and I am amazed by some things and not amazed by others. I found you to be among the most knowledgeable of people in fiqh.' I said: 'What prevents her? She is the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the daughter of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq.' I found you knowledgeable of the genealogies of the Arabs and their battle-days. I said: 'What prevents her? Her father was the most learned of Quraysh.' But I am only amazed that I found you knowledgeable of medicine—so from where?' She said: 'O ʿUrayya, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had many illnesses, and we used to treat him.'"],[6055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told her a hadith while he was with her under a blanket. She said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah. If you had not told me this hadith, I would have thought it was a Khurafa.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is the hadith of Khurafa, O ʿAʾisha?' She said: 'When something is not real, it is said: \"a Khurafa tale.\"' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The truest of speech is the hadith of Khurafa—a man from Banu ʿUdhra whom the jinn captured. He used to be with them, and when they eavesdropped on the heavens, they would inform him, and he would inform the people, and they would find it as he said.'"],[6056,"When one of you buys a slave-girl, let the first thing he feeds her be sweets, for that is best for her disposition."],[6057,"The peak of intellect after faith in Allah is showing affection to people."],[6058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a choice—was that a divorce?"],[6059,"In the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers and good things are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[6060,"This verse was revealed: “And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, to abide therein” after the one in al-Furqan: “And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right” by six months."],[6061,"Whoever eats from these two trees should not come near our mosque, and if you must eat them, then kill them by cooking."],[6062,"There is no state in which the servant is more beloved to Allah than for Him to see him prostrating, rubbing his face in the dust."],[6063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque with some women of the Ansar, and he admonished and reminded them, saying: “There is not among you a woman who loses three of her children except that she enters Paradise.” A woman—one of the noblest among them—stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, what about one who loses two?” He said: “And one who loses two.”"],[6064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade throwing pebbles, and said: “No game is hunted with it, and no enemy is incapacitated by it, but it breaks a tooth and gouges an eye.”"],[6065,"If you can be behind the imam, then do so; otherwise, be on his right."],[6066,"Our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last third of the night has passed, and says: “Is there any servant of My servants who calls upon Me, that I may answer him? Is there any wrongdoer against himself who calls upon Me, that I may forgive him? Is there any whose provision is straitened? Is there any oppressed who remembers Me, that I may help him? Is there any captive who calls upon Me, that I may aid him?” He said: “It continues thus until the dawn shines, then our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, ascends to His Throne.”"],[6067,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda'."],[6068,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped and gave the cupper his fee."],[6069,"The Prophet ﷺ asked a man from his companions, saying: “Did you visit a sick person today?” He said: “No.” He said: “Did you give any charity?” He said: “No.” He said: “Did you pray over a funeral?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then have relations with your wife.” He said: “No.” He said: “Then do so with them, for it is a charity from you to them.” And that was on Friday."],[6070,"I am the witness over Allah that no rational person slips except that He raises him until He makes his final abode Paradise."],[6071,"There is nothing more noble in the sight of Allah than the believer."],[6072,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Ali as a commander over Yemen and sent Khalid b. al-Walid over the mountain. He said: If you meet, Ali is in charge of the people. So they met and obtained spoils the like of which they had never obtained. Ali took a slave girl from the fifth. Khalid b. al-Walid called Buraydah and said: Seize this opportunity and inform the Prophet ﷺ of what he did. So I arrived in Madinah and entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in his house, and some of his companions were at his door. They said: What is the news, O Buraydah? I said: Good. Allah granted victory to the Muslims. They said: What brought you? He said: A slave girl whom Ali took from the fifth, so I came to inform the Prophet ﷺ. They said: Then inform him, for it will cause him to fall from the sight of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard the talk and came out angry, saying: \"What is the matter with people who belittle Ali? Whoever belittles Ali has belittled me, and whoever leaves Ali has left me. Indeed, Ali is from me and I am from him. He was created from my clay, and I was created from the clay of Ibrahim, and I am more excellent than Ibrahim: 'Offspring, one of another; and Allah is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.'\" Then he said: \"O Buraydah, do you not know that Ali has more right than the slave girl he took, and that he is your guardian after me?\" So I said: O Messenger of Allah, by the companionship, extend your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you anew upon Islam. He said: I did not leave him until I pledged allegiance to him upon Islam."],[6073,"Acts of kindness protect against evil fates, secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord, maintaining family ties increases lifespan, and every good deed is charity. The people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter. The first to enter Paradise are the people of good."],[6074,"The Prophet ﷺ and I used to bathe from a single vessel."],[6075,"The Prophet ﷺ would become junub, then sleep, then wake up, then sleep again, without touching water."],[6076,"They set out toward Kufah, and Umar b. al-Khattab preceded them, holding his sandals in his left hand, and he outran them by about three miles until he reached Banu Abd al-Ashhal. He said: You are about to enter a city whose inhabitants have a buzzing like the buzzing of bees. So reduce your narration from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I am your partner in that."],[6077,"Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row."],[6078,"Fadalah b. Ubayd used to say: O Allah, I ask You for contentment after the decree, a pleasant life after death, the delight of looking at Your face, and longing to meet You, without harmful adversity or misleading trial. He claimed that these were supplications with which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate."],[6079,"The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ, and while they were sitting with him, he turned to them and said: A fruit you call such-and-such, and a fruit you call such-and-such—until he described the colors of all their fruits. A man from the people said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah. By Allah, if you had been born in the heart of Hajar, you would not have been more knowledgeable than you are now. I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Your land was raised up for me since you sat with me, and I looked from its nearest part to its farthest. The best of your fruits is the barni; it removes disease, and there is no disease in it.\""],[6080,"These words are a cure for every disease: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah and all His names, generally, from the evil of poisonous and harmful creatures, from the evil of the evil eye, from the evil of the envier when he envies, and from the evil of Abu Qatarah and what he begot. Thirty-three angels came to their Lord and said: There is an epidemic in our land. He said: Take soil from your land, then wipe it over your sick. This is the ruqyah of Muhammad ﷺ. Whoever takes payment for it or conceals it from anyone will never prosper."],[6081,"I said to Aishah: What do you think about the saying of Allah, may His remembrance be exalted: 'Then We caused to inherit the Book those We have chosen of Our servants; and among them is he who wrongs himself, and among them is he who is moderate, and among them is he who is foremost in good deeds by permission of Allah'—the verse? She said: As for the foremost, he has passed away during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he bore witness for him to Paradise. As for the moderate, he is the one who followed their footsteps and acted according to their deeds until he joins them. As for the one who wrongs himself, he is like me and you and whoever follows us. She said: And all of them are in Paradise."],[6082,"Umm Sulaym used to treat the wounded in the army of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would supplicate to Allah for my son. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Unays?\" She said: Yes. So he seated me before him and wiped his hand over my head, then said: \"O Unays, the Muslims will build cities after me. Among the cities they will build is one called al-Basrah. If you enter it, beware of its flood, its market, and the gate of its ruler, for there will occur in it sinking, metamorphosis, and pelting. The sign of that time is that justice will die, oppression will spread, adultery will increase, and false testimony will become widespread.\""],[6083,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman walking in front of the funeral procession."],[6084,"It was said to Ibn Umar: \"You pray on your mount when you head toward Makkah, so why do you do that when you return to Madinah?\" He said: \"If I had not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it, I would not do it.\""],[6085,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fed Khadijah grapes from Paradise."],[6086,"The Prophet ﷺ married his maternal aunt Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[6087,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped his head once."],[6088,"We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and we continued praying two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, until we returned."],[6089,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting: \"And by the male and the female.\""],[6090,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[6091,"The child is a master for seven years, a servant for seven years, and a minister for seven years. If you are satisfied with his assistance by twenty-one, then fine; otherwise, strike his side, for you have excused yourself before Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[6092,"Jacob ﷺ had a brother with whom he was bound in friendship. One day the brother said to him: \"O Jacob, what took away your eyesight and what bent your back?\" He said: \"As for what took away my eyesight, it was weeping over Joseph. As for what bent my back, it was grief over Benjamin.\" Then Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: \"O Jacob, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends you greetings of peace and says to you: 'Are you not ashamed to complain of Me to someone other than Me?'\" Jacob said: \"I only complain of my anguish and grief to Allah.\" Gabriel said: \"Allah knows best what you complain of, O Jacob.\" Then Jacob said: \"O Lord, will You not have mercy on the old man? You took away my eyesight and bent my back. Return to me Joseph, my sweet basil, that I may smell him once before death. Then do with me, O Lord, as You will.\" Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: \"O Jacob, Allah sends you greetings of peace and says to you: 'Rejoice and let your heart be glad. By My might, if they were both dead I would resurrect them for you. Prepare food for the poor, for the most beloved of My servants to Me are the poor. Do you know why I took away your eyesight and bent your back, and why Joseph's brothers did what they did to him? Because you slaughtered a sheep, and a fasting poor man came to you, but you did not feed him any of it.'\" After that, whenever Jacob's midday meal came, he would order a caller to proclaim: \"Whoever among the poor wants the midday meal, let him eat with Jacob.\" And if he was fasting, he would order a caller to proclaim: \"Whoever among the poor is fasting, let him break his fast with Jacob.\""],[6093,"Blessed is the one who saw me, and the one who saw the one who saw me, and the one who saw the one who saw the one who saw me\" three times."],[6094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn Sayyad: \"I have hidden something for you.\" He said: \"It is al-dukhkh.\" He said: \"Scram!\""],[6095,"We used to pray with the Messenger of God ﷺ on Friday, and the walls had no shade to be used for shelter."],[6096,"Your Prophet ﷺ was commanded fifty prayers, so he asked his Lord to make them five prayers."],[6097,"He was sitting while two sheep were fighting, and one of them butted the other and caused it to miscarry. The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed. It was said to him: What makes you laugh? He said: I wonder at it. By the One in whose hand is my soul, it will surely be avenged for on the Day of Resurrection."],[6098,"I persisted in it for more than two years, performing a full bath every Friday night, praying two rak'ahs in which I recited 'Say: He is God, the One' a thousand times, out of longing to see the Prophet ﷺ in a dream. Then one Friday night I prayed two rak'ahs and recited in them 'Say: He is God, the One' a thousand times. When I lay down, I had a seminal emission, so I got up, performed a full bath, and prayed two rak'ahs in which I recited 'Say: He is God, the One' a thousand times. When I finished them, it was the time of predawn. I leaned against the wall with my face toward the qiblah. Then the Prophet ﷺ entered upon me in his described form and attributes, wearing two cloaks of these Yemeni cloaks, having wrapped one around his waist and thrown the other over his shoulder. He came and stood on his left leg, keeping the right one raised. Muhammad b. 'Ukkasha said: I wanted to say, 'May God greet you,' but he preceded me and said, 'May God greet you.' I had been longing to see his broken front tooth, so the Messenger of God ﷺ smiled, and I looked at his broken front tooth. I said: O Messenger of God, the jurists have confused me, and I have two fundamental principles of the Sunnah. May I present them to you? He said: Yes. I said: Acceptance of God's decree, submission to God's command, patience with His ruling, taking what God has commanded, refraining from what God has forbidden, sincere devotion in action for God, faith in destiny, its good and its evil from God, abandoning disputation and quarrels in religion, wiping over the leather socks, waging jihad with every caliph, performing the Friday prayer with every righteous and wicked person, praying over whoever dies from among the people of the qiblah, faith being statement and action that increases and decreases, the Quran being the speech of God uncreated, patience under the banner of the ruler whether he is just or unjust, not revolting against rulers with the sword even if they are unjust, not assigning any of the people of the qiblah to Paradise or Hell, not declaring any of the people of monotheism an unbeliever even if they commit major sins, refraining from speaking ill of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the best of people after the Messenger of God ﷺ being Abu Bakr, then 'Umar. Muhammad b. 'Ukkasha said: I paused at 'Uthman and 'Ali, for I held the Prophet ﷺ in too much awe to prefer 'Uthman over 'Ali. I said to myself: 'Ali is his cousin, and 'Uthman is his son-in-law. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled as if he knew, then said: 'Uthman, then 'Ali. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: This is the Sunnah; hold fast to it. He clasped his fingers and made a count of ninety-three, pressing his thumb over his fingers. Muhammad b. 'Ukkasha said: I presented these principles to him for three nights; each night I would pause at 'Ali and 'Uthman, and he would smile when I paused, as if he knew ﷺ, then he would say: 'Uthman, then 'Ali; hold fast to it. Muhammad b. 'Ukkasha said: I was presenting these principles to him while his eyes were streaming with tears. When I said, 'And refraining from speaking ill of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ,' he sobbed until his voice rose ﷺ. Muhammad b. 'Ukkasha said: After my vision I found a sweetness in my mouth and heart, so for eight days I did not eat any food until I became too weak to perform the obligatory prayer. When I ate food, that sweetness left my mouth."],[6099,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cut off for a shield whose value was three dirhams."],[6100,"Regarding the statement of God, Mighty and Majestic: 'None knows them except a few,' Ibn 'Abbas said: I am among those few: Maksamlitha, Tamlikha - and he is the one sent with the silver coins to the city - Martulas, Yathbunus, Dhartunus, Kafashtitiyus, Mantunawasisus - and he is the shepherd - and the dog's name is Qitmir, below the Kurdish dog and above the Egyptian dog; I do not think above the Egyptian dog."],[6101,"Whoever visits the grave of his parents or one of them every Friday will be forgiven, and will be recorded as dutiful."],[6102,"A man said: O Messenger of God, is there any supplication that is not rejected? He said: Yes, say: I ask You by Your name, the Most High, the Most Mighty, the Most Glorious, the Most Generous."],[6103,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me when he married me to his other daughter: If I had ten, I would marry you to them one after another, for I am pleased with you."],[6104,"Seek good from those with handsome faces."],[6105,"He saw a person afflicted with a trial, so he said: Perhaps you asked Him to hasten the trial for you. He said: Yes. He said: Why did you not ask God for well-being and say: O God, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire?"],[6106,"The Prophet ﷺ gathered the Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib and said to them: If any of you is afflicted by anxiety, grief, distress, illness, or hardship, let him say: God is my Lord; I do not associate anything with Him, three times. He said: And that was the last speech of 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz at death."],[6107,"Abstention from the world brings rest to the heart and the body."],[6108,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would greet to his right until the whiteness of his right cheek could be seen: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” and to his left likewise."],[6109,"The woman has no sanctity except in her face."],[6110,"I am amazed at the believer: if good befalls him, he praises Allah and gives thanks; and if a calamity befalls him, he praises his Lord and remains patient. Thus the believer is rewarded in every situation, even in a morsel he lifts to his mouth."],[6111,"From this mountain pass there will come to you the best of a man of Yemen, on whose face is the touch of an angel. He said: There was not a man among the people but wished that he might be from him, when a rider appeared before them. He came up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, dismounted from his camel, came to the Prophet ﷺ, took his hand, greeted him, pledged allegiance, and migrated. He said: “Who are you?” He said: “I am Jarir b. ʿAbd Allah al-Bajali.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated him beside him, and passed his hand over his head, face, chest, and belly, until Jarir bent over out of modesty lest his hand go under his waist-wrapper, while he prayed for blessing for him and his offspring. Then he wiped his head and back, praying for him."],[6112,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: “I am the best of people for the worst of my community.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, how are you for the best of them?” He said: “As for the best of my community, they will enter Paradise by their deeds; and as for the worst of them, they will enter Paradise by my intercession.”"],[6113,"The Banu Murrah b. ʿUbayd sent me with the zakat of their wealth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I arrived in Madinah and found him sitting among the Muhajirun and the Ansar. I came to him with camels that looked like the roots of the arta tree. He said: “Who is the man?” I said: “ʿIkrash b. Dhuʾayb.” He said: “Raise in lineage.” I said: “Son of Ḥurquṣ b. Jaʿdah b. ʿAmr b. al-Nazzal b. Murrah b. ʿUbayd. These are the zakat of Banu Murrah b. ʿUbayd.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, then said: “These are the camels of my people, these are the zakat of my people.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that they be branded with the branding iron of the zakat camels and added to them. Then he took my hand and went with me to the dwelling of Umm Salamah, and said: “Is there any food?” A large bowl of tharid and meat was brought to us, and we began to eat from it. I started to roam my hand around its sides, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took my right hand with his left hand and said: “O ʿIkrash, eat from one place, for it is one food.” Then a dish was brought to us with various kinds of fresh dates. I began to eat from in front of me, and the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ roamed in the dish. Then he said: “O ʿIkrash, eat from wherever you wish, for it is not one food.” Then water was brought to us, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ washed his hands, then wiped his face, forearms, and head with the wetness of his palms. Then he said: “O ʿIkrash, this is how ablution is done after eating what fire has changed.”"],[6114,"I witnessed Qays b. ʿAsim while he was giving his last instructions. He gathered his sons, and they were thirty-two males, and said: “O my sons, when I die, appoint your eldest as your leader, and you will succeed your father. Do not appoint your youngest, lest that bring you low in the eyes of your peers. Do not set up a wailing woman over me, for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid wailing. Attend to improving wealth, for it ennobles the generous and makes one independent of the vile. Give the necks of the camels only in their due right, and do not withhold them from their right. Beware of every vein of evil, for whatever day pleases you, what displeases you is more. Beware of the sons of your enemies, for they are enemies to you on the path of their fathers. When I die, bury me in a place where the people of this quarter of Bakr b. Waʾil cannot see me, for there were scratches between me and them in the pre-Islamic era, and I fear they might dig me up from my grave, and you would spoil their worldly life, and they would spoil your hereafter.” Then he called for his quiver and ordered his eldest son, who was named ʿAli, and said: “Take out an arrow from my quiver.” He took it out, and he said: “Break it.” He broke it. Then he said: “Take out two arrows.” He took them out, and he said: “Break them.” He broke them. He said: “Take out three arrows.” He took them out, and he said: “Bind them with a bowstring.” He bound them. Then he said: “Break them.” He could not break them. So he said: “O my sons, thus are you in unity, and thus are you in division.” Then he began to recite: “Glory is only what the truthful father built, and the offspring revived his deeds. Glory suffices, along with courage and forbearance, when chastity and generosity adorn them. And thirty, O my sons, when they are bound by covenants for calamities, are like thirty arrows when a strong binding for provision ties them: they do not break. But if the arrows scatter, dispersal destroys their gathering. The elders and those of manly virtue are more deserving, if their like are to be made leaders. Upon them is the care of the young until the youngest reaches the age of accountability, striving.”"],[6115,"A camel is for seven, and a cow is for seven, in sacrificial animals."],[6116,"Whoever sleeps through a prayer or forgets it, let him pray it when he remembers it. Then he recited: “And establish prayer for My remembrance.”"],[6117,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying: “Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah.” He said: “Have you performed Hajj for yourself?” He said: “No.” He said: “Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.”"],[6118,"The worst usury is one of you stretching his tongue against the honor of his Muslim brother."],[6119,"When he looked at the House, he would say: “O Allah, increase this House of Yours in honor, veneration, reverence, righteousness, and awe, and increase those who honor it and venerate it—those who perform Hajj or ‘Umrah—in veneration, honor, reverence, righteousness, and awe.”"],[6120,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, deeds will be brought in sealed scrolls. Then the Blessed and Exalted will say: “Accept this and leave that.” The angels will say: “By Your might, we wrote nothing except what he did.” He will say: “You have spoken the truth, but his deed was for other than My sake, and today I accept only what was for My sake.”"],[6121,"Every newborn is born upon the fitrah."],[6122,"The first thing placed in a servant’s scale is his spending on his family."],[6123,"A safeguard for my community from drowning when they board ships or the sea is that they say: “In the name of Allah, the King. They have not appraised Allah with true appraisal, while the earth entirely will be in His grip on the Day of Resurrection and the heavens folded in His right hand. Glorified is He and Exalted above what they associate. In the name of Allah is its course and its mooring. Indeed, my Lord is Forgiving and Merciful.”"],[6124,"Indeed, among the things that make Allah’s mercy incumbent are three: when a person sees a right from the rights of Allah, he does not postpone it to days he may not reach; that he performs righteous deeds openly based on a foundation of his deeds in secret; and that he combines with what he does the rectitude of what he hopes for.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Thus is the friend of Allah,” and he counted thirty with his hand."],[6125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never delivered a sermon to us except that he commanded us to give charity and forbade us from mutilation."],[6126,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."],[6127,"A minor retains the right of preemption until he reaches maturity. When he reaches maturity, if he wishes he may take it, and if he wishes he may leave it."],[6128,"He forbade leasing land except for gold or silver."],[6129,"In the last days there will be young in age, foolish in intellect. They will speak the best words of people, but they will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through its target. They are the worst of creation and creatures. Glad tidings to the one who kills them or whom they kill."],[6130,"Faith is a restraint against assassination."],[6131,"People will come from the east, reciting the Quran, but it will not pass beyond their throats. They will scatter it as dates fall from the palm. They will depart from the religion, then not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch. Shaving the head will be widespread among them."],[6132,"The best of you is the one who is best to his family."],[6133,"The Prophet ﷺ sprinkled water on the grave of his son Ibrahim."],[6134,"When Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ arrived from Yemen, the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'With what did you enter ihram?' He said: 'With the same as the Prophet ﷺ.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Were it not that I have a sacrificial animal with me, I would have exited ihram.'"],[6135,"Part of the honor my Lord bestowed upon me is that I was born circumcised, and no one ever saw my private parts."],[6136,"When Anas narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and finished, he would say: 'Or as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.'"],[6137,"I entered Paradise and heard a rustling sound before me. I said: 'O Jibril, what is this rustling?' He said: 'Bilal walking ahead of you.'"],[6138,"Use ithmid (antimony) at bedtime, for it clears the eyesight and makes the hair grow."],[6139,"Whoever conceals a private fault, it is as if he brought back to life a girl buried alive from her grave."],[6140,"There will be trials in which the believer will not be able to change anything with his hand or his tongue. Ali b. Abi Talib said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will that diminish their faith?' He said: 'No, except as a drop diminishes a water skin.' He said: 'And why is that?' He said: 'They detest it in their hearts.'"],[6141,"Whoever comes to his home and is attacked for an injustice, then fights and is killed, he is killed as a martyr. And whoever is asked for charity and gives, then is attacked, then fights and is killed, he is killed as a martyr."],[6142,"Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from ill-gotten gains."],[6143,"Whoever Allah takes away his sight and he is patient and seeks reward, it is incumbent upon Allah, as an obligation, that his eyes will never see the Fire."],[6144,"Whoever recites the surah in which the family of 'Imran is mentioned on Friday, Allah and His angels send blessings upon him until the sun sets."],[6145,"We were sitting around Mu'awiya's bed, and he said: What were you talking about? They said: We were discussing one of the reports about the Ansar. He said: Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."],[6146,"The worst of lies is that a man claims to belong to other than his father, or lies about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or lies about his own eyes."],[6147,"Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or give it to his brother."],[6148,"In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan; none will enter it on the Day of Resurrection except those who fast."],[6149,"When he broke his fast with a household, he said: May the fasting break their fast with you, may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you."],[6150,"Two blessings about which many people are deceived: health and free time."],[6151,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying with his garment hanging down, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came close to him and folded his garment back over him."],[6152,"No Muslim goes out in the path of Allah, as a fighter or a pilgrim, raising his voice in talbiya, except that the sun sets with his sins and he comes out of them."],[6153,"Allah is not worshipped with anything better than understanding in religion. One jurist is harder on Satan than a thousand worshippers. Everything has a pillar, and the pillar of this religion is fiqh."],[6154,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even if it is like a sandgrouse's nest, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."],[6155,"A man will enter Paradise; no household or chamber will remain without saying, \"Welcome, welcome, welcome to us.\" Abu Bakr ؓ said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of this man on this day?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, and you are he, O Abu Bakr.\""],[6156,"There is no marriage without a guardian."],[6157,"The one who remembers Allah in Ramadan is forgiven, and the one who asks Allah in it is not disappointed."],[6158,"Whoever remembers Allah and his eyes overflow from fear of Allah until some of his tears fall to the ground, Allah will not punish him on the Day of Resurrection."],[6159,"Whoever had a prayer during the night but his eyes overcame him, Allah writes for him the reward of that night, and his sleep was a charity from Allah."],[6160,"The angels said, \"O our Lord, You have given the children of Adam so they eat, drink, ride, and wear clothes, while we glorify You with praise and do not eat, drink, or play. So as You made the world for them, make the Hereafter for us.\" He said, \"I will not make the offspring of the one I created with My two hands like the one to whom I said, 'Be,' and he was.\""],[6161,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I want to ask you about a matter about which I will not ask anyone after you: Who is our father?\" He said, \"Adam.\" He said, \"Who is our mother?\" He said, \"Eve.\" He said, \"Who is the father of the jinn?\" He said, \"Iblis.\" He said, \"Who is their mother?\" He said, \"His wife.\""],[6162,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade mut'ah with women."],[6163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit the House every night of the nights of Mina, then perform tawaf and pray two rak'ahs for his tawaf, and return to Mina before dawn overtook him."],[6164,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, is there jihad upon us?\" He said, \"Yes, your jihad is this House.\""],[6165,"\"O assembly of the Ansar, who is your leader?\" They said, \"Jadd b. Qays, though we consider him miserly.\" He said, \"He is not your leader; rather, your leader is 'Amr b. al-Jamuh,\" and he was generous."],[6166,"We bought a sacrificial animal, and a wolf attacked it and cut off part of it. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about that, and he said, \"No harm upon you; sacrifice it.\""],[6167,"Among the supplications of Dawud the Prophet ﷺ was: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from wealth that becomes a trial for me, from a child who becomes a burden upon me, from an evil wife who brings on old age before its time, and I seek refuge in You from an evil neighbor whose eyes watch me and whose ears listen to me; if he sees a good deed, he buries it, and if he sees an evil deed, he spreads it."],[6168,"The Prophet ﷺ married while he was in a state of ihram."],[6169,"While we were sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a woman passed by. Some of the people said, “This is the daughter of Muhammad.” Abu Sufyan said, “The example of Muhammad among the Banu Hashim is like a fragrant herb in the midst of stench,” or he said, “straw.” The woman went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He came out with anger recognizable on his face and said, “What is the matter with people who harm me concerning my family?” Then he said, “Allah created the seven heavens and chose the highest one, so He dwelt therein, and He settled the rest of His heavens with whomever He willed of His creation. And He created the seven earths and chose the highest one, and He settled therein whomever He willed of His creation. Then He created creation, and He chose from creation the Children of Adam, and He chose from the Children of Adam the Arabs, and He chose from the Arabs Mudar, and He chose from Mudar Quraysh, and He chose from Quraysh the Banu Hashim, and He chose me from the Banu Hashim. Thus I am from the best to the best. Whoever loves the Arabs, it is out of love for me that he honors them; and whoever hates the Arabs, it is out of hatred for me that he hates them.”"],[6170,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wear a white cap."],[6171,"Learn knowledge, and learn for knowledge calmness and dignity, and be humble toward those from whom you learn."],[6172,"Love your beloved moderately, for he may become your enemy one day; and hate your enemy moderately, for he may become your beloved one day."],[6173,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Hudaybiyyah, and that night we were rained upon with a heavy rain. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you know what your Lord said?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He repeated this three times, and they repeated their answer. Then he said, “Your Lord said: Whoever says, ‘We were given rain by such-and-such a star’ has disbelieved in Me and believed in that star. And whoever says, ‘Allah gave us water’ has believed in Me and disbelieved in that star.”"],[6174,"We were sitting with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq when a funeral procession passed by. He stood up, so we stood up. Then we prayed, and he removed his sandals. We said, “O successor of the Messenger of Allah, you removed your sandals while the people are putting on their sandals.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever walks barefoot in obedience to Allah, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will not ask him on the Day of Resurrection about what He has obligated upon him.”"],[6175,"Whoever does not show mercy to the Muslims, Allah will not show mercy to him."],[6176,"Seek refuge in Allah from the pit of sorrow.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is the pit of sorrow?” He said, “A valley in Hell from which Hell itself seeks refuge with Allah from its evil four hundred times every day. Those who are thrown into it are the deceivers.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, who are the deceivers?” He said, “Those who show off their deeds in the world.”"],[6177,"What a bad food is the food of a wedding feast: the one who is full is invited to it, while the hungry one is kept away from it."],[6178,"Whoever prays over a funeral receives a qirat of reward, and whoever prays over it or walks in it until it is buried receives two qirats, and the qirat is like Mount Uhud."],[6179,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas: Which charity is best? He said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, I said: Which charity is best? He said: \"Water.\" I said: O Prophet of God, which charity is best? He said: \"Water. Do you not see that the people of the Fire, when they call for help from the people of Paradise, they cry out: 'Pour upon us some water or whatever God has provided you?'\""],[6180,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to hasten in the bottom of the valley between al-Safa and al-Marwa."],[6181,"We used to place the vessel for the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would pour water over his hand and wash it until he cleaned it thoroughly, then he would pour with his right hand over his left, and wash his private part, then he would pour over his head three times, then bathe."],[6182,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to propose to a woman, he would send Umm Sulaym to look at her, and she would smell her sides and look at her heels."],[6183,"If one of you eats or drinks out of forgetfulness, let him complete his fast, for it is only God who has fed him and given him drink."],[6184,"Al-Hasan or al-Husayn urinated on the Prophet's belly, so they went to take him away, but the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not interrupt my son,\" or \"Do not rush him.\" So they left him until he finished urinating, then he called for water and poured it over it."],[6185,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a bride on his first arrival in Madinah, and with her were women, and one of them was saying: \"And he gifted her rams that are comfortable in the enclosure, and your husband is in the gathering and knows what tomorrow brings.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not say that, but say: 'We have come to you, we have come to you, so greet us and we greet you.'\""],[6186,"Whoever has three daughters and supports them, shelters them, and restrains them, Paradise is assured for him. We said: And two? He said: \"And two.\" We said: And one? He said: \"And one.\""],[6187,"There is no Muslim person who prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night except that God builds a house for him in Paradise."],[6188,"Two phrases I memorized from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I would love for you to memorize them: God does not punish for a sin in this world, for God is more just than to repeat his punishment; and God does not forgive a sin in this world, for God is more generous than to return to something He has forgiven. And a cover between you and the jinn: 'In the name of God.'"],[6189,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married me and consummated the marriage with me in Shawwal."],[6190,"I agreed with my Lord in three things, and He agreed with me in three. I said: O Messenger of God, this is the standing place of our father Ibrahim; if only we took it as a place of prayer. Then God, mighty and majestic, revealed: 'And take the standing place of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.'"],[6191,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'What do you think of the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: \"As We sent down upon the muqtasimīn\"—who are the muqtasimīn?' He said: 'The Jews and the Christians.' He said: 'Those who made the Qur'an into ʿiḍīn—what are ʿiḍīn?' He said: 'They believed in some of it and disbelieved in some of it.'"],[6192,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: 'Which of the people has the most beautiful voice in [reciting] the Qur'an?' He said: 'One who, when he recites, you see that he fears Allah.'"],[6193,"We were seven in a house, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to us and said: 'The last of you to die will be in the Fire.' None remained except me and Samurah."],[6194,"Some people from Kufa spoke against Saʿd in the presence of ʿUmar, saying: 'He does not perform the prayer well.' ʿUmar said: 'Call Abū Isḥāq for me.' When he came, ʿUmar said: 'These people claim that you do not perform the prayer well.' He said: 'As for me, I lead them in prayer with the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, not omitting anything from it. I prolong the first two rakʿahs and shorten the last two.' ʿUmar said: 'That is what is expected of you, O Abū Isḥāq.'"],[6195,"I was among those concerning whom Saʿd b. Muʿādh gave judgment. He looked at my pubic area and found that it had not grown hair, so he set me free."],[6196,"Let food cool down, for hot food is devoid of blessing."],[6197,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in his dwelling and saw a man with disheveled hair. He said: 'Could this man not find something with which to wash his garment and tidy his disheveled hair?'"],[6198,"I was with my paternal uncle in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon. He said: 'The affair of my community will remain sound until twelve caliphs have passed.' He lowered his voice while saying this, so I said to my uncle, who was in front of me: 'What did he say, O uncle?' He said: 'All of them will be from Quraysh.'"],[6199,"Pardon one another for the prescribed punishments that occur among you. For whatever reaches me, it becomes binding."],[6200,"I heard Maymūn al-Kurdī when he was with Mālik b. Dīnār. Mālik b. Dīnār said to him: 'Why does the shaykh not narrate from his father? Your father met the Prophet ﷺ and heard from him.' He said: 'My father would not narrate to us from the Prophet ﷺ for fear of adding or subtracting. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\" But I will narrate to you from him a hadith that I heard him narrate more than once, twice, or three times. He would say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Any man who marries a woman and on the day he marries her does not intend to give her her dowry, he will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection as an adulterer. And any man who takes a debt not intending to repay it, then dies without repaying it, he will meet Allah, Blessed and Exalted, as a thief.\"'"],[6201,"While I was sitting, Jibrīl ﷺ came and poked me between my shoulders. I stood up to a tree in which there were things like two bird nests. He sat in one of them and I sat in the other. It rose and ascended until it blocked the two horizons. I was turning my gaze, and if I had wished to touch the sky, I would have touched it. I turned and saw Jibrīl ﷺ as if he were a worn-out saddlecloth clinging [to the ground]. Thus I recognized the superiority of his knowledge of Allah over mine. A gate of heaven was opened for me, and I saw the greatest light. A veil was let down before me—a fluttering of pearls and rubies. Then Allah revealed to me what He willed to reveal."],[6202,"Two qualities—no Muslim servant guards them in his day and night except that Allah will admit him to Paradise. They are easy, yet few guard them.' They said: 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'The servant says subḥān Allāh ten times after every prayer, alḥamdulillāh ten times, and lā ilāha illā Allāh ten times. That is one hundred and fifty in his day and night, and with Allah it is one thousand five hundred good deeds. And he says subḥān Allāh thirty-three times, alḥamdulillāh thirty-three times, and Allāhu akbar thirty-four times. That is one hundred, and with Allah it is one thousand good deeds. So that is two thousand five hundred good deeds.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how is it that we do not guard them?' He said: 'When one of you finishes his prayer, Satan comes to him and reminds him of his needs, so he gets up before saying them. When he goes to his bed, Satan comes to him and distracts him from them until he falls asleep.'"],[6203,"In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to call it the Protector, and indeed in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, it is a surah. Whoever recites it every night has done much and done well—meaning: Tabarak."],[6204,"A man from Banu Fazarah argued with me about the man whom Musa followed. He said: I said, 'He is al-Khidr.' The Fazari said, 'He is another man.' Then Ubayy b. Ka'b passed by us. Ibn Abbas said: I called him and asked him, 'Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the one whom Musa ﷺ followed?' He said, 'Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: While Musa was sitting among a company of the Children of Israel, a man said to him, \"Is there any man more knowledgeable about Allah than you?\" He said, \"I do not think so.\" Then Allah reproached him for not referring the matter to Him, and Allah revealed: \"Rather, My servant al-Khidr.\" So he asked for a way to meet him, and Allah made the fish a sign for him when he would lose it, and his affair was as Allah related.'"],[6205,"He used to supplicate with these words: 'O Allah, You are the First, so there is nothing before You, and You are the Last, so there is nothing after You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of every creature whose forelock is in Your hand. I seek refuge in You from sin and laziness, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of wealth and the trial of poverty. I seek refuge in You from wrongdoing and debt. O Allah, purify my heart from sins as You purified the white garment from filth. O Allah, distance between me and my sins as You distanced between the east and the west.' This is what Muhammad asked his Lord: 'O Allah, I ask You for the best of asking, the best of supplication, the best of success, the best of deeds, the best of reward, the best of life, and the best of death. Make me firm, weigh down my scales, raise my degree, accept my prayer, forgive my sin, and I ask You for the highest degrees of Paradise. Amin. O Allah, I ask You for Paradise. Amin. O Allah, I ask You for the best of what is done and the best of what is worked, the best of what is hidden and the best of what is apparent, and the highest degrees of Paradise. Amin. O Allah, I ask You to raise my mention, remove my burden, set right my affair, purify my heart, guard my private parts, illuminate my heart, forgive my sin, and I ask You for the highest degrees of Paradise. Amin. O Allah, save me from the Fire.'"],[6206,"The teacher of good—everything seeks forgiveness for him, even the fish in the seas."],[6207,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[6208,"A man led some people in prayer and spat toward the qiblah while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching. When he finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This man should not lead you in prayer.' Later, the man wanted to lead them again, but they prevented him and informed him of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said. He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said, 'What they did was good.' And I think he said, 'You offended Allah,' or something like that."],[6209,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, 'There is no god but Allah.' When they say, 'There is no god but Allah,' they have protected their wealth and their lives from me, except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[6210,"Snakes—we have not made peace with them since we have been at war with them. Whoever sees any of them, let him kill it, for their Muslims will not appear to you. Whoever leaves any of them out of fear is not from us."],[6211,"Do not combine my name and my kunyah. I am Abu al-Qasim; Allah gives, and I am the distributor."],[6212,"There is no leader of ten but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in chains, until justice releases him or oppression destroys him."],[6213,"Whoever takes a span of land without right will be made to wear it as a collar on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."],[6214,"If someone peeks at you in your house and you throw a pebble at him and put out his eyes, there is no sin upon you."],[6215,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a bed frame woven with palm leaves, over which was a black cloak. We seated him on the palm leaves. Abu Bakr and Umar entered while the Prophet ﷺ was sitting on it. They looked and saw the marks of the bed frame on the side of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Bakr and Umar wept. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, \"What makes you weep?\" They said, \"We weep because the roughness of this bed frame has left marks on your side, while Chosroes and Caesar are on silk and brocade furnishings.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed the end of Chosroes and Caesar is the Fire, and the end of this bed frame of mine is Paradise.\""],[6216,"I came with my mother Qurayra bt. al-Harith al-Utwariyya among women of the Emigrants, and we gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he had a tent pitched at al-Abtah. He took from us that we should not associate anything with Allah—the entire verse. When we affirmed and extended our hands to give him allegiance, the Prophet ﷺ said: \"I do not touch the hands of women.\" So he sought forgiveness for us, and that was our allegiance."],[6217,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about it on the day of Arafah? He said: \"It is true,\" meaning the atirah."],[6218,"Whoever corrupts a slave against his master."],[6219,"A beggar stood before Ali b. Abi Talib while he was bowing in voluntary prayer. He took off his ring and gave it to the beggar. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of that, and this verse was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Your guardian is only Allah, His Messenger, and those who believe—those who establish prayer and give zakah while bowing.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it, then said: \"Whomever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\""],[6220,"Speech about destiny has been deferred for the worst of this nation."],[6221,"When dinner is served and the prayer is called, begin with dinner."],[6222,"A paternal aunt may not be married along with a brother's daughter, nor a maternal aunt along with a sister's daughter."],[6223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while traveling on his mount."],[6224,"We prayed Zuhr with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina, when the people were most numerous and secure—two rak'ahs."],[6225,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: \"Ride it.\""],[6226,"You will be presented, and over your mouths will be the fidam. The first thing to speak from any of you will be his hand and his thigh."],[6227,"When he wanted to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity (junub), he would perform the ablution of prayer, and when he wanted to eat, he would perform ablution."],[6228,"The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ used to learn this supplication when the year or the month began: 'O Allah, bring it upon us with security and faith, safety and Islam, and pleasure from the Most Merciful, and protection from Satan.'"],[6229,"Islam will spread until the traders differ in the sea, and until the horses plunge in the path of Allah. Then a people will appear who recite the Qur'an, saying: 'Who recites better than us? Who has more understanding than us? Who is more knowledgeable than us?' Then he said to his Companions: 'Is there any good in those?' They said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'Those are from you, from this nation, and those are the fuel of the Fire.'"],[6230,"Indeed, your Lord has, in the days of time, fragrant breezes, so expose yourselves to them. Perhaps one of you may be touched by a breeze and never be miserable after it, ever."],[6231,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered al-Fadl b. Abbas to prepare water for his purification. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went off to relieve himself. When he needed to relieve himself, he would go far away until he was almost hidden from view. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished relieving himself, he came back and passed by a woman at the grave of her deceased, while she was wailing and lamenting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood over her while she did not recognize him, and he said to her: 'Fear Allah and be patient.' She said: 'O servant of Allah, go about your business.' He said it to her three times, then he left. He came and took the water container from al-Fadl. Al-Fadl got up and went to the woman and said to her: 'What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you?' She stood up and said: 'Woe to her! This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I did not recognize him.' She hurried until she caught up with him at the door of the mosque and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I did not recognize you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'Patience is only at the first shock.' He said it three times."],[6232,"Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought Hasan and Husayn to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his final illness. She said: 'These are your two sons, so give them an inheritance.' He said to her: 'As for Hasan, he has my composure and my dignity; as for Husayn, he has my courage and my generosity.'"],[6233,"A man asked Abdullah b. Umar, saying: 'My maternal uncle divorced his wife, and he became distressed and grieved about that. I want to marry her, but he did not instruct me to do so, and he does not know about it.' Ibn Umar said: 'No, unless you marry her in a desired marriage. If she suits you, you keep her; if you dislike it, you divorce her. Otherwise, we used to consider this in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as fornication.'"],[6234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a child who had an amulet hung on him. He said: 'Why do you hang things on your children? You should use costus, which is dissolved in water and then given as a nasal drop.'"],[6235,"Fever was cursed one day in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not curse it, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, it removes the sins of the believer just as the bellows removes the dross of iron.'"],[6236,"Neither one suckling nor two sucklings make (marriage) forbidden."],[6237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and addressed the people on the pulpit in Ramadan, saying: 'I have stood on this pulpit while I know the Night of Decree. So seek it in the last ten nights, on the odd nights.'"],[6238,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ promised her that she would pray in the House, and he instructed her to pray in the Hijr. She said: 'You promised me that I would pray in the House.' He said: 'It is part of the House. Were it not that your people are recently out of polytheism, I would have attached it to the House.'"],[6239,"You will be sifted until you become among the dregs of people. Their covenants have become corrupted, and their trusts have been ruined.\" One of us said, \"What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"You should act upon what you know and abandon what you disapprove of, and say: 'Ahad, Ahad (One, One). Help us against those who wrong us, and suffice us against those who transgress against us.\""],[6240,"I saw Uthman b. Affan perform ablution and run his fingers through his beard, then he said, \"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and run his fingers through his beard.\""],[6241,"Faith is knowledge in the heart, affirmation by the tongue, and action by the limbs."],[6242,"The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: Labbayka ilaha al-haqq (Here I am, O God of Truth)."],[6243,"I entered upon Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and found the Prophet ﷺ praying in a single garment, having tied it at the back of his neck. I said to Umm Habibah, \"Does the Prophet ﷺ pray in a single garment?\" She said, \"Yes, and it was the one in which there had been what there had been.\""],[6244,"We used to say that attending the 'atamah (night prayer) is better than standing in prayer for half the night, and attending the morning prayer is better than standing in prayer for a whole night."],[6245,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Maghrib at Muzdalifah. When he made his camel kneel, he said, \"Prayer with an iqamah.\""],[6246,"There will come at the end of time people whose faces will be like the faces of humans, but their hearts like the hearts of devils, like ravenous wolves. There will be no mercy in their hearts. They will shed blood and will not refrain from evil. If you follow them, they will deceive you; if you stay away from them, they will backbite you; if they speak to you, they will lie to you; if you trust them, they will betray you. Their children will be wicked, their youths shameless, and their elders will not enjoin good nor forbid evil. Seeking honor through them is humiliation, and seeking what they possess is poverty. The forbearing among them will be led astray, the one who enjoins good among them will be accused, the believer among them will be oppressed, and the sinner among them will be honored. The Sunnah among them will be considered innovation, and innovation among them will be considered Sunnah. At that time, Allah will set their worst ones over them, and their best ones will supplicate but will not be answered."],[6247,"He was in a house, and a man looked into his house, so he reached for an arrow and aimed it at him, so the man stepped back."],[6248,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: \"You must hear and obey in what you like or dislike, unless you are commanded to disobey, for there is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah.\""],[6249,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Abu Bakr and Umar appeared. He said, \"Praise be to Allah who has supported me with them.\""],[6250,"Had it not been for what the Corner has been stamped with from the impurities of the Jahiliyyah and its filths, and the hands of the wrongdoers and sinners, those with ailments would have sought healing from it."],[6251,"Islam is built upon the testimony that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fast of Ramadan. It was said to him: 'The fast of Ramadan and the pilgrimage to the House?' He said: 'No, not except thus he said.'"],[6252,"If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend."],[6253,"Umar said to Asma': 'We have preceded you in emigration.' She said: 'By Allah, you have indeed preceded us in emigration. We were among the naked and barefoot, while you were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who taught your ignorant and your knowledgeable, and commanded you to noble character.' And she said: 'I will surely go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and inform him.' He said: 'The people have one emigration, but you have two emigrations.'"],[6254,"Perhaps the counter counted for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a single sitting: 'Forgive me and accept my repentance; You are the Accepting of Repentance, the Most Forgiving' one hundred times."],[6255,"I asked Ibn Umar about the sacrificial animal, whether it is obligatory. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah offered sacrifice, and the Muslims after him.'"],[6256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about donkeys. He said: 'Nothing has come regarding them except this unique, comprehensive verse: \"So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it\" (Quran 99:7-8).'"],[6257,"There is no zakah on horses or slaves, except that on slaves there is the sadaqah of fitr."],[6258,"The least punished of the people of the Fire is the one who has two sandals of fire from which his brain boils."],[6259,"Do not compel your sick to eat or drink, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink."],[6260,"A man may attain through forbearance the rank of one who fasts and prays at night, and a man may be recorded as a tyrant while he controls only his own household."],[6261,"I asked Aisha ؓ about a man who wants to enter ihram and applies perfume. She said: 'Apply the best perfume you can, and it is as if I am looking at the gleam of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in ihram.'"],[6262,"Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seventy autumns."],[6263,"There was a day of the year when the wives of the Prophet ﷺ gathered with him, one day until nightfall. She said: On that day he said: 'The quickest of you to join me will be the longest of you in arm.' She said: So we began measuring among ourselves which of us had the longest arms. She said: Sawdah had the longest arms. When Zaynab died, we knew that she had been the longest of them in arm in goodness and charity. She said: Zaynab used to spin yarn and give it to the Prophet's ﷺ expeditions, and they would sew with it and use it in their campaigns. She said: On that day he said: 'What about one of you when the dogs of al-Haw'ab bark at her?'"],[6264,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled regarding the eggs of an ostrich that a pilgrim in ihram damages: their value."],[6265,"The two-faced one in this world will come on the Day of Resurrection with two faces of fire."],[6266,"Two hungry wolves in a sheepfold are not quicker in causing corruption than the pursuit of wealth and status in the religion of a Muslim man."],[6267,"Whenever she heard someone reciting 'By those sent forth in succession' (al-Mursalat), she would say: The Prophet ﷺ recited al-Mursalat in the Maghrib prayer, then he did not lead us in Isha prayer until Allah took him."],[6268,"Uthman b. Affan came when he equipped the army of hardship with a thousand dinars, and he poured them into the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. Abd al-Rahman said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ turning them over with his hand and saying: 'Nothing will harm Ibn Affan after what he has done today.'"],[6269,"Allah loves that His concessions be taken, just as He loves that His firm commands be taken. I said: And what are His firm commands? He said: 'His obligations.'"],[6270,"A servant may reach, through good character, the degree of one who fasts and stands in prayer, and I think he said: the one who strives in the path of Allah."],[6271,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he accepted her pledge on the condition that she would not commit adultery, steal, or bury her daughters alive, whether openly or secretly. I said: 'As for open infanticide, I know it, but as for secret infanticide, I did not ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not tell me, but it occurred to me that it is the corruption of the child. By Allah, I will never corrupt a child of mine.'"],[6272,"From Jibril ﷺ who said: I turned over the easts of the earth and its wests, and I did not find a man more excellent than Muhammad ﷺ, nor did I see a house more excellent than the house of Banu Hashim."],[6273,"I spent a night with the Prophet ﷺ, and I saw a figure with him. He said: 'Did you see him, O Hudhayfah?' I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'This is an angel who has not descended to me since I was sent. He came to me tonight and gave me the good news that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.'"],[6274,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ passed by Hassan b. Thabit while he was in the mosque reciting poetry. Umar ؓ said to him: 'Here?' Hassan said to him: 'Yes, I recited it to one better than you.' Then Hassan turned to Abu Hurayrah and said: 'I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Hurayrah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Respond on my behalf; O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit\"?' Abu Hurayrah said: 'O Allah, yes.' So Umar fell silent and went on."],[6275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution washing each part once, and said: \"This is the ablution of one without which Allah does not accept his prayer.\" Then he performed ablution washing each part twice, and said: \"Whoever performs ablution like this, Allah will double his reward twice.\" Then he performed ablution washing each part three times, and said: \"This is the complete ablution, and this is my ablution and the ablution of Allah's intimate friend Ibrahim ﷺ . Whoever performs ablution like this, then says upon finishing: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, Allah will open for him eight gates of Paradise; he may enter from whichever he wishes.\""],[6276,"Accept gifts, and the best of gifts is perfume: the lightest to carry and the sweetest in scent."],[6277,"When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, I came to him and he said to me: \"O Jarir, for what purpose have you come to us?\" I said: \"To embrace Islam at your hands, O Messenger of Allah.\" So he threw his cloak to me, then turned to his companions and said: \"If a nobleman of a people comes to you, honor him.\""],[6278,"Whoever persistently seeks forgiveness, Allah will grant him relief from every worry, a way out from every distress, and provide for him from where he does not expect."],[6279,"When he wanted to relieve himself, he would go far away."],[6280,"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness."],[6281,"The first of the emigrants to arrive in Madinah was Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, and he was the first to lead the Friday prayer there. He gathered them for prayer before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived and led them in prayer."],[6282,"Remain chaste and your women will remain chaste. Honor your fathers and your sons will honor you. Whoever is apologized to by his Muslim brother for something that reached him about him, and he does not accept his excuse, he will not come to me at the pond (of al-Kawthar)."],[6283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day to his companions while I was present: \"If one of you owned this pillar, he would dislike it being cut down. How then could one of you deliberately cut short his prayer, which belongs to Allah? So complete your prayers, for Allah does not accept anything but the complete.\""],[6284,"Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: \"Convey greetings to 'Umar, and tell him that his approval is a judgment and his anger is a source of strength.\""],[6285,"A man had anal intercourse with a woman during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and the people disapproved of that. Then Allah revealed: \"Your wives are a tilth for you.\""],[6286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the people of the Suffah when their voices had risen and they had burst into loud laughter. That angered him, and he said: \"You were not created for laughter,\" and he rebuked them for that. Then Jibril ﷺ came to him from Allah, whose remembrance is exalted, and said: \"Allah commands you to make things easy and not difficult, and to give good tidings and not drive people away.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to them, gave them good tidings, and interacted with them kindly, and opened up to them."],[6287,"When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, a caller will call out: \"O people of Paradise, eternity without death therein! And O people of the Fire, eternity without death therein!\""],[6288,"Kill the gecko, even if it is in the interior of the Kaʿbah."],[6289,"Whoever reaches ʿArafah before the break of dawn has caught the Hajj."],[6290,"Allah does not conceal a sin for a servant in this world but that He will conceal it for him in the Hereafter."],[6291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: \"They follow that which is ambiguous thereof.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah has warned you. When you see them, know them.\""],[6292,"Allah made His Sacred Precinct inviolable; it is inviolable until the Day of Resurrection. Its trees shall not be cut down, its herbage shall not be uprooted, its lost property shall not be picked up except by one who announces it, and its game shall not be made lawful."],[6293,"Abu ʿUbayd said to him: \"Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, not once, not twice, not thrice: 'When the believing servant performs ablution and rinses his mouth and sniffs water, sins fall away from the corners of his eyes. When he washes his hands, sins fall away from his fingernails. When he washes his feet, sins fall away from his toenails. Then when he finishes that, that is his share of his ablution. If he then stands and prays two rakʿahs, turning with his heart and his gaze to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, he departs from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.'\""],[6294,"I was with ʿAli when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed him over Yemen, and I acquired some ounces along with him. When he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"I found Fatimah had sprinkled the house with perfume, so I stepped over it.\" She said: \"What is the matter with you? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has ordered his companions, and they have exited ihram.\" He said: \"I said to her: 'I entered ihram with the same intention as the Prophet ﷺ.'\" He said: \"'I have driven the sacrificial animal and performed qiran.'\" And he said to his companions: \"'If I had known at the beginning of my affair what I know at its end, I would have done as you have done, but I have driven the sacrificial animal and performed qiran.'\" Then he said: \"'Slaughter sixty-seven or sixty-six of the camels, and keep for yourself thirty-three or thirty-four, and keep a piece from each camel.'\""],[6295,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to ask our permission when it was the day of one of us, after the verse was revealed: \"You may defer whom you will of them and receive whom you will.\" Muʿadhah said: \"I said: 'What would you say?' She said: 'I would say: If that is up to me, I would not prefer anyone over myself.'\""],[6296,"\"I wish the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had given us the call to prayer.\" I said: \"Why that?\" He said: \"They will have the longest necks of the people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6297,"There will come after me rulers over you; the righteous will rule you with his righteousness, and the wicked with his wickedness. Hear and obey them in everything that conforms to the truth, and pray behind them. If they do good, it is for you and for them; if they do evil, it is for you and against them."],[6298,"The pilgrims and those performing ʿumrah are the delegation of Allah. If they call upon Him, He answers them; if they seek His forgiveness, He forgives them."],[6299,"It was forbidden to drink from the mouth of the waterskin."],[6300,"I said: O Messenger of God, my age has grown old and my bones have become thin, so guide me to a deed that will admit me into Paradise. He said: Excellent, excellent! You have asked! Glorify God one hundred times, and that is better for you than one hundred slaves you would set free. Praise God one hundred times, and that is better for you than one hundred saddled and bridled horses you would ride in the way of God. Declare God’s greatness one hundred times, and that is better for you than one hundred garlanded and adorned camels you would send to the House of God Most High. And say: There is no god but God, one hundred times, and that is better for you than all that the heavens and the earth encompass. And on that day no deed will be raised for anyone better than what will be raised for you, except one who says the like of what you said or more."],[6301,"God sends down upon the people of the mosque—the mosque of Makkah—every day one hundred and twenty mercies: sixty of them for those circumambulating, forty for those praying, and twenty for those looking."],[6302,"He was building the mosque, and Ammar b. Yasir was carrying two rocks. He said: Woe to the son of Sumayya! The transgressing party will kill him."],[6303,"The Messenger of God ﷺ seated Husayn on his thigh. Then Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: Is this your son? He said: Yes. He said: Your community will kill him after you. The eyes of the Messenger of God ﷺ shed tears. He said: If you wish, I will show you the soil of the land where he will be killed. He said: Yes. Gabriel brought him some dust from the dust of al-Taff."],[6304,"I lost a donkey of mine, so I went out looking for it at Arafah. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ among them at Arafah, and Abu Bakr ؓ was standing at the standing places of Quraysh."],[6305,"When his father Ubadah b. al-Samit was dying, his son Abdullah said to him: O my father, advise me. He said: Seat me up for my son. They seated him. He said: O my son, fear God. You will never fear God until you believe in God. You will never believe in God until you believe in destiny, its good and its evil, and know that what befalls you would never have missed you, and what misses you would never have befallen you. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Destiny is upon this. Whoever dies upon other than this, God will admit him into the Fire."],[6306,"Reflect upon the favors of God, and do not reflect upon God."],[6307,"One day we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque, and he made food for us, and we ate. Then the prayer was established, and we prayed without performing ablution."],[6308,"A gift of food was given to me and to Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, while we were fasting. One of us said to the other: Would you like to break the fast? She said: Yes. So we broke our fast. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us, and we said: O Messenger of God, a gift was given to us, and we desired it, so we broke our fast. The Prophet ﷺ said: No harm upon you two; fast a day in its place."],[6309,"When Abu Talib died, I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: Your uncle, the old man, has died. He said: Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me. So I buried him, then came to him. He said: Go and perform a full bath, and do not do anything until you come to me. So I performed a full bath, then came to him. He supplicated for me with supplications that I would not trade for red camels."],[6310,"The people of two religions do not inherit from each other in anything."],[6311,"Seven will Allah shade in His shade on the Day when there is no shade but His: a just ruler; a young man who grew up in worship of Allah; two men who loved each other for the sake of Allah, meeting and parting on that; a man whose heart is attached to the mosque, who does not leave it until he returns to it; a man whom a woman of beauty and position invited to herself, and he said, 'I fear Allah'; a man who gave charity and concealed it from his left hand, so that his left hand did not know what his right hand spent; and a man who remembered Allah in solitude and his eyes overflowed."],[6312,"When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right, and when he takes them off, let him begin with the left, or let him put them both on or take them both off."],[6313,"Kill dogs,\" raising his voice with that."],[6314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid selling dates until they were ripe, and he forbade muzabanah."],[6315,"The example of one who flees from death is like the example of a fox that the earth demands for a debt, so it kept running until, when it became tired and out of breath, it entered its burrow, [and the earth said to it, 'O fox, my debt,'] so it came out with a rapid gait, and it kept doing that until its neck broke and it died."],[6316,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was granted permission to pray, and he said: 'Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' Then he fainted, and when he recovered, he said: 'Did you tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer?' We said: 'Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man; if he leads the people in prayer, he will not make them hear. If only you would order 'Umar to lead the people in prayer.' He said: 'Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, for you are like the women of Yusuf. There may be one who says and one who wishes, but Allah and the believers refuse.'"],[6317,"Ibn 'Umar saw a man slaughtering his camel while it was kneeling, so he said: 'Make it stand, for that is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[6318,"Do not precede it—meaning the month of Ramadan—fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it, and if it is obscured to you, then complete thirty."],[6319,"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, it is as if he prayed them in the night; and whoever prays them after 'Isha', they are like the same from the Night of Qadr; and when a Muslim meets a Muslim and takes his hand, and they are sincere, they do not part until they are forgiven."],[6320,"For a man to commit adultery with ten women is lighter for him than to commit adultery with his neighbor's wife, and for him to steal from ten houses is lighter for him than to steal from his neighbor's house."],[6321,"I said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'We were with you, and we left and returned, and we prayed two rak'ahs?' He said: 'That is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ, even if you dislike it.'"],[6322,"O Banu 'Abd Manaf, if you are given authority over worldly affairs, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating the House or praying at any time."],[6323,"A bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in the sands, and among us there is menstruation, major impurity, and postpartum bleeding? He said: You must use the earth."],[6324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in Khaybar for six months, praying Zuhr and Asr together, and Maghrib and Isha together."],[6325,"He is not a liar who says good, or spreads good."],[6326,"The best of you is one who learns the Quran and teaches the Quran."],[6327,"Gabriel ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Your Lord sends you greetings of peace, and sent me to you with this cluster of grapes for you to eat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it."],[6328,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Your Lord sends you greetings of peace, and sent me to you with this cluster of grapes for you to eat.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it."],[6329,"Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row."],[6330,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by people from Aslam while they were practicing archery. He said: Shoot, O sons of Ishmael, for your father was an archer.\""],[6331,"The Mufassal was revealed in Makkah, and we remained for years reciting it, nothing else was revealed."],[6332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and addressed the people on the pulpit in Ramadan. He said: I have stood on this pulpit, and I know Laylat al-Qadr. Seek it in the last ten nights, on an odd night."],[6333,"Indeed Allah forbids you from three things: gossip, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."],[6334,"A dinar for a dinar, and a dirham for a dirham, no excess between them. Whoever has a need for gold should exchange it for silver, and whoever has a need for silver should exchange it for gold, hand to hand."],[6335,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the evening prayer, praying in a single garment, wrapped in it."],[6336,"From Thaqif will emerge a liar and a destroyer."],[6337,"Isaf and Na'ilah were a man and a woman, and Allah transformed them into two stones, and they were in Makkah."],[6338,"I came to visit him during the illness in which he died. He was saying: 'When I die, do not put a shirt on me, for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ neither shirted nor turbaned.'"],[6339,"Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void. If he has consummated the marriage, then she is entitled to her dowry because of what he has made lawful of her private part. If they dispute, then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."],[6340,"Indeed, Allah forbids you from approaching women in their anuses."],[6341,"Abu Bakr gave us a leg of a sheep as a gift. I sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the darkness of the night cutting it up. Masruq said: I said: 'Why did you not light a lamp?' She said: 'If we had a lamp, we would have used it as a condiment (dipped bread in its oil).'"],[6342,"The family of Muhammad ﷺ never ate their fill of wheat bread for three consecutive days since we came to Madinah."],[6343,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he fell behind to relieve himself, then he caught up with me and said: 'Is there any water?' So he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then he caught up with the army and led them in prayer."],[6344,"Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at a man who approaches a woman in her anus."],[6345,"When you meet the polytheists on the road, do not greet them first with salam, and force them to its narrowest part."],[6346,"The one in whose hand is the marriage tie is the husband."],[6347,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to me one day and said, “Do you have anything, O daughter of Ḥuyayy? For I am hungry.” I said, “No, by God, O Messenger of God, except a mudd of flour.” He said, “Then heat it up.” She said, “I put it in the pot and cooked it. Then I said, ‘It is cooked, O Messenger of God.’ He said, ‘Do you know if there is anything in the butter-skin of the daughter of Abū Bakr?’ I said, ‘I do not know, O Messenger of God.’ She said, ‘So he went himself until he came to her house and said, “Is there anything in your butter-skin, O daughter of Abū Bakr?” She said, “There is nothing in it except a little.” So he brought it himself and squeezed its sides into the pot until I saw what came out in the place of his hand. Then he said, “In the name of God,” and invoked blessing. Then he said, “Call your sisters, for I know that they feel the same as I do.” So I called them, and we ate until we were full. Then Abū Bakr came and asked permission, and he entered. Then ʿUmar came, and then another man came. She said, “And they ate until they were full, and there was still some left over from them.”"],[6348,"The Prophet ﷺ was one of the most cheerful of people with a child."],[6349,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade going out to meet the caravans. If someone meets them and buys, the owner of the goods has the option when the goods reach the market."],[6350,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar walking in front of the funeral procession."],[6351,"Whoever vows to obey God, let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Him, let him not disobey Him."],[6352,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a fasting person who ate and drank out of forgetfulness. He did not command him to make it up, and he said, “It is only food that God fed him.”"],[6353,"There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses."],[6354,"His tooth-stick and comb never left the mosque of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would look in the mirror when he combed his beard."],[6355,"Muʿāwiyah gave a sermon to the people, and he mentioned in his sermon that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade certain things, and I convey that to you and forbid you from them: wailing, poetry, images, the skins of wild animals, gold, and silk."],[6356,"Indeed, God has chosen ones among His creation whom He keeps alive in well-being, and when He takes them to His paradise, they are the ones over whom trials pass like patches of dark night while they remain in well-being."],[6357,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed toward a spear."],[6358,"Whoever misses the prayer due to drunkenness even once, it is as if he possessed the world and all it contains and then was stripped of it. And whoever gets drunk four times, it is incumbent upon God to make him drink from the mud of khabāl.” It was said, “What is the mud of khabāl, O Messenger of God?” He said, “The juice of the people of Hell.”"],[6359,"Hilal came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with tithes of honey of his, and asked him to protect for him a valley called Salabah. So the Messenger of God ﷺ protected that valley for him."],[6360,"She saw in a dream that three moons fell into her room. She mentioned that to Abu Bakr. When the Messenger of God ﷺ died and was buried in her house, Abu Bakr said: “This is the best of your moons.”"],[6361,"People will come out of the Fire."],[6362,"I prayed Zuhr with the Messenger of God ﷺ in Madinah, four rak‘ahs. Then he set out on one of his journeys, and he led us in ‘Asr at the tree, two rak‘ahs."],[6363,"She was with ‘A’ishah when it was said to her that Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri reported from the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: “It is not lawful for a woman to travel three days except with a mahram.” ‘Amrah said: ‘A’ishah turned to us and said: “Not all of you have a mahram.”"],[6364,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood on the pulpit and said: “Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl.”"],[6365,"The Messenger of God ﷺ combined Zuhr and ‘Asr, and Maghrib and ‘Isha’ during the expedition of Tabuk, until we returned."],[6366,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal and said: “He will come to you from here,” and he pointed with his hand toward the east."],[6367,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, as if birds were on our heads, none of us speaking, when some people came and said: “O Messenger of God, give us a ruling about such-and-such, give us a ruling about such-and-such.” He said: “O people, God has removed hardship, except for one who borrows from his brother’s honor a loan; that is the one who is in hardship and perishes.” They said: “Should we seek medical treatment, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Yes. God has not sent down any disease but He has sent down for it a cure, except one disease.” They said: “What is it, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Old age.” They said: “Who is the most beloved of God’s servants to God?” He said: “The best of them in character.”"],[6368,"Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."],[6369,"This community will remain upright in its affair, victorious over its enemy, until twelve caliphs pass from among them, all of them from Quraysh.” When he returned to his home, Quraysh came to him and said: “Then what will happen?” He said: “Then there will be chaos.”"],[6370,"Whoever becomes attached to the mosque, God becomes attached to him."],[6371,"I was riding behind Abu Talha, and my knee was touching the knee of the Prophet ﷺ, and they did not cease crying out with the Hajj and the 'Umrah."],[6372,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about gold for gold, and his trade and the trade of Zayd b. Arqam were [in that], so he said: \"There is no harm in it, hand to hand.\""],[6373,"He forbade muhaqalah, mukhabarah, and muzabanah, and that palm trees be sold until they ripen."],[6374,"Abu Bakr went out during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a merchant to Busra. The Prophet's ﷺ stinginess with Abu Bakr and his companionship did not prevent Abu Bakr from his share of that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prevent Abu Bakr from departing, despite his love for his company and his love for Abu Bakr and his avarice for his companionship, out of admiration for the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ approval of trade and his admiration for it."],[6375,"The Prophet ﷺ bought from a Bedouin—I think he said: from Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah—a load of qaraz, or a load of khabat. When he concluded the deal with him, the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Choose.\" The Bedouin said: \"If I have ever seen a day like today, may Allah grant you long life, from whom are you?\" He said: \"From Quraysh.\""],[6376,"Umm Mistah entered upon me, then she went out to a hut for a need, and Umm Mistah trod upon a bone or a thorn, and she said: \"May Mistah perish!\" I said: \"What a bad thing you have said! Do you insult a man from among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said: \"I bear witness that you are one of the heedless believing women. Do you know what has been spread about you?\" I said: \"No, by Allah.\" She said: \"When was your last contact with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" I said: \"The Messenger of Allah does with his wives whatever he likes; he begins with whom he loves and postpones whom he loves among them.\" She said: \"It has been spread about you such-and-such.\" I fell down in a swoon. My mother Umm Ruman heard of it, and when she heard that 'A'ishah had learned of the matter, she came to me and carried me, and I went to her house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ learned that 'A'ishah had heard of the matter, so he came to her and entered upon her and sat with her and said: \"O 'A'ishah, Allah has made repentance ample.\" I increased in evil upon what was with me. While we were like that, Abu Bakr came and entered upon me and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what are you waiting for with this one who betrayed you and disgraced me?\" She said: \"I increased in evil upon evil.\" She said: \"He sent for 'Ali and said: 'O 'Ali, what do you think about 'A'ishah?' He said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'You must tell me what you think about 'A'ishah.' He said: 'Allah has made women ample, but send for Barirah, her servant, and ask her; perhaps she has observed something of her affair.' So he sent for Barirah, and she came, and he said to her: 'Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'If I ask you about something, do not conceal it from me.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, there is nothing you ask me about but I will inform you of it, and I will not conceal anything from you, if Allah wills.' He said: 'You have been with 'A'ishah; have you seen anything from her that you dislike?' She said: 'No, by the One who sent you with prophethood, I have not seen from her since I have been with her except a trait.' He said: 'And what is it?' She said: 'I kneaded dough for myself, and I said to 'A'ishah: Guard this dough until I fetch a firebrand to bake. She stood up to pray and became heedless of the dough, and a sheep came and ate it.' Then he sent for Usamah and said: 'O Usamah, what do you think about 'A'ishah?' He said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'You must tell me what you think about her.' He said: 'I think you should remain silent about her until Allah sends down something to you concerning her.' She said: 'It was only a short while before revelation came down. When it came down, we began to see joy in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and her vindication came from Allah, Mighty is His mention. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rejoice, O 'A'ishah! Then rejoice, O 'A'ishah! Allah has brought you your vindication.\" I said: \"Not by your praise or the praise of your companion.\" She said: \"At that she spoke, and when he came to her he used to say: 'How is that one of yours?\""],[6377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing praying with them when he left, then he came and his head was dripping water. He said: \"I stood with you, then I remembered that I was in a state of janabah and had not performed ghusl, so I left and performed ghusl. Whoever of you is affected by the like of what affected me or finds a movement in his stomach, let him leave and perform ghusl, then come and resume his prayer.\""],[6378,"If I were to appoint anyone over my Ummah without consultation from them, I would appoint over them Ibn Umm 'Abd."],[6379,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the two rak'ahs after 'Asr, so bring me anyone who heard him commanding them."],[6380,"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and among the good things he commanded us was that we should not wail. A woman said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the women of the family of so-and-so helped me in mourning, so I will not pledge allegiance to you until I help them.\" She said: \"So she helped them, then she pledged allegiance to him. No woman fulfilled it except her and Umm Sulaym.\""],[6381,"We used to be commanded to go out for the two 'Ids, including the secluded maiden and the virgin. She said: \"And the menstruating women go out, and they are behind the people, saying takbir with the people.\""],[6382,"A group from the tribe came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and heard him say: \"The one among you with the most Qur'an should lead you in prayer.\" So they put me forward among them while I was a boy, and I used to lead them in prayer in a patched burdah, and it was tight, so when I prostrated my buttocks would show. They said to my father: \"Will you not cover his buttocks from us?\" And I used to encourage them to learn the Qur'an.\" Zuhayr said: \"He remained the imam of his people in prayer and over their funerals.\""],[6383,"Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, it will benefit him one day of his lifetime, after whatever befell him before that."],[6384,"Ibn Abbas said: There is no prostration in the Mufassal. Then I went to Abu Ubaydah b. Abdullah b. Masud and mentioned to him what Ibn Abbas said, and he said: Abdullah b. Masud said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, and the Muslims and the polytheists, in (Surah) al-Najm, and we have not ceased prostrating."],[6385,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we made a night halt while we were with him, nearly a thousand riders, and he prayed two rak'ahs. Then he turned his face toward us with his eyes shedding tears. Umar b. al-Khattab stood up to him, may his father and mother be his ransom, saying: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I asked my Lord's permission to seek forgiveness for my mother, but He did not permit me, so my eyes shed tears out of mercy for her from the Fire. And I had forbidden you three things: from visiting graves, but visit them, and let their visitation increase you in good; and I had forbidden you from the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, but eat and keep whatever you wish; and I had forbidden you from certain drinks, but drink, and do not drink any intoxicant."],[6386,"When a fasting man sits with people while they are eating, the angels send blessings upon him until the fasting person breaks his fast."],[6387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate after the prayer: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from those four.\""],[6388,"Indeed, Allah has those freed from the Fire every day and night, and for every Muslim every day and night there is an answered supplication."],[6389,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I have sworn by the number of these—and he gestured to the fingers of his hands, which were ten—that I will not follow you or follow what you have brought. So I ask you by Allah, what is your religion with which Allah sent you? He said: Allah sent me with Islam. He said: And what is Islam? He said: \"That you say: I have submitted myself to Allah, and I have turned my face to Him, and you establish prayer and give zakah. Two brothers who are helpers, and that Allah will not accept from anyone a repentance if he associated partners after his Islam.\" I said: What is the right of our wives upon us? He said: \"Feed when you eat, clothe when you are clothed, do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not abandon except in the house.\" Then he said: \"Here you will be gathered,\" and he gestured toward Syria, \"on foot and riding, on your faces. You will come to Allah on the Day of Resurrection with muzzles on your mouths. The first thing that will speak from one of you will be his thigh. You will complete seventy nations, you are the last of them and the most noble of them to Allah. And there is no master who comes to his master and asks him for some surplus he has and he withholds it, except that a serpent will come to him on the Day of Resurrection lolling its tongue at him. And a man from those before you, Allah gave him abundant wealth and children, until when one pressing passed and one pressing remained, when death came to him, he said to his family: What kind of man was I to you? They said: The best of men. He said: I will take back everything I gave you or you will do what I command you. They said: We will do what you command us. He said: When I die, throw me into the fire, and when I become charcoal, crush me, then scatter me on a windy day. Then he called upon Allah, and he came as he was. He said: What made you do what you did? He said: Fear of You, O Lord. He said: And he recited about him: 'And my Lord'\""],[6390,"Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but by taking away the scholars. When the scholars are gone, people will take ignorant leaders who are asked and give fatwas without knowledge, so they go astray and lead others astray from the right path."],[6391,"I have pardoned you from the zakah of horses and slaves."],[6392,"Umar b. al-Khattab mentioned the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then said to them: The hand of Allah is upon the congregation, and the solitary one is with Satan. And the truth is a root in Paradise, and falsehood is a root in the Fire. Indeed, my companions are the best of you, so honor them, then the generation that follows them, then the generation that follows them, then lying and turmoil will appear."],[6393,"The Prophet ﷺ urinated at a people's rubbish dump, [then] performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[6394,"I asked Jibril ﷺ : Do you see your Lord? He said: Between me and Him are seventy veils of light; if I saw the nearest of them, I would be burned."],[6395,"A poor woman came to me carrying two sons of hers. I gave her three dates to eat. She gave each of her two sons one date, and they ate them. Then her two sons asked her for more food. She split the date that she herself intended to eat between them. She said: I was impressed by her action, and I mentioned what she had done to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Indeed Allah has made Paradise obligatory for her and freed her from the Fire.'"],[6396,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed of his prophethood at the age of forty. He remained in Makkah for ten years. Then Allah took his soul at the age of sixty, and there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."],[6397,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife does not repel the hand of one who touches her. He said: 'Divorce her.' He said: I love her, and she is a beautiful woman. He said: 'Then enjoy her.'"],[6398,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah), then said: Your Lord said: O son of Adam, I sent down upon you seven verses: three are for Me, three are for you, and one is between Me and you. As for those which are for Me: 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, the Compassionate, the Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment.' And the one between Me and you: 'You alone we worship and You alone we ask for help'—from you is worship and upon Me is help for you. As for those which are for you: 'Guide us to the straight path'—this is for you—'the path of those upon whom You have bestowed favor, not of those who have incurred wrath'—the Jews—'nor of those who go astray'—the Christians."],[6399,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer one day and omitted a surah from the Quran. When he finished his prayer, Ubayy said: O Messenger of Allah, has such and such verse been abrogated? He said: 'No.' Ubayy said: But you did not recite it. He said: 'Why did you not prompt me with it?'"],[6400,"A man came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was giving the Friday sermon to the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Stand and pray two rak'ahs, and make them brief.'"],[6401,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while his face was beaming and he was joyful. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you are in a state in which I have never seen you before. He said: 'And what prevents me? Jibril ﷺ came to me just now and said: Give glad tidings to your ummah that whoever sends one blessing upon you, Allah will record for him ten good deeds and erase from him ten evil deeds.'"],[6402,"Any man who has camels"],[6403,"Do not trade fresh dates until they are clearly ripe, and do not trade gold except like for like."],[6404,"The best prayer after the obligatory prayer is prayer in the depth of the night, and the best fasting after the month of Ramadan is the month of Allah which you call al-Muharram."],[6405,"We used to set out as pilgrims with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and no sooner would we reach al-Rawha' the next day than our throats would become hoarse."],[6406,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from the mouths of water-skins."],[6407,"A woman in ihram must not wear a face veil, nor gloves, nor a burqa. If she wants to enter ihram while she is menstruating, let her enter ihram and stand at the standing places, except for tawaf around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa."],[6408,"Allah (Mighty and Sublime) did not send any prophet except that he was a young man, and no scholar was given knowledge except that he was a young man."],[6409,"Jibril ﷺ descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Judge by the oath along with the witness.\" And he said: \"Wednesday is a day of persistent ill omen.\""],[6410,"The one who serves water to the people is the last of them to drink."],[6411,"The Prophet ﷺ pronounced the talbiyah from the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah."],[6412,"Injury caused by an animal is without liability, injury from a well is without liability, and injury from a mine is without liability; and on buried treasure, one-fifth is due."],[6413,"A man called Ibn Jurayj, who was argumentative, came to Ibn Umar and said: \"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I saw you do something no one else does.\" He said: \"Oh? Oh? O Ibn Jurayj, you keep bringing me strange things.\" He said: \"I saw you not raising your voice with the talbiyah until your mount stood upright with you; I saw you trimming your moustache closely; I saw you liking yellow dye; and I saw you wearing sandals made of tanned leather.\" He said: \"As for my talbiyah when my mount stands up straight with me, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not raising his voice with the talbiyah until his mount stood up straight with him. As for clipping my moustache closely, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ clipping his moustache closely. As for the yellow dye, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ liking yellow dye. As for wearing tanned-leather sandals, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ liking them, and he performed ablution while wearing them.\""],[6414,"My father died, leaving me and a brother of mine, and he did not leave us any wealth. Then my paternal uncle came from Madinah and brought us to Aishah. He brought me inside with her into the curtained area because I was a girl, but he did not bring in the boy. My uncle complained to her of his need, so she ordered for us two fariḍah (garments), two ghazarah (garments), two mu'aqqad (garments), and a hisl (garment). Then she said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The Hour will not come until children become a source of anger, rain is hot, the wicked overflow in abundance, the noble dwindle away, the young are insolent toward the old, and the vile are insolent toward the noble.'\""],[6415,"Indeed a man may act for a period of his life with the deeds of the people of Paradise, then when it is just before his death he changes and acts with the deeds of the people of the Fire, then dies and enters the Fire. And a man may act for a period of his life with the deeds of the people of the Fire, then when it is just before his death he changes and acts with the deeds of the people of Paradise, then dies and enters Paradise."],[6416,"He had a brother whose kunyah was Abu Umayr, and he had a nughar (small bird), and it died. The Prophet ﷺ entered upon us and said: \"What is wrong with Abu Umayr?\" They said: \"His nughar perished.\" So he began saying while joking with him: \"Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr? Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?\""],[6417,"Umar b. al-Khattab consulted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about his property at Thamgh, whether to give it as charity. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give as charity what you see fit, and retain its original principal; it is not to be sold, nor inherited.\""],[6418,"Iblis entered Iraq and fulfilled his need; he entered Syria and they drove him away until he reached Sibaq; and he entered Egypt and laid eggs there, hatched them, and spread his fine carpet."],[6419,"The Muslims will soon be besieged in Madinah, until the farthest of their outposts is Salāḥ."],[6420,"I and Ḥafṣah began the day fasting voluntarily, and a gift was given to us, and we desired it, so we ate it. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us. ʿĀʾishah said: Ḥafṣah beat me to it, for she was her father's daughter, and she asked the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"No harm upon you two; fast a day in its place.\""],[6421,"God and His angels send blessings upon those who take the pre-dawn meal."],[6422,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, O cousin of mine, if the one who comes to you comes, can you inform me of him?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"Yes, O Khadījah.\" Khadījah said: One day Jibrīl came to him while I was with him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Khadījah, this is my companion who comes to me; he has come.\" So I said to him: \"Stand and sit on my right thigh.\" So he stood and sat on my right thigh. Then I said to him: \"Do you see him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" I said to him: \"Move and sit on my left thigh.\" So he sat, and I said: \"Do you see him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" I said to him: \"Then move and sit in my lap.\" So he sat, and she said to him: \"Do you see him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" Khadījah said: Then I uncovered myself and threw off my veil, and I said to him: \"Do you see him?\" He said: \"No.\" So I said to him: \"This, by God, is a noble angel; no, by God, this is not a devil.\" Khadījah said: I mentioned that to Waraqah b. Nawfal b. Asad b. ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā b. Quṣayy, just as..."],[6423,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had a mat and a small palm-fiber mat that he would pray on."],[6424,"The fingers take the place of the siwāk when there is no siwāk."],[6425,"We were sitting in a circle in which were ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUmar and ʿUbayd b. ʿUmayr. A man came to us and stood over us and said: \"Answer so-and-so, answer so-and-so.\" The people disliked that intensely, and Ibn ʿUmar lowered his head. ʿUbayd b. ʿUmayr raised his head and said: \"O son of our brother, excuse us, excuse us.\" Then Ibn ʿUmar raised his head and said: \"Let us get up; there is no exemption in this. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever is invited and does not respond has disobeyed God and His Messenger.'\""],[6426,"When one of you prays witr, let him pray two rakʿahs; if he then stands (for the night prayer), those two count for him, otherwise they are for him."],[6427,"Indeed, in Friday there is an hour; no Muslim servant coincides with it asking God for good except that He gives it to him."],[6428,"We attended the wedding of ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib and Fāṭimah bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we did not see a wedding finer than it in terms of ḥays. The Messenger of God ﷺ prepared for us oil and dates, and we ate. Their bed on their wedding night was the skin of a ram."],[6429,"Indeed, God has an angel who, if it were said to him: 'Swallow the seven heavens and the seven earths in one morsel,' he would do it. His glorification is: 'Glory be to You, wherever You are.'"],[6430,"When the sun declined, the Messenger of God ﷺ would pray the Friday prayer, and we would return and find no shade to shelter in."],[6431,"What is between my house and my minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is over my cistern."],[6432,"He would stay at Dhu al-Hulayfah as long as it seemed fit to him. When he wanted to enter ihram, he would pray in the mosque, then he would pronounce the talbiyah when his mount stood upright with him."],[6433,"Whatever intoxicates in large quantities, a small quantity of it is unlawful."],[6434,"Surat al-An'am was revealed accompanied by a host of angels, filling the space between the two horizons, with a loud chanting of glorification and sanctification, and the earth was shaking,\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying: \"Glory be to Allah, the Almighty; glory be to Allah, the Almighty."],[6435,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressing the people. He turned around and did not see Abu Bakr, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Abu Bakr, Abu Bakr, the Holy Spirit Jibril ﷺ .\""],[6436,"The best prayer in the sight of Allah is the Maghrib prayer. Whoever prays two rak'ahs after it, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise in which he will come and go."],[6437,"There are three truths: Allah will not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share. No servant turns to Allah but that He turns him to other than Himself. No man loves a people except that he will be gathered with them."],[6438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered one day and saw a piece of bread thrown away. He walked to it, took it, wiped it, and ate it. Then he said: \"O 'A'ishah, treat Allah's blessings well, for they rarely depart from a household and are about to return to it.\""],[6439,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drinking with three breaths, mentioning Allah's name at the first and praising Him at the last."],[6440,"O Allah, strengthen Islam with 'Umar b. al-Khattab."],[6441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to present himself every year to the tribes of the Arabs so that they would give him refuge among their people until he conveyed the words of Allah and His messages, and they would have Paradise. No tribe responded to him until Allah willed the manifestation of His religion, the support of His Prophet, and the fulfillment of what He had promised him. Allah drove him to this neighborhood of the Ansar, and they responded to him, and Allah made for His Prophet ﷺ the abode of his migration."],[6442,"I heard 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr while we were with him. We had gone out to perform 'umrah. When we descended from the hillock into the valley, Ibn al-Zubayr performed ghusl and prayed two rak'ahs, and we performed ghusl with him and prayed two rak'ahs with him. Then he began the talbiyah: 'Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk. Labbayk, You have no partner, labbayk. Indeed, all praise and favor are Yours, and the dominion; You have no partner.' 'Abd Allah b. 'Urwah said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr say: 'By Allah, this is the talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and this is what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did: he entered ihram after the prayer."],[6443,"Whoever peers into his neighbor's house and looks at the private parts of his Muslim brother, or at a woman's hair, or at any part of her body, it is incumbent upon Allah to admit him to the Fire."],[6444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came on the day of Khaybar, and it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the donkeys have been exhausted.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Abu Talhah, and he called out: 'Allah and His Messenger forbid you the flesh of domestic donkeys, for it is an abomination.'"],[6445,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when we reached Dhul-Hulayfah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and prayed two rak'ahs, then he entered ihram after the prayer for Hajj and 'Umrah together."],[6446,"There is no human being but has two gates from heaven through one his deeds ascend and through the other his provision descends. When the believing servant dies, they both weep over him."],[6447,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ take his uncle al-'Abbas by the hand, then he said: 'O 'Abbas, there is no prophethood but that it is followed by a caliphate. And from your descendants there shall rule in the end of time seventeen: among them al-Saffah, among them al-Mansur, among them al-Mahdi — and he is not a Mahdi — among them al-Jamuh, among them al-'Aqib, among them al-Wahin from your offspring. And woe to my Ummah from him! How he will wound it and destroy it and take its wealth, he and his followers, upon other than the religion of Islam. Then when allegiance is given to his young son, with the eighteenth, their state will be cut off and the people of the west will come forth from their homes.'"],[6448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-'Abbas: 'The world will not pass away until one from your descendants, O uncle, rules in the end of time at the cutting off of their rule, and he is the eighteenth. With him will be a blind and deaf tribulation; from every ten thousand, nine thousand nine hundred will be killed, and none will escape but a few. Their fighting will be at a place in Iraq.' He said: 'Then al-'Abbas wept.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'What makes you weep? They are the worst of my Ummah; they pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the target. They seek the world and do not care about the Hereafter.'"],[6449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the 'Asr prayer. When he was in the fourth rak'ah, al-Hasan and al-Husayn came forward until they climbed onto the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He placed them before him, and al-Hasan came forward. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ carried al-Hasan on his right shoulder and al-Husayn on his left shoulder. Then he said: 'O people, shall I not tell you of the best of people in grandfather and grandmother? Shall I not tell you of the best of people in paternal uncle and paternal aunt? Shall I not tell you of the best of people in maternal uncle and maternal aunt? Shall I not tell you of the best of people in father and mother? They are al-Hasan and al-Husayn. Their grandfather is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and their grandmother is Khadijah bint Khuwaylid. Their mother is Fatimah bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and their father is 'Ali b. Abi Talib. Their paternal uncle is Ja'far b. Abi Talib, and their paternal aunt is Umm Hani' bint Abi Talib. Their maternal uncle is al-Qasim son of the Messenger of Allah, and their maternal aunts are Zaynab, Ruqayyah, and Umm Kulthum, the daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Their grandfather is in Paradise, and their father is in Paradise, and their grandmother is in Paradise, and their mother, their paternal uncle, and their paternal aunt are in Paradise, and their maternal aunts are in Paradise, and their maternal uncle is in Paradise, and they are both in Paradise, and their sister is in Paradise.'"],[6450,"Every Ummah has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this Ummah is Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[6451,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr, and 'Umar, and all of them used to raise their hands when they began the prayer, when they said the takbir for ruku', and when they raised their heads, they said the takbir for sujud."],[6452,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no god but Allah.' When they say it, they have protected from me their blood and their property except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."],[6453,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a sandal that had a strap in the middle."],[6454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two horned rams, one on behalf of himself and his household, and the other on behalf of himself and those of his Ummah who did not offer a sacrifice."],[6455,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage, while he was on his she-camel, his hand on ʿAlī's shoulder: 'O God, have I conveyed? O God, have I conveyed? This is my cousin and the father of my offspring. O God, overturn into the Fire whoever opposes him.'"],[6456,"The worst person killed is one killed between two rows, one of which seeks kingship."],[6457,"I heard Marwān say to Abū Hurayrah: 'By God, I love you, were it not that you love al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī.' Abū Hurayrah said to Marwān: 'Why should I not love him, when I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ come to their door one day and say: \"Ḥasan,\" and al-Ḥasan came out to him, so he put his mouth to his and sucked his tongue and embraced him. By God, I will never cease loving him.'"],[6458,"I heard ʿAmmār b. Yāsir at Ṣiffīn on the day he was struck, calling out: 'I have met the All-Compelling, and I have married the wide-eyed houris. Today we meet the beloved, Muḥammad and his party.' The Messenger of God ﷺ had pledged to me: 'The last of your provision from this world will be a drink of milk.'"],[6459,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me and said: 'Give the people glad tidings that whoever says: There is no god but God alone, with no partner, will enter Paradise.'"],[6460,"He should only take it like for like."],[6461,"Two men came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. One of them said: 'O Messenger of God, judge between me and this man. My son was a hired worker for his wife. My son was a virgin who had not yet had intercourse, and he committed adultery with her. I asked those who did not know, and they told me that my son must be stoned, so I ransomed him from that with such and such. Then I asked those who know, and they told me that my son is not to be stoned.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'I will indeed judge between you with truth. As for what you gave, he must return it to you. As for your son, he is to be flogged one hundred lashes and exiled for a year. As for his wife, she is to be stoned.'"],[6462,"It was said to the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'Where were you, O Messenger of God, regarding the daughter of Ḥamzah?' Or it was said: 'Will you not propose to the daughter of Ḥamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib?' He said: 'Ḥamzah is my brother through suckling.'"],[6463,"There were two brothers at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and one of them was superior to the other. The superior one died, then the other lived forty nights after him and then died. The virtue of the first over the last was mentioned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he said: 'Did he not pray?' They said: 'Yes.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'And he was not objectionable?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'And what will tell you how far his prayer reached?' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The likeness of prayers is like a deep, sweet river at a man's door into which he plunges five times every day. What do you think that leaves of his filth? You do not know what his prayer accomplished.'"],[6464,"Anas b. Mālik arrived in Madinah, and ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz sent me, saying: 'Ask him about the ḥadīth that al-Ḥajjāj b. Yūsuf reported concerning a group who rebelled in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he blinded two, amputated two, and crucified two.' Anas said: 'Those people had professed Islam and settled in Madinah, then they left it out of aversion to Islam, joined the polytheists, raided the livestock of Madinah, and drove it off. The Prophet ﷺ was informed of them, so he sent in pursuit of them and seized this group.' He said: 'ʿUmar sent back to him, saying: \"Would that you had not reported this ḥadīth to al-Ḥajjāj. These people turned away from Islam, joined the polytheists, and raided the livestock of Madinah, but al-Ḥajjāj considered this lawful against those who did not intend to leave Islam or join the polytheists.\"' ʿUmar said: 'And ask him: Did the Prophet ﷺ dye his hair? For we see here some of his hair as though it has been colored.' Anas said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ was blessed with black hair. If I were to count what I saw of white hairs on his head and beard, I would not count fifteen. I do not think this hair you find has been colored except from the perfume that was put in the hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[6465,"The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not betray him nor forsake him. The Muslims are one hand against those besides them; their blood is equal, and the lowliest of them may give protection on their behalf."],[6466,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Ḍubāʿah to stipulate in the ḥajj and say: 'My place of leaving iḥrām is wherever You detain me.'"],[6467,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in his house like one of you in his house: he would sew his garment and work as one of you works."],[6468,"Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of God ﷺ to come to her in her home and pray in it, so that she could make it a place of prayer. He did so. He came to her, and she went to a mat of theirs and sprinkled it with water, and the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed, and they prayed with him."],[6469,"Concerning His saying, “God was well pleased with the believers when they pledged allegiance to you under the tree” [Qur’an 48:18], Jabir said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ that we would not flee, and we did not pledge allegiance to him upon death."],[6470,"Umar b. al-Khattab addressed us in Syria and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us in a position like my standing among you, and said: “I enjoin you to treat my companions well, I enjoin you to treat my companions well, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will spread until a man testifies before he is asked to testify, and swears an oath before he is asked to swear. Whoever desires the best part of Paradise, let him adhere to the community, for Satan is with the lone individual, and he is farther from two. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and distressed by his evil deed is a believer.”"],[6471,"The two parties to a sale have the option [to cancel] in their sale as long as they have not separated, or it is an option."],[6472,"Abu Talhah sent me to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a harīrah (a kind of porridge) that he had made for him, singling him out for it. He said: “Go and call the Messenger of God ﷺ for me.” He said: So I went to him, and when the Messenger of God ﷺ saw me among his companions, he fixed his gaze on me until all the people looked at me, and I became embarrassed. He said: “Has Abu Talhah sent for us?” I said: “Yes.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Arise.” He said: So the people arose with him. I went running to Abu Talhah and told him the news. He went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I only made something for you that will not be enough for them.” He said: “It will be enough for them, God willing.” The Messenger of God ﷺ entered and invoked blessing, then said: “Give permission to ten.” He said: So they entered and ate until they were satisfied, then they left. He said: “Give permission to ten others.” Ten entered and ate until they were all satisfied. Then he took what remained, gathered it, invoked blessing upon it, and it returned to what it had been. He said: “Take this.”"],[6473,"We did not fast with the Messenger of God ﷺ twenty-nine [days] more than we fasted thirty."],[6474,"It is as if I am looking at Mūsā b. ʿImrān in this valley, in ihram, between two Qaṭawānī cloaks."],[6475,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ as the tenth of ten, and a man from the Ansar came and said: “O Prophet of God, who is the shrewdest of people and the most resolute of people?” He said: “The one who remembers death most and is most prepared for death before death descends. Those are the shrewd ones. They have attained the honor of this world and the dignity of the Hereafter.”"],[6476,"The rewards of my community were shown to me, even a speck of dirt that a man removes from the mosque. And the sins of my community were shown to me, and I did not see a sin greater than a verse or a sūrah given to a man, then he forgot it."],[6477,"The letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ came to us: “Do not benefit from the carcass by its hide or sinew.”"],[6478,"Whoever says: “Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is greatest,” for every letter ten good deeds are written for him. Whoever aids in a false dispute remains in God’s wrath until he desists. Whoever intercedes to block one of God’s prescribed punishments has opposed God in His command. Whoever slanders a believing man or woman, God will confine him in the mire of putrefaction on the Day of Resurrection until he emerges from what he said, but he will not emerge."],[6479,"I met Bilal and said: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray inside the Kaaba? He said: He prayed two rak'ahs between the two pillars, and he placed the middle pillar on his right."],[6480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from cauterization, but we cauterized ourselves, and we neither prospered nor succeeded."],[6481,"The Dajjal will surely be encountered by one who met me, or he will surely be close to my death."],[6482,"This verse was recited in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'O mankind, eat from whatever is on earth that is lawful and good.' Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah that He make me one whose supplication is answered. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: O Sa'd, make your food wholesome and you will be one whose supplication is answered. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, a servant casts a forbidden morsel into his belly and no deed is accepted from him for forty days. And any servant whose flesh grows from illicit gain and usury—the Fire is more deserving of him."],[6483,"A month and a half would pass and we would not kindle a fire in the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a lamp or anything else. I said: Glory be to Allah, from what did you live? She said: On water and dates. We had neighbors among the Ansar who had milk-giving animals, and sometimes they would gift us some milk."],[6484,"The houris in Paradise sing, saying: 'We are the fair houris, guided to noble husbands.'"],[6485,"A woman in post-natal bleeding and a menstruating woman performs ghusl, enters ihram, and performs all the rites except that she does not circumambulate the House until she becomes pure."],[6486,"Whatever inheritance was divided in the Jahiliyyah remains according to the division of the Jahiliyyah, and whatever inheritance Islam came upon is according to the division of Islam."],[6487,"I was the first to hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'None of you should urinate facing the qiblah,' and the first to narrate that to the people."],[6488,"Some people entered upon him to visit him during an illness of his, and he said: O slave girl, bring something for our companions, even if only unripe dates, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Noble character traits are among the deeds of Paradise.'"],[6489,"When Adam committed the sin he committed, he raised his head toward the Throne and said: I ask You by the right of Muhammad to forgive me. Allah revealed to him: And what is Muhammad? And who is Muhammad? He said: Blessed be Your name. When You created me, I raised my head to Your Throne, and there was written upon it: 'There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' So I knew that no one is greater in Your sight than the one whose name You placed with Your name. Allah revealed to him: O Adam, he is the last of the prophets from your offspring, and his nation is the last of the nations from your offspring. Were it not for him, O Adam, I would not have created you."],[6490,"I was given permission to narrate about an angel from among the bearers of the Throne: his feet are in the lowest earth, and the Throne is upon his horn, and between the lobe of his ear and his shoulder is a distance of seven hundred years of bird flight. The angel says: 'Glory be to You, wherever You are.'"],[6491,"There is no household among whom someone dies and they give charity on his behalf after his death, except that Jibril ﷺ presents it to him on a platter of light, then stands at the edge of the grave and says: 'O dweller of the deep grave, this is a gift your family has sent to you, so accept it.' Then it enters upon him, and he rejoices at it and is delighted, while his neighbors who are not sent anything grieve."],[6492,"Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it. It is at one of the gates of Paradise. And this 'Ayr is a mountain that hates us and we hate it. It is at one of the gates of the Fire."],[6493,"Allah revealed to Ibrahim: 'O My intimate friend, improve your character, even with the disbeliever, and you will enter the abode of the righteous. For My word has preceded that whoever has good character, I will shade him under My Throne, give him to drink from the enclosure of My Holiness, and bring him near to My proximity.'"],[6494,"Gold dinars and silver dirhams are the seals of Allah on His earth. Whoever comes with the seal of his Master, I will fulfill his need."],[6495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to judge between my people. I said: 'I am not good at judging.' He said: 'Judge between them, for Allah is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately incline to injustice.'"],[6496,"Whoever relates a hadith and someone sneezes in his presence, then it is true."],[6497,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, a caller will call out: 'Indeed, let the adversaries of Allah stand up, indeed they are the Qadariyyah.'"],[6498,"The people of the Fire will be presented on the Day of Resurrection in rows. The believers will pass by them. A man from the people of the Fire will see a man from the believers whom he had known in the abode of this world, and he will say: 'O so-and-so, do you not remember the day you sought my help for such-and-such a need?' And he will say to him: 'Do you not remember the day I gave you such-and-such?' That believer will remember, and he will intercede for him to his Lord, and his intercession will be accepted for him."],[6499,"Whoever fasts one day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seventy autumns. And whoever dies while guarding the frontier, he will be protected from the trial of the grave, and his provision will continue to flow to him."],[6500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him and called him, so he came out to him and walked with him until he reached the mosque. Then he left, performed ghusl, and returned. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and on him was the trace of ghusl. The Prophet ﷺ asked him about his ghusl. He said: 'I heard your call while I was having intercourse with my wife, so I got up before finishing and performed ghusl.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Water is only required from water.' Then after that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory.'"],[6501,"When death approached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he stretched out his hand and said: 'O Jibril, where are you?' Then he would withdraw it and extend it, doing that repeatedly while saying: 'O Jibril, intercede for me with my Lord to make death easy for me.' Abu Hurayrah mentioned that he heard A'ishah say: 'I heard from Jibril what no ear has ever heard, and he was saying: Labbayk.'"],[6502,"Whoever enters ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah from al-Masjid al-Aqsa to al-Masjid al-Haram, his past and future sins will be forgiven, and Paradise will be guaranteed for him."],[6503,"I prayed behind Anas b. Malik a prayer in which he made us forget, and he prostrated after the salam. Then he turned to us and said: Indeed, I did not do anything but as I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do."],[6504,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he called for water for purification, dipped his hand in it, then performed ablution. We followed him and drank the leftover water. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: What made you do what you did? We said: Love of God and His Messenger. He said: If you love that God and His Messenger love you, then fulfill trusts when you are entrusted, be truthful when you speak, and be good to those who neighbor you."],[6505,"Whoever feeds his brother bread until he is full and gives him drink until he is quenched, God will distance him from the Fire by seven trenches."],[6506,"The oath in blood had already existed in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[6507,"A man committed adultery with a woman, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be flogged with the prescribed punishment. Then he was informed that he was married, so he ordered that he be stoned."],[6508,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ not knowing anything, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Say in every sitting: Al-tahiyyatu lillahi wa al-salawatu wa al-tayyibatu lillahi, salamun 'alayka ayyuha al-nabiyyu ﷺ, al-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahi al-salihin, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allahu wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu."],[6509,"While I was traveling with the Messenger of God ﷺ, his mount descended with him from a mountain pass, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was riding alone. When the road became easy for him, he laughed and said the takbir, so we said the takbir because of his takbir. Then he rode a short distance, then laughed and said the takbir, so we said the takbir because of his takbir. Then we caught up with him, and the people said: O Messenger of God, we said the takbir because of your takbir, but we do not know why you laughed. He said: Jibril ﷺ led the she-camel for me, and when the road became easy, he turned to me and said: Rejoice and give glad tidings to your community that whoever says: There is no god but God alone, with no partner, will enter Paradise, and God has forbidden the Fire for him. So I laughed and said the takbir, and I rejoiced for my community."],[6510,"The seal of the Prophet ﷺ was entirely of silver. Then it was with Abu Bakr, then with Umar, then with Uthman as long as God willed, then it perished with Uthman."],[6511,"Abu Bashir al-Ansari, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, saw me praying the Duha prayer when the sun had risen, and he criticized me for that and forbade me. Then he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not pray until the sun has risen high, for it rises between the two horns of a devil."],[6512,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ after performing ablution, and he had left on his feet a spot the size of a fingernail dry. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: Go back and perfect your ablution."],[6513,"I kept using the siwak until I feared it would make my teeth fall out."],[6514,"God will raise for this community at the head of every hundred years someone who will renew its religion for it."],[6515,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to write to the kings of the non-Arabs, so some non-Arabs with him said: \"They, O Messenger of God, do not accept a letter unless it has a seal.\" So he adopted a silver ring, as if I am looking at its whiteness on his palm, then engraved on it: Muhammad, Messenger of God."],[6516,"I am the most self-sufficient of partners with regard to association. Whoever performs a deed in which he associates someone else with Me, I am free of it, and it belongs to the one he associated."],[6517,"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."],[6518,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us that one of us put on sandals while standing, and that he cleanse himself with bone or with what comes out of the stomach."],[6519,"The Jews and Christians do not dye, so differ from them."],[6520,"Islam is built on the testimony that there is no god but God, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the Hajj of the House, and the fast of Ramadan."],[6521,"Beware of the supplication of the oppressed."],[6522,"The price of a dog is not lawful, nor the fee of a soothsayer, nor the dowry of a prostitute."],[6523,"There is no contagion, no evil omen, and the evil eye is true."],[6524,"Pray in the sheepfolds, and do not pray in the resting places of camels."],[6525,"What the Messenger of God ﷺ would disclose: I am upon the faith of Gabriel and Michael (peace be upon them)."],[6526,"Were it not for servants of God bowing in prayer, suckling infants, and grazing beasts, punishment would be poured upon you abundantly, then crushed utterly."],[6527,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ during his illness in which he was taken, and there was Fatimah at his head. He said: She wept until her voice rose, so the Messenger of God ﷺ raised his glance to her and said, \"My beloved Fatimah, what makes you weep?\" She said, \"I fear the loss after you.\" He said, \"O my beloved, do you not know that God looked upon the earth with a look and chose from it your father, then sent him with His message? Then He looked upon the earth with a look and chose from it your husband, and revealed to me that I should marry you to him. O Fatimah, we are a household to whom God has given seven qualities that He has not given to anyone before us, nor will He give to anyone after us: I am the Seal of the Prophets and the noblest of the prophets before God, and the most beloved of creatures to God, and I am your father. My successor is the best of successors and the most beloved of them to God, and he is your husband. Our martyr is the best of martyrs and the most beloved of them to God, and he is Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, and he is the paternal uncle of your father and the paternal uncle of your husband. And among us is one who has two green wings, flying in Paradise with the angels wherever he wishes, and he is the cousin of your father and the brother of your husband. And among us are the two grandsons of this community, and they are your two sons, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, and they are the masters of the youths of the people of Paradise, and their father—by the One who sent me with the truth—is better than them. O Fatimah, by the One who sent me with the truth, from them is the Mahdi of this community when the world becomes chaos and confusion, and trials become widespread, and paths are cut off, and people attack one another, so no elder has mercy on a child, nor does a child honor an elder. At that time, God will send from them one who opens the fortresses of misguidance and sealed hearts, demolishing them completely. He will uphold the religion at the end of time just as I upheld it at the beginning of time. He will fill the earth with justice just as it was filled with oppression. O Fatimah, do not grieve and do not weep, for God is more merciful and compassionate to you than I am, because of your place with me and your position in my heart. And God has married you to your husband, who is the noblest of my household in lineage, the most honorable of them in status, the most merciful of them to the subjects, the most just of them in equity, and the most insightful of them in judgment. And I have asked my Lord that you be the first of my household to join me.\" 'Ali b. Abi Talib said: \"When the Prophet ﷺ was taken, Fatimah did not remain after him except seventy-five days until God joined her to him ﷺ.\""],[6528,"\"Whoever speaks much, his slips increase; and whoever's slips increase, his sins increase; and whoever's sins increase, the Fire is more deserving of him. So whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him say what is good or remain silent.\""],[6529,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution once (i.e., washing each part once)."],[6530,"\"In Paradise there is a palace of pearls, with no crack in it and no weakness, which God has prepared for His friend Ibrahim.\""],[6531,"Abu Hind, the freedman of Banu Bayadah, was a cupper who cupped the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to look at one in whose heart God has formed faith, let him look at Abu Hind.\" And he said: \"Marry him off, and marry into his family.\""],[6532,"'Umar b. al-Khattab asked the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was at al-Ji'ranah, after returning from al-Ta'if, saying: \"O Messenger of God, I vowed in the time of ignorance to observe i'tikaf for a day in the Sacred Mosque. What do you think?\" He said: \"Go and observe i'tikaf for a day.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ had given him a slave girl from the khums. When the Messenger of God ﷺ freed the captives of the people, he heard their voices saying, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ has freed us.\" So he asked, \"What is this?\" They said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ freed the captives of the people.\" 'Umar said: \"Go to that slave girl and set her free.\""],[6533,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not look in any direction except that he saw Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith fighting. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Abu Sufyan is the best of my family,\" or \"among the best of my family.\""],[6534,"\"I was praying on a moonlit night, and I had tethered my horse. It bolted, and I was startled, so I entered the house. When morning came, I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Those were the angels who came to listen to your recitation of Surat al-Baqarah in the last part of the night.'\""],[6535,"Among the supplications of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: \"O God, cool my heart with hail, snow, and cold water, and purify me from sins as You purified the white garment from dirt.\""],[6536,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ and I used to bathe from a single vessel due to janabah.\""],[6537,"The owner of the mount has more right to its front."],[6538,"\"People exaggerated about performing ghusl on Friday, but that was only in my house. A group of people from al-'Aliyah entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ on a hot day, having worked in their palm groves, wearing their woolen garments. They entered with unpleasant odors, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'When this day comes, then perform ghusl.'\""],[6539,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate: “O Allah, forgive me my error, my ignorance, and my extravagance in my affair, and what You know better than I. O Allah, forgive me my earnestness and my jesting, my mistake and my deliberate act, and all of that is with me.”"],[6540,"None of you will enter Paradise by his deeds.” Some of them said: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with His mercy.”"],[6541,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away and the Arabs apostatized, ʿUmar said: “O Abu Bakr, do you intend to fight all the Arabs when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: there is no god but Allah’?” Abu Bakr said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only said: ‘When they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, establish the prayer, and give the zakat, they have protected from me their blood and their wealth.’ By Allah, if they withheld from me a young she-goat that they used to pay to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would fight them over it.”"],[6542,"Whoever Allah clothes with a blessing, let him increase in praising Allah. Whoever has many worries, let him seek Allah’s forgiveness. Whoever finds his provision slow in coming, let him often say: ‘There is no might and no power except with Allah.’ Whoever stays with a people, let him not fast except with their permission. Whoever enters the home of a people, let him sit where they tell him, for the people know best the private areas of their home. Among the sins for which its perpetrator is detested are malice, envy, laziness in worship, and straitened livelihood.”"],[6543,"Every son of Adam will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with a sin he has committed, which He will punish him for if He wills or have mercy on him, except Yahya b. Zakariyya, for he was a master, chaste, and a prophet among the righteous.” The Prophet ﷺ reached for a speck from the ground, took it, and said: “His male organ was like this speck.”"],[6544,"Whoever laughs excessively will have his rights belittled. Whoever jokes excessively will lose his dignity. Whoever engages in excessive jesting will lose his solemnity. Whoever drinks water on an empty stomach will have his strength weakened. Whoever talks excessively will make many slips. Whoever makes many slips will have many sins. Whoever has many sins, the Fire is more deserving of him.”"],[6545,"The best of my community are those who, when they do wrong, seek forgiveness; when they do good, rejoice; and when they travel, shorten the prayer and break the fast.”"],[6546,"When Jaʿfar b. Abi Talib arrived from the land of Abyssinia, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met him. When Jaʿfar saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he hopped in reverence for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed him between his eyes and said to him: “O my beloved, you are the most similar of people to me in my physical appearance and character, and you were created from the same clay from which I was created, O my beloved.”"],[6547,"While I was traveling along the outskirts of Badr, a man emerged from a pit with a chain around his neck. He called out to me: “O servant of Allah, give me water! O servant of Allah, give me water!” I do not know whether he knew my name or called me by the Arabs’ generic address. Then a black man came out from that pit holding a whip. He called to me: “O servant of Allah, do not give him water, for he is a disbeliever.” Then he struck him with the whip until he returned to his pit. I came to the Prophet ﷺ in haste and informed him. He said to me: “Did you see him?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “That was the enemy of Allah, Abu Jahl b. Hisham, and that is his punishment until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[6548,"I was serving the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a roasted chick was presented. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You and to me to eat with me from this chick.” ʿAli came and knocked on the door. Anas said: “Who is this?” He said: “ʿAli.” I said: “The Prophet ﷺ is occupied,” so he left. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ moved aside and ate. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You and to me to eat with me from this chick.” ʿAli came and knocked on the door with a strong knock. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard it and said: “O Anas, who is this?” I said: “ʿAli.” He said: “Let him in.” He entered, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I asked Allah three times to bring me the most beloved of His creation to Him and to me to eat with me from this chick.” ʿAli said: “And I, O Messenger of Allah, came three times, and each time Anas turned me away.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Anas, what made you do what you did?” I said: “I wanted the supplication to reach a man from my people.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man is not blamed for loving his people.”"],[6549,"I have a river between Sanaa and Ayla, with vessels numbering the stars. It is colder than snow, sweeter than honey, and whiter than milk. Whoever drinks a sip from it will never thirst again, and whoever does not taste it will never be quenched."],[6550,"A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he guards his tongue."],[6551,"There is no breastfeeding after weaning, and no orphanhood after puberty."],[6552,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by two graves whose occupants were being punished. He said: \"They are being punished, and they are not being punished for something major. One of them did not protect himself from urine, and the other used to go about spreading malicious gossip.\" Then he called for a fresh palm branch, broke it in two, and placed one piece on this grave and one on that. He said: \"Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they do not dry out.\""],[6553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on Mount Hira, and it shook with them. The Prophet ﷺ struck it with his foot and said: \"Be still, for upon you are a Prophet, a Siddiq, and two martyrs.\" Upon it were the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman."],[6554,"Do not revile my Companions, for if one of you were to spend gold equal to Mount Uhud, he would not reach the mudd of one of them, nor even half of it."],[6555,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Night of Decree. He said: \"I saw it, then I was made to forget it, so seek it in the latter half.\" Then he returned and said: \"In the twenty-third night that passes of the month.\""],[6556,"Sahla bt. Suhayl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I see in the face of Abu Hudhayfa something because of Salim entering upon me?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Breastfeed him.\" She said: \"He is a grown man with a beard.\" He said: \"Breastfeed him, and what is in Abu Hudhayfa's face will go away.\""],[6557,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my father has taken my wealth.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the man: \"Go and bring me your father.\" Then Jibril descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Allah sends you greetings of peace and says: When the old man comes to you, ask him about something he said within himself that his ears did not hear.\" When the old man came, the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Your son keeps complaining that you take his wealth?\" He said: \"Ask him, O Messenger of Allah, do I spend it except on one of his paternal aunts or maternal aunts, or on myself?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Leave this matter; let us move on from this.\""],[6558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Call your father and your brother so that I may write a document, for I fear that someone might say something or someone might wish for something, but Allah and the believers refuse anyone except Abu Bakr.\""],[6559,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is Umrah obligatory, its obligation like the obligation of Hajj?\" He said: \"No, but if you perform Umrah, it is better for you.\""],[6560,"The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the Muhajir is the one who abandons what Allah has forbidden.\""],[6561,"Selling animals that have been left unmilked to deceive the buyer is a deception, and it is not lawful to deceive a Muslim."],[6562,"I fear for you three things, and they will surely occur: the slip of a scholar, the argument of a hypocrite using the Quran, and a worldly life that is opened up to you."],[6563,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed sheep among his companions, allotting one sheep to every ten people."],[6564,"The Prophet ﷺ granted safety to the people on the day of the conquest of Makkah, except for four individuals: 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Khatal, Miqyas b. Subabah al-Kinani, 'Abd Allah b. Sa'd b. Abi Sarh, and Umm Sarah, a woman. As for 'Abd al-'Uzza, he was killed while clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah. He said: A man from the Ansar vowed to kill 'Abd Allah b. Sa'd b. Abi Sarh if he saw him. He was the foster brother of 'Uthman b. 'Affan. 'Uthman brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ to intercede for him. When the Ansari saw him, he grasped his sword and went out seeking him. He found him in the circle of the Messenger of God ﷺ and was afraid to kill him. He kept hesitating and disliked approaching him because he was in the circle of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ extended his hand and accepted his pledge of allegiance. Then he said to the Ansari: 'I was waiting for you to fulfill your vow.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, I was in awe of you. Could you not have signaled to me?' He said: 'It is not for a prophet to signal.' As for Miqyas, he had a brother who was killed by mistake while with the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent with him a man from Banu Fihr to collect the blood money for him from the Ansar. When he had collected the blood money and returned, the Fihri fell asleep. Miqyas jumped up, took a stone, and struck his head with it, killing him. Then he came forward saying: 'The soul is healed of one who spent the night in the open, propped up, / His two garments stained with the blood of his veins. / The anxieties of the soul before his killing / Used to stir and make me forget the softness of beds. / By him I have settled my vengeance and achieved my revenge, / And I was the first to return to the idols.' As for Umm Sarah, she was a freedwoman of Quraysh. She came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and complained of need, so he gave her something. Then a man came to her and handed her a letter for the people of Makkah, seeking favor with them so that his family would be protected, for he had family there. Jibril informed the Messenger of God ﷺ of that. He sent 'Umar b. al-Khattab and 'Ali b. Abi Talib after her. They caught up with her and searched her but found nothing. They turned back. One of them said to the other: 'By God, we have not lied, nor have we been lied to. Let us go back to her.' So they returned to her, drew their swords, and said: 'By God, we will make you taste death unless you hand over the letter to us.' She denied it. Then she said: 'I will give it to you on the condition that you do not bring me back to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' They accepted that from her. She untied the band of her head and brought out a letter from her hair, handing it to them. They returned with it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and gave it to him. He sent for the man and said: 'What is this letter?' He said: 'I will tell you, O Messenger of God. There is no one with you but has someone in Makkah to protect his family, except me. So I wrote this letter so that they would look after my family.' Then God revealed: 'O you who believe, do not take My enemy and your enemy as allies, offering them affection...' to the end of the verses."],[6565,"It is as if I am looking at the hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ, with his locks reaching to this place—and he put his hand on his chest, between his breasts."],[6566,"The Messenger of God ﷺ liked cucumbers."],[6567,"I have never seen anyone with better character than the Messenger of God ﷺ. I saw him when he mounted me behind him on his camel at night after Khaybar. I began to doze, and my head would hit the rear of the saddle. He would touch me with his hand and say: 'O this one, gently; O daughter of Huyayy, gently.' When he reached al-Sahba', he said: 'Indeed, I apologize to you, O Safiyyah, for what I did to your people. They said such-and-such to me and such-and-such to me.'"],[6568,"You are in a time of prophethood and mercy, and there will be a caliphate and mercy, then there will be such-and-such and such-and-such, then there will be a biting kingship. They will drink wine and wear silk, and in that they will be granted victory until the Hour rises."],[6569,"Love is from God, and reputation is in the heaven. When God loves a servant, He says: 'O Jibril, indeed your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him.' He said: Then Jibril calls out, and he brings down love for him upon the people of the earth."],[6570,"Mudar will not leave any servant of God without afflicting him or killing him, until they do not protect even the tail of a watercourse. He said: They said: 'He says this, while you are a man of Mudar?' He said: 'Should I not say what the Messenger of God ﷺ said?'"],[6571,"Whoever sits in a gathering in which there is much idle talk and says before he leaves: 'Glory be to You, O our Lord, and praise be to You. There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You,' it will be an expiation for what was in that gathering."],[6572,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'O Buraydah, shall I teach you words which, if God intends good for a person, He teaches them to him and he never forgets them?' I said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Say: O God, I am weak, so strengthen my weakness in Your pleasure, and take me by my forelock to goodness, and make Islam the utmost of my satisfaction. O God, I am weak, so strengthen me; I am lowly, so honor me; I am poor, so enrich me.'"],[6573,"Whoever builds a mosque for God, God will build for him a house in Paradise."],[6574,"Beware of injustice, for injustice will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection."],[6575,"We entered upon Ibn Abbas, and he ordered us to exchange currency. Then I entered upon him another time, and he said: \"We used to order you, but now we forbid you from it.\" I said: \"How should we deal with what we ordered the people to do?\" He said: \"I met one of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ who is more knowledgeable about that than I, and he forbade me. So I forbid you as he forbade me.\""],[6576,"\"Poor, poor, poor is the man who has no wife, even if he has much wealth. Poor, poor, poor is the woman who has no husband, even if she has much wealth.\""],[6577,"Backbiting is more severe than adultery. It was said: \"How so?\" He said: \"A man commits adultery and then repents, and God accepts his repentance. But the one who backbites is not forgiven until his companion forgives him.\""],[6578,"The family of the Messenger of God ﷺ had a wild animal. It used to come and go, but when the Messenger of God ﷺ entered, it would lie down and not stir, out of dislike to disturb the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[6579,"\"O Messenger of God, what is the thing that it is not lawful to withhold?\" He said: \"Water, salt, and fire.\" She said: \"Water we know, but what about salt and fire?\" He said: \"Whoever gives salt is as if he gave charity with all that the salt seasons. Whoever gives fire is as if he gave charity with all that the fire cooks. Whoever gives a Muslim a drink of water where water is found is as if he freed a slave. Whoever gives a Muslim a drink of water where water is not found is as if he revived him.\""],[6580,"The Prophet ﷺ climbed onto the grave of Sa'd b. Mu'adh and said: \"If anyone were to be saved from the squeezing of the grave, Sa'd would be saved. Yet he was squeezed tightly, then released.\""],[6581,"One day I entered the market with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He sat by the cloth sellers and bought a pair of trousers for four dirhams. There was a weigher for the people of the market. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Weigh and give more.\" The weigher said: \"I have never heard this phrase from anyone.\" Abu Hurayrah said: \"I said to him: 'It is enough of ignorance in your religion that you do not know your Prophet ﷺ.' So he threw down the scale and leaped to the hand of the Prophet ﷺ to kiss it. The Messenger of God ﷺ pulled his hand away from him and said: \"This is what non-Arabs do to their kings. I am only a man from among you. Weigh and give more.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ took the trousers. Abu Hurayrah said: \"I went to carry it for him, but he said: 'The owner of something has more right to carry it, unless he is weak and unable, in which case his Muslim brother helps him.'\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, do you really wear trousers?\" He said: \"Yes, by night and day, in travel and at home, for I have been commanded to cover myself, and I have not found anything that conceals better.\""],[6582,"\"Do not abandon the evening meal, even if it is a handful of dates, for abandoning it causes weakness.\""],[6583,"\"Gabriel fed me harisah, which strengthens my back for standing in night prayer.\""],[6584,"The Messenger of God ﷺ spent the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah at the start of his journey... and he prayed in its mosque."],[6585,"People from among those who were with me will come to me, but when they are brought up to me and I see them, they will be snatched away before me. I will say: \"O Lord, my companions, my companions!\" It will be said: \"You do not know what they innovated after you.\""],[6586,"\"The Children of Israel appointed a caliph over themselves. He stood praying in the moonlight on the roof of the Temple. He recalled things he had done, so he lowered himself by a rope. In the morning the rope was hanging from the mosque, and he had gone. He set off until he came to a people on the seashore. He found them making bricks. He asked them how they were paid for these bricks. They told him, so he worked with them, eating from the labor of his own hands. When prayer time came, he performed ablution and prayed. That worker was reported to their governor: 'There is among us a man who does such and such.' So the governor sent for him, but he refused to come. Then the governor came himself, riding on his mount. When the man saw him, he fled. The governor pursued him, but the man outran him. The man said: 'Wait for me so I can say a word to you.' He stopped and spoke to him, telling him that he had been a king and that he had fled out of fear for his sin. The governor said: 'I will join you.' So he worshiped God at the sands of Egypt.\" Abdullah b. Mas'ud said: \"If I were in Egypt, I would show you the place, by the description the Messenger of God ﷺ gave us.\""],[6587,"A prophet among the prophets besieged the people of a city until he feared that he would conquer it, and he was concerned that the sun would set. He said: \"O sun, you are commanded, and I am a commanded servant. I adjure you to halt for me for an hour of the day.\" He said: So God held it back for him until he conquered the city. Whenever they obtained spoils, they would offer them as a sacrifice, and fire would come and consume it. When they obtained what they obtained, they placed it, but the fire did not come to consume it. They said: \"O prophet of God, why are our offerings not accepted?\" He said: \"There is embezzlement among you.\" They said: \"O prophet of God, how can we know who has the embezzlement?\" He said: \"You are twelve tribes; let the head of each tribe pledge allegiance to me.\" He said: So the head of each tribe pledged allegiance to him, and the hand of the Prophet ﷺ stuck to the hand of one of them. He said: \"The embezzlement is in your tribe.\" He said: \"How can I know who has it?\" He said: So he had them pledge allegiance man by man, and he did that, and his hand stuck to the hand of a man among them. He said to him: \"Do you have the embezzlement?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"What is it?\" He said: \"A golden bull's head that pleased me, so I embezzled it.\" So he brought it and placed it with the spoils, and the fire came and consumed it. Ka'b said, while he was with Abu Hurayrah: \"God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. It is thus in the Book of God. O Abu Hurayrah, did the Prophet of God ﷺ tell you which prophet it was?\" He said: \"No.\" Ka'b said: \"Yusha' b. Nun, the companion of Musa. And he told you which city it was?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"It is the city of Ariha.\""],[6588,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Mina when a man passed by us calling out: \"These are days of eating, drinking, and remembrance of God.\" I stood up to see who he was, and he was a man called Ibn Hudhafah. He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to do this.\""],[6589,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out, and I found no one following him. 'Umar b. al-Khattab became alarmed and brought him a water vessel. He found the Prophet ﷺ prostrating in an upper room, so he withdrew from behind him until the Prophet ﷺ raised his head. He said: \"You did well, O 'Umar, when you found me prostrating and withdrew from me. Jibril came to me and said: 'Whoever from your community sends blessings upon you once, God sends blessings upon him tenfold and raises him by it ten degrees.'\""],[6590,"The heat of Hell upon my community is only like the heat of a bathhouse."],[6591,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would put his head into my room while he was in i'tikaf, and I would comb his hair. He would not enter his house except for human need."],[6592,"It was my night, and the Prophet ﷺ was with me. Fatimah came to him, and 'Ali preceded her. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"O 'Ali, you and your companions are in Paradise; you and your Shi'ah are in Paradise—except that among those who claim to love you are people who will distort Islam and then abandon it. They recite the Qur'an, but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They have a nickname: they are called the Rafidah. If you encounter them, fight them, for they are polytheists.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, what is their mark?\" He said: \"They do not attend Friday prayer or congregational prayer, and they defame the early predecessors.\""],[6593,"Whoever recites the Qur'an—or he said: whoever collects the Qur'an—has an answered supplication with God. If He wills, He may hasten it for him in this world, and if He wills, He may delay it for him in the Hereafter."],[6594,"He entered upon 'Ali, who called for his sword and brought out from inside the sword a piece of Arabian leather. He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not leave with us anything other than the Book of God that was revealed except that I have conveyed it—except this.\" He read it, and in it was: \"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Muhammad is the Messenger of God ﷺ. Every prophet has a sanctuary, and my sanctuary is Madinah. Whoever introduces an innovation therein or harbors an innovator, God will not accept from him any obligatory or supererogatory act.\""],[6595,"'Umar allotted for Usamah b. Zayd three thousand five hundred, and for his own son three thousand. 'Abd Allah said to his father: \"Why did you favor Usamah over me? By God, he did not precede me to any scene of battle.\" He said: \"Because Zayd was dearer to the Messenger of God ﷺ than your father, and Usamah was dearer to the Messenger of God ﷺ than you. So I preferred the beloved of the Messenger of God ﷺ over my own beloved.\""],[6596,"'Umar b. al-Khattab proposed to 'Ali for Umm Kulthum. 'Ali said: \"She is too young for that.\" 'Umar said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Every bond and lineage will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my bond and my lineage.' So I wanted to have a bond and lineage from the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" 'Ali said to al-Hasan and al-Husayn: \"Marry your paternal uncle.\" They said: \"She is a woman among women; she chooses for herself.\" 'Ali stood up angry, and al-Hasan grabbed his garment and said: \"We cannot bear your separation, O father.\""],[6597,"We were in a house with a group of the Ansar and the Muhajirun. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us, and every man made room hoping that he would sit beside him. Then he went to the door and took hold of its two posts and said: \"The leaders are from Quraysh. I have a great right over you, and they have that right as long as they do three things: when mercy is sought from them, they show mercy; when they judge, they act justly; and when they make a covenant, they fulfill it. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people.\""],[6598,"Spread peace, for it brings God's pleasure."],[6599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught al-Hasan b. Ali that when he entered the mosque he should send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and say: \"O Allah, forgive us our sins and open for us the gates of Your mercy,\" and when he left he should send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and say: \"O Allah, open for us the gates of Your bounty.\""],[6600,"Did you hear this from Yahya? He said: \"More than a hundred times.\" Abu Hafs said: I saw Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi come to the circle of Yahya b. Said and Muadh b. Muadh, and he sat outside the circle on Friday before the prayer. Yahya said to him: \"Enter the circle.\" Abd al-Rahman said to him: \"You narrated to me from Muhammad b. Ajlan, from Amr b. Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sitting in circles on Friday before the imam comes out.\" Yahya said to him: \"I saw Habib b. al-Shahid, Hisham b. Hassan, and Said b. Abi Aruba sitting in circles on Friday before the imam came out.\" Abd al-Rahman said: \"These people knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sitting in circles on Friday, yet they still did it.\" Yahya fell silent."],[6601,"I was asking people about Adi b. Hatim while he was beside me in Kufa. I went to him and said: \"What is this hadith that has reached me from you?\" He said: \"The Prophet ﷺ was sent when he was sent, and I was among the people who most detested him, until I fled and reached the land of Syria. While I was in that state, news reached us that Khalid b. al-Walid had been dispatched against us. I fled until I reached the land of the Byzantines. While I was sitting in the shade of a wall, a woman in a howdah approached. I went to her and found she was my aunt. She said: 'O Adi b. Hatim, you fled and left me. As soon as you left us, Khalid b. al-Walid raided us in the morning, took the women and children captive, and killed the fighters. They took us until we came to Madinah. One day as I was sitting, the Prophet ﷺ passed by me on his way to prayer. I said: \"O Muhammad, the father has perished and the one who should come has fled. Free me, may Allah free you.\" He said: \"Who is your one who should come?\" I said: \"Adi b. Hatim.\" He said: \"The one who fled from Allah and His Messenger?\" and went on. The next day he passed by me on his way to prayer. I said: \"O Muhammad, the father has perished and the one who should come has fled. Free me, may Allah free you.\" He said: \"Who is your one who should come?\" I said: \"Adi b. Hatim.\" He said: \"The one who fled from Allah and His Messenger,\" and went on without answering me. On the third day he passed by, and I was too shy to say anything to him. Ali b. Abi Talib nudged me, so I said: \"O Muhammad, the father has perished and the one who should come has fled. Free me, may Allah free you.\" He said: \"Who is your one who should come?\" I said: \"Adi b. Hatim.\" He said: \"The one who fled from Allah and His Messenger.\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Allah has freed you. Stay here and do not leave until something comes to us so we can equip you.\" I stayed three days. Then a caravan from Sarh arrived carrying food. He mounted me on this camel and gave me provisions. \"O Adi b. Hatim, go to him, go to him, and take your share from him before someone unlike you from your people beats you to it.\" So I set out until I came to Madinah. The people looked at me and said, \"Adi b. Hatim has come.\" I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"O Adi b. Hatim, are you the one who fled from Allah and His Messenger?\" I said: \"I have a religion.\" He said: \"I know your religion better than you. Are you not a Rakusi? Are you not a chief of your people? Do you not take a quarter of the spoils?\" I felt ashamed. He said: \"Nothing prevents you from submitting except that you see those around us in need, and you see people united against us. O Adi, the time is near when a woman will travel from al-Hirah to the House without any protection, and the time is near when the treasures of Kisra will be opened for us.\" I said: \"Kisra b. Hurmuz?\" He said: \"Kisra b. Hurmuz. And the time is near when a man will take out his charity and not find anyone to accept it from him.\" He said: \"I was among the first cavalry to raid the treasures of Kisra, and I saw a woman travel from al-Hirah until she reached Makkah without any protection. By Allah, the third will surely happen, for the word of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is true.\""],[6602,"Muawiya heard that Ibn al-Zubayr was cursing Abu Sufyan. He said: \"By my life, how bad is what he says about his uncle. But I will not say anything about Abu Abdullah except good, may Allah have mercy on him. He was a righteous man. Abu Sufyan went out to his desert estate with Hind riding behind him, and I went walking in front of her, as I was a boy on my donkey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with us. Abu Sufyan said: 'Get down, O Muawiya, so that Muhammad can ride.' I got off the donkey, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode it. He rode ahead of them for a little while, then turned to them and said: 'O Abu Sufyan b. Harb and O Hind bt. Utba, by Allah, you will surely die, then you will surely be resurrected, then the doer of good will enter Paradise and the doer of evil will enter the Fire. What I say to you is true, and you are the first of those warned.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: 'Ha Mim. The revelation from the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate' until he reached: 'They said: We come willingly.' Abu Sufyan said to him: 'Have you finished, O Muhammad?' He said: 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got off the donkey, and I rode it. Hind turned to Abu Sufyan and said: 'For this lying sorcerer you made my son get down?' He said: 'By Allah, he is neither a sorcerer nor a liar.'\""],[6603,"The Quran is one million and twenty-seven thousand letters. Whoever reads it patiently, seeking reward, will have for every letter a spouse from the houris with wide eyes."],[6604,"Whoever is given a favor should repay it. If he cannot find anything to repay it, he should praise the one who did it. Whoever does so has shown gratitude, and whoever leaves it has disbelieved. Whoever adorns himself with what he has not been given is like one who wears a garment of falsehood."],[6605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \"What is the righteousness of Hajj?\" He said: \"Feeding people and speaking kindly.\""],[6606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited to us: \"Every day He is in a matter.\" We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is that matter?\" He said: \"To forgive a sin, relieve a distress, raise a people, and lower others.\""],[6607,"A person will have what he earns, and upon him is what he acquires, and every person will be with those he loves."],[6608,"I am with My servant as long as he remembers Me and his lips move with My mention."],[6609,"Whoever is cupped on the morning of the seventeenth, it will be a cure for him from every disease."],[6610,"The womb is a branch attached to the Throne. The one who maintains ties is not the one who reciprocates, but the one who maintains ties is the one who, when his womb ties are severed, reconnects them."],[6611,"Two or more constitute a congregation."],[6612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had dispatched a military detachment, so I bade farewell to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A man who was riding on a saddle said to me: 'I will not go out unless you give me three dinars.' I disliked returning to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after I had bidden him farewell, so I gave them to him. When I completed my military expedition, I informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Give them to him; they are his share of his expedition in this world and the Hereafter.'"],[6613,"The witr is upon the people of the Quran."],[6614,"He who seeks guidance (istikharah) is not disappointed, he who seeks counsel is not regretful, and he who is moderate is not in need."],[6615,"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should we not enjoin good until we act upon all of it, and not forbid evil until we avoid all of it?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Rather, enjoin good even if you do not act upon all of it, and forbid evil even if you do not avoid all of it.'"],[6616,"Whoever is put in charge of any community of my ummah, small or large, and does not deal justly with them, Allah will cast him on his face into the Fire."],[6617,"When one of you is invited and he comes with the messenger, that is his permission."],[6618,"Knowledge is among the Quraysh, and trustworthiness is among the Azd."],[6619,"The Prophet ﷺ used to complete the bowing and prostration, and lighten the standing and sitting in the prayer."],[6620,"Whoever drags his clothes, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[6621,"My believing servant is dearer to Me than some of My angels."],[6622,"The first to enter the Fire from this ummah are the tyrants/oppressors."],[6623,"If a day passes me by in which I do not increase in knowledge, then there is no blessing in the rising of the sun of that day."],[6624,"I was with Ibn Mas'ud at Arafah, and Uthman prayed Zuhr as four rak'ahs and Asr as four rak'ahs. Ibn Mas'ud said: \"Here I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with Abu Bakr and Umar, and they did not pray except two rak'ahs.\" I said: \"Will you not go to him?\" He said: \"Be quiet, for disagreement is evil.\""],[6625,"It was said to him: \"Did you see Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes, he died while young, the most resembling of people to him ﷺ. Had it been decreed that there be a prophet after him, his son Ibrahim would have lived.\""],[6626,"A woman's travel with her servant is a loss."],[6627,"Whoever gives a man security for his blood and then kills him, I am innocent of the killer, even if the victim is a disbeliever."],[6628,"Whoever is constant in these prescribed prayers in congregation will be the first to cross the Sirat like dazzling lightning, and Allah will gather him in the first group of the followers, and for each day and night that he is constant in them, he will have the reward of a thousand martyrs killed in the path of Allah."],[6629,"Ali said to me: \"O Usamah, what is wrong with you that you do not come out with us? You are only a man from the Ahl al-Bayt.\" I said: \"You have spoken the truth. There is no one more deserving for me to go out with than you, but by Allah, I will not fight those who pray after the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Did you not leave him, or split open his heart and look into it?'\""],[6630,"The woman with istihadah performs ghusl from one menstrual period to the next."],[6631,"Whoever walks in the darkness of the night to the mosques, Allah will give him light on the Day of Resurrection."],[6632,"The Prophet ﷺ ate from the shoulder of a sheep, then prayed and did not perform wudu."],[6633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a ring of gold, and he flung it away among his companions, then said: 'I will never wear it again.' So the people flung away their rings. Then he took a ring of silver, with which he used to seal documents, until it fell into the well of Aris and was lost."],[6634,"Bring a quarter of the tithe: when it reaches two hundred dirhams, five dirhams are due."],[6635,"There is no zakat on what is less than five awsuq; there is no zakat on what is less than five dhawd; and there is no zakat on what is less than five awaq."],[6636,"No people keep a dog—except a hunting dog (and Abu Hurayrah added: \"or a farm dog\")—but that their rewards are diminished every night by two qirats."],[6637,"A child cannot repay his parent, unless he finds him enslaved and buys him and then sets him free."],[6638,"Sometimes I would go out with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Fitr or Adha, and he would not pray before it or after it."],[6639,"I met my uncle carrying the standard and said, \"Where are you heading?\" He replied, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and he ordered me to kill him and take his property.\""],[6640,"Allah has not permitted a prophet to chant the Qur'an melodiously."],[6641,"He used to say: \"Allah hears the one who praises Him; our Lord, to You be praise.\" Then, before prostrating, he would say: \"O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so.\" Then he would say the takbir and prostrate, until Allah revealed: \"You have no part in the matter\" (Qur'an 3:128)."],[6642,"Whoever is trusted by a man with his blood and then kills him, I am innocent of the killer, even if the victim is a disbeliever."],[6643,"They both heard the Prophet ﷺ say at the end of his sermon: \"Whoever guards these prescribed prayers in congregation will be the first to cross the Sirat like flashing lightning, and Allah will gather him in the first group of the followers, and for every day and night that he guards them he will have the reward of a thousand martyrs killed in the path of Allah.\""],[6644,"They heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proclaim the talbiyah for both together: \"Labbayk, 'umrah and hajj.\""],[6645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would find a man's shoulder protruding beyond his companion's, and he would straighten it and say: \"Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.\""],[6646,"On Friday at dawn prayer he used to recite: \"Alif Lam Mim, the revelation\" (Surah al-Sajdah) and \"Has there come upon man\" (Surah al-Insan)."],[6647,"Whoever prays one rak'ah of the dawn prayer and then the sun rises, let him pray another one to it."],[6648,"He would not say the salam in the two rak'ahs of witr."],[6649,"The mouse is a metamorphosis, and the sign of that is that it drinks sheep's milk but does not drink camel's milk."],[6650,"When he saw something he liked, he would say: “Our Lord, by Your blessing righteous deeds are completed, so to You belongs praise.” And when he saw something he disliked, he would say: “Praise belongs to Allah in every situation.”"],[6651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would see semen on a garment of one of us and then rub it off."],[6652,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and I recognized in his face that something had occurred. He did not speak until he performed ablution, then he went out and ascended the pulpit. I clung to the room. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, Allah says: Command the right and forbid the wrong before you call upon Me and I do not answer you, and you ask Me and I do not give you, and you seek My aid and I do not aid you. He did not add anything to them until he returned."],[6653,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ continue the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[6654,"While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Hijr, al-Hakam b. Abi al-As passed by, and the Prophet ﷺ said: Woe to my ummah from what is in the loins of this one."],[6655,"If one of you passes his hand to his penis, let him perform ablution."],[6656,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper."],[6657,"Whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ, and whoever goes to him without believing him, no prayer is accepted from him for forty days."],[6658,"Verily the angels curse one of you when he points at his brother with a piece of iron, even if he is his full brother."],[6659,"Perish the filthy ones."],[6660,"Three things do not break the fast: cupping, vomiting, and wet dreams."],[6661,"When we saw a man curse his brother, we considered that he had committed one of the major sins."],[6662,"Flesh that grows from unlawful earnings will not enter Paradise; the Fire is more deserving of it."],[6663,"Whoever is taken to account for his deeds will be ruined."],[6664,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque on Friday, he would greet those sitting near his pulpit; then when he ascended the pulpit, he would turn to the people and greet them."],[6665,"I said: O Messenger of God, a man whose mouth is dry—should he use the toothstick? He said: 'Yes.' I said: How should he do it? He said: 'He should put his finger in his mouth.'"],[6666,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I want to go on a military expedition in the path of God. He said: 'You should go to Syria, and then adhere to Ascalon of Syria; for when the mill turns among my community, its people will be in ease and well-being.'"],[6667,"Those before you were destroyed only because they magnified their kings by standing and sitting for them."],[6668,"He forbade temporary marriage (mut'a)."],[6669,"There is no jizya (poll tax) upon a Muslim."],[6670,"Three men from those before you went out to get provisions for their families, and rain overtook them, so they took refuge in a cave."],[6671,"I was eager to find someone to tell me that the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the Duha prayer, but I found no one to tell me except Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib. She told me: The Messenger of God ﷺ came to me after the day had risen on the day of the conquest of Makkah. He ordered a garment, and it was screened for him, then he performed ghusl. Then he stood and prayed eight rak'ahs. I do not know whether his standing, bowing, or prostration was longer—all of that was similar in them. I did not see him pray before it or after it."],[6672,"Whoever is two-faced in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[6673,"A person’s nobility is his piety, his manliness is his intellect, and his lineage is his character."],[6674,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head toward the sky and said: “The stars are a safeguard for the inhabitants of the sky, and I am a safeguard for my Companions, and my Companions are a safeguard for my Ummah.”"],[6675,"At the top of every camel’s hump is a devil, so humble them (i.e., the camels) by using them."],[6676,"An angel came to me who had never descended to the earth before, with a message from my Lord. He placed one foot above the lowest heaven and the other on the earth, and it could bear him."],[6677,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[6678,"One of the Banu Ja‘far b. Abi Talib came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, send with me someone to buy me sandals and a ring.” So the Prophet ﷺ called Bilal b. Rabah and said: “Go to the market and buy him sandals; let them be new, and not black. And buy him a ring whose stone is carnelian.”"],[6679,"Indeed, Allah has placed truth upon the tongue and heart of ‘Umar, and he speaks by it."],[6680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: “Alif Lam Mim Tanzil” (Surah al-Sajdah) and “Hal ata ‘ala al-insan” (Surah al-Insan)."],[6681,"To You all hopes come to an end, O Giver of well-being."],[6682,"Al-Ramlah is al-Rabwah."],[6683,"There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah than these ten days (of Dhu al-Hijjah).” They said: “Not even jihad in the cause of Allah?” He said: “Not even jihad in the cause of Allah, except for a man who goes out with his life and wealth and returns with neither.”"],[6684,"The Prophet ﷺ was not prevented from reciting the Qur'an except by major ritual impurity."],[6685,"When we prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' none of us would bend his back until he was upright in prostration."],[6686,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment?' He said, 'Does every one of you find two garments?'"],[6687,"When the verse 'And those who hoard gold and silver' was revealed, they said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what wealth should we hoard?' He said, 'A grateful heart, a remembering tongue, and a righteous wife.'"],[6688,"A man made a slave a mudabbar (one to be freed upon his death) while he was in need, so the Prophet ﷺ sold him."],[6689,"These privies are attended by devils, so when one of you enters it let him say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils.'"],[6690,"Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."],[6691,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us last year and said: 'Indeed, nothing better has been distributed among people than well-being after certainty. Verily, righteousness and truthfulness are in Paradise, and verily, lying and wickedness are in the Fire.'"],[6692,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the going out of young women on the two Eids. He said: 'Let them go out.' It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if she does not have a garment?' He said: 'Let her wear the garment of her companion. Have you not heard that Allah says: And to complete the number and to magnify Allah for that which He has guided you.'"],[6693,"A woman extended her hand with a letter to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he withheld his hand from her. She said, 'Why did you withhold your hand from me?' He said, 'A man or a woman?' She said, 'A woman.' He said, 'If you were a woman, you would have changed your nails with henna.'"],[6694,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'If we have a leader who acts contrary to obedience to Allah, should we listen and obey?' He turned away from him, then he repeated it, and he turned away from him, then he said: 'They bear what they are burdened with, and you bear what you are burdened with.'"],[6695,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn and circumcised them on the seventh day."],[6696,"The safety of the earth from flooding is the rainbow, and the safety of my community from dissension is allegiance to Quraysh—Quraysh are the people of Allah, (he said it) three times. If any Arab tribe opposes them, they become the party of Iblis."],[6697,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a deceased person after he had been buried."],[6698,"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have set the time of the Isha prayer at midnight."],[6699,"He used to pray on his mount whichever direction it faced. He was asked, 'Is it a Sunnah?' He said, 'A Sunnah.' They said, 'Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He smiled and said, 'I heard it.'"],[6700,"He entered the state of ihram for Hajj when his mount set off with him, and he said, 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enter ihram when his mount set off with him.'"],[6701,"During the illness in which he died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Pour over me from seven water skins whose mouths have not been untied, so that I may give my final instructions to the people.' Aisha said, 'So we seated him in a tub belonging to Hafsa and poured water over him from those skins.'"],[6702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Aktham b. Abi al-Jawn al-Khuza'i, 'Go on military expeditions with people other than your own tribe, and your character will improve and you will be honored by your companions. O Aktham, the best number of companions is four, the best vanguard is forty, the best detachment is four hundred, and the best army is four thousand. Twelve thousand will never be defeated due to lack of numbers.'"],[6703,"Do not make use of anything from a dead animal, neither its hide nor its sinew."],[6704,"Jibril came to me with something like a white mirror in his hand, in which there was a black spot. I said, 'What is this, O Jibril?' He said, 'This is Friday. Your Lord sent it to you to be a festival for you and for your community after you.' I said, 'What do we have in it?' He said, 'You have abundant good. You are the last and the foremost on the Day of Resurrection. In it there is an hour in which no Muslim servant praying asks Allah for anything but He gives it to him.' I said, 'What is this black spot?' He said, 'This is the hour. It occurs on Friday, which is the master of days, and we call it the Day of Increase.' I said, 'O Jibril, what is the Increase?' He said, 'Your Lord has taken a valley in Paradise, broad, of white musk. When it is Friday among the days of the Hereafter, the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, descends from His Throne to His Footstool. The Footstool is surrounded by pulpits of light, and the prophets sit upon them. The pulpits are surrounded by chairs of gold, and the martyrs sit upon them. The people of the chambers come down from their chambers and sit on dunes of musk, not seeing that those on the chairs and pulpits have any superiority over them in the assembly. The Owner of Majesty and Honor appears to them and says, \"Ask Me.\" They say, \"We ask You for Your pleasure, O Lord.\" He says, \"My pleasure has caused you to dwell in My abode and granted you My honor.\" Then He says, \"Ask Me.\" They all say, \"We ask You for Your pleasure.\" He makes them testify to His pleasure. Then He says, \"Ask Me.\" They ask Him until every servant among them has finished. Then He bestows upon them what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined.'"],[6705,"Hakim b. Hizam bought food supplies and sold them before taking possession. Umar forbade him and said, 'Indeed the Prophet ﷺ forbade selling food before taking possession.' So he returned his capital to him."],[6706,"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I saw written on the gate of Paradise: 'Charity is rewarded tenfold, and a loan eighteenfold.' I said, 'O Jibril, why is a loan better than charity?' He said, 'Because a beggar asks while he has something, but one who seeks a loan does so only out of need.'"],[6707,"Anas b. Malik used to place his hands over his ears and say, 'May they be deaf if I did not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\"'"],[6708,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the fetus, and he said: \"Its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother.\""],[6709,"The wailing women will have upon them garments of tar."],[6710,"Hajj is jihad, and 'umrah is voluntary."],[6711,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was eating, and he said: \"Come.\" I said: \"I am fasting.\" He said: \"Come, let me tell you: Allah has relieved the traveler of fasting and half of the prayer.\""],[6712,"Abdullah b. Umar accompanied me and a companion of mine as I was leaving Madinah for Iraq. When he was about to turn back, he said: \"I have nothing to give you two, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When Allah is entrusted with something, He preserves it.' I entrust Allah with your religion, your trusts, and the final outcomes of your deeds.\""],[6713,"Whoever hates Umar has hated me, and whoever loves Umar has loved me. Allah boasted to the angels about the people on the evening of Arafah in general, and He boasted about Umar in particular. He has not sent any prophet except that there was in his nation a muhaddath, and if there is one in my nation among them, it is Umar.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how is he a muhaddath?\" He said: \"The angels speak upon his tongue.\""],[6714,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar prostrated in [Surah] Sad."],[6715,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth and children, and my father wants to take all of my wealth.\" He said: \"You and your wealth belong to your father.\""],[6716,"I asked al-Minhal about currency exchange, and he said: \"I and a partner of mine bought hand-to-hand and deferred for deferred.\" We mentioned that to al-Bara' b. 'Azib, and he said: \"I and my partner Zayd b. Arqam did that.\" We mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"What was hand-to-hand, take it; and what was deferred, leave it.\""],[6717,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[6718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Abu Taybah, and he cupped him at the setting of the sun, at the time of breaking the fast. Then he asked him: \"How much is your due?\" He said: \"Two sa's.\" So he reduced it by one sa'."],[6719,"The funeral procession for which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood was the funeral of a Jew, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Its odor annoyed me.\""],[6720,"Salama, the nursemaid of Ibrahim the son of the Prophet ﷺ, said: 'O Messenger of God, you give glad tidings to men of every good but you do not give glad tidings to women?' He said: 'Did your companions send you for this?' She said: 'Yes, they ordered me.' He said: 'Would not any one of you be pleased that when she is pregnant from her husband and he is pleased with her, she has the like of the reward of one who fasts and stands in prayer in the path of God? Then when labour pains strike her, the inhabitants of heaven and earth do not know what has been hidden for her of delight of the eyes. Then when she gives birth, no sip comes out of her milk nor does the child suck a suck except that for every sip and every suck there is a good deed for her. Then if the child keeps her awake a night, she has the like of the reward of seventy slaves whom she frees in the path of God. Salama, do you know for whom I intend this? For the women who are content, righteous, obedient to their husbands, those who do not deny the husband's favours.'"],[6721,"When the call to the Maghrib prayer was given, the people would rush to the pillars, praying two rak'as at a time, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was among them."],[6722,"She said: 'O Messenger of God, advise me.' He said: 'Abandon sins, for that is the best emigration. Guard the obligatory duties, for that is the best jihad. And increase in remembrance of God, for you will not come to God with anything more beloved to Him than abundance of His remembrance.'"],[6723,"Indeed, part of honouring the majesty of God is honouring the grey-haired Muslim, the just ruler, and the carrier of the Qur'an who does not go to extremes in it nor neglect it."],[6724,"We raided with the Messenger of God ﷺ and captured some sheep. The Messenger of God ﷺ divided a portion of them among us and placed the remainder in the spoils."],[6725,"When God defeated the polytheists on the day of Hawazin at Hunayn, the Messenger of God ﷺ appointed Abu 'Amir al-Ash'ari over the cavalry of pursuit. He pursued them, and among those he pursued, Ibn Durayd ibn al-Simmah confronted him. Ibn Durayd turned to him and killed Abu 'Amir and took the banner. I rushed at Ibn Durayd and killed him and took the banner. Then I returned to find the people. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw me carrying the banner, he said: 'Has Abu 'Amir been killed?' I said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hands supplicating for Abu 'Amir and said: 'O God, give Your servant Abu 'Amir and place him among the most numerous on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[6726,"We camped at Dabiq and Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah was over us. Habib ibn Maslamah heard that the ruler of Cyprus had gone out intending the patrician of Adharbijan, and with him were emeralds, rubies, pearls, gold and silk brocade. He went out with cavalry and killed him and brought what was with him. Abu 'Ubaydah wanted to take a fifth of it. Habib said: 'Do not deprive me of it; it is provision God has provided me, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ assign the spoils to the killer.' Mu'adh said: 'Gently, O Habib, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A person only has what his leader is pleased to give.'"],[6727,"He used to deliver two sermons on Friday, sitting between them."],[6728,"Two bands of my community God has protected from the Fire: a band that raids India and a band that will be with Jesus son of Mary."],[6729,"Dreams are of three kinds: among them are terrors from Satan to sadden the son of Adam, among them is what a man is concerned with in his waking state and then sees in his sleep, and among them is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood.' I said to him: 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[6730,"The farthest outposts of the Muslims will soon be at Salah, and Salah is near Khaybar."],[6731,"Moderation in spending is half of livelihood, friendliness to people is half of intelligence, and good questioning is half of knowledge."],[6732,"Whoever says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is greatest, and there is no might nor power except with Allah, an angel folds its wings over these words and does not return with anything until it reaches the Throne with them, and it does not pass by anything except that it sends blessings upon these words and upon the one who said them. And glorification is declaring Allah free from every evil. And whoever says: There is no might nor power except with Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent, Allah says: My servant has submitted and surrendered."],[6733,"He used to give one salutation, facing his face."],[6734,"If you wish, I will inform you about leadership. They said: What is it? He said: Its beginning is blame, its second is regret, and its third is punishment on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who is just."],[6735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in his Hajj which he performed, and he was pleased and happy with his Ummah because of what he saw of their unity and their great number. Then he returned sad. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you went out from me happy with your Ummah and returned to me sad? He said: I entered the Kaaba, and I wish that I had not entered it, fearing that I may cause hardship to my Ummah."],[6736,"The divorce of a slave woman is two pronouncements, and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles."],[6737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: Beware of oppression, for oppression will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity or indecency. Beware of miserliness, for miserliness destroyed those before you: it commanded them to sever their ties of kinship and they severed them. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is most virtuous? He said: That your blood be spilled and your horse be hamstrung. He said: Which emigration is most virtuous? He said: That you abandon what your Lord dislikes. There are two emigrations: an emigration for the settled and an emigration for the bedouin. As for the emigration of the bedouin, when he is called he answers, and when he is commanded he obeys. As for the emigration of the settled, it is the more severe of the two in trial and the greater of the two in reward."],[6738,"A prayer in the Sacred Mosque is more virtuous than a hundred prayers elsewhere."],[6739,"The two sons of al-‘As are believers, and ‘Amr b. al-‘As is in Paradise."],[6740,"O Messenger of Allah, the women of Banu al-Mughira have held their mourning for al-Walid b. al-Walid b. al-Mughira. So he permitted her, and she stood saying: I weep for al-Walid b. al-Walid b. al-Mughira; I weep for al-Walid b. al-Walid, the brother of the clan."],[6741,"Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, Allah will free, for every limb of the freed one, a limb of him from the Fire."],[6742,"When the Prophet ﷺ ordered the expulsion of Banu al-Nadir, some of their people came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you have ordered our expulsion, and we have debts owed to us by people that have not yet become due. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Reduce the amount and collect early."],[6743,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ‘Umar did not appoint a judge. The first to appoint a judge was ‘Umar. He said: Relieve me of the people in disputes over a dirham or two."],[6744,"Judges are three: two are in the Fire and one is in Paradise. A man who sits for the people and judges between them without knowledge of judging, thus destroying their rights; a man who has knowledge but acts unjustly while knowing; and a man who has knowledge and judges by his knowledge with truth—this one is in Paradise."],[6745,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, my knee touching his knee, when someone came to him and clung to his ear. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed, and blood rushed to his forehead. Then he said: 'This is the messenger of Amir b. al-Tufayl threatening me and threatening those beside me. But Allah has sufficed me against him through my son from the descendants of Isma'il, through the two sons of Qaylah.' Hisham said: 'Meaning the Ansar.'"],[6746,"I have not seen anyone among the people after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more forbearing than Mu'awiyah."],[6747,"The Milky Way in the sky is the sweat of the serpent beneath the Throne."],[6748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought protection for me with the Opening of the Book, blowing spittle."],[6749,"Nu'ayman said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a severe fever.' He said: 'Where are you, O Nu'ayman, compared to Mahya'ah?' And it was an unhealthy land."],[6750,"A man complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about poor work. He said: 'Lord, small,' then he asked him and said: 'A foal, or a slave girl, or a servant boy.'"],[6751,"I heard a man ask Ibn 'Umar: 'Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I jest, but I speak only the truth\"?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[6752,"He said on the day of Hunayn at al-Ji'irranah: 'Ten things are permissible for the Muslims in their military expeditions: honey, water, oil, vinegar, salt, earth, stone, wood as long as it is not carved, fresh hide, and food that is taken out.'"],[6753,"Nothing infects anything. A Bedouin said: 'O Messenger of Allah, camels are in the sands like gazelles; a camel falls among them with a sore on its lip or at the base of its tail like the first sign of mange, and no camel remains among them but that it becomes mangy.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A defect and a decree.'"],[6754,"I was riding behind Ibn 'Umar when a shepherd passed by playing a pipe. He struck the face of the she-camel and turned her away from the road, then put his fingers in his ears and said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do this.'"],[6755,"Whoever sells fruit and it is stricken by a calamity, let him not take anything from his brother. Why should any of you take the wealth of his Muslim brother?"],[6756,"Hisham b. 'Abd al-Malik paid off seven thousand dinars on behalf of al-Zuhri. Then Hisham said to al-Zuhri: 'Do not repeat the like of this.' Al-Zuhri said: 'O Commander of the Faithful.'"],[6757,"\"Islam is built on five: bearing witness that there is no god but Allah, alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and messenger; establishing prayer; giving zakat; performing Hajj to the House; and fasting Ramadan.\" A man kept repeating them, saying: 'Fasting comes before Hajj.' 'Abd Allah said: \"And performing Hajj to the House, and fasting Ramadan.\""],[6758,"Whoever buys a sheep that has been left unmilked for a time (to increase its milk) and then milks it for three days has the option: if he wishes he may keep it, or else he may return it along with a sa' of dates."],[6759,"Whoever honors a person of innovation has helped in the destruction of Islam."],[6760,"I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years, and he never said to me about something I did: 'Why did you do such and such?' nor about something I did not do: 'Why did you not do such and such?'"],[6761,"The Prophet ﷺ cut off the hand of a thief."],[6762,"Let one of you eat with his right hand and drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand, takes with his left hand, and gives with his left hand."],[6763,"Allah looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives all of His creation except an idolater or one harboring malice."],[6764,"He used to recite ten verses from the end of Surah Al 'Imran every night."],[6765,"There will be in this community people who say there is no divine decree—they are the Magians of this community."],[6766,"'Ali b. Abi Talib wrote a document for me and said: The Prophet ﷺ commanded me with it. He said: 'When you go to bed, say: I seek refuge in the noble face of Allah and His perfect words from the evil of what You seize by the forelock. O Allah, You remove debt and sin. O Allah, Your army is not defeated, Your promise is not broken, and the wealth of the wealthy avails not against You. Glory be to You and praise.' Abu Ishaq said: I mentioned it to Abu Maysarah al-Hamdani, and he narrated the like of it to me from 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, except that he said: 'from the evil of what You grasp by the forelock.'"],[6767,"By Allah, Allah does not make beautiful the physical form and character of a man and then have the Fire consume him ever."],[6768,"May Allah brighten [the face of] a servant who hears my words and does not add anything to them. Many a bearer of a word [conveys it] to one more receptive than himself. Three things no believer's heart will be corrupted by: sincerity to Allah, giving good counsel to those in authority, and holding fast to the community of Muslims, for their supplication encompasses [all] behind them."],[6769,"Whoever wears silk in this world will be deprived of it in the Hereafter."],[6770,"He performed ablution three times [for each body part] and said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution like this ablution of mine, like this.'"],[6771,"There is no newborn except that Satan touches him at birth, so he cries out loudly from his touch, except Maryam and her son.' Then Abu Hurayrah says: 'Recite, if you wish: \"And I seek refuge for her and her offspring from Satan the accursed.\"'"],[6772,"The Prophet ﷺ turned to the people and said: 'While a man was driving a cow, he intended to ride it. It turned to him and said: We were not created for this; we were created only for plowing.' Those around him said: 'Glory be to Allah! A cow spoke?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I believe in it, and Abu Bakr and 'Umar,' though they were not there. Then he said: 'A man said: While I was among my sheep grazing them, a wolf came and took a sheep. I pursued it and took it back from him. He said: What will you do on the Day of the Beast when it will have no shepherd but me?' They said: 'Glory be to Allah! A wolf spoke?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I believe in it, and Abu Bakr and 'Umar,' though they were not there."],[6773,"Judges are three: two in the Fire and one in Paradise. A judge who abandons the truth while knowing it, and a judge who judges without truth while not knowing [it], so he destroys people's rights—these two are in the Fire. And a judge who judges with truth, this one is in Paradise."],[6774,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the time of prayer. When the sun declined, Bilal called the adhan for Zuhr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him, so he performed the iqamah and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for 'Asr when we thought a man's shadow was longer than him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him, so he performed the iqamah and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for Maghrib when the sun set. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him, so he performed the iqamah and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for 'Isha when the whiteness of day was gone, that is the twilight. Then he ordered him, so he performed the iqamah and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for Fajr when dawn broke. He ordered him, so he performed the iqamah and he prayed. Then Bilal called the adhan the next day for Zuhr when the sun declined. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed it until the shadow of everything was equal to it. He performed the iqamah and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for 'Asr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed it until the shadow of everything was twice its length. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him, so he performed the iqamah and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for Maghrib when the sun set. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed it until the whiteness of day was almost gone, that is the first of twilight as it appears. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him, so he performed the iqamah and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for 'Isha when the twilight disappeared. We slept, then woke up several times. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: 'No one among the people is waiting for this prayer except you. You will remain in prayer as long as you wait for it. Were it not that I would make it difficult for my Ummah, I would have ordered delaying this prayer until midnight or close to midnight.' Then he called the adhan for Fajr and delayed it until the sun was almost about to rise. He ordered him, so he performed the iqamah and he prayed. Then he said: 'The time is between these two times.'"],[6775,"No people withhold zakah except that Allah afflicts them with years [of drought]."],[6776,"You have a right over Quraysh, and they have a right over you. As long as they make covenants, they fulfill them; when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; and when they judge, they are just; and when they are entrusted, they deliver. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."],[6777,"Adam is in the lowest heaven, and 'Isa and Yahya are in the second, and Yusuf is in the third, and Idris is in the fourth, and Harun is in the fifth, and Musa is in the sixth, and Ibrahim is in the seventh."],[6778,"There will be a migration after a migration. The best people on earth will be those who migrate to the place of Ibrahim's migration ﷺ . The worst of its people will remain in it. The earth will cast them out, and Allah's self will loathe them. Then Allah will send upon them a fire that will gather them with the apes and pigs. It will rest when they rest, and move when they move, and consume whoever lags behind. A people will be raised in the east; whenever a generation arises, a generation will be cut off. The Dajjal will emerge among them."],[6779,"I came to pray Fajr while the Prophet ﷺ was in prayer. I prayed two rak'ahs, then joined the prayer. When he finished, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Which of them did you count, the first two or the last two?'"],[6780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to urinate in his bathing place, and said: “It causes waswas (whisperings/obsessive doubts).”"],[6781,"Whoever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion."],[6782,"Do not curse the night and the day, nor the sun, nor the moon, nor the winds, for they are a mercy for some people and a punishment for others."],[6783,"Was permission granted for women to pray while mounted on riding animals? She said: “Permission was not granted for them in that, neither in hardship nor in ease.”"],[6784,"From Ibn ʿUmar, that he proposed marriage to the daughter of Nuʿaym b. ʿAbd Allah al-ʿAdawi al-Nahham, and she was a virgin. Nuʿaym said to him: “I have an orphan under my care, and I will not prefer anyone over him.” The mother of the girl, the wife of Nuʿaym, went out until she came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him about that, and she informed the Prophet ﷺ of her own and her daughter's aversion to the orphan. The Prophet ﷺ sent for her father and said: “Make her and her daughter content.”"],[6785,"Revere Allah, and He will forgive you."],[6786,"Remorse is repentance."],[6787,"Paradise is adorned for Ramadan from the beginning of the year to the next year. When the first day of Ramadan comes, a wind blows from beneath the Throne and causes the leaves of Paradise to rustle over the ḥūr al-ʿīn, and they say: “O Lord, appoint for us spouses from Your servants by whom our eyes will be delighted, and their eyes will be delighted by us.”"],[6788,"Let none of you come to me on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck that bellows, and he says: “O Muhammad,” and I say: “I have no power to do anything for you; you have been conveyed the message.” Let none of you come to me on the Day of Resurrection with a sheep on his neck that bleats, and he says: “O Muhammad,” and I say: “I have no power to do anything for you; you have been conveyed the message.”"],[6789,"He entered upon ʿĀʾishah on the day of ʿArafah and said: “Give me something to drink.” ʿĀʾishah said: “O boy, give him honey to drink.” Then she said: “Are you not fasting, O Masrūq?” He said: “No, for I fear that it might be the day of sacrifice.” ʿĀʾishah said: “It is not that. The day of ʿArafah is the day the imam stands at ʿArafah, and the day of sacrifice is the day the imam slaughters. Have you not heard, O Masrūq, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ equated it with fasting a thousand days?”"],[6790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning a daughter, a son's daughter, and a full sister: that the daughter gets half, the son's daughter gets one-sixth, and the sister gets what remains."],[6791,"Regarding an ostrich egg: “fasting a day or feeding a poor person.”"],[6792,"When he sent out collectors of zakah, he commanded them that whatever they took of zakah should be placed among the relatives of those from whom it was taken, the closest then the next closest. If he had no relatives, then among the people of the clan, then among the needy neighbors and others."],[6793,"Whoever does good in what remains will be forgiven what has passed, and whoever does evil in what remains will be taken to account for what has passed and what remains."],[6794,"I have made obligatory upon you five prayers, and I have made a covenant with Myself that whoever guards them at their times, I will admit him to Paradise."],[6795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to a tribe of the Arabs calling them to Islam, but they did not accept the letter and returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said: 'Indeed, if I had sent it to a people on the coast of Oman from the Azd Shanu'ah, and they became Muslim, they would have accepted it.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to al-Julanda calling him to Islam, and he accepted it and became Muslim. He sent a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it arrived after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had passed away. Abu Bakr made the gift an inheritance and divided it between Fatimah and al-Abbas."],[6796,"Four hundred men from Daws came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Welcome to the people with the best faces, the sweetest mouths, and the greatest trustworthiness.'"],[6797,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[6798,"He would give salutations to his right and to his left, until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[6799,"I saw the first army of my nation that will ride the sea, and they have made [Paradise] obligatory. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah that I be with them.' He said: 'O Allah, make her among them.'"],[6800,"If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what women have introduced after him, he would have forbidden them from attending the mosques, just as the women of the Children of Israel were forbidden."],[6801,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a young man, and I fear hardship for myself, and I do not find the means to marry women. Do you permit me to castrate myself?' He said: He was silent. Then I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a young man, I do not find the means to marry women. Do you permit me to castrate myself?' And I said the third time the like of that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Abu Hurayrah, the pen has dried concerning what you will meet, so castrate yourself or leave it.'"],[6802,"Sulayman b. Dawud asked Allah for three things, and He gave him two, and I hope He gave him the third. He asked Him to judge with a judgment that coincides with His judgment, and he was given that. He asked Him for a kingdom that would not befit anyone after him, and he was given that. He asked Him that any servant who comes to the Sacred House (Bayt al-Maqdis) intending only to pray in it, that he would be free of his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him."],[6803,"I have been favored over people with four things: generosity, courage, frequent sexual intercourse, and great strength."],[6804,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray 'Asr when the sun was white and high."],[6805,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until when we were at the watering place that belonged to Sa'd, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, Ibrahim was Your servant and Your close friend, and he supplicated to You for the people of Makkah for blessing. Muhammad is Your servant and Your Messenger, and I supplicate to You for the people of Madinah that You bless them in their sa' and their mudd as You blessed the people of Makkah, and with the blessing, two blessings.\""],[6806,"When news reached him of the arrival of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he came to him as a delegate, accepted Islam, and asked him to write a document for him by which he would call to Islam. He wrote for him on a piece of leather: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a document from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, for Malik b. Ahmar and those Muslims who follow him, granting them security as long as they establish prayer, give zakat, follow the Muslims, avoid the polytheists, and render the fifth of the spoils, and the share of the debtors, and the share of such-and-such, and the share of such-and-such. They are secure with the protection of Allah and the protection of Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from one of the districts of Madinah intending to pray, but he found that the people had already prayed. So he went to his house, gathered his family, and then led them in prayer."],[6808,"You must observe the night prayer, even if it be a single rak'ah. One day he went out for the morning prayer and found a man performing rak'ahs, so he said: \"Will you not stop? Two prayers together?\""],[6809,"\"O Messenger of Allah, advise me.\" He said: \"Abandon sins, for that is the best emigration. Guard the obligatory prayers, for that is the best jihad. And remember Allah much, for you will not come to Allah with anything more beloved to Him than abundant remembrance of Him.\""],[6810,"He forbade eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, forbade nabidh in earthen jars, and forbade visiting graves. Then afterwards the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I had forbidden you from eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, so now eat as you wish. I had forbidden you from nabidh in jars, so drink, but every intoxicant is unlawful. I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them, but do not say anything that displeases Allah.\""],[6811,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best?\" He said: \"A word of truth in the presence of a tyrannical ruler.\""],[6812,"I asked 'A'ishah: \"What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in the witr prayer?\" She said: \"In the first rak'ah he would recite the Mother of the Qur'an and 'Say: He is Allah, the One,' in the second rak'ah the Mother of the Qur'an and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,' and in the third rak'ah the Mother of the Qur'an and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.'\""],[6813,"A leg of a wild donkey was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Kura' al-Ghamim, but he returned it to its owner, apologizing and saying: \"We are in a state of ihram.\""],[6814,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey, a man who was in ihram fell and died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him, shroud him in his garment, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[6815,"I said to 'Ali b. Abi Talib: \"People claim regarding the saying of Allah, exalted be His mention: 'And a witness from him follows him,' that you are the one who follows?\" He said: \"I wish I were him, but it is the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[6816,"Regarding His saying, the Exalted: “until when he reached his full strength” (Q 46:15 etc.), he said: thirty-three, and he is the one upon whom Jesus son of Mary ﷺ was raised."],[6817,"The world will not come to an end until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name."],[6818,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote to us while we were in the land of Juhaynah: Do not make use of anything from carrion, neither sinew nor hide."],[6819,"Abu Jandal b. Suhayl and al-Harith b. Mu'awiyah passed by Bilal, the muezzin of the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he was performing ablution at the ablution place of the mosque of Damascus. They asked him about wiping over the leather socks, and he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the head covering."],[6820,"We were forbidden to drink from the broken piece of a cup."],[6821,"Najdah wrote to Ibn 'Abbas asking him about some matters. I witnessed Ibn 'Abbas when he read the letter and when he wrote his reply. Ibn 'Abbas said: Were it not that I might turn him away from an error he has fallen into, I would not write to him, nor would it be a favor to him. So he wrote to him: You asked about the share of the near relatives whose matter God has mentioned. We used to consider that we were the relatives of the Messenger of God ﷺ, but our people refused that to us. You asked about the orphan: when does his orphanhood end? When he reaches marriageable age and sound judgment is seen in him, his property is handed over to him and his orphanhood ends. You asked whether the Messenger of God ﷺ killed any of the children of the polytheists. The Messenger of God ﷺ did not kill any of them. You asked whether a woman and a slave have a fixed share when they are present. They do not have a fixed share, except that they may be given something from the spoils of the people."],[6822,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and the companions of the Prophet ﷺ saw in him such vigor and energy that amazed them. They said: O Messenger of God, if only this were in the path of God. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: If he went out striving for his young children, then he is in the path of God. If he went out striving for two elderly parents, then he is in the path of God. If he is striving for himself to keep himself chaste, then he is in the path of God. But if he went out for show and pride, then he is in the path of Satan."],[6823,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ being asked about the 'aqiqah. He said: For a boy, two sheep; for a girl, one sheep."],[6824,"As for the Fire, people will be thrown into it, and it will say: Is there any more? until its Lord, Blessed and Exalted, comes to it and places His foot upon it, and it shrinks and says: Enough, enough. As for Paradise, God will create for it a creation as He wills."],[6825,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: O Messenger of God, we know how to greet you with peace, but how should we invoke blessings upon you? He said: Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. And grant blessings to Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You granted blessings to Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy and Glorious."],[6826,"God has forbidden the singing slave-girl, her sale, her price, her teaching, and listening to her."],[6827,"On the Day of Resurrection, God, Blessed and Exalted, will grant Adam's intercession for all his progeny: for one hundred thousand thousand and ten thousand thousand."],[6828,"It was said to him: 'None shall enter Paradise except one who has migrated.' I said: 'I will not come to my home until I go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and ask him.' So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'This man stole a cloak of mine,' referring to a man who was with him. He ordered that his hand be cut off. I said: 'O Messenger of God, I have given it to him as a gift.' He said: 'Why not before you brought him to me?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, they say that none shall enter Paradise except one who has migrated?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'There is no migration after the conquest of Makkah, but there remains jihad and [good] intention, and when you are called to march forth, then march forth.'"],[6829,"A woman came wanting [to see] the Messenger of God ﷺ, but she did not find him, so she sat until he came. When he came, I said: 'O Messenger of God, this woman has a need for you.' He said: 'What is your need?' She said: 'O Messenger of God, my father married me to his nephew in order to raise his lowly status, and he did not consult me. Do I have any authority over myself?' He said: 'Yes.' She said: 'I would not reject anything my father has done, but I wanted women to know whether they have authority over themselves or not.'"],[6830,"He would not lie down to sleep at night or during the day and then wake up except that he used the toothstick before performing ablution."],[6831,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed in the house of Umm Sulaym on a green mat, and they prayed behind him."],[6832,"When it was a cold night or a rainy night, the caller of the Messenger of God ﷺ would call out: 'Pray in your dwellings.'"],[6833,"Whoever says 'I am a scholar,' he is ignorant."],[6834,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would present himself to the people at the [pilgrimage] station, saying: 'Is there not a man who will carry me to his people, for Quraysh have prevented me from conveying the speech of my Lord?' A man from Hamdan came to him, and he said: 'From what tribe are you?' He said: 'From Hamdan.' He said: 'Do you have protective strength?' He said: 'Yes.' Then the Hamdani man feared that his people would betray him, so he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'I will go to them, then I will meet you in the coming year.' He said to him: 'Go.' And the delegations of the Ansar came in Rajab."],[6835,"The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ complained to him of thirst. He called for a wooden bowl and called for water, pouring it into it. The Messenger of God ﷺ placed his palm in the bowl and said: 'Drink.' I saw water gushing forth as springs from between the fingers of the Messenger of God ﷺ until the people had drunk."],[6836,"A letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ came to us, to the people of Oman: 'Peace. To proceed: Affirm the testimony that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, pay the zakah, and build mosques; otherwise I will raid you.' Abu Shaddad said: 'We did not find anyone to read the letter to us until we found a black slave boy, and he read it to us.'"],[6837,"O young men of Quraysh, guard your private parts. Indeed, whoever guards his private part will have Paradise."],[6838,"The muezzins will have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection, and there is nothing that hears him but that it will testify for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[6839,"I migrated with my brother to the Messenger of God ﷺ in Madinah. When I was partway along the road, my brother said to me: 'Sit down, O Umm Ishaq, for I have forgotten my provisions in Makkah.' I said: 'I fear for you from the wicked man, my husband.' He said: 'No, God willing.' She said: 'I waited for some days, and a man I knew—whom I will not name—passed by me and said: 'What makes you sit here, O Umm Ishaq?' I said: 'I am waiting for Ishaq; he went for provisions of his in Makkah.' He said: 'You have no Ishaq; your wicked husband caught up with him and killed him.' So I came, and I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was performing ablution. I said: 'O Messenger of God, Ishaq has been killed,' and I was crying, and he looked at me. When I looked at him, he lowered [his gaze] during the ablution, then he took a handful of water and sprinkled it in my face."],[6840,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he commanded her to stipulate a condition."],[6841,"Whoever arrives for hajj should perform tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwah before going to Mina."],[6842,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ. He prayed two rak‘ahs before zuhr, two after it, two after maghrib, two after ‘isha, and two before fajr."],[6843,"The Prophet ﷺ threw the jamarat at the sun’s decline with pebbles like those thrown with the fingers, while mounted on his riding camel."],[6844,"I went out walking with my father at the edge of the harrah. Abu Hurayrah met me and said to me, “Who is this?” I said, “My father.” He said, “Do not walk in front of your father; rather walk behind him or beside him. Do not let anyone come between you and him. Do not walk on a roof under which your father is. Do not eat a bone your father has looked at, for perhaps he desired it.” Then he said, “Do you know ‘Abd Allah b. Khidash?” I said, “No.” He said, “I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, ‘His thigh in Hell will be like Uhud, and his molar tooth like al-Bayda’.’” Abu Hurayrah said, “I said, ‘Why is that, Messenger of Allah?’ He replied, ‘He was disobedient to his parents.’”"],[6845,"Four people begin the morning in Allah’s anger and end the day in His wrath.” I said, “Who are they, Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Men who imitate women, women who imitate men, the one who has intercourse with an animal, and the one who has intercourse with men.”"],[6846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never equated anyone from his companions with me and Khalid b. al-Walid since we embraced Islam."],[6847,"Those who love one another for the sake of Allah’s majesty will be in Allah’s shade on the day when there is no shade except His shade."],[6848,"He used to pray in his sandals."],[6849,"He used to wipe over the leather socks and command wiping over the leather socks,” and he said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that.”"],[6850,"Muhammad b. ‘Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, [ ] from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the middle of Sha‘ban comes, there is no fasting except Ramadan.” No one narrated this hadith from al-Zubaydi except Baqiyyah."],[6851,"Among the signs of the Hour is the swelling of the crescent moons, until the crescent is seen for its first night and it is said, “It is for two nights.”"],[6852,"Indeed, Allah laughs at the despair of His servants and their despondency, and at the nearness of mercy to them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, does our Lord laugh? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, indeed He laughs."],[6853,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invoked blessing upon three things: the pre-dawn meal (sahur), tharid, and the measuring (kayl)."],[6854,"Whoever forgets to mention Allah at the beginning of his meal, let him mention the name of Allah at its end, and let him recite: 'Say: He is Allah, [who is] One.'"],[6855,"A dirham that I give for blood money is dearer to me than a hundred for something else."],[6856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Duba'ah bt. al-Zubayr and said: 'Will you not perform Hajj?' She said: 'I am weak and unable.' He said: 'Perform Hajj and stipulate: My place of release is wherever You withhold me.'"],[6857,"When a slave is jointly owned and one of the partners frees him, the slave is valued at the highest price, and the one who freed him pays the remaining share, and the slave is freed."],[6858,"Do not give 'umra or ruqba. If you do, it belongs to the recipient of 'umra and the recipient of ruqba. I said: How is that? He said: 'Umra is when you say: It is yours for your lifetime. Ruqba is when you say: It belongs to the last of us to die."],[6859,"Regarding the words of Allah: 'And remember your Lord when you forget,' he said: 'If you forget to make an exception, then make it when you remember.' He said: 'This is specific to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and none of us may make an exception except in connection with an oath.'"],[6860,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at Abu Bakr and Umar and said: 'These two are the masters of the middle-aged men of Paradise.'"],[6861,"He forbade secret marriage."],[6862,"I used to cover my lower body while menstruating, and then the Prophet ﷺ would embrace me."],[6863,"A red velvet blanket was placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6864,"It is as if I am looking at the yellowness of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in ihram, from the oil he applied when entering ihram."],[6865,"The Prophet ﷺ used to offer as sacrifice a ram."],[6866,"I am pleased for my ummah with what Ibn Umm ʿAbd was pleased for it."],[6867,"Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock."],[6868,"Whoever would like his lifespan to be extended and his term to be delayed, let him fear Allah and maintain his kinship ties."],[6869,"ʿAli gathered the people in al-Rahbah while I was present, and said: I adjure by Allah any man who heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever's mawla I am, ʿAli is his mawla. Eighteen men stood up and testified that they had heard the Prophet ﷺ say that."],[6870,"O Allah, bless my ummah in its early morning."],[6871,"By the One who sent me with the truth, if the drop from which Allah took the covenant were cast upon a rock, Allah would create from it a human being."],[6872,"I used to cover my lower part while I was menstruating, and then the Prophet ﷺ would have intimate contact with me."],[6873,"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from miserliness."],[6874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away between my chest and my throat, while I had leaned him against my chest. ʿAbd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr came with a tooth-stick, and the Prophet ﷺ called him, took the tooth-stick from him, and began trying to use it but could not. I took the tooth-stick from him, softened it, and gave it back to him, and he began to clean his teeth with it. Then his hand grew heavy, and I began to hear him say: \"In the highest company.\" And he passed away while I was unaware."],[6875,"Do not name grapes 'al-karm'."],[6876,"When one of you is invited, let him respond."],[6877,"It is enough evil for a man that fingers be pointed at him in matters of religion or this world, except for one whom Allah protects."],[6878,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard your supplication last night, and what reached me of it was that you said: O Allah, forgive me my sin, expand for me my home, and bless me in what You have provided me. He said: \"Do you think they leave anything out?\""],[6879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about kalāla, and he said: \"The verse of summer suffices you.\""],[6880,"There will be after me affairs and selfishness. They said: What do you command, O Messenger of Allah, for one who lives to see that? He said: \"You fulfill the duty that is upon you and ask Allah for what is yours.\""],[6881,"Hearts have rust. They said: What polishes them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Their polish is seeking forgiveness.\""],[6882,"Allah sent me with the perfection of noble character and the completion of excellent deeds."],[6883,"What a man spends on himself, his children, his family, his relatives, and his kin is charity for him."],[6884,"Allah does not accept charity from ill-gotten gains, nor prayer without purification."],[6885,"Dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell never gather in the belly of a Muslim man."],[6886,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every beast with fangs and every bird with talons."],[6887,"If you doubt in your prayer, let the doubt be about the fifth or the fourth."],[6888,"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition to Tabuk. He used to combine Zuhr and Asr, praying Zuhr at the end of its time and Asr at the beginning of its time. Then he would travel and pray Maghrib at the end of its time, as long as the twilight had not disappeared, and pray Isha at the beginning of its time, when the twilight disappeared. Then, when he drew near, he said: 'We will camp tomorrow, God willing, at Tabuk, so let no one get to the water before us.' Mu'adh said: 'I was the first to race to the water, but there were two men who had beaten me to it. They had drawn water into two water-skins they had with them and muddied the water. I said: \"After the Messenger of God's ﷺ prohibition, you two have beaten us and drawn water?\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came and said: \"Did I not forbid you that no one should get to the water before us?\" He asked for the two water-skins and they were emptied into the water. Then he performed wudu, rinsed his mouth in the water, and supplicated to God, and the water overflowed. Then he said: \"Indeed you, O Mu'adh, if your life is prolonged, will see that this place here has been filled with gardens.\""],[6889,"A gift to a ruler is misappropriation."],[6890,"Abu Rimthah led us in prayer and said: I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ praying. Then he gave the greeting to his right and to his left, until we saw the whiteness of his cheeks."],[6891,"Regarding His saying: 'I ask of you no reward for it except love of kinship,' he said: 'There was no clan of Quraysh except that the Messenger of God ﷺ had close kinship with them.' So He said to him: 'Say: I ask of you no reward for it except that you love me because of my kinship with you.'"],[6892,"There will be in this nation earthquakes, peltings, and metamorphosis among those who keep singing-girls, wear silk, and drink wine."],[6893,"God is beautiful and loves beauty. He loves high-minded matters and dislikes their lowly ones."],[6894,"A man should not wipe his forehead of dust until he finishes the prayer, but there is no harm in wiping sweat from his temples."],[6895,"My brother Moses ﷺ said: 'O Lord, show me the one You showed me in the ship.' God revealed to him: 'O Moses, you will see him.' It was only a short time before al-Khidr came to him, fragrant of scent, with beautifully white garments. He said: 'Peace be upon you, O Moses son of Imran. Your Lord sends you greetings of peace and the mercy of God.' Moses said: 'He is the Peace, from Him is peace, and to Him returns peace. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, whose blessings I cannot count, and I am unable to thank Him except by His help.' Then Moses said: 'I want you to give me advice that God will benefit me with after you.' Al-Khidr said: 'O seeker of knowledge, the speaker is less weary than the listener, so do not bore your companions when you speak to them. Know that your heart is a vessel, so look at what you fill your vessel with. Turn away from this world and cast it behind you, for it is not a home for you, nor do you have a place of settlement in it. It is made as a provision for the servants, so that they may take from it provisions for the Hereafter. O Moses, accustom yourself to patience and you will attain wisdom. Clothe your heart with piety and you will obtain knowledge. Train yourself to patience and you will be free from sin. O Moses, devote yourself to knowledge if you want it, for knowledge is only for those who devote themselves to it. Do not be excessively talkative or verbose, for much talk disgraces scholars and exposes the faults of the foolish. But upon you is moderation, for that is part of success and right guidance. Turn away from the ignorant and forbear with the foolish, for that is the merit of the wise and the adornment of scholars. If an ignorant person insults you, remain silent before him with a peaceful attitude and avoid him with prudence, for what remains of his ignorance toward you and his insults to you is greater and more severe. O son of Imran, do you not see that you have been given only a little knowledge? For reckless plunging and straying come from impetuosity and affectation. O son of Imran, do not open a door whose closing you do not know, and do not close a door whose opening you do not know. O son of Imran, one whose desire for this world never ends and whose longing for it never ceases—how can he be a worshipper? One who belittles his own state and accuses God of what He has decreed for him—how can he be an ascetic? Can one whose passion has overcome him refrain from desires? Will knowledge benefit him while ignorance encompasses him? For his journey is to his Hereafter while he is turning toward his world. O Moses, learn what you learn in order to act upon it, and do not learn it merely to talk about it, lest it become a burden upon you and its light be for someone else. O Moses son of Imran, make asceticism and piety your clothing, and knowledge and remembrance your speech. Increase in good deeds, for you will certainly encounter evil deeds. Shake your heart with fear, for that pleases your Lord. Do good, for you must inevitably do something besides it. You have been admonished if you remember.' Then al-Khidr departed, and Moses remained sad and distressed."],[6896,"My nation is a nation shown mercy. Punishment has been lifted from them, except their punishing themselves with their own hands."],[6897,"After me there will be rulers who are given wisdom upon their pulpits, but when they descend, it is taken from them. Their hearts and bodies are worse than carrion."],[6898,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ applying kohl with ithmid while he was fasting."],[6899,"The Prophet ﷺ cut and crucified those who drove off the grazing livestock of the Messenger of God ﷺ in Madinah."],[6900,"There is no vow in disobedience [to Allah]."],[6901,"In Paradise there is a rolling-place of musk like the rolling-place of your mounts in this world."],[6902,"Whoever is gentle with my community, be gentle with him; and whoever is harsh with them, be harsh with him."],[6903,"We said: O Messenger of Allah, when we leave you we engage in the talk of the Jahiliyyah. He said: When you sit in those gatherings that you fear for yourselves, say when you stand up: Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You. What you have incurred in it will be expiated for you."],[6904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[6905,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: When I die, and Abu Bakr, and Umar, then if you are able to die, then die."],[6906,"None of you should look at his reflection in water."],[6907,"A believer is not stung from the same hole twice."],[6908,"O Aishah, a house in which there are no dates, its people are hungry."],[6909,"Adhere to contentment, for contentment is wealth that does not run out."],[6910,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their property except for its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[6911,"As for me, I do not eat reclining."],[6912,"Shortening the prayer is a resting of the people of the Fire."],[6913,"The best of this Ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then Umar."],[6914,"There is no marriage except with a guardian and two witnesses."],[6915,"The Prophet ﷺ gave the grandmother one-sixth."],[6916,"There is no wudu' except from a sound or smell."],[6917,"Whoever is killed defending his property, he is a martyr."],[6918,"Whoever increases in the remembrance of Allah, he has freed himself from hypocrisy."],[6919,"Ja'far b. Abi Talib passed by with Jibril and Mika'il, having two wings that Allah gave him in place of his hands, and he greeted, then..."],[6920,"Whoever is put in charge of ten people and judges between them according to what they like or dislike, he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand tied to his neck. If he judged by other than what Allah sent down, an extra fetter will be added to his fetter. If he judged by what Allah sent down, and did not deviate in judgment, and did not take a bribe, his right hand will be released."],[6921,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib, and he was hungry. She said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have in-laws who have sought refuge with me, and Ali b. Abi Talib is not deterred by any blame in the cause of Allah. I fear that he will learn of them and kill them, so grant safety to whoever enters my house until they hear the word of Allah.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted them safety.' Then he said: 'Do you have any food for me to eat?' She said: 'I have some dry pieces of bread left overnight, and I am ashamed to present them to you.' He said: 'Bring them.' She brought them and some salt. He said: 'O Umm Hani', is there any condiment?' She said: 'I have nothing but a little vinegar.' He said: 'Bring it.' When she brought it, he poured it over his food, then ate from it. Then he praised Allah and said: 'What an excellent condiment vinegar is, O Umm Hani'. A house that has vinegar will never be poor.'"],[6922,"When Fatimah, the mother of Ali b. Abi Talib, died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took off his shirt and clothed her with it, and lay down with her in her grave. When the earth was leveled over her, some of them said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we saw you do something you have not done for anyone else.' He said: 'I clothed her with my shirt so that she may wear from the garments of Paradise, and I lay down with her in her grave so that the squeezing of the grave may be lightened for her. She was the best of Allah's creation to me in kindness after Abu Talib.'"],[6923,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting and Asma' bt. Umays was near him, he returned the greeting and then said: 'O Asma', this is Ja'far b. Abi Talib with Jibril and Mika'il (peace be upon them). They passed by and greeted us, and I returned their greeting. He told me that he met the polytheists on such-and-such a day, and I was struck in my body, in my front, seventy-three times between a stab and a blow. Then I took the banner with my right hand and it was cut off, then I took it with my left hand and it was cut off. Allah compensated me for my hands with two wings with which I fly with Jibril and Mika'il in Paradise. I descend from it wherever I wish, and I eat of its fruits whatever I wish.' Asma' said: 'Congratulations to Ja'far for the good Allah has granted him, but I fear that people will not believe me. Ascend the pulpit, O Messenger of Allah, and inform the people.' So he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'O people, Ja'far b. Abi Talib passed by with Jibril and Mika'il, having two wings with which Allah compensated him for his hands, flying with them in Paradise wherever he wishes, and he greeted me.' He told them how his affair was when he met the polytheists. It became clear to the people after that day that Ja'far had met them, and he was named Ja'far al-Tayyar (the flyer) in Paradise."],[6924,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ was with Gabriel ﷺ on al-Safa. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “O Gabriel, by the One who sent you with the truth, the family of Muhammad has no husk of flour or handful of barley meal left for the evening.” No sooner had he spoken than he heard a thunderous sound from heaven that startled him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Has God commanded the Hour to come?” He said, “No, but God commanded Israfil, and he came down to you when he heard your words.” Israfil came to him and said, “God has heard what you mentioned, and He has sent me to you with the keys of the treasures of the earth. He commanded me to present them to you: if you wish, I will make the mountains of Tihamah move with you as emeralds, rubies, gold, and silver, and I will do it. If you wish, you may be a prophet-king, and if you wish, a prophet-servant.” Gabriel gestured to him to be humble. He said, “Rather, a prophet-servant,” three times."],[6925,"Some people of my community will come after me; each of them would wish to buy seeing me with his family and wealth."],[6926,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in three garments."],[6927,"I never saw the Prophet ﷺ honor anyone as he honored al-Abbas."],[6928,"Tranquility is a soft, gentle wind."],[6929,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is called, begin with the evening meal."],[6930,"Hearing news is not like seeing with one's own eyes."],[6931,"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ, thinking it was only for Hajj."],[6932,"The Prophet ﷺ saw him while the lice of his head were falling onto his face. He said, “Do your lice bother you?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then shave your head, and offer a sheep as sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed six poor persons.”"],[6933,"The Prophet ﷺ said concerning the Ansar: “Only a believer loves them, and only a hypocrite hates them. Whoever loves them, God loves him, and whoever hates them, God hates him.”"],[6934,"He entered the mosque while the Messenger of God ﷺ was bowing, so he bowed before reaching the row. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said, “O Abu Bakrah, may God increase you in keenness, but do not repeat it.”"],[6935,"A man from the Bedouins died and had no male relatives, but he had a freed slave whom he had manumitted. That was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Was he not angry when he was angry and pleased when he was pleased?” They said, “Yes.” So he made him inherit the wealth of his former master."],[6936,"If one of you needs to relieve himself and the prayer time comes, let him first relieve himself."],[6937,"There is no harm if one of you, when he wants to give charity, makes it on behalf of his parents; nothing will be diminished from their rewards."],[6938,"When he prayed the dawn prayer while traveling, he would walk."],[6939,"Has your Haruri not come denying it? How often we heard the Prophet ﷺ mention him—meaning the Dajjal."],[6940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade (drinking from) gourds, hollowed stumps, and green jars."],[6941,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and water became scarce. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel and placed his hand in it. I saw water gushing from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6942,"An Umrah to the next Umrah is an expiation for what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[6943,"The Prophet ﷺ ate from a shoulder (of meat), then prayed without performing ablution."],[6944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was six years old, and I was taken to his house when I was nine. I stayed with him for nine (years), then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when I was eighteen."],[6945,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died and left nothing in my house except a measure of barley. I ate from it until I became weary of it, then I measured it and it was finished. Would that I had not measured it."],[6946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me in Shawwal and consummated the marriage with me in Shawwal. Which of his wives was more favored with him than me?"],[6947,"I was commanded to use the siwak so much that I feared for my teeth."],[6948,"If a person had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills a person's belly but dust. Then God turns [in mercy] to whoever repents."],[6949,"Faith has seventy-some branches, the highest of which is 'there is no god but God', and the lowest of which is removing harm from the road."],[6950,"Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas struck his wife and broke her hand. She was Jamila bt. Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. Her brother came to complain to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for Thabit b. Qays and said: 'Take what she is owed from you and release her.' He said: 'Yes.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded her to wait for one menstrual period and return to her family."],[6951,"He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'Which part of the night is best for supplication?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The last part of the night.' Then he said: 'Pray as much as you wish until you pray the morning prayer, then stop until the sun rises, for it rises between the horns of Satan, and at that time the disbelievers prostrate to it. Then pray if you wish, until midday when you should stop, for Hell is stoked at that time. When the shadow declines, pray as much as you wish until you pray the afternoon prayer, then stop, for the sun sets between the horns of Satan, and at that time the disbelievers prostrate to it.' He said: I asked him about purification, and he said: 'When you rinse your mouth, you expel its sin. When you wash your hands, you wash away the sin of your hands, your nails, and your fingertips. When you wash your feet, you wash away your sin from the soles of your feet. When you pray and turn to God with your heart, it is an expiation, and if you sit, your reward is assured.'"],[6952,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying, he heard a man supplicating: 'Praise be to God, abundant, good, blessed praise, as befits the honor of our Lord's countenance and the might of His majesty.' When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said: 'Which of you said such-and-such? I saw twelve angels rushing to it.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ raised his gaze until it disappeared behind the veil, and said: 'It is yours with its seal on the Day of Resurrection and the like of it.'"],[6953,"It is as if I am looking at the gleam of the Messenger of God's ﷺ ring when he came out to us in the last third of the night and said: 'The people have prayed and slept, but you will remain in prayer as long as you wait for it.'"],[6954,"I never saw a lighter prayer than that of the Messenger of God ﷺ, yet complete in bowing and prostration."],[6955,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, the well is without liability, the mine is without liability, and on buried treasure the fifth is due."],[6956,"He came to Umar b. al-Khattab while he was feeding the people lunch. A man passed by him, or greeted him, and Umar said to him: 'Come.' He said: 'I am fasting.' He said: 'Which days of the month do you fast?' He said: 'From every month, its beginning and middle.' Umar said: 'Call for me Abdullah b. Mas'ud and Ubayy b. Ka'b.' He named men from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ. They came, and he said: 'Do you remember the day a man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a rabbit in such-and-such a valley on such-and-such a day?' They said: 'Yes.' Umar said: 'Then tell the man.' They began to tell the man, saying: 'We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in such-and-such a valley on such-and-such a day when a shepherd brought him a roasted rabbit as a gift. The shepherd said: \"I saw blood on it.\" He ordered the people to eat, but he did not eat. He said to the shepherd: \"Sit and eat with them.\" The shepherd said: \"I am fasting.\" He said: \"How do you fast?\" He said: \"I fast three days every month.\" He said: \"Which three do you fast?\" He said: \"From its middle and its end, and as it happens.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Fast the three white days.\""],[6957,"Ugly matters spread in Kufa, so the reciters of Kufa gathered and went out to Umar. Umar said: 'What have I done that the reciters of Kufa have come to me?' Abdullah b. Amr said: 'Ugly matters spread among them.' He said: 'I adjure you by God, O Abdullah b. Amr, do you obey God in what you are commanded regarding your hearing?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then regarding your sight?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then how can I establish the affairs of the nation of Muhammad ﷺ on what you yourself cannot remain upright in regarding your hearing and sight? We have from people only what the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to fight people until they say 'there is no god but God' and establish prayer and give zakat. If they do that, they protect from me their blood and wealth, except by its right, and their reckoning is with God.\""],[6958,"The Prophet ﷺ entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah wearing a black turban."],[6959,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ enjoining [good treatment of] the neighbor until we thought he would make him an heir."],[6960,"She entered upon Aishah, the Mother of the Believers, with her was a stick, chasing the gecko to kill it. I said: O Mother of the Believers, what is the matter with this gecko? She said: When Ibrahim was thrown into the fire, everything would repel it except this one, so we were commanded to kill it."],[6961,"Regarding His saying: 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory' (48:1), it was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon his return from al-Hudaybiyyah, while his companions were mixed with grief and despondency. They had been prevented from their rites, and they had sacrificed the sacrificial animals at al-Hudaybiyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than the entire world.' He recited it to them to the end of the verse. A man from the people said: 'Congratulations and blessings to you, O Messenger of Allah, from Allah. You have what He does for you, but what does He do for us?' So Allah revealed on that day: 'That He may admit the believing men and believing women to gardens beneath which rivers flow' (48:5) to the end of the verse."],[6962,"While I was circumambulating the House with Abdullah b. Umar, a man intercepted him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say about the confidential talk? He said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will call His servant and place His covering over him, saying to him: 'Did you not do on such-and-such day such-and-such sin?' The servant will say: 'Yes, O Lord.' Then He will say: 'Indeed, I concealed it for you in the world, and I forgive it for you today.'"],[6963,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined me with three things that I will not abandon whether traveling or settled: sleeping on an odd number (of rak'ahs of witr), fasting three days of every month, and two rak'ahs after Friday prayer. Then Abu Hurayrah made the two rak'ahs after Friday prayer the two rak'ahs of al-duha."],[6964,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the temporary marriage (mut'ah) of women."],[6965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah during the umrah until he touched the Black Stone."],[6966,"When any of you sets out for the Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[6967,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu in a basin, so I took it and poured it into a well of ours."],[6968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Hunayn the sale of spoils until they are distributed, and pregnant women from being approached until they deliver what is in their wombs, and he said: 'Would you water the seed of another?' And he forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and the meat of every predator with fangs."],[6969,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her lawfully, consummated the marriage lawfully, and married her at Sarif."],[6970,"We reminded each other while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: which is more virtuous, the Mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or the Bayt al-Maqdis? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than four prayers there, and it is an excellent place of prayer. It is near that a man will have the like of the tip of his bow's curve of land, from where he can see the Bayt al-Maqdis, better for him than the entire world.'"],[6971,"No Muslim spends two pairs from his wealth in the path of Allah except that the gatekeepers of Paradise call him: 'Come, this is good.'"],[6972,"He was ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah; his name was ‘Abd al-Kallub, and the Messenger of God ﷺ named him ‘Abd al-Rahman. He passed by him while he was performing ablution, and he said, “Come, O ‘Abd al-Rahman.” The Prophet of God ﷺ said to him: Do not seek positions of authority, for if you seek it and are given it, you will be left to it; but if you do not seek it, you will be helped in it."],[6973,"A report is not like seeing with one’s own eyes."],[6974,"I said: O Messenger of God, I am a man who swears an oath about something, then regrets it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and expiate for his oath."],[6975,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and said in his sermon: Verily, I am about to be called and to answer. After me, governors will rule over you who do what you know and who do what you recognize, and obeying them is obedience. You will remain like that for a time. Then after them, governors will rule over you who do what they do not know and do what you do not recognize. Whoever ransoms them and gives them sincere counsel—those have perished and caused others to perish. Mix with them in your bodies, but part from them in your deeds, and bear witness that the doer of good is a doer of good and that the doer of evil is a doer of evil."],[6976,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray witr at the beginning of the night, in the middle of it, and at the end of it, so that the Muslims would follow his example. Whichever of these is acted upon is correct, God willing."],[6977,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray witr at the beginning of the night, in the middle of it, and at the end of it."],[6978,"Do not name [your children] Aflah (most prosperous), Najih (successful), Yasar (wealth), or Tazidanna; he said it three times."],[6979,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah while the Jews were fasting on ‘Ashura’. He asked them, and they said: This is a day on which Moses ﷺ prevailed over Pharaoh. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You have more right to Moses, so fast it."],[6980,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and said: The best of you is the one who defends his clan, as long as he does not commit sin."],[6981,"God gave me the choice between forgiving half of my community or my intercession, and I chose my intercession, hoping that it would be more comprehensive for my community. Were it not for the righteous servant who preceded me, I would have hastened my supplication. When God relieved Isaac of the distress of the sacrifice, it was said to him: O Isaac, ask and you will be given. He said: By God, I will hasten it before the promptings of Satan. O God, whoever dies not associating anything with You and does good, forgive him and admit him to Paradise."],[6982,"He heard Mu‘awiyah on the pulpit on the day of ‘Ashura’ say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ commanding the fast of this day."],[6983,"Regarding His saying: “And beneath it was a treasure belonging to them” [Q 18:82], he said: Gold and silver."],[6984,"Regarding His saying: “Then he began to pass his hand over their legs and necks” [Sad 38:33], he said: “He cut their necks and their legs.”"],[6985,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to make the two rak`ahs of Fajr so short that I would say: “He does not complete the Opening of the Book.”"],[6986,"When he saw something he liked, he would say: “Our Lord, by Your blessing righteous deeds are completed, so to You belongs praise.” And when he saw something he disliked, he would say: “Praise belongs to Allah in every situation.”"],[6987,"Whoever is tested with daughters and treats them well, they will be a shield for him from the Fire."],[6988,"I do not fear for you regarding mistakes, but I fear for you regarding deliberate actions."],[6989,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to visit Sad b. al-Rabi al-Ansari, whose house was in al-Aswaq. His wife spread for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a shelter of palm branches, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and we sat with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man from the people of Paradise will now appear before you.” Abu Bakr appeared. Then he said: “A man from the people of Paradise will appear before you.” Umar appeared. Then he said: “A man from the people of Paradise will appear before you,” and Uthman appeared."],[6990,"There is no guardian of three persons but that he will meet Allah with his right hand chained: his justice will release it, or his oppression will bind it."],[6991,"The Prophet ﷺ addressed them and said: “May Allah brighten a man who hears a saying from us and preserves it, for many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding carries it to one who has more understanding than him.”"],[6992,"Whoever builds a mosque, not desiring thereby show or reputation, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."],[6993,"It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, who is the master?” He said: “That is Yusuf b. Ya`qub b. Ishaq b. Ibrahim.” They said: “Is there no master in your community?” He said: “Yes, a man who is given lawful wealth and granted generosity, so he draws near the poor, and his complaints about people are few.”"],[6994,"We were at a watering place on the road, and caravans of those who had met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pass by us. I asked them to recite the Qur’an, until I had learned a great deal of Qur’an. My father went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group from the tribe. When they returned, they said: “We were commanded such and such, and we were commanded that the one among us with the most Qur’an should lead us in prayer.” They looked at the people of the watering place, and I was the one with the most Qur’an, so they put me forward. I was wearing a striped cloak, and when I prostrated it almost reached my buttocks. A woman from the tribe said: “Cover from us the private parts of this reciter of yours.” So they bought me a garment from this lot, and a woman from the tribe cut it into a shirt for me, and they clothed me with it. I rejoiced over it as I had never rejoiced over anything like it. I used to lead them in prayer, and at that time I was eight years old."],[6995,"A man's prayer in his house is one prayer; his prayer in the mosque of the tribes is twenty-five prayers; his prayer in the mosque in which the Friday prayer is held is five hundred prayers; his prayer in the Aqsa Mosque is fifty thousand prayers; his prayer in the mosque of the Ka`bah is one hundred thousand prayers; and his prayer in this mosque of mine is fifty thousand prayers."],[6996,"When Allah accepted my repentance, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not know anyone whom Allah has tested in truthfulness as He tested me. Part of my repentance is that I will not speak except truthfully as long as I live, and that I divest myself of all my wealth for Allah and His Messenger, because of the favor He bestowed upon me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A third of your wealth is sufficient for you.\""],[6997,"I entered upon Aisha while she was wearing a patched garment. I said: Why do you not cast off this garment? She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If it pleases you to meet me, do not discard a garment until you patch it, and do not store food for a month.\" I will not change what he commanded me until I join him, if Allah wills."],[6998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing women and children."],[6999,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a bowl that was boiling, so he hurried his hand into it, then lifted his hand and said: \"Allah has not fed us fire.\""],[7000,"The ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with Abu Bakr during his caliphate, and with Umar during his caliphate, and with Uthman during part of his caliphate. It was at a well called Bi'r Aris, and the ring fell into it. They drained the well but did not find it."],[7001,"Regarding His saying: \"And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting\" (Qaf 50:39), he said: \"Before the rising of the sun is the Fajr prayer, and before its setting is the Asr prayer.\""],[7002,"May Allah curse those who revile my Companions."],[7003,"When one of you enters the mosque while the people are bowing, let him bow when he enters, then move while bowing until he enters the row, for that is the sunnah.\" Ata said: \"I saw him doing that.\" Ibn Jurayj said: \"I saw Ata doing that.\""],[7004,"Pour over me from seven water skins from different wells so that I may go out to the people and give them my final instructions.\" He said: He came out with his head bandaged ﷺ until he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"A servant among Allah's servants was given the choice between this world and what is with Allah, and he chose what is with Allah.\" No one understood it except Abu Bakr, and he wept, saying: \"We ransom you with our fathers, mothers, and children.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Take it easy. The best of people to me in companionship and generosity is Ibn Abi Quhafa. Look at these doors opening into the mosque and close them, except what is from the door of Abu Bakr, for I saw light upon it.\""],[7005,"Whoever consistently recites Ya Sin every night and then dies, dies as a martyr."],[7006,"Be steadfast, and you will never be able to fully reckon; know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and none will preserve ablution except a believer."],[7007,"May Allah brighten [the face of] a servant who hears my words, understands them, and conveys them; for many a bearer of knowledge is not a scholar, and many a bearer of knowledge conveys it to one more learned than himself."],[7008,"Do not bid against one another, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be brothers as Allah has commanded you."],[7009,"If one of them were to say: I seek refuge in Allah from the Shaytan, his anger would go away\" or \"his anger would subside."],[7010,"Whoever gives four things will be given four things, and the explanation of that is in the Book of Allah. Whoever gives remembrance, Allah remembers him, for Allah says: 'Remember Me and I will remember you.' Whoever gives supplication is given response, for Allah says: 'Call upon Me and I will answer you.' Whoever gives gratitude is given increase, for Allah says: 'If you are grateful, I will surely increase you.' Whoever gives seeking forgiveness is given forgiveness, for Allah says: 'Ask forgiveness of your Lord; indeed He is ever Forgiving.'"],[7011,"Whoever frees a share of a slave, then upon him is to free the rest of him; if he does not have wealth, the slave is made to work to pay for his value."],[7012,"When the deceased is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him—and indeed he hears the tapping of their sandals—two angels come to him, sit him up, and say: 'What did you used to say about this man?' meaning Muhammad ﷺ. As for the believer, he says: 'I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His messenger.' Then it is said to him: 'Look at your seat in the Fire; Allah has replaced it for you with a seat in Paradise,' and he sees them both together."],[7013,"It will be said to the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection: 'Do you think that if you had the fill of the earth of gold, would you ransom yourself with it?' He will say: 'Yes.' Then it will be said to him: 'You lied; you were asked for what is easier than that and you refused.'"],[7014,"I only perform qunut so that you may supplicate to your Lord and ask Him for your needs."],[7015,"There is no divorce before marriage."],[7016,"When the Prophet ﷺ and his companions came to Madinah and the Ansar sheltered them, the Arabs shot at them from a single bow.\" Then the verse was revealed: 'He will surely cause them to succeed in the land...'"],[7017,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution three times, three times."],[7018,"I said to Jabir b. Samurah: 'Did you sit with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes, he was of long silence; his companions would recite poetry in his presence and remind one another of the accounts of their early days, and sometimes he would smile with them ﷺ.'"],[7019,"It is not lawful for a believer to boycott his brother for more than three days."],[7020,"The Prophet ﷺ granted a concession for selling 'arāyā by estimating their amount as a measure."],[7021,"\"Whoever leaves a hair on his body and does not wash it, such-and-such will be done to him in the Fire.\" 'Ali said: \"From that time I treated my hair as an enemy,\" and he used to pull his hair."],[7022,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ counting tasbīḥ on his fingers."],[7023,"Allah has not sent down any disease but He has sent down a cure for it; those who know it know it, and those who are ignorant of it are ignorant of it."],[7024,"The gates of heaven are opened on Mondays and Thursdays, and Allah forgives everyone who does not associate anything with Him except two people who have forsaken each other."],[7025,"He ordered the cutting of bells."],[7026,"The Prophet ﷺ was not prevented from reciting the Qur'an except by major ritual impurity."],[7027,"On buried treasure, one-fifth is due."],[7028,"He embraced Islam and came to the Prophet ﷺ, who ordered him to bathe with water and lote-tree leaves."],[7029,"When the time for prayer comes and one of you needs to relieve himself, let him begin with relieving himself."],[7030,"A servant does not believe until he believes in divine decree, its good and its evil."],[7031,"The angels do not accompany a group in which there is a bell."],[7032,"He used to pray while it lay crosswise in front of him, like a bier is laid crosswise."],[7033,"Loyalty belongs to the one who manumits."],[7034,"When dinner is served and the prayer is called, begin with dinner."],[7035,"He used to kiss while fasting."],[7036,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Shoot! May my father and mother be your ransom.'"],[7037,"Actions are only by intentions, and a person gets only what he intended. Whoever's migration is to Allah and His Messenger, his migration is to Allah and His Messenger. And whoever's migration is to a worldly gain he attains or a woman he marries, his migration is to what he migrated to."],[7038,"The Prophet ﷺ established brotherhood between the Muhajirun and the Ansar in the house of Anas."],[7039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out of the door of the house intending to go to the room, and he heard people disputing about predestination. One of them was saying, 'Didn't Allah say in such-and-such a verse?' and the other was saying, 'Didn't Allah say in such-and-such a verse?' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out of the door of the room, and it was as if a pomegranate seed had been burst on his face. He said, 'Is this what you were commanded with?'—or 'Is this what you were sent with?'—'Those before you were destroyed only by things like this; they struck the Book of Allah against itself. Allah commands you with a matter, so accept it, and He forbids you from something, so desist from it.' Then no one was heard speaking about predestination after that until the nights of al-Hajjaj. The first to speak about predestination was Ma'bad al-Juhani, and al-Hajjaj killed him."],[7040,"When he extended—or raised—his hands in supplication, he would not withdraw them until he wiped his face with them."],[7041,"'Who will take these words from me and act upon them, or teach them to someone who will act upon them?' Abu Hurayrah said, 'I said, I will, O Messenger of Allah.' So the Prophet ﷺ took my hand and counted five on it, saying: 'Avoid what is forbidden, and you will be the most devout of people. Be content with what Allah has apportioned for you, and you will be the richest of people. Be good to your neighbor, and you will be a believer. Love for people what you love for yourself, and you will be a Muslim. And do not laugh excessively, for excessive laughter kills the heart.'"],[7042,"The Prophet ﷺ sent for a wound and ordered that it be treated and compensated, and he set its term at a year."],[7043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Budayl al-Khuza'i to announce during the days of Tashriq: 'Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking.'"],[7044,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away and did not appoint a successor. Had he appointed anyone, he would have appointed Abu Bakr."],[7045,"A man said: O Messenger of God, may a man pray in a single garment? He said: Does each of you find two garments?"],[7046,"People will come to you seeking knowledge. When they come to you, treat them kindly."],[7047,"Regarding God's words, Mighty and Majestic: 'The Hajj is [during] well-known months.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Dhu al-Qa'dah and Dhu al-Hijjah. So whoever makes the Hajj obligatory upon himself within them.' Ibn Umar said: 'The talbiyah and ihram. So no rafath—sexual intercourse with women; and no fusuq—insulting; and no jidal—disputing.'"],[7048,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade spreading something on the door of the house, and said: 'Remove it from it a little.'"],[7049,"When one of you prays, let him pray in two garments. If he has only one garment, let him wrap it around his waist and then pray. Do not wrap yourselves as the Jews do, for God is more deserving that one adorn oneself for Him."],[7050,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the one who consumes riba, the one who pays it, its two witnesses, its scribe, the one who makes a woman lawful for her first husband, and the one for whom she is made lawful, the woman who tattoos and the woman who is tattooed, and the one who withholds zakat."],[7051,"Fatimah said to Ali: O cousin, work and the handmill have become hard for me, so speak to the Prophet of God ﷺ. He said to her: Yes. The Prophet of God ﷺ came to them the next day while they were sleeping under one blanket, and he put his leg between them. Fatimah said: O Prophet of God, work has become hard for me. Would you order a servant for me from what God has granted you as spoils? He said: Shall I not teach you what is better for you than that? Glorify God thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times. That is one hundred on the tongue and one thousand in the scale, because God says: 'Whoever brings a good deed shall have ten times its like, up to a hundred thousand.'"],[7052,"I do not fear for my nation a believer or a polytheist. As for the believer, his faith restrains him; and as for the polytheist, his disbelief humbles him. But I fear for them a hypocrite with a knowledgeable tongue, who says what they recognize and does what they reject."],[7053,"A cover between the private parts of the children of Adam and the jinn, when one of them removes his garment, is to say: In the name of God."],[7054,"I was at the she-camel of the Messenger of God ﷺ when he entered ihram for the Farewell Hajj. When his mount set off with him, he said: Labbayk for a Hajj and an Umrah together."],[7055,"I had forbidden you from pairing dates together, but God has expanded provision for you, so pair them together."],[7056,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained that she had been married off against her will. So he removed her from her husband. She had been previously married, and afterwards she married Abu Lubabah."],[7057,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a black slave woman and said, “O Messenger of God, I owe a believing slave. Will this one suffice for me?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “Do you testify that there is no god but God?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “Do you testify that I am the Messenger of God?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “Free her, for she will suffice.”"],[7058,"“This son of mine is a sayyid, and God will reconcile through him two factions of the Muslims.”"],[7059,"Ibn Jurmuz came asking permission to enter upon Ali. He said, “Give the killer of al-Zubayr tidings of the Fire. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘Every prophet has a disciple (hawari), and al-Zubayr is my disciple.’”"],[7060,"“No man has worn sandals or ridden a saddle like Ja'far b. Abi Talib.”"],[7061,"“If someone comes to you whose religion and character you approve of, then marry [your daughters] to him. If you do not, there will be tribulation in the land and widespread corruption.”"],[7062,"“Seventy thousand of my community will enter Paradise without reckoning: they are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqya, and do not believe in omens.” Imran said, “We have cauterized, and we have neither prospered nor succeeded.”"],[7063,"“What a bad food is that to which the rich are invited while the poor are barred. Whoever is invited to it and does not respond has disobeyed God and His Messenger.” Then he said, “By God, it is not I who say it.”"],[7064,"A man said, “O Messenger of God, I have left no need or desire but I have fulfilled it.” He said, “Do you testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then this covers all of that.”"],[7065,"“Whoever asks when he has enough to make him self-sufficient only increases his share of the stones of Hell.” They said, “What is ‘enough to make him self-sufficient’?” He said, “An evening meal.”"],[7066,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed, and I do not know whether he added or omitted. When he finished, he was told, so he prostrated twice."],[7067,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was traveling on one of his journeys during part of the night, he heard the sound of singing. He said, “What is this?” He looked and saw a man exchanging songs with another: “My disciple’s bones will keep gleaming; war turned away from him lest he go mad and be buried.” He said, “O God, plunge them both into tribulation, and thrust them into the Fire of Hell.”"],[7068,"A man asked Ibn ʿUmar about the nabīdh of earthen jars, and he said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked it.” Saʿīd went to Ibn ʿAbbās and told him what Ibn ʿUmar had said, and he said: “Ibn ʿUmar spoke the truth.”"],[7069,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ would divide their hair into four braids. When they performed ghusl, they gathered it at the middle of their heads and did not undo it."],[7070,"A group from Muzaynah, a group from Hudhayl, and a group from Juhaynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we set out for Makkah on foot, while other people set out riding.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who walks has the reward of seventy Ḥajjs, and the rider has the reward of thirty Ḥajjs.”"],[7071,"During the campaign of Tabūk, the Prophet ﷺ was brought some cheese. He took a knife, cut it, and said: “Eat, in the name of Allah.”"],[7072,"“Gently, by Allah, gently! Were it not for humble young men, bowing old men, suckling infants, and grazing beasts, punishment would have been poured upon you abundantly, then you would have been crushed to powder.”"],[7073,"I said to Anas b. Mālik: “Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not dye his hair?” He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had not reached that point, but Abū Bakr dyed with ḥinnāʾ and katam.”"],[7074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among his Companions and said: “Perform ghusl on Friday. Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, it will be an expiation for what is between it and the next Friday, plus three days.”"],[7075,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, my father has seized my wealth.” He said: “You and your wealth belong to your father.”"],[7076,"“Whoever among you is able to prostrate, let him prostrate. Whoever is not able should not raise anything to his forehead to prostrate on, but should incline his head for bowing and prostrating.”"],[7077,"I entered upon al-Mukhtār b. Abī ʿUbayd while he had two cushions. He said: “O slave girl, bring a cushion.” I said: “This is a cushion.” He said: “No, this is one from which Jibrīl has just risen, and this one from which Mīkāʾīl has just risen. By Allah, nothing prevented me from striking him with my sword except a ḥadīth that ʿAmr b. al-Ḥamiq narrated to me. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever gives a man security for his blood and then kills him, he will be in the Fire, even if the slain man was a disbeliever.’”"],[7078,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on the paved area wearing his sandals. He spat under his left foot, then rubbed it on the ground."],[7079,"The Prophet ﷺ came to one of the gatherings of the Anṣār, where a group of them were present. He greeted them with salām, and they returned the greeting. The Prophet ﷺ disliked that gathering for them. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is a gathering where our fathers used to sit in the Jāhiliyyah. We wanted to maintain it and sit in it.” He said: “If you insist on doing so, then return the greeting, lower your gaze, and guide the way.”"],[7080,"It was said: O Messenger of God, so-and-so did not sleep last night. He said: \"And why?\" It was said: A scorpion stung him. He said: \"Indeed, if he had said when he retired to his bed: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created, it would not have harmed him.\""],[7081,"He used to pray two rakʿahs sitting after his witr."],[7082,"Perhaps the Prophet ﷺ would call for lunch and not find it, so he would impose fasting upon himself.\""],[7083,"\"Beware of fornication, for in it are four traits: it removes radiance from the face, cuts off sustenance, angers the Most Merciful, and causes eternity in the Fire.\""],[7084,"The Prophet ﷺ told them on the night he was taken on the Night Journey, saying: I ascended with Gabriel to the lowest heaven, and there I saw an angel called Ishmael, who is the keeper of the lowest heaven, and before him were seventy thousand angels, with each angel his host of one hundred thousand.\" Then he recited this verse: \"And none knows the hosts of your Lord except He.\""],[7085,"I said: O Messenger of God, all your wives have entered the House except me. He said: \"Go to your relative, to Shaybah, and let him open the door for you, then enter it.\" So I sent to him: The Prophet of God has permitted me that you open the door for me so I may enter it. He said: Did the Prophet of God ﷺ command you that? I said: Yes. So he took the keys and came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, did you command ʿAʾishah that the door be opened for her? He said: \"Yes.\" He said: No, by God, I have never opened it at night, neither in the Time of Ignorance nor in Islam. He said: \"Then consider what you used to do and do it, and what you would not do, then do not do it. And you, O ʿAʾishah, go and pray two rakʿahs in the Hijr, for a portion of it is part of the House, and your people fell short in funds, so they left out a portion of the House.\""],[7086,"Every intoxicant is unlawful. ʿUmar said: O Messenger of God, your statement: \"Every intoxicant is unlawful\". Then the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Drink, and when it begins to ferment, then leave it.\""],[7087,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave Mujjāʿah b. Murārah of Banū Salmā a piece of land in al-Yamāmah called al-ʿAwzah. He said: And he wrote for him a document: \"From Muhammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ, to Mujjāʿah b. Murārah of Banū Salmā. I have given you al-ʿAwzah, so whoever opposes me concerning it, then the Fire.\""],[7088,"It reached ʿAlī that some people in al-Baṣrah had apostatized from Islam. He sent for them and they were brought to him. He inclined food toward them for two weeks, then called them to Islam, but they refused. So he dug a pit for them, then stood over it and said: \"I will surely fill you with fat and flesh.\" Then he brought them, struck their necks, and threw them into the pit. Then he threw firewood upon them and burned them. Then he said: God and His Messenger have spoken truly. Suwayd b. Ghafalah said: When he departed, I followed him and said: I heard you say: God and His Messenger have spoken truly. He said: \"Woe to you, around me are ignorant people, but when you hear me say: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, then falling from the sky is dearer to me than saying about the Messenger of God ﷺ what he did not say.\""],[7089,"Indeed a righteous trait can be in a man, and through it God sets right all his deeds. A man's purification for his prayer: his purification expiates his sins, and his prayer becomes supererogatory."],[7090,"The Messenger of God ﷺ met Abū Dharr and said: \"O Abū Dharr, shall I not guide you to two traits that are lighter on the back and heavier in the scale than others?\" He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: \"You must have good character and prolonged silence, for by the One in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, creation has done no deed more beloved to God than these two.\""],[7091,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a choice, and it was not a divorce.\""],[7092,"O 'Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for authority, for if you ask for it, you will be left to it, and if you do not ask for it, you will be helped with it. And when you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do that which is better and expiate your oath."],[7093,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he prayed the morning prayer, would raise his voice so that his companions could hear, saying: 'O Allah, set right my religion, which You have made a protection for me'—three times. 'O Allah, set right my worldly life, in which You have placed my livelihood'—three times. 'O Allah, set right my Hereafter, to which You have made my return'—three times. 'O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath'—three times. 'O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment'—three times. 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from You'—three times. 'O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.'"],[7094,"Do not boast of your forefathers who died in the Jahiliyyah—do you boast of them? Shall I not tell you? The likeness of your forefathers who died in the Jahiliyyah is that of a king who built a palace on the main road, prepared food in it, and appointed men to it, saying: 'No one shall pass unless he partakes of this food of mine.' So when a man passed in fine appearance and fine clothes, they would go to him, cling to him, and bring him until he ate from that food. And when a man came in shabby appearance and worn clothes, they would prevent him. When that went on for a long time, Allah sent an angel from among the angels in shabby appearance and worn clothes, and he passed by their side. They rose to him and pushed him away. He said to them: 'I am hungry, and food is prepared only for the hungry.' They said: 'No, the king's food is eaten only by the righteous,' and they pushed him away, so he left. Then he came in a handsome form and fine clothes, and passed by as if he did not want them, at a distance from them. They went to him, clung to him, and said: 'Come, partake of the king's food.' He said: 'I do not want it.' They said: 'We will not leave you; if it reaches the king that someone like you passed and did not partake of his food, it would be hard on him, and we fear that punishment from him might befall us.' So they compelled him and brought him in until they came with him to the food and brought the food near to him. Then he did thus with his clothes in the food. They said: 'What are you doing?' He said: 'I came to you in shabby appearance and worn clothes, and I told you that I was hungry, but you prevented me. And I came to you in fine appearance and fine clothes, and you compelled me and overcame me and refused to leave me. May Allah disfigure you and disfigure your king! Your king prepares this food only for this world, and he has no share with Allah.' He said: Then the angel ascended, and punishment descended upon them."],[7095,"Whoever sells a house and does not buy another, there is no blessing in its price."],[7096,"He entered upon Fatimah bt. Qays, the sister of al-Dahhak b. Qays; her husband was Abu 'Amr b. Hafs b. 'Umar b. al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi. She said: 'Abu 'Amr b. Hafs sent me my divorce while he was going with an army to Yemen. I asked his guardians for maintenance and lodging, and they said: He did not send us anything about that, nor did he instruct us about it. So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu 'Amr b. Hafs sent me my divorce, and I asked for lodging and maintenance, but his guardians said: He did not send us anything. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Maintenance and lodging are only for the woman if her husband has the right to take her back. But if she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband, then she has no maintenance and no lodging.'"],[7097,"Shall I not teach you what Jibril ﷺ taught me? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: 'O Allah, forgive me my errors, my intentional acts, my jesting, and my seriousness, and do not deprive me of the blessing of what You have given me, and do not put me to trial in what You have withheld from me.'"],[7098,"We said: What is wrong with us, O Messenger of Allah, that when we are with you our hearts are in the Hereafter, but when we return that goes away from us? He said: 'If you were, when you returned, as you are when you are with me, the angels would visit you in your homes and shake hands with you with their palms. And if you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin, and He would forgive them.' I said: O Messenger of Allah..."],[7099,"'Umar b. al-Khattab passed by Mu'adh b. Jabal while he was sitting at the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping. He said: 'O Mu'adh, what makes you weep? Perhaps you remembered your brother; if you remembered him, he is worthy of that.' He said: 'No, but what made me weep was something I heard from him in this gathering of mine, or in this place of mine, saying ﷺ: The slightest showing off is shirk. Indeed, Allah loves the God-fearing, the hidden, the righteous; those who, when they are absent, are not missed, and when they are present, are not recognized. Their hearts are lamps of guidance; they come out of every dark, pitch-black trial.'"],[7100,"When one of his daughters was proposed to, he would sit by the curtain and say: 'So-and-so is proposing. If she remains silent, her silence is her consent; and if she dislikes it, she will push against the curtain. That from her is a sign of dislike.'"],[7101,"Whoever builds a mosque, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."],[7102,"Whoever eats anything of this meat, let him wash his hands."],[7103,"He accompanied Ibn 'Umar on a journey, and when Suhayl rose, he said: 'May Allah curse Suhayl, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: He was a tax collector who wronged them and usurped their wealth, so Allah transformed him into a shooting star and placed him where you see.'"],[7104,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man praying while seated. He said: Whoever prays standing, that is better; whoever prays seated has half the reward of the one standing; and whoever prays lying down has half the reward of the one seated."],[7105,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over a woman who died in her postpartum bleeding. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for the prayer over her at her middle."],[7106,"When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory."],[7107,"Paradise boasted over the Fire and said, 'I am better than you.' The Fire said, 'No, I am better than you.' Paradise said to it, questioning, 'And in what way?' It said, 'Because in me are the tyrants, Nimrod, and Pharaoh.' So it was silenced. Then Allah revealed to it: 'Do not submit; I will adorn your two corners with al-Hasan and al-Husayn.' So it swayed as a bride sways in her bridal chamber."],[7108,"He was afflicted with major ritual impurity and had no water with him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: It suffices you to wipe your face and your palms with dust—one strike for the face and one strike for the two palms."],[7109,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Makkah and asked him, 'From whom are you?' He said, 'I am from Banu Dubay'a b. Rabi'a.' The Prophet ﷺ said: The best of Rabi'a is 'Abd al-Qays, then the clan you are from. And he dispatched him with an army to Yemen."],[7110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the woman with prolonged menstrual bleeding. He said: That is a kick from Satan in her womb."],[7111,"O son of Adam, there are two things, neither of which is yours: I have given you a share in your wealth when I seize your soul, to purify you and cleanse you by it, and the prayer of My servants over you after the end of your term."],[7112,"He asked, 'How many years do you count for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after his emergence?' They said, 'Ten in Makkah and ten in Madinah.' He said, 'Do you really say that?' We said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Yes, and five and seven, in accordance with what 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ said.'"],[7113,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a delegation to Yemen and appointed over them a commander from among them, though he was the youngest of them. He stayed for some days without setting out. The Prophet ﷺ met one of them and said, 'O so-and-so, what is the matter with you? Have you not departed?' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, our commander is complaining of pain in his leg.' The Prophet ﷺ came to him and blew over him: 'In the name of Allah and by Allah, I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what is in it,' seven times, and the man recovered. An old man said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, will you put him in command over us when he is the youngest of us?' The Prophet ﷺ then mentioned his recitation of the Qur'an. The old man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, were it not that I fear I would take it as a pillow and not rise with it, I would learn it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Learn it, for the likeness of the Qur'an is like a leather bag you have filled with musk and then tied its opening. If you open it, the fragrance of musk spreads; and if you leave it, it remains musk set aside. Similarly is the likeness of the Qur'an when you recite it or when it is in your heart.'"],[7114,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some people in Makkah, and they began to poke at the back of his neck and say, 'This is the one who claims he is a prophet, and with him is Jibril.' Jibril poked with his finger, and something like a fingernail fell on their bodies and became sores, until they stank, and no one could approach them. Then Allah revealed: 'Indeed, We have sufficed you against the mockers.'"],[7115,"Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it has a qirat of reward; and if he waits until its burial is completed, he has two qirats. They said, 'What is a qirat, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Like Mount Uhud.'"],[7116,"When any of you is brought perfume, let him touch some of it; and when he is brought sweets, let him take some of them.”"],[7117,"There is no good in the gathering of women, except at a funeral, for when they gather they say, and they say.”"],[7118,"On the Day of Badr, the Prophet ﷺ was brought a leather mat from the spoils, and it was said, “Shade yourself with it, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Would you like for one among you to shade himself with a shade of fire on the Day of Resurrection?”"],[7119,"On the Day of Badr, the Prophet ﷺ was in the shade while his companions were in the sun fighting. Jibril came to him and said, “You are in the shade while the Muslims are in the sun fighting?” So he stood up and moved into the sun.”"],[7120,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a funeral, and he saw some people who had thrown off their cloaks and were walking in their shirts. He said, “Are you adopting the practice of the Jahiliyyah, or are you imitating the ways of the Jahiliyyah? I was about to invoke against you a supplication that you would return in forms other than your own.” So the people took their cloaks and put them back on.”"],[7121,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two rak‘ahs after ‘Asr."],[7122,"I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set a time limit for the traveler of three days and their nights, and for the resident of a day and a night, to wipe over the leather socks.”"],[7123,"Whoever gives a fasting person something to break his fast has the like of his reward, without diminishing anything from the reward of the fasting person. And whatever good deeds he performs, his reward is like that of the one who provided the food, according to the strength the food gave him."],[7124,"A woman in ihram should not wear a face veil, nor a burqa‘, nor gloves.”"],[7125,"Some dates were gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he distributed them. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was eating rapidly, and I realized that only hunger had driven him to that.”"],[7126,"O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, and I seek refuge with You from knowledge that does not benefit."],[7127,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Jibril, “Which places are best?” He said, “I do not know.” He said, “Then ask your Lord about that.” Jibril ﷺ wept, then said, “O Muhammad, are we allowed to ask Him? It is He who informs us of what He wills.” Then he ascended to the heaven, then came back to him and said, “The best places are the mosques, the houses of Allah on earth.” He said, “And which places are worst?” He ascended to the heaven, then came to him and said, “The worst places are the markets.””"],[7128,"Whoever hastens to praise Allah when someone sneezes will be protected from pain in the loins and will never complain of toothache."],[7129,"There is no amputation except for ten dirhams."],[7130,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage. The Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself, then returned and performed ablution, wiping over his leather socks."],[7131,"My beloved friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I will never abandon until I die: fasting three days every month, performing the Friday ritual bath, and never sleeping except after performing Witr prayer."],[7132,"The asking of a wealthy person is a disgrace on his face on the Day of Resurrection."],[7133,"Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: \"Your Lord loves four of your companions and commands you to love them.\" Some of his companions said: \"Name them for us, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Indeed, Ali is one of them.\" The next day they said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who are the group whom Allah told you He loves and commanded you to love?\" He said: \"Indeed, Ali is one of them.\" On the third day they said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who are the group whom Allah told you He loves and commanded you to love?\" He said: \"Indeed, Ali is one of them.\" Then he said: \"Ali, Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad, and Salman al-Farisi.\""],[7134,"Make tharid even if only with water."],[7135,"When the Prophet ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey, he said: \"O Jibril, my people accuse me and do not believe me.\" He replied: \"Even if your people accuse you, Abu Bakr believes you.\""],[7136,"Whoever makes the mosque his home, Allah guarantees him comfort, mercy, and safe passage over the Sirat to Paradise."],[7137,"In the end of time, a woman will enter her private chamber and find her husband transformed into a monkey because he did not believe in divine decree."],[7138,"Riba has seventy-two doors, the least of which is like a man committing incest with his mother, and the worst riba is a man's attack on his brother's honor."],[7139,"The neighbor has more right to his adjacent property."],[7140,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died at the age of sixty-three. Abu Bakr died at the age of sixty-three. ʿUmar was killed at the age of sixty-three.\" Muʿawiya said, \"And this is my day: I am fifty-seven.\" Then he lived after that twenty years."],[7141,"The two prostrations of forgetfulness in prayer suffice you for every addition and omission."],[7142,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and I left my father following me. He said, \"A cursed man will now appear.\" I was afraid it might be my father, so I kept going out and coming in until al-Hakam b. Abi al-ʿAs appeared."],[7143,"He had a thread by which he reminded himself."],[7144,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ one day and saw him looking changed. I said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, why do I see you looking changed?\" He said, \"Nothing has entered my stomach for three days that enters the stomach of any living being.\" So I went and found a Jew watering his camels. I drew water for him, for each bucket a date. I gathered dates and brought them to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"Where did you get this, O Kaʿb?\" I told him. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you love me, O Kaʿb?\" I said, \"May my father be your ransom, yes.\" He said, \"Poverty comes faster to one who loves me than a flood to its destination. And affliction will befall you, so prepare for it a coat of armor.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ missed him and said, \"What has Kaʿb done?\" They said, \"He is sick.\" He went out walking until he entered upon him and said, \"Rejoice, O Kaʿb.\" His mother said, \"Congratulations on Paradise, O Kaʿb.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Who is this swearing by God?\" He said, \"She is my mother, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"What makes you know, O mother of Kaʿb? Perhaps Kaʿb said what does not benefit him, or withheld what does not avail him.\""],[7145,"Settle in your dwellings. Emigration has ceased, but there remains jihad and intention. If you are called out, then go forth."],[7146,"We were with Anas b. Malik, and people who had left the Friday prayer met him. He entered a house and said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever is not ashamed before people is not ashamed before God.\""],[7147,"A man may free of his slave whatever he wishes: if he wishes a third, or a fourth, or a fifth. There is no compulsion between him and God."],[7148,"One of the Prophet's ﷺ family borrowed some silver and lost it, so the Prophet ﷺ made good for it."],[7149,"Destiny was mentioned in the presence of ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, and ʿAbd Allah said, \"The Qadarites were cursed on the tongue of seventy prophets, among them our Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. On the Day of Resurrection, when God gathers people on a single plain, a caller will call out, audible to the first and the last: 'Where are the adversaries of God?' Then the Qadarites will stand.\""],[7150,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married me to a woman who was either a hairdresser or a perfumer. The Prophet ﷺ saw me with perfume on and said, \"Will you not wash off this stench from yourself?\" or \"Will you not wash off this filth from yourself?\" So I went to a river and washed until the water turned yellow. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ with traces still on me, and he said, \"Go and wash it off.\" So I went and washed it, but it did not go away until I washed it with earth."],[7151,"The punishment of my community is in its worldly life."],[7152,"No orphan sits with a people at their food bowl but a devil draws near their bowl."],[7153,"Ablution before and after food dispels poverty, and it is from the practices of the Messengers (peace be upon them)."],[7154,"Regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'On the Day the earth will be changed to other than the earth,' he said: 'A white earth as if it were silver, on which no sacred blood has been shed and no sin has been committed.'"],[7155,"When Abu Bakr was mentioned in his presence, Ali would say: 'You mention the foremost one, you mention the foremost one. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, we never raced to any good but Abu Bakr beat us to it.'"],[7156,"O My servants, all of you are astray except those whom I guide, and weak except those whom I strengthen, and poor except those whom I enrich. So ask Me and I will give you. If your first and your last, your humans and your jinn, your living and your dead, your fresh and your dry were to gather on the heart of the most devout servant among My servants, they would not increase in My dominion even a mosquito's wing. And if your first and your last, your living and your dead, your fresh and your dry were to gather on the heart of the most wicked servant among My servants who belongs to Me, they would not decrease from My dominion even a mosquito's wing. That is because I am One. My punishment is a word, and My mercy is a word. Whoever is certain of My power to forgive, it is not too great for Me to forgive his sins, even if they are many."],[7157,"The witr is three rak'ahs, like the three of the Maghrib prayer."],[7158,"Some people will come to my cistern, and I will recognize them, but they will be snatched away from me. I will say: 'They are from me.' It will be said: 'You do not know what they innovated after you.'"],[7159,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head towards the ceiling of the house, he would say: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.' Aishah said: 'I asked him about these words.' He said: 'I was commanded to say them.'"],[7160,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Jibril on the night he was taken on the Night Journey: 'My people will not believe me.' Jibril said to him: 'Abu Bakr will believe you, and he is al-Siddiq.'"],[7161,"How will you be with peoples whose leader enters Paradise while their followers enter the Fire? They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, even if they act like their deeds?' He said: 'Even if they act like their deeds.' They said: 'How can that be, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'The leaders enter Paradise because of what was predestined for them, and the followers enter the Fire because of what they innovated.'"],[7162,"The key to prayer is purification; its sanctity is the takbir; its release is the taslim."],[7163,"I saw Ali see a man wearing a shining striped garment. He said: 'I think it contains silk.' He then brought together its two edges and tore it, saying: 'I do not envy you for it, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid silk and brocade.'"],[7164,"Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and Umar."],[7165,"Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, used to enter upon her while she had taken off her clothes. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Breastfeed him, and you will become forbidden to him.\""],[7166,"He used to pray on a mat."],[7167,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man on a red camel during the days of Mina, and he called out: \"O people, these are days of eating and drinking, so do not fast.\""],[7168,"Gabriel promised me an appointment, and he was delayed from me. Then he said: \"What prevented me from that was the sound of a bell or an image in the house.\""],[7169,"There are no two Muslims who lose three children who have not reached puberty, except that Allah will admit them both to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.\""],[7170,"Every amusement is disliked except a man's playing with his wife, his walking between the two targets, and his training his horse.\""],[7171,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrate on the fold of his turban."],[7172,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, clothe me.\" He turned away from him. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, clothe me.\" He said: \"Do you not have a neighbor who has an extra two garments?\" He said: \"Yes, more than one.\" He said: \"Allah will not gather you and him together in Paradise.\""],[7173,"He ate garlic and prayed with the Prophet ﷺ. When they finished, the smell of garlic was detected from him. He said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"I had a chest complaint, so I ate it.\" He did not rebuke him."],[7174,"The scholars of this nation are two men: a man whom Allah gave knowledge, and he gave it freely to the people and did not take any gain for it nor buy any price with it—for him the fish of the sea, the beasts of the land, and the birds in the air seek forgiveness, and he will come before Allah as a noble master until he accompanies the messengers. And a man whom Allah gave knowledge, but he withheld it from Allah's servants, took gain for it, and bought a price with it—that one will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire, and a caller will call out: \"This is the one whom Allah gave knowledge but he withheld it from Allah's servants, took gain for it, and bought a price with it,\" and so on until the reckoning is finished."],[7175,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf came to the Prophet ﷺ with traces of yellow on him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Mahyam?\"—and that was his word when he wanted to ask about something. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I got married.\" He said: \"For how much?\" He said: \"For the weight of a date pit of gold.\" He said: \"Hold a wedding feast, even if with a sheep.\" Anas said: \"We estimated it as a quarter of a dinar.\""],[7176,"There is no prayer after Fajr except the two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer.\""],[7177,"Slaughter with anything that cuts the jugular veins and lets the blood flow, except the tooth and the nail.\""],[7178,"The Dajjal will emerge from the direction of Isfahan."],[7179,"There is nothing more noble in the sight of God than the believer."],[7180,"For a man to gather firewood on his back and sell it is better for him than to beg from people."],[7181,"No man severs the right of a Muslim man by his oath except that God forbids Paradise for him and makes the Fire obligatory for him.\""],[7182,"The Messenger of God ﷺ combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha in Madinah while he was a resident, without fear or travel; he only intended thereby ease for his community.\""],[7183,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ retired to his bed, he would say: O God, I seek refuge in You from evil, eagerly, and from hunger, as a bedfellow.\""],[7184,"Does not the one who raises his head before the imam and lowers his head fear that God will turn his head into the head of a donkey?\""],[7185,"I saw Ali b. Abi Talib displaying a sword of his in the open area of Kufa and saying: 'Who will buy this sword of mine from me? By God, I have polished away with it more than one distress from the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and if I had the price of a waist-wrapper I would not sell it.'"],[7186,"I heard al-Nu'man b. Bashir saying on the pulpit in Kufa: The Messenger of God ﷺ would stand in prayer at night until his feet cracked. It was said to him: O Messenger of God, has not God forgiven you your past and future sins? He said: Should I not be a grateful servant?"],[7187,"Whoever says after the Fajr prayer: There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; He gives life and causes death; in His hand is all good; and He has power over all things, one hundred times before he folds his legs, he will on that day be the best of the people of the earth in deeds, except one who says the like of what he said or increases upon what he said.\""],[7188,"He used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil (Surah al-Sajdah) and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan (Surah al-Insan)."],[7189,"The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and the Christians split into seventy-two sects, and my Ummah will exceed them by one sect. All of them will be in the Fire except the great majority (al-sawad al-a'zam)."],[7190,"While the Prophet ﷺ was praying 'Asr during the Battle of Badr, he smiled. When he finished the prayer, it was said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, you smiled during the prayer?' He said: 'Mika'il passed by me with dust on his wing, and he laughed at me, so I smiled.'"],[7191,"Whoever seeks Laylat al-Qadr should seek it in the last ten nights."],[7192,"There is no man who says when he reaches the morning: 'O Allah, I have entered the morning calling You to witness, and I call the bearers of Your Throne, Your angels, and all Your creation to witness that You are Allah, there is no god but You alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger' except that Allah forgives him whatever sin he commits that day. And if he says it when he reaches the evening, Allah forgives him whatever sin he commits that night."],[7193,"The Prophet ﷺ used to come to the first row from its beginning to its end, straightening the rows, the people and their shoulders, saying: 'Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first rows.'"],[7194,"Muhammad ﷺ obligated on the wealth of the Muslims: from every forty dirhams, one dirham; on the wealth of the people of the covenant (ahl al-dhimmah): from every twenty dirhams, one dirham; and on the wealth of those who have no covenant: from every ten dirhams, one dirham."],[7195,"Ibn Mas'ud wanted to build a house, and the Quraysh said: 'Should we not prevent Ibn Umm 'Abd from building a house among us?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If I were to command that, I would be an oppressor. Allah does not sanctify a nation that does not take for its weak from its strong.'"],[7196,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on the pulpit saying: 'When one of you goes to the Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl.'"],[7197,"We do not have a bad example: the one who takes back his gift is like the one who goes back to his vomit."],[7198,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ with two young boys, one of whom she was nursing. She asked the Prophet ﷺ for something, but he could not find anything to give her until he found three dates with one of his wives. He gave them to her. She gave one date to this boy and one date to the other, and kept one date for herself. One of the boys cried, so she split the date into two halves and gave half to this one and half to the other. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Pregnant, giving birth, nursing, merciful to their children—were it not for what they do to their husbands, those among them who pray would enter Paradise.'"],[7199,"Four things, whoever is given them has been given the best of this world and the Hereafter: a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, a body patient in affliction, and a wife who does not seek to betray him in herself or his wealth."],[7200,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the freedmen of the Ansar."],[7201,"Part of faith is that a man loves a man whom he loves only for the sake of Allah, without any wealth that he gave him; that is faith."],[7202,"The nations are about to invite one another to come upon my community as diners invite one another to a platter of food."],[7203,"He forbade fasting on Friday, unless it is accompanied by fasting another day."],[7204,"Perform ablution from what fire has changed."],[7205,"I said: O Prophet of Allah, my neighbor's house is where my house is, but his door is far from my door, while another's door is opposite my door and his house is farther than that one's house. Which of them should I begin with? He said: With the one whose door is opposite your door."],[7206,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Abu Bakr while he was praying, lowering his voice, and he passed by Umar while he was praying, raising his voice. When morning came and they gathered with the Prophet ﷺ, he said to Abu Bakr: O Abu Bakr, I passed by you while you were praying, lowering your voice? He said: I made myself heard by the One I was confiding in. He said: Raise your voice a little. And he said to Umar: I passed by you, O Umar, while you were praying, raising your voice? He said: I feared Satan, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Lower your voice a little."],[7207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in prayer during his illness while seated, so they stood. He gestured to them, and they sat. Then he said: The imam is to be followed. When he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate; and when he prays seated, pray seated."],[7208,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque and saw few people. He said: If a man were to call the people to a bone with meat on it and a flat loaf of bread—meaning by a flat loaf—they would answer him, yet they stay behind from this prayer. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I was about to order young men to gather bundles of firewood, then burn the houses of people who hear the caller and do not answer him."],[7209,"Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talha and al-Zubayr are in Paradise, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman is in Paradise. And the ninth, if I wished, I would name him. They said: Who is he? He said: He is the one who was. When they pressed him, he said: I am he, and he wept."],[7210,"Recite the Quran with the melodies and voices of the Arabs, and beware of the melodies of the People of the two Books and the people of wickedness. For there will come after me a people who trill the Quran like singing, monastic chanting, and wailing; it does not pass beyond their throats. Their hearts are tempted, and so are the hearts of those who admire their ways."],[7211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who pursues a woman unlawfully: may he marry her mother? Or he pursues the mother unlawfully: may he marry her daughter? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The unlawful does not make the lawful unlawful. Only what occurs through a lawful marriage makes unlawful."],[7212,"We came as a delegation to the Messenger of God ﷺ and caught up with him at al-Juhfa. The people rejoiced at our arrival, and we embraced Islam. He instructed them to proceed with him to Madinah. Their brothers from among the people used to attend to them every evening, and to the strangers among the Muslims who had come to the Prophet ﷺ. He used to urge [them] regarding their share, saying: “Your brothers are your guests. Each person [should help] according to what God has made ample for him.” So a man would rise and take one man, or two men, and the one who took three was ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf.\""],[7213,"The Prophet ﷺ encamped at Khaybar. The ruler of Khaybar was a defiant, fierce man. He approached the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Muhammad, is it [permissible] for you to slaughter our donkeys, eat our dates, enter our houses, and strike our women?” The Prophet ﷺ became angry and said, “O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, mount your horse and call out among the people: ‘Paradise is not lawful except for a believer, and gather for prayer.’” So they gathered, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed. Then he said, “God has not made it lawful for you to enter the houses of the People of the Book except with permission, nor to consume their wealth, nor to strike their women, when they give you what is due from them, except what they give willingly. Does a man think, having eaten his fill until he is satiated, lounging on his couch, that God has not forbidden anything except what is in this Qur’an? Verily, by God, I have forbidden and commanded and admonished with things that are like the Qur’an or more. Verily, it is not lawful for you [to eat] any predatory animal with fangs, nor domestic donkeys.\""],[7214,"A man was heading to prayer when his wife met him, and he bent over her and took hold of her. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he did not forbid him."],[7215,"It is part of the Sunnah that when a man sits, he removes his sandals and places them beside him."],[7216,"The Prophet ﷺ had promised al-ʿAbbās a small herd of camels. He sent me to him, so I spent the night at his place. It was the night of Maymūna bt. al-Ḥārith. The Prophet ﷺ slept for only a little while. I rested my head on the pillow that the Messenger of God ﷺ had used. Then the Prophet ﷺ got up, performed ablution, made it thorough, and used only a small amount of water. Then he stood and began the prayer. I got up, performed ablution, and stood on his left. He reached back with his hand, took hold of my ear, and made me stand on his right. Maymūna was menstruating; she got up, performed ablution, and sat behind him remembering God."],[7217,"He used to perform the ritual bath on Friday, on the day of al-Fiṭr, on the day of al-Naḥr, and on the day of ʿArafa."],[7218,"I saw ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb come to the [Black] Stone, place his hands on its two sides, then kiss what was between them. Then he said, “By God, I know that you are a stone, and that you can neither harm nor benefit. Had I not seen the Messenger of God ﷺ kiss you, I would not have kissed you.”"],[7219,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ pronounce the talbiya for both of them together: “Labbayka for a ḥajj and an ʿumra together.”"],[7220,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying, “O Messenger of God, which deeds are most beloved to God and closest to God?” He said, “Prayer at its proper time.”"],[7221,"I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ until he passed away, and behind Abū Bakr and ʿUmar until they passed away. I never heard any of them recite “Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm” aloud in prayer; they used to begin with “al-Ḥamd [li-llāhi rabbi l-ʿālamīn].”"],[7222,"Whoever sends one ṣalāh upon me, God sends ten upon him. Whoever sends ten upon me, God sends a hundred upon him. Whoever sends a hundred upon me, God writes between his eyes a declaration of freedom from hypocrisy and freedom from the Fire, and God will lodge him on the Day of Resurrection with the martyrs."],[7223,"The days of al-Tashrīq are days of eating and drinking."],[7224,"When the Prophet ﷺ married Fatimah to Ali, he said, “Give her something.” He said, “I have nothing.” He said, “Where is your H utamiyyah armor?”"],[7225,"Shall I not tell you about the best of your governors and the worst of them? They said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “The best of them are those who are best to you, whom you love and who love you, for whom you pray to God and they pray to God for you. The worst of them are those who are worst to you, whom you hate and who hate you, against whom you pray to God and they pray to God against you.” They said, “Should we not fight them, O Messenger of God?” He said, “No, leave them as long as they pray and fast.”"],[7226,"A man was reviling Abu Bakr in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, while Abu Bakr remained silent. When the man stopped, Abu Bakr responded with a word, so the Prophet ﷺ got up, and Abu Bakr followed him. He said, “O Messenger of God, he reviled me while you were sitting, and when I responded—or defended myself, or something like that—you stood up?” He said, “There was an angel responding on your behalf, saying, ‘You lie.’ But when you spoke, Satan took your place, and I disliked sitting.” Three things, O Abu Bakr, all of them true: no servant is wronged by an injustice and overlooks it seeking the Face of God, except that God grants him victory by it. No servant opens a door of giving, seeking the Face of God or kinship, except that God increases him in abundance by it. And no servant opens a door of asking, seeking abundance by it, except that God increases him in scarcity by it."],[7227,"Give gifts, and you will love one another. Emigrate, and you will bequeath glory to your children. And overlook the slips of the noble.”"],[7228,"When God created the intellect, He said to it, “Come forward,” and it came forward. Then He said to it, “Turn back,” and it turned back. He said, “By My might, I have not created any creation more pleasing to Me than you. Through you I take, through you I give, through you is reward, and upon you is punishment.”"],[7229,"The group who came to the Messenger of God ﷺ were jinn of Nasibin; they came to him while he was at Nakhlah."],[7230,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ, “Do not precede me in saying Amin.”"],[7231,"Whoever reproaches his brother for a sin will not die until he commits it himself."],[7232,"O father, what is this prayer? He said, “I saw my beloved, the Messenger of God ﷺ, pray six rak’ahs after Maghrib, and he said, ‘Whoever prays six rak’ahs after Maghrib, his sins will be forgiven, even if they were like the foam of the sea.’”"],[7233,"The Prophet ﷺ gave us a sermon one day and said, “Indeed, God has made the Friday prayer obligatory upon you in this station of mine, in this hour of mine, on this day of mine, in this month of mine, in this year of mine, until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever leaves it without excuse, under a just imam or an unjust imam, his affairs will not be gathered for him, nor will he be blessed in his matter. Indeed, he has no prayer, no Hajj, no righteousness, and no charity.”"],[7234,"The Prophet ﷺ detained someone on suspicion."],[7235,"My name in the pre-Islamic era was Abd Kulal, and the Prophet ﷺ named me Abd al-Rahman."],[7236,"Honor me with regard to my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then lying will become widespread until a man testifies before he is asked to testify, and swears an oath before he is asked to swear, and offers himself with false speeches. So whoever wants the spaciousness of Paradise, let him keep to the community (jama'ah), for the hand of God is upon the community, and Satan is with the lone individual, and he is farther away from two. And let no man be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. And whoever is troubled by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed is a believer."],[7237,"Go early in seeking provision and needs, for the early morning is blessing and success.\""],[7238,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed with his Companions, then said: \"Did any of you just recite during the prayer?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I say: I should not be contended with in the Qur'an.\" And the people stopped reciting with him when he said that.\""],[7239,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered Budayl to hold the captives and property at al-Ji'ranah until he came to him. So they were held."],[7240,"The first prayer in which we bowed was 'Asr. I said: \"O Messenger of God, what is this?\" He said: \"With this I was commanded.\""],[7241,"He used to pray voluntary prayers on his riding beast, whichever direction it faced."],[7242,"I heard al-Hasan b. 'Ali say: \"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream clinging to the Throne, and I saw Abu Bakr holding the Prophet's ﷺ waist, and I saw 'Umar holding Abu Bakr's waist, and I saw 'Uthman holding 'Umar's waist, and I saw blood pouring from heaven to earth.\" Al-Hasan related this hadith while some Shi'a were with him, and they said: \"And what did you see of 'Ali?\" Al-Hasan said: \"There was no one more beloved to me to see holding the Prophet's ﷺ waist than 'Ali, but it was a dream I saw.\" Abu Mas'ud said: \"You relate from al-Hasan b. 'Ali about a dream he saw. We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a campaign, and the people were struck with hardship until I saw gloom on the faces of the Muslims and joy on the faces of the hypocrites. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that, he said: 'By God, the sun will not set until God brings you provision.' 'Uthman knew that God and His Messenger would prove true, so 'Uthman bought fourteen camels with their loads of food and sent nine of them to the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw that, he said: 'What is this?' They said: ''Uthman sent it to you as a gift.' Joy was seen on the faces of the Muslims and gloom on the faces of the hypocrites. I saw the Prophet ﷺ raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was visible, supplicating for 'Uthman with a supplication the like of which I never heard him make for anyone before or after: 'O God, give 'Uthman; O God, do for 'Uthman...'\""],[7243,"Banu Fulān came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, we have submitted and done so, and we have not fought you while the Arabs have fought you.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ turned to Abu Bakr and 'Umar and said: \"Do you two say this?\" They said: \"No.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Their understanding is little, and Satan has spoken falsely on their tongues.\""],[7244,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sent to the Arabian Peninsula and filled it with equity and justice.\" Then Abu Bakr led them on, and he led them on a prosperous journey.\" \"Then 'Umar led them on, and he led them on a prosperous journey.\""],[7245,"Gabriel ﷺ used to dictate to the Prophet ﷺ."],[7246,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a house in which were Fāṭimah and 'Alī, and Ḥasan and Ḥusayn, and he said: \"I am at war with those you war against, and at peace with those you make peace with.\""],[7247,"When the people crowded around the Prophet of God ﷺ, he would hasten his pace; when he found an opening, he would slow to a normal pace. When he looked at the people, he said: \"O people, piety is not in hastening.\""],[7248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate: “O Allah, set right for me my religion which is the safeguard of my affairs, and set right for me my worldly life in which is my livelihood, and set right for me my Hereafter to which is my return, and make life an increase for me in every good, and make death a relief for me from every evil.”"],[7249,"The most beloved of women to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was Fatimah, and of men, Ali."],[7250,"Ibn Abbas said to me: “O son of Utbah, do you know the last surah of the Quran that was revealed complete?” I said: “Yes, ‘When the victory of Allah comes.’” He said: “You are right.”"],[7251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was from the middle of Quraysh, with all of whom he had ties of kinship. He said: “Say: ‘I ask of you no reward for it, except affection among relatives’ — that is, that you love me because of the kinship between me and you.”"],[7252,"“O son of Adam, when you remember Me, you thank Me, and when you forget Me, you disbelieve Me.”"],[7253,"Al-bidʿ is what is between three and nine."],[7254,"Whoever revives dead land, it is his, and there is no right for a vein of an unjust person."],[7255,"Allah has obligated upon His servants five prayers in every day and night."],[7256,"Idris ﷺ was a friend of the Angel of Death. He asked him to show him Paradise and Hellfire. So he ascended with Idris and showed him Hellfire, and he was terrified by it and nearly fainted. The Angel of Death wrapped him with his wing. The Angel of Death said: “Have you not seen it?” He said: “Yes, and I have never seen the like of it before.” Then he took him until he showed him Paradise, and he entered it. The Angel of Death said to him: “Have you not seen it?” He said: “Yes, by Allah, this is Paradise.” The Angel of Death said to him: “Come, you have seen it.” He said: “Where to?” The Angel of Death said: “To where you were.” Idris said: “No, by Allah, I will not leave it after having entered it.” It was said to the Angel of Death: “Did you not enter him into it? Indeed, no one who enters it may leave it.”"],[7257,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed, he would spread his fingers."],[7258,"May Allah have mercy on the one who hears this saying of mine and memorizes it until he conveys it to another. Three things: no heart of a Muslim person should begrudge them — sincerity of action for Allah, giving good counsel to the leaders of the Muslims, and adhering to their community, for their supplication encompasses what is behind them. Whoever has the world as his intention, Allah will place his poverty before his eyes, and Allah will scatter his estate for him, and nothing of it will come to him except what is written for him. And whoever has the Hereafter as his intention, Allah will place his richness in his heart, and suffice him his estate, and the world will come to him while it is compelled."],[7259,"When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, a man will stand and say: “O Lord, permit me to cultivate.” He will permit him, and he will sow his seed. Before he turns around, every ear of grain will return to a length of twelve cubits. Then he will not leave his place until there is from it heaps like mountains.” A bedouin said: “O Messenger of Allah, you will not find this man except a Qurashi or an Ansari.” The Prophet ﷺ laughed."],[7260,"Whoever is not content with Allah's decree and does not believe in Allah's predestination, let him seek a god other than Allah."],[7261,"Wealth is not from an abundance of goods; rather, wealth is contentment of the soul."],[7262,"A dream is not to be related except to a scholar or a sincere adviser."],[7263,"Amputation is for a dinar or ten dirhams."],[7264,"Indeed, the people of blessings have enviers, so beware of them."],[7265,"I used to prepare nabidh for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a green jar."],[7266,"While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a young man came to him to ask for a ruling. He mentioned that he had met a woman, kissed her, touched her, wrestled with her, and desired her but was unable to have intercourse. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not give him any ruling. When he left, he sent a man after him, called him back, and recited this verse to him: 'And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the first hours of the night...' The man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is this for him alone or for all people?' He said, 'Rather, for all people.'"],[7267,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the takbir during the days of tashriq from the Zuhr prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until he left Mina, saying the takbir after every prescribed prayer."],[7268,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[7269,"There is no gulp greater in reward with Allah than a gulp of anger that a Muslim suppresses seeking the pleasure of Allah."],[7270,"Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange as it began, so blessed are the strangers."],[7271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ suffered from a sore throat (al-'udhra) until it caused him a headache, and that was visible on him. Then Jibril came to him and said, 'Your Lord has sent me to you to perform ruqyah on you.' The Prophet ﷺ uncovered his head, and he said, 'In the name of Allah, I perform ruqyah on you, from everything that harms you, from the evil of every envious eye, I perform ruqyah on you.' He said, 'He repeated it three times, and the Prophet ﷺ was cured.'"],[7272,"I was standing over my paternal uncles, giving them some of their date wine to drink, when a man came and said: 'Wine has been forbidden.' They said: 'Spill it!' So I spilled it. I said: 'What was it?' He said: 'Unripe dates and ripe dates.'"],[7273,"A man came after the Prophet ﷺ had prayed, and he stood to pray alone. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who will trade with this man and pray with him?'"],[7274,"Is any of you unable to recite one third of the Qur'an every night? They said: 'And who can do that?' He said: 'By reciting: \"Say: He is Allah, the One.\"'"],[7275,"The Prophet ﷺ was in a garden belonging to a man from the Ansar when a man came seeking permission to enter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Arise, O Anas, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will be in charge of my community after me.' I arose and opened for him, and behold, it was Abu Bakr. I gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and he praised Allah, then entered. Then another came and knocked at the door, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Arise, O Anas, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will be in charge of my community after Abu Bakr.' I opened for him, and behold, it was Umar. I gave him glad tidings, and he praised Allah, then entered. Then another came and knocked at the door, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Arise, O Anas, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will be in charge of my community after Abu Bakr and Umar, and that he will face severe hardship from the subjects until they go so far as to shed his blood. At that time I will command him to refrain.' I opened for him, and behold, it was Uthman b. Affan. I gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and he praised Allah. Then I informed him of his coming authority and that they would go so far as to shed his blood. He said: 'Indeed, to Allah we belong and to Him we return,' then entered."],[7276,"Any hide that has been tanned has become pure."],[7277,"We used to take provisions from the meat of the sacrificial animals at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ back to Madinah."],[7278,"We were with Abdullah b. Umar when a man from the people of Kufa asked him: 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, tell me about Uthman b. Affan: did he witness the Battle of Badr?' He said: 'No.' The man said: 'Allah is greatest.' He then asked: 'Tell me, was Uthman among those who turned back on the day the two armies met?' He said: 'Yes.' The man said: 'Allah is greatest.' He then asked: 'Tell me, did Uthman witness the Day of the Pledge of Ridwan?' He said: 'No.' The man said: 'Allah is greatest,' and then left. I said to Ibn Umar - while still in my place: 'This man is from Kufa, and they love Ali and hate Uthman.' He said: 'Bring the man back to me.' So he was brought. Ibn Umar said: 'You asked me whether Uthman witnessed Badr, and I told you no, but I will tell you about that: the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was ill, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Stay behind to care for my daughter?\" He replied: \"As you wish.\" The Prophet ﷺ then said: \"It is dearer to me that you stay behind to care for her.\" And he assigned him a share and a reward equal to one who was present, so say one: \"Allah is greatest.\" As for your saying that he was among those who turned back on the day the two armies met, Allah has informed us that He pardoned them, so say two: \"Allah is greatest.\" As for your saying that he did not witness the Pledge of Ridwan, the Prophet ﷺ had sent Uthman to the people of Makkah. When he ordered the pledge, the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Allah, Uthman is on Your business and the business of Your Messenger. This is my hand, and this is the hand of Uthman,\" and he struck one of his hands with the other, pledging on his behalf.'"],[7279,"The Muhajirun said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'We have come to a people the like of whom we have never seen: none better in sharing even in little, and none more generous in giving in abundance. By Allah, they have taken care of the expenses and shared with us in the good things. We fear they will take all the reward.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'No, as long as you praise them for it and pray for them.'"],[7280,"There are people from among those who say 'There is no god but Allah' who will enter Hell because of their sins. The people of al-Lat and al-Uzza will say to them: 'What did your saying \"There is no god but Allah\" avail you, when you are with us in Hell?' Then Allah will become angry on their behalf, bring them out, and cast them into the River of Life. They will recover from their burns as the moon recovers from its eclipse, and they will enter Paradise, where they will be called 'the Jahannamiyyin.' A man said: 'O Anas, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' Anas said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell.\" Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say this.'"],[7281,"The child of fornication is the worst of the three, if he acts according to the deeds of his parents."],[7282,"I entered upon Aishah, and she said: 'What is the matter with Abu al-Hasan that he kills his companions, the Qur'an reciters?' I said: 'O Mother of the Believers, we found among the slain one with a breast like a woman's.' She gasped - or took a deep breath - and then said: 'One who conceals testimony is like one who gives false witness. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The best of my community will kill this group.\"'"],[7283,"Whoever would like to adorn his child with a bracelet of fire, let him adorn him with a bracelet of gold. But as for silver, do with it whatever you wish."],[7284,"Whoever mutilates something and does not repent from it, he will be mutilated with it on the Day of Resurrection."],[7285,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to marry Arab women."],[7286,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Bakr and Umar: Praise be to Allah who has strengthened me with you two. Were it not that you two disagree with me, I would not have disagreed with you."],[7287,"Do not shake hands with the Jews and Christians."],[7288,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded cutting the swings."],[7289,"When he began the prayer, he would say: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, then he would remain silent for a little while."],[7290,"It is part of righteousness to maintain ties with your father's friend."],[7291,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two rak'ahs before dawn and the two rak'ahs after sunset: Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One."],[7292,"The ruler of Alexandria, al-Muqawqis, sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a Syrian kohl container of wood, a mirror, and a comb."],[7293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Abu al-Darda' walking in front of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and said: O Abu al-Darda', you walk ahead of a man than whom the sun has not risen, after the prophets, on anyone better. After that, Abu al-Darda' was never seen walking except behind Abu Bakr."],[7294,"The days were shown to me, and Friday was shown among them. It was like a beautiful mirror, and in its middle was a black spot. I said: What is this? It was said: The Hour."],[7295,"Ali b. Abi Talib heard a clamor in the mosque, with people reciting the Qur'an and teaching it. He said: Glad tidings to these; these were the most beloved people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7296,"The Prophet ﷺ used to come to us and visit us. When the prayer time arrived, we would place a vessel for him, which we estimated he would take one mudd or a mudd and a half. He would wash his palms three times, rinse his mouth three times, and sniff water into his nostrils three times. He would wash his face three times, then wash his hands three times each. He would wipe his head once, wash his ears—their outer and inner parts and their folds—and wash his feet three times each, passing his fingers between his toes.\""],[7297,"Faith is three hundred and thirty-three branches; whoever fulfills one of them will enter Paradise."],[7298,"Clean between your teeth, for it is cleanliness, and cleanliness leads to faith, and faith will be with its possessor in Paradise."],[7299,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform Witr with 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High', 'Say, O disbelievers', and 'Say, He is Allah, [who is] One'."],[7300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to lock the door, cover the vessel, tie the water-skin, and extinguish the lamp."],[7301,"When a servant stands in prayer, his sins are gathered upon his head; when he bows, they are dispersed."],[7302,"The people of the 'knot' have perished, by the Lord of the Kaaba. By Allah, I do not grieve for them, but I grieve for those of the nation of Muhammad ﷺ who have been destroyed."],[7303,"Among the signs of the Hour is that the world will be dominated by Luqāʿ ibn Luqāʿ (the lowly son of the lowly). The best of people then will be a believer between two noble ones.\""],[7304,"The most beloved food to Allah is that upon which many hands gather."],[7305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿAlī: 'You will be given authority and appointed as successor, and you will be killed, and this will be dyed from this'—his beard from his head."],[7306,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me saying: 'Indeed, to Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. An opening has been made in the barrier of Gog and Magog like this,' and he made a circle of ninety. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?' He said, 'Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.'"],[7307,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not bring his wife into the bathhouse. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him hasten to the Friday prayer. Whoever is distracted from it by entertainment or trade, Allah will be indifferent to him, and Allah is Self-Sufficient, Praiseworthy.\""],[7308,"The Prophet’s wives ﷺ asked him about the hem of the garment. He said: “Make it a span.” They said: “A span does not cover the private parts.” He said: “Make it a cubit, and do not add more than that.”"],[7309,"I do jest, but I say nothing but the truth."],[7310,"Beware of sins that are deemed insignificant, for sins deemed insignificant are like a people who encamped in the bottom of a valley, and one came with a stick and another came with a stick, until they gathered enough to cook their bread. And when sins deemed insignificant are held against their perpetrator, they destroy him."],[7311,"Allah, exalted be His mention, has permitted me to speak of a rooster whose feet have pierced the earth and whose neck is bent beneath the Throne, and it says: ‘Glory be to You, how great You are, our Lord.’ He replies to it: ‘No one who swears falsely by Me knows that.’"],[7312,"Four things have been decreed for the son of Adam: his physical creation, his character, his provision, and his lifespan."],[7313,"Whoever walks to fulfill his brother’s need, it is better for him than retreat in the mosque for ten years. And whoever retreats one day seeking Allah’s countenance, Allah places between him and the Fire three trenches, each trench farther than the distance between the two horizons."],[7314,"The Prophet ﷺ came out with a knot tied between his shoulders. A Bedouin said to him: “What is this, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Woe to you, O Bedouin, I wore it only to suppress pride.”"],[7315,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not consider a person of nobility greater or lesser except by piety."],[7316,"A scorpion stung the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying. He said: “May Allah curse the scorpion; it stings the one praying and the one not praying. Kill it whether in the sacred precinct or outside it.”"],[7317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by land belonging to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf in which there was cultivation. He said: “O Abd al-Rahman, do not consume usury nor feed it to others, and do not cultivate except in land that you inherit, that you will bequeath, or that is given to you.”"],[7318,"There is no suckling after weaning, no orphanhood after puberty, no silence for a day until nightfall, and no divorce except after marriage."],[7319,"We used to be taught the istikhara supplication as we were taught a surah from the Quran: when a man intends a matter, he should say: ‘O Allah, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek ability by Your power, and I ask of Your vast bounty. For You have power and I have none, and You know and I know not, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this matter which I desire’—and he names it—‘is good for me in my religion, good for me in my worldly life, good for me in my hereafter, and good for me in the outcome of my affair, then facilitate it for me and bless me in it. But if it is evil for me in my religion, evil for me in my worldly life, evil for me in my hereafter, and evil for me in the outcome of my affair, then turn it away from me, and facilitate for me the good, and decree it for me, then make me content with Your decree.’"],[7320,"Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: How are you this morning, O Messenger of Allah? He replied: Well, in a good state, better than a man who has not arisen fasting, nor visited a sick person, nor followed a funeral procession."],[7321,"Among what Allah created is a rooster whose claws are on the seventh earth, and whose comb is folded beneath the Throne, and whose wings encompass the two horizons. When the last third of the night remains, it beats its wings and then says: Glorify the King, the Holy; glory be to our Lord, the King, the Holy, there is no deity for us other than Him. He said: Then all between the east and west hear it except the jinn and humans. He said: Then they see that the roosters only beat their wings and cry when they hear that."],[7322,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of Adam, was he a prophet? He said: Yes, he was a prophet, a messenger, to whom Allah spoke directly before that. He said to him: O Adam, dwell, you and your wife, in Paradise."],[7323,"Whoever recites Qul huwa Allahu ahad, it is as if he has recited a third of the Quran."],[7324,"The Ansar are my legacy and my trust. Accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers."],[7325,"I see that your dreams have agreed upon the last ten nights, so seek it in the last ten nights."],[7326,"The Prophet ﷺ was distributing the spoils of Hunayn while Jibril was beside him. An angel came and said: Your Lord commands you such and such. The Prophet ﷺ feared it might be a devil, so he said to Jibril: Do you know him? He said: He is an angel, and not all the angels of your Lord do I know."],[7327,"The people of the highest degrees will surely see those below them as you see the brilliant star on the horizon of the sky. Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent they are."],[7328,"The one who remembers Allah in Ramadan is forgiven, and the one who asks Allah in it will not be disappointed."],[7329,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the minbar while people were around him: O people, be truly shy of Allah. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we are shy of Allah. He said: Whoever among you is shy, let him not spend a night except with his death before his eyes. Let him guard the stomach and what it contains, and the head and what it gathers. Let him remember the graves and decay, and let him abandon the adornment of the worldly life."],[7330,"I passed by Kufa and entered the mosque. There I saw a group sitting as if their heads had been cut off. I sat at the edge of the group and said to a man: O servant of Allah, who is this man? He said: You seem to be a stranger. I said: Yes. He said: If you were from its people, you would know him. This is Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman. He began to narrate to the people, saying: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about good, but I used to ask him about evil, so that I might avoid it, and I knew that good would never pass me by. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, after this good, is there evil? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and act according to what is in it. Then he said: Yes, a trial and disagreement. I said: Will there be good after that? He said: Yes, a community with impurities, and a truce upon corruption. I said: O Messenger of Allah, after that good, is there evil? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and act according to what is in it. He asked him three times in the same manner, and he said the same. Then he said: Yes, there will be a trial whose gates have callers to the Fire. To die while biting onto a tree stump is better than following any one of them."],[7331,"Whoever repents before the sun rises from the west, Allah will accept his repentance."],[7332,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. Among us were those who fasted and those who did not fast. The one fasting did not criticize the one not fasting, nor did the one not fasting criticize the one fasting."],[7333,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution washing each part once, then he stood up and prayed."],[7334,"When you place your dead in the graves, say: In the name of Allah and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7335,"He ordered a caller who called out on a rainy night: Pray in your dwellings."],[7336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled by an oath with a single witness."],[7337,"Regret is repentance."],[7338,"The most beloved religion to Allah is the tolerant monotheism."],[7339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mixing fresh dates and unripe dates, and raisins and dates, to be soaked together."],[7340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and circumambulated the House on his mount, touching the corner with his staff. Then he said, 'O Abbas, is there any drink there?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'From what the pilgrims have stirred with their hands, or from what is in the house?' He said, 'From what the pilgrims have stirred with their hands.' He brought a wooden cup and raised it to his face, but he disliked it and turned away. Then he said, 'The raisins of Taif have a strong bite.' Then he said, 'Bring me a bucket of water.' A bucket of water was brought, and he poured it over it, then he drank and gave his companions to drink."],[7341,"I said, 'Did you used to say to anyone from the people of the qiblah: You are an unbeliever?' He said, 'No.' I said, 'Did you used to say: You are a polytheist?' He said, 'I seek refuge with Allah.'"],[7342,"This is a day of festival which Allah has made for the Muslims. Whoever comes to Friday prayer should perform ghusl, and if he has perfume, he should apply some of it, and you should use the tooth stick."],[7343,"A man was admitted to Paradise and saw his slave above his station. He said, 'My Lord, this is my slave above my station in Paradise?' He said to him, 'Yes, I rewarded him for his deeds and rewarded you for your deeds.'"],[7344,"The first driver to Paradise will be a slave who obeys Allah and obeys his masters—or his master."],[7345,"No charity is better than charity given to a slave who is under a bad master."],[7346,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have a spear planted for him, and he would pray facing it—I think he said—while caravans passed in front of him."],[7347,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say in his supplication: O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, and pardon me among those You have pardoned, and take me under Your care among those You have taken under Your care, and bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, for You decree and none can decree against You, and he whom You befriend is never humiliated. Blessed and exalted are You, our Lord."],[7348,"The pilgrim in the state of ihram may not marry, nor propose, nor have a proposal made on his behalf."],[7349,"The confederates distracted us on the day of the trench from the afternoon prayer, so he said: What is wrong with them? May Allah fill their graves and their houses with fire. They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set."],[7350,"Mu'adh b. Jabal used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, then go to his people and lead them in prayer. He led them in a prayer and recited to them [Surah] al-Baqarah. A man shortened his prayer and prayed a light prayer. That reached Mu'adh, so he said: He is a hypocrite. That reached the man, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people who work with our hands and water with our camels, and last night Mu'adh led us in prayer and recited al-Baqarah, so I shortened my prayer. He claimed that I am a hypocrite. The Prophet ﷺ said: O Mu'adh, are you a troublemaker? — three times — O Mu'adh, recite [Surah] al-Shams wa Duhaha and [Surah] Sabbih Isma Rabbika al-A'la and similar surahs."],[7351,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to her and said: Do you have any food? I said: No. He said: Then I am fasting. Then another day he came, and 'A'ishah said: O Messenger of Allah, we have been given a gift of hays. He called for it and said: I began this day fasting."],[7352,"Do not drink from vessels of gold and silver, and do not eat in them."],[7353,"The Prophet ﷺ disliked the marking of a horse with three white legs and one white foreleg (shikal) in horses."],[7354,"Whoever frees a share in a slave and has wealth, the entire slave becomes free; otherwise, only what he freed becomes free."],[7355,"Bad omens were mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and they said: In the house, the woman, and the riding beast. The Prophet ﷺ said: If there is any of that, it is in the good omen."],[7356,"Among the trees there is no tree that is more like the Muslim man among people than it. Ibn Umar said: Nothing prevented me from asking him except that I was the youngest of the people. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: It is the date-palm."],[7357,"Circumambulation is a prayer, so minimize speech during it."],[7358,"Ka'b b. Malik asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a slave girl of his who slaughtered a sheep with a sharp stone; he said: Eat it."],[7359,"Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat is deducted from his deeds every day."],[7360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the earnings of a cupper."],[7361,"An angel calls out: O Allah, hasten a replacement for the spender and ruin for the miser."],[7362,"I heard the Truthful, the Trusted ﷺ relating from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted: The good deed is ten or more, and the evil deed is one or I forgive it. Whoever meets Me—not associating anything with Me—with the earth's fill of sins, I will make for him the like of it as forgiveness."],[7363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came forward until when he was at al-Ji'ranah, the people gathered around him and his cloak caught on a tree. He said: Give me back my cloak. Do you fear that I would not distribute among you? If there were livestock as numerous as the trees of Tihamah, I would distribute them among you, then you would not find me cowardly, miserly, or lying. Then he said: Return the needle and the thread, for embezzlement is disgrace, fire, and shame upon its people on the Day of Resurrection. And he said: I have no right to any of this spoils except one-fifth, and the one-fifth is returned to you."],[7364,"The killer of al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam came seeking permission to enter upon Ali. He said: Grant him permission and give him tidings of the Fire. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam."],[7365,"The difference between a woman's pleasure and a man's pleasure is like the trace of a needle in clay, except that Allah covers them with modesty."],[7366,"Were it not that your people are recent in disbelief, I would demolish the Kaaba and rebuild it upon the foundations of Ibrahim, and I would include in the House several cubits from the Hijr, and I would make for it two doors and attach them to the ground."],[7367,"He is not one of us who imitates other than us. Do not imitate the Jews or the Christians. The greeting of the Jews is a gesture with the fingers, and the greeting of the Christians is with the palms. Do not shave the forelocks, trim the mustaches, and leave the beards. And do not walk in mosques and markets except with shirts and under them waist-wrappers."],[7368,"The one who eats and is grateful is like the one who fasts and is patient."],[7369,"Ali stood on the pulpit of Kufa and said: Shall I not tell you of the best of this community after its Prophet? Indeed, the best of this community after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then Umar. And if I wished to inform you of the third, I would have informed you."],[7370,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: Were it not that I have garlanded my sacrificial animal, I would have exited the state of ihram."],[7371,"She informed him that she entered the state of ihram for umrah before the hajj during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and that she menstruated and did not become pure so that she could circumambulate the House, until the Day of Arafah. She mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Undo your hair, then comb it, then declare the intention for hajj and abandon the umrah. She said: So I did so until I completed my hajj. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ sent Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr with me and ordered me to perform the umrah from al-Tanim in place of my umrah that the hajj had overtaken and from which I had not exited."],[7372,"A person in the state of ihram must not marry, nor arrange a marriage, nor propose marriage."],[7373,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and supplicated with a supplication the like of which the people had never heard, and he sought refuge with a seeking of refuge the like of which the people had never heard. Some of the people said to him: How can we supplicate as you supplicated, and seek refuge as you sought refuge, O Messenger of God? He said: Say: O God, we ask You of what Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, asked You, and we seek refuge from what Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, sought refuge from."],[7374,"I missed the evening meal one night with the Prophet ﷺ, and none of our brothers called me. I prayed the evening prayer, then I wanted to sleep but could not, and I wanted to pray but could not. Then there was a man at the Prophet's room, so I went to him and found it was the Messenger of God ﷺ praying. He prayed, then leaned against the pillar toward which he had prayed and said: Who is this? Abu Hirr? I said: Yes. He said: Did you miss the evening meal with us tonight? I said: Yes. He said: Go to the house and say: Bring the food that you have. They gave me a bowl containing porridge with dates. I brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and placed it before him. He said to me: Call the people of the mosque for me. I said to myself: Woe to me from the little food I see, and woe to me from disobedience. I would come to a man sleeping and wake him, saying: Respond. I would come to a man praying, saying: Respond. Until they gathered at the Prophet ﷺ. He placed his fingers in it and pressed its sides, and said: Eat in the name of God. They ate until they were full, and I ate until I was full. He said: Take it, O Abu Hirr, and return it to the family of Muhammad, for there is no food in the family of Muhammad that any living being eats other than it. A man from the Ansar gave it to us as a gift. I took the bowl and lifted it, and it was as it had been when I placed it, except that it bore the traces of the lines of the fingers of the Prophet ﷺ."],[7375,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade six things: wine, gambling, musical instruments, reed pipes, the drum, and the kubah."],[7376,"Al-Harith b. Hisham came to the Prophet ﷺ once on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: O Messenger of God, you urge maintaining ties of kinship, kindness to neighbors, sheltering orphans, feeding guests, and feeding the poor. All of this Hisham b. al-Mughira used to do. What do you think of him, O Messenger of God? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Every grave whose occupant does not bear witness that there is no god but God is a brand of fire. I found my uncle Abu Talib in a flood of fire, and God brought him out because of his closeness to me and his kindness to me, and placed him in a shallow part of the fire."],[7377,"We prayed one of the two evening prayers with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he finished, he turned his face to us smiling and said: Will you not ask me why I laughed? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: I marveled at God's decree for the Muslim servant. Indeed, everything God decrees for him is good, and not every decree of God is good except for the Muslim servant."],[7378,"Do not let the people of the desert overcome you regarding the name of your prayer. God called it al-Isha, while they call it al-Atamah."],[7379,"Hafsah and I began the day fasting, and a gift was given to us, so we ate from it. The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us, and we informed him of that. He said: Fast another day in its place."],[7380,"The wedding feast on the first day is a duty, on the second day it is a good deed, and on the third day it is showing off and seeking a good reputation."],[7381,"The truthful, trustworthy merchant will be with the martyrs on the Day of Resurrection."],[7382,"No boy is born in a household except that a glory arises among them that was not there before."],[7383,"The parable of a man and death is like a man who has three friends. He said, “O Allah, this is my wealth; take from it what You will, give what You will, and leave what You will.” The second one said, “I am with you, I will serve you, but when you die, I will leave you.” The third one said, “I am with you; I will enter with you and exit with you, whether you die or live.” As for the one who said, “This is my wealth; take from it what You will and leave what You will,” that is his wealth. The other one is his kinsfolk. The other one is his deeds, which enter with him and exit with him wherever he is."],[7384,"If people knew what I know about being alone, no rider would ever travel alone at night, and no man would ever sleep alone at night."],[7385,"When a servant tells a lie, the angel distances himself from him by a mile, because of the stench of what he has brought."],[7386,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, then touches some of his best perfume, wears some of his finest clothes, then goes early, and does not separate between two people until he stands from his place, then listens attentively until the imam finishes his sermon, will be forgiven for what is between the two Fridays, plus three extra days."],[7387,"Travel, and you will be healthy and safe."],[7388,"The shroud is to be taken from all of the wealth."],[7389,"The best charity is that given when one is wealthy."],[7390,"The Azd are the Azd of Allah on earth. People want to lower them, but Allah refuses only to raise them. A time will surely come upon people when a man will say, “Would that my father were an Azdi! Would that my mother were an Azdiyyah!”"],[7391,"A bowl - or a drinking cup - containing milk and honey was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Two condiments in one vessel? I will not eat it, nor do I forbid it.”"],[7392,"When a woman perfumes herself for other than her husband, it is but a fire in a scandal."],[7393,"The best of your dates is al-Barnī; it removes disease, and there is no disease in it.\""],[7394,"Perform ablution from camel meat, and do not pray in their resting places; and do not perform ablution from sheep meat, and pray in their folds."],[7395,"\"Shall I not teach you a supplication that the Messenger of God ﷺ taught me?\" He said: \"When you see people competing over gold and silver, then supplicate with these supplications: O God, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter, and I ask You for determination upon right guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your blessing, and patience in Your trial, and I ask You for excellence in worship of You, and contentment with Your decree, and I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue, and I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know.\""],[7396,"He forbade wearing weapons in the lands of Islam on the two Eids, unless it be in the presence of the enemy."],[7397,"The two binding matters: whoever dies not associating anything with God enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating something with Him enters the Fire.\""],[7398,"A resident shall not sell on behalf of a bedouin, and whoever buys a musarrāh (an animal whose milk has been withheld) has the choice of the two options: if he wishes, he may return it and return with it a sāʿ of dates.\""],[7399,"When one of you cleanses himself with stones, let him make it odd, for God is odd (witr) and loves the odd. Do you not see the heavens are seven, and the days, and the earths are seven, and the circumambulation, and the pebbles.\" And he mentioned other things.\""],[7400,"\"The Fire has been kindled, and Paradise has been brought near. O people of the chambers, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.\""],[7401,"No charity is more excellent than the remembrance of God."],[7402,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: Recite the Quran in a month. I said: I have strength. He said: \"Then recite it in three [days].\""],[7403,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Muʿādh b. Jabal and Abū Mūsā to Yemen, and said: Support each other, obey each other, make things easy, and do not repel. Muʿādh addressed the people, urging them to Islam, and commanded them to seek understanding and the Quran, and said: \"I inform you of the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire: when a man is mentioned with good, he is of the people of Paradise, and when he is mentioned with evil, he is of the people of the Fire.\""],[7404,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ in a funeral procession, and we reached the grave while it had not yet been dug. The Messenger of God ﷺ sat down, and we sat around him—then he mentioned the hadith of the punishment of the grave."],[7405,"He prohibited a woman from traveling with someone other than a mahram relative for more than three days."],[7406,"Deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday: there is one who seeks forgiveness and is forgiven, and one who repents and is turned to in mercy, while the people of grudges are turned back on account of their grudges until they repent."],[7407,"On the day of Hunayn we saw something black descending between the sky and the earth. It fell to the ground and crawled like ants, and it routed the polytheists."],[7408,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ near the room of Aisha supplicating: 'O God, bless us in our mudd, bless us in our sa', and bless us in our Sham and our Yemen.' Then he faced the east and said: 'From here emerges the horn of Satan, and the earthquakes and trials, and from here come the loud boasters.'"],[7409,"Forty qualities by which God admits into Paradise, the highest of them in rank is lending a ewe for its milk."],[7410,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to send the sacrificial animal, and he would twist its garlands, then he would not refrain from anything that a pilgrim in ihram refrains from."],[7411,"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to use the tooth stick at every prayer."],[7412,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to wake his family during the last ten nights of Ramadan, and every young and old who could pray."],[7413,"Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is deficient, deficient, deficient."],[7414,"I prayed before the people."],[7415,"Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are four: Fatimah bt. Muhammad, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Maryam bt. Imran, and Asiyah bt. Muzahim."],[7416,"Indeed, Allah does not listen as He listens to one who chants the Qur'an with a melodious voice."],[7417,"Whoever swears a false oath deliberately to deprive a Muslim of his property, he will meet Allah while He is angry with him."],[7418,"A blind man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'I hear the call to prayer, but perhaps I cannot find a guide and it is hard for me; shall I set up a mosque in my house?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Does the call reach you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then answer it when you hear the call.'"],[7419,"We used to soak nabidh for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a green jar."],[7420,"A woman should not refuse herself to her husband, even if she is on a camel's saddle."],[7421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never given a choice between two things but he chose the easier of them, as long as it was not a sin; if it was a sin, he was the farthest of people from it."],[7422,"O Messenger of Allah, Aflah asked permission to enter upon me, but the wife of his brother suckled me? He said: 'Admit him, for he is your paternal uncle.'"],[7423,"If the ghoul (a desert demon) appears to you, then call the adhan, for when Satan hears the call, he turns tail and runs, passing wind."],[7424,"I was holding a branch of the tree above the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was taking the people's pledge of allegiance. He did not take their pledge to death, but he took their pledge that they would not flee."],[7425,"Indeed, the deceased knows who washes him, who shrouds him, and who lowers him into his grave."],[7426,"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black, whereas a prophet was sent only to his own people; I was aided with terror (cast into the hearts of enemies) for a month's journey; I was given the spoils of war, and no one before me was given them; the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification; and there is no prophet but was given a supplication which he hastened to use, but I have delayed my supplication as intercession for my nation, and it will reach—if Allah wills—whoever dies without associating anything with Allah."],[7427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the Muslims in Makkah when their tribes were harsh to them: 'Spread out in the land,' so they dispersed to the land of Abyssinia. Quraysh sent 'Abd Allah b. Abi Rabi'a and 'Amr b. al-'As. Among what 'Amr and 'Abd Allah said to the Negus was: 'They do not greet you with the greeting with which those of us who enter upon you greet you.' He said to Ja'far and his companions: 'Why do you not greet me as your companions greet?' They said: 'We greet you with the greeting of our Prophet ﷺ: Peace.'"],[7428,"He used to deliver the sermon leaning on a wooden post. When the pulpit was made and he went to ascend it, the post moaned. He descended and touched it, and it became still."],[7429,"Use the toothstick, clean yourselves, and perform Witr, for Allah is Witr (One) and loves the Witr.'\""],[7430,"Whoever has affection for his brother in his heart should let him know that."],[7431,"Eat together and do not separate, for the food of one is enough for two, and the food of two is enough for four. O Allah, bless the people of Madinah in their sa', and bless them in their mudd.'\""],[7432,"The Prophet ﷺ designated al-'Aqiq as the miqat for the people of the east."],[7433,"He and a companion of his came to 'A'ishah looking for the Prophet ﷺ, but did not find him. 'A'ishah fed us a lunch of dates and 'asidah. It was not long before the Prophet ﷺ came, walking with a slight limp, swaying. He said: \"Have you two eaten?\" We said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the prayer?\" He said: \"Perform ablution thoroughly, run your fingers through your fingers, and exaggerate in sniffing water into the nose unless you are fasting.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife\"—and he mentioned her vulgarity—he said: \"Divorce her.\" I said: \"She has been my companion and has children.\" He said: \"Admonish her; if there is any good in her, she will do it. Do not strike your wife as you strike your slave-girl.\" While we were like that, a shepherd raised a newborn lamb in his hands in the sheep pen. He said: \"Has it given birth?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"What?\" He said: \"A female lamb.\" He said: \"Slaughter a sheep in its place.\" Then he turned to me and said: \"Do not think—and he did not say, 'Do not think'—that we slaughtered it only for your sake. We have a hundred sheep; we do not like to increase beyond that. When the shepherd delivers a female lamb, we order him to slaughter a sheep in its place.\""],[7434,"We used to eat with the Prophet ﷺ and we would hear the food glorifying Allah."],[7435,"An animal was brought to the Prophet ﷺ to ride. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A man is more entitled to the front of his mount.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is for you.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode and seated Mu'adh behind him.'\""],[7436,"Among what people have retained from the words of the earlier prophets is: 'If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'\""],[7437,"Allah has obligated upon you the fast of Ramadan, but He has not obligated its night prayer. Its night prayer is something you have introduced, so persist in it. For some people among the Children of Israel innovated an innovation, and Allah criticized them for abandoning it. He said: 'And monasticism, which they innovated; We did not prescribe it upon them except seeking the pleasure of Allah, but they did not observe it with due observance'—until the end of the verse."],[7438,"When food is served and the prayer is established, begin with the food.'\""],[7439,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sneezed, he would cover his face and lower his voice.'\""],[7440,"I was a man who emitted madhy. I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"When you see madhy, wash your private part and perform wudu\"; and when you see the gushing water, perform ghusl.\""],[7441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed five [rak'ahs] with the people. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?\" He said: \"Why is that?\" They said: \"You prayed five.\" So he prostrated twice."],[7442,"When Adam descended to the earth, he wept over Paradise for a hundred autumns. Then he looked at the expanse of the earth and said: \"O Lord, is there no dweller to inhabit Your earth besides me?\" Then Allah revealed to him: \"Indeed, yes. Houses will be raised in which My name is mentioned, and I will settle you in one of them, a house which I single out for My honour, which I permit My grandeur, and which I name My House. I will speak of it by My grandeur, though I will not dwell in it, for it is not fitting for Me to dwell in houses, nor do they contain Me. Rather, I am on My Throne and the seat of My grandeur, and it is not fitting for anything I have created to escape My grasp or My power. You will maintain it, O Adam, as long as you live, then the generations after you will maintain it, nation after nation, century after century, until it reaches a son of your descendants called Ibrahim, whom I shall make one of its maintainers and inhabitants.\""],[7443,"The Imam is appointed only to be followed. So when he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he says, 'Allah listens to the one who praises Him,' say, 'O Allah, our Lord, to You be praise'; when he prostrates, prostrate; and when he prays sitting, all of you pray sitting.\""],[7444,"He sent to 'A'ishah and asked her about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: \"He used to pray and leave off, but I never saw him omit the two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer, whether travelling or resident, healthy or ill.\""],[7445,"O Ibn 'Abbas, [it is] two rak'ahs before the morning prayer at the fading of the stars, and two rak'ahs after Maghrib at the passing of the prostration.\""],[7446,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wiping over the khuffs. He said: \"Three [days] for the traveller, and a day and a night for the resident.\""],[7447,"Beware of 'it was said and he said', of withholding and demanding, of undutifulness to mothers, of burying daughters alive, and of squandering wealth.\""],[7448,"Allah has imposed obligations, so do not neglect them; He has set limits, so do not transgress them; and He has remained silent about many things out of mercy, not out of forgetfulness, so do not burden yourselves with them. [This is] a mercy from Allah, so accept it.\""],[7449,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My father is an old man; if I carry him, he cannot hold on.\" He said: \"Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\""],[7450,"Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Washsha' narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Umara b. Abi Hafsa, from 'Ikrima, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of it. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'ba, from 'Umara, except Abu 'Asim; 'Abd Allah b. Muhammad al-Zuhri was alone in narrating it.\""],[7451,"'Ali took me by the hand and entered upon al-Hasan b. 'Ali while he was ill. Abu Musa was with him. He said: \"Are you a visitor or a person paying a sick visit?\" He said: \"Rather, I am paying a sick visit.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No Muslim visits a sick Muslim except that Allah appoints seventy thousand angels to send blessings upon him, if it is evening until morning, and if it is morning until evening, and He prepares for him rooms in Paradise.'\""],[7452,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, when is the Hour?' He said: 'What have you prepared for it?' He said: 'By God, I have not prepared for it much in the way of deeds, except that I love God and His Messenger.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'A man is with the one he loves.'"],[7453,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in a garden when a bird was brought to him. He said: 'O God, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me from this bird.' Then 'Ali came and knocked on the door. I said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'I am 'Ali.' I said: 'The Prophet ﷺ is occupied with something.' So he left. Then he came back and knocked on the door. I said: 'Who is that?' He said: 'I am 'Ali.' I said: 'The Prophet ﷺ is occupied with something.' Then he came and knocked on the door. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Go and open it.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'What kept you, may God have mercy on you?' He said: 'These are three returns; each time Anas told me that you were occupied with something.' He said: 'O Anas, what made you do that?' I said: 'I heard your supplication, so I wanted it to be a man from my people.'"],[7454,"He went out one night and delayed the 'Isha' prayer until a little while or an hour had passed, while the people were waiting for him in the mosque. He said: 'What are you waiting for?' They said: 'We are waiting for the prayer.' He said: 'Indeed, you will remain in prayer as long as you wait for it.' Then he said: 'Indeed, it is a prayer that no one among the nations before you has prayed.' Then he raised his head to the sky and said: 'The stars are a safeguard for the sky; when the stars are obliterated, what is promised for the sky will come. And I am a safeguard for my Companions; when I am taken, what is promised for my Companions will come. And my Companions are a safeguard for my community; when my Companions are taken, what is promised for my community will come.'"],[7455,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had ordered for me a portion of dates that was with a man from the Ansar, but he delayed giving it to me. I spoke to the Messenger of God ﷺ about it. He said: 'Go with him, O Abu Bakr, and get his dates for him.' He said: 'Abu Bakr promised to meet me at the mosque when we prayed the morning prayer. I found him where he had promised, and we set off. Whenever a man saw Abu Bakr from afar, he would greet him. Abu Bakr said: 'Do you see what virtue the people are bestowing upon you? No one beats you to the greeting.' He said: 'So whenever a man appeared, we would hasten to greet him before he greeted us.'"],[7456,"There was a woman from Banu Qurayzah called Tamimah, married to 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Zubayr. He divorced her, then Rifa'ah, a man from Banu Qurayzah, married her. Then he separated from her, and she wanted to return to 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Zubayr. She said: 'O Messenger of God, by God, he has nothing from me but like the fringe of my garment.' He said: 'By God, O Tamimah, you will not return to 'Abd al-Rahman until another man tastes your sweetness.' She said: 'O Messenger of God, he did come to me once.'"],[7457,"Three things God loves: hastening the breaking of the fast, delaying the pre-dawn meal, and striking one hand upon the other in prayer."],[7458,"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given: the spoils of war were made lawful for me, and they were not lawful for any prophet before me; the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification, whereas those before us used to pray in their sanctuaries; I was sent to every black and red, whereas a man was sent specifically to his own people; I was aided with terror for a month's journey ahead of me—a people between whom and me there is a month's journey would hear of me and be terrified of me, and terror was made a victory for me; and it was said to me: 'Ask, and you will be given.' So I made it an intercession for my community, and it will be obtained by whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, associating nothing with God."],[7459,"It is enough for a man's faith that he says: 'I am pleased with God as Lord, with Muhammad as Messenger, and with Islam as religion.'"],[7460,"Whoever does not care about the affairs of the Muslims is not one of them, and whoever does not begin his day and end it as a sincere adviser to God, His Messenger, His Book, His leader, and the common Muslims is not one of them."],[7461,"Whoever is distressed by his evil deed is a believer."],[7462,"When Abraham was taken up, he saw a man committing adultery with a woman, so he prayed against him, and he was destroyed. Then he saw a servant committing a sin, so he prayed against him. God revealed to him: 'O Abraham, whoever worships Me, his palace from Me has three characteristics: either he repents, and I accept his repentance; or he seeks My forgiveness, and I forgive him; or there comes forth from his loins one who worships Me. O Abraham, do you not know that among My names is that I am the Forbearing?'"],[7463,"Abu Musa al-Ash'ari led us in the prayer of fear in Isfahan, and there was no great fear; he did it to show us the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He stood and said the takbir, and a group of the people said the takbir with him, while another group stood facing the enemy, bearing arms. He prayed one rak'ah with them, then they departed and took the place of their companions. The other group came, and he prayed another rak'ah with them, then he said the salam. Then each of them prayed the second rak'ah individually."],[7464,"The master of condiments in this world and the Hereafter is meat, and the master of drinks in this world and the Hereafter is water, and the master of fragrant herbs in this world and the Hereafter is the fāghiyah."],[7465,"I said: O Messenger of God, I am a poet, so what do you think of poetry? He replied: For what is between your chest and your pubic area to be filled with pus and ichor is better than for it to be filled with poetry."],[7466,"The Quraysh were troubled by the affair of the Makhzūmī woman who stole. They said: Who will speak to the Messenger of God ﷺ about her? They said: Who would dare to approach him except Usāma b. Zayd, the beloved of the Messenger of God ﷺ? So they spoke to him about that, and he came to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Verily those before you were destroyed because when a noble person among them stole, they would leave him alone, and when a weak person stole, they would impose the legal punishment upon him. By God, if Fāṭima bt. Muḥammad were to steal, I would cut off her hand. Then he cut off her hand."],[7467,"A woman entered the Fire because of a cat of hers. She had tied it up, neither feeding it nor letting it eat from the vermin of the earth."],[7468,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by two men who were tied together as pilgrims in fulfilment of a vow, and he said: Untie your tying together. They said: O Messenger of God, it is a vow. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Untie your tying together, then perform the pilgrimage."],[7469,"The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the robber does not commit a robbery, while the believers raise their heads to look at him, while he is a believer."],[7470,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not perform qunūt in any of the prayers except in the witr. When he was at war, he performed qunūt in all the prayers, supplicating against the polytheists. Abū Bakr did not perform qunūt, nor ʿUmar, nor ʿUthmān, until they died. Nor did ʿAlī perform qunūt until he fought the people of Syria, and he used to perform qunūt in all the prayers. Muʿāwiya also used to supplicate against him, each of them supplicating against the other."],[7471,"Muʿāwiya wrote to him, meaning al-Mughīra, asking him about what he had heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He wrote back to him. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Verily God hates for you three things: disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding while demanding, and it was said and he said, and excessive questioning, and squandering wealth."],[7472,"Two traits are easy, but few act upon them. No one persists in them but enters Paradise: after every prayer, ten takbīrs, ten tasbīḥs, and ten taḥmīds; that is one hundred and fifty on the tongue and one thousand five hundred in the Balance. And when he goes to his bed, he glorifies God thirty-three times, praises Him thirty-three times, and magnifies Him thirty-four times; that is one hundred on the tongue and one thousand in the Balance. So which of you would commit two thousand five hundred sins in a day and night? Some of them said: Indeed this is a matter in which action is easy. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Verily Satan comes to one of you when he finishes his prayer and says: Remember such-and-such need and such-and-such need."],[7473,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up after the two rakʿas of the noon prayer, and the people clapped and glorified God to alert him, until he realized that he had forgotten. He continued until his prayer was complete, then he prostrated two prostrations while sitting before he said the salutation."],[7474,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing shabby clothes and looking disheveled. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: Do you have wealth? He said: Yes, of all kinds of wealth. He said: Then let what God has provided you be seen upon you."],[7475,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us not to throw the pebble until the sun has risen."],[7476,"The Prophet ﷺ came to the door of a man of the Ansar and greeted, while the Ansari was with his wife. He responded while he was still on her, then he greeted a second time, and he responded but did not get up. Then he left when he was not given permission. The other man got up before finishing and went out following the Prophet ﷺ seeking him. Abu Hurayrah said: We came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was standing, and we gathered around him. The man bathed in a river beside his house, then came having bathed. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He bathed, though ghusl was not obligatory on him.' The man came apologizing to the Prophet ﷺ and told him his situation. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'You bathed, though ghusl was not obligatory on you.'"],[7477,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'My mother died and she did not make a will or give charity. Will it be accepted if I give charity on her behalf?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Will that benefit her?' He said: 'Yes, even if it is with a burnt sheep's trotter.'"],[7478,"O Messenger of Allah, tell me a saying by which Allah may benefit me, and be brief, that I may understand it. He said: 'Do not get angry.' Then he repeated, saying: 'Do not get angry.'"],[7479,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given al-Kafit."],[7480,"I was given verses from a treasure house beneath the Throne that no prophet before me was given, and no one after me will be given. The earth was made a mosque and a means of purification for me, our rows were made like the rows of the angels, and I was aided with terror from a month's distance."],[7481,"A man from Thaqif, called Ghaylan b. Salamah, embraced Islam while he had ten wives. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to choose four of them and leave six."],[7482,"We fasted the day of Ashura before Allah made the fast of Ramadan obligatory. When Allah made the fast of Ramadan obligatory, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever wishes may fast it, and whoever wishes may leave it.' It was a day on which the Kaaba was covered."],[7483,"The siwak is a purification for the mouth, a pleasure to the Lord, and a sharpener for the eyesight."],[7484,"If there is ill omen in anything, it is in the house, the woman, and the horse."],[7485,"We were discussing righteousness with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began to narrate to us. He said: Among the nations before you there was a devout man, an inhabitant of a hermitage, called Jurayj. He had a woman—or a mother—who used to come to him and call him, and he would look over at her and speak to her. One day she came to him while he was in his prayer, facing it. She called him—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ imitated her, placing his hand on his forehead—and she kept calling him, raising her head toward him and placing her hand on her forehead: 'O Jurayj, O Jurayj,' three times, each time three calls. Each time Jurayj said: 'O Lord, my mother or my prayer?' She became angry and said: 'O Allah, do not let Jurayj die until he looks into the faces of prostitutes.' He said: The daughter of the king of the village became pregnant and gave birth to a boy. They said to her: 'Who did this to you? Who is your companion?' She said: 'He is the inhabitant of the hermitage, Jurayj.' Jurayj was unaware until he heard the sound of axes at the base of his hermitage. He began asking them: 'Woe to you, what is the matter with you?' But they did not answer him. When he saw that, he took a rope and lowered himself down. They began pulling his nose and beating him, saying: 'Hypocrite, deceiving people with your deeds!' He said: 'Woe to you, what is the matter with you?' They said: 'What about the daughter of the chief of the village, the king's daughter whom you made pregnant?' He said: 'What did she do?' They said: 'She gave birth to a boy.' He said: 'Is the boy alive?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Turn away from me.' He turned away, prayed two rak'ahs, then walked to a tree and took a branch from it. Then he came to the boy in his cradle and struck him with that branch, saying: 'O tyrant, who is your father?' He said: 'My father is so-and-so the shepherd.' They said: 'If you wish, we will rebuild your hermitage with gold, and if you wish, with silver.' He said: 'Restore it as it was.' Abu Harb claimed that none spoke in the cradle except three: Isa son of Maryam, the witness of Yusuf, and the companion of Jurayj."],[7486,"On the day of Uhud, the people of Madinah were thrown into confusion. They said: 'Muhammad has been killed,' until there were many shouts in a part of Madinah. A woman from the Ansar went out girded, and she was met with her son, her father, her husband, and her brother—I do not know which of them she was met with first. When she passed the last of them, she said: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Your father, your brother, your husband, your son.' She said: 'What has happened to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' They said: 'He is ahead of you.' She was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she took hold of the edge of his garment, then said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah! I do not care who has perished as long as you are safe.'"],[7487,"Among the past nations there was a man called Muwarriq, who was devout. While he was standing in prayer, he thought of women and desired them, and he became erect until he broke off his prayer. He became angry, took his bow, cut its string, and tied it around his testicles, fastening it to his heels. Then he stretched his legs and pulled them off. Then he took his two worn garments and his sandals and went to a land with no human or wild animal. He made a hut and began praying. Every morning the earth split open and something came out with a vessel containing food, and he ate until he was full. Then it went in and came out with a vessel containing drink, and he drank until he was satisfied. Then it went in and the earth closed up. In the evening, the same thing happened. He said: Some people passed near him, and two men from the group came to him and passed by him at night. They asked him about their destination, and he pointed with his hand, saying: 'This is your destination,' and said: 'This is your destination where you want to go.' They traveled a short distance, and one of them said: 'What makes this man stay here, in a land with no human or wild animal? If only we returned to him to learn his knowledge.' They returned and said to him: 'O servant of Allah, what makes you stay in this place, a land with no human or wild animal?' He said: 'Go about your business and leave me.' They refused and insisted. He said: 'I will tell you on condition that whoever of you conceals it from me, Allah will honor him in this world and the Hereafter, and whoever of you reveals it about me, Allah will disgrace him in this world and the Hereafter.' They said: 'Yes.' So they dismounted. When morning came, the one came out from the earth with the same amount of food as usual and twice as much, and they ate until they were full. Then it went in and came out to them with drink in a vessel like the one it used to bring every day and twice as much, and they drank until they were satisfied. Then it went in and the earth closed up. One of them looked at his companion and said: 'Why should we hurry? This is food and drink, and we know our direction. Stay until evening.' So they stayed, and in the evening it brought out to them the same as it had at the beginning of the day. One of them said to his companion: 'Stay with us until morning.' So they stayed. In the morning, it brought out the same to them. Then they mounted and left. One of them stayed at the king's gate until he became one of his close companions and nightly entertainers. The other turned to his trade and work. That king would not let anyone in his kingdom who told a known lie go unpunished except by crucifixion. While they were one night in the evening gathering telling him about the wonders they had seen, that man began to narrate. He said: 'I will tell you, O king, a story more amazing than anything you have ever heard.' He told the story of the man whose affair he had witnessed. The king said: 'I have never heard a greater lie than this. By Allah, you must bring me proof of what you said, or I will crucify you.' He said: 'My proof is so-and-so.' He said: 'Agreed. Bring him to me.' When he came, the king said to him: 'This man claims that you passed by a man, and then such and such happened.' The man said: 'O king, do you not know that this is a lie? This is something that cannot happen. If I told you this, it would be right for you to crucify me for it.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth and acted rightly.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The man who concealed it was admitted into his close companions and nightly entertainers, and the other was ordered to be crucified.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The one of them who concealed it, Allah honored him in this world and the Hereafter, and the one who revealed it, Allah disgraced him in this world, and He will disgrace him in the Hereafter.' Then Bakr b. Abdullah looked at Thumamah b. Abdullah b. Anas and said: 'O Abu al-Muthanna, did you hear your grandfather narrate this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[7488,"Part of a man's devotion to his father after his death is his keeping the people whom his father loved after him."],[7489,"Whoever fasts a day without breaking it, ten good deeds are written for him."],[7490,"Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah, command me to a deed that will admit me to Paradise. He said: Believe in Allah, and speak good, and it will be recorded for you; and do not speak evil, lest it be recorded against you. He said: Shall we be held accountable for what we say? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"And do people get thrown onto their faces in the Fire except for the harvests of their tongues?\""],[7491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed during his Hajj—while we were with him—by a man who had completed his Hajj. He said to him: Has your Hajj been accepted for you? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"Begin the work afresh.\""],[7492,"Whoever is invited to a wedding feast and does not respond has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."],[7493,"A man came once and asked permission to enter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Give him permission and give him the glad tidings of Paradise. It was Abu Bakr. Then another man came, and he said: \"Give him permission and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.\" It was 'Umar. Then another came and asked permission. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give him permission and give him the glad tidings of Paradise with a tribulation\"—or as he said—and it was 'Uthman. 'Uthman said: \"I ask Allah for patience.\""],[7494,"The waters were scarce during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when it was summer the people would pray Zuhr and then go out to take the afternoon breeze. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr and then went out, and they went out with him to the courtyard of the mosque. He stayed until the call to prayer, then he sent me to the house of Umm Salamah to bring him water for ablution. I entered and brought him a bowl two-thirds or half full. He performed ablution. When he finished his ablution, there remained some leftover water from his ablution in the bowl. He raised his head and saw the people standing. He said: \"What are these?\" Anas said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, they cannot find water with which to perform ablution. He said: \"Call them.\" So I did, and the people came. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ put his hand into the bowl in the leftover from his ablution. By the One in whose hand is my soul, not one of them remained who did not perform ablution from what was in the palm of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a little remained in the bowl. I returned it to the house."],[7495,"I used to travel with the Prophet ﷺ, and I never saw him pray after 'Asr or after Fajr at all."],[7496,"He was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shake hands? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never met me a single time that I greeted him except that he shook my hand, except for one time, and it was the most generous of them. I entered upon him while he was ill, and I leaned over him, and he embraced me."],[7497,"I asked Ibn 'Umar about the fasting of the traveler. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out when fourteen days of Ramadan had passed. He made his mount kneel and placed one of his feet in the stirrup and the other on the ground, then he called for some of its milk and drank."],[7498,"Whoever withdraws a hand from the community will come on the Day of Resurrection with no argument for himself, and whoever dies not in obedience dies a death of ignorance."],[7499,"He forbade that three ride on one mount."],[7500,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[7501,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out with his head bandaged, ascended the steps of the pulpit, and said: \"What are these writings that I have heard you are writing? A book alongside the Book of Allah? It is imminent that Allah will become angry for His Book, and it will be taken away by night, leaving not a single letter in any page or heart but He will remove it.\" Those present asked: \"How then with the believing men and women, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Whoever Allah intends good for, He leaves in his heart 'there is no god but Allah'.\""],[7502,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a horse called al-Murtajiz."],[7503,"Whenever he intended to enter a town, he would not enter it until he said: \"O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, I ask You for the good of this town and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it.\""],[7504,"Nothing prohibits (marriage) through suckling except what pierces the intestines and was in the body like food."],[7505,"Whoever has two daughters, or two sisters, or two paternal aunts, or two maternal aunts, and supports them, the eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him. O servants of Allah, help him; O servants of Allah, give him; O servants of Allah, lend him."],[7506,"Whoever brings joy into the household of a Muslim family, Allah will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise."],[7507,"Whoever spends the evening weary from the work of his own hands, spends the evening forgiven."],[7508,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to prostrate on seven body parts."],[7509,"We used to eat, drink, and give out the zakat al-fitr, then go out to the prayer place."],[7510,"On Friday, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stand twice on the pulpit and sit twice. When he came out, he would sit; when the muezzin called the adhan, he would stand and deliver the sermon, then sit and rest, then stand and deliver the sermon."],[7511,"Bilal came to the Prophet ﷺ to inform him of the dawn prayer. He said: \"Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" He returned to him and saw heaviness in him, so he said: \"Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" He went and called the adhan, and added in his adhan: \"Prayer is better than sleep.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"What is this that you have added in your adhan?\" He said: \"I saw heaviness in you, and I wanted you to become active.\" He said: \"Go and add it in your adhan, and tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\""],[7512,"The Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: “Fear God as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims.” Then he said: “If a drop of zaqqūm were to fall into the seas of this world, it would ruin the livelihoods of the people of this world. So how about the one whose food it is?”"],[7513,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “The transgressing party will kill you.”"],[7514,"A man in the state of iḥrām was killed when his she-camel crushed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not perfume him, and do not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.”"],[7515,"There is no discretionary punishment above ten lashes."],[7516,"There is no servant upon whom God bestows a blessing and makes it abundant for him, and then places some of the people’s needs before him, and he shows annoyance, but he has exposed that blessing to removal."],[7517,"It is sufficient for one of you to place his hand on his thigh and greet his brother to his right by saying, “Peace be upon you and the mercy of God,” and to his left similarly."],[7518,"Everything has an adornment, and the adornment of the Qur’an is a beautiful voice."],[7519,"Whoever conceals knowledge that he has will be bridled by God on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."],[7520,"Ibn ʿUmar fell ill, and a man said: “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the deserts have become verdant. If you were to buy some goats and take a leisurely outing, you would regain your health.” He replied: “None of us has been given permission to live in the desert except Aslam.”"],[7521,"If one of you, when he goes to his wife, says: ‘O God, keep us away from Satan and keep Satan away from what You provide for us,’ and a child is decreed between them, Satan will never harm it."],[7522,"A flock of sheep was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[7523,"We asked our Prophet ﷺ about the pace of walking with a funeral procession. He said: “Walk with it at a pace slower than a trot. If it is good, it will be hastened for him; and if it is evil, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral procession is followed, not following.”"],[7524,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, there appeared to us some camels with their milk retained, taking shelter by the trees, with no herdsman with them. Some of us said, \"If only we got up and milked them.\" Others said, \"How can we milk them while the Messenger of God ﷺ is among us and we have not consulted him?\" Then some of us said, \"He has remained silent, and his silence is permission.\" So we got up to them, but he called us and said, \"What do you think if a people came to you while you were asleep and took what was in your provision bags—would they have harmed you?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, what is in the udders of these camels is like what is in your provision bags.\" We said, \"O Messenger of God, what is lawful for a man from his brother's wealth if he is in need of it?\" He said, \"He may eat but not carry away, and drink but not carry away.\""],[7525,"Whoever asks people to increase his wealth, it is only a live coal from Hell. So whoever wishes may ask much, and whoever wishes may ask little."],[7526,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he prayed, would follow every prescribed prayer with two rak'ahs, except the dawn prayer, for he would make those two before it."],[7527,"Fever is the believer's share of the Fire."],[7528,"\"Do you not know that the Messenger of God ﷺ, when two disputants brought their case to him and agreed on a time, then one of them came and the other did not, he would judge in favor of the one who came against the one who did not come?\" Abu Musa said, \"That was only in the case of a riding beast, a sheep, or a camel, but what we are dealing with is the affair of people.\""],[7529,"The Messenger of God ﷺ spent the evening talking to us and said, \"There will come upon people a time when the best wealth a person can have will be sheep among the trees, eating from the trees and going to the watering places. Their people will eat from their milk, drink their milk, and wear from their hair—or he said, from their wool. Trials will surge among the strongholds of the Arabs. By God, they will be tested; by God, they will be tested; by God, they will be tested.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said it three times."],[7530,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the prayer of fear with one of the two groups, one rak'ah, then the other group came forward and he prayed with them one rak'ah, then he performed two prostrations."],[7531,"The best of the believers is a man who is easy-going in selling, easy-going in buying, easy-going in paying his debts, and easy-going in collecting what is owed to him."],[7532,"Whoever washes a dead person and fulfills the trust in it—meaning that he does not disclose anything that appears during the washing—his sins will be as on the day his mother gave birth to him. He said, \"And the one who washes him should be the closest of people to him; otherwise, someone whom you know to have a share of piety and trustworthiness.\""],[7533,"We used to prepare nabidh for the Messenger of God ﷺ in a water skin, tied at the top and with an opening at the bottom. We would prepare it in the morning and he would drink it in the evening, and we would prepare it in the evening and he would drink it in the morning."],[7534,"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before the noon prayer, God will forbid him from the Fire."],[7535,"Among my community is one who, if he came to one of you and asked for a dinar, you would not give it to him; if he asked for a dirham, you would not give it to him; if he asked for a fils, you would not give it to him; but if he asked God for Paradise, He would give it to him—wearing two worn-out garments, to whom no one pays attention. If he swore by God, God would fulfill his oath."],[7536,"When the Prophet ﷺ broke his fast, he would say: \"In the name of Allah. O Allah, for You I fasted, and with Your provision I break my fast.\""],[7537,"Fasting three days of every month is fasting for a lifetime: the white days, the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth."],[7538,"I am determined to order my young men to gather bundles of firewood, then go to people who pray in their homes without any excuse and burn their houses down upon them."],[7539,"When he was traveling, if the sun declined before he set out, he would pray Zuhr and Asr together. If he set out before the sun declined, he would combine them at the beginning of the time of Asr. He would do the same with Maghrib and Isha."],[7540,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[7541,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have the strength to fast while traveling. Is there any sin upon me? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is a concession from Allah. Whoever takes it, it is good. Whoever prefers to fast, there is no sin upon him.\""],[7542,"A mudd suffices for ablution and a sa' for the ritual bath."],[7543,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a single blanket while I was menstruating."],[7544,"A man should not comb his hair except every other day, or every four or five days."],[7545,"Whoever among you prays after Friday, let him pray four."],[7546,"A time will come upon people when they will vie with one another in the number of mosques, but they will not fill them except rarely."],[7547,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque waiting for the prayer. A man stood up and said: \"I have committed a sin.\" He turned away from him. When the Prophet ﷺ had finished the prayer, the man stood and repeated his words. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Did you not pray this prayer with us and perform its ablution well?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then it is an expiation for your sin.\""],[7548,"A slave girl came tending sheep of mine, and a wolf ate a sheep, so I struck the slave girl's face. Then I regretted it and went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, if I knew that she was a believer, I would free her.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Who am I?' She said, 'The Messenger of God.' He said, 'Then who is God?' She said, 'The One who is in the heaven.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Free her, for she is a believer.'"],[7549,"Pardon the slips of people of good character."],[7550,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ after I had married, and he said, 'How much did you give as a bridal gift, O Abu Hadrad?' I said, 'Five awaq.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, 'If you were to scoop from Buthan, you would not add more.'"],[7551,"You must be truthful, for truthfulness guides to Paradise."],[7552,"The Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Khaybar and gave it to its Jewish inhabitants on a half-share basis. When the fruit ripened, he sent Abdullah b. Rawahah to them, who said, 'Take from me sixty wasqs of dates, and ours is what is on the tops of the palm trees.' They said, 'Then you would wrong us.' He said, 'Then give me sixty wasqs, and yours is what is on the tops of the palm trees.' They said, 'By this the heavens and the earth are maintained, and by this you are aided.'"],[7553,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote to his governors about the regulations of the alms tax: 'For forty sheep, one sheep, up to one hundred and twenty. If they increase by one, then two sheep, up to two hundred. If they increase by one more, then three sheep, up to three hundred. If the sheep become numerous, then for every hundred sheep, one sheep.' And he wrote regarding the alms tax on cattle: 'For every thirty cattle, a one-year-old; and for forty cattle, a two-year-old.' And he wrote regarding the alms tax on camels: 'For five camels, one sheep; for ten, two sheep; for fifteen, three sheep; for twenty, four sheep; for twenty-five, a bint makhad, up to thirty-five. If they increase by one, then a bint labun, up to forty-five. If they increase by one more, then a hiqqah that is ready to be mounted by a stallion, up to sixty. If they increase by one more, then a jadha'ah, up to seventy-five. If they increase by one more, then two bint labuns, up to ninety. If they increase by one more, then two hiqqahs, up to one hundred and twenty. If the camels become numerous, then for every fifty camels, a hiqqah; and for every forty camels, a bint labun.'"],[7554,"I regretted that I did not ask the Messenger of God ﷺ to make al-Hasan and al-Husayn callers to prayer."],[7555,"There is no prayer for one who has no tashahhud."],[7556,"Indeed, Paradise has yearned for four of my Companions, and my Lord commanded me to love them. Suhayb al-Rumi, Bilal b. Rabah, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman, and Ammar b. Yasir were singled out. They said, 'O Messenger of God, who are these four so that we may love them?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'O Ammar, you—God has made you recognize the hypocrites. As for these four, one of them is Ali b. Abi Talib, the second is al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad al-Kindi, the third is Salman al-Farisi, and the fourth is Abu Dharr al-Ghifari.'"],[7557,"A hypocrite does not memorize Surah Hud, Bara'ah, Ya Sin, al-Dukhan, and 'Amma yatasa'alun."],[7558,"The supplication of the Prophet ﷺ after the tashahhud in the obligatory prayer was: 'O God, we ask You for all good, the immediate and the deferred, what we know of it and what we do not know; and we seek refuge in You from all evil, the immediate and the deferred, what we know of it and what we do not know. O God, we ask You for what Your righteous servants have asked You, and we seek refuge in You from what Your righteous servants have sought refuge. Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire. Our Lord, indeed we have believed, so forgive us our sins and expiate our evil deeds, and make us die with the righteous. Our Lord, grant us what You promised us through Your messengers, and do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, You do not break Your promise.' Then he would greet to his right and to his left."],[7559,"The supplication of the Prophet ﷺ on the two Eids was: 'O God, we ask You for a pious life, a sound death, and a return that is not shameful or scandalous. O God, do not destroy us suddenly, and do not seize us unexpectedly, and do not hasten us away from a right or a bequest. O God, we ask You for chastity and sufficiency, piety and guidance, and a good outcome in the Hereafter and in this world. And we seek refuge in You from doubt and discord, hypocrisy and reputation in Your religion. O Turner of hearts, do not let our hearts deviate after You have guided us, and grant us mercy from Yourself. Indeed, You are the Bestower.'"],[7560,"Whoever forgets wiping the head and remembers while he is in prayer, and finds moisture in his beard, let him take some of it and wipe his head with it, for that will suffice him. But if he finds no moisture, let him repeat the ablution and the prayer."],[7561,"Parse the Qur'an grammatically, for whoever recites the Qur'an and parses it grammatically, for every letter he gets ten good deeds, expiation of ten evil deeds, and elevation of ten degrees."],[7562,"People are of two kinds: a scholar and a learner; they are equal in reward, and there is no good in the rest of people."],[7563,"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the two feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four things: about his life in what he spent it, his body in what he wore it out, his wealth from where he earned it and where he placed it and where he spent it."],[7564,"When the last ten days entered, the Messenger of God ﷺ would tighten his waist wrapper and keep away from women."],[7565,"When the journey became pressing for him, he would combine two prayers, Maghrib and Isha."],[7566,"Whoever has an imam, the imam's recitation is a recitation for him."],[7567,"Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. He said 'May God have mercy on you' to one of them and did not say it to the other. So the other said: 'O Messenger of God, you said it to so-and-so but did not say it to me?' He said: 'He praised God, but you did not praise Him.'"],[7568,"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog."],[7569,"The blood money for a mu'ahid is half the blood money of a Muslim."],[7570,"Bilal came to the Prophet ﷺ to call him for the morning prayer, and found him asleep. He said: 'Prayer is better than sleep.' And it was established in the morning call to prayer."],[7571,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded in three white sahuli garments of cotton."],[7572,"There was among those before you a man who bought wine and mixed it, making some of it water. Then he went off with it and sold it and took dinars. He put them in a purse and boarded a ship, carrying with him a monkey. When they were at sea, the monkey took the purse, climbed up, and ascended until it sat on the top of the mast. Then it untied the purse and began throwing one dinar into the sea and one dinar into the ship until it had thrown all that was in the purse. The monkey did that because the man had cheated."],[7573,"He was on a journey and performed ablution while al-Mughirah poured water for him. Then we reached the people, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf had led them in prayer. We prayed what we caught up with and made up what we had missed. Al-Mughirah said: I went to inform him, and he said: \"Leave him.\""],[7574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he halted at a place, would not depart until he prayed Zuhr, and he would pray when the sun had passed its zenith."],[7575,"The fixed prostrations are four: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil (the prostration), Ha Mim (the prostration), al-Najm, and Iqra' bismi rabbika."],[7576,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have intercourse with his wives and then not touch water. If morning came and he wanted to repeat, he would repeat; and if he did not want to, he would perform ghusl."],[7577,"People will continue to hold fast as long as knowledge comes to them from the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ and from their elders. But when it comes to them from the young ones, then they will be destroyed."],[7578,"Each of you will be spoken to by his Lord, with no interpreter between him and Him. He will look to his right and see what he has sent forth, and to his left and see what he has sent forth, and in front of him, and behold, the Fire. So fear the Fire, even with half a date."],[7579,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.\""],[7580,"The Prophet ﷺ forgot before completing the prayer, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness before the salam, and said: \"Whoever forgets before completion should prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness before the salam; and if he forgets after completion, he should prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salam.\""],[7581,"There is no one of my ummah who is put in charge of any affair of the people and does not guard them as he guards himself and his family, except that he will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."],[7582,"A sin that is forgiven, a sin that is not forgiven, and a sin for which one is requited. As for the sin that is not forgiven, it is associating partners with Allah. As for the sin that is forgiven, it is your deed between you and your Lord. As for the one for which you are requited, it is your wronging your brother."],[7583,"Whoever hears a hadith from me and disbelieves it has disbelieved three: Allah, His Messenger, and the one who narrated it."],[7584,"When one of you asks permission three times and is not given permission, let him return."],[7585,"Sometimes I scraped the semen from the garment of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[7586,"When a slave woman commits adultery, then commits adultery, then commits adultery, sell her even for a rope."],[7587,"The Messenger of God ﷺ missed two rak'ahs before the afternoon prayer, so when he finished he prayed them, then he did not pray them after that."],[7588,"He used to command the killing of all snakes, until Abu Lubabah b. 'Abd al-Mundhir informed him that the Prophet ﷺ forbade killing the snakes that are in houses. And he narrated that the Prophet ﷺ went to touch the Black Stone, and a scorpion stung him, so he said: \"What is the matter with you? May God curse you! If you would have left anyone, you would have left the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[7589,"The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted the killing of five creatures for the pilgrim in the state of ihram: the crow, the kite, the vicious dog, the scorpion, and the mouse."],[7590,"Do not sell fruits until their ripeness appears. He forbade the seller and the buyer."],[7591,"The two parties to a sale have the option, each one of them, as long as they have not separated and they are together, or one of them gives the other the choice. If one of them gives the other the choice and they conclude the sale on that basis, then the sale is binding."],[7592,"The poor will enter Paradise before the rich by five hundred years."],[7593,"God does not accept prayer from a woman until she covers her adornment, nor from a girl who has reached menstruation until she wears a head covering."],[7594,"Whoever fasts six days after breaking the fast of Ramadan consecutively, it is as if he fasted the entire year."],[7595,"Whoever has a debt and intends to repay it, with him is help from God, and God causes provision for him."],[7596,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to wear on the day of Eid a red burdah."],[7597,"In the year he performed Hajj, Uthman b. Affan ؓ was brought a tharidah containing some of this sandgrouse that the people outside the sanctuary had obtained. Some of the people said, 'Ali dislikes this.' So he sent for Ali and invited him. He was mending some of his fodder, so he shook off his hand and then came. Uthman said to him, 'You never cease to disagree about something. They claim that you say this is not permissible.' Ali became angry and said, 'Is it about this that you tell me I disagree? I adjure by God anyone who heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in the year he performed Hajj, when he was brought the leg of a wild donkey, \"Feed it to the people outside the sanctuary, for we are in ihram.\" More than one person stood up and testified for him. Then he said, 'I adjure by God anyone who heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in the year he performed Hajj, when he was brought ostrich eggs: \"Feed them to the people outside the sanctuary, for we are in ihram.\" More than one person stood up and testified for him. Then they dispersed from that bowl.'"],[7598,"The deeds will be presented to God on the Day of Resurrection. The prayer will come and say, 'O Lord, I am the prayer.' God will say, 'You are upon good.' The charity will come and say, 'O Lord, I am the charity.' He will say, 'You are upon good.' The fasting will come and say, 'O Lord, I am the fasting.' He will say, 'You are upon good.' Until Islam comes and says, 'O Lord, You are al-Salam and I am Islam.' God will say, 'You are upon good; by you I take today and by you I give.' Then God will say: 'Indeed, the religion with God is Islam. And whoever seeks a religion other than Islam, it will never be accepted from him, and in the Hereafter he will be among the losers' [Quran 3:85]."],[7599,"The first thing the servant will be asked about on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer. He will say, 'Look at the prayer of My servant. If he completed it, it will be said, \"O Lord, he completed it.\" And if he fell short in it, it will be said, \"O Lord, he fell short in it.\"' God will say, 'Look, does My servant have any voluntary prayers?' It will be said, 'Yes, many.' He will say, 'Then complete My servant's obligatory prayer from his voluntary prayers.' Then the deeds will be taken according to that measure."],[7600,"Do not face the qiblah nor turn your back to it for urination or defecation, but turn east or west."],[7601,"Fatimah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a pot of hers in which she had prepared some hasa', carrying it on a tray. She placed it before him. He said to her, 'Where is your cousin and your two sons?' She said, 'In the house.' He said, 'Go and call them.' So she came to Ali and said, 'Answer the Messenger of God ﷺ, you and your two sons.' Umm Salamah said: Ali came walking, holding the hands of al-Hasan and al-Husayn, and Fatimah walked with them. When he saw them approaching, he stretched out his hand to a cloak that was on the bed, spread it out, and seated them on it. He took the four corners of the cloak with his left hand and drew it over their heads. Then he raised his right hand to his Lord and said, 'O God, these are the people of my household, so remove from them impurity and purify them thoroughly,' three times."],[7602,"They asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'Did you ever commit anything forbidden with women in the pre-Islamic era?' He said, 'No. I was upon two appointments; as for one of them, my eye overcame me from it, and as for the other, the night-time talk of the people intervened between me and it.'"],[7603,"Indeed, the birds will strike the earth with their beaks and shake their tails from the terror of the Day of Resurrection, and the false witness will not speak, nor will his two feet settle on the ground until he is thrown into the Fire."],[7604,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to open the prayer with the takbir and the recitation of 'Al-hamdu lillahi rabb al-alamin' [Quran 1:2]. When he bowed, he did not lower his head nor raise it, but kept it in between. He used to say in every two rak'ahs the tashahhud, and he used to conclude the prayer with the taslim."],[7605,"A man asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'What an evil brother of the clan.' When he entered, he turned to him with his face and spoke with him. When he left, I said, 'O Messenger of God, you said, \"What an evil brother of the clan,\" but when he entered you turned to him with your face and spoke with him.' He said, 'Among the worst of people is the one from whose evil people guard themselves.'"],[7606,"The people suffered drought in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Muslims came to him and said, 'O Messenger of God, the rain has ceased, the trees have dried up, the livestock have perished, and the people are afflicted with famine. Ask your Lord to send us rain.' He said, 'On such-and-such a day, go out and bring your charities with you.' When that day came, the Messenger of God ﷺ and the people went out, walking with tranquility and dignity until they reached the prayer place. The Prophet ﷺ advanced and led them in two rak'ahs, reciting aloud. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the two Eid prayers and the rain prayer in the first rak'ah the Opening of the Book and 'Sabbih isma rabbika al-a'la' [Quran 87], and in the second rak'ah the Opening of the Book and 'Hal ataka hadith al-ghashiyah' [Quran 88]. When he finished his prayer, he faced the people, turned his cloak inside out, then knelt on his knees, raised his hands, and said the takbir once before supplicating for rain. Then he said, 'O God, give us water and succor us. O God, give us rain—a succoring, ample, spring-like, intense, torrential, covering, abundant, wholesome, pleasant, fertile, pasturing, heavy, all-encompassing, pouring, enveloping, continuous, flowing, beneficial, not harmful, swift, not delayed, rain. O God, by it revive the lands, succor the servants, and make it a provision for the present among us and the traveler. O God, send down upon our land its adornment, and send down upon our land its inhabitants. O God, send down upon us from the sky purifying water, and revive thereby a dead land, and give drink from what You have created for us—many cattle and people.'\" He said: They did not depart until small clouds approached, joined together, and then it rained upon them for seven days and their nights, not ceasing over Madinah. The Muslims came to him and said, 'O Messenger of God, the land has been flooded, the houses have collapsed, and the roads have been cut off. Pray to God to turn it away from us.' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed while he was on the pulpit until his molars appeared, in amazement at how quickly the children of Adam become weary. Then he said, 'O God, around us and not upon us. O God, upon the tops of the hills, the places where trees grow, the bellies of the valleys, and the backs of the high grounds.' He said: It dispersed from Madinah, and it rained in the surrounding pastures like a shield, while not a drop fell in the city."],[7607,"We do not accept the froth of the polytheists."],[7608,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me while I was among the sheep of ʿUqbah, and he wiped my head and said: “May God have mercy on you; you are a boy who will be taught.”"],[7609,"I asked my father privately, “O father, who is the best of this community after its Prophet?” He said, “Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah.” I said, “Then whom?” He said, “Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab.”"],[7610,"The woman with istihadah takes one purificatory bath, then performs wudu — meaning for every prayer."],[7611,"He used to have intimate contact with her while she was menstruating, and she had a waist-wrapper reaching to her knees."],[7612,"Muhammad b. al-Marzuban narrated to us: Muhammad b. Hakim al-Razi narrated to us: al-Harith b. Muslim narrated to us: Bahr b. al-Saqqa narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to me from ʿUrwah from ʿAʾishah, that she said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ used to lie with me while I was menstruating, and we used to perform ghusl together from one vessel.”"],[7613,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[7614,"This Ramadan has come; in it the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained. Far removed is the one who reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven; if he is not forgiven in it, then when?"],[7615,"Withdrawal (ʿazl) was mentioned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “It does not matter if you do not do it; it is only destiny (qadar).”"],[7616,"When he oiled his beard, he began with the hair beneath his lower lip (ʿanfaqah)."],[7617,"Al-Baraʾ b. ʿAzib met me, took my hand, shook it, and smiled in my face, then said: “Do you know why I took your hand?” I said: “No, except that I thought you did it only for good.” He said: “The Prophet ﷺ met me and did that to me, then said: ‘Do you know why I did that to you?’ I said: ‘No.’ The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘When two Muslims meet, shake hands, and each smiles in the other’s face, doing that only for God, they do not part until they are forgiven.’”"],[7618,"There has been no association of partners with God (shirk) since Adam was sent down from heaven to earth except that its beginning was denial of destiny (qadar), and no community has associated partners with God except through denial of destiny. You will surely be tested by this, O community; when you meet them, you should be the ones asking, and do not give them access to the religion, lest they introduce doubts among you."],[7619,"God created the creation, decreed the decree, and took the covenant of the prophets while His Throne was upon the water. He took the people of faith by His right hand, and He took the people of misery by His left hand, and both hands of the Most Merciful are right. He said: “O people of the right hand.” They said: “At Your service and obedience.” He said: “Am I not your Lord?” They said: “Yes.” Then He mixed them together, and one of them said: “Our Lord, why did You mix us together?” He said: “They have deeds other than that which they will do, so that you may not say on the Day of Resurrection, ‘We were unaware of this,’ or say, ‘It was only our fathers who associated partners before, and we were descendants after them.’” So God created the creation, decreed the decree, and took the covenant of the prophets while His Throne was upon the water. The people of Paradise are its people, and the people of Hell are its people. A man among the people said: “Then what is the point of deeds, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Every people works for what they were created for; the people of Paradise by the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the people of Hell by the deeds of the people of Hell.” ʿUmar b. al-Khattab said: “O Messenger of God, do you consider these deeds of ours something we initiate or something already decreed?” He said: “Something already decreed.” He said: “Then now we will strive in worship.”"],[7620,"Nabhan apostatized three times, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O God, grant me power over Nabhan with a black rope around his neck.” I turned and there was Nabhan, seized, and they had put a black rope around his neck. They brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ took the sword in his right hand and the rope in his left to kill him. A man from the Ansar said: “O Messenger of God, would that you step aside from him.” He said: So he handed the sword to a man and said: “Go and strike his neck.” He said: So he went off with him, but Nabhan laughed and said: “Will they kill a man who bears witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God?” So he let him go."],[7621,"He used to pray at night two rak’ahs, then two rak’ahs, then two rak’ahs, then two rak’ahs, then three."],[7622,"The Messenger of God ﷺ granted a concession for wiping over the leather socks: three days and their nights for the traveler, and for the resident one day and one night."],[7623,"I saw ‘Umar b. al-Khattab striking the hands of men during the fast of Rajab until they put them into the food, and saying: “Rajab, and what is Rajab? Rajab is only a month that the people of the Jahiliyyah used to venerate; when Islam came, it was abandoned.”"],[7624,"Salman al-Farisi came to me to greet me, wearing a Qatwani cloak wrapped around himself. I threw him a cushion, but he did not return it and instead rolled up his cloak and sat on it. He said: “It suffices you what you have attained of position.” Then he praised God for a while, said “God is greater,” and invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ. Then he said: “Where is your companion?”—meaning Abu al-Darda’. I said: “He is in the mosque.” So he went to him, and then they both came back. Abu al-Darda’ had bought meat for a dirham, and it was in his hand, hanging. He said: “O Umm al-Darda’, bake and cook.” So we did. Then we brought the food to Salman. Abu al-Darda’ said: “Eat with Umm al-Darda’, for I am fasting.” Salman said: “I will not eat until you eat.” So Abu al-Darda’ broke his fast and ate with him. When the hour came in which Abu al-Darda’ used to stand (in prayer), he went to stand, but Salman made him sit. Abu al-Darda’ said: “Do you forbid me from worshipping my Lord?” Salman said: “Your eye has a right over you, and your family has a share over you.” So he prevented him until it was near dawn. Then they stood and prayed some rak’ahs and performed witr, then went out to the morning prayer. They mentioned their situation to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “What is with Salman, may his mother be bereaved of him? He has indeed been filled with knowledge.”"],[7625,"I said to ‘Uthman: “O Commander of the Believers, what made you place Bara’ah among the Mi’in and al-Anfal among the Mathani, joining them together and placing them in the Seven Long Surahs, without writing ‘In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful’ between them?” ‘Uthman said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ, among what was revealed to him of surahs, there were those of multiple verses. When a verse was revealed to him, he would say to one of those who wrote: ‘Place this verse in such-and-such surah.’ Al-Anfal was among the first to be revealed in Madinah, and Bara’ah was the last of the Qur’an. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ died without clarifying it for us. I saw that their story resembles her story, so for that reason I joined them together and did not write ‘In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful’ between them.”"],[7626,"Using the toothpick is a sunnah."],[7627,"We entered upon the Prophet ﷺ on Friday, and there was food before him. He said: “Come near and eat.” We said: “We are fasting.” He said: “Did you fast yesterday?” We said: “No.” He said: “Then do you intend to fast tomorrow?” We said: “No.” He said: “Then eat, for Friday is not to be fasted alone; it is taken as a festival.”"],[7628,"The witr is not obligatory, but it is a sunnah established by the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[7629,"The letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ came to us while we were in the land of Juhaynah: “Do not benefit from the carcass by its hide or sinew.”"],[7630,"If the strap of one of your sandals breaks, he should not walk in a single sandal."],[7631,"The purification of the vessel of one of you, if a dog licks in it, is to wash it seven times."],[7632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and saw a man in the mosque not performing his bowing and prostration completely. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The prayer of a man who does not complete the bowing and the prostration is not accepted.\""],[7633,"When a warrior goes out in the path of Allah, his sins are made into a bridge over the door of his house. When he leaves it behind, he leaves all his sins behind, so not even the wing of a mosquito remains upon him. Allah guarantees four things for him: that He will replace him in what he left behind of family and property; that by whatever death he dies, He will admit him to Paradise; that if He returns him, He will return him safe with whatever he obtained of booty or reward; and that the sun does not set except that it sets with his sins."],[7634,"Whoever marries has completed half of faith, so let him fear Allah in the remaining half."],[7635,"A man went out and commanded his wife not to leave her house. Her father was in the lower part of the house, and she was in the upper part. Her father fell ill, so she sent to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: \"Obey your husband.\" Then her father died, so she sent to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Obey your husband.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ sent to her: \"Indeed Allah has forgiven her father because of her obedience to her husband.\""],[7636,"The family of Muhammad ﷺ awoke as nine households, not having a sa' of food among them."],[7637,"The wellbeing of the first part of this community was through asceticism and certainty, and its destruction will be through miserliness and [long] hopes."],[7638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never struck a woman, nor a servant of his, nor did he ever strike anything with his hand except when fighting in the path of Allah. Nor was anything taken from him such that he would take revenge on its owner, except if the sanctities of Allah were violated, then he would take revenge for Allah. Nor was he ever given a choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them, unless it was a sin; and if it was a sin, he was the furthest of people from it."],[7639,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, the well is without liability, the mine is without liability, and on treasure-trove one-fifth is due."],[7640,"He used to wake up in a state of major ritual impurity from intercourse, not from a wet dream, and he would fast."],[7641,"We used to travel with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we would not remove our leather socks if we had put them on while in a state of ritual purity, for three days, except for major ritual impurity, but [we would wipe over them] because of defecation, urination, or sleep."],[7642,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, were it not that I would make it difficult for the believers, I would never stay behind any expedition in the path of Allah. But I do not find what to mount them on, and they do not find the means to follow me, and it would not please their souls to stay behind after me."],[7643,"I would love to fight in the path of Allah until I am killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed."],[7644,"When evening came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: 'We have entered the evening, and the dominion belongs to Allah, the One, the Subduer. Praise be to Allah, who has taken away the day and brought the night, while we are in well-being from Him. O Allah, this is a new creation of Yours that has come. Whatever evil I have done in it, then overlook it; and whatever good I have done in it, then accept it and multiply it many times over. O Allah, You know all my needs, and You are able to accomplish all of them. O Allah, fulfill every need of mine tonight, and do not increase me in my worldly life, and do not decrease me in my Hereafter.' And when morning came, he would say the like of that."],[7645,"Avoid this foul tree; whoever eats it, let him not come near our mosque."],[7646,"Two great factions will fight, their call being one. While they are thus, a renegade group will secede from them; the party closest to the truth will kill them."],[7647,"I was in Syria, and Abu Umamah Sudayy b. 'Ajlan, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, was there, and he was a friend of mine. Some heads of the Haruriyyah were brought and thrown on the steps. Abu Umamah came, entered the mosque, prayed two rak'ahs, then turned toward the heads. I said: 'I will follow him until I hear what he says.' I followed him until he stood over them and wept. Then he said: 'Glory be to Allah! What is Iblis doing to this ummah?' Then he said: 'Dogs of the Fire, dogs of the Fire, dogs of the Fire.' Then he said: 'The worst of those killed who were killed under the shade of the sky, and the best of those killed are those who killed them.' Then he recited this verse: 'On the Day when some faces will be white and some faces black; as for those whose faces turn black, \"Did you disbelieve after your belief?\"' (Q 3:106). Then he turned to me and saw me. Abu Ghalib said: 'He took me by my forearm' and said: 'You are in a land where these are many?'—meaning Iraq. I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'May Allah protect you from being one of them.' I said: 'O Abu Umamah, do you think your saying \"dogs of the Fire\" was your own opinion, or something you heard?' He said: 'Glory be to Allah! I would then be bold. No, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, not once, not twice, not three, not four, not five, not six, not seven.'"],[7648,"Allah revealed to an angel among the angels: 'Overturn such-and-such a city upon its inhabitants.' He said: 'In it is Your servant so-and-so, who has not disobeyed You for the blink of an eye.' He said: 'Overturn it upon him and upon them, for his face has never once frowned for My sake for an hour.'"],[7649,"Forty of the companions of the Negus came to the Prophet ﷺ and fought with him at Uhud. They had wounds among them, but none of them was killed. When they saw the need of the believers, they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are people of means. Permit us to bring our wealth and console the Muslims with it.' So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning them: 'Those to whom We gave the Book before it—they believe in it' (Q 28:52) up to: 'Those will be given their reward twice for what they patiently endured' (Q 28:54). He made for them two rewards. He said: 'And they repel evil with good' (Q 28:54), meaning the spending with which they consoled the Muslims, until this verse was revealed. He said: 'Then the People of the Book boasted over the Muslims until this verse was revealed. They said: \"O assembly of Muslims, whoever of us believes in your Book will have two rewards, and whoever does not believe in your Book will have one reward like your rewards.\" So Allah revealed: \"O you who believe, fear Allah and believe in His Messenger; He will give you a double portion of His mercy and make for you a light by which you will walk\" (Q 57:28), giving them the light and forgiveness.' He said: 'Lest the People of the Book know that they have no power over anything of Allah's bounty.'"],[7650,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling the fifth before it was divided, and forbade having intercourse with women until they had given birth, if they were pregnant."],[7651,"The sadaqat al-fitr for every person is two mudds of flour or wheat, and of barley a sa', and of sweets—raisins or dates—a sa' each."],[7652,"For grazing horses, for every horse a dinar."],[7653,"I witnessed with 'Ali the battle of the Nahrawan. When he finished killing them, he said: 'Search for the mukhaddaj.' They searched for him but did not find him. He ordered that a reed be placed on every corpse. They found him in a hollow in a pool of water—a black man, foul-smelling, in the place of whose hand was something like a breast, with hairs on it. When he looked at him, he said: 'Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.' One of his two sons—meaning al-Hasan or al-Husayn—was heard saying: 'Praise be to Allah, who has given rest to the ummah of Muhammad ﷺ from this band.' 'Ali said: 'If only three of the ummah of Muhammad ﷺ remained, one of them would be upon the opinion of these. They are in the loins of men and the wombs of women.'"],[7654,"I was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones."],[7655,"Do not make use of anything from the dead animal, neither hide nor sinew."],[7656,"I and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to bathe from a single vessel, and we would both plunge into it together. I did not do more than scoop three handfuls over my head."],[7657,"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night, God builds for him a house in Paradise."],[7658,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when the delegation of Banu Tamim came to him, led by Qays b. 'Asim, 'Amr b. al-Ahtam, and al-Zibriqan b. Badr. The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Amr b. al-Ahtam: 'What do you say about al-Zibriqan b. Badr?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, he is obeyed among his people, formidable in argument, and protective of what is behind him.' Al-Zibriqan said: 'O Messenger of God, he knows more about me than he described, but he envied me.' 'Amr said: 'By God, O Messenger of God, he is lacking in manliness, meager in property, base in character, and foolish in his father. By God, O Messenger of God, I did not lie at first, and I have spoken truth at last. But I was pleased and said the best I knew, and I became angry and said the worst I knew.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery, and some poetry is wisdom.'"],[7659,"When two Muslims meet, shake hands, and ask about each other, God sends down between them a hundred mercies: ninety-nine for the more cheerful, the more open, the more dutiful, and the better inquirer about his brother."],[7660,"Four mountains are among the mountains of Paradise, and four rivers are among the rivers of Paradise. As for the mountains: al-Tur, Lubnan, Tur Sina', and Tur Zayta. And the rivers from Paradise are: al-Furat, al-Nil, Sayhan, and Jayhan."],[7661,"The lowest of all the people of Paradise in rank will have ten thousand servants standing at his head, each one holding two platters, one of gold and the other of silver. In each platter is a color not found in the other. He eats from the last of it just as he eats from the first, and finds in its last the same fragrance and pleasure as in its first. Then it becomes like the scent of pungent musk. They do not urinate, defecate, or blow their noses. They will be brothers on couches facing one another."],[7662,"'Ali b. Abi Talib said: 'O Messenger of God, which is dearer to you: me or Fatimah?' He said: 'Fatimah is dearer to me than you, and you are mightier to me than her. It is as if I see you at my basin driving people away from it. Upon it are pitchers like the number of stars in the sky. I, you, al-Hasan, al-Husayn, Fatimah, 'Aqil, and Ja'far will be in Paradise as brothers on couches facing one another. You are with me, and your Shi'ah are in Paradise.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited: 'Brothers on couches facing one another; none of them will look at the back of his companion.'"],[7663,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, is not a martyr only one who is killed in the path of God?' He said: 'O 'A'ishah, then the martyrs of my community would be few. Whoever says twenty-five times in a day: \"O God, bless me in death and in what comes after death,\" and then dies on his bed, God gives him the reward of a martyr.'"],[7664,"Marry virgins, for they have more productive wombs, sweeter mouths, less deceit, and are more content with little."],[7665,"Whoever recites ten verses is not recorded among the heedless. Whoever stands in prayer with a hundred verses is recorded among the devout. Whoever stands with two hundred verses is recorded among the worshipers."],[7666,"Regarding wiping over the leather socks, he said: 'Three days and their nights for the traveler, and for the resident one day and one night.'"],[7667,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by two graves of the Banu al-Najjar. They were being punished for talebearing and urine. He took a palm branch, split it, and placed one half on this grave and one half on that grave. He said: 'Their punishment will continue to be lightened as long as these remain moist.'"],[7668,"Ibn Mas'ud passed by, and there was Abu Jahl giving up his soul. He came and sat on his chest. Abu Jahl raised his head and said, \"Are you not a little shepherd boy yesterday in Makkah? You have climbed a difficult ascent.\" He cut off his head and came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"This is the head of Abu Jahl.\" He said, \"By Allah?\" He said, \"By Allah, it is his head.\" He said, \"Then he ordered it to be thrown into the well.\""],[7669,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have a slave girl, and I practice coitus interruptus with her. I desire from her what men desire, but I dislike that she becomes pregnant. The Jews claim that al-azl is the minor burying alive of daughters.\" He said, \"The Jews lie. If Allah wanted to create him, no one could avert it.\""],[7670,"Between the servant and disbelief is abandoning the prayer, and between the servant and polytheism is abandoning the prayer."],[7671,"There is no contagion, no evil omen, and no hamah. A Bedouin stood up and said, \"A mangy camel slipped among my camels and made them mangy.\" He said, \"That is destiny. Who made the first one mangy?\""],[7672,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal has fasted the entire time."],[7673,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that the Quran be taken to the land of the enemy, fearing that the enemy would get hold of it."],[7674,"He was present with Zayd b. Kharijah when he spoke after he had died and been covered. He said: The first thing he said was: \"Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness truly. Abu Bakr, weak in the eyes of people, is strong in the cause of Allah, I bear witness truly. Umar b. al-Khattab, the strong and trustworthy, I bear witness truly.\""],[7675,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the mirbad and saw Uthman leading a camel loaded with flour, ghee, and honey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Make it kneel.\" So he made it kneel. He called for a clay pot and put in it some of the ghee, honey, and flour. Then he ordered a fire to be lit under it until it was cooked. He said, \"Eat.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate from it and then said, \"This is something the people of Persia call khabis.\""],[7676,"I saw Abdullah b. al-Zubayr standing on his minbar in Makkah while delivering a sermon, saying: \"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines. Thus I heard your Prophet ﷺ say.\""],[7677,"May Allah have mercy on the one who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for perhaps the one to whom it is conveyed is more attentive than the one who hears it."],[7678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me on the day of the conquest of Makkah while I was fasting. He said, \"Drink.\" I said, \"I am fasting.\" He said, \"Is it a make-up fast?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then drink.\" So I drank."],[7679,"The one who prostrates before the imam and raises his head before him, his forelock is in the hand of a devil."],[7680,"The virtue of praying in congregation over praying alone is twenty-seven degrees."],[7681,"She said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"I have grown old and become weak, so direct me to a deed I can do while sitting.\" He ﷺ said: \"If you say Allahu akbar one hundred times, it is better for you than one hundred fine, adorned, accepted camels. If you glorify Allah one hundred times, it is better than freeing one hundred slaves. If you praise Allah one hundred times, it is better for you than one hundred saddled and bridled horses that you ride in the path of Allah. If you say la ilaha illa Allah one hundred times, no deed will surpass it and no sin will remain with it.\""],[7682,"Before the Hour, usury, adultery, and wine will appear openly."],[7683,"Poetry is in the same position as speech; its good is like good speech, and its ugly is like ugly speech."],[7684,"The most beloved of you to me are those with the best character, those who are easygoing and gentle, who befriend and are befriended. The most hateful of you to Allah are those who spread malicious gossip, create divisions between loved ones, and seek hardship for the innocent."],[7685,"When a black person is hungry, he steals, and when he is full, he commits adultery. Indeed, there are in them two traits of truth: generosity and courage."],[7686,"He forbade writing on graves."],[7687,"Whoever equips a warrior, or provides iftar to a fasting person, or equips a pilgrim, will have the same reward as him, without diminishing the other's reward at all."],[7688,"Umar touched the corner (the Black Stone) and kissed it, saying: \"I know that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit. Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you, I would not have kissed you.\""],[7689,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat me in his lap, wiped my head, and said: \"O Allah, teach him wisdom.\""],[7690,"I stood for prayer with Umar b. al-Khattab, and the elders among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were with him. A man came in front of the row, looking at the faces of the people, until when he was opposite me, he nudged me hard and stood in my place. When Umar said the salam, he asked: \"Did what I did to you upset you?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"We used to be commanded to take the first row, so I looked at the faces of the people and did not disapprove of anyone except you.\" I said: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"Ubayy b. Ka'b.\""],[7691,"A group of people passed by Jesus son of Mary ﷺ , and he said: \"One of these will die today, if Allah wills.\" They went on, then returned to him in the evening carrying bundles of firewood. He said: \"Put them down.\" Then he said to the one about whom he had said he would die that day: \"Untie your bundle of firewood.\" He untied it, and in it there was a black snake. He asked: \"What did you do today?\" He said: \"I did nothing.\" He said: \"Consider what you did.\" He said: \"I did nothing, except that I had a piece of bread in my hand and a poor person passed by me and asked me, and I gave him part of it.\" He said: \"By that it was warded off from you.\""],[7692,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that anyone pray with his garment tucked up."],[7693,"That he greeted the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was urinating, and he did not return the greeting until he had finished."],[7694,"That a delegation came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he questioned them, and some of them lied to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Were it not for generosity in you and God's mercy upon you, I would have made you an example to delegations of your people."],[7695,"Indeed, Satan loves red, so beware of red and every garment of fame."],[7696,"That he was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he and Abu Talha, and Safiyya was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ. His she-camel stumbled with him, and Abu Talha jumped up and said, \"Are you hurt?\" He said, \"No, mind the woman.\" So I threw my garment over my face and then threw it over her. When we were at the Harra, or when we came within sight of Madinah, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Returning, repenting, worshiping—if God wills—praising our Lord."],[7697,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, the Friday prayer is obligatory upon him—except a slave, a woman, or a child. And whoever is distracted by amusement or trade, God has no need of him, and God is Self-Sufficient, Praiseworthy."],[7698,"Whoever humbles himself before his Muslim brother, God raises him; and whoever elevates himself over him, God lowers him."],[7699,"We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. The family of Muhammad only eats from this wealth."],[7700,"If I do not appoint a successor, then the Messenger of God ﷺ did not appoint one; and if I do appoint a successor, then Abu Bakr did appoint one."],[7701,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray witr with five rak'ahs, not sitting between them."],[7702,"The Hour will not come until every people is ruled by its hypocrites."],[7703,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to relieve himself, he would go far away."],[7704,"Whoever says before the Fajr prayer on Friday three times: 'I seek forgiveness from Allah, besides whom there is no deity, and I turn to Him in repentance,' his sins will be forgiven, even if they are more than the foam of the sea."],[7705,"The most beloved words to Allah are four: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no deity but Allah, and Allah is greatest. It does not harm you with which of them you begin."],[7706,"We were forbidden to follow our eyes the shooting star when it falls, and we were commanded to say at that time: 'Whatever Allah wills, there is no power except with Allah.'"],[7707,"While a man was walking between two cloaks, impressed with himself, Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he is sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."],[7708,"The best judge among us is Ali, and Ubayy is the best reciter among us."],[7709,"He forbade the private parts of women."],[7710,"We stayed in Madinah for two years before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, establishing the prayer and building the mosques."],[7711,"A gift of hunted meat was given to the Messenger ﷺ while he was in ihram, and he returned it."],[7712,"Prayer is disliked in the middle of the day, except on Friday, for Hell is not stoked then."],[7713,"There is nothing wrong if one of you gives voluntary charity and makes it on behalf of his parents, so that they get its reward and nothing is diminished from his own reward."],[7714,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus and said four takbirs over him."],[7715,"Indeed, an evil deed does not expiate an evil deed, but a good deed expiates an evil deed."],[7716,"The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon and said in his sermon: \"Indeed, the lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. And whoever grazes around a protected sanctuary will soon trespass into it.\""],[7717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a man from the Ansar, called Ibn al-Lutbiyyah, to collect the sadaqah. When he returned, the Prophet ﷺ sent for him to settle his account. He said: \"This is for you, and this was given to me as a gift.\" That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We appoint men from among you over what Allah has entrusted to us. When one of them returns, he says: 'This is for you, and this was given to me as a gift.' Why did he not sit in the house of his father and mother and see whether he would be given gifts? Whoever of you works for us, let him bring us all of it, the small and the great. And let one of you beware of coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck that bellows, or a cow that moos, or a sheep that bleats\"—or he said—\"that bleats.\""],[7718,"Khuzaymah b. Thabit—not the Ansari—was in a caravan belonging to Khadijah, and the Prophet ﷺ was with him in that caravan. He said to him: \"O Muhammad, I see in you certain qualities, and I bear witness that you are the Prophet who will emerge from Tihamah. I have believed in you, so when I hear of your emergence, I will come to you.\" He was delayed from the Prophet ﷺ until the day of the conquest of Makkah, then he came to him. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he said: \"Welcome to the first emigrant.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what prevented me from being among the first to come to you, while I believe in you, not denying your pledge, and not breaking my covenant with you, and I believed in the Quran and disbelieved in the idol, was only that after you left us we were struck by severe, consecutive years of drought, which left the marrow thin and the riding camels gaunt, their milk dried up and their flesh wasted, and the young camels became huddled and the qantah or the thorny trees became dry, and the reeds became twisted; the fresh vegetation withered in the land, and it consumed all the dry plants and destroyed the roots of the reeds, until the qantah was cut off. I came to you not breaking my covenant, and not denying my pledge.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Take it from you: Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, stretches out His hand at night for the one who sins by day to repent, and if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance; and He stretches out His hand by day for the one who sins by night to repent, and if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance. Indeed, the truth is heavy, like its heaviness on the Day of Resurrection, and falsehood is light, like its lightness on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah.\""],[7719,"The woman whose husband dies should not wear dyed garments of safflower or those dyed with red clay, nor jewelry, nor apply henna, nor use kohl."],[7720,"The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is the one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."],[7721,"May Allah curse a people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."],[7722,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, and no one had collected the Quran except four: Abu al-Darda', Mu'adh, Abu Zayd, and Zayd b. Thabit."],[7723,"Whoever of you is one who prays on Friday, let him pray four [rak'ahs]."],[7724,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Teach me—or guide me—to a deed that will admit me to Paradise.\" He said: \"Be a mu'adhdhin.\" He said: \"I cannot.\" He said: \"Be an imam.\" He said: \"I cannot.\" He said: \"Then stand next to the imam.\""],[7725,"Whoever says after every prayer: 'I seek forgiveness from Allah, besides whom there is no deity, the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining, and I turn to Him in repentance,' will be forgiven, even if he fled from the battlefield."],[7726,"My beloved friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ enjoined me with seven things: love of the poor and being close to them; to maintain ties of kinship even if they cut me off; to say 'There is no might and no power except with Allah,' for it is one of the treasures of Paradise; not to fear the blame of any blamer for the sake of Allah; to speak the truth even if it is bitter; to look to those who are below me and not look to those who are above me; and not to take anything from people."],[7727,"Prostration is on seven limbs."],[7728,"While we were with the Prophet ﷺ, a Jewish man—called Thaʿlaba b. al-Ḥārith—came and said, “Al-sāmu ʿalayka, O Muḥammad.” He replied, “And upon you.” The Jew said, “You claim that in Paradise there is food, drink, and spouses.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Yes. Do you believe in the tree of musk?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “And do you find it in your scripture?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed, urine and janāba will be sweat flowing like musk from beneath their forelocks to their feet.”"],[7729,"That ʿAmra bt. al-Jawn sought refuge from the Messenger of God ﷺ when she was brought to him. He said, “You have sought refuge with a mighty refuge,” and he divorced her and ordered Usāma to give her a gift of three garments."],[7730,"I saw henna dye in the sideburns of the Prophet ﷺ."],[7731,"ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān had a doorkeeper, who would go out before him to prayer. One day he went out and prayed with the doorkeeper before him. Then he came and the doorkeeper sat to one side, wrapped his cloak and placed it under his head, lay down, and put the whip before him. ʿAlī came wearing a waist-wrapper and a cloak, with a staff in his hand. When the doorkeeper saw him from afar, he said, “This is ʿAlī coming.” ʿUthmān sat up, drew his cloak over himself, and ʿAlī came and stood at his head and said, “You bought the estate of the family of so-and-so, and the waqf of the Messenger of God ﷺ has a right in its water. I knew that no one but you would buy it.” ʿUthmān stood up and words passed between them that I will not repeat until I meet God. Al-ʿAbbās came and intervened, and ʿUthmān raised the whip against ʿAlī, and ʿAlī raised the staff against ʿUthmān. Al-ʿAbbās began calming them, saying to ʿAlī, “The Commander of the Faithful,” and to ʿUthmān, “Your cousin.” He continued until they calmed down. Then on the evening of the next day, I saw them, each holding the other’s hand, conversing."],[7732,"I have never seen anyone whose prayer more resembled the Messenger of God ﷺ than the son of Umm Sulaym."],[7733,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, teach me a supplication through which I may obtain good.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Say: O God, pardon me, for You are Pardoning, Generous.”"],[7734,"When you send an envoy, send one with a handsome face and a good name."],[7735,"Son of Adam, if you committed sins filling the earth, as long as you do not associate anything with Me, I will grant you forgiveness filling the earth."],[7736,"There is no servant who begins the day fasting except that the gates of heaven are opened for him, his limbs glorify God, and the inhabitants of the lowest heaven seek forgiveness for him until he is veiled. If he prays one or two voluntary rakʿas, the heavens shine with light for him, and his wives from the ḥūr al-ʿīn say, “O God, take his soul to us, for we long to see him.” And if he says ‘lā ilāha illā Allāh,’ or glorifies God, or magnifies Him, seventy thousand angels receive it and write it down until he is veiled."],[7737,"I used to come to the Prophet ﷺ while he was performing iʿtikāf in the mosque, and I was menstruating. He would put his head out of the mosque to me, and I would comb and oil his hair while I was menstruating."],[7738,"Whoever’s soul departs his body while he is free of three things enters Paradise: arrogance, misappropriation of spoils, and debt."],[7739,"Ṣafiyya bt. Ḥuyayy menstruated while she was with the Messenger of God ﷺ. She had performed the ifāḍa before that. When the Messenger of God ﷺ departed from Minā, it was said to him, “Ṣafiyya has menstruated.” He said, “She may delay us.” They said, “O Messenger of God, she has performed the ifāḍa.” He said, “Then let her depart.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ departed with her while she was in her blood."],[7740,"Beware of covetousness, for it is present poverty itself; and beware of anything for which an excuse must be made."],[7741,"No community has ever differed after its Prophet except that the people of falsehood among them prevailed over the people of truth."],[7742,"Whoever leads a people in prayer must fear Allah and know that he is a guarantor, answerable just as he has guaranteed; if he does well, he receives an equal reward to that of those who pray behind him, without any of their rewards being diminished, and whatever shortcoming occurs is upon him."],[7743,"Part of the completion of a servant's faith is that he says 'if Allah wills' in every statement he makes."],[7744,"When the sky begins to form in a seaward direction, then veers northward, it is a source of abundant water."],[7745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ imposed upon us the charity of Ramadan: one sa' of barley or one sa' of dates."],[7746,"When travel became pressing upon him, he combined Maghrib and 'Isha'."],[7747,"Abu Hurayrah said to me: 'O Farazdaq, I see that you have small feet; if you can secure a place for them at the Pond, then do so, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"My Pond is between 'Uman and Aylah; its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey; its vessels are as numerous as the stars of the sky; whoever drinks from it a single drink will never thirst again.\"'"],[7748,"We said to 'Abdullah b. Ja'far: 'Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and what you saw of him, and do not narrate to us from anyone else, even if he is trustworthy.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"What is between the navel and the knee is 'awrah.\"'"],[7749,"Asking is not lawful for a wealthy person, except from a relative or a ruler."],[7750,"Whoever seizes the property of a Muslim by a false oath will meet Allah while He is angry with him."],[7751,"When one of you comes to a row and it is already complete, let him pull a man to himself and make him stand beside him."],[7752,"Whoever performs ablution on Friday, it is good and excellent; and whoever takes a bath, the bath is more virtuous."],[7753,"I should not find any of you placing one leg over the other, then singing, and abandoning the recitation of Surat al-Baqarah."],[7754,"When the Prophet ﷺ was asked for something and he wanted to do it, he said, \"Yes,\" and when he wanted not to do it, he remained silent. He never said \"no\" to anything. A bedouin came to him and asked him, and he remained silent. Then he asked him again, and he remained silent. Then he asked him again, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him in a rebuking manner: \"Ask whatever you wish, O bedouin.\" We envied him and said: Now he will ask for Paradise. The bedouin said: I ask you for a mount. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"That is yours.\" Then he said: \"Ask.\" He said: I ask you for provisions. He said: \"And that is yours.\" He said: We were amazed at that, so the Prophet ﷺ said: How far is the bedouin's request from the old woman of the Children of Israel. Then he said: \"When Musa was commanded to cross the sea, and he reached it, the faces of the animals were struck, and they turned back. Musa said: What is the matter with me, O Lord? He said to him: You are at the grave of Yusuf, so carry his bones with you. The grave had become level with the ground, so Musa did not know where it was. They said: If any of you knows where it is, the old woman of the Children of Israel might know where it is. Musa ﷺ sent for her, and said: Do you know where the grave of Yusuf ﷺ is? She said: Yes. He said: Guide me to it. She said: No, by Allah, not until you give me what I ask. He said: That is yours. She said: I ask you that I be with you in the same degree in Paradise that you will be in. He said: Ask for Paradise. She said: No, by Allah, but to be with you. Musa kept arguing with her, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to him: Give her that, for it will not diminish anything from you. So he gave it to her, and she guided him to the grave. He extracted the bones and crossed the sea.\""],[7755,"Whoever seizes the right of a person by an oath he swears on my pulpit without right, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[7756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never stood among us except that he commanded us to give charity and forbade us from mutilation."],[7757,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while food was in front of him. He said: \"Come near, eat, mention the name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.\""],[7758,"I entered the mosque of Kufa on a Friday evening while 'Ali was addressing the people. They rose from the corners of the mosque shouting \"arbitration!\" He gestured with his hand like this, then said: \"A word of truth by which falsehood is sought. I await the judgment of Allah regarding you, to judge by the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ, and to divide among you equally. Nothing prevents you from praying in this mosque as long as your hands are with our hands, and we will not fight you until you fight us.\""],[7759,"Whoever embraces Islam, no jizyah is due from him."],[7760,"The people with the severest punishment are the image-makers."],[7761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing in prayer when a sheep went to pass in front of him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raced it until he pressed it against the wall. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Nothing interrupts the prayer, but ward off what you can.\""],[7762,"We said: O Messenger of Allah, the affairs of Mina are astonishing; it is narrow, but when the people descend upon it, it becomes spacious. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The likeness of Mina is that of the womb; it is narrow, but when it becomes pregnant, Allah expands it.\""],[7763,"Do not revert after me to disbelief, striking the necks of one another."],[7764,"Indeed, I have a cistern, and I will be your forerunner to it."],[7765,"For every five camels that graze freely, one sheep is due as charity."],[7766,"No one ever raises his voice in the talbiyah except that he is given good tidings, and no one ever says the takbir except that he is given good tidings.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, of Paradise?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[7767,"Regarding the verse 'You are only a warner, and for every people there is a guide,' he said: \"The Messenger of God is the warner, and the guide is a man from Banu Hashim.\""],[7768,"I entered upon al-Mukhtar, and when I was about to leave, he said: \"O Abu 'Umar, will you not help us with this throne, for Gabriel has just left it?\" I said: \"Yes, I will help you by burning it and scattering it completely into the sea.\" Rifa'a said: I reached for the hilt of my sword and said to myself: \"Should I not kill this liar?\" Then I remembered the words of my brother 'Amr b. al-Hamiq that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever entrusts a man with his life and then kills him, I am innocent of the killer, even if the victim is an unbeliever.\""],[7769,"We used to sit with the Prophet ﷺ as if birds were on our heads; none of us would speak except Abu Bakr and 'Umar."],[7770,"We used to be commanded to finish our provisions after three days—meaning the sacrificial animals."],[7771,"I went with Ibn 'Umar on an errand to Ibn 'Abbas, and Ibn 'Umar completed his errand with Ibn 'Abbas. His talk that day was that he said: A man passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ in one of the streets, having just come from relieving himself of urine and feces, and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting. When the man was about to disappear into the street, he struck his hand on the wall and wiped his face, then struck his hand again on the wall and wiped his forearms, then returned the man's greeting. He said: 'Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I was not in a state of purity.'"],[7772,"When the Banu al-Hakam reach thirty in number, they will treat the religion of God as a deception, the servants of God as their slaves, and the wealth of God as something to be passed around among themselves."],[7773,"An oath in a sale promotes the goods but wipes out the profit."],[7774,"A man from the Ansar came hurrying after his camel, and when the Maghrib prayer was called, he went to the mosque and found Mu'adh b. Jabal leading them. He began reciting Surat al-Baqarah or Al 'Imran. When the man saw that, he left and prayed by himself, then caught up with his camel. The people of Madinah said: 'So-and-so has become a hypocrite.' When the man heard that, he went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him. The Prophet ﷺ called Mu'adh and said: 'Are you a troublemaker? Why did you not recite \"By the sun and its brightness\" or \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High\"?'"],[7775,"There is a moment on Friday in which no servant ever asks God for anything except that God grants it to him."],[7776,"I said to Ibn 'Umar: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, some people order us to ascend the pulpits and speak, but when we descend, by Allah, if one of us were to fall from the sky, that would be dearer to him than to persist in any of that. He said: That was considered hypocrisy in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7777,"I watched the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not cease the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-'Aqabah."],[7778,"I performed the Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I was between the neck of the Prophet's ﷺ she-camel while she was chewing her cud and her saliva was flowing between my shoulders, and I heard him say: Verily, Allah has given every possessor of a right his right; there is no bequest to an heir; the child belongs to the bed, and the fornicator gets the stone."],[7779,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ for more than forty mornings during the expedition of Tabuk reciting in the two rak'ahs before dawn: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, the One.'"],[7780,"Part of the Sunnah is that when a man invites his brother, he should get up with him until he leaves."],[7781,"Ubayy b. Ka'b used to swear by Allah that the Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-seventh, without making an exception. He said: We said to him: How did you know that? He said: By the verse which—"],[7782,"Suwayd b. Ghafalah, Zayd b. Suhan, and a third person were with them on a journey. One of them found a whip and took it. His two companions said to him: Throw it away. He said: I will make use of it; if its owner comes, we will return it to him. That is better than leaving it for wild beasts to eat. Then he met Ubayy b. Ka'b and mentioned that to him, and he said: You were both right and wrong. He said: I found one hundred dinars during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and brought them to him. He said: Announce it for a year. I announced it, but it was not recognized, so I returned to him and he said: Announce it for a year. I announced it for a year, two or three times, but it was not recognized. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Know its number, its container, and its tie, mix it with your wealth, and if its owner comes, give it to him."],[7783,"The neighbor has more right to his property, as long as it is adjacent."],[7784,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted cupping for the fasting person."],[7785,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years. He used to perform ghusl with a sa' of water and wudu with a mudd."],[7786,"I memorized ten prayers from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: two rak'ahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after 'Isha, and two before Fajr."],[7787,"Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his parents or settles a debt on their behalf, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with the righteous."],[7788,"When one of you begins the prayer, let him raise his hands and face their palms toward the qiblah, for Allah is in front of him."],[7789,"When one of you is in the mosque, let him not let anyone hear his voice, and let him point with his finger toward his Lord, Blessed and Exalted."],[7790,"What the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us regarding leasing land was that a man leases out his land on condition that whatever he points to is his; this is what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us."],[7791,"When this verse was revealed, it weighed heavily on the Muslims, and they deemed it grave that twenty should fight two hundred and a hundred should fight a thousand. So Allah lightened it for them and abrogated it with the verse after it: \"Now Allah has lightened [your burden] for you, and He knows that there is weakness in you. So if there are among you one hundred steadfast, they will overcome two hundred; and if there are among you a thousand, they will overcome two thousand by Allah's permission.\""],[7792,"The verse of stoning and the suckling of an adult ten times were revealed, and it was in a sheet under my bed. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, we were distracted by his death, and a domestic animal entered and ate it."],[7793,"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by Musa while he was standing praying in his grave at the red sand dune."],[7794,"Wrap your lower garments as I saw the angels wrap theirs. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how did you see them?\" He said, \"To the middle of their shins.\""],[7795,"It is the right of a Muslim that he should not pass two nights without writing his will, if he has anything to bequeath."],[7796,"The Prophet ﷺ came out with a piece of gold in one hand and a piece of silk in the other, and said, \"These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah and permitted for their females.\""],[7797,"Maintaining family ties increases wealth, creates love among the family, and delays death."],[7798,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by his father while he had his thigh uncovered, and said, \"Cover it, for it is part of the 'awrah.\""],[7799,"I attended a funeral with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he wanted to pray over it, he turned and saw a woman, so he ordered that she be moved away until he did not see her, then he came forward and said four takbirs over it."],[7800,"Ma'iz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I have committed adultery.\" He turned away from him. Then he came to him again and said, \"I have committed adultery.\" He turned away from him, until he came to him four times. Then he ordered that he be stoned. When the stones struck him, he turned and ran. A man met him and struck him with the jawbone of a camel, knocking him down. His flight when the stones touched him was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Why did you not leave him?\""],[7801,"Fasting is a shield, as long as he does not tear it. He said: It was said, \"What tears it?\" He said, \"A lie or backbiting.\""],[7802,"Be upright toward Quraysh as long as they are upright toward you. If they do not, then put your swords on your shoulders and destroy their green [wealth]. If you do not, then be wretched tillers, eating from the labor of your hands."],[7803,"God cursed wine, its drinker, its pourer, its presser, the one who has it pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, the one who consumes its price, and its buyer."],[7804,"He used to cup at this spot on the front of his head, and he called it Umm Mughith."],[7805,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the woman with istihada (abnormal vaginal bleeding). He said: \"She should count the days of her regular periods, then perform ghusl at each time of purity, then use a cloth and pray.\""],[7806,"There were not twenty white hairs in the head and beard of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[7807,"Bilal gave the adhan for the Messenger of God ﷺ in pairs, and gave the iqama likewise."],[7808,"Numbness of the face from nabidh causes good deeds to scatter."],[7809,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent us in an army and appointed Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah over us. Our provisions ran out, so we came to the seashore and found a creature like a sand hill that the sea had cast up. We secured it, ate from it, and took provisions. We mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"It is game that God fed you.\""],[7810,"At his death he said: \"I do not grieve over anything of this world that I missed except three things: fasting in the midday heat, not having stood with my feet spread in prayer—meaning prolonged prayer—and my requesting to be released from the pledge of allegiance.\""],[7811,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to begin the recitation with 'Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds.'"],[7812,"When you see my Ummah fearing the wrongdoer to say to him, 'You are a wrongdoer,' then farewell has been bidden to them."],[7813,"There is no riba except in nasi'ah (deferred payment)."],[7814,"Ibn Umar did not pray before the Eid prayer or after it. He was asked about that, and he said, 'I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray before it or after it.'"],[7815,"I used to soak dates for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then I would take a handful of raisins and throw them into it."],[7816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us the meat of domestic donkeys."],[7817,"The Prophet ﷺ performed wudu three times (for each limb)."],[7818,"The Prophet ﷺ did not abandon four things: fasting Ashura, the ten (days of Dhul-Hijjah), three days of every month, and the two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer."],[7819,"Two camel drivers were with us on the night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept through the prayer until the sun rose."],[7820,"He used to pray four rak'ahs before Zuhr."],[7821,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped and gave the cupper his wage, a dinar."],[7822,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you enter the privy and no trace of filth is seen from you.' He said, 'Did you not know, O A'ishah, that the earth swallows what comes out of the prophets, so nothing of it is seen?'"],[7823,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a woman who had stolen, and he cut off her hand. He said, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, if Fatimah bint Muhammad had stolen, I would cut off her hand.'"],[7824,"He forbade praying in (only) a sirwal (loose trousers)."],[7825,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade us to name (anything) Kalb or Kulayb."],[7826,"I accompanied Ibn Umar from Jamʿ (Muzdalifah) to Mina, and I said: I have vowed to fast on Wednesday, and it coincides with this day, so what do you think? He said: Allah has commanded the fulfillment of vows, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on this day."],[7827,"This community will split into seventy-three sects, all of them in the Fire except one. They said: And which sect is that? He said: \"Those who are upon what I and my Companions are upon today.\""],[7828,"I was aided by the east wind, and ʿAd was destroyed by the west wind."],[7829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a donkey named ʿUfayr."],[7830,"Beware of the insight of the believer, for he sees with the light of Allah. Then he recited: \"Indeed in that are signs for those who discern\" (15:75)."],[7831,"The Prophet ﷺ made me stand on his right side."],[7832,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away between my chest and my throat. She said: \"I thought that Allah would return his soul to him.\" She said: \"And that is how it is done with the prophets.\" He stirred, so I said: \"If you are given the choice today, you will not choose us.\" And it was said: That is what he said to Bilal: \"Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. You women are like the companions of Yusuf.\" So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I only said that because Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, and if he stands in your place he will not be able to pray."],[7833,"Prayer during travel is two rakʿahs; whoever abandons the Sunnah has disbelieved."],[7834,"My husband divorced me with three divorces, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You have no right to housing or maintenance."],[7835,"Do not divorce women except on account of clear misconduct, for Allah does not love men who frequently taste (marriage) nor women who frequently taste (marriage)."],[7836,"I saw ʿAli perform ablution: he washed the face three times, the forearms three times, wiped his head, and washed the feet three times up to the ankles. Then he took the leftover water of his ablution and drank it while standing, and said: \"Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.\""],[7837,"When one of you fights, let him avoid the face, for God created Adam in the image of His face."],[7838,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some children and greeted them."],[7839,"Gifts to rulers are a misappropriation."],[7840,"Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer."],[7841,"When he came out of the privy, he washed his posterior three times."],[7842,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother, when it has hair."],[7843,"The first dispute to be judged on the Day of Resurrection is between two goats: one with horns and one without horns."],[7844,"Charity is not lawful for a wealthy person, nor for one who is strong and able-bodied."],[7845,"O Messenger of God, do you think that if I pray the obligatory prayers, deem lawful what is lawful, deem unlawful what is unlawful, and do not add anything to that, I will enter Paradise? He said: \"Yes.\""],[7846,"A man manumitted six slaves during his illness. The Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them, then freed two and returned four to slavery."],[7847,"The Prophet of God ﷺ sent Umar b. al-Khattab as a collector of zakat. He came to al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib, and al-Abbas was harsh with him. So Umar came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"O Umar, do you not know that a man's paternal uncle is of the same stock as his father? Al-Abbas had paid his zakat to us in advance for this year last year.\""],[7848,"He gave a horse as charity during the time of the Prophet of God ﷺ. Then he saw its owner selling it for a low price, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about that. He said: \"Do not buy back your charity.\""],[7849,"A man manumitted a slave of his upon his death. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered him, and he sold him for eight hundred dirhams."],[7850,"The Prophet ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[7851,"He would wake up in a state of ritual impurity, then complete his fast."],[7852,"A man put up a commodity for sale and swore by God, besides whom there is no deity, that he had been given for it what he had not been given, in order to deceive a Muslim. Then the verse was revealed: 'Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of God and their oaths for a small price...'"],[7853,"Whoever sends ahead three who have not reached the age of sin, they will be a strong fortress for him from the Fire. Abu al-Darda said: \"I sent ahead two.\" He said: \"And two.\" Ubayy b. Kab, the leader of the reciters, said: \"I sent ahead one.\" He said: \"And one, but that is at the first shock.\""],[7854,"Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he was blind. He complained to him and asked him to grant him a concession regarding the evening and dawn prayers, saying: \"Between me and you there are grey-haired men.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do you hear the call to prayer?\" He said: \"Yes, once or twice.\" He did not grant him a concession in that."],[7855,"Ali sent a man to the Messenger of God ﷺ to ask him about pre-seminal fluid, disliking to be the one asking because of Fatimah's position. He said: \"O Messenger of God, a man sees a woman on the road and emits pre-seminal fluid; is a full bath required of him?\" He said: \"That is met by men's virility; ablution is sufficient for you for that.\""],[7856,"He used to come every Thursday and stand, not sitting. He would say: \"Do not kill people, for among them are the elderly, the weak, and the needy.\" Then he would say: \"These are two matters: the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, the truest speech is the Book of God, the worst of affairs are their innovations, and every innovation is misguidance. Indeed, the wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the blessed is he who takes admonition from others. Let not time grow long for you, nor hope distract you, for everything that is coming is near, and only what is not coming is far. Among the worst of people is the idle by day and the corpse by night. Killing a believer is disbelief, and reviling him is sin. It is not lawful for a Muslim to shun his brother for more than three days. Indeed, the worst of mounts are the mounts of lying. Lying is not suitable, whether in seriousness or jest, nor that a man promise his child then not fulfill it. Indeed, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire; truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. The truthful is said of him: he spoke truth and acted righteously; the liar is said of him: he lied and acted wickedly. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A servant keeps telling the truth until he is recorded with God as a truthful one, and he keeps lying until he is recorded with God as a liar. Do you know what slander is? It is he said and it was said; it is talebearing that corrupts between people.\""],[7857,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us the sermon of need, saying: \"Praise be to God. We praise Him and seek His help. We seek refuge in God from the evils of our souls. Whomever God guides, there is none to mislead him, and whomever He misleads, there is none to guide him. I bear witness that there is no deity but God alone with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\""],[7858,"No people ever sat down to remember Allah but that angels surrounded them, tranquility descended upon them, mercy enveloped them, and Allah mentioned them among those with Him.”"],[7859,"Do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three [days], such that when they meet, this one turns away and that one turns away. The one who initiates the greeting of peace will be foremost to Paradise."],[7860,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O ‘Imran.” I said, “At your service.” He said: “Say: O Allah, I seek guidance from You to be directed aright in my affair, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul.”"],[7861,"Mahmud narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Sabbah al-Jarjara’i narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from ‘Abd Allah b. Nafi‘, from his father, from Ibn ‘Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, with the hadith of the cave.” No one narrated this hadith from ‘Abd Allah b. Nafi‘ except Jarir. Muhammad b. al-Sabbah was unique in narrating it."],[7862,"I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr, and ‘Umar, that when they said the takbir they would recite: “Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.”"],[7863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted the Muslims about what would gather them for prayer. They said, “The horn,” but he disliked it because of the Jews. Then they mentioned the bell, but he disliked it because of the Christians. That night, the call was shown to a man from the Ansar called ‘Abd Allah b. Zayd, and to ‘Umar b. al-Khattab. The Ansari went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night, “and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal, and he gave the call to prayer with it.” ‘Umar said, “Indeed, I saw the like of what he saw, but he preceded me.”"],[7864,"Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him will enter Paradise, and whoever meets Him while associating something with Him will enter the Fire."],[7865,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying while carrying the daughter of Abu al-‘As. He would carry her when he stood and put her down when he sat, until he finished his prayer."],[7866,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the shepherds to throw the pebbles at night."],[7867,"A woman lifted up a son of hers in a cloth and said, “O Messenger of Allah, is there a Hajj for this one?” He said, “Yes, and for you is a reward.”"],[7868,"Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah will have the like of his reward, and whoever looks after a warrior’s family with good, or spends on his family, will have the like of his reward."],[7869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate, saying: “O Allah, let me enjoy my hearing and my sight until You make them the inheritor from me, and grant me well-being in my religion, and gather me upon what You have given me life, and support me against those who have wronged me until You show me my revenge from them. O Allah, I have submitted my religion to You, and I have turned my face to You, and I have entrusted my affair to You, and I have leaned my back upon You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your messengers whom You have sent, and in Your Book which You have sent down.”"],[7870,"He would perform Witr with three rak‘ahs, and he would place the qunūt before the rukū‘."],[7871,"He is not from us who does not trim his moustache."],[7872,"Today is the placing of bets, and tomorrow is the race, and the goal is Paradise or the Fire. I am the first, and Abū Bakr is the second, and ‘Umar is the third, and the people after are upon precedence, the first then the first."],[7873,"The Prophet ﷺ was approached by two disputants, and he said: “Judge between them, O ‘Uqbah.” I said: “Should I judge while you are present?” He said: “Judge between them.” I said: “On what basis?” He said: “If you exert yourself and you are correct, then you have two rewards, and if you err, then you have one reward.”"],[7874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and saw a piece of bread thrown away, so he walked to it, wiped it, and said: “O ‘Ā’ishah, be a good neighbor to the favors of Allah, for they rarely depart from a household and then almost return to it.”"],[7875,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped after he had said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7876,"Whoever says when he retires to his bed: “Praise be to Allah who is exalted and thus prevailed, who is hidden and thus knows, and who owns and thus has power. Praise be to Allah who gives life and causes death, and He is over all things competent,” will come out of his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him."],[7877,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying barefoot and wearing sandals. I saw him drinking standing and sitting. I saw him turning away from prayer to his right and to his left. I saw him fasting while traveling and breaking his fast."],[7878,"Islam is ten portions, and he has failed who has no portion: the testimony that there is no deity but Allah, and it is the religion; the second is prayer, and it is the natural disposition; the third is zakāh, and it is the purification; the fourth is fasting, and it is the shield; the fifth is Hajj, and it is the sacred law; the sixth is jihād, and it is the firm handhold; the seventh is enjoining good, and it is faithfulness; the eighth is forbidding evil, and it is the proof; the ninth is the congregation, and it is the affection; and the tenth is obedience, and it is the protection."],[7879,"When the Prophet ﷺ established brotherhood between his Companions, between the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār, and he did not establish brotherhood between ‘Alī b. Abī Ṭālib and anyone among them, ‘Alī went out angry until he came to a small stream of the earth and rested his head upon his forearm, and the wind blew dust upon him. The Prophet ﷺ sought him until he found him, and he nudged him with his foot, and said to him: “Arise, for you are only fit to be Abū Turāb. Are you angry with me because I established brotherhood between the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār and did not establish brotherhood between you and any one of them? Are you not pleased that you are to me in the position of Hārūn to Mūsā, except that there will be no prophet after me? Indeed, whoever loves you will be surrounded by security and faith, and whoever hates you, Allah will cause him to die a death of the pre-Islamic ignorance and will hold him to account for his deeds in Islam.”"],[7880,"Good deeds are multiplied on Friday."],[7881,"Indeed the soul becomes weary, and one of you does not know the extent of the period, so let him look to what worship he is able to bear, then let him persist in it, for the most beloved deeds to Allah are those done persistently, even if they are few."],[7882,"I walked with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to a woman of the Ansar, and she spread for him a palm-leaf mat and slaughtered a sheep for him. While we were thus, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A man from the people of Paradise will surely come to you.' Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq came. Then he said, 'A man from the people of Paradise will surely come to you.' Then Umar b. al-Khattab came. Then he said, 'A man from the people of Paradise will surely come to you. O Allah, if You will, make him Ali.' Then Ali b. Abi Talib came. Then food was brought to us and we ate. Then we arose and prayed Zuhr without performing ablution. Then we returned to the remainder of our food and ate, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not renew ablution, nor did any of us."],[7883,"It is not for a Muslim to humiliate himself. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how does he humiliate himself?' He said, 'He exposes himself to affliction that he cannot bear.'"],[7884,"Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have ordered their killing. So kill from them every jet-black one. And whoever keeps a dog for other than hunting, or crops, or sheep, a qirat of sin like Uhud returns to him every night. And when a dog laps in the vessel of any of you, let him wash it seven times, one of them with dust."],[7885,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[7886,"Allah made the prayer obligatory as two rak'ahs, then He increased it for residence and kept it as it was for travel."],[7887,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in Makkah in the year of the conquest for fifteen [days] shortening the prayer."],[7888,"Whoever prays behind an imam, the imam's recitation is a recitation for him."],[7889,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey during Ramadan, and he broke his fast with ajwa dates."],[7890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pass by boys, greet them, and supplicate for blessings for them."],[7891,"No servant conceals a secret except that Allah clothes him with its garment: if good, then good; and if evil, then evil."],[7892,"He used to take fresh dates with his right hand and watermelon with his left, and he would eat the fresh dates with the watermelon. It was the fruit most beloved to him."],[7893,"Ammar will be killed by the rebellious party. Muawiya said, 'You keep pulling at your urine; did we kill him? It was only those who brought him out [to battle] who killed him.'"],[7894,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ while we were performing ‘umrah. His companions exited ihram, but I had menstruated and did not become pure until I reached Makkah. Then ‘Arafah came and I still had not become pure. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Undo your hair, perform ghusl, then perform Hajj.” Then when it was the night of departure from Mina, he said to ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr: “Take her out of the Haram, then let her perform ‘umrah.”"],[7895,"The polytheists used to say the talbiyah: “Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka illa sharikan huwa laka, tamlikuhu wa ma malak” (Here I am, O God, here I am. Here I am, You have no partner except a partner who is Yours; You own him and what he owns). So God revealed: “Do you have among those whom your right hands possess any partners in what We have provided for you, so that you are equal in it, and you fear them as you fear yourselves?”"],[7896,"The most beloved of deeds to God after the obligatory acts is bringing joy to a Muslim."],[7897,"Whoever fulfills his desires in this world will be barred from his desires in the Hereafter. Whoever casts his eye toward the adornment of the luxurious will be despised in the dominion of this world. Whoever patiently endures severe hardship with beautiful patience, God will settle him in Firdaws wherever He wills."],[7898,"When you are among reeds, muddy ground, or snow, and the prayer time arrives, then gesture by nodding."],[7899,"How excellent is a man’s death in defense of his right."],[7900,"My father abandoned praying with us. I said: “What is wrong with you that you abandoned praying with us?” He said: “You make it too light.” I said: “What about the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: ‘Among you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need’?” He said: “I heard ‘Abdullah b. Mas‘ud say that.” Then he prayed three times longer than what you pray."],[7901,"Three traits are in a hypocrite: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays."],[7902,"I suffered from a pain, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ. He made me stand in his place, and he stood praying, and he threw the edge of his garment over me. Then he said: “You have been cured, O son of Abu Talib; no harm upon you. I have never asked God for anything except that I asked the like of it for you, and I have never asked God for anything except that He gave it to me, except that it was said to me: ‘There is no prophet after you.’”"],[7903,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: “Which earning is purest?” He said: “A man’s work with his own hand, and every righteous sale.”"],[7904,"It is disbelief for a man to claim a lineage he does not know, or to deny it, even if it is insignificant."],[7905,"God will shade in the shade of His Throne on the Day of Resurrection the one who grants respite to a debtor in difficulty, or helps a clumsy person."],[7906,"He used to shorten the prayer at al-‘Aqīq."],[7907,"Two men went out on a journey, and the time for prayer came upon them while they had no water with them, so they performed tayammum with clean earth and prayed. Then they found water afterwards within the time. One of them repeated the prayer and the other did not. Then they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said to the one who did not repeat: “You have followed the Sunnah, and your prayer is sufficient for you.” And he said to the one who performed wudu and repeated: “You have the reward twice.”"],[7908,"Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq did not sit in the seat of the Messenger of God ﷺ on the pulpit until he met God. And ‘Umar did not sit in the seat of Abū Bakr until he met God. And ‘Uthmān did not sit in the seat of ‘Umar until he met God."],[7909,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of snakes during iḥrām and within the Ḥaram."],[7910,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be called out: “Where are the sons of sixty?”—and it is the lifespan about which God Almighty said: “Did We not give you life long enough for whoever would remember to take heed? And the warner came to you.”"],[7911,"Whoever sees from his brother a fault in his religion and conceals it for him, he will have a good deed on the Day of Resurrection."],[7912,"Whatever is irrigated by rainfall or by natural springs, then one-tenth is due on every ten."],[7913,"When the Prophet ﷺ gave his wives the choice, the one who chose herself was a woman from Banū Hilāl."],[7914,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to travel a distance of three nights except with a maḥram of hers."],[7915,"When the Prophet ﷺ performed the pilgrimage with his wives, he said: “It is only this one; then upon you is to ride on the backs of the ḥuṣur (saddle cushions).”"],[7916,"The angels do not accompany a group that has a bell in it."],[7917,"Whatever is cut from a live animal, that which is cut from its flesh—no one should eat it."],[7918,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he found in it three hundred and sixty idols. He pointed with his staff to every idol and said: 'Truth has come, and falsehood has vanished. Indeed falsehood is ever bound to vanish.' The idol would fall without him touching it."],[7919,"Every intoxicant is unlawful, and every intoxicant is khamr."],[7920,"The truce between the Prophet and the people of Makkah was at al-Hudaybiyah for four years."],[7921,"The Prophet ﷺ raced horses and made a prize between them, and he placed in it a horse covered with a saddlecloth, and said: 'No prize except in a hoof or an arrowhead.'"],[7922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set aside as a protected pasturage: 'al-Naqi' for the horses of the Muslims.'"],[7923,"Whoever is invited to a wedding feast and does not attend it has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."],[7924,"A woman was found killed in one of the Prophet's ﷺ military expeditions, and the Prophet ﷺ disapproved of that and forbade killing women and children."],[7925,"The Prophet ﷺ was told while he was at al-Mu'arras, meaning Mu'arras al-Shajarah: 'You are in a blessed valley.'"],[7926,"He forbade selling or giving away wala'."],[7927,"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his ihram when he entered ihram, and for his exiting ihram before he performed tawaf al-ifadah, with the best perfume I found."],[7928,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every khamr is unlawful; its small amount and large amount are equal."],[7929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined cupping and said: 'Nothing people take is better than it, or a drink of honey.'"],[7930,"When one of you performs ablution, let him rinse his mouth three times, for sins come out from his face, and let him wash his hands, and wipe his head three times, then insert his hands into his ears, then pour water over his feet three times."],[7931,"The two men of the Ansar whose houses were farthest from the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were Abu Lubabah b. Abd al-Mundhir, whose family was in Quba, and Abu Abs b. Jubayr, whose dwelling was among the Banu Harithah. They would pray the afternoon prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then come to their people, and they had not prayed it because of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hastening the afternoon prayer."],[7932,"I came with twelve riders until we alighted with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My companions said: 'Who will tend our camels while we go and learn from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Then when he returns, we will convey to him what we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I said: 'I will.' Then I said to myself: 'Perhaps I am being cheated; my companions will hear what I do not hear from the Prophet of Allah ﷺ.' So one day I attended and heard a man say: 'The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs a complete ablution, then stands for his prayer, his sins are as on the day his mother gave birth to him.\"' I was amazed at that. Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'How would it be if you heard the other statement? You would be even more amazed.' I said: 'Tell me, may Allah make me your ransom.' Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah the Exalted, the gates of Paradise are opened for him; he may enter from whichever he wishes, and it has eight gates.\"' Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ came out to us, and I sat facing him, but he turned his face away from me. I got up and faced him, and he did that three times. When it was the fourth time, I said: 'O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, why do you turn your face away from me?' He turned to me and said: 'Is one dearer to you or twelve?' twice or thrice. When I saw that, I returned to my companions."],[7933,"A group of my nation will remain standing upon Allah's command; those who oppose them will not harm them. They will fight their enemies. Whenever a war ends, a war of another people breaks out. Allah will raise a people and provide for them from it until the Hour comes to them.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They are the people of Sham."],[7934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would place the vessel for her and she would drink, then he would perform ablution with the leftover of her water."],[7935,"He used to serve the Prophet ﷺ, and when he finished his service, he would come to the mosque and lie down in it."],[7936,"We entered upon Yazid b. al-Aswad to visit him, and Wathilah b. al-Asqa entered upon him. When he saw him, he extended his hand, took his hand, and wiped it over his face and chest, because he had pledged allegiance with it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to him: 'O Yazid, what is your expectation of your Lord?' He said: 'Good.' He said: 'Then rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Allah the Exalted says: I am as My servant thinks of Me. If good, then good; and if evil, then evil.\"'"],[7937,"Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I give you the drink of a special group or the drink of the general public?' He said: 'Rather the drink of the general public.'"],[7938,"May Allah brighten [the face of] a servant who hears this speech of mine and does not add to it. For many a carrier of a word conveys it to one who is more receptive than he. Three things about which the heart of a believer does not harbor treachery: sincerity of action for Allah, sincere counsel to those in authority, and holding fast to the community of Muslims, for their supplication surrounds those behind them."],[7939,"Verily, asceticism in this world is not by prohibiting the lawful, nor by wasting wealth. But asceticism in this world is that you not be more confident in what is in your hands than in what is in Allah's hands, and that you be more desirous of the reward of the calamity when it befalls you than of it if it had remained with you."],[7940,"On the Day of Resurrection will be brought the one deprived of intellect, the one who died in the interval [between prophets], and the one who died as a child. The one deprived of intellect will say: 'O Lord, if You had given me intellect, no one whom You gave intellect would have been happier with his intellect than me.' The one who died in the interval will say: 'O Lord, if a covenant from You had come to me, no one to whom a covenant from You came would have been happier with his covenant than me.' The one who died as a child will say: 'If You had given me a lifetime, no one whom You gave a lifetime would have been happier with his lifetime than me.' The Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will say: 'I command you with a command; will you obey Me?' They will say: 'Yes, by Your might.' He will say: 'Go and enter the Fire, and if they entered it, it would not harm them.' He said: 'Then flames will burst upon them, and they will think that they have destroyed everything Allah has created, so they will return quickly.' He said: 'They will say: \"We came out, O Lord, by Your might, wanting to enter it, but flames burst upon us and we thought they had destroyed everything Allah has created.\" Then He will command them a second time, and they will return likewise, saying the same as their previous words. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: \"Before I created you, I knew what you would do, and upon My knowledge I created you, and to My knowledge you will return.\" Then the Fire will seize them."],[7941,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed which, if I do it, I will enter Paradise.' He said: 'Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are punished and burned. Obey your parents, even if they turn you out of your wealth and all that is yours. Do not deliberately abandon prayer, for whoever deliberately abandons prayer, Allah's protection is free from him. Do not drink wine, for it is the key to every evil. Do not contend with the people of authority over their affair, even if you think it is yours. Spend from your surplus on your family, and do not lift your staff from them; keep them in awe of Allah.'"],[7942,"Whomever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in religion."],[7943,"The last food the Prophet ﷺ ate was food containing onions."],[7944,"I do not care what I have done or what I have committed if I drink an antidote, or hang an amulet, or utter poetry from myself."],[7945,"If a leader seeks faults in his subjects, he corrupts them."],[7946,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[7947,"Three things I heard from Allah's Messenger ﷺ about Banu Tamim, after which I shall never dislike Banu Tamim: 'A'ishah vowed to free a freedman from the descendants of Isma'il, so captives from Banu al-'Anbar were brought. Allah's Messenger ﷺ said to her: 'If you wish to free from the descendants of Isma'il, then free from these.' Thus Allah's Messenger ﷺ made them from the descendants of Isma'il. Then some camels from Sa'd's zakat camels were brought, and when their beauty amazed him, he said: 'This is the charity of my people.' Thus Allah's Messenger ﷺ called them his people. And he said: 'They are the fiercest of people in fighting during the great battles.'"],[7948,"People are like a hundred camels; you can hardly find one riding camel among them."],[7949,"People are like a hundred camels; no riding camel is found among them."],[7950,"We came to Madinah while the Prophet ﷺ was there, and I had camels with me. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, command the people of the lowlands to treat me well and to help me.' He said: 'So they stood with me.' When I sold my camels, I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to me: 'Come near.' Then he wiped over my forelock and prayed for me three times."],[7951,"The delegation of Allah's Messenger ﷺ passed by Umm Zubayb and took her carpet. Zubayb caught up with the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, the delegation took my mother's carpet.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Return his mother's carpet to him.' Then he took from the one who had taken his mother's carpet a sa' of barley, his sword, and his belt. Then the Prophet ﷺ raised his hand and wiped Zubayb's head with it, then said: 'May Allah bless you, O boy, and may Allah bless your mother through you.'"],[7952,"She said: O Prophet of God, I want to free a slave from the children of Ishmael, deliberately. The Prophet of God ﷺ said to her: Wait until the caravan of al-'Anbar comes tomorrow. The caravan of al-'Anbar came, and the Prophet of God ﷺ said to her: \"Take from them four boys, bright-faced, handsome, whose heads are not to be hidden.\" 'Ata' b. Khalid said: My grandmother took Rudayh, and she took the son of my paternal uncle Samura, and she took the son of my paternal cousin Rukhayy, and she took my maternal uncle Zubayb. Then the Prophet ﷺ raised his hand, wiped their heads with it, and blessed them. Then he said: \"These, O 'A'ishah, are from the children of Ishmael, deliberately.\""],[7953,"My maternal uncle Jadd b. Qays invited me among seventy riders, those who had taken the pledge to the Prophet ﷺ from the Ansar. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us with his uncle al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib and said: O uncle, receive the pledge from your maternal relatives. The seventy said to him: O Muhammad, ask your Lord for yourself whatever you wish. He said: \"As for what I ask for my Lord, it is that you worship Him and associate nothing with Him; and as for what I ask of you for myself, it is that you protect me from what you protect yourselves from.\" They said: What is for us if we do that? He said: \"Paradise.\""],[7954,"The banner of the Messenger of God ﷺ was black."],[7955,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gathered his parents for me on the day of Uhud."],[7956,"If people were given whatever they claimed, men would claim the wealth and blood of other people."],[7957,"No one has the right to prevent his neighbor from placing a piece of wood on his wall."],[7958,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to inspect the eye and the ear (of sacrificial animals)."],[7959,"Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."],[7960,"Indeed, God has granted you an additional prayer that is better for you than red camels: the Witr. It is for you between the 'Isha' prayer and the rising of dawn."],[7961,"While I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man from the Ansar came to him and said: O Messenger of God, is there anything left of dutifulness to my parents after their death with which I may be dutiful to them? He said: Yes, four traits: praying for them, seeking forgiveness for them, fulfilling their promises after their death, honoring their friends, and maintaining the ties of kinship that you have only through them."],[7962,"I reached the elderly women while they were praying the obligatory prayers with the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[7963,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said when he sent me to Thaqif: \"Keep the prayer short, O 'Uthman, and lead the people in prayer according to the weakest of them, for among them are the weak, the one with a need, the pregnant, and the nursing. Indeed, I hear the crying of a child and I shorten it.\""],[7964,"The believer is not one whose neighbor is not safe from his harms."],[7965,"The Prophet ﷺ never slept a night nor woke up but that he used the siwak."],[7966,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married off Fatimah, he said: O Ali, do not enter upon your wife until you give her something. He said: I have nothing, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Give her your shield, the Hutamiyyah."],[7967,"The one who forbids the lawful is like the one who permits the unlawful."],[7968,"The prayer time arrived while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when a wooden bowl of water was brought, so we performed ablution from it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it with his hand, then placed his palm over its mouth, then said: Tip over the ablution water. So we performed ablution from it, and water flowed out upon us from the bowl from between his fingers until we finished. I said to him: How many were the people, O Abu Hamzah? He said: Two hundred men. And Humayd al-Tawil also narrated to me, he said: They were eighty men."],[7969,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we sell it? He said: Indeed the One who forbade drinking it has forbidden its price. Pour it out."],[7970,"I will not take the beloved of My servant and then accept for him any reward other than Paradise."],[7971,"He used to recite on Friday at dawn: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil and Hal Ata."],[7972,"When we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a tree separated us, then when we met, some of us would greet others."],[7973,"The support of my nation is through its wicked ones."],[7974,"If I were invited to a trotter, I would answer."],[7975,"Whoever hears 'Hayya 'ala al-falah' and does not respond, has abandoned the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ."],[7976,"that the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed five prayers at Mina: the noon prayer, the afternoon prayer, the sunset prayer, the last evening prayer, and the dawn prayer."],[7977,"he used to pray two rak'ahs after the Friday prayer."],[7978,"May God fight so-and-so! He sells wine, though he heard the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'God cursed the Jews. Fat was forbidden to them, but they sold it.'"],[7979,"The Messenger of God ﷺ combined the noon and afternoon prayers, and the sunset and evening prayers, delaying the sunset prayer and hastening the evening prayer, and prayed them together."],[7980,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would see semen on his garment, then scrape it off and pray in it."],[7981,"al-Mundhir b. Sawa came as a delegate from al-Bahrayn until he reached the city of the Messenger ﷺ, and with al-Mundhir were some people, while I was a young boy who did not understand, holding their camels. He said: They went with their weapons and greeted the Messenger of God ﷺ. Al-Mundhir put down his weapon, put on clothes that he had with him, and wiped his beard with oil. Then he came to the Prophet of God ﷺ and greeted him, while I was with the camels looking at the Prophet of God ﷺ. Al-Mundhir said: The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'I saw in you what I did not see in your companions.' I said: 'And what did you see in me, O Prophet of God?' He said: 'You put down your weapon, put on your clothes, and applied oil.' I said: 'O Prophet of God, is it something I was created with or something I have introduced?' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'No, rather it is something you were created with.' Then they greeted the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to them: 'Abd al-Qays accepted Islam willingly, and people accepted Islam unwillingly. May God bless Abd al-Qays and the clients of Abd al-Qays.' My father said to me: I looked at the Prophet of God ﷺ just as I am looking at you, but I did not understand. He said: And my father died at the age of one hundred and twenty years."],[7982,"A man came to Ibn 'Umar and asked him, so he threw his turban to him. Some of the people said: 'If you had given him a dirham it would have sufficed.' Ibn 'Umar said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'It is part of righteousness for a man to maintain the ties of friendship of his father,' and this was a friend of 'Umar."],[7983,"Whoever follows a funeral until the prayer is offered over it will have a qirat of reward, and whoever walks with a funeral until it is buried will have two qirats of reward, and the qirat is like Mount Uhud."],[7984,"He forbade selling the offspring of the offspring of a pregnant camel."],[7985,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a robe with silk trim on its collar, and he said: 'A collar of fire on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[7986,"The Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon when a man entered stepping over people's necks. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'One of you comes late, then steps over people's necks and harms them.' The man said: 'I did nothing more than hear the call and perform ablution.' He said: 'Is this a day of ablution?'"],[7987,"Quraysh said to the Jews: 'Give us something to ask this man about.' They said: 'Ask him about the spirit.' So they asked him, and it was revealed: 'And they ask you about the spirit. Say: The spirit is from the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little.' They said: 'We have been given abundant knowledge.' Then it was revealed: 'Say: If the sea were ink for the words of my Lord...' the verse."],[7988,"The Prophet ﷺ faced the east and said, \"From here the horn of Satan rises, and here are trials and earthquakes, and the boasters, and hard-heartedness.\""],[7989,"None of you will enter Paradise by his deeds, nor be saved from the Fire.\" They said, \"Not even you, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Not even I, unless God envelops me with His mercy.\""],[7990,"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me."],[7991,"A stomach ailment and drowning are martyrdom."],[7992,"When you come to Friday prayer, perform the purificatory bath."],[7993,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a land called ʿAdhira (Dung) and named it Khadira (Green)."],[7994,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ in the year of the conquest and found him branding the camels he had acquired."],[7995,"Two qualities never combine in a hypocrite: good demeanor and understanding in religion."],[7996,"Whoever kills a covenanted person without just cause will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its fragrance is found at a distance of a hundred years."],[7997,"A gift was given to ʿAʾishah and Ḥafṣah while they were fasting, and they ate from it. They mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Make up a day in its place, and do not do it again.\""],[7998,"Whoever draws his sword and then puts it down, his blood is forfeit."],[7999,"No one swears a false oath at the pulpit but that he takes his seat in the Fire."],[8000,"I mentioned Qays in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: May Allah have mercy on Qays, may Allah have mercy on Qays. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you invoke mercy upon Qays? He said: Yes, for he was upon the religion of our father Isma'il b. Ibrahim, the friend of Allah. O Qays, greet Yaman; O Yaman, greet Qays. Indeed Qays are the horsemen of Allah on earth. By the One in whose hand is my soul, there will come upon people a time when this religion will have no helper other than Qays. Indeed Allah has horsemen from the people of heaven who are marked, and horsemen from the people of earth who are known. The horsemen of Allah from the people of earth are Qays. Qays is but an egg that split open from us, the People of the House. Indeed Qays are the harm of Allah—meaning the lions of Allah."],[8001,"Some people among the Arabs said: O Messenger of Allah, we have submitted but we have not fought you, while the Banu so-and-so fought you. So Allah revealed: They consider it a favor to you that they have submitted. Say: Do not consider your submission a favor to me—the verse."],[8002,"That he divorced his wife during her menstrual period, and that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he commanded him to take her back and not have intercourse with her until she becomes pure. Then when she becomes pure, if he wishes he may divorce her, and if he wishes he may keep her."],[8003,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[8004,"Do not supplicate for death, nor wish for it. Whoever is going to supplicate, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die when death is good for me."],[8005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking and eating from vessels of gold and silver."],[8006,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate: O Ever-Living, O Self-Subsisting."],[8007,"Whoever wears silk or drinks from silver is not of us, and whoever corrupts a woman against her husband or a slave against his masters is not of us."],[8008,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ obtained spoils, he would command Bilal, who would call out to the people three times so that the people would bring their spoils, and then we would take one-fifth and divide it. Then a man came to him after that with a rope of hair, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is from what we had taken as spoils. He said: Did you not hear Bilal call out three times? The man said: Yes. He said: What prevented you from bringing it? The man apologized to him, and he said: You will bring it on the Day of Resurrection, and I will never accept it from you."],[8009,"None of you should say: I have cultivated (zara'tu), but let him say: I have tilled (harathtu)."],[8010,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out before the sun declined, he would delay the noon prayer until the time of the afternoon prayer, then he would dismount and combine them. If the sun declined before he set out, he would pray the noon prayer and then mount."],[8011,"Cool down with the prayer in intense heat, for intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell—or he said: from the opening of the gates of Hell."],[8012,"The color most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was green."],[8013,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulating the House on his she-camel, touching the Black Stone with his staff."],[8014,"A man came to Umar and said, 'I have divorced my wife irrevocably while she was menstruating.' Umar said, 'You have disobeyed your Lord and separated from your wife.' The man said, 'But did not the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command Ibn Umar, when he separated from his wife, to take her back?' Umar said to him, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to take her back because he still had a divorce remaining, but you have nothing left with which to take your wife back.'"],[8015,"Do not make your houses into graves, and do not make my grave into a place of festivity. Send blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me wherever you are."],[8016,"He used to accept gifts and give something in return for them."],[8017,"Allah loves that His concessions be taken, just as He loves that His obligatory duties be fulfilled."],[8018,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[8019,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a gold ring on a man's hand, so he struck his finger with a stick he had until he threw it away."],[8020,"The Jews said, 'If a man has intercourse with his wife from behind, his child will be born cross-eyed.' Then the verse was revealed: 'Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish'—whether from behind or otherwise, as long as it is in the same orifice."],[8021,"He used to pray on the khumrah (a small mat)."],[8022,"He forbade a man to place one of his legs over the other while reclining."],[8023,"Whoever equips a warrior for battle has the like of his reward, and whoever looks after a warrior's family in his absence has the like of his reward."],[8024,"I said: O Messenger of God, who are your wives in Paradise? He said: You are among them. It seemed to me that he had not married a virgin other than me."],[8025,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in Madinah saying: O God, place in it twice the blessing that is in Makkah."],[8026,"I said: O Messenger of God, we love a people whose deeds we do not attain. He said: You will be with those you love. The people said: And we are like that, O Messenger of God? He said: You are like that."],[8027,"The place of a whip in Paradise is better than what is between heaven and earth."],[8028,"Kisra will perish, and there will be no Kisra after him, for he says: I am the king of kings. Caesar will perish, and there will be no Caesar after him, for he says: I am the king of kings."],[8029,"Jesus will descend and break the cross and kill the pig."],[8030,"Whoever fears God will enter Paradise, enjoying bliss therein without misery, living without dying, his clothes not wearing out and his youth not fading."],[8031,"The Sunnah is that a man perform ghusl when entering ihram and when entering Makkah."],[8032,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: O 'Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it upon request, you will be left to it, and if you are given it without request, you will be helped in it. And if you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath."],[8033,"With the boy is his 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him. Charity to the poor is charity, and your charity to your relative is two charities."],[8034,"He said regarding recitation behind the imam: Listen to the recitation as you have been commanded, and the imam will suffice you for that."],[8035,"The drinking cup of the Prophet ﷺ cracked, and he put a silver chain in place of the crack."],[8036,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked questions and found fault with them, but when Abu Razin asked him, he liked that and answered him."],[8037,"He prohibited the earnings of a slave woman unless she had a known, fixed trade."],[8038,"Do not exploit a slave woman unless she is skilled with her hands."],[8039,"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and among what he took upon us was: that we dye with a deep dye, comb with honey, and not leave our hands devoid of dye."],[8040,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us, if one of us is able, to wear two silver bracelets on her hands; if she is not able, then to tie her hands even with a leather strap. And he said: Do not resemble men."],[8041,"Do not wish to meet the enemy; you do not know what may happen in that."],[8042,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said: You will see your Lord plainly as you see this moon, and you will not be harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome and miss a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so. Then he recited: And glorify with praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting."],[8043,"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good."],[8044,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the reward of guarding the frontier, and he said: Whoever stands guard one night behind the Muslims has the like of the reward of those behind him who fast and pray."],[8045,"Give charity, for charity is your ransom from the Fire."],[8046,"Sa'd came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died without making a will. Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes, and you should give water."],[8047,"No prophet ever had a wet dream; wet dreams are from Satan."],[8048,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded fasting on Ashura."],[8049,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[8050,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed while she was lying crosswise in front of him."],[8051,"In every prayer there is recitation, even if only the Opening of the Book. What the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited aloud to us, we recite aloud, and what he recited quietly, we recite quietly.\""],[8052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade breaking the coinage of the Muslims that is current among them, except for a valid reason.\""],[8053,"Whoever recites the Verse of the Throne after every prescribed prayer, nothing prevents him from entering Paradise except that he dies."],[8054,"Whoever is killed,\" or he said: \"Whoever dies defending his property is a martyr."],[8055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed Abdullah b. Khatal on the day of the conquest,\" they brought him out from under the curtains of the Kaaba, and he struck his neck between Zamzam and the Maqam. He said: \"No Qurayshi will be killed by execution after this."],[8056,"When he observed i'tikaf, his bed and his cot were placed for him at the pillar of repentance on the side facing the qiblah, then he would lean against it."],[8057,"There is no woman whose husband asks her for something and she refuses, so he spends the night angry with her, except that the angels curse her until morning.\""],[8058,"The molar of the disbeliever in the Fire, or the canine tooth of the disbeliever, is like Mount Uhud, and the thickness of his skin is a distance of three days' journey."],[8059,"Pray in the sheepfolds, but do not pray in the camel resting places.\""],[8060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fruit until its ripeness appears."],[8061,"Umar said to the six: 'They are those from whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed this world while he was pleased with them.' He said: 'Swear allegiance to the one to whom 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf pledges allegiance. If you pledge allegiance to the one to whom 'Abd al-Rahman pledges allegiance, then whoever refuses, strike his neck.'"],[8062,"Umar entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while a man was massaging his back. Umar asked him, and he said: 'The she-camel exhausted me last night.'"],[8063,"The Prophet ﷺ performed a single tawaf for both his Hajj and his Umrah."],[8064,"No one remained with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud except four, one of whom was 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud."],[8065,"There is no prayer for the one who has no ablution, and no ablution for the one who does not mention the name of Allah over it."],[8066,"On Friday there is an hour in which no sincere servant praying to Allah happens to be except that He answers him."],[8067,"She saw the Prophet ﷺ at the Jamrah saying: 'Do not kill one another, and throw pebbles like the small stones of khazf.'"],[8068,"A whole nation entered Paradise, with its leaders and followers, for they did not practice ruqya, nor cauterize, and upon their Lord they relied."],[8069,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man who performs ghusl from janabah but the water misses some part of his body. He said: 'Let him wash that place and then pray.'"],[8070,"Whoever conceals the private shame of his brother, it is as if he has brought a buried infant girl back to life."],[8071,"Do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it, but if you are given it because of asking, you will be left to it. And if you swear an oath and then see something better than it, then do that which is better and expiate for your oath."],[8072,"He forbade the sale of uncertainty (gharar)."],[8073,"We used to perform the Friday prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then return and take a midday nap (qaylulah)."],[8074,"Whoever looks into a people's house without their permission, it becomes lawful for them to gouge out his eye."],[8075,"I used to pour the water for the Messenger of God's ﷺ ablution while I was menstruating."],[8076,"God permitted three types of women: marriage with inheritance, marriage without inheritance, and possession by the right hand."],[8077,"A fire will be sent upon the people of the east and will drive them to the west. It will spend the night with them wherever they spend the night, and take the midday nap with them wherever they take the midday nap. It will consume whoever falls behind or lags, driving them like the driving of a broken-down camel."],[8078,"When three people go on a journey, let them appoint one of them as their leader (amir)."],[8079,"When there are three people on a journey, let them appoint one of them as their leader (amir)."],[8080,"I was in the vicinity of Makkah when a man came and greeted me while I was among my sheep. I said, 'Who are you?' He said, 'I am the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ.' I said, 'Welcome to the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ! What do you want?' He said, 'I want the zakat of your sheep.' So I brought him a ewe that had just given birth. When he saw it, he said, 'Our right is not in this one.' I said, 'Then in what is your right?' He said, 'In the thaniyyah (a sheep in its third year) and the jadha'ah (a sheep in its second year) and the lahyah (one with a beard-like mark).'"],[8081,"The woman is 'awrah (that which must be covered); when she leaves her house, Satan seeks to tempt her, and the closest she is to God is in the innermost part of her house."],[8082,"Seek sustenance in the hidden treasures of the earth."],[8083,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ in the house of Umm Salamah praying in a single garment wrapped around himself."],[8084,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[8085,"I was holding the halter of the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ she-camel, leading him, and ʿAmmār was driving it, or ʿAmmār was leading him and I was driving it, when twelve men with covered faces met us. He said, “These are the hypocrites until the Day of Resurrection.” We said, “O Messenger of Allah, will you not send for each man among them and kill him?” He said, “I dislike that people should say that Muhammad kills his companions; and perhaps Allah will suffice us against them with the dubaylah.” We said, “What is the dubaylah?” He said, “A flame of fire that is placed on the vein of the heart of one of them and kills him.”"],[8086,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled concerning the fetus with a ghurrah: a male slave, a female slave, a horse, or a mule. The one against whom the ruling was made said, “Should I pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out at birth? Such a one should be disregarded.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “This man speaks with the speech of a poet. In it is a ghurrah: a male slave or a female slave or a horse or a mule.”"],[8087,"A people complained to the Prophet ﷺ about walking, so he said, “You should use the nasalān (a brisk pace).” He said, “So we did nasalān and found it lighter.”"],[8088,"He used to soak dates separately and unripe dates separately, and he would say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Soak each of them separately.”"],[8089,"He was asked about coitus interruptus, and he said, “Not from every fluid is a child born. If Allah intends to create something, nothing can prevent it.”"],[8090,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks, and prayed, and he placed me on his right side."],[8091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and spat into his garment, then rubbed it."],[8092,"It was made obligatory upon them that one should fight ten, and that became heavy and hard for them, so it was reduced for them to a man fighting two. Then Allah sent down concerning that: “If there are among you twenty patient, they will overcome two hundred” to the end of the verses. Then He said: “Were it not for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took,” meaning: Were it not that I do not punish those who disobey Me until I have given them prior warning. Then He said: “O Prophet, say to those in your hands among the captives” – the verse. Al-ʿAbbās said, “It was revealed concerning me, by Allah, when I informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of my Islam and asked him to account me for the twenty ūqiyyahs that I had taken with me, and he gave me in return twenty slaves, each of them trading with my wealth in his hand, along with what I hope from the forgiveness of Allah, may His mention be exalted.”"],[8093,"If my ummah does not steal from the spoils, no enemy will ever prevail over them."],[8094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Qarn as the miqat for the people of Iraq."],[8095,"I asked Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, “Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say about this verse: ‘Perhaps those who disbelieve will wish that they had been Muslims’?” He said, “Yes, I heard him say: Allah will bring out people from the believers from the Fire after He has taken His vengeance from them. He said: When Allah admitted them into the Fire with the polytheists, the polytheists said to them, ‘You claimed that you were the allies of Allah in this world, so what is the matter with you that you are with us in the Fire?’ When Allah heard that from them, He permitted intercession for them. The angels and the prophets intercede, and the believers intercede until they come out by Allah’s permission. When the polytheists see that, they say, ‘Would that we were like them and intercession would reach us and we would come out with them.’” He said, “That is the saying of Allah: ‘Perhaps those who disbelieve will wish that they had been Muslims.’ They will be called in Paradise the Jahannamīs because of blackness in their faces. They will say, ‘Our Lord, remove this name from us.’ Then He will command them, and they will bathe in a river of Paradise, and that name will be removed from them.”"],[8096,"O Abu Bakr, suppose you found a man with Umm Ruman—what would you do? He said: I would do him harm. Then he said: O Umar, suppose you found a man—what would you do? He said: By Allah, I would kill him. He said: And you, Suhayl b. Bayda'? He said: May Allah curse the farthest one, for he is wicked; and may Allah curse the farthest woman, for she is wicked; and may Allah curse the first of the three—he mentioned it. He said: O Ibn Bayda', you have interpreted the Quran: 'And those who accuse their wives...' to the end of the verse."],[8097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold and silk."],[8098,"A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he stood up. It was said: It is the funeral of a Jew. He said: We stood only for the angels."],[8099,"In Paradise there is a palace of pearl, with no crack in it and no weakness; Allah has prepared it for His friend Ibrahim ﷺ as a gift."],[8100,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform witr with 'Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High', 'Say: O disbelievers', and 'Say: He is Allah, the One'. When he gave the greeting, he would say: 'Glory be to the King, the Holy' three times, raising his voice on the third, and he would say: 'Lord of the angels and the Spirit'."],[8101,"The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was six years old, and consummated the marriage with her when she was nine."],[8102,"While I was praying one night, I saw what looked like lamps—a light descending from the sky. When I saw that, I fell down in prostration. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Why did you not go on, O Abu 'Atik? He said: I could not do anything but fall down in prostration when I saw it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If you had gone on, you would have seen wonders. Those were the angels descending for the Quran."],[8103,"The Prophet ﷺ kissed while fasting."],[8104,"There will be four tribulations: a tribulation in which blood is deemed lawful; the second in which blood and wealth are deemed lawful; the third in which blood, wealth, and private parts are deemed lawful."],[8105,"When the Prophet ﷺ passed away, his companions sat around him grieving and weeping. A tall, handsome, eloquent man came, wearing a waist-wrapper and a cloak, with hair on his shoulders and chest. He stepped over the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he grasped the doorposts, and he wept over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a while. Then he said: In Allah there is consolation for every affliction, a successor for every loss, and a substitute for everything missed. So to Allah turn in repentance, and to Him direct your desire, for the truly afflicted is the one whom reward does not restore. The people said: Do you recognize the man? They looked right and left but saw no one. Abu Bakr said: This is al-Khidr, the brother of the Prophet ﷺ."],[8106,"There will be a man from Banu Umayyah in Egypt who will assume authority, then he will be overcome in his authority or it will be taken from him, then he will flee to the Romans, and the Romans will come against the people of Islam; that is the first of the great battles."],[8107,"No fruit may be sold until its ripeness appears, and that is when the red or yellow color becomes evident."],[8108,"A man said: O Messenger of God, which prayer is most excellent? He said: \"Length of standing in supplication.\" He said: Which charity is most excellent? He said: \"The effort of one with little.\" He said: Which believers are most complete in faith? He said: \"The best of them in character.\""],[8109,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the tashahhud after raising his head from the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[8110,"Whoever prays one rak'ah of the dawn prayer before the sun rises, and one rak'ah when it has risen, has caught the prayer. And whoever catches two rak'ahs of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets, and two rak'ahs after it has set, has caught it."],[8111,"He used to say the takbir at every lowering and raising."],[8112,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to the door of Ali for forty mornings after he had entered upon Fatimah, and said: Peace be upon you, O people of the house, and the mercy of God and His blessings. The prayer, may God have mercy on you. God only desires to remove impurity from you, O people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly."],[8113,"An eye will flow from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, saying: I have been assigned three: every arrogant tyrant, and whoever sets up another god with God, and whoever kills a soul without a soul."],[8114,"The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam; in it is food that nourishes and healing from sickness. The worst water on the earth is the water in the valley of Barhut in a dome in Hadramawt, upon which are like the legs of locusts of venomous creatures. In the morning it flows abundantly, and in the evening it has no moisture."],[8115,"When I take the two precious ones of a servant, and he is patient and seeks reward, his recompense will be nothing but Paradise."],[8116,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ascended the pulpit. When he placed his foot on a step, he said: \"Amin.\" Then he ascended and said: \"Amin.\" Then he ascended and said: \"Amin.\" He said: Gabriel came to me and said: Whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and dies without being forgiven, may God distance him. I said: Amin. He said: And whoever reaches his parents or one of them and dies without being forgiven, may God distance him. I said: Amin. He said: And whoever I am mentioned in his presence and he does not invoke blessings upon me, may God distance him. I said: Amin."],[8117,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey. The time of sacrifice came, and we slaughtered a camel for every ten people."],[8118,"While I was in Egypt, the doorkeeper came and said: A bedouin on a camel is at the door seeking permission. I said: Who are you? He said: Jabir b. Abdullah al-Ansari. I looked over at him and said: Should I come down to you or will you come up? He said: I will not come down and I will not come up. A hadith has reached me that you narrate from the Prophet ﷺ about covering the faults of a believer. I have come to hear it. I said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: Whoever covers the faults of a believer, it is as if he has revived a buried infant girl. Then he struck his camel and returned."],[8119,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs after the witr while seated."],[8120,"I asked Anas b. Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye (his hair)? He said: \"He did not reach the point of dyeing; there were white hairs in his beard.\" I said: Did Abu Bakr dye (his hair)? He said: \"Yes, with henna and katam.\""],[8121,"He used to appoint Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over Madinah, leading the people in prayer."],[8122,"Hasten to do good deeds before six things: the Dajjal, the smoke, the beast of the earth, the rising of the sun from its west, the matter of the general public, and the private affair of any one of you."],[8123,"When a man becomes drowsy while praying, he should leave, for perhaps he is supplicating in his prayer and invokes against himself without realizing."],[8124,"When Ramadan enters, all the gates of Paradise are opened, and not one of them is closed until the end of the month; the gates of Hell are closed, and not one of them is opened until the end of the month; the rebellious devils are chained; and Allah has those freed from the Fire at the time of every breaking of the fast."],[8125,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the Hour. He said: \"Among its signs are three, one of which is seeking knowledge from the young.\""],[8126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with Umm Salamah, and he carried Hasan on one side and Husayn on the other, with Fatimah in his lap, and said: \"The mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you, O people of the house; indeed He is Praiseworthy, Glorious.\""],[8127,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[8128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw on him a garment dyed with safflower and said: \"What is this?\" Abdullah went and burned it with fire. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"What did you do with your garment?\" He said: \"I burned it.\" He said: \"Why did you not clothe someone with it?\""],[8129,"The one who waits for the prayer after the prayer is like a horseman whose horse runs swiftly in the path of Allah with full flank; the angels pray for him as long as he does not break his ablution or stand, and he is in the greater ribat."],[8130,"I went with my father to the Prophet ﷺ and found him with his lower garment loosened. My father went behind him and placed his hand on the seal (of prophethood)."],[8131,"The neighbor of a house has more right to the house."],[8132,"I saw Jabir b. Abdullah and Jabir b. Umayr al-Ansari shooting arrows at each other. One of them got tired and sat down. The other said to him: 'Have you grown lazy? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Everything that is not from the remembrance of Allah is idle and neglect, except four traits: a man walking between two targets (for archery), training his horse, playing with his family, and learning to swim.'"],[8133,"There is no sin except in killing a Muslim three times."],[8134,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: 'There is no god but Allah.' When they say it, their wealth and their blood are protected from me, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[8135,"No one withholds (goods) except a sinner."],[8136,"The Prophet ﷺ used to go out to the two Eids with a spear and a shield."],[8137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Abu Talib: 'Did you benefit him?' He said: 'I brought him out of Hell to a shallow part of it.'"],[8138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Khadijah, that she died before the obligations and rulings were revealed. He said: 'I saw her on a river from the rivers of Paradise, in a house of reeds, with no idle talk or toil.'"],[8139,"He ate food and walked in the markets."],[8140,"When one of you eats from this vegetable (garlic), then let him not harm us in our mosque."],[8141,"He said to a woman: 'Perform Umrah in Ramadan, for an Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj with me.'"],[8142,"The Prophet ﷺ did not laugh more than that until we could see, or his premolars would appear."],[8143,"Before the Hour, usury and wine will appear."],[8144,"Whoever has daughters or three sisters, and fears God, and takes care of them, will be with me in Paradise like this."],[8145,"The Prophet ﷺ was walking on a road, and a black woman passed by. A man said to her, \"The road!\" She said, \"The road is that way.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Leave her, for she is defiant.\""],[8146,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ: When he entered Makkah, Abdullah b. Rawahah walked in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: \"Clear the way of the sons of the disbelievers from his path; today we strike you upon its interpretation, a strike that removes heads from their resting places and makes a friend forget his friend.\" Umar said, \"O Ibn Rawahah, in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ and in the sanctuary of God, you recite poetry?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Leave him, O Umar, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, this is harder on them than the falling of swords.\""],[8147,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ used to recite the Quran from beginning to end in the obligatory prayers."],[8148,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition, and he met the enemy. I heard him say: \"O Master of the Day of Judgment, You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help.\" He said: \"I saw men being struck down; the angels were striking them from in front of them and from behind them.\""],[8149,"A man from the Ansar set free a slave of his upon his death, and he was in need. That was mentioned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he called him and said, \"Did you free your slave?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You are more in need of him.\" Then he said, \"Who will buy him?\" Nuaym b. Abdullah said, \"I will.\" So he bought him. The Prophet ﷺ took his price and gave it to his owner."],[8150,"I was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ on a donkey, and he said to me, \"O Muadh, what is the right of God upon the servants?\" I said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.\" Then he said, \"O Muadh, what is the right of the servants upon God if they do that?\" I said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That He not punish them.\""],[8151,"I and my brother bought one hundred shares of the shares of Khaybar. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"O Asim, two hungry wolves that attack a flock whose owner has neglected it are not more destructive to it than a man's love of wealth and honor is to his religion.\""],[8152,"Her mother Umayrah bt. Sahl, the companion of the two sa's whom the hypocrites slandered, told her that he went out with his zakat with a sa' of dates, and with his daughter Umayrah, until he came to the Prophet ﷺ and poured it. Then he said, \"O Messenger of God, I have a need to you?\" He said, \"What is it?\" He said, \"You supplicate to God for me and for her for blessing, and you wipe her head, for I have no child other than her.\" She said, \"So the Messenger of God ﷺ placed his hand on me. I swear by God, it was as if the coolness of the Messenger of God ﷺ was upon my liver.\""],[8153,"When Talhah b. al-Bara met the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"O Messenger of God, command me with whatever you like, and I will not disobey any command of yours.\" The Prophet ﷺ was amazed at that, and he was a young boy. He said to him then, \"Go and kill your father.\" He said, \"So he went out, turning away to do it. Then he called him and said, 'Come back, for I have not been sent with severing ties of kinship.'\" After that, Talhah fell ill. The Prophet ﷺ came to visit him in winter, in cold and clouds. When he left, he said to his family, \"I do not see Talhah except that death has occurred in him. So notify me so that I may witness him and pray over him, and hasten him.\" The Prophet ﷺ had not yet reached Banu Salim b. Awf when he died, and night fell upon him. Among what Talhah said was: \"Bury me and join me with my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and do not call the Messenger of God ﷺ, for I fear the Jews for him, and that he may be harmed because of me.\" The Prophet ﷺ was informed in the morning, and he came until he stood at his grave. The people lined up with him, and he said, \"O God, meet Talhah while You laugh at him and he laughs at You.\""],[8154,"Indeed, in Friday there is an hour in which no Muslim coincides with it while praying and asking God for good except that He gives it to him."],[8155,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[8156,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled regarding the 'umra that it belongs to the recipient during his lifetime and after his death."],[8157,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, my mother died without making a will. Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: \"Yes.\""],[8158,"'Umar stood at Mina and asked the people: Who has knowledge of the inheritance of a woman from the blood money of her husband? Al-Dahhak b. Sufyan al-Kilabi stood up and said: Enter your tent and I will inform you. So he entered, and he came to him and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to me commanding me to give inheritance to the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi from the blood money of her husband."],[8159,"\"If he is from a people who are enemies to you while he is a believer, then the freeing of a believing slave.\" He said: A man would come to the Prophet ﷺ and embrace Islam, then return to his people and be among them while they were polytheists, and the Muslims would strike him in error during a raiding party or a military expedition, and the one who struck him would free a slave. \"And if he is from a people between whom and you there is a covenant,\" he said: \"He is a man who has a treaty, and his people are people of a covenant, so he pays the blood money to them, and the one who struck him frees a slave.\""],[8160,"The pilgrim in ihram may kill five harmful creatures: the crow, the mouse, the vicious dog, and the kite."],[8161,"No one should milk the livestock of another without his permission. Would any of you like his storeroom to be entered, its door broken, and its contents scattered? For what is in the udders of their livestock is the food of any one of them."],[8162,"The asking of a wealthy person is a blemish on his face."],[8163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for the funeral of a man from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf until he reached the cemetery, then said: Peace be upon the people of the graves, three times: those of you who are believers and Muslims. You are our forerunners, and we are followers after you. May Allah grant well-being to us and to you."],[8164,"The worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal from his prayer? He said: \"He does not complete its bowing or its prostration.\""],[8165,"My father entered upon me while I was bathing on Friday, and said: Is this bath of yours from janaba or for Friday? I said: From janaba. He said: Take another bath, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever bathes on Friday remains in a state of purity until the next Friday."],[8166,"I entered upon 'Umar b. al-Khattab, and I took hold of the doorposts while he was covered with a cloth. I said: How do you see him? They said: As you see. I said: Wake him with the prayer, for you will not wake him with anything more startling to him than the prayer. So they said: The prayer, O Commander of the Believers. He said: The prayer, ha, by Allah then, \"and there is no right in Islam for the one who abandons the prayer.\" So he prayed while his wound was flowing with blood."],[8167,"He prohibited looking at the stars."],[8168,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[8169,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I broke the fast on a day of Ramadan. He said: \"Without excuse or journey?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Evil is what you have done.\" He said: Indeed, so what do you command me? He said: \"Free a slave.\" He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have never owned a slave. He said: \"Then fast two consecutive months.\" He said: I am not able to do that. He said: \"Then feed sixty poor persons.\" He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I do not fill my own family. He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ was brought a basket in which there were dates, and he said: \"Give this as charity to sixty poor persons.\" He said: To whom shall I give it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"To the poorest person you know.\" He said: There is no household more needy than us. He said: \"Then return with it to your dependents.\""],[8170,"Abu Bakrah entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was bowing, so he bowed, then walked until he joined the row. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: May Allah increase you in keenness, but do not repeat it."],[8171,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed of the Night of Decree, and he came intending to inform us of it, but he heard clamor in the mosque."],[8172,"The signs of hypocrisy: one who lies when he speaks, betrays when he is entrusted, and breaks his promise when he promises."],[8173,"Muawiyah mentioned fleeing from the plague in his sermon. Ubadah said: Your mother Hind is more knowledgeable than you. He completed his sermon, then prayed, then sent for Ubadah. Some men of the Ansar went with him, and he detained them. Ubadah entered, and Muawiyah said to him: Do you not fear Allah and feel ashamed before your imam? Ubadah said: Do you not know that I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of Aqabah, that I do not fear in Allah the blame of any blamer? Then Muawiyah came out at Asr, prayed Asr, then took hold of the pulpit's leg and said: O people, I mentioned to you a hadith on the pulpit, then I entered the house and found the hadith to be as such."],[8174,"The first to practice coitus interruptus were a group of the Ansar. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: A group of the Ansar practice coitus interruptus. He was startled and said: The soul that is created will surely come into being, so I do not command nor forbid."],[8175,"When one of you dies, his seat is shown to him morning and evening, whether he is of the people of Paradise or of the people of the Fire. It is said: This is your seat until Allah resurrects you on the Day of Resurrection."],[8176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade traveling to the enemy with the Quran, fearing that the enemy might seize it."],[8177,"When Abdullah prayed the congregational prayer, he would return to his house and pray two prostrations, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[8178,"The Christians had the fast of the month of Ramadan. A king ruled over them and fell ill. They said: If Allah heals him, we will add eight days. Then a king after him ate meat and felt pain. They said: If Allah heals him, we will add eight days. Then a king after him said: We will not leave any of these days without completing them, and we will make our fast in spring. He did so, and it became fifty days."],[8179,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for thirteen years, and he died at the age of sixty-three."],[8180,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from pursuing the confederates and entered Madinah, he laid down his armor, bathed, and performed istijmar."],[8181,"When you narrate to people about their Lord, do not narrate to them what frightens them and is difficult for them."],[8182,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remember Allah much, engage in little idle talk, lengthen the prayer, shorten the sermon, and he did not disdain to walk with a widow or a needy person to fulfill their need."],[8183,"Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the front row. The mu'adhdhin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and whoever hears him from moist and dry things affirms him, and he has the like of the reward of those who pray with him."],[8184,"Regarding the one who forgets the prayer, he said: He prays when he remembers."],[8185,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed four rak'ahs in Madinah and two rak'ahs at Dhu al-Hulayfah, then he spent the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah until morning. When he mounted his riding camel and it stood upright with him, he entered the state of ihram."],[8186,"A virgin is not married until she is asked for permission, and her permission is her silence. A previously married woman has more right to her affair as long as she does not call for displeasure. If she calls for displeasure and her guardians call for what pleases Allah, the matter is raised to the ruler."],[8187,"When he saw rain, he would say: O Allah, make it a beneficial downpour."],[8188,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were all young men and said: You should marry, for whoever is unable to should fast, for it is a shield for him."],[8189,"He forbade excessive questions."],[8190,"Whoever asks for something while having enough to spare, he increases his share of the hot stones of Hell. They said: What is having enough to spare? He said: The evening meal of a night."],[8191,"The tribes were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and they asked him about Banu 'Amir. He said: A bright camel that eats from the edges of trees. They asked him about Hawazin, and he said: A flower that follows its water. They asked him about Banu Tamim, and he said: Firm-footed, sound in judgment, large-headed, the strongest of people against the Dajjal in the end times, a red hill that is not harmed by whoever opposes it."],[8192,"It was said: O Messenger of God, will you not marry among the Ansar? He said: \"They have intense jealousy.\""],[8193,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray at night during Ramadan. Some people came and stood behind him, so he prayed and would lighten it, then enter his house and pray, then come out and lighten it. When morning came they said: O Messenger of God, we stood behind you last night, and you would enter your house then come out. He said: \"I only did that because of you.\""],[8194,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: His mother died; will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: \"Yes.\" He said: I have a garden, and I call you to witness that I have given it in charity on her behalf."],[8195,"The Prophet ﷺ had two freedmen: an Abyssinian and a Copt. One day they quarreled while the Prophet ﷺ was listening. One of them said to the other: \"O Abyssinian,\" and the other said: \"O Copt.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not say this; you are but two men from the family of Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[8196,"\"Its thorn trees shall not be cut, its game shall not be startled, its fresh herbage shall not be cut, and its lost property is not lawful except for one who announces it.\" Al-Abbas said: \"Except idhkhir (a kind of grass)?\" He said: \"Except idhkhir.\""],[8197,"He forbade that a woman be married along with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."],[8198,"He used to say when he said \"God listens to the one who praises Him\": \"O God, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will after that.\""],[8199,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper; whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not let his wife enter the bathhouse; and whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not sit at a table where wine is passed around,\" or he said: \"where wine is drunk.\""],[8200,"O Burayda, there will be expeditions; be in the expedition of Khurasan and dwell in the city of Marw, for it was built by Dhu al-Qarnayn, who prayed for blessing upon it, so no harm will ever afflict its people."],[8201,"A slave belonging to poor people cut off the ear of a slave belonging to rich people. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not award them anything."],[8202,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to announce during the days of Mina: \"No one should fast during these days, for they are days of eating, drinking, and remembrance of God.\""],[8203,"\"Indeed God, Mighty and Majestic, boasts to His angels on the evening of Arafah, saying: 'My servants have come to Me disheveled and dusty.'\""],[8204,"While I was praying, a devil appeared before me. I seized him by the throat and choked him until I felt the coldness of his tongue on my hand. Had it not been for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have been tied up for you to see."],[8205,"A woman used to pick up debris from the mosque. When she died, the Prophet ﷺ was not informed of her burial. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'When one of you dies, inform me.' Then he prayed over her and said: 'I saw her in Paradise because she used to pick up debris from the mosque.'"],[8206,"Whoever looks into a people's house without their permission, and they gouge out his eye, there is no blood money for them and no retaliation."],[8207,"My nation will come on the Day of Resurrection with radiant faces and limbs from the traces of ablution."],[8208,"When the Prophet ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey, he passed by people whose lips were being cut. He said: 'O Jibril, who are these?' He said: 'These are the preachers from your nation who enjoin righteousness upon people and forget themselves, while they recite the Book. Do they not understand?'"],[8209,"There is no divorce except after marriage, and no manumission except after ownership."],[8210,"The best treatment you use is cupping and sea costus."],[8211,"Al-Zubayr was a blind man. Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Al-Zubayr passed by me on the day of Bu'ath and freed me, so grant him to me that I may repay him.' He said: 'He is yours.' He said to al-Zubayr: 'Do you recognize me?' He said: 'Yes, you are Thabit.' He said: 'I bestow a favor upon you as you bestowed a favor upon me on the day of Bu'ath.' He said: 'Will you benefit me? Where is my family?' He returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'Grant me his family.' He said: 'He granted him his family.' He came to him and informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had returned his family to him. He said: 'O son of my brother, what benefit is it to me to live as bodies? Where is the wealth?' He returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, grant me his wealth.' He said: 'And his wealth is yours.' He returned to him and said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has returned your wealth to you, and Allah Almighty has intended good for you.' He said: 'O son of my brother, what has happened to Huyayy b. Akhtab, the master of the settled and the Bedouin?' He said: 'He has been killed.' He said: 'O son of my brother, what has happened to Zayd b. Buta, the protector of the Jews?' He said: 'He has been killed.' He said: 'O son of my brother, what has happened to Ka'b b. Ashta, whose beauty the virgins of the tribe would marvel at?' He said: 'He has been killed.' He said: 'What has happened to the two assemblies?' He said: 'They are like yesterday that has passed.' He said: 'Between me and meeting the loved ones is only the emptying of a bucket. I ask you by my hand upon you, unless you join me with the people.' He said: 'Then he killed him.'"],[8212,"His father wrote a letter to the disbelievers of Quraysh while he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he had witnessed Badr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned 'Ali and al-Zubayr and said: 'Go until you catch up with a woman who has a letter, and bring it to me.' They went until they met her and said: 'Give us the letter you have.' They informed her that they would not leave until they stripped every garment from her. She said: 'Are you not two Muslim men?' They said: 'Yes, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ...'"],[8213,"The earth is Allah's earth and the servants are Allah's servants. Whoever revives dead land has the most right to it."],[8214,"He was the tenth of ten with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Hira'. Hira' shook, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Be still, Hira', for upon you is none but a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.' Sa'id said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say after that: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, 'Umar is in Paradise, 'Uthman is in Paradise, 'Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf is in Paradise, and Sa'd is in Paradise.' Al-Mughirah said to Sa'id: 'Mention to us who is the ninth?' He said: 'Leave me.' He did not cease until he said: 'I am the ninth.'"],[8215,"We discussed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ which is better: the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or the mosque of Jerusalem. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A prayer in my mosque is better than four prayers in it, and it is an excellent place of prayer. Soon a man will have a piece of land the size of a bow's end from where he can see Jerusalem, and that will be better for him than the world and all it contains.'"],[8216,"I went out as a merchant to al-Sham in the Jahiliyyah. When I was near al-Sham, a man from the People of the Book met me and said: “Do you have a man who has claimed prophethood?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Do you recognize his image if you see it?” I said: “Yes.” He took me into a house containing images, but I did not see the image of the Prophet ﷺ. While I was thus, a man from among them entered upon us and said: “What are you doing?” We informed him, so he took us to his house. The moment I entered, I looked at the image of the Prophet ﷺ, and there was a man holding the heel of the Prophet ﷺ. I said: “Who is this man holding his heel?” He said: “There was no prophet except that a prophet came after him, except this one, for there is no prophet after him, and this is the caliph after him.” And it was the description of Abu Bakr."],[8217,"He asked 'A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers, about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: “He used to pray after the later 'Isha' between it and Fajr thirteen rak'ahs, including two rak'ahs with Fajr.” Then I asked her about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: “His most frequent fasting besides Ramadan was in Sha'ban; he used to fast it or most of it.”"],[8218,"We prayed Zuhr with 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz, then we left until we entered upon Anas b. Malik, and we found him praying 'Asr. We said: “Uncle, what is this prayer that you have prayed?” He said: “'Asr, and it is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that we used to pray with him.”"],[8219,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[8220,"What is given from abundance has no greater reward than what accepts when he is in need."],[8221,"Some people of my community will recite the Qur'an and delve deeply into religion. Satan will come to them saying: “Would you not go to the kings and obtain some of their worldly goods, while you keep away from them with your religion?” Indeed, that will not be except as nothing is harvested from tragacanth except thorns; likewise nothing is harvested from closeness to them except sins."],[8222,"The Prophet ﷺ used to kiss while fasting, and he was the most in control of his desires among you."],[8223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who slept until morning. He said: “Satan urinated in his ear.”"],[8224,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about dough into which drops of blood had fallen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating it."],[8225,"A woman has two covers. It was said: “What are they?” He said: “The husband and the grave.” He said: “Which of them is better?” He said: “The grave.”"],[8226,"A moderate spender never becomes poor."],[8227,"Observe the crescent of Sha'ban for the sighting of Ramadan."],[8228,"Whoever meets the enemy and remains steadfast until he is killed or kills them will not be tested in his grave."],[8229,"Whoever takes land upon paying its jizya has thereby sought to rescind his emigration, and whoever removes the humiliation of a disbeliever from his neck and places it on his own neck has turned his back on Islam."],[8230,"Indeed, part of the obligation of forgiveness is to bring joy to your Muslim brother."],[8231,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit down until he prays two rak'ahs."],[8232,"Whoever ties the jizya around his neck has disassociated himself from Allah, Exalted is He, and His Messenger."],[8233,"Whoever grants respite to a debtor in hardship, Allah will shade him in His shade on the Day of Resurrection, and every good deed is charity."],[8234,"The lineage of people is sound up to Ma'add b. 'Adnan."],[8235,"There is no ill omen, but good fortune may be in a horse, a woman, and a house."],[8236,"Whoever looks at his brother with a look of affection, having no rancor in his heart toward him, will not blink before his past sins are forgiven."],[8237,"'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ sent Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah in the year of the famine to distribute shares among the Arabs. When he returned, 'Umar gave him a thousand dinars as compensation, but he refused to take it. 'Umar said: \"Take it, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered this for us, and we disliked it, but he ordered us to take it.\""],[8238,"O Allah, strengthen Islam with 'Umar."],[8239,"Any man who becomes bankrupt while he has the exact property of another man, from which he has not received anything, then the owner is more entitled to his exact property. But if he has received something from it, then he is like the other creditors."],[8240,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a grave recently dug for burial, so he asked about it. It was said to him: The grave of so-and-so. He descended and prayed over it, and I was among those who prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ over that grave. He said the takbir four times."],[8241,"It was said: O Messenger of God, who is forbidden to the Fire? He said: The gentle, the soft, the easy, the near."],[8242,"She said: A man drew near with wealth from his own property on behalf of his father, so his father came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him of that. He sent to him: Return to your father what you have withheld from him, for you and your wealth are like an arrow from his quiver."],[8243,"The Prophet ﷺ went out between Abu Bakr and Umar, and said: Thus shall we be raised on the Day of Resurrection."],[8244,"When the evening meal is placed and the prayer is called, then begin with the evening meal."],[8245,"I entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah, then I met Umar, and he said: You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ."],[8246,"When Adam died, the angels washed him with water an odd number of times, and a niche was dug for him, and they said: This is the Sunnah of Adam and his descendants."],[8247,"It is from the Sunnah to begin with burying the deceased, and to throw dust upon him from the direction of the qiblah."],[8248,"When God manifested Himself to Musa b. Imran, seven mountains flew apart. In the Hijaz there are five of them, and in Yemen two: in the Hijaz: Uhud, Thabir, Hira, Thawr, and Warqan; and in Yemen: Hasur and Sabir."],[8249,"I placed, or the washing water was placed for the Messenger of God ﷺ. He poured with his right hand over his left until he cleaned them both, then he poured with his right hand over his private part and washed it with his left hand and what touched it until he cleaned it. Then he placed his hand on the wall on the dust, then washed it until he cleaned it, then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, and performed wudu as for prayer. Then he poured water over his head and over his body, and he moved from his place and washed his feet."],[8250,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Ali b. Abi Talib to a people to fight them, then he sent a man to him and said: Do not call him from behind him, and say to him: Do not fight them until you invite them."],[8251,"Four things are never satisfied with four: an eye with looking, and earth with rain, and a female with a male, and a scholar with knowledge."],[8252,"Clothing manifests wealth, oil removes misery, and kindness to the slave—through it God subdues the enemy.”"],[8253,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ on the pulpit saying: “Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe.”"],[8254,"I said: “O Messenger of God, gray hair has come to you quickly.” He said: “Hud, al-Waqi‘ah, ‘Amma yatasa’alun, and Idha al-shamsu kuwwirat have made me gray.”"],[8255,"Whoever enters upon a people for food to which he was not invited, and eats until full, has eaten what is unlawful.”"],[8256,"There is no will for a killer.”"],[8257,"Whoever performs ablution on Friday, it is good and sufficient; and whoever bathes, bathing is better.”"],[8258,"From my community are lifted mistake, forgetfulness, and what they are compelled to do.”"],[8259,"Musa b. Jumhur narrated to us: Muhammad b. Musaffa narrated to us: al-Walid narrated to us from Malik, from Nafi‘, from Ibn ‘Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it.”"],[8260,"Musa b. Jumhur narrated to us: Muhammad b. Musaffa narrated to us: al-Walid b. Muslim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ‘Ata’, from Ibn ‘Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it.”"],[8261,"Musa b. Jumhur narrated to us: Muhammad b. Musaffa narrated to us: al-Walid narrated to us from Ibn Lahi‘ah, from Musa b. Wardan, from ‘Uqbah b. ‘Amir, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it. “No one narrated the hadith of al-Awza‘i from ‘Ata’ from Ibn ‘Abbas except al-Walid b. Muslim. And no one narrated the hadith of Malik from Nafi‘ except al-Walid. And no one narrated the hadith of Ibn Jurayj except al-Walid. And no one narrated the hadith of ‘Uqbah b. ‘Amir except Musa b. Wardan, and no one narrated it from Musa except Ibn Lahi‘ah. Al-Walid is alone in it.”"],[8262,"He used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim silently."],[8263,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying supererogatory prayer on a camel, facing whatever direction it turned.”"],[8264,"Any wealth—even if it be beneath seven earths—whose zakah is paid, is not a treasure (kanz). And any wealth whose zakah is not paid, even if it is in plain sight, is a treasure."],[8265,"Someone from the household of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ borrowed a wooden bowl, and it was lost, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ guaranteed it."],[8266,"Beware of qusāmah. We asked: What is qusāmah? He said: \"Something that is shared among people, and it is diminished from it.\""],[8267,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting, so he said: \"You should observe the white days: three days of every month.\""],[8268,"When the sun set at ʿArafah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed, and from al-Muzdalifah before sunrise."],[8269,"Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq wrote to ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ: \"Peace be upon you. To proceed: Your letter has reached me, mentioning what the Romans have gathered of troops. Allah did not grant us victory alongside His Prophet ﷺ by numerous numbers or by numerous soldiers. We used to raid with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had only a few small horses, and we would but take turns riding the camels. On the day of Uḥud we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had only one horse, which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode. He would grant us victory and aid us against those who opposed us. Know, O ʿAmr, that the most obedient of people to Allah are those with the strongest hatred for sins. So obey Allah, and command your companions to obey Him.\""],[8270,"ʿAlī disputed with al-ʿAbbās regarding the water distribution (siqāyah). Ṭalḥah b. ʿUbayd Allāh, ʿĀmir b. Makhramah b. Nawfal, and Azhar b. ʿAbd ʿAwf testified that the Prophet ﷺ handed it over to al-ʿAbbās on the day of the Conquest."],[8271,"Allah has reserved this religion for Himself. Nothing suits your religion except generosity and good character. So adorn your religion with these two."],[8272,"Seek help against women by means of nakedness."],[8273,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, do not ask for authority. If you are given it without asking, you will be assisted in it; if you are given it through asking, you will be left to it. If you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do the better thing and make expiation for your oath.\""],[8274,"The harm caused by an animal is without liability (jubār), the harm caused by a well is without liability, and on buried treasure (rikāz) one-fifth is due."],[8275,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man with disheveled hair and said: \"Why does one of you disfigure himself?\" and gestured with his hand."],[8276,"She was asked about nabidh, and she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade al-hantam, al-dubba', and al-naqir."],[8277,"None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."],[8278,"When a servant intends to pray at night, the angel comes to him and says: 'Get up, morning has come, so pray and remember your Lord.' Then Satan comes to him and says: 'You have a long night ahead, and you will get up, so sleep for a while.' If he gets up and prays, he rises in the morning energetic, light in body, and with cool eyes. If he obeys Satan until morning, Satan urinates in his ear."],[8279,"Death, compared to what comes after it, is only like the butt of a goat."],[8280,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Abd Allah b. Jud'an: 'When you buy sandals, get good ones; when you buy a garment, get a good one; when you buy a riding beast, get a strong one; and if you have a noble woman of a people, honor her.'"],[8281,"There is no divorce before marriage, and no manumission before ownership."],[8282,"The Prophet ﷺ led them in prayer and forgot something, so he performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[8283,"Whoever denies the divine decree has denied what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ."],[8284,"The prayer is cut off by: the black dog, the donkey, and the woman. I asked Abu Dharr: 'What is it about the black dog as opposed to the red or yellow?' He said: 'I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said: The black dog is a devil.'"],[8285,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Have you seen your Lord?' He said: 'Light; how could I see Him?'"],[8286,"I was a Christian, and I entered ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah. I came to 'Umar, and he said: 'You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.'"],[8287,"I was among those about whom Sa'd b. Mu'adh gave judgment. He ruled regarding Banu Qurayzah that their fighters be killed and their women and children taken captive. He looked at me, and since I had not yet grown pubic hair, he joined me with the captives."],[8288,"He cursed ten: the female tattooer, the female who is tattooed, the woman who scrapes her face, the woman who extends hair, the woman whose hair is extended, the consumer of riba, its witness, the withholder of charity, the man who imitates women, and the woman who imitates men."],[8289,"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom."],[8290,"That his father's front tooth fell out, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to bind it with gold."],[8291,"That the Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon, and he recited the end of al-Zumar in his sermon, and the pulpit moved twice."],[8292,"Umar b. al-Khattab said on the pulpit: O people, be humble, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever humbles himself for Allah, He raises him."],[8293,"Learn of your lineages that by which you may maintain your ties of kinship."],[8294,"Whoever says: O Allah, to You is praise, there is no god but You alone, without partner, You are my Lord and I am Your servant, I believe in You, making my religion sincerely Yours, I have entered the morning upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able, I repent to You from my evil deeds, and I seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You—he says that three times. Whoever says it during his day, Allah forbids him to the Fire."],[8295,"Visiting the sick on the first day is a sunnah, and whatever is after that is voluntary."],[8296,"The menstruating woman should observe what is between her and ten days. If she sees purity, she is pure. If she exceeds ten, she is in a state of istihada; she should perform ghusl and pray. If the blood overcomes her, she should insert cotton, secure it, and perform wudu for every prayer. The woman in postnatal bleeding should wait what is between her and forty nights. If she sees purity before that, she is pure. If she exceeds forty, she is in the position of one in istihada; she should perform ghusl and pray. If the blood overcomes her, she should insert cotton, secure it, and perform wudu for every prayer."],[8297,"Raid, and you will gain spoils; fast, and you will be healthy; travel, and you will be free of need."],[8298,"Modesty and faith are in one cord; when one of them is taken away, the other follows it."],[8299,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about purification. He said: There is no Muslim who rinses his mouth except that Allah forgives him every sin his tongue committed that day, nor does he wash his hands except that Allah forgives him what his hands have sent forward that day, nor does he wipe his head except that he becomes like the day his mother gave birth to him."],[8300,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they said: \"He has bewitched the sun.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ recited: \"The Hour has drawn near, and the moon has split. And if they see a sign, they turn away and say: 'Passing magic.'\""],[8301,"There is no hour that passes by the son of Adam in which he did not remember God with good except that he will be at a loss because of it on the Day of Resurrection."],[8302,"O Mu'adh, indeed the believer is restrained by the Qur'an from much of his own desire."],[8303,"Rinse your mouth and sniff water into your nostrils, and the ears are part of the head."],[8304,"O people, offer sacrifices and seek reward by their blood, for the blood, even if it falls upon the earth, falls into the protection of God, Mighty and Majestic."],[8305,"O Abu Razin, when a Muslim visits his Muslim brother, seventy thousand angels escort him, praying for him, saying: 'O God, just as he maintained ties for Your sake, so maintain ties with him.'"],[8306,"When he needed to relieve himself, he tied a piece of cloth to his ring."],[8307,"Do you know which charity is best? They said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'The best charity is a grant, one of you giving the use of a dirham or the back of a riding beast.'"],[8308,"The Ansar said: 'The walking between al-Safa and al-Marwa is from the affairs of the pre-Islamic era.' So God Almighty revealed: 'Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the rites of God. So whoever performs Hajj to the House or performs 'Umrah, there is no blame upon him to walk between them.'"],[8309,"He used to give salutations to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of God. Peace be upon you and the mercy of God.'"],[8310,"The earth will surely be filled with oppression and injustice. When it is filled with oppression and injustice, God will send a man whose name is my name, who will fill it with equity and justice just as it was filled with oppression and injustice."],[8311,"I never saw the knee of the Messenger of God ﷺ in front of a companion of his ever, and the Prophet ﷺ never shook hands with anyone and withdrew his hand from his until he was the one who withdrew it."],[8312,"Whoever imitates a people is one of them."],[8313,"Between every two calls [to prayer] there is a prayer for whoever wishes, except for the Maghrib."],[8314,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on his deathbed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, advise us. He said: I enjoin you to [be good to] the first of the Muhajirun, and their descendants after them. If you do not do so, neither an obligatory nor a voluntary deed will be accepted from you."],[8315,"We used to see no harm in renting out land, and Rafiʿ mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ forbade it."],[8316,"There is no right of return after four days, and the two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated."],[8317,"There is no household from which no one goes forth to fight, or equips a fighter with a thread, a needle, or its equivalent in silver, or takes good care of his family in his absence, but that Allah will strike them with a calamity before the Day of Resurrection."],[8318,"Whoever intends a matter and consults a Muslim about it, Allah will guide him to the most upright of his affairs."],[8319,"You must engage in jihad in the path of Allah, for it is one of the gates of Paradise by which Allah removes worry and grief."],[8320,"He used to prefer, when he traveled, to set out on Thursday."],[8321,"When the deceased was placed in the grave, he said: In the name of Allah, and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah."],[8322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to kiss while fasting."],[8323,"A man during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made over to another man a share of his property. The man died without knowing what it was, so the matter was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he assigned him one-sixth of his property."],[8324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me, took my hand, and shook it. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I used to think that shaking hands was only for the non-Arabs.\" He said, \"We are more entitled to shaking hands than they are. There are no two Muslims who meet and one of them takes the hand of his companion with love and sincerity except that Allah casts their sins down between them.\""],[8325,"Use this tree as a condiment, meaning olive oil, and apply this ithmid (antimony) as kohl, for it clears the vision. And whoever is offered perfume, let him take some of it."],[8326,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the earnings of a cupper: \"May I eat from it?\" He said, \"No.\" I said, \"Then may I feed it to orphans under my care?\" He said, \"No.\" Then he allowed him to feed it to his water-carrying camel."],[8327,"Your smiling in the face of your brother is charity, your removing harm from the road is recorded for you as charity, your pouring water into your brother's bucket is charity, your enjoining good and forbidding evil is charity for you, and your guiding a lost person is charity."],[8328,"Whoever his brother tells him a hadith, it is a trust with him, even if he did not ask him to keep it secret."],[8329,"Good character is the greatest of Allah's character traits."],[8330,"When the heart of a believer trembles in the path of Allah, his sins fall away as the date cluster falls from the palm tree."],[8331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Hakim b. Hizam a dinar and ordered him to buy a sacrificial animal with it. He bought one, then someone came to him offering a profit, so he sold it. Then he bought another, and then came to the Prophet ﷺ with a dinar and a sheep. He said, \"What is this?\" He replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, I bought, sold, and made a profit.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"May Allah bless your trade,\" and he took the dinar and gave it as charity, and took the sheep and sacrificed it."],[8332,"If I were to take an intimate friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, but your companion is the intimate friend of Allah."],[8333,"When you mention the name of Allah, say 'Allahu Akbar' (Allah is the Greatest)."],[8334,"When he began the prayer, he would say: \"Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. Blessed is Your name, and exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god other than You.\""],[8335,"Indeed, Allah has favors upon some people which He keeps with them as long as they are engaged in fulfilling the needs of people, as long as they do not become weary of them. When they become weary of them, He transfers those favors from them to others."],[8336,"Three men from those before you went out."],[8337,"Whoever did not take part in a military expedition with me, let him fight in the sea."],[8338,"You should take concubines, for they are blessed in the wombs."],[8339,"There are no days of this world in which deeds are better than the days of tashriq. A man said: \"Nor the like of them in the path of God?\" He repeated it three times, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him on the third: \"Except for the one who does not return.\""],[8340,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"If she has a discharge as a man discharges, then she must perform ghusl; if she does not discharge, then nothing is required of her.\""],[8341,"Nothing is more honorable to God than the believer."],[8342,"He forbade the sale of years."],[8343,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded for zakat al-fitr a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley."],[8344,"Indeed, this world is sweet and green. Whoever takes it with its right will be blessed in it, and whoever takes it without its right is like the one who eats but is never satisfied. Woe to the one who squanders the wealth of God and the wealth of His Messenger from the punishment of Hell on the Day of Resurrection."],[8345,"Whoever deceives us is not of us."],[8346,"The noblest of gatherings is that which faces the qibla."],[8347,"Indeed, God tests the servant to see how he acts. If he is content, he is blessed; and if he is not content, he is not blessed."],[8348,"Regarding wiping over the leather socks: for the traveler, three days and their nights; for the resident, a day and a night."],[8349,"The Prophet ﷺ heard the muezzin and said as he said, until he said: 'Come to prayer,' then he said: 'There is no might and no power except with Allah.'"],[8350,"The first to embrace Islam was Abu Bakr."],[8351,"When you see those who revile my Companions, say: 'May Allah curse the worst of you.'"],[8352,"The false witness's feet will not cease on the Day of Resurrection until the Fire becomes obligatory for him."],[8353,"He was ten years old when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah. He said: 'My mothers used to urge me to serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'So I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years; his life in Madinah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when I was twenty years old.' He said: 'I was the most knowledgeable of people about the matter of the hijab when it was revealed.' Ubayy b. Ka'b used to ask me about it. He said: 'The first thing revealed regarding the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ marriage to Zaynab bt. Jahsh was that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became a bridegroom with her. He invited the people, and they ate the food. Then they left, but some of them remained with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and stayed long. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up and went out, and I went out with him so that they might leave. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked and I walked with him until he came to the threshold of Aisha's room. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at them: had they left? He returned and I returned with him until he entered upon Zaynab, and behold, they had left. Then a screen was struck between me and them, and the verse of hijab was revealed.'"],[8354,"Three things make your brother's love sincere for you: greet him when you meet him, make room for him in gatherings, and call him by the most beloved of his names to him."],[8355,"Whoever is not pleased with Allah's decree and destiny, let him seek a god other than Him."],[8356,"The greatest name of Allah, which when He is called by it He answers, is in three surahs: al-Baqarah, Al Imran, and Ta-Ha."],[8357,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: 'Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill?' He said: 'The more complete of them.'"],[8358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in three white Yemeni Sahuli garments, with no shirt and no turban; he was wrapped in them."],[8359,"He used to have intercourse and then wake up in a state of janabah, then perform ghusl and fast."],[8360,"He prohibited the leasing of land."],[8361,"We used to lease land, then we abandoned that when we heard the hadith of Rafi' b. Khadij from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked a man: 'Where did you alight?' He said: 'At so-and-so's (a woman's).' He said: 'Did she close her door on you?' He said: 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked that."],[8363,"A man may not enter upon a woman unless she has a mahram with her."],[8364,"It is not lawful for a woman to fast in the presence of her husband except with his permission, and whatever she gives in charity from his earnings, half of it belongs to him. She was created from a rib; if you are gentle with it, you will enjoy it, but if you try to straighten it, you will break it, and its breaking is divorcing her."],[8365,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a stray sheep. He said: 'It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.' Then he asked him about a stray camel. He said: 'What do you have to do with a stray camel? It has its own water-skin and its own shoes; it can come to water and eat trees. Leave it until its owner finds it.'"],[8366,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[8367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man announcing a lost item in the mosque, so he said: 'May you not find it. Say: May you not find it. The mosques were not built for this.'"],[8368,"Whoever takes a span of land from a Muslim's right without right, Allah the Exalted will make him wear it as a collar around his neck on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."],[8369,"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you send us out and we pass by a people and ask them for hospitality, but they refuse us. What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Ask them for the hospitality due to a guest, which is his right. If they refuse, then take it from them even if they dislike it. How evil is the people who do not offer hospitality to the guest.'"],[8370,"A man looked into a hole in the door of the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a comb with which he was scratching his head. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If I knew that you were looking at us, I would have poked your eye with it. Permission was only made because of the sight.'"],[8371,"The Jews and Christians do not dye, so differ from them."],[8372,"The two parties to a transaction have the option (to annul it) until they separate, or one of them gives the other the option and he chooses."],[8373,"That after Abu Lubabah informed him from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of what he told him, when he saw him, he would threaten him and stand up to him, and sometimes he would order Nafi' to carry him until he threw him aside to the side of the houses."],[8374,"The people spoke excessively about the Friday bath, but that was only in my house and in my presence: people from the 'Awali came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when they arrived, and the people at that time wore wool, and he detected an odor from them, so he said: \"If only when this day comes you would bathe.\""],[8375,"Whoever sells palm trees after pollinating them, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."],[8376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that one of you sell over his brother's sale until he gives it up, except for spoils of war and inheritances, and that one of you propose to a woman over his brother's proposal until he gives it up."],[8377,"There is no harm in a man selling his 'ariyya of palm trees for their estimated amount of dried dates, meaning: that the other may eat it."],[8378,"That Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, spoke to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ about the hems of women's garments when he forbade dragging the garment, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They may let them down a span.\" She said: \"(Then) it would be uncovered.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Then a cubit, and no more than that.\""],[8379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon 'A'isha while her sister Asma' was with her, wearing Syrian garments with wide sleeves. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at her, he stood up and left. 'A'isha said to her: \"Move aside, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw something he disliked.\" So she moved aside, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered. 'A'isha asked him: \"Why did he stand up?\" He said: \"Did you not see her appearance? It is not (permissible) for a Muslim woman to show anything of herself except this\" – and he took hold of his sleeves and covered his palms with them until nothing showed of his palms except his fingers, and he placed his palms on his temples until nothing showed except his face."],[8380,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we stopped at al-Qaha, and there was no water there. He went down into the upper part of the valley and dug with his hand in the pebbly ground, and it became moist. He sat and dug, and water gushed forth, and he drank and gave drink to those with him. He said: \"This is a drink that Allah has given you to drink,\" so it was called al-Suqya."],[8381,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man in Baqi' al-Gharqad on the eighteenth of Ramadan while he was being cupped, and he said: \"The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.\""],[8382,"The earth was folded up for me so that I saw its easts and its wests, and I was given the two treasures, the yellow and the white, meaning gold and silver, and it was said to me: \"Your community's dominion will reach where the earth was folded up for you.\" And I asked Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for three things: that He not send upon my community a famine that would destroy them generally, that He not send upon them an enemy that would destroy them, and that He not make them into factions and make some taste the might of others. And it was said to me: \"When I decree a matter, there is no averting it. I will not send upon your community a famine that would destroy them, nor will I send upon them an enemy that would destroy them, even if all between its regions gather against them, until some of them establish others and some kill others.\" And among what I fear for my community are misleading leaders, and when the sword is placed among them it will not be lifted until the Day of Resurrection. And tribes of my community will worship idols, and tribes of my community will join the polytheists. And before the Hour there will be lying deceivers, about thirty in number, all of them claiming to be a prophet, but there is no prophet after me. And a group of my community will continue to be upon the truth, victorious, not harmed by those who oppose them, until the command of Allah comes."],[8383,"Abu Jahl said: \"If Muhammad returns to pray toward the qibla, I will surely kill him.\" So he returned, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: \"Read in the name of your Lord who created...\" up to His saying: \"Let him call his associates. We will call the guards of Hell.\" When it was said to Abu Jahl that he had returned, he said: \"Indeed something has come between me and him.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"By Allah, if he had moved, the angels would have seized him while the people were watching.\""],[8384,"The neighbor has more right to the preemption of his neighbor; it is awaited for him even if he is absent, when their path is one."],[8385,"I heard a man asking ʿAṭāʾ b. Abī Rabāḥ about the Yemeni Corner while he was circumambulating the House. ʿAṭāʾ said: Abū Hurayrah narrated to me that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Seventy are assigned to it. Whoever says: 'O Allah, I ask You for pardon, well-being, and mutual forgiveness in this world and the Hereafter. Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and protect us from the punishment of the Fire,' they say: Amen.\" When he reached the Black Corner, he said: \"O Abū Muḥammad, what has reached you regarding this Black Corner?\" ʿAṭāʾ said: Abū Hurayrah narrated to me that he heard the Beloved ﷺ saying: \"Whoever circumambulates the House seven times, speaking nothing but: 'Glory be to Allah, there is no deity but Allah, Allah is Greatest, and praise be to Allah, and there is no power except with Allah,' ten evil deeds will be erased from him, ten good deeds will be written for him, and he will be raised by ten degrees. And whoever circumambulates and speaks while in that state wades through mercy with his feet as one wades through water with his feet.\""],[8386,"Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at an adulterous old man or an adulterous old woman."],[8387,"Part of the excellence of a person's Islam is his leaving what does not concern him."],[8388,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a state of major ritual impurity and wanted to eat or sleep, he would perform ablution."],[8389,"They said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what is ill-omen?\" He said: \"Bad character.\""],[8390,"The accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise. He said: \"What is its righteousness?\" He said: \"Feeding food and good speech.\""],[8391,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ at Muzdalifah, three and two, with one iqāmah."],[8392,"While Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq was eating with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, there was revealed to him: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.' Abū Bakr raised his hand and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I will indeed see whatever evil I have done, even an atom's weight.' He said: 'O Abū Bakr, do you see what you dislike in this world? That is due to the atoms' weights of evil, and the atoms' weights of good are stored for you until you receive them in full on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[8393,"We passed by Abū Dharr at al-Rabadhah, and I asked him about tamattuʿ in Hajj. He said: 'We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were pronouncing the talbiyah for Hajj. When we reached Makkah, he commanded us, so we exited the state of iḥrām and had intercourse with women. The Prophet ﷺ did not exit the state of iḥrām because he had brought the sacrificial animal.' Then he said: 'It is not to be for anyone after you.'"],[8394,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me one day and said: 'O ʿĀʾishah, today I did something I wish I had not done: I entered the House, and I wish I had not entered it. Someone from my community will come and think it is obligatory upon him to enter the House, and I fear that I have made things difficult for my community.'"],[8395,"Women have no reward in following funeral processions."],[8396,"I entered with the Messenger of God ﷺ upon Abu Salama while he was dying. When his gaze became fixed, the Messenger of God ﷺ leaned toward him and closed his eyes, and his family cried out, so he calmed them. Then he said: 'When the soul departs, the sight follows it, and the angels attend the deceased, saying ameen to what the deceased's family says.' Then he said: 'O God, raise the degree of Abu Salama among the rightly guided, and be his successor among his offspring who remain, and forgive us and him, Lord of the worlds.'"],[8397,"When God wills to take a servant in a certain land, He creates a need for him there, and he does not cease until he arrives there.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited the end of Surah Luqman: 'Indeed, God has knowledge of the Hour' until he completed it. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'These are the keys of the unseen; none knows them except God.'"],[8398,"He prohibited plastering graves, or building over them, or sitting on them."],[8399,"The Maghrib prayer is the witr of the day, so perform witr for the night prayer."],[8400,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us, when we were two, to stand in a row together."],[8401,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led the people in prayer. When he finished, he saw a man standing alone praying behind the people, so he said: 'O you who pray alone, why did you not join the row or take the hand of a man from the people and stand in a row with him? For there is no prayer for you alone, so repeat your prayer.'"],[8402,"He used to raise his hands with the takbir in every prayer, and over funerals."],[8403,"There is no zakat on fewer than five camels, no zakat on less than five awaq, and no zakat on less than five awsuq."],[8404,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[8405,"The best of the qualities of the fasting person is the siwak."],[8406,"When a young man asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about kissing (while fasting), he forbade him, but when an old man asked him, he permitted him, and said: 'A young man is not like an old man.'"],[8407,"Fatima said when the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away: 'O father, to his Lord how near he is; O father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode; O father, to Gabriel we announce his passing.'"],[8408,"Qasamah was a custom of the Jahiliyyah, and the Messenger of God ﷺ upheld it so that people would refrain from shedding blood."],[8409,"I enjoin upon you two things: Do not ask for an office, for if you are given it after asking, you will be left to it alone; but if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it. And if you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath."],[8410,"An oath is only either a sin or regret."],[8411,"Whoever hoards food for forty days, waiting for a rise in prices, has disowned God and God has disowned him. And any people in whose gathering a hungry person remains, the protection of God is withdrawn from them."],[8412,"What would the Messenger of God ﷺ say when he stood to pray? And with what would he begin? She said: He would say Allahu Akbar ten times, praise God ten times, glorify God ten times, declare God’s oneness ten times, seek forgiveness ten times, and say: ‘O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me’ ten times, and he would say: ‘O God, I seek refuge in You from distress on the Day of Reckoning’ ten times."],[8413,"Any man who gives another man safety for his life and then kills him, he will be made to carry the banner of treachery on the Day of Resurrection."],[8414,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to follow funerals, and he commanded us to accept invitations, and the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from drinking from vessels of gold."],[8415,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform ghusl from janabah with a sa‘, and ‘A’ishah likewise."],[8416,"That the Prophet ﷺ commanded them on the day of Hudaybiyyah that seven of them should share in a camel."],[8417,"‘Ali b. Abi Talib had eighteen merits; if he had only one of them he would have been saved by it. Indeed he had thirteen merits that no one in this ummah possessed."],[8418,"I have been commanded to fight the oath-breakers, the deviators, and the renegades."],[8419,"Whomever I am his mawla, ‘Ali is his mawla."],[8420,"Every people has a source of support, and the source of support for Quraysh is their clients."],[8421,"Nothing prevented us from witnessing Badr, I and my father Hisl, who is al-Yamān, except that the disbelievers of Quraysh intercepted us while we were heading to the Prophet ﷺ. They said, “You intend to go to Muḥammad.” We said, “We do not intend him.” They said, “Then give us a covenant and a solemn pledge that you will not fight alongside him.” So we gave it to them, and they let us go. Then we came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of the news. He said, “We will fulfill their covenant, and we will seek Allah’s help against them. Go back to Madinah.” So we returned."],[8422,"Abū Dharr al-Ghifārī stood before Banū Ghifār and said: “O Banū Ghifār, the truthful one who is believed ﷺ informed me that people will be gathered in three groups: a group who are fed, clothed, and mounted; a group who walk and hasten; and a group whom the angels urge on and the Fire drives from behind them.” They said: “We know these and these, but what about those who walk and hasten?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Affliction will be cast upon beasts of burden, and no riding animal will remain, until one of you gives another his well-equipped garden in exchange for an old camel with a saddle, and he will not find one.”"],[8423,"Whoever gives a fasting person something to break his fast with will have a reward like his, without diminishing the fasting person’s reward in any way."],[8424,"I saw myself while we were perfuming the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with ghāliyah, then he entered iḥrām."],[8425,"Let no one enter your house except a pious person, and do not entrust your favor except to a believer."],[8426,"I am jealous, and Allah is more jealous than I, and Allah loves the jealous among His servants."],[8427,"A servant may call upon Allah while He loves him, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: “O Jibrīl, fulfill this need of My servant but delay it, for I love to keep hearing his voice.” And a servant may call upon Allah while He hates him, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: “O Jibrīl, fulfill this need of My servant and hasten it, for I dislike hearing his voice.”"],[8428,"No man is punished for a sin except that Allah makes it an expiation for the sin he committed."],[8429,"Whoever finds his property in the war booty before it is distributed is more entitled to it, but if he finds it after it has been distributed, he has no right to it."],[8430,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about the Bayt al-Maqdis.” He said: “Go to it and pray in it.” I said: “How, when the Byzantines are between us and it?” He said: “Send oil to it to be used in its lamps.”"],[8431,"Every intoxicant is forbidden, and Allah has pledged that whoever drinks an intoxicant will be given to drink from the ṭīnat al-khabāl on the Day of Resurrection, the extract of the people of the Fire."],[8432,"Your Lord said: 'Whoever I take his two precious ones (eyes), then he remains patient and seeks reward, his recompense is Paradise.'"],[8433,"Were it not that I would impose hardship on my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer."],[8434,"Line up in rows as the angels line up before their Lord. They said: 'O Messenger of God, how do the angels line up before their Lord?' He said: 'They complete the rows and join their shoulders.'"],[8435,"Was the Messenger of God ﷺ in the habit of oiling his hair and combing it? She said: 'If we had found oil, we would have used it as a condiment. I saw the family of Muhammad, and at that time they were nine households, having nothing but a saa' of barley. And the Messenger of God ﷺ departed from this world without ever being satiated with red wheat.'"],[8436,"Whoever recites ten verses in a night, two qintars of reward are written for him, and a qintar is better than the world and all that is in it. So when the Day of Resurrection comes, your Lord says: 'Recite and ascend; for each verse a degree,' until he comes to the last verse he has with him. Your Lord says to the servant: 'Take hold,' and the servant opens his hand. He says: 'My Lord, You know best.' He says: 'By this is eternity, and by this is bliss.'"],[8437,"Do you know upon whom the Fire is forbidden? They said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'Upon the gentle, the mild, the easy-going, the close one.'"],[8438,"We were with Umar b. al-Khattab, between Makkah and Madinah, and I had sharp eyesight. We looked for the new moon, and no one saw it except me. I began to say: 'Yes, don't you see it?' Then Umar said: 'I will see it while reclining on my bed.' Then he began to tell us about the people of Badr, and said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ showed us the places where the people of Badr would be slain the day before, saying: \"This is the place where so-and-so will be slain tomorrow, and this is the place where so-and-so will be slain tomorrow, God willing.\"' Then Umar said: 'By the One who sent him with the truth, they did not miss the boundaries that the Messenger of God ﷺ had set.' He said: 'They were thrown into a well, one on top of another.' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ went until he reached them and said: \"O so-and-so son of so-and-so, and O so-and-so son of so-and-so, did you find what God and His Messenger promised you to be true? For I have found what God promised me to be true.\"' Umar said: 'O Messenger of God, how do you speak to bodies with no souls?' He said: 'You are not more able to hear what I say than they are, except that they cannot reply at all.'"],[8439,"Bilal was commanded to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd."],[8440,"He would wake up in a state of janabah without having had a wet dream, then he would perform ghusl and fast."],[8441,"Whoever would be pleased to meet God, Mighty and Majestic, tomorrow as a Muslim, let him be diligent in the five prayers when the call is given for them."],[8442,"When Ali came to Basra, he came to the house and said: 'Is Abu Muslim here?' We said: 'Yes.' He came out to him, and Ali said to him: 'Will you not help us in this matter?' He said: 'Yes. O slave girl, bring me that sword.' She brought his sword, and it was a sword of wood. Abu Muslim said to him: 'Your cousin, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, enjoined me that when there is a fitnah among the Muslims, I should take a sword of wood.' Ali turned away angrily and said: 'We have no need of you or your sword.'"],[8443,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: 'Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar.'"],[8444,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."],[8445,"The Hour will not be established until people vie with one another in (building) mosques."],[8446,"Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the falsest of speech. And do not spy, and do not hate one another, and do not envy one another, but be, O servants of Allah, brothers."],[8447,"Today a gap has been opened in the barrier of Gog and Magog like this—and he made a circle with his thumb and index finger, (meaning) ninety (miles)."],[8448,"The Prophet ﷺ heard him while he was in a riding party saying, 'By my father!' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Whoever swears, let him swear by Allah or be silent.'"],[8449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to bring out the secluded women to the two Eid (prayers). It was said, 'And the menstruating women?' He said: 'Let them witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims.' A woman said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what if one of us does not have a garment?' He said: 'Let her companion clothe her from part of her garment.'"],[8450,"The fortunate one is he who was fortunate in his mother's womb."],[8451,"The people of two religions do not inherit from one another."],[8452,"He used to apply perfume before entering ihram."],[8453,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque on Friday and found Abu Isra'il standing in the sun. He asked about him, and they said, 'He vowed to stand and not sit, not speak, not seek shade, and not break his fast.' He said: 'Let him sit, speak, seek shade, and not break his fast.'"],[8454,"When 'Ali was killed, al-Hasan b. 'Ali stood up and praised and extolled Allah, then said: 'Now then, by Allah, you have killed tonight a man on a night in which the Qur'an was revealed, and in which Joshua b. Nun, the servant of Moses, was killed, and in which Jesus son of Mary was raised up. No one before him surpassed him, and no one after him reached him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send him on a military expedition with Gabriel on his right and Michael on his left. By Allah, he left neither gold nor silver except seven hundred or eight hundred dirhams, which he had set aside to purchase a servant.'"],[8455,"We were reciting the Qur'an to one another at the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one contesting with a verse and another with a verse. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out looking as if pomegranate seeds had been burst on his face, and said: 'O you people, is it for this that you were sent, or were you commanded to do this? Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking one another's necks.'"],[8456,"Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, something similar. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Suwayd; 'Abd al-Rahman was alone in transmitting it."],[8457,"The Prophet ﷺ died when he was sixty-five years old."],[8458,"He used to give one taslim."],[8459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the two doorposts while we were in the house and said, \"O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, is there anyone among you from other than yourselves?\" They said, \"A son of a sister of ours.\" He said, \"The son of a people's sister is one of them.\" Then he said, \"O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, when distress, hardship, or difficulty befalls you, say: Allah, Allah, our Lord, He has no partner.\""],[8460,"Whoever says: 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great,' Allah plants for him a tree in Paradise for each one of them."],[8461,"Whoever builds a mosque for the sake of Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise, and if he dies that day he is forgiven. And whoever digs a grave for the sake of Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise, and if he dies that day he is forgiven."],[8462,"Whoever shelters an orphan or two orphans, then remains patient and seeks reward, I and he will be in Paradise like these two,\" and he moved his forefinger and middle finger."],[8463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded placing the palms and setting the feet upright in prayer."],[8464,"The Commander of the Faithful 'Umar wrote to me when Syria had laid down its burdens, with wheat and honey, that I should march to India, and I was averse to that. He said: India in our minds that day was Basra. A man said: Fear Allah, O Abu Sulayman, for trials have appeared. He said: And Ibn al-Khattab is alive? They will only occur after him, while the people are at Dhi Billiyan, at such-and-such a place and such-and-such a place. A man will look and think whether he can find a place where nothing like what has befallen his current place of trial and evil has occurred, and he will not find it. Those are the days that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned before the Hour, the days of harj. So seek refuge with Allah that those days may overtake me and you."],[8465,"Is any of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an every night?\" They said, \"Who can bear that or is able to do that?\" He said, \"Recite: 'Say: He is Allah, the One.'\""],[8466,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped, gave the cupper his wage, and used a nasal medicament."],[8467,"Verses were abrogated from this surah, meaning Surat al-Ma'idah: the verse of the necklaces, and His saying: 'So judge between them or turn away from them.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given a choice: if he wished he could judge between them, and if he wished he could turn away from them and return them to their own rulings. Then it was revealed: 'And judge between them by what Allah has revealed, and do not follow their desires.' He was commanded to judge between them according to our Book."],[8468,"There is no zakah on less than five awsuq; no zakah on less than five awaq; and no zakah on less than five camels."],[8469,"He had on his hand a ring of silver, its bezel was of silver, and its inscription was: Muhammad, Messenger of God. The Prophet ﷺ used to turn its bezel to the inside of his palm. Then he entered Hafsah's house and threw it away in aversion or out of aversion."],[8470,"Whoever has hair, let him honor it."],[8471,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the Hajj in ifrad (i.e., without combining it with 'umrah)."],[8472,"\"Whoever prays over a funeral gets a qirat, and whoever sits until it is buried gets two qirats.\" They said, \"Like these qirats of ours?\" He said, \"No, rather like (the mountain of) Uhud.\""],[8473,"Two women came to Dawud ﷺ , each claiming the remaining child, as a wolf had eaten one of their two sons. He judged in favor of the elder one. When they went out, they came to Sulayman, who asked, \"How did he judge between you?\" They told him. He said, \"Bring me a knife.\" Abu Hurayrah said: The first time I heard the word \"knife\" was from the Messenger of God ﷺ; we used to call it al-mudyah. The younger woman said, \"Why?\" He said, \"To split him between you two.\" She said, \"Give him to her.\" The elder woman said, \"Split him between us.\" So Sulayman judged in favor of the younger woman. They said, \"If he were your son, you would not agree to split him.\""],[8474,"Woman was created from a rib. If you try to straighten it, you will break it. So deal gently with her, and you will live with her."],[8475,"When one of you takes, let him take with his right hand; when he gives, let him give with his right hand; when he eats, let him eat with his right hand; and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand. For Satan takes with his left hand, gives with his left hand, eats with his left hand, and drinks with his left hand."],[8476,"There will be rulers who lie and oppress. Whoever believes their lies and helps them in their oppression is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin. Whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their oppression is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Basin."],[8477,"\"Fasting is for Me, and I reward it.\" The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks his fast, he rejoices, and when he meets God, He will reward him and he will rejoice. \"The change in the mouth of the fasting person is more pleasant to God than the scent of musk.\""],[8478,"The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; this ummah comprises eighty rows of them."],[8479,"I was sitting beside Ibn 'Umar when a man came to him and said, \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, tell me about 'Uthman: did he witness Badr?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Did he witness the Pledge of al-Ridwan?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Was he among those who turned away on the day the two armies met?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The man turned away. Then another man said to 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, \"This man will now go and tell people that you have disparaged 'Uthman.\" He said, \"Did I do that?\" He said, \"That is what he claims.\" So he said, \"Bring the man back to me.\" They brought him back, and he said, \"Do you know what I said to you?\" The man said, \"I asked you: Did 'Uthman witness Badr? You said no. I asked you: Did he witness the Pledge of al-Ridwan? You said no. I asked you: Was he among those who turned away on the day the two armies met? You said yes.\" Then 'Abd Allah said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of Badr: \"'Uthman has been detained in the service of God and His Messenger,\" and the Messenger of God ﷺ allotted a share for him, and he did not allot a share for anyone else who was absent. And on the day of the Pledge of al-Ridwan, the Messenger of God ﷺ sent 'Uthman to Makkah to seek permission from them regarding the sacrificial animals and entering Makkah. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ took the Pledge of al-Ridwan while he intended to enter Makkah, and he said: \"'Uthman is in the service of God and His Messenger, so I pledge God on his behalf,\" and he struck one of his hands upon the other. And God said: \"Indeed, those of you who turned back on the day the two armies met, it was Satan who caused them to slip because of some of what they had earned, but God has already pardoned them.\" So go, for God has pardoned. Now go and do your utmost against me."],[8480,"Whoever among you is able to ensure that nothing comes between him and Paradise—[even] a handful of blood that he sheds as if slaughtering a chicken, every time it presents itself at one of the gates of Paradise, it comes between him and it—and whoever among you is able to put nothing in his belly except what is good, for the first part of a person to putrefy is his belly."],[8481,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited celibacy."],[8482,"God cursed seven of His creation from above His seven heavens, and He repeated the curse upon one of them three times, and He cursed each of them with a curse sufficient for him. He said: Cursed is the one who does the deed of the people of Lot; cursed is the one who does the deed of the people of Lot; cursed is the one who does the deed of the people of Lot; cursed is the one who sacrifices to other than God; cursed is the one who comes upon any of the beasts; cursed is the one who is undutiful to his parents; cursed is the one who joins a woman and her daughter; cursed is the one who alters the boundaries of land; cursed is the one who claims affiliation to other than his patrons."],[8483,"Hasten to do good deeds before six things: what are you waiting for except wealth that causes tyranny, or an illness that corrupts, or old age that debilitates, or a death that comes suddenly, or the Dajjal—and he is an evil awaited—or the Hour, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter."],[8484,"I saw Muʿāwiya b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar performing ablution: he rinsed his mouth, snuffed water, washed his face three times, washed his hands three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet three times. Then he said: This is how I saw ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar perform ablution. And ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar said: This is how I saw ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān perform ablution. And ʿUthmān said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution."],[8485,"God is more intensely joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you who fell upon his camel after he had lost it in a desolate land."],[8486,"A servant is born a believer, lives a believer, and dies a believer; and a servant is born a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a disbeliever; and a servant works for a period of his life with felicity, then what was written for him overtakes him, and he dies a disbeliever; and a servant works for a period of his life with wretchedness, then what was written for him overtakes him, and he dies felicitous."],[8487,"The Messenger of God ﷺ freed me and made my manumission my dower."],[8488,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I was weeping. He said: O daughter of Ḥuyayy, what makes you weep? She said: It has reached me that ʿĀʾisha and Ḥafṣa disparage me and say: We are better than her; we are the daughters of the paternal cousin of the Messenger of God ﷺ and his wives. He said: Did you not say: How can you two be better than me when my father is Hārūn, my uncle is Mūsā, and my husband is Muḥammad?"],[8489,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while in front of me were four thousand date-pits with which I was glorifying God. He said: O daughter of Ḥuyayy, what is this? I said: I am glorifying God with them. He said: I have glorified God since I stood at your head more than this. I said: Teach me, O Messenger of God. He said: Say: Glory be to God by the number of everything He has created."],[8490,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded in three white cotton garments from Sahul."],[8491,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited three hours in which we pray or bury our dead: when the sun rises shining until it ascends, when the midday heat stands still, and when it declines for its setting. I said to ʿUqba: Is burial done at night? He said: Yes; Abū Bakr was buried at night."],[8492,"Give the obligatory shares to those entitled to them. Whatever remains after the obligatory shares is for the nearest male relative."],[8493,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urged charity, and a man said, \"I have a dinar.\" He said, \"Spend it on yourself.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"Spend it on your servant.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"You know best.\""],[8494,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[8495,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, and give zakah. If they do that, their blood and property are protected from me, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[8496,"When Allah revealed to His Prophet: \"And warn your closest kinsfolk,\" the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"O assembly of Quraysh, save yourselves from the Fire. O assembly of Banu Abd Manaf, save yourselves from the Fire. O assembly of Banu Ka'b b. Lu'ayy, save yourselves from the Fire. O assembly of Banu Hashim, save yourselves from the Fire. O Fatimah bt. Muhammad, save yourself from the Fire, for I can avail you nothing before Allah, except that you have ties of kinship and I will uphold them.\""],[8497,"The demise of my ummah will be through stabbing and the plague. It was said, \"What is the plague, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"A piercing of your enemies from among the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom.\""],[8498,"Indeed Allah has placed this matter among you and you are its guardians. It will not cease to be among you as long as you do not perform deeds that cause it to be taken from you. If you do that, Allah will set upon you the worst of His creation, and they will strip you as a branch is stripped."],[8499,"He used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: \"Alif Lam Mim. The Prostration\" and \"Has there come upon man.\""],[8500,"Regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: \"He is worthy of fear and worthy of forgiveness,\" he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah said: I am worthy to be feared, so no partner is associated with Me, and I am worthy, for the one who fears associating partners with Me, to forgive him.\""],[8501,"Whoever Allah promises a reward for an action, He will fulfill it for him; and whoever He promises punishment for an action, He has the choice."],[8502,"The example of the sinner among people is like a people who boarded a ship at sea and divided it, each man having a place. One of them went to his place and made a hole in it. They said, \"What is wrong with him? Does he intend to destroy us?\" He said, \"What concern is it of you? I am in my own place.\" He said: \"If they leave him, they will drown and he will drown with them; but if they seize his hand, they will be saved and he will be saved with them. Thus is the example of the sinner.\""],[8503,"My intercession is for the people of major sins among my ummah."],[8504,"My uncle and I went out to Madinah, and I was stricken with severe hunger. I entered a garden and found crops that had ripened, so I began to rub them and eat. The owner of the garden came and beat me and took my cloak. I complained about him to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'You did not feed him when he was hungry, nor discipline him when he was ignorant. Return his cloak to him.'"],[8505,"To swear ten oaths that Ibn Sayyad is the Dajjal is more beloved to me than to swear once that he is not, because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to his mother and said: 'Ask her how long she carried him.' I asked her, and she said: 'Twelve months.' He said: 'Ask her how his cry was when he was born.' She said: 'The cry of a one-month-old infant.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'I have hidden something for you; what is it?' He said: 'A bone of a reddish sheep.' He kept trying to say 'smoke,' saying: 'dukh, dukh.' The Prophet said: 'Be off! You will never surpass the decree.'"],[8506,"If a pilgrim in ihram cannot find a waist-wrapper, he may wear trousers; and if he cannot find sandals, he may wear leather socks."],[8507,"When the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, the whiteness of his armpits could be seen. Then when he said the salam, he turned his face to his right until the whiteness of his cheek was seen, and to his left."],[8508,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bt. Jahsh, he invited the people and they ate. Then he made as if to get up, so those who were going to leave got up, but a group remained seated. When he saw that, he got up, and then they left after that. I informed the Prophet ﷺ, and he came. I went to enter, but he let down the veil between me and him.\" He said: \"And the verse of the veil was revealed. He recited it: 'Then when you have eaten, disperse.'"],[8509,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he went to relieve himself. Then he gestured to me, so I went and brought him water. He was wearing a Syrian jubba that had no sleeves, and he threw it over his shoulder. He said: 'Pour water on me.' So I poured water on him, and he performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks. Thus it became a sunnah: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident one day and one night."],[8510,"A man came to 'Abd Allah and said: 'There is no grudge between me and any of the Arabs. I passed by the mosque of Banu Hanifah, and they were sitting affirming Musaylimah.' 'Abd Allah sent for them and they were brought. He asked them to repent, except Ibn al-Nawwahah. He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Were it not that you are a messenger, I would strike your neck. But today you are not a messenger. Stand, O Qarazah, and strike his neck.\"' So Qarazah b. Ka'b stood and struck his neck in the market. And he said: 'Whoever wants to look at Ibn al-Nawwahah, let him look in the market.'"],[8511,"The best characteristic of the fasting person is the siwak."],[8512,"When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me."],[8513,"The prayer of al-Adha is two rak'ahs, the prayer of al-Fitr is two rak'ahs, the prayer of the traveler is two rak'ahs, and the Friday prayer is two rak'ahs, complete and not shortened, on the tongue of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8514,"I tell you a hadith that perhaps Allah will benefit you by: Know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Hajj and 'Umrah, and no Qur'an was revealed to abrogate it, and he did not forbid it until he died.\" A man said by his own opinion whatever he wished."],[8515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: 'Your brother the Negus has died, so stand and pray for him.' So we stood and lined up for him as one lines up for a deceased person, and we prayed for him as one prays for a deceased person."],[8516,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to sleep in his prostration, and we would not recognize his sleep except by his breathing; then he would stand up in his prayer."],[8517,"Whoever sells wine, let him also slaughter pigs."],[8518,"Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog nor a livestock dog, his reward decreases every day by a qirat.\" Then he mentioned that they were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and they passed by the grave of Abu Righal. He said: \"This is the grave of Abu Righal, and he is the father of Thaqif. He was a man from Thamud. His dwelling was within the sanctuary, and when God destroyed his people with what He destroyed them, he was protected by his place in the sanctuary. He went out until when he reached here he died and was buried, and a branch of gold was buried with him.\" So we hastened to it and extracted it."],[8519,"Ali commanded Ammar to ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about prostatic fluid, and he said: \"He should wash his private parts and perform ablution.\""],[8520,"When Ka'b b. Malik repented and God accepted his repentance, he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, God saved me only through truthfulness. Part of my repentance is that I will never speak a lie, and that I will divest myself of my wealth for God and His Messenger.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Keep some of your wealth; that is better for you.\" Ka'b b. Malik said: \"Then I will keep my share from Khaybar.\""],[8521,"His brothers complained about him to the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: \"He squanders his wealth and is extravagant with it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"O Qays, what is the matter with your brothers complaining about you? They claim that you squander your wealth and are extravagant with it.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I take my share of the fruits and spend it in the way of God and on those who accompany me.\" He said: \"Then the Messenger of God ﷺ struck his chest and said: 'Spend, and God will spend on you' three times.\" After that, I went out in the way of God with a mount. He said: \"I am the wealthiest and most prosperous of my household today.\""],[8522,"The one who pretends to have been given what he has not been given is like one who wears two garments of falsehood."],[8523,"Humaid b. al-Aswad narrated to us, from Hisham b. Urwa, from Fatima bt. al-Mundhir, from Asma' bt. Abi Bakr, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[8524,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed for rain, he would say: 'O God, give us a drink that is ample, gentle, and beneficial, by which You satisfy the wealth and the souls, a pleasant, wholesome, covering, enveloping rain, with which You shower our desert and our settled areas, by which You send down blessings of the heavens and bring forth for us blessings of the earth, and make us among the thankful for it. You are the Hearer of supplication.' And when he prayed against locusts, he said: 'O God, kill their large ones, destroy their small ones, spoil their eggs, and cut off their offspring.'"],[8525,"A man shall not sell over the sale of his brother, nor propose over the proposal of his brother. Do not bid against each other to raise prices, and a settled person shall not sell on behalf of a nomad. A woman shall not ask for the divorce of her sister in order to empty her vessel, for she will have only what is destined for her. Do not leave the udders of camels and sheep unmilked to deceive buyers. Whoever buys such an animal has the choice between two options: if he returns it, he must return with it a saa' of dates."],[8526,"God has forbidden the singing girl, her sale, her price, her teaching, and listening to her."],[8527,"O Messenger of God, one of us may have thoughts about something concerning the Lord, such that falling from the sky to the earth would be dearer to him than speaking of it. He said: 'Have you found that?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'That is pure faith.'"],[8528,"I placed some dates before the Prophet ﷺ, and they began eating two at a time, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not eat two at a time."],[8529,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed in the house of Umm Salamah on a green mat. She sprinkled it with water, and he prayed on it, and they prayed behind him."],[8530,"She brought a gift to the Prophet ﷺ, but his wives refused to accept it, saying: We will not take it. So the Prophet ﷺ ordered them, and they took it. Then he granted her a valley, and Abdullah b. Jahsh bought it from Hasan b. Ali."],[8531,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[8532,"Abu Isra'il vowed to stand in the sun from daytime until night and not speak, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to sit down and speak."],[8533,"Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of God."],[8534,"The imam is responsible, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted. O God, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins."],[8535,"Whoever eats from this tree should not approach our mosques."],[8536,"We were carrying bricks for the construction of the mosque, one brick at a time, while Ammar was carrying two bricks at a time. The Messenger of God ﷺ dusted off his shoulders and said: Woe to you, O son of Sumayyah! The transgressing party will kill you."],[8537,"Whoever intercedes to prevent one of the limits set by God has opposed God in His dominion. Whoever assists in a dispute without knowing whether it is true or false is under God's wrath until he withdraws. Whoever walks with a people thinking he is a witness while he is not is like a false witness. Whoever claims to have seen a dream falsely will be tasked with tying a knot between two barley grains. Reviling a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[8538,"Quraysh came to Abu Talib and said: O Abu Talib, your nephew comes to us in our Kaaba and our gathering and makes us hear what hurts us. If you see fit to restrain him from us, then do so. He said to me: O Aqil, find your cousin for me. So I brought him out from one of the ravines of the mountain pass of Abu Talib—or he said: one of the ravines of Abu Talib; Ibrahim b. Abi Suwayd was uncertain—and he came walking with me, seeking shade with all his effort but unable to find any until he reached Abu Talib. Abu Talib said to him: O nephew, by God, I did not know that you were disobedient to me. Your people have come claiming that you go to them in their Kaaba and their gathering and make them hear what hurts them. I think you should refrain from them. He raised his eyes to the sky and said: By God, I am no more able to abandon what I have been sent with than one of you could ignite a flame of fire from this sun. Abu Talib said: By God, he has never lied. Go back rightly guided."],[8539,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray while traveling on his mount, wherever it turned, gesturing with his head, and he made the prostration lower than the bowing."],[8540,"It was forbidden to drink from the mouth of a waterskin."],[8541,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked about the Hour. He [Anas] said: The prayer was about to begin, so the Prophet ﷺ stood and prayed. Then the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Where is the one who asked about the Hour?' He said to him, 'What have you prepared for it?' He replied, 'I have not prepared for it any great deed or prayer, except that I love Allah and His Messenger.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A person will be with those whom he loves.' Anas said, 'I never saw the Muslims rejoice over anything after [the coming of] Islam as much as they rejoiced over this.'"],[8542,"The best of deeds is prayer at the beginning of its time."],[8543,"Some cloaks were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he distributed them among his companions. My father Makhramah said, 'Let us go to him; perhaps he will give us something from them.' My father came to the door and said, 'Is he here?' The Prophet ﷺ heard his voice and came out with a cloak, and it was as if I could see him showing my father the fine qualities of the cloak, saying, 'I kept this for you, I kept this for you.' I said to my father, 'Why did the Prophet ﷺ do this for Makhramah?' He said, 'He used to be wary of his tongue.'"],[8544,"Umarah b. Qurs al-Laythi went on a military expedition of his and stayed in it as long as Allah willed. Then he returned until he was near al-Ahwaz, where he heard the call to prayer. He said, 'By Allah, I have not attended prayer with a congregation of Muslims for a long time.' He headed toward the call, intending to pray, and found himself among the Azariqah. They said to him, 'What has brought you here, O enemy of Allah?' He said, 'Are you not my brothers?' They said, 'You are a brother of Satan, and we will surely kill you.' He said, 'Will you not accept from me what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted?' They said, 'What did he accept from you?' He said, 'I came to him as a disbeliever, and I testified that there is no god but Allah and that he is the Messenger of Allah, and he let me go.' They seized him and killed him."],[8545,"Increase in remembering the destroyer of pleasures, for no one remembers it in times of hardship except that Allah widens things for him, and no one remembers it in times of ease except that it narrows things upon him."],[8546,"Beware of oppression, for oppression will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of miserliness, for miserliness led astray those before you; it drove them to shed their blood and to make lawful what was forbidden to them."],[8547,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the virtue of 'Say: He is Allah, [who is] One.' He said, '[It is] a third of the Qur'an, or it equals it.'"],[8548,"Indeed, before the Hour there will be tribulations like patches of dark night, during which a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, or a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning. The one sitting during them is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one running. So break your bows, cut your bowstrings, and strike your swords with stones. If one of you is entered upon in his house, let him be like the better of the two sons of Adam."],[8549,"A man freed six of his slaves upon his death, and he had no property other than them. The Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, so he called them, divided them into portions, and drew lots among them. He freed two and kept four in bondage."],[8550,"Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Are you in pain, O Muhammad?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah for you, from every ailment that harms you, and from the evil of every soul or eye. May Allah heal you. In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah for you.'"],[8551,"Whoever fears Allah will enter Paradise: he will not be miserable, he will live and not die, his clothes will not wear out, and his youth will not fade."],[8552,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[8553,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ counting tasbih on his fingers."],[8554,"Extinguish the fire with takbir."],[8555,"The Prophet ﷺ recited over the funeral four times: 'Al-hamdu lillahi rabbi al-'alamin' [Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds]."],[8556,"Whoever touches his private part, ablution becomes obligatory upon him."],[8557,"I asked Anas b. Malik about wiping over the leather socks, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over them."],[8558,"A child cannot repay his parent, unless he finds him enslaved, buys him, and then sets him free."],[8559,"When two Muslims meet with their swords, both the killer and the killed are in the Fire."],[8560,"Whoever claims a lineage that is not known has disbelieved in Allah, and disowning a lineage, even if it is distant, is disbelief in Allah."],[8561,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade snatching, plundering, animals tied and shot, and eating every fanged beast of prey."],[8562,"Whoever enters the mosque and spits, let him dig a hole and bury it. If he does not, then let him spit in his garment and then take it out."],[8563,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ suffered a wound, I would apply henna to it."],[8564,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw wind or clouds, it would show on his face, and he would turn back and forth. If it rained, he would be pleased and it would leave him. She said: I asked him, and he said: \"I feared it might be a punishment sent upon my Ummah.\" And when he saw rain he would say: \"Mercy.\""],[8565,"Faith is knowledge in the heart, affirmation with the tongue, and action with the limbs."],[8566,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an expedition, and he said: \"Acquire many sandals, for a man remains a rider as long as he wears sandals.\""],[8567,"Delay in payment by a rich man is wrongdoing, and if one is referred to a wealthy man, let him follow up."],[8568,"None of you should withhold surplus water to prevent thereby the growth of herbage."],[8569,"He used to combine Maghrib and Isha when he was in a hurry to travel."],[8570,"It is part of the Sunnah that one of you women should place something on her hands, her feet, her neck, or her ears that will be stripped from her when she is placed on the washing bier."],[8571,"Ma'qil b. Yasar sold a house of his for one hundred thousand. He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Any man who sells a piece of property without need, Allah will send upon it a destroyer who will ruin it.'\""],[8572,"The Imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the Imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins."],[8573,"He forbade the sale of water."],[8574,"If one of the People of the Book greets you, say: 'And upon you.'"],[8575,"Loyalty belongs to the one who frees."],[8576,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken, Fatimah used to uncover her head when a boy entered, but when a man entered she covered it."],[8577,"Indeed, the one addicted to wine, the one disobedient to his parents, and the one who reminds others of his gifts will not enter the enclosure of holiness."],[8578,"I rode to 'Abd Allah b. Unays in Egypt to ask him about the hadith of retribution. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection on a single plain, barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. The farthest of them will hear the voice as the nearest of them hears it. He will say: I am the King. It is not appropriate for anyone from the people of Paradise to enter Paradise while someone from the people of Hell has a claim against him for a slap or more.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how, when we are barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised?\" He said: \"From your deeds.\""],[8579,"O Allah, forgive the pilgrim and the one for whom the pilgrim seeks forgiveness."],[8580,"Whoever is subjected to a detailed reckoning on the Day of Resurrection will perish. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, where then is the word of Allah: 'He will be reckoned with an easy reckoning'?\" He said: \"That is the presentation. Whoever is subjected to a detailed reckoning on the Day of Resurrection will perish.\""],[8581,"She cursed a camel of hers, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"It should not accompany us.\""],[8582,"The next day after being given allegiance, Abu Bakr stood up and addressed the people, saying: \"O people, I have relieved you of your opinion. I am not the best of you, so give allegiance to the best of you.\" They stood up to him and said: \"O successor of the Messenger of Allah, you are, by Allah, the best of us.\" He said: \"O people, people entered Islam willingly and unwillingly, so they are Allah's protected ones and His neighbors. If you can avoid Allah demanding anything of His protection from you, then do so. I have a devil that attends me, so if you see me angry, avoid me. I will not mutilate your hair and skins. O people, check the earnings of your servants, for it is not fitting for flesh grown from unlawful earnings to enter Paradise. Indeed, watch me with your eyes. If I am upright, follow me; if I deviate, correct me. If I obey Allah, obey me; if I disobey Allah, disobey me.\""],[8583,"Indeed, among Gog and Magog a man dies and the least offspring he leaves is a thousand or more. And behind them are nations: Mansik, Tarik, and Taris."],[8584,"He said to those around him: \"Guarantee me six traits and I will guarantee you Paradise.\" I said: \"What are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Prayer, zakat, trustworthiness, chastity, the stomach, and the tongue.\""],[8585,"He prohibited temporary marriage on the day of Khaybar."],[8586,"Abu Bakr asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sitting with his thighs uncovered, and he granted him permission. 'Umar asked permission and he granted him permission while he was in the same state. Then 'Uthman b. 'Affan asked permission, and he reached for his garment and covered his thighs. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is as if you disliked 'Uthman seeing you?\" He said: \"Indeed, 'Uthman is modest and veiled; the angels are shy of him.\""],[8587,"O 'A'ishah, this is the condiment of this."],[8588,"Permission is not granted to the one seeking permission until he begins with the greeting of peace."],[8589,"The Imam is only to be followed. So when he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; and when he says, 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah,' say, 'Al-hamdu lillah.' And when he prays sitting, then pray sitting, all of you."],[8590,"My mother prepared some food and said, 'Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and invite him.' So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke to him secretly. I said, 'My mother has prepared something.' He said to his companions, 'Get up.' Fifty men stood up with him. He sat at the door, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Let in ten at a time.' They ate until they were full, and there remained about as much as before."],[8591,"Regarding the saying of Him, Mighty and Majestic: 'Whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell,' he said: 'If He recompenses him.'"],[8592,"Modesty is part of faith, and faith leads to Paradise. Obscenity is part of harshness, and harshness leads to the Fire."],[8593,"A man came to Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash and said, 'I heard a man say: Allah did not speak to Musa directly.' He said, 'No one says this except a disbeliever. I recited to al-A'mash, and al-A'mash recited to Yahya b. Waththab, and Yahya b. Waththab recited to Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman recited to 'Ali b. Abi Talib, and 'Ali recited from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'And Allah spoke to Musa directly.'"],[8594,"Indeed Allah records for the sick person the best of what he used to do in his health as long as he is in his confinement, and for the traveler the best of what he used to do when he was resident."],[8595,"Seeking the lawful is obligatory upon every Muslim."],[8596,"Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim."],[8597,"O 'Abd al-Rahman, if you swear an oath and then see something else better than it, then expiate for your oath and do that which is better."],[8598,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a funeral procession. He sat beside a grave among them and said: 'Not a day passes upon this grave but that it calls out with a clear, piercing voice: O son of Adam, how have you forgotten me? Do you not know that I am the house of solitude, the house of estrangement, the house of desolation, the house of worms, and the house of constriction, except for the one for whom Allah expands me.' Then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'The grave is either a garden from the gardens of Paradise or a pit from the pits of the Fire.'"],[8599,"Whoever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion."],[8600,"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he departed."],[8601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted from Safiyyah what a man wants from his wife. He said, \"Is she holding us back?\" It was said, \"She has already departed before she menstruated.\" He said, \"Then let her set out.\""],[8602,"He forbade that an animal be shot and then eaten, but rather it should be slaughtered."],[8603,"There was a man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whose name was Aswad, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Abyad."],[8604,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ghusl from janabah, he would begin by pouring water over his hands, then he would put them into the vessel, then he would wash his private part and what the sexual act had touched, then he would perform wudu as for prayer, then he would pour three handfuls of water over his head, running his fingers through the roots of his hair, then he would pour water over his body, then he would wash his feet when he finished."],[8605,"If I were to stone anyone without evidence, I would stone so-and-so because of what has appeared from her of suspicion in her appearance, her speech, and those who enter upon her."],[8606,"These character traits are from Allah. Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him a good character, and whomever He intends evil for, He grants him an evil one."],[8607,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal, he comes out of his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him."],[8608,"Whoever changes his religion, kill him."],[8609,"He said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"What do you think of those who believe in you but have not seen you, and affirm you but have not seen you?\" He said, \"Glad tidings for them, then glad tidings for them. They are from us, and they are with us.\""],[8610,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who does something to endear herself to her husband. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A provision in this world, but no share in the Hereafter.\" She said, \"What do you think about a woman who sees in her sleep a wet dream, should she perform ghusl?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If she sees the fluid, then let her perform ghusl.\""],[8611,"The thief is not to be punished by amputation except for what reaches the value of a shield."],[8612,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ accepted a pledge, he would accept it upon: bearing witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, establishing prayer, giving zakat, hearing and obeying God and the Messenger, and giving sincere counsel to every Muslim."],[8613,"The daughter of Nu'aym b. 'Abd Allah al-'Adawi came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My daughter's husband has died. She was married to al-Mughira al-Makhzumi, and she has a complaint in her eye. May she apply kohl?\" He said: \"No.\" Then she was silent for a while, then said to him again: \"She has a complaint in her eye. May she apply kohl?\" He said: \"No.\" Then he said: \"It is not lawful for a woman to mourn beyond three days, except for a husband.\""],[8614,"She informed him that Barira was married to a slave. When she was freed, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: \"You have more right to yourself. If you wish, you may remain with your husband; and if you wish, you may separate from him, so long as he has not touched you.\""],[8615,"The one who strives to support his parents in order to suffice them or make them independent of people is in the way of God. And whoever strives to support a spouse or child to suffice them and make them independent of people is in the way of God. And the one who strives to support himself to make himself independent and suffice himself from people is in the way of God. And the one who strives for abundance is in the way of Satan."],[8616,"A man greeted the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and the Prophet ﷺ replied with a gesture. When he finished, he said: \"We used to return the greeting during prayer, but we were forbidden from that.\""],[8617,"The prayer is two rak'ahs at a time, two rak'ahs at a time. You recite the tashahhud in every two rak'ahs, and you humble yourself, show awe, and display neediness. Then you raise your hands—he said: you lift them to your Lord, facing their palms toward your face—and you say: 'O Lord, O Lord.' Whoever does not do that, his prayer is deficient."],[8618,"Preserve the love of your father; do not cut it off, lest God extinguish your light."],[8619,"Whoever supplicates with these five phrases, he will not ask God for anything except that He gives it to him: 'There is no god but God, and God is greatest. There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. There is no god but God, and there is no might nor power except with God.'"],[8620,"God, blessed and exalted, descends in the last three hours that remain of the night. In the first of them He looks into the Book that no one other than Him looks into, and He erases what He wills and confirms. Then in the second hour He looks into the Garden of Eden, which is His dwelling where He resides; none will be with Him therein except the prophets, the martyrs, and the truthful ones. In it is what no eye has seen and what has not crossed the heart of any human. Then He descends in the last hour of the night and says: 'Is there any who seeks forgiveness, that I may forgive him? Is there any who asks, that I may give him? Is there any who calls upon Me, that I may answer him?' until dawn breaks. That is His saying: 'And the Qur'an of dawn; indeed, the Qur'an of dawn is witnessed'—God and His angels witness it."],[8621,"A man came to him and mentioned that his urine had been retained and he was afflicted with a urinary stone. So he taught him a ruqya that he had heard from the Prophet ﷺ: 'Our Lord is God who is in heaven. Sanctified be Your name. Your command is in heaven and earth. As Your mercy is in heaven, so place Your mercy on earth, and forgive us our sins and errors. You are the Lord of the good. Send down healing from Your healing and mercy from Your mercy upon this pain.' So he would be cured. He commanded him to perform the ruqya with it, so he did, and he was cured."],[8622,"Whoever says in the morning: 'So glory be to God when you reach evening and when you rise in the morning' up to 'Thus you will be brought forth,' he will attain what he missed in his day. And whoever says them in the evening will attain what he missed in his night."],[8623,"Some Muslims were with the polytheists, swelling the ranks of the polytheists against the Messenger of God ﷺ. An arrow would be shot and strike one of them, and he would be killed. Then God, majestic is His glory, revealed: 'Those whom the angels take in death while wronging themselves,' they said, 'In what condition were you?' up to His saying: 'and evil is the destination.'"],[8624,"The world is [but] a provision, and the best provision of it is a righteous spouse."],[8625,"The wife of Rifāʿa al-Quraẓī came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I married ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Zubayr, and by God he has nothing with him but the like of this fringe.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Perhaps you want to return to Rifāʿa? No, [not] until he tastes your honey and you taste his honey.\""],[8626,"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt."],[8627,"There is no person who forsakes a Muslim in a situation where his honor is diminished and his sanctity is violated except that God will forsake him in a situation where he would love His help. And there is no person who helps a Muslim in a situation where his honor is diminished and his sanctity is violated except that God will help him in a situation where he would love His help."],[8628,"There will surely come upon the people a time when the truthful one will be disbelieved and the liar will be believed; the trustworthy one will be deemed treacherous and the treacherous one will be entrusted; a man will testify even though he is not asked to testify; a man will swear an oath even though he is not asked to swear; and the happiest of people with the world will be Lukaʿ b. Lukaʿ, one who does not believe in God and His Messenger."],[8629,"Whoever offers an excuse to his brother and he does not excuse him or accept his excuse, upon him is the like of the sin of a tax collector."],[8630,"Whoever honors a Muslim person, he only honors God."],[8631,"When a father looks at his child and it pleases him, the child has [the reward of] freeing a slave. It was said: \"O Messenger of God, even if he looks three hundred and sixty times?\" He said: \"God is greater.\""],[8632,"A child cannot repay his parent, unless he finds him enslaved and then sets him free."],[8633,"A man said: \"O Messenger of God, which charity is best?\" He said: \"That you give it while you are desirous, miserly, hoping for a long life and fearing poverty; and do not delay until, when death approaches you, you say: 'For so-and-so is such-and-such, and for so-and-so is such-and-such,' when it already belongs to him.\""],[8634,"The likeness of one who gives charity at the time of death, or frees a slave at the time of death, is like one who gives a gift after he is full."],[8635,"We prayed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Minā. Then there were two men at the back of the mosque who had not prayed. He summoned them, and their flanks were trembling. He said: \"What prevented you both from praying with us?\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, we had already prayed at our camps.\" He said: \"Do not do that. If you both have prayed at your camps and then you come to the imam and he has not yet prayed, then pray with him, for it will be a supererogatory [prayer] for you both.\""],[8636,"Whoever enters into anything of the Muslims' prices in order to raise it against them, it is incumbent upon Allah to cast him into a great part of the Fire."],[8637,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day while he was standing in the mosque praying, and the door was ajar on the side facing the qiblah, set apart from the mosque. I asked for permission to enter, and when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard my voice, he reached out with his hand and opened the door, then continued his prayer."],[8638,"‘Ali b. Abi Talib entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, so he stood at his side and prayed following his prayer. Then a scorpion came until it reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then it left him and went toward ‘Ali, so he struck it with his sandal until he killed it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw no harm in killing it."],[8639,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the one that has been established."],[8640,"The liar is not the one who goes about reconciling between people and conveys good with his words."],[8641,"If any of you catches the two rak‘ahs on Friday, he has caught the Friday prayer. If he catches one rak‘ah, he should pray another to it. If he does not catch a rak‘ah, he should pray four rak‘ahs."],[8642,"My master accused me, so he made me sit on the fire until my private parts were burned. ‘Umar said to her: Did he see that from you? She said: No. He said: Did you confess anything to him? She said: No. So ‘Umar said: Bring him to me. When ‘Umar saw the man, he said: Do you punish with the punishment of Allah? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I suspected her regarding herself. He said: Did you see that from her? The man said: No. He said: Did she confess it to you? He said: No. He said: By Him in Whose hand is my soul, had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A slave is not to be killed in retaliation from his master, nor a child from his parent, I would have had her retaliated against you. So he brought him out and struck him with one hundred lashes. Then he said: Go, for you are free for the sake of Allah, and you are the freedwoman of Allah and His Messenger. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever is burned with fire or mutilated is free, and he is the freedman of Allah and His Messenger."],[8643,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper. And whoever of your women believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse."],[8644,"He passed by Mu‘adh b. Jabal while he was standing at his door, gesturing with his hand as if he were talking to himself. ‘Abdullah b. ‘Amr said to him: What is the matter with you, O Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman, talking to yourself? He said: What is the matter with me? The enemy of Allah wants to divert me from what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to me: You now toil throughout your life in your house; will you not go out to the gathering? Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever strives in the path of Allah is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever visits a sick person is guaranteed by Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Whoever goes early to the mosque or returns is guaranteed by Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Whoever enters upon a ruler to honor him is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever sits in his house and does not backbite anyone with evil is guaranteed by Allah. So the enemy of Allah wants to make me leave my house for the gathering."],[8645,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque and said: I have burned myself. He said: \"What is that?\" He said: I had intercourse with my wife, and that was in Ramadan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Give charity.\" He said: I have nothing. So he sat down, and a person came driving a donkey carrying food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Where is the one who burned himself just now?\" He said: Here I am. He said: \"Take this and give it in charity.\" He said: To someone more needy than me, O Messenger of Allah? My family has no food. He said: \"Then eat it.\""],[8646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray twelve rak‘ahs at night. When dawn became clear, he prayed two rak‘ahs, then lay down on his right side until he went out to the prayer."],[8647,"I spent the night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood and prayed two rak‘ahs, two rak‘ahs, until he reached ten rak‘ahs, then he performed witr with three rak‘ahs, then he lay down and slept until he snored. His sleep involved snoring. Then the muezzin called him for the morning prayer, and he went out without performing ablution."],[8648,"We mentioned onions and leeks in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and a man said: 'There, what is worse than it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'And what is that?' He said: 'Garlic. Would you forbid it, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'No, but whoever eats it should not approach the mosque until its smell goes away.'"],[8649,"A man from al-Bahrayn came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he did not return his greeting. He had a ring of gold on his hand and a silk jubbah on him. The man left sorrowful, and complained of that to his wife. She said to him: 'Perhaps the Messenger of God ﷺ disliked your jubbah and your ring, so throw them away.' He threw them away, then went early to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he returned his greeting. He said: 'O Messenger of God, I came to you just now and you turned away from me?' He said: 'Indeed, there was in your hand an ember from the Fire.' He said: 'Then I have come with many embers.' He said: 'Indeed, what you came with is no more availing to you than the stones of the harrah, but it is the enjoyment of the life of this world.' He said: 'Then with what should I wear a ring?' He said: 'A band of silver, or iron, or brass.'"],[8650,"A man manumitted in his will six slaves of his, and he had no property other than them. That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he became angry with him. Then he drew lots among them, and brought out one-third of them."],[8651,"Abd Allah b. Abbas passed by Abd Allah b. al-Harith b. Rabi'ah while he was praying with his hair plaited and tied behind him. He stopped over him and did not leave until he untied the knot of his hair. Abd Allah b. al-Harith acknowledged him until he finished untying it, then he sat down. When Ibn al-Harith finished the prayer he came to him and said: 'Why did you do what you did to my head just now?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The likeness of the one who prays with his head tied behind him is like the one who prays wrapped up.\"'"],[8652,"A journey in the evening or in the morning in the path of God is better than what the sun has risen upon and set."],[8653,"'Will the Hour come while the Romans are the most numerous of people?' Amr said: 'Mind what you say.' He said: 'I say to you what I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.' Amr b. al-As said: 'If you say that, indeed among them are four traits: They are the swiftest of people to return after flight, they are the best of people to a poor, needy, and weak person, they are the most forbearing of people at a time of turmoil, and the fourth is good and beautiful: they are the most resistant of people to the oppression of kings.'"],[8654,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform tahajjud after his sleep, and he used to use the tooth-stick before performing tahajjud."],[8655,"Does one of you think that if he stands at night praying until morning he has performed tahajjud? Tahajjud is only prayer after a nap, then prayer after a nap, then prayer after a nap. That was the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[8656,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said while the people were around him: 'Let me not find any one of you, when a matter of mine comes to him while he is reclining on his couch, saying: \"Whatever we find in the Book of God, Mighty and Majestic, we act upon it.\"'"],[8657,"Wickedness is seventy parts: one part is in the jinn and humans, and sixty-nine are in the Berbers."],[8658,"God divided wickedness into seventy parts: He placed in the Berbers sixty-nine parts, and for the two heavy species one part."],[8659,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came one day from a mountain pass after relieving himself, and before us was food that had been touched by fire, on a shield or a leather shield. We invited him to it, and he sat and ate with us, and he did not touch water."],[8660,"When he prostrated, he drew his hands away from his armpits, so much so that I could see the whiteness of his armpits."],[8661,"His grandmother Khayrah, the wife of Ka'b b. Malik, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with some jewelry of hers and said, 'I have given this in charity.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A woman has no authority over her property except with her husband's permission. Did you ask Ka'b?' She said, 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Ka'b and said, 'Did you give Khayrah permission to give this jewelry of hers in charity?' He said, 'Yes.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted it from her."],[8662,"The sun set while we were with 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, and we traveled on. When we saw that it had become dark, we said, 'The prayer.' He remained silent and traveled on until the twilight had disappeared and the stars had come out. Then he dismounted and prayed the two prayers together. Then he said, 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was in a hurry to travel, he prayed like this prayer of mine, saying: He combined them after nightfall.'"],[8663,"He said when they killed 'Uthman b. 'Affan: I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There will be a tribulation; the one who sits during it is better than the one who walks, and the one who walks is better than the one who runs.' It was said to him, 'What do you think if he enters my house upon me or extends his hand to me to kill me?' He said, 'Be like the son of Adam.'"],[8664,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while we were sitting on a carpet, 'There will be a tribulation.' They said, 'What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?' He moved his hand to the carpet and grasped it, saying, 'You will do like this.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned to them one day, 'There will be a tribulation,' but many of the people did not hear him. Mu'adh b. Jabal said, 'Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is saying?' They said, 'What did he say?' He said, 'There will be a tribulation.' They said, 'What should we do, O Messenger of Allah, or how should we act?' He said, 'Return to your first affair.'"],[8665,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray in a single garment, warding off the heat of the ground and its cold with its excess."],[8666,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prostrate on the day of Dhu al-Yadayn."],[8667,"Time will draw near, knowledge will decrease, tribulations will appear, and harj will increase.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is harj?' He said, 'Killing.'"],[8668,"He asked Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, about a man who prays in his home, then comes to the mosque and catches that same prayer. Should he repeat it with the people or not? Abu Ayyub said, 'We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said, \"Yes, he should repeat it, and that is a share of the gathering.\"'"],[8669,"Tamim al-Dari prayed two rak'ahs after 'Umar b. al-Khattab had forbidden prayer after 'Asr. 'Umar came to him and struck him with the whip. Tamim gestured to him to sit while he was still in his prayer. 'Umar sat until Tamim finished, then said to 'Umar, 'Why did you strike me?' He said, 'Because you prayed these two rak'ahs, and I have forbidden them.' He said, 'I prayed them with one better than you, with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' 'Umar said, 'My concern is not with you, O company, but I fear that after you there will come people who will pray between 'Asr and Maghrib until they pass through the hour in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade praying, just as they pray between Zuhr and 'Asr, then they will say, \"We saw so-and-so and so-and-so praying after 'Asr.\"'"],[8670,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me about lost property.' He said, 'Recognize its container and its tying cord, and announce it for a year. If its seeker comes, return it to him; otherwise, spend it.' He said, 'Then tell me about a stray sheep.' He said, 'Take it, for it is yours, or your brother's, or the wolf's.' He said, 'Then tell me about a stray camel.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until his cheeks reddened, then said, 'What do you have to do with it? It has its own shoes and its own water-skin; it goes to water and eats from trees. Leave it until its owner comes to it.'"],[8671,"We presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a ruqyah for fever, and he permitted us to use it, saying, 'They are only covenants.' The ruqyah is: In the name of Allah, a wound of the horn, a salty sea, Qafta."],[8672,"He used to pray wherever he was near the House. 'A'ishah said to him: 'O Messenger of God, sometimes you pray in the place where a menstruating woman passes; why not take a mosque in which to pray?' He said: 'How astonishing you are, O 'A'ishah! Do you not know that a believer's prostration purifies the spot down to seven earths?'"],[8673,"The Messenger of God ﷺ—no one would take his hand and he would pull his hand away from that person until the man himself let go. His knee was never seen protruding beyond the knee of the person sitting with him. And no one spoke to him without him turning his face to him, and he would not turn it away until the man had finished speaking."],[8674,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, one of us commits a sin.' He said: 'It is written against him.' He said: 'Then he seeks forgiveness for it and repents.' He said: 'He is forgiven and it is not recorded against him.' He said: 'Then he returns and sins again.' He said: 'It is written against him.' He said: 'Then he seeks forgiveness for it and repents.' He said: 'He is forgiven and it is not recorded against him, and God does not tire until you tire.'"],[8675,"The killer does not inherit."],[8676,"One day I was in the mosque when Abu Jahl approached and said: 'I vow to God that if I see Muhammad prostrating, I will trample on his neck.' I went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ and entered upon him and told him what Abu Jahl had said. He went out ﷺ angry until he entered the mosque. He hastened to enter through the door, then leaped over the wall. I said: 'This is a day of evil.' I wrapped my lower garment around me, then followed him. I entered while the Messenger of God ﷺ was reciting: 'Read in the name of your Lord who created, created man from a clinging clot.' When he reached the passage about Abu Jahl: 'No! Surely man transgresses, when he sees himself as self-sufficient,' a man said to Abu Jahl: 'O Abu al-Hakam, this is Muhammad.' Abu Jahl said: 'Do you not see what I see? By God, the horizon of the sky has been blocked from me.' When the Messenger of God ﷺ reached the end of the surah, he prostrated."],[8677,"It is obligatory for every Muslim once every seven days to purify himself one day and wash his head."],[8678,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Prophet of God, my daughter is a bride, and she has been afflicted with measles and her hair has fallen out. May I add hair extensions to it?' He said: 'God has cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the woman who asks for it.'"],[8679,"Gabriel came down to me and I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him. After that I saw the Messenger of God praying the noon prayer when the sun declines; sometimes he delayed it in intense heat. He prayed the afternoon prayer while the sun was white and high, so that a man could travel after finishing it to Dhu al-Hulayfah, six miles, before sunset. He prayed the sunset prayer when the sun had set, and the evening prayer when the horizon had darkened. He prayed the dawn prayer while it was still dark, then one day he prayed it when it had become light, then he never returned to praying it when it was light until God took him."],[8680,"A man from the Ansar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'You commanded us to give zakah, the zakah of fitr, and we give it. But what about us if we live to see rulers who do not put it in its proper places?' He said: 'Give it to your rulers, for they will be held accountable for it.'"],[8681,"Some men of Quraysh passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ dragging a sheep of theirs like a donkey. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them: 'Why not take its hide?' They said: 'It is carrion.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Water and qaraz (acacia pods) purify it.'"],[8682,"A group of people entered upon Zayd b. Thabit and said: 'Tell us some of the hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said: 'What shall I tell you? I was his neighbor, and when revelation came down he would send for me, and I would write down the revelation. When we mentioned the Hereafter, he mentioned it with us; when we mentioned this world, he mentioned it with us; and when we mentioned food, he mentioned it with us. So should I tell you all this about him?'"],[8683,"A little understanding is better than much worship. It is enough of understanding for a man that he worships God, and it is enough of ignorance for a man that he is impressed with his own opinion. People are only two: a believer and an ignorant person. So do not harm the believer, and do not keep the company of the ignorant."],[8684,"There is no believer except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection with a Jew or a Christian, saying: 'This is my ransom from the Fire.'"],[8685,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[8686,"You will soon conquer a land in which the qirat is mentioned. Treat its people well, for they have a covenant and a bond of kinship. When you see two men fighting over a place of a brick, leave it."],[8687,"We used to rank the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman—then the people were equal. That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he did not object to it."],[8688,"The dowry of a fornicatress is unlawful, and the price of a dog—except a hunting dog—is unlawful."],[8689,"When the people fled from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud, eleven men from the Ansar remained with him, along with Talha b. Ubayd Allah, while he was ascending the mountain. The polytheists caught up with them, so he said: 'Is there anyone for these?' Talha b. Ubayd Allah said: 'I, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Stay where you are, O Talha.' A man from the Ansar said: 'Then I, O Messenger of Allah,' so he went forth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended with those who remained with him. Then the Ansari was killed and they caught up with him. He said: 'Is there anyone for these?' Talha said the same as his first statement, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him the same as his statement. A man from the Ansar said: 'I, O Messenger of Allah,' so he gave him permission. He fought like the fighting of his companion and the fighting of his companion, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended and his companions ascended. Then he was killed, and they caught up with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept saying the same as his first statement, and Talha would say: 'I, O Messenger of Allah,' but he held him back. A man from the Ansar would ask permission to fight, and he would grant him permission, and he would fight like those before him, until none remained with him except Talha. They surrounded them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who is for these?' Talha said: 'I,' and he fought like the fighting of all those before him. Some of his fingertips were struck, so he said: 'Has!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Talha, if you had said: In the name of Allah, or remembered Allah, the angels would have raised you while the people were watching, until they carried you into the sky.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Talha ascended to their companions while they were gathered."],[8690,"Whoever finds a Muslim in a private fault and conceals it, it is as if he revived a buried infant girl from her grave."],[8691,"I only speak the truth. Those around him said: 'You joke with us, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'I only speak the truth.'"],[8692,"The likeness of this world in comparison to the Hereafter is only as if one of you dips his finger into the sea and then takes it out—so what does it bring back?"],[8693,"A man's standing in the battle row in the cause of Allah is better than sixty years of worship."],[8694,"Islam consists of three hundred and thirteen sacred laws, none of which a person meets Allah with except that he enters Paradise by it."],[8695,"There is no amputation except for a quarter of a dinar."],[8696,"Qays b. Saʿd b. ʿUbādah was appointed commander over us during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. We were struck by severe hunger, so he slaughtered seven fat camels for us. Then we descended to the seacoast, and suddenly we came upon a huge fish. We stayed by it for three days, and we loaded from it as much as we wished of its fat into waterskins and sacks. Then we traveled until we arrived before the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him about that. He said: \"If we knew that we would reach it before it departs, we would have loved to have some of it with us.\""],[8697,"The heart of the son of Adam is only between two fingers of the fingers of the Merciful."],[8698,"There is no shepherd who is entrusted with a flock but will be asked about it on the Day of Resurrection: did he uphold God's command concerning it or neglect it?"],[8699,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and said: \"O people.\" She said: I heard him while I was combing my hair, so I told my hairdresser to stop, then I came forward until I was at the front of the room. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O people, I precede you at the Basin. You will be brought to me in groups, and some of you will be pushed away from me. I will say: 'Where?' It will be said: 'They changed after you.' Then I will say: 'Away! Away!'\""],[8700,"Beware of three things: the slip of a scholar, the argument of a hypocrite, and a worldly life that cuts your necks. As for the slip of a scholar: if he is guided, do not imitate him in your religion; but if he slips, do not cut off your hopes from him. As for the argument of a hypocrite using the Qur'an: the Qur'an has a beacon like the beacon of a road; whatever you recognize, take it, and whatever you reject, refer it to its knowledgeable one. As for a worldly life that cuts your necks: whoever God places richness in his heart, he is truly rich."],[8701,"\"Islam began as something strange and will return to being strange, so glad tidings to the strangers.\" It was said: \"And who are they, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Those who set things right when the people are corrupt.\""],[8702,"There will be a tribulation that is deaf, dumb, and blind. Whoever exposes himself to it, it will overwhelm him. The tongue in it will be like the strike of a sword."],[8703,"From wheat comes wine, from barley comes wine, from raisins comes wine, from dates comes wine, from grapes comes wine, and from honey comes wine. And I forbid every intoxicant."],[8704,"When two men conduct a transaction, each of them retains the option as long as they have not separated and are still together, or one of them gives the other the choice. If one of them gives the other the choice and they transact on that basis, the sale becomes binding. If they separate after transacting, even if neither of them has abandoned the sale, the sale becomes binding."],[8705,"No prophet was sent but that there was a successor after him, and he had two close companions: one who commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and one who spares no effort to corrupt him. Whoever is protected from the evil companion has indeed been protected."],[8706,"I heard Muʿāwiyah, while he had the women's petition, saying: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever adds to his hair something that is not from it is adding falsehood to it.\""],[8707,"\"I fell ill and My servants did not visit Me; I was thirsty and My servants did not give Me drink.\" He said: \"You, O Lord?\" He said: \"Yes. My believing servant falls ill, and if he were visited, it would be for Me. My servant becomes thirsty in the desert, and if he were given drink, it would be for Me.\""],[8708,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: 'Which deeds are best?' He said: 'Faith in God and striving in God's path.' He said: 'Which slaves are best?' He said: 'The most expensive in price and the most precious to their owners.' He said: 'What do you think if I cannot do some of the deed?' He said: 'Then you help a craftsman or make something for an unskilled person.' He said: 'What do you think if I am weak?' He said: 'Then you refrain from harming people.' He said: 'Indeed it is a charity you give to yourself.'"],[8709,"A righteous dream is from God, and a bad dream is from Satan. Whoever sees something he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge from Satan, for it will not harm him, and Satan cannot appear in my form."],[8710,"A man keeps asking people until he comes on the Day of Resurrection with no morsel of flesh on his face. And he said: The sun on the Day of Resurrection will draw near until sweat reaches half the ear. While they are in that state, they will seek help from Adam, and he will say: 'I am not the one for that.' Then Moses, and he will say likewise. Then Muhammad ﷺ, and he will intercede, and judgment will be passed among the creatures. Then he will walk until he takes hold of the ring of Paradise. On that day, God will raise him to a praiseworthy station, for which all the people of the gathering will praise him."],[8711,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Khaybar, selling the Jews a piece of gold for two or three dinars. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Do not sell gold except weight for weight.'"],[8712,"Whichever of you women goes out to the mosque, let her not come near perfume."],[8713,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to sleep while junub, he would wash his private part and then perform ablution as for prayer."],[8714,"No prize is lawful except for a horse or a camel."],[8715,"Whoever frees a slave, the slave's property belongs to him, unless the master stipulates his property, then it belongs to the master."],[8716,"The best charity is that given from surplus wealth. Begin with those you support."],[8717,"If a man says to another, 'O disbeliever,' then disbelief is incumbent upon one of them."],[8718,"Whoever gives the call to prayer for twelve years, Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and sixty good deeds are written for him each day for his call, and thirty good deeds for each iqamah."],[8719,"We slaughtered with the Messenger of God ﷺ a camel for seven people. We said to Jabir: 'And a cow?' He said: 'It is like it.'"],[8720,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed with the people, then he removed his sandals. When the people sensed that, they removed their sandals. When he finished the prayer, he turned to the people and said: \"The angel came to me and informed me that there was some impurity on my sandals. So when one of you comes to the door of the mosque, let him turn over his sandals; if he sees anything in them, let him wipe them, then pray in them if he wishes, or remove them.\""],[8721,"He was on a rooftop and saw the people departing, so he said: \"What is the matter with the people?\" It was said: \"They are departing because of the plague.\" He said: \"O plague, take me.\" His nephew said to him: \"You wish for death, while the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Do not wish for death, for it cuts off deeds and does not leave a man to be asked to return (to life)?'\" He said: \"I fear that six things may overtake me, which I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ mention: injustice in judgment, disregard for blood, leadership of fools, severing family ties, many police, and a people putting forward a man who is not the best of them nor the most knowledgeable, who sings the Quran.\""],[8722,"God does not take away knowledge from you after giving it to you by snatching it away, but He takes the scholars with their knowledge, and the people remain ignorant, so they are asked and they give legal opinions, and they go astray and lead others astray."],[8723,"He forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, mukhabarah, and renting land, and he said: \"Either cultivate it, let your brothers cultivate it, or leave it.\""],[8724,"A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, all my wealth is charity.\" He said: \"Then his parents became poor until they sat with the destitute. Then they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, our son was among the wealthiest of the Ansar, but he gave his wealth as charity, and we became poor until we sat with the destitute.' He said: 'Your son's charity is to be returned to you.' Then they died, and the Messenger of God ﷺ sent to their son: 'Return the charity, for charity is not inherited and not subject to 'umra.'\""],[8725,"There will be a trial in which the safest of people—or he said: the best of people—will be the western army. Ibn al-Hamiq said: \"For that reason I came to you in Egypt.\""],[8726,"He was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition. One night we sought shelter at a high place, and we were struck by severe cold, until we saw men digging holes and entering them, covering themselves with their shields. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that, he said: \"Who will guard us tonight? I will supplicate to God for him with a supplication that will bring him its merit.\" A man stood up and said: \"I will, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Who are you?\" He said: \"I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, the Ansari.\" He said: \"Come closer.\" He came closer, and he took hold of some of his garments, then began the supplication. Abu Rayhanah said: When I heard what the Messenger of God ﷺ was supplicating for the Ansari, I stood up and said: \"I am a man, O Messenger of God.\" He asked me as he had asked him, and said to me: \"Come closer,\" as he had said to him, and he supplicated for me with a supplication less than what he had supplicated for the Ansari. Then he said: \"The Fire is forbidden for an eye that stays awake in the path of God, and the Fire is forbidden for an eye that weeps from fear of God.\""],[8727,"\"Whoever is pleased with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.\" Abu Sa'id said: So I praised, magnified, and testified. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"And another, O Abu Sa'id: God raises its people in Paradise one hundred degrees, between each two degrees as between heaven and earth.\" I said: \"What is that, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Jihad in the path of God.\""],[8728,"The Hour will not come until you fight a people with red faces, small eyes, as if their faces are shields covered with leather."],[8729,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in one of the gardens, and the Dajjal was mentioned. He drew near to his matter, until some of us turned around thinking that he had come upon them."],[8730,"God, Mighty and Majestic, afflicts His servant with illness until it expiates every sin of his."],[8731,"Gentleness in livelihood is better than some trade."],[8732,"He said: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: “Worship God and associate nothing with Him.” He said: O Messenger of God, give me more. He said: “When you do wrong, then do good.” He said: O Messenger of God, give me more. He said: “Be upright, and let your character be good.”"],[8733,"Ghurafa b. al-Harith—who was a Companion and fought with ʿIkrima b. Abī Jahl in Yemen during the Ridda—a Christian from the people of Miṣr called al-Mandaqūn passed by him, and he invited him to Islam. The Christian mentioned the Prophet ﷺ and reviled him. That was brought to ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ, so he sent for them and said: “We have given them a covenant.” Ghurafa said: “God forbid that covenants and pacts should be on condition that they revile us regarding God and His Messenger. We only gave them [the covenant] on condition that they be left alone with their churches, so they may say in them whatever they wish, and that we not burden them with what they cannot bear, and that we fight on their behalf, and that we leave them to their own judgments—unless they come to us so that we judge between them by what God has revealed.” ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ said: “You have spoken the truth.”"],[8734,"There will be after me twelve caliphs, among them Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, who will not remain after me except a short while, and the owner of the millstone of the Arab domain, who will live praiseworthy and die as a martyr.” A man said: “Who is he?” He said: “ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned to ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān and said: “O ʿUthmān, if God clothes you with a shirt and the people want you to take it off, do not take it off. For by God, if you take it off, you will not see Paradise until the camel enters the eye of the needle.”"],[8735,"He used to go out on the day of Fiṭr and Aḍḥā with the short spear, then plant it in front of him until he stood to pray."],[8736,"The jihād of the elderly, the weak, and the woman is the Ḥajj and the ʿUmra."],[8737,"He saw ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar, when he prostrated and raised his head from the first prostration, sit on the tips of his toes and say: “It is from the Sunna.”"],[8738,"He was at the callus of the she-camel of the Messenger of God ﷺ in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage, and when it rose with him, he said: “Labbayka, ʿUmra and Ḥajj.”"],[8739,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought, while he was in the house of Maymūna and Khālid b. al-Walīd was with him, some meat of a ḍabb lizard. Maymūna said: “Tell the Messenger of God ﷺ what it is.” When he was told, he left it. Khālid said to him: “Is it forbidden, O Messenger of God?” He said: “No, but I find it distasteful.” Khālid began to pick the meat from its bones."],[8740,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, and ʿIshāʾ, and slept a short sleep at Minā, then rode to the House and circumambulated it."],[8741,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated two prostrations on the day of Dhū al-Shimālayn after the salutation."],[8742,"He used to kiss while fasting."],[8743,"He asked her about the verse from Sūrat al-Nisāʾ: “If you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphans…” She said: “It was revealed concerning the orphan girl who is with a man and is his partner in wealth, and he marries her for less than what she is given, then treats her badly.”"],[8744,"Regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'They ask you for a ruling concerning women. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning them and what is recited to you in the Book'—it was sent down about a man who has an orphan girl under his care, whose affairs he controls; he does not marry her, but desires her and withholds her until she dies, and then he inherits from her."],[8745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed that I said: 'I will certainly fast all time and stand in prayer all night.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Are you the one who says: I will certainly fast all time and stand in prayer all night as long as I live?' I said: 'I did say that, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said to me: 'You will not be able to do that. So fast and break your fast, pray and sleep, and fast three days of the month, for a good deed is multiplied ten times; that is like fasting all time.' I said: 'I can do better than that.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Fast one day and break your fast one day; that is the fast of Dawud ﷺ, and it is the most balanced fasting.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I can do better than that.' He said: 'There is nothing better than that.'"],[8746,"He heard Mu'awiyah while he was addressing the people in Madinah, saying: 'O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: This is the day of Ashura, and its fasting has not been prescribed for you.' Mu'awiyah said: 'I am fasting, so whoever wishes to fast may fast, and whoever wishes to break his fast may break his fast'—meaning himself by that."],[8747,"When Friday comes, there are angels at every door of the mosque recording the people in order of arrival. When the imam sits down, they fold up the scrolls and come to listen to the remembrance."],[8748,"Were it not that your people are close to disbelief, O Aishah, I would command that the Kabah be demolished, then I would make its door level with the ground and give it two doors."],[8749,"It is honey. By Allah, I will never taste it again. Then when it was Hafsah's day, she said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a need with my father; I have some allowance kept with him, so permit me to go to him.' He permitted her. Then he sent for his slave woman Mariyah and brought her into Hafsah's house, and he lay with her. Hafsah came and found the door locked, so she sat by the door. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, alarmed and with his face dripping sweat, while Hafsah was weeping. He said: 'What makes you weep?' She said: 'You only gave me permission for this. You brought your slave woman into my house and then lay with her on my bed. You would not do such a thing with any of the other wives. By Allah, this is not lawful for you, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'By Allah, you have not spoken the truth. Is she not my slave woman whom Allah has made lawful to me? I call you to witness that she is forbidden to me, seeking your pleasure thereby. Take care not to inform any of the other wives of this, for it is a trust with you.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left, Hafsah knocked on the wall between her and Aishah and said: 'Shall I give you good news? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has forbidden his slave woman to himself, and Allah has relieved us of her.' Aishah said: 'By Allah, I was already suspicious that he was staying because of her.' Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: 'O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful to you?' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: 'And if you two support one another against him'—that is Aishah and Hafsah. They claimed that neither of them used to keep anything secret from the other. I had a brother among the Ansar; when I was present and he was absent at some of his property, I would tell him what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and when I was absent at some of my property [he would tell me]."],[8750,"Abu Talhah came to Umm Sulaym—she is the mother of Anas, and Abu Talhah was his stepfather—and said: 'Do you have anything, O Umm Sulaym? I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was teaching Surah al-Nisa to the people of the Suffah, and he had tied a stone on his stomach from hunger.' She said: 'I had some barley.' She said: 'I ground it, then he sent me to the markets—the markets were their walled gardens—and I brought some firewood, and I made a loaf from it. Then he said: 'Do you have any condiment?' She said: 'I had a small skin of clarified butter, but I do not know whether anything remains in it.' She brought it and squeezed it. He said: 'The squeezing of two is more effective than the squeezing of one.' So they squeezed together and extracted the like of a date. He said: 'She spread it on the loaf, then he called me and said: 'O my son, do you know the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I left him with the people of the Suffah teaching them, so invite him, but do not invite anyone else with him. Be careful not to disgrace me.' So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he saw me, he said: 'Perhaps your father sent you to us?' I said: 'Yes.' He said to the people: 'Go.' They set off that day, and they were eighty men. He took me by the hand. When I drew near the house, I pulled my hand from his, then I went ahead until I reached him and told him the news. He began looking for me in the house and throwing stones at me, saying: 'You have disgraced me before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Then he went out to him and told him the news. He said: 'It will not harm you.' He asked them to sit, then he entered, and we brought the loaf. He said: 'Is there any condiment?' Umm Sulaym said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we had a small skin of butter, and Abu Talhah and I squeezed it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Bring it, for the squeezing of three is more effective than the squeezing of two.' It was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he squeezed it with them, and they extracted from it the like of a date. They wiped the loaf with it; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped it with his hand, then he supplicated for blessing in it, then he said: 'Invite ten at a time for me.' So I invited ten, and they sat and ate until they belched from fullness. They kept entering ten at a time until they were all full. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat, and we ate with him until there was some left over."],[8751,"Whoever Allah wishes good for, He gives him understanding in the religion. These are only the divisions, and Allah gives. There will continue to be in this nation a group standing firm upon the command of Allah; those who oppose them will not harm them until the command of Allah comes while they are victorious over the people."],[8752,"I heard Ibn Abi Sufyan, while in his hand was a lock of hair, saying: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the like of this, saying: The Children of Israel were punished when their women adopted this.'"],[8753,"On the night he was taken on the Night Journey to Iliya, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought two cups: wine and milk. He looked at them, then took the milk. Jibril said to him: 'Praise be to Allah who guided you to the natural disposition. Had you taken the wine, your nation would have gone astray.'"],[8754,"Do not make nabidh in gourds or in vessels smeared with pitch."],[8755,"By Allah, I seek forgiveness from Allah and turn to Him in repentance more than seventy times a day."],[8756,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the prayer has caught the prayer."],[8757,"The likeness of the one who goes early to prayer is like the one who offers a camel as a sacrifice; then the one who comes after him is like the one who offers a cow; then the one who comes after him is like the one who offers a ram; then the one who comes after him is like the one who offers a chicken; then the one who comes after him is like the one who offers an egg."],[8758,"Whatever I forbid you from, avoid it; and whatever I command you to do, do as much of it as you are able. Indeed, those before you were destroyed only because of their excessive questioning and their disagreement with their prophets."],[8759,"I saw 'Amr b. Luhayy b. 'Amir al-Khuza'i dragging his intestines in the Fire; he was the first to dedicate animals to idols."],[8760,"O Allah, I have made a covenant with You, and You will not break it. So any believer whom I have insulted or flogged, make that a means of nearness for him to You on the Day of Resurrection."],[8761,"May Allah destroy the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship."],[8762,"When the muezzin fell silent after the first call of the Fajr prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stand and pray two light rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer, after dawn had become clear. Then he would lie on his right side until the muezzin came to him with the iqamah."],[8763,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Fajr, and believing women would attend with him, wrapped in their cloaks. Then they would return to their homes, and no one would recognize them due to the darkness."],[8764,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate in the prayer: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the punishment of the grave, I seek refuge with You from the trial of the false messiah, and I seek refuge with You from the trials of life and death. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from sin and debt.\" 'A'ishah said: Someone said to him: How often you seek refuge from debt, O Messenger of Allah! He said: \"When a man is in debt, he speaks and lies, and he promises and breaks his promise.\""],[8765,"Whoever misses the 'Asr prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his property."],[8766,"Whoever tells a lie about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[8767,"While I was sleeping, I saw people being presented to me, wearing garments. Some reached the chest and some reached below that. 'Umar b. al-Khattab was presented to me, wearing a garment that he was dragging. They said: What did you interpret it as, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"The religion.\""],[8768,"Umar b. al-Khattab asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while some women of Quraysh were with him, speaking to him and asking him much, their voices loud. When Umar asked permission, they hastened to the screen. Umar entered while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was laughing. Umar said, 'May Allah make your tooth laugh, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I was amazed at these women who were with me; when they heard your voice, they hastened to the screen.' Umar said, 'You were more deserving that they should fear you.' Then Umar said, 'O enemies of your own selves, do you fear me and not fear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' They said, 'Yes, you are harsher and rougher than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, Satan never meets you traveling on a path except that he travels on a path other than your path.'"],[8769,"While I was sleeping, I saw myself at a well, and I drew from it as much as Allah willed. Then Ibn Abi Quhafa drew a bucket or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness—may Allah forgive him. Then it turned into a large bucket, and Umar b. al-Khattab took it. I have never seen a mighty man among the people draw as he drew, until the people struck their camels' resting place."],[8770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was lying across in front of him like a funeral bier, until when he wanted to pray witr, he touched me with his foot and woke me, and I prayed witr."],[8771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he was between my collarbone and my chin. I will never hate the severity of death for anyone ever after what I saw from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8772,"The example of the one who strives in the path of Allah is like the example of the devout worshipper standing in prayer who does not slacken from fasting or prayer until he returns. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no one is wounded in the path of Allah—and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path—except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection with the color the color of blood and the scent the scent of musk. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I wish that I could be killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed.' Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it three times."],[8773,"Iblis said to his Lord, 'By Your might and Your majesty, I will not cease misleading the children of Adam as long as their souls are in them.' His Lord said to him, 'By My might and My majesty, I will not cease forgiving them as long as they seek My forgiveness.'"],[8774,"Hasten to do good deeds before trials like patches of dark night, in which a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, or a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning, selling his religion for a paltry worldly gain."],[8775,"The sun does not rise nor set on a day greater than Friday. There is no creature except that it is terrified on Friday, except the two heavy ones: the jinn and mankind. Angels stand at every gate of the mosque on Friday, recording the first then the next; like the one who brings a camel, like the one who brings a cow, like the one who brings a sheep, like the one who brings a bird, like the one who brings an egg. When the imam comes out, the scrolls are rolled up."],[8776,"How will you be, O Abdullah, when you remain among the dregs of people whose trusts and covenants have become confused, and they differ and are like this?'—and he interlaced his fingers. Abdullah said, 'What do you command me, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Do what you know, leave what you reject, attend to your own self, and leave the common people alone.'"],[8777,"If a slave woman commits adultery, flog her; if she commits adultery, flog her; if she commits adultery, flog her; then sell her, even for a rope of hair."],[8778,"The Prophet ﷺ would not pray maghrib while fasting until he broke his fast, even with a sip of water."],[8779,"Whoever marries has completed half of faith, so let him fear Allah in the remaining half."],[8780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and Sa'd b. al-Rabi'. He took him to his family and said, 'Choose whichever of my wives you wish, and I will divorce her for you, and my wealth is yours, half and half.' 'Abd al-Rahman said, 'May Allah bless you in your family and wealth. Show me the market.' So they showed him, and he did not return until he had acquired something. He married a woman from the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone of gold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met him with traces of yellow perfume on him, and said, 'Mahyam?' He said, 'I married a woman from the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone of gold.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep.'"],[8781,"The best of faith is that you know that Allah is with you wherever you are."],[8782,"I and my Ummah will be on a hill on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah will clothe me in a green robe. Then He will grant me permission, and I will praise Him as He deserves. That is the Praiseworthy Station."],[8783,"The worst of people is the one who is harsh with his family. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how is he harsh with his family?' He said, 'When the man enters his house, his wife becomes subdued, his child runs away, and his servant flees. When he leaves, his wife smiles and his household becomes cheerful.'"],[8784,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, with what do you perform Witr?' He said, 'With \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High\" (Sabbihisma Rabbika al-A'la), \"Say: O disbelievers\" (Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun), and \"Say: He is Allah, [who is] One\" (Qul huwa Allahu ahad).'"],[8785,"The fire does not heal anyone."],[8786,"A servant may remain a believer for ages, then ages, then die while Allah is angry with him. And a servant may remain a disbeliever for ages, then ages, then die while Allah is pleased with him. Whoever dies as a slanderer, a backbiter, one who gives people nicknames, his mark on the Day of Resurrection will be that Allah brands him on the snout from both sides."],[8787,"A man from Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a man of great wealth, with family and a settled home. Tell me how I should spend and what I should do.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Pay the Zakat from your wealth, for it is a purification that purifies you, maintain ties with your relatives, and acknowledge the right of the beggar, the neighbor, and the poor.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, make it less for me.' He said, 'Then give the relative his due, and the poor, and the wayfarer, and do not squander wastefully.' He said, 'That is enough for me, O Messenger of Allah. If I pay the Zakat to your messenger, will I be absolved of it before Allah and His Messenger?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes, if you pay the Zakat to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, you are absolved of it, and you have its reward, and its sin is upon the one who changes it.'"],[8788,"The angels discuss matters in the 'anan—'anan means clouds—concerning affairs on earth, and the devils overhear a word from them and cast it into the ears of soothsayers, adding a hundred lies to it."],[8789,"Abu Bakr married Asma' bt. 'Umays after Ja'far b. Abi Talib. He came to enter upon Asma' and found a group of men sitting in his house, so he returned to the Prophet of Allah and told him. He said, 'O Abu Bakr, what is that?' He said, 'I did not see anything wrong.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah has cleared her of that.' Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ stood and said, 'No man should enter upon a woman whose husband is absent unless someone else is with him.'"],[8790,"When a woman prays her five prayers, fasts her month, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, she may enter from whichever of the gates of Paradise she wishes."],[8791,"The Jews used to say, 'If a woman is approached from her rear, her child will be born cross-eyed.' Then this verse was revealed: 'Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish.'"],[8792,"A man should not have skin-to-skin contact with another man, and a woman should not have skin-to-skin contact with another woman."],[8793,"Abu Bakr and Umar are the two chiefs of the mature men of the people of Paradise, from the first and the last. And do not inform them, O Ali."],[8794,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, his wives sent Uthman b. Affan to Abu Bakr to ask him for their inheritance from what God had bestowed as spoils. Aisha said: I kept turning them away from that, and I said: Will you not fear God? Did you not hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. The family of Muhammad only eats from the wealth of God."],[8795,"When someone died, the people would bring him to the Messenger of God ﷺ so that he could pray over him. He would ask: 'Does he owe any debt?' If they said yes, he would ask: 'Did he leave anything to pay off his debt?' If they said yes, he would pray over him; otherwise he would say: 'Pray over your companion.' When God granted him the conquests, he said: 'I am closer to the believers than their own selves. Whoever dies owing a debt, it is upon us; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs.'"],[8796,"O God, whichever servant I have cursed, make that a means of nearness for him to You on the Day of Resurrection."],[8797,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never set out on a journey or dispatched an expedition except on Thursday."],[8798,"We are more entitled to doubt than our father Ibrahim, when he said: 'My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead.' He said: 'Do you not believe?' He said: 'Yes, but to put my heart at rest.' And may God have mercy on my brother Lut; he used to seek refuge in a strong pillar. And had I stayed in prison as long as Yusuf did, I would have answered the caller."],[8799,"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer should perform the major ablution."],[8800,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered Sahla bt. Suhayl to breastfeed Salim so that what was in Abu Hudhayfa's mind would go away."],[8801,"Sleep is the brother of death, and the people of Paradise do not sleep."],[8802,"How excellent a condiment is vinegar."],[8803,"The Messenger of God ﷺ heard a man's voice, so he jumped up with a strong leap and went out to him. I followed him, and there he was leaning on the mane of his own horse, and he was Dihya al-Kalbi, wearing a turban with its end let down between his shoulder blades. When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered, I said: 'You jumped with a strong leap and went out, and it was Dihya al-Kalbi?' He said: 'Did you see him?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'That was Jibril ﷺ . He ordered me to go out to Banu Qurayza.'"],[8804,"The Messenger of God ﷺ asked forgiveness for the first row three times, for the second row twice, and for the third once."],[8805,"“A previously married woman should not be married without her consent, and a virgin should not be married except with her permission.” They said: “How is her permission?” He said: “That she remains silent.”"],[8806,"Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven; and whoever stands in prayer on the Night of Decree out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[8807,"He prostrated in “When the sky has split.”"],[8808,"“Recite the Qur’an; do not eat by it, nor seek abundance through it, nor exceed the limits regarding it, nor abandon it. Learn the Qur’an, for it will intercede for its companion on the Day of Resurrection. Learn the two bright ones: Surah al-Baqarah and Ali ‘Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks, interceding for their companion on the Day of Resurrection. Learn Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is a blessing, leaving it is regret, and the idle cannot handle it.”"],[8809,"There will come people who will lead you in the prayers. If they complete them, then it is for them and for you; but if they fall short, then it is against them and for you."],[8810,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the privy, he would say: “In the name of God. O God, I seek refuge in You from the impure filth, the wicked deceiver, the accursed devil.”"],[8811,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out when the sun had passed its zenith, stood at ‘Arafah, addressed the people, called God as a witness over them, and made them witness over themselves, saying: “You will be asked about me, so what will you say?” They said: “We bear witness that you have conveyed (the message).” He said: “O God, bear witness.” Then he spoke at length. The muezzin called the adhan for the noon prayer, then he stood and prayed the noon prayer after the sermon. Then he gave the iqamah for the afternoon prayer and prayed it. Then he mounted and stood, and when the sun set he pushed on to Muzdalifah, where he prayed the sunset and night prayers with one adhan and two iqamahs. Then he lay down until dawn broke, prayed the dawn prayer, and stood (at al-Mash’ar al-Haram)."],[8812,"I saw myself with the Messenger of God ﷺ at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah, and we were rained upon with rain that did not even wet the soles of our sandals, when the caller of the Messenger of God ﷺ announced: “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[8813,"“By the One who sent me with the truth, God will not punish on the Day of Resurrection one who has mercy on the orphan, speaks gently to him, shows compassion for his orphanhood and weakness, and does not look down on his neighbor because of the favor God has given him.” And he said: “O community of Muhammad, by the One who sent me with the truth, God will not accept on the Day of Resurrection charity from a man who has needy relatives and diverts it to others instead of them. By the One in whose hand is my soul, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8814,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of God ﷺ, died, the Messenger of God ﷺ wept. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ said: “You are most worthy of knowing God’s right.” He said: “The eye tears, the heart grieves, and we do not say what displeases the Lord. Indeed, O Ibrahim, we are saddened by your loss.”"],[8815,"Ka’b b. ‘Ujrah met me while I was at al-Balat and I had interlaced my fingers. He said: “Where are you heading?” I said: “I am heading to the mosque.” He said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘When one of you performs ablution and then goes out intending the mosque, he is in prayer as long as he does not interlace his fingers.’”"],[8816,"Bilal entered with the Messenger of God ﷺ al-Aswaf, and the Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself, then they came out. Usama said: I asked Bilal what he did, and Bilal said: He went to relieve himself, then performed ablution, washing his face and hands, wiping his head, and wiping over his leather socks, then he prayed."],[8817,"He said: 'I will certainly fast as long as I live, and I will certainly pray at night as long as I live.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'Are you the one who said: I will certainly fast the whole time as long as I live, and I will certainly pray at night as long as I live?' Abdullah b. Amr said to him: 'I said that, O Messenger of God.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Fast and break your fast, pray and sleep, and fast three days of the month, for every good deed is multiplied tenfold.' He said: 'I find myself able to do more than that.' He said: 'Fast one day and break your fast for two days.' He said: 'I find myself able to do better than that.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Fast one day and break your fast one day.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, I find myself able to do more than that.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'There is nothing better than that.'"],[8818,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[8819,"When one of you touches his private part with his hand, ablution becomes obligatory upon him."],[8820,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray on a small mat and prostrate on it."],[8821,"That I attend the dawn prayer, then sit remembering God until the sun rises, is dearer to me than carrying spoils on swift horses in the path of God."],[8822,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning the zakat of vineyards: 'They are estimated as palm trees are estimated, then their zakat is paid as raisins just as the zakat of palm trees is paid as dates.'"],[8823,"The Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: 'And if you turn away, He will replace you with another people, and they will not be like you.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, who are these people who, if we turn away, will replace us with a people other than us, and they will not be like us?' The Messenger of God ﷺ struck the thigh of Salman al-Farisi, then said: 'This one and his people. If religion were suspended from the Pleiades, men from the Persians would attain it.'"],[8824,"He used to recite in the first rak'ah of the witr: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' in the second: 'Say, O disbelievers,' and in the third: 'Say, He is God, the One,' and the two protective surahs."],[8825,"Whoever forgets a prayer, its time is when he remembers it."],[8826,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her and called for water for ablution. A vessel was brought that held a mudd and a third or a mudd and a half, by the mudd of the Prophet ﷺ. He performed ablution, washing his face, washing his hands, wiping his head, wiping his temples, wiping the front of his head, and wiping the back of his head until he reached the middle in every wipe, and washed his feet."],[8827,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked, and it was said to him: 'One of us wakes up and has not prayed witr, overcome by sleep.' He said: 'Then let him pray witr when he wakes up.'"],[8828,"No one among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ narrated more hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ than I did, except Abd Allah b. Amr b. al-As, for he used to write while I did not write."],[8829,"Let me not find one of you, when a matter of my affair comes to him—something I forbade or something I commanded— reclining on his couch, saying: “We do not find it in the Book of God, so we will not follow it.”"],[8830,"There will be after me leaders who pray the prayer at other than its proper time. If they do that, pray the prayer at its proper time, and make your prayer with them a supererogatory prayer."],[8831,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; his due hospitality is a day and a night, and hospitality lasts three days. Whatever is beyond that is charity. It is not lawful for a guest to stay with him until he causes him hardship. And whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent."],[8832,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived at Khaybar in the morning while they had already opened the fort, so they came out carrying their shovels. When they saw him, they returned to the fort and said: “Muhammad and the army! Muhammad and the army!” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God is greatest! God is greatest! Khaybar is ruined. When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned.”"],[8833,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, they differed. They said: “Let us seek guidance from our Lord; let us send for the one who digs a lahd [side niche] and the one who digs a darih [central trench]. Whichever of them arrives first, we will use.” So they sent for both, and the lahd-digger arrived first, so they made a lahd for the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[8834,"A woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I have committed a sin in my womb, so carry out the punishment on me.” He said: “We do not kill what is in your womb for your sin. Go away until you give birth to what is in your womb.” So she went away. When she had given birth, she came and said: “I have given birth.” He said: “Go away and breastfeed him until you wean him.” When she had weaned him, she came and said: “I have weaned him, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Go away and take care of him.” So she went away and then came walking with her sister. The Messenger of God ﷺ was amazed at her patience and ordered that she be stoned. Then the Prophet ﷺ said to a man: “Go, and when she is placed in her pit, stand in front of her so that she can see you, and signal to her.” And he ordered a man, saying: “Go to a huge stone, come at her from behind, and throw it at her to crush her.”"],[8835,"Horses were sent out during the time of al-Hajjaj, while al-Hakam b. Ayyub was governor of Basra. When the horses came, we said: “Let us go to Anas b. Malik and ask him: O Abu Hamzah, did you used to hold horse races for stakes during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” So we came to him while he was in his palace at al-Zawiyah, and we asked him: “O Abu Hamzah, did you used to hold horse races for stakes during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ? Did the Messenger of God ﷺ race for stakes?” He said: “Yes, by God, he raced a horse of his called Subhah, and it beat the people, and he rejoiced at that and was pleased.”"],[8836,"I came to Anas b. Malik and said: “O Abu Hamzah, the place is far, and we would like to visit you.” He raised his head and said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Any man who visits a sick person plunges into mercy, and when he sits with the sick person, mercy envelops him.’”"],[8837,"I never prayed behind anyone a prayer that was lighter or more concise yet complete than that of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[8838,"Umar b. Abd al-Aziz led us in the noon prayer, then we went to Anas b. Malik to visit him. When I entered upon him, he said: “You have prayed?” We said: “Yes.” He said: “O girl, bring me water for ablution. I have not prayed behind any imam after the Messenger of God ﷺ whose prayer was more like that of the Messenger of God ﷺ than this imam of yours.”"],[8839,"The chief of your condiments is salt."],[8840,"He entered upon Anas b. Malik and said to him: O Abu Zilal, when did you lose your sight? He said: I do not remember. He said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ narrated to us from Jibril ﷺ , from his Lord, the Exalted? He said: 'Allah said: O Jibril, what is the reward of My servant when I take his two precious things (eyes) except that he may look at My face and be My neighbor in My abode.' And I saw the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ weeping around him, wishing that their eyesight would go."],[8841,"The son of Adam hurts Me; he reviles time, and I am time. In My hand is the command; I alternate the night and the day."],[8842,"He forbade that a man walk in one sandal or one khuff."],[8843,"The king of Dhu Yazan gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a hulla (garment), which he acquired for thirty-three camels or thirty-three she-camels. He wore it for a while during the day, then he discarded it."],[8844,"A man does not believe until I am more beloved to him than his child, his parent, and all people."],[8845,"The son of Adam ages, but two things remain young with him: greed for wealth and greed for life."],[8846,"By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, a man does not believe until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."],[8847,"When the Prophet ﷺ performed ghusl from janaba, he performed wudu as for prayer: he poured water over his hands three times, then washed his private part, then washed his left hand three times, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his forearms three times, then poured water over his head and body."],[8848,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a need outside Madinah. He passed by a well from which water was drawn, and said: 'The owner of this well will carry it on the Day of Resurrection if he does not give its due.' Then he came upon some sheep and said: 'The owner of these sheep will have such-and-such done to him if he does not give their due.' Then he came upon some camels and said the like. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which wealth is best? He said: 'There is no good in wealth.' I said: Then what will sustain us? He said: 'A servant who serves you; when he prays, he is your brother. Or your horse upon which you fight in jihad.'"],[8849,"The heart of an old person remains young in love of two things: life and wealth."],[8850,"The poor of the Muslims will enter Paradise before their rich by half a day. I said: What is half a day? He said: 'A day with your Lord is like a thousand years.' He said: 'And they will all enter in the form of Adam.' I said: What is the form of Adam? He said: 'He was twelve cubits tall; his height in the sky, and six cubits wide.' I said: By which cubit? He said: 'The cubit is like the height of a tall man among you.'"],[8851,"One day I was sitting with a group of the weak among the Muhajirun, and a man among us was reciting the Qur'an to us and supplicating for us. Some of us was covering himself with another because of nudity and hardship. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us. When our reciter saw him, he stopped reciting. He came and sat with us, then gestured with his hand, and the circle of people turned to face him. He said: Were you not exchanging talk among yourselves? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, our companion recites the Qur'an to us and supplicates for us. He said: 'Return to your talk.' The man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I recite while you are among us? He said: 'Yes.' Then he said: 'Praise be to Allah who has placed in my ummah those with whom I have been commanded to keep myself patient.' Then he said: 'Rejoice, O company of poor believers, with success on the Day of Resurrection over the rich by five hundred years, while the others are held back, detained by the excess that was in their hands.'"],[8852,"The household of Muhammad ﷺ never had their fill of wheat bread for three [consecutive days] until he passed away, nor did any leftover morsel remain from his table until he passed away ﷺ."],[8853,"The best of this community is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."],[8854,"I do not fear for my community anything except weakness of certainty."],[8855,"A man invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to [a meal of] barley bread and rancid melted fat. He [the narrator] said: I indeed heard him once say: 'By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, there did not remain with the household of Muhammad a saa' of dates, nor a saa' of wheat,' and he had at that time nine wives. He had pawned a coat of mail of his with a Jew in Madinah in exchange for food, and he could not find anything with which to redeem it."],[8856,"He entered upon her while she was weeping, and he said: 'What makes you weep?' She said: 'Whenever I wish to weep, I weep. The Prophet ﷺ died without ever having his fill of wheat bread twice in one day, and then the world was opened upon us.' She also said: 'We remained for four months with no food except water and dates, and he died while his coat of mail was pawned, until Abu Bakr redeemed it.'"],[8857,"One night a leg of a sheep was gifted to us from the house of Abu Bakr. She said: 'By Allah, I was holding it for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was cutting it,' or 'the Messenger of Allah ﷺ held it while I was cutting it.' I said: 'O Mother of the Believers, was that by a lamp?' She said: 'If we had had lamp oil, we would have eaten it. A month would pass upon the household of Muhammad ﷺ in which they neither baked bread nor cooked.'"],[8858,"I entered with the Prophet ﷺ into one of the gardens of Madinah, and he began eating green unripe dates. He said: 'Eat, O Ibn Umar.' I said: 'I do not desire it, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'You do not desire it? It is the first food the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has eaten in four days.'"],[8859,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send us out on a military expedition while we had no provisions except the 'salf' of dates [dates that are still unripe and sour], which we would divide by handfuls until we would end up with a single date each. I said: 'O father, what can a single date avail you?' He said: 'Do not say that, O my son. Once we lost it, we felt its loss.'"],[8860,"O son of Adam, you have what suffices you, yet you seek what will make you tyrannical? O son of Adam, you are not content with little, nor are you satisfied with much? O son of Adam, when you wake up healthy in your body, secure in your dwelling, with your daily sustenance at hand, then let the world perish."],[8861,"A Jew came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Abu al-Qasim, do you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink therein?' He said: 'Yes, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, a man will be given the strength of a hundred in eating, drinking, desire, and intercourse.' The Jew said: 'But the one who eats and drinks will have need [to relieve himself], while Paradise is pure?' He said: 'The need of one of them will be a sweat that flows from his skin like the fragrance of musk, and then his belly will become flat.'"],[8862,"Jibril ﷺ told me: 'A man will enter upon the houri and she will receive him with embrace and handshake.' Thabit said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'With what fingertips will she greet him? If some of her fingertips were to appear, their light would overpower the light of the sun and the moon. If a lock of her hair were to appear, it would fill the space between east and west with its fragrance. While he is reclining with her upon his couch, a light appears from above him, and he thinks that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has looked upon His creation, when it is a houri calling him: \"O friend of Allah, do we not have a turn with you?\" He says: \"Who are you, O this one?\" She says: \"I am of those concerning whom Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'And with Us is more.'\" So he turns to her, and she has of beauty and perfection what the first did not have. While he is reclining with her upon his couch, a light appears from above him, and it is another houri calling him: \"O friend of Allah, do we not have a turn with you?\" He says: \"Who are you, O this one?\" She says: \"I am of those concerning whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'No soul knows what is kept hidden for them of comfort for their eyes, as a reward for what they used to do.'\" He will not cease moving from one wife to another.'"],[8863,"If the adornment of the least adorned person among the people of Paradise were weighed against the adornment of all the people of this world, what Allah will adorn him with in the Hereafter would be superior to the adornment of all the people of this world."],[8864,"Whoever it pleases that Allah give him wine to drink in the Hereafter, let him leave it in this world, and whoever it pleases that Allah clothe him in silk in the Hereafter, let him leave it in this world."],[8865,"If even a fingernail's weight of what is in Paradise were to appear, it would adorn all that is between the extremities of the heavens and the earth, and if a man of the people of Paradise were to look out and his bracelet were to appear, its light would blot out the light of the sun just as the sun blots out the light of the stars."],[8866,"The disbeliever will be bridled with his sweat on account of the severity of that day, meaning the Day of Resurrection, until he says: 'O Lord, grant me relief even if it is to the Fire.'"],[8867,"Whoever's concern and distress is the world, and he stares at it, and for it he toils and seeks, Allah will place his poverty before his eyes, scatter his affairs, and nothing of it will come to him except what is decreed for him. And whoever's concern and distress is the Hereafter, and he stares at it, and for it he toils and seeks, Allah will place his richness in his heart, gather his affairs for him, and the world will come to him submissively."],[8868,"Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms like a dog."],[8869,"My Lord promised me that He would admit into Paradise one hundred thousand of my community. Abu Bakr said: 'O Prophet of Allah, increase us.' He gestured with his hand like this and scooped with it. Then he said: 'O Prophet of Allah, increase us.' He gestured with his hand like this. Then he said: 'O Prophet of Allah, increase us.' He gestured with his hand like this. Umar said: 'Enough for you, O Abu Bakr.' Abu Bakr said: 'What is it to you, O Ibn al-Khattab?' Umar said: 'Allah is able to admit all people into Paradise with a single handful.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Umar has spoken the truth.'"],[8870,"Whoever is two-tongued, Allah will give him two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[8871,"Straighten your rows when you bow and prostrate, for I see you from behind my back."],[8872,"Two men will indeed come to me at the Cistern, and when I see them they will be raised up for me, then they will be snatched away from me."],[8873,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to dye himself with saffron. I said: 'What is dyeing with saffron?' He said: 'Perfuming oneself with it.'"],[8874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer with the two shortest surahs of the Quran. When he finished his prayer, he turned his face toward us and said: 'I hastened, or hurried, so that the mother might attend to her child, and he heard the sound of the child.'"],[8875,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and found a rope stretched between two pillars. He said: 'What is this?' They said: 'This is for so-and-so, she prays, and when she becomes weary she holds onto it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ untied it and said: 'Let one of you pray as long as he is energetic, and when he becomes weary, let him lie down.'"],[8876,"Bilal used to give the iqamah for prayer, and the Prophet ﷺ would enter, and a man would meet him and speak to him about some need until some of the people began to nod their heads."],[8877,"Wine was forbidden, and at that time they had no nabidh except from unripe and ripe dates. I was serving Abu Talhah, Suhayl b. Bayda', and Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, when suddenly the caller of the Prophet ﷺ called out twice: 'Indeed wine has been forbidden.' So we poured it out, and it was nothing but unripe and ripe dates."],[8878,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon me while I was a boy playing with the children. He greeted us, then called me for an errand. Were it not that it was a secret of his, I would have told you about it, but I will not tell the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to anyone among the people."],[8879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the words of Ibrahim: 'So whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me, indeed You are Forgiving and Merciful,' and the words of 'Isa: 'If You punish them, they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, indeed You are the Mighty, the Wise.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hand and said: 'O Allah, my ummah, my ummah,' and wept. Then Allah said to Jibril: 'Go to Muhammad, and your Lord knows best, and ask him what makes him weep.' Jibril came to him and asked him, and the Prophet ﷺ informed him. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said to Jibril: 'Go to Muhammad and say to him: We will surely please you regarding your ummah and will not grieve you.'"],[8880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not recite less than twenty verses in the Fajr prayer, and he would not recite less than ten verses in the 'Isha' prayer."],[8881,"While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he heard the people saying: 'Which deeds are best, O Messenger of Allah?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Faith in Allah and His Messenger, jihad in the path of Allah, and an accepted Hajj.' Then he heard a call in the valley saying: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'And I bear witness.' Then he said: 'No one bears witness to them except that he is free from shirk.'"],[8882,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the minbar: 'Indeed the people are the outer garment, and the Ansar are the inner garment. If the people were to take one valley and the Ansar another, I would follow the valley of the Ansar. Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar. Whoever is put in charge of any of their affairs, let him be good to their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers. And whoever frightens them has frightened this which is between these two,' and he pointed to his chest, meaning his heart."],[8883,"A son of his died at 'Usfan, and he said: 'O Kurayb, have the people gathered for him?' I went out and found that the people had gathered for him. He said: 'Have forty gathered for him?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Bring him out, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No Muslim man dies and forty men stand over his funeral, not associating anything with Allah, except that Allah grants them intercession for him.'"],[8884,"Respond to the one who sneezes three times; if he does it more, then it is a cold."],[8885,"Whoever kills a gecko, Allah erases seven sins from him."],[8886,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed a turban on 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, letting four finger-widths hang down, and said: 'When I ascended to the heaven, I saw most of the angels wearing turbans.'"],[8887,"She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has there ever been a day more difficult for you than the day of Uhud?' He said: 'I suffered from your people, and the worst I suffered from them was the day of al-'Aqabah, when I presented myself to Ibn 'Abd Yalil b. 'Abd Kulal, and he did not respond to what I wanted. I went away distressed, and I did not regain myself until I was at Qarn al-Tha'alib. I raised my head and saw a cloud shading me. I looked and saw Jibril in it. He called me and said: Allah has heard the words of your people and how they replied to you, and He has sent the Angel of the Mountains to you so that you may command him whatever you wish concerning them. Then the Angel of the Mountains called me, greeted me, and said: O Muhammad, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has heard the words of your people. I am the Angel of the Mountains, and your Lord has sent me to you so that you may command me with whatever you wish. If you wish, I will crush them between the two mountains. I said: Rather, I hope that Allah will bring forth from their loins those who worship Allah without associating anything with Him.'"],[8888,"Umm Sulaym, the mother of Anas b. Malik, came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, what do you think about one of us who experiences what a man experiences in sleep until she finds wetness? He said: If one of you finds that, let her perform ghusl."],[8889,"The approach of the Hour is that the year will be like a month, the month like a week, the week like a day, the day like an hour, and the hour like a burning spark of fire. And one of you will surely sleep while his term is before his eyes."],[8890,"He entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ when he had forsaken his wives, and found him on a bed, leaning on a leather cushion stuffed with palm fiber. Umar said: I turned and saw a worn-out cloak whose smell had become strong, so I wept and said: O Messenger of God, you are the Messenger of God ﷺ and His chosen one, while this is Kisra and Caesar in gold and silk? The Messenger of God ﷺ sat up straight and said: Are you in doubt, O Ibn al-Khattab? Those are a people whose good things have been hastened for them in the life of this world."],[8891,"A child is not to be subjected to retaliation for [killing] a parent."],[8892,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married me at Sarif while we were in a state of ihrām, after he returned from Makkah."],[8893,"He forbade cutting the mustaches."],[8894,"When one of you puts his hand to his penis, let him perform wudu."],[8895,"When Bilal wanted to call the iqamah for prayer, he would say: Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. The prayer, may God have mercy on you."],[8896,"The Prophet ﷺ had a wrapper dyed with wars; he would wear it in his house, go around to his wives in it, and pray in it."],[8897,"I have not seen anyone whose prayer more closely resembled the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ than this boy, meaning Umar b. Abd al-Aziz."],[8898,"A clan of the Ansar called Banu Salima, the people of Muadh b. Jabal, came. He said: O Banu Salima, who is your chief? They said: Judd b. Qays, though we consider him miserly. The Prophet ﷺ said: And what disease is more harmful than miserliness?"],[8899,"On the day of the conquest, the Messenger of God ﷺ poured out the wine, broke its jars, and forbade selling it and selling idols."],[8900,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived on the fourth of Dhul-Hijjah. When he had circumambulated the House and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwa, he said: “Make it an ‘umrah, except for those who have the sacrificial animal with them.” On the Day of Tarwiyah they circumambulated the House but did not walk between al-Safa and al-Marwa."],[8901,"We do not inherit from the People of the Book, nor do they inherit from us, unless a man inherits his male slave or his female slave. We may marry their women, but they may not marry our women."],[8902,"The prophets were shown to me, and I resemble Ibrahim ﷺ ."],[8903,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to pray, and I stood on his left, so he turned me to his right. Then Jabbar b. Sakhr came and stood on his left, and the Messenger of God ﷺ stepped forward, and we stood behind him."],[8904,"The Prophet ﷺ threw Jamrat al-‘Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice in the forenoon, and he threw the pebbles on the Days of Tashriq after the sun had passed its meridian."],[8905,"Indeed, I have chosen this religion for Myself, and nothing befits it except generosity and good character, so honor it with these two as long as you keep it company."],[8906,"He saw a plowshare and something of the tools of tillage, and said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘This does not enter the house of a people except that God brings humiliation upon them.’”"],[8907,"While they were circumambulating the idol, they heard a speaker saying: “And if he had fabricated against Us some sayings, We would have seized him by the right hand, then We would have cut from him the aorta.” We were alarmed by that and said: “What is this speech that we do not recognize?” Then we looked, and there was the Prophet ﷺ going on his way."],[8908,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came forward with a group of men until he stopped at al-Qarn, below al-Murayta’, raising his hands, facing the qiblah, supplicating."],[8909,"Silk has been permitted for the females of my Ummah and forbidden for its males."],[8910,"Good and evil will be set up before the people on the Day of Resurrection. As for good, it will promise its people Paradise and give them glad tidings. As for evil, it will say to its people: “Come to me, come to me,” and they will be able only to cling to it."],[8911,"Whoever meets God without having associated anything with Him in the world, and then has sins like mountains, God will forgive him."],[8912,"He drank while standing, and it was said to him: \"Will you drink while standing?\" He said: \"That I do; indeed I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do it. If I drink standing, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ drink standing; and if I drink sitting, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ drink sitting.\""],[8913,"He witnessed Ali when he fought the people of al-Nahrawan, while he was standing on his mule, and he said: \"Look among them for one with a deformed hand, or a crushed hand, or a lumpy hand?\" They looked but did not find him, so Ali said: \"Turn them over.\" They turned them over and brought out a tall black man from a stream, on whose upper arm there was something like a woman's breast, with black hairs on it. Then I heard Ali say: \"God is greatest, God is greatest. Were it not that you would look, I would tell you what God promised those who fought them on the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ.\" When I heard him mention the Prophet ﷺ, I drew near to him until I took hold of the bridle of his mule while he was standing, and I said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, did you hear this from the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes, by the Lord of the Kaba.\""],[8914,"I ate a tharida with fatty meat, then I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was burping. He said: \"Restrain your burping, O Abu Juhayfa, for the most satiated of people in this world will be the longest in hunger on the Day of Resurrection.\" Abu Juhayfa never ate to the fill of his stomach until he departed this world; when he had lunch he would not have dinner, and when he had dinner he would not have lunch."],[8915,"It is not lawful to abandon a fellow Muslim for more than three days. If they meet and one of them greets the other and the other returns the greeting, they share in the reward; but if the other refuses to return the greeting, this one is free of the sin and the other bears it. I fear that if they die while they are estranged, they will not meet in Paradise."],[8916,"I created creatures whose tongues are sweeter than honey, but whose hearts are more bitter than aloes. So I have sworn to afflict them with a trial that will leave the forbearing among them bewildered. In Me they are deceived, and against Me they are emboldened."],[8917,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ had removed his garment from his thigh. Abu Bakr came seeking permission, and he granted him permission while the Prophet ﷺ was in that state. Then Umar came seeking permission, and he granted him permission while the Prophet ﷺ was in that state. Then Uthman came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ took his garment and wrapped it around himself. They spoke, then left. I said: \"O Messenger of God, Abu Bakr and Umar and some of your companions came while you were in that state, but when Uthman came you wrapped your garment around yourself?\" He said: \"Should I not be shy before one before whom the angels are shy?\""],[8918,"He was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he went to relieve himself, then he came back and said: \"Is there any water for purification?\" I brought him water, and he washed his hands and face, then he went to wash his forearms, but the jubba was too tight for him—it was a jubba of the Roman style—so he pulled his arms out from under the jubba and washed his forearms. I reached for the khuffs, but he said: \"Leave the khuffs, for I put my feet into them while they were pure,\" and he wiped over the khuffs."],[8919,"Indeed God loves the believer who earns his livelihood."],[8920,"An angel at one of the gates of heaven says: \"Whoever lends today will be recompensed tomorrow,\" and an angel at another gate says: \"O God, give to the one who spends wealth a replacement, and give to the one who withholds wealth ruin.\""],[8921,"Whoever mentions a person with what is not in him to defame him with what is not in him, God will confine him in the fire of Hell until he brings about the fulfillment of what he said about him."],[8922,"Zakat is the bridge of Islam."],[8923,"I, Tawus al-Yamani, Amr b. Dinar al-Makki, Mak-hul al-Shami, and al-Hasan al-Basri gathered in the mosque of al-Khayf, and we discussed divine decree until our voices rose and our clamor increased. Tawus stood up and said: \"Listen, I will tell you what I heard Abu al-Darda relate from the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God has imposed obligations upon you, so do not neglect them; He has set limits for you, so do not transgress them; He has forbidden you things, so do not violate them; and He has remained silent about things out of mercy, not out of forgetfulness, so do not burden yourselves with them. Accept them. All matters are in the hand of God; from God is their origin, and to Him is their return. The servants have no authority or will in them.\""],[8924,"When God intends humiliation for a servant, He makes him spend his wealth on building."],[8925,"I said: O Muhammad, how does he come to you?—meaning Jibril ﷺ . The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"He comes to me from heaven; his wings are pearl and the soles of his feet are green.\""],[8926,"No servant says 'There is no god but God and God is greatest' except that God frees a quarter of him from the Fire. If he says it twice, God frees half of him from the Fire. If he says it three times, God frees three quarters of him from the Fire. If he says it four times, God frees him entirely from the Fire."],[8927,"A man from the Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Abu al-Qasim, has God, Mighty and Majestic, veiled Himself from His creation with anything other than the heavens and the earth? He said: Yes. Between Him and the angels around the Throne are seventy veils of fire, seventy veils of light, seventy veils of darkness, seventy veils of embroidered brocade, seventy veils of fine silk, seventy veils of white pearl, seventy veils of red pearl, seventy veils of yellow pearl, seventy veils of green pearl, seventy veils of radiance that shines from the fire and light, seventy veils of snow, seventy veils of water, seventy veils of clouds, seventy veils of hail, and seventy veils of God's majesty that cannot be described. He said: Then tell me about the angel of God who is next to Him. The Prophet ﷺ said: Have I spoken truthfully in what I told you, O Jew? He said: Yes. He said: The angel next to Him is Israfil, then Jibril, then Mika'il, then the Angel of Death—may God bless them all."],[8928,"Whoever eats with his left hand, a devil eats with him; and whoever drinks with his left hand, a devil drinks with him."],[8929,"The Hour will not come until the people of the mudy prevail over their mudy, the people of the qafiz over their qafiz, the people of the irdabb over their irdabb, the people of the dinar over their dinar, the people of the dirham over their dirham, and people return to their lands."],[8930,"There is no owner of gold or silver who does not pay its due except that it will be made into plates of fire, then heated in the fire of Hell, and his forehead and back will be branded with them on a day whose length is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among the people; then he will see his way, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of camels who does not pay their due—and part of their due is milking them on the day they come to water—except that they will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, not missing a single young camel, and he will be thrown on his face for them in a wide, level plain; they will trample him with their hooves and bite him with their mouths. Every time the last of them passes over him, the first of them returns to him, on a day whose length is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among the people. And there is no owner of cattle or sheep who does not pay their due except that they will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, then he will be thrown on his face for them in a wide, level plain, with none among them hornless or broken-horned; they will trample him with their cloven hooves and gore him with their horns, on a day whose length is fifty thousand years. Every time the last of them passes over him, the first of them returns to him, until judgment is passed among the people; then he will see his way, either to Paradise or to the Fire."],[8931,"\"O people, give charity and draw near to God\"—three times—but no one brought anything, until it was seen in the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then he said: \"O people, give charity and draw near to God.\" A man from the Ansar stood up and brought a piece of a bracelet, and he took it from him. When the people saw that, they followed one another in giving charity, and the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ brightened. Then he said: \"Whoever establishes a good practice in Islam will have its reward and the like of the reward of those who act upon it until the Day of Resurrection, without any decrease in their rewards. And whoever establishes an evil practice will bear its sin and the sin of those who act upon it until the Day of Resurrection, without any decrease in their sins.\""],[8932,"Harming [heirs] through a bequest is among the major sins."],[8933,"Command your husbands to wash away traces of excrement and urine, for I am too shy to command them to do that. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to do it."],[8934,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered his wives and children on the night of Muzdalifah, with me among them, and they departed at dawn until we prayed the morning prayer at Mina."],[8935,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade prayer at midday."],[8936,"Hands are not to be cut off during military expeditions."],[8937,"The hand is not to be cut off except for (theft of) a quarter of a dinar or more."],[8938,"A person will be with those whom he loves."],[8939,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died only from pleurisy."],[8940,"Rafi' b. Khadij came to us saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a practice that was beneficial to you: he forbade muhaqala and muzabana, and he prohibited renting out land."],[8941,"When the reciter says Amin, say Amin, for whoever's Amin coincides with the angels' Amin will have his previous sins forgiven."],[8942,"Every road of Makkah is a place of sacrifice."],[8943,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rak'ahs."],[8944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the 'atamah (night prayer), then pray in the mosque before returning home seven rak'ahs, saying the salam in the four every two rak'ahs, and performing witr with three, reciting the tashahhud in the first two of the witr as he did at the final salam, and performing witr with the mu'awwidhat (the last three surahs of the Quran). Then when he returned home, he would pray two rak'ahs and sleep. When he woke from his sleep, he would say: 'Praise be to Allah who made me sleep in well-being and woke me in well-being.' Then he would raise his head to the sky and reflect, then say: 'Our Lord, You have not created this in vain. Glory be to You, so protect us from the punishment of the Fire.' Then he would recite until he reached: 'Indeed, You do not break Your promise.' Then he would perform ablution, then stand and pray two rak'ahs, prolonging the recitation, bowing, and prostration, and making abundant supplication in them, so much so that I would sleep and wake up. Then he would finish and lie down and doze, then turn over and speak like he had spoken the first time. Then he would stand and pray two rak'ahs that were longer than the first two, with even more humble supplication and seeking of forgiveness, until I would say: 'Will he finish?' That would continue until the end of the night. Then he would finish and doze a little, and I would say: 'Has he dozed or not?' until the muezzin came to him. Then he would say the same as he had said the first time, then sit and call for the siwak, clean his teeth, perform ablution, then pray two light rak'ahs, then go out to the prayer. Thus his prayer was thirteen rak'ahs."],[8945,"I asked 'A'ishah: Were women given a concession to pray on mounts? She said: They were not given a concession for that, neither in hardship nor in ease."],[8946,"Three things: whoever preserves them is truly my ally, and whoever neglects them is truly my enemy: prayer, fasting, and ritual purity from major impurity."],[8947,"I am Allah, there is no god but Me, Owner of kings and King of kings. The hearts of kings are in My hand. When the servants obey Me, I turn the hearts of their kings toward them with compassion and mercy; and when the servants disobey Me, I turn their hearts against them with wrath and vengeance, and they inflict upon them severe punishment. So do not occupy yourselves with supplicating against kings, but rather occupy yourselves with remembrance and humble entreaty to Me, and I will suffice you against your kings."],[8948,"The one who takes back his gift is like the dog that eats until it is full, then vomits, then returns to its vomit."],[8949,"The people were shown Laylat al-Qadr in the last seven nights of Ramadan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, and it was said: The people saw it in the last seven nights. He said: Seek it in the last seven nights."],[8950,"Whoever frees a share of a slave, the rest is appraised at value on him, with his wealth, if he has any. If he has nothing, the slave is appraised at fair value, then made to work to pay it off without hardship."],[8951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who sees something in his dream but sees no wetness, or sees wetness but sees nothing. He said: If one of you finds wetness but sees nothing, let him perform ghusl. If he sees something but sees no wetness, he does not need to perform ghusl."],[8952,"Barirah was married to a slave. When she was freed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: You have more right to yourself. If you wish, remain with your husband; and if you wish, separate from him, as long as he has not touched you."],[8953,"He used to pray with her in front of him, between the Prophet of Allah and the qiblah."],[8954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a race between lean, trained horses, and they were sent from al-Hafya', and the course ended at Thaniyyat al-Wada'. He also held a race for untrained horses, and they were sent, and the course ended at the mosque of Banu Zurayq."],[8955,"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he has taken full possession of it."],[8956,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on a camel, facing whatever direction it turned."],[8957,"We used to pay zakat al-fitr at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as two mudds of wheat, using the mudd with which they measured their staple food."],[8958,"He forbade making nabidh in glazed jars, gourds, and hollowed-out stumps."],[8959,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas a young goat and ordered him to sacrifice it."],[8960,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Umar b. al-Khattab at the time of the conquest, while he was at al-Batha, to go to the House and erase every image in it, and he did not enter it until every image in it had been erased."],[8961,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote before he died to Kisra, Qaysar, the Najashi, and every obstinate tyrant."],[8962,"Islam began as something strange and will return to being strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers.\" They said: \"Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Those who set things right when the people are corrupt."],[8963,"Every soul will be gathered according to its inclination. Whoever inclined to disbelief will be with the disbelievers, and his deeds will not benefit him at all."],[8964,"Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days of Shawwal will have a whole year of fasting.\" Or: \"A year of fasting will be recorded for him."],[8965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning the plague: \"The one who flees from it is like the one who flees on the day of battle, and whoever remains patient in it will have the reward of a martyr."],[8966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in the prayer of fear on the day of Muharib, performing one rak'ah and two prostrations with each group."],[8967,"Horses have goodness and blessing tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, and their owners are helped through them. Adorn them with garlands, but do not adorn them with bowstrings."],[8968,"A man said: \"How are you this morning, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Better than one who has not arisen fasting, has not visited the sick, and has not followed a funeral procession."],[8969,"Do not enter upon women whose husbands are absent, for Satan flows through a person like blood.\" They said: \"And through you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"And through me, but Allah helped me against him, so he became Muslim."],[8970,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the sun rose, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the Day of Resurrection, people will come to Allah with light like the sun.\" They said: \"Are we they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"No, but you have much good. They are the poor emigrants who will be gathered from the ends of the earth."],[8971,"Glad tidings to the strangers.\" We said: \"Who are the strangers?\" He said: \"A righteous few among many evil people; those who disobey them are more than those who obey them."],[8972,"No Muslim plants a tree or sows a crop, and then a human, a bird, or anything eats from it, except that he earns a reward for it."],[8973,"Two adversaries brought a dispute before 'Amr b. al-'As, and he judged between them. The one against whom judgment was given was displeased, so he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When a judge judges and strives, then if he is correct, he has ten rewards; and if he strives and errs, he has two rewards.\""],[8974,"Sulayman b. Dawud asked Allah for three things, and He gave him two of them, while I hope that He has also given him the third. He asked Allah for a judgment that would coincide with His own judgment, and He gave him that. He asked for a kingdom that would not befit anyone after him, and He gave him that. And he asked Him that any man who leaves his house intending nothing but prayer in this mosque—meaning the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis—would come out of his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him."],[8975,"The thing I fear most for you is what Allah will bring out for you of the blessings of the earth.\" It was said: \"What are the blessings of the earth?\" He said: \"The splendor of this world.\" A man said: \"Does good ever bring evil?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent until we thought that revelation would descend upon him. Then he began wiping the sweat from his forehead and said: \"Where is the questioner: 'Does good ever bring evil?'\" The man said: \"Here I am.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, good does not bring anything except good\"—three times—\"and this wealth is green and sweet. Everything that the spring rain causes to grow can kill or nearly kill, except the animal that grazes on green pasture: it eats until its flanks are full, then it faces the sun, chews the cud, defecates, and urinates, then returns to eat again. Indeed, this wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it rightfully and spends it rightfully, what an excellent help it is. And whoever takes it without right is like one who eats but never feels full.\""],[8976,"Blessing is with your elders."],[8977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[8978,"Allah boasts to the inhabitants of heaven—the angels—about the people of 'Arafat, saying: \"Look at My servants, they have come disheveled and dusty.\""],[8979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Amin, Amin, Amin.\" It was said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, you did not used to do this.\" He said: \"Jibril ﷺ said to me: 'May his nose be rubbed in dust—or: may he be far removed—a servant upon whom Ramadan enters and he is not forgiven.' So I said, 'Amin.' Then he said: 'May his nose be rubbed in dust—or: may he be far removed—a servant who attains his parents or one of them and they do not admit him to Paradise.' So I said, 'Amin.' Then he said: 'May his nose be rubbed in dust—or: may he be far removed—a servant in whose presence you are mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you.' So I said, 'Amin.'\""],[8980,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me along with him one night and said: \"A group of jinn—fifteen, brothers and cousins—will come to me tonight, and I will recite the Quran to them.\" I went with him to the place he intended. He drew a line for me, seated me inside it, and said: \"Do not leave this.\" I stayed there until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me at dawn, holding in his hand a dry bone, a piece of dung, and a piece of charcoal. He said: \"When you go to relieve yourself, do not clean yourself with any of these.\" The narrator said: When morning came, I said: \"I will certainly know where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been.\" So I went and saw the spot of seventy camels."],[8981,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that causes most people to enter the Fire?\" He said: \"The two hollow organs: the private part and the mouth.\""],[8982,"\"Have I not been informed that you pray at night and fast during the day?\" I said: \"I do that.\" He said: \"If you do that, you will damage your eyes. Fast three days every month, for that is the fasting of a lifetime.\" I said: \"I find myself strong.\" He said: \"Fast the fast of Dawud: he used to fast one day and break his fast the next.\""],[8983,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ asking his permission to go on jihad. He said: \"Are your parents alive?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then strive in serving them.\""],[8984,"The best of you are those who are best in repaying debts."],[8985,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set out from Makkah for Hajj, Umrah, or a military expedition. When he was on part of the road he said: 'Who will fill for us the cisterns of al-Uthaya?' Jabir said: I said: 'I will, O Messenger of God.' So we went on until we came to al-Uthaya, and I filled the cistern. Then in part of the night a man came and dismounted, and behold it was the Messenger of God ﷺ. He went off and relieved himself, then came and performed ablution from the cistern, then came and prayed, wearing a waist-wrapper, wrapped in it. I performed ablution, then came and stood on his left, and he took my hand and placed me on his right, then he prayed two rak'ahs."],[8986,"She used to order talbina for the sick and for the grieving over the deceased, and she would say: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Talbina soothes the heart of the sick and takes away some of the grief.\"'"],[8987,"When the verse of inheritance shares in Surat al-Nisa was revealed, the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade withholding."],[8988,"Place between yourselves and what is forbidden a covering. Whoever does that is more upright in his honor and religion. Whoever falls into it is like a grazer beside a protected pasture, about to fall into it. Indeed, every king has a protected pasture, and indeed God's protected pasture on earth is His forbidden things."],[8989,"Faith has seventy-some branches, the highest of which is the testimony that there is no god but God, and the lowest is removing harm from the road. And modesty is a branch of faith."],[8990,"When I was taken into Paradise, I saw in it a palace of gold. I said to Jibril: 'For whom is this palace?' He said: 'For a man of Quraysh.' So I hoped that I might be him. I said: 'And who is he?' He said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab.'\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned that to Umar, and said: 'Were it not for what I know of your jealousy, O Abu Hafs, I would have entered it.' Umar wept and said: 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, would I be jealous of you, O Messenger of God?'"],[8991,"Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ gave protection to Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi' b. Abd Shams, and the Prophet ﷺ approved her protection."],[8992,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Attab b. Usayd: 'I have sent you over the people of God, the people of Makkah. Forbid them from selling what they have not received, from profit on what they have not guaranteed, from two conditions in one transaction, from a sale combined with a loan, and from a sale combined with an advance.'"],[8993,"When Ramadan drew near, he would say: 'This month of yours has drawn near, and by the oath of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ with which he swore, nothing like it has passed over the Muslims. God writes its reward and its supererogatory acts before it enters, and He writes its burden and its misery before it enters. That is because the believer prepares his spending and his provision for his family, while the wicked prepares for the heedlessness of the Muslims and their private failings. So it is a blessing for the believer and a punishment for the disbelievers.'"],[8994,"The Messenger of God ﷺ swore an oath to stay away from his wives. His foot had been dislocated, so he stayed in an upper room for twenty-nine nights. Then he came down and they said: 'O Messenger of God, you swore a month.' He said: 'The month is twenty-nine.'"],[8995,"Whoever follows a funeral until he prays over it will have a qirat, and whoever follows it until it is buried will have two qirats, the smaller of which is like Mount Uhud."],[8996,"Part of the Sunnah is that when a man marries a virgin in addition to a previously married woman, he stays with her for seven days, and when he marries a previously married woman in addition to a virgin, he stays with her for three days."],[8997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for me and ordered me to take my clothes and my weapon. I came to him while he was performing ablution. He looked up at me, then lowered his gaze and said: \"O ʿAmr, I intend to send you on a military expedition, may Allah grant you victory and keep you safe, and I will give you a good portion of wealth.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I did not become Muslim out of desire for wealth; rather, I became Muslim out of desire for Islam and to be with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"Excellent! And how excellent is good wealth for a righteous person.\""],[8998,"The merciful ones will be shown mercy by the Merciful. Show mercy to those on earth, and the One above the heavens will show mercy to you."],[8999,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not turn around when he walked. Sometimes his cloak would get caught on a tree or something, and he would not turn around until they lifted it off him. They used to laugh and joke, and they were safe from him turning around."],[9000,"Every act of kindness is charity."],[9001,"My nation will be afflicted with the diseases of the nations.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what are the diseases of the nations?\" He said: \"Recklessness, arrogance, mutual turning away, competing for worldly gains, mutual hatred, and miserliness, until there is transgression, then there will be killing.\""],[9002,"Whoever says when he moves at night: 'Bismillah' (In the name of Allah) ten times, and 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah) ten times, and 'Amantu billah wa kafartu bil-taghut' (I believe in Allah and disbelieve in false gods) ten times, will be protected from everything that could harm him, and no sin will be able to reach him up to the like of it."],[9003,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning things he prohibited: and the price of a dog."],[9004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the zakat of vineyards: 'It is estimated as palm trees are estimated, then its zakat is paid as raisins just as the zakat of palm trees is paid as dried dates.'"],[9005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took zakat al-fitr from the Bedouin people in the form of dried curds."],[9006,"Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom."],[9007,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited mukhābarah (sharecropping for a portion of the produce), muzābanah (selling fresh dates for dry dates by measure), muḥāqalah (selling wheat in the ear for pure wheat by measure), and selling fruit until it is ripe and edible, except for ʿarāyā (a concession allowing the sale of fresh dates on the tree for dry dates by estimation for eating)."],[9008,"He used to pray while she was lying crosswise between him and the qiblah."],[9009,"When the reciter says amin, then say amin, for whoever's amin coincides with the amin of the angels, his past sins will be forgiven."],[9010,"When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'O My servants, will you ask Me for anything that I may give you more?' They will say: 'O our Lord, what is better than what You have given us?' He will say: 'My good pleasure is greater.'"],[9011,"Regarding His saying: 'And I do not know what will be done with me or with you' (Quran 46:9), he said: 'The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came to know after that what would be done with him when Allah revealed: 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory' (Quran 48:1).' Hammam said: 'Then he narrated to us from Anas b. Malik that when this verse was revealed to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than the entire world.\" When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ recited it, a man from the people said: \"Congratulations to you, O Prophet of Allah. Allah has made clear to you what will be done with you. But what will be done with us?\" So Allah revealed: \"That He may admit the believing men and the believing women to gardens beneath which rivers flow...\" (Quran 48:5).'"],[9012,"The water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for."],[9013,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[9014,"My basin is a month's journey in extent; its corners are equal; its water is whiter than silver; its fragrance is more pleasant than musk; its drinking cups are like the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst again."],[9015,"Indeed Allah detests the eloquent man who rolls his tongue as a cow rolls its tongue over pasture."],[9016,"During his Hajj, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man being supported between his two sons between Makkah and Madinah. He said: 'What is this?' They said: 'He vowed to walk to the House.' He said: 'Indeed Allah has no need for this man to torment himself. Let him ride.'"],[9017,"Anas b. Malik passed by us in the mosque of Banu Rifa'ah after we had prayed the dawn prayer. With him was a group of people, and one of them gave the call to prayer. He then prayed the two rak'ahs, then the iqamah was given, and Anas b. Malik stepped forward and led them in the dawn prayer. When he finished his prayer, he sent for two cushions, and they were brought to him. He turned to us and sat down to talk to us. Among what he said was..."],[9018,"This House is a pillar of the pillars of Islam. Whoever performs Hajj or Umrah to the House is under Allah's guarantee. If he dies, He will admit him to Paradise; and if He returns him to his family, He will return him with reward and spoils."],[9019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest wearing a helmet on his head, not in ihram. When he removed it, a man came to him and said: 'Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah.' He said: 'Kill him.'"],[9020,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping performed while he was in a state of ihrām due to a disease in his head."],[9021,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fruit until it had ripened. It was said to him: \"And what does it mean to ripen?\" He said: \"Until it turns red.\""],[9022,"A group of eight men from ʿUkl came to Madinah and embraced Islam, but they found the climate unhealthy. They went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and complained to him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"Go out to the camels and drink from their milk and urine.\" They went and stayed among them as long as Allah willed, then they killed the herdsman and drove away the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent someone to pursue them, and they were brought to him. He cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes."],[9023,"I did not prohibit fasting on Friday; rather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited it."],[9024,"When people brought dates to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would ask about them. If they said, \"It is sadaqah,\" he would say, \"Eat,\" and he would not eat. If they said, \"It is a gift,\" he would eat with them."],[9025,"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him, except fasting, which is for Me, and I reward it. And the unpleasant odor of the mouth of a fasting person is more fragrant with Allah than the scent of musk."],[9026,"The destitute person (miskīn) is not the one who goes around begging and is turned away by a morsel or two, or a date or two. Rather, the destitute person is the one who does not find enough to suffice him and does not ask people so that they give him."],[9027,"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him, but fasting is for Me, and I reward it. The unpleasant odor of the mouth of a fasting person is more fragrant with Allah than the scent of musk. He gives up his wife, his desire, his food, and his drink for My sake, so it is for Me, and I reward it. The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast, and a joy when he meets Me. Fasting is a shield; if anyone fights or insults him, he should not respond but say, 'I am fasting.'"],[9028,"I entered upon Anas b. Mālik in the afternoon on a day when people were unsure whether it was Ramaḍān, intending to greet him. He called for food and ate. I said, 'Is this what you are doing a Sunnah?' He replied, 'Yes.'"],[9029,"Every kind word or deed of goodness is charity, and among the acts of goodness is to meet your brother with a cheerful face and to pour from your bucket into your brother's vessel."],[9030,"When Muḥammad b. al-Munkadir mentioned the Qadariyyah, he would say: 'The Qadariyyah are the polytheists.'"],[9031,"Whoever exercises patience, Allah will grant him patience. Whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will make him self-sufficient. And whoever asks us, we will give him. No one is given a provision more spacious than patience."],[9032,"I said: O Messenger of God, which people are most severely tried? He said: \"The prophets.\" I said: Then who? He said: \"Then the righteous. One of them would be tested with poverty until he found nothing but a date or something like it. One of them would be tested with lice until he threw off the lice. And one of them would be more joyful at trial than at ease.\""],[9033,"A man from Thaqif gave the Messenger of God ﷺ a container of wine after wine had been forbidden. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered it to be split open. A man said: If only you had ordered it to be sold. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The One who forbade drinking it forbade selling it.\""],[9034,"Do not depart on the Day of Arafah until the imam departs."],[9035,"He used to say: \"O God, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, and I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit.\""],[9036,"A woman and her husband had a dispute, and they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The woman said: This is my husband. By the One who sent you with the truth, there is nothing on earth more hateful to me than him. The husband said: This is my wife. By the One who sent you with the truth, there is nothing on earth more hateful to me than her. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered them to come close to him, then he prayed for them. They did not leave him until she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, God has not created anything more beloved to me than him. And the husband said: By the One who sent you with the truth, God has not created anything more beloved to me than her."],[9037,"Jabir b. Abdullah visited him, then said: I will not leave until you undergo cupping, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Cupping is a cure.\""],[9038,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ in the year of the conquest say: \"God has forbidden the sale of wine, dead animals, pigs, and idols.\" It was said: O Messenger of God, what about the fat of dead animals? It is used to grease ships, grease leather, and people use it for lamps. He said: \"It is forbidden.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said at that: \"May God curse the Jews. God forbade them fat, but they rendered it, then sold it and consumed its price.\""],[9039,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of a cat."],[9040,"Gifts to the imam are embezzlement."],[9041,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mukhabarah, muzabanah, and muhaqalah."],[9042,"No zakat is due on any of the crops, palm trees, or vines until its harvest amounts to five wasqs."],[9043,"A man came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Have you prayed?\" He said: No. He said: \"Then pray two rak'ahs.\""],[9044,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a man to place one of his legs upon the other while lying on his back."],[9045,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ upon his return from Hunayn, while in Bilal’s garment there was silver that he was taking from and giving to the people. He said, “O Muhammad, be just.” He said, “Woe to you! Who will be just if I am not just? I would have failed and lost if I were not just.” Then Umar b. al-Khattab said, “Let me kill this hypocrite.” He said, “God forbid that people should say that I kill my companions. This man and his companions recite the Quran, but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They pass out of the religion as the arrow passes through the game.”"],[9046,"The sun set while the Messenger of God ﷺ was at Sarif, and he prayed Maghrib in Makkah, and between them were ten miles. And the sun set at Dhat al-Jaysh, and he prayed Maghrib in Madinah, and between them were eleven miles."],[9047,"He forbade eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days. Then he said after that, “Eat, and take provisions, and store.”"],[9048,"He forbade eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, and that a man eat with his left hand, and that he walk in one sandal."],[9049,"A cow is for seven, and a camel is for seven."],[9050,"Close the door and tie the water-skin."],[9051,"The Prophet ﷺ bought a camel from a Bedouin of Banu Amir b. Sa’sa’a. When the sale was concluded for him, the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Choose.” The Bedouin said to him, “If I have ever seen a sale better than your sale today, may God grant you long life. From whom are you?” He said, “From Quraysh.”"],[9052,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came from the mountain having relieved himself, and in front of them were dates on a shield. They invited him to it, and he sat down to eat with us, and he did not touch water."],[9053,"When the verse “Say: He is able to send upon you a punishment from above you” was revealed, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I seek refuge in God from that,” “or from beneath your feet,” the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I seek refuge in God from that,” “or confound you with sects,” he said, “This is easier.” And had he sought refuge from it, He would have granted him refuge."],[9054,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ camped at al-Hijr during the expedition of Tabuk, he stood and addressed the people, saying, “O people, do not ask your Prophet about signs. These are the people of Salih. They asked their Prophet to bring them a she-camel, and he did. It used to come from this mountain pass and drink their water on the day of its watering, and they would milk from its milk the like of what they used to obtain from the day of its absence. Then it would return from this mountain pass. But they rebelled against the command of their Lord and hamstrung it. Then God gave them a respite of three days, and God’s promise was not belied. Then the cry came to them, and God destroyed all who were among them between heaven and earth except a man who was in the sanctuary of God, and the sanctuary of God protected him from God’s punishment.” It was said, “O Messenger of God, who is he?” He said, “Abu Righal.”"],[9055,"I am your forerunner before you at the cistern, whose size is like the distance between Ayla and Makkah. And men and women will come, but they will not taste anything from it."],[9056,"Coarseness of hearts and harshness are among the people of the East, and faith and tranquility are among the people of the Hijaz."],[9057,"A slave girl belonging to one of the Ansar came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"My master forces me into prostitution.\" So God revealed: \"And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution if they desire chastity.\""],[9058,"When one of you is impressed by a woman and she captures his heart, let him go to his wife and have intercourse with her, for that will repel what is in his heart."],[9059,"Do not deem provision slow to come, for no soul dies until it reaches the end of its provision. So seek provision in a goodly manner, and beware of the unlawful."],[9060,"On the Day of Resurrection, we will be upon an elevated place above the people. The nations will be called by their idols and by what they used to worship, one after another, until our Lord comes to us after that and says, \"What are you waiting for?\" We will say, \"We are waiting for our Lord.\" He, Blessed and Exalted, will say, \"I am your Lord.\" They will say, \"Until we look at You.\" Then He will manifest Himself to them, then depart, and they will follow Him. Then every person, hypocrite and believer, will be given a shade on the day it covers them. Then they will follow Him, and the hypocrites will be with them upon the bridge over Hell, in which there are hooks and thorns that seize whomever God wills. Then the light of the hypocrite will be extinguished, and the believer will be saved. The first group to be saved will have faces like the moon on the night of the full moon—seventy thousand who will not be called to account. Then those who come after them will be like the brightest star in the sky, and so on. Then intercession will take place, and they will intercede until there comes out one who said, \"There is no god but God\" and in whose heart there is a barley grain's weight of faith. They will be placed at the courtyard of Paradise, and the people of Paradise will pour water upon them until they grow like vegetation carried by a flood. Then they will ask God until one of them is given the like of the dominion of this world and ten times its like."],[9061,"This community will be tested in its graves. When the believer enters it and his companions turn away from him, an angel of tremendous awe will come to him and say, \"What did you used to say about this man?\" The believer will say, \"I say that he is the Messenger of God and His servant.\" The angel will say to him, \"Look at your seat in Paradise which you see, and at your seat from which God has saved you from the Fire.\" He will see both of them. The believer will say, \"Let me go give glad tidings to my family.\" It will be said to him, \"Be still.\" As for the hypocrite, his family will turn away from him, and it will be said to him, \"What did you used to say about this man?\" He will say, \"I do not know; I used to say what the people said.\" It will be said to him, \"You did not know. Look at your seat in Paradise which you had—it has been replaced with your seat in the Fire.\""],[9062,"A group of my community will not cease fighting upon the truth, victorious until the Day of Resurrection, and between a man and disbelief is the abandonment of prayer."],[9063,"A group of my community will fight upon the truth, victorious until the Day of Resurrection, then Jesus son of Mary will descend. Their leader will say, \"Come forward and lead us in prayer.\" He will say, \"No, for some of you are leaders over others—so that God may honor this community.\""],[9064,"A dinar you give to a needy person, a dinar you give for freeing a slave, a dinar you spend in the path of God, and a dinar you spend on your family—the best of them is the dinar you spend on your family."],[9065,"Shurahbil b. al-Simt said to 'Amr b. 'Abasa, \"Will you relate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, with no forgetfulness and no falsehood?\" He said, \"Yes. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'God said: My love is due for those who love one another for My sake, and My love is due for those who support one another for My sake. There is no believing man or believing woman who offers up to God three children from his loins who do not reach puberty but that God will admit him to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy toward them.'\""],[9066,"The woman was created from a rib, and she will not be straight for you upon a single disposition. If you try to straighten her, you will break her. So deal with her gently, and you will live with her."],[9067,"\"Do you love that you should have a sixth of Paradise?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God, whose width is the heavens and the earth.\" He said, \"Then a fifth of it?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then a fourth?\" They said, \"That is even more.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I hope that I will be the remaining half.\""],[9068,"Whoever loves for the sake of God, hates for the sake of God, gives for the sake of God, and withholds for the sake of God has perfected faith."],[9069,"Perhaps your lifespan will be extended until you are one of those put in command over ten when the people inhabit the villages. Beware of being put in command over ten or more, for no man is placed over ten or more but that he will come to God with his hand chained to his neck, and nothing will release him from that chain except justice, if he was just among them. And do not inhabit the villages, for the one who inhabits the villages is like the one who inhabits the graves."],[9070,"The Kharijites are the dogs of Hellfire."],[9071,"No one intends evil for Madinah but that God will melt him as salt melts in water."],[9072,"He forbade cauterization."],[9073,"O Messenger of God, is it from pride that one of us has a fine, swift she-camel? He said: No. He said: Is it from pride that one of us has a beautiful garment? He said: No. He said: Is it from pride that one of us has a good pair of sandals? He said: No. He said: Is it from pride that I prepare food and invite my people, and they walk behind me and eat with me? He said: No. He said: Then what is pride, O Messenger of God? He said: That you belittle the truth and disparage people."],[9074,"Ali ؓ used to teach the people how to invoke blessings upon the Prophet of God, saying: O God, You who spread out the spread-out earth, created the raised heavens, and shaped hearts according to their innate natures, both their wretched and their blessed, make the most noble of Your blessings, the increasing of Your barakah, and the highest of Your greetings upon Muhammad, Your servant and messenger, the seal of what has passed, the opener of what was closed, the one who makes the truth known by the truth, and the crusher of the assaults of falsehood, as he fulfilled and undertook Your command in obedience to You, seeking Your pleasure fully, without any deficiency in his resolve or weakness in his determination, calling to Your revelation, guarding Your covenant, and pressing forward in carrying out Your command until he brought light, smiling, to a seeker of fire. Through him hearts were guided after the blunders of trials and sin, with the clear signs, the joys of Islam, and the noble qualities of the rulings. He is Your trusted, trustworthy one, the treasurer of Your stored knowledge, Your witness on the Day of Judgment, Your sent one as a blessing, and Your messenger with the truth as a mercy. O God, expand for him a spacious place in Your justice, and reward him with multiplied good from Your bounty, delightful and unspoiled, from the known reward of Your recompense and the abundant grant of Your giving. O God, raise his edifice above the edifices of those who remain, honor his resting place and his hospitality with You, and perfect for him his light and his reward from Your choosing him, accepted in testimony, pleasing in speech, one of just words, decisive speech, great proof and evidence."],[9075,"She granted protection to two men from Banu Makhzum on the day the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Makkah. Ali entered upon her and said: What is this, O Umm Hani? I will surely kill them. She said: So I locked the door on them, then went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and found him bathing while his daughter Fatimah was shielding him with a cloth. He bathed, then took the cloth and wrapped himself, then prayed the Duha prayer, eight rak'ahs. Then he said: What is the matter with you, O Umm Hani? I said: I have granted protection to two men from among my relatives, and Ali came wanting to kill them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: We have granted safety to those you have granted safety, and we have granted protection to those you have granted protection."],[9076,"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom."],[9077,"I find a fallen date, so I take it and eat it."],[9078,"Do not force your sick to eat or drink, for God feeds them and gives them drink."],[9079,"There is no fasting for one who has not intended it before dawn."],[9080,"My beloved ﷺ enjoined me to do three things: to pray the Duha prayer, not to sleep except after praying Witr, and to fast three days of every month."],[9081,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was bathing. He took a handful of water and threw it in my face, and said: \"Keep back, O Lakāʿ!\""],[9082,"We heard a sound from the sky falling to the earth, like the sound of a pebble falling into a basin. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw that pebble, and we were defeated."],[9083,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was wounded in his face on the day of Uhud, his father Mālik b. Sinān sucked the blood of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and swallowed it. It was said to him: \"Do you drink blood?\" He said: \"Yes, I drink the blood of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My blood has mixed with his blood; the Fire will not touch him.\""],[9084,"Throw the pebbles of Muḍar. Each tribe used to throw one pebble."],[9085,"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr was asked: \"What was the worst thing you saw the polytheists do to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"The worst thing I saw them do to him was that I saw them plot against him one day. While he was circumambulating, they seized the edge of his cloak and said: 'Are you the one who reviles our gods and forbids us from what our fathers worship?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Yes, I am that one.'\" He said: \"Abu Bakr was holding him, saying at the top of his voice: 'Would you kill a man for saying, My Lord is Allah, when he has come to you with clear proofs from your Lord?' while his eyes were flowing with tears.\""],[9086,"A woman's prayer in her house is better than her prayer in her courtyard, and her prayer in her courtyard is better than her prayer in her home, and her prayer in her home is better than her prayer outside."],[9087,"A man asked ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar: \"I have a maternal uncle who separated from his wife, and he became distressed and it was hard for him. I want to marry her, but he did not order me to do so, and he does not know.\" Ibn ʿUmar said: \"No, unless you marry with a desirable marriage: if she suits you, you keep her, and if you dislike her, you separate. For we used to count this in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as fornication.\""],[9088,"Whoever is appointed as a judge has been slaughtered without a knife."],[9089,"The people at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: a praying person would pray following his prayer, and his gaze would not go beyond the place of his feet. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, and Abu Bakr became the leader, and when one of the people stood to pray, his gaze would not go beyond the place of his sides. Then Abu Bakr passed away and ʿUmar became the leader, and when one of them stood, his gaze would not go beyond the place of the qiblah. Then ʿUthman b. ʿAffān became the leader, and when one of them stood, he would not turn right or left in the prayer.\""],[9090,"Muʿādh b. Jabal went out looking for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ but did not find him. He searched for him in his houses but did not find him. He followed him from alley to alley until he was directed to him on Mount Thawāb. He went out and climbed Mount Thawāb, looking right and left, and caught sight of him in the cave that people have made a path to, leading to the Mosque of Victory. There he was, prostrating. I descended from the top of the mountain while he was still prostrating, and he did not raise his head until I thought ill of him, thinking that he had passed away. When he raised his head, I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I thought ill of you and thought you had passed away.\" He said: \"Gabriel ﷺ came to me at this spot and said: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sends you greetings and says: What would you like Me to do with your community?' I said: 'Allah knows best.' He went away, then came back and said: 'He says: I will not displease you regarding your community.' So I prostrated. The best means of drawing near to Allah is prostration.\""],[9091,"He went out with ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, and ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever gives his pledge of allegiance and then breaks it will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection without his right hand.\""],[9092,"There never was a prophet but he had among his community devoted disciples from his companions who followed his command and were guided by his sunnah."],[9093,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain, so he delivered a sermon before the prayer, faced the qiblah, turned his cloak inside out, then descended and prayed two rak'ahs, saying only one takbir after another in them."],[9094,"I was with Musa b. Talhah in the mosque, then al-Sa'ib b. Yazid entered. He said: Go to that shaykh and say to him: My uncle Musa b. Talhah says to you: Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? So I went to him and said: Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I did see him. \"We entered upon him, myself and some boys with me, and found him eating dates from a basket, and with him were some of his companions. He took a handful of dates for us, one handful after another, and wiped his hand over our heads.\""],[9095,"The Prophet ﷺ set out on the expedition to Tabuk. When he was on part of the road, he went to relieve himself and I followed him. When he had finished, I said: Here is water, O Messenger of Allah. He moved away from me, and I moved away from him. He cleansed himself with water, then said: \"Pour it over me.\" So I poured water over him, and he washed his face three times, his hands three times, wiped his head, and wiped over his leather socks."],[9096,"From 'Abd Allah Dhu al-Bijadayn, who died during the Tabuk expedition, that he died in the middle of the night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended into his grave and said to Abu Bakr and 'Umar: \"Lower your brother to me.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his lahd, he said: O Allah, I am pleased with him, so be pleased with him. Abu Bakr said: By Allah, I wish I had been the one in the grave."],[9097,"Do you marvel at what these two birds do with their chicks? By Him who sent me with the truth, Allah is more merciful to His servants than these two birds are to their chicks. Then we turned back, and when we were at the Harrah of Waqim, the Bedouin woman who came with her son carrying a waterskin of milk and a sheep presented herself to us, and she offered it as a gift to him. He said: What has happened to your son? Has anything befallen him of what used to afflict him? She said: By Him who sent you with the truth, nothing has befallen him of what used to afflict him. And he accepted her gift. Then we went on until we were at a slope of the Harrah, a camel came trotting. He said: Do you know what this camel said? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is a camel that has come to me seeking refuge from its master. It claims that it has been plowing for him for years, until when he made it mangy and emaciated and advanced in age, he wanted to slaughter it. Go with it, O Jabir, to its owner and bring him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not know its owner. He said: It will guide you to him. He said: It went ahead of me, freed, until it stopped with me at the assembly of Banu Khatmah. I said: Where is the owner of this camel? They said: So-and-so, son of so-and-so. I went to him and said: Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came out with me until he came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: This camel of yours seeks my protection against you. It claims that you plowed with it for a time, until you made it mangy and emaciated and advanced in age, then you wanted to slaughter it? He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, that is indeed so. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Sell it to me. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he bought it from him, then let it loose among the trees until it raised its hump. And whenever any of the Emigrants or the Helpers had something wrong with one of their water-carrying camels, he would give it to him. That continued for a time. Ibrahim b. al-Mundhir said: Muhammad b. Talhah said to me: The expedition of Dhat al-Riqa' used to be called the expedition of wonders. This hadith was not narrated from Sharik b. 'Abd Allah except by 'Abd al-Hakim b. Sufyan, nor from 'Abd al-Hakim except by Muhammad b. Talhah; Ibrahim b. al-Mundhir was alone in transmitting it."],[9098,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Abu Jahm b. Hudhayfah over the spoils, and he struck a man with his bow, causing a wound that exposed the bone. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for it fifteen camels as diyah."],[9099,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed a man from his companions over the alms. He came back and said when he brought it: This is for you and this is for me. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he addressed the people and said: What is the matter with me that I appoint one of you over things from what Allah has entrusted to me, and he comes back and says: This is for you and this was gifted to me? Would one of you sit in the house of his father and the house of his mother until he is given a gift? Then he said: Would one of you sit in the house of his father and the house of his mother until he is given a gift? Then he said: None of you should come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a camel on his back that grunts, or a cow that moos, or a sheep that bleats. Then he raised his hands to the sky and said: Have I not conveyed?"],[9100,"'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf sold a vineyard to 'Uthman for forty thousand dinars. 'Uthman ordered 'Abd Allah b. Sa'd b. Abi Sarh, and he gave him the price. 'Abd al-Rahman divided it among the Banu Zuhrah, the poor of the Muslims, and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Miswar said: I came to 'A'ishah, and she said: What is this? I said: 'Abd al-Rahman sent it. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: None will be compassionate toward you after me except the patient ones. May Allah give Ibn 'Awf to drink from Salsabil of Paradise."],[9101,"The Prophet ﷺ went early to Banu Qurayzah on a bare donkey called Ya'fur."],[9102,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: This pulpit of mine is upon one of the streams of Paradise."],[9103,"He entered upon him and said: Remove the affliction, O Lord of mankind, from Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas. Then he took some dust from Buthan, put it in a bowl containing water, and poured it over him."],[9104,"He sold a plot of land that the Messenger of God ﷺ had granted him as a fief, near the house of Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, to Sa'd for eight thousand dirhams. He said: There was a man who had previously been ahead of him for it, and he offered him ten thousand dirhams for it, but he refused to sell it to him. Abu Rafi' said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The people of a rukh are more entitled to their rukh.” And Sa'd was closer."],[9105,"As for what I hear you saying—that Quraysh used to insult the Messenger of God ﷺ—indeed, the most I saw was that his house was between the house of Abu Lahab and 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt. The Messenger of God ﷺ would return to his house and find wombs and blood and filth that had been placed at his door, and he would push that aside with the tip of his bow and say: “What bad neighbors these are, O assembly of Quraysh!”"],[9106,"God, mighty and majestic is He, revealed to His Prophet ﷺ in Makkah: “The host will be routed and they will turn their backs” (Q 54:45). 'Umar b. al-Khattab said: “O Messenger of God, which host?”—and that was before Badr. He said: When the day of Badr came and Quraysh was defeated, I looked at the Messenger of God ﷺ in their tracks, brandishing his sword, saying: “The host will be routed and they will turn their backs.” And it was for the day of Badr. Then God, mighty and majestic is He, revealed concerning them: “Until, when We seize their affluent ones with punishment…” (Q 23:64) and the rest of the verse. And God revealed: “Have you not seen those who exchanged the favor of God for disbelief…” (Q 14:28) and the rest of the verse. And the Messenger of God ﷺ threw at them, and the throw spread over them and filled their eyes and mouths, so that a man would be killed while he was blinking his eyes, having been struck by it. Then God revealed: “And you did not throw when you threw, but God threw” (Q 8:17). And God revealed concerning Iblis: “When the two hosts saw each other, he turned on his heels and said: ‘I am innocent of you; I see what you do not see; I fear God, and God is severe in punishment’” (Q 8:48). And 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah and some people with him from the polytheists said on the day of Badr: “These people have been deceived by their religion.” Then God revealed: “When the hypocrites and those in whose hearts was disease said: ‘These people have been deceived by their religion’” (Q 8:49)."],[9107,"Abu Barzah al-Harithi came on the day of Badr carrying three heads to the Messenger of God ﷺ. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw him, he said: “Your right hand has succeeded.” He said: “O Messenger of God, as for two of them, I killed them, but as for one, I saw a white, handsome man with a beautiful face strike off its head.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “That was So-and-so, an angel from among the angels.”"],[9108,"I looked at al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib and he was like an idol, his eyes flowing with tears. When I looked at him, I said: “May God repay you, O relative, with evil—you fight your nephew alongside his enemy?” He said: “What has he done? Has he been killed?” I said: “God is mightier and more supportive for him than that.” He said: “What do you want with me?” I said: “Captivity, for the Messenger of God ﷺ has forbidden killing you.” He said: “This is not the first of his kindness.” So I took him captive, then brought him to the Messenger of God."],[9109,"On the day of Badr, the people gathered around Umayyah b. Khalaf, and I approached him. I looked at a piece of his armor that had broken off from under his armpit, and I stabbed him with the sword in it with a stab that killed him. And I was shot with an arrow on the day of Badr, and my eye was put out. The Messenger of God ﷺ spat in it, then supplicated for me, and nothing has harmed me in it since."],[9110,"The angels did not fight alongside the Prophet ﷺ except on the day of Badr. On other occasions they were only reinforcements. And the Prophet ﷺ had no horses with him except two: one belonging to al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad and the other to Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi."],[9111,"Abu Jahl b. Hisham said: “Muhammad claims that if you do not obey him, he will have a slaughter among you.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “And I say that, and you are among that slaughter.” When he saw him killed on the day of Badr, he said: “O God, You have fulfilled what You promised me.” Then he sent Abu Salamah b. 'Abd al-Asad toward Abu Jahl."],[9112,"Arbad b. Qays b. Juzayy b. Khalid b. Ja'far b. Kilab and 'Amir b. al-Tufayl b. Malik b. Ja'far came to Madinah to the Messenger of God ﷺ. They came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was sitting, and they sat before him. 'Amir b. al-Tufayl said: “O Muhammad, what will you give me if I become Muslim?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You will have what the Muslims have, and you will owe what they owe.” 'Amir said: “Will you give me the command after you if I become Muslim?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You will have what the Muslims have, and you will owe what they owe.” 'Amir said: “Will you give me the command after you if I become Muslim?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “That is not for you or for your people, but you may have the reins of the horses.” He said: “I now have the reins of the horses being dragged. Give me the nomads and you keep the settled people.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No.” When Arbad and 'Amir left, 'Amir said: “O Arbad, I will distract Muhammad with talk while you strike him with the sword. If you kill Muhammad, the people will not do more than accept blood money and dislike war, and we will give them the blood money.” Arbad said: “I will do it.” They came back to him, and 'Amir said: “O Muhammad, come with me so I may speak with you.” The Messenger of God ﷺ stood with him, leaning against the wall, and the Messenger of God ﷺ stood with him talking to him. Arbad drew the sword, but when he put his hand on the sword, it stuck to the hilt, and he could not draw it. Arbad delayed striking 'Amir, and the Messenger of God ﷺ turned and saw 'Amir and what he was doing, so he left them. When 'Amir and Arbad left the Messenger of God ﷺ, they went until they were at al-Harrah—the Harrah of Banu Waqim—and they dismounted. Sa'd b. Mu'adh and Usayd b. Hudayr came out to them and said: “Depart, O enemies of God!” 'Amir said: “Who is this, O Sa'd?” He said: “Usayd b. Hudayr, the one of the battalions.” They left, and when they were at al-Raqm, God sent a thunderbolt upon Arbad and it killed him. 'Amir went on until he was at al-Khuraym, and God sent an ulcer that afflicted him. Night overtook him in the house of a woman from Banu Sulul, and he began touching the ulcer in his throat and saying: “A gland like the gland of a camel in the house of a Sululi woman,” wishing that he would die in her house. Then he mounted his horse and spurred it until he died on it while returning. Then it was revealed concerning them: “God knows what every female carries and what the wombs decrease or increase…” up to His saying: “…and they have no protector besides Him” (Q 13:8-11). He said: The guardian angels from the command of God protect Muhammad ﷺ. Then He mentioned Arbad and what killed him, saying: “It is He who shows you the lightning, causing fear and hope…” up to His saying: “…and He is mighty in strength” (Q 13:12-13)."],[9113,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sat on the pulpit on Friday. When he sat down, he said: “Sit down.” 'Abd Allah b. Rawahah heard the Prophet ﷺ saying “Sit down,” so he sat down among Banu Ghanm. It was said: “O Messenger of God, that is Ibn Rawahah sitting among Banu Ghanm. He heard you telling the people to sit down, so he sat down in his place.”"],[9114,"'Abd Allah b. 'Umar passed by a man sitting in his prayer who had placed his left hand over his eye during prayer. He said to him: “The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘Do not sit in the sitting posture of a people who have been punished.’”"],[9115,"When one of you wakes up from sleep, he should not put his hand into the vessel until he has washed it, for he does not know where it spent the night; and he should mention God's name before putting it in."],[9116,"Seven whom God will shade in the shade of His Throne on the Day of Resurrection: a just ruler, a man who gives charity with his right hand and conceals it from his left, a man whom a woman of noble lineage and beauty offered herself, and he said, 'Truly, I fear God, Lord of the Worlds,' a man who remembers God in solitude and his eyes overflow with tears from fear of God, and a man who meets a man and says, 'By God, I love you for the sake of God,' and the other says, 'And I love you for the sake of God.'"],[9117,"The Messenger of God ﷺ heard a man say, 'Here, take it, a green one,' so he said, 'O Labbayk, we take your good omen from your mouth.'"],[9118,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed over the Negus and said five takbirs over him."],[9119,"There is no day on which God sets free more servants from the Fire than the Day of Arafat. He draws near and boasts about them to the angels, saying, 'What do these people want?'"],[9120,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ at Arafat, with my uncle riding behind me, and he was placing one of his two fingers over the other. I said, 'What does the Messenger of God ﷺ say?' He said, 'He says: Throw the pebbles like the small stones used for throwing.'"],[9121,"The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever."],[9122,"There has never been a prophet but that in his community there was a teacher or two teachers. And if there is one of them in my community, it is Umar b. al-Khattab. Indeed, the truth is upon Umar's tongue and heart."],[9123,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be called out: 'Where are the sons of sixty?' That is the age about which He said: 'Did We not give you life long enough for whoever would remember to remember, and the warner came to you?' (35:37)."],[9124,"I witnessed Badr with no hair on my face except one hair, and afterward God made the beards abundant."],[9125,"Whatever is between the east and the west is a qibla."],[9126,"He brought a sheep's shoulder to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he ate it and did not perform ablution."],[9127,"I met the Messenger of God ﷺ among his companions in the market, so I said, 'Where does the Messenger of God intend to go?' They said, 'He intends to mark out a mosque for your people.' He said, 'Then I came, and he had marked out a mosque for them and had planted a piece of wood in its qibla and set it up as a qibla.'"],[9128,"His father died leaving a debt of thirty wasqs owed to a Jewish man. Jabir asked for a delay, but he refused. Jabir spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, seeking his intercession. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and asked the Jew to take all his dates, but he refused. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him to grant a delay, but he refused. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the garden and paid him thirty wasqs, and ten wasqs remained surplus for Jabir. Jabir came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to tell him of the surplus and found him praying 'Asr. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished, Jabir came to him and told him that he had paid the debt in full, and informed him of the surplus that remained. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Tell that to 'Umar b. al-Khattab.' Jabir went to 'Umar and informed him, and he said: 'I knew when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked through it that Allah would surely bless it.'"],[9129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared the trees of Madinah inviolable for a distance of one barid in every direction. He sent me to mark the sanctuary: at Sharaf Dhat al-Jaysh, at Sharith, at Makhid, and at Nabt."],[9130,"It is not lawful for a believer to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[9131,"Al-bid' is between seven and ten."],[9132,"I am an Arab, the Qur'an is Arabic, and the language of the people of Paradise is Arabic."],[9133,"The hyena is game, and the pilgrim in ihram is forbidden to kill it."],[9134,"Abu Burda b. Niyar slaughtered a sacrificial animal just before dawn. When he finished, he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: 'Whoever slaughters before the prayer, that is not a sacrifice. The sacrifice is only what is slaughtered after the prayer. Go and offer a sacrifice.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I cannot find another animal for sacrifice; I have only a jadha' from goats.' He said: 'Go and sacrifice it, but there is no allowance in that for anyone after you.'"],[9135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent my father, Abu Hathamah, as a date-estimator. A man came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Hathamah has overestimated against me.' He summoned Abu Hathamah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Your cousin claims that you have overestimated against him.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I left out the 'ariyya for his family, what is given to the poor, and what the wind affects.' He said: 'Your cousin has increased your due and been fair.'"],[9136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. Sahl went with him. When they were at al-Harra, a snake bit 'Abd al-Rahman b. Sahl. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Summon 'Amr b. Hazm for me.' He was summoned, and he presented his ruqya to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'There is no harm in it; recite it over him.' He said: 'Ibn Hazm placed his hand on him and said: O Messenger of Allah, he is dying—or: he has died.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Recite it over him, even if he is dying—or has died.' So he recited it over him, and 'Abd al-Rahman recovered and went on his way."],[9137,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years. I never knew anything I did that pleased him, nor anything I did that displeased him. He accepted whatever Allah ordained. Even if one of his wives would say: 'If only you had done such-and-such; why did you do such?' he would say: 'Let him be, for nothing happens except what Allah wills.' I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ take revenge for himself over anything, unless a sacred limit of Allah was violated; if a sacred limit was violated, he was the most intense of people in anger for Allah's sake. And never were two matters presented to him but that he chose the easier of them, as long as it involved no displeasure to Allah; if it involved displeasure to Allah, he was the furthest of people from it."],[9138,"If he refuses, push him back; if he refuses, fight him; for he is only a devil—concerning the one who passes in front of a person praying."],[9139,"A desert Arab came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour come?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'And what have you prepared for the Hour?' The Arab said: 'I have not prepared much of deeds for it, except two things: that I love Allah and His Messenger.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Then you will be with those you love.'"],[9140,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out when the sun had declined, and led them in the noon prayer. When he had said the salam, he stood on the pulpit and mentioned the Hour, and mentioned that before it there would be great matters. Then he said: \"Whoever wishes to ask about something, let him ask about it. By Allah, you will not ask me about anything except that I will inform you of it as long as I am in this position of mine.\" Anas said: The people wept much when they heard that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeatedly said: \"Ask me about whatever you wish.\" So Abdullah b. Hudhafah al-Sahmi stood up and said: \"Who is my father?\" He said: \"Your father is Hudhafah.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeatedly said: \"Ask me,\" Umar stood up on his knees and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell silent when Umar said that. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, Paradise and the Fire were shown to me in the width of this wall, and I have never seen a day like today in good and evil.\""],[9141,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated the House on his riding camel, touching the corner with his staff."],[9142,"Whoever swears by al-Lat and al-Uzza, let him say: \"There is no god but Allah.\" And whoever says to his companion: \"Come, let me gamble with you,\" let him give charity."],[9143,"Whoever Allah wishes good for, He gives him understanding in religion. I am only a distributor, and Allah, may His mention be exalted, gives."],[9144,"Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah—the freed slave of a woman from the Ansar—was adopted by Abu Hudhayfah just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ adopted Zayd b. Harithah. In the time of ignorance, whoever adopted a man, people would call him to that man and he would inherit from his estate, until Allah revealed: \"Call them by their fathers; that is more just in the sight of Allah.\""],[9145,"A woman used to borrow jewelry during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then deny having it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that her hand be cut off."],[9146,"The sun eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he led the people in prayer."],[9147,"He used to narrate about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day the sun eclipsed in Madinah, that he did not pray more than two rak'ahs, like the morning prayer."],[9148,"Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."],[9149,"While I was sleeping, I saw myself circumambulating, and there was a man of brown complexion with lank hair between two men, with water dripping from his head. I said: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"Jesus son of Mary.\" Then I went away and turned, and there was a man of ruddy complexion, of large build, with curly hair and blind in the right eye, as if his eye were a floating grape. I said: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"The Dajjal. The person most resembling him among people is Ibn Qatan.\""],[9150,"The Jews will fight you, and you will be given power over them, until the stone will say: \"O servant of Allah, there is a Jew behind me, so kill him.\""],[9151,"A group of seventy thousand from my nation will enter Paradise, with their faces shining like the light of the full moon on the night of the full moon."],[9152,"When you say to your companion on Friday, \"Listen,\" while the imam is delivering the sermon, you have engaged in idle talk."],[9153,"Abu Bakr entered the mosque while Umar was speaking to the people. He went on until he entered the room of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which he had died—and it was in the room of A'ishah—and he uncovered the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from a striped Yemeni cloak with which he was covered, looked at his face, and bent over him and kissed him."],[9154,"He heard Umar's last sermon, when Abu Bakr sat on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that was the day after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died."],[9155,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her while she was screened by a curtain on which there were images of figures. He tore it down and then said, \"The people who will be most severely punished are those who imitate the creation of Allah.\""],[9156,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up one day looking gloomy. Maymunah said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have noticed a change in your appearance today.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained in that state for the rest of that day. Then it occurred to him that there was a puppy under a bed of ours. He ordered that it be taken out. Then he took some water in his hand and sprinkled it in its place. When evening came, Jibril ﷺ met him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"You had promised to meet me last night.\" He said, \"Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[9157,"Whoever goes to a soothsayer, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights."],[9158,"Allah favored Quraysh with seven qualities: He favored them because they worshipped Allah for ten years when no one worshipped Him except a Qurayshi; He favored them because He gave them victory on the Day of the Elephant while they were polytheists; He favored them because a surah of the Quran was revealed concerning them, in which no one else was included: \"For the familiarity of Quraysh\"; He favored them because among them are prophethood, the caliphate, the hijabah, and the siqayah."],[9159,"Shall I not direct you to what removes the rancor of the heart? Fasting three days of every month.\""],[9160,"When one of you enters the mosque, he should not sit down until he prays two rak'ahs."],[9161,"While a man was walking in a fine suit, admiring himself, the earth swallowed him up, and he will sink into it until the Day of Resurrection."],[9162,"Intercession was made only for those who commit major sins among my ummah."],[9163,"Some people of this ummah will delve so deeply into matters that one of them will say: \"This is Allah who created me, so who created Him?\"\""],[9164,"Whoever has intercourse with women in their anuses has disbelieved."],[9165,"The player of backgammon is like one who dips his hand in the flesh of a pig, and the one who watches it is like one who dips his hand in the blood of a pig."],[9166,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Prophet of God, I saw last night in a dream that there is no servant who bears witness that there is no god but God and bears witness that you are the Messenger of God except that God raises him a degree in Paradise, except the people of the shah—and that is chess.'"],[9167,"The caravan that has a bell—the angels do not accompany it."],[9168,"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn: 'I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of God, from every devil and poisonous creature, and from every evil eye.'"],[9169,"The woman with chronic bleeding leaves off prayer for the days of her menstrual periods in which she used to sit, then she performs one ghusl, then she performs ablution for each prayer."],[9170,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he stipulated upon me what he stipulated upon the believing women, then he said: 'In what you are able.'"],[9171,"Abdullah b. Abbas called al-Fadl on the day of Arafah and said: 'I am fasting.' Abdullah said: 'Do not fast, for the Prophet ﷺ had a milking vessel with milk brought near to him, and he drank from it on this day, and the people follow your example.'"],[9172,"No one who severs ties of kinship will enter Paradise."],[9173,"Shall I show you how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution? He took water with one of his hands, sniffed it, then brought the other hand to it and poured, and he poured it over his face, and washed his hands, then wiped his head and ears, then wiped over the tops of his feet over the sandal, then stood and prayed."],[9174,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey to Makkah, and when the Messenger of God ﷺ went out to relieve himself he would go far away so that no one would see him. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ noticed two trees far apart, and he said: 'O Ibn Mas'ud, go to these two trees and say to them: The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to come together for him so that he may conceal himself with you.' So one of them walked to the other, and the Messenger of God ﷺ relieved himself, then they returned to their places. Then he went on until we reached the alleys of Madinah, and a camel came rushing until it prostrated to the Messenger of God ﷺ, then stood before him with its eyes shedding tears. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Who is the owner of this camel?' They said: 'So-and-so.' He said: 'Call him to me.' So they brought him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'What is your affair with this camel that it complains about you?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, this camel—we have been drawing water on it for twenty years, then we wanted to slaughter it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'It complained of that. What a bad way you have repaid it. You used it for twenty years, and when its bones became thin and its skin became thin, you wanted to slaughter it. Sell it to me.' They said: 'Rather it is yours, O Messenger of God.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered it, and he sent it with the riding animals. Then his companions said to him: 'O Messenger of God, this camel prostrated to you, and we are more deserving of prostration.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'God forbid that anyone should prostrate to anyone. If anyone were to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.'"],[9175,"If My servant remembers Me alone, I remember him alone; if he remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering of angels; and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him at speed."],[9176,"God singled out His Messenger ﷺ from this fay' with something He gave no one else. God Almighty said: 'And what God restored to His Messenger from them, you did not spur on for it any horse or riding camel' (Qur'an 59:6). This was exclusively for the Messenger of God ﷺ. By God, he did not choose it instead of you, nor did he keep it for himself to your exclusion. He gave it to you, until there remained of it this wealth that remains. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ would spend on his family their yearly maintenance from this wealth, then take what remained and put it in the place of God's wealth. The Messenger of God ﷺ acted accordingly throughout his life until he passed away. Then 'Umar later said to 'Uthman, 'Abd al-Rahman, al-Zubayr, and Sa'd, while they were with him: 'I adjure you by God, do you know that?' They said: 'Yes.'"],[9177,"The prayer was commenced, so we stood and straightened the rows before the Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us."],[9178,"Righteousness is not fasting while traveling."],[9179,"When we raised our heads from bowing, none of us would put his head down until we saw the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrating."],[9180,"When the call to prayer is made, Satan retreats between him and al-Rawha' so that he does not hear the sound of the adhan, and the gates of heaven and the gates of Paradise are opened, and supplication is answered."],[9181,"Eat olive oil and anoint yourselves with it, for it comes from a blessed tree."],[9182,"The Messenger of God ﷺ slaughtered seventy camels on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, sharing every seven in one camel."],[9183,"The Messenger of God ﷺ shaved his head at al-Hudaybiyah, and many of his companions shaved. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'May God have mercy on those who shave.' A man said: 'O Messenger of God, and those who shorten?' He said: 'May God have mercy on those who shave.' He said on the third time: 'And those who shorten.'"],[9184,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, while mentioning the false messiah: 'I will tell you a word about him that no prophet before me has said: he is one-eyed, and God is not one-eyed. Between his eyes is written: disbeliever.' Jabir said, from the Prophet ﷺ: 'Every believer, literate or illiterate, will read it. He will roam the earth for forty days, reaching every town except these two: Madinah and Makkah, which God has forbidden to him. One of his days will be like a year, one like a month, one like a week, and the rest of his days like these days of yours. Nothing will remain except forty days.'"],[9185,"Umm Salamah asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission to have cupping done, and he permitted her. She sent for a foster-mother of hers, who cupped her."],[9186,"There is no servant but has on his head a knotted thread. When he wakes up, praises God, stands, performs ablution, and prays, the knots are undone. If he wakes up and does not praise God, Satan says to him: 'You have a long night ahead; sleep,' and Satan ties the thread upon him."],[9187,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent us with Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, and we were six hundred and some odd men, to intercept a caravan of Quraysh. The Messenger of God ﷺ found no provision for us except a bag of dates. He would give us one date each day, which we would suck and then drink water over it. We felt its loss when it was exhausted. Then we turned to the leaves of trees, striking them with our sticks, then we would grind them and drink water over it, until we were called the Army of the Leaves. We passed by the seashore, and the sea cast up for us a creature called al-'anbar, like a large sand dune. Abu 'Ubaydah said: 'It is carrion, not lawful for us.' Then he later said: 'Rather, we are in the path of God, and we are compelled.' So we ate from it for about half a month and more, and we cut many strips from it. We would scoop the fat from the place of its eye with jars until we finished it. Then thirteen of our men sat in the place of its eye. Then Abu 'Ubaydah took one of its ribs, set it up on its two ends, ordered the tallest camel in the caravan, and had it saddled. A man rode on it and passed beneath the rib without his head touching it. We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'Do you have any of it with you?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Feed us from it.' We sent him a strip, and he ate from it."],[9188,"How will you be when the son of Maryam descends among you, while your imam is one of you?"],[9189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up one night saying: “Glory be to Allah! What treasures have been sent down, and what trials have been sent down? Who will wake up the occupants of the chambers? Many a woman is clothed in this world yet naked in the Hereafter.”"],[9190,"The liar is not the one who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good. She said: I did not hear him grant a concession regarding anything that people say as a lie except in three cases: in war, in reconciliation, and in a man’s speech to his wife."],[9191,"A woman came to me with her two sons, and I found nothing for her except a date, so I gave it to her, and she divided it between them."],[9192,"He prohibited every beast of prey having a canine tooth."],[9193,"He stood between the two jamarat during the Hajj he performed, and that was on the Day of Sacrifice, and said: “This is the day of the greater Hajj.”"],[9194,"He prohibited wrapping oneself in the sammaʾ (a manner of wearing a garment that leaves no opening for the arms) and for a man to sit with his legs drawn up in a single garment with nothing covering his private part."],[9195,"Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. Whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys my commander has disobeyed me."],[9196,"From ʿAʾishah that she said, mentioning Zaynab bt. Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: “I have never seen a woman better in religion than Zaynab: more God-fearing, more truthful in speech, more maintaining of kinship ties, greater in charity, and more devoted to exerting herself in work by which she gave charity and sought nearness to Allah.”"],[9197,"She brought her son to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he had reached the age of eating food, and she told him that her son had urinated in the Prophet’s lap ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and sprinkled it over his urine, but did not wash it thoroughly."],[9198,"Saʿd b. ʿUbadah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a vow that was upon his mother and whether he should fulfill it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to fulfill it on her behalf."],[9199,"My ummah will come on the Day of Resurrection with radiant faces and limbs from the traces of ablution. Whoever among you is able to increase his radiance, let him do so."],[9200,"The Prophet ﷺ asked for water for ablution, and it was said to him, “We did not find any except in the skin of a dead animal.” He said, “Did you tan it?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “Then bring it, for that is its purification.”"],[9201,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Abtah, and the Prophet ﷺ was in a leather tent. He performed ablution in a stone basin, and Bilal came out with the leftover water. He prayed Zuhr and Asr, while a man, a woman, and a donkey passed in front of him, beyond the spear."],[9202,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he checked on some men at the morning prayer and said, “Where is so-and-so, and where is so-and-so?” He said, “There is no prayer heavier upon the hypocrite than the Isha and Fajr prayers. If they knew what was in them, they would come to them even if they had to crawl.”"],[9203,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer while still completing it fully."],[9204,"“Whoever seizes the right of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah has made the Fire obligatory for him and forbidden Paradise for him.” A man said, “Even if it is something small, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Even if it is a stick of Arak.”"],[9205,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years. He never said to me about something I did, “Why did you do it?” nor about something I did not do, “Why did you not do it?” He said: And Ma‘mar added for me in it: “ever.”"],[9206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting on top of his house and said, “O Salma, bring me water for washing.” I came to him with a vessel containing water mixed with lote-tree leaves, and I strained it for him. Then he knelt on a cushion stuffed with palm fiber while I poured water over his head, and he washed it. I saw every drop falling from his head into the vessel, as if it were gleaming pearls. Then I brought him water and he washed with it. When he finished his washing, he said, “O Salma, pour out what is in the vessel in a place where no one will step over it.” I took the vessel and drank some of it, then poured out the rest. He said to me, “What did you do with what was in the vessel?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I envied the earth for it, so I drank some of it and poured the rest on the ground.” He said, “Go, for Allah has thereby forbidden you to the Fire.”"],[9207,"When one of you has a ringing in his ear, let him remember me and invoke blessings upon me, and let him say: “May Allah remember with good the one who remembered me.”"],[9208,"Every nation has Magians, and every nation has Christians, and every nation has Jews. Indeed, the Magians of my nation are the Qadariyyah, their Christians are the Khashabiyyah, and their Jews are the Murji’ah."],[9209,"Gold for gold, and silver for silver, like for like."],[9210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the people of Madinah: “O Allah, bless them in their sa‘ and their mudd.”"],[9211,"Uthman came when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was equipping the army of hardship with a thousand dinars in his sleeve, and he poured them into the lap of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ put his hand into them and turn them over, saying, “What harm can come to Ibn Affan after what he has done today?” He said it twice."],[9212,"Whoever would like the children of Adam to glorify him while standing, the Fire is due for him."],[9213,"Every sin, it may be that God will forgive it, except one who dies a polytheist, or a believer who kills a believer deliberately."],[9214,"The believer continues to advance in righteousness as long as he does not shed forbidden blood; but when he sheds forbidden blood, he falters."],[9215,"Whoever changes the religion of God, kill him."],[9216,"Three people: their prayer is not accepted, and no good deed of theirs ascends to God: the drunkard until he sobers up, the wife with whom her husband is angry, and the runaway slave until he returns and places his hand in the hand of his masters."],[9217,"Any slave who dies while he is a runaway enters the Fire, even if he is killed in the path of God."],[9218,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the stud fee of a stallion, selling water, and selling crops (before they are ripe)."],[9219,"The right of way of the road is seven cubits."],[9220,"I was presented to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr when I was thirteen years old, and the Messenger of God ﷺ rejected me. Then I was presented to him on the day of Uhud when I was fourteen, and he rejected me. Then I was presented on the day of the Confederates when I was fifteen, and I was allowed."],[9221,"Whoever enters ihram from the Sacred House enters forgiven."],[9222,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and took his hand, and it was softer than silk and cooler than snow."],[9223,"He forbade sleeping before the evening prayer and engaging in conversation after it."],[9224,"He used to shorten the prayer at al-ʿAqīq."],[9225,"When you come to prayer, let one of you walk calmly and with dignity; then pray whatever you have caught up with, and make up what was missed."],[9226,"Whoever relieves a hardship from among the hardships of a Muslim in this world, Allah will relieve a hardship from among the hardships of the Hereafter for him. Whoever conceals the faults of a Muslim in this world, Allah will conceal his faults in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever eases things for one in difficulty in this world, Allah will ease things for him in this world and the Hereafter. And Allah is in the aid of the servant as long as the servant is in the aid of his brother."],[9227,"If the inhabitants of the heavens and the inhabitants of the earth were to gather together to kill a believing man, Allah would cast them all into the Fire."],[9228,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him what Allah has made lawful for a man from his wife while she is menstruating. He said: \"What is above the navel.\""],[9229,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying while I was facing him."],[9230,"He forbade urinating in stagnant water, and then performing ablution from it."],[9231,"Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise; its banks are of gold, and it flows over pearls and rubies."],[9232,"When the Prophet ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey to the heavens, the adhan was revealed to him. He descended with it, and Jibrīl taught it to him."],[9233,"The Sunnah of recitation in prayer is that you recite in the first two rakʿahs the Fātiḥah and a surah, and in the last two rakʿahs the Fātiḥah."],[9234,"A servant from among the servants of Allah said: 'O Lord, to You belongs praise as befits the majesty of Your face and the greatness of Your authority.' The two recording angels were confounded, so they ascended to the lowest heaven and said: 'O Lord, Your servant has said a statement, and we do not know how to record it.'"],[9235,"I passed by the Prophet ﷺ while he was sitting in al-Ḥijr. He said: \"O Umm al-Faḍl.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"You are pregnant with a boy.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how can that be when Quraysh have sworn not to approach women?\" He said: \"It is as I tell you. So when you give birth, bring him to me.\" She said: \"When I gave birth, I brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He called the adhān in his right ear and the iqāmah in his left ear, and he placed some of his saliva in his mouth, and named him ʿAbd Allāh. Then he said: 'Take away the father of the caliphs.'\" She said: \"I went to al-ʿAbbās and informed him. He was a handsome man who dressed well, of medium stature. He dressed up and then came to the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he stood up to him, kissed him between his eyes, then seated him at his right. Then he said: 'This is my uncle. Whoever wishes, let him boast about his uncle.' Al-ʿAbbās said: 'Some of the talk, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Why should I not say this, O uncle? You are my uncle, the equal of my father, the remnant of my forefathers, and my inheritor, and the best of my family whom I leave behind after me.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Umm al-Faḍl said such and such.' He said: 'It is yours, O ʿAbbās, after one hundred and thirty-two [years]. Then from you will be the Saffāḥ, the Manṣūr, and the Mahdī. Then it will be in their descendants until the last of them is the one who will pray with the Messiah, ʿĪsā b. Maryam.'"],[9236,"The hand of the giver is the upper hand, and the best charity is that which leaves [one] free of need, and begin with those you support. Your wife says, 'Spend on me or divorce me,' and your child says, 'O father, to whom are you entrusting us?' and your servant says, 'Feed me and employ me.'"],[9237,"I saw 'Ammar b. Yasir mention 'Uthman b. 'Affan, so I said [to myself], 'If only I could get the better of this one.' On the Day of Siffin, he was wearing armor and began charging until he entered the ranks, then came out. I looked and saw that the armor had slipped from his knee and leg. I aimed my spear at him and thrust it into his knee, then killed him. 'Amr b. al-'As said, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: His killer and his despoiler will be in the Fire.'"],[9238,"Pride is My cloak, and whoever contends with Me for My garment, I will cast him into the Fire."],[9239,"Does the one who raises his head before the imam feel secure that God will turn his head into the head of a donkey?"],[9240,"The Messenger of God ﷺ dispatched a detachment in which I was present. Our shares reached twelve camels per man, and the Messenger of God ﷺ gave us an additional camel each after that."],[9241,"Whoever suppresses anger while able to carry it out, God will let him choose any of the wide-eyed maidens on the Day of Resurrection; whoever gives up a beautiful garment while able to have it, God will clothe him in the cloak of faith on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever arranges a marriage for a slave, God will place the crown of sovereignty on his head on the Day of Resurrection."],[9242,"I said to Anas b. Malik, 'Show us how the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed.' He stood and prayed, raising his hands with every takbir. When he finished, he said, 'This is how the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed.'"],[9243,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus and said four takbirs over him."],[9244,"The angels washed Adam with water and lote-tree leaves, shrouded him, dug a niche grave for him, and buried him. They said, 'This is your practice, O children of Adam, for your dead.'"],[9245,"I went with my father to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and behold, he had long hair with traces of henna, wearing two green garments."],[9246,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led them in the noon prayer and raised his voice, reciting, 'By the sun and its brightness' and 'By the night when it covers.' Ubayy b. Ka'b said to him, 'O Messenger of God, have you been commanded something regarding this prayer?' He said, 'No, but I wanted to set a time for your prayer.'"],[9247,"The Messenger of God ﷺ allowed [the picking up of] a staff, a whip, a rope, and the like, which a pilgrim in ihram may take and keep for himself."],[9248,"Do not persist in looking at lepers."],[9249,"The most excellent worship is understanding in religion, and the most excellent religion is scrupulousness."],[9250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once prayed Fajr and made it very dark, then he prayed it another day and let it become light, then he said: \"The time is between those two.\""],[9251,"Ma'mar b. 'Abd Allah al-'Adawi shaved the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of Sacrifice."],[9252,"The key to prayer is purification; its sanctity is the takbir; and its release is the taslim."],[9253,"Whoever does not recite the Mother of the Book in his prayer, it is deficient."],[9254,"The most wretched of the wretched is one upon whom the poverty of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter are combined."],[9255,"Thirty [years] of prophethood and kingship, then thirty of kingship and tyranny, and after that there is no good in it."],[9256,"The great battles will be at the hands of the fifth of the family of Heraclius."],[9257,"When you see Allah giving a servant what he loves while he persists in disobedience to Him, that is only a gradual lure from Him to him. Then he recited this verse: 'So when they forgot what they had been reminded of, We opened for them the gates of everything, until when they rejoiced in what they had been given, We seized them suddenly, and they were plunged into despair. So the last remnant of the people who wronged was cut off, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'"],[9258,"When 'Ubada was near death and I was at his head weeping, he said, 'What makes you weep?' I said, 'Why should I not weep over your benefit to me and my benefit from you?' He said, 'By Allah, I have not concealed from you a single word I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except one, and I will tell it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever says \"There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner,\" with his heart obedient to it and his tongue humble with it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.'"],[9259,"The thief is not fined when the legal punishment has been carried out on him."],[9260,"Prayer was originally prescribed as two rak'ahs when it was first made obligatory. Then it was increased for the resident prayer, while the traveler's prayer remained two rak'ahs."],[9261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Ibn Sayyad while he was playing with some boys. He recognized him, so he went up to him and said, \"Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" Ibn al-Sayyad said, \"I bear witness that you are the Prophet of the unlettered. Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I believe in Allah and His messengers.\""],[9262,"Do not kill locusts, for it is the mighty army of Allah."],[9263,"The records of the people of the earth are copied into the records of the people of heaven every Monday and Thursday, and every Muslim who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except a man between whom and his brother there is enmity."],[9264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite Surah al-Jumu'ah in the Friday prayer, thereby stirring the believers, and in the second rak'ah Surah al-Munafiqun, thereby alarming the hypocrites."],[9265,"Three will not be terrified by the great fright, nor will they be brought to account: they will be on a hill of musk until Allah finishes the reckoning of His servants: a man who recites the Qur'an seeking the face of Allah and leads a people in prayer while they are pleased with him; a caller who calls to the five prayers seeking the face of Allah; and a slave who excels in what is between him and his Lord and in what is between him and his masters."],[9266,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[9267,"If the believer were in a hole, Allah would appoint someone in it to harm him."],[9268,"I was with 'A'ishah, and Ka'b al-Ahbar was with her. He mentioned Israfil, and 'A'ishah said, \"O Ka'b, tell me about Israfil.\" Ka'b said, \"You have the knowledge.\" She said, \"Yes, so tell me.\" He said, \"He has four wings: two wings in the air, one wing with which he is enshrouded, and one wing upon his shoulder. The Throne is upon his shoulder and the Pen is upon his ear. When revelation descends, the Pen writes, then the angels study it. The angel of the Trumpet is kneeling on one knee, with the other knee raised, and he has put the Trumpet to his mouth, his back bent, his gaze fixed on Israfil. He has been commanded that when he sees Israfil fold his wing, he should blow the Trumpet.\" 'A'ishah said, \"Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say.\""],[9269,"They used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he bowed, they bowed, and when he said, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' they remained standing until they saw him place his face on the ground, then they followed him."],[9270,"I entered Paradise and found myself before a palace. I said, 'Whose is this?' It was said, 'For 'Umar b. al-Khattab.'"],[9271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Surah al-Najm, and when he reached the prostration, he prostrated."],[9272,"O Mughira, when you intend to marry a woman, do not marry her until you have looked at her."],[9273,"I gathered some property of mine from charity and came to Aisha. I said, 'O Mother of the Believers, I have gathered some property of mine from charity. Ask the Messenger of God ﷺ in which of these I should place it: in a slave I free, or in the way of God, or upon a hard-pressed husband and orphaned nephews?' The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Aisha, and she mentioned it to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Give it in charity on behalf of a hard-pressed husband and orphaned nephews. Charity given to relatives doubles the reward twice.'"],[9274,"Pray the dawn prayer when it is bright, for that is greater for the reward."],[9275,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to breathe three times in the vessel, mentioning God's name at each breath, and giving thanks at the last of them."],[9276,"There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses."],[9277,"Whoever digs a grave, God builds for him a house in Paradise; and whoever washes a dead body, he comes out of his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him; and whoever shrouds a dead body, God clothes him with garments from the robes of Paradise; and whoever consoles a grieving person, God clothes him with piety and sends blessings upon his soul among the souls; and whoever consoles an afflicted person, God clothes him with two garments from the robes of Paradise that the world cannot equal; and whoever follows a funeral procession until its burial is complete, three qirats are written for him, each qirat greater than Mount Uhud; and whoever sponsors an orphan or a widow, God shades him in His shade and admits him to His Paradise."],[9278,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'I seek refuge in You from the trial of the false messiah, the Dajjal, and from the punishment of the grave, and from the trial of the grave, and from the evil of the trial of wealth, and from the evil of the trial of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the trial of the false messiah, the Dajjal. O God, wash away my sins with water of snow and hail, and purify my heart from sins as You purified the white garment from dirt, and I seek refuge in You from laziness, senility, sin, and debt.'"],[9279,"Whoever swears a binding oath in which he is lying, let him take his seat in the Fire facing it."],[9280,"Abdullah b. Umar was approached and told, 'Ibn Abbas commands mut'ah marriage.' Ibn Umar said, 'Glory be to God! I do not think Ibn Abbas would do this.' They said, 'Yes, he commands it.' He said, 'Was Ibn Abbas anything but a young boy when the Messenger of God ﷺ —' Then Ibn Umar said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from it, and we were not fornicators.'"],[9281,"The polytheists do not dye their beards, so change the white hair."],[9282,"Whoever among you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."],[9283,"He would not arrive from a journey except at forenoon, and he would begin with the mosque, praying two rak'ahs in it, then he would go to his family after that."],[9284,"He used to encourage the people to stand in prayer during Ramadan without commanding them to do so as an obligatory matter. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away and the matter remained thus, and it remained thus during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and part of the caliphate of Umar ؓ."],[9285,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr with nine rak'ahs."],[9286,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night while the moon was rising on the night of the full moon. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, you will see your Lord in Paradise just as you see this moon; you will not be harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome and miss the prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.\" Then he recited: \"And glorify the praises of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting.\""],[9287,"Whoever is generous to his family on the day of Ashura, Allah will be generous to him for the entire year."],[9288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out while the Abyssinians were playing, and I was looking through a small window of mine. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came close to me, so I placed my hands on his shoulders and began to watch. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They are the daughters of Arfida.\" I continued watching them playing and dancing until I was the one who stopped."],[9289,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ needed to relieve himself, he would go far away. One day he went for that need, then performed ablution and put on one of his leather socks. A green bird came, took the other sock, flew up with it, and then dropped it, and a black slithering creature came out of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is an honor with which Allah has honored me.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the evil of what walks on its belly, from the evil of what walks on two legs, and from the evil of what walks on four.\""],[9290,"Talha b. Ubayd Allah spoke harshly to Amir b. Fuhayra about something. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Gently, O Talha, for he witnessed Badr just as you witnessed it, and the best of you are the best to their freed slaves.\""],[9291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping performed on his head after he was poisoned."],[9292,"The Prophet ﷺ lay down on a mat, and the mat left marks on his skin. When he woke up, I began to wipe those marks and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, why did you not let me know before sleeping on this mat so that I could spread something over it to protect you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What have I to do with this world? What has this world to do with me? I and this world are but like a rider who rests in the shade of a tree, then leaves it and moves on.\""],[9293,"When this verse was revealed: 'The Messenger believes in what has been sent down to him from his Lord, and so do the believers,' the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it. When he reached 'Our Lord, Your forgiveness, and to You is the final return,' Allah said: 'I have forgiven you.' When he said: 'Our Lord, do not hold us accountable if we forget or fall into error,' Allah said: 'I will not hold you accountable.' When he said: 'And do not place upon us a burden like that which You placed upon those before us,' Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'I will not place a burden upon you.' When he said: 'And do not impose upon us that which we have no strength to bear,' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I will not impose upon you. And pardon us,' He said: 'I have pardoned you.' When he said: 'And forgive us,' He said: 'I have forgiven you.' When he said: 'And have mercy on us,' He said: 'I have had mercy on you.' When he said: 'And grant us victory over the disbelieving people,' He said: 'I have granted you victory over the disbelieving people.'"],[9294,"When the Prophet ﷺ woke up, he would say: 'Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection.' And when the Prophet ﷺ slept, he would say: 'In Your name, O Allah, we die and we live.'"],[9295,"The example of the one who upholds the limits set by Allah, the one who flatters concerning the limits set by Allah, and the one who violates the limits set by Allah is like three people who were on a ship. They divided its quarters, and one of them got the place where water seeped in and where water was bailed out, so they were bothered by him. He took an axe and began to chop at his place. One of the remaining two said to the other: 'Do you not see this one who wants to breach our ship and drown us?' The other replied: 'Leave him, for he is only breaching his own place.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If they stop him, he and they will be safe; but if they leave him, he will drown and they will drown.'"],[9296,"When the Prophet ﷺ performed ghusl from janabah, he washed his palms three times before dipping them into the vessel. Then he poured with his right hand over his left, washing his private part until he cleansed it with his left hand. Then he performed wudu as for prayer.\" She said: \"He had hair, and he would take water and insert it into the roots of his hair, running his fingers through it, until when he had cleansed the skin, he poured over his head three times, then poured over his body."],[9297,"One of evil disposition will not enter Paradise. Cursed is one who harms a Muslim or deceives him."],[9298,"Fatimah said: What grief for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: O my daughter, there has come upon your father a matter from which Allah will leave no one until the meeting of the Day of Resurrection."],[9299,"The Prophet ﷺ visited me and said: \"Do you know who the martyrs of my Ummah are on the Day of Resurrection?\" The people remained silent, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, the one killed in the path of Allah, the patient one who seeks reward is a martyr. He said: \"If the martyrs of my Ummah were only these, they would be few indeed. The one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr; the one who drowns is a martyr; the one who dies of a stomach disease is a martyr; the plague is martyrdom; and the woman who dies in childbirth, her child will drag her by her umbilical cord to Paradise.\""],[9300,"Five prayers Allah has made obligatory upon His servants. Whoever performs their ablution well and prays them at their times, and completes their bowing, prostration, and humility, has a covenant with Allah that He will forgive him. And whoever does not do that has no covenant with Allah; if He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him."],[9301,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform wudu with one mudd."],[9302,"The womb (rahm) is a branch of the Most Merciful (al-Rahman), attached to the waist of the Most Merciful. It says: O Allah, maintain ties with the one who maintains ties with me, and sever the one who severs me."],[9303,"We stopped at a place and fleas annoyed us, so we cursed them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not curse them, for what a fine creature it is: it woke you up to remember Allah.\""],[9304,"Regarding the saying of Allah: 'Among them are those We have related to you and among them are those We have not related to you,' he said: Allah sent an Abyssinian slave as a prophet, and he is among those not related to Muhammad ﷺ."],[9305,"When he went on a raid and did not fight at the beginning of the day, he did not hasten until the prayers were due, the winds blew, and the fighting became good."],[9306,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ curse women who pluck their eyebrows, those who file their teeth for beauty, those who tattoo, and those who change the creation of Allah."],[9307,"Whoever cannot find an izar while in ihram but finds trousers, let him wear them; and whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear leather socks, cutting them below the ankles."],[9308,"It is as if I am looking at the glistening of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reciting the talbiyah."],[9309,"The first prayer that was made obligatory upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the Zuhr prayer."],[9310,"How will it be with you when your young men become dissolute and your women become tyrannical? They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will that indeed happen?\" He said, \"And worse than that will come. How will it be with you when you see good as evil and evil as good?\""],[9311,"Do not pluck white hairs, for they are light. Whoever grows one white hair in Islam, ten good deeds are written for him, one sin is erased from him, and he is raised one degree in rank."],[9312,"Whatever intoxicates in a large amount, a sip of it is unlawful."],[9313,"We asked Ali about the daytime prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"You would not be able to perform it.\" They said, \"We would like to know it.\" He said, \"He would wait until when the sun was in the east like it is in the west at the time of Asr, he would go to his family and take a midday nap if he wished. Then when the sun declined, he would stand and pray four rak'ahs, and he would pray two rak'ahs after Zuhr and four rak'ahs before Asr.\""],[9314,"There is no Muslim who greets me except that Allah returns my soul to me so that I may return the greeting."],[9315,"There will come a generation after sixty years who will neglect prayer and follow desires; they will meet with ruin. Then there will come a generation who recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their throats. Three types of people recite the Quran: a believer, a hypocrite, and a wicked person."],[9316,"In the last part of my Ummah there will be women who are clothed yet naked, with something like the humps of camels on their heads. Curse them, for they are cursed. If there were a nation behind you, they would serve them as the women of the nations before you serve you."],[9317,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing ablution and wiping water over his feet."],[9318,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ called Salman and said, \"The Prophet of Allah wishes to grant you some words from the Most Merciful, by which you may seek His favor and supplicate with them during the night and day: O Allah, I ask You for soundness in faith, and faith in good character, and a salvation followed by success, and mercy from You and well-being, and forgiveness from You and good pleasure.\""],[9319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: “Indeed, Allah commands you to render trusts to their owners” up to His saying: “Indeed, Allah is ever Hearing and Seeing,” placing his thumb on his ear and the finger next to it on his eye. He said to us, \"Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite, placing his two fingers.\""],[9320,"When you hear the muezzin, say as he says, then invoke blessings upon me; for whoever invokes blessings upon me once, Allah will bless him ten times. And ask Allah for al-Wasilah for me, for it is a station in Paradise which is not fitting for anyone except a servant from among the servants of Allah, and I hope that I am he. Whoever asks al-Wasilah for me, intercession becomes due for him."],[9321,"I came to 'Uqbah b. 'Amir and said, 'Will you not be amazed at Abu Tamim al-Jayshani? He prays two rak'ahs before the Maghrib prayer.' 'Uqbah said, 'As for us, we used to do that in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[9322,"If there is healing in anything, it is in the incision of a cupper, or a drink of honey, or cauterization with fire that causes pain; but I do not like to be cauterized."],[9323,"Whoever from my community carries a debt, then strives to repay it, and dies before paying it off, I am his guardian."],[9324,"Three things: if there is healing in anything, it is the incision of a cupper, or a drink of honey, or cauterization with fire that causes pain. And I dislike cauterization and do not love it."],[9325,"Whoever attacks us at night is not from us."],[9326,"The right of a believer over another believer is six traits: to greet him when he meets him, to respond when he sneezes, to accept when he invites him, to visit him when he is ill, to attend his funeral when he dies, and to advise him sincerely when he is absent."],[9327,"Being killed in the path of Allah expiates everything except debt."],[9328,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what suffices me of this world?' He said, 'Whatever satisfies your hunger and covers your nakedness. And if you have a house to shelter you, that is enough. And if you have a mount, then excellent!'"],[9329,"A spear was planted in front of the Prophet ﷺ at 'Arafat, and he prayed toward it while donkeys passed beyond the spear."],[9330,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he stood for prayer. He stood for a long time, then bowed for a long time, then stood for a long time, then bowed for a long time, then prostrated, then repeated the same. 'Ikrimah said: Ibn 'Abbas said: I was beside the Prophet ﷺ and did not hear the recitation."],[9331,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the hour that is on Friday while on the minbar, and he indicated its brevity."],[9332,"Whoever eats garlic or onion should keep away from us—or: let him keep away from our mosque—or: let him stay in his house."],[9333,"O Abu Basra, the disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine."],[9334,"Drinkers used to be beaten in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ with hands, sandals, and sticks."],[9335,"Whoever has intercourse with a forbidden relative, kill him."],[9336,"There is no prophet but that he warned his community of the Dajjal, and I warn you of the matter of the Dajjal. He is one-eyed, and my Lord is not one-eyed. Written between his eyes is 'kafir,' which the literate and the illiterate can read. With him are a garden and a fire; his fire is a garden and his garden is a fire."],[9337,"Whoever humiliates a friend of Mine has declared war on Me. None of My servants draws near to Me with the like of fulfilling My obligations, and My servant continues to draw near to Me with supererogatory deeds until I love him. When I love him, I am his eyes with which he sees, his ears with which he hears, his hand with which he strikes, and his legs with which he walks. If he calls Me, I answer him; if he asks Me, I give him. I have never hesitated about anything I do as I hesitate about his death, because he hates death and I hate to sadden him."],[9338,"Fame is only here,\" and he pointed with his hand toward the sky."],[9339,"None of you should approach with his garment over his nose, for that is the branding of Satan."],[9340,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying one night, so I stood behind him praying his prayer. When he sat, he made his standing brief and prayed two short rak'ahs, then gave the greeting. Then he stood and prayed two rak'ahs, then gave the greeting so that I could hear it. Then he turned to me and said: 'Take on of deeds what you can bear,' saying it three times."],[9341,"When morning came he used to say: 'I have entered the morning, O Lord, calling You to witness, and calling Your angels, Your prophets, Your messengers, and all Your creation to witness my testimony about myself: I testify that You are God, there is no god but You alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and messenger. I believe in You and rely on You'—he said it three times."],[9342,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited mut'ah. It was only for those who could not find [a wife]. When marriage, divorce, waiting period, and inheritance were revealed, he prohibited it."],[9343,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while there was a curtain hung in the house with pictures on it. I recognized anger in the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I cut it up and made it into two cushions."],[9344,"There is no good in the gathering of women except in a congregational mosque or the funeral of a slain person."],[9345,"When the fitnah of Ibn al-Zubayr occurred, the Haruriyyah sent to him, 'Come to us.' He came to them, stood, and addressed them. He praised Allah. They said, 'We know that your inclination is with us, so come forward so that we may make you caliph.' He said, 'By Allah, my insight concerning you before today was certain, and today my insight concerning you has increased. How can I be with you when I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There will emerge from this nation people who will pass through the religion just as an arrow passes through its target.'"],[9346,"Do not revile 'Ali, for he is devoted to the essence of Allah."],[9347,"Indeed the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution three times [for each limb], and wiped his head once."],[9348,"\"O Messenger of Allah, before you we were People of the Book, and we were commanded to wash away feces and urine.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Indeed Allah has become pleased with you, praised you, and loved you, so do not abandon it.'"],[9349,"We entered upon Umm Salamah, and she said, 'Where are you from?' We said, 'From the people of Kufah.' She said, 'Are you the ones who revile the Prophet ﷺ?' I said, 'I do not know anyone who has reviled the Prophet ﷺ.' She said, 'Rather, you curse 'Ali and those who love him, and the Messenger of Allah used to love him.'"],[9350,"Indeed, when the people of Hell are driven to it, it will meet them and blast them with a scorching blast, leaving no flesh upon bone except that it casts it upon the heel tendons."],[9351,"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said to Marwan b. al-Hakam: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not weep over the religion when you entrust it to its people, but weep over it when you entrust it to other than its people.'"],[9352,"There is no man who is put in charge of ten people except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand bound to his neck, until judgment is passed between him and them."],[9353,"When one of you prays, let him wear his two garments, for Allah is more deserving that one adorn oneself for Him. Whoever does not have two garments, let him wrap a lower garment when he prays, and let none of you wrap himself in his prayer as the Jews wrap themselves."],[9354,"When Allah intends evil for a servant, He makes him enthusiastic about bricks and clay until he builds."],[9355,"I recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Allah is the One who created you from weakness' and he said, 'from weakness.' Then: 'then made after weakness strength' and he said, 'then made after weakness strength.' Then: 'then made after strength weakness' and he said, 'after strength weakness.'"],[9356,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: “And you will drink as the thirsty camels drink.”"],[9357,"A bird was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “O Allah, bring to me the most beloved of Your creation to You, to eat with me from this bird.” Then Ali b. Abi Talib came."],[9358,"A woman may not be married except with the permission of her guardian."],[9359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated at a people's garbage dump, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[9360,"Indeed, when Allah—may His mention be exalted—created Adam, He grasped two handfuls from his loins. Every good one fell into His right hand, and every vile one into His other hand. Then He said: “These are the people of the right, and I do not care; these are the people of Paradise, and these are the people of the Fire.” Then He returned them to Adam's loins, and they are being produced upon that until now."],[9361,"From the signs of the Hour's approach: the crescent moon will be seen in advance, so it will be said, “It is for two nights”; mosques will be taken as thoroughfares; and sudden death will appear."],[9362,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about one who shaved before slaughtering. He said: “No harm.”"],[9363,"Do not benefit from the carcass by its hide or sinew."],[9364,"Bilal stood before the Prophet ﷺ and said: “So-and-so has died and found rest.” The Prophet ﷺ became angry and said: “Only the one forgiven has found rest.”"],[9365,"O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to walk to the House. He said: “Command her to ride, for Allah will not do anything with this hardship of hers.”"],[9366,"He has not honored his father who casts an angry glance at him."],[9367,"Talha approached, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever would like to look at a man who has fulfilled his vow, let him look at Talha.”"],[9368,"The quickest good in reward is maintaining ties of kinship, and the quickest evil in punishment is severing ties of kinship."],[9369,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was among his companions in front of the House, my father came. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever wishes to look at one freed from the Fire, let him look at Abu Bakr."],[9370,"The world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever."],[9371,"Were it not that your people are recent from the age of ignorance, I would order the House to be demolished and insert into it what was taken out of it: the Hijr."],[9372,"When the prayer is called, do not stand until you see me."],[9373,"An infusion was made for the Messenger of God ﷺ in a stone vessel, and he would drink from it that day of his."],[9374,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and began asking the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw his poor appearance, he said: Do you have any wealth? He said: Yes, from all kinds of wealth. God has given me camels, sheep, and horses. He said: If God gives you wealth, let it be seen on you."],[9375,"She had a sheep that she milked. The Prophet ﷺ missed it and said: What happened to your sheep? They said: It died. He said: Why did you not make use of its hide? We said: It is carrion. He said: Its tanning makes it lawful, just as vinegar makes wine lawful."],[9376,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and the ear."],[9377,"What an excellent death it is for a man to die defending his right."],[9378,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ offer the salam to his right and to his left, until the whiteness of his cheeks could be seen."],[9379,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."],[9380,"It is not permissible for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three [days]."],[9381,"Muhammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ, looked at his Lord, Blessed and Exalted. 'Ikrimah said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas: Muhammad looked at his Lord? He said: \"Yes; He made speech for Moses, friendship for Abraham, and the look for Muhammad, ﷺ.\""],[9382,"The Prophet ﷺ married Safiyyah and made her manumission her dower, and he gave a wedding feast of hais on a leather mat."],[9383,"I was given something of it that no one was given except the Messenger of God, ﷺ—meaning sexual intercourse."],[9384,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped and paid the cupper; had it been unlawful, he would not have given him."],[9385,"It used to be said: Among the words of prophethood that people have retained is: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish."],[9386,"The Prophet's ﷺ ring was made of silver."],[9387,"Ibn Mas'ud would narrate for a month without saying, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ.' But when he mentioned the Messenger of God ﷺ, he would say 'like this,' or 'something like this,' or 'close to this,' and he would tremble."],[9388,"A person is with the one he loves."],[9389,"I entered upon 'A'ishah and with her was a blind man; she was cutting citron for him and feeding it to him with honey. I said: Who is this, O Mother of the Believers? She said: This is Ibn Umm Maktum. He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while 'Utbah and Shaybah were with him, and he turned to them, so it was revealed: 'He frowned and turned away because the blind man came to him.' She said: Ibn Umm Maktum."],[9390,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."],[9391,"The servant's feet will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four things: about his life and how he spent it, about his body and how he used it, about his wealth and how he earned it and on what he spent it, and about his love for us, the People of the House."],[9392,"There is no sadaqah (zakat) on the war-horse of a warrior or on his slave."],[9393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade ten traits: dyeing gray hair, plucking it, using saffron (as a dye), letting the lower garment hang below the ankles, tying amulets, playing with dice, seeking refuge by means of incantations (ta‘widhat), wearing a gold ring, displaying adornment inappropriately, withdrawing semen from its proper place, and harming a child without making it unlawful."],[9394,"The Prophet ﷺ offered the funeral prayer for the Negus."],[9395,"She was given as a gift to the Prophet ﷺ, and she had her dolls with her."],[9396,"My standing place was between the shoulders of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the salam, he would say: 'O Allah, make the best of my life its end; O Allah, make the seal of my deeds Your good pleasure; O Allah, make the best of my days the day I meet You.'"],[9397,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in a garment, part of which was on me."],[9398,"He entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together. When he appeared from al-Qadisiyyah, two riders passed by him while he was reciting the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah together. One of them said: 'Do you not hear?' The other said: 'Leave him; he is more astray than his camel.' I was deeply affected by that, and I traveled on until I met someone who informed me about them. I said: 'Who are these two riders?' He said: 'This is Salman b. Rabi‘ah al-Bahili and Zayd b. Suhan.' I came to Madinah and went to ‘Umar and told him what they had said. He said: 'They erred and you were right; you have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.' Then he sent for them and forbade them."],[9399,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him about wiping over the khuffs. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have come to ask you about knowledge.' He said: 'The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge out of love for what he seeks. And about which knowledge do you ask?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, about wiping over the khuffs.' He said: 'Yes. For the resident, one day and one night; and for the traveler, three days, from defecation or urination. Then renew your wudu.'"],[9400,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to announce among the people of Madinah: 'In every prayer there is recitation, even if only the Opening of the Book.'"],[9401,"Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it."],[9402,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ facing the Ka‘bah, sitting with his arms around his legs."],[9403,"The best speech is the Book of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, the worst of matters are their newly invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance. Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs; and whoever leaves a debt or dependents, then it is upon me."],[9404,"Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Aqsa Mosque."],[9405,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw me not holding on to anything—rather I would spend it all—he said to me: 'O Jarir, there is no harm in your holding on to your wealth, for this matter has a duration.'"],[9406,"Seek out the best for the eye and the ear."],[9407,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not complete the fast of any month after Ramadan except Rajab and Sha'ban."],[9408,"Whoever dust enters his interior will never enter the Fire."],[9409,"I caught a bird in Banu Harithah, and Rafi' b. Khadij took it and released it, saying: 'Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared sacred what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah?'"],[9410,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to show kindness to the children of fornication."],[9411,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, he said: 'Allah and His Messenger have forbidden you the drinking of wine and its price, and forbidden you the eating of carrion and its price, and forbidden you pigs, their eating, and their price.' And he said: 'Trim the mustaches, let the beards grow, and do not walk in the markets except with lower garments on you. Indeed, he is not of us who practices a custom other than ours.'"],[9412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon 'Umar with some people from his companions and said: 'Are you believers?' They remained silent—three times—then 'Umar said at the last of them: 'Yes, we believe in what you have brought us, we praise Allah in ease, we are patient in affliction, and we believe in the divine decree.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Believers, by the Lord of the Ka'bah.'"],[9413,"Indeed, Allah's justice on the Day of Resurrection will reach such an extent that He will exact retribution for the hornless sheep from the horned one."],[9414,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once for each limb."],[9415,"Umar b. al-Khattab addressed the people one day on the pulpit of Madinah and said in his sermon: 'Indeed, in the Gardens of Eden there is a palace with five hundred gates, at each gate five thousand houris with wide eyes; none enters it except a prophet.' Then he looked at the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'Congratulations to you, O companion of the grave.' Then he said: 'Or a truthful one.' Then he turned to the grave of Abu Bakr and said: 'Congratulations to you, O Abu Bakr.' Then he said: 'Or a martyr.'"],[9416,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[9417,"I said to Umm Salamah: What was the most frequent supplication of the Prophet ﷺ? She said: “O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.” I said: O Messenger of God, why is this supplication of yours so frequent? He said: “Indeed, the hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful; whichever He wills, He causes to deviate, and whichever He wills, He keeps firm.”"],[9418,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade laughing at passing wind."],[9419,"Ali was commanded to fight the oath-breakers, the transgressors, and the renegades."],[9420,"Were it not that it would become an established practice, I would have commanded the use of the tooth-stick before every prayer."],[9421,"Whoever prays twelve rakʿahs, God will build for him a house in Paradise."],[9422,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, the hyena has devoured us. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, the world will be opened up for you, and would that my community not wear silk brocade.”"],[9423,"A man will be approached in his grave. If he is approached from the direction of his head, his recitation of the Qur’an will repel it; if he is approached from the direction of his hands, his charity will repel it; and if he is approached from the direction of his feet, his walking to the mosques will repel it, and patience will be his shield.” He said: “Indeed, if I were to see a close friend I would be his companion.”"],[9424,"Whoever revives my Sunnah has loved me, and whoever loves me will be with me in Paradise."],[9425,"The Prophet ﷺ did not wipe his face during the prayer."],[9426,"Whoever performs ablution and does it well, and visits his sick Muslim brother seeking reward, will be distanced from Hell by a distance of sixty years’ travel."],[9427,"There is no Muslim man who sees a fault of his brother and conceals it except that God will admit him to Paradise because of it."],[9428,"Fasting makes the flesh wither and keeps one away from the heat of the Blaze. Indeed, Allah has a table spread upon which is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined. None shall sit at it except those who fast."],[9429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us at the mosque of al-Khayf in Mina and said: May Allah brighten [the face of] a person who hears my words and memorizes them, then conveys them to one who has not heard them. For many a bearer of fiqh is not a faqih, and many a bearer of fiqh conveys it to one who has more fiqh than him. Three things do not cause the heart of a believer to harbor treachery: sincerity of action for Allah, sincere counsel to those whom Allah has placed in authority over you, and adhering to the community of Muslims, for their supplication encompasses [them] from behind them."],[9430,"For the people of La ilaha illa Allah there is no loneliness at death, nor at the grave."],[9431,"Whoever recites Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad fifty times every day will be called on the Day of Resurrection from his grave: Arise and enter Paradise."],[9432,"The people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter."],[9433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a Bedouin while he was supplicating in his prayer, saying: O You whom eyes do not see, and thoughts do not mix with, and describers cannot describe, and events do not change, and who does not fear misfortunes. He knows the weights of mountains, the measures of seas, the number of raindrops, the number of leaves on trees, and the number of what the night darkens upon and the day shines upon. No heaven can conceal from Him another heaven, nor any earth another earth, nor any sea what is in its depths, nor any mountain what is in its rugged paths. Make the best of my life its end, the best of my deeds their final ones, and the best of my days the day I meet You. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned a man to watch the Bedouin and said: When he finishes praying, bring him to me. When he had prayed, the man brought him. Some gold from certain mines had been gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Bedouin came to him, he gave him the gold and said: From which tribe are you, O Bedouin? He said: From Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you know why I gave you the gold? He said: Because of the kinship between us and you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Kinship has its right, but I gave you the gold because of your excellent praise of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[9434,"I entered upon A'ishah and she said: From where are you? I said: From the people of Egypt. She said: How did you find Ibn Khadij in this expedition of yours? I said: We found him the best of commanders; whenever a horse of one of our men died, he gave him a horse. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: O Allah, whoever is given authority over any affair of my Ummah and is gentle with them, be gentle with him; and whoever makes it hard for them, make it hard for him."],[9435,"He never prayed an obligatory prayer without performing Qunut in it."],[9436,"The lightest of women in dowry are the greatest of them in blessing."],[9437,"Indeed, Allah has an angel who calls out at every prayer: O children of Adam, rise to your fires that you have kindled upon yourselves, and extinguish them with prayer."],[9438,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[9439,"Whoever dies while seeking knowledge will meet Allah and there will be nothing between him and the prophets except the degree of prophethood."],[9440,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done and gave him his wages."],[9441,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ sat in prayer, he placed his left foot under his left thigh, spread his right foot, put his left hand on his knee, put his right hand on his right thigh, and pointed with his finger."],[9442,"He entered the house upon ʿUthmān while he was besieged in it, and he heard Abū Hurayrah asking ʿUthmān for permission to speak, so he permitted him. He stood, praised God, and extolled Him, then said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'After me there will be trials and differences.' A man among the people said: 'Who is for us, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'Adhere to the amīr and his companions,' and he was pointing to ʿUthmān."],[9443,"Guard yourselves from people by suspicion."],[9444,"A man will be given allegiance between the Rukn and the Maqām, as many as the people of Badr. Then the bands of the people of Iraq and the abdāl of the people of Syria will come to him. An army from the people of Syria will raid him, until when they are at al-Baydāʾ, they will be swallowed up. Then a man from Quraysh whose maternal uncles are from Kalb will raid them. They will meet, and God will defeat them. So the loser is the one who loses out on the spoils of Kalb."],[9445,"A man from my household will rule, with a broad forehead and a hooked nose. He will fill the earth with fairness and justice just as it was filled with oppression and tyranny. He will live for this—and he spread his right palm, and spread two fingers beside it, and spread his left palm."],[9446,"We were forbidden to follow a funeral procession accompanied by wailing."],[9447,"On my door was a durnūk with horses having wings. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Remove this.'"],[9448,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray at night while I was lying across between him and the qiblah. When he wanted to perform witr, he woke me, and I slipped away from in front of him."],[9449,"I have pardoned you regarding horses and slaves, and there is no zakāh on what is less than two hundred."],[9450,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution and wipe his head once."],[9451,"Makkah is sacred; its residents are not expelled, its trees are not cut, and its game is not startled."],[9452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from the flesh of domesticated donkeys, in order to spare the riding animals."],[9453,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Muzdalifah, he ordered the weak members of his family to go ahead at night, and he said: \"Do not throw the pebbles at the Jamrah until the sun rises.\""],[9454,"All of Muzdalifah is a place of standing (Mash'ar), but keep away from the interior of 'Uranah. All of 'Arafat is a standing place, but keep away from the valley of Muhassir."],[9455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pass his hand over our shoulders during the prayer and say: \"Make the shoulders level, straighten the rows, and do not differ, lest your hearts differ.\""],[9456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[9457,"Allah erases whatever He wills except wretchedness and happiness, and life and death."],[9458,"The Prophet ﷺ took hold of the muscle of my calf."],[9459,"Ya'qub b. Ishaq narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Wahb b. Jarir narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, from Qays b. Sa'd, from al-Hajjaj b. Artah, from al-Minhal b. 'Amr, the hadith of the grave, the hadith of Zadhan, from al-Bara', from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of al-A'mash. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hajjaj except Qays b. Sa'd, and no one from Qays b. Sa'd except Jarir b. Hazim, and no one from Jarir except Wahb. Ishaq b. Abi Isra'il was alone in transmitting it."],[9460,"The forelocks are not placed (shaved) except in Hajj or 'Umrah."],[9461,"The Prophet ﷺ trained horses and made them race. He saw me riding a camel and said: \"O Jabir, you will keep on urging it,\" meaning, you will keep on beating it."],[9462,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf on his mount, and in his hand was a staff with a hooked end with which he touched the corner."],[9463,"There is no loneliness in their graves or at their resurrection for the people of \"La ilaha illallah,\" and it is as if I am looking at the people of \"La ilaha illallah\" shaking the dust from their heads and saying: \"Praise be to Allah who has removed from us sorrow.\""],[9464,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set out on a military expedition and said: \"No one who has harmed his neighbor may accompany us today.\" A man from the group said: \"I urinated at the base of my neighbor's wall?\" He said: \"You will not accompany us today.\""],[9465,"The Messenger of God ﷺ disliked seven parts of the sheep: the gall bladder, the urinary bladder, the uterus, the penis, the two testicles, the gland, and the blood. And the part of the sheep most beloved to the Messenger of God ﷺ was its front portion."],[9466,"Regarding the words of God, Mighty and Majestic: \"Forgiver of sin, Accepter of repentance, severe in punishment, Owner of abundance. There is no deity except Him; to Him is the destination\" (Q 40:3). He said: \"Forgiver of sin\" for the one who says, \"There is no deity except God\"; \"Accepter of repentance\" from the one who says, \"There is no deity except God\"; \"severe in punishment\" for the one who does not say, \"There is no deity except God\"; \"Owner of abundance\" means Owner of richness. \"There is no deity except Him\"—the disbelievers of Quraysh did not declare His oneness, so He declared His own oneness. \"To Him is the destination\"—to Him returns the one who says, \"There is no deity except God,\" and he enters Paradise; and the one who does not say, \"There is no deity except God\" returns, and He will make him enter the Fire."],[9467,"Regarding the words of God, Mighty and Majestic: \"And by the witness and the witnessed\" (Q 85:3). He said: The witness is my grandfather, the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the witnessed is the Day of Resurrection. Then he recited this verse: \"Indeed, We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of good tidings, and a warner\" (Q 48:8). Then he recited: \"That is a day for which the people will be assembled, and that is a day witnessed\" (Q 11:103)."],[9468,"There is no servant who prays the morning prayer, then sits remembering God until the sun rises, except that he will have a screen from Hell."],[9469,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to seek forgiveness seventy times in the pre-dawn hours."],[9470,"Some Bedouins came to the Messenger of God ﷺ at midday, wearing swords and wrapped in striped cloaks. The Messenger of God ﷺ urged the people to give them charity, saying: \"Let the owner of a dinar give from his dinar, the owner of a dirham from his dirham, the owner of wheat from his wheat, the owner of barley from his barley, and the owner of dates from his dates, before a day comes upon him when he will look ahead and see nothing but the Fire, look to his right and see nothing but the Fire, look to his left and see nothing but the Fire, look behind him and see nothing but the Fire, and he will not find anything with which to protect his face from the Fire.\""],[9471,"The imam is responsible, and the muezzin is entrusted. O God, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."],[9472,"The best charity is that which leaves one self-sufficient. The upper hand is better than the lower hand. And begin with those you support."],[9473,"Indeed, the people of Paradise will see the people of the highest chambers just as the people of this world see a brilliant star in the sky. And indeed, Abu Bakr and 'Umar will be among them, and how excellent they are."],[9474,"We entered upon al-Mughira b. Shu'ba while he was governor of Kufa, and Sa'id b. Zayd was with him. Ghunaym b. 'Alqama entered and said: \"Who is 'Ali?\" Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Abu Bakr is in Paradise, 'Umar is in Paradise, 'Ali is in Paradise, and 'Uthman is in Paradise.'\""]]);
